onological order given I can still refer back to the tapes if I needed to \u2013 but screw it. I prefer relying on my brain even if it is a little scrambled. A vamp I didn\u2019t know showed up not long after Truman, Rebecca, and Neon. They call themselves Anarchs but they seem pretty cool to me. Truman said the new vamp\u2019s name was Lacey Hart and she was friends with Maxwell, the leader of the city. I decided I\u2019d be the one to make contact this time and it was weird. She acted like she knew me, but no surprise, I had no recollection of her. And I think I would\u2019ve remembered someone like her. She was lovely and just had a way about her. I\u2019m not saying I was attracted to her but for the first time that I\u2019m aware of I can honestly say I looked twice at another woman. She was just neat to be around you know? She was charming. Not like Anders but still. I went back to my guy pretty quickly. Not because I was running from Lacey, I just wanted to be with my date. Unfortunately that\u2019s when we discovered that Chandra\u2019d left the security room. With at least four, maybe more vampires in the house.<br /> <br /> Alexia found her and based on what I could hear through the curl Chandra convinced Alexia that she was safe to be off and floating along around the party guests. The invisibility thing she can do I guess. But that didn\u2019t mean one of the vamps wouldn\u2019t see her. We don\u2019t know what all they can do after all. I let Alexia know how bad an idea this was, but considering she was already agitated by whatever Chandra had said it didn\u2019t really make much of a difference. Alexia was in a bad mood for the rest of the night and that\u2019s just not natural.<br /> <br /> The party was well underway when a couple of Doc\u2019s werewolf friends showed up, none of us have a problem with them so that was no big deal. Except not long after that Zed and two others from Mallard\u2019s pack came in too. Now the Bluffs\u2019 technically in Mallard\u2019s pack\u2019s territory but it\u2019s Simon\u2019s damn house. Doc got to them first and told them they were welcome but so were his friends from the other pack. One of the were\u2019s got pissed at him for it and took it as an insult or something. Pretty sure Simon smoothed things over later but what the hell man?<br /> <br /> I get you don\u2019t go into someone else\u2019s territory, but the Bluffs is OUR territory and we damn well say who is and isn\u2019t welcome. Simon\u2019s word is law here \u2013 literally. So that werechick needed a serious attitude adjustment but apparently we weren\u2019t giving those out last night. No, instead we played nice and Doc left them alone. Jazz warned Deidre and Tanya that they were there but they were cool, they weren\u2019t interested in causing problems. Neither was Noriko when she showed up\u2026well, not the gonna get violent kind of problems anyway.<br /> <br /> At one point I caught her stalking something or someone in the lounge and Doc went to check it out. Guess he thought he was being cute baiting the werecat with a curtain tie-back but trust me, he did not get the reaction he was looking for! Noriko pounced him and I\u2019m not sure she wouldn\u2019t have succeeded in having her way with him if we weren\u2019t connected through the ear curls. I started up a stream of \u201cYou\u2019re not seriously\u2026dude, my eyes\u2026Nat\u2019s gonna kill you\u201d sort of crap and he jumped back. Let Noriko down gently from what I could hear but I was also in the process of picking on him as Nat asked for the video footage for later funtimes.<br /> <br /> That chick ain\u2019t right sometimes I swear. Still, hey, if it helped her see Doc was the one for her then by all means. She could have the footage. I think me agreeing to that embarrassed Doc and disgusted Jazz. But what the hell right? I don\u2019t know maybe it was tasteless to agree to it, but I kind of want Nat to get jealous. Maybe if that happens she\u2019ll give Doc the attention he deserves. He\u2019s a damn good guy even if he does piss me off on occasion (seriously, who doesn\u2019t?). And good guys are in short supply in the world. I was OK with this whole triangle deal she, Karen, and Doc set up to begin with but it seems to me like Doc gets the short end of the stick most of the time so I\u2019m getting less cool with it. Anytime Nat starts falling apart she goes to Karen. If Karen gets jealous then she gets like hours or maybe days of Nat\u2019s focus. What does Doc get? To bust his ass so he can impress his girl with a romantic dance at her goth ball and she just sort of \u201cMeh\u2019s\u201d it away and returns to her booth. I know. I know. Judge not\u2026but damnit, I am SO judging!<br /> <br /> And yeah, I jumped ahead in the night but dude? My damn journal. I can bounce around if I want to. See, it was getting late, like around two or so I think? And Doc asked for the dance he\u2019d requested. Nat seemed kind of reluctant, but put on one of her compositions (again as he requested) and came down to the dancefloor. A circle was formed, kind of like when BonnieLynn &amp; Marshal danced (I\u2019ll get to that in a minute) and Simon made the spotlights appear \u2013 considering the Sheriff (sort of an enforcer for the vamp big wigs) of the city just showed up that might not\u2019ve been the best idea \u2013 but what do I know? Anyway it was a gorgeous dance. You could tell Doc really worked hard because three weeks ago? He was tripping over his own feet and stepping on toes. He\u2019s been practicing. Jazz and I were both feeling the love considering how much effort he put into that but once it was done Nat just went back to work. Not even a kiss.<br /> <br /> Y\u2019know, considering how many of the weres are lusting after Doc maybe he should take \u2018em up on it. I\u2019m not sure Nat\u2019s worth it in the romance department. Maybe she\u2019s too enamored with women to truly give this thing with Doc a go? I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019d say she\u2019s giving it her best shot and Doc would tell me to butt out if I ever said anything (which I won\u2019t\u2026for now) but anyway, I\u2019m beginning to think they might not be the best match.<br /> <br /> Speaking of matches I totally made one last night! Jazz was kind of sad (all those goths, and the sad one is the Olympic athlete \u2013 so weird) and she was talking with Alexia about how she felt so alone and a bit ignored. OK \u2013 first \u2013 she was a freakin\u2019 shadow most of the night and second \u2013 the woman is not approachable! She\u2019s a sweetheart and she cares deeply but she looks so remote. I can tell you men are intimidated by that sort of look, so she kind of got herself into that position all on her own. Still, given I overheard all this through the ear curls I asked Anders if he would dance with her. He said he would but thought she\u2019d be uncomfortable dancing with my date. (side note: I kind of thought he was gonna say boyfriend or something but he stopped at the last minute \u2013 probably reading too much into things but is he looking to make this thing more\u2026exclusive?) Anyway I sort of cursed and had to agree with him so I headed downstairs pulled Simon\u2019s earcurl out (made him jump which was kind of funny) and asked him if his friend (the guy, not the mysterious chick) was single. He seemed kind of confused at first but said he was. When I explained I wanted him to get the guy to dance with Jazz he readily agreed.<br /> <br /> I stuck around so I could see if things worked out. Honestly I was only wanting her to get a dance, nothing major, but about the time Simon talked to his friend that Sheriff guy came in and Jazz went to the shadows to track him. I couldn\u2019t get a read off him, but he gave me a look\u2026yeah, that look like I give people when I\u2019m reading them. Not sure what he got off it, but he didn\u2019t make any threatening moves and our vampire friends took off so they didn\u2019t come into contact with him so nothing to worry about.<br /> <br /> That being the case I badgered Jazz until she reappeared and just as she made the snarky comment about no one lining up to see her Julian approached. SCORE! The look on her face\u2026I think I might blow up the video still from that moment. Shock doesn\u2019t begin to describe it, HA! Then she went off and danced with him\u2026and danced with him again\u2026and then let him get her a drink and they talked for the rest of the night. I so rock in finding her a dude that seems to get her! *fistpump*<br /> <br /> Oh yeah \u2013 I almost forgot \u2013 Bonnie Lynn and Marshal had a beautiful moment. Doc took care of Marshal and Jazz played ladies maid to Bonnie. They escorted them to the stairs, they met on the landing and Marshal took Bonnie Lynn\u2019s hand and led her to the floor. Simon took care of the effects, Nat had the perfect music for them and everyone there could tell it was a truly special moment for them. Good for Marshal, he stuck around, he stayed to guard the woman he loved, he deserved the happy ending.<br /> <br /> When Jazz married the two of them at dawn they faded away, moving on to share their afterlife and for that moment I think we all felt pretty good. Jazz was actually happy, I mean the smile reached her eyes and there was no sadness in her eyes. I think I was happier about that than anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> June 14 Monday \u2013 Midnight<br /> <br /> My god we have got drama in the Bluffs!<br /> <br /> My hand was cramping and my coffee cup was empty after I finished writing about the party so I went downstairs to get a refill and give the writing a break. I came into the kitchen to hear Alexia proclaiming that she was responsible! (yes, you could hear the exclamation point) Jazz had her \u201cthis is serious and I\u2019m displeased\u201d look on her face. Damnit all to hell we just had her happy less than eight hours ago! I had to know what put that look on her face so I asked what was going on. Alexia didn\u2019t want to talk about it so I refilled my coffee and Jazz went back upstairs with me to fill me in.<br /> <br /> It seems that Chandra\u2019s disappearing act at the party happened because she\u2019s been feeding off Trinh, Jazz\u2019s student they helped out while I was road tripping. Alexia asked Chandra to stop this a while back but our resident blood sucker is a bit obsessed with her, so she apparently hung around her until she left the Bluffs Saturday night. That obsession? It\u2019s caused by Chandra\u2019s compulsion to make Trinh a Penanggalan like her. Do I really need to say how much of a bad idea this is? If Chandra does anything to that girl I will kill her. It\u2019s that simple. I get she\u2019s a different kind of vampire so the whole stake through the heart thing might not work for her (does it work for the more common vamps? I\u2019m going to need to investigate) but one way or another she\u2019s toast if she does it. Apparently, according to Jazz the only reason Chandra isn\u2019t indulging her need to procreate is Alexia. Since Alexia asked her not to she won\u2019t do it, but Jazz says the implication is clear. The minute Alexia gives the OK, Trinh is Chandra\u2019s very own bloodshake. And the sad thing is? Alexia will give the OK. She\u2019s a marshmellow when it comes to Chandra. She can\u2019t say no to her for long, she enjoys making her happy and normally I\u2019d think that\u2019s pretty cool \u2013 but lets not forget Chandra\u2019s a damn vampire! She acts like a brainless idiot but she\u2019s no dummy. We have no idea how long she\u2019s been on this earth and she knows exactly how to play Alexia.<br /> <br /> And you know something? Even ignoring the fact that I\u2019m one step away from going Buffy on that chick there\u2019s all those other vampires out there. I\u2019m pretty sure they\u2019d notice if a newbie vampire showed up. And I can\u2019t see that going well.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not a great situation but Jazz and I decided we needed to talk to Nat, Simon, and Doc about the situation. They need to know about it so they can keep an eye on Alexia and make sure she doesn\u2019t pull an \u201cOh, you\u2019re so sweet, of course you can drain that kid dry!\u201d<br /> <br /> We tabled everything since Nat was holed up with Karen (I\u2019ve been on my soapbox on that topic, not going there again\u2026today) and neither of us had seen Doc and Simon had left early that morning. I didn\u2019t want to be cooped up in my room all day so I went downstairs with Jazz to help with the cleanup efforts. No way were we getting a cleaning crew in this house so it was up to us. I was picking up trash in the ballroom when Tavia and Chandra came through. I did good not threatening Chandra. But then Tavia asked to see the security tapes. Well hell, I\u2019d already wiped them so I told her so. She nodded and continued on as if nothing was said but Chandra stopped and waited until she was out of the room before telling me that Tavia never needs to see the footage as she\u2019s certain the girls Simon danced with at the party were in danger.<br /> <br /> OK, now let\u2019s put this into perspective. The bloodsucking vampire is worried about the girls Simon danced with and Tavia the Unstable is trying to be casual about getting a better look at those girls. Uh, hell no. C\u2019mon now, I\u2019m not an idiot, I made backups to the footage just in case. But my file system is not exactly logical to anyone but me so I didn\u2019t figure she\u2019d find them if she decided to go looking. Just in case though I went up to the security room and sure enough she was there and staring at the computer.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if she even knows how to use a computer but I was not about to let Tavia go messing with the state of the art system I put together. I explained once more that the footage was gone but I don\u2019t think she believed me. Her eyes went kind of flat and emotionless. When she left I shut the door texted Doc a 911 and waited for him to get there. Well I told him about Tavia and he said Simon hooked up with someone else but he didn\u2019t know how serious the hookup was. He also told me that Simon and Tavia were together \u2013 it isn\u2019t just in Tavia\u2019s head like we kind of thought it was. I mean I knew he was playing the part of lord of the manor with her as his lady, but I didn\u2019t realize it was more than just placating her. He\u2019s involved with her and apparently someone else as well \u2013 isn\u2019t that just perfect? Since Doc\u2019s taken on this whole big brother role for both Simon and Tavia I suggested he talk to Tavia and try to get her to get off the murderous rampage. We\u2019ll see if it works. When he left you better believe I encrypted and transferred the backups onto a flash drive and pocketed it. It\u2019s going to the office \u2013 or maybe a safe deposit box tomorrow. The security computer is now password protected to the point that I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019m the only one that will be getting into that system any time soon.<br /> <br /> Simon got back a bit before dinner and Doc drafted him and some of Alexia\u2019s cookies into going over to Mallard\u2019s so he could apologize for the insult to Erin. Total crap as far as I\u2019m concerned but hey \u2013 I\u2019m not the \u201cface\u201d or the one that has to play nice in this Krewe. I\u2019m here to protect the rest of them and make sure the ghosts are able to move on to their just rewards, end of story. Over dinner Doc told us that Mallard accepted the apology and Doc seemed to think he\u2019d be talking to Erin about the situation as well. I hope it\u2019s to give her a smackdown.<br /> <br /> Simon left again after dinner. He said he had to get some things from the store and Alexia gave him a list of things as well. Nat went to clean up the dj area and Doc headed to the library to research something. Jazz and Tavia decided to clean up Bonnie Lynn\u2019s room so I took the opportunity to take off and go have a beer and watch the game with some folks that would be blessedly drama free. Cops. But damnit the Tigers beat the Pirates by one freakin\u2019 run. Time for bed, least in my dreams the Pirates are already in the world series.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, June 14 \u2013 Lunch<br /> <br /> Uneventful morning at the office but the backups are tucked away and safe. The highlight was email flirting with Anders, he can be quite talkative when he feels like it. We\u2019re giving the Finding Ritual this afternoon. Hopefully will get a bead on Shatina\u2019s brother. If not, at least we\u2019re going to meet Cock Robin tonight, he should be able to give us a better idea about what to do with these fetches. And now\u2026lunch.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> Dramadramadramadramadrama<br /> <br /> First note, Jasmine was more on the money then Doc was about Chandra and Tavia's hand signals. This would explain Doc's players reaction though.<br /> <br /> I'd note that Old Man Malard's name is less...ducky...then Gwen's spelling. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'll also note the meeting with Cock Robin was slated for Tuesday, not Monday...that will be important later.<br /> <br /> So people seem to be having it out for people's SOs. That's fascinating. Certainly creating tension within the Krewe. I asked Doc's player how it felt to be the sanest member of the Krewe. He said Doc was cool with it but he was terrified....he along with Natalie being the PTSD sufferers.<br /> <br /> Chandra's discussion with Alexia and Jasmine was pretty extensive, moreso then Jasmine recorded in terms of their issues especially with pregnant women (and Chandra's attempts to avoid pregnant women) and some pretty serious love declarations (Chandra said she would rather have been stillborn then never meet Alexia, and that meant becoming a vampire).<br /> <br /> Natalie actually spent more of the first day after asleep then anything else. Chemicals did a number on her body the day before, Psyche resistance or no.<br /> <br /> Comments and questions welcome.<br /> <br /> Join us next time when our heroes plans go awry and they learn the difference between Owlspiders and Spiderowls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T02:53:44-08:00","id":16025,"title":"","content":"ournals time! As per, most arrived last minute. No Gwen journal this time, her player has threatened to\u2026we may get a combo journal or she may send it individually\u2026if she does I will add it here. Anyway, we ready?<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0745 Hours, Wednesday, June 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Well this has been exciting and informative. In much the same way as learning about new artillery while being in the firing line is exciting and informative. I think the Owlspider left bigger holes though. I\u2019m getting ahead of myself...and I might also still be a little drunk. We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Rose got the Finding ceremony to work this time and did so very well. She had a strong sense of what direction Jamie was in so we loaded up with Ronin and Snowflake driving before heading out. Unsurprisingly, I noticed we were heading into the shitty part of town. We never get to deal with bizarre scary things in the ritzy part of town. Anyway, we pulled up to an area surrounded by and old rusty fence. The fence wasn\u2019t locked so Cupcake opened the gate and we headed in.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m no urban planner but when we immediately started seeing bookshelves overgrown with thorny vines, I was pretty sure we skipped Kansas altogether. None of the books looked weathered or water marked, Cupcake even pulled one off the shelf. Nothing happened so we asked our compass where North was. Rose said we had pulls from two directions but that the gate we came in was gone. Now don\u2019t ask why we all had to turn around to verify she wasn\u2019t making it up, but all we could see was down the same path we were standing on. No sign of our cars or anything about the normal world. Poda Kansas. That was about the time Ronin started bugging out. Rose said she thought we were in the Hedge, the magical otherworld of the Changelings. Ronin never really pays attention to the Faerie stuff, so when Rose said Hedge in her accent (we were rattled, accents happen) Ronin heard \u201cHidge\u201d and had no idea what that referred to. After a few minutes of almost comical repetition, I finally stepped and translated hoping we could focus on getting out. So while we\u2019re all looking around for the Yellow Brick Road, Cupcake tries to use her phone. That\u2019s when she hears someone already on the other end asking where we are. He told her something about not worrying because he\u2019d find us. If he said anything about her little dog too, I missed that part. Likely because Cupcake lost her shit about that time. It was more than a little disconcerting to be in a place where none of the normal rules apply. I mean the Dominions have the Old Laws and the Underworld has the Rivers, so there\u2019s also some control. I thought maybe Snowflake could just zone out and look around to find another way out, so I said as much. His trance went weird though as he didn\u2019t just go into a trance but went catatonic and started drooling. I snapped him out of it eventually and made sure he was still as together as when we started. Snowflake said that when he looked around it just went on forever. Then he said he wanted to try something else. This time I stayed by him to monitor...not sure what I thought I could do other than slap him to get him to come to, but still. Snowflake was able to look around a little more and found these human-sized, spider-mouthed owls in robes tending to the books on the shelves. In a different section was a blood-covered horse, just walking around. So many cowboy jokes now but it was terrifying at the time. Then he found the truly horrible creatures we were trying to mentally prepare for; whispering wolves with children\u2019s faces, all looking for something\u2026likely us.<br /> <br /> Now we had the lay of the land in as much as we were willing to let Snowflake sacrifice what\u2019s left of his mind to find out. We had to figure out what to do with this recon intel. The Dog let me know that there was no Twilight here. Apparently it\u2019s an all in one kinda deal. The others seemed to come to that same conclusion. That\u2019s about the time Rose unlocked her Primeval Caul and went all Cat Girl. There was a slight glow coming from Ronin\u2019s eyes as she started looking around. I\u2019m pretty sure she supertuned her senses because she started hearing where things were before anyone else. She found one of the upright walking owls, with spider mandibles and eight eyes so I decided to try and talk to it. It looked at us but didn\u2019t seem to care. I tried to speak with it in English but that didn\u2019t get very far. Then I unlocked the Primeval Marionette. I didn\u2019t think I could control it, but it helps when talking to animals. And it worked this time too. It gave what it even said were bad directions for a way to get out. Not the first left, but one of the others. Polite conversation kept it talking a little. Apparently dreams help them make these books. I saw it spin one before shelving it, while it ate another before we started talking. It said that books were filled with knowledge. I looked at a few but they were written in a language and scripting style I\u2019d never seen before. Probably some crazy dream language only Changelings can read.<br /> <br /> I thanked the Spiderowl and moved ahead based on his directions. We skipped the first left altogether, but noticed a big freakish tree on the right with purple fruit the size of my head. I don\u2019t know why we even thought about it, but we determined as a group that it would not be a good idea to eat any. Maybe it\u2019s because we didn\u2019t have any food or had no idea how long we\u2019d be struck there. You know, little things. Then we came to section of shelves with books scattered all over the ground. For a second, I had a mental image of the Howling Dead charging through the silent halls of the Underworld library. I didn\u2019t really have time to say anything because the ground started rumbling and this car-sized spider with two eyes and an owl\u2019s beak crawled up in front of us. Five more the size of Great Dane\u2019s scuttled out as well. It was weird because they looked like they were trying to be as quiet as something that makes the ground rumble could be. Made me think there was something more bad ass nearby they didn\u2019t want to deal with. <br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure if it was because I had the Primeval Marionette unlocked or just stupid luck (ha, luck witch has bad luck) but the big Owlspider decided to attack me first. I didn\u2019t have any Shroud up yet, so it would have torn out my liver if I hadn\u2019t Bulwarked the hit. Still hurt like taking shrapnel though. I immediately put up my Primeval Shroud at that point. Which was good considering the damn thing bit into me again right after that. That didn\u2019t hurt nearly as bad. More like a knife wound. But it did piss me off, so I grew my own pointy claws from my Shroud, slashed the hell out of it, and snarled like a real beast. Then I channeled Plasm into my body to make myself stronger and tougher. I could feel my muscles ripple and swell just before it hit me again, but this time it was really minor. What I didn\u2019t think about at the time was that I was tapping myself out too fast. Ronin finished it off with her Stillness Rage. I mean I guess that\u2019s what she did. She didn\u2019t make any sound and suddenly pieces of the thing sliced off like daggers were going crazy on it. Between us, we put it down but that still left the \u201cbaby\u201d ones.<br /> <br /> I had been pretty busy with the big one, and really didn\u2019t think about what it could do to me. I was just keeping it from hurting the others until we could take it down. The others were dealing with the smaller beasts and honestly having a much better time of it. I mentioned that I was going through Plasm too fast before, but I didn\u2019t really realize until I turned to fight the rest of this nest. I got a glancing shot off one just before it took a chunk out of my arm. But instead of white smoke, all I had was real blood running out. Rose had been handling things as one was down and several others were looking bad. One was kind of swimming in the dirt very slowly and Snowflake was causally walking away so I turned and ripped into it. By the time, I looked back they had finished with the rest too. At that point, Plasm and adrenaline weren\u2019t keeping me up anymore...and neither did my legs. I was a pile of steaming white smoke and blood. I tore up my shirt to bind my wounds in hopes that I could stop the bleeding, then noticed that Cupcake and Ronin needed some healin\u2019 done too. I didn\u2019t have the Plasm to even heal me, but I could make us all stop bleeding so that was the first order. Well after getting me on my feet again anyway. I was the worst of us, though Ronin wasn\u2019t far behind me and Cupcake was just caught off guard but it was still not a pretty sight. We knew we couldn\u2019t just sit around and wait since the wolves were out there so Ronin and Rose helped me move til Ronin heard something again. <br /> <br /> Rose went to scout it out since it was off to the left of the path. She came back a little bit later and said that we\u2019d want to go that way, but we really shouldn\u2019t. No one really felt like arguing the point so we kept moving. This time I was able to walk on my own at least so we organized with Rose and Cupcake up front, Nightshade and Snowflake in the middle, and Rose and me in the back. This seemed like the best formation right now given our list of injuries. The next left came up, but Rose found a lake with a sign that said \u201cBeware of \u201c and had a huge jagged bite taken out at the bottom. Clearly not the way, so we kept moving. I was feeling better as we went, but I knew I\u2019d be wet paper if we got into any real fight. The next left we found Rose didn\u2019t find anything but more books so we headed that way. Moving a little ways in, we started hearing books slamming together. When we looked behind, books were flying off the ground into a humanoid shape. It seems silly now, but we tried to talk to this one too. It growled and started pulling more books off the vine-wrapped shelves and getting bigger. That was NOT what we needed. But things got even more special because Ronin heard something else coming from the way we had been and still should have been going. Rose immediately went to check it out.<br /> <br /> We were slowly backing up and trying to figure out what the hell we could do to a huge pile of books when Ronin got a weird look on her face and turned back in the direction Rose ran off. She said something about Rose found Mongler. The next thing I know, there\u2019s a Tyrannosaurus Rex with beefy human arms, wielding this massive great axe made from what looked like dinosaur teeth running straight for us with Rose racing to keep up. Rose was waving us off so we didn\u2019t attack and it ran right past us. This thing was like twelve foot tall and roaring. I didn\u2019t really want to deal with that ever so I was glad to know it was on our side. When I turned back, it was the Battle of the Colossi. The Book Beast had grown from all the extra books and DinoMan was just huge to start with. We were beaten, bruised, and bloody but there was no way we were going to just run like Mongler was yelling for us to do. I still had my claws, Ronin had her Rage, and Nightshade smiled and held out a lighter to Cupcake. Rose was up in the fight already. We knew what to do.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not proud of destroying knowledge and I\u2019d never sanction a book burning, but in this one case those books held knowledge that could kill. We walked away from the smoldering pile with Mongler, or Grin or whatever the hell his nickname is. But the weird started creeping back in again. Mongler said it was lucky we went missing on a day we were suppose to meet with him. I was confused. Rose never gets her schedules mixed up and she specifically said that we were meeting Mongler tomorrow. That\u2019s when we learned that we\u2019d lost a day and it was now Tuesday night. Eventually we came to a spot that he knew something about and opened a door into his office. It was about midnight or so on Tuesday according to the clock in his office. Though Mongler looked like Mongler again and that big ass axe looked like a normal walking stick. Ronin could still see something as she briefly started tracing out where the axe was. Guess she could still see through the Illusion or something. That\u2019s good to know.<br /> <br /> We realized that the cars were still in the shit hole where we left them. Ronin, Nightshade, Snowflake, Rose, and Cupcake\u2019s phones start receiving notifications for everyone that was freaking out looking for them. My phone was silent. I knew that the one that should be worried about me was right there with me the whole time and I had protected her as best I could. Still even Mongler had a call from Gretchen waiting and he hadn\u2019t been gone for almost two days. I\u2019m not entirely sure why it weighed on me so much, but I suddenly knew what it meant to have a heavy heart. Thankfully I was pulled from my emoboy thoughts by the realization that we couldn\u2019t go home yet until we had the cars. Cupcake offered to just loan her Jeeps out so we could split up and get everything taken care of. I asked Mongler if he wanted to see something cool and then \u201cpressed a button\u201d on Cupcake\u2019s shoulder. She popped out both Jeeps from her arms and Mongler\u2019s eyes got really big. That was worth it. Cheered me up for the moment too. Then Cupcake let the others take one Jeep to get their cars, and she drove Nightshade and I back to Dark Haven Bluffs.<br /> <br /> I headed straight for the liquor cabinet while Karen and Chandra had a fit over Nightshade and Cupcake coming in. Tavia was a basket case even though she had already talked to Snowflake on the phone. I had already finished off a bottle of Grey Goose, gotten the Johnny Walker Double Black down, and found my suture kit by the time the others got home. I was just going to stitch myself up as best I could and drink the rest of the pain away. Snowflake and Nightshade keep enough booze in the house for me to get at least a little drunk and that\u2019s what I was working on. Rose offered to help stitch me back together...and I could tell that she wanted desperately to help. I\u2019ve never let anyone else stitch me up, but I figured what the hell. I asked Nightshade for her handcuffs, chained myself to the couch so I couldn\u2019t jump too far, and keep the bottle with me. I was not drunk enough to let someone else stitch me up. I managed to not scream like a baby and just kept drinking. Nightshade actually kept bringing me water, which was not helping to dull the pain, but she was paying me attention so I made no complains. Keeping me hydrated was a good plan, I just wasn\u2019t running on good plan mode. I called Sebastian to apologize for not showing up and said I got mugged. Then I went back to my room to finish the Johnny Walker I had. I went to sleep after a bottle of Jim Beam Knob Creek and one of Bombay Sapphire. Four bottles in about two hours I think. Yeah I\u2019m gonna have to refill the bar this afternoon.<br /> <br /> But now I gotta get a shower and go to work. Meditation, breakfast, and all that. Mmmm eggs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, June 15, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> It seems odd, having missed a day in my diary, mostly because I actually lost a day.<br /> <br /> Yesterday afternoon we all gathered in the evening to do the Finding ritual to locate Shatina\u2019s brother, Jamie. This time I managed to complete the ritual easily, and the small pendant around which I\u2019d wrapped Jamie\u2019s hair tugged me in the right direction quite insistently. We drove through the city, following the ritual until we arrived at an abandoned, run-down industrial park surrounded by a high chain-link fence. When we entered the area, we discovered that it was full of bookshelves that almost formed walls, and the shelves were stacked with countless books. And even though they were all slightly overgrown with thorny vines, the books and shelves did not show any signs of damage from exposure to the elements. It was terribly mysterious.<br /> <br /> Then I noticed that the gate we\u2019d entered through was no longer behind us. Instead, a maze of bookshelves stretched in all directions around us. Somehow we had wandered out of our world. The krewe panicked a bit, and I realized that I knew where we were. We were in the Hedge, a place Mongler has told me about. I tried to explain it to the others, but I really couldn\u2019t explain it well until someone, Simon I think, made a comparison to the Underworld. Like the Underworld, the Hedge connects to our world but also serves as a gateway to deeper, darker realms beyond. And it is somewhere within, or maybe beyond the Hedge that the beings Mongler calls the Gentry live, which, as I think Gwen observed, makes them not unlike the Kerberoi.<br /> <br /> In a panic, Alexia pulled out her cell phone to try and call someone, but there was no signal. Yet as soon as she opened it, a voice answered, and taunted Alexia by saying that it would find her! It was very disconcerting, especially for Alexia, who was put completely out of sorts by the experience.<br /> <br /> We gathered our wits quickly enough, though. We didn\u2019t have any provisions, so we couldn\u2019t afford to wander around for too long, and we weren\u2019t certain if it was even safe to eat or drink any food or water we might find in the Hedge. We also quickly determined, more by instinct than anything else, that it would be a bad idea to try and force our way through the walls of shelving and thorns. So solving the maze might be our only way out. Of course, I was a bit worried that solving the maze might just lead us into the clutches of the Gentry. It was obvious, at this point, that they already had Jamie, so he was sadly beyond our help.<br /> <br /> Simon tried using Boneyard to have a look at the maze. The first attempt left him momentarily catatonic as his mind was stunned by the enormity and chaos of what he saw. But then he tried again! I feared he might lose his mind completely, but he was able to focus a bit better and got an idea of what lay around us, including a few spots we should avoid.<br /> <br /> Among the things he saw were some things that looked like human-sized owls with the faces of spiders. They seemed to be tending to the books, and occasionally ate one or spun new ones from the silk that whispered in gossamer strand from their spider-like mouths.<br /> <br /> Since the owl-spiders seemed like librarians, we decided we might ask them to help us find the way out\u2026cautiously, of course, since we had no idea whether they would be hostile or not. We soon found some and though we couldn\u2019t understand them, Doc managed to communicate by using his Primeval Marionette to attune to the ways of beasts. The owl-spiders did not know of any sure way out, but seemed to think there was an exit nearby if we continued down the path we had been traveling and took a left turn. They didn\u2019t know exactly which left turn, though.<br /> <br /> As Doc was relating all of this to us, he also observed that much like our local Underworld, this section of the Hedge was a dedicated library. Apparently that\u2019s the effect New Haven has on these other realms. The owl-spiders told him that the books contained knowledge from dreams, but they were all written in languages we couldn\u2019t understand.<br /> <br /> We continued onward, looking for the exit, until we were ambushed by a car-sized spider-beast with owl\u2019s eyes and a vicious, owl-like beak. It was accompanied by five of its much smaller offspring. They fell upon like a pack of ravenous wolves, and we were forced to fight for our lives.<br /> <br /> Doc distracted the largest of the beasts while he summoned his powers, and it wounded him badly before he was able to lash out and kill it. Meanwhile, Alexia held her own against a couple of the beasts after manifesting her extra arms, and Gwen tore a couple of them apart with her Rage. Simon used the unpleasant powers of the Pit to trap one of the creatures in the ground. Natalie, however, was trying desperately to defend herself from spider-owl that leapt at her, so I ignored the one that rushed me to help save her. I drew the Primeval Caul and Cold-Wind Shroud about me and grabbed her attacker, and after several moments I froze its flesh and broke it in two. Meanwhile, the other was attacking me, but I maneuvered to avoid its blows, and my shroud absorbed any of its attacks that managed to hit, leaving me unscathed throughout the whole fight.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we bested the creatures. Doc was a match for the biggest one, but the rest of us helped to take it down in the end because Doc was badly injured by it, and then Alexia and I finished off the rest. We patched up our wounds, and as we continued, I helped Doc along.<br /> <br /> We eventually encountered a series of left turns, and began investigating them. Simon tried using Boneyard again, but the shock of what he couldn\u2019t quite comprehend left him catatonic for several moments again, and we decided it was too risky to use Boneyard in the Hedge. So we agreed that I should scout ahead invisibly to see if I could find any sign of an exit before everyone else followed. Gwen wasn\u2019t happy about me going off on my own. She was rightfully worried that the paths might change and leave me isolated, but I was willing to take the risk. Still, I didn\u2019t stray too far from the others.<br /> <br /> We passed several passages before we got to one that looked promising, including one path that led to trees bearing delicious-looking fruit, and another that led to a pool in which faceless nymphs were playing. The nymphs seemed like they were having a great deal of fun, and I almost felt tempted to join them, but I also had the feeling that the rest of the krewe would gladly jump in and start and orgy with them, which turned my stomach, so recommended we avoid that path. Yet another path led to a lighthouse the color of lavender and dusk that rose from the thorns like a monument and had a \u201cBeware of...\u201d sign in front. I can\u2019t say exactly what I was to beware, because that part of the sign had been bitten away. It\u2019s perhaps best that I never found out.<br /> <br /> I kept noticing rather conspicuous piles of scattered books here and there along the paths. I had noticed them first just before we were attacked by the spider-owl, but I could not determine whether the other piles had any significance, though they might have been related to the creature we encountered a bit later. I should ask Mongler about it tomorrow when we meet to go see Cock Robin.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we found a promising path, but as we passed by, books began tearing themselves from the shelves and vines and assembling into a hulking humanoid figure. We decided to flee it, but then Gwen heard something coming from the direction we were running. I ran ahead to find out what it was, and was relieved to see Mongler charging our way with a huge axe!<br /> <br /> In the Hedge, apparently, his true appearance is obvious, so it was the first the others had seen him looking like a cross between an ogre and a dinosaur! He feared we had gone missing and had come to rescue us. With his help, Simon\u2019s curses, and Alexia\u2019s clever use of fire, we were able to defeat the book-creature. Had Mongler not been there, I fear we might not all have survived that encounter.<br /> <br /> Mongler explained that he grew concerned when we didn\u2019t show up to meet him and go see Cock Robin. I was confused, and thought he\u2019d gotten the days mixed up, but it turns out we had been gone from the world for over a full day, and when he came for us, it was already Tuesday evening, not Monday! We\u2019d only been in Hedge for four or five hours, so it was a huge shock to learn that we\u2019d been missing for so much longer than that.<br /> <br /> Mongler led us to the exit and out of the Hedge. He agrees that Jamie is lost to the Gentry now, and also believes that one of the Gentry wanted us to wander into its trap because it knew we were searching for Jamie. That\u2019s a frightening prospect, as it means one of the Gentry has taken notice of us.<br /> <br /> In any event, we\u2019re all back safe and sound now. Chandra, Tavia, and Karen were out of their minds with worry. And I called Jean to apologize for missing our training session this morning. It was quite late, and I think I woke him, but I owed him an explanation. Not that I really had one prepared. I simply told him something came up and I couldn\u2019t call. He must think I\u2019m terrible.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes<br /> <br /> Accent</u><br /> I could tell the Gwen was panicking a bit after we entered the Hedge when I tried to explain where we were and she somehow heard \u201cHidge\u201d when I said \u201cHedge.\u201d She very aggressively asked me \u201cWhat the hell is a Hidge!?\u201d which confused me a bit until I realized she\u2019d misinterpreted my Kiwi accent.<br /> <br /> Not that my accent is completely Kiwi. I got most of it from my mum, but I had to study British English in school, and my Taiwanese accent creeps in as well, so I guess my English accent is quite confused\u2026mostly Kiwi, but not quite. That\u2019s what my cousins in New Zealand have told me, anyway.<br /> <br /> Richard always told me it was completely enchanting. But Gwen didn\u2019t seem to think so when we were in the Hedge. Fortunately Doc stepped in to interpret and help settle Gwen down a bit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday, June 14th<br /> <br /> -Ritual underway, and away we go!<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s time to take a ride. I am gonna ride with Doc and Simon I think<br /> <br /> -Well this certainly looks\u2026run down.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, June 15th<br /> <br /> -Sweet Virgin Mary\u2019s Garters!<br /> <br /> -My girlfriend is gonna KILL me.<br /> <br /> -I could tell you what just happened but I think everyone would think I was on LSD again.<br /> <br /> -Karen is more relieved then anything else, good. Apparently trying to keep Tavia calm did wonders for her own sanity.<br /> <br /> -Apologies for the Radio Silence friends, supplicants and lovers! I abruptly found myself without an Internet signal (and had reasons besides to not mess with my phone.)<br /> <br /> -crapcrapcrap<br /> <br /> -LOL Simon had more missed messages then I did. I\u2019d be peevish if they were not nearly all from one person.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is officially discombobulated.<br /> <br /> -Karen and Tavia were driving around looking for us. I kinda hate I missed that conversation. It sounds like a sitcom episode.<br /> <br /> -I am trying to imagine a rescue mission with Chandra, Tavia and Karen. Hilarious but probably tragic.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up! Sorry about the missing one with no word! Won\u2019t happen again!<br /> <br /> -Fuck it only feels like 10 pm and it\u2019s apparently 2 am a day later. I\u2019m gonna see the damn sunrise.<br /> <br /> -I have forums to catch up with. Can the Internet live without me? Best not tempt fate.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> End Session XLIII<br /> <br /> </i>And that, good friends and true, is why you don\u2019t enter the hedge.<br /> <br /> One detail that was not mentioned by either party was when Doc was hurt Natalie gave him her one Capri-Sun drink she had with her\u2026in theory a sign she cares given they did not know for how long they would be stuck. Anyway. The other note is Jasmine and Doc put the &quot;beware of&quot; sign in different places. It was outside the purple lighthouse. Oh, the &quot;nymphs&quot; Jasmine had to make a Resolve+Composure+Psyche roll to resist going in...her Virtue and Vice actually gave her a +2 and -2 which canceled each other out. Fortunately, Jasmine rocks at those rolls, and easily defeated the temptation to play with the nymphs.<br /> <br /> As you can see through careful scouting and occasional Boneyard (I made Simon\u2019s player make Resolve + Composure rolls when he used it) they avoided many of the perils, having to fight only the Book Giant (with help) and some Owlspiders. I\u2019ll note the Owlspiders made for Combat number 4 and 5 in the campaign, which is a year and \u00be old now, and the first time we had two in a single session. Also, it seems like someone gets horribly wounded every time, first Alexia with the Ivory Claws, then Jasmine against the Rose Bride, then Doc vs. the Big Owlspider. I told Gwen\u2019s player it\u2019s her turn next. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But they managed to escape the Hedge without too much problem.<br /> <br /> Check out our next session, where our heroes meet a very strange Darkling, Jasmine discoverers there is something in the humidifier, we jump ahead about a month in time, and discussion comes up about a very peculiar, very disturbing marionette/puppet show from 2/3 of the Krewe\u2019s childhood. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T02:55:48-08:00","id":16026,"title":"","content":"OK, Journals this time are spotty, apologies for that. Neither Doc's nor Jasmine's nor Natalie's covered the end of the session. Now with Jasmine it turns out that is a plus for reasons I will go into after the journals, but unfortunate otherwise. Natalie's tweets are particularly unfinished for various reasons. Posted are what little got done on them.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Journals up in here<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1425 Hours, Wednesday, June 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Today hasn\u2019t been too bad. Lifting stock was interesting but things were okay otherwise. I\u2019ve been a little slower than usual, but that was just to keep from ripping out the stitches Rose put in me. While I had less free time thanks to moving slower, I did get some drawing in. <br /> <br /> Nightshade came over for lunch again today. She brought more Capri-Sun than usual today. I\u2019m not sure if she expected me to still need hydrating or not. When I saw them, I remembered that she had given me one while we were in the Hedge. I know I was appreciative at the time, but I\u2019m not sure I actually said anything to her about it. Nightshade is, due to a number of reasons, very focused on keeping herself out of harm\u2019s way from outside forces. We had no way of knowing how long we might be stuck there and she gave me her only guaranteed source of drinkable fluid. I should have said something about it to her at the time. But I did notice so I brought up how thankful I was to have her around when I needed help. It was kinda surreal. We had one of those conversations back when I was still in the wheelchair. Hopefully she understood and it wasn\u2019t too awkward. <br /> <br /> After that, I shifted the topic to the 27 Club. I hadn\u2019t heard much about it lately so it\u2019s cool to hear what\u2019s been going on with that. They have reached the point of waiting to hear from other people before they can move forward with any of the properties. That sounded like a really good thing to me. It\u2019s my own fault that I don\u2019t have more to do with this endeavor but I\u2019m so jealous of Karen for being able to share this with Nightshade. Still it\u2019s good to hear about their progress so I know where they stand in case I can ever help.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1615 Hours, Wednesday, June 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Just got off the phone with Karen. We had another information exchange. Apparently baby Nightshade has a lot of pull on Nightshade already. Karen thinks she might spend lots of money on the kid. She said that baby Nightshade was very \u201csweet talkie\u201d and already getting good at being manipulative as her mom. I did remind Karen that trying to interfere with how Nightshade handles her money is a very bad idea, for me more than others, but anyone in general. The overall concern is that Nightshade will be convinced that her little girl needs a car and Karen felt very strongly that Nightshade could not afford such an expense. Before I realized what I was saying, I made some comment about how it was like paying for college tuition. I\u2019m not really sure where that came from but it was a low blow against someone that was honestly trying to help. Karen only paused for a second before continuing on like I hadn\u2019t said anything. That\u2019s probably for the best.<br /> <br /> It was somewhere in here that I had a new idea for images of a charm tattoo. A spectral or skeletal dragon head and wings rising up behind it with \u201cMeddle Not In The Affairs of Dragons\u201d emblazoned underneath it. It might have been coincidence or it might have been ironic timing. I know the rest of the Krewe would turn on Karen like a pack of wild dogs given the fact that baby Nightshade is her family and her responsibility, while Karen is neither. I have no intention of mentioning this fact to them, but the situation feels very Ancient Rome to me. I\u2019ll keep my eyes open on the situation as much as I can, but I\u2019m not sure Karen is going to like how this one turns out. I\u2019m also not sure I care.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s time to get ready to close up. We\u2019ve got plans to meet Cock Robin tonight. I also need to check with Tavia to see how the portrait of Nightshade is coming.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2215 Hours, Wednesday, June, 16, 2010<br /> <br /> I should not be this tired so early at night. But it\u2019s been an interesting evening.<br /> <br /> We went to Mongler\u2019s office before heading to finally meet the mysterious Cock Robin. Mongler wanted to have a serious moment with us before we went. He needed for us to know that Cock Robin liked to touch for no known reason. I think his depictions of previous violence against Cock Robin shocked at least Rose. We should keep in mind at all times that Cock Robin was dangerous honestly insane and very powerful in dreams. We were not to hurt or kill it. If \u201che\u201d reached for anything inappropriate Mongler promised to break its arm. We didn\u2019t need to leave any residue from powers or it might get interested in us. This being was crazy even for Changelings, which really didn\u2019t mean anything to any of us. I took it to mean that in all ways I should handle it as though it were a mental patient. I was okay with that, but I\u2019m not sure all the others were on the same page as I was.<br /> <br /> We gathered up and head out. We went to a place that I\u2019m not sure I even knew was there, which made me a little uneasy after our random trip to the Hedge. The building was made of corrugated metal and I spotted holes in the roof. There were four different private property signs around the building, just from what I could see from the car. Mongler led the way by beating on the door and announcing our arrival before going in. <br /> <br /> The being calling itself Cock Robin was a short, pale thing with a huge curved nose. It acted like a Skeksi from the Dark Crystal. We told him what information we had about Shatina and the Hedge while Mongler stood to keep us separate from it. Ronin did most of the talking, which might not have been the best option, but she spoke up first so it directed its answered to her. At one point, it left to get a book. Nightshade made a Gelfing joke and we all agreed as to just how broke this thing was. When it came back, we got to the very surreal moment when it announced to us as much as to the air that \u201cFetches always have something wrong.\u201d I glanced at Mongler to see if something was happening we needed to be aware of, but he seemed intent on bringing Cock Robin back to task. It let us know that it kept its fetch downstairs. This led to an uncomfortable discussion about Mongler\u2019s fetch, which is apparently still around, but totally off limits to Cock Robin. Ultimately we left Cock Robin to its crazy with the understanding we needed to get \u201ca piece\u201d of Shatina for it to study. We decided that we would get a brush, a mirror, and at least temporarily her phone. That would give us hair to give to Cock Robin, a way for Snowflake to keep watch on her, and information for Ronin to do her detective thing.<br /> <br /> I think Ronin, Rose, and Snowflake are going out tonight to do that. I\u2019m going to stay home with my dog and try not to hurt. I\u2019m not really able to help much in this area anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1930 Hours, Thursday, June 17, 2010<br /> <br /> Today was blissfully uneventful.<br /> <br /> Lunch with Nightshade was relaxing as always.<br /> <br /> During dinner, we had the Krewe news session like always. The Magic Thieves had some excitement last night. Rose is the best at getting in and around places unseen so she went in with Rose ready to bolt and Snowflake watching the whole place like an all-seeing eye. Not that we really needed much more evidence, but given what Rose dealt with, we\u2019re pretty sure not only is Shatina a fetch, but also that what Mongler calls the Gentry are still keeping watch on her. The short version is that most of the room gave Rose the feeling something was there watching her and a humidifier seemed to be making some strange mist shapes in the pink night light. Rose looked inside but when she put the lid back on, she realized that she had no idea what she\u2019d just seen. Snowflake apparently had the same reaction from his vantage point and he could see through illusions. This led to Rose throwing the lid off and even though she was invisible this negative copy of her reached from the water and tried to grab her. I didn\u2019t understand all the details but something about the room changed after that, since she came back to return Shatina\u2019s phone. This is bad juju.<br /> <br /> On a happier note, Ronin let us know that she had successfully invested two of the gold bars this morning, and the funds from this were going into an offshore account to which we would each receive a debit card. The original total before we start earning the interest is just about $2.5 million! Hurray Gold! I have no idea what 20% interest is on that much money, but I don\u2019t think we\u2019ll need to worry about expenses if we ever need to travel. I can foresee the medical station and our alchemy lab going live sooner rather than later now. Holy shit\u2026I don\u2019t even know what else to say.<br /> <br /> On a related note, we\u2019re leaving tomorrow for the Flesh Fair in New Orleans. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll take my journal as I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ll have time to write in it and I damn sure don\u2019t want anyone to go through it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0210 Hours, Tuesday, June 22, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m about to drop but I wanted to get this down first. The Flesh Fair and New Orleans was wild, as per. Other than just fun stuff, I mingled with some of the other medic types at the Fair. I barely remember names and have no time for nicknames, so I\u2019ll just summarize. In general, Sin-Eaters either don\u2019t help and/or don\u2019t talk about other supernatural creatures. What I did get a few people to admit follows:<br /> <br /> Vampires are hard to patch up. (I knew this already)<br /> If a werewolf needs help healing, dig a hole.<br /> Changelings are a little too out there for anyone to admit to knowing.<br /> <br /> If there\u2019s anything else with a name running around, no one was offering up information.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to bed. Tomorrow I need to take these stitches out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, June 16, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I had a chat with Jean this morning about all the strange things that have happened with me lately. I could tell he was concerned. After all, first I couldn\u2019t meet for a week because I\u2019d been badly burned, and then I disappeared entirely for a day. But he never asked if anything strange was going on\u2026not really. I guess Gwen is right, and Jean and I aren\u2019t going to work out. Not that I\u2019ve thought we would for some time, really. I guess I\u2019m not really approachable in the right way for him.<br /> <br /> That said, I tried to help him understand. I explained my recent injury and disappearance by telling him the truth, more-or-less. I told him that I and my house mates are part-time paranormal investigators, and that we sometimes run into odd or dangerous things. He was not as surprised as I thought he might be. In fact, he seemed to accept it fairly readily. Mostly, he was just worried about what other dangers that line of work might present. He does care about me, after all.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, June 16, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> We visited Cock Robin today to see if he could help us learn more about Shatina and whether or not she is a fetch. Mongler gave us plenty of warnings about Cock Robin before going to see him, enough to give us the impression that he could be quite dangerous under the right circumstances. But Mongler was with us, and apparently bullies his smaller associate to keep him in line, so I really felt more sorry for Cock Robin than anxious about anything he might try. I assume that Mongler knew what he was doing, but still, his threats seemed a bit excessive.<br /> <br /> Cock Robin was a scrawny changeling who resembled a cross between a person and a featherless baby bird. He was quite grotesque, actually, and I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve every seen anyone who look so obviously mad. But he seemed quite a lot about fetches.<br /> <br /> He believes, from our description, that Shatina is a fetch, but we are going to fetch some bits of hair or fingernail clippings from her so that he can test them and find out more. If Shatina is a fetch, then Shatina is likely trapped beyond the Hedge with one of the gentry. And as for Jamie, his fetch may have failed, which would explain the set of left-over clothes Shatina found. So, tonight, Gwen, Simon and I are going to go collect something of Shatina\u2019s that Cock Robin can use to tell if she\u2019s really a fetch or not.<br /> <br /> I should also note that Gwen informed us tonight that she\u2019s managed to convert a couple of our gold bars into cash. She\u2019s set up a krewe account and gave us all debit cards. Apparently we have well over $2 million in the account! I don\u2019t really have any use for that much money, and I hope the others don\u2019t fritter it all away on extravagant things.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, June 16, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> Gwen, Simon and I secretly visited Shatina\u2019s home tonight, and I crept in to find evidence that she really is a fetch. Simon remained in the car with Gwen and kept watch with Boneyard in case anything went wrong. Meanwhile, I unlocked the Caul of Stillness and crept into the house as living shadow.<br /> <br /> I managed to gather one of her hairbrushes and a few fingernail clippings, which should be plenty for Cock Robin to perform whatever experiments or rituals he uses to learn more. and I took her phone to Gwen, who copied its data just in case. I also found an old pocket watch. It was not working and had a cracked face, but it must have been in Shatina\u2019s family for awhile and it resonated with death. I thought it would make a nice charm for Simon, so I stole it. I retrospect, I think it was a horrible thing to do, but Shatina isn\u2019t really Shatina, is she? It will do more good in our hands than buried forgotten in one of her vanity drawers.<br /> <br /> As I searched Shatina\u2019s room, I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that there was definitely something wrong there. Shatina was sleeping peacefully, but I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that I was being watched. Also, there was a humidifier that produced an odd, swirling mist that seemed to make strange patterns in the pinkish glow produced by Shatina\u2019s night light. I reinforced my stealth by unlocking the Stillness Shroud to become invisible shadow, and then lifted the lid off the humidifier to have peek inside. But I immediately replaced it with no memory of what I had seen. I later learned that Simon had a similar experience watching with Boneyard.<br /> <br /> Disturbed by the odd sensation of missing a moment of my life, I decided to brave another look and this time tossed the lid aside so I couldn\u2019t immediately replace it. And when I did, I saw my own vague reflection in the water inside the humidifier (even though I was invisible), and it reached out to grab me with long, spectral arms! I managed to dodge away in time, and then the thing in the humidifier disappeared.<br /> <br /> I decided to leave well-enough alone for now. I didn\u2019t know what I was dealing with, though perhaps I should have removed the humidifier altogether. Instead, I replaced the lid so nothing would seem amiss when Shatina awoke. It was then that I noticed the door to the room had closed, even though I know I left it open. I was eager to leave then, and phased through the wall to deliver the evidence and phone to Gwen. But when I returned a few minutes later to replace the phone so Shatina wouldn\u2019t miss it, the door was open again. It was quite spooky, and none of us, even Simon, know what we\u2019re up against.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll make sure to get the evidence to Mongler tomorrow so he can pass it along to Robin.<br /> <br /> <br /> [Excerpts from Jasmine\u2019s Diary Entries, June 17 to July 5, 2010]<br /> <br /> Saturday, June 19, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We have arrived and enjoyed our first day at the flesh fair in New Orleans. I\u2019d never been to New Orleans before. It seems like a fascinating city, though perhaps a bit boisterous for my tastes. The flesh fair itself has been terribly interesting, though I\u2019m not really sure what to make of it. I\u2019ve never met so many other sin-eaters before. And they are all so different, so unique. It\u2019s easy, when one deals with supernatural things as we do, to begin stereotyping. But really, we\u2019re all as different and unique as normal people. I mean, Natalie and I are almost as different as can be, and yet we\u2019re both Silent.<br /> <br /> Honestly, the fair has been a bit overwhelming. Mostly I\u2019ve just stuck with Gwen, not really knowing what else to do with myself. I was hoping to trade for some charms, but they are in high demand and I really didn\u2019t have anything to trade for them. So I\u2019ve mostly been staying quiet and out of the way, except when Gwen tries to shove me into the spotlight. She means well, but it\u2019s been a little uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Visiting some of the jazz clubs has been wonderful, though. Gwen doesn\u2019t really care for it, so I\u2019ve had to slip away on my own. There\u2019s something so cozy and romantic about listening to the live music in a city known for its jazz. I found this really nice place that has a sort of 60\u2019s era jazz feel. It\u2019s a little\u2026\u201dbeatniky,\u201d but aside from that I felt perfectly at home there. Well, as much as I feel at home anywhere. Anyway, it made me think of Audrey Hepburn\u2019s film Funny Face, which is one of my favorites.<br /> <br /> Doc and Natalie have stuck together throughout our trip so far, and it\u2019s nice to see her paying so much attention to him. I suppose I\u2019ve been a bit unfair toward Natalie over the past weeks. She really is trying to make her relationship with Doc work, even if she does still have a lot of challenges to overcome. Natalie and I don\u2019t really communicate well with each other, but I can still see some of the positive changes she\u2019s been making in her life. I don\u2019t know if it\u2019s Doc or the way she\u2019s reconnecting with her daughter, but it seems like she\u2019s doing less drugs, and I don\u2019t think she\u2019s been sleeping around any now that she\u2019s formalized her relationship with Doc and Karen. I still think that three-way relationship is a bad idea and that Karen\u2019s a crutch who is going to make it harder for Natalie to overcome some of her issues in the long run, but at least she\u2019s giving it all her best. I just hope the trend continues.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, June 3, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> I met with Mongler today, and he gave me what information Cock Robin was able to learn about Shatina\u2019s fetch. There\u2019s no longer any doubt that she is a fetch, for one thing. Also, she doesn\u2019t know what she is. She thinks she really is Shatina. But if she awakens to what she really is, either on her own or when prompted by her creator, she will gain access to a host of supernatural powers that will make her quite dangerous indeed. Unfortunately, there\u2019s not much else we can do right now other than keep an eye on her and make sure we\u2019re ready to act if she shows any signs of awakening. It might be a good idea to eliminate the fetch immediately, but Mongler seems to think waiting and watching will be best, and he knows far more about these matters than I do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, June 24, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> It seems that my house mates are trying to expand the range of their supernatural abilities. Simon asked me to help him almost drown so that he can learn how to manipulate the Tear-Stained Key. That key is one of my specialities, even though I don\u2019t really use it as much as the Stillness or Primeval keys these days. Plus, I\u2019m a swimmer with extensive life guard training and experience, so who better to keep him from really killing himself? Fortunately, things went well, and though the experience was unpleasant for both of us, Simon came through all right.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Gwen decided to attune herself to Pyre-Flame by getting struck my lightning. Honestly, she\u2019s so flamboyant! Why couldn\u2019t she do it safely by burning herself a bit like Alexis did? Anyway, Gwen found her way to the roof during a thunderstorm tonight and managed to the be hit. Fortunately, Doc was on site to make sure she was okay, but I still think it was foolish and I let her know as much!<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, June 30, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> Julian came for dinner tonight! I helped Alexia prepare dinner and cooked ba-wan dumplings, which are one of my favorite Taiwanese dishes. Julian seemed to like the ba-wan, which made me happy. He was just as charming as I remember him being at the party, and he chatted about his graduate studies and told us anecdotes from his past with Simon, all of which were both entertaining and endearing. I wanted to ask Julian to walk with me in the garden cemetery after dinner, but thought it might be too forward of me, so I contented myself with enjoying his company with the rest of the krewe over dinner and then afterward, in the parlour. Still, the others did manage to conspire to leave the two of us alone to chat for a bit after dinner. It was enchanting! The Bride certainly agrees, but her thoughts very much mirror my own these days, so I was hardly surprised. She says Julian reminds her of her lost love, but I think perhaps that she is projecting a bit.<br /> <br /> In any event, it was a good evening.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 2, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> Since the krewe has a bit of a lull in its activities right now, I\u2019ve decided to go back to Taiwan to visit my father. It\u2019s been almost a year since I\u2019ve been home, and he and I weren\u2019t exactly happy with each other last time I left for America. He still wants me to stay in Taiwan, and I simply cannot do that. But I miss him, and want to see him. And I know he misses me terribly. It\u2019s hard for him, with mum dead and his daughter living halfway around the world. It\u2019s been unkind of me to go so long without visiting.<br /> <br /> My flight leaves on Monday, and I\u2019m planning on staying about two weeks. It will be nice to be back in Taipei, though I don\u2019t think it will feel like home anymore.<br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Julian</u><br /> I asked Simon a bit about Julian, and was relieved to learn that Julian already knows quite a bit about the occult, and even about sin-eaters. Apparently Julian has been a friend of Simon\u2019s for a long time, and has always known that Simon\u2019s family dabbled in the occult. Julian often helped Simon with his arcane pursuits, and after Simon became a sin-eater, before we found him, Julian helped Simon experiment with his new powers.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t express how relieved I was to hear that Julian has already been initiated into the world of the supernatural. As I\u2019m learning with Jean, becoming involved with someone who doesn\u2019t know what he\u2019s getting into is\u2026challenging. Not that I\u2019m really involved with Julian\u2026.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Fetches</u><br /> <br /> Cock Robin explained how fetches are made. Each one is built on a \u201cpiece\u201d of a person, like her shadow, reflection, regrets, dreams, or practically anything else you could imagine. Other things are mixed in to give the fetch form, and once it is enchanted, even changelings can\u2019t tell what it is on sight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>American Culture and Idioms</u><br /> <br /> The Dark Crystal<br /> <br /> Natalie made a creepy comment while we were interacting with Cock Robin. Something like \u201cSmells like gelfling.\u201d As usual, I had no idea what she was talking about, but Gwen later explained that Cock Robin reminded them of creatures called \u201cskeksis\u201d from a Jim Henson film called The Dark Crystal. We watched the movie later, and Cock Robin really was a lot like the skeksi characters. Though it wasn\u2019t actually a skeksi that said \u201cSmells like gelfling.\u201d<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the film. It was quite magical, though a bit odd and scary. I was surprised by how convincing and realistic the puppetry was!<br /> <br /> <br /> Evil Twins<br /> <br /> Gwen was quite agitated when Simon and I told her what had happened with the humidifier in Shatina\u2019s room. She apparently feared that if the thing in the humidifier had gotten me, then my \u201cevil twin\u201d might show up, which I suppose is reasonable, given Shatina\u2019s situation. That said, I was completely confused when Gwen started going on about goatees. Eventually she managed to explain that in the Star Trek show, evil twins had goatees or dressed strangely, and that they were the opposite of the person they were based on. I pointed out that if that were so, my evil twin would be delightfully happy and probably insatiably randy, and therefore instantly recognizable, which seemed to amuse Gwen enough to calm her worries. Of course, if a double did show up, it probably wouldn\u2019t be so obvious. Shatina\u2019s fetch certainly seems like the real thing.<br /> She did become quite cross with me when I got Star Wars and Star Trek mixed up, though.<br /> Honestly, I think she watches too much TV.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Drowning</u><br /> <br /> I tried not let it show, but helping Simon almost drown to learn the Tear-Stained key was quite painful and traumatic for me. I kept remembering how I died, paralyzed and floating beneath the surface of the pool, unable to even struggle against the inevitable as my lungs filled with water and I realized that I was going to lose not only my life, but my love as well. Returning to that dark memory was almost more than I could bear, even if it is what defined me as a sin-eater.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, June 16th<br /> <br /> -Barely up in time for lunch with Doc. Yesterday completely screwed my sleep schedule.<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc!<br /> <br /> -Doc is still drawing stuff. I am still a delicious Strawberry deathcake.<br /> <br /> -Picking up booze with Karen and Simon, woo!<br /> <br /> -That\u2019s only two underage people. Technically.<br /> <br /> -Gonna pass on the George Dickel.<br /> <br /> -Karen with a bottle of wine in her hand\u2026mmmm\u2026what were we talking about?<br /> <br /> -I am such a perv today.<br /> <br /> -I am given to understand that at least for purposes of an upcoming meeting that the bird is, in fact, the word.<br /> <br /> -Yea, I feel bad just typing that.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIV</i><br /> <br /> Most events were pretty well covered in the journals to a point.<br /> <br /> I was terribly proud of the scene with the humidifier. The room got pretty quiet and the PCs were less...cocky...in their approach with it, but the Shatina storyline is one of the few that really has seemed to rattle them IC. They were pretty...careful, which was cool.<br /> <br /> As noted a couple new keys, though they have not picked them up yet. Alexia also picked up Marionette, and Natalie maxed Boneyard.<br /> <br /> The last 45 minutes or so of the game covered Tavia's drawing the TV show Candle Cove to the PCs attention. Mainly Gwen, at first. After some research they all had a discussion; Natalie (and Jasmine, though she was retconned out of the scene) did not remember not being locals, but Simon, Gwen, Doc, and Alexia, being locals as kids, did. The show involved marionettes and puppets, as well as one live girl and omnipresent calliope music. The more people remembers (with Int+Composure rolls) the more sinister the show seemed to be, with little things they missed as kids and some things they understood all too well. Some even remembered a &quot;final episode&quot; with screaming and crying that they felt compelled to turn off. They resolved to investigate it, and that investigation was the focus of last night's session. More details will, no doubt, be forthcoming then.<br /> <br /> Jasmine and Gwen's players had to miss last nights session. As such, it was assumed Jasmine was still in Taiwan (hence the ending of her journal implying she would be, and retonning her from the show discussion) and Gwen was otherwise occupied. There will probably be a short Jasmine journal covering events in Taiwan according to her player.<br /> <br /> I'll see you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T02:59:08-08:00","id":16028,"title":"","content":"Hello folks, I hope this message finds you well.<br /> <br /> Good news and bad news. The good news is Doc and Jasmine journals. Bad news is neither actually covers the session 2 weeks ago. Doc's entirely covers the downtime during the session a month ago, and Jasmine's covers her trip to Taiwan. This is partially because both Jasmine and Gwen's players had to miss two weeks ago due to illnesses, last enough minute we were unable to reschedule (not the players faults at all, of course!). So Doc's journal is actually covering the timeframe covered by the end of Jasmine's last journal, not anything in her current journal. It's out of sync, but you know. Jasmine's journal does cover stuff that came up in the game tonight, however. Long as that's clear, lets roll.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc's Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1955 Hours, Friday, June 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019d feel like I should say it\u2019s been a crazy week, but we haven\u2019t done much. Not as a Krewe anyway. I have been trying like crazy to make sure everything in the shop is perfect in case I get one of the \u201csurprise\u201d inspectors to check out my new tattoo area, before the state approves my permit.<br /> <br /> I said we haven\u2019t done much, but that\u2019s not to say nothing happened since we got back from New Orleans. Ronin has been looking into learning a new Key. Because I\u2019ve spent a lot of time in the Library lately, I\u2019ve been around while she looked up things on Pyre-Flame. She really wasn\u2019t thrilled with sticking her hand in an oven or something like that. Wednesday, we were supposed to have a thunderstorm. Now I\u2019m not completely happy about this, but she decided to go up on the roof and do the Lambada with one of the lightning rods. She did at least have the good sense to tell me she was going to do it first, so I could be there in case something went wrong though. I didn\u2019t enjoy sitting on the roof during a downpour, but I wasn\u2019t about to let her get struck so her heart could stop or something dumb like that. We face enough ways to die without the random stuff making life harder.<br /> <br /> While she was prancing around, she slipped. I lunged for her to keep her from falling off the roof. I don\u2019t know if she put on extra jewelry or found some metal bracers or what, but as soon as I grabbed for her, this huge flash hit and knocked her back into the roof. Unfortunately, it also arced over into me and blasted me backwards too. I was blinded and having a hard time moving when I realized Ronin was laughing to my right. I reached over until I could feel what I hoped was her shoulder and dragged her to me. She made some joke about buying her dinner first before I kicked her in the shin. I would have felt bad about it later until she belted me in the solar plexis. After I could breathe again, I just wanted to go inside. I didn\u2019t tell Ronin that I was hit too as the rest of the Krewe were trying to get us off the roof. We didn\u2019t need anyone blaming her for something that might have happened to me.<br /> <br /> <i>You speak as though your presence was by accident and yet you know you aided The Angel\u2019s vessel in finding her knowledge. The level of humility you strive for is confusing. Seeking undue accolades holds no honor, but hiding from honor that is yours serves no purpose.<br /> </i><br /> He keeps me straight even when I don\u2019t want it I guess. But then that might be why we get along like we do.<br /> <br /> The other reason I\u2019m writing this is because Rose got some news back from Cock Robin about our tests the other night and I haven\u2019t written it down yet. The person we recognize as Shatina is in fact a Fetch. She apparently has the power to trap the real Shatina (who would now be a Changeling of some kind) in a mirror. By all accounts, Cock Robin found she has used no supernatural powers to date. The likelihood is that she has no idea she is a Fetch. This both is relieving and makes things more complicated.<br /> <br /> We talked about Manchurian Candidates a few times while I was still at Camp Lejune. Ignoring the macho bullshit, no one was really sure what to think about it. It was a scary thought that someone we knew and trusted could just be \u201cactivated\u201d one day and become something else. This is the most logical comparison I can draw to Shatina\u2019s situation. <br /> <br /> At least we were able to give Mongler a heads up that someone might be coming out of the Hedge and will need help. Not that we have a clue where, when, or if.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2015 Hours, Monday, June 28, 2010<br /> <br /> We had a guest for dinner tonight. Julian dropped by. I\u2019m not sure if Snowflake set it up or if he just came to see Rose, but she was very adorable and excited. She helped Cupcake in the kitchen and surprised us all with another Taiwanese dish. Ba-wan dumplings aren\u2019t something I was familiar with but Rose thought they were authentic; Cupcake made them delicious and our special guest seemed impressed.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure just how serious this might turn out, but Rose seems very eager to find out, in as much as she\u2019s eager for anything. This could definitely go somewhere. I just wish Snowflake would let me know before he does stuff like this. Tavia doesn\u2019t need help getting doe-eyed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0415 Hours, Tuesday, June 29, 2010<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even know exactly how to write this. I\u2019m not in the habit of documenting my sex life. But something has changed in Nightshade. I\u2019m not going to get into graphic details, but what she\u2019s after seems to have changed. I\u2019m not sure how to take this. Does she want to freak me out or is she thinking (directly) about having another baby?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have the brain power to go into it all now, but my mind is blown.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2015 Hours, Friday, July 2, 2010<br /> <br /> Being that it\u2019s Practice Night, I had Rose teach me the ceremony to dedicate charms. I\u2019ve been reading up on them in the library for a while now. I\u2019m pretty sure I can make tattoos into charms if I have the right materials. I\u2019ll need to be really careful with those materials though. Not the kind of stuff I keep with the rest of my tattooing supplies ever.<br /> <br /> So now my drawing is more important than just getting an image out of my head. It can be a way for us to really move in Sin-Eater circles. Some day. First I have to get everything together and get some work visible.<br /> <br /> Gotta get back to this drawing thing. Art is calling! <br /> <br /> Yeah that sounded just as lame in my head. I was hoping on paper would look better. Nope.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2115 Hours, Monday, July 5, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been spending a lot of time in the Library while we\u2019re taking it easy and learning a little more about supernatural politics and drawing whenever I get the chance. Sebastian has been working with me again and I think I\u2019m really getting the hang of a few other dances.<br /> <br /> Rose flew back to Taiwan this morning. She\u2019s been talking with her Father which is new. Apparently they weren\u2019t on great terms before so she\u2019s going home to spend some time with him and just visit in general. Two weeks without Rose around will definitely feel different.<br /> <br /> After we dropped her off at the airport, everyone just kinda drifted into different directions in a daze. I managed to find Nightshade before Karen made off with her. I really needed to know what exactly she wanted. The change in her actions had not only continued, but intensified. And I didn\u2019t know any way to ask other than just straight to the point. Her response was possibly the most haunting thing I\u2019ve ever heard. She told me that she wanted a lot of things. Just seeing the words doesn\u2019t really tell the whole story. She was so sad when she said it, like everything she wanted was out of her reach. I knew that yes she did want another child, apparently with me, and I\u2019m not sure how that will work. But there was so much more meaning in those few words. I don\u2019t know everything she meant but I knew she was feeling unfulfilled and not in a sexual way. It was heartbreaking. I really don\u2019t like the idea, but I think I\u2019m going to have to talk to Karen to see is she understands this anymore than I do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1930 Hours, Saturday, July 10, 2010<br /> <br /> So no more information on what\u2019s going on with Nightshade and I haven\u2019t been able to talk to Karen privately yet either. But I did get a surprise when Nightshade got up for lunch today. She announced that we were going to look at the possible sites for the 27 Club. It\u2019s Socializing day so that kinda fit. Karen tagged along and the three of us drove around looking at multiple places around town. A few were available for us to look in, probably because they have been around so much, but I didn\u2019t complain. It was nice to finally get involved in this process. I thought I wanted to do this with just Nightshade but Karen was actually very helpful in showing me some things I didn\u2019t notice or explaining things I didn\u2019t already get. I took notes at each place and when we got back to the house, we discussed what I thought of each place. There were a few concerns I had with one or two locations and I\u2019m not sure that my input mattered but Nightshade discussed them like they weren\u2019t really in the running anymore. I finally felt like I was becoming a part of this piece of Nightshade\u2019s life.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re going to hook back up with Snowflake and go clubbing I think.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, July 5, 2010, In Flight<br /> <br /> Gwen drove me to the airport this morning, and my flight to Taiwan has been uneventful so far, except that the young American man in the seat beside me kept yacking at me for the first two hours. I really wasn\u2019t interested because he seemed to be flirting with me and trying to practice his terrible Chinese. The worst part was that he was trying to speak Cantonese, which is the wrong dialect for Taiwan. As a result, I couldn\u2019t understand half of what he was saying, which led him to conclude that I wasn\u2019t really from Taiwan either, and that my Chinese was worse than his! Still, my coldness must have put him off, because he eventually gave up and stopped trying to chat. I think that when I started writing in fluent Chinese in my diary, he realized what a fool he had been and finally shut up.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s still several hours until I land in Taipei, and the time zone is nearly opposite Connecticut, so I\u2019m going to get some sleep to help mitigate the jet lag.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, July 6, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a good day. My father was at the airport to pick me up, and when we saw each other, it was like all the bitterness over my decision to stay in America evaporated. I didn\u2019t think coming back to Taiwan would feel like coming home again, but with my father there, welcoming me with open arms, it really did.<br /> <br /> Even though I was worn out from my flight, we decided to stop by one of my favorite restaurants on the way to my father\u2019s house, and had a nice conversation over dinner where we caught up a bit. Getting real bubble tea was delightful! Then, once we returned home, I showed him pictures of people back in New Haven. He said that he\u2019d worried that Richard\u2019s death had changed me, and that talking to me now and seeing the pictures of my friends, he can see that it did change me. But it wasn\u2019t a bad change. And now, he can see that while I\u2019ve changed, I\u2019m also still the same little girl that he raised.<br /> <br /> We talked about that for awhile. We needed to. He wasn\u2019t really surprised that I live in creepy old house with a bunch of odd house-mates. I\u2019ve always been interested in the occult and something of an outsider, so when he stopped to think about it, it only seemed natural. Honestly, he said he was just glad I had friends now. And as for how I\u2019ve been changed by Richard\u2019s death, well, that\u2019s only natural too. He said that in retrospect, he\u2019d be more worried about me if I hadn\u2019t been changed by it. After all, it\u2019s the nature of existence to flow and shift.<br /> <br /> I want to tell my father what really happened to me when Richard died, but I don\u2019t know if he\u2019s ready for that now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 11, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve spent much of the last week spending time with my father, training in tai chi, helping out around my father\u2019s antique shop, and visiting family and places I\u2019ve missed since I\u2019ve been away. The family visits are largely a matter of function. About half my extended family dislikes me. The stigma of my paranormal abilities still clings to me, so they don\u2019t really want too much to do with me anyway. Ironically, I think they\u2019re also displeased that I\u2019ve decided to live in America instead of Taiwan. The other half think I\u2019m grand because of my Olympic career, but they don\u2019t really have much to do with me because I was away so often even before I went to America. At least some of my younger second-cousins think its \u201ccool\u201d that I live in America. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever been described as \u201ccool\u201d before.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve noticed a few antiques around my father\u2019s shop that carry the residue of death. I\u2019ve asked him about them, but he didn\u2019t really know the history of most. He was curious why I was asking, and I told him, as honestly as I could, that I still have a sixth sense for things, and those items in particular seemed to resonate with me. Still, I think he knows I\u2019m not telling him everything. I could never read objects like that when I was a girl, and if I could, he would know about it since I was raised around the store and never really kept my abilities from him. I kept them from my mum, because she didn\u2019t really understand, but not from my father.<br /> <br /> Maybe I\u2019ll convince my father to let me have one of the items before I head back to America.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 12, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> I got a little bored today, and decided to have a look around the neighborhoods surrounding my father\u2019s house to see if I couldn\u2019t locate any Avernian gates or haunts. I made sure to check places where I knew people had died, particularly people whose deaths I had foreseen. I found both a haunt and a gate in a small, abandoned Buddhist shrine some distance from the antique shop. I remember that the lone priest who maintained the shrine hung humself for mysterious reasons, reasons that remain unsolved as far as I know. It happened when I was a child, and I had a horrible vision of the priest\u2019s lingering death some days before he killed himself. Afterward, a rumor started in the neighborhood that I caused his death somehow because of my vision. It was one instance where my gift was interpreted as a curse by those around me, and so I stopped sharing my visions after that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 14, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve just learned that my uncle Guang Sung has disappeared, apparently from his home. He\u2019s been missing at least a week now, probably more, but since he\u2019s sort of a loner and an outsider among the family, no one really noticed at first.<br /> <br /> The police don\u2019t really have any leads, so his disappearance is a complete mystery. Hearing about it sparked a lot of memories about Uncle Guang. I haven\u2019t really thought about him for years, but when I was just a girl, he was quite interested in me because of my supernatural gift. He was a student of the occult, though I don\u2019t think he has any supernatural gift of his own.<br /> <br /> I decided to look into the disappearance, so I found out where he lived and went to investigate. I didn\u2019t find any leads either, but I can say with certainty that he was performing a ritual of some sort just before he vanished. Most of the ritual implements and many of his other occult books and supplies had been removed by the time I was able to look about, so I can\u2019t say what he was trying to do, but I suspect that something supernatural is behind his disappearance. Also, I sensed the residue left when someone died in the place, yet it wasn\u2019t quite right. I had the distinct feeling that no one had actually died there, just that the residue of death draped the place as though someone had. It was a very odd feeling, and made me worry for my uncle.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to see what else I can dig up before my flight back to Connecticut.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 18, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> My father treated me to a bit of private party with a few of our closest relatives before I go back to America tomorrow. It was fun, though of course I don\u2019t really get along well with such festive occasions. Still, I put on my best face for dad. He gave me a gift during the party. It was one of the items I asked about in the shop: a century-old string of jade Buddhist prayer beads. He had a few stories about its history, but he doesn\u2019t know which is actually true. It resonates with the Primeval Key, so I look forward to turning it into a charm and treasuring it as a token of my father\u2019s affection.<br /> <br /> Sadly, I haven\u2019t learned anything else about my uncle\u2019s disappearance. It frustrates me to leave without being able to help him, but I really have no choice. Maybe the krewe can arrange a visit to Taiwan soon to follow up on thing. I could certainly use their help. I don\u2019t know if my uncle is alive or dead, but either way, I feel I should do what I can for him.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d best get some sleep. My flight leave quite early tomorrow morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 19, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I\u2019m on my flight back to Connecticut. I\u2019m sad to leave my father, but I need to return to the krewe. Still, I\u2019m glad I had such a pleasant visit. It was not without its frustrations, but all in all, it was good to be home.<br /> Though it wasn\u2019t really home anymore, was it? I mean, Taiwan will always be my home, but it isn\u2019t where I belong anymore. Reflecting on that saddens me, but like my father said, things change. People change. And that\u2019s the way it should be. Meditating on that makes me worry that parts of me aren\u2019t changing like they should. But it also gives me more hope for others, especially Natalie, who <i>is </i>changing, I think. Funny how absence helps me see the good in things.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>My Father </u><br /> <br /> My father dressed up to come meet me at the airport, like it was a very special occasion (he looked quite handsome for a fifty-year-old man!) For him, I think meeting me in person after almost a year without seeing one another really was a very special occasion. He loves me a lot, and I think he wanted to put aside the angry words we shared when we last parted. We\u2019ve talked since then, of course, but we had to meet in person to sweep those bad feelings aside.<br /> <br /> My father has always been a pillar of strength for me. I was distressed when my mum died and I sensed his strength waver. But no matter what, he has always supported and encouraged me. He knew I was special even before I started to foresee death. And he\u2019s always encouraged me to treasure that gift and ignore the accusations of those who don\u2019t understand it.<br /> <br /> I owe a lot of who I am to my father. He taught me all I know about Buddhism and Taoism. And he taught me most of my tai chi and martial arts skills. He\u2019s a very capable martial artist too, and teaches a tai chi class in his off time. He always pushed me in my swimming career, never once letting me become discouraged and attending every swim meet, competition, and event.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>My Father\u2019s Antique Shop</u><br /> <br /> By trade, my father runs a large antique shop, and his home is on the second story above it. My mum had an interest in antiques, which is how they met. She found his shop on one of her business trips to Taiwan while looking for some authentic Chinese additions to her collection, and the two of them just hit it off. I used to help out in the antiques shop a little when I was younger, and I think it contributed to my occult education. You would be surprised how many odd items come through the doors.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Uncle Guang</u><br /> <br /> Uncle Guang was an awkward loner who didn\u2019t have much interest in other people, but he was always interested in me when I was a girl, and went out of his way to talk to me. Eventually, the family stepped in and I never saw him again. I didn\u2019t understand at the time, but I know now that they thought he was molesting me. Even though there was no real evidence of it, they still thought he was trying to take advantage of me somehow, and so they separated us.<br /> <br /> But he wasn\u2019t molesting me. He never touched me, and all he really wanted to talk about was my gift. He was the only one in my family who wanted to know more about it. Most feared it. But he wanted to understand it, to know more about my experiences. His interest was very academic, and even though he was kind to me, I don\u2019t think he was all that interested in me as a person, really. That said, it was sometimes very scary talking about what I saw when I had my visions, and I remember that he always tried to be comforting. I don\u2019t know whether that was because he really cared about my feelings or because he felt that it would help me talk more freely about my gift, but at the time, I was just happy that someone other than my father was being supportive of my abilities.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLV</i><br /> <br /> OK that should give some more downtime info. Again, for Jasmine's perspectives some of what Doc mentioned, see the last journals.<br /> <br /> Natalie's melancholy is complicated. Her reconnection to her daughter has given her some desire to have a child she won't &quot;fail&quot; though she is a sensible person (sorta) and is not doing anything risky. She sees it as difficult for her relationship with Karen if it happened, so that also keeps her from it. At the same time, her desire to marry Karen is strong, very strong, but she can't do it without hurting Doc, which is pretty much the sole reason she and Karen are not engaged now. Natalie feels she cannot have what she wants without hurting those she cares for, and is unwilling to deliberately hurt either Doc or Karen, both of whom she has become somewhat reliant on. As Jasmine noted, she has stopped going out and partying as much, and spends less time drunk or high then she did. Granted, her heroin use has shot up (no pun intended) since becoming physically involved with Doc as she has to deal with flashbacks and feelings of defilement after sex a lot. Natalie probably loves Doc and Karen a similar amount, but her physical desires are for women, and her flashbacks to being raped are not helping her deal with Doc. This was not planned when the relationships started, but sometimes characters go their own way, whatever their players want.<br /> <br /> Jasmine's trip was largely her player's work (much as Sebastian is Doc's) though the Guang stuff was information I fed her player and I was of course consulted before a Charm was added to Jasmine's repertoire. I think it is pretty awesome myself.<br /> <br /> A quick summery of what happened, we covered two days. The group went to the TV station using Natalie's credentials, and found reels of the show. They also met a lovely reporter who charmed pretty much everyone. Oracle revealed a tall marionette like skeleton in a long white coat, white hat, and with white hair dropped the reels off, with an illusion of humanity. She also apparently filmed it. The reporter Becky Franklin got them a couple names to look for, the then manager and receptionist who accepted the tape and later died under mysterious circumstances. They copied the reels, and discovered they could not see or hear them...except the Little Prince, Simon's Geist...a child. Chandra, when using Auspex, could hear it, but not clearly. The next day, to find out when kids were watching it, Alexia and Karen, with Simon in the trunk, tried to drive near some schools Simon could Boneyard. Driving slowly around playgrounds in antique cars draws attention, and the guileless Alexia near got arrested but for Karen's help. They returned with Karen driving her car and got a time. Predictably, only the Little Prince could hear it or see it. Then they played card/drinking games with monopoly money, because it was game night.<br /> <br /> OK well next update will probably cover two sessions for Doc and Jasmine will be back to reporting her experiences with the group. We had the whole jolly band of outlaws there tonight and while we did not make major story advances, the information on Candle Cove was discussed and disseminated, and plans were made for the next step using the information gleaned two weeks ago. Also some tentative plans for getting back in the saddle on the DeCastro ghost issue, and some discussions of Jasmine's uncle in Tiawan. Also, Doc and Simon make a IED.<br /> <br /> I'll see you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T03:01:54-08:00","id":16030,"title":"","content":"Hello folks. This session\u2019s journals for Doc and Jasmine cover this session and the one two weeks before. Natalie\u2019s tweets just covers the last session. That\u2019s about it so I will let them do the talking. If you want to read the original Candle Cove Creepypasta they are discussing, it is <a href=\"http://www.ichorfalls.com/2009/03/15/candle-cove/\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a><br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2125 Hours, Sunday, July 18, 2010<br /> <br /> Nothing new on the Nightshade front. I\u2019ve gone on patrol several nights and been back to train with Sebastian a few others. I\u2019m trying not to worry or stress over it too much. Apparently I\u2019m not hiding this well. Sebastian told me that I was not focusing pretty much as soon as we started Wednesday night.<br /> <br /> Karen doesn\u2019t really hang around the rest of us so it\u2019s been harder for me to talk to her without making it noticeable that that\u2019s what I\u2019m doing. Given the conversation with Chandra about not turning Trinh, I don\u2019t really want to make that a public announcement. Not that I have the slightest fucking idea of how to go about this conversation with Karen either. \u201cHey so, the woman we\u2019re both seeing wants to have a baby with me. Thought you should know. Oh yeah, and do you have any ideas as to what\u2019s going on?\u201d Karen is a little awkward around me sometimes as it is, I\u2019m sure that will be the most comfortable conversation ever.<br /> <br /> In more horrific news, Ronin came in this afternoon before dinner and spoke to Tavia. That in itself was a little scary but Tavia mentioned that while shopping for another Snoopy toothbrush, she heard some kids talking about a TV show that she recognized. It was called Candle Cove. At the mere mention of the name, a wall in my mind started to crack. I started to remember. The two different little girls named Janice, the pirate Skin-Taker, the longer cape after the first Janice \u201cleft\u201d, and the screaming. Oh God, the screaming! I felt my blood run cold. The dead marionette eyes staring while the jaw slid back and forth. The feeling of dread when I was five.<br /> <br /> I was broken from my traumatic trip down Memory Lane when Snowflake pointed out that he and Tavia always enjoyed the show when they were little. Tavia\u2019s brother never liked it though, which raised a few flags in my mind. First, I\u2019m alot older than Snowflake and Tavia and that show went off the air after the dreaded second season. So how the hell did they ever see it? Second, Tavia\u2019s brother was actually her half brother. The only real distinction there is the Outsider connection Tavia shares with Snowflake. Cupcake said something about the show when she was a kid and she\u2019s older still, so I\u2019m not even sure how any of this is possible.<br /> <br /> We talked about how maybe the television station could be haunted, but Nightshade checked the Internet and said the station moved way back when I was like still a little kid, so if that was the case, the ghost moved too. Just as we were discussing other possibilities, Snowflake started humming that damned calliope music and Nightshade mentioned something about a radio signal. All that together combined in my head to form possibly the most horrifying sci-fi nightmare I\u2019ve ever imagined. Back in the \u201860s, we shot radio and TV signals into space as part of the Space Race. The thought was that they could send examples of human life for friendly Extra Terrestrials to see and want to come visit. But the people that did that didn\u2019t know about the other realms out there. That\u2019s what I needed to think about. Sleeping will be fun tonight.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m headed for the library with sketchpad in hand. I don\u2019t know I\u2019ll get any more research done on our supernatural neighbors and their sociopolitical climate, but I know I can draw in peace and try to think. Well, unless I find Gretchen eating dust again. Then I\u2019ll go on patrol.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Monday, July 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation ran long again. Was cutting it close getting to the shop in time for open. I\u2019m sure it\u2019s because I don\u2019t know exactly what\u2019s up with Nightshade. That still doesn\u2019t help the matter. And the \u201cJohn Carpenter\u2019s The Thing meets Michael Bay\u2019s...well anything\u201d nightmare likely also made it more difficult.<br /> <br /> Work was pretty smooth for a Monday morning. I rotated some of the perishables, dusted, and then started drawing some possible designs to get familiar with them. Just really simple things to start with since I\u2019m still getting use to the whole drawing thing. I\u2019m not worried about the gloves or the equipment, those things I\u2019m used to dealing with and keeping clean. I\u2019m just concerned with the art. If I\u2019m going do to this by appointment, I need to make it worth my time and the customer\u2019s.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1830 Hours, Monday, July 19, 2010<br /> <br /> At lunch, Nightshade came around and as usual brightened up my day. Then she told me about a plan she and Snowflake hatched to head over to the local TV station and try to get more information and maybe a copy of the Candle Cove show. They know I need to be around to run the shop but this was serious. With Rose still in Taiwan and Ronin out researching another case, I really didn\u2019t think letting them walk into a possible hostile zone was a great idea. So after lunch, Cupcake, Snowflake, Nightshade, and I all went to the WTNH News 8 station. <br /> <br /> When I was a kid they called it Action News, then they switched the name to News Channel when I was in high school. It was a big scandal for the old folks. I think I was a sophomore because I remember getting my license and hearing people bitching about it on the radio on the way to school in the mornings after Christmas.<br /> <br /> This whole Candle Cove thing has me thinking alot about the times before my death. I\u2019ll try to reminisce about the old days later. Anyway, Nightshade had a plan to get us in the station without too many questions. She told the folks up front she was working on a parody of old shows and needed to see several. This would give us more time. Given her reputation as a new wave Elvira, no one really questioned the matter. It took us a while to find the reels we needed because all the stuff from when they moved (something like 20 years ago if I remember right) was stuck in a closet stacked up on a table. Then we had to sort through all that to find the actual Candle Cove reels. Cupcake found them and we pulled them out into the main room where Nightshade had her laptop and video equipment. Before we tried to do too much, Cupcake object read the reels. They haven\u2019t been shown since 1974. I wasn\u2019t born in 1974! Cupcake sketched out a picture of \u201cperson\u201d that brought the reels in originally. She was a very thin woman that stood about 6\u20195\u201d with nearly white blonde hair. But as she continued to draw, that was just an illusion. She, it, was actually a skeleton in a long white coat that moved like a marionette. This thing was visible outside of Twilight. We also learned that it was the same one that filmed the show. This thing has to be at least Geist level powerful, possibly even moreso. Cupcake also sketched out the lady that accepted the reels for the station back in the day. She was apparently very nervous around the skeleton like there was something off, but she didn\u2019t see through the illusion.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad I was only there to serve as body guard. My mind was reeling from all the memories and the truth of the matter. I had that same feeling of dread I felt while the final episode was airing. I figured out pretty quickly after I died that I had always been marked by Death in some way. That explained why I could see how people would die growing up. But this whole thing started before I was born and has affected so many children throughout all of New Haven since. I couldn\u2019t shake the feeling that I was one of the lucky ones. I turned the TV off. What about all those kids that didn\u2019t? And even more terrifying to me, what if this was what started it all for me? What if this was all engineered somehow so that I would end up a Sin-Eater?<br /> <br /> I came back to acute focus as Nightshade threaded the reels and prepared to copy the old film into a digital format. Oddly, when it started none of us could see anything. There was only static. Snowflake looked over his shoulder and looked confused. He said the Little Prince could see the show. I possessed the Dog but still didn\u2019t see anything more than static. When Snowflake did the same, he informed us that he could see while looking through the Little Prince\u2019s eyes. The Little Prince also agreed with us that there was something odd about the show. I had a terrible thought that maybe this was being rebroadcast from beyond. I mean we knew these originals had not been used since before I was born and Cupcake might have seen the original airing but we\u2019re not sure. I voiced that fear as I couldn\u2019t think of anyone else that I could talk to about it. Nightshade mentioned dead signals worked sort of like that. Broadcasts that only transmit within the Underworld. If something like that can happen, who\u2019s to say that this transmission isn\u2019t coming BACK from space? Or worse yet...from Outside?<br /> <br /> Snowflake changed the subject to consider Boneyarding around schools to try and learn when the show is airing now. Then Nightshade started talking about sex at school. I know she actually enjoys the idea of sex in a church, but apparently not in a school. Still there were ideas that happily took over my attention for a few minutes to drown out the mounting terror rising in my mind. Just at the end of that conversation, a very pretty, twentysomething woman walked in. She introduced herself as Becky Franklin, an employee of the station. She heard that Nightshade was in the building and wanted to come and meet her. Cupcake and Nightshade were both suddenly VERY attentive. All I could do was smile. Becky quickly proved to be just as intelligent as she was cute. She seemed to be aware of Candle Cove and had researched it a bit on her own. Nightshade immediately became very flirtatious and pumped her for information. Becky also claimed to be able to hear something while Nightshade was copying the reels, but that might have just been her excitement talking. As it happened, Becky knew where to find records for the people involved with Candle Cove at the station. Snowflake volunteered to stay behind with the equipment while the rest went with our new associate. I knew he would be watching us with Boneyard so this was amusing to me.<br /> <br /> In the records room, we learned that the woman Cupcake sketched was Evelyn Peters. Becky told us that Evelyn hanged herself sometime back. There was no real investigation even though there were strange circumstances. The family didn\u2019t like to talk about it either. I made a mental note to have Ronin look up obituaries and try to get any other public record on Ms. Peters later. The station manager at the time was a man named Amos Wright. Becky said that he was very well loved at the station and there were still people around that thought highly of him. He lives in New York now and we found his number. By that point, Nightshade decided that Becky was useful enough to keep in contact so email was exchanged. I just shook my head as we headed back to the storage closet. When we got back, Snowflake was bopping around to thankfully unheard calliope music.<br /> <br /> Given that we\u2019d spent most of the day at the station, we left after Nightshade had copied both seasons of the show. Since we didn\u2019t have Rose around to be displeased with bad choices, and I\u2019m unlikely to get bitchy about food considering how much we work it off, we ordered pizza and chocolate pie for dinner.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0315 Hours, Tuesday, July 20, 2010<br /> <br /> After dinner I walked into Karen grilling Nightshade about being bad. I\u2019m not entirely sure what they were arguing about, although I suspected it had something to do with Becky. Given that I was there with both of them the whole time, I knew nothing had happened. And I got vaguely annoyed that Karen didn\u2019t trust Nightshade (or me either I guess) any more than that. I knew it would go badly if I got involved so I went down into the Library for a while. While I was down there, I think I just started fuming because my annoyance intensified. I called a cab and snuck out. I\u2019m still not completely sure I knew what I was doing, but I sent to a fabric shop and bought a ten foot strip of silk print. It was black with a red pattern in the center. Given that my intention was to use this to tie Nightshade up, the symbolism was heavy.<br /> <br /> I got back in time to find Chandra floating around as a head in front of Karen. I know this probably isn\u2019t the first time and Karen certainly didn\u2019t seem phased by it, but something about that whole situation seemed wrong. Possibly more disturbing was that Chandra said she could hear something on the digital recordings of Candle Cove Nightshade was working on. Not well enough to really make anything out, but between the Little Prince and Chandra they determined that she was correct.<br /> <br /> After that, we started watching Twin Peaks as a group on Netflix. The surreal hits just keep on coming. After a few hours of that, I headed out to go on patrol. I knew I needed to get away for a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1430 Hours, Tuesday, July 20, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been an interesting day. I got up a little earlier than normal, but my mind was not at peace. It took two hours to meditate this morning. I really didn\u2019t have time to really even speak to the others, just run out the door. I\u2019ve gotten a group of folks that have taken to coming in on Tuesdays and they all came in throughout the morning so I was helping customers, staying busy, and not really able to draw. I can\u2019t complain though. With all the strangeness of my shop hours lately, I\u2019m just glad I have some loyal customers left.<br /> Nightshade came over for lunch and we talked alot. Not really about my concerns, but the concerns of the Krewe. Apparently, they believe I need an employee. Now I have considered that, since I will get more income from the tattoo and massage appointments, but other than Leslie de la Poer, no one was immediately coming to mind. In talking with Nightshade, Elise, Trinh, Clarissa, and Deanna all hit the list. Though to be honest, I don\u2019t want Deanna around as she\u2019d spent most of the day trying to figure out how to mix the right things together to get high. Clarissa has the added problem of destroying the shop if someone pisses her off. Having two that could work might be good considering Leslie, Elise, and Trinh are all in college so will have class schedules to deal with. The high school girls are really not even an option. Elsie has less issues from the start, given Trinh is still targeted by Chandra and I know she has an uncomfortable history with Nightshade. All three have some knowledge of the occult, though Elsie is again less likely to get involved, given a choice anyway. Definitely something to consider. I wonder if I could bring in enough for all three.<br /> <br /> After lunch, things stayed slow so I went back to drawing. I\u2019ve been working on some protective symbols. I think some of my special clients might be looking for those. Thinking about it, Leslie might need some of those.<br /> <br /> Nightshade just sent me a text saying the others were successful in figuring out when the show comes on TV again. Also sounds like Cupcake was almost arrested before they figured it out too. I\u2019m not sure I want to know what that\u2019s about.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0115 Hours, Wednesday, July 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Karen and Cupcake took Snowflake out to spy on the schools. Apparently this involved Cupcake driving Snowflake\u2019s 1970s ride very slowly around playgrounds. It\u2019s a miracle they weren\u2019t arrested. They even had Snowflake in the trunk so that was very special too. Eventually they switched out to Karen\u2019s car and managed to not get spotted as easily. This is good as we have to pick Rose up later today and having to explain to her that one of the Krewe was arrested for creeping around playgrounds would not have been a conversation in which I wanted to be involved. But since it was Game Night and we were still Rose-less, we enjoyed ourselves with faux debauchery. We played cards with booze and monopoly money. I won a few rounds, avoided excess drinking in general but then lost the last hand. By then, Tavia had past out, Karen and Chandra were frisky, and that pretty much ended the night. Karen and Chandra were dragged off and I carried Tavia up to her room. Snowflake and I just sort of looked around at the silence in the house and sighed. I left him to his thoughts and came to my room. I don\u2019t think I\u2019m ready for sleep yet, but just to be on the safe side, I\u2019m staying in tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *******************<br /> <br /> Session 46<br /> <br /> ___________<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Wednesday, July 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Apparently I\u2019ve needed some extra sleep or more alcohol. I woke up on time and got ready for my meditation. Given how hard it\u2019s been lately, I was really surprised when I was centered before I realized it. I feel completely at peace.<br /> <br /> I came to work after breakfast with the Krewe. They are going to pick Rose up from the airport today so that\u2019s going to be happy. As difficult as she can be sometimes, it\u2019s been weird not having Rose around for the last two weeks. Actually she stayed over an extra two days, but still. The important thing is that she\u2019s coming back. I\u2019m sure we\u2019re going to be very busy for a while now. I think I\u2019ll draw until Nightshade gets here for lunch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1645 Hours, Wednesday, July 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade came by for lunch and told me Rose is home already but is sleeping off the jet lag. Probably a good call really. I noticed Nightshade seemed a little tired but she did drink more than just when she lost. Still, there was more involved there. But it was not for me to worry about. Today, here in the shop, she was my smiling Strawberry Deathcake. I might have been a little more affectionate than usual but she didn\u2019t seem to mind. It\u2019s the moments we have together like these that remind me just how happy we can be together.<br /> <br /> After she left, I started working on another drawing. This one was more detailed and less likely to be a tattoo. It was difficult because I\u2019m still not used to drawing faces. I decided to try and actually draw Nightshade as Strawberry Deathcake. If I can ever get good at this, maybe I\u2019ll draw a comic of it. A gothic femme fatale that leads a group of wayward women back to their own sense of gothic purpose and self confidence. I have no idea. I\u2019m just enjoying the challenge and I suspect Nightshade would really like it if I can finish. But now I should probably get the shop ready to close up. I\u2019m sure everyone is going to want to hear all about Rose\u2019s trip.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0350 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Well tonight was certainly what you could call exciting.<br /> <br /> When I got back to the House, Rose was just getting around again. She brought quite a bit of presents back with her and \u201cStuff (TM)\u201d for the House. She was obviously very happy to be back too. That\u2019s a major change for Rose as she\u2019s rarely very happy about anything. Over dinner, we caught her and Ronin up on all the Candle Cove developments. It was a little strange because half the Krewe had never heard of this show before a few days ago, while the other half had pretty effectively blocked it from memory. There was lots of discussion about trying to jam the signal. Ronin found the obituary for Evelyn Peters fairly quickly. There wasn\u2019t much there, but then she pulled up the police records on it. Her friend Officer Tart had worked that case. She\u2019s going to talk to him when she can to see what he remembers. The main plan we\u2019ve put together so far is to plant a device in the TV station that will broadcast over the right frequency. If it works like Nightshade and I think, then this would block the Candle Cove signal. Ronin and Nightshade are putting together the device and programming to make this happen. Snowflake and I are working on the distraction piece of our plan. See there\u2019s no way we can get into the station and hook this up while the employees are still there. I don\u2019t remember who thought a bomb threat was a good idea, but we stuck with that to clear out the people. Even with getting everyone out, if we plant our device with a bomb threat it will be found. So Snowflake decided that the illusions should become a bit more real. We determined we could make a fake bomb for the authorities to find. They could pretty quickly figure out that it was a hoax and everything go back to normal. So I got a two pair of surgical gloves so nothing we bought could have fingerprints and then Snowflake and I went shopping. I knew the metal box and wires we could get at Radio Shack. The Play-Doh, alarm clock, and newspaper were from wherever we thought of first in different areas.<br /> <br /> When we got back, Ronin was coming in as well. She called us all together to fill us in. Tart, the believer in everything, was one of the officers that worked the investigation of Evelyn Peters. From the reports gathered at the scene, Evelyn\u2019s grandchildren were watching television. She became irrationally angry and forced everyone to leave the home. Tart had several details that were not included in the reports. He said the children claimed to be watching Candle Cove when Evelyn entered the room and she became hysterical. She had apparently told her own children never to let the grandchildren watch that show. Of course, we now know the adults would have no way of determining this, but apparently Evelyn could see it. After telling everyone to get out, Evelyn locked herself in the house. Tart said they found her hanging in front of the television, facing the screen. He also noted that there was a strange feeling of being watched in the room with the television. But strangely no one would turn it off. He asked another officer about it and was told that it wasn\u2019t necessary to turn it off. Tart compared the overall weird feeling to the way he felt while searching for children in the Patch.<br /> <br /> After that, Rose needed to talk to us before we went back to our various other projects. While she was in Taiwan, she learned that her uncle had disappeared. She said the family was not really fond of him as he was odd. Her description of Sung Guang seemed more scientific but her family thought he either was or planned to molest her as a child. However what Rose told was a very different story. He provided her with a place to discuss her visions of death without stigma unlike most of her family. She couldn\u2019t say if he was only interested in that or not, but it was still an outlet for her as a child. She of course investigated his home while still in Taiwan. She noted an odd sensation in the house but could not determine from what. There was also evidence of an occult ritual which took place before he vanished, but she was unaware of its purpose or origin. Lastly, and most importantly for me, she also found an Avernian Gate nearby. She asked, once we were less pressed for time in other problems, if the Krewe could help her learn the truth. I think it was fair to say I spoke for the Krewe when I told her we could help her find out about her uncle. But when I said I\u2019d also pop over for proper take out once she taught me the language, she actually smiled. It was a real smile, filled with Hope; something she rarely does.<br /> <br /> After that we split off into our working groups to finish preparing for our station raid. Snowflake and I were stumbling through what I thought would be a simple design in the Library when we heard a door slam and then a loud crash. We met the others as we ran upstairs. All the Krewe and companions were accounted for. It was the room with the weapons rack and the normal sarcophagus. When we opened the door, we could weapons and the Egyptian coffin stuck into the wall and door...as it hurled with great force. I checked with Snowflake, but this room wasn\u2019t one of the trap rooms. We couldn\u2019t find any visible reason so Snowflake checked for any hidden people. The House was clear, but it was apparent something had been there. Cupcake checked one of the weapons sticking out of the door for any psychic impressions and we hit the jackpot. An intruder was lured into the room and attacked. It had a male voice when it screamed as the blades and sarcophagus flew towards him. Ronin ran back to the control room and checked the cameras. Fu was playing in the hallway when he looked up and walked into a room as if looking for something. Then the door to that room closed. A blurry image appeared in the hallway above the kitchen. That put him dangerously close to our rooms. Strangely all the doors to our rooms closed and locked before he got to them. As we watched the video, we could see how the House was herding this uninvited guest down each hall until finally he came to this room. Then the door to that room slammed and we all heard the crash. I unlocked my Stigmata Shroud and stepped into Twilight.<br /> <br /> I ran to the window and scanned the withered landscape. All I could find were a few ghost cars on the road and Marguerite trying to get home again. It was a long shot as I estimated our stranger had about a 25 minute head start. I suspected a vampire because of the blurry video image, but I had no idea of any that might be able to step into Twilight. That alone was disconcerting. Though the fact that we were all being protected by the Fish God below was oddly comforting; at least to everyone but Ronin. She was greatly insulted that someone had sidestepped her security in such a way. We walked back to the room and Cupcake object read the floor where Snowflake pointed. She was able to give a slightly better description. He had yellow eyes, greyish green skin and his fingernails were very long. We couldn\u2019t get a good look at his face because he wore a hood with a cloth over his face. Almost like he expected and prepared for something like object reading. The only other details the floor could tell us were about his slippers and that he was average weight for his size. Once we got all that, we put the sarcophagus and weapons back in their original locations. Snowflake and I noted we\u2019d probably need to repair the walls since we wouldn\u2019t have the supplies to do so until tomorrow, but that was the least we could do in thanks to the House.<br /> <br /> I called Truman to see what he might know of such a creature as we discovered. I think they were watching a movie based on the background noise. Truman strongly disputed that a vampire could do something like that. Though he was very interested in trying to create a bloodline that he called the Teleportessi, which could do just that. That sounded like the late night, goofy ramblings of a college dorm, but I didn\u2019t mention it. We finished up and I thanked him as always. I heard Neon ask before Truman hung up if he was high. I took that to be a good sign we needed to go back to our bomb making. We finally finished it in such a way as to be believable a little before 0200 Hours. After that, I left for a short night of patrols.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to bed.<br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 21, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> I\u2019m back in New Haven, and it\u2019s late at night. I\u2019d probably be dead asleep right now if I hadn\u2019t slept off some of the jet lag this afternoon; I think I slept almost 6 hours.<br /> <br /> Gwen, and Alexia picked me up at the airport. I was really happy to see them again, and I got the feeling I was missed while I was away. It\u2019s nice to feel that you\u2019re a part of something like the krewe. Coming back from Taiwan, where I\u2019ve always been a bit of an outsider even in my own family (my father and mother excepted, of course), I was reminded of how much of a family the krewe is. And it made me feel good.<br /> <br /> Gwen and Alexia updated me on some things the krewe has been dealing with over the past couple of days, but they waited until dinner so that the whole krewe could discuss all the details and get everyone caught up. Gwen\u2019s been away on a new case, so to some degree, she needed filling in as well. So over dinner we had a long talk about all the horrible new things that have suddenly cropped up.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll try to summarize as best I can, but there\u2019s a lot of information, and I\u2019m not as familiar with it as most of the others. Essentially, we\u2019ve discovered evidence of a locally broadcast show called Candle Cove, which local children have been talking about lately. Doc, Tavia, Simon, Alexia, and Gwen all remember seeing the same show when they were growing up.<br /> <br /> The show itself sounds absolutely ghastly. It involved several mismatched pirate puppets and a little girl named Janice who got into adventures in a place called Candle Cove. The villain in the show was a terrifying marionette called the Skintaker that would frequently stare at the audience and say \u201cI\u2019m going to take your skin!\u201d while grinding its teeth back and forth. Everyone of us who had seen it remembered it being terrifying, and also seemed to recall that only children could see the show; adults saw only staticy noise on the screen while it was showing.<br /> <br /> The show ran two seasons, but the girl who played Janet changed at some point, and after that happened, the Skintaker\u2019s cape had grown longer. Doc and the others have a very strong, if vague suspicion that the original Janet had died and the Skintaker had taken her skin to add to his cape.<br /> <br /> The last episode of the show was apparently quite terrifying, with everyone screaming while the Skintaker ground his teeth and horrid, discordant calliope music played in the background. All the krewe members who saw the show felt a sense of dread and turned it off before the episode ended, but stories of missing children suggest that not all children were so wise, and that something terrible might have happened to those who watched the episode to its unpleasant end.<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, I\u2019m glad I didn\u2019t see the show when I was a child. What\u2019s odd is that the show seems to be a constant thing, appearing to most children in New Haven when they are around the age of five or six. That\u2019s when Doc and the others saw it, even though they are all very different ages.<br /> <br /> One other disturbing detail is that Tavia and Simon weren\u2019t bothered by the show, and in fact liked it, even though Tavia\u2019s late brother reacted just like everyone else. That certainly suggests that this show carries the taint of the Outsiders; after all, Tavia and Simon have Outsider blood. Of course, they are also a bit mad, which could also explain it.<br /> <br /> Candle Cove is currently airing at 4:00 every week day, and at the rate the episodes seem to be playing, we only have a couple of weeks before the show reaches its final episode. So we have to stop it before then.<br /> <br /> The others have already started on this. To gain access to the TV station\u2019s old footage, Natalie, Doc and Alexia made up a story about needing old tapes to film a parody show like Elvira, whatever that is. They managed to dig up the show\u2019s original tapes, and Alexia used the Industrial key to unlock her oracular abilities, and learned that the tapes haven\u2019t been shown since 1974, which makes their continued broadcast even more mysterious. She also got a glimpse of the woman who delivered them to the TV station, and sketched a ghoulish image of a tall, thin woman with a skull face and long, snow white hair and a white coat. She says the woman moved like a marionette, but her appearance was hidden by an illusion.<br /> <br /> She also learned that a woman named Evelyn Peters received delivery of the tapes. Gwen\u2019s going to investigate her tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Doc and the others also learned that the station manager when the tapes were originally shown was a man named Amos Wright. He\u2019s now retired and living in New York, but contacting him might not be a bad idea as well.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Doc and the others viewed the tapes at the station, but saw only static. Simon\u2019s geist, the Little Prince, could see the show plainly, though, as could Simon when he possessed his geist. Also, they later discovered that Chandra can apparently hear or see vague sounds or images on the tapes, but nothing clearly, likely thanks to her heightened vampiric senses.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know if its significant or not, but the krewe also met a young reporter named Becky Franklin while investigating the tape. Becky\u2019s been researching the Candle Cove phenomenon for some time, and was able to fill in some of the details. I got the impression that Alexia and Natalie were altogether too taken with Becky.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m a bit\u2026put off by my krewe-mates\u2019 plans in regard to the Candle Cove investigation. Granted, I can\u2019t really think of anything better, but I would prefer something a little less\u2026unethical. First off, the day before I returned from Taiwan, Alexia, and Karen decided to stalk the schools, with Simon using the Boneyard to eavesdrop on the schoolchildren and see if they were talking about the show. Naturally, the police accosted them and they never really learned anything useful.<br /> <br /> And now, they\u2019re planning on infiltrating a local radio station to secretly commandeer one of their unused broadcast signals in order to create a signal that should, hopefully, jam the frequency on which Candle Cove is being broadcast. It may only be a temporary solution to buy us more time to resolve the situation, but the idea itself is quite sound, and I approve. What I don\u2019t approve of is the method the others settled on to gain access to the station machinery. Simon and Doc and building a fake bomb, which they intend to plant in the station and then phone in a bomb threat to force everyone to leave the place! I can hardly believe we\u2019ve even considered such a plan! I disapprove.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I\u2019ll have no part of at, as I\u2019ll be investigating another matter entirely. Time is running out for us on resolving the ghosts of Sansbury Hall since students will be returning in less than a month, so I\u2019m going to get started on that. We had a bit of a revelation. We know that one of Alonia DeCastro\u2019s anchors is her amulet, and that the other is Adolphe\u2019s corpse. We\u2019ve been fools not to realize before now that his corpse must be somewhere in Sansbury Hall; otherwise, Alonia wouldn\u2019t be haunting the place! We just need to find it. If we can do that, we can resolve Alonia.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we still don\u2019t have Adolphe pistols, and it doesn\u2019t look like Ildefonso is going to be able to produce them. So the best we can do now is removing Adolphe from Sansbury Hall by letting Simon establish his own dominance over the building, thus destroying its value as an anchor for Adolphe. Then he will be solely bound to his pistols, wherever they are. Hopefully we\u2019ll be able to track them down soon.<br /> <br /> We also discussed moving Marjorie into Nilan Hall now that Bonnie-Lynn is truly gone. It would be a good way to keep the haunt there active, though I do feel a bit bad that we\u2019ve moved her around so much. The poor ghost is confused enough as it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 21, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve mostly been involved in preparing for our different plans since dinner. The bomb threat and signal jamming attempt at the radio station is going to happen tomorrow, so Doc and Simon spent the day constructing their fake bomb, while Natalie and Gwen have been working on software to generate the signal.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Alexia and I have been working on translating all the Taiwanese recipes I got from my great-aunt. All the recipes are in Taiwanese, and while I don\u2019t have any trouble translating most of the text from Chinese to English, I don\u2019t actually know what some of the ingredients are in English, so Alexia\u2019s help in sorting that out has been invaluable. I\u2019ve enjoyed working on it with her, and it\u2019s nice to see her becoming excited over all these new culinary possibilities.<br /> <br /> Gwen also had a chat with her police friends, and learned that Evelyn Peters committed suicide some years ago, though really we suspect that Candle Cove claimed her life somehow. Apparently she caught her grandchildren watching Candle Cove, and in an angry fit drove her family from the house. When they returned, she\u2019d hanged herself in front of the TV. And the police, while investigating, felt no desire to turn off the television. Very odd.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 21, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve had an intruder! Someone appeared inside the house and began looking about. It\u2019s not clear from the camera footage whether he meant to be here or not, as he seemed somewhat lost. But he was unable to investigate much in the house, because the will of the house itself channeled the trespasser into a certain room by locking all doors except those it wanted him to open. The room it led him to was full of weapons. As soon as the trespasser entered the room, the door slammed shut and the weapons flew from their racks to impale the intruder, but he teleported away just in time to avoid death. It was the slamming door that alerted us to something amiss, but the intruder was long gone before we arrived. I suspected at first that the trespasser might have been Maria attempting to further satisfy her curiosity over the house and its ley lines, but it wasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Thanks to Alexia\u2019s oracular abilities, we were able to learn that the intruder was a figure wearing a hooded cloak, and that he was a ghoulish thing with cold, grayish skin, long, yellowed nails and teeth, and yellow eyes. We have no idea what it might be. It\u2019s not a werewolf, and it seems unlikely that it\u2019s a vampire. According to Doc (who called his friend Truman to confirm the details), vampires can\u2019t teleport. While they might seem to do so by vanishing from sight, they are still present, just invisible, and in this case a vampire would have been slain by all the weapons. It\u2019s conceivable that it might have been a changeling, so I\u2019ll ask Mongler about it tomorrow. Until then, we really have no leads.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Doc is a Sweetheart</u><br /> <br /> Over dinner, I told the krewe about the mystery of my uncle\u2019s disappearance, and asked that they help me find out what happened to him once the more pressing matters of Candle Cove and Sansbury Hall have been resolved. They were all very willing to help out. And the Doc surprised me by asking if I\u2019d found any Avernian gates while I was in Taipei. I had, of course, and so he said we could head there whenever we liked through the Underworld. He has a ritual, one I\u2019ve considered learning myself, that will let us travel there quickly. So getting back to Taiwan to investigate what happened to my uncle will be far easier that I thought<br /> <br /> It brightened my day, and I can\u2019t express how grateful I am to Doc for giving me a little bit more hope. He even offered to use the ritual to pop in to Taipei for some authentic take-out from time to time after we\u2019ve figured out what\u2019s happened to Uncle Guang. Of course, he had one condition: I have to teach him to speak Mandarin. Which of course I\u2019d be happy to do.<br /> <br /> I hope Natalie realizes how lucky she is to have someone like Doc.<br /> <br /> <u>American Culture and Idioms</u><br /> <br /> <u>Angel</u><br /> <br /> Gwen says that I will absolutely adore a show she likes called Angel. It\u2019s not on the air anymore, but that hardly matters with her collection of DVDs and Netflix. Apparently it has a lot to do with vampires; she referenced it when we were discussing vampires and the fact that they don\u2019t actually have all the weaknesses the fictions say they do, like being unable to enter a home without being invited in first. I don\u2019t really think I would like a show about vampires, but Gwen seems convinced, so maybe I\u2019ll give it try.<br /> <u><br /> Home Security</u><br /> <br /> I think most of us were happy to see with our own eyes how the house protects it own. I have severe reservations about the violence with which it did so, but at the same time, the camera footage showed that it even made an effort to protect my kitten, Fu, by luring him safely away from the intruder.<br /> <br /> Gwen was not happy, though. She was upset that her security system had not detected the intruder, or perhaps that the intruder had foiled her system by simply teleporting in. This led to a discussion of motion sensors and other additional security measures that the rest of us decided were really too much.<br /> <br /> I made the mistake of saying that Gwen\u2019s system probably just couldn\u2019t be expected to handle some of the supernatural threats we are likely to face. Honestly, with my Caul and Shroud of Stillness, I could bypass it without too much trouble. But Gwen did not want to hear that. The system is her child, after all, and not to be insulted.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 21st<br /> <br /> -Tequila for the Tequila God!<br /> <br /> -Had too much Tequila last night. Possibly too much Girlfriend, my jaw hurts.<br /> <br /> -TMI?<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Jazzy comes back today.<br /> <br /> -Been doing research for the Big Secret. More information coming!<br /> <br /> -Hint: It\u2019s bigger than a breadbox!<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m not actually sure I have handled a breadbox.<br /> <br /> -Today seems more a Cognac for the Cognac God day. I don\u2019t think I need more Tequila anytime soon.<br /> <br /> -Jasmine looked happy to see me. That\u2019s nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Maybe being Strawberry Deathcake helps.<br /> <br /> -She is taking a no doubt badly needed nap. Europe is rough enough a flight I cringe to consider Asia.<br /> <br /> -Dinner at the Addams House. Filling Jazzy and Gwen in on Candle Cove stuff.<br /> <br /> -I feel a little left out Jasmine and I are the only ones who have not seen it. They all talk about stuff they all remember and it\u2026can make one feel left out.<br /> <br /> -They don\u2019t mean it of course, Bless \u2018em.<br /> <br /> -Explaining Tesseracts to Chandra.<br /> <br /> -There is such thing as a Tesseract.<br /> <br /> -Madeline L\u2019Engle, much like Fred Rogers, is the sort of Christian I wish all the rest were. On the offchance you are Christian and reading this, take them as your role models.<br /> <br /> -Time for Strawberry Deathcake to work with Gwen on a project!<br /> <br /> -\u2026huh.<br /> <br /> -Chez Satanique may be deadlier than expected.<br /> <br /> -Oh wow Substitutiary Locomotion.<br /> <br /> -Treguna Mekoides and Trecorum Satis Dee!<br /> <br /> -Hmm nothing happened. I must not be witchy enough.<br /> <br /> -Need moar Poisoned Dragon\u2019s Liver.<br /> <br /> -Wow, that movie is old.<br /> <br /> -Poor Gwen is freaking out.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d make her feel better if I could, but she would probably think it makes her weak. Or something.<br /> <br /> -Doc and Simon are back to working on their project. I can\u2019t go into what it is, just surprised Doc is so gung ho about it. I wouldn\u2019t be.<br /> <br /> -I mean if I were Doc. But then if I were Doc I\u2019d also be taller and have a deeper voice. Would reaching things on high shelves spoil me? It\u2019s a mystery.<br /> <br /> -Not on drugs, honest. :P<br /> <br /> -Man my childhood, at least the fantasy parts of it, have really been springing to mind. I blame this Candle Cove bullshit.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -OK, time to reassure Karen the House won\u2019t kill her. Again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVI</i><br /> <br /> The Teleportessi were a joke, obviously.<br /> <br /> A little poking around on the web should give you some information on Candle Cove. It is positively delightful little creepypasta. Of course, they have gotten back on the DeCastro plot by and large, but Candle Cove will be waiting.<br /> <br /> Always waiting.<br /> <br /> One tiny correction to Jasmine's journal Alexia, Karen, and Simon did discover the time of the show with their driving around schools hijinx.<br /> <br /> Well I hope you enjoyed stay tuned next time when an evil doll proves the most popular NPC I have introduced in this entire campaign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T15:51:27-08:00","id":16314,"title":"","content":"Hello folks, it\u2019s time for some journals. Just Doc and Jasmine today, though Natalie should have one next time unless something unexpected happens. As a note, some of the content this time may be a little triggery for some people, so just bear that in mind.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1120 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Bomb-making is hard work, least when you have no real idea what you\u2019re doing. Meditation took a bit this morning, but nothing unnecessary. I was able to eat breakfast with the Krewe and still get to the shop without any trouble. It\u2019s been a pretty normal day. I like that. Hopefully it\u2019ll stay that way.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019m going to start doing a little more planning for my drawings. Title a few that I plan to use as tattoos, organize the more elaborate images, and try to coordinate the Strawberry Deathcake ideas with things I can understand clearly how to draw. That should keep me busy for a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1410 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade came over for lunch today. There\u2019s an unspoken question hanging in the air but I\u2019m trying to keep everything positive. Driving her away now is really not the best idea I\u2019ve had lately. I am going to have to corner Karen and soon. When she left, I went back to drawing to help clear my head.<br /> <br /> A little later, Nightshade called me on a conference line so the Krewe could discuss new information. Rose spoke to Mongler about Changelings and our intruder. According to him, Changelings have to use doors. The weird part of that is that they have to use doors to travel between realms, similar to how we use Avernian Gates, or at least that\u2019s how I understood it. Monger did say that he thought it might have been wizards. The dinosaur man says they are around and they use big magics. I don\u2019t know if he means wizards like the kind of magic Snowflake and I use, or if there\u2019s something else out there that we haven\u2019t found yet. Knowing what Snowflake and I have uncovered and future talents we could develop, I don\u2019t want to think about any \u201cbig magics\u201d that we might have to deal with.<br /> <br /> In other news, Gretchen has officially crossed a boundary from crazy chick in the Library into Occult Researcher with Secrets of the Beyond. The good part of this is she knows it\u2019s not good for anyone else to deal with and wants nothing to do with involving other people. That means we don\u2019t need to kill her at least. Mongler is apparently doing well with dating Gretchen...so much so that she doesn\u2019t want him knowing about her work to protect him. She\u2019s unfortunately told him enough about it to make him want to keep her safe from whatever terrible thing she always talks about killing her. I talked to her about these things a while back before she and Mongler were together. By the sound of things, she\u2019s found significantly more now and expects to pay for her transgressions with her life and more. Given that she\u2019s been researching what (not who) originated the de la Por branch of the family, this puts Outsiders high on the list of possibilities. With that thought in mind, I have to wonder if it\u2019s ever going to be safe for Gretchen to leave Dark Haven Bluffs in any sort of permanent way? Anyway, this all came up because Mongler told Rose how worried he was. Rose, being very concerned over this budding relationship, spoke to Gretchen about things. I won\u2019t lie, I can only imagine how awkward and uncomfortable that whole conversation was. Rose didn\u2019t take well to the notion that Mongler should just be okay with Gretchen suddenly disappearing so her eternal soul could be tormented, or whatever Gretchen thinks is going to happen to her. We pretty casually committed our intention to find, stop, and somehow remove whatever might be coming. Snowflake entered the conversation about then and, even though I wasn\u2019t there, I could just see the look of cautious confusion on his face. He wanted to know, given his actual ancestry, where this put him. I immediately answered that he was not part of the problem. It\u2019s weird how he really does seem like my little brother. I don\u2019t know for sure, but I think sometimes he\u2019s afraid we\u2019ll forget that he isn\u2019t something from Outside. It\u2019s times like that that I really want to try and explain to him what a real family is like and how our Krewe is one. Either way, we are pretty sure that Gretchen is on the trail of Outsiders. And that means it becomes of interest to us. <br /> <br /> More immediately pressing, the Triangulation experiment is at 1600 Hours today after Snowflake, Rose, and Cupcake do some more elaborate recon of Sainsbury Hall. They are planning to wear the ear curls so we can all keep up with what\u2019s going on. I think someday we should record one of these little outings for something like an old style radio horror. I should probably talk to Nightshade and Ronin about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1550 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Well, this was a damned eventful afternoon.<br /> <br /> I was walking around the shop with my ear curl in, which kinda bothered a few of my more paranoid customers, so I could keep tabs on what the others were up to. It was a little tense to be honest. I mean Ronin and I were MIA when they first went to this place. Neither of us were going this time so we just had to listen. All the intel we had before today was that Aldophe and Alonia were sadistic and used magic to bind things and people to their will. Nightshade hated them from the start and I can\u2019t say I was part of their cheering section. So when the first thing Rose reports was seeing Alonia, I think we all tensed. The self-professed Djinn never caught Rose\u2019s position, but she also never stopped looking. That told me she was very aware someone was in the house. The last time they were at Sansbury, Snowflake hadn\u2019t mastered the art of controlling whole buildings with his Boneyard. I don\u2019t know why that sounds as dirty as it does when I reread it. Anyway, this time it was old hat for him and he immediately found two secret doors in dorm rooms on the top floor. What he described sounded like it used to be the master bedroom before they built a wall for the school\u2019s use. Behind door number one was a small bedroom. Adolphe was there sitting in a chair seemingly unaware. That Snowflake could see him meant that he was corporeal. That alone gave me a bad feeling. But as there was no attempt to counter Snowflake\u2019s scrying, he continued to the next room. Door number two was a larger bedroom with the walls painted black, furniture painted red, and a child\u2019s skeleton on the bed. Rose slipped in and looked around without the drawbacks of Snowflakes Boneyard. The skeleton had no skin but the bones were still holding together. That gave the medic in me fits, but the Sin-Eater didn\u2019t even blink. That\u2019s a weird disconnect to realize in your own mind. Anyway, there was also a red bow on the skull. I couldn\u2019t really say anything as there was an old woman in the shop at the time, but in my mind a million different torture scenes flickered by. Finally Rose noted some kind of ghostly effect on the skeleton. She opened one of the drawers in the room when a cloth doll suddenly sat up and looked at the skeleton. The skeleton of what used to be a little girl pushed its legs over the side of the bed and sat up. Then it started flailing around near the drawer. Tell me button eyes aren\u2019t creepy now. Rose made it nearly impossible to hit her and avoided the skeleton. Snowflake then initiated what would become a battle of wills. Using his control of the Boneyard, Snowflake opened the other drawer. The skeleton ripped its arm off and hurled it in front of the drawer. Nobody really saw that coming. Then the nightstand slid against the door to block any attempt at an exit. Meanwhile the cloth doll pulled itself into a standing position, which I\u2019m completely glad I did not see. It apparently started looking around while the skeleton continued to flail all around the room trying to attack an invisible invader. Rose was still in the room so it wasn\u2019t too far off. They both noticed a necklace that could be a charm in the drawer.<br /> <br /> Rose left the room with her shadow mastery, but the doll came out behind her and bolted. Somehow Rose and Snowflake both knew it was headed for the Evil Magic Circle room in the basement. Snowflake immediately checked but neither ghost, as apparently Alonia was corporeal too, seemed to notice. Snowflake mentally used a hall table to bash the doll and try to stop it from going downstairs. This worked for one slam, but then the doll threw the table off. I started having Puppet Master flashbacks at that point. Thinking on his feet, Snowflake used the doll\u2019s size and lack of fingers against it by locking all the doors around it in the hall, especially the one leading downstairs. That gave Rose and Snowflake some time to plan. <br /> <br /> With Snowflake controlling everything in the building and Rose able to move through walls, the plan became very simple. Snowflake would throw open all the doors, drawers, and anything else in Adolphe\u2019s room then Rose could run through and get a good look at everything. Even though I had some concerns with this idea, I kept quiet...really I think I was afraid if I spoke I would give them away somehow. But when Rose bolted in the room, Adolphe had transformed into some kind of demonic battle form. He was definitely looking for a fight but still couldn\u2019t see Rose. She got a good look at rings with the same stylistic design as the binding chest, so likely the proper keys. A red leather-bound book with a locking clasp sat inside the desk. A black cloak hung in the closet with ghosts sewn into it. In another drawer there was a long braid of ebony hair. Something other than the braiding held the thick mane together but it was the strange writing on the hardened braid that stood out. Rose took it to be Arabic in that frantic moment, which suggested it was perhaps Alonia\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Since Adolphe seemed unable to detect Rose, Snowflake glanced back to his captive in the hallway. But to his shock, the foot tall cloth doll was carrying a sofa toward the stairwell. Using the sofa as a battering ram, the doll crashed through the door then apparently made an obscene gesture at the shattered door. Snowflake, now fully invested in this challenge, latched the lock of the broken door just to make sure the doll realized this was far from over. Snowflake described the doll as being infuriated while it ran at top speed for the basement. I don\u2019t know how you can determine emotions on the face of a cloth doll, but I think I\u2019m glad I wasn\u2019t there to see it. <br /> <br /> Adolphe finally left the room to investigate the noise from the door, leaving Rose alone in the secret chamber. There was a brief moment when Snowflake and Rose both realized there was nothing stopping them from looting the entire room. Adolphe moved quickly down the stairs but apparently stopped short when Rose grabbed the braid of hair. Snowflake noted that in fact both ghosts reacted when that was touched. Both moved back toward the room, though Adolphe seemed more urgent to get there before anything happened, while Alonia was more ...eager to see if something happened. Snowflake\u2019s description was disturbing even beyond everything else that was going on. Fortunately when he saw them both coming, he immediately told Rose to get out. She phased through the wall and meet Snowflake as Cupcake lead him away from the building. At that point I was so wound up I had to demand to know what the fuck was going on? The timing was perfect as Cindy, the 9 year old that gets candles for her grandma, had just left. All I got back was Cupcake\u2019s very succinct description of the scene. <br /> <br /> And I quote, \u201cIt\u2019s really scary. We\u2019re running away!\u201d<br /> <br /> Once he knew Rose was clear, Snowflake dropped his Boneyard and they ran for the car. I don\u2019t know who was driving anymore, but I do remember Snowflake talking about how the whole house seemed to be angry and looking for them. There was also the doll. It was pressed...no leaned against a window on one arm and watched them (staring with its cold, dead, button eyes) drive away. Snowflake thinks that Adolphe has something bound in the doll and destroying the doll would set it free. That would likely be very bad for the DeCastros, but it\u2019s just as likely to be bad for everyone else.<br /> <br /> Now I think we\u2019re going to work on the triangulation. Nightshade should be here to get me soon. Ronin is at her office with Anders. The others, once they are clear of DeCastro\u2019s reach are still on the north side of town. Hopefully this works. I need to get the shop mostly together so I can close, again. And there\u2019s Nightshade. At least that part is always pleasant.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1650 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that didn\u2019t take long at all.<br /> <br /> The equipment worked the way I remembered and Nightshade thought it should. Unfortunately we figured out pretty quickly that the signal was bouncing off the atmosphere. Looking at the readings I got and hearing from the others, I figured we\u2019d have to be within 50 feet of the actual antenna to be able to pinpoint this thing. That wasn\u2019t what we were looking for, but you know you still have to hope.<br /> <br /> Cupcake noticed there was some really dark clouds starting to gather back towards AMC. We were trying to pretend it was just coincidence until we got back to Dark Haven Bluffs. Rose got a video message from Mongler asking, \u201cWhat did you do?\u201d We all thought this was amusing until we watched.<br /> <br /> The skies directly over Sainsbury Hall had blackened into midnight swirls of hate. Lightning arced from the Hall into the sky like stabbing blades and ball lightning spun and bounced around the building as if setting up a perimeter. Rain fell in sheets and pooled around the grounds, making the electrical fields all the more deadly. The Hall itself held an air of malice as if every window looked angrily for a target at which to last out. The entire scene pulsed with a sense of anger. Most frightening of all, just before the video ended a figure, too small to be human, climbed to the window sill on the top floor and looked directly at the camera.<br /> <br /> Talking with Mongler directly through speakerphone, we learned that the entire building somehow lurked upward about a foot. That caused such a tremor on campus that he went to investigate. His best description suggested that the house tried to jump or stand. The foundation and below were still visibly different than the rest of the wall. Even with the rain, the earth stained walls stood out. This just topped our list of things that have to be fixed...like now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2215 Hours, Thursday, July 22, 2010<br /> <br /> This is just the day that never ends.<br /> <br /> After we got back and had dinner, we all gathered together to inspect the loot. Before anything else, I took the braid of hair because I really wanted to see what the inscription said. The hair itself had been treated in some kind of solution which hardened and generally preserved the fibers. It reminded me of petrified wood for some reason. First of all, it wasn\u2019t written in Arabic \u2026 at least not any Arabic I\u2019ve ever seen. It looked more like some kind of code using Arabic as the base. Having some context for what I was looking at is really the only thing that helped me. The translated phrase read, \u201cFor Binding Djinn Alonia Nazeed\u201d<br /> <br /> We knew that rumors said Alonia wasn\u2019t human but her claims to be a Djinn just made her sound crazier. The fact that she is a ghost means she\u2019s clinging to memories of life. Still, given Adolphe\u2019s penchant for binding things, I had some worrying questions. Cupcake decided to start the night of object reading with the braid so we got the sketch pad and pencils, dictionaries, and anything else we might need and she went to it. The first sketch showed how the braid was made. A weathered Arabic man chanted while treating the hair which had obviously just been cut from Alonia, who knelt in what seemed to be a catatonic state nearby. The finished braid was over a 100 years old, but that did fall within Alonia\u2019s natural lifetime. The problems started when Cupcake tried to find out how it worked. She described her image as she saw it. Adolphe was trying to force Alonia to have sex with him while choking her with the braid. Alonia was already playing the part of Djinn, trying to kill him and seeing this as less a violation and more just another step in some kind of harsh ritual. Adolphe thought that if he could \u201cclaim\u201d her then it would allow him to conquer her into his own service. That\u2019s about the time Nightshade looked like she might be sick. Alonia, after having been \u201cconquered\u201d intended to steal Adolphe\u2019s soul anyway. Nightshade jumped up and ran out of the room at that point. Cupcake, like the others, realized too late that this would deeply affect Nightshade. Thankfully she didn\u2019t draw anything from the vision, as committing it to paper and creating a tangible image would have been worse, I\u2019m sure. I went after Nightshade at that point while the others were trying to apologize. But I stopped them from following. I wasn\u2019t rude or angry, I was in full medic mode by then. At that moment, Nightshade needed to be in a very controlled and safe environment and they were not part of that environment in this case. I\u2019m sure that sounded terrible and Cupcake especially was beside herself for triggering such a reaction.<br /> <br /> I found Nightshade in the fetal position in her room with Karen trying to understand what just happened. I stopped at the threshold of the room, not wanting to enter the control area. Karen looked up at me and I could tell she wanted to scream at me. I\u2019d seen that look before from friends and lovers of patients I\u2019d had before. I called her outside so I could explain. For her part, Karen handled the situation pretty well. She seemed to knew exactly why I was reacting the way that I was and the urge to scream at me went away. At least the obvious need on her face faded. I made sure that Karen knew I\u2019d be around tonight if or when Nightshade needed me. Otherwise, I would be around in case Karen needed anything. This might be the closest thing Karen and I can share to battle stresses. We have to be able to rely on each other to do what\u2019s best for Nightshade. It\u2019s times like this that I forget she\u2019s only 20. When I remember again, I feel sorry for her just like did all the soldiers that had to learn how to survive like this at that age. But these are the choices we make to protect those that are important to us.<br /> <br /> I went back down to give the Krewe a status report and try to calm Cupcake down a little bit. This was not a moment for assigning blame. Once that was as settled as we could be, Cupcake pulled out the lock picks and popped the lock on the Big Red Book (TM). She opened the book but then she suddenly looked terrified and slammed it back quickly. We were all concerned, then she said \u201csomething\u201d almost happened so she knew she had to close the book or else. Back to object reading again. Timing is everything after all. Cupcake figured out that opening the book without speaking a magical phrase caused a gout of fire to spray into the face of whoever opened the book and destroy the contents. The magical phrase was something else in that faux Arabic. I understood the mangled word for Master in there somewhere. Adolphe placed the spell on the book, which tells us he knows some kind of magic with which Snowflake and I aren\u2019t remotely familiar. While I can guarantee that won\u2019t last much longer, what the book actually contained was more disturbing yet. The names and trigger words for creatures bound to Adolphe as well as other various notes, all in that same code, were committed to the pages herein. I suspect Snowflake and I will be pouring over said pages in the days to come.<br /> <br /> Finally we came to the full length black cloak, made of fine, rich tapestry cloth. It was really nice until we saw the ghost face in the cloak. It, he just seemed to loll around unaware of much of anything anymore. Cupcake object read this as well. And while we had yet to find any redeeming qualities for the DeCastros, the history of this garment passed the final judgement for me. Adolphe wove another spell into the cloak and there were three names of entities bound into it. Only one was of a human nature. The cloak was imbued with the power to bestow the sight of Twilight to the wearer for a time when enough blood has been poured over it. Additionally, during that time of Twilight access, the wearer can will himself to be untouched by ghost, spirit, even Outsider. This made us all pause and consider what else may be bound in the well tailored cloth before us. I\u2019m not sure if Cupcake was just desensitized by that point or was just angry, but her next bits of information really grabbed the tiger by the tail. The most recent, emotionally charged moment involving the cloak gave our diviner images of Adophe binding a woman-spider hybrid spirit into a cloth doll. Of this scene, she did sketch an image. A sexuality or feminity spirit was eaten by, more likely feed to, a spider spirit. We suspect DeCastro needed it to be able to relate on more of a human level. Snowflake stared at the image of the button-eyed doll for some time with a look that I might describe as malicious. Eventually Cupcake pulled the sketchbook back, breaking Snowflake\u2019s concentration on the hated doll. This time she asked the cloak for it\u2019s most emotionally charged moment of all time. I don\u2019t think I could have inflicted such an image on myself, but Cupcake has perceived through madness time and again. It terrifies me that I can write that so casually. Anyway, she refused to draw the images she received. And in fact, she would only relay a few key points to us. There was a very bad sexual event between Alonia and something which was left as, \u201cit was bad, don\u2019t ask.\u201d This awful union was merely a component of another ritual by Adolphe to summon a creature Snowflake identified with some shock as a Golmuth. This one appeared to DeCastro as \u201cbeing made of Darkness with a feminine form.\u201d Yes the d is capitalized based on the description. By all accounts, this was an Outsider which Adolphe so brazenly summoned. Given the horror stories from victims and rumors from Sainsbury Hall, nothing convinces me that the DeCastros have even slowed down in their dealings with the Outside. <br /> <br /> But they will. <br /> <br /> For most ghosts, I want to follow our mandate and help them find freedom and release them from whatever bonds chain them to this world. But in this one instance, I have become the judge and jury. The DeCastros have raped, tortured, murdered, and then bound whatever was left of countless entities through the years. There will be no pardon or release for Adolphe. There will be no unchaining of the beast that is Alonia. For them, Justice will not be merciful or swift. Their sentence will be an eternity of bondage, the same fate they have forced so many creatures into for their own pleasure. I will see this reign of slavery and torment end.<br /> <span style=\"color:red\"><br /> This I swear in blood.</span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, July 22, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not meeting Jean for training again until next week, but I went to Albertus Magnus this morning to ask Mongler about our nocturnal visitor last night. He didn\u2019t think the visitor sounded like any changelings he knew, and changelings don\u2019t have the power to teleport like our intruder did, if only because they can only travel through doors, and our trespasser didn\u2019t seem to do that, exactly.<br /> <br /> But Richard also wanted to talk to me about Gretchen. She\u2019s convinced that she\u2019s going to die eventually as a result of her research, and has told him to be prepared for that. She won\u2019t tell him any more or let him try to help because she doesn\u2019t want him to get tangled up in whatever is going cause her so-called \u201cinevitable demise.\u201d Richard is naturally quite upset and anxious about this. He loves her, and feels shut-out and helpless.<br /> <br /> So I went home and had a heart-to-heart chat with Gretchen about it. I thought maybe she was worried that Tzipporah de la Poer would eventually kill her, but there\u2019s more to it than that. Everyone else who has ever researched the ultimate origins of the de la Poers and Fishbornes has vanished without a trace, and Gretchen assumes some dark thing from outside the balance of shadows has killed them or otherwise stolen them away to some sort of horrible elsewhere. She thinks it\u2019s only a matter of time before the same happens to her, yet she\u2019s not willing to abandon her research. Indeed, she thinks the only reason something hasn\u2019t come for her is because it fears the Thing Under the House.<br /> <br /> So, I got the others involved, and we talked Gretchen into letting Richard help more. She doesn\u2019t want him to be hurt, but shutting him out like that is selfish. And he really might be able to help protect her. After all, he has a lot of experience dealing with god-like entities from outside our world, what with the Gentry and all. She eventually relented, and I hope she really will let Richard (and us, for that matter) be a part of what she\u2019s doing so that we can help keep her from falling to the same twisted fate that befell her predecessors.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, July 22, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> What an exciting evening! I haven\u2019t felt such an adrenaline rush since we fought the Rose Bride. I really feel like we\u2019ve accomplished something, though I must admit a bit of trepidation over the consequences of my actions tonight.<br /> <br /> Late in the afternoon, we split into three groups to triangulate the source of the <i>Candle Cove</i> broadcast signal. Ultimately, we didn\u2019t have much luck. Natalie says the signal is bouncing off the atmosphere, making it very hard to locate.<br /> <br /> However, Simon, Alexia and I formed the group going to Albertus Magnus, and we had a secondary agenda. We were going to explore Sansbury Hall more thoroughly to try and find Adolphe DeCastro\u2019s corpse and anything else that might be helpful in sealing him and Alonia away. We never managed to find the corpse, unfortunately, but we found many other things that we hope will help us conquer the DeCastros.<br /> <br /> I drew the Shroud of Stillness around me, vanishing from sight, while Simon entered a trance just outside Sansbury Hall so that he could help me navigate the place. Alexia remained outside to watch over Simon. The place seemed deathly quiet at first, but the ghosts became aware that something was wrong fairly quickly. When I saw Alonia wandering around, looking for an intruder, I unlocked my Caul with the Stillness key so that I was little more than an invisible shadow. I remained so well hidden that neither the ghosts nor their servants ever knew exactly where I was.<br /> <br /> Alonia seemed vulnerable and harmless when I saw her, but I am pretty resistant to such charms, and easily realized that it was a trick designed put me off my guard. But since Alonia was lurking on the lower floors, I decided to avoid her at first and, at Simon\u2019s prompting, moved upstairs, where he had detected two well-hidden secret rooms.<br /> <br /> Instead of trying to sort out how to open the secret doors, which would have given away my position anyway, I simply phased ghost-like through the walls into the rooms. The first was a small, dusty room painted in disturbing shades of black with blood red furniture. A little girl\u2019s skeleton lay on the bed, her wispy hair still clinging to her skull, bound by a red hair bow.<br /> <br /> I quietly explored the room, and when I opened the night stand drawer, a worn rag doll sat up and looked around. It was possessed by some sort of spirit, and it immediately animated the child\u2019s skeleton, which began flailing erratically around the room in search of the intruder. In order to avoid it, I became an incorporeal shadow, and remained that way, becoming solid again only enough to swipe what items I though might be useful to us.<br /> <br /> While the skeleton flailed around the room, I managed to steal a necklace resting in another drawer in the room. Simon helped out quite a lot by using his complete mastery over the place to open drawers and cabinets and boxes for me as I prowled about. We made a fantastic team!<br /> <br /> Eventually, the doll decided there was no one there to find, and it left the room, heading toward the ritual rooms in the basement. Simon wisely decided to keep it from going there, and used his control over the building to toss furniture on top of the doll to pin it, but it was surprisingly strong (though perhaps no stronger than a person), and was able to push the furniture off and keep going. So Simon closed and locked the doors around it, leaving it trapped.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I slipped into the other secret room, which was furnished like a bedroom with a wardrobe, chest, and night stands. Adolphe\u2019s ghost was there, sitting on the bed with a look of terrible concentration on his face. He was waiting, ready to act if necessary. It would have been too risky for me to open anything myself, which would have given away my position, so Simon again helped out by simultaneously opening everything in room so that I could see what there was to see.<br /> <br /> When he did that, Adolphe transformed into a warped, twisted creature that was only vaguely human anymore. I\u2019d heard that some ghosts could do such things, but it was still quite terrifying. With Adolphe there, I couldn\u2019t really take anything from the room, but then the doll downstairs began tossing furniture into the doors to destroy them. The crashes drew Adolphe\u2019s attention, and he dashed from the room to see what was wrong. I took that opportunity to snatch everything I could find in the room and then leave the building by phasing through the wall and dropping shadow-like to the ground below. I didn\u2019t reappear until I was safely at the car with Simon and Alexia, who also fled when I told them I\u2019d escaped with Adolphe\u2019s possessions.<br /> <br /> I managed to escape with several items:<br /> <br /> The necklace from the doll room (which I can make into a charm).<br /> <br /> A locked book bound in red leather.<br /> <br /> A few rings inscribed with arcane sigils that match those on some of the drawers of the Obsidian Box (keys to the box?)<br /> <br /> A ritual cloak with ghosts bound into it.<br /> <br /> A bound braid of Alonia\u2019s hair, which has been shellacked in some form of oil and has Alonia\u2019s name painted on it in occult markings onto it.<br /> <br /> Adolphe was extremely upset when I snatched Alonia\u2019s hair, and the entire house roared! As we made our escape, the place shuddered and shook. According to Mongler (who sent video from his phone), clouds gathered over campus shortly after we left, and a lightning storm danced around Sansbury Hall for an hour or so. The entire building seemed to be fiercely watching and looking for us. I\u2019ve never seen a ghost so furious before! Binding Adolphe and Alonia into their anchors is not going to be easy, I\u2019m afraid.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, July 22, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> Alexia has had an opportunity to examine the DeCastro objects and to read a bit of their past by manifesting the Oracle. The DeCastros were terrible, horrid people. I don\u2019t even want to write about some of the things they did. But I think the most important discovery is that Alonia isn\u2019t a djinni at all, but was insane enough to believe she was, and somehow Adolphe used that to dominate her sexually and control her. But she always wanted to kill him in return, which we might be able to use to our advantage.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes<br /> <br /> Wizards</u><br /> <br /> Mongler suggested that out nocturnal trespasser might be something that serves a wizard. Of course there are wizards. Why wouldn\u2019t there be? There are vampires, werewolves, ghosts, and faeries, after all. But even saying that, wizards seem somehow more fantastic than the rest of the lot.<br /> <br /> According to Mongler, the wizards he knows of have powers much greater than those offered by the simpler occult magics that Simon and Doc have been exploring. They are more like Gandalf from the <i>Lord of the Rings</i> than country witches or Taoist mystics.<br /> <br /> I wonder if Maria Smith is a wizard. The intruder doesn\u2019t seem like something she would use, but then again, we don\u2019t really know anything about her.<br /> <u><br /> <br /> American Culture and Idioms</u><br /> <br /> <i>Bedknobs and Broomsticks</i><br /> Mongler mentioned a movie called <i>Bedknobs and Broomsticks</i> when we were discussing the existence of wizards. No one has really told me what the movie is about, or whether it\u2019s realistic or not, but apparently it has to do with witches and wizards.<br /> <br /> Fizban<br /> Also when we were talking about wizards, Gwen mentioned a wizard named Fizban. I\u2019ve heard of Harry Potter and Gandalf and whoever Christopher Lee was (I\u2019m half Kiwi, so of course I know about the <i>Lord of the Rings</i>\u2026), but I\u2019d never heard of Fizban. Apparently neither had anyone else aside from Gwen. He\u2019s apparently a wizard from some fantasy novel she read.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Protectiveness</u><br /> While we were discussing Mongler\u2019s wish to help protect Gretchen, Alexia seemed to realize for the first time that Chandra has a very similar desire to protect her. She\u2019s right, though I think the situations are also a bit different, if only because Alexia is far more capable of protecting herself than Gretchen is. Still, the sentiment is the same.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I find that sort of chivalry romantic. I love the way Doc is always standing by Natalie to watch over and protect her. It would be nice to have someone like that in my life. But it seems the Bride and I have become very good at protecting ourselves and others. I wouldn\u2019t want Julian or Jean or even Karl putting themselves at risk for me. As romantic as the gesture might be, I wouldn\u2019t be able to live with myself if they were hurt of killed on my behalf. Which is, of course, what Gretchen is going through. So I feel a bit hypocritical advising her to let him help. Is it so selfish to prefer your own death to that of those you love?<br /> <br /> In any case, I suppose I can justify it because unlike Jean and Julian, Mongler is more than capable of handling supernatural horrors. I can think of no one better to help keep Gretchen safe and sound.<br /> <br /> <u>The DeCastro Objects</u><br /> Here are the most important things Alexia learned about the DeCastro objects:<br /> <br /> <u>Alonia\u2019s Hair Braid</u><br /> The braid was made over 100 years ago, but well within Alonia\u2019s mortal lifetime. The hair seems to have been taken from her against her will, and Adolphe established his dominion over her by dominating her sexually while she tried to kill him. This revelation shook Natalie\u2019s fragile psyche, and the poor girl had to leave us to cope with her own flashbacks of being raped. I felt terrible for her, but Doc assured us that it was something she would have to work through on her own.<br /> <br /> I wonder if we might be able to use the hair braid to prevent Alonia from attacking us. Maybe we can even get her to attack Adolphe.<br /> <br /> <u>DeCastro\u2019s Book of Binding</u><br /> The red-bound book was guarded by a protective fire spell that must be deactivated each time it is opened. The books contains Adolphe\u2019s notes on the creatures he has bound and the methods for doing so.<br /> <br /> <u>The Ritual Cloak</u><br /> The ritual cloak was worn by DeCastro when he conducted rituals. A ghost and two other spiritual entities are bound into the cloak. It was last used when Adolphe bound a spirit into the doll. The spirit was a spider spirit who had consumed (and fused with) a spirit of femininity or fertility or something similar. The cloak was also used when he committed a sickening ritual to summon and bind an outsider - something known as a gulmoth. He had a conversation with the gulmoth, but I we don\u2019t now exactly what it was about.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLVII<br /> </i><br /> I can\u2019t stress how amused people were with the doll. Seriously. They wanted to take it home and make it a mascot.<br /> <br /> I felt that the information gathering mission went well. There seemed an appropriate amount of danger, and the PCs did a good job of using their manifestations intelligently. And I think Simon\u2019s player got rather a charge from using Boneyard. Jasmines combination of powers to be invisible and pass through walls proved extremly effective...her player's use of Caul, Shroud and Keys is remarkably effective.<br /> <br /> Industrial Oracle is extremely handy. We have three Spooks with Oracle, but Alexia gets a lot of use with hers especially. Though Aura Perception for Gwen is always handy\u2026though it costing Plams limits it a little.<br /> <br /> Again the DeCastro story is inspired by The Terrifying Tale of James Magnus from Ghost Stories for New World of Darkness.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s breakdown does not remove her from the game for long. She made her Resolve + Composure roll and was back in the action relatively early on in the next session. She was due for a few cracks to appear in her armor, and Alexis\u2019s rather vivid descriptions seemed as good a place as any. She had to go back to her \u201cclean\u201d room at her townhouse for the night, but she was back participating the next session though fear not (or much to your consternation, depending on how you feel about Natalie I guess. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> Stay tuned till next time, true believers, when the team returns to Sansbury Hall, Natalie goes on TV and they commit an act of terrorism. Next session focuses mostly on the DeCastroes, though the end relates to <i>Candle Cove</i>. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T15:54:55-08:00","id":16317,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s that time friends, last session of 2011. Let\u2019s see what our heroes are up to. Note Gwen is not present as her player was under the weather and had to miss.<br /> <i><br /> Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0230 Hours, Friday, July 23, 2010<br /> <br /> I thought we were finished with the loot, but after I stomped off and wrote my last entry, I came back to learn of one more thing we needed to know about. It was a silver oval necklace with a smooth gem on the plate. <br /> <br /> Cupcake did her object reading thing and learned it belonged to a dark-haired woman and possibly her daughter as well. Cupcake watched the images in her head, turned white, then green, than jerked her eyes open and started sketching. The woman, it turns out, was Denise James. The same Denise James whose ghost-ridden corpse holds Alonia\u2019s locket in her grave. This just gets better and better. I hope I get to beat on Adolphe at least a little before we lock him in the guns. I suspect Nightshade would like a piece of Alonia too. Anyway, back to the reading. The little girl was Denise\u2019s daughter and also the skeleton from Sainsbury Hall. This was the possible charm Rose found. I realized that it could be used for either Passion or Stillness. When Rose brought it up, Cupcake turned a little green again and immediately refused to let Rose do anything with the necklace related to Passion. Given the past of the ghosts we are dealing with, no one asked any questions.<br /> <br /> Nightshade came back in just after that, thankfully, and was very reserved. She let us know she was going to her townhouse for the night. She already reminded me, almost apologetically, that she wouldn\u2019t make lunch today due to recording the show for tonight. I wanted to take the right middle ground, so I assured her that I loved getting to spend my lunches with her, but just like me being gone during the day, we all have to work sometimes. That seemed to go over okay. She was definitely still not happy with the world, but she was stable. She hugged me and gave me a soft kiss before she left. I told her to call me if she needed anything. Still not going out tonight just in case.<br /> <br /> After that, Snowflake and I took the Big Red Book (TM) down into the Library for me to translate. Cupcake made sure I knew the code word before we left. Tavia and Chandra were playing chess with Karen venting about what happened to Nightshade. Gretchen was studying in another corner of the Library. Karen looked a little sheepish when she saw me but I understand how frustrating it can be. I made sure she was actually okay, given how out there things have been. I know that\u2019s awkward, but sometimes you need to know that someone else that understands is there when you need it. <br /> <br /> After all the touchy-feely moments were past, I made a general announcement that no one should try to say the words I would be using as terrible things were in this book. The last thing I need is for someone to mispronounce the key as a joke and the book explode. Tavia rambled about how you have to be careful when dealing with extra dimensional things for the same reason, but sometimes getting traps like this to suck people in works really well. She stopped talking when even Snowflake could only stare in response. She takes the concept of \u201clittle sisters are weird\u201d to a whole new level. This pseudo-code was some bastardization of Arabic and took me a little bit to get accustom to it, but after that it was just a matter of reading and writing it down in a journal that won\u2019t involve fire to the face. I read through things before writing it down as Snowflake and I agreed that some things didn\u2019t need to be readily available. Usually if I had to have him help me understand what a translation meant, I didn\u2019t write it down. The short version of the notes were scary enough as it is. There was some mostly useless blackmail information on all the neighbors at the time. That was at least slightly amusing. Then we found various people Adolphe had programmed to gather his stuff in case he ever vanished. That was a longer list than I was comfortable with. However Denise was on that list. As was Deacon James, her husband (we think), who was to come and collect several of Adolphe\u2019s more important personal affects. This could easily be where the pistols are. My blood ran cold when I realized the address was Deanna\u2019s house. Clarissa Walthstone\u2019s friend Deanna James might actually be the key to removing Adolphe and Alonia. That was truly terrifying.<br /> <br /> We learned, though it wasn\u2019t as surprising as I thought at first, that Adolphe occasionally traded books with one Erasmus Fishborn. Snowflake nodded and pointed to the old family tree that was now hanging on the Library wall. Erasmus was several greats back, but he was there...listed as having lost himself to his work in \u201849. Erasmus was also on the list of people to collect Adolphe\u2019s things, though not on the programmed list. He was charged with damage control, looking after the books, and keeping people out of the house that we know as Sainsbury Hall. Erasmus had a wife, Petunia, that was noted for gnawing on Alonia at social functions. Adolphe listed in his notes that Alonia should take it so personally as Petunia does this to alot of people. Snowflake filled me in that Petunia had problems with enjoying the taste of flesh a little too much. She developed the habit of gnawing on people to help keep the problems down. But after the second child when missing, they put her in a sanitarium. Well that\u2019s not what he said, but that\u2019s what I think he meant. Either way, she was listed on the family tree as having died of Hoof and Mouth disease in \u201836. I didn\u2019t really believe any part of that, but by this point, I knew better than to ask. Whatever part of Erasmus\u2019 work he was lost to led to the Rat Section of the House being closed off. Tavia noted that he was one of the Rat Talkers in the family, like Alistair. Enough said there. I also found strange recipes for what looked like perfectly normal shoe shine/polish and laundry instructions written in the side margins of the book of evil. There is no fucking way this is legit. I don\u2019t know what kind of code this is, but I will break it. Snowflake might have a healthy obsession with taking control of all Adolphe\u2019s possessions, but I will know his secrets. And when I do, I will lay them bare and use them against him.<br /> <br /> As I could tell Gretchen was trying to spy on us, like a curious little kid, I took a break and pulled her into the conversation. We talked about her research and I tried to get her to accept our help officially. The best I could do is get her to agree to let us know when she thought she was on to something. The whole bit about Mongler being worried didn\u2019t sit completely well with her, but it did lead into an interesting discovery about Snowflake. He has apparently learned a ceremony which allows a way to cheat Death. He called it the Devil\u2019s Bargain, which was appropriately sinister for something that can extend your life. The short version is that someone has to willingly give up years of their life so that another can be granted that same amount of time. If the recipient would normally die during that time, they live on until the time runs out. If they are killed during that time, they live on as well. I\u2019d think it was much worse if it didn\u2019t involve the willing transfer of years. I\u2019m going to make sure neither Rose or Nightshade hear about this, but for very different reasons. Gretchen thought this was a great way to make money. Using it as an insurance policy, parents would gladly through their life away to guarantee their children would live on. I gave her a dirty look that I think Rose would have approved of...I mean damn. This is what could make it much worse.<br /> <br /> After that I realized what time it was and decided to call it a night. I made sure my phone was on charge and the ringer up just in case Nightshade needed me. Now that I have this written out, I think I\u2019m going to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Friday, July 23, 2010<br /> <br /> I woke up in a brief panic that Nightshade had called and I didn\u2019t hear. But I checked the phone and found nothing was waiting and no missed calls. Meditation took about an hour this morning, but I got up early, so no big deal. <br /> <br /> Snowflake was up for breakfast this morning, which was odd. He was all dressed up and awake which I didn\u2019t understand at first. But before I left, he let me know he was going to go and meditate in his grave. I have no idea why but it somehow makes him feel more confident afterwards. Maybe I\u2019ll ask him to explain to me someday. <br /> <br /> After that I went to work. And it\u2019s been a slow morning. I had a group of guys come in to get supplies before they left for a camping trip this weekend, but after that it\u2019s been pretty quiet. We\u2019ll see how long that lasts.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1425 Hours, Friday, July 23, 2010<br /> <br /> About the time Nightshade would normally stop in for lunch, I started getting a stream of random texts and pics on my phone. I\u2019m pretty sure she was nervous and releasing tension. It was really cute. She was flustered about the wig she wanted to wear and this or that about her clothes. I told her she was going to be gorgeous in any outfit she put on. While I think she appreciated the sentiment, it wasn\u2019t terribly useful in helping her sort out her dilemma. There was a lull in texting and then I got one from Karen telling me to tell Nightshade not to wear a damn wig. This was really funny to me, but I wisely kept that to myself. I got another text from Karen a few minutes later telling me that Gretchen was running around in a school girl uniform. Without the \u201cbenefit\u201d of hearing Gretchen, that was briefly a nice thought.<br /> <br /> Then we settled down as Rose, Snowflake and Cupcake were going back out to Sainsbury Hall to check for bodies underground. They were in a little too much of a hurry to get away before to really do much with it. Ear curls in place, Rose called Mongler to let him know they were coming. He didn\u2019t think this was a great idea since the house was still visibly angry, but Rose assured him they weren\u2019t going to be in sight of the house this time. I really hate every recon mission we go on these days. As soon as they got settled a building or so away, Snowflake let us know he found the bodies. Yeah that\u2019s not singular. There were eight bodies buried below the basement. Nothing gave us any clue as to which one, if any, were Adolphe or Alonia. To make matters worse, Snowflake found a cavern under the house. The underground river that feeds AMC connected to a cave leading to the cavern. In the cave there as a 16\u2019 long black blob with two huge eyes and no face. It was making noises that Snowflake could really only compare to a crying baby. He had no idea what it was, other than the strong possibility of an Outsider. That was enough for the recon. Not much any of us can do with the house looking to eat us and a monster underground.<br /> <br /> That lead to our discussion of trying to use the braid to resolve Alonia\u2019s connection to Adolphe\u2019s body. That way at least we could force her away from Adolphe while we either deal with him or try to take care of her and Denise. Either way, it was something we weren\u2019t ready to do right then. The headed back to the Bluffs and I went back to drawing.<br /> <br /> Hopefully tonight will work out better.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2245 Hours, Friday, July 23, 2010<br /> <br /> We did it!<br /> <br /> Rose, Snowflake, Nightshade, and Ronin headed out with the materials, while I walked into town with my Phantasmal Shroud up. For once, I could be sure no one that saw me would know who I was. Wearing gloves so there would be no prints, I placed the call from a pay phone. Then I caught a cab back to a random house out past Malard\u2019s. Through the curl, I could hear as Snowflake killed the security, then Rose and Nightshade snuck in. I\u2019m pretty sure Ronin was mumbling to herself about how she could find a way to make security against this kind of thing. She just does not give up. Anyway, they all managed to do their thing without a hitch and Ronin got them the hell out of there before anyone was the wiser. We all met back at the House where Cupcake had prepared Post-Bomb threat Brownies. <br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re just winding down from the adrenaline and nerves. All in all, I think this was a good day.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, July 23, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I had an especially good meditation this morning. I reached such a transcendent sense of calm and tranquility that I almost felt as though all was right with the world. I haven\u2019t been so at peace since Richard died.<br /> <br /> Last night, Doc and Simon did some research using Adolphe\u2019s journal. They discovered a lot of blackmail material on the DeCastro\u2019s neighbors, and that the DeCastros had borrowed books from Erasmus Fishborne, one of Simon\u2019s forebears (but that\u2019s hardly surprising, now is it?). They also learned more about Denise James, the woman who was buried with Alonia\u2019s locket and whose necklace we found in the child\u2019s room in Sansbury Hall. Denise and Deacon James were friends of the DeCastros, and the DeCastro\u2019s must have \u201cprogrammed\u201d them to remove certain items from Sansbury hall when the DeCastros died. We think they must have Adolphe\u2019s pistols, so we need to find a way to get them. The problem is that Denise and Deacon are the great-great grandparents of Deanna James, who is Clarissa\u2019s friend (Clarissa the psychokinetic). Actually this might be a good thing, since we sort of know her, but also bad because we\u2019d rather she not become tangled up in all of this.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 23, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> Natalie came home today, and I was glad to see she was doing much better than when she left last night. She seems to have managed to put down the traumatic memories triggered by Alexia\u2019s descriptions of the DeCastro\u2019s horrid activities. I think this is a good sign. She seem to be recovering, and regaining more psychological stability. Doc\u2019s been a good influence on her, I\u2019m sure.<br /> <br /> When she arrived home, she ran across Simon and I chatting, and announced that she was going to go play piano. I think we both got the impression that an audience would be welcome, so we went and listened. She mostly played swing songs like the Andrews Sisters, which suited me just fine. And she played them well.<br /> <br /> After that, she had to go get ready for her show. She hadn\u2019t talked much to me about it aside from a few words over dinner or breakfast (I think it\u2019s something that came up while I was in Taiwan), but she\u2019s filming host segments for a sort of vintage horror movie show that will be aired later tonight. I certainly wished her luck. It sounds like just her thing, and I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll perform wonderfully. Unlike some of us, she likes being on camera.<br /> <br /> Doc is at work, Gwen\u2019s off on a case again, and Natalie is filming now. So it\u2019s up to Simon, Alexia and I to investigate Sansbury Hall more this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 23, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s filming was a success. She seems pleased with it, anyway. I suppose we\u2019ll all watch her show tonight. I don\u2019t expect to enjoy the movie, but I\u2019d like to support Natalie, at least.<br /> <br /> Simon, Alexia and I returned to Sansbury Hall this afternoon. I called Mongler to let him know, and he was a bit anxious about it since the building is still agitated. We didn\u2019t go within sight of the building, and remained hidden behind a neighboring dormitory. I was prepared to venture into the place under the cloak of my Shroud again, but it wasn\u2019t necessary. Simon unlocked his Boneyard with the Grave-Dirt Key and scanned the grounds for buried bodies.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, he found eight of them. And we have no idea which belongs to Adolphe. That\u2019s not all, though. There\u2019s an underground river running beneath Albertus Magnus, and it run close to Sansbury Hall\u2019s foundations. Near it is a sealed chamber that contains some sort of outsider beast that Simon described as a black, shadowy blob with two huge eyes and moth that mewed like a whimpering baby. I\u2019m not one to curse, but I really want to right now. This haunting is becoming more and more tangled all the time, and I intensely dislike the DeCastros meddling with outsiders, summoning them into this world where they certainly don\u2019t belong. If I weren\u2019t so centered from my morning mediatations, I think I would be really, really angry about all of this. Angry enough to want to destroy Adolphe DeCastro utterly. But as it is, I\u2019m simply resolved to end the stain of his abominable practices once and for all.<br /> <br /> We left the area of Sansbury Hall then. Simon\u2019s going to do more research in Adolphe\u2019s book. I called Mongler to let him know what we had found, and we discussed the krewe\u2019s plans to seal the DeCastro\u2019s into their anchors. He didn\u2019t like that idea, and warned that things that are sealed away often find a way to escape eventually, though it may take centuries. I assured him that we really didn\u2019t have any other options in this case, because we aren\u2019t going to be able to resolve Adolphe and Alonia peacefully.<br /> <br /> After returning home, Simon called Deanna to see if she\u2019d be willing to help us out. I didn\u2019t think it was a good idea to get her involved, but Simon managed to engage her interest by suggesting that she had an opportunity to become involved in something paranormal, not unlike her friend Clarissa. I was a bit cross with Simon after his conversation, and I made him promise not to lead the poor girl on with false promises.<br /> <br /> In any event, Deanna was a bit wary. She doesn\u2019t really know us. So she and Simon are going to meet at a caf\u00e9 tomorrow to talk about it more.<br /> <br /> I stayed on campus for awhile and swam. It was so refreshing to get back into the pool and to lose myself to in the water again. After my meditation today and all the frustrations of dealing with the DeCastros, I feel a strong desire to lose myself deep in the ocean like I did when the Bride was helping me grasp the Primeval Key.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 23, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> We executed the krewe\u2019s ill-advised plan to stage a terrorist bombing on the radio-station today. I\u2019m still against it, but I didn\u2019t have much choice but to help them, since the rest of them had made up their minds, and they needed someone to sneak in and plant the fake bomb. I\u2019m really the only one who could pull that off, so I did it, but I\u2019m not proud of it.<br /> <br /> The rest of the plan went off well. Doc placed an anonymous bomb-threat call and once the radio station was cleared out, Natalie slipped inside to program the jamming signal that we hope with shut down the Candle Cove broadcast for a time.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad that\u2019s over with.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes<br /> <br /> The Necklace</u><br /> <br /> Last night, after Alexia finished reading the DeCastro objects through her oracle and Doc and Simon disappeared to do some research, Alexia and I set about turning the necklace I liberated from Sansbury Hall into a charm. According to Alexia, it once belonged to a friend of Alonia\u2019s named Denise James - the same Denise James who we believe may have helped store some of the DeCastro\u2019s things, and who is currently buried with the Alonia\u2019s locket. The little girl\u2019s skeleton probably belonged to Denise\u2019s daughter.<br /> <br /> With Alexia\u2019s help, I threaded some black ribbon through the necklace\u2019s chain and turned it into a charm of Stillness. I wanted to make something for one of the other krewe members, but Stillness was the best fit for the necklace, so I\u2019ll keep it for now. If any of the others need it, I\u2019ll be happy to let them use it.<br /> <br /> <u>Spooky</u><br /> <br /> Since I got back from Taiwan, Natalie has seemed much more pleased to see me. I get the impression that she really missed me when I was gone. I confess I missed her too. For all of her rough edges, she is a part of my family\u2014the krewe. Maybe the time apart did us both some good.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s also been calling me \u201cSpooky\u201d lately. The nickname\u2019s obviously calling attention to my ghostly appearance and morose personality\u2014more of the \u201cgoth\u201d thing Natalie has attributed to me\u2014so I feel like I should be annoyed by the nickname, but I\u2019m not. Not at all. In fact, I like it. It\u2019s an affectionate nickname, and makes me feel loved. And maybe I\u2019ve come to accept that I really am a bit spooky and \u201cgothic.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> July 23rd, 2010<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m awake. Sleeping alone is terrible, but last night I really had to. Even an innocent sleep with another person is usually better than alone.<br /> <br /> -I feel better now though.<br /> <br /> -Gonna miss lunch with Doc, which makes me a sad Gloomberry. But I gotta get ready to go on the air.<br /> <br /> -It is time for a musical interlude.<br /> <br /> -Back at Chez Doom. Jazzy and Alexis and Simon are headed out.<br /> <br /> -Short Vlog up! Your Mistress will be on the tube tonight if you are in the New Haven area.<br /> <br /> -My girlfriend is playing the na\u00efve, innocent make up girl. She is treading on dangerous ground. I have to be somewhere\u2026<br /> <br /> -She is occasionally slightly more dismissive of a couple of my foibles than I would prefer.<br /> <br /> -Karen is actually pretty good at this.<br /> <br /> -I feel so pretty!<br /> <br /> -Looks like they decided to find a different way to try and handle things at Sansbury Hall.<br /> <br /> -That whole thing gives moi the willies.<br /> <br /> -Chandra had a nice conversation with my cleavage. She is worse than a lot of guys. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -And I am off like a prom dress!<br /> <br /> -OK, acting gig seemed to go well. I will record it tonight so I can watch it when I am eighty and talk out loud to the empty house about how pretty I was while I drink.<br /> <br /> -Time to get ready for hijinx!<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m a Blue Jean Queen and I can\u2019t be tamed!<br /> <br /> -I have not worn this much denim since high school. Or a bandana since\u2026ever.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m just gonna take a nap in the back of this car now.<br /> <br /> -Whoop, I am on!<br /> <br /> -\u2026And out. Let\u2019s not do that again hmmm?<br /> <br /> <i><br /> End Session XLVIII</i><br /> <br /> OK well that was fun.<br /> <br /> Not much to report on not covered. There was a lot of OOC chatter so less got done, but it was still a good session. Jasmine's player got a really good Meditation roll...I forget the number of successes but it was amazing. Thus Jasmine was rather laid back much of the session. Natalie was playing piano as much of her time as a young girl she played a lot of Andrews Sisters and some Christian Rock, Amy Grant type stuff...if you can imagine. Now she does not feel...comfortable with some of that but the Andrews Sisters music is still a comfort to her, as she noted in session.<br /> <br /> She also, wanting to look different, wound up in blue jeans, white t-shirt, denim jacket and red bandanna to sneak into the station. It was about as different as I could think of.<br /> <br /> Also, once again got to say skin crawlingly creepy/dirty things IC as Gretchen. That is always fun. Also from Tavia &quot;Remember when we were little and thought Great Aunt Petunia was going to rise from the dead to eat us? Remember when she did? That was scary, we should not have played near her sarcophagus!&quot;<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, when the Krewe gets a much better idea of the story behind the intruder, Natalie sends out a large number of hilariously sleep dep'd tweets, and the session ends in a cliffhanger. Be there or, uh, be somewhere else I suppose. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:00:49-08:00","id":16320,"title":"","content":"The last session was an exciting session, to be sure. Let\u2019s see what 3 of our Krewe members had to say.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0435 Hours, Saturday, July 24, 2010<br /> <br /> The Post Bomb-threat Brownies were had while we watched Nightshade\u2019s show. The movie was some terribly low-budget director\u2019s indulgence. I think it was called Werewolf, but the main female lead was trying to use a Swedish (I hope that\u2019s what she was trying for) accent so it was Wherewoffa, Verevolf, warenwoof, and others that my mind refuses to remember. Nightshade said before it started that she would not be upset if we thought the movie was terrible. And it was. Rose was really scandalized by Nightshade\u2019s dress or lack of it. I had to try very hard not to laugh. We all forgot she has never seen one of these Friday Night Monster Flicks. Thus we explained that there has to be a really scantily clad hostess to keep the people interested, because the movie sure won\u2019t do it. She agreed but I don\u2019t think she could really get past how much cleavage Nightshade was showing. It was quite a bit more than usual but no one else seemed to have an issue.<br /> <br /> After we suffered through the movie and enjoyed Nightshade\u2019s commentary, both on-screen and off, we got back to work. We had to plan how to deal with Deanna and her link to the DeCastros. The major hold up came in that most people didn\u2019t think the girl was mature enough to be told anything real for fear that she would do something stupid and get herself killed or worse. Eventually we settled on just getting her out of the house, learning if anyone else was home, and then moving to sack the house. Nightshade sent Deanna a text to meet for coffee later today. That would get her out and talking. Then Rose and Snowflake could check the house if it was clear. I checked the maps and made sure on distances, but the James house was close enough to the Firehouse Church that Rose could teleport herself. So if we found the guns and anything else, we could move them quickly to a place we could secure and defend if necessary. Then we\u2019ll need to move on Sainsbury to break the link to Adolphe holds to the dorm. All while holding Alonia off. No sweat.<br /> <br /> With that plan in place, Snowflake and Jasmine went out to hit the Haunts for Plasm around 0100 Hours. Karen and I went to the Piano room to listen to Nightshade play. We\u2019d been talking about old songs, listening to Nightshade, all in all a few hours when Rose and Snowflake got back. Rose looked confused and exhausted. She told us that they found our intruder, or rather he found them at AMC. The music of course stopped but Rose had no intention of telling the story several times and she was up way past her bedtime. She assured me that she and Snowflake were okay and this would keep til morning. With that she left us to go to bed. Nightshade decided that she would stay up til breakfast. I don\u2019t see this going well, but for now I\u2019m going to bed myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Saturday, July 24, 2010<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t have to go and open the shop so I was a little lazy this morning. I finally rolled out of bed around 0815 and started Meditation. Before I knew it, I was back downstairs for breakfast by 0900. Some days meditation is just like that.<br /> Nightshade was at breakfast and about as keyed up as I was afraid she\u2019d be. But Rose finally decided to fill us in on last night\u2019s events. Apparently she spotted something jumping to the top of a dorm at AMC before they could leave. She tried to follow it, but it seemed to know where she was at all times. Rose is not use to things knowing where she is when she doesn\u2019t want them too so I think she saw this as a challenge. She left Snowflake, which was probably not the best idea, and turned into a flock of birds to chase our intruder down. She thought she had him cornered before he turned into mist and flowed through a window sill into another building. Rose\u2019s determination is sometimes its own liability. This was the case last night it seems as she crashed through the window still as a flock of birds and swooped to get close to stranger. He promptly vanished. Snowflake, after being abandoned on a spectrally hostile campus, sat down and unlocked a Boneyard so he might have some idea what was happening. He followed the chase and even heard our intruder utter a phrase in Mandarin before disappearing. Rose has translated and it means, \u201cHow the devil did she do that?\u201d The great mystery from last night was revealed when Rose explained she now knew what and possibly who this Jiang Shi was. Since none of us had a clue what she was talking about, Rose gave us the Chinese vampire 101 lesson. Chinese vampires are really nothing like western vampires at all. I should probably be shocked but after learning about Chandra this was almost expected. They aren\u2019t Embraced like the vampires I know or even infected like a Penagallen. These creatures are the results of certain curses, specific rituals, and strangely also occur randomly from bad burials. They also aren\u2019t like western vampires due to possessing anchors like ghosts, which along with their graves, they can teleport between. Ronin must have thought it the same time I did as she started staring at Rose and becoming more and more annoyed. Finally, after Ronin\u2019s normal morning grumbling turned aggressive, she announced that Rose was an anchor. With that out in the open, we decided to pump Rose for all the info she could tell us. Jiang Shi drink blood and have anchors like ghosts. They are paralyzed in sunlight, not destroyed by it. They have no good way to make others and they can\u2019t be resolved like a ghost can. Lovely.<br /> <br /> It was about this time that I took Nightshade up to her room and put her to bed. She was wobbling and not really getting it anymore. I came back down to hear our first Mandarin lession will be to make sign outside to try and convince this thing to talk to us. Oh yeah, important note, we now think this Jiang Shi is either Rose\u2019s uncle Guang or working for him. The plan is now to make signs saying, \u201cAttention Jiang Shi. Would like to speak.\u201d It was followed by Rose\u2019s real name but that would defeat the point of having nicknames. I have no idea what I\u2019m writing now, I\u2019m just following what Rose has drawn in front of me. Now I need to get to it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1400 Hours, Saturday, July 24, 2010<br /> <br /> After we made up the signs for Rose, a trip to the Library was in order. Snowflake, always the one to find horrible rituals, found one that would change a Jiang Shi into a \u201cnormal\u201d vampire, they just have to eat the soul of the western vampire, losing all Jiang Shi powers and becoming whatever type of vampire the western one was originally. They are very instinctual but not necessarily mindless, which works in our favor. Apparently they can turn into a large bird, likely why it was confused when Rose did the whole murder thing last night. A bit of good news is they can\u2019t be bound by blood of western vampires. The less good news is that they are hard to kill. They must be completely destroyed by fire to kill them outright. They are also tough, strong, and fast like most vampire legends. Hopefully if this is Guang, it won\u2019t come to that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1630 Hours, Saturday, July 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Since everyone else is taking their Mary Sweet Time!, I might as well give an update so far.<br /> <br /> Nightshade got up about 1430 Hours so we all prepared to finally meet the infamous Adolphe DeCastro. But there was no guarantee we\u2019d find anything, so things could have gone very boring. Honestly I don\u2019t think that ever happens to people that have already died once.<br /> <br /> I got my knife and Cupcake drove over to the Firehouse church. Ronin took Rose and Snowflake to the ancestral James home while Nightshade chatted Deanna up at a coffee shop. Cupcake and I were really just here as backup since I checked the map and Rose would be able to teleport here from the house. We all had the ear curls in to keep up with the situations in all locations. After a few minutes Ronin scared the shit outta me when she started looking for signs of ghostly power. She didn\u2019t find anything except Rose\u2019s powers, but she didn\u2019t say that at first. I informed her she was a shithead. Then things went downhill. Snowflake was outside keeping watch through Boneyard. He found a painting sealed into the wall, but there was no light so he couldn\u2019t see what it was. Ronin found Deanna\u2019s weed stash. Figures. Somehow, Rose managed to slip into the wall space and look at he painting. It was very similar to one of Tavia\u2019s Outsider paintings. She described it as an open night sky, with dark figure, back to the viewer, on a hill in the distance. She said she felt and urge to step into the painting and go speak to the dark stranger. We didn\u2019t have what we needed to deal with that, but at least with it sealed in the wall, it\u2019s as safe as it could be. Next they moved into the attic. You ever notice how nothing good is ever in an attic? They found a large trunk that required two keys. Simon handled that rather easily with his control of the area. There was another chest inside. Inside the chest was our missing pistol case, an arm-length stick with strange symbols carved end to end and a loop on the end, plus a pair of brass rings with a symbol on each of them. This was the jackpot.<br /> <br /> Rose says she\u2019s in the church now so I should probably loo...FUCK!<br /> <br /> The skies overhead just turned as black as midnight and twice as churning. I think we might have gotten some attention X~\u2019 \\l<br /> <br /> Damn it, Adolphe is here and everyone is screaming for me to leave him be. He\u2019s going for his guns and Rose is still in there with him. The wind out here is picking up like a hurricane is coming. I\u2019m putting up Stigmata Shroud because this will not end without some kind of a fight. Cupcake is worried that someone will get possessed and take the guns out or just take the whole lockbox. That\u2019s a good point. I\u2019ve told Ronin to get more chains and locks so we can effectively bolt the thing down to a shelf or the wall.<br /> <br /> This is not the way I expected this to play out. And they still won\u2019t let me at least distract him. Nightshade is better at the whole ghost command but I know I can do this. Hell I\u2019m only still writing this because if I don\u2019t all I can do it stare at an open door.<br /> <br /> Nightshade just got here and has a new plan. She\u2019s going to ward him inside and lock him down for a few days, then we can go deal with his body. Rose is actually outside with us, finally so I don\u2019t have to worry about that right now. I like this plan, but we still need to lock those pistols down more securely. Ronin has the chains and everything so she\u2019s going to go in and move for the guns while Rose and I keep this asshole busy. <br /> <br /> Nightshade, I\u2019m leaving this with you so I don\u2019t make it out, you already know I love you. Be safe.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, July 23, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> After watching Natalie\u2019s show earlier tonight, we discussed what to do about the DeCastros. Simon and Natalie thought that Deanna\u2019s parents were away most weekends, and so Natalie and Simon offered to go and chat with Deanna tomorrow at a caf\u00e9, luring her out of the house so that Gwen and I could sneak in and look for the DeCastro pistols. Once we had them, we feared Adolphe\u2019s ghost would come to see what was happening to his anchor, so to keep him away from Deanna\u2019s place, I would then get them to the firehouse church (which we now own and which is very isolated) as quickly as possible. Doc and Alexia would be waiting at the church to help out against Adolphe once I arrived, and we would lock the pistols away in a lockbox there. This way, Adolphe won\u2019t be able to harm Deanna\u2019s family once we sever his connection to Sansbury Hall. Then it will be a matter of sealing him into his pistols.<br /> <br /> Doc and Simon are also researching whether it\u2019s possible to sever Alonia\u2019s connection to Adolphe by destroying her braid, since it\u2019s the ritual object that tied her to him in the first place. If we can do that, then we won\u2019t have to deal with her in Sansbury Hall. We can resolve her at her grave, without Adolphe there to interfere.<br /> <br /> In order to prepare for tomorrow, Simon and I decided to go prowling around some of our haunts to draw off some plasm, as we were both a bit low, and knew we might be spending a lot tomorrow. We briefly stopped into Murder Ballads and then went to AMC to visit Nilan and Rose Halls. It was while we were on our way between them that I happened to notice a figure in the shadow of a nearby building.<br /> <br /> When it realized I was looking at it, it fled, and made an amazing leap onto the top of a dormitory. I saw more of it then, and recognized the gray skin that Alexia attributed to our intruder of a few nights ago. I quickly gave chase with a short warning to Simon, who hadn\u2019t seen the thing and was a bit confused.<br /> <br /> It became quickly obvious that I wouldn\u2019t be able to catch up to it on foot, so I transformed into a flock of crows and flew after it. It knew exactly where I was, and ducked into a building by phasing through a wall, not unlike what I can do. Determined to follow it, I flew in after it, smashing through a window. I was going to reform into my normal body and confront it, but it uttered a brief Chinese curse and disappeared. Before it vanished, I noticed that much of its face was hidden by a cloth wrapped around it, as though it was trying to conceal its features, and it was dressed in modern Taiwanese factory-worker\u2019s clothing. That struck me as very odd until I put the pieces together and realized what it all meant.<br /> <br /> I returned to Simon to find him sprawled out on the campus lawn in a Boneyard trance. I shook him out of it, and asked if he\u2019d seen anything I hadn\u2019t. He was only able to confirm that it seemed to have a supernatural sense of my location, and that when I turned into crows, it muttered, \u201cHow the devil did she do that!?\u201d (in Mandarin, which Simon was able to repeat back with some difficulty).<br /> <br /> I knew then what the thing was, and had a suspicion about why it was here. I briefly filled Simon in, but decided to wait until tomorrow morning to give all the details, as I don\u2019t think we\u2019re in any danger from it, and I wanted to tell everyone at once. Unfortunately, this meant convincing Natalie to be up early, and she decided to just stay awake through the night. She doesn\u2019t deal well with lack of sleep, which surprises me.<br /> <br /> Here is my theory:<br /> <br /> The intruder is a Jiang Shi, a type of Chinese vampire-ghost. It knew where I was because I\u2019m its anchor, which works much like a true ghost\u2019s anchor. And I believe that the Jiang Shi either is my uncle Guang who disappeared recently, or is working for him. It\u2019s far more likely that it really is my uncle, though, since it seems to want to hide from me., like it doesn\u2019t want to be recognized. Because I\u2019m it\u2019s only anchor here, it can only appear near me, but it probably doesn\u2019t dare appear in the house anymore since the house tried to kill it. I presume it has a grave of some sort in Taiwan, so it can return there at will, but it seems to be curious about New Haven.<br /> <br /> I need to find out what it\u2019s after and why I\u2019m its anchor. If it is my uncle Guang, then he\u2019s become attached to me for a reason, and it might have to do with his death. I\u2019d like to help him if possible, but I need to talk to him first. I think I\u2019ll make some signs that say, in Mandarin, \u201cJiang Shi. Uncle Guang. Please talk to me. Xiao Ming.\u201d I\u2019ll put them up outside the house and maybe one in my office at AMC. Hopefuly that will encourage him to approach me instead of fleeing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, July 24, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> I had a good meditation this morning, though not as good as yesterday. Simon and I discussed our encounter with the Jiang Shi with the others over breakfast, and I shared my theories. I don\u2019t think the Jiang Shi means us any harm, but it wasn\u2019t easy to convince Gwen of that. After breakfast, Doc, Simon, Gwen and I went down to the library to research Jiang Shi more, and learned a bit a more than what I already knew from growing up in Taiwan.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, July 24, 2010, Afternoon<br /> I\u2019m writing this in Gwen\u2019s SUV. We\u2019re driving at breakneck speeds to AMC, where Adolphe has unleashed the amorphous shadow creature that he had stored beneath Sansbury Hall, and that we discovered in our follow-up investigations there.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have long to write, and Gwen\u2019s driving makes it very hard to keep my pen steady, so I\u2019ll have to be brief. Our plan for acquiring the pistols worked very well. Simon, Gwen and I went to the James\u2019 house and while Simon waited outside, Gwen and I broke in and searched for the pistols, which took far longer than we would have liked.<br /> <br /> In the process, Simon sensed a painting sealed away in the narrow space between two walls. I phased in to have a look at it, which was not easy, and discovered that it was much like the Outsider paintings Tavia has painted. It pictured a nighttime landscape with a lonely figure on the crest of a hill. I felt compelled to enter the painting and join that figure there, but I shook off the comuplsion and phased out of the wall. For now, the painting\u2019s probably as safe as it\u2019s going to be, and we have other things to worry about.<br /> <br /> We finally found the pistols, and I took them, box and all, and phased directly out of the upper-story attic, then, as I fell toward the ground, I used my Cold Wind Caul to become one with the winds and disappear. A minute later, I rematerialized outside the firehouse church. I was invisible the whole time, of course, so I had to tell Doc and Alexia that I\u2019d arrived so that they would be prepared. Poor Alexia seemed terribly nervous, but I knew she would stand firm if things got bad, and Doc looked like he was ready start a fight.<br /> <br /> I ran to the basement and locked the pistols away in a lockbox. Meanwhile, the skies above the firehouse church filled with roiling black clouds and lightning, and then a vapour spiraled down from the clouds and coalesced into a humanoid shape. It was Adolphe, and he ignored all of us, even Doc\u2019s bravado, and strode directly toward the pistols. Alexia got out of his way, and so did Doc, wisely.<br /> <br /> Gwen arrived about then with a safe and chains to lock the pistols away and make them more secure. Natalie drove up then as well, worried sick about Doc (and for good reason, as I thought Doc might decide to attack Adolphe then and there, the way he was stomping about). She cut herself to create a stigmatic ward that would trap Adolphe at the church for a few days, which we hope will prevent him from possessing anyone or causing any more trouble than he already has.<br /> <br /> But as Gwen began locking away the pistols, Adolphe told us in voice that boomed like thunder that to punish us for the theft of his pistols, he had unleashed the Abyssal beast he kept hidden beneath Sansbury Hall. We have to get there as quickly as possible and stop it before it does any more harm than it already has. I hope we\u2019re not too late. I hope I can reach Mongler!<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Elvira</u><br /> We watched Natalie\u2019s show Friday night. She was playing hostess to a terrible old movie from the 80\u2019s called Werewolf or something like that. The main actress was foreign and even I could tell that her English was bad. But Natalie did a good job, even if she was dressed rather inappropriately for public television. She showed an awful lot of cleavage. According to Natalie and Gwen, that\u2019s part of the tradition, started by other movie host actresses who called themselves Vampira and Elvira. I do hope Natalie\u2019s not trying to become the next in that line. It just seems so...trashy. Not that Natalie isn\u2019t a bit trashy as it is.<br /> <br /> I did comment to Natalie that her real smile looks much nicer than the fake one she was using on the show. I think she appreciated that.<br /> <br /> <u>Sleep Deprivation</u><br /> <br /> Natalie doesn\u2019t deal with sleep deprivation well. She becomes a bit of a wally, almost like she\u2019s drunk or high on a stimulant or something. I don\u2019t think she was drunk or high\u2026 Maybe it was the nervous tension of her TV appearance catching up with her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Jiang Shi</u><br /> <br /> Here\u2019s what I remember about Jiang Shi from growing up in Taiwan (and being fascinated by the occult even as child):<br /> <br /> Jiang Shi are a form of Chinese vampire, but they have a lot in common with ghosts too, in that they are bound to their grave and possibly other anchors.<br /> <br /> Like ghosts, they can manifest near their anchors, but once manifested, they are physical beings.<br /> <br /> Jiang Shi aren\u2019t \u201cinfected\u201d like western vampires. Instead, they are created by esoteric rituals or, more commonly, when a person is not properly buried.<br /> <br /> They are sometimes created as servants to those practiced in the occult.<br /> <br /> They are sometimes called \u201chopping vampires\u201d because they are capable of impressive leaps. Some legends and popular fictions say they bunny hop everywhere, but that\u2019s not true.<br /> <br /> And here\u2019s the additional information we learned with our research:<br /> <br /> Jiang Shi can turn into birds (instead of bats, like western vampires).<br /> <br /> They can consume the soul of a western vampire (which is something all western vampires can do as well, though fortunately they consider it a terrible act), and by doing so, they become a western vampire, permanently taking on the qualities of whatever type of vampire they consumed.<br /> <br /> Unlike western vampires, they cannot be bound to the power of another\u2019s blood (becoming the slave of that vampire), but cannot bind others either.<br /> <br /> They are difficult to destroy unless they are killed with fire, and tend to disappear back to their graves if threatened with destruction.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie's Tweets</b><br /> <br /> July 23rd 2010<br /> <br /> -Watching my performance.<br /> <br /> -Jasmine is trying to be flattering. She is a sweetie.<br /> <br /> -She seems a little scared of my boobs. My boobs are not scary.<br /> <br /> -Just ask Chandra she will tell you.<br /> <br /> -Giving Jasmine some history.<br /> <br /> -I suspect Karen has a hidden denim fetish.<br /> <br /> -I probably sounded overly critical of Elvira, given yes she was ripping off Vampira but I am so ripping her off too.<br /> <br /> -I generally don\u2019t go crazy with the cleavage though\u2026not my best utilization of physical assets.<br /> <br /> -That was fun all around. Goddess <i>Werewolf</i> is terrible.<br /> <br /> -I did not have pre written lines though. That was<br /> <br /> -OMG Spooky complemented me on my smile ALL MELTY<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s time for some quiet time on the piano.<br /> <br /> -Doc and Karen both seem to have sought me out for my quiet time on the piano. But are behaving.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s less quiet time on the piano now. But still piano time.<br /> <br /> -Someone is all grabby.<br /> <br /> -I love singing<br /> <br /> -Jazzy wants me awake till breakfast. Uh, OK.<br /> <br /> -She and Simon have discovered something, but she has a sleepy.<br /> <br /> <br /> July 24th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Ok no more sing. I am all out of sing. I love sing, but have no sing left.<br /> <br /> -I can handle this being waited on hand and foot thing.<br /> <br /> -Shall I demand a pedicure?<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d go to bed now, but need to stay up for breakfast.<br /> <br /> -Imma gonna stay up all night long mama!<br /> <br /> -If I ever went near the dreaded coffee, now would be the time.<br /> <br /> -40s music is crazy catchy.<br /> <br /> -Sent Karen to bed. She is of no use to me here especially when she is flirty and I am supposed to be staying awake and alert.<br /> <br /> -Everything is funny. It\u2019s like I am tweaking but I am not tweaking.<br /> <br /> -What color stockings do you think look good on a girl. I always use black, but red can, assuming you are not being brainwashed to think \u201cred=bad person\u201d<br /> <br /> -You would think someone properly mysterious could at least keep Monsters Cereals stocked in her pantry year round.<br /> <br /> -In the room the women come and go, talking of Michelangelo<br /> <br /> -I just kinda accepted a song called \u201cHold Tight\u201d would be about seafood as a kid, but it seems weird.<br /> <br /> -Am I holding tight waiting for seafood?<br /> <br /> -I guess I may have been overly accepting of a song called \u201cBeat Me Daddy Eight to the Bar\u201d too.<br /> <br /> -I keep forgetting I have pants on and can sit however I want.<br /> <br /> -I love love love skirts but man they are so much trouble sometimes, with the sitting.<br /> <br /> -Not been up 24 hours yet I am not weak!<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t even know who my favorite member of Shonen Knife is. All of them?<br /> <br /> -Come on if you don\u2019t want to kiss everyone in that band you are wrong.<br /> <br /> -I guess it is both, now. What happened to that third girl anyway?<br /> <br /> -If the Muppet show were still around Shonen Knife would be awesome on it.<br /> <br /> -So would I. But I don\u2019t think I would get along with Miss Piggy.<br /> <br /> -Is she Mrs. Piggy now? Is Muppets Take Manhattan Canon?<br /> <br /> -Tricking someone into marrying you is dirty pool.<br /> <br /> -Wikipedia is so useful!<br /> <br /> -IMDB is better tho because I am on it. 8-)<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d make a Vlog but you only think I am vapid on here\u2026<br /> <br /> -Last thing I need is video evidence of me Boxxying out.<br /> <br /> -Is it wrong that I still think Christina Aguilera looks good?<br /> <br /> -So she had some weight problems and looks like an adult now. Screw those people who don\u2019t care because she does not look like a skinny teenager.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d do her. Right now.<br /> <br /> -I have heard the Mermaids singing, each to each.<br /> <br /> -I do not think they will sing to me.<br /> <br /> -I need to go walking outside at night again. The sun will rise soon though so I don\u2019t want to do that.<br /> <br /> -I might burn into flames and ruin my complexion.<br /> <br /> -Or worse, get a tan and ruin my lovely pallor!<br /> <br /> -Almost sunrise, why do they eat breakfast so late.<br /> <br /> -Do I Dare to eat a peach?<br /> <br /> -I am such a poser. Too much TS Eliot, too little music lyrics.<br /> <br /> -Bad goth Natalie, bad goth.<br /> <br /> -I feel like slumping shapeless in a bathchair. I am just saying.<br /> <br /> -What ever happened to Poe I lost track of her after<i> Haunted</i>.<br /> <br /> -The Internet is so useful\u2026she has been kinda busy.<br /> <br /> -Maybe I can do an interview.<br /> <br /> -Holy crap I am late for breakfast!<br /> <br /> -OK intruder might be Jasmine\u2019s Dead (?) uncle. Makes\u2026sense I guess.<br /> <br /> -Could be worse things I guess.<br /> <br /> -Gwen is paranoid about it. Shocking.<br /> <br /> -I sleep now! Sleep I tell you.<br /> <br /> -O_O<br /> <br /> -Uh, wow I typed a lot. Sleep depping and the Internet do not go together.<br /> <br /> -Out to be a distraction. I am so very distracting!<br /> <br /> -Deanna is freaking adorable.<br /> <br /> -And a little bit high, I think.<br /> <br /> -XD<br /> <br /> -You guys still investigating? It\u2019s been\u2026awhile.<br /> <br /> -Deanna and Clarissa are not a couple. Oh well.<br /> <br /> -They would be ADORABLE together.<br /> <br /> -Would not even be hot, just all AWWWWWWWW<br /> <br /> -Action time. Deanna is gone and I have to be sure Doc does not do something stupid.<br /> <br /> -Don\u2019t do something stupid, Doc.<br /> <br /> -Our heroine saves the day. Or something.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m going to have to bleed, and no one here to drink it.<br /> <br /> -Such a waste. Doc doesn\u2019t drink blood but if I could get Karen here\u2026oh well.<br /> <br /> -I get such\u2026chills watching it run out and pool on my leg.<br /> <br /> -Grrrrrrrrrr<br /> <br /> -Oh shit.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLIX</i><br /> <br /> Natalie was loopy partially because that was night #2 without sleep, she slept little the night before either due to anticipation for her show and bad memories. On that subject, Natalie also does not usually do the cleavage thing so much as midriff and skirts\u2026more her style. Natalie refers to <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=QSpTwzOs-E8\" target=\"_blank\">Hold Tight</a> and <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=qZv6hL6aYfQ&amp;feature=related\" target=\"_blank\">Beat Me, Daddy, Eight to the Bar</a> by the Andrews Sisters. Link helpfully provided in case your Andrews Sisters lore is off. Natalie prefers Goth music and style, but she loves most types of music and, as she notes, she sang Andrews Sisters as a little girl so it has a nostalgic safety to it. I don't have time for everything else she made random reference to. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Jiang Shi are in Wicked Dead, same book that has Penanggalan.<br /> <br /> Werewolf really is a terrible movie. Please be sure you miss it, or watch it on MST3K if you must see it.<br /> <br /> And that was a dramatic stopping off point, wasn\u2019t it? Natalie to keep De Castro trapped had to use Stigmata Boneyard twice, taking two lethal each time as DeCastro shook off the first attempt. She was down half her health by the end of the session and into the next. It was four health levels lost to blood loss, so she was back to being a little out of it though not as rambly.<br /> <br /> Next session (that we just had) is Session 50, and quite a session it was. Be there to see the showdown with an Abyssal creature, Jasmine wrestles a doll, more cops then any given session so far, and Officer Tart finally faces the Wookalar in epic battle. Sort of.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll see you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:04:31-08:00","id":16323,"title":"","content":"Alright, ready for an action-packed session? It is action packed.<br /> <br /> <i>Session L</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2025 Hours, Saturday, July 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Welcome to Clusterfucksville.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not exactly accurate considering we all lived and were more successful than we expected. Actually, locking an asshole Yellow Bones in an abandoned firehouse and destroying an Outsider is pretty good for a day\u2019s work. I\u2019m just tired and grumpy because of the price we paid and I\u2019m well past coming off the adrenaline high.<br /> <br /> After I finished freaking out before, Ronin locked the guns down before we all jumped back in a car. Ronin drove Rose and Cupcake like a bat outta hell. Snowflake drove Nightshade\u2019s car as she was already experiencing mild delirium from Hemodynamic shock. Even with my training, seeing Nightshade sitting in that big of a pool of her own blood shook me up. The best I could manage was to be angry things got that far as I destroyed my shirt to bandage her as best I could. She keeps her tools clean, but she doesn\u2019t make shallow incisions when she\u2019s in a hurry. Ronin called Chuck on the way and called for a full scale lock down of AMC while Rose tried to call Mongler. I remember thinking it was more weird that we couldn\u2019t find the Faerie quickly than it was that Ronin could just call in a lock down of a public institution. Yeah I don\u2019t know either.<br /> <br /> Mongler eventually got back to Rose so she gave him the Incoming report. I was upset that Nightshade had wounded herself that much, mainly because I couldn\u2019t help her right then. Snowflake got us there as quickly as he could, but it was a long drive for me. I could have blown my energy healing Nightshade, but then I\u2019d be next to useless in the coming fight. She kept telling me to calm down but then saying things about how pretty the blood was. Snowflake was rightly concerned since he was driving someone else\u2019s car and that someone else was covered in her own blood in the back seat. The cops would have truly made this a bad situation so I was glad we managed to get through before the police barricades went up. Ronin may have had something to do with that too for all I know. When I could see the entrance to campus, I put up my Primeval Shroud to be prepared for anything. When the car stopped, I opened the door and The Dog of War leapt out. That was cool and all, but then I had to go back and get my ear curl. Less awesome. <br /> <br /> There was no noise on campus. The birds were gone, the wind was still, and even the bugs were quiet. That is never a good sign. The movies actually get that one right. Mongler arrived shortly in an camper squealing tires as he skidded to a stop followed by two patrol cars which slid into a Y behind him. This was really loud given how still campus was, so we all knew something was happening. I didn\u2019t go rushing around as I didn\u2019t need cops to shoot me for being a monster. Mongler did something, then we heard a man scream and one of the patrol cars peeled out. Snowflake stayed with Nightshade at the car. He dropped into a Boneyard trance and immediately gave us bad news while I went to find Rose, Ronin, and Cupcake. This Outsider that DeCastro released didn\u2019t go very far. Actually it just possessed the whole campus. So it was in effect doing something similar to Snowflake\u2019s Boneyard. I focused my anger through my Shroud and felt myself become stronger and faster. I was no longer simply trying to protect...I NEEDED to fight. Primeval seems to do that as when I found Rose, she was similarly in her Feline Caul stalker form with Ronin and Cupcake following behind. With one blood-covered goth girl, my comatose body, and one kid laying unconscious in a car, two animal monsters stalking around, one gun wielding ex-cop, one chef with six knife-waving arms, a Faerie dinosaur-man, and a creature from Beyond the universe, Albertus Magnus was officially the most horrifying location in the whole state of Connecticut, if not a much larger area. Sadly with all that we brought to bear, there was no target. Ronin grabbed her phone and called Dark Haven Bluffs. She got Tavia on the phone and told her to go look up anything in the Library that might help us. She gave all the information we knew and Tavia immediately went to work. She seemed to have a better idea what we were dealing with just based on that description than the rest of us. I forget that Tavia is so very dangerous in some ways.<br /> <br /> While we researched by proxy, Rose decided that we animal people should go and investigate Sainsbury Hall. We headed into the dorm with no real attempt at stealth. When we got in unmolested, I called out in Arabic to the Djinn Alonia Nazeed. I commanded her to appear before me. After a few tension seconds, we realized she wasn\u2019t actually home. So much for my occult abilities. We decided to use the time to cut off Sainsbury Hall from Adolphe and deal with the eight bodies, effectively sealing Alonia off, all at once. There was nothing we knew we could do to force the Outsider to manifest back into the material world so that was the best option we had. While Snowflake handed off Boneyard duties to Nightshade so he could go get the crest he made, Rose and I went looking for trouble in the upper floors. She led the way back up to a secret chamber and moved with determination to a very nice desk set into the wall. When she opened the top drawer, a cloth doll sprang out at her face with a ragged hanger. I had no idea what was happening but she apparently expected it and snatched the animated rag out of the air without flinching. She started scolding it like a kid that really screws something up when they know better. She had claws but for some reason didn\u2019t just rip its head off and step on the mangled knot of a body as it hit the floor. She claimed that it didn\u2019t want to fight us but Adolphe\u2019s control was too strong for it to disobey. I have no idea how she got all that from a rag doll, waving a hanger like a knife, with buttons for eyes and a stitch for a mouth, but either way I wasn\u2019t buying it. It was still trying to get loose and she wouldn\u2019t let me just rip it to shreds and be done with it. <br /> <br /> About that time, we got a call over the ear curl that Ronin\u2019s delusional cop friend, Tart just arrived on the scene. I didn\u2019t understand until Snowflake described the \u201cspecial armor\u201d Tart was wearing. I\u2019ve heard Tart ramble about Wookalars before. I don\u2019t know him like Ronin so I can\u2019t really say he\u2019s nuts, but I suspect. His partner was killed by something...though no one knows what. I suspect if he really isn\u2019t schizophrenic, that something supernatural did kill his partner but altered his memories just enough to let his paranoia fill in the blanks. Either way, he had an unlicensed and totally unstable homemade flamethrower strapped to his back and some pieced together bits of \u201carmor.\u201d It\u2019s great that at least one cop believes in the supernatural, but this old guy was in way over his head. We needed to get him and the other two cops still hiding in their patrol car from Mongler, out of there. Snowflake and Ronin discussed what has to be the most cartoon-like idea we\u2019ve ever had to get rid of all the normal people. That sounds so condescending. Maybe we should call them Neverdead. That at least makes them sound cooler. Anyway, so Snowflake made an illusion for all the cops present after we consulted Tavia on what a Wookalar is supposed to look like. As I understand it, a 20 foot tall, boar-like humanoid came out to face Tart, Godzilla-style. There was some broken English taunting about the smell of a fallen meal, I don\u2019t know. Whatever Snowflake did enraged Tart and left the other cops pissing themselves in their cars. I could hear the flamethrower going off and Tart screaming. It was briefly like being back in Afghanistan. That sound in his battle cry. He was ready and willing to die avenging his fallen brother. Suddenly this was much more serious and a whole lot less funny. I told Snowflake to make sure he earned the kill. There was no way this man, this warrior could be denied true vindication. I\u2019m not sure if the Dog was getting into the scene of battle or if the Primeval instincts and memories of war were getting in the way, but thinking about it now, this seems really odd.<br /> <br /> Sadeeuk, your honor could not allow this deception to be another humiliation to one who knew true service and loss. There is nothing odd in this.<br /> <br /> Well at least I can feel better about that now. It\u2019s interesting how the Dog has started to understand my motivations before I do. Anyway, after the vanquished Wookalar dissolved into some kind of black ash and sank into the ground, Tart, along with the other officers left campus secure in the belief that one of their number had saved the day. Then Snowflake started bringing his stuff into Sainsbury Hall to lay claim to it and chop off one more tendril of Adolphe\u2019s power. <br /> <br /> Not long after he got inside, Nightshade came over the ear curl sounding really strange. Apparently after Snowflake went back inside the last time, something tried to get into her head. She fought it off, but she didn\u2019t know if she could do it many more times. I called for Snowflake to go out and get her so she wasn\u2019t alone. Rose and I reverted back to normal form, as nothing was happening and the power can only be sustained so long without expending ourselves more than we already had. Rose locked the doll in Snowflake\u2019s trunk about the time Tavia finally called back. We never did find out what this damn thing was called, but she found enough about it to tell us what we needed. It wasn\u2019t as powerful in sunlight, but that didn\u2019t mean it was weak. If the whole place was blessed, it would be forced to manifest, which Ronin could handle. It could possess people, which Nightshade could attest, so we immediately instituted the buddy rule. We all just kind of looked around when Tavia said it could absorb people whole. While it would eventually dissolve them, they would drown in the abyssal void within before that could happen. It was pretty much immune to anything that didn\u2019t do some kind of chemical or elemental damage. That left me pretty much high and dry, so I took Nightshade with me and declared I was going to find the Science building to make \u201cSomething (TM),\u201d while Ronin (with a hidden Rose) went about blessing the campus. Once we found the damn Chem Lab, I mixed up some test tubes with slivers of Phosphorus in kerosene with a bit of added sulfur compounds, just to make things a little less stable. I didn\u2019t want to take the time in a strange lab to try and do something elaborate anyway. I managed to safely put together six vials of what I hoped would be a chemical explosive. It\u2019s always hard to tell what will count when you are dealing with things from outside the known universe. Yeah it\u2019s weird to read and write that.<br /> <br /> While we were gone, the rest of the Krewe figured out that the Outsider could only possess the campus proper, nothing past the recognized boundaries. So we worked it out that Mongler, Cupcake, and I would leave campus, then circle around so we could rush the area where Ronin finished the mass blessing. Rose was of course still in hiding nearby so we could be able to get to Ronin quickly. At least that was the plan. Cupcake and I powered up (Monstered-Out, if you will), and got ready for a big fight. Mongler is apparently always ready but we can\u2019t see it. When Ronin completed the last of the rites, we heard \u2026 well nothing at first. Ronin apparently flung her silent daggers of Rage into the beast as soon as it appeared but then it just swallowed her before we even realized the fight started. Rose called us in and joined the fray. Nightshade was doing something with Boneyard as I know Snowflake doesn\u2019t call the lightning. We moved knowing that Ronin was already losing air and Rose was there alone against the Outsider. Mongler said something about the heart of an antlion as soon as we got in sight of the mobile darkness as another bolt of lightning stabbed the darkness from above. Rose tried to get the beast to attack her as I could feel the cold winds blowing from her flowing veils. Amusingly, the darkness still failed to strike her. I hurled one of my vials of Greek Fire at the blob. It exploded, but I couldn\u2019t really tell how well it worked. Lightning arced down once again before Rose chilled the creature with her frozen touch. I quickly realized Cupcake had nothing she could do and gave her three of my vials. She put one to good use as well, and the explosion definitely had some effect. But before we could press our attack, the blackness disappeared with Ronin standing still. I was confused as we couldn\u2019t have killed it that easily, but then my heart sank. Ronin opened her eyes and they shone with a luminescent blackness. No I don\u2019t know how to say it otherwise. Black light was coming out of her eyes. I ran up and swung, hoping to knock her out. It was all I could think of as I wasn\u2019t about to use my claws. Terrifyingly, as I struck my Krewemate as a seven foot dog-man full on the chin, she turned her head to the side from the blow, then looked back in anger at me. Before I could consider all the possible ways I could die, Mongler leveled a massive blow that took her off her feet and planted her flatly on her back. We knew that if we could do enough damage, The Angel could allow Ronin to pass out. And thankfully, It seemed to recognize this as well. We gathered a mostly safe distance around Ronin\u2019s fallen form, when a churning, inky cloud of blackness poured out of her mouth. Rose slapped it with her frigid strike while Cupcake both threw dud vials. Then, like some final scene from a horror movie, Ronin\u2019s eyes flew open and she threw her invisible Rage into the cloud. I threw my last vial of Greek Fire (which did explode) just before another crackling bolt of icy blue lightning crashed into the blob. Then it seemed to fall almost in slow motion, then dispersed into nothing, and was gone.<br /> <br /> We gathered Ronin and moved back to Sainsbury where I could setup a temporary infirmary. I convinced Nightshade to come upstairs so I could try and heal some of her wounds. While we were upstairs, we heard through the ear curl that the Chief of Police was downstairs and \u201cinterviewing\u201d Ronin. From what we could hear, that went much better than it could have. The Chief seemed to know about my nocturnal activities and a bit about our otherwise unknown reputation as paranormal investigators. He already had a report about the Wookalar and while he suspected Officer Tart would be sanctioned from those up the chain for abandoning his post while on duty, little of any lasting damage would happen to him. Surprisingly, the only real snag came when Ronin tried to explain we still needed to take one of the eight bodies that Nightshade at some point raised to the front lawn. Snowflake stepped in at that point and \u2026 well I\u2019m not sure what he did. I\u2019ll simplify it by saying he put the whammy on the Chief. Suddenly one of the eight bodies was accepted to be the child\u2019s skeleton upstairs. Snowflake placed another illusion over the area so we could grab DeCastro\u2019s skeleton. We took it back to Dark Haven Bluffs while Snowflake and Rose remained at Sainsbury Hall. I heard Mongler tell the Chief they had permission from school officials as we were leaving. I figure Snowflake will have laid claim to the Hall by morning and that will be one less anchor for Adolphe. <br /> <br /> But that\u2019s enough fighting for one night. I know that Nightshade is stable and I\u2019ll be able to keep working with her so she heals faster. For now though, I\u2019m going to fall down myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Journal</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, July 24, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been an exhausting day, but all\u2019s well that ends well, as they say.<br /> <br /> We all hurried to Albertus Magnus to stop DeCastro\u2019s Outsider beast from rampaging about. I was with Gwen and Alexia, and we arrived first, thanks to Gwen\u2019s reckless driving. Simon drove Doc and Natalie separately and arrived a bit after we did.<br /> <br /> After arriving, Gwen, Alexia and I began prowling the campus, looking for any signs of the amorphous beast\u2019s presence. But we found nothing except absolute stillness. There were no birds to be seen and even the insects were quiet.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d already called Mongler via Gretchen, so I knew he was on his way. And Gwen called in a favor from her friend Clevon Norris, who got the police to blockade the campus under some story that there was a shooter or serial killer or something there. We didn\u2019t want anyone getting hurt, so the fewer people on campus, the better. Of course, when Mongler did arrive, the police were trying to stop him, but he frightened them away with a big, toothy grin. Since I doubt they could see what he really looks like, I must assume he used the fear powers of his kind to scare them off.<br /> <br /> The next few hours were a bit chaotic. When we arrived, I unlocked my Primeval nature and allowed the Caul and Shroud to come over me, adopting my feline features and growing vicious, spectral claws. Doc remained with Natalie in Simon\u2019s car in a trance, projecting his consciousness clad in the guise of the Dog of War to fight whatever we might encounter. Alexia grew additional, knife-wielding arms, and Simon sank into a Boneyard trance to search the campus for our adversary. Gwen was ready to go in guns blazing.<br /> <br /> But Simon discovered that the beast was not manifested. It had possessed the campus, and seemed to lurking in that state, waiting. We had no idea how to draw it out, and I think Doc and I, locked in our Primeval states like we were, felt the restless pull of the predator\u2019s instinct. I know I, for one, was a bit frustrated that we couldn\u2019t simply face the beast. I\u2019m sure it affected my later behavior.<br /> <br /> By the time Mongler joined us, we were looking for other ways to confront the beast, and Gwen had called Tavia to have her research the thing, hoping she could dig up enough information to help us. While we were waiting on that, we decided to go investigate Sansbury Hall. With DeCastro gone, we could unearth the corpses beneath the place and destroy DeCastro\u2019s body. Furthermore, we though Alonia might know something that would help us, if we could force her to share.<br /> <br /> But Alonia was not at the hall. She had no doubt fled to her other anchor, which left Sansbury Hall at our disposal. The ritual chambers in the basement did not hold any answers, so I marched right upstairs and into the secret room where I had found the doll before. I opened the drawer and the beastly thing jumped at me! But I was faster and snatched it out of the air, holding it quite securely in one of my clawed hands as I gave it a piece of my mind! I told it we were tired of its mischief and that it could either settle down and help us free it from its master\u2019s iron grip or we could do things the hard way. After all, the spirit possessing the doll isn\u2019t inherently evil, it\u2019s just been forced to serve DeCastro. After I made our intentions clear, its struggles quieted somewhat. It was still trying to attack me, for it had no choice under DeCastro\u2019s control, but its efforts became almost lethargic. Once this is all over, hopefully we\u2019ll be able to free the poor thing, or at least give it a better home.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Doc trusted the doll. He didn\u2019t seem convinced that it wasn\u2019t still intent on killing me, and continued to threaten it for the next bit while I carried the thing around to keep it out of trouble. Unfortunately, it didn\u2019t seem to know anything that would help us.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, some of the police, including a certain Officer Tart, began preparing to enter the campus to search for whatever was causing the disturbance. I don\u2019t really understand exactly what the situation was, but apparently the officer in question believes in the supernatural and thought some sort of beast that killed his late partner was lurking about. We couldn\u2019t have him getting involved, so Simon manufactured an illusion of this imaginary beast and let the officer have it out, ultimately slaying the thing. Simon them made the remains dissolve. Officer Tart seemed placated, though I\u2019m certain his superiors are unhappy. Still, several of his fellow officers witnessed the whole thing, so hopefully he won\u2019t be committed or fired.<br /> <br /> With that crisis averted, Simon hurried home to get his family crest so that we could establish our dominion over Sansbury Hall while Alonia and Adolphe were out. That way, Adolphe would no longer be able to use it as an anchor, and if we could destroy Adolphe\u2019s body, then Sansbury Hall would also be safe from Alonia. Natalie, still lying in the car, took Simon\u2019s place monitoring things through the Boneyard, protected by Alexia.<br /> <br /> It took Simon awhile to place the crest and perform the rituals necessary to claim Sansbury Hall, and while he was busy with that, Doc and I continued to prowl restlessly, waiting for word from Tavia. I locked the doll in the trunk of Simon\u2019s car (it seemed to understand why I had to do it). Natalie used her Boneyard mastery of Grave Dirt to unearth all the bodies beneath Sansbury Hall, shifting them onto the grounds outside, where Gwen\u2019s oracular insight easily let her determine which belonged to Adolphe. Meanwhile, I crept into the basement and found the spot where the Sansbury Hall\u2019s plasm collects. I absorbed in the plasm and then marked the place with our krewe mark and our sign for \u201chaunt.\u201d<br /> <br /> We had a close call, though, as Natalie was very nearly possessed by the thing through her Boneyard. She managed to fend it off, but the experience seemed to sober her up a bit, as she had been quite loopy from blood loss (and I suspect she was exaggerating her behavior).<br /> <br /> Eventually, Tavia called back information on the beast. Here\u2019s a bit of what Tavia learned:<br /> <br /> In order to force it manifest, we would need to bless the entire campus. Then it would mostly manifest near someone who it perceived as alone and vulnerable.<br /> <br /> It can possess people.<br /> <br /> In its physical form, it is an amorphous creature that cannot be harmed by most physical attacks. Only spiritual attacks or attacks that cause a substantial chemical reaction, such as burning, electricity, or freezing would harm it.<br /> <br /> It can envelop people in its shadowy mass, imprisoning them there so that they suffocate. Eventually, those trapped inside<br /> <br /> it would be dissolved, but the process would take a long time, and a victim would be dead from suffocation long before they were digested.<br /> <br /> We had also figured out that the beast\u2019s possession and awareness only extended to the boundaries of campus, so we decided that Gwen would set about blessing the grounds to draw the beast out. To ensure that it would come for one of us, Gwen would seem to be alone, though in truth, I would be hidden invisibly with her to help defend her from the beast once it appeared. The others would wait just outside of campus to avoid the beast\u2019s notice, but close to the final spot Gwen would bless so that they could rush in to help us as quickly as possible.<br /> <br /> Also, Doc realized that he and Alexia had no real way to harm the beast, so he went to the science department\u2019s chemistry lab and concocted a few flasks of incendiary chemicals. Doc really is an ingenious and versatile man when he puts his mind to it.<br /> <br /> The plan worked, though I can\u2019t say it went smoothly. As Gwen completed the Catholic blessing, the beast appeared like a pool of shadow pouring from thin air, its gaping mouth and hideous eyes staring ravenously at Gwen. She immediately attacked it with the force of her Rage, while I shrugged off my Stillness Shroud and donned the Cold-Wind. Unfortunately, I was not quick enough, and the beast enveloped Gwen. She\u2019s a tough one, though, so it didn\u2019t stop her from tearing at it with her Rage until the others arrived. Doc and Alexia came in tossing the incendiaries at it, while Natalie expended virtually all of her spiritual strength blasting it with arcs of electricity through her Cold-Wind Boneyard. Simon remained out of the fight, protecting Natalie\u2019s body.<br /> <br /> The beast tried to attack me, and I was willing to let it envelop me since I was cloaked in my Cold-Wind Shroud and knew I could freeze it from within. But it seemed to sense the danger and recoiled from me. Then it possessed Gwen. She turned against us. Doc and Mongler wasted no time knocking her out of action with a couple of well-placed punches. With its host unconscious, the beast was forced to manifest again. I froze bits of it, and then Natalie killed it once and for all with a final strike of electricity.<br /> <br /> The rest was just clean-up. By this time, the police chief had shown up, and the police were moving onto campus and establishing a crime scene. Gwen managed to smooth it over, and I think we have some clout now as paranormal investigators who really know what we\u2019re doing. The chief was not happy, but whether or not he actually understands what happened tonight, he trusts Gwen and was generous enough to conspire with us to remove DeCastro\u2019s body before the police took it so that we can destroy it as soon as possible. Actually, I\u2019m not so so certain that Simon didn\u2019t use some of his tricks to hide DeCastro\u2019s corpse and convince the chief that it was all for the best, but in any event, we were able to steal the body without any trouble from the police.<br /> <br /> While the others removed DeCastro\u2019s corpse to Darkhaven Bluffs, Simon and I remained on campus and made a quick stop by Murder Ballads to absorb the plasm that had managed to collect there since we last did so. We were both quite drained, and in fact I had nothing left. It felt good to strengthen my chi with the infusion of spiritual energy, especially after such an exhausting few days.<br /> <br /> Then we made our way home and incinerated the body in the incinerator that\u2019s built into one of the garden mausoleums. I don\u2019t really want to know why Simon\u2019s family has a corpse-sized incinerator in the garden, but I will admit that it could be handy for situations like this.<br /> <br /> Now we just have to go deal with Alonia and Adolphe, which will be a challenge, but should be much easier than it might have been had we dealt with them together as Sansbury Hall.<br /> <br /> For now, though, I\u2019m going to get some much deserved rest.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>John McClane</u><br /> I don\u2019t recall exactly how it came up, but somehow as we were hunting for DeCastro\u2019s beast on campus, Gwen said something to the effect that she was ready to \u201cGo all John McClane on the thing.\u201d I misunderstood and after a moment of puzzling over it, asked exactly how Republican politics would help us. Gwen looked at me like I was crazy for few seconds until she realized my error and explained that she meant John McClane, a character from an action movie called Die Hard, not John McCain, the presidential candidate.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> <br /> -Woops here we go. I\u2019m gonna be riding with Simon.<br /> <br /> -Hee hee I look like a scream queen in a vampire movie.<br /> <br /> -Man Gwen drives like a bat outta hell.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s creepy here.<br /> <br /> -Doc looks all passed out since he became magic Baskerville Hound.<br /> <br /> -Simon is scanning the area so I am chillin\u2019.<br /> <br /> -I am kinda light headed, actually.<br /> <br /> -Looks like Alonia fled the doom monster and so the house is clear\u2026Simon\u2019s gonna claim it.<br /> <br /> -They are Heading back to the place. Simon Driving and Doc all passed out.<br /> <br /> -No Vlogs today. Maybe tonight.<br /> <br /> -Why did I not get new clothes?<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is having an adventure!<br /> <br /> -My turn to see forever!<br /> <br /> -This is fun.<br /> <br /> -And the Graves shall vomit forth their dead!<br /> <br /> -Hey, something tried to get in my head!<br /> <br /> -I have enough emotional problems without a thing that must not be being in my head thankyouverymuch.<br /> <br /> -hee hee Jasmine called the evil doll a wanker.<br /> <br /> -wanker\u2026<br /> <br /> -Are they for real?<br /> <br /> -Simon is going to create a magical fake monster for a cop to fight. My brain asplode.<br /> <br /> -I am apparently missing quite a show.<br /> <br /> -Simon and I in evil land.<br /> <br /> -Looks like the big throw down is about to happen. Simon is tagging me in for some Jovian mischief.<br /> <br /> -Well, less rapey Jovian mischief.<br /> <br /> -That was nasty. Poor Gwen.<br /> <br /> -Doc is patching me up!<br /> <br /> -Cheese it the fuzz!<br /> <br /> -So\u2026many\u2026cops outside. Maybe we should not have made a phantom pig man.<br /> <br /> -Police make me nervous.<br /> <br /> -Gwen has this.<br /> <br /> -Maybe.<br /> <br /> -Maybe Simon and Gwen has this.<br /> <br /> -OK, time to go home, and not a moment too soon.<br /> <br /> -Waaaaah I want clean clothes. X-O<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session L</i><br /> <br /> Roman Numerals are cool till you get to session L.<br /> <br /> So they met their first Abyssal Entity face to face, a Gulmoth. Fortunately, it could not stand against the combined efforts of the entire Krewe, and they managed to kill it. Probably.<br /> <br /> FYI Grin (Mongler) used Fleeting Autumn on the Gulmoth so it would not run away (a worst case scenario) by removing it's ability to feel fear. He similarly used Fleeting Autumn on the Police. The creature generally tried to possess people who were alone. It could possess an area as marked by peoples understanding of the boarders...ie the campus for example.<br /> <br /> They also have drawn more police scrutiny, which may become a problem long term. In the meantime, they managed to, uh, give Timothy Tart a chance to revenge his fallen partner on an evil Wookalar, at least in his head. That encounter was\u2026no pre-planned\u2026I mean when Officer Tart lost his shit and went and got his Wookalar killing gear I knew how that would work but I did not pre-plan it for this session. I have to say it was not conducive to a horror mood but once it started it was it\u2019s own beast. I got a private suggestion that the final battle for the Krewe should be against a Wookalar. We will see. I have not even decided if they exist or not.<br /> <br /> Also Jasmine called a possessed doll a wanker.<br /> <br /> Next session was almost entirely Rping the following day. Join us for when Simon and Doc have a serious talk about women, Alexia, Jasmine and Gwen do girl stuff, and Natalie expresses a desire for her own Dreamy Boom Boom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:08:58-08:00","id":16325,"title":"","content":"OK, time for the Middle Shadows Krewe to get some R&amp;R. That is what session LI is all about!<br /> <i><br /> Session LI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1030 Hours, Sunday, July 25, 2010<br /> <br /> Today has been pretty helpful in unwinding. Last night really took it out of us all the way around. I got up around 0800 Hours. Meditation took no time at all and I was down for breakfast already showered, dressed, and aware. <br /> <br /> Karen was there for breakfast, but no Nightshade as usual. I could hear the whole AM/PM conversation in my head just thinking about it. We talked about whom to go after next, since no matter how much I dislike Rose\u2019s constant push to get everything done, we really are on a short time table. We had to choose between Alonia or Denise, keeping in mind that we\u2019d have to at least briefly deal with both of them. Rose and I are two of the best at resisting possession but we\u2019d like to actually resolve Denise. After dealing with Adolphe\u2019s \u201cDead Man Switch,\u201d the Krewe was fairly depleted, as far as using our abilities went so another big fight was not a happy thought. Karen spoke up when I discussed being a distraction for Alonia. She reminded us that Nightshade knew the ceremony to trap ghosts in a bottle. It was also fairly quick. That did help the planning stages, although I think I visibly tensed when Karen entered the conversation. The battle plan at the end of breakfast stood with us planning to trap Denise in a bottle then bind Alonia into her locket.<br /> <br /> Now I need to go and find Karen. She needs to understand my issues and I want to ask her something anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1620 Hours, Sunday, July 25, 2010<br /> <br /> That went better than I expected.<br /> <br /> I found Karen and asked her if she had time to talk. Something had been bothering me since Karen moved in and I kept my mouth shut because I couldn\u2019t figure out what it was at first...plus it would look bad on my part to randomly have unexplained problems with my girlfriend\u2019s girlfriend. Especially since I freely agreed to the arrangement. When Karen entered the discussion this morning, I finally figured out exactly what it was that bugged me so much. I\u2019m probably the worst Gatekeeper that ever took the Bargain but I understand now. My segregationism comes from trying to keep people safe, ghosts too but in this town they don\u2019t need much help. People normally don\u2019t have any way to deal with ghosts that are bothering them and are normally scarred by trying if they do find some way to deal with them. Thus I try to get involved to keep that from happening. The living stay living, the dead stay dead, and everyone is happy. Theoretically. But Karen got thrown into this. Yes she agreed to find out and yes I believe Nightshade tried very hard to make sure Karen knew what she was getting into. But she is still just a normal, if fairly intelligent, mortal. Normal men and women don\u2019t have ways to deal with the supernatural if they are unlucky enough to get involved. And I had no option to keep Karen from getting involved. Now that she is, she is trying to learn as much as she can so she can keep up. I feel that way with the vampires we know, so I understand the feeling. And she\u2019s done a pretty good job for someone that\u2019s mostly been forced to stay on the sidelines. Tavia isn\u2019t just a normal person so she\u2019s into everything that isn\u2019t combat-related. Karen has nothing. She carries a target on her back with nothing to cover it or shield herself. I don\u2019t like that. It\u2019s not fair and eventually it won\u2019t be safe. So once we moved into the sitting room, I explained all that. I didn\u2019t try to be condescending or anything, because she shouldn\u2019t be able to deal with these things. I think (and hope) she understood why I\u2019m concerned. Now this is the part that proves I\u2019m a terrible Gatekeeper. Once I got all that out and off my chest, I asked her what she thought about the magic that Snowflake and I use. She said that she was normally a skeptic about anything like that, but being around us made it harder to discount out right. Then I asked her if she would be interested in learning something like that? She was a little taken aback as I don\u2019t think she was expecting me to offer to teach her, but that\u2019s basically what I was doing. I don\u2019t like that she\u2019s been thrown naked into a minefield. At the very least, I want to give her some clothes and maybe a better shot at seeing them, if not dodging them altogether. So Snowflake and I will soon have a new apprentice magician. Then it was Karen\u2019s turn. She asked if any of us dealt with many normal people very often. I felt bad that she needed to make the distinction but I guess it\u2019s fair. It was a little amusing to have to defend Rose\u2019s taskmaster approach, but really we don\u2019t have time to take off. I told her about the people at the shop for me and Cupcake, the students and coffee friends with Rose, Ronin has her clients and old police friends, and Nightshade has her and the people at the clubs. Even Snowflake has his group of normal friends up in Rhode Island. Karen told me that Nightshade really doesn\u2019t go out that much anymore and she\u2019s worried that never being around regular people will mess with her head. I think there\u2019s some merit in the thought, but Nightshade goes out to the places when she\u2019s low on Plasm...still, she may move around people less than any of the rest of us at this point. That bit of information was kind of surprising.<br /> <br /> About that time, Nightshade came in and informed me I needed a bidet in my shop, as she laid across both me and Karen. She gave Karen some kind of expectant look, the my new apprentice started immediately massaging Nightshade\u2019s feet. I poked Nightshade for being rude then gave Karen some pointers to keep her hands from getting sore as quickly. A small part of me wanted to show her how it was supposed to be done, but I don\u2019t need to start getting competitive now. We also covered a very bizarre tale of Nightshade\u2019s first and last acid trip. Tavia and Chandra wanted to know if anyone was interested in playing paintball with them, but we needed to rest up. Tonight should be another major ordeal. We also realized about then that Cupcake, Rose, and Ronin were missing. There was a mess in the kitchen like Cupcake had been working on something but no other signs of any of them. I immediately called Ronin, fighting off the sudden panic urge that something had managed to get into the House. She answered her phone but told me they were fine. Said they were at the spa doing \u201cgirl stuff\u201d and would be back later. I asked her why the hell she was there if they were doing girl stuff but she hung up on me.<br /> <br /> We all grabbed lunch after that and Snowflake followed us back into the sitting room. After continuing some of our previous conversations, I filled him in on the new magic partner. He was surprised but seemed to enjoy the thought. Anytime we can bring someone else in that can share something intellectual with him, Snowflake tends to like it. After a bit of that, it was my turn to be a little rude. Snowflake needed to talk about relationships, so I excused us to go have a \u201cman talk.\u201d Yes that was probably the worst thing I could have said, but Snowflake needed to talk and I didn\u2019t know how comfortable he would have been admitting or displaying how naive he really is to Karen or Nightshade. Once we moved off into the gallery, Snowflake confessed that he really doesn\u2019t want to be with Tavia in any capacity. We both knew that this would not go well and that Andrea would officially be in danger when it came out. I asked, even though I didn\u2019t think it was the right option, if Tavia would accept being told \u201cMaster of the House\u201d-style that he was going to have a mistress? We could never really be sure of what might happen there. He wants to go out and be normal, screw up, make mistakes, basically live...all on his own terms. I usually forget that he\u2019s only 20 so this really does make sense. I told Snowflake he needed to decide if he has permanently lost interest in Tavia, because that may also have a great deal to do with how things need to be handled. Now that I think about all this together, it\u2019s more than a little terrifying that Tavia and Chandra are out playing soldier together.<br /> <br /> Rose, Ronin, and Cupcake came back then and Rose seemed pretty happy. When she used the phrase \u201cVa Va Voom,\u201d I was pretty sure the End Times were upon us. Cupcake\u2019s mad cackling didn\u2019t help that thought any either. With that, I dragged Snowflake down into the Library. Since we\u2019ve got designs on setting up an alchemy lab, I figured it was about time we started to learn about it. I was surprised when he offered to help me do the research. I thought it was just understood that he was the smart one, but apparently he handed the lead to me now. I was honored and floored, but we did well working together. In about twenty minutes I managed to put together what we needed to work out the kind of alchemy that would affect us, not stuff. Stuff will be next, but one step at a time. <br /> <br /> Now I think it\u2019s time to really rest up and coordinate how we\u2019re going to deal with tonight. I\u2019m pretty sure Nightshade has already woken Clyde up from his not so eternal slumber.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> During my meditation just now, I had an insight. Well, really just a confirmation on something I\u2019ve been thinking about for awhile now. I think the Bride and I need to find a way to grasp the Phantasmal Key and learn how to unlock a manifestation of the Oracle. Gwen and Alexia are already quite proficient with the Oracle, but as I\u2019ve become the definitive scout for the krewe, I think it would be useful if I could see past illusions and invisibility. After all, I know how potent one can be when one is unseen, and I don\u2019t want to overlook something hidden when I\u2019m supposed to be preparing the way for my krewe. Certainly in many cases Simon can support me with his Phantasmal Boneyard, but it would be nice to see things on my own, especially for cases when I\u2019m sneaking into places and Simon is not around.<br /> <br /> So I\u2019ve resolved to ask Gwen to help me figure out the Oracle, and to ask Simon for help finding my own Phantasmal Key. The Bride seems pleased, and I think she knows something about the trials of acquiring the Phantasmal Key, something that she thinks will be good for me. She\u2019s remaining surprisingly quiet about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> Breakfast was constructive this morning. Natalie was not there, but everyone else attended and we had some delightful crepes with fruit and creme. They reminded me of the ones my mother used to make occasionally.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve laid plans for our next move against the Decastros. We will eliminate Alonia next. Her only remaining anchor is the locket buried with Denise James, and once we\u2019ve dug it up, I\u2019m going to bind Alonia into the locket with the Fetter\u2019s Binding ceremony. It\u2019s not going to be easy, as we\u2019ll have to keep Alonia at bay for several minutes while I do so. Meanwhile, Denise\u2019s ghost will be a problem, but we plan to have Natalie imprison her temporarily with another ceremony. Once Alonia has been trapped, we can resolve Denise at our leisure.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m worried about Alonia. Doc assures us that he can hold her at bay, but I\u2019m still anxious. She has a potent ability to possess people, and I worry what might happen if she possesses Doc. He is confident that won\u2019t happen, and I think I can trust his confidence.<br /> <br /> We will go to the cemetery to deal with Alonia and Denise tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Late Morning<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve just had a very troubling experience, and I need to sort it all out in my head. I understand why the Bride was so eager for me to experience a vision from my subconscious.<br /> <br /> I asked Simon to help me find the Phantasmal Key. He assured me that I was already in tune with the sort of illusory qualities necessary to learn the key, and all that remained was for me to have an experience in which my perceptions were altered by a potent, mind-bending, illusory encounter or hallucination, one in which my understanding of reality is temporarily shifted far enough to provide me with some sort of unique insight into my own subconscious. At least, that\u2019s how Simon explained it, and to me it sounded a bit like the more misguided practices of certain Taoist mystics.<br /> <br /> Simon offered to help by inflicting an illusory reality upon me, one drawn from my own subconscious. We went down to the ritual chamber in the cellars for some privacy, and Simon use his phantasmal powers on me. I experienced a powerful vision which I believe tells me a lot about my own wishes, desires, and frailties, at least in regard to my current romantic prospects. But\u2026he vision has left me feeling extraordinarily guilty, and still confused.<br /> <br /> In my vision, I thought I was alone in a nice, romantic parlour with both Julian and Karl. The entire atmosphere was cozy and sensual, with a subtle yet comforting aroma and soft candlelight. I somehow knew that both Julian and Karl were trying to win my affections. Karl set next to me on a sumptuous sofa and gently placed a book of the most beautiful poetry in my hands. He looked at me with his awkward face and told me he loved me, and that the poetry expressed just a fraction of what he felt. My heart soared, and I was about to respond, when I felt Julian\u2019s hand caress my cheek and then brush a lock of hair over my ear. I turned to him and he flashed a charming smile that made me melt. Before I even realized what was happening we kissed. It was such a luxurious, wonderful kiss.<br /> <br /> Remembering Karl, I turned back to him, and I could see the heartbreak on his face, and that\u2019s when I began to notice that the candles had grown cold on his side of the room, and they flickered not in a gentle breeze, but in a watery current. Despite the cold, or maybe because of it, I felt at home there, yet the primeval fishes that swam by reminded me of Karl\u2019s lineage, and I felt a sense of revulsion, not toward Karl, but toward his family. To temper my guilt, I turned away from him and back to Julian, and doing so was like emerging from the cold depths onto a sunlit beach. He wrapped his arms around me and we kissed and caressed and soon I was laying on the sofa as he slowly, sensually removed my clothing. I remember sensing Karl slowly, sadly walk away, shoulders slumped and spirit broken, but I was far too enamoured of Julian\u2019s affections to care. It has been so long sense I\u2019ve made love and it felt so good to surrender to Julian\u2019s charms, even though, somewhere deep inside, I felt as though somehow it was all wrong.<br /> <br /> And then the vision ended, and I came back to myself with my clothes in disarray and Simon sitting across the room from me, trying desperately not to look at me. I admit I was a bit embarrassed, but I tried to put that aside and focus on what the vision meant. I told Simon briefly what had transpired, but I have a lot to think about now.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, I already talked to Gwen about learning Oracle and told her what I was doing with Simon, and I think she\u2019s booked us a spa appointment for this afternoon. She\u2019s such a wonderful friend. I\u2019m pretty sure she assumed my vision would have to do with Richard, and I think that may have devastated me. Perhaps it\u2019s a good thing that my subconscious decided to focus on Karl and Julian. Maybe it means I\u2019m finally moving on. Then again, maybe that\u2019s one reason I feel so guilty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Gwen, Alexia and I have returned from a nice afternoon at the spa. The massages and facials were wonderful. And during it all, I talked to them about my vision and what it might mean, which led to a long discussion about what I really wanted in romance and whether Karl or Julian could give me what I need.<br /> <br /> Gwen was a bit confused by my affection for Karl. She seemed to think that Julian was perfect. As she says, I \u201clight up\u201d around him, which I suppose is true. But I worry that my interest is based purely on his charms, and I don\u2019t know how sincere those are. He certainly hasn\u2019t made any effort to ask me out or see me aside from the times we\u2019ve invited him to dinner. I suppose it\u2019s always possible that he doesn\u2019t know I\u2019m interested in him. I do have a tendency to be a bit cold toward people, especially when I\u2019m anxious around them. Gwen didn\u2019t seem to think I\u2019d been cold to Julian at all though. And if that\u2019s the case, I fear Julian simply isn\u2019t interested in me. I suppose he must have many less awkward girls to choose from in Providence. Of course, Gwen and Alexia would hear none of that sort of talk.<br /> <br /> Eventually, I think Gwen began to understand a bit of what I see in Karl. She\u2019s seen me with Julian, but she never saw any of the long and deep conversations I shared with Karl as we discussed poetry and literature. Gwen was impressed to learn that Karl and I regularly send each other books to read. She\u2019s still put off by his appearance, but I told her that I don\u2019t feel it is fair to judge Karl or discount him as a romantic prospect based on his looks. She asked me whether I could see myself making out with Karl, and I confess that I hesitated a bit, which only deepened my confusion and guilt. At the same time, I do think Karl would be very romantic if given the chance, and as Gwen explained to Alexia, the Bride and I are the sorts of girls who need poetry and roses in our romance. I\u2019m certain Julian is good at being romantic too. I just wonder if he would be as sincere as Karl.<br /> <br /> I still don\u2019t know what to think or do. But Gwen and Alexia made me feel better. And Gwen even admitted that even though Karl might not have Julian\u2019s \u201cva-va-voom\u201d (which make Alexia laugh every time we said it), he seemed to be sincere and charming in his own way. But the matter of his family is not such a trivial thing, and Gwen pointed out that I\u2019m not the only one who has concerns about the Fishbornes. Even if I were to accept becoming a part of the family, Gwen doesn\u2019t think the Fishbornes would accept me. She compared it to <i>Romeo and Juliet,</i> only realizing after she said it how much I love that play, and for a moment I think she feared I might throw myself into a doomed romance just because it\u2019s tragic. But I\u2019m far more prudent than that, which I suppose is one reason this whole issue is giving me such difficult time.<br /> <br /> At any rate, Gwen and Alexia are definitely supportive, and it\u2019s good to have friends I can rely on to keep me from doing anything terribly foolish. And besides, I\u2019m probably over thinking all of this. I\u2019m honestly surprised Gwen didn\u2019t chide me about that, but maybe she realizes I need to work this out somehow.<br /> <br /> We returned home after our spa day to find Natalie, Simon, and Doc deeply involved in a conversation of their own. I have no idea what it was about, but they seemed amused that Gwen, Alexia and I had been doing \u201cgirl stuff\u201d. Chandra and Tavia apparently went out to play paint ball, so I\u2019m sure Tavia is going to be in no shape to move about later. And Alexia needs help cleaning up the kitchen, which she left in terribly disarray when we left for the spa, so I think I\u2019ll go help her.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> Gwen, Alexia and I spent the rest of the afternoon (after cleaning up the kitchen) discussing the Oracle more. It seems my regular meditations have prepared me well for opening my eyes to spiritual perception, and I caught on to the concepts very easily. Since Alexia also masters the Phantasmal Key, she was able to help me understand how to unlock the Oracle with Phantasm. I\u2019m still learning, but I think I\u2019m beginning to understand the basics. I spent awhile wandering through the unused wings of Darkhaven Bluffs to practice. The rats watched me, but I don\u2019t think they were upset by my trespass.<br /> I suppose I should start preparing for tonight.<br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Simon &amp; Tavia</u><br /> <br /> In the morning, before I became distracted by my vision, Simon and I chatted a bit about romance, and his dismay at Tavia\u2019s obsession over him came up again. I reiterated my opinion that he needs to find romance on his own terms. If he doesn\u2019t love Tavia, then her obsession should not force him into a relationship with her, no matter what the consequences might be. Even if problems might arise when he breaks things off with her, he cannot enslave his heart to her will. He has to consider his own desires in matters of the heart, and I told him that I approve of him trying to find love on his own terms. He knows I will support him in whatever way I can. I know Tavia will be unhappy with this, and I do feel sad for her, but she is not so much in love with Simon as psychotically obsessed with him, and that has to end some time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -It\u2019s a day in Da-Dake! The water is blue and Natalie\u2019s awake!<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Hmmm where is everyone.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m in a good mood given the blood loss!<br /> <br /> - XD<br /> <br /> -Doc and Karen are colluding.<br /> <br /> -Colluding is fun.<br /> <br /> -Oooh, I get to be decedent, decedent I say!<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is well taken care of.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is not, however, a The Pushmi-pullyu.<br /> <br /> -Or a Wookalar.<br /> <br /> -Wait, Doolittle did not have <i>Dreamy Boom Boom</i> did he? That was some other Doctor?<br /> <br /> -Aw, Simon is lookin\u2019 glum!<br /> <br /> -He has not even lost half his blood what the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Ah, girl problems.<br /> <br /> -I know all about girl problems.<br /> <br /> -Hell, I AM girl problems.<br /> <br /> -Speaking of girls Jasmine, Alexia, and Gwen are doing \u201cgirl stuff\u201d<br /> <br /> -Whatever \u201cgirl stuff\u201d is<br /> <br /> -When does stuff become \u201cgirl stuff\u201d<br /> <br /> -Do guys talk about \u201cboi stuff?\u201d \u201cNah man, we are just doing \u2018boi stuff.\u2019\u201d<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress meditates on the questions of the universe.<br /> <br /> -Wow, the conversation took at \u201cnot for present company\u201d turn.<br /> <br /> -Doc has to help poor Simon.<br /> <br /> -I am pretty sure relationship issues are not \u201cboi stuff\u201d<br /> <br /> -Fear not, Your Mistress is still attended to.<br /> <br /> -Geeze you people OK \u201cboy stuff\u201d happy? X-D<br /> <br /> -Gang\u2019s all here!<br /> <br /> -Apparently getting a massage is \u201cgirl stuff\u201d. I guess everyone likes \u201cgirl stuff\u201d then.<br /> <br /> -I have never dated anyone who was like \u201cA massage? HELL NO\u201d<br /> <br /> -I am not sure what \u201cInternal Alchemy\u201d is but it sounds dirty.<br /> <br /> -Time for my checkup!<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s \u201cquotation marks day\u201d<br /> <br /> -Oh my, Zombie Time already!<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s do this thing!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LI</i><br /> <br /> Jasmine's Vision was part of the requirement for learning the Phantasmal Key, as per our house rules listed earlier. The PC was not given to psychoactive drugs (and contrary to everyone's expectation, Natalie did not have any.)<br /> <br /> So pretty much a big roleplaying session. The group was split most of the session, with Natalie Doc and Simon at the house and Jasmine, Gwen and Alexia at the Spa. Fortunately, we got detailed journals of both groups.<br /> <br /> Join us next session, when the Krewe deals with Alonia and Denise and Natalie takes a major step toward meeting her daughter.<br /> <br /> ...It was Dr. Snuggles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:11:55-08:00","id":16327,"title":"","content":"You folks ready for the battle with Alonia? Because that is what we have. And more...read on.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0215 Hours, Monday, July 26, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m exhausted for as early as it is. Probably from emotional fatigue.<br /> <br /> We went out well after dark so we could get to the cemetery and not interrupt or disrupt any events at the church. Before we moved in, we opened the trunk and traded Clyde for Cupcake. She used her new Marionette powers to manifest as the Cracked Cook before we closed the trunk again and moved on. Nightshade struggled with putting the guard to sleep, but eventually the power of her Stillness Boneyard won out. But before we could make it to the grave, we spotted some of Nightshade\u2019s groupies from the Ball. Ronin went to menace them so they would be safe from whatever Alonia might do. That became a comedy show before it was over with. They apparently got permission to be there by the guard before they came in with ashtray to smoke in peace. Eventually Snowflake saved the day with his illusions and the girls left since \u201cthe guard\u201d came and told them something dangerous was going on. I\u2019m not sure exactly as I was laughing too hard at the situation Ronin got herself into.<br /> <br /> Finally without any spectators, Rose drew a wide spiral centered on the grave for her ritual. We all prepared ourselves as best we could. Snowflake drove the coffin to the surface and the party got started. Denise immediately possessed her own body and started trying attack. Alonia went for Rose but learned quickly that a contest of wills with Rose is like slamming your head against a brick wall. Painful, frustrating, and ultimately unproductive. Denise, apparently more of a physical girl, took a swing at Rose. She missed by a mile but Rose used her smooth Tai Chi to grab the pendant and rip it off Denise. Cupcake moved in on Alonia but didn\u2019t get anywhere. Alonia lived up to her advertising. She was not easy to touch and was very strong willed. Ronin did something that made her look afraid but she still lashed out at Rose, which was equally pointless. By that point, I sliced my hand open and splashed some blood on her before commanding the Djinn Alonia Nazeed to move away from Rose and sit. I knew she wouldn\u2019t follow my orders but my blood compelled her. If she wished to disobey, she would struggle to do so. Snowflake also placed a curse of his own on Alonia, further weakening her. Denise was really no threat but she was a problem. Cupcake grabbed her and held her still until Nightshade could complete her ceremony to trap her in the old wine bottle she got from Snowflake. After another blast from whatever crippling fear Ronin unleashed within Alonia, I tried to hold her at bay until Rose could finish her ceremony. I still had a hard time getting to her however. The upside was that Alonia was so reduced in power that she had a very hard time possessing anyone. Which was good since Cupcake and I both had trouble getting a grip on her. Clyde stood next to Snowflake to one side. They had a similar expression on their faces.<br /> <br /> I finally looped an arm about Alonia to hold her still, but she immediately slipped out of my hold. Cupcake had better luck and held her tightly. Snowflake got another shot in on her that weakened her somehow, but I really don\u2019t know what other than it came from the Boneyard.<br /> <br /> Thirty fucking minutes later, Rose finally finished the etching on the pendant. I\u2019m not really complaining that Rose did things the right way, just more frustrated that Alonia had to be contained for so long. When the etching completed, there was a ripple and then a swirling whirlpool opened through the pendant. Alonia\u2019s eyes flew open wide as she fought to get out of Cupcake\u2019s hold but the pull of the fetter was far too strong. The horrible spectre howled, struggled, and flailed wildly as she was locked into her final resting place. The fetter would have allowed us to possess people, but having bodies of our own, that\u2019s less useful. That left us with a dangerous fetter and a spirit trapped in a bottle. We also took the body with us to burn at the House. Snowflake took care of returning the grave to a more normal and less robbed state then we left.<br /> <br /> We tried to think of the best way to deal with Denise, but given the last thing she saw was us fighting with Alonia and stealing her anchor, I was a little confused as to how we\u2019d get through to her. Nightshade and Cupcake worked out a plan. And man we didn\u2019t see that one coming. Nightshade got her laptop before Cupcake took the bottle and they headed into the Evil Magic Circle room. The rest of us were outside with the ear curls. When Nightshade opened the bottle, Denise came out ready for a fight. Cupcake, who had been in a completely different form during the fight so not necessarily involved, talked her down enough to get her to listen. Nightshade told Denise about her own daughter and how much she missed her. They reminded Denise that she also had a daughter, one that was taken from her. Denise remembered but claimed that she died in an accident. Cupcake told her the real story, and I have to say actually hearing that almost turned my stomach. When the story was over, Nightshade let her know that Justice had been served. There was no reason for her to guard Alonia and Alonia has been and will be punished for what she did, including what happened to Denise\u2019s daughter. But there was no justice in keeping Denise away form her daughter any longer. I\u2019m pretty sure I was not the only one with tears in their eyes outside the door to that room. Denise was quiet for a little bit then thanked Nightshade and Cupcake and we felt the rush of spiritual energy flush through as Denise James finally passed on.<br /> <br /> Cupcake immediately called me into the room. I ran in to find Nightshade crying in front of her laptop, staring at the picture of her little girl. I pulled her into me and held her close to comfort her. The crying wasn\u2019t outright sobbing, but I could tell she needed me. I took her upstairs to bed. She told me as I was stroking her hair that she wanted to bring baby Nightshade up to Dark Haven Bluffs. I started out okay with the idea until she said that at 16, she could handle living here. I was very careful when I pointed out that she was not in the best emotional state to make long term plans. But I did think baby Nightshade coming for a visit was a fair idea. She agreed that now was probably not the time to make plans, but asked me to talk to the Krewe at breakfast about little Nightshade coming up for a week before school started. I promised and held her until she fell asleep.<br /> <br /> Now I think I\u2019m going to curl up next to her and not leave her alone through the night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Monday, July 26, 2010<br /> <br /> Sleeping with Nightshade is great but I was a little out of sorts this morning. I slipped out of bed to go meditate about 0730 Hours and I knew it would take a little bit. About an hour later, I was finally centered and got ready for the day.<br /> <br /> I came down for breakfast to find Nightshade awake and anxious. I asked her why she was up, since I did promise to ask the Krewe. She was too nervous though and I thought it would mean more anyway, so she stayed up and asked about baby Nightshade. I knew it would be fine but Nightshade seemed so surprised and excited when everyone said it was a great idea.<br /> <br /> Then Rose brought everyone back to earth and reminded us that we would be dealing with DeCastro tonight and then we had to worry about Candle Cove, probably before baby Nightshade came to visit. No real surprises there.<br /> <br /> Now let\u2019s see what kind of day Monday will have for me.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve managed to imprison Alonia, so all in all not a bad night\u2019s work. It was not easy, but thanks to our planning and preparation, we bound her to her anchor without anything going terribly wrong. Since Alonia is very good at possessing people, things could have gone badly very quickly, but fortunately we are made of sterner stuff.<br /> <br /> We infiltrated the graveyard after dark. Two of Natalie\u2019s groupies were smoking there but otherwise not doing anything wrong, but we still had to convince them to leave, so Gwen pretended she was still a policeman and made them to leave for their own safety. Meanwhile, Simon remained in the car so that he could support us with the Grave Dirt Boneyard, and since Alexia feared being possessed, she stayed with him, but projected herself by possessing her geist, the Cracked Cook, through the powers of her Phantasmal Marionette.<br /> <br /> I etched a large spiral centered on Denise James\u2019 grave so that when Simon unearthed the casket and Alonia appeared, she would already be trapped in the coils of the Fetter\u2019s Binding ceremony. And then we began. Simon used his mastery of the graveyard to draw the casket to the surface, and as soon as it appeared, its lid flew open and Denise\u2019s corpse lurched out, flailing around with bony fingers to claw at those who were disturbing her grave. Denise was possessing it, of course, but Natalie would deal with that soon enough. I was quicker, though, and before Denise was even able to get her bearings, I ducked past her clawing arms and snatched Alonia\u2019s pendant from her neck. She threw herself at me then, but I was able to sidestep her attacks with the help of my Shroud and withdrew to a position where I could kneel and begin etching the pendant with the symbols and seals that would imprison Alonia.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m certain Denise would have continued attacking me, but her corpse soon fell limp as Natalie performed a quick ceremony to draw Denise\u2019s ghost out of her body and into a centuries-old wine bottle Simon had given her for that purpose. And with Denise trapped, we only had Alonia to worry about. And she was worrisome indeed. She knew instantly what I was trying to do, and glared at me as she tried to take control of my body. But I focused on the ceremony and centered myself in a sort of meditation, and my soul was closed to her, making her attempt to possess me quite futile.<br /> <br /> By then, Gwen, Doc and Simon were able to bring their mystical powers to bear against Alonia. Gwen used her skill at manipulating emotions to draw Alonia\u2019s fears to the surface, while Doc commanded her to be still with the Stigmata key. Simon sapped her will to fight us, but she still resisted fiercely, first trying to possess Gwen yet failing due to the restraints our efforts had placed on her. Doc and the Cracked Cook (Alexia) struggled with Alonia until finally the Cook managed to grab and hold her for the long minutes it took me to finish the Fetter\u2019s Binding ceremony. But we did it. Alonia is locked away in the pendant, and now we just have to figure out how to resolve Denise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We have resolved Denise, though it seemed hopeless at first. After imprisoning Alonia, we realized that even if we were to release Denise from the bottle in which Natalie had trapped her, we didn\u2019t really know how to resolve her connection to Alonia\u2019s pendant. She felt she had to protect it on behalf of Alonia, and her dedication to that evil woman was positively fanatical.<br /> <br /> However, Natalie came through for us. She and Alexia released Denise in a private, safe room of the house, and then Natalie spoke to her. She showed her pictures of her own daughter, and talked to Denise about how much she missed her daughter and longed to be with her. She reminded Denise that Denise also had a daughter, the girl that Adolphe and Alonia had so brutally murdered in one of their summoning rituals. Denise never knew what had happened; she had been told her daughter had been killed in an unfortunate mystical accident or some such, not that she had been tortured and abused to death in order to call forth a horrid beast from the Abyss. And in the end, Natalie convinced Denise that it was time to go be with her daughter again. And so Denise let go, and passed on into the Underworld. I hope she finds her daughter there, though I fear her daughter\u2019s soul is no more. At least now Denise is at peace.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 26, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I will resume my training sessions with Jean this morning. It seems amazing that I returned from Taiwan less than a week ago!<br /> <br /> The krewe chatted as normal over breakfast about what to do next. Naturally, we plan to bind Adolphe into his guns as soon as we can, but first, this afternoon, I\u2019m going to seal and hide Alonia\u2019s pendant. I also had to remind everyone that the Candle Cove problem is still looming over us. We\u2019ve bought ourselves some time, but we need to resolve the problem quickly, especially since we might have a visitor soon: Natalie\u2019s daughter.<br /> <br /> We were surprised to see Natalie at breakfast, and her presence was soon explained when she asked quite timidly if she could invite her daughter up to visit for a week or so. Naturally, we all said that would be delightful. Natalie misses her daughter and wants to reconnect with her so badly that I think she should have her visit. Of course, Natalie needs to clean up her act a bit, but Gwen beat me to that point when he told Natalie she had to remove all drug paraphernalia so that her daughter would in no way be exposed to such nonsense.<br /> <br /> If only this were a step toward cleaning Natalie up for good. Maybe it is.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u><br /> Final Solution</u><br /> <br /> We discussed what to do with the pendant in which Alonia is trapped, though I had already made up my mind about what to do with it before we ever discussed it. We plan to seal the pendant in a locked box, which we will seal in a small block of concrete. I will then take the concrete to the bottom of the ocean some distance off the coast, where I will bury it beneath the sea floor where, hopefully, it will never be found. We will likely do the same with Adolphe\u2019s fetter, though Simon and Natalie have been arguing that we should keep one of these fetters as it could be useful to us in days to come. But I\u2019m anxious about keeping, much less using, something invested with such warped and evil power. If it were simply an ancient and evil yellowbones, I might feel differently. But Adolphe and Alonia aren\u2019t just powerful, insane ghosts, they are infected with the evil of the Outsiders, and they have reveled in sick and twisted things, the very thought of which turns my stomach.<br /> <u><br /> Natalie</u><br /> <br /> We discovered a few weeks ago that Natalie is not Natalie\u2019s real name. Her daughter\u2019s name is Natalie, and she adopted the name as a sort of stage name, I suppose, out of fondness for her daughter (though why she would want to drag her daughter\u2019s name through the mud of her professional life is beyond me). Anyway, Natalie\u2019s real name is Allison, which is a very nice name, in my opinion. Karen calls her that sometimes, but the rest of us still call her Natalie. I don\u2019t know what we\u2019ll call her when her daughter comes to visit, as continuing to call her Natalie might be somewhat awkward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, July 25th<br /> <br /> -Here we are, the place we should not be.<br /> <br /> -Damn willful guard. HAS A SLEEPY WILL J00?<br /> <br /> -Ooooooh a certain someone is here<br /> <br /> -Stay on task, damnit!<br /> <br /> -Look at me, all staying on task!<br /> <br /> -That\u2019s us. Subtle!<br /> <br /> -Radio Silence, stuff happening.<br /> <br /> -OK, taking little miss sloshy back to the house. Could have gone worse.<br /> <br /> -Why do I volunteer to do things I know is going to be emotionally punishing?<br /> <br /> -No no, that\u2019s not it, I am only a <i>physical</i> masochist.<br /> <br /> -Goddamnit here I go.<br /> <br /> -i am not gonna type anymore tonite.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 26th<br /> <br /> -That was terrible. I am not gonna do that again.<br /> <br /> -OMG they\u2026are gonna let me do it. Even Spooky.<br /> <br /> -SQEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE!<br /> <i><br /> End Session LII</i><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026<br /> <br /> The scene with Natalie and Denise was not preplanned\u2026but the result of a lot of IC and some OOC discussion. There was a bit of frustration about how to get Denise to move on given the initial antagonistic encounter. After some time the concept using the stuff with her daughter came up and then the idea crystallized. it was a very emotional scene (I think).<br /> <br /> The push over bringing the daughter over was similarly unplanned but made sense at the time.<br /> <br /> Natalie had a great deal of trouble and had to spend a fair amount of plasm trying to put the guard to sleep with the Stillness Boneyard. Channeling Boneyard effects is expensive (as it should be).<br /> <br /> The next session was not so weighty, however. The PCs bought a yacht with their found gold and took some time off to have a yacht party before finishing the job. Stranger things I guess. But it should prove well worth your time. Come join us then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:14:08-08:00","id":16330,"title":"","content":"Sometimes a session goes in a different direction then you expect. Sometimes this different direction involves a yacht party. This is a tale of one such a time. This is\u2026<br /> <i><br /> Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1425 Hours, Monday, July 26, 2010<br /> <br /> Work went pretty normally for a Monday. I got some more drawing in before and after Nightshade stopped by for lunch. We talked more about baby Nightshade coming up and plans for when she gets here. I really need to think of a different name for her. A 17 year old is not going to stand for being called baby anything. Belladonna might work.<br /> <br /> Okay that\u2019s weird. I just got a text from Nightshade asking if I wanna ride onna boat? It says to come home early. That was an old Navy pickup line but I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s never heard it...wait, no she probably has. Just not from me. Looks like it\u2019s a good thing I\u2019m having a slow afternoon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2045 Hours, Monday, July 26, 2010<br /> <br /> Snowflake said last night that he was going to get a boat. He bought a fucking party yacht! When I got back to the Bluffs there was this unbelievable ship docked at the pier. I suspect Snowflake and I will be renovating the pier soon as that rickety thing does not fit with this modern day ship of the line. Well it\u2019s not a ship of the line yet. I asked what armaments it had and Rose looked at me like I was completely insane. She then chastised me for assuming we\u2019d need anything besides ourselves. She\u2019s forgetting that we have some \u201cdistant relatives\u201d that hold sway with magic. Also I like Karl but I imagine not everyone from Cold Harbor is quite as social as he seems to be. Snowflake seemed to understand and we\u2019ll talk about that later. Tavia brought two bottles of champagne down. We used one to christen the SS <i>Saturnine Dreamer</i>, the other we left to chill in the galley. I hadn\u2019t been back on a boat since I got out of the hospital so this was the greatest thing we could have done as far as I\u2019m concerned. Granted now I\u2019m going to have to learn to pilot the damn thing. I\u2019ve already gotten the funny looks.<br /> <br /> We took the <i>Dreamer </i>out with our whole Krewe and \u201ccrew\u201d aboard. I think we could easily haul everyone we trust in New Haven and still have no problems with enough space. Once we put out to sea, Rose was all business, like usual. She took the concrete-encased lock box with Alonia\u2019s pendant, summoned her Tear-Stained Veils, then dove off the starboard. While she was gone, Nightshade and Karen explored the boat together. I decided I probably didn\u2019t want to follow too close. We had gotten kinda worried about 15 minutes of not seeing Rose, even though we know she can breath underwater. I was about to jump in with my knife to make sure she didn\u2019t get stuck on or attacked by anything. But after about a half hour, Rose broke the surface. She was absolutely beaming as she climbed the rope ladder. She apologized to me when I asked her if she had any problems getting back up. At first she made some comment about the octopus being scary, but when Ronin started laughing I realized she was trying to make a Goonies joke. Apparently she just sat on the ocean floor and meditated for a while.<br /> <br /> With that she went to take a shower in one of the SIX staterooms and we got the ship ready for an impromptu party. Nightshade told us after Rose got back that she was going to summon a familiar soon. I didn\u2019t realize it but she has working with low magic as well. I think she probably did it to start with because it sounded good to be a witch. But now she\u2019s learned how to draw a spirit of Hecate to her as an aid, likely in the form of a cat. She wanted everyone to be aware and make sure there wouldn\u2019t be an problems before she did it. I told her that I didn\u2019t care as long as it didn\u2019t cause problems with Xerxes. With that bit of \u201cbusiness\u201d out of the way, we had the good champagne and partied on the dance floor. That\u2019s right, this ship has a dance floor on the weather deck!<br /> <br /> We docked after 1900 Hours, so I suggested we get German take-out to save us time and not stress Cupcake for thinking up dinner. Over schnitzel and sp\u00e4tzle, we planned out how tomorrow will go. The way we are preparing, I will weaken his resistance like I did with Alonia, while Nightshade tries to bottle him. Then we\u2019ll help Rose get her ceremony ready before we pour him back out. Since Adolphe isn\u2019t as big on possession as Alonia was, we\u2019re expecting more straight forward fighting. I can\u2019t say I\u2019m upset at the chance to beat on DeCastro but I do have to remember that he is more dangerous in a one on one fight. But we\u2019ll have to see. Hopefully we can work this out as smoothly as we did Alonia. If not, then I\u2019ll probably find out first hand how much of a bad ass this monster really is. And of course, I\u2019ll have to close early again. But the fate of the city is worth it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Dairy<br /> </b><br /> Monday, July 26, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> Training with Jean went well this morning. He has kept up with his training quite diligently, though he did unconsciously revert to a couple of minor bad habits without my watchful guidance. He has a tendency to want to fight the water instead of moving with it, which makes him expend more energy, so we worked today on getting him in tune with the water again. I wonder if some tai chi would help him?<br /> <br /> After training, I retreated to my office to catch up on school email and voice mail since this is the first day I\u2019ve been back since my vacation, and while there, I got a call from Stanly, who wants to meet me at Lulu\u2019s at the normal time today. Apparently he needs my help with something, though I got the impression it was nothing too dire like the situation with Shatina. I haven\u2019t been to Lulu\u2019s since I returned from Taiwan, so it\u2019s time I dropped in anyway.<br /> <br /> Mongler also stopped by my office to inform me there had been another \u201cMen in Black\u201d siting, no doubt due to the events at Sansbury Hall. During the conversation, Anders came up. Mongler apparently discovered that Gwen is dating him, and he doesn\u2019t know Anders, but seemed a bit put off by his \u201cpreppie\u201d style. I assured Mongler that Anders was a good man who is considerate and caring and good for Gwen, and also that he\u2019s a sin-eater like me. I don\u2019t know if I improved Mongler\u2019s impression, but I think he appreciated my take on Anders.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 26, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I met Stanly at Lulu\u2019s, and apparently he wants my help shopping for some stylish clothing. You see, he has a date with another somewhat younger man named Adam (who I think is in thirties, while Stanly is in his early fifties). Adam is a talented floutist and a very sharp dresser, and Stanly wants to impress him. It has been awhile since Stanly\u2019s been on a date since his partner died, and he\u2019s a bit anxious to make a good impression.<br /> <br /> Naturally, I agreed to help. I suppose Stanly thought to ask me because I try to dress nicely as well, but I confess that I don\u2019t know much about dressing to impress for someone like Adam, so I asked if I might bring Natalie along. I\u2019m certain she knows exactly what would be good to wear in a situation like this.<br /> While I was out, Simon and Doc sealed Alonia\u2019s pendant in a small block of concrete, and Simon marked it with the family seal so that in the event someone does manage to dredge it up from the depths (something I\u2019ll try to prevent), it will hopefully be returned to us. Simon\u2019s gone to buy a boat so we can carry it offshore a distance, and we\u2019re just getting ready to go down the private docks to meet him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, July 26, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Simon didn\u2019t just buy a boat, he bought a huge luxury yacht! Quite frankly I\u2019m surprised we don\u2019t need a crew to pilot it! It\u2019s really far beyond what we need, and I told Simon that I hope he didn\u2019t spend too much of our krewe money on it, as it seems an unnecessary extravagance. It has a small dance hall in it! Why do we even need that?<br /> <br /> Still, I suppose I should just accept it. The rest of the krewe seemed thrilled with it. We even had a small party on it, with music played from a small DJ booth attached to the \u201cparty\u201d room that has the dance hall. I\u2019ll admit that I let the others\u2019 infectious excitement get the best of me and I even danced a bit when Simon played \u201cRock Lobster\u201d by the B-52s for me. It really was the most appropriate choice, since I\u2019d been at the bottom of the ocean just an hour earlier.<br /> <br /> Before our impromptu party, I was able to take the pendant, sealed in its concrete block, to the ocean floor. I donned the Tear-Stained Shroud and swam all the way to the bottom, which took about twenty or thirty minutes. With my intuition enhanced by the Primeval Oracle, I found a good place where I could sink the block deep in the silt of the ocean floor where it will hopefully never be found. I confess that the Drowned Bride and I felt a pang of guilt as we did so, since we remember being lost at the bottom of the ocean for many decades before she escaped the tomb of her sunken vessel. But now the ocean depths feel almost like home, and I lingered there in the almost lightless depth for about twenty minutes, just enjoying the tranquil sensation of peace.<br /> <br /> By the time I returned the to surface, the others had already explored the yacht (which Simon has appropriately named the <i>Saturnine Dreamer</i>). They asked if everything went okay, and I told them that \u201cthe octopus was very scary.\u201d They looked shocked for a moment until Gwen got the reference, which I only know because she explained it to me after we watched The Goonies a few months ago. Then she laughed and explained to the others, but I suppose my attempt at a joke failed. I\u2019m not really cut out for jokes.<br /> <br /> I showered in one of the cabins and then rejoined the others, and we spent the late afternoon just enjoying ourselves for a time. Though I did eventually dance a bit, and I\u2019m glad I did, I resisted at first. For one thing, it was a bit depressing realizing that I\u2019m the only member of the krewe without a paramour. It\u2019s not the first time I\u2019ve made that observation, but for some reason I couldn\u2019t just shrug it off and have fun at first. At least not until I got up and danced. And then, for once, I was able to let it all go and just enjoy myself.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad I have the krewe. They are my family.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Trouble in Africa<br /> </u><br /> Jean was quite worried this morning. Apparently there has been some sort of uprising in his home country, the Ivory Coast, and the military is occupying his hometown. The military of many places in Africa, including the Ivory Coast, has a history of violence against its people, so Jean\u2019s family might be in danger, and he\u2019s worried about them. I tried to comfort and encourage him, but what could I really say?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Something to Prove</u><br /> <br /> Stanly and I chatted about Natalie a bit over coffee. He thinks that some of her issues have to do with the fact that she\u2019s still trying to prove some things to herself, and that once she\u2019s done so, she\u2019ll get over it. I\u2019m not entirely sure what he meant, but I got the distinct impression that he had gone through a similar phase. I do think Natalie is insecure and confused, and that she\u2019ll be much better off if she can ever get over the lingering trauma of the bad choices she\u2019s made in her life. I still worry about the lack of parity in her relationship with Doc and Karen. She really does lavish much more affection on Karen than on Doc, even if she does visit Doc at work every day. Aside from those visits and our krewe duties, she and Karen are virtually inseparable. Doc seems to be content with it, but I still feel it\u2019s unfair to him, though largely unavoidable in a two-way relationship like they have. I used to think that she should focus her attention entirely on Doc, because he\u2019s good for her. But as time goes on and her preferences become clearer, I\u2019m not so sure. Maybe she should just dedicate herself to Karen (not that I approve of that relationship) and stop leading Doc on, freeing him up to find love with someone who can really return it without all of Natalie\u2019s issues. I don\u2019t think much would change between them. Doc already seems to be just a very close and supportive friend with benefits, and if they broke things off, I imagine all they would lose would be the \u201cbenefits\u201d part of the relationship.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> American Culture and Idioms</u><br /> <u><br /> -Back to the Future</u><br /> <br /> I described our plans for Alonia\u2019s pendant to Mongler, and he thought we should also douse it in radiation so that it would kill anyone who got too close. I realize he wasn\u2019t serious, but he also said that plutonium is harder to acquire than Michael J. Fox had led him to believe. I had no idea what he was talking about, and asked Gwen later. She explained that in the movie Back to the Future, starring Michael J. Fox, a scientist acquires plutonium quite handily from some terrorists. I\u2019m sure that Gwen will insist on showing me the movie now.<br /> <br /> <u>-Pinky and the Brain</u><br /> <br /> Gwen also explained to me an absolutely absurd-sounding cartoon involving a smart lab rat and a stupid lab rat who attempt to take over the world every night. I\u2019m not sure I understand the appeal, but Gwen seemed to get a kick out of it. I wonder which rat she identifies with more?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Natalie\u2019s Familiar</u><br /> <br /> Natalie is a practicing witch, much like Simon and Doc are studying ceremonial hedge magic. She told us that she\u2019s learned a new ritual which allows her to summon a familiar. I was a bit worried it would be a demonic entity of some sort, but she assures us it\u2019s no such thing. It\u2019s just a spirit in the shape of a cat. She\u2019ll be informing Mr. Malard of its arrival so that the werewolves are aware of the presence of a new spirit. I was a bit concerned about how it would get along with Fu, but Natalie says it won\u2019t cause any trouble.<br /> <br /> I hope it\u2019s a cute cat and not creepy-looking Halloween cat.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday, July 26th<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Sleep? Yea, nap is not gonna happen. Too keyed up. I guess I slept enough to survive the day.<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc!<br /> <br /> -Restless, what to do!<br /> <br /> -Visit your local library!<br /> <br /> -In your Mistress\u2019s case, \u201clocal\u201d means \u201cin her haunted mansion\u201d but you folks can make do ^_^<br /> <br /> -Reading reading.<br /> <br /> -Gwen is here too. Being very Gwen-like.<br /> <br /> -You can\u2019t cower the books, Gwen! ^_^<br /> <br /> -^_^<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is going to be witchy soon!<br /> <br /> -Research is done. Need to find some feet to play with.<br /> <br /> -Noms. ^_^<br /> <br /> -This is the life. Little girl coming up soon, Girlfriend\u2019s extremely kissable feet in my face and I was just told we all soon will meet on my friend\u2019s new yacht. Yes new yacht.<br /> <br /> -I think this means upgrading Simon from friend to good friend. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Also going shopping with Spooky and Stanly.<br /> <br /> -Wait Spooky and Stanly? I SMELL SITCOM.<br /> <br /> -Maybe not. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is on a boat!<br /> <br /> -Note to self. Being on a yacht is a turn on for my gloom cookie.<br /> <br /> -Second note to self. She owes me now. ^_^<br /> <br /> -I bet a certain namesake of mine might also enjoy this boat.<br /> <br /> -I may have to leave lady nom-y toes behind to save embarrassment. XD<br /> <br /> -(Just kidding sweetie XOXO)<br /> <br /> -XD<br /> <br /> -Watching Jasmine dive is nice.<br /> <br /> -Laying out on a boat with a drink is even better.<br /> <br /> -Egads! What will this do to my pallor?<br /> <br /> -I cannot get\u2026a tan. How awful!<br /> <br /> -The very idea!<br /> <br /> -Spooky is cheerful. That makes me happy.<br /> <br /> -Spooky also made a Goonies reference. That is almost scary.<br /> <br /> -I blame Gwen.<br /> <br /> -Spooky and I are the people from Islands. Others don\u2019t understand. Of course she was from a huge island compared to Ocracoke.<br /> <br /> -Ocracoke was a native word for tiny-ass island (not really ^_^)<br /> <br /> -Doc put on some neoswing for us.<br /> <br /> -\u2026After some B-52s for Spooky.<br /> <br /> -Rock Lobster is sort of a strange song.<br /> <br /> -Also, some Caravan Palace<br /> <br /> -Swing Bro, Brother Swing!<br /> <br /> -You can dance if you want to.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress needs boofy renfair cloths, a high looking blonde, and a midget.<br /> <br /> -Wait. No. Nothing like that.<br /> <br /> -Girlfriend is all smiles (she better be at this point ^_^)<br /> <br /> -Alas, we must return to land for din-dins.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is channeling her inner Bavarian Hausfrau.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is unsure how she would look in traditional Bavarian outfits, has no plans to discover.<br /> <br /> -Vlog soon then\u2026mischief! ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LIII</i><br /> <br /> That was kind of a strange session. A good session, mind, but odd. Kinda between big battles, our heroes elected to have a Yacht party. Some impromptu research on smart phones took place, and we kinda settled on a picture. Mostly just a lot of chatter. Not a bad session, though, because it is always fun when we can just settle in and play our characters.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add really, high roleplaying low rollplaying session.<br /> <br /> In interesting news, we are in the process of getting a map made of the most used area of the estate. I will be putting that up when I can\u2026.still some work to do. Jasmine\u2019s player\u2019s skills have been quite useful with it so far, actually, as have the sketches Simon\u2019s player has made working on it. I think getting it crystallized will be good\u2026I think in my Falkenstein campaign having the map of the house the lodge uses has been helpful, and this will be nice when/if we have another party hosting.<br /> <br /> Anyway, hope you enjoyed, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-th