<br /> Investigation 3<br /> Occult 1<br /> <br /> Athletics 1<br /> Brawl 3<br /> Larceny 2<br /> Stealth 1<br /> Survival 5 (Gardening)<br /> Weapons 2 (Knives)<br /> <br /> Empathy 3<br /> Expression 4<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 4<br /> Socialize 3<br /> Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> Resources 3<br /> <br /> Keystone (0) Meat Cleaver: Forgotten Threshold, Industrial, Phantasmal Keys, Intimidation Skill<br /> Deathmask (4) White Mask: Torn Threshold, Pyre-Flame Key, Firestarter Numina<br /> Charm (1) Nutcracker: Phantasmal Key<br /> <br /> Psyche 4<br /> Synergy 7<br /> Willpower 4<br /> Health 8<br /> <br /> Keys: Industrial Key, Phantasmal Key, Pyre-Flame Key<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Caul 5 Marionette 4 Oracle 5<br /> <br /> Ceremonies: (1) Finding;<br /> <br /> Weapon of Choice: Bowie Knife<br /> Wheels: Honda Accord<br /> Armor: None<br /> Defense: 3 Initiative: 6 Size: 5 Speed: 12<br /> <br /> Languages Spoken: English (3), French (2)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Comments or Questions welcome. Back to journals in a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:18:40-08:00","id":16332,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to see the end of this DeCastro business. It was a hard battle and not without sacrifice, but I will allow the Krewe the telling.<br /> <i><br /> Session LIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019 Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Tuesday, July 27, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation this morning took far longer than normal. When I was finally centered I had just enough time to get cleaned up, grab food and run out the door. I stopped short when I found Malard on the other side carrying his shotgun. I was not expecting that and almost choked on my toast. He apologized if he startled me and explained he was there to talk to my lady friend's familiar. That I understood and wished him a good day as I ran for the cab. The cabbie was really not sure what to think, but I told him everything was fine. Eccentric neighbor. I was kinda surprised he bought that but whatever. Obfuscation via truth seems to work for me more than most.<br /> <br /> I put a sign on the door that I\u2019d be closing early today and zipped around getting everything together. One of my usual customers asked if I was okay. Said he was a little concerned with all the schedule changes he\u2019d seen lately. I thanked him for noticing but assured him I was fine. I\u2019m really going to have to talk to people about hiring some folks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1530 Hours, Tuesday, July 27, 2010<br /> <br /> I came home around 1500 Hours to find Karen carrying a cat around. Not Fu, but a grown cat. I was then introduced to Elpheba, Nightshade\u2019s new familiar. Rose came to the armory as I was deciding what I might need to talk with me. She rather uncomfortably carried Stanton Marshall\u2019s rifle. The refinished stock shimmered even in that light and I knew the charm was ready. The others are preparing too. Hopefully, I\u2019ll have a new entry in a few hours.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2045 Hours, Tuesday, July 27, 2010<br /> <br /> Well we all made it back, though Nightshade and Cupcake weren\u2019t completely in one piece. Not that I was, but I\u2019m not worried about putting me back together right now. I\u2019m getting way ahead again.<br /> <br /> We must of looked like a freak show when we got to the Firehouse. Rose wore Bonnie Lynn\u2019s wedding dress, I had my Blood Diamond bullet and the rifle (I really have to think of a name for that), Ronin had her hat; basically we all came packing mementos. The windows of the basement had frost on them and the ones upstairs was fogged up a little, so we knew something was up. Nightshade cast her Boneyard and found Adolphe very quickly, though she noted we weren\u2019t going to like this. Whatever he was doing called a cold wind inside and everything very cold, the frost would be tricky for moving. With that in mind, we prepared before entering the basement. Cupcake wisely used her caul to widen her feet. She didn\u2019t really care about the frosty floors after that.<br /> <br /> Adolphe was just a big black morass in the shape of a cloak with glowing eyes and a goatee when we came down. I wanted to make some joke about having his cloak put away, but given I looked like the Mask of the Red Death and the misogynistic bastard never learned how to respect women, he attacked me first thing. This huge black pincer claw shot out of the blackness; the claw had mandibles and mouths in the middle. It grabbed me and held me up off the ground. I couldn\u2019t fight my way out because I couldn\u2019t pull my arms out of the claw. Nightshade immediately got started casting the bottle ceremony, but he trapped her the same way. Rose pounced on Adolphe at the point and held him away from us. I think he may have hit her with some of his nastiness too, but she was too proud to say anything. Cupcake ripped Nightshade\u2019s claw to pieces so she could go back to the ceremony. Ronin shot at mine but it must have glanced off the carapace. I was just stuck and really pissed that I was useless. Nightshade trapped him in the bottle pretty quickly after that though and the arm holding me vanished.<br /> <br /> We unlocked the box and took the gun case outside where it wasn\u2019t so cold. We decided to wait about an hour for our magic wounds to go away and plan a little more. Ronin also called Anders in for more backup. No one really said anything but when she said it, we all looked around at each other and knew. Ronin was scared. And that fact made us all a little more terrified than we might have been before. The new plan, after we were all together and healed up, would be for Nightshade to hide and drain Adolphe\u2019s essence through her Boneyard while Rose does her ceremony invisibly. Cupcake and I would keep him busy in general, which would likely cost us, but we were prepared for that. Then we revised it slightly with Snowflake making an illusion of Rose casting the ritual to distract Adolphe that much more. Anders would be striking terror into his ghostly heart (which I don\u2019t believe he ever had), and then Nightshade would drain his essence and try to control him. With that agreed, we all geared up in our own way. If I were to make a proper military reference to this, it would have looked like a SEAL team moving in with no backup coming. We brought the big guns to start with this time. Anders changed into what I can only say looked like a huge tribal Tikki Lion. I let my body fall away, then shrouded the Dog of War in the Stigmata armor. Cupcake grew more arms and was no longer the cute, perky pastry chef. Nightshade and my body stayed in the car, then we were set.<br /> <br /> Ronin broke the seal on the wine bottle and out popped a very pissed Adolphe. He immediately sent a claw at what we could only guess was Snowflake\u2019s illusion of Rose. Anders roared at the ghost and his eyes got really big. Ronin leveled her Stare of the Hell Worse than Death and you could sense the unseen, gut-wrenching fear slam into the ghost. Because we couldn\u2019t attack him very much, I encouraged the illusion of Rose being trapped by slicing open the claw. Cupcake used all the distractions to slip up behind Adolphe and grab him. The ghost was not happy and blasted her with... something. To me it looked like black flames, while Rose said later she thought it was boiling blood and bone spikes. Anders finished breaking the claw right before Cupcake proved she was made of more than frosting by throwing Adolphe\u2019s face in the dirt and holding him there. Anders and I ran over to help if she needed it, but really when you\u2019ve pissed off Cupcake, you\u2019ve made a mistake. Though we couldn\u2019t see it, I know Nightshade was removing anything she could as the fight continued. Unfortunately as an act of desperation, Adolphe blasted Cupcake again and left her smoking that time, but she never let go. And just like that the real Rose appeared. I don\u2019t care if I\u2019m a terrible person, the look of horror on his face as the pistols pulled his corpus into them made me smile. Then I looked around and realized Cupcake really was in bad shape. When I got to her, she was delusional from pain. I carried her back to the car and found Nightshade bloody again from all she had done to Adolphe. Strangely Rose was completely unscathed. We loaded up and got back home quickly.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve healed both of them a little because I didn\u2019t want to tap myself out. I think I can heal them holistically from here and they\u2019ll be okay. As they were stabilized, we started talking about the guns. I knew Snowflake wanted them so he could hold power over Adolphe. While I thought that was true justice, it also make it a little too easy for an accident to happen. Rose, of course, wanted them on the bottom of the ocean. Eventually someone realized I was remaining quiet and asked me directly. I was hoping they\u2019d forgot to ask what I thought. I told them, after hearing the other options and thinking on it, it would be best to use the construction we\u2019re planning for the backyard as a cover. Make a sealed concrete chamber under a statue or other structure so the entire chamber is underground. Then we can keep the gun case in the chamber. If we need them, Rose can use her powers to retrieve them. This was tweaked for a gazebo, but in general it was acceptable to everyone.<br /> <br /> After that, I went back to the Armory. I needed to talk to the Dog. We\u2019d helped Ronin learn the Rage manifestation before. Now I felt it was time to do the same. I spent some time alone, channeling the anger I felt from various points in my life until I could feel it, almost like a phantom weapon, firmly in my hands. I plan to spend some time out by the fireplace soon as well. It\u2019s all well and good that I can protect myself from harm and make myself stronger, but now it\u2019s time to create a different kind of weapon. One I don\u2019t need to carry...and no one can take away from me.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, July 27, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> I meditated and then went to train with Jean this morning as usual. My meditations helped to quiet the anxiety I feel over our upcoming attempt to imprison Adolphe. Alonia might have been more insidious with her ability to possess people, but I think Adolphe will be more physically dangerous, and we have no idea what kinds of powers are at his disposal.<br /> <br /> There is still no word from Jean\u2019s family. I hope they are okay.<br /> <br /> On my way out to campus, I crossed paths with Mr. Malard, who was coming to visit and looked very serious. He was carrying a shotgun. I realized that he was coming to investigate Natalie\u2019s cat familiar, but I feared he might try to kill it. But as we said our good mornings to each other, he assured me that he was just going to have a chat with spirit to make sure it didn\u2019t even think of starting any trouble. I do hope he doesn\u2019t frighten it too much.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve just returned home. As soon as Doc arrives, we\u2019ll go to the firehouse church and deal with Adolphe.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, July 27, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> What a tremendous relief! We\u2019ve sealed Adolphe away into his pistols. I was not easy, and we suffered for our efforts, but we were victorious and now, hopefully, we will have some time to rest and recover.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at the church, Natalie dropped into a trance and used the Boneyard to locate Adolphe in the basement of the church. We went in to face him, and Simon took over the Boneyard so that Natalie could perform the ritual to trap Adolphe in a bottle, like she had done with Alonia, so that he could not interfere as I created the ritual spiral that would allow me to trap him in his anchors. I was clad in Bonnie-Lynn\u2019s wedding dress, which largely blended with the tattered veils of the Drowned Bride when I possessed her to deal with Adolphe.<br /> <br /> The church was buffeted by a fiercely cold wind that was a bit jarring in July, and the interior of the church, especially the basement, was freezing cold. It was so cold that had we stayed too long, it would have been dangerous. Adolphe was waiting for us, shrouded in mist and shadow, and as we emerged into the basement, he furiously attacked. The magic that cloaked him erupted into biting tentacles of smoky darkness, and one lashed out at Doc, crushing him in a toothy maw. Doc roared in anger as he struggled against the tentacle while Simon used some sort of curse to sap Adolphe\u2019s will.<br /> <br /> Gwen immediately tried to help Doc, shooting at the tentacle but with little effect. Meanwhile, Alexia and I both dashed across the frost-slick floor to try and grab Adolphe. We hoped that we could immobilize him in such a way that he wouldn\u2019t be able to continue attacking us. But as we neared him, another of his black tentacles struck Natalie, interrupting her ceremony and wounding her. Alexia (who was possessing her own geist) bravely said she would help Natalie, so she struck at the tentacles with her knives and quickly destroyed it, freeing Natalie so that she could complete her work.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, I managed to slip behind Adolphe and quickly immobilized him, forcing him face first to floor so that he could not see my companions to attack them. The cloak of black mist that surrounded him was freezing cold, and my Primeval shroud provided little protection, though enough for me to shrug off the chill in order to maintain my hold. Then Adolphe\u2019s body erupted in bony spines and boiling blood, which pierced and seared my flesh. Fortunately, I was able to ignore much of the pain and maintain my grip.<br /> <br /> Natalie did her work quickly and well, and suddenly, Adolphe was sucked from my grasp and into the bottle. Doc and Natalie were injured, and I had exerted a more energy than was really necessary in preparing for the fight. Natalie tremulously suggest that we should finish dealing with Adolphe later once we had a chance to recover a bit, but I was not willing to put it off until later. We came to the church to deal with Adolphe one and for all, and that is what I intended to do. So I insisted that we stay and finish what we had started.<br /> <br /> We spent an hour recovering. Doc patched up what wounds we could not buffer with plasm while Gwen retrieved the pistols from the safe in the church basement. I drew a large binding spiral on the church grounds. Gwen decided we needed more backup, so she called Anders to come and help.<br /> <br /> I realized that it would be all too easy for Adolphe to interrupt my attempts to bind him, at least until he was immobilized, so we discussed our options. Alexia volunteered to grab and hold Adolphe to prevent him from striking back at us, but the spines and gore with which he had attacked before meant that she could only do so for so long, unless Adolphe\u2019s spiritual essence was depleted. So Simon and Natalie planned to use their powers to steal his will and his essence. Doc, Anders, and Gwen would help to weaken him with Rage, Phantasm, and Stigmata. And it was agreed that I would perform the ritual while cloaked in the Shroud of Stillness so that Adolphe would be unable to see me and therefore unable to interrupt my ceremony. Simon would assist in the deception by creating an illusion of me as a decoy.<br /> <br /> Our plan worked well. Gwen broke the bottle, freeing Adolphe, who immediately lashed out at Simon\u2019s illusion while I remained safely hidden. The combined efforts of my krewe-mates quickly weakened Adolphe. Natalie spilled her own blood to drain his essence. Alexia deftly grabbed Adolphe, holding him fast and forcing his face to the ground so that he could not see to attack anyone else. But he was still dangerous, and before his essence was completely depleted, he unleashed a fury of bone and blood that burned and tore through Alexia\u2019s flesh. Yet she held on and prevented him from escaping.<br /> <br /> The practice I had dealing with Alonia was very instructive, so this time I finished the ritual in just fifteen minutes. Adolphe shrieked in anger as he was trapped in his pistols, a just fate for someone who had bound so many others in the past. Doc rushed to Natalie as she swayed and nearly collapsed from blood loss. I rushed to Alexia, who, despite her injuries and pain, smiled brightly, almost deliriously really, and simply said, \u201cI did it!\u201d<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve returned home now. Doc has treated Natalie and Alexia\u2019s wounds, though they\u2019ll still need some time off to recover. But it is a huge relief to be rid of Adolphe and Alonia, and I know I will sleep more easily tonight knowing they are sealed away.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes<br /> </u><br /> <u>The Pistols</u><br /> <br /> We\u2019ve placed the pistols in a safe for now. We had a long discussion about what to do with them. I wanted to sink them into the ocean floor and let them remain there, as we did with Alonia\u2019s pendant, but Simon wants to keep and use them. They grant access to a ghostly numina that allows one to strike enemies from afar, and the utility of such a thing in a fight appealed to Simon. But I think there is more to it than that. I think he liked the idea of having at item of power like that, and of controlling Adolphe. I suppose it only makes sense. He and his geist represent Authority in our krewe\u2019s mythos. I don\u2019t like it, and neither did Gwen or Alexia, but we eventually relented and decided to keep the pistols, but only if they could be sealed away somewhere that only we could get them. After all, we can\u2019t have Simon\u2019s family, and especially not Tzipporah, getting their hands on them.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019ve decided to construct a sealed vault with no entrances, and to place the pistols in that vault, buried in the cemetery. I will still be able to retrieve them when we need them, since I can pass through walls. But they should be safe there from others.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -FUCK!<br /> <br /> -Witchy got a kitty!<br /> <br /> -Malard is an odd duck. Or should I say wolf?<br /> <br /> -Vlog up!<br /> <br /> -Yesterday was awesome. Was told my daughter could come up, Went to lunch with Doc, did witchy research, nom\u2019d all the toes, got invited shopping with a dapper gay fellow, went to a yacht party, got laid something serious.<br /> <br /> -So how are you gonna compare to that TODAY? You up for this?<br /> <br /> -Got kitteh, that helps.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress has a Kitteh! Her coat is black and her name is Elphaba.<br /> <br /> -Kitteh seems to already be hanging out with my girlfriend. :-/<br /> <br /> -Gettin\u2019 ready for adventure!<br /> <br /> -Radio silence till time done with doom.<br /> <br /> -Have ouch, need sleepy.<br /> <br /> -Man Alexia is loopy.<br /> <br /> -Kitteh is annoyed.<br /> <br /> -Granted in less then 24 hours since arrival Elphaba has been menaced by a werewolf with a shotgun and had her master critically wound herself partially through self inflicted injury. A little annoyance is understandable.<br /> <br /> -Less sore, thanks to superman.<br /> <br /> -Trying to decide what to do with evil artifact.<br /> <br /> -Evil artifact is evil.<br /> <br /> -Aren\u2019t Gwen and her boyfriend cute!<br /> <br /> -Sorry can\u2019t discuss specifics due to possible evil hackers. Evil artifact is gonna be gone very shortly.<br /> <br /> -Man I am a tired Gloom Cookie. I have a bite out of me and everything.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> End Session LIV </i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add, the session was mostly either combat, setting up for combat, or recovering from combat.<br /> <br /> The DeCastros were crazy powerful for ghosts, but if you want to challenge Sin-Eaters with ghosts that\u2019s what you have to do. Non-ghosts have an easier row to hoe since they can\u2019t be shut down out of hand so easily. Not a complaint, mind, but a note for anyone using the system.<br /> <br /> Natalie picked up a Familiar as per Hedge Witch.<br /> <br /> That covers it I think...comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:20:50-08:00","id":16333,"title":"","content":"Here is your off-week post. Jasmine\u2019s player saw some of our Krewe stated two weeks ago, and decided to transfer her stats to an email for me to put up, so I have them for you. This is as of the end of Session 55. Natalie\u2019s updated, as so as long as I was putting Jasmine\u2019s up I figured I would put her update up too, and copypasta is easy.<br /> <br /> Here you go.<br /> <br /> Xiao Ming \u201cJasmine\u201d Sung<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Jasmine Sung (Chinese name: Sung Xiao Ming)<br /> Sin-Eater<br /> Geist: The Drowned Bride<br /> Threshold: The Silent<br /> Archetype: Mourner<br /> Concept: Mourning Bride in search of True Love<br /> <br /> Virtue: Prudence<br /> Vice: Lust<br /> <br /> POB Taipei, Taiwan<br /> DOB: April 4, 1984 (<a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tomb_Sweeping_Day\" target=\"_blank\">Tomb Sweeping Day in Taiwan</a>)<br /> RIP: March 9, 2009<br /> Height: 5'5\u201d<br /> Eyes: Dark Brown (Black)<br /> Hair: Black<br /> Aliases: Spooky (Natalie's nickname for her); Rose (Doc's callsign for her)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 2<br /> Wits 4<br /> Resolve 5<br /> <br /> Strength 3<br /> Dexterity 4<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Presence 1<br /> Manipulation 2<br /> Composure 5<br /> <br /> Academics 2<br /> Crafts 1<br /> Investigation 1 (+2 from pledge to Mongler)<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 4<br /> <br /> Athletics 4 (Swimming)<br /> Brawl 3 (Tai Chi)<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Stealth 4<br /> Survival 2<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 3<br /> Empathy 3<br /> Expression 1 (Poetry)<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 1<br /> Socialize 1<br /> <br /> <br /> Resources 1<br /> Fame 1 (Olympic Swimmer)<br /> Intractable (3-dot merit; may add Resolve or Composure to Social roll once per session)<br /> Death-Touched (5-dot version; +2 to interact with ghosts in a non-confrontational manner)<br /> Striking Looks (2-dot version)<br /> <br /> Keystone (0) Drowned Bride's Locket: Prey Threshold, Cold Wind, Tear-Stained Keys, Expression Skill<br /> Vanitas (2) Lost Love Poem<br /> Charms (1 each): The Silent Doll (Stillness), Loop Earring Charm (Cold Wind), Bonnie-Lynn's Wedding Dress (Tear-Stained), Jade Prayer Beads (Primeval), Oval Gem Necklace (Stillness)<br /> <br /> Psyche 4<br /> Synergy 9<br /> Willpower 10<br /> Health 9<br /> <br /> Keys: Cold Wind, Tear-Stained, Stillness, Primeval, Phantasmal<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Caul 5, Oracle 2, Shroud 5<br /> <br /> Ceremonies: (1) Krewe Binding, Finding, Pass On, One Last Song; (3) Dedicate Charm, Moment of Absolution; (4) Bind Anchor; (5) Fetter's Binding<br /> <br /> Weapon of Choice: Martial Arts / Primeval Shroud Claws<br /> Armor: Shroud Manifestation<br /> Wheels: Charcoal Gray 2008 Volkswagen Beetle<br /> Defense: 4 - Initiative: 9 - Size: 5 - Speed: 12<br /> <br /> Languages Spoken: Mandarin Chinese (3), English (2)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Natalie Knight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> Natalie Caroline Knight<br /> Sin-Eater<br /> Geist: The Laughing Lady<br /> Threshold: The Silent<br /> Archetype: Necromancer<br /> Concept: Mistress of the Dead<br /> <br /> Virtue: Hope<br /> Vice: Lust<br /> <br /> POB Ocracoke Island, North Carolina, United States<br /> DOB: October 27, 1980<br /> RIP: January 1, 2008<br /> Height: 5\u20194\u201d<br /> Weight: 130lbs.<br /> Eyes: Blue (Left) Green (Right), sometimes Gold (from contacts)<br /> Hair: Black (dyed Black)<br /> Aliases: Natalie, Mistress of the Dead; Chastity Alison Lousler (her old name), Evelyn Ampersand, Nightshade (Doc\u2019s Callsign for her)<br /> Tattoos: Silent style scales on lower back, Scorpio scorpion on her left hip (just peeking above skirt line) Chinese number 4 on upper right leg (just below skirt line)<br /> <br /> Intelligence 3<br /> Wits 3<br /> Resolve 4<br /> <br /> Strength 2<br /> Dexterity 3<br /> Stamina 2<br /> <br /> Presence 4<br /> Manipulation 4<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Academics 2 (Music)<br /> Computer 2 (Social Networking)<br /> Investigation 1<br /> Medicine 1<br /> Occult 4<br /> Politics 1<br /> Science 2<br /> <br /> Athletics 2<br /> Firearms 1<br /> Larceny 1<br /> Stealth 1<br /> <br /> Empathy 2<br /> Expression 3 (Piano)<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 4 (Seduction)<br /> Socialize 3 (Parties)<br /> Streetwise 1<br /> Subterfuge 2<br /> <br /> Fame 2<br /> Resources 2<br /> Striking Looks (2)<br /> Krewe Fate 4<br /> <br /> Fighting Style: Social Maneuvers 4 (Sugar Lips, Honey Tongue; Stick and Move; New Approach; Chip Away<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Low Magic: Hedge Witch<br /> Enchantment (4)<br /> Familiar (4)<br /> See Spirits (2)<br /> <br /> Keystone (0) Compact: Silent Threshold, Stigmata, Stillness Keys, Socialize Skill<br /> Deathmask (4) Corset Mask: Stricken Threshold, Phantasm Key, Phantasm Numina<br /> Vanitas (2) Piano Piece<br /> Charm (1) Music Box: Cold Wind Key<br /> <br /> Psyche 4<br /> Synergy 6<br /> Willpower 7<br /> Health 7<br /> <br /> Keys: Cold Wind Key, Grave-Dirt Key, Stigmata Key, Stillness Key<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Boneyard 5 Marionette 5 Oracle 3<br /> <br /> Ceremonies: (1) Cigarette Dawn, Speaker of the Dead; (2) Faces in the Smoke; (3) Lemure\u2019s Lure; (4) Warding the Household; (5) Crash the Gates, Fetter\u2019s Binding, Sepulchral Gateway, Spectral Captivity;<br /> <br /> Fighting Style: Social Maneuvers<br /> <br /> Weapon of Choice: Colt M1911 Pistol \u201cNatalie Bane\u201d<br /> Armor: None, or Reinforced Clothing<br /> Wheels: Refurbished Black 1980 Cadillac El Dorado<br /> Defense: 3 Initiative: 6 Size: 5 Speed: 10<br /> <br /> Languages Spoken: English (3), German (2)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Note the Intractable Merit is from Danse Macabre (her player has a Requiem game going on right now so was familiar with the merit. Ours is the non-Social Combat version. Comments and Questions welcome as always, next journals in a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:23:16-08:00","id":16334,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a special playing with dolls edition of Balance of Shadows. Well, a doll anyway. Come, let us learn what the hell I am talking about together.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Wednesday, July 28, 2010<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think getting in touch with my inner Sith Lord is conducive to proper meditation. It took something like an hour and a half to get centered this morning. Which of course meant that I was running late yet again. I got in on time but just barely. I got the lights on and register unlocked when the first customer came in.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been running around since and I just got a chance to stop. I\u2019m not trying to complain about my responsibilities, but I am beginning to notice how it seems like I\u2019m working at least two full time jobs. Three if you count, and I get back to it, the Night Watch. I realize taking a break for a while after Sainsbury Hall is probably a good idea given the police chief was aware of me, but it feels like I\u2019m abandoning my duties. And it\u2019s not like I can call anything I do a thankless job. The people I keep healthy, the ghosts we help move on and/or the people we keep from being haunted, and those I rescue on the streets are all damn thankful.<br /> <br /> <i>You hold yourself to a standard far above that of any other, Sadeeq. Your tribe is right to wish for you to find assistance. How can you fight if you cannot stand? The greatest of rulers have all had advisers and servants. Follow their noble example. And recall that even the dead must rest.</i><br /> <br /> There\u2019s something irrefutable about perspective from within. Maybe I can look at calling some of the prospects this weekend. For now, I\u2019m going to make sure I\u2019m ready for Nightshade to get here with lunch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1645 Hours, Wednesday, July 28, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade came in and we spent lunch together like usual. It helped me relax a little bit. She\u2019s still working on the 27 Club and getting excited about having Bella Donna come up. Lots of things that I\u2019d be able to be a part of if I had help around the shop.<br /> <br /> When she left, I immediately reached for my sketch pad. I drew for the rest of the day, in-between customers, anyway. It was a pretty calm and stress free day. I needed that. And then the text message came. Nightshade sent me a message that means something very bad has happened.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen you get home, it is NOT my fault. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0410 Hours, Thursday, July 29, 2010<br /> <br /> I came home expecting ...well I don\u2019t know what I was expecting. I looked around for everyone but only found Tavia in the kitchen at first. She said that Snowflake and Ronin were out back in the gazebo. As I didn\u2019t know we had a gazebo, this was a little weird. When I walked out, I saw what Tavia meant, but I still couldn\u2019t understand what Nightshade\u2019s text meant.<br /> <br /> The gazebo was pretty big; looked like we could have a barbecue for everyone and still be comfortable. Snowflake was sipping tea and Ronin had a beer while they relaxed in the shade. They told me to go ahead and get a beer, then come back out. When I got back out and sat down, I got to hear all about the doll. This was what Nightshade texted me about. The short version is that Rose made peace with the bloodthirsty little washcloth and now Lily (don\u2019t ask me where they get a name like that for a mutated spirit summoned from beyond Twilight) is staying with us. Apparently Cupcake made cookies so she and Rose could go talk to Malard about adopting another spirit. He even told them the Azlu, a type of powerful spider spirit, part of the doll could infest an area quickly. They could get so powerful that any ghosts in Twilight basically went on the menu. But Rose made Lily promise not to lay any eggs. I was so pissed off I didn\u2019t know what to do. Figured the best thing for me was to finish my beer and take a few deep breaths. I was trying to be calm about things as I don\u2019t trust this thing as far as Tavia can throw a boulder. But since Rose apparently considers Lily someone we\u2019ve rescued from the DeCastros, I\u2019m willing to give her a chance. Now if she screws up, I\u2019ll happily tear her dolly ass to shreds and wait for whatever pops out in Twilight. I also thought I should go talk to her once I was a little more together.<br /> <br /> Snowflake told me she would be up in Rose\u2019s room. Sure enough, the door was cracked when I knocked and I could see the doll kicking her legs on the edge of the bed. She waved at me when I opened the door. I told her that we needed to talk and she nodded as if it was all very normal. But I took her down to the Armory as it felt weird staying in Rose\u2019s room without her there. To make myself feel better, I told Lily I thought it would be a fair trade for her to watch out for anything in Twilight around the house. Since she can basically feast on all the femininity essence our Krewe plus must produce, this seemed like an even trade to me. Lily nodded her agreement then left me to think about how I\u2019d just damned us all. I walked back out to the gazebo and talked to Karen, Ronin, and Snowflake. I think I was a little too hung up on things. I really kinda hammered on Ronin for being \u2026 well not feminine. It went too far before I really understood and now I think Ronin is upset. Like, I might have actually hurt her feelings. Yeah I\u2019d say I didn\u2019t think that was possible, but that\u2019s kinda the way I got into this. <br /> <br /> Rose, Cupcake, and Nightshade came home from shopping with Stanley a little late to make dinner and with Ronin partly on the warpath, Tavia ordered pizza to help ease the tension. After dinner, I took Nightshade and Cupcake back to their rooms and helped each of them with their remaining wounds. I expect they will both show improvement tomorrow. After that, it was about 2100 Hours so I slipped out to the big fireplace/oven/crematorium in the backyard. I stayed in front of the fire til just a little bit ago. The Pyre-Flame Key is almost mine. But during all the time, I did alot of thinking. I realized I\u2019ll need to do something to apologize to Ronin. And I\u2019ll have to remember to pay more attention and not let myself get so caught up in everything.<br /> <br /> Lily has wandered past my door at least twice while I\u2019ve been writing this. Having seen at least the first two Puppet Master movies, that creeped me right the fuck out. But now I\u2019m tired so I\u2019m going to lock my door and go to sleep.<br /> <br /> Damn it.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 28, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> Meditation was extremely good this morning. I felt very centered afterward. Liberated, almost.<br /> <br /> Training with Jean went well, though I\u2019m sad to report that he has still had no word from his family. I do hope they are all right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 28, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> When I returned home after training this morning, I decided it was time to free the doll from the trunk of Simon\u2019s car, and see what it planned to do now that Adolphe\u2019s grasp over it has been released. We would also need to take it by to see Mr. Malard so that he could give it his blessing. Alexia had baked a tin of cookies just for that purposes, and she joined me as I opened the trunk.<br /> <br /> The doll leapt at me again, and I caught it, as usual, then sternly informed it that there was no call for that anymore, because Adolphe had been sealed away. The doll abruptly ceased struggled and hung contentedly in my hand then, so Alexia and I asked what it wanted to do now. Did it want to go back to the spirit world, or stay around in the doll? In response, it shrugged, but it gave the distinct impression it would rather stay in the doll, if only because that would allow it to remain in the \u201creal\u201d world instead of Twilight.<br /> <br /> I confess that I\u2019ve grown to feel a bit of responsibility toward the doll and its spirit, so I wasn\u2019t entirely displeased that it wished to stay. Still, we had to get Mr. Malard\u2019s blessing on it, so we headed to his house with the doll.<br /> <br /> Mr. Malard was a bit grumpy about the arrival of a second spirit (we had to assure him that Natalie\u2019s familiar, Elphaba, wasn\u2019t responsible). He seemed troubled when he examined the doll, and took it aside to talk to it privately. When he returned, he told us that it was a unique spirit, but a potentially dangerous one. It was a fusion of a spirit of femininity and a voraciously predatory spider-like spirit known as an azlu. Azlu can be quite dangerous, but Mr. Malard felt that the spirit in the doll might less feral and therefore less prone to causing trouble than a true azlu. He said that if the femininity spirit part of it is more dominant, then it might behave itself just fine if it can soak up the essence of femininity on a regular basis. And with people like me, Alexia and Natalie around, that shouldn\u2019t be a problem. Furthermore, there\u2019s only so much she can do while she inhabits the doll body.<br /> <br /> Alexia and I returned to the mansion and discussed our findings with Gwen, Natalie, and Simon (Doc was at work). Gwen was opposed to keeping the thing around, but relented a bit when I explained that I\u2019d made a promise to help the doll free itself from Adolphe\u2019s clutches and therefore felt a sense of responsibility toward it. That said, I was quite willing to send it back to the spirit world if necessary, and if that is what the krewe decided. I don\u2019t want to endanger anyone unnecessarily.<br /> <br /> Still, we think the femininity aspect of the doll is far more dominant and should be content to live off the femininity around Dark Haven Bluffs. That\u2019s good, because I\u2019m starting to become attached to the doll, which is quite charming now that it\u2019s not trying to attack me all the time. Alexia and I decided to call her Lily, and she\u2019s very adorable. She seems to like it when I baby her a bit. I suspect that she\u2019s encouraging the motherly side of my feminine nature so that she can soak up the essence.<br /> <br /> Once we decided to keep her, I told Lily the rules. She could go anywhere she liked in the house, as long as she was respectful toward others and didn\u2019t mess with anything that looked dangerous or that was obviously off-limits, and she could go outside with supervision (but we don\u2019t want her roaming around drawing attention by herself). And she is not, under any circumstance, the attempt to lay eggs or reproduce. She was not happy about the last rule, but she accepted it as the trade off for a caring and comfortable home.<br /> <br /> Lily will be staying in my room when she wishes to rest. I\u2019ll need to arrange some sort of place for her there, perhaps in one of the closets.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 28, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Natalie, Alexia and I went out to help Stanly shop for clothes for his date with Adam. After the stress of getting Lily settled in, it was refreshing to go out for a bit. I\u2019m glad I asked Natalie and Alexia to come. I felt out of my depth, really, and I fear I would have been boring company for Stanly. He spent most of the time chatting with Alexia and Natalie, trying to get the details on their relationships. He\u2019s such a gossip! I was fairly quiet, I suppose. It\u2019s odd how I revert to my shy and reclusive inner self in normal social situations like that. I\u2019m much better with the dead. I don\u2019t even feel like I was much help in picking out clothes, though I do think my conservative input kept the others in check a bit.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I had fun doing something \u201cnormal\u201d with Natalie and Alexia for a change. And I think we helped bolster Stanly\u2019s confidence. I do hope his date goes well for him. Like me, we\u2019ve both lost someone very precious to us, so more than anyone, I think I can identify with how much this means to him and what a big step it is for him to take. I wish I could have expressed that to him, but I think he knows.<br /> <br /> We went on to have a delightful dinner at a nice restaurant. Then we bid Stanly good night and headed home. When we arrived home, the krewe gathered to discuss Lily. Doc was taking it better than I thought he might. He wasn\u2019t happy at all, but he apparently made a deal with Lily. She\u2019s supposed to help keep an eye on the house for us (specifically what\u2019s going on in Twilight) in exchange for a home. While we discussed it, she was still running about the house, and would occasionally peer around the kitchen door and wave at me. It was so cute!<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Lily</u><br /> <br /> According to Mr. Malard and Simon, Lily is half femininity spirit and half azlu. The azlu are a dangerous pestilence in the spirit world. They are spider-like spirits that consume other spirits, and they have an aspect of fertility that encourages them to reproduce quickly, laying clusters of eggs throughout any territory they have claimed as their own. The more spirits they eat, the bigger and more fearsome they become, and they can control vast colonies of their young. They are also hard to kill, for unless they are attacked with something like fire that will saturate an entire area, attacking them only causes them to split into many smaller azlu, which try to escape to propagate elsewhere.<br /> <br /> The fact that Lily is half azlu is disturbing and a bit scary, and I don\u2019t think any of us are comfortable with that, least of all Doc and Gwen. Simon seemed interested in using Lily as a weapon by making her lay eggs in the home of an enemy! He frightens me sometimes.<br /> <br /> The femininity spirit part of her is like any other normal type of spirit, encouraging and feeding off of the behavior it represents. She can apparently make herself appear to be the perfect woman in order to attract lovers, which could be bad if she finds a way to use that power to reproduce.<br /> <br /> We will have to keep an eye on Lily. I hope she doesn\u2019t misbehave, because if she does, we will have to destroy her. Fortunately, she shouldn\u2019t be able to reproduce as long as she is bound into the doll, unless she somehow entices someone to\u2026make love to the doll. Which would be disgusting. If she were freed from the doll, that would be another matter entirely, but hopefully that won\u2019t be a problem.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Tomboy</u><br /> <br /> Poor Gwen. All the talk about femininity today led to some rather insensitive remarks toward her. Even I called her a tomboy, and therefore not the best example of femininity in the household. I didn\u2019t mean anything by it. I didn\u2019t think she would mind, because she seems to flaunt the fact that she doesn\u2019t care for most \u201cfeminine\u201d things all that much. But I think she was offended anyway. Doc was positively unkind when he made a remark on the masculinity of her character. As if to make a point, Gwen started behaving in a far more masculine way than usual, but I\u2019m not sure that really helped her case.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Vault</u><br /> <br /> Simon and Gwen built a frame for the sealed vault in which we will store the pistols, and by the time I returned from training Jean this morning, they were ready for me to get inside it to make sure I\u2019d fit well before they finished it. They did a marvelous job, and everything looked good, so they set about pouring the concrete. Once it\u2019s dry, I\u2019ll put the pistols inside, where they should be safe. They\u2019\u2019ll be putting a prefabricated gazebo on top of the vault, and are building a secret hatch into the floor of it to grant access to the solid concrete wall through which I\u2019ll enter the vault when we need the pistols.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, July 28th<br /> <br /> -I am up! A lovely flower.<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc!<br /> <br /> -It is evil doll day in the Twilight Zone<br /> <br /> -Spooky likes the evil doll. This is all opposite.<br /> <br /> -OMG go go gadget surrogate mom!<br /> <br /> -I am gonna see if we start inadvertently comparing notes on Natalie and Lily now.<br /> <br /> -I have no mouth and I must shop<br /> <br /> -Going out with Stanly, Spooky, and Lexie.<br /> <br /> -I clearly need new boots. As does Karen. I should have brought her.<br /> <br /> -On second thought, playing with my girlfriends feet is not conducive to shopping.<br /> <br /> -Stanly is a riot.<br /> <br /> -I hope Natalie does not ask how Karen and I met\u2026.<br /> <br /> -Aw Lexie is all shy about her and Chandra now. Cute.<br /> <br /> -I clearly need to hang out with Stanly more.<br /> <br /> -If Stanly bangs this Adam guy in a public place it will be at least partially my fault.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is being a bad example.<br /> <br /> -To be fair, the fellow Your Mistress is hanging out with is also a bad example.<br /> <br /> -I guess we are just corrupting Lexie then.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jog.<br /> <br /> -Why is my familiar always being petted by my girlfriend? I trow she spends more time with her than I do.<br /> <br /> -Pronouns. Karen spends more time with Elphaba than I do.<br /> <br /> -Superman is home\u2026time to hide.<br /> <br /> -Superman does not like Lily, even hugging Jasmine\u2019s leg.<br /> <br /> -Poor Gwen, she is getting so much shit from Doc<br /> <br /> -I suppose telling her I like being dominated and fucked by tomboys would not help\u2026<br /> <br /> -\u2026sorry I was just thinking about something.<br /> <br /> -An uneasy truce is in place in chez evil.<br /> <br /> -I had not really thought about it but this house really is full of women.<br /> <br /> -How can Doc and Simon stand it LOL.<br /> <br /> -We make big chains braiding each other\u2019s hair that extends between rooms (OK, not really)<br /> <br /> -Hey Chandra could be being braided on one end and braiding on the other!<br /> <br /> -&lt;_&lt; &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> -This doll is making me think cutesy thoughts. Maybe not a good thing after all.<br /> <br /> -And there she is waving at Jasmine from a doorway. Cute.<br /> <br /> - \u2026yeah\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LV</i><br /> <br /> So the recurring doll in the trunk was let out, and much of the session was spent dealing with it. Being smart little spooks, they took it to Old Man Malard, who had the spirit lore to identify it. Fine with me\u2026it was actually scarier if you knew just what it was.<br /> <br /> If you are concerned how an Azlu could be remotely friendly, remember it is now changed from the feminity spirits it, now she was fed. I won\u2019t say she is exactly benign, but she does feel a certain loyalty to the Krewe, at least for now. Now if she is more trouble than she is worth is something the Krewe will have to answer for themselves. As is, as you can see the ladies are getting more feminine while the less feminine among them have been shamed somewhat.<br /> <br /> And of course, Simon was interested in weaponizing her.<br /> <br /> Shopping trip has some neat rping. Stanley gently prodded the girls on their relationships (it came up Natalie met Karen when she won a contest to appear briefly on stage with Natalie at a nine inch nails concert and that they had sex off to the side of the stage. Alexia was a bit shyer at discussing her sex life. Also, Stanley is an absolute riot to run as an NPC.<br /> <br /> Next time we may be short Doc and Gwen for most or all the session, we will see what happens. Should be good times regardless though. However, next week look for the floor plans of Dark Haven Bluffs, all laid out for you in their sinister glory, with credit to Jasmine and Simon\u2019s players for their work on them, Simon\u2019s players original maps and Jasmine\u2019s players art program-fu were both needed. Of course there was feedback from everyone.<br /> <br /> Hope folks enjoyed, see you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:25:10-08:00","id":16335,"title":"","content":"OK for the \u201coff week\u201d this time we are going to have a map of Dark Haven Bluffs. These were made by Jasmine\u2019s player using rough maps drawn by Simon\u2019s player, so kudos to both. The whole group had a lot of input from there. I will go over each map with you\u2026linking rather than posting, as it will probably be easier to read following links.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/DarkHavenBluffs1st.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">First Floor</a><br /> <br /> You can see the bottom of two turrets at the front of the <span style=\"color:green\">House</span>. That was something there was a lot of discussion on.. Also mapping out the Kitchen side rooms as to which was the parlor, which was the game room, etc. we eventually divided them to how you see there. Chandra leaves her body in the walk in freezer while her head flies off. Also, note the Jacuzzi in the exercise room. That\u2019s new. There was talk of having a partition that can be used for privacy in the Jacuzzi. You know in case someone was up to something. The music room is where the piano is and the impromptu jam sessions have taken place as Natalie plays everything from the Cure to the Andrews Sisters. This is also where Natalie uses her Vanitas. Some Vlogs happen there. The Triage room is, IIRC, where the make up room was during the party. Finally, note there are two whole other wings unmapped. The <span style=\"color:green\">House</span> is big, people.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/DarkHavenBluffs2nd.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Second Floor</a><br /> <br /> OK second floor. Now, compared to my Scion and Castle Falkenstein games the PCs have not managed to be baby factories thus far, despite a larger percentage of female characters than either game (granted, CF lacks the pill). I don\u2019t really foresee that changing, unless Tavia gets (or is) pregnant (or possibly Gretchen, though dating a Changeling it is less likely). Despite this we have fine maternity facilities, a nursery, etc for if someone goes that way. Other red-letter things to note Gwen\u2019s hidden security room and the war room. Placing the room took some doing to have it align with descriptions we had given. You may have begun to notice how big the Library is. It is pretty huge, actually working as the Library Merit from Second Sight. Also we discussed it and had divided the bedroom on floors early on. Doc\u2019s room and Alexia &amp; Chandra\u2019s room are here. Note each of the bedrooms have two closets\u2026that was so they could <span style=\"color:green\">House</span> two servants, but it just makes sense especially with the couples. Simon and Tavia\u2019s rooms, being the masters of the house, are larger, though Tavia divides her time between her and Simons rooms and Simon sometimes sleeps in his crypt as well as his room. Most of Tavia\u2019s time is spent in her studio.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/DarkHavenBluffs3rd.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Third Floor</a><br /> <br /> Third floor. The \u201cDo not open\u201d Sarcophagus is here, as is the weapon room that menaced Jasmine\u2019s uncle (who is, atm, still scared to return given his first two trips). Whether or not the Sarcophagus contains a Wookalar remains unknown. The Sympathetic Magic room is the one with all the dummies. You will note many empty rooms; those are to be filled by whatever weird stuff crosses our minds. The Meditation room is here, as is Jasmine\u2019s room (just next door, again appropriate), Gwen\u2019s room, and Natalie and Karen\u2019s room. Jasmine and Gwen tend to mediate on their Vanitases in their bedrooms. Many of Natalie\u2019s Vlogs come from her room, as more people want to watch if her bed is visible behind her. Natalie\u2019s Alter for her Hedge Witch Magic is also in this room. Her two closets are full of her stuff where Karen\u2019s clothes go is a mystery\u2026it\u2019s long established Natalie\u2019s room is FULL of clothes at any given moment and she has probably commandeered some of the bathroom closet. Unfortunately Karen being a little taller and a little thinner they have trouble sharing. Bonnie Lynne\u2019s room where her dress was kept (and where her ghost wandered) is there and not really used right now. Natalie will likely suggest her daughter to sleep on this floor in the guest room between sitting rooms. That or the large guest room below.<br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/DarkHavenBluffs4th.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Fourth Floor</a><br /> <br /> 4th Floor! Not heavily used. Note there are two widows walks Jasmine and Natalie use. Natalie sometimes films Vlogs so that she is standing in front of the rock railing and outdoors behind her. She also uses the terrace and turrets for her Vlogs. Note the fabled and storied Foreigner-Eating Bedroom is on this floor. There really are more questions than answers about that room. Also, some bedrooms used by visiting DeLaPoers IIRC. Dollars to Doughnuts when not staying on Campus Leslie DeLaPoer will be on this floor. It is mostly a popular choice for getting away from the others, especially for those who often find themselves needing time for brooding.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/DarkHavenBluffsBasement.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Basement</a><br /> <br /> Basement! OK the Drain is noteworthy as (I think) something only Simon and Tavia knows about\u2026the secret way into the caves deep below the <span style=\"color:green\">House</span> where the Fish God sleeps. Because really, a <span style=\"color:green\">House</span> needs a Fish God. The Magic Circle room is where they do their keeping the paintings sealed magic (hence the handy dandy storage room nearby). Tavia also performs her Apostle of the Dark One magic there. The Ceremonial Magic room is where Doc and Simon do their magic. The Mirror room is where Simon\u2019s father\u2019s chair that used to be in the television room is and all the mirrors Simon has used his ceremony on are so he can sit in there and view people through them. Also a popular room for Simon to Boneyard the <span style=\"color:green\">House</span> from. You may notice the large library here as well as the three floors above and note how it is the Krewe (or Gretchen or Tavia) can research there without ever running into each other or realizing others are doing the same thing. Finally, gold storage there since they moved it out of Simon\u2019s crypt.<br /> <br /> On a personal note, if I had a house this big, I would have a different room for every game I ran, and could just leave the books in that room and sorta shift the decoration to fit. It would be <i>awesome</i>. That said man cleaning it would suck.<br /> <br /> Doc and Gwen\u2019s players had to miss last session, though Doc hopes to have a log to generally cover his activities during the time he was down\u2026you will have to depend on Jasmine and Natalie to cover the days events. The Krewe, flushed with the defeat of the DeCastros, decides to see if they can find some answers on the whole Candle Cove situation.<br /> <br /> They find some all right.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">It\u2019s green cuz of the Fish God.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:26:53-08:00","id":16336,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to New Haven, and our Krewe. We were down two players, but that did not stop the Krewe from stirring up quite a bit of trouble. Note this means Doc\u2019s Log does not describe any events that happened in game. It just covers what he was up to outside the session events, so if you usually just read that for your account you should probably read Jasmine\u2019s this time, otherwise read as per usually\u2026Doc\u2019s being first should build the suspense. It\u2019s back to <i>Candle Cove</i>, and a horrifying trip back to two PCs childhood.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1115 Hours, Thursday, July 29, 2010<br /> <br /> The heat took more out of me then I thought. I slept through my alarm and might not have woken up when I did, but Cupcake started screaming at the Cracked Cook again. There was no chance for meditation but I did make to work on time. Barely.<br /> <br /> Business was pretty steady until about 1100 Hours so I cleaned up a little and now I\u2019m writing this. Looking forward to Nightshade coming over for lunch today. I fully expect to hear the latest on when Bella Donna is going to come up. Should be soon. <br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1520 Hours, Thursday, July 29, 2010<br /> <br /> Lunch was fun as always. Nightshade was pretty funny as I could tell her head was in the clouds about Bella Donna coming soon. She really is adorable when she gets so excited. Her smile lights up the whole shop. It\u2019d totally ruin her hard won gothic image.<br /> <br /> After Nightshade left, I grabbed my sketchpad and started drawing again. I\u2019m definitely getting more comfortable with drawing different things. I need to start practicing on bodies instead of paper though. Not sure the best way to do that. Probably have to start drawing on myself to begin with. <br /> <br /> Just heard an ad on the radio for the Yankees game tonight. Maybe I can treat Ronin to a few beers. She can pick the spot and I catch the tab. Cool. Just called her office. She\u2019s okay with the idea. We\u2019ll just leave from The Bluffs since there isn\u2019t anything going on but TV night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2140 Hours, Thursday, July 29, 2010<br /> <br /> Plans got a little shifted around tonight. Ronin met me in the Liberty as soon as I got out of the cab. Said I could buy her dinner too. I almost made a joke about asking Anders about that, but decided not to press my luck. But that\u2019s also why I still have my Log with me.<br /> <br /> We went to some ancient drive-in place for dinner. I was expecting some nasty, deep fried thing, but it was actually pretty good. Ronin can\u2019t remember shit about herself but she still knows a good place to grab quick food. I\u2019d walked past the place before, but at night it looks like it\u2019s abandoned. Who knew?<br /> <br /> The Yanks are killing the Indians tonight and Ronin couldn\u2019t be happier. Big screen TV, cold beer, guys screaming and cheering Oh shit. Just got an SOS from Karen. Gotta go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> When I awoke this morning, Lily was sitting very quaintly on the cushioned chair in my room, looking for all the world like she had been placed there just so. Even if she is a little creepy-looking, she\u2019s still quite adorable, and she waved at me when I wished her a good morning.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast this morning, Alexia, Simon and I chatted about what we needed to do next on the Candle Cove problem. Alexia was full of energy and was quite insistent that we take care of it as quickly as possible, and I couldn\u2019t agree more. I imagine most of the krewe would have liked another day or two to rest, but we\u2019re all worried about the dangers of Candle Cove, and we don\u2019t know exactly how much time we bought with our TV station stunt or how long it will be until the show\u2019s final episode airs and some poor child disappears, no doubt taken by the show\u2019s Skintaker. Not having seen the show, I don\u2019t think I fully understand the horror we\u2019re facing, but Alexia certainly does, and seeing her motivated as she is by fear is a bit shocking.<br /> <br /> There is still no word from Jean\u2019s family. I know the worry must be eating him up inside, but he\u2019s putting his all into his training. I suppose he\u2019s trying to find something to focus on other than his worry. I wish I could do more for him.<br /> <br /> While I was out this morning, Alexia called Amos Wright, who was the station manager when Candle Cove was first delivered to the studio for its local programming. After I returned home from training Jean, she and Simon told me what she had learned, which gave us the address of the supposed studio where the show had been filmed. Oddly, it was in a run-down industrial area that is now almost completely abandoned. Amos also said that he dealt with a tall, pale woman named Janine Calliope, who delivered the episodes to the studio. He found her unsettling, and she seemed to react strangely to mundane questions, becoming puzzled, for instance, when asked about her husband. It\u2019s a blessing that Mr. Wright could not see Janine for the skeletal doll-thing she really is.<br /> <br /> Amos also thought the show was unpleasant, more like a dark parody of a children\u2019s show, and he would not have aired it if he wasn\u2019t required to do so by the local programming laws of the time.<br /> <br /> We will visit the address where the show was filmed later this afternoon. Unfortunately, Doc is away right now on some other business, and Gwen is working a case, I think. It\u2019s hard to say with her. I think they\u2019ll meet us at the site whenever they are able.<br /> <br /> Given what we know about Janine Calliope, I began to suspect she might be a servant of one of the beings Mongler calls the Gentry. So I called him and asked him if he knew anything that might help. He contacted a changeling called Creepshow who patrols the industrial area where the makeshift studio is located. There don\u2019t seem to be any signs of faerie activity there, so Mongler didn\u2019t think one of the Gentry was involved, but agreed to accompany us anyway just in case. If we end up running across the Hedge again, I\u2019d rather have him with us.<br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> We are about to leave to investigate the studio. Natalie and Alexia asked Becky (the journalist they met when first investigating the show) to find out if the little girl who played in Candle Cove was reported as missing when she disappeared. If she was local, there was no report of her disappearance, which seems suspicious.<br /> <br /> I finished the book I was reading, which was very good and thought provoking. I thought Karl might like it, so I wrote him a letter, just to chat a bit, and included it in a package with the book, which I\u2019ll drop by the post office tomorrow morning on my way to train Jean.<br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> There is an English expression that describes our krewe\u2019s experiences tonight: \u201cstirring a hornet\u2019s nest.\u201d Though if I understand it correctly, the idiom suggests causing trouble for one\u2019s own amusement, which was not our purpose. Perhaps it would be more appropraite to just say that me almost got in over our heads.<br /> <br /> We found the makeshift studio\u2019s address. It was a collapsing warehouse surrounded by a dirt lot and a couple of awful-looking whitish trees. As we looked around the outside, I found a porcelain doll\u2019s arm from one of the puppets and also the prop used for Pirate Percy\u2019s sailing ship, a strange little boat with a face. It was half buried in the dirt outside the warehouse, so Alexia dug it up and then read its past to find out what had happened to it. The skeletal Puppeteer (Janine Calliope) was the last to use it, but it had been manufactured by mundane means is an ordinary toy factory. Alexia couldn\u2019t tell what had happened to Janine from the ship, but the last time it had seen Janine was in 1976, about the time the show\u2019s original run ended.<br /> <br /> While Alexia was reading the ship, Simon and I heard a faint, discordant sound like calliope music, and Alexia began to hear the doll\u2019s voices from within, calling out to Janice for help. It sounded as though they thought Alexia was Janice. Simon used Boneyard to peer into the warehouse and found that many of the puppets used in the show were still inside, gathering dust on sagging shelves or lost underneath debris from the slowly collapsing roof. The show\u2019s sets and cameras seemed to occupy the main room of the warehouse along with a broken-down calliope, and there was a storage room and office near the main door. The main door was nearly rusted off its hinges and stood ajar. Perhaps most shocking was the presence of a skeleton that lay in front of the calliope. Simon thought the skeleton looked like its bleached bones had ended up there long after the corpse\u2019s death, as there were no other signs of decay. I thought it might be useful to use the Oracle to view the moments of its death, but we were a bit uncertain whether or not we should enter without Gwen and Doc. But since the doll\u2019s were reacting to our presence, we decided to go ahead and have a look inside despite Alexia\u2019s reluctance.<br /> <br /> I pried the door open and we entered. Once inside, Alexia found the Pirate Percy puppet in the entry hall. She said he was terrified and cried out to her to protect him, so she picked him up and carried along protectively. Simon looked around the office, and I made my way through the entry hall to the door to the main warehouse. And when I opened that door, that\u2019s when I \u201cstirred the hornet\u2019s nest.\u201d<br /> <br /> The puppets in the warehouse arose and began moving about on their strings as the skeleton that lay crumpled near the calliope rose as though carried by its own strings. Seen in person, it became obvious that it was Janine Calliope. the Puppeteer, and she hung from her strings, clad in her white coat with her white hair streaming around her skeletal face as she controlled the other puppets. I immediately closed the door.<br /> <br /> There was a horrible wailing sound from both the door I\u2019d closed and from outside the warehouse, like children moaning in pain and anger, and we could hear small figures begin to beat on the doors. Eventually, their words became clearer as they screamed \u201cHe\u2019ll take your skin!\u201d Mongler moved to block the door to the studio room while Alexia and I moved to intercept whatever was trying to come in from the outside door. Both doors burst open, and a small horde of skinless children poured in, throwing themselves at us with ravenous abandon. Natalie took cover against the wall and drew her gun. Simon found himself attacked by the Skintaker, a skeletal puppet in a top had a cape of children\u2019s skin. But the rest of us couldn\u2019t see or defend him from the Skintaker. It was as though the puppet had chosen Simon because of his child geist, the Little Prince, and only the Little Prince could face it. So the rest of us did what we could to prevent anything else from attacking Simon. Mongler blocked the door to the studio and used his fae strength to smash the undead children aside, easily destroying them with one blow after another. I grew my Primeval claws and assumed the panther-like power of my Caul and began slashing at the children who were pouring in through the outside door, and Alexia grew her additional limbs and fought side-by-side with me. I tried to draw most of their attention, and though they landed a few hits on me, I was able to avoid most of their blows.<br /> <br /> As the Skintaker descended on Simon, it became clear that it was not an even match. But Simon is very clever, and he fought back intelligently, using his Boneyard to fling the Skintaker away. He assumed complete control over the building, and telekinetically tossed the calliope at Janine while Natalie shot at her, hitting her twice. Their attacks did their job, and the Puppeteer flew off as though jerked away by her own puppet strings.<br /> <br /> But the skinless children remained, and we had out hands full fighting them off. That\u2019s when Gwen\u2019s car screeched to a stop in the dirt outside and she and Doc jumped out to help us!<br /> <br /> [Player\u2019s note: Entry to be continued after next session]<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Natalie\u2019s Daughter</u><br /> <br /> Natalie has made arrangements to bring her daughter in a day or so, so we\u2019ll have a guest. I hope she doesn\u2019t cause any trouble, but even if she does, her visit will do Natalie a lot of good, so I\u2019m glad she\u2019s coming. We\u2019ll put her up in one of the guest rooms near our end of the third floor. We chatted a bit with Natalie about what to call her while her daughter is here. I mean, her daughter, who is really named Natalie, knows that her mother uses her name, but it will be awkward to call them the same thing while younger Natalie is here. Our Natalie doesn\u2019t really want to be called by her real name, Allison, which is odd to me because I think it is a very nice name.<br /> <u><br /> The Scarecrow Ministry</u><br /> <br /> Mongler, Tommy Knocker, and Creepshow all belong to a group of changelings who call themselves the Scarecrow Ministry. According to Mongler, they try to scare innocent mortals away from dangerous places by making the threat posed by such locations all the more obvious. It sounds as though they perform a good, if unrecognized service for the mortals of New Haven.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29th<br /> <br /> -Mm, I am such a spoiled princess.<br /> <br /> -I get spoiled right!<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Morning creepy doll!<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc!<br /> <br /> -OK shifted gears then to the whole Candle Cove mess again then.<br /> <br /> -Alexia conducted an interview. Now my turn.<br /> <br /> -Gwen may have broke Jasmine for life.<br /> <br /> -Jasmine reminded me not to have sex with Becky. Why I almost forgot!<br /> <br /> -&gt;:-/<br /> <br /> -Ok, managed to get a little information from Becky and I even managed to stay out of her britches (somehow). Being over the phone helped, I am sure.<br /> <br /> -I wonder if Jasmine playing with Lily is a deliberate attempt to use cuteness to soothe my irritation.<br /> <br /> -EEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE<br /> <br /> -Ok, Natalie will be coming up\u2026like\u2026soon.<br /> <br /> -I wonder how we will adjust to two Natalies.<br /> <br /> -I dunno if Natalie will call me Allison or Mom. I kinda want her to call me Mom.<br /> <br /> -I told the others they can call me Allison. I am not super crazy about it but it might save confusion, and they are all very close.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m still Natalie, now. Allison has been put out of her misery.<br /> <br /> -No need to dwell on that though when MY LITTLE GIRL IS COMING UP HERE.<br /> <br /> -Tavia is hung up on bugs again.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is going to do some Urban Exploring.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up, UE edition!<br /> <br /> -Why, how delightfully not good this is!<br /> <br /> -Do all Faeries have code names?<br /> <br /> -Glad scary T-rex man is here.<br /> <br /> -This place is not creepy or anything.<br /> <br /> -Looks like we found the toy boat for the \u201claughingstock\u201d buried outside, mostly. Also a doll arm.<br /> <br /> -Creepy.<br /> <br /> -Why yes, I do hear Calliope music. Why no, I am not happy about it.<br /> <br /> -Well I dunno about my Krewe here but I have seen enough.<br /> <br /> -Karen\u2026sweetie\u2026the address at home? Never come here.<br /> <br /> -I feel I should point out going inside is not good just because a boat puppet told us to.<br /> <br /> -I am going to fucking die right before I see my daughter aren\u2019t I?<br /> <br /> -Ok, radio silence<br /> <br /> -97234bgbgbgbgbgbgbg0osgsdbo8y<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVI</i><br /> <br /> Lot happened, it was pretty crazy. Session actually ran over. \u201cLet\u2019s do this thing\u201d they said. We wound up stopping in mid combat\u2026people had to be up, you know.<br /> <br /> As you may have guessed, while Jasmine had a good theory, <i>Candle Cove</i> was not the work of the gentry. It does not fall neatly into the phatsplats of the WoD. While there is an explanation, it is not as simple as it being a specific critter.<br /> <br /> So\u2026Sin-Eaters are powerful as all hell, but a well-built changeling is scary. Grin was absolutely destroying the skinless children pretty much one per turn, especially as they relied on high health not good dodge. With the Stone Contracts he was throwing around Strength and Stamina in double digits and light armor. He was taking damage much faster then Jasmine, but his health also being in the double digits he did not care. Also, he was absorbing so much glamour from the PCs he pretty much had unlimited glamour. I\u2019ll also note I did not make up the Scarecrow Ministry. They are a Changeling thing. Actually, they are my favorite Entitlement\u2026When I play Changeling again I will almost certainly be a Scarecrow Minister.<br /> <br /> The Skin-Taker targeted Simon because only Simon could see it, and even then only when possessing his Geist, the Little Prince. As such, only Simon can actually face the Skin-Taker. As the Skin-Taker does aggravated Damage to those children who can see him, this puts Simon in a particularly dangerous place. He handled it quite well, using Pit and Curse to keep the Skin-Taker from being able to do\u2026much of anything really. Simon Also used Industrial Boneyard to throw the dolls into each other and hit the Puppeteer with a calliope, which Simon\u2019s player was quite pleased with. As Jasmine could not see it, I will note the slamming the calliope into the Puppeteer was when all hell broke loose and the children arrived.<br /> <br /> Natalie was able to shoot the Puppeteer as she relied on a huge dodge (17) to avoid being hit, but dodge does not help with firearms so Natalie\u2019s mediocre die pool did fine. This is noteworthy as the first time Natalie has fired her pistol \u201cNataliebane\u201d in over two years of play. The Puppeteer could not counter with the calliope, as it could not fit through the doorway between her and the Krewe, though she did throw a TV camera with her strings at Natalie, who had the presence of mind to quip that \u201cWell, this is ironic\u201d before the TV camera hit her. It only did one Bashing level to her though. Jasmine took some lethal, Alexia took some lethal, and Simon is only standing after bulwarking all his health levels from aggravated damage. Grin has taken 9 levels, but he has around 9 more left. Jasmine has a pretty low amount of Plasm going in and Simon\u2019s is not plentiful, so that was a handicap. Natalie and Alexia were OK on Plasm, though both were also wounded going into the fight, though not much.<br /> <br /> Pirate Percy was a Charm, so Alexia object read him and immediately got a derangement from failing a Resolve + Composure roll from seeing the last big emotional thing that happened with it. That\u2019s not a good pool for her. I would also be remiss in not noting the voice of the Laughingstock kept telling the PCs \u201cYou have\u2026to go\u2026inside!\u201d as well as Percy\u2019s plaintive calls. When the combat started Percy did not fight for or against the PCs, he just screamed and screamed.<br /> <br /> The Skinless Children and the puppets have structure, not health. The Children do lethal to anything with skin, bashing to anything without. Like Vampires (unless shot in the head or heart) and Zombies in my setting, Bullets do one bashing only if they hit regardless of roll. Fortunately no one was trying to shoot them.<br /> <br /> As implied, Doc and Gwen will be there for the clean up, but the Puppeteer has withdrawn and about half the skinless children are gone, so it will be mostly clean up.<br /> <br /> Woo. OK I think that covers everything. Next week I will put up a little thing I passed out with <i>Candle Cove</i> info, not a formal document just a quick who\u2019s who. But ask any questions you may have and I will try to clarify. Hope folks enjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T16:29:19-08:00","id":16338,"title":"","content":"Just a quick off week update. These notes were sent to the players re: <i>Candle Cove</i><br /> <br /> Pirate Percy- Antique, porcelain head did not match body on a marionette. Cowardly, did not want to visit places because he was scared.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Janice- Little girl who visited Candle Cove in her imagination. Was the brave one, helping Pirate Percy be brave. Changed actresses suddenly in second season.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Laughingstock- Percy\u2019s ship, which had a face. Normally a wooden model with smiling face, it would switch to a puppet face for close ups, saying \u201cYou have\u2026to go\u2026inside!\u201d when Percy was afraid to go in a cave or house for treasure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Horace Horrible: Puppet villain with Mustache above teeth and a monocle. Was replaced at the end of the second season by Pirate Percy\u2019s nemesis Milo for Skin-Takers henchman<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The Skin-Taker: Dirty Skeleton marionette wearing a brown tophat and cape, glass eyes too big for his skull, lowered from above. Mouth moved from side to side. Said \u201cTO GRIND YOUR SKIN\u201d to the camera, not actress when asked about his mouth. Cape got longer when they got a new actress\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Milo: Pirate rival for Percy in second season. Worked with Skin-Taker at the end and was killed offstage. Puppet. Voice was different in final scenes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Banana King- Minor character, gave Percy advice. Stopped appearing during second season without comment.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> -Constant Calliope Music<br /> <br /> -Final episode everyone screaming, Skin-Taker gnashing his teeth wildly, Janice crying for the whole episode.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, since we have an off week post, here are some stat updates<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Natalie Knight<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') 