 Nutcracker: Phantasmal Key<br /> <br /> Psyche 4<br /> Synergy 7<br /> Willpower 4<br /> Health 8<br /> <br /> Keys: Industrial Key, Phantasmal Key, Pyre-Flame Key<br /> <br /> Manifestations: Caul 5 Marionette 5 Oracle 5<br /> <br /> Ceremonies: (1) Finding;<br /> <br /> Weapon of Choice: Bowie Knife<br /> Armor: None<br /> Defense: 3 Initiative: 6 Size: 5 Speed: 12<br /> <br /> Derangements: Phobia, Skeletons (Minor)<br /> <br /> Languages Spoken: English (3), French (2)<br /> </div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> See folks next week with the continuation of our story, some combat, recriminations, and offspring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:15:33-08:00","id":16347,"title":"","content":"pologies for the late start, but I have the Geist journals here now. One came as we were sitting down to the game, so did not get a chance to get them up earlier. I hope you enjoy nonetheless<br /> <i><br /> Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0415 Hours, Friday, July 30, 2010<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have enough time or paper to hold all the swearing flying through my head. And what makes things even worse is that Ronin has said everything I\u2019ve thought, and I do mean EVERYTHING. Having seen and heard what my words would do to the Krewe has hurt me, as much as it hurt them. This doesn\u2019t make any sense without the actual problem. Good job, Doc.<br /> <br /> Your fury is but one of many weapons in your arsenal, Warrior. You have long known this to be truth. The strength to cage that wrath is far more powerful. It grants you both fear and respect from others. Witnessing what you could have done is always worthy of study. She who bound with The Angel has no door on her cage. Her teeth are bared at all times. While dangerous, it also makes her predictable. Reflect on these thoughts and memories to help guide your reactions in the future.<br /> <br /> Right. I\u2019m sure that will all make me stop and think later. Currently it doesn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Karen sent us an address so we jumped in Ronin\u2019s SUV and tore out. I can\u2019t really say how far away we were, but I know we got there in 7 minutes. They came out to some old factory that was falling in on itself. I\u2019m pretty sure none of us were anywhere near a safe Plasm reserves and I KNOW Nightshade and Cupcake weren\u2019t 100% healthy yet. So why the fuck did they go and engage something??? As pissed as Ronin and I were, I decided to get some practice with my new Rage powers. When we ran in the rusted walkway, we found all the doors ripped off the hinges and Mongler fighting what looked like skinless zombie children. He waved us inside as there were pieces of fallen zombies around him. Obviously he didn\u2019t need any help. We moved in further to find Rose surrounded by five of the same things. I tried to conjure an illusion of a flame whip to strike one but nothing happened. Ronin did her normal unseen attack and got one\u2019s attention. It charged and slashed her. That was more than I could handle. I let loose a howl and three spectral hounds surged into one of the other kids on Rose. Snowflake, having possessed The Little Prince had drawn one off of her and was going hand to hand with it. I was impressed even though his form was terrible. The kid tried to dive on him but managed to trip and smash its face on the concrete. Ronin made short work of the cannibal corpse on her. I sent a spectral bear at the excess on Rose, though she was fairing much better once the numbers weren\u2019t stacked so much against her. Ronin had already started bitching before the fight was even over so Rose snapped the last kids neck while firing back at Ronin. <br /> <br /> Before we could really get anywhere, I turned to look everyone over. Nightshade was in an office, her pistol still smoking while Cupcake was more wide-eyed than normal. I was only barely keeping it in check when I asked what the hell they were thinking. Cupcake instantly crumbled under the pressure and confessed it was Rose\u2019s fault. I\u2019m sure that will be funny when I\u2019m not pissed and in pain. Somehow it wasn\u2019t surprising that Rose thought she could take on the world. As best I could piece together from the arguing and twitchy accounts, they went to do recon on the address to see if it was worth looking at. They even took Dino-action Mongler with them in case there may have been anything Gentry-related going on. Out front, they found the model ship half buried and doll parts (arms and legs) scattered around. Boneyard showed a the inside of a factory covered in dust with TV cameras, a skeleton, and lots of the puppets used in Candle Cove. I was completely fine with the story to this point. Then they started hearing calliope music, next the voice of the ship from the show telling them they had to go inside. This is the point where I think Nightshade said they should go back. Because they weren\u2019t recharged like we wanted to be, Rose couldn\u2019t turn herself invisible but decided she would be okay anyway. Snowflake apparently also thought following the vocal advice of the disembodied boat was the best course of action. Once inside, Pirate Percy started calling out for Janice because he was scared. Cupcake immediately assumed that roll and tried to comfort the puppet. Things get a little fuzzy at this point, but as best I can tell Snowflake was bitten by an unseen attacker. He possessed his geist to find the Skintaker engaging him. They noticed the puppets were all coming to life and realized they were all connected with strings to the skeleton. That was actually the Puppeteer. She stood up and all hell broke loose. Snowflake managed to throw the calliope at the her, that much he was proud of. Just before we came in, Nightshade fired on and damaged the skeleton before she took off like some bad WB villain through the ceiling and flew away. Cupcake started flipping out as the Puppeteer ripped Pirate Percy away from her. Not sure if she was playing the part of Janice too well or what was happening. That\u2019s when the zombabies started crawling out of the ground. The Krewe was flanked from the beginning. Mongler had originally faced eight of the little monsters with the other five inside. I never understood which side of which door they were on as at least part of the story was that they tried to hold the doors closed to keep the kids out. Somehow all the doors got ripped off, but I\u2019m not sure if that was Mongler, the kids, or Snowflake. That was about how things looked when we got there anyway.<br /> <br /> Rose accepted it was a bad idea but I could tell neither she nor Ronin was done. I also knew this wasn\u2019t helping. Everyone was a little wounded, but mostly just bruises. Mongler didn\u2019t seem to notice but he was sliced up pretty good. He said he\u2019d be fine, he just needed to eat. Rose was unsurprisingly the next most shredded, but either because she wanted to be stubborn, she just wanted to hide the fact that she paid for her hubris with her flesh, or because she was trying not to set me off again, I couldn\u2019t tell. She played it off like she was fine. With everything cleared out, they decided to look around for anything remaining. There was a decapitated Milo puppet that would make a charm. It was Torn so that was more than a little unnerving. Several of the backdrops for Candle Cove were in frames against the wall. Snowflake mentioned that someone had drown in the seascape, so we made sure they were all cut from their frames. Oddly Rose\u2019s hands were wet and smelled like sea water afterwards. That pretty much guaranteed these things were headed for the basement. Snowflake warned us to watch out for the puddle of what looked like chewed up hot dogs while we walked around. Said he made the Skintaker sick. By that point, I just made sure we picked up all the parts and pieces of puppets. The others found an old scrap sheet in the office with information for Temp workers, the address for a toy shop, and a video equipment rental outfit. All this stuff was beyond our normal reach in a little town outside New Haven called Glenwood. That came back with us to Dark Haven Bluffs.<br /> <br /> We got back to the Bluffs about 2300 Hours. Cupcake immediately ran for Chandra. We got everything inside and I thought maybe I could just go beat the bag or something and let go of things. But then Rose stopped in front of everyone and told Gwen to finish. I have no idea what made her think this was a good idea. I told Snowflake he needed to learn how to throw a punch and took him to the Armory. This was probably the best idea for me to channel the anger constructively. Snowflake had no idea what he was doing, but he\u2019s a quick study. We worked on his balance, stance, and even how to shift his weight so he\u2019s not flat on his back when he throws a punch. We\u2019d covered most of the basics when the music nearly exploded from the new exercise room. I figured that meant Ronin and Rose were done for the night. Round two must have gone to Rose. But I was distracted so Snowflake landed right cross in the jaw. I didn\u2019t drop and thankfully I didn\u2019t swing back. It was a good solid hit. So next I showed him the solar plexus and how to use it. I did move when he tried to practice that one.<br /> <br /> After we practiced enough to take the edge off, I went back to check on Natalie. She and Karen were lying opposite each other, painting the others toes. I asked if everyone was okay. They said they were but then Nightshade told me it was okay to come in and hang out. I made sure Karen didn\u2019t seem to have any issues with it then sat down with them. I\u2019m no good with nail polish but fortunately they were just happy with my company. I realized when Nightshade rolled over, that I still needed to heal for the evening. I took care of Nightshade first, then went to Cupcake\u2019s room. She came to the door in her pajamas, but had me come in. Thankfully I hadn\u2019t interrupted anything so it wasn\u2019t weird. It was nearly 0200 Hours, but I still needed to see to Rose. I went to her room and knocked, hoping she wasn\u2019t asleep already. Lily opened the door. Yeah that\u2019s what I said. Lily can already open doors. Rose wasn\u2019t in, so I went to look for her. I found eventually found her sitting in lotus position out by the cliffs. She had her back to me and the night winds rustled her hair as I walked up. I could tell when her eyes opened, even though she didn\u2019t move. Must have looked like a scene from an awesome samurai movie. Anyway, I tended her wounds without mentioning any of the issues with tonight. I figured it wouldn\u2019t help and she\u2019d already heard everything from Ronin. When I finished with Rose, I glanced through the glass into the exercise room. Ronin was trying to do yoga and it wasn\u2019t going so well. Round two definitely went to Rose.<br /> <br /> Once everyone was dealt with and the fighting was over for the night, I headed out to the oven again. Igniting the flames, I just sat in front for a few minutes....watching. Fire means something to me. Not lighters or little campfires, but bigger flames. The kind that seem to always threaten to take everything from you, if they could just get out. That\u2019s the type of fire that burns in the outside oven. I started having flashbacks while I stared this time. I wasn\u2019t setting outside a creepy haunted mansion in Connecticut anymore. I was lying in a patch of red sand staring at the flames eating my flesh. The screams I heard weren\u2019t mine; they were Rocky and Tommy. We were all back in the Sand and all dying again. This was the same fire. It lived and burned only to take from those that couldn\u2019t stop it. The screams faded and I was in New Haven again. The fire looked back at me then, the flashback over. It had taken from me and I grew stronger for it. Now it wanted to give me something back; just this once. I had come for this, come to take back what was mine. I thrust my hand into the flames and knew I had what I needed. I slammed my hand down in the bucket of water I had with me and took care of everything as best I could. No more illusions of flame; no more nightmares of burning in a destroyed transport. I\u2019ve finally regained everything I lost to war... except my friends. I\u2019m sure they will be waiting for me when I\u2019m finally done. Until then, I will make them proud.<br /> <br /> But now I need to take my empowered ass to bed. Today is still a work day.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Friday, July 30, 2010<br /> <br /> I guess it shouldn\u2019t be a surprise, but meditation was a snap today. Rose was still there working to center herself when I left for breakfast. Nightshade was a breakfast for some reason. Probably because Bella Donna comes today and she\u2019s too excited to sleep. Apparently she\u2019s learned a way to talk with Lily. She has her own form of magic so it\u2019s not surprising, just unexpected.<br /> <br /> I got to work with no trouble today and everything has been pretty smooth. I have to admit I\u2019m kinda getting excited to meet Bella Donna at this point too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1310 Hours, Friday, July 30, 2010<br /> <br /> I got an email from Ronin. They found the toy shop in Glenwood online. It was closed but there were still toys inside. Urban explorers talking about how creepy the place was. This is probably a good start.<br /> <br /> Lunch was fun. Nightshade is completely giddy about her little girl coming. I got the feeling that she really wants me to be a part things once Bella Donna gets settled and accustomed to everything. I think I\u2019m okay with this because both mother and daughter need the other one. That Bella Donna only knows that we are supernatural investigators means we don\u2019t have to drag her into our world just yet. I have little doubts that she\u2019ll be apart of it sooner than I\u2019d like, but steps have been taken. Anyway, I did ask Nightshade if she could look into any cemeteries in Glenwood that might have be a haunt or have an Avernian Gate. She said she\u2019d also check the Twilight Network so we didn\u2019t accidentally start claim jumping. I want this operation to run like clockwork when we move this time. Hopefully I can keep it organized enough that it does just that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1915 Hours, Friday, July 30, 2010<br /> <br /> Well nothing like getting all ragey just after a lovely dinner. The Krewe gathered before Nightshade left to get Bella Donna for a final dinner without secrets. It was spaghetti of course. Everything was fine until we finally coaxed Cupcake into telling us why we had to move against the Puppeteer during the daylight. She told us that she had object read the doll; because of this, she watched the Skintaker each the skin off of the second Janice. Now she can\u2019t bear the thoughts of dealing with the skeleton. This sounds like it might be a phobia. I\u2019ve seen them before. I\u2019m not the best person to try and treat phobias, damn it. And after how pissed Ronin and I were last night, I\u2019m not sure Cupcake is going to want to talk to me about the situation that made me so mad to start with. We changed the subject slightly as Tavia found out about the backdrops and became fascinated with trying to paint a fictional place for us to all go. Nightshade had to leave to pick up Bella Donna from the airport so that conversation didn\u2019t last too long. We let her go alone so she could have some private moments with her little girl, but I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s actually what Nightshade wanted. I\u2019m going to have to do something to get my mind off things again so I don\u2019t scare anyone when Bella Donna gets here.<br /> <br /> Ah, I can drag Karen and Snowflake into the Library for a while. That should help me focus.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2045 Hours, Friday, July 30, 2010<br /> <br /> That was a worthwhile research trip. With the help, I managed to put enough information together for us to actually learn the kind of Alchemy that lets us affect ourselves. I think that was a good initiation for Karen.<br /> <br /> Snowflake left right after we got finished to get ready for Bella Donna\u2019s arrival. I showed Karen where we kept our completed research for ceremonial magic so she could access the same information we already had. Then we heard Nightshade and Bella Donna coming down into the Library. They were talking about how Tavia looked like Bill the Cat. I didn\u2019t really see it, but I did see Karen kind of stiffen and shift behind me a little. Nightshade pulled Bella Donna in front of her, proving immediately that her \u201clittle girl\u201d was actually an inch taller. I smiled and said hi. We made some small talk. I did think it was cool but weird when Nightshade pointed out that Bella Donna could trust me. Karen didn\u2019t know what say or do at first, but she eventually survived introductions. Nightshade went looking for Snowflake so I asked Karen if she was okay. She finally relaxed a little and said she guessed so. I guess we\u2019ll see. She followed them after that so I hope she\u2019s a little more okay with this whole baby momma thing that\u2019s just been thrust upon her. That is kinda funny, in a really terrible way. This should be a very interesting weekend.<br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> [Player\u2019s note: Entry continued from previous session]<br /> <br /> After Gwen and Doc arrived at the warehouse to help us out, we were able to make short work of the remaining undead, skinless children that the Puppeteer had raised to fight us. I continued to draw much of their attention for as long as I could, and managed to avoid all but a few minor scratches. The others were a bit worse off, but they will be fine shortly.<br /> <br /> We spent some time examining the site, and ended up taking with us several of the backdrops used in the Candle Cove TV show since according to Simon and Alexia, they sometimes because almost real and one of the two girls who played Janice was allegedly killed inside one of the painted landscapes, her skin eaten off by the Skintaker. It reminds me a bit too much of Tavia\u2019s paintings for my comfort, but best that we lock them away ourselves rather than leave them for someone else to find.<br /> <br /> Mongler also arranged for an anonymous tip to the police about the site so that they could take care of identifying and burying the bodies.<br /> <br /> But before we could get very far with any of that, Gwen unleashed a barrage of admonishments against us for wandering into such a dangerous situation. Actually, she started even while we were still fighting. I was honestly shocked at how angry she was, and I confess that I still don\u2019t completely understand why she is so angry. She believes that we were rash and foolish to get in over our heads like we did, and refused to listen when we explained that we had taken every precaution and investigated the place as thoroughly as we could from outside before we even thought about entering. I don\u2019t think our actions or the outcome would have been any different had she and Doc been there, as I suspect that they would have agreed that, as things certainly appeared relatively docile inside the warehouse, a closer look wouldn\u2019t hurt. But since Gwen wasn\u2019t there at the time, she is only concerned about the fact that we might have died, which might have led to others\u2019 deaths when we resurrected had Karen or someone else wandered along looking for us. Also, Gwen is justifiably upset that our quarry fled and that we may have missed an opportunity to end the Candle Cove menace once and for all. But again, we did the best we could and made our decisions based on the information we had.<br /> <br /> She and I argued a bit at the site, but since we needed to leave as quickly as we could, we cut it short. Both Gwen and I were still rather cross with one another, but I think Simon and Alexia were simply cowed by her fury. After we returned home and stored the painted backdrops away, I grew tired of Gwen\u2019s fuming silence, so I told her to go ahead and finish. And so she did. We argued a bit more, and I made the mistake of telling her that she could stop berating us. She triumphantly pointed out that I was the one who asked her to continue, and she was right. What I should have said \u2014 what I meant to say \u2014 was that she should stop berating Simon and Alexia and Natalie. I still don\u2019t think we made a poor choice based on what we had to go on and the fact that Mongler was with us, but it was me who insisted that we go in and get a closer look. So if Gwen wants to be angry with me, that\u2019s fine. But Alexia and Simon had a bad enough time of it already, and she should leave them be.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that\u2019s not what I said, and Gwen\u2019s retort put me off so badly that I simply turned around and walked away. We both needed time to cool off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> When I returned to my room to angrily write my last entry, Lily found me. I think she heard the arguing, and could no doubt sense that I was upset. She gave me a hug and it made me feel a lot better. She\u2019s so sweet. I suggested we go for a walk, since I needed to center myself, so I took Lily out for walk through the cemetery and to the cliffs overlooking the sea behind the house. I wanted to dive into the ocean and sink deep into the depths to reach the comforting tranquility and isolation that I always find there, but with my reserves of plasm nearly spent, the Bride and I couldn\u2019t afford to cloak ourselves in our Tear-Stained Shroud. Having to refrain from that solace made me ache inside, but I managed to content myself with sitting on the cliff and enjoying the cool, salty night breeze while I closed my eyes to meditate. Lily tried to meditate with me for awhile, but soon grew bored and wandered back to the house.<br /> <br /> It took me nearly an hour and half to achieve a true state of calm. I\u2019m not used to being so angry. Normally, when I get angry, it happens quickly and then it\u2019s over. But this gnawed at me more deeply. Still, I was able to eliminate it and return to a state of tranquility. I\u2019m not angry with Gwen anymore, and I hope that she\u2019s gotten over it too since she spent half the night working out to the sound of her loud and obnoxious music.<br /> <br /> Sadly, my mood is still dark. I\u2019m not angry anymore, just depressed again. Since I returned from Taiwan, my mood has been relatively upbeat. For me, at least. It was nice, but I should have known it wouldn\u2019t last. I fear I\u2019ve settled into a long period of melancholy. The Bride and I are comfortable here, though.<br /> <br /> As I was finishing my meditations, Doc found me and tended to my wounds. We didn\u2019t really talk about my altercation with Gwen, though I know Doc is angry as well. He just controls it better. He is so good for the krewe.<br /> <br /> When I returned to my room, I passed by Natalie\u2019s door and saw that she was chatting with Lily. Apparently she\u2019s learned a ritual to allow her to communicate with spirits. I asked if I could learn it too, but it isn\u2019t something I can learn without dedicating myself to her religion, so I suppose I will simply have to rely on her to translate for me.<br /> <br /> Lily followed me back to my room. I was going to just read some poetry, but Lily was not happy that I seemed depressed, and insisted that I play some of my more upbeat music. She already associates it with my brighter moods, though I don\u2019t think she realizes that it\u2019s my mood that determines the music, not the music that determines my mood. I wanted to listen to the Cure or something else that complemented my feelings, but to placate Lily, we listened to the Go-Go\u2019s. And it did cheer me up a bit, especially seeing Lily dance on my bed. I should teach her some of the dances Richard taught me when we used to go out dancing on retro nights, like the Twist, Watusi, or Mashed Potato.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 30, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> The day has been fairly uneventful. Gwen seems to have gotten over being angry, which is good.<br /> <br /> Jean\u2019s performance was barely satisfactory today, and I know it\u2019s because he\u2019s anxious about his family since he still hasn\u2019t heard from them. I asked him if he wanted to join me for a cup of coffee at Lulu\u2019s later in the afternoon to talk about it, and he readily accepted. So we met and chatted about his family and other things. I think it helped Jean relax a bit, for a time, anyway, though of course nothing short of positive word from the Ivory Coast will truly help him feel better.<br /> <br /> I need to talk to Doc about arranging a foray to Jean\u2019s home through an Avernian gate to try and safeguard Jean\u2019s family, assuming they are still okay. The sooner the better really.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 30, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Natalie went to the airport to pick up her daughter. I suppose I\u2019ll refer to the elder Natalie as \u201cOur Natalie\u201d to differentiate her from her daughter. She went alone so as not to crowd her daughter at the airport (and I also think she needed the time to let her emotions outwithout all of us watching), but she took younger Natalie around the house to meet everyone when the two of them returned home. It is fortunate that Our Natalie warned her daughter about Lily, because I couldn\u2019t really hide her when they came to my room for introductions. I hope I didn\u2019t come across as too cold or spooky. I tried to be warm and inviting, but it was a bit difficult given my melancholia. I suspect Our Natalie took care to prepare her daughter for our idiosyncrasies. I wonder if she\u2019s told her daughter the nickname she calls me sometimes?<br /> <br /> Anyway, the younger Natalie seemed nice during our short introduction, though a bit overwhelmed. I expect she will be less reserved tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Further Investigation &amp; Planning</u><br /> <br /> Since we drove the Puppeteer from her primary residence, we had to use what means we had to track her down. Fortunately, Alexia and Gwen were able to make a good guess based on what information they dug up. We think she might have gone to a secluded, abandoned toy factory in Glenwood, a town near New Haven. The factory still has some creepy-looking toys in it and is sometimes visited by curious urban explorers. All the more reason for us to deal with the Puppeteer quickly, as it won\u2019t do for some hapless teenager to wander into her clutches.<br /> <br /> So we plan to visit Glenwood, and to take things more carefully this time. First off, we\u2019re going to look into some of the local haunts and see if we can\u2019t claim some new sources of plasm. This may also have the benefit of introducing us to some ghosts in need of resolution. We\u2019re going to spend a day or more just doing that this time.<br /> <br /> Once we have been able to recover some plasm and have hopefully established a presence in the neighborhood, we will move on to the toy factory, hopefully capturing the Puppeteer unaware and trapping her this time. But we will need to investigate the factory more thoroughly without being detected first, so I suspect my talents will be required. I should work hard to improve my mastery of the Oracle over the next day or so.<br /> <br /> Sadly, we still don\u2019t know just what the Puppeteer is. She\u2019s not a ghost or spirit or one of the Gentry. She might be an Outsider, but we don\u2019t know for sure.<br /> <u><br /> <br /> Ragdoll Cupid</u><br /> <br /> Natalie informed me today that Lily is very curious about the love lives of the house\u2019s residents. Natalie filled her in as well as she could. Lily also regards me as her mother, and she\u2019s very concerned that I don\u2019t seem to be happily involved in a romance of my own. Natalie thinks that Lily will probably try to intervene and help me out. I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s a good thing or a bad thing, but I\u2019m pleased to know that Lily wants to be supportive.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, July 29th<br /> <br /> -OK emergency over with. Now time for the yelling.<br /> <br /> -Someone has to be wrong. It can\u2019t just be work things out and let live. No mistakes allowed. Only yelling.<br /> <br /> -Reminds me of something. :9<br /> <br /> -Granted Jasmine is usually the one being excessively accusing, but she is on the receiving end this time.<br /> <br /> -Maybe this will make her grow a little being on the receiving end of unnecessary rage. Not that I am at all pleased to see her being attacked.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t even care about this anymore; I want to get away from angry people.<br /> <br /> -Blame blame blame blame<br /> <br /> -Agh!<br /> <br /> -OK, time to try to calm down. Gonna paint nails, that always makes me happy.<br /> <br /> -Women\u2019s feet are so delicate looking. Like they could break.<br /> <br /> -Damnit I can hear yelling from up here.<br /> <br /> -Is it just me or do shouts and screams travel further in this house than laughter does?<br /> <br /> -Gonna relax. Gonna not get drunk. No candy, it\u2019s put away.<br /> <br /> -Looks like I picked the wrong week to \u201cquit\u201d narcotics.<br /> <br /> -Gwen wants everyone to remember she is angry.<br /> <br /> -Having a conversation with a doll.<br /> <br /> -This doll is nosey!<br /> <br /> -And wants a man (creepy)<br /> <br /> -Doc\u2019s around. Kinda rage-y but not putting me on edge too much.<br /> <br /> -No sense of humor though.<br /> <br /> -Talk about calming things. Like mini me.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d enjoy Doc\u2019s company tonight more if I could not sense the rage under the surface. It scares me.<br /> <br /> -Ok I am going to go to sleep and hope everyone has gotten over themselves tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, July 30th<br /> <br /> -Today is the big day.<br /> <br /> -EEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEEE<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc<br /> <br /> -Note to self: I need to explicitly invite Doc to things. He wants to give me space, and that is sweet, but I tend to assume he is OK with whatever when I think he wants to be told it is OK.<br /> <br /> -OK, seeing if anyone in Glenwood is on the Twilight Network.<br /> <br /> -Getting room ready<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Had to not, uh, mention anything.<br /> <br /> -That would put years on me. &lt;_&lt; &gt;_&gt;<br /> <br /> -Working on room, took a break to play some Music Box Dancer.<br /> <br /> -Din Din!<br /> <br /> -OK, so I need to do this alone, then. For the best.<br /> <br /> -I haven\u2019t told Natalie too much\u2026I think she will figure out most of the relationships herself.<br /> <br /> -Fear is the Mind Taker. As are panic attacks.<br /> <br /> -The fact Karen and I and Alexia and Chandra share rooms may be a clue.<br /> <br /> -I realize it is only a matter of time till she figures out we are weird supernatural critters.<br /> <br /> -OK, broke down crying in the airport. Maybe it won\u2019t happen now once she is here.<br /> <br /> -ohgodohgodohgodohgod<br /> <br /> -Nope, so much for that idea. Good job Allison, bawl your eyes out on meeting your daughter. It builds respect. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Allison is dead and buried. Don\u2019t know why I was talking to her.<br /> <br /> -One hundred scenarios in my head for meeting Nattie and it was not like any of them.<br /> <br /> -She is taller than me! I almost told her she had gotten so tall, but I realized that would make me like 60.<br /> <br /> -On the plus side, she is willing to call me \u201cMom.\u201d I mean she was on the net but it is nice face to face.<br /> <br /> -She still likes my eyes. That\u2019s sweet.<br /> <br /> -She even said I look great that is awesome.<br /> <br /> -Ok time to take her back to meet the \u201cfamily\u201d<br /> <br /> -Tavia mildly creeped her out. Doc was warm and polite. Gwen was Gwen\u2019s version of friendly, and Karen looked like a deer in headlights. Interesting start.<br /> <br /> -Alexia and Jasmine went fine. Where is Simon?<br /> <br /> -She handled Lily about as well as I think she could be expected to. Least she knows we are not crazy.<br /> <br /> -We picked up a Karen following us.<br /> <br /> -Aaaah there he is. Wow he is all charming.<br /> <br /> -Should I be worried? =-O<br /> <br /> -She took Karen and I sharing a room fine, seemed a little more surprised about Alexia.<br /> <br /> -She likes her room! ^_^<br /> <br /> -OK, met all but Gretchen and Chandra. Gretchen is off to see her BF for the weekend, and Chandra is\u2026not in a state Nattie needs to see her in.<br /> <br /> -Haven\u2019t cried in over two hours. Can it last????<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVII</i><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have a great deal to add to that. Much of the drama was IC clashing between Gwen and Jasmine. Doc was pretty upset too, but Gwen sorta took over for the hostilities. No one confronted Natalie directly so she never opened up her verbal guns on anyone. She and Simon sorta defended that they did not realize how dangerous it was and that Boneyard was used extensively. Alexia rapidly and enthusiastically blamed Jasmine, which did not go over well but was hilarious that the eldest of the Krewe is occasionally 7. Granted, Natalie is occasionally 14 and Jasmine is occasionally 17, but what can you do.<br /> <br /> So we went over the changes, and most were determined to be used. I have the Rage users the last word on Rage, Caul users last word on Caul. There was very long discussion about Haunts refilling. I put forth that refilling daily to me meant the PCs could use their powers without real problem; this meant that the Sin-Eaters effectively had no weakness, and I was running horror/mystery not super heroes here. Not that I mind Super Heroes, of course, I mean I run two Scion games even in addition to Castle Falkenstein (which is not super heroes but is over the top pulpy action) and I want my Geist and Vampire games to be horror/mystery. It was also put forth that they had to spend a lot of downtime to refuel themselves, though I noted they had a huge amount of Plasm they could hold for getting it back so quickly. In the end we compromised, giving the PCs core haunt a per day refill, and tentatively giving other haunts a per week refill unless they had an active ghost. It was noted Sin-Eaters could not easily seek out Plasm as Vampires could Blood or Changelings Glamour, those being the New WoD games our group had by far the most experience with outside Geist; the only single monster campaigns we have run in New WoD were Geist, Changeling, and Vampire, though we had had Mage, Promethean, and Werewolf PCs in crossover, we had only ever had in toto two Mages and one each Promethean and Werewolf played verses somewhere around 12 Sin-Eaters, 14 Changelings (with another 6 for a soon to be game created but not yet played for 20) and 7 Vampires. It was also noted Resonance seemed neat but was very, very very hard to use in game. No real answers were come to. For example, using Lust with Mourner for Jasmine was\u2026difficult\u2026and Wrath with Gatekeeper for Doc was easier but sorta what he was trying to move away from.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s where we are. Next session\u2019s notes will cover a rather short session as a bit less then half the time was spent hashing out the 1.1 rules. But we will see some of the following day. Please do join us, I will try and make it worth your while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:22:01-08:00","id":16349,"title":"","content":"Looks like a Shorter Session, but a Session nonetheless. Here is our recap of last session<br /> <br /> <i>Session LVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1045 Hours, Saturday, July 31, 2010<br /> <br /> Damn proud it\u2019s Saturday. Got up like normal but it took forever to center this morning. I almost missed breakfast while anything was still warm...not that that matters with Cupcake\u2019s cooking, but that\u2019s beside the point. It was odd because Nightshade came to breakfast AND got there before me.<br /> <br /> Rose brought up another possible Magical Adventure (TM) that she was concerned about. Apparently Jean, her student slash not-boyfriend slash whatever, has been really unfocused lately during practice. She found out that his family is still back in the Ivory Coast and things are \u201cnot okay\u201d over there. He\u2019s worried about his family and with all the power mad warlord, he has every reason to be. But the short version is, she wants us to go check it out. I\u2019m the one that would get us there and I still don\u2019t mind the idea of taking the Krewe all over the world for the price of Plasm. However, bringing my Krewe into a war zone is different than popping over to Hong Kong for take out Dim Sum. I know that Rose can take care of herself more than, as her physician, I\u2019m comfortable with, but none of them have actually had to witness that war is like. This is a bonus because it means for the most part, they can still sleep at night. I didn\u2019t turn her down, but I did try to gently yet seriously point out this fact. Cupcake just got herself rattled from dealing with horrible images at the warehouse. Taking the whole Krewe into a place where there is no Rule of Law, living or otherwise, may take more away from them then they are willing to lose. In the end, we agreed that Candle Cove has to be the top priority, but we\u2019ll look into Jean\u2019s village after that. In fact, I think Snowflake was hoping to get a mirror or something similar to give us eyes on the ground. At least we\u2019re not going into this one completely blind.<br /> <br /> At some point during this discussion, Lily climbed up the back of Rose\u2019s chair and tried to braid her hair. It was kind of pitiful since Lily doesn\u2019t actually have hands, being a rag doll. Eventually Rose reached up and helped her. Bella Donna came down riding the smell of bacon at that point and stopped short for a second. She recovered quickly but it was a little much for her first thing in the morning. Poor kid. It didn\u2019t take her long to shake it off because she asked about going clubbing after she sat down with her plate. Karen was standing behind her looking at me shaking her head. We were able dodge that one by claiming official business and we scrambled to get ready to hit Glenwood for recon. I made sure Karen had her ear curl with her, just in case.<br /> <br /> Now to see how well the Krewe can perform an Intel mission, before we hit with a fully armed Search and Destroy. This will be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1315 Hours, Saturday, July 31, 2010<br /> <br /> Well, it\u2019s been a interesting trip so far. <br /> <br /> Our first stop was a large cemetery. If it had a name, we entered from the side without the sign. We noticed right away that it had a really well made fence. I couldn\u2019t help but remember that they put those up to keep things in as well as out. Pretty sure say it too. We split up to look for Haunts or ghosts. Rose and Nightshade each found some odd markings on two different mausoleum walls. Looked like the few werewolf symbols we\u2019ve seen before, but not the same thing. I took pictures with my phone so we could show Malard or Dierdre later. Snowflake became one with the graveyard and found a chamber under the crypt with the weird cup symbol. There were two rooms. One down a ladder from the surface and another behind the big stone door. Then Nightshade tagged in and they switched Boneyards, while grumbling about Bella Donna trying to grill Karen about who her real father was. I felt sorry for Karen because I\u2019m certain she doesn\u2019t actually know what Bella Donna is trying to learn. Anyway, Nightshade found an Avernian Gate and the tiniest Haunt ever. Thus we took our cue and headed down. Rose, Ronin, and I went first, then Cupcake, Nightshade, and Snowflake would follow us. The size of the Haunt wasn\u2019t really exciting, but the Avernian Gate meant easy access. Just as Ronin made it off the ladder, we were ambushed by a spirit. It was solid, shiny black, flying on membraneless chitinous wings, with bone scythes for arms. It\u2019s head was a skull with green faceted fly eyes. The comparison to one of Ridley Scott\u2019s aliens wasn\u2019t too far fetched, except this one flew and didn\u2019t have any legs. It screeched and dove at Ronin. I don\u2019t really want to think about what it could have done with those bony blades. But Rose jumped on it and wrapped it up before it could land a hit. I tried to hit it with my Phantasmal Rage. I think there\u2019s something blocking me sometimes. Nothing happened. Then Ronin returned fire with her own Rage attack. It kept shrieking repeatedly and managed to fight its way out of Rose\u2019s hold, not a good sign. Before it could really do anything, Rose grabbed it again and this time she slammed it into the crypt wall, pinning it against the stone. I yelled for Nightshade to talk to it. She said it was only trying to guard the tomb and we were intruders. I tried to take on a less hostile posture but it never stopped screaming or fighting against Rose. Ronin stopped short of attacking it and asked who the creature was working for. Nightshade it was guarding this place for the Predator Kings. That sounded like one of those groups of werewolves Malard warned us about to me, so I called for a retreat. Ronin and I backed up to the ladder and I told Rose to get ready to drop it and run. I had Ronin go first, then I started up the ladder. When I was up far enough I knew we could all get out, I yelled for Rose to pull out. She flew up the ladder almost on my heels like I figured. Thankfully, the damn screaming stopped once we were gone. Nightshade managed to distract an old lady that heard the alarm so we could get away. Snowflake was busy keeping the groundskeeper that also heard the noise from finding us. But somehow we managed to get back to the cars without anyone being hurt or interrogated.<br /> <br /> So now we know about a Haunt being watched by a pack of werewolves that Malard thinks are bad news. With that and the horrible shit in the old toy shop, Glenwood is a hell of a place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, July 31, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> Over breakfast this morning, I decided to discuss the possibility of using an Avernian gate to go to the Ivory Coast and check on Jean\u2019s family. I was nervous abut how the idea would be received, but everyone seemed to be willing to help out. That said, Doc and Gwen were extremely cautious, and warned the rest of us that if we were to go into a war zone like that, we would see things we might not be prepared for. Natalie and Karen argued a bit about whether Natalie should even go, and for once I can\u2019t blame Karen. In fact, I don\u2019t really know if it\u2019s a good idea for Natalie, Simon or Alexia to go. A smaller group would probably be better, and I\u2019m not sure Natalie or Simon are up to it physically, and I\u2019m not confident that Natalie or Alexia are mentally prepared. But they seem determined to help, and I certainly won\u2019t turn them away. If we end up running across any ghosts (which is almost an inevitability), their skills will be quite valuable, but if they get hurt I\u2019ll not be able to forgive myself.<br /> <br /> As long as we have a rough idea of where we\u2019re going, Doc thinks he can find an Avernian gate there. Simon suggested that if Jean has something reflective that might have caught Jean\u2019s family\u2019s image, he might be able to spy on them using his mirror-scrying ceremony. I hadn\u2019t even thought of that, but if he can do so, we might not even have to go to the Ivory Coast. Not if Jean\u2019s family seems to be safe.<br /> <br /> I called Jean to ask about getting something like that from him. Simon suggested perhaps a camera, which would have caught his parents\u2019 reflection on its mirror or lens. I gave Jean an excuse about needing it for a Buddhist prayer ritual to invite good fortune onto his family during their time of need, but I don\u2019t think he entirely believed me. I think I even saw Natalie cringe because of how painfully awkward my conversation must have been. But Jean agreed, and I hope to be able to visit him this evening to pick up whatever he can provide.<br /> <br /> In any event, we agreed that we needed to deal with the Candle Cove problem first. I am a bit anxious to leave Jean\u2019s family in danger any longer than necessary, but hopefully Simon\u2019s scrying will give us a better idea of the urgency of our trip to the Ivory Coast.<br /> <br /> Also, during breakfast, Lily climbed on the back of my chair and tried to braid my hair. It was absolutely charming. Sadly, her fingerless hands can\u2019t really braid well, so I eventually reached back and helped her, gathering my hair into locks for her to weave into a braid. It was nice. I haven\u2019t had my hair braided in ages, and never really had friends to do it for me, just my mum when I was a little girl.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, July 31, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> We began our investigation of Glenwood today. We started with Glenwood Cemetery. After looking around a bit, we found some odd markings on some of the mausoleums. At first we thought they might be krewe marks, but then Doc and Simon suggested that they were werewolf signs. Two of the marks were identical sets of crossed lines, while the other looked like a rough image of a cup with a halo over it. Glenwood doesn\u2019t fall under Malard\u2019s pack\u2019s territory, which meant we were probably in the territory of a pack we didn\u2019t know. That was a frightening prospect, but we decided to look around anyway. It is what we came for, and if any werewolves came for us, we would deal with them when it happened.<br /> <br /> Simon dropped into a Boneyard trance and discovered that there was a strange subterranean chamber beneath the mausoleum marked with the cup and halo mark. Se we decided to break in and have a look. Alexia fiddled the lock open and we went in. There was a trap door with a ladder leading down into a short hallway that led into the underground room Simon had seen.<br /> <br /> I went down first, followed by Doc and then Gwen. Simon and Natalie remained outside to watch for anyone coming our way and Alexia anxiously brought up the rear. I approached the door to the underground room, but then a spirit manifested and threw itself at Gwen, who was still on the ladder. The spirit was ghastly, thin and black with a skull head and hands like sickle blades. Its eyes glowed with a sickly green light and as it attacked, it cried out with an ear-splitting shriek. I didn\u2019t want it to hurt Gwen, so I reacted as quickly as it appeared and wrapped it in a loose grapple that threw it off balance and kept it from striking. Gwen and Doc quickly responded by unleashing their Rage manifestations at it, but only hurt it a bit, which in the end was probably a good thing.<br /> <br /> After that, it struggled free of my grasp briefly, but I shifted my stance and grabbed it again, this time pinning it against the wall so that it couldn\u2019t escape. Considering I didn\u2019t activate any of my manifestations, I think I performed fairly well.<br /> <br /> Natalie tried talking to the thing, but according to her, all it did was scream \u201cIntruders!\u201d We briefly discussed what to do, and decided that we had better leave the spirit be since it was probably put there by the werewolves to guard the place, and we didn\u2019t want to antagonize the pack. So everyone withdrew while I held the spirit, and then once they were al out, I released it, pushing it away to give myself enough time to escape as well. We all made it out with no further incident.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the spirit\u2019s screams attracted the attention of a few of the cemetery\u2019s visitors, including one of the caretakers. But Simon managed to keep them away with a clever application of the Pit, which confused them and kept them from ever reaching the mausoleum until we were already gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Footnotes<br /> <br /> <u> The Wrong Message</u><br /> <br /> I was going to take some dinner to Jean when I went so that I could keep him company for a bit and hopefully make him feel better, but Gwen\u2019s reaction to that idea reminded me that it might send the wrong message. I don\u2019t want him to think my interest is romantic. The Bride and I have already given up on Jean. Then again, we seem to have given up on pretty much all of our romantic interests. We haven\u2019t heard from Julian since we returned from Taiwan (and he knew when I was supposed to return), so we can only assume he isn\u2019t interested in me. We haven\u2019t really given up on Karl, but the issues surrounding his family are daunting.<br /> <br /> The truth is, we\u2019re feeling quite neglected, and where we don\u2019t feel neglected, we feel intimidated by the prospects of becoming any more involved with the Fishbornes than we already are. It only deepens our longing to see everyone else in the house happily involved in their own romantic relationships. An angry part of me envies the way people like Chandra, Karen, and Anders are so aggressive with their pursuit of their paramours while my romantic prospects all seem reserved and cold. Perhaps it\u2019s me.<br /> <br /> Maybe a part of us does want to send the wrong message to Jean, in the hopes that it might actually be the right one.<br /> <br /> <u>Sibling Scuffles<br /> </u><br /> On the way to Glenwood, Natalie, Doc and I rode with Simon while Alexia rode with Gwen. On the way, Natalie starting whining about Doc being on her side of the car, which sounded exceptionally childish, not to mention that fact that in Simon\u2019s back seat, there\u2019s a console that neatly separates the right and left seats.<br /> <br /> It seems Natalie was making light of the sort of sibling scuffles that are common on long road trips when two children sit in the back. Once she explained what she was doing, I recalled some of my cousins in New Zealand doing something similar to antagonize each other on road trips. I suppose it\u2019s just my mental state, but it made me miss my mum.<br /> <br /> <u>Haunt: Glenwood Mausoleum</u><br /> The Glenwood Mausoleum was only a weak haunt with a minimum amount of residue and spiritual fluidity. I want to know what lies inside the underground chamber, and if we are to claim the haunt, we will need to enter it to gather the haunt\u2019s plasm. But claiming it might be a bit of an issue with an unfamiliar werewolf pack at hand. Perhaps we should appeal to Malard for advice again. I\u2019m certain he won\u2019t mind the cookies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Saturday July 31st<br /> <br /> -Morning. Bleh. AM for going to bed, PM for waking up.<br /> <br /> -Breakfast with the Krewe. Discussing options.<br /> <br /> -Hmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmmm this could lead to tears.<br /> <br /> -Ok so\u2026right. Well. The problem with being able to go anywhere in the world is you can go anywhere in the world.<br /> <br /> -Not that I won\u2019t go, mind.<br /> <br /> -Listening to Jasmine on the phone is painful.<br /> <br /> -My lady will try to help take care of my little girl if I vanish forever in a third world country. How sweet.<br /> <br /> -Vlog up.<br /> <br /> -Had to do that before Mini Me got up and about.<br /> <br /> -\u201cMini\u201d good lord she is tall.<br /> <br /> -She may get taller then that!<br /> <br /> -I mean she still may be shorter then anyone else in the Krewe, but she is taller then me damnit!<br /> <br /> -Telling Mini Me I had to go out for the afternoon seemed to go over OK. Fortunately she gets along with Karen.<br /> <br /> -She really wants to go clubbing. I told her I\u2019d think about it. Karen smirked at me.<br /> <br /> -The damn island was not exactly clubbing central.<br /> <br /> -I do not live on Natalie\u2019s pinkie finger, and Karen can cease holding hers up to imply such.<br /> <br /> -On the road again.<br /> <br /> -Are we there yet? Doc is on myyyyyy siiiiide.<br /> <br /> -OK, Jasmine did not think that was funny.<br /> <br /> -Grrr Simon needs to give me control of the tunes.<br /> <br /> -Siiiiimon\u2026ooooobeeeey the Nataliiiiiiiiie\u2026<br /> <br /> -Nope, mind control does not work.<br /> <br /> -My sweetie is taking Mini Me out to see New Haven<br /> <br /> -Sigh. Mini Me does not give up easy. So stubborn.<br /> <br /> -Wonder where she got that. :-x<br /> <br /> -It gets creepy, seeing someone who is <i>that much like you.</i><br /> <br /> -Karen says it is weirder for her, and we practically sit the same way.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s a good thing Spooky and I can\u2019t have a kid. We would have to murder them.<br /> <br /> -Heck, as is I can\u2019t imagine her having an easy time of her future offspring\u2019s teenage years whoever the other parent is.<br /> <br /> -OK, radio silence, got an investigation to do.<br /> <br /> -Goddess forbid anything should be easy.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LVIII<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Almost half the game time was spent discussing the 1.1 changes. The results of that discussion can be found in the previous entry.<br /> <br /> Oh let\u2019s see\u2026Mostly roleplaying. Lily remains more popular then expected. Trying to keep Natalie the Younger present but not hogging the spotlight so it is not an NPC party. I don\u2019t have a storyline, other then the obvious, attached for that reason.<br /> <br /> Our heroes are in Pure territory, that is always fun.<br /> <br /> Anyway, more coming soon, hope you enjoyed. See ya then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:24:25-08:00","id":16350,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s about that time again. Actually, it\u2019s past that time. Apologies. Please enjoy three accounts of last session, from the usual suspects.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1905 Hours, Saturday, July 31, 2010<br /> <br /> That was something. I\u2019m still trying to figure out what kind of something.<br /> <br /> Our next stop was St. Mary\u2019s. It was a fairly nice, if not particularly notable, parish. And I mean that not as an insult. Everything about this town is fairly low key and the Catholics were no different. The fence around the cemetery was closed and locked, which did seem a little strange since they would be having services soon. Unless Catholicism has changed since I was a boy...and I\u2019m pretty sure it hasn\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Snowflake became the graveyard again and pretty quickly found another mausoleum with werewolf marks, glyphs I think is the right word, scratched on the stone. It had the Danger glyph and Fire-Touched symbol. I remembered that one from Malard\u2019s Werewolf 101. Bad news. Nightshade took over the boneyard and immediately found another Avernian Gate in a different mausoleum. Lots of mausoleums in this town. The Gate was staying open because something female (ish) was moving in and out. Once she got a better look, Nightshade determined that this was a possible Geist, saying something in Latin. Snowflake translated after she spoke the words. It was some kind of prayer, but the cadence was wrong for normal Catholic prayers. That\u2019s probably why Nightshade didn\u2019t catch it. I\u2019m pretty sure she got irritated by missing that, but she\u2019ll be okay. I was technically Catholic once and I still haven\u2019t learned Latin. It\u2019s on my list though. Anyway, the place was a haunt with a ghost, maybe a Geist, holding an Avernian Gate open. That was all the invitation Rose needed. She climbed the fence like she was hopping over a baby gate and made her way toward the mausoleum before we could think of a good argument to slow her down. Ronin immediately pulled out her camera and slowly started lining up pictures of architecture so we would have a cover story if anyone questioned us snooping around. Nightshade kept watch and we kept communication through the ear curl. The ghost, almost definitely a Geist based on Rose\u2019s description, came out of the sealed tomb to greet her. We all tensed while Snowflake quickly translated through secondhand sources. Apparently the Geist wanted to touch Rose\u2019s face. She wore a sealed metallic mask, with generic features worked into the dark steel. Rose allowed the contact and I realized that the ghost was blind, either in general or because of the mask. That was her only way of visualizing who she was speaking with. It was a fairly common practice among the blind, though not what they did to people they had never met before. It\u2019s kinda like the difference between a handshake and a warm hug for a greeting. The Geist felt Rose\u2019s face several times, particularly her eyes before finally motioning for her to follow into the Gate. I knew as soon as we heard the translation that Rose was going to do it. <br /> <br /> Rose doesn\u2019t understand what it means to work in a unit. Her sport is a solitary one and she only knows how to rely on herself and the Bride. She thinks we\u2019re just worried for her, but it\u2019s more that than. Ronin is bad to be too aggressive but she understands me on this. Nightshade has some pretty strong convictions on the public consciousness involving preconceived notions of a woman\u2019s place. But she also realizes that, regardless of gender, you can\u2019t do everything on your own. I think of all of us, Snowflake is the most grateful to have others around; a surrogate family for him. Cupcake has some confidence issues but would rather not face everything we have to deal with alone all the same. Only Rose believes that she should be able to operate completely on her own and no one be upset or worried about it. Yes I walk the streets at night, looking for trouble. I\u2019m also looking to help people, normal people, that can\u2019t help themselves. Maybe I am a terrible hypocrite, but Rose believes that she can handle anything that comes at her, even in the Underworld.So far, she\u2019s been right. I know better and try to pick my battles. But she doesn\u2019t realize that she endangers the Krewe every time she goes off like this. We deal with powerful entities, things far worse than any of us have ever imagined. Soon enough they will learn. And when that day comes, we\u2019ll need Rose. But she\u2019ll be off by herself, confident that everything will be fine. I\u2019m getting preachy now, so I should stop.<br /> <br /> Rose made it back without a problem, but she did see some very odd things in the Underworld. The Geist led her across a narrow stone bridge over nothingness to what looked like a cathedral carved into the stone of the Underworld. There skeletal nuns had what looked like a baptism ceremony room with black water waiting. They were not hostile but more disappointed that Rose declined their offer. That explained why the Pure had broken then resealed the tomb. Some of the others thought we should go down and close the Gate. Normally this would have been up my alley, but the tomb was sealed with concrete. Sure I could open it with time and a sledgehammer, but if the Geist isn\u2019t taking people and they don\u2019t know to go in, I don\u2019t know that it\u2019s a problem. Plus, the Geist could just reopen it anyway. Rose looked shocked that anyone would want to close the Gate. I think she\u2019s grown closer to her Geist than to her own emotions, if that\u2019s even possible. Either way, she asked Snowflake and Nightshade to help translate for her through the ear curl so she could talk to the Geist. Through this awkward conversation, we learned the nuns wanted to baptise us to protect us from something called Garlise. Garlise was a particular something \u201cfrom Below,\u201d which we took to mean beyond the Rivers, one of the Dead Dominions. They nuns need help keeping it out. The black water, which is probably taken from the nearest River, seems to hurt the creature. That explained why they were using it to baptise others. The Geist calls herself the Beckoning Initiate. Rose told the Initiate that we would return and do what we could to help. Then she tagged the mausoleum with our own symbols. When she was finished the stone bore the mark of the Middle Shadows, Inhibited, Gate, and of course, Danger. After that, Rose climbed back over the fence and we loaded up to check out the toy shop.<br /> <br /> Ronin and I both, without prompting reminded everyone when we got to the shopping center that this was only recon. We were not here to challenge or engage anything. As if on cue, a scruffy guy started walking our way. He dressed like homeless people do with utility and durability in mind, but he just didn\u2019t seem like a vagrant. He warned us, since we were looking at the toy shop, to stay out. He was very cryptic without revealing anything and without being overtly threatening, but I could still hear it in his words if not his voice. He was likely a werewolf and that meant there were probably more nearby. Not a fight we wanted or could handle given we were all still nearly tapped out. He clearly knew something was up with us too, but didn\u2019t seem as concerned about that as keeping us out of the building with two Danger glyphs on it. One much bigger than the other. He said there were some teens that saw something in there, maybe we could go talk to them instead of anything involving going in. He mentioned it had been a bad couple of days. We made some very light introductions. His name was Ral and he was happy to let Rose tag the building with anything if it meant more people would keep away. This didn\u2019t really fit with Malard\u2019s description of the Pure, so maybe Ral was with a different pack or something. Either way, he was certainly trying to help. And then the problems started. Just when Rose started marking the building, the werewolf saw something and was suddenly bigger. Not all wolfed out, but beefier by a lot. He told us all to move away and it was an order. Before we could even think about it, the calliope music started from somewhere inside. I\u2019m not sure if it was my imagination or if Ral got even bigger as he followed us to the car, never turning his back on the building. When we were all in the car, he punched something into a smart phone. We pulled out and he kind of bolted back to the parking lot for the EB Games and leaned against a car like he\u2019d been there the whole time. Not the smoothest recon, but we all made it out and confirmed our target. Still a success, if a messy one.<br /> <br /> Rose asked that we check out the drive-in next. She said she thought it might be good for dates. I was very confused, but I couldn\u2019t see why this would be a bad thing. On the way, Nightshade opened up to all of us with a question she needed help with. Bella Donna was being rather persistent in trying to learn who her father was. In itself, that didn\u2019t seem like a bad thing. Nightshade told us that the father had no idea he had a daughter as she had never told anyone, including her mother. I knew she had gotten pregnant very young and the whole thing was very secret. I didn\u2019t realize that no one, including Bella Donna, knew the truth. The question was what to tell Bella Donna. Nightshade didn\u2019t think that anyone would be happy with the truth, but she didn\u2019t want to immediately start lying to her daughter now that they were reconnecting either. Ronin didn\u2019t see that as a problem, but then she can\u2019t remember her parents so that\u2019s not entirely surprising. Rose disapproved of course, but she didn\u2019t know what the best option might be. I broke with normal tradition and gave my opinion without anyone directly asking what I thought. I told Nightshade that she should just tell Bella Donna that her father doesn\u2019t actually know he has a daughter so knowing who won\u2019t help her. I don\u2019t know if that will slow Bella Donna down necessarily, but it is the truth. That\u2019s a start. Thankfully we arrived at the drive-in about that time so the subject changed. <br /> <br /> Apparently most of the Krewe thought Ronin meant a drive-in theater not a drive-in restaurant. That explained why Rose thought it might be a good date spot. The food was good, in the so horrible it\u2019s wonderful way. Rose and Nightshade were disappointed that it wasn\u2019t a theater, but otherwise everything worked out okay. After that, we stopped at an abandoned fairground, as it was old and it had a locked fence. I think maybe we\u2019re drawn to that. Cupcake jumped out and popped the lock with her picks, but it really just looks like she wiggles a finger on the lock. That will never not be cool to watch. Snowflake investigated the place using Boneyard and found signs that the local werewolves gather for rituals here. There was also a manifested ghost standing on top of the decrepit skeleton of a roller coaster. Based on his clothes, he died in the late 60s or early 70s. From what Snowflake said, it sounded like whatever killed him pulverized his face in the process. I\u2019m sure he\u2019ll be simple to deal with. That was enough for one afternoon though, so we headed back home.<br /> <br /> Rose is going to visit Jean and get a camera that reflected his parents. Snowflake can try to find out what\u2019s going on with them that way. Then we can see if they need help or if we can even help them. But now, I\u2019ll leave off. With Rose leaving, Cupcake is slinking around with a boardgame in her hands. I think there may be illicit game playing about to happen.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2345 Hours, Saturday, July 23, 2010<br /> <br /> Jasmine came back and Snowflake did his farseeing. What he could see wasn\u2019t encouraging. Jean\u2019s parents were alive but in a dark, warehouse-like place, surrounded by many others. They looked worried. Snowflake couldn\u2019t tell if they were hiding or being held prisoner. Either way, not okay. Rose became even more concerned and I knew she would want to go. I started asking the important questions. Can we speak the language. Cupcake speaks French so we\u2019re likely okay there. She also has the jeeps swallowed so that could be very useful. I know next to nothing about the Ivory Coast so I used the old maps Snowflake had and cross-referenced the satellite images Ronin could gather on her computer. Not only will I need to have some idea of where we\u2019re going, we\u2019ll need to have a clear picture of where to get Jean\u2019s parents to keep them safe. The US Embassy is the currently assumed safe zone, so they can claim political asylum. We\u2019ll go with that as Plan A, but it won\u2019t be the only one.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t like taking the Krewe into a warzone. This isn\u2019t a news flash. But in general, they haven\u2019t seen what war really is. Hollywood does a good job sometimes, but two hours with popcorn in your lap is moving, not scarring. Ronin has the slightest understanding, but even that is locked in her head. I thought the things I\u2019d seen during times of war were just a precursor; when I became a Sin-Eater and learned what my role was, I thought for sure I\u2019d find things much worse. I was wrong. I don\u2019t mean to say I haven\u2019t seen anything new or shocking. I have. But what I\u2019ve seen as a Sin-Eater is still a much smaller scale, if no more acceptable. What we\u2019ll find in the lawless area will be such cruelty that it breaks the people\u2019s will to fight. Others will be driven mad with rage, fear, loss, or some combination thereof. We are all broken in one way or another. But together we mostly mend as a family. I know what war did to me. I don\u2019t even want to write down what I\u2019m afraid will happen to the rest of the Krewe.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll stop here for now. Almost time to get more plasm. We\u2019re totally going to need it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, July 31, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> We spent the remainder of the afternoon investigating a second cemetery and the toy store where we now know the Puppeteer is hiding. The cemetery was connected to St. Mary\u2019s, a catholic church, and we had to be a bit surreptitious with outr investigation since the gates were locked and people were active in the church. We saw some more werewolf marks that implied great danger. Simon had a look around with his Boneyard, and discovered an open Avernian Gate inside one mausoleum that had been sealed with concrete. A powerful ghost, probably a geist, was wandering back and forth through the gate. Most likely, she was trying to keep it open.<br /> <br /> We argued a bit about whether to do anything about it or not, but I think we were all worried about what the geist might be up to, so we ultimately decided to check it out. But since we couldn\u2019t all go tromping inside for fear of drawing too much attention, we decided I would go check it out....carefully, of course. I scaled the iron-wrought fence and made my way to the mausoleum. Meanwhile Gwen began taking pictures of the architecture so that the group wouldn\u2019t look quite so suspicious standing there. There was no way to open the door without a sledgehammer, but as I was considering donning the Shroud of Stillness to slip through the wall, the geist emerged and confronted me.<br /> <br /> She was dressed in a long, heavy robe that obscured her figure, and her face was covered with a dark metal mask with no eye-holes. Her fingers were long and spindly, maybe twice as long as they should be. But she spoke soothingly in Latin, and when she reached gently for my face, and I got the distinct impression that she meant no harm. In fact, I realized that she was blind, and wanted to \u201csee\u201d me with her touch. So I let her explore my features. I also asked Simon to translate her Latin for me though our ear curls.<br /> <br /> She called herself the Beckoning Initiate and wanted me to follow her through the Avernian Gate. I knew it might be dangerous, but we hadn\u2019t really learned anything of value and the Bride and I were confident that she meant no harm, so I told the others I would be right back, and after summoning the Shroud of Stillness, I followed her. On the way, I paused for several moments to absorb the chi of the mausoleum, and it was nice to recover a bit of plasm.<br /> <br /> The Underworld opened onto a long, stony span over a vast, dark pit. I following the Initiate across the pit to a stone church that looked like a very old catholic abbey, partially carved into the stone walls of its surrounding and filled with candles that gave off reddish light. Inside there were skeletal nuns, and they also spoke to me in Latin. I couldn\u2019t understand a thing they were saying, so I tried to make it clear with gestures that I wanted to help and understand, but couldn\u2019t speak the language. They beckoned toward a basin filled with black water, but since I didn\u2019t know what exactly it was, I decided to leave for the time being. I gestured for the Initiate to follow me out again, and none of the ghosts there made a move to stop me. Perhaps it was just my imagination, but they may have seemed disappointed and saddened though not upset that I wouldn\u2019t do as they wished.<br /> <br /> Once I was back out of the Underworld, I had to endure a brief and entirely justified tirade from Gwen, who felt I was being reckless by following a geist into the Underworld alone. I agree that it was a bit daring, but I also felt that it was the only way we could find out whether the situation at St. Mary\u2019s demanded our immediate attention or not.<br /> <br /> But once I was out, I managed to communicate with the Initiate as best I could using Simon to translate and feed me lines in Latin to speak to her. It was a laborious process, but we managed to learn that the ghostly convent tried to beckon people into its church in order to baptize them in \u201cthe black water.\u201d Anyone baptized in the water becomes one of them when he or she dies, whenever that might happen. They are recruiting ghosts in order to defend against a powerful and dangerous entity called \u201cGarlize\u201d from below the Autochthonous Depths. Whatever it is, it sounds quite dangerous, and I think we all agree that we should do something to help the nuns, when we are able. But we won\u2019t be getting baptized. For one thing, I\u2019m not really willing to convert to a different religion. In any event, there was nothing to be done at the moment, so I wished the Initiate farewell with a promise to return and help, and I marked the Mausoleum with several of our krewe marks, claiming it as our own and noting the Avernian Gate and the danger.<br /> <br /> We then moved on to the toy store (I was under the mistaken understanding that it was a toy factory, but apparently that\u2019s not the case). It stood in an abandoned strip mall area, and though several other businesses flourished around it, it seemed very isolated.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t get too involved in investigating the place because it became quickly obvious from the faint calliope music that the Puppeteer was indeed inside. Moreover, we were approached by an unkempt yet ruggedly handsome young man named Rawl, who informed us that the place was dangerous and that we should stay away. Doc believes Rawl is a werewolf type known as the Pure, who are enemies of Mr. Malard\u2019s type of werewolf, which are known as the Uratha. The calliope music got louder after I placed the krewe mark for \u201cdanger\u201d next to the door (alongside more werewolf signs saying the same), and in response, Rawl started to transform, but didn\u2019t actually \u201cwolf out\u201d as Natalie put it. Odd expression, grammatically, but I suppose it says what it must.<br /> <br /> We believe the werewolves attacked the place after the Puppeteer arrived and were rebuffed. Also, people have gone missing there, but most recently a teenaged couple fled the place in terror, though apparently unharmed. Gwen is going to follow up on that lead by trying to contact them.<br /> <br /> On our way home, we stopped by an abandoned fairground which is said to be haunted, and found that it also bore werewolf marks. Doc and Simon seemed to think it was a werewolf meeting place, so we decided not to go inside, but we did see a ghost with a crushed head lurking on the rickety remains of an old roller coaster there. We also stopped by the drive-in that Gwen was so excited about. I was under the impression that it was a drive-in theater, and was enthused about that because those places have such a classic charm and, quite frankly, can be romantic and fun places to go on dates. Sadly, the \u201cdrive-in\u201d was a drive-in restaurant, not a theater, which also had its charm, but since I don\u2019t really eat the sort of food they serve at places like that, I was disappointed. Gwen certainly seemed to relish her hot dog, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, July 31, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> I brought dinner with me to Jean\u2019s apartment and spent a few of hours with him, just chatting and trying to keep him company and his hopes up. Unfortunately, I\u2019m not very good at cheering people up, so I don\u2019t know how much I helped. I think just being there was good for him, so that\u2019s something at least. I hope we can find out what has become of his family soon, and I hope they are okay. Jean did nothing to imply any romantic interest in me despite Gwen\u2019s suggestion that I would be sending a very flirtatious message by bringing food, but of course he\u2019s far too worried about his family. It is terribly selfish for a part of me to have wished he had shown some interest beyond what he\u2019s already shown. But I guess my own cold manner breeds the same in others. Certainly I dwell on that too much in my diary, but that\u2019s what diaries are for, aren\u2019t they? To dwell on the things that trouble or inspire us?<br /> <br /> I returned home to find the others gathered together and talking. I handed Jean\u2019s camera over to Simon, and he performed a ritual to scry Jean\u2019s family through the reflective surface of the lens. At that moment, his family were huddled in a large building with many other people. They seemed unharmed but quite frightened.<br /> <br /> I think that seeing their plight galvanized the krewe to do something about it. Doc and Gwen both agreed that we should go try to help Jean\u2019s family as soon as possible. We need more preparation before we go to deal with the Puppeteer, and though the Candle Cove show itself might be ending soon, at least the werewolves seem to be keeping people away from the toy store. Jean\u2019s family, on the other hand, needs help immediately.<br /> <br /> Doc isn\u2019t happy about us going into a war zone, and I completely agree. But we don\u2019t have any choice. So we will travel there tomorrow through an Avernian Gate using Doc\u2019s ceremony. I\u2019m anxious about it, but resolved to save Jean\u2019s family. If we can just find them and get them to the American embassy, that will be enough. And hopefully they can come to America as refugees to escape the unrest in their country.<br /> <br /> Several of us are off in a bit to visit some of our local haunts to recharge a bit before we head to the Ivory Coast tomorrow. We will probably need all the strength we can muster, though I admit that to some extent, the specter of mortal foes seems to pale in comparison to the mortal danger of real specters. It\u2019s the horrors of people killing other people that I\u2019m most anxious about. Doc has tried to prepare us for it, but he knows that his words cannot really steel us against what we might encounter. Perhaps we will all come out of this more hardened, and I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s a good thing. But it\u2019s worth it for the sake of Jean and his family.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>The Underworld</u><br /> <br /> There was another reason I did not shy away from following the Beckoning Initiate into the Underworld. I don\u2019t really fear the Underworld. It\u2019s not that I don\u2019t recognize how dangerous it is. I just don\u2019t feel like it\u2019s an entirely dark place, just different. I suppose my closeness to the Bride is to blame for this attitude, but that\u2019s not a bad thing. The Underworld beckons us a bit, and I find myself wishing to spend more time there. I certainly don\u2019t want to exchange it for the living world, but I somehow feel that I might be better served in my current state by striving for some sort of balance between the living world and that of the dead. Is that really so strange? My sympathies already lie more with the dead than with the living. And I suspect that in time the krewe will spend more time exploring the Underworld. If so, I would like to be more familiar with it so that I can ensure our safety while we are there.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that explains why I was so averse to closing the Avernian Gate at St. Mary\u2019s. It doesn\u2019t seem to be doing any real harm, not since the mausoleum is sealed, anyway, and when Gwen and Doc suggested closing it up so no one would accidentally wander in, the Bride and I both recoiled from the idea. Of course we don\u2019t want it to be a danger to mortals. But there\u2019s nothing wrong with the connections between the Upper Shadow and the Lower Shadow, not so long as we, the Middle Shadows, are here to balance them. Doc disagrees with me, of course, being a Gatekeeper. But I was able to convince the others to leave the gate be for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Younger Natalie\u2019s Father</u><br /> <br /> On the way home from exploring Glenwood, Natalie asked for our advice on whether or not to tell her daughter who her real father is. It is apparently someone the girl knows, but he doesn\u2019t know she\u2019s his daughter (Gwen was understandably dubious about just how ignorant he really is, though). I confess I was out of my depth with that, but after some of the others suggested she might obscure the truth by lying about it, I argued that if she felt uncomfortable telling Natalie, then she shouldn\u2019t. But she should be honest about it and about her reasons for choosing to hide the father\u2019s identity. I think Natalie has taken my advice to heart. I hope so, anyway.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Saturday July 31st<br /> <br /> -Graveyard #2<br /> <br /> -Oooh this one is pretty.<br /> <br /> -May not be much here\u2026wait.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t think this is a good idea.<br /> <br /> -At least Gwen is here and won\u2019t be able to yell at us if things go wrong.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -OK, I foresee the yelling, though \u201cus\u201d may be \u201cJasmine\u201d<br /> <br /> -Skeletal Nuns? What?<br /> <br /> -Oh it\u2019s just a Catholic little nightmare. How\u2026cute.<br /> <br /> -OK escaped with minimal grumpage.<br /> <br /> -Jasmine seems to not be deterred by being unable to speak the local tongue.<br /> <br /> -OK, the toy store.<br /> <br /> -Cap\u2019n Scruffy says go away.<br /> <br /> -Bet\u2019cha Capn\u2019 Scruffy is a Warwolf<br /> <br /> -His name is Rawl? Odd.<br /> <br /> -What\u2019s that Cap\u2019n Scruffy? Two kids? At the old creepy store?<br /> <br /> -OK, not investigating toy shop. Heard music, confirmed enough.<br /> <br /> -Drive-In next! Then necking! (wait, no necking)<br /> <br /> -\u2026Well, that is a Drive-In. Technically. Color me disappointed.<br /> <br /> -OK, gotta ask what is on my mind.<br /> <br /> -I almost got what I did not expect I guess. Maybe.<br /> <br /> -Maybe I am not a terrible mother after all. I mean, I am, but not in that particular way.<br /> <br /> -That counts for something, right?<br /> <br /> -Sure is a long car ride. I want to see my daughter.<br /> <br /> -They really don\u2019t want me taking Mini Me to a club do they?<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jog<br /> <br /> -Looks like we will start showing Jasmine Firefly.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me has not seen it either\u2026I guess she was a bit young when it came out.<br /> <br /> -o_o<br /> <br /> -\u2026why does my girlfriend embarrass me so?<br /> <br /> -Do Superman\u2019s friends make Kryptonite jokes to him?<br /> <br /> -They do not understand.<br /> <br /> -Seekrit gaming!<br /> <br /> -Spooky is back. I am almost disappointed she did not stay the night. Would have left her SO much less high strung.<br /> <br /> -But she is back so show.<br /> <br /> -Hrm. While I was getting the room set up everyone decided not to watch. Waaah.<br /> <br /> -Well, gonna hang with Mini Me some<br /> <i><br /> End Session LIX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add. The mix up with the \u201cdrive-thru\u201d totally happened when Gwen \u2018s player looked it up on her phone and mentioned it, then when we arrived and I started to describe it she clarified what sort of drive thru she meant. We Had a huddle and informally decided everyone misconstrued what Gwen said. Seemed more entertaining that way.<br /> <br /> The game this past Sunday was cancelled due to my being out of town for Vacation, same thing that made this post late. As such, no journals in two weeks. Fear not though, I will have something for you. A short fiction will be posted taking place between sessions 59 and 60 and concerning Natalie and her daughter, which gives more of Natalie\u2019s backstory and sets up a little wrinkle for the PCs when they get up the next day. Do drop by. Comments and Questions in the meantime are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:33:48-08:00","id":16353,"title":"","content":"There was no game 2 weeks ago due to the wife and I being on Vacation. However I have a story for you, which takes place between Session 59 and Session 60, with the two Natalies. Enjoy, and I will see you in two weeks unless someone has a comment or question for me which are welcome as always.<br /> <br /> <b>Being Mary Magdalene</b><br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026and you are going where tomorrow?\u201d Natalie asked as she plopped down on her mother\u2019s bed. \u201cI really can\u2019t say,\u201d the elder Lousler girl sighed. \u201cIt\u2019s complicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay. Anything else you can tell me about these people you are going with? You don\u2019t say much about them.\u201d<br /> <br /> The elder Natalie sighed. \u201cI rarely do sweetie. OK. Who do you want to know about? I won\u2019t say too much about them though, not my business.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAll of them.\u201d<br /> <br /> I should have guessed,\u201d The elder girl began brushing her hair. \u201cWell, Doc is the most reliable, the sanest. If you have to trust someone, trust Doc. If you have to talk to someone who is not Karen or I, talk to Doc. He is a former soldier and medic. He was over in Afghanistan, which is a real hellhole.<br /> <br /> \u201cYikes\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut he is here now. Doc looks out of all of us. He is our doctor and our tactician. He reminds us to be cautious. And occasionally keeps us from strangling each other. He is a hero, and a great man. He gets tongue tied easily but don\u2019t hold that against him. I trust him with my life.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou seem to think the world of him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do; I hope Doc stays in my life for a long time to come.\u201d Natalie paused several moments. \u201cGwen next. Gwen is an ex-cop, and she still has all the biases that come with that. She is nice and tries to be caring, but she can be pretty abrasive. She used to be a lot more abrasive apparently though\u2026.I did not know her then. I doubt we would have gotten along. She is an odd combination of reticent and reckless. Outside that, she is pretty good with computers and a crack driver, though I don\u2019t recommend trying to drive like her. Outside of her team resume, She likes sports a lot. And apparently arguing with Jasmine here recently.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKaren seems to like her\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrust me I am aware,\u201d Natalie sighed. \u201cKaren has interesting taste in women.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe really likes you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2026doesn\u2019t mean her interests in women are healthy. Karen attaches to strong personalities and she likes to, uh,\u201d Natalie paused. \u201cAnyway Gwen acts like a lot of the dykes I know and would get along with them even if she were not so cute. But she approaches dating like a tee-er, like a fifteen year old,\u201d Natalie corrected herself quickly. \u201cDon\u2019t look to her for dating advice. She has some frankly unfair opinions on how men should behave in courting a girl, and this is me saying that. Now, not all of us are terrible to ask for dating advice. Actually anyone but her and Jasmine are fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger girl grinned, \u201cYou had a thing for Jasmine didn\u2019t you? Don\u2019t deny it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell she IS cute. Jasmine is the only one I will mention her dating status\u2026she isn\u2019t. Unfortunately, I don\u2019t see that changing. At this point she is in love with being in love, and has standards no man, or woman, is going to meet. Unfortunately, her personality is such that that is a major identity pole for her. She sees herself by her dating status and who her mate is, which means she will likely be miserable for some time. She really is broken that way, and I\u2019d love to fix her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI bet\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026yea I am not going to date Jasmine ever. I can\u2019t say I\u2019d kick her out of bed or have no attraction to her, but I don\u2019t need to deal with the baggage of trying to date her. I mean I\u2019d love to help her but she is stubborn, and that stubbornness is going to keep her miserable for the foreseeable future. There\u2019ll probably going to be a chain of &quot;not good enough&quot; men come into and out of her life, who would be dynamite husband material otherwise. I\u2019d\u2026I\u2019d really like to help her, but I can\u2019t, and it breaks my heart. I just try to be there for her as a friend. She could be a perfect forlorn Goth ideal, but I\u2019d rather Jasmine be happy than be that ideal. But I don\u2019t know how to make her happy. She needs a submissive man or woman who won\u2019t want to argue with her because she is so stubborn to make the relationship work, but she is not attracted to submissive people. That plus her standards means she won\u2019t be happy anyway, and I am helpless to change it\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYea, on the plus side,\u201d Natalie put down her brush, \u201cShe is really good at keeping us organized, and great in a fight. Did you know she had been an Olympian?\u201d The teenager shook her head, \u201cYea, in swimming. Jasmine is more than eye candy. \u201c<br /> <br /> Younger Natalie smirked, \u201cYou seem to have sized up everyone.\u201d \u201cIt\u2019s something I do,\u201d her mother replied. \u201cAlexia is the eldest of us, just as Simon and Jasmine are the youngest. You\u2019d never know it from how she acts. I swear that girl tokes when I\u2019m not\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTokes?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSmokes Marijuana.\u201d \u201cAh.\u201d \u201cAnyway never seen her toke but she acts like every pothead I know except she is full of energy. Some people have an inner child. She has an inner adult.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know she is with that Chandra girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYea\u2026.figured you would notice. I swear, Gwen completely set off my \u2018dyke alarm\u2019 and Alexia totally snuck under the gaydar. I have never struck out for finding family like I did with those two. Anyway, Alexia is a chef. She cooks pastries, which keep me fat. She provides sugar and cheer in large quantities, and offsets Jasmine\u2019s gloominess. It\u2019s even a bit much for me at times. \u201c<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Simon?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026this is Simon\u2019s house. He is the scion of a large and old family, with a lot of old houses and a lot of old secrets, more than you know. Heck, more than he knows. Simon almost functions as the outsider looking in; he keeps things in perspective as only someone who is unfamiliar with our folkways and mores..\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026with how people usually behave,\u201d Natalie made a note to scale back her vocabulary, \u201c he can sometimes point out how strange our behavior is. We kept a normal person for that but they ran off screaming.\u201d The pair laughed. \u201cSimon is very knowledgeable on the occult, which is good in the ghost investigating biz. He is fairly smart too, just in general. Of course, Simon is also very unsure of himself\u2026a lot of people are at his age. I was.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWill I be?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know. I hope you are better off than I was though.\u201d<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> After a bit, the younger girl asked \u201cSo you used to be really really Christian. What happened?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her mother\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cThat was a long time ago dear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, but I\u2019d like to know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell\u2026it\u2019s embarrassing but you are my daughter so\u2026fuck. OK. When I had you I admit I felt I\u2019d failed somehow, you know, as a Christian. I mean, I fucked a guy I barely knew and got knocked up. Someone mentioned the whole Mary Magdalene thing to help me, and how she was accepted by Jesus despite her sins. So I latched onto that. I\u2026latched on a little too much.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat does that mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Goth sat down in front of her vanity mirror. \u201cI read up, and read enough especially with the whole wedding that clearly she and Jesus hooked up and got married. If you read the Gospel according to John, you will find where they asked Jesus about wine at the Marriage at Cana where the bridegroom is unlisted, and he provided it. That suggested he was organizing it\u2026perhaps like he got married. This was before the Dan Brown shit you may have heard about that made that famous. The Gospel according to John does not specify, but I assumed it was to Mary Magdalene who asked, because they were marrying. I figured if a woman could go from being a harlot to marrying the son of God I had hope too.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnyway I started identifying with Mary Magdalene a lot.\u201d The elder girl avoided the question. \u201cThat was my online name. I had a couple \u2018pictures\u2019 of her, and I think in my mind to some degree I was her. Not a reincarnation exactly but\u2026parallel?\u201d Anyway\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> The dark haired girl closed her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cI discovered, when I was fifteen that Mary Magdalene was never like that. Some sexist fuckhead, specifically Pope Gregory I, said she was a prostitute to discredit women. She had illnesses cured but Mary Magdalene was a good and perfect girl, not some whore like me who got knocked up. Jesus never accepted a sinful girl into his bed, and he would never accept me. And I\u2026couldn\u2019t take it.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie slowly opened her bi-colored eyes, blue and green reflecting her daughter.<br /> <br /> \u201cI took a lot of sleeping pills. They took me to the hospital. I could never explain. How could I? I looked like a fucking loser,\u201d Natalie closed her eyes again, \u201cI was being watched closely by my parents, who were freaking out, when sometime in my depression I watched The Craft. I was almost sixteen. At the time I believed it, maybe, sorta, but it was more a gateway into Paganism than something showing truths itself. I discovered that there were gods and goddesses who did not loathe girls who liked sex. I became Pagan while sixteen. I never stopped believing in God, but I ceased to be His follower. We just disagree too much about women.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve\u2026I\u2019ve never told anyone about this. Not Karen, not Doc, not Sonia not Christina, no one.\u201d Natalie opened her eyes once more. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026not pleasant.\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger girl looked overwhelmed. \u201cWell\u2026but it\u2019s OK? And sex is good I guess?\u201d<br /> <br /> Her mother laughed. \u201cIndeed, I recommend it. But be careful sweetheart. Don\u2019t have sex with men unless you are on the pill. Be careful about sex with anyone. Protect yourself. I won\u2019t say don\u2019t do it, because it is wonderful, but be careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Pot is OK?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow about you finish High School before trying any drugs? Pot isn\u2019t bad, but don\u2019t try it just now. I don\u2019t recommend harder stuff, like Heroin or Cocaine. And don\u2019t do any Speedballing, whatever you do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHeh why not Speedballing especi-,\u201d Natalie Lousler looked up at her mother sitting in front of the vanity mirror, and her eyes widened. Her words died in her throat as she took a step back her hands over her mouth.<br /> <br /> After a moment\u2019s paralysis, she turned and ran out of the room.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:34:20-08:00","id":16354,"title":"","content":"Hello folks, it is time to look at our friendly neighborhood ghostbusters and what they are up to. Doc and Gwen\u2019s players had to miss last session, so Jasmine has the bulk of the info with Natalie giving her perspective as per. Doc has a short story about his activities. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> They sat in the office, laptops and cellphones fully charged. Spread out on the table between them was a World Time Zone map with several circles penciled in. They both wanted information, but their channels were very different.<br /> <br /> Gwen focused on contacting various embassies to verify all requirements for asylum requests. Doc looked more toward On-the-Ground intel and terrain. After several late night phone calls to the Naval base, Doc was directed to a non-military line.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes sir, Colonel Dupree please.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo sir, I did not realize that was you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaster Chief Hospital Corpsman Torrenz, sir. Retired....Medical Discharge. Yes sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYe...yes sir. IED. Thank you sir. I had no idea you were at my award ceremony sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo sir, I don\u2019t miss the desert weather. Connecticut suits me all times of year.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell Colonel....yes sir. Frank. ...Doc is fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was told through channels that you might know some information I\u2019m looking for.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo sir, I\u2019m not looking for the Iraqi gold... I\u2019m sure it is very annoying sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was asked to assess a situation by a civilian acquaintance... No sir, I don\u2019t work in contracts, but I can understand the confusion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would like to know anything declassified you might be able to tell me about the Ivory Coast.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry to hear that sir... Yes I believe I may know of Petty Officer Brison. Admin on the base, yes sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. Well thank you sir. I\u2019ll be sure to tell Brison \u2018Frank said hello\u2019 for you sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEnjoy your afternoon sir. I hope the consulting keeps up for you. Yes sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc hung up with a resigned sigh. He glanced over at Gwen as she talked on her cell and searched the Internet relentlessly at the same time. Sliding his own laptop back toward him, he decided to go back to studying maps between the village and the embassy.<br /> <br /> At a point much closer to dawn than Doc would have liked, he noticed a new email notification on his laptop. Opening his new message, he found a single line of text from <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#4220302b312d2c322d2c02252f232b2e6c212d2f\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"284a5a415b4746584746684f45494144064b4745\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>.<br /> <br /> \u201cFrank said hello.\u201d<br /> <br /> Attached to the message were several compressed files. Opening each in turn, Doc\u2019s eyes widened a bit.<br /> <br /> \u201cGwen, wake up! I need you to make my laptop connect to your printer.\u201d<br /> <br /> Lifting her head with one eye open, Gwen growled as the glow of dawn began to paint the wall behind her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, yeah. I\u2019ll go make you coffee. I need to print this stuff out though so let\u2019s go.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc smiled and left the room as she flipped him off and grumbled unintelligibly.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, August 1, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> We have decided to postpone our trip to the Ivory Coast for a day. After a night of preparation, Doc and Gwen discovered that they needed to do quite a bit more to get ready for the trip, and decided to spend today making further arrangements. Hopefully, the additional preparations will help to ensure our success and the safety of Jean\u2019s family after we\u2019ve rescued them.<br /> <br /> However, that was hardly the highlight of my morning. When I went into the meditation room to meditate, I found younger Natalie there. She looked frightened and distraught, and seemed not to have slept at all last night. I do recall hearing her run past my room last night, but thought nothing of it at the time, even after I heard Our Natalie following her.<br /> <br /> I asked her if she was okay, and in response she asked if her mother was dead.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t quite know how to react, and I think I must have stumbled over my words a bit, because she followed her question up by explaining that while talking with Our Natalie last night, she had seen an image of her mother\u2019s death in the mirror and then, when she looked at Natalie, she saw her as a walking, talking corpse. Frightened out of her wits, she fled.<br /> <br /> I had to try and explain that Our Natalie was not dead, and what she had seen was a near death experience that had almost claimed her mother\u2019s life. But I assured her that Natalie was just as alive as she was. I could not explain why she saw Natalie as dead, but I tried to comfort her by sharing that I too had sometimes experienced visions of others\u2019 deaths, and that it was such a vision that cost me my husband.<br /> <br /> As I was sadly hinting at my own story, she screamed, backing desperately against the wall of the room. I looked around to see what was the matter, but she was staring wide-eyed at me. She cried out, \u201cYou\u2019re dead too!\u201d I tried to calm her down, and managed to keep her from fleeing, but she screamed about my broken neck, and that\u2019s when I realized that she truly was seeing me as I must have looked when they dragged my body from the pool, neck broken and head flopping loosely to the side, skin pale and blue, lungs overflowing with water.<br /> <br /> Somehow, I managed to keep her from completely breaking down, and with gentle words, I helped her to understand that we weren\u2019t dead, but that something strange and supernatural had happened to us, which explained why she sometimes saw as dead. I don\u2019t really remember what I said to her or how I convinced her to trust me, but somehow I managed. She would not look at me, though, and kept her eyes tightly shut as I guided her back to her room and tucked her into bed to get some sleep. The poor dear was exhausted, and fell unconscious almost immediately.<br /> <br /> Of course, after I finally meditated, I went downstairs to inform Simon and Alexia about what had happened. Karen was there too, and she told us that Natalie was abjectly heartbroken over her daughter\u2019s behavior, and was blaming herself for being such a terrible mother. Perhaps it is a bit cruel of me, but it did cross my mind that Natalie is quite justified to think such things. After all, she did abandon her daughter to run off and attempt a drug-addled career, and left her daughter under the care of the same people whom she claims damaged her childhood so badly. In my opinion, Natalie has been a terrible mother. But that sort of accusation will do no good now, so I kept those thoughts to myself. And, to her credit, Natalie is sincerely trying to make up for the errors of her past, and I intend to do what I can to support her in her efforts.<br /> <br /> We asked Karen to send Natalie down whenever she awoke (she had fallen into a tearful, exhausted sleep as dawn approached). In the meantime, I explained my encounter with younger Natalie to everyone else, and Simon made the observation that she must be able to see some sort of death echo when we thought about our own deaths, which was apparently what was happening when she saw her mother\u2019s corpse-visage as well. It\u2019s very odd, and Alexia had a minor fit about how difficult it is to avoid thinking about something when you know you aren\u2019t supposed to be thinking about it. She certainly didn\u2019t want younger Natalie seeing the swollen-tongued visage of her poisoned corpse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, August 1, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> I spent the morning reading. I feel as though I haven\u2019t had enough time to do so lately, but worry for Jean\u2019s family plagued my thoughts, making it difficult to focus on my book. Meanwhile, Alexia gardened and Simon made his Sunday rounds of the cemetery.<br /> <br /> When Our Natalie awoke around noon, we gathered in the kitchen to tell her what had happened. She was quite relieved to learn that it was nothing she had done, but was quite concerned for younger Natalie. We realized that we would not be able to hide the truth from younger Natalie for long, and resolved to tell her what we were. However, we feared that she might decide to try and become one of us if she knew that those who suffer visions of death are more likely to become sin-eaters, so we agreed not to tell her about that detail, and to make it very clear that it was sheer luck that any of us were granted a second chance at life.<br /> <br /> Younger Natalie awakened soon after, and we told her what we could. Natalie explained that having died awakened supernatural powers within us, which is what makes us such good paranormal investigators. She accepted it rather easily, though she was distressed that her mother had tried to commit suicide. I explained that all of us lived only because we wanted to live; Natalie\u2019s desire to live for her daughter gave her a second chance, and that is the most important thing.<br /> <br /> We have decided to visit the yacht and take it out for a short cruise to relieve some of the tension and to make younger Natalie feel more comfortable again. Then later this afternoon, while we wait for Doc and Gwen to return, we plan to visit the safer local portions of the Underworld, perhaps to visit the diner we heard about later and connect the mansion\u2019s Avernian Gate to the rest of our current map. I\u2019m looking forward to it, as I\u2019ve been wanting to spend more time in the Underworld and learn better how to navigate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, August 1, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Alexia, Simon, Natalie and I delved into the Underworld this afternoon and evening, and were able to find passages connecting the Darkhaven Bluffs Avernian Gate to the rest of our map. Natalie opened the gate for us. Alexia and I cooperated to navigate, and I was glad to have her experienced eye to help me as I learn. Simon kept our maps.<br /> <br /> We could hear the sea nearby, and decided to find a way to the coastal Underworld before making our way to the Underworld diner we had heard about before. On our way to the former, though, we encountered another tableau. This one was more disturbing than the skeleton-filled lecture hall we encountered before. An gore-soaked Native-American sat with a pot of boiling human body parts, eating from his macabre stew despite the tomahawk in his back that was bleeding his life out. We examined the tableau and Simon realized that it was an admonition against gluttony; the feasting indian could have saved his own life by removing the weapon in his back, but chose to feast instead.<br /> <br /> We soon encountered a cliff-like drop off and made our way down the treacherous ledges toward the sound of waves below. Alexia slipped and nearly fell at one point, but I managed to catch her. Eventually we passed by a cave-like chamber filled with a statue that resembled the fish-god that rests beneath the mansion, and it was surrounded by strange mudskipper fish with children\u2019s faces. Simon thought they were cute, but I thought them rather grotesque and worry that they were symbolic of the Fishbornes.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we came to a beach on the edge of a vast subterranean sea. In the distance, anchored just off shore, we saw two old sailing ships. One was battered and worn, the other clean and new. I felt oddly compelled to investigate the battered ship, and when I looked closer, I noticed it was called the Richard. For Simon, it was named for his father, and Alexia and Natalie also saw it named for someone or something important that was lost to them.<br /> <br /> We realized that venturing onto that ship might well reunite us with what we had lost, but that succumbing to that temptation might well mean never returning. And there was no way to know if it was real or a trap, so we agreed to turn from the ships for now. I tried to keep my head about me and do the wise thing, but my desire to venture onto that battered ship and let it take me to Richard or to my doom was almost overpowering.<br /> <br /> Eventually, we left and returned up the cliffs to the more familiar parts of the Underworld, making our way to the library and then to the diner itself. It was a very charming 50\u2019s diner, run by a ghost with piled hair who looked like she belonged there. Both Simon and I decided to order some of the food, which was quite good. I had a milk shake that tasted exactly like the best milk shake I\u2019ve ever had, one I shared with Richard in a little restaurant in California during our honeymoon. Simon had an entire meal, but Natalie and Alexia refrained from eating anything. All it cost was a bit of plasm or a bauble from the mortal world; I paid with the little panda trinket attached to my cell phone.<br /> <br /> We also met a ghost named Janice in the diner. She was clad in a luxurious fur coat. She seemed to know something about the prior krewe of sin-eaters, and Natalie jumped on the opportunity to learn more. However, Janice was only willing to tell us what she knew in exchange for a service, and she gave us several options:<br /> <br /> \u2022 We can get her information on her descendent (daughter? granddaughter?), Alicia Walstone, and find out what happened to her fur coat, the one in the mortal world. If we find it, she wants Clarissa, her great granddaughter (our short-tempered psychic) to have it.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Alternately, she might simply want to visit the world. She has no anchor there anymore (which implies that her coat may not even exist now).<br /> <br /> If we can do one of those things for her, Janice will share what she knows. She was kind enough to give us a bit of information on the local underworld, free of charge. We already knew about the library and diner, and had just discovered the coast. According to her, if you follows the coast far enough, you will reach a river that leads deeper into the Underworld, or maybe one of the rivers that divides the Underworld (I wasn\u2019t quite clear on the details). This is good news for us as it might make finding the Athenaeum easier when we finally journey there.<br /> <br /> Janice also told us that above the library, if one goes high enough, is the Manor. The manor is a mysterious place. Most never enter it, for it can only be entered by invitation. Those who are invited in are never seen again, though Janice wondered if this wasn\u2019t because they were simply too happy there to deign to return to the lower Underworld. I suspect the truth is rather more unpleasant.<br /> <br /> After spending an hour in the diner, we said our goodbyes to Janice and headed home to find that Doc and Gwen had returned. Tomorrow, we will go to the Ivory Coast. I called Jean a short while ago to tell him I would be unavailable for his training sessions for the next few days because something important has come up and I have to go out of town suddenly. I encouraged him to continue his training regimen without me. I know he probably feels a bit neglected right now, but that doesn\u2019t matter if I can help save his family.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Seeing Death</u><br /> I feel some empathy for younger Natalie and her plight, because of course I grew up seeing premonitory images of death too. My own experience helped me to understand and talk to her about the things she was seeing. It truly is a curse. Were it not for such visions, both Natalies and I would no doubt have had much happier childhoods, and I might not have lost Richard.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>A Solution for Gwen</u><br /> As we discussed younger Natalie\u2019s visions, Simon and I both suddenly realized that if younger Natalie can see the circumstances of our deaths by looking into a mirror while we are thinking of those fatal moments, then she might be able to see who killed Gwen! If she can, then it might allow Gwen to track down the fragments of her past and come to peace with her death.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u><br /> Surfing</u><br /> Somehow as we were hiking through the Underworld, surfing came up, probably because of the coastal nature of the Underworld near Darkhaven Bluffs. In any event, I mentioned how disappointing it was that the local beaches aren\u2019t really good for surfing because of Long Island, and said I\u2019d like to visit somewhere with good waves and surf again. It was something Richard and I sometimes did together, and I miss those times, surfing in California or on Honeymoon Bay in Taiwan.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Battered Ship</u><br /> I cannot get my mind off the battered ship that might reunite me with Richard again. How am I to move on now that I know there might be a way to be reunited with my husband? Even if he is dead, even if the ship might be a trap to ferry me off to my doom, isn\u2019t it worth the risk to see my Richard again? To sink into his embrace and lavish him with my kisses? The only thing preventing me from venturing onto that ship right now is my responsibility to the krewe and to others who are still living. But I must know if that ship can really take me to Richard, and there may be only one way to find out. Doc and Gwen might think me foolish and rash to even consider taking that ship to shores upon which wait my lost love, but they don\u2019t understand\u2014they can\u2019t understand the pain and desire that compels me to do whatever it takes to find once again the one I have lost.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets<br /> </b><br /> Sunday August 1st<br /> <br /> -I feel like I have been hit by a truck spiritually and emotionally. That is to say, I feel much better than last night.<br /> <br /> -Apparently Alexia is our Tavia handler.<br /> <br /> -No Vlog right now, am busy.<br /> <br /> -\u201cBusy\u201d serves as a good euphemism for completely shagged out.<br /> <br /> -How did I ever even get by without Karen to help me? I am not sure.<br /> <br /> -Soon as the kidlet is up gonna have a sit down.<br /> <br /> -And here I am pacing again. I thought I got over that.<br /> <br /> -OK here goes. Gonna go quiet a bit.<br /> <br /> -That could have gone worse<br /> <br /> -She is awful nosey about\u2026a certain thing though.<br /> <br /> -Some mothers only have to worry about normal conversations with their daughters.<br /> <br /> -A boat? What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -My daughter wants pictures of herself taken on a Yacht to post for high school friends at home. She is far too much like me. =-O<br /> <br /> -I can never stay away from the sea.<br /> <br /> -This is what being born on an island does to you I think.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t especially want to go back can we stay out a bit longer.<br /> <br /> -Need to do a \u201cV on the Sea\u201d at some point. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Gotta get ready for some exploring.<br /> <br /> -Magnesium flares scare me. Need big flashlight.<br /> <br /> -Grrr am not steady. Damn hands.<br /> <br /> -Jasmine has shorter shorts than I do. What is wrong with this picture?<br /> <br /> -OK going incommunicado for a bit.<br /> <br /> -And back. Home again home again jiggity jog.<br /> <br /> -Gonna light a candle for Persephone when we get there.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Doc's Log references his background.<br /> <br /> The Gwen thing honestly came to me while discussing what Young Natalie sees. It was not pre-planned.<br /> <br /> Younger Natalie does indeed see Sin-Eaters as dead sometimes when their death crosses their minds. This happened when Natalie brought up Speedballing, and Jasmine referenced her death. If there is a mirror, the death plays out there\u2026both Natalie\u2019s see/saw people who were going to die soon in a mirror as dead versions of that person (Elder Natalie referenced seeing the results of a car accident which traumatized her). This will make younger Natalie a bit awkward to have around. It also came up she may or may not see something truly frightening with Chandra. Natalie insisted she had not committed suicide when she died (though she freely admitted to having attempted it before then) but was behaving recklessly as she did not fear death at that point. Younger Natalie attempted to challenge her with details but Elder Natalie ended the conversation angrily.<br /> <br /> And the underworld excursion was always fun. Poor Alexia has a rough time with any mental resistance rolls (she is kinda a cream puff) and physical are not really her forte (but the same could be said of Natalie or Simon). Still her notably low mental resistance stats came up a couple times. Alexia saw her mother's name on the ship, Natalie the name of a girl she had an unrequited crush on who died of an overdose.<br /> <br /> Also, Tableaux are fun.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll see you next time, but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:35:48-08:00","id":16355,"title":"","content":"OK you folks ready? It\u2019s Geist journal time, Heart of Darkness edition. Note given Natalie is not tweeting there her part only covers events up to heading into Africa.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Session LXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019 Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1645 Hours, Monday, August 2, 2010<br /> <br /> I was up a good bit of the night and into the morning, so we all slept in today. We wanted to make sure when we got to the Ivory Coast it would be sufficiently dark to help hide our movements. I got up around 1300 Hours and went to meditate. I knew I would need everything balanced before I returned to live combat. There have been easier things to do than will myself into a state of calm knowing I\u2019m about to lead five of my closest friends into a death trap.<br /> <br /> An hour and a half later, I walked out of the Meditation Room centered, but not at peace. I met the others as they were trying to prepare. It struck me how much like a military unit we\u2019d become. Ronin got everyone a black Camelbak. They looked suspiciously like our hydration units in Iraq, but maybe REI sells the same models now. Nightshade had her knife and was loading her pistol. Ronin was already locked and loaded. Snowflake reminded me we had some magical prep work to do. Cupcake looked as afraid as any first time soldier about to be deployed, but she tried to help with anything she could. I hated myself at that moment.<br /> <br /> Just then Rose came in and I pulled her into the Drawing Room to talk privately. I knew that the only time I would be able to talk with her about my concerns was while I was calm. This was the only shot. I explained that I don\u2019t doubt her abilities at all and I didn\u2019t want to sound like I was in any way condemning her. I remained as even toned as when I had to amputate. Describing to her how I knew her sport was predominantly a solitary endeavor, I then gave her examples of how we may need her as a team. I didn\u2019t want to wear the sports analogy thin, so I switched to more military terminology. With her going off on \u201cindividual missions,\u201d the rest of us were weaker. I told her that where we were going, her skills were going to be greatly needed. But she needed to remember the Krewe she left behind before she moved ahead. I watched as realization settled over her ashen features. She thanked me for explaining it to her this way. I simply nodded and told her that I wanted us all to come home as close to the way we left as possible. Then I gave her a hug. She didn\u2019t pull back or act shocked. I think she realized how afraid I am for everyone. After that, we joined the others back in the entry hall.<br /> <br /> Nightshade had something to show the girls when I was leaving with Snowflake to cast our magic. Snowflake talked to me about what he had enhanced with his own magic. Given our extra equipment and the fact that most of us suck at being quiet, being lucky while sneaking seemed like the best option. I was glad he was there to help me decide. The only things in my head were bullet wounds, explosions, and death. When we finished and joined the others, all the girls except Nightshade looked like they might be sick. I decided it was better I didn\u2019t ask. Karen was keeping Bella Donna away while we left, but when I saw her last she was a nervous wreck. Sometimes I really wonder how she can manage with all that she\u2019s forced to deal with. My respect for her grows even faster than my pity.<br /> <br /> With Tavia and Chandra tasked with keeping the House \u201csafe,\u201d we made our final equipment check. Camelbaks and bulletproof vests for all, then any individual weaponry. Ronin also had a GPS. I had my Mossberg fully loaded and packed another 30 rounds in my fatigues. My survival knife was strapped to my leg and I was ready. Now we\u2019re going to storm the Cote d'Ivoire.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Tuesday, August 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t felt this kind of anguish and rage since I died. I want to have that fully loaded M60 again and just unload it into the patrols and guards. I don\u2019t even care that they are kids. What these people are doing \u2026 I have to focus or what I\u2019ll do will be just as bad as they are.<br /> <br /> We moved to the House Gate and I started by writing the name of the village on the stone wall. I kept writing the arcane symbols around the inside of the Gate until after about half an hour my Sepulchre Gateway finally opened. I warned everyone that we had to stay on the path. Anyone that got off would be lost in the Underworld. That made everyone very nervous. Then we joined hands and all walked in. I\u2019d never actually used the ceremony before so it was a little surreal to move through this bizarrely silent tunnel through the Underworld. The bones making up the path did not help that sensation anymore than the three or four ghosts that stared in from the edge of the tunnel as we continued. We moved along our osseous road for twenty minutes before we came to another Avernian Gate. I looked back at everyone to make sure they were ready. Fearful nods were my only response.<br /> <br /> We emerged into complete darkness and were hit with a smell that made my soul ill and my blood boil. Rotten flesh. The air was thick with that putred scent. I tried to keep everyone calm as I knew this would not end well. Surprisingly, it was Ronin that puked until she was dry heaving. I moved to the sound and held her doubled over form until she could manage to stand. There were no jokes this time. I needed her to know it was okay and she would be all right. Of course she was pissed off, but not at me at least. I told everyone that we were in a mass grave and that we were going to have to find a way out. After everyone was as prepared as I could make them, I let the heat from my mounting anger ignite into the Pyre-Flame Shroud. The white-hot ghost flames wrapped around me and formed full tactical armor. But more importantly, my protection also lit our surroundings. The bodies were piled up on all sides and above us. The ravine was filled and the Gate we exited was merely a flat spot in the earth. I could feel my compassion singing from the heat of my own rage. We noticed moonlight coming from one corner. Before I could make a move, Cupcake drew her cleaver and said she\u2019d get us out. I started to ask if she was sure, but she cut me off, held up her weapon, and told me again that she\u2019d get us out. I stepped back and told the others to turn around. The skill that Cupcake had with hacking the bodies apart was appalling and I\u2019m not entirely sure she hadn\u2019t been taken over by The Cracked Cook. Relentlessly, she chopped through limbs and torsos, steadily opening an escape route from that disgraceful tomb.<br /> <br /> When we could finally climb the hill out, we found ourselves standing on the edge of a camp. While Cupcake wiped away as much of the gore as she could, we looked around. There were two buildings surrounded by trees. The camp looked abandoned, but given the number of bodies in the ravine, that wasn\u2019t surprising. We heard soft whimpering in one of the buildings so Cupcake, Ronin, and Rose went to investigate. They found two little girls, the oldest might have been 16, the younger closer to 10, huddled against the far wall. They were wearing only dirty shirts and were obviously terrified. Just before they entered, I noticed Rose stopped short and they all backed away. The door had been booby trapped with a grenade. Since Cupcake could speak the language, we had her call into the building and tell the girls to turn away from the door. Then I sent Rose to flow into the room and talked her through disarming the cowardly bomb. When she opened the door, Rose held the grenade uncomfortable in her hands. I took it and clipped it to my Camelbak strap. I knew just how to use this and had no problems with doing so at this point.<br /> <br /> Through Cupcake, we talked to the girls and learned that those that did this were not from a familiar tribe and didn\u2019t speak French. The uniforms they described suggested Liberian Mercs. I knew nothing good would come from here out. I had Cupcake explain that I was a doctor and wanted to make sure they were okay. I sent Snowflake away, kept Cupcake near, and had Nightshade stand behind me. By this point, it was obvious the girls had been savagely raped and Nightshade easily made it known with her very presence that no man would be able to harm these girls while she was there. This put me at the mercy of the strong women and made me less of a threat. Both girls were bruised and dehydrated but were physically intact otherwise. I gave them each some water from my pack; I could make no claim on their mental state, but through Cupcake I assured them we would make those responsible pay. Nightshade was so enraged when I stood again, she trembled. She looked straight through me and mumbled about all the zombies she could raise from the ravine. Her broken phrases were filled with half formed threats of killing anyone that stood against us. I told her that wasn\u2019t helping, but I doubt I sounded convinced myself.<br /> <br /> Snowflake scouted the grounds surrounding our position and found the other building had a few supplies but it was also booby trapped. Since no one was inside and I still had my Shroud up, I moved to the door and disarmed it. That\u2019s two grenades for me. Inside we found two AK-47s and three full clips. Ronin seized both assault rifles, threw one strap across the opposite shoulder each, pocketed the clips and then turned around. I have seen Ronin happy, grumpy, and just plain pissed off...she\u2019s always fairly intimidating. But nothing has ever been as frightening as the look of unwavering cold she had right then. There was also some fresh clothes and half melted chocolate bars which we gave to the girls. We could all hear helos in the air but none seemed to be getting any closer. Using the GPS and my study of the maps, we determined the camp was roughly three miles south of Jean\u2019s village. That gave us all the intel we needed right then, so we explained that we were moving to the girls and told them they had to be very quiet. There was no way we were leaving them behind even though they would endanger us even more.<br /> <br /> We moved about 20 minutes north through the jungle when we found the first tripwire. I disarmed it after Cupcake calmed the girls again and added a third grenade to my makeshift bandolier. After a few more minutes, we stopped again. This time due to voices speaking heavily accented English. Everyone looked to me for orders, so I sent in Rose. She looked at me with appreciation and I knew she was thinking about our talk from earlier. We couldn\u2019t use the ear curls for fear of being picked up on enemy communications, so it was radio silence. Normally I would have been really worried and impatient for Rose to get back. But here in the jungles of Africa, I knew that silence was our shepherd. Rose eventually returned with perfect intel. Ten mercs, children really. She estimated them to be aged 10 to 18. The leader seemed to be the oldest and he also had a strap of hanging grenades. The others were all heavily armed with pistols and more AKs. They moved back and forth, which I explained was part of a perimeter patrol. Apparently they radioed in over walkie talkie every 2 minutes. The person they spoke to on the other end had a French accent. They seemed to become much more tense when they neared the highway to the west and stayed hidden. I thought it would be best to get a more complete view of the area, so we activated Snowflake to scout the greater target zone. It became very apparent that we had come at a time of a standoff. The forces in the village and all points south were apparently government and mercenary troops. Snowflake reported between 30 and 50 soldiers while they kept roughly 100 villagers as prisoners. They were separating people by gender in the hotel. It seemed to Snowflake they were keeping potential \u201csoldiers\u201d (ie children) with the women. The men were less likely to survive at all. There was a definite tension between the leaders and the soldiers in the south as if they were expecting two different things. We pieced enough together to determine they were looking to move. The several buses which were little more than exploded piles of scrap helped in that regard. While he couldn\u2019t see all of the forces to the north, he could easily determine they had many more men fielded versus the superior armaments of the south. The soldiers to the north were on guard, but far less tense. The lesser number of machine guns did not diminish their capability given they outnumbered their targets. Snowflake also pointed out a Jeep driving through the mostly untraveled village. It was a patrol of southern forces and three of the riders carried RPGs.<br /> <br /> After processing all this information, I took a moment to think what we could do. As I crouched in the jungle, I heard the sounds of birds over the distant helos. Glancing over, the girls seemed terrified of every noise around them. And then I understood what we had to do. Mercs and governments forces alike were tribal and already very tense. In general, tribal people have a tendency to be superstitious. Yes that\u2019s horribly stereotypical of me. I\u2019ll be sure to ignore it the next time someone addresses me as \u201cHey, Mexican\u201d as punishment. Anyway, we figured out how most of us could cause the most psychological disturbances to the morale of the soldiers while others helped secure the hostages. First we need to cross the highway to the west and hide the girls in the jungle there. Once we confirm they\u2019ll be safe, I will call the birds into the village to suddenly act very strangely. If a few soldiers suddenly start bleeding from their orifices, Ronin and I will be pleased. Snowflake can cause all sorts of illusions to terrify and break the ranks. Cupcake can control and maybe even explode several of their vehicles. Ronin can focus her rage to break their will through fear. Nightshade can raise some of the bodies Snowflake found outside the village as zombies and I just won\u2019t ask what they will do. Plus she can use her own magic to call in a sudden fog to help cover our movements as well as further spook the soldiers.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t jinx us and say we\u2019re golden, but I do feel more comfortable with our 50 to 6 odds right now. We\u2019ll see how upbeat I am once this is over. We\u2019ll also see if Nightshade and I come home with new undying servants.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s time to move.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, August 2, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> We are about the head to the Ivory Coast. We spent most of the day resting. I\u2019m quite anxious about it, because I know we might encounter some terrible things of a wholly mortal nature, and that upsets me. Doc\u2019s warnings about the horrors of war have certainly had an impact.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve packed bottled water, granola bars and a few other things for the trip to Africa, though when I saw the preparations others were making, I felt as though I wasn\u2019t prepared enough. Doc provided us all with kevlar vests. At first I wasn\u2019t going to accept one, but it didn\u2019t seem to get in the way too much, so I decided to wear it after all.<br /> <br /> Natalie cornered the women in the krewe privately and offered us a sort of\u2026rape deterrent device, as well as morning-after pills. She\u2019s quite worried that if things go poorly, the women in the group might be raped, and sadly, she\u2019s probably right to be concerned. But I couldn\u2019t really accept what she offered us. Well, I took the pills, but not the\u2026other thing. Unless I\u2019m unconscious or completely drained of plasm, I\u2019m certain I can escape any would-be rapists. Gwen and Alexia also took the pills, just in case. The experience rattled me a bit, not just because of what Natalie offered us, but because it made the dangers we might be facing much more real.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 2, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We are in the Ivory Coast, and have just laid plans for a massive rescue which we hope will free Jean\u2019s parents and some of the other captive innocents.<br /> <br /> We traveled through Doc\u2019s sepulchral gateway and arrived in a charnel pit that held the rotting bodies of a fifty or so dead. Emerging into such a horrifying place brought the reality of what we were facing crashing down on us. We all reacted differently. Simon remained somewhat detached, as always, and Doc very much became the soldier. Natalie became uncharacteristically quiet. Once Gwen got over being sick at the sight and stench, she was all business, and I think Alexia withdrew and let the Cracked Cook take over. As for me, I could almost feel something shift inside me. All the anxiety I had been feeling before we arrived evaporated, only to be replaced with a cold, steely determination that, now that I reflect on it, is a bit frightening. Once this is all over, I may very well have a breakdown, but for now I\u2019m focused.<br /> <br /> Alexia moved some of the bodies and made a way out of the charnel pit. The pit lay inside a small village. It was abandoned, probably because everyone had been killed by the rapacious mercenary forces we soon<br /> learned were operating in the area.<br /> <br /> Actually, it wasn\u2019t completely deserted. There were two girls, about ten and sixteen, trapped inside a small shack. We heard them whimpering from outside, and I quietly crept up to have a look in through the hovel\u2019s single, small window. The place was rigged with a grenade, which would go off if the door was opened. Alexia talked to the girls from outside the shack, telling them to shield their eyes, while I phased through the wall and, with Doc\u2019s coaching, disarmed the makeshift bomb.<br /> <br /> The girls were starving and dehydrated. They had been beaten, raped, and left as bait for a cruel trap. The people who did this are monsters, mercenaries who work for the corrupt government forces. Natalie seethed with barely contained anger, and kept muttering to herself about raising a zombie army to slaughter every last soldier in the country. After what we\u2019ve seen, I can understand her feelings, but it was still a bit scary. I wonder if we didn\u2019t made a mistake bringing her. Her post-traumatic stress could make her do something unwise, and we can\u2019t afford any blunders here.<br /> <br /> We gave the girls water and food, and took them with us as we left the village and moved north toward the nearest town, where Jean\u2019s family are. They believe we are U.N. agents. I\u2019m not sure what we will do with them when we enter the town, but we can\u2019t take them into that war zone with us.<br /> <br /> Using night\u2019s darkness for cover, we moved through a wooded area until we heard a group moving ahead of us. Doc sent me forward to investigate, and I crept close enough to see a patrol of about ten people, mostly well-armed adolescents. Their disarrayed uniforms marked them as mercenaries. They didn\u2019t seem to want to move past a nearby highway. When I returned to the others, Simon dropped into a boneyard trance to have a look at our surroundings and the nearby town, part of which was just inside his range.<br /> The opposition forces are to the north, while the government and mercenary forces are to the south. The government forces seem to be preparing for a withdrawal, and helicopters provide constant air cover for both sides (we can hear them quite clearly). The opposition forces hold the hospital, and are tending to wounded with the help of U.N.-affiliated doctors. The government forces, however, are better-armed. Doc believes they are withdrawing for strategic reasons, possibly because more U.N. support is on the way.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, they have a couple hundred people, including Jean\u2019s family, held captive in a hotel. There are about forty or fifty mercenary soldiers holding the hotel, and they were separating the men from the women and children, moving each to different floors. Gwen, Doc and Natalie suspect that they are waiting for trucks to take the women and children away as slaves and future soldiers, and they will probably kill all the men. They must be stopped.<br /> <br /> We spent the next half-hour deciding what to do. We decided to unleash the force of our supernatural abilities to cause a panic among the superstitious mercenary soldiers as a distraction. Natalie is going to create a few zombies after all. Even though the zombies won\u2019t stand up to armed men with machine guns, they should frighten and demoralize the mercenaries. She also plans to use her hedge witch magic to summon a spooky mist throughout the town. Meanwhile, Simon will use ghostly illusions to keep the soldiers off-balance and scared, while Doc will call upon the birds using the Primeval Marionette, bringing flocks of them into the town as a bad omen. Alexia will take control of several military machines, possibly even a helicopter, and use them against the mercenary troops.<br /> <br /> Under the cover of those distractions, those of us who can will attempt to infiltrate the hotel. Gwen and I are responsible for that part of the operation, and my job will be to find Jean\u2019s family while neutralizing any guards I encounter. The prospect of fighting and possibly killing other living people instead of supernatural horrors or spirits is unsettling, but I\u2019m focused, and will do what I must to ensure the safety of Jean\u2019s family.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Team Player</u><br /> <br /> Doc spoke to me in private as we were making final preparations. We had a long talk about my tendency to operate independently\u2014things like going alone into the Underworld to investigate the chapel or chasing after Black Shuck on my own as a flock of birds.<br /> <br /> Doc expressed his confidence in my abilities, but he also said that I need to be more aware of the krewe as a team. I\u2019m a part of that team, and regardless of my faith in my own abilities, I need to remember that if I go off to take care of something on my own, I\u2019m leaving the rest of the team \u201cin the lurch\u201d as they say. I realized he was right when he pointed out that my sport, swimming, is largely independent. I rely on myself and no one else\u2026except for relays, of course, but I almost always swam in solitary events. I don\u2019t really have much experience with team sports, and I\u2019ve spent much of my life on my own, until I met Richard, of course. I suppose I hadn\u2019t realized how much that has affected the decisions I make.<br /> <br /> I understand better now why Gwen has been so upset with me recently. I\u2019m thankful we have someone like Doc who is observant and wise and can not only see these things, but also knows how to talk to us in ways we can accept and understand. I mean no offense to Gwen, but she simply doesn\u2019t have that talent, not when she\u2019s angry, anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Civil War</u><br /> <br /> The forces at war in the Ivory Coast include the corrupt government forces, which have hired a number of Liberian mercenaries. They are opposed by the opposition forces that are trying to liberate their country. The opposition forces are supported by the United Nations, which I suppose makes them the lesser of two evils, although I wonder if they would be any better than the government forces if they weren\u2019t so worried about losing U.N. support.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday August 1st<br /> <br /> -OK the others are here.<br /> <br /> -Planning, planning.<br /> <br /> -Well they seem to know what they are doing\u2026<br /> <br /> -Ha talked everyone into sleeping in! Will Doc and Spooky manage?<br /> <br /> -I won\u2019t know I will be dreaming little Goth dreams.<br /> <br /> -OK I think we have a plan.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -OK, got the last night on earth speech. Ta-Ta!<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday August 2nd<br /> <br /> -I am so not ready for this.<br /> <br /> -But I will go.<br /> <br /> -Short Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Karen is keeping Mini Me calm. She knows something big is going down but has been\u2026quiescent since the whole dead people thing.<br /> <br /> -Poor Karen is a wreck though; she just does not want to show it.<br /> <br /> -I know what it is like having to be tuff.<br /> <br /> -OK time to try to protect the girls.<br /> <br /> -I may have traumatized Spooky.<br /> <br /> -I really, really hope it will never be more to them then Natalie being paranoid and stupid. I hope they never see the need for what all I offered.<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s see, gun, ammo, bulletproof vest, ritual offerings, all ready!<br /> <br /> -If we wind up stuck in the dark least I got candles!<br /> <br /> -OK, radio silence. I hope you will be hearing from me in a few hours.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLI</i><br /> <br /> Well wasn\u2019t that something.<br /> <br /> The device Natalie offered the girls was a Rape-aXe \u201canti-rape condom.\u201d She had two. Natalie has issues. Also, morning after pills and pills to dehydrate slightly and reduce the need to urinate so they would not have to be \u201cvulnerable\u201d in forest.<br /> <br /> The PCs needed to disarm two relatively simple IEDs with grenades and fishing lines. I was a bit worried about the first one as the PCs did not send Doc near the house and thus operated at a large (-4) difficulty to detect it (Doc would have had no penalty due to experience). Fortunately, it was spotted anyway. Granted, this is New WoD, and Grenades don\u2019t really do that much damage all told. I mean it would be grim to have several hit but one is not going to kill anyone, even Simon.<br /> <br /> I will note, in the interests of transparency, that I got some dates wrong. The civil war in the Cote d'Ivoire does not begin until December with the elections in the real world, not the end of July. So yea, I got some dates wrong. Decided to leave it going anyway. World of Darkness, very mysterious, blah blah bah. I\u2019ll note too I stressed that in many places it looked more western then some folks may have expected\u2026this is not the bush, this is more forest with fairly western style cities.<br /> <br /> I was pleased that the group, cautious to begin with, was even more cautious here. This is not a situation to enter half cocked, and the role-playing lent the situation an appropriate amount of gravitas I think.<br /> <br /> Well I think that covers everything. Folks will be here soon for the next chapter, so there you go. If you have any questions or comments they are, as always, welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:57:28-08:00","id":16372,"title":"","content":"Hello there, Apologies for the late posting, but we had vacations for two players which delayed play for a day, and apparently journaling. But here we are with journals from folks covering further operations in Cote D\u2019Ivoire.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0400 Hours, Tuesday, August 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what\u2019s causing the most trouble here. Either we are more unskilled than I think or this mercs are special forces. At least I\u2019m only bruised from all the bullets...for now.<br /> <br /> I summoned the birds of the area and gave them their orders just as Nightshade\u2019s fog rolled into town. The birds and fog together should have unnerved most of those mercs that were pressed into service. At least, that was the plan. If they were rattled, they damn sure didn\u2019t show it. I managed to sneak into the village, dodging patrols and remaining behind cover without any problems. My intention was to wait until we were ready to move and then sow more horror and/or pick off an patrols I could while the others prepared the hotel for our attack. Before we were ready, I heard an explosion coming from the direction Ronin and Rose headed. I didn\u2019t give my position away, but I did find one of the Jeep patrols and they were on heightened alert. They must have spotted Ronin as I doubt anyone could have seen Rose. I cut my hand open and threw the blood droplets in the direction of the driver of the fading Jeep. Through the fog, I heard some screaming and then the Jeep stopped. That at least worked, so I moved in. When I was close enough to see my targets, I noticed the driver trying to stop the bleeding while the others had their weapons drawn and were searching. Before I could do much else, Rose appeared from the fog and started screaming at them to attack her. That definitely got their attention, but I shot one before they could level one of my Krewe. Another started bleeding and I knew Ronin was around. Unfortunately, I also heard a chopper coming. One of the other soldiers threw a grenade into the building while the others turned their guns on me. I guess Ronin was hiding in the building. I shot the one throwing grenades to keep him from catching Ronin without enough cover. Before I was completely mowed down, Rose turned into this massive wave and crashed into the two remaining soldiers. They were pretty beaten up from getting hit with that much force and bouncing around the concrete and Jeep. But not enough that they didn\u2019t unload their machine guns on Rose. I shot the remaining guy holding the RPG, which was still loaded when he fell. Unfortunately, we were not quiet and before I could really do anything but turn around, two more Jeeps pulled up behind me. They each had 3 machine gunners, 1 RPG soldier, plus the drivers. They spread out when they realized I had my own grenades, but that wasn\u2019t helping me any. A third Jeep with the same personnel reinforced them as two helos moved into position between the buildings above me. I knew this was not going to end well. Rose screamed for me to run just before she crashed into as many of the soldiers as she could with another of her giant tidal waves. One of the helos opened up on the remaining guns trained on me and I realized at that moment that Cupcake and Snowflake were in position. One of the mercs fired his RPG at the chopper while three more machine guns opened up on Rose. She didn\u2019t seem to even register the bullets, though I couldn\u2019t tell for sure. There was still several machine guns pointed at me. When the shit went down, I dove for the shop window across the street. Between the bullets, the shattering glass, and the rubble already scattered across the cement flooring, I was less than happy. I Bulwarked most of the damage, but I was grateful for the vest. I finally managed to put up my Primeval Shroud and crawled to what would have to work for cover. Someone used our makeshift click radios to let me know they were circling the building. Great. I heard the click code to hold as I was looking for a way out. I guess Nightshade\u2019s Zombie Horde was almost in position. I had just run out the back and down the side alley across the street when the government forces ringed my last position. The grenades and machine gun fire told me I got out just in time.<br /> <br /> We regrouped to let Rose heal up a little. Apparently she fakes being okay better than I thought. Ronin watched over her while she soaked in a tub for just short of two hours. She could heal up that way and made me feel less worthless as I was out of Plasm again. Snowflake watched over the forces and gave us a better idea of troop movements. 36 inside the hotel, 9 outside, and all heavily armed. This is fabulous. I was waiting for the Zombie attack to start before I moved in, but before anything could start, the two helicopters moved over to the hotel and that was unexpected. What was a little weird was that they weren\u2019t flying normally, like someone either didn\u2019t know how to fly or was having real trouble with it.<br /> <br /> I knew just when the Zombies moved in because the screams from the hotel preceded three waves of gunfire. I was impressed they were disciplined enough to fire together like that. The Zombies were still up when I heard the chorus of firing pin clicks. I came out of my building and noticed one of the choppers had drifted away from the hotel. The other was still seeming to have trouble but remained over the hotel. I decided to chance it and moved to engage. Snowflake informed me that there were 11 men with grenades in the hotel waiting for the Zombies. Nightshade pulled them back and I fired into the group of soldiers struggling to get back inside the barricade hotel. When the Zombies started reciting the Apostle\u2019s Creed I knew we were going to have some wait time. I\u2019ve been writing this against the corner of the building across the street where I have a 4-corners vantage. I just hope Rose and Ronin are doing okay inside. It\u2019s getting a little too quiet...except for the Zombies.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Dairy<br /> </b><br /> Tuesday, August 3, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> Things have not gone exactly as planned in our supernatural attack on the hotel. That\u2019s not to say that things didn\u2019t turn out okay, but we certainly drew more attention than we had hoped on our approach.<br /> <br /> We set about enacting our plan well enough. Simon, Alexia and Natalie tracked down a warehouse where the mercenaries had been tossing their dead, and then Natalie raised them as zombies to attack the hotel as a distraction when the time was right. Natalie also used her witch magic to summon a thick fog to both give us cover and to unnerve the mercenaries. Doc called upon the birds to swoop into town and frighten the soldiers with bad omens.<br /> <br /> Then we made our approach to the hotel. Simon and Alexia quietly infiltrated a nearby four-story building that gave them a good view of the hotel\u2019s surroundings so that they could interfere with the mercenaries\u2019 machinery. Doc made his own way toward the hotel to back up Natalie\u2019s zombies once they began to attack. And Gwen and I approached the hotel\u2019s far side, which was barricaded against intruders but would hardly pose an obstacle to us.<br /> <br /> But that\u2019s when things went wrong. I was shadowing Gwen invisibly, but as she crossed from one alley to the next, a patrol happened by in a jeep and they caught sight of her. They fired a rocket grenade at Gwen, but we were both able to dodge to cover without only minor injuries. Then the patrol came barreling in and cornered Gwen inside the building she had chosen to hide.<br /> <br /> I was confident Gwen could escape through the back as long as I kept the mercenaries from pursuing her, so I made myself visible and charged at them, screaming to draw their attention. Gwen used her Stigmata Rage to force the blood from one of the soldier\u2019s bodies. Unfortunately, at the same time, Doc barged out of an alley further down the street and began firing blasts from his shotgun and using his own Stigmata powers to kill a couple of the mercenaries.<br /> <br /> The mercenaries fired their machine guns and rocket grenades at me, but I had already shifted into my Tear-Stained Caul, and combined with my Shroud, most of their bullets either passed harmless through me or were caught up and dispersed in the veils of the Bride\u2019s dress. A few tore at me, though, but my wounds were still minor, so I transformed into a spiraling, crashing torrent of water and swept over the soldiers, knocking them off their feet and badly bludgeoning them. That got their attention and they forgot all about Gwen, who was able to get away.<br /> <br /> A few more jeeps showed up then, each loaded with more soldiers. I would have turned invisible and escaped then myself, but Doc\u2019s presence made that impossible. I could tell from the spectral vapors that steamed from his wounds that he had already bulwarked several hits, yet he had not manifested his Shroud! Had I left him, his bravado would have gotten him killed. So instead of disappearing, I again turned into a torrential burst of water and smashed into a group of mercenaries who were about to unload their automatic rifles on him. The force of the water blew them off their feet, but they quickly recovered and shot at me instead. Even with cover and my supernatural defenses, a few of the bullets found me, and I was forced to turn invisible to escape.<br /> <br /> But my sacrifice had bought Doc enough time to flee. He jumped through a window into a bullet-ridden building and escaped unseen. I wish he hadn\u2019t come out to attack. If he hadn\u2019t, Gwen and I could have escaped rather more cleanly, and I wouldn\u2019t have nearly died. I suppose he had the same idea I did, but he never should have taken such a risk without his defenses up!<br /> <br /> By the time we escaped, helicopters had arrived as well, but it seems that Alexia and Simon took care of them. One of them even fired on the mercenaries, no doubt thanks to Alexia\u2019s ability to possess machines.<br /> <br /> As it was, I was in bad shape. All in all, I think I withstood a dozen bursts of machine gun fire and a couple of rocket grenades fairly well, but I was still bleeding badly from several wounds and the pain was immense. I was also a bit shaken. I\u2019ve never been attacked so ferociously by other people before, and it was unsettling. Getting shot at rattles the nerves. But I quickly recovered my composure.<br /> <br /> I found Gwen doubling back to help Doc and me, and stopped her. I became visible again, and practically fell against her as she helped me away from the mercenary patrols. She asked how bad it was, and I told her honestly that it was \u201cpretty bad.\u201d But I knew that if I could just get to some water, the power of my caul would let me recover from my wounds in an hour or so. We would have to delay the attack, but I wouldn\u2019t be much good otherwise.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m writing this entry as I\u2019m soaking in a bathtub in an abandoned residential building. Gwen is keeping guard while I heal. I can feel my wounds knitting, almost as though the Drowned Bride\u2019s gentle fingers as caressing them away. I just hope this delay doesn\u2019t cost us.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 3, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> We resumed our approach to the hotel. This time, though we still had to dodge a few more patrols and lie low a bit, we managed to make it in. I phased through the wall and made my way invisibly to the fourth floor, then lowered a rope for Gwen to climb up. On the way up, I scouted the area and discovered that the women and children were locked in rooms on the 3rd floor, guarded by two soldiers, while the men were locked on the 2nd floor. They were also guarded by two soldiers, but three others were setting explosives. They planned to simply kill all the men after they had evacuated the hotel with the women and children! They truly are monsters!<br /> <br /> While Gwen was climbing into the hotel, Natalie had her zombies attack from the front, and Doc stood ready to move in after them. The distraction kept the bulk of the soldiers occupied. All Gwen and I had to do was take out the few guards left to watch the upper floors. I had shifted into my Primeval Shroud and moved on one of the 3rd floor guards, taking him by surprise and knocking him out quickly and quietly. Meanwhile, Simon, it seems, sank into a Tear-Stained Boneyard trance and assisted Gwen by making the other guard feel as though he was drowning. He went down without much of a fight.<br /> <br /> We then made our way to the 2nd floor. As on the 3rd floor, I silently rendered one patrolling guard unconscious and Gwen similarly dispatched the other. Simon, meanwhile stopped the remaining guards, the ones setting the bombs, with his Boneyard. While they were rendered helpless, Gwen and I disarmed and bound the guards we had knocked out. We were about to do the same to the ones Simon had immobilized, when we heard a group of soldiers moving up the stairs from the first floor, apparently concerned that they hadn\u2019t heard in from the upper story patrols.<br /> <br /> But Gwen knew what to do. She gathered the grenades the unconscious mercenaries had been carrying and made her way to the stairwell while giving me the nod to go ahead and take care of the three guards who had been setting the explosives. I could only assume that Alexia was keeping the helicopters busy outside and that Doc and Natalie were okay below\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Killing</u><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never seen people die like I have here, and several at the hands of my friends. I\u2019ve become accustomed to slaying supernatural creatures. It seems necessary. But killing other people affects me differently, and the indifference with which Doc and Gwen seem to do so is shocking, though I imagine they are not so much indifferent as hardened by their experiences on their respective battlefields.<br /> <br /> And yet, the horrors these mercenaries have wrought upon others are unforgivable. I can\u2019t help but feel that they deserve death for the evils they\u2019ve committed. I have yet to kill anyone myself, and hope that I do not have cause. But if I do, how will I feel? How will it affect me? The Bride and I represent the Resolution of Death, and I know that I have steeled myself to kill before. In the back of my mind, I am prepared to kill Tavia, if the need arises and her paintings cannot be stopped. If I am prepared to do that, then I should easily be prepared to kill one of these horrid mercenaries if I must. Resolve is not something I lack.<br /> <br /> But the aftermath of the act is what I fear. Resolve will only carry me through the act itself. Once it is done, I will have to deal with the remorse of having taken another mortal life.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday August 2nd<br /> <br /> -OK, radio silence. I hope you will be hearing from me in a few hours. <i>6 hours ago</i><br /> <br /> NAREK @NatalieKnight- I miss you honey I love you. Please be alright.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XLII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Well wasn\u2019t that exciting. Obviously we did not finish Cote D\u2019Ivoire that time.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s weather witchery was a result of her picking up Weather Control (actually delaying Psyche 5) as she is a Witch. The idea was to use it to penalize perception rolls and apply a creepy, unnerving backdrop to the siege.<br /> <br /> I should note Gwen is in no way incompetent nor was her player unprepared, nor did she make any foolish errors. It was a matter of terrible luck. Even with the \u20132 penalty on Perception rolls the soldiers got she was still spotted and was unable to get away from them. Later she was told she simply had to pass a Stealth roll to get by them and they would not be able to roll to spot her unless she failed due to guard positioning and Natalie\u2019s weather effects. She still failed\u2026a couple times. Again, not due to craptastic stats or poor planning but awful luck. The plan was pretty sound\u2026well, except Doc charging headlong into a group of troops without a plan to get out.<br /> <br /> At this point Doc is out of Plasm and Gwen and Jasmine have it, IIRC, in the single digits. So it has gotten tense. Also, with Alexia around, it seems it is safer outside a helicopter or jeep then inside it. Odd thing with fighting Sin-Eaters I suppose.<br /> <br /> I am not exactly sure how they are going to solve this one but it should be exciting to find out. No \u201ccausalities\u201d so far, either temporary deaths or loss of Synergy, but it remains to be seen if that will last.<br /> <br /> This yarn will be wrapped up next time. You should come check it out. In the meantime, if you have any comments or questions lemme know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T17:59:20-08:00","id":16373,"title":"","content":"OK it is time to finish the Africa leg of our storyline, at least those parts taking place in Africa. The conclusion and our\u2026protagonists\u2026return is the subject of<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXIII<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0130 Hours, Tuesday, August 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I should know better than to mention when it\u2019s quiet or going well. I might remember it after this.<br /> <br /> I reloaded after I finished the last entry. Then I started hearing explosions from inside the hotel. They weren\u2019t coming from the lobby but that didn\u2019t help us any. Nightshade sent in the Zombie Republic at that point before shadowing them into the lobby. I followed just after that as I figured the zombies would keep everyone\u2019s attention. Just inside the door, I crouched down beside a splintered luggage cart and looked around. It looked like a zombie apocalypse movie. There were roughly twenty soldiers trying to keep the walking dead at bay. Two of the zombies were down but one of the soldiers that had fallen was getting back up and trying to eat the other mercs. I know that would have terrified me. Just then, two AK-47s opened up from the entrance to the stairs. I hadn\u2019t seen them before, but they obviously got a good look at me. Based on the number of holes, I think I got hit with full auto. I couldn\u2019t bulwark and I couldn\u2019t pass out, so I stumbled back out the door. Leaving a trail of blood, I shuffled back to my building corner and slid down the wall. Snowflake came over the radio to let us know five of the mercs were running out the back. I looked at my shotgun and remember shaking my head, just to remind myself I couldn\u2019t stop them.<br /> <br /> There were four more explosions from the back. That was hopefully the men trying to clear their own barricade. I had to smile at that. At least the plan worked before it was too late. Ronin checked in. They were okay but there were still explosives in place upstairs. Snowflake confirmed the mercs were blowing their way out and were decidedly on the run. Unfortunately, Snowflake also alerted us to the buses heading in. Four of them actually. One driver and one heavily armed soldier each. Great. I dragged myself inside the building so I couldn\u2019t be a sitting duck when they got to me. And I also bandaged myself to staunch the bleeding.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how long it was before I heard the buses pull up. I had kind of zoned out from blood loss I think. I got up and watched from the window as four soldiers with machine guns got off the bus. They were very cautious, weapons at the ready, as they moved forward. One stayed with the buses as the other three advanced on the door. Just as they opened it, one of the zombies ran at them. Zombies, at least Nightshade\u2019s zombies, are tough, but not three machine guns at point blank range tough. There were more gun shots from inside too. I thought one of them sounded like Nightshade\u2019s pistol. I had to do something to keep those machine gunners from finding her in there. The windows were all boarded up but there were a few open spots. As quietly as I could, I got a grenade ready. It was hard to stand up so throwing was a joke. But I didn\u2019t have any other way. I threw the grenade with everything I had and then fell against the side wall. It went off and then there was a weird sound from somewhere to the left of my window view. I could only see that a stream of water was running down the street toward the hotel. There was more small arms fire from inside the hotel and I could hear the zombies but no one was coming back out. For a second, the engine of the bus in front stalled out. I couldn\u2019t think about that very long because more machine gun fire tore through the hotel lobby. Then everything was eerily quiet. I heard the buses and my own heartbeat...and that\u2019s it. I jumped when Snowflake broke that silence over the radio when he and Cupcake warned us of real commando units coming from the north on foot.<br /> <br /> I knew I couldn\u2019t stop the buses from leaving, but I was hoping Cupcake was still on top of that. Rose and Ronin came running out of the hotel and moved for the buses. Rose leapt up on top of the first bus and tried to drag the driver out the window before he knew what was happening. She was still all whiskers and muscle so I was surprised when the driver didn\u2019t fly out. Then I realized he was strapped in. Laughing hurt, but it was almost worth it. Instead she jumped through the window and ...I don\u2019t know what she did once inside the bus. Ronin also took a direct route, though more her style. She moved into line of sight with the drivers and ordered them out at gunpoint. I don\u2019t know if they spoke English or not, but that\u2019s never stopped Ronin before. The driver in the third bus got out and put his hands behind his head. The second bus driver tried to be a hero and drive off but his bus swerved into a building. He didn\u2019t look great but he fell out the doors and ran off. The first driver ran out of his bus with Feline Rose right behind him. The last driver was old and just walked up grumbling without any problems.<br /> <br /> By that point, Rose and Ronin started asking about me. I told them over the radio I was inside. When they asked why, I told them the truth. Holes. I staggered out slowly, barely keeping my shotgun up so the drivers didn\u2019t get any ideas. I knew Snowflake saw what happened, but I hadn\u2019t mentioned it. When the rest of the Krewe saw me, Rose and Nightshade came running over and helped me along. I think Ronin was busy tying the drivers together. But the town was saved.<br /> <br /> With the commandos coming, we needed to get the hell out. Cupcake hotwired a jeep and we loaded up. On the road back, I made Ronin stop long enough for us to call the girls out of the woods. We told them to follow the road north and stay with the villagers. That way they could be evacuated with the hostages and avoid unwanted questions. With everyone else safe, it was time to go home. Nightshade gave everyone gravedirt and performed the ceremony as I was in no condition. It took her less time to open the path than it did for me, which was nice.<br /> <br /> The massive grandfather clock was just striking midnight when we came back through the Gate in Dark Haven Bluffs. They got me up into the infirmary and on the slab pretty damn quick. Snowflake and Nightshade cleaned and bandaged me while Cupcake kept the water filled. Rose worked on Ronin in the other bed. Once they would let me move, I headed back to the Plasm Chamber and drained the House before going back up and healing with my ceremony. I\u2019m still pretty shot up, but it only hurts when I move now...not everything I breathe. The infirmary passed its trial run. I think I\u2019ll stay here for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Tuesday, August 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I woke up around 1030 Hours to find Tavia sitting next to me...staring. I was a little confused until I tried to move. The pain that seared through me brought all the memories flooding back. Once I assured Tavia I was okay, just in pain, she started gossiping. That\u2019s how I know Tavia trusts me. Apparently Rose was out all night until earlier this morning. I thought maybe she tried to walk my beat, but Tavia said she was wearing Bonnie Lynn\u2019s dress and was soaking wet. Not sure what to think about that. Ronin slept here but got up and left without talking to anyone. Nothing new there. At some point this morning, Lily had been dancing on a table. That sounded even more weird coming from Tavia. Then she scooted a little closer and whispered that Nightshade slept here last night but she was singing now. I knew what that meant.<br /> <br /> I asked about Karen and Bella Donna. Apparently Karen took Bella Donna to stay with Chandra, before completely breaking down. I don\u2019t know if she was making guesses from the cat or just knew...but she was not okay. I\u2019ll have to go and see her later. After trying to get up a second time and realizing there was no way I could get back to the shop, I asked Tavia if she could talk to the others about putting up a sign on my shop. She immediately jumped up and stated that she would take care of it for me. Crazy but so very sweet.<br /> <br /> Nightshade came in after Tavia left. She brought a walkie talkie in case I needed anything. We talked for a little bit. I knew she was suffering from all the mental trauma, but otherwise seemed okay. She brought me some food before she and Rose set up one of the couches in the Music room for me. I\u2019ve been in here for almost an hour listening to Nightshade sing. It\u2019s soothing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 3, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> We have safely returned to Darkhaven Bluffs, though we are all worse for the wear. The remainder of our time in the Ivory Coast was chaotic and not as cleanly executed as I would have liked, but there is only so much a small group such as ours can do.<br /> <br /> As our \u201ccommando\u201d raid on the hotel continued, Gwen took care of the squad of mercenaries who were coming up to the second floor by dropping a couple of grenades on them while I went back and neutralized the remaining guards, who were still paralyzed by Simon\u2019s Tear-Stained Boneyard. After they were knocked out, bound, and relieved of their weapons, I began investigating the explosives they were setting up. Fortunately, they had only managed to set two, but the bombs were on the doors of rooms that held captives and I assumed that any attempt to open the door would kill the people inside.<br /> <br /> Gwen returned at about that time, and I asked if she had any experience with bombs. She did not. So I said I\u2019d try to take care of it while she went downstairs to support the others, who were having a bit of trouble against the mercenaries entrenched in the lobby. I really had no business fiddling with any bombs, but I had seen a bit of what the soldiers had done to set them earlier.<br /> <br /> So Gwen jogged off downstairs and I began working on deactivating the first bomb using what I\u2019d seen. It took me a good long while to defuse the first bomb while the fighting continued below, but eventually I was able to do it. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever been more nervous in my life!<br /> <br /> There really wasn\u2019t time to defuse the second bomb, but since it was set on a room adjacent to the one I opened, I thought I might be able to free the captives there through the connecting door between the two rooms. When I entered the first room, I gave the twenty or so men crowded inside a shock, because I was still wearing my Primeval Caul and must have looked a beastly fright. But the strength of my Caul allowed me to smash through the locked door into the adjacent room and free those men as well. I explained to the few that spoke English that they were free, and that they should free the others. I also used my chalk to mark the door with a bomb so that no one would open it and kill themselves.<br /> <br /> Then I went downstairs to help the others, but by the time I arrived, most of the mercenaries had fled in terror except for two that were fighting a couple of zombies. Doc was nowhere to be seen, and I later learned that he had been badly wounded in the fight. Natalie had taken cover behind a sofa and was shooting with her pistol, though I really didn\u2019t think she had any business endangering herself by drawing fire like that, so it is a good thing the zombies were demanding most of the remaining mercenaries\u2019 attention. Gwen was handling herself well, though, shooting from behind the cover of the lobby\u2019s main counter.<br /> <br /> As I entered the fray, I guess I was still in a focused, predatory state because of my Caul, and I fluidly grabbed a knife from a dead soldier\u2019s body and threw it at one of the remaining mercenaries before pouncing on him and nearly rendering him unconscious. It was a very odd thing for me to do, as I\u2019ve never thrown knives before, but it seemed quite natural at the time. Now, though I shudder to think that I might have killed the man. It was Natalie who did that, though, with a final shot from her pistol.<br /> <br /> The fight was over, but the busses arrived then to claim the women and children. Fortunately, Simon and Alexia were outside, and Simon began messing with the drivers as Alexia shut down the busses, turning off their engines whenever the drivers started them. She even moved other cars to block the busses\u2019 exit from the drive in front of the lobby. We quickly dealt with the bus guards and frightened off the drivers.<br /> <br /> There were reports that U.N. commandoes were moving in to find out why the mercenaries were in retreat, so we left as quickly as we could, making our way back to the charnel pit and returning to Darkhaven Bluffs through the Avernian Gate there. Doc was badly wounded, so Natalie and I helped him along, and once we returned, we got him situated in the mansion\u2019s infirmary. I wanted to help him out, but Natalie and Tavia were there, and it rapidly became apparent that I would only be in the way, so I went and cleaned up instead. As I emerged from the bath, Lily greeted me with big hug. She was worried, and could tell that I was upset. But having her there to comfort me made a big difference. And I let her know how much I appreciated it.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, now that the excitement of the day\u2019s events is over and the adrenaline has quieted, I am overwhelmed by the killing I\u2019ve seen, and by the murderous intent of the soldiers we fought. I need to meditate quite deeply to come to terms with it all, otherwise I fear I will succumb to what Doc calls \u201cshell shock\u201d myself, much like Natalie. It is still night here, so I think I will go to the sea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 3, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> After my last entry, I went down to the ocean. I needed to meditate very deeply, and I do that best when I\u2019m deep under the water. But I also needed to somehow come to terms with all the death and killing I had been a part of. Even though I did not kill anyone personally, the krewe as a whole did, and the trauma of that affected me deeply, as did the trauma of seeing other people intent on killing <i>me</i>.<br /> <br /> I am the Resolution of Death in the krewe. I needed to remember that, and to attune myself to death again in order to deal with what had happened in the Ivory Coast. So I donned Bonnie-Lynn\u2019s wedding dress and went down to the sea. I dove in and sank until I began to drown enough to threaten my life. It might seem like an odd thing to do, but it brought me back to my own death, and reconnected me to the Bride\u2019s death as well. We experienced our dying moments once more, and reaffirmed our irrevocable connection to Death itself. It did not make the killing and danger of the Ivory Coast acceptable. Far from it. But it helped me enter a state of mind in which I could absorb the killing and the death as something horrible yet necessary.<br /> <br /> Before I blacked out, I donned my Tear-Stained Shroud and Caul, and sank even further into the depths. I drifted there for a few hours, lingering in silent meditative isolation. I mourned the people who had died under the abuse of the mercenaries, and I mourned the mercenaries we killed. I mourned the part of me that can never be the same. And eventually, I found some peace. My melancholy has deepened once again. But that is as it should be.<br /> <br /> I eventually returned to the surface just before dawn. I will have to get the wedding dress dry-cleaned now. Lily was anxiously waiting for me. She hates to see me sad, and wanted to cheer me up. She gave me many very affectionate hugs. Then she insisted that I play the B-52s, not understanding that it is my mood that determines what I listen to, not the other way around. Nevertheless, I put on the music have enjoyed watching her dance as I write this entry.<br /> <br /> The others have been dealing with things in their own ways as well. Alexia is cooking. Simon has disappeared to his private chambers, and Gwen was playing loud, aggressive music while she drove herself to exhaustion exercising. Doc is on the mend, but still not well. However, I think somehow we\u2019ve all come through this with some sort of newfound strength, as though our connection to the Underworld has deepened.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Natalie is Psychotic</u><br /> <br /> Natalie was acting very oddly throughout our exploits in the Ivory Coast. I understand she was quite upset by the way the mercenaries had abused the people there; we were all horrified by the atrocities those monsters had committed on the innocent people of the town and village.<br /> <br /> But Natalie was edgy and excited and almost gleeful as she sent her zombies against the soldiers and fired her pistol with murderous abandon. She was giving her zombies fanciful names and making them sing odd tunes, as though the slaughter of the mercenaries was a circus and not the dire killing that it was. I suppose something must have snapped in her, but it was frightening to see her behaving like that when the rest of us were so grimly focused on the unpleasant task before us.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m worried about the state of her mind and what this says about her. And I was not comforted when she spent most of the next day quietly playing piano and singing softly to herself. There was a strong hint of madness in that. I suppose we all deal with trauma in different ways, but I worry about Natalie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Gwen and I</u><br /> <br /> To use a popular turn of phrase, I think Gwen and I \u201cbonded\u201d over the course of our exploits in the Ivory Coast. Ever since our argument, we\u2019ve been a bit cold toward one another. Relying on each other like we did made the disagreement seem distant and insignificant. It\u2019s good to be friends again.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday August 2nd<br /> <br /> -Sweet Goddess thank goodness that\u2019s over.<br /> <br /> -My girlfriend has totally lost her shit.<br /> <br /> -Doc is hurt kinda bad too. I don\u2019t have the emotional resilience for this.<br /> <br /> -Thank goodness Mini Me is OK. Owlish Housemate says Chandra was looking after her.<br /> <br /> -Very quiet tonight.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m going to sleep. Harder then I have in\u2026about two and a half years, actually.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 3rd<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t feel\u2026well. My fingers and knees hurt.<br /> <br /> -No, it is nothing sexy.<br /> <br /> -Doc is asleep.<br /> <br /> -I wish Doc would be more careful. :-/ <br /> <br /> -He is awesome for looking out for us and terrible for looking out for himself.<br /> <br /> -I will have to put my stompy boot down when he is more mobile.<br /> <br /> -Karen apparently had a nervous breakdown. She is\u2026quiet. And sleeping a lot.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me is OK other then having her guardian have a breakdown.<br /> <br /> -Music<br /> <br /> -Doc is awake.<br /> <br /> -Music<br /> <br /> -Keeping Doc and Karen nearby. I am OK with that.<br /> <br /> -Music<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXIII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s odd behavior (in Cote D\u2019Ivoire) was mostly due to the cocaine she took after arriving. At home it was her retreating into happy songs from her childhood. The zombies were named after various reindeer, plus \u201cSatan Claws\u201d when she ran out of reindeer names. But that\u2019s why she went from quiet and moody to kinda wild. Cocaine is a hell of a drug.<br /> <br /> The general poor rolls continued. Doc, out of Plasm, had to pass a Stealth roll, not resisted to slip in where the soldiers were fighting the zombies without being noticed. He failed, thus was shot to hell. This kind of mimicked Gwen\u2019s awful luck the last session. But Doc did not just waltz in there; at least, such was not his intent.<br /> <br /> The Demolitions rules are pretty unforgiving. I don't have a problem with that (it's horror, not action/adventure) but it was still surprising to some. The actual rules for explosives going off are still wonky I think.<br /> <br /> In the end, they avoided having to make Synergy rolls, but they did have to avoid taking some easier actions (like killing to heal themselves) to avoid it. When I ran Changeling Clarity was all over the place but these folks do not want to drop below 6 Synergy it seems (or 9 in Jasmine\u2019s case).<br /> <br /> Natalie and Jasmine both gained a little Plasm, Jasmine for near drowning Natalie for snorting a good deal of Heroin. Jasmine took some damage Natalie had to make a Stamina + Psyche to see if she went into cardiac arrest. Doc actually got some for being shot up in Cote d\u2019Ivoire, and Gwen got a little for killing. All these rewards were 1-2 but reserves were pretty low. Better living through masochism.<br /> <br /> At the end everyone but Alexia (who lacked enough points) raised their Psyche to 5. I refreshed their Plasm pool because, man, they needed it. The weekly haunts had been hit for the week, it was only Tuesday, and some folks were very low on Plasm. I expect Alexia will next session, or failing that whenever she gets enough XP.<br /> <br /> Well we shall have to see what they get into next. Join us if you would. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:03:16-08:00","id":16375,"title":"","content":"New Geist session, as our heroes (?) recover from the exertions in Cote D\u2019Ivoire. But still a lot is going on. Note Gwen\u2019s player had to miss this session.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Wednesday, August 4, 2010<br /> <br /> I woke up around 0800 Hours and eased out of bed so I wouldn\u2019t scream. Nothing like intense pain before the caffeine to get you going in the morning. I really did feel better than yesterday though. I made my way up to the meditation room because I thought it might help to center my mind before I tried to heal my body. I also wanted to be quiet as I didn\u2019t really want to wake Bella Donna or the rest of the Krewe. When I shuffled into the Meditation Room, Rose was already setup with her music. I was just going to begin my own meditation and not bother her. But apparently I ruined the flow of the room or something, because her eyes flew open before I got started and she lectured me about being up. I really couldn\u2019t blame her. If it\u2019d been me, I\u2019d have still wanted most anyone else to go to a hospital if they looked like I did. But I\u2019m not anyone else and we can\u2019t really explain to the nice triage nurse and police officer that I had an unfortunate accident involving automatic weapons. Not and expect it to go well, anyway. So I explained to Rose as calmly as I could that I was resting and meditation was not a strenuous activity. She relented but only insofar as my meditating. She was still waiting for me when I finished, about an hour later and made sure I was okay going downstairs to meet the others for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Snowflake and Rose are apparently going to check on the toy shop to make sure the Puppeteer hasn\u2019t pulled up roots or anything worse. I didn\u2019t have it in me to argue, I just asked that they see about getting Ral\u2019s phone number, since the werewolf obviously worked well with phones, that being his only apparent possession. Before they left, Tavia pointed out we received a letter from Leslie asking when she could get here for the Fall semester. That prompted us to look at dates more seriously for a moment. Karen\u2019s birthday is the 11th (good to know), Bella Donna is here through the end of the week, we can have Karen\u2019s birthday celebrations, then receive Leslie on\u2026.Friday the 13th. Great. But we also talked about how weird it was that Leslie didn\u2019t call or email. So then I got paranoid and asked Snowflake to check the letter for codes. Figured Leslie might be in trouble and used this as a way of asking for help. He looked over it but couldn\u2019t find any secret messages. What he did find though was that it was very formal and had extremely neat handwriting. We quickly decided that Tzipporah must have written the note, but we couldn\u2019t figure out why. She would know what plans we make with Leslie so why go through the trouble of this exquisite forgery? Someone remembered Cupcake could object read, so we had her check it out. And we were right, Tzipporah did write the letter. This led to a lively discussion about how we should have Nightshade make Clyde write all our letters so if anyone object reads our messages, they will only see a skeletal zombie. We got a good laugh out of it, but I might think about that more seriously if we need to send \u201csuggestions\u201d to our vampiric associates.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Wednesday, August 4, 2010<br /> <br /> After breakfast, Rose went to go train Jean again but stopped short and fussed at me again to not strain myself. I narrowly resisted the urge to call her Mom. Didn\u2019t think she would take that the right way. Once she was gone, I immediately headed into the Library and gathered all the information available on electronic wiring and explosives. If we ever deal with bombs and booby traps again, I want to know more than which part of the fishing line to cut. Science isn\u2019t really the focus of our Library, so in about a half hour I had everything useful. Which mostly consisted of a book from the 1800s about how to make dynamite and another, from about the same time, about blowing bridges up. The latter was written by Eustace Fishborn. I\u2019m betting he had a thick, black villain's moustache. Anyway, that does give me a pretty good basis, and if I ever need to blow up a bridge, Uncle Eustace has got my back.<br /> <br /> OH! I got an invitation to check out the possible site for Nightshade\u2019s 27 Club. I had to promise I could travel before she\u2019d let me go. Rose has everyone spooked I think. Karen\u2019s driving and Bella Donna is going too. This should be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1430 Hours, Wednesday, August 4, 2010<br /> <br /> That was fun. The building seems to be in good shape and Nightshade definitely has the designs for everything well in hand. I mean it\u2019s not the greatest location in New Haven for a club, but it\u2019s not in the middle of a slum either. I was still looking around when Nightshade burst from out of the back with Bella Donna following right behind. Karen and I stood and watched while Bella Donna tried (again apparently) to suggest the woman they both called Mom for a while was actually bi. The reasoning behind this was that all the women she helped at church seemed always have large breasts. I was leaning on Karen in pain and laughter as Nightshade was sputtering, walking in circles waving her arms erratically, and being generally uncomfortable. After that, Nightshade composed herself slightly and declared that it was time for lunch. <br /> <br /> Lunch went better for Nightshade and we all enjoyed each other\u2019s company. After that, we loaded up and headed back to Dark Haven Bluffs. Karen flipped out and suddenly Nightshade pulled me down into her lap. Apparently they spotted Rose, Cupcake, and Snowflake coming our way. It hurt like hell to get pulled down like that, but apparently no one saw me. I guess that was worth it. I know they were trying to keep Rose from starting in on me but I think I would have preferred that. When we got back to the Bluffs, I found pillows in my bed that made it look like someone was in the bed. Tavia most have panicked when Rose came home too. She told me that the others had gone to check the shop but she was was sure they wouldn\u2019t do anything that would lead to yelling. I couldn\u2019t do anything but smile about that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1910 Hours, Wednesday, August 4, 2010<br /> <br /> The others got back around 1700 Hours and all had milkshakes. That was weird. About a half hour after they were back and settled, there was a loud knock at the door. The kind of loud that usually set me ready to jump. But I was still too tore up for that. But surprisingly, when we opened the door, it was Karl. He said that he got a call from here but could only hear a strange noise on the phone. When he tried to call back, the line was always busy. Thus he dove straight into Cold Harbor and here he is. Karl is nothing if not awesome. And I think I know a certain imp of a ragdoll that played matchmaker today. That\u2019s okay, Rose lit up like a carnival ride when Karl agreed to stay for dinner. The whole Krewe likes Karl and ... well okay Ronin thinks he\u2019s creepy, but what can you do with her? Anyway, Karl is okay in our book so the fact that he makes Rose this happy is great. I mean I\u2019m not going to be the one to point out how ironic it is that Rose is falling for a member of the Fishborn clan (that isn\u2019t even human), after the fit she threw about Snowflake and Tavia especially. Snowflake declared that we should take Karl out on the boat tomorrow and this was immediately championed by Bella Donna, who apparently didn\u2019t seem at all bothered by Karl. The kid\u2019s got guts. After dinner, Karl and Rose went out to the pier to watch the sunset. Rose was actually wearing her swimsuit so I don\u2019t expect them back anytime soon. Let them have their romantic date. They deserve it.<br /> <br /> I went back to the Infirmary and gathered my ritual components. I was tired of hurting. It took me a little concentration but when I was done, I was whole again. Down alot of Plasm yet again, but I\u2019ll just deal. Now I think I\u2019ll stretch out here on the slab and take a little nap.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0845 Hours, Thursday, August 5, 2010<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t spent that much time on an operating table since I got back from the Sand. Must have really needed the sleep though. I woke up at 0800 Hours without any alarm and headed up the Meditation Room. Rose was just coming in and we were able to meditate together rather quickly, for me at least. 30 minutes later, we were walking out to find Bella Donna sitting outside her door, waiting for us. Her room is just across the hall from the Meditation Room but I didn\u2019t think she could hear our music. Apparently she was already up and hoping to talk before Nightshade was up and around. It might have been better now to tell Rose about the issue, but oh well. Bella Donna was sent here with a secret mission. Once she finally conquered the Mom, Grandma, Matron X (my name for Nightshade\u2019s Mother) issue, Bella Donna told us that Nightshade has her mother all wrong. It was only through the efforts of Matron X that Bella Donna could be here, as their father had flatly refused at first. Bella Donna is convinced that Matron X is far more forward thinking that Nightshade has ever led me believe. I suspect this may have come about when Matron X thought she\u2019d lost one daughter due to stifling restriction, but I remained silent. The young woman pleaded with me to convince Nightshade to at least speak with her mother. The picture she painted was of a woman tormented by the lost of a child, only to learn that child was still alive...then find she wanted nothing to do with her. While I know Nightshade will not see it this way, I could understand the sort of anguish Bella Donna described. I told her that I could not promise anything, but I would try to help. I also tried to gently advise her to consider taking this at a slower pace. She could do better at slow introduction of ideas when dealing with Nightshade than to throw everything at her to process. That Nightshade had very recently been traumatized was not at all helpful, but I left that part out.<br /> <br /> Through it all, I felt pretty good. Bella Donna already trusted us, and me specifically, to ask for help in healing their family. I don\u2019t think this will be a quick or smooth process, but I do think it will go a long way towards mending some of Nightshade\u2019s scars.<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s time for breakfast.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 4, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I held Lily last night when I went to sleep. She seemed like she wanted to help comfort me, and I felt the need to hold her like a child clutching a favorite doll. She didn\u2019t mind. In fact, she invited the attention.<br /> <br /> This morning I was surprised to see Doc join me for meditation. He is in no state to be up and about yet, though he is on the mend. I told him he needed to take it easy, but he didn\u2019t really listen to me, and stayed to meditate despite my fretting. I could sense that he had difficulty focusing, though. His meditation was troubled and it took him a long time to find his center. I stayed with him until he was done even though I centered myself well before he was finished.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast, Simon mentioned that he had received a letter from Leslie asking about the arrangements for her arrival to start school at Albertus Magnus in the fall. There was something odd about the letter; it was too proper and formal for Leslie, so Alexia read its spirit and learned that it had actually be composed by Tzipporah. There is nothing specifically wrong with that, since she would need to be informed of any arrangements anyway. It\u2019s simply odd that she would have taken the pains to forge a letter as though her daughter had written it.<br /> <br /> In any event, we\u2019re planning for Leslie to arrive next Friday, the 13th.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 4, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Jean has heard from his family! They are safe and sound under U.N. protection. I\u2019m so relieved, and so is Jean. He hasn\u2019t been himself lately, but now he\u2019s finally back to his confident, driven self. It\u2019s nice to know that our efforts were not in vain, and that they have brought a real smile back to Jean\u2019s face.<br /> <br /> Karen, Our Natalie, and the Younger Natalie have gone out to look at a possible site for Natalie\u2019s club. I went to check in on Doc when I got home, but he wasn\u2019t in the infirmary. I hope he\u2019s resting in his room and isn\u2019t out doing anything he shouldn\u2019t be doing, given his injuries. I know from experience that you can\u2019t push these things. If you don\u2019t give yourself time to heal up properly, you could risk more permanent injury.<br /> Simon and I are going to go out with Alexia in a bit to check on the toy store and make sure the Puppeteer is still there and isn\u2019t up to anything horrible. Or at least nothing any more horrible than normal. We\u2019re not going in, of course, but Simon will have a look with his Boneyard.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 4, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Things seem quiet at the toy store. Simon had a good look with his Boneyard, and it seems the Puppeteer has repaired the puppets damaged in our previous fight using parts of other dolls. She is also building a new calliope out of odds and ends, like an old Speak n\u2019 Spell. It appears that the calliope is important to her, though I\u2019m not sure why since she doesn\u2019t need it to create the creepy calliope music that always manifests near her.<br /> <br /> There were two mean-looking homeless men keeping an eye on the toy store, and we assumed they were werewolves connected to Rawl\u2019s pack. So while Simon was looking into the toy store, Alexia and I visited the video game store in the shopping center nearby so that we would not arouse the werewolves\u2019 suspicion. We attracted a lot of attention inside, though I was a bit irritated by all the sports video games available. I think I must have put off the store employees.<br /> <br /> In any event, we headed home after that, and Simon shared some theories on how we might deal with the Puppeteer. It\u2019s possible that the puppets are all aspects of her, and that to defeat them, we need to focus on defeating her. Perhaps only Simon can really defeat her, because of the Little Prince. We might need to play out the story the Puppeteer is trying to tell. Perhaps if Simon becomes her next victim, the only true opportunity to defeat her will emerge at the climax of the story.<br /> <br /> When we returned home, a pleasant surprise awaited us. Karl was there! I felt a surge of happiness when I saw him. We\u2019ve been in touch, writing letters back and forth, but I haven\u2019t seen him since I went to Taiwan.<br /> <br /> He was very concerned, though relieved to see we were safe. He told us that he had received a call from the house and heard a strange noise, but nothing else. He tried to call back, but the line was busy. He was worried, so he came as quickly as he could.<br /> <br /> I quickly realized that Lily was responsible. The poor dear has been so worried about me that she called Karl to get him to come see me. And he ploy worked, because my mood brightened considerably as soon as I saw Karl. Lily is a mischievous one, but she means well, and she got Karl to visit. I think I need him right now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 4, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve had a wonderful night! Karl joined us for dinner, and then invited me out swimming in the ocean. We had such a wonderful time in the depths, and then sat together and just talked on the pier overlooking the moonlit sea. It was quite romantic, and I felt better and more\u2026alive than I have in a long time. Karl is staying in one of the guest rooms tonight, and will remain here through tomorrow at least, which is good, because I\u2019m not ready for him to leave yet.<br /> <br /> And I have Lily to thank for it. I made sure she knew how grateful I was. I think she\u2019s just happy to see me in better spirits.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Video Games</u><br /> <br /> While Alexia and I were in the video game store, I really looked at the assortment of games for sale, and was surprised by some of what I saw. Of course there are plenty of unnecessarily violent games out there, and after our recent excursion, I find it hard to imagine anyone enjoying the simulated experience of bloody combat. Or so I thought at first until I really examined my own thoughts and realized that there is a certain thrill to it that might be appealing to some were real lives not at stake.<br /> <br /> But what really annoyed me were all the sports games. There are games for tennis, for football (real football, not American football, though they had games for that too), for track and field, practically anything you can imagine.<br /> <br /> I can understand the appeal of sports games, but if a person wants to enjoy sports, then why don\u2019t they just go out and play them for real? It\u2019s more fulfilling and much healthier. There are plenty of facilities around to enjoy such sports for a reasonable fee, certainly no more expensive than buying all these games. If the games were more abstract, like they were when I was younger, I would understand the appeal because then they really are games, and not simulations. But moderns sports games seem to be trying to make the experience as realistic as possible, and if that\u2019s the case, you might as well play for real.<br /> <br /> Alexia argued that some people didn\u2019t have the facilities or talent to play sports for real, but I don\u2019t think that\u2019s a good excuse. I suppose it could be disheartening to lack skill in a team sport when you are playing with others much better than you. Video games might provide a form of false empowerment to make up for that. And Alexia is right that not everyone has a team to play with or against. But I still think there are enough opportunities out there that most people could find a way to play real sports instead of wasting their energies on a video game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Karl and the Deep Green Sea</u><br /> <br /> I felt happier and more at peace tonight with Karl than I have in a long time. Though he seemed a bit anxious and shy, he was very romantic. He complimented me several times, and spoke with such poetry that I couldn\u2019t help but melt a little as we talked.<br /> <br /> We watched the sunset. It was beautiful. And when darkness fell, we went swimming. It was delightful. We both feel so at home in the sea. The sea is a part of us, albeit for different reasons. Karl asked if it would upset me if he changed into his fish-man form during our swim, and of course I told him I wouldn\u2019t mind at all. After all, he\u2019s seen me changed into a bestial half-cat thing. When I reminded him of that, he said that I was beautiful no matter what form I took. He\u2019s so sweet and romantic!<br /> <br /> When we sank to the blackest of the night-darkened depths, he even showed off a bit, lighting up with a soft, blue-green bioluminescence. The way it lit the sea floor with a pale, ghostly glow was beautiful. I experienced a sense of wonder I haven\u2019t felt in a long time.<br /> <br /> There was something special and unique about swimming together in the deep green sea. I often feel like I\u2019m one with the sea, and I could share that part of myself with Karl in a way no one else could ever fathom. He knows what the depths mean to people like us. He understands their comforting embrace.<br /> <br /> Later, when we sat together on the pier and talked, I completely lost track of time. We chatted about the books we\u2019d shared recently, and the books we\u2019re reading now. I told him about our terrible experience in the Ivory Coast. I leaned against him, and he put an arm around my shoulders. It felt nice.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m glad he\u2019s staying at least another day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 4th<br /> <br /> -Hmmm\u2026awake somehow. Feel almost human<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Time to check out the Seekrit Project<br /> <br /> -Doc, Karen, and Mini Me are going.<br /> <br /> -Given I am 5\u20194, Mini Me is 5\u20195 and Karen is 5\u20196, we could be gothic nesting dolls.<br /> <br /> -Karen is driving\u2026she is only a mildly scary driver.<br /> <br /> -And she says *I* go too fast?<br /> <br /> -Oh she says she is talking about my hands. Nm. ^_^<br /> <br /> -The fact Karen has never been with a boi is pretty obvious sometimes.<br /> <br /> -I generally think one should sleep with a member of both sexes to see what they like.<br /> <br /> -That said, while I am awesome even I would be nervous representing womankind in the sack.<br /> <br /> -And on that note, here we are.<br /> <br /> -Only appropriately run down.<br /> <br /> -Looks nice<br /> <br /> -Splitting up, we will cover more ground that way. I am taking Mini Me and Doc is talking to Karen.<br /> <br /> -I bet this place will be awesome.<br /> <br /> -A good club has bathrooms you can get in a fistfight in or fuck in, possibly at the same time.<br /> <br /> -I dunno what I am gonna do with the old Kitchen. It is not very big but I don\u2019t need a kitchen, do I?<br /> <br /> -OMG<br /> <br /> -OMG OMG OMG OMG<br /> <br /> -There is something WRONG with my daughter holy shit.<br /> <br /> -I, uh, BWA?<br /> <br /> -Gothic Ballerinas dancing Swan Lake gothic Ballerinas dancing Swan Lake gothic Ballerinas dancing Swan Lake OK head is cleared.<br /> <br /> -So\u2026nice place, right? Right.<br /> <br /> -LUNCH!<br /> <br /> -OMG It\u2019d the parents hide Doc! =^_^=<br /> <br /> -Doc is on myyyyyyyyyyyy siiiiiiiiiiiiide<br /> <br /> -Noms!<br /> <br /> -Like a family, sorts, kinda<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s go back<br /> <br /> -Mini Me knows I like women on leashes but did not know I did a piano version of \u201cI Miss You\u201d as background music on MTV once.<br /> <br /> -You know what this piano needs? A gigantic candelabra.<br /> <br /> -I hope Miss Merryweather gets back soon I am in need of the noms.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Karl is here. What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -So the evil dolly did it. And everyone is cool with that.<br /> <br /> -I need evil dolly powers.<br /> <br /> -I could have my hair in darling ringlets!<br /> <br /> -Dinner with the family.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me is taking this well<br /> <br /> -Just as well she promised not to talk about it. No one would believe her<br /> <br /> -Looks like it is time to pair off for a bit. Karl is going swimming with Spooky. Scandalous!<br /> <br /> -Boat ride tomorrow. Woo.<br /> <br /> -I shall have to Vlog from the briny sea.<br /> <br /> -Hmm heels\u2026um\u2026yea\u2026I\u2019m\u2026gonna disappear till dawn I think.<br /> <br /> -Hehe<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXIV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see here. Game overall went pretty well. Gwen\u2019s player was under the weather, but we soldiered on. The Karl thing was actually totally spontaneous on Lily\u2019s part. I did not preplan it either. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Everyone is Psyche 5 now.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add really. Jasmine\u2019s player lacks her rather strong disdain for sports games, for the record, but you should probably not assume a lot of what is said necessarily conforms to real world beliefs of the players. Of course, some do.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:08:19-08:00","id":16381,"title":"","content":"New Geist session ready for post. We get our usual Doc, Jasmine and Natalie combo but also something from Simon! Let\u2019s see what the Middle Shadows have been up to.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXV<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1010 Hours, Thursday, August 5, 2010<br /> <br /> We came down to find Cupcake setting out waffles and fruit, which is one of Rose\u2019s favorites. Karl came in and I could tell he wanted to help, but his etiquette told him to stay out of the way. It was really sweet watching Rose and Karl be so chaste and so completely lost in one another. But even with that, something about Bella Donna\u2019s story kept nagging at the back of my mind. That Nightshade\u2019s death was not welcomed but even though she was 3000 miles away, Matron X never questioned it. She knew...<br /> <br /> THAT\u2019S IT! She knew because she\u2019d SEEN it! That\u2019s also why Bella Donna and Nightshade shared such similar experiences. Matron X is a death seer. She knew Nightshade would die and how, but not that she would come back! Matron X had witnessed Nightshade\u2019s death possibly before she ever left the East Coast. So when Bella Donna found her alive, it was more than just a shock. That explains why Bella Donna described Matron X as so desperate to reconnect with Nightshade. ...I realize this is purely speculation, but it takes all the pieces of this puzzle and fits them together perfectly. I\u2019ll need to think on this a little more. Getting to meet Matron X might be helpful as well.<br /> <br /> I was not so insightful at breakfast. Now I think I\u2019m going to talk to Karl and Lily to see about learning the Spirit\u2019s tongue. Since Rose is going to training anyway. I figure Karl could use some company.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1345 Hours, Thursday, August 5, 2010<br /> <br /> Well I talked to Karl about learning the Spirit tongue. Then we had an intellectual discussion on the few similarities and many differences of the various shapechangers. Okay mostly just what\u2019s different between Uratha and Brineborn. I\u2019m not sure what they would call Noriko, since apparently it\u2019s all different. The important difference in reference to my request was that the Spirit tongue is actually werewolf speech and he was not as good at it. Deirdre didn\u2019t actually tell me that. And Lily would have loved to help but as she frantically gestured and pointed, she has no mouth to speak. Snowflake came in about that time and mentioned something about trying to improve his fencing skills. That give Karl an idea. He got his trident (!) from somewhere, stamped huge fishing corks on the tines and put red paint on the ends. Snowflake and I got sabers from upstairs and trained with him in the Great Hall. The rules in the beginning where simple. If the red paint got on you from a hit, you were stabbed. This was bad. As we continued, Karl moved on to parrying larger opponents without losing our weapon. Karl is a big dude so it was a little difficult at first, but then he shifted into his Fishman form. The first time either of us tried to parry the trident, we were hit with such force, I lost my blade and Snowflake got knocked backward. It\u2019s really intimidating when this 8\u2019 Fishman is constantly moving and shifting and twirling a massive trident. We were gathering an audience as Lily, Cupcake, even Rose just stopped and watched. Next, Karl asked us to try to disarm him. I think he meant for us to give him a challenge since there were two of us. That really didn\u2019t happen.<br /> <br /> When Cupcake offered to help out with multiple arms, Karl looked impressed. Snowflake and I, covered in bruises and red paint, gladly stepped aside. That may have been the scariest sparring match I\u2019ve ever seen. Karl was obviously not use to dealing with multiple arms moving independently but still coordinated. Our blades certainly weren\u2019t. So Cupcake gave him a good workout and made us look really bad. I mean Karl was in his Fishman form the whole time with her. When it was over Rose brought in lemonade and a beer for Ronin; I have no idea when she came in. I know that Karen and Nightshade started to walk in earlier but saw Snowflake fly backward from Karl before Karen stopped and walked back out. As they likely had Bella Donna with them, that was a good call. I did hear November Rain on the piano coming from the Music Room. But Snowflake and I needed a shower before we went out on the boat.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1925 Hours, Thursday, August 5, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was actually more relaxing than I expected. For obvious reasons, Lily didn\u2019t go in the water. Chandra stayed with Nightshade and Karen as they sat under black camisole parasols. Snowflake looked like something out of Magnum P.I. with his ascot and captain\u2019s hat. He walked around with his scotch and watched the rest of the Krewe and friends. Tavia joined the rest of us in the water and I was reminded she was also part Cold Harbor Fishborn. She can swim faster than I can. I stayed near Bella Donna so she wouldn\u2019t be swimming by herself in the ocean. That\u2019s just never fun. Unless you\u2019re Rose. And speaking of Rose, she and Karl went for another couples swim as the rest of us climbed back on deck. I figured they might be awhile and apparently so did Nightshade. As soon as their heads were under, Bella Donna had a wine cooler handed to her. I was not amused. But that might have made it a little easier to explain why Rose and Karl weren\u2019t coming back up very quickly. Cupcake provided her latest example of refreshment, a gourmet milkshake. Lemon milkshake to be precise. They were very good.<br /> <br /> Now I need to get ready for dinner. They are talking seriously about watching Firefly for TV Night.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0315 Hours, Friday, August 6, 2010<br /> <br /> To say that Rose\u2019s reaction to the Chinese in Firefly was amusing would be a gross understatement. I\u2019m sure Nightshade was watching Rose as much as she was the movie. After we had the mandatory, \u201cWho would you do?\u201d or \u201cWho is your favorite?\u201d discussion, Rose and Karl slipped off for another swim. By that point, it was around 2200 Hours so I got ready and slipped up for an early patrol. Things were peaceful and I appreciated that. I knew Rose and Karl were out enjoying the calm depths and each other\u2019s company so everything just seemed right. Now I\u2019m going to bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Friday, August 6, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation was back to about an hour this morning, but that\u2019s okay. It felt good to be back out on patrol after not going for so long. I should probably call Sebastian at some point and make sure he\u2019s still cool with working with me too.<br /> <br /> Breakfast became another planning session before Bella Donna got up. The discussion focused on the Puppeteer, but eventually developed into how Snowflake could play out the story to defeat The Skintaker. I was impressed to hear someone besides me suggest we learn more about how they work before we face the Puppeteer again. The plan for now is to investigate the paintings when Rose gets back from training today. After she left, Snowflake and I decided that we needed to look the part if we were going to be in a story about pirates. Thus we went shopping and came back with almost movie quality costumes. We already had the cutlasses before earlier, so we are set.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1530 Hours, Friday, August 6, 2010<br /> <br /> We moved all the paintings into what Snowflake calls the Dwarven Throne Room, a large chamber in the forward center of the basement with massive stone pillars. I got some rope while Snowflake used his spyglass to look into the first painting. Tying the rope to the stone pillars, I hoped we\u2019d make it easier to get back out.<br /> <br /> I looped the rope around my waist and everyone prepared for anything. I went first and entered the Beach image. The image never changed. Even as I walked on the sand, it still looked like yellow sand from a kid\u2019s drawing. The sand felt like sand, but it was weird. Somehow it was like it felt like I remembered sand should feel, but still off. After I looked around and even slipped into the water without anything coming to kill me, I tried to follow the rope back out of the painting. The problem was, the rope never stopped. Eventually the rope pulled tight and Snowflake drug me out. Apparently they could see and hear me, moving through the image. But once inside, I had no direct link to the outside world, even with the rope. That changed our strategy a little. Ronin, Karl, and Tavia were then going to stay outside and help us leave; well Ronin was going to cover us in case of trouble. I could only imagine what a bullet fired into the painting would do.<br /> <br /> Snowflake, Rose, Cupcake, and I all headed back into the Beach scene. We swam out to the boat. It was a little hard to see as the water was blue like the picture, not like water normally is. Just as we boarded the boat, the rope started pulling against me. I didn\u2019t know what to expect so I draw my cutlass and looked up and around for trouble. Then Rose vanished. I started calling out for Rose and anyone that might have heard before the rope started pulling again. We started searching the boat for Rose when she suddenly seemed to dive onto the deck. She let us know that Karl pulled her out but our rope was no good. When we got to the boat, we actually switched paintings while the rope was still in the original one. And not even Karl could pull it out once we were in the new scene. Rose vanished again, then after a few minutes her voice suddenly boomed from above us like thunder. She returned again and we noticed this huge cannon-looking barrel in the sky. Rose told us it was a pipe back in the world what would let Karl and Tavia speak to us. Tavia started talking and it was terrifying. Her voice was huge and it came like a storm over the sea. Rose realized she was being loud on purpose and chastised her for it. The next comment was much less God-like.<br /> <br /> Snowflake mentioned we had to go below decks, using that goofy boat puppet voice. And suddenly, we were all below decks...before Rose vanished again. Snowflake wasn\u2019t worried anymore so he suggested we keep searching the ship quarters. Rose reappeared as expected and let us know about a communications SNAFU. We had to go back above deck so the pipe could be removed and they could follow us. After that, they were much better about keeping up. The only other issue we seemed to have was when we searched inside the individual rooms. Karl said that they couldn\u2019t see us at all when we entered, as they were not part of the painting. Since they were all the same, we didn\u2019t go in any after the first.<br /> <br /> [To Be Continued...]<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, August 5, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I was surprised upon leaving meditation today to find Young Natalie waiting to talk to Doc and me. She thinks that her grandmother\u2014Natalie\u2019s mother\u2014wants to make up with Our Natalie. But Our Natalie is being stubborn about it, and isn\u2019t keen on the idea. I was at a loss for any advice to give the girl, but Doc advised her to bring up positive things about Natalie\u2019s mother so that Our Natalie could see how she\u2019s changed.<br /> <br /> Young Natalie said that her grandmother was shocked to learn that Our Natalie was still alive. I have a nagging feeling that\u2019s significant somehow. Could it be that Natalie\u2019s mother has visions of death just like her daughter and granddaughter? If so, she might have seen Natalie\u2019s death.<br /> <br /> Thursday, August 5, 2010, Afternoon<br /> Lily tried to follow me out to campus today. She was quite adorable, walking behind me on my way to the car with a little bag slung over her shoulder just like I carry a small satchel off to work every morning. Unfortunately, I had to send her back into the house. It\u2019s dangerous for her to follow me, and I don\u2019t want her getting up to any mischief. I convinced her that she needed to stay with Karl and keep him company while I was away.<br /> <br /> When I returned home, I found Simon, Doc, and Karl doing some sparring in the entry hall. Simon was working on his fencing skills in preparation for fighting the Skintaker, and Doc was simply brushing up on his training, I think. Karl was amazing, though. He wielded his trident with a fluid, predatory quickness that one would never have expected from his hulking frame. It was very handsome, actually. Of course, I\u2019ve seen him at home in the water, where he swims with the same agile grace, but I think the others were surprised. The Bride was practically swooning as she imagined that Karl was fighting for her honor. It was a charming thought.<br /> <br /> The women of the house watched the men practice, and Alexia and I prepared some lemonades for refreshment when they were done. Right now, however, we\u2019re getting ready to go out on the yacht for a bit of an afternoon party.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, August 5, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> The yacht was fun, though I did have to apologize to Karl for how decadent it all was. He didn\u2019t seem to mind. Apparently I\u2019m the only one who does, and it honestly doesn\u2019t bother me that much. I simply don\u2019t have the same attraction to expensive goods that the others do. I suppose it\u2019s my Buddhist convictions.<br /> <br /> I any event, most of us were dressed for swimming and spent some time enjoying the ocean, though Natalie, Chandra, and Karen chose to remain aboard, shielded from the sun by charming little parasols. All in all it was a fun afternoon, and Karl and I even disappeared under the waves for a time to enjoy the cool, dark depths.<br /> <br /> I was a bit upset when Gwen referred to Karl\u2019s \u201cgoogly eyes.\u201d It was unkind, though Karl didn\u2019t seem to care. Gwen\u2019s a good sort, though not always very tactful. There seemed to be something on her mind today, though. She was quiet and withdrawn, and didn\u2019t really smile much. Later in the evening, I think she spent a lot of time with her investigation materials, looking back over the details of her murder and her brother\u2019s disappearance. I wonder if she hasn\u2019t had a new lead? I do hope she is okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, August 5, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> After dinner and TV night, Karl and I went out swimming again, and then sat on the pier to enjoy the night air like we did last night. And that is when Karl made my heart soar.<br /> <br /> He took my hand gently and told me that he cares deeply for me, and would like to start dating me. It was so gentlemanly! The Bride was ecstatic. So was I, though I fear the coldness of my demeanor may have made that hard for Karl to see. I asked if this meant he would stay around more. If we are to be a couple, I want to be together. Of course he answered that he would stay.<br /> <br /> We kissed, and somehow the fishy taste of his lips seemed welcome. I could sense the warmth of his heartbeat and felt safe and comfortable as he draped his arm around me and held me close. I haven\u2019t felt that way in over a year since Richard died. And though I did feel a pang of regret and the ache of guilt when I thought of Richard, I also felt peace. Karl may seem a monster to some, but I know and love him for the gentle, sensitive, intelligent, and capable man he is.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 6, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> We discussed what to do about the Puppeteer over breakfast. We have more-or-less decided that we will need to play out her story in order to defeat her. At the very least, we will need to maneuver Simon into a position so that he can finish her off personally. But we are still uncertain how to do any of that. We simply don\u2019t have enough information to go on. However, Tavia suggested that we explore the painted backdrops we took from the Puppeteer\u2019s original \u201cstudio.\u201d She says that it is possible to enter those paintings, and thereby enter the sets themselves, so we plan to explore them later this afternoon, once I\u2019ve returned from training Jean.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 6, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> We have begun exploring the backdrops. Doc, Natalie, Simon, Alexia and I managed to enter one of the paintings, a backdrop of a beach. We tied a rope to Doc first, and he stepped inside to have a look about, then the rest of us followed, leaving Gwen, Karl, and Tavia to keep an eye on the paintings and to help us escape if necessary. And indeed it seems their assistance is necessary, for once inside one of the paintings, one cannot leave without being pulled out by someone on the outside.<br /> <br /> The space inside the paintings seems to be infinite, though the scope of the terrain is limited to only what can be seen in the picture itself. We also discovered that it is possible to move from one painting to another\u2014one scene to the next, as it were, simply by saying we planned to do so, just as they apparently did in the Candle Cove show. If I were to say to the others, \u201cLet\u2019s return to the ship,\u201d then we would appear on the pirate ship backdrop. It\u2019s not unlike the experience of Using the Cold Wind key to become one with the winds, but it\u2019s a bit more jarring.<br /> <br /> To test our limits, we tried swimming to the Candle Cove pirate ship instead of \u201cwarping\u201d there. We could see it off the shore of the first backdrop we entered. We arrived on the ship easily enough, but shortly after appearing there, Doc felt a tug on the rope, as though our friends outside were trying to signal us. We didn\u2019t understand what they were trying to say, but then I was pulled out of the painting by Karl. I was quite shocked. Karl, Gwen and Tavia seemed very worried and told me that they had briefly lost track of us when we \u201cjumped\u201d paintings. Moreover, they could no longer pull us out by the rope that was stuck in the first backdrop. They could grab the rope that followed Doc into the pirate ship painting, though, and it\u2019s a relief that they can pull us out directly. They can also hear us quite clearly from inside the painting, but we cannot hear them. So I ran upstairs and fetched a metal tube from somewhere, then stuck it into the painting and tried to talk through it. The others on the ship could hear me perfectly well then, though my voice was projected quite loudly, it seems. Tavia took the tube from me and I dove back into the painting.<br /> <br /> Inside the painting, the speaking tube poked out of the sky like a monstrous cannon, and when Tavia spoke, her voice was thunderous. But at least we could communicate.<br /> <br /> We began exploring the ship, and Simon derived altogether too much pleasure from \u201cwarping\u201d above and below decks just by saying where he wanted to go. Below deck, all the cabins were identical bedrooms with spartan furnishings and little else. As we were looking through those rooms, I was again snatched out of the painting by Karl, though more gently this time. He apologized as he delicately set me down, and he called me \u201cdear.\u201d I don\u2019t know why, but just hearing that word from him seemed to crystallize that we are a couple now, and though there\u2019s no telling what will become of our fledgling relationship, in that moment I was really able to accept that I have found love again. The Bride was all aflutter about it too.<br /> <br /> Karl had taken me from the painting because when we entered the rooms on the ship, we disappeared from the painting entirely. There simply wasn\u2019t a painting of the rooms, only one of the below decks hallways that led to the rooms. Karl didn\u2019t like seeing me disappear like that, and asked that we not enter the rooms if we could help it. I returned to the painting and share the information with the others. None of us want to be trapped here forever, so I think we are all more than happy to remain in the sight of our allies on the outside.<br /> <br /> [Entry to be continued]<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Firefly</u><br /> <br /> After dinner, we spent a few hours watching episodes of a show that Natalie enjoys called Firefly. It was a western, after a manner, but it was also a science fiction. I did enjoy the characters, whom we discussed for some time after we finished watching. It seems everyone had his or her own favorite. I personally liked Shepherd Book. His calm and mysterious wisdom provided a refreshing bit of stability to the crew. I think it surprised the others when I admitted that I also liked Inara. Her open sensuality aside, she was also a source of wisdom and stability for the crew, and I thought that the distant longing shared between her and Malcolm was touching.<br /> <br /> Karl was of two minds about the show. He seemed to like several characters a great deal, but was uncomfortable with some of the foolish choices they made to drive the plot. He understands that characters in fiction do such things from time to time (he is an avid reader), but in this case, I don\u2019t think he expected to enjoy the characters and their unwise decisions quite as much as he did.<br /> <br /> However, I do wish my krewe-mates had warned me about how terrible the language on the show was. I\u2019m certain Natalie didn\u2019t say anything because she wanted to see my reaction. It wasn\u2019t so bad in English, but I was positively mortified by some of the things the characters said in Chinese! The others wanted me to translate, but I refused. I couldn\u2019t possibly say some of the things they said, especially not in front of Karl!<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, August 5th<br /> <br /> -I am awake! Woo.<br /> <br /> -Where my young \u2018un at?<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m a young \u2018un.<br /> <br /> -\u201cBriny V-Log\u201d in a bit.<br /> <br /> -Got K&amp;N, let\u2019s see what the others are doing.<br /> <br /> -Uh, OK, I will be honest I did not expect to see that. OK.<br /> <br /> -Why don\u2019t we do an exciting something else!<br /> <br /> -Mini Me is jamming on my girlfriend\u2019s electric guitar.<br /> <br /> -Oh good she knows \u201cBohemian Rhapsody\u201d<br /> <br /> -hehehe this is fun<br /> <br /> -Man I have not played the guitar solo of \u201cNovember Rain\u201d on Piano in forever.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me scared me, asking what song \u201cNovember Rain\u201d is. She knew the song at least whew.<br /> <br /> -Heh go Karen! Not a bad version on the guitar there.<br /> <br /> -She can do \u201cTemple of Love\u201d and I am firing up some drums on the keyboard.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress does not sound like Andrew Eldritch, nor does she care.<br /> <br /> -OK boat time.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me needs a bikini to help her attract bois (or girls)<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is bringing a bathing suit but not wearing one.<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s see if Karen gets all crazy cuz of the movement of the boat again.<br /> <br /> -OK so shockingly we are starting with B-52s, Go-Gos, and Beach Boys.<br /> <br /> -This is so not goffik.<br /> <br /> -Little Mermaid. Really. Sigh.<br /> <br /> -Thank goodness I have my big lacy umbrella to guard my lovely pallor.<br /> <br /> -I snuck some of The Damned in there.<br /> <br /> -\u201cBriny V-Log\u201d is up!<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m on a boat!<br /> <br /> -Mom\u2019s gone. Quick, the wine coolers!<br /> <br /> -LOL I am a terrible influence on Mini Me!<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is having fun.<br /> <br /> -But in the shade, not the sun.<br /> <br /> -Ball of Fire bad. ~Hiss~<br /> <br /> -Back inside.<br /> <br /> -Ooh Firefly.<br /> <br /> -Everyone is picking favorites, heh. It seems to be a thing now.<br /> <br /> -Kaylee eats a strawberry and the room is silent<br /> <br /> -Spooky likes Book. Gwen likes Jayne, Tavia likes Mal, Chandra likes Zoe (a lot) and Alexia likes Kaylee.<br /> <br /> -I am, as always between Kaylee and Inara. There are worse places to find oneself\u2026<br /> <br /> -Wait, did Gwen just say Jayne was gay?<br /> <br /> -Oh, no. Still crazy, but no.<br /> <br /> -OK, Karen\u2019s right, I do like the footsies in this show.<br /> <br /> -The sheer amount of slash involved in what Tavia just said blows the mind.<br /> <br /> -Music time again before the bois start smacking each other around again<br /> <br /> -Oh got Simon this time. Apparently he was tired of being beaten down by Karl.<br /> <br /> -Where is Doc?<br /> <br /> -Oh he is patrolling. Think Spooky is up to hijinx. Good for her.<br /> <br /> -A screaming orgasm or two would do her a WORLD of good. Seriously.<br /> <br /> -We be jammin\u2019<br /> <br /> -We need a band name.<br /> <br /> -\u201cStrange High House on the Hill.\u201d Hmmmm<br /> <br /> -\u201cNatalie and the Knight Riders\u201d is the most terrible name possible, actually. Thanks.<br /> <br /> -\u201cKnightline.\u201d Hahahahaha no.<br /> <br /> -Your mistress is losing her voice, and should retire to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 6th<br /> <br /> -Aaaaah, waking up not alone. Nothing better.<br /> <br /> -Beds are warmer with two.<br /> <br /> -\u2026possibly even warmer with three, but you did not hear that from me. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s time to whack the hornet\u2019s nest. Always a good idea.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019ve heard of someone putting me in the picture but this is ridiculous.<br /> <br /> -If you don\u2019t ever hear from me again, it is because I am stupid. Just FYI.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Simon\u2019s Musings</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, 2010 August 5<br /> <br /> The schedule is collapsing around me \u2013 to work on practice day, to practice on TV day, it strains the mind. I know, intellectually, that these are the crutches of a man with two working legs, but I remember the early days, those first breaths of freedom, free of the fog of madness but covered in blood. I have my Krewe, my new family, and tomorrow, I do not know that I will practice. I shall speak with my father about it this Sunday. That day will never change \u2013 I owe him that.<br /> <br /> Today, the family Fishborne of New Haven prepared for its renaissance. All things according to their plans. I recently revisited the family tree after Doc brought up Eustace, the family's most notable dynomiteer. So much like a tree it looks, a vibrant and delightful spiral of branches resting above a narrow trunk bearing the burden of its ancient weight. The future needs new roots, for what is left, without the support of the other lines, is myself, the last scion of my line as my father was before me, and his father before him, and Tavia, the woman born to ensure this line could go on.<br /> <br /> Perhaps I should revisit the notion of embracing Doc into the fold. His mind and body are strong, and he stands resolute in the shadow of the ever-impending darkness of eternity what threatens to crash over our meager flood-gates. We stood together as Carl sparred with us, trained us more like, for the time will come, dangerously soon I fear with the puppeteer, when every bruise I earned from his painted cork tipped trident is one less blade sunk into my chest. I was nervous at the notion, but he is a gatekeeper, and to be one in one more sense would suit his cosmic role as a protector and healer.<br /> <br /> The twist of it all, however, is Carl and Jasmine. I really did not foresee this, not that I am much for foreseeing, sadly. When Tavia compelled me to the circle yesterday to cast Luck Magic to him for the purpose of wooing her, I will admit to feeling rather guilty. Bold-faced hypocrisy, I know, but Jasmine, she is not like the girls in the clubs. She is a beautiful, intelligent, deadly creature, and above all, she is like family. Yes, I keep a lot from her, for fear of her reprisal or disappointment, but to manipulate her seems wrong. It's what struck me poorly about Julian \u2013 He'd be terrible for her. He's handsome, clever, and destructive. She seemed happy, but Julian didn't, I know him. The Prince and I had a terrible discussion on that, suggesting I just bribe him with gold, because that's how relationships work \u2013 in his day, perhaps \u2013 but he's something like 12 \u2013 I'm don't want to think of this any longer. Anyway, Carl and Jasmine make so much unforeseen, wonderful sense.<br /> <br /> We took the yacht out today after the lengthy battle practice, and as I donned my father's boating attire, relaxing among the in-group of those I need not wear my outside mask, the vast ocean in front of us was as the limit of our future, Alexia\u2019s delectable lemon milkshakes the ambrosia of gods to be. Everyone enjoyed themselves, although Gwen seemed contemplative. I know I may not connect with her the best, but it is more a recognition that she, unlike the rest of us, remains grounded in the outside world, full of knowledge and wisdom of the society of humanity that never makes sense to me, and as the rest of us retreat into the palace of the mind, the solace of the ocean, the ecstasy of the dream, or the madness of the art, her eyes remain fixed on the world of man, as if she and I are the sentinels of entirely different planes of being. She is normally fond of relaxing, so I wonder what it is she is uniquely aware of.<br /> <br /> Young Natalie rather enjoyed herself. I've tried to be the most hospitable host to her I can be, while yet not appearing to be a demented chocolate factory entrepreneur. She is to leave Monday, but I do hope she can be brought here. It is an awkward long game \u2013 My motives are not base, for I fear for her and her family. Her parents do not understand, or they do which might be worse, and our Natalie suffered dearly for that. My parents suffered dearly for our misunderstanding, and I cannot stand idly by and watch what pain might follow. She seems to get along well with the group of us, her and her true mother especially \u2013 this could work. Her departure is Monday \u2013 we've got the weekend to enjoy her company. Then Leslie arrives on Friday. Trading teenagers, apparently.<br /> <br /> This evening's TV day event was to watch a show called \u201cFirefly\u201d. I guess the person behind the show was also responsible for Buffy and Angel. Those shows never failed to make me laugh. There was some literary discussion between Carl and Jasmine, and Jasmine was embarrassed by whatever Chinese they were speaking. There was, what I suppose is obligatory, discussion on who was each of our favorite character, or which character we found most attractive. I believe there might have been a parallel made between myself and the character of the same name, and our eccentric sisters. On the other hand, I was distracted by the gripping question \u201cIf Mal is Han Solo, who is Chewbacca?\u201d I posit Jane, for he hairy and frequently incoherent.<br /> <br /> Friday, 2010 August 6<br /> <br /> Over pancakes, fruit, and whipped creme, while beside Carl and Jasmine holding hands, on a morning full of promise, we have elected to investigate the paintings further. As the contemporary theory is that we may need to insinuate ourselves (or at least myself) into the paradigm of the piratical adventure, I felt the need to look the part. Thus, while Jasmine was off training Jean, whose family seems to have been rescued magically, I was off to procure costuming. I believe the tri-corner hat is somewhat dashing, and I've never had as comfortable a scabbard for my sword as I do now.<br /> <br /> If you are reading this in some future year, I may be trapped in a painting in the basement. If you are somehow my decedent, then to paraphrase the puppet boat \u2013 You have to go inside. If nothing else, so you can explain how I had decedents while you get me back out of there<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> More of that role-playing. I was wondering when/if they would use the backgrounds for the CC show.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been pointed out I have issues with paintings, and that\u2019s just not true. I have issues with mirrors.<br /> <br /> The comment Tavia cleared the room with came from a discussion of whether Mal/Zoe or Mal/Jayne was the series\u2019 Han Solo and Chewbacca. Tavia said it could not be Mal and Zoe because they were very obviously not sleeping together.<br /> <br /> Now the bad news. Due to changes in her work schedule and load, this session was the last for Gwen Cooper's player as a regular player. We have discussed it and are going to implement Gwen being out of the area for the foreseeable future. Her player has expressed an interest in coming back some during the Summer if possible, and what will probably happen is me discussing how to end her story arc with her player and her coming back to do that over the summer, this or next (or both) as I hope the game will be healthy for another couple years though we, as a group, will make that determination as we go; our posse is not near running out of stuff to do even from stuff I plotted at the end of '09.<br /> <br /> I've managed to get a player to come in, however...one who is local and has been reading the journals. If you follow <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;t=57061\" target=\"_blank\">The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a> Vampire game it is the same player as Jocelin de La For\u00eat. Also, if you follow that game, you can still see activity from Gwen's player as Eleanor Gray. I'm going to wait until she appears before revealing anything about her except that she was originally conceived in July \u201910 as a result of reading these journals.<br /> <br /> We all hate to see Gwen go, but her player has been good to deal with and the change is understandable. She had a good run for the first 65 sessions though, and as I say it is my hope you have not seen the last of her, though we won't likely have her as a regular.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, see you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-22T18:09:48-08:00","id":16382,"title":"","content":"This was the first session with our new member, Sara Rowan, a Torn Advocate. Ironically, but not intendedly (is that a word? Spellcheck says no) the same as Gwen. She did rather jump in with both feet, getting immediately involved in the Candle Cove business. Lets catch up with the Krewe.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1945 Hours, Friday, August 6, 2010<br /> <br /> [Continued from last session]<br /> <br /> Once we were satisfied the ship was clear, Snowflake warped us to the island. I really hate hearing him say, \u201cWe have to go inside.\u201d<br /> <br /> The scene was like the rest, nothing we couldn\u2019t see from the pictures. The entrance to the cave just looked like a black spot of paint. Rose had an idea and had Karl pull her back out. She came back after just a few minutes with a rock. Throwing it at the cave, we were surprised when the rock bounced off the opening. That left Snowflake\u2019s new favorite way to travel. We drew our swords and spoke the words.<br /> <br /> The first thing I noticed was Tavia\u2019s scream as if coming from far away and still echoing in the cave. Karl calmed us, sorta, by letting us know that the skeleton was looking in a different direction. Now it was facing us. I was pretty relieved when Rose didn\u2019t go charging off. Instead, we talked about different options we could try. I suggested trying to walk around it to see if it followed. Rose mentioned either harassing or molesting it from invisibility. It took us a moment to realize she still didn\u2019t realize all the meanings of that word. I blame Ronin. Tavia shrieked again, which was very surreal to be honest, and Karl let us know that while we weren\u2019t looking, the skeleton had shifted to face us fully instead of just looking our way. That prompted a little more direct testing. Cupcake remained at the cave entrance, keeping her distance from the skeleton. Snowflake and I kept our eyes on the stack of bones while Rose moved to pillage the treasure. The irony here was thick. She found that the coins were all part of the chest, as was the skeleton. Moving the chest also meant taking the skeleton with us. One look at Cupcake said that was a bad idea. So we came to the end of our magical journey. Retracing our steps to get the rope back, we were hauled out by Karl. Rose reached into the island painting and removed the very obvious real rock.<br /> <br /> Once we were out and okay, Ronin rushed upstairs saying something had come up with Jaime. She didn\u2019t really give any more detail. Rose said when she went up to check on her, she was packing. I don\u2019t know what her brother did, but I sure hope he\u2019s got a really good excuse. Otherwise, when she does find him, it could be really bad. So with Ronin leaving, I\u2019m not really sure how the Krewe will react. I mean, I\u2019m not really sure how I\u2019ll react. We all know there\u2019s no point in trying to talk her out of it. I just hope she realizes how much a part of this family she\u2019s become. I\u2019m gonna miss her while she\u2019s gone.<br /> <br /> As always, we didn\u2019t have much time to process anything as Rose gathered us up to brainstorm our next move. Just this once, I agree with her. We need to focus on something other than one of our sisters leaving. And time really is running out before the end of the season of Candle Cove. We were in the kitchen discussing the few ideas we had, when someone knocked on the front door. With Karl being an obvious exception, we just don\u2019t get visitors that often. So when Tavia got up to answer the door, the rest of us just kinda blinked wondering who it could be? She came back to let us know a young woman was asking for Snowflake. The calm but still cold tone told me to pay attention just in case. When he came back, he led Bright Eyes in with him. We first met her through Ronin and Nightshade at the Flesh Fair. Apparently they were all in a discussion about Oracle together. I\u2019m sure Nightshade just hated to look at her too. Bright Eyes came to town with the carnival and remembered we were in the area. I noticed Tavia seemed to instantly relax and just go back to being lady of the house once it came out Bright Eyes was a Sin-Eater. For the best really. I don\u2019t want to have put her back together again.<br /> <br /> Anyway Bright Eyes is staying with us for a while and that meant we needed to tell her about Candle Cove. Rose pointed out that we couldn\u2019t really ask her to help us with this as it\u2019s our problem and she just got to town. Bright Eyes blew that off and said it was the least she could do for putting her up. She\u2019s nice and cute. That promises to be interesting when Karen meets her. Once back on task, Tavia mentioned that maybe we should focus on the Skintaker instead of the Puppeteer. The whole idea that the Puppeteer was a slave to her story and that story needed to be played out. It\u2019s never surprising when Tavia says something intelligent but it is sometimes a little odd when she has a strategically sound idea. That we didn\u2019t have any other ones didn\u2019t hurt either. But with that in mind, we put our assault team together. Nightshade will Boneyard from the car with Chandra there to protect her and guard the door. Bright Eyes and I would work specifically on the Puppeteer. Rose will focus on cutting the puppets\u2019 strings in the hopes that we can at least remove them from the Puppeteer\u2019s control if not from the fight. Cupcake plans to get to Pirate Percy and through him try to deal with Horace Horrible. That leaves the Skintaker for Snowflake.<br /> <br /> Everyone broke up at that point to gear up. I went up and got the Crimson Destroyer as I figured having a charm rifle would be a good thing for this fight. Snowflake met me on the stairs on the way back down and reminded me we needed a little Luck. Now that we\u2019ve given ourselves a boost, it\u2019s time to go. I just hope the Puppeteer doesn\u2019t run away again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0345 Hours, Saturday, August 7, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Snowflake drove, since we were at full numbers. Cupcake and Chandra came with me and Nightshade. As soon as we got there, Chandra got a weird, almost sickened look on her face. With her heightened senses, the Panagallen saw a swarm of flies intentionally torture and dismember a roach. Snowflake walked over and even waved off the flies. They came right back. I possessed The Dog to look around in Twilight. It was disgusting. The whole area was overlayed with this decaying mirror image. The building spirits all looked sick and dying. There were no ghosts here at all. And then I noticed the toy shop. That was the only place in the whole area that looked normal. Like it was somehow resisting the spiritual disease affecting everything else in town. Snowflake told us there were signs of Abyssal taint here and it was definitely separate from the Puppeteer. Rose donned her Primeval Caul and unlocked her Oracle, but immediately hissed like a cat and recoiled from the vision she got of the area. This was not something we prepared for, so we needed to keep moving with the Puppeteer.<br /> <br /> Cupcake picked the lock on the storefront before Rose took point. Bright Eyes ignited her Pyre-Flame Caul and bathed the whole entryway in soft ghostflame. Snowflake drug the Cave painting out of the car as calliope music started from inside. Rose pressed in and immediately had to duck a castle from above as Horace Horrible struck from ambush. Yeah it\u2019s surreal to write it too. Rose reacted like a cat and leapt up at Horace to cut his strings, landing on top of a wall shelf. Nightshade reported we had a new addition over the ear curl. Another standing shelf fell over just as Bright Eyes and Cupcake tried to get through the entryway. They were able to push it off as Snowflake and I ran through. As soon as we cleared the door, a coffee maker flew at Snowflake but I couldn\u2019t see what was happening. Apparently he could as he unfurled the painting against the wall, drew his sword, looked at the table and stated, \u201cWe have to go inside.\u201d Then Snowflake jumped into the painting. Before I could react, I saw the Skintaker appear in the picture with him. I was about to take a shot at the puppet in the picture when Rose suddenly found a string attach to her back. Snowflake would have to take him the old fashion way. Cupcake tried to punch Horace and missed, but taunted him anyway. I moved past, rifle in hand, looking for the Puppeteer. I felt Bright Eyes fall in behind me and suddenly I felt like I was back in the Sands. We cleared buildings basically the same way over there. It was a cold comfort, but it did help me focus. A pot fell on Cupcake behind us but she shrugged it off and carried Percy to find Horace. When a woman with six arms is hunting you, you\u2019d be stupid not to hide.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes and I were ahead of the others when Rose called out that the strings would try to control you. Lily came running in about that point with a pair of scissors duct taped to her hand. I kept moving as I did not have time to deal with that. We rounded the last corner when I spotted the Puppeteer hovering near the roof. I basically shouldered the rifle and fired as I cleared the turn. Bright Eyes rushed her but missed with the butterfly knife. Gotta get her a bigger blade. Next thing I know, there\u2019s a string snaking around and stabbing me in the back. I knew that would be a problem. Then Lily ran into the room with us. Worse and worse. Bright Eyes came for my string but couldn\u2019t cut through it. Hell I can\u2019t fault her, I tried to shoot through it but somehow missed it.<br /> <br /> [To be continued...]<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Dairy</b><br /> <br /> Friday, August 6, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> [Entry continued]<br /> <br /> The rest of our foray into the paintings was largely uneventful. Having worked out most of the details of how the paintings operated, moving about and exploring the island painting and the cave was not difficult. The only thing of note that we discovered was a skeleton guarding a treasure chest full of painted gold and jewels in the cave. The skeleton is the only thing in the paintings that seemed to move, for it turned its head to watch us as we entered, giving Tavia a bit of a fright as she observe it from outside the painting. And of course, Alexia, with her aversion to skeletons, didn\u2019t go near it.<br /> <br /> In any event, we retraced our steps and left the paintings, returning the Tavia, Karl, and the real world. Then we moved into the kitchen to sit and discuss what to do about the Puppeteer. The paintings, though strangely wondrous and terrifying, did not actually reveal to us anything helpful in fighting our enemy, so we began to consider just attacking her. After all, it appeared from our prior battle that she could be hurt, and presumably destroyed, through mundane means. The biggest problem was the Skintaker, whom only Simon could face.<br /> <br /> Simon suggested drawing the Skintaker into one of the paintings to fight him there. Perhaps if things go badly, we might trap him there, or we might be able to assist Simon from outside the painting somehow. I don\u2019t really claim to understand Simon\u2019s logic, really, but I do trust that he has an intelligent plan.<br /> <br /> I think it might also be possible to sever the strings that connect the Puppeteer to her puppets, so I suggest we try that as well. When we go fight her, I\u2019ll make that my chief priority.<br /> <br /> As we were discussing our plans, there was a resounding knock on the door. We are so unaccustomed to visitors that we all just looked at each other for a moment as Tavia went to answer the door, followed quickly by Simon.<br /> <br /> They invited our visitor inside. She was another sin-eater, a young woman we met at the Flesh Fair in New Orleans this summer. Her name is Sara Rowan, and she is, or rather was, a fortune-teller and circus performer before her death. Now she still tells fortunes to get by, but has yet to find a krewe. She was traveling through the area and remembered our invitation to visit should she pass through New Haven, and stopped by, hoping we could put her up for a few days. Of course we were happy to welcome her into our home, as she seems an earnest sort. I didn\u2019t really get to know her well at the Flesh Fair, but I think she made an impression on Natalie and Alexia. She seems quite pleasant.<br /> <br /> While Tavia was preparing a guest room for her, Sara joined us in the kitchen and we explained that we were trying to plan an attack on a strange being that was threatening the local children through a twisted television show. She seemed to take it all in stride, so I imagine she has seen some strange things since she died. Indeed, she offered her assistance, saying that it was the least she could do in exchange for our hospitality. I did not want to draw her into such danger, but the others seemed keen to have her help, so Simon and Alexia explained all we know about Candle Cove and the Puppeteer.<br /> <br /> Afterward, Sara went upstairs to settle into the second-floor guest room while the rest of us made preparations for an attack on the toy store where the Puppeteer is hiding. Hopefully we will be able to defeat her tonight. Chandra will accompany us, but not Karl, since his presence in territory belonging to the Pure werewolves might incite an attack.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 6, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> The fight against the Puppeteer was grueling, but it seems she is not the only evil to lurk in Glenwood. There is something else there, something otherworldly. An Outsider. It was barely noticeable at first, little more than a bad feeling. But when Chandra noticed several flies plucking the legs from a still-living cockroach, the area around the toy store took on a much more menacing air. I shifted into my cat-like Primeval Caul, donned my Primeval Shroud and called upon the heightened senses of the Phantasmal Oracle so that I could better see the Puppeteer\u2019s strings, and then the full impact of affliction plaguing the area became so obvious that I couldn\u2019t help but cringe and hiss, cat-like, as the ill feeling threatened to overwhelm me. I could tell that Chandra felt the same way. Oddly, the sickness barely intruded on the toy store, so it appears that the Puppeteer\u2019s presence there is keeping it at bay. Simon says that the Puppeteer must have been imprinting some sort of reality upon her new home.<br /> <br /> The others prepared as well, unlocking manifestations with keys. Natalie stayed outside, safe and sound in a boneyard trance while Chandra protected her. The rest of us went inside. Alexia transformed into her multi-armed caul-form, while Doc drew his Shroud around him and Simon prepared his Tear-Stained curses to defend himself against the Skintaker. He also brought the painting of the cave, planning to unfurl it and jump inside to lure the Skintaker there. Sara, it seems, is a master of Pyre-Flame and Passion, and she prepared by clothing herself in the Pyre-Flame Caul, which spread across her body as a brilliant glow that started at a bird tattoo on her calf. She was armed with a knife, and planned to help me deal with the puppets and strings while Doc, wielding Marshall\u2019s rifle, was to attack the Puppeteer directly. Alexia was to find Pirate Percy and stay with him, taking the role of Janice from the show.<br /> <br /> I entered the store first, hunting down the puppets, and quickly found Horace the Horrible. He threw old boxes and toys at me, but I dodged easily and struck at his strings, which, despite my fearsome claws, were more resilient that I expected. Before I could sever his connection to the Puppeteer, he toppled a shelf onto Sara and Alexia. They weren\u2019t hurt badly, and Alexia quickly found Percy and protected him from the other puppets. The narrow aisles of the store were difficult to navigate, with many hiding places for our enemies, but I leapt atop the shelving and managed to continue attacking Horace until a thin, ephemeral string snaked out of the store\u2019s back room and attached itself to me. I could feel the pull of the Puppeteer\u2019s will trying to force me to act against my wishes. I fought off her influence and slashed at the string attached to me, severing it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Sara disentangled herself from the fallen shelf and followed Doc into the back room to attack the Puppeteer directly. The Puppeteer was there, floating amidst a wash of calliope music, but her rapid, erratic movements made her difficult to attack. Doc shot her once with the rifle, blasting a chunk of her bone-like body away, but then she lashed out at him with a string like the one that struck me. Fearing what the Puppeteer might make him do, Sara slashed at the string, but her knife wasn\u2019t able to tear through the mystical cord as easily as my spectral claws, so I told her and Doc to hold on while I made my way to them.<br /> <br /> Alexia withdrew with Percy to the front of the store, near Simon. Simon unfurled the painting of the cave and jumped into it as the Skintaker flitted through the cluttered shelves, tossing heavy objects. The Skintaker followed Simon, disappearing into the painting and leaving Alexia to keep an eye on the duel from outside the canvas.<br /> <br /> [Entry to be continued]<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Gwen\u2019s Departure</u><br /> <br /> Gwen has left suddenly. She said something about new leads on her murder and her brother\u2019s disappearance, and then departed as soon as she could after we emerged from the paintings. She packed for a long trip, and I\u2019m a bit bewildered by the suddenness and mystery of her departure. We offered to join her, but she said that she had to take care of this on her own. I do hope she is okay and that she knows what she is doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Friday, August 6th<br /> <br /> -OK, that\u2019s done, did not die. Not die good.<br /> <br /> -Chatting chatting.<br /> <br /> -Guest like substance?<br /> <br /> -WOW there are a pair of eyes.<br /> <br /> -Yes. Eyes. What?<br /> <br /> -Pervs. ^_^<br /> <br /> -One of us! One of us!<br /> <br /> -@NAREK looks like there is another bound who dropped in. Does not seem insane.<br /> <br /> -Tavia is strange.<br /> <br /> -So this means we can hang here right? Not go to outer nowhere?<br /> <br /> -No? No.<br /> <br /> -But we can show her the yacht?<br /> <br /> -Well droopygoths. Gotta go after all.<br /> <br /> -OK gotta get ready for tonight.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -@NAREK Maybe better keep Mini Me away. I think she might would be intimidated by, you know, the guns.<br /> <br /> -@NAREK Also you gotta check this girl out. I think she may be up your alley.<br /> <br /> -@NAREK Thanks. :P<br /> <br /> -Gwen is off being a grownup. That means I am drivin\u2019<br /> <br /> -OK, can\u2019t leave Simon behind his boat does not have the pickup my bad girl does.<br /> <br /> -Awww aren\u2019t the girls in my back seat cute. Behave back there!<br /> <br /> -Hehehehehehehe<br /> <br /> -Here we are and I am already bored.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -OK I don\u2019t complain about being bored again.<br /> <br /> -Damn breaking horror movie rules.<br /> <br /> -@NAREK OK Glenwood? Never come here. Ever.<br /> <br /> -Yeeeeeeeeeeesh<br /> <br /> -OK Radio Silence.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXVI</i><br /> <br /> Well, mostly an action session. I have not had a chance to put up Sara\u2019s picture but I will in the very near future. Anyone else\u2019s pic you wanna see? I have a long list of NPCs I don\u2019t mind sharing their pics especially if it helps people wrap their brain around who people are\u2026I wager my players benefit from ones at the table.<br /> <br /> The Skin-Taker and Simon\u2019s battle was especially brutal, but that does not mean others were having a cake walk either. People seriously plasm dumped this time. On the plus side, it served as a good introduction to the system for Sara\u2019s player, if something of a trial by fire.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned to next session, where the Candle Cove arc is resolved and Natalie, Alexia, and their ladies play dress up with Sara for a night on the town.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:14:31-08:00","id":16974,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s about time for the spooky crew. This session concludes the Candle Cove storyline (or does it?) and has some bonding time for the group. As a bonus, there is something from Alexia at the very end.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0345 Hours, Saturday, August 7, 2010<br /> <br /> [Continued from last session]<br /> <br /> Rose rushed in to help with the string. She yelled for me to throw the rifle to Bright Eyes. I glanced down with some confusion. But then before I could think about it any more, I ran back into the room with the puppets and threw the rifle to Horace Horrible. The sight of a puppet shouldering a weapon I received from the ghost of a Mafia hitman was jarring to say the least. Bright Eyes tried to cut my string again but apparently missed. Horace shot Cupcake, who had been whipping his ass. The white steam pouring out the wound let me know she Bulwarked the wound and would be fine. She thrust Percy out and ordered him to take the rifle away. Somehow, the cowardly puppet was driven by Cupcake\u2019s words and the little guy did it. The struggle over my rifle ended when Horace lost his grip and dropped it on the shelf. Cupcake then used the cleaver in one of her other arms to chop Horace\u2019s string.<br /> <br /> There was almost a pause as Horace looked at his fallen string and then smiled. The pause didn\u2019t last long as I turned to see Lily jump on the Puppeteer\u2019s head. The fact that she still had scissors duct taped to her hand made that a lot less cute. I grabbed the rifle off the shelf just as the Puppeteer ripped Lily off. The next moment I felt a pressure disappear as Bright Eyes cut through my string. Cupcake then pinned Horace so he couldn\u2019t run away. I lifted the rifle as I turned to target the Puppeteer again. Rose was busy trying to cut through the Skintaker\u2019s string but I had other targets. As soon as the Puppeteer was in my sights, I fired. I felt another string stab into me at almost the same moment. Bright Eyes was thankfully there to start hacking away again.<br /> <br /> Before anything else could go wrong, Lily stood up amongst the trash and debris around us. She looked toward the Puppeteer and I know I felt malice. Her arms raised up (scissors still attached) like something out of an old horror movie. But then several Barbies and a baby doll pulled themselves out of the various piles of toys. All at once, they turned their heads to fix their cold, plastic stare on the Puppeteer. Rose sliced into my string but still didn\u2019t make it through. I was about to fire at the Puppeteer again when suddenly I realized I was aiming for Lily. It was a poor shot and the doll was still standing, but both she and Rose were pissed. Bright Eyes frayed a little more of my string and then we all just kind of watched in horror. The dolls under Lily\u2019s control began crawling all over the Puppeteer. She couldn\u2019t see to direct things as there were dolls everywhere she tried to look. Rose slashed through my string mumbling very angrily about shooting her doll. I promised I wasn\u2019t trying to hurt Lily but she was talking to the Puppeteer.<br /> <br /> Under my own control again, I leveled one final shot at the Puppeteer just as another string stabbed into Rose. That must have done it. Suddenly all the lights that didn\u2019t come from Bright Eyes went out as a cacophony of children screamed as if in terror and agony. Then the calliope stopped, all the strings disappeared, and the only sound left was Percy screaming...constantly. I moved to the painting and almost panicked as there was not Snowflake, Skintaker, or the chest. The skeleton lay to one side, not really looking at anything. Cupcake said they moved into another painting, which was not part of the plan. When I looked over, she was carrying Percy and an armless Horace. When I asked about the arms, Cupcake pulled them out of her pocket. I was a little too out of it to think about that too hard. Then Snowflake popped back into the painting and I dragged him out. The painting felt very different than before. Snowflake was covered in dry paint so at first I didn\u2019t noticed the sword wounds. He said he defeated the Skintaker, but that it looked kind of like a pi\u00f1ata, a really nasty pi\u00f1ata. Once we cleaned him off a little, I stopped the bleeding and called for everyone to load up. We needed to get the hell out of here.<br /> <br /> On the way home, Percy and Horace went to sleep. Snowflake seemed to think something could probably wake them up again, but we aren\u2019t sure what. When we got back, we found that all the paintings had dried and had lost their magic. That was great to hear, but not until after I finished healing Snowflake in the Infirmary. While we were getting cleaned up the rest of the way, Cupcake gave Bright Eyes the tour of the House. Given that it was a little after midnight, I was going to go back out on patrol, but Nightshade came and asked that I stay home and talk. That doesn\u2019t happen very often so I went back into the TV Room and we all talked and hung out. It was fun to just sit around, talk, watch Rose and Karl stare at each other with stars in their eyes, you know. Since Nightshade and Karen basically drug each other away, I decided to just go to sleep. Instead I came in and wrote this out. I think once Bella Donna goes back home, I\u2019ll need more time alone with Nightshade. Now I\u2019m going to sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Saturday, August 7, 2010<br /> <br /> I got up about 0830 Hours this morning, oddly. I guess I was just more rested than I thought. My meditation was very quick as well. I was able to get cleaned up a little before everyone shuffled in for breakfast. We were all in good spirits after our victory last night, but I know I glanced over at Ronin\u2019s empty seat and felt a little sad every time I did.<br /> <br /> That did lead me to start thinking more about our current situation. We don\u2019t know when Ronin will be back but we\u2019re down a car. She was one hell of a driver so there\u2019s no way we\u2019ll be able to replace that, but I was thinking about getting a vehicle again. Since Nightshade said she\u2019d really rather I not get a motorcycle and we need a way to get around, I saw an opportunity. Technically we have way more than enough funds to buy anything I want. But I don\u2019t want to use the Krewe money that way. Besides, if things work out at all like what I\u2019m hoping with having employees, I won\u2019t even be out very much on my own. I wonder how much Snowflake knows about engines?<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1400 Hours, Saturday, August 7, 2010<br /> <br /> I caught up with Snowflake just after lunch. He was not expecting me to ask him to help me build a car. Admittedly, it\u2019s not something I would normally do. But I explained that there were several reasons I thought this would be a good idea. First, he could teach me what he knew and then we could learn together. Second, if we built something from parts, it could very well be cheaper. But the final point was most important, at least as far as Snowflake was concerned. While we were in New Orleans for the Flesh Fair, I saw a Memento car. It was a street rod and all tricked out, but it was still an enchanted relic of Death. If we searched for the frame from a junkyard, we could spot if any of the cars there would work the same way. Then we could restore it, fix it, and when I used my Sepulchre Gateway ceremony, we could just all jump in and drive to wherever we\u2019re going. I could tell Snowflake was excited, he had that look in his eye, though I think he had other plans for today. He asked a little hesitantly if I wanted to get started right away. Since he was even willing to help, I was in no rush.<br /> <br /> That was about the time Nightshade came around and needed to talk. She told me that they were taking Bella Donna to Gotham City tonight. Given Saturday was \u201cGay Night,\u201d they wanted the girl to be exposed in a more safe environment to see if she really did have an attraction to other women, or if she was just trying to emulate Nightshade. They were very specifically not taking her to Murder Ballads and I thought that was probably a good idea. I was being told this because I was welcome to come, but Nightshade didn\u2019t think I would have much fun. I appreciated the thought, and if I thought going would have been helpful, I\u2019d have gone anyway. But given that she basically said there was no reason for me to go, I figured I\u2019d sit this one out and let the girls have a night out. She kissed me and said that if they moved to a different club, they\u2019d call or stop back for me. As we walked back to a slightly concerned looking Snowflake, she told him the same thing. I could tell he was all for going out, but relationships are hard enough for Snowflake without sending the wrong signals. I was sure we\u2019d find Barrett from the Sleeping Giant pack there, but like I said, why not let the girls have their fun.<br /> <br /> Snowflake did have another idea after that. We were both interested in going clubbing if Nightshade and the others decided to change locations, but he wanted to be around people in general. Something about pool came up and from there we ended up deciding that it might be fun to go and hustle pool using Luck Magic and Boneyard. We\u2019d just go out dressed for clubbing and if we got the call, we\u2019d head out from there. This is hilarious and also maybe a bad idea, but Snowflake and I don\u2019t go out for \u201cBoys\u2019 Night\u201d and I think that\u2019s really what he wants.<br /> <br /> Either way, it sounds like tonight should be fun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, August 6, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> [Entry continued]<br /> <br /> As our fight against the Puppeteer continued, someone arrived to help us. Lily! She must have stowed away in the car again (a habit I need to talk with her about). She charged into the back room with a pair of scissors duct-taped to her mitten hand. Doc had just been snared by one of the Puppeteer\u2019s strings, and I shouted for him to throw his rifle to Sara, hoping he could do so before the Puppeteer made him shoot one of us with it, but the Puppeteer was too quick, and before I could sever Doc\u2019s string, he was forced to run out into the main room and toss the rifle to Horace.<br /> <br /> In response, Lily threw herself at the Puppeteer, latching onto her face and blinding her until the Puppeteer could throw her off. I was impressed with Lily\u2019s bravery! She was quite helpful during the fight, but I still worry for her and don\u2019t want her getting involved in such danger. While Lily was distracting the Puppeteer, I slashed to Doc\u2019s string and severed all be a but tenuous strand, which Sara deftly finished cutting with her knife. I\u2019m glad she was with us.<br /> <br /> Alexia wasted no time in facing Horace. He shot at her, but fortunately the bullet only grazed her. Then she was upon him, holding him down and slashing the remnants of his string with her multiple arms while Percy struggled with him for the gun. Eventually, Percy managed to take the rifle from him, and Alexia tossed it to back to Doc, who shot another hole in the Puppeteer. Horace seemed like he just wanted to escape the Puppeteer at that point, but Alexia kept him from going anywhere. She was quite vicious, and even ripped his puppet arms off to keep him out of trouble!<br /> <br /> The Puppeteer was still hovering madly about the back room, and sent out another string to attach to Doc just before Lily stood up on a table and animated several other dolls in the store. She looked adorable, waving her little arms above her head like that. The dolls threw themselves at the Puppeteer, distracting her, but she was still able to force Doc to shoot Lily! Poor thing, she was hit and some of her stuffing exploded out of her. Sara went to work on Doc\u2019s string to make sure the Puppeteer couldn\u2019t make him shoot anyone else, and I finished neatly cutting the string just in time for Doc to spin and blast the Puppeteer\u2019s head into splinters with a final shot.<br /> <br /> The Puppeteer died in a cacophony of discordant calliope music and the screams of children, and all the lights dimmed and died. Only the glow of Sara\u2019s Pyre-Flame Caul lit the store.<br /> <br /> But we were worried how Simon had fared in his duel against the Skin-taker, so we all rushed to the painting to see where he might be. The painting had changed\u2014it was horrifying, filled with ragged children\u2019s skins, but Simon was okay. The painting was rapidly losing its magic, but Doc pulled Simon out before he was trapped there forever. Simon tells us that the Skintaker nearly got the best of him, but that he had managed to weigh the puppet down with so many curses that he was able to best the horrid thing with his well-honed fencing skills. When the Skintaker died, it exploded like a \u201cpinata\u201d full of children\u2019s skins. Quite disturbing.<br /> <br /> We returned home after that, and along the way, Percy and Horace, both of whom Alexia kept, went to sleep and became dormant. I don\u2019t know if they can be awakened again, but Alexia thought they might be, under the right circumstances. They hardly seem dangerous without the Puppeteer, and Alexia locked them away in storage. Karen and Younger Natalie were anxiously awaiting our return with Tavia. As we were all getting settled in, Karl, Sara and I rolled up all the Candle Cove paintings and put them in storage. I wanted to burn the all, but Simon seemed to think they might hold some academic interest and asked that we preserve them. I don\u2019t suppose it will do any harm since they are inert now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, August 7, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Today has been rather lazy and slow. Having just finished off a dire threat to the community, we relaxed a bit. There are still things we have to do, such as visiting the Athenaeum, looking into the problem at the Underworld Abbey, and figuring out what is behind the pestilent aura in Glenwood, but they don\u2019t seem quite a urgent as the Candle Cove mess was.<br /> <br /> Karl and I sat for a few hours in the morning talking in the parlour while I finished repairing Lily. Lily was a bit fidgety and impatient about it, but she bore up well. Alexia guided Sara on a detailed tour of the house, giving her all the appropriate warnings, I\u2019m told. Sara is quite pleasant, and though I sense a flicker of mischief in her eyes, I don\u2019t think she is foolish enough to bother things best left undisturbed.<br /> <br /> Our Natalie is taking Karen and Younger Natalie out clubbing tonight. Doc and Simon aren\u2019t going with them, which seems a bit sad to me. Doc seems to get left behind a lot in his two-way relationship with Natalie and Karen. I feel sorry for him. He didn\u2019t seem upset about it, though. Maybe the girls are going somewhere he doesn\u2019t want to go. Sara will be going with them, and the whole group has been spending the afternoon picking out clothes and experimenting with make-up.<br /> <br /> As for me, Karl asked me if I\u2019d like to go out tonight, and of course I said yes! It will be our first real date. Well, honestly our night-time swims in the ocean depth have been dates, but this will be the first time we\u2019ve gone out somewhere in public. The Bride and I are both very excited, and she\u2019s fussing around in my head, reminding me over and over of all the little things I need to do to get ready. I don\u2019t really mind her doting, though. Our thoughts echo each other so much it\u2019s hard to tell the difference sometimes between her mind and my own.<br /> <br /> I think Karl and I will go to that posh Italian place I recommended to Mongler and Gretchen. Afterward, we might visit the local Barnes &amp; Noble to browse and sit chatting over cups of tea or coffee.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been wanting to go hiking at Sleeping Giant State Park. I wonder if Karl wouldn\u2019t enjoy doing something like that, if I could get Doc to arrange things with Deirdre and her pack. They do owe us, after all, and Karl means them and their territory no harm.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>American Language</u><br /> <br /> Pi\u00f1ata - a fancifully sculpted and decorated paper container made to hold candy or other treats so that children can smash it open to claim its prizes. It\u2019s a Spanish word and convention. I\u2019m not sure I can think kindly on pi\u00f1atas since the term was first used by Simon to describe how the Skintaker died\u2026 I do appreciate Simon explaining what a pi\u00f1ata is to me, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>A Misbehaving Child</u><br /> <br /> After our fight with the Puppeteer, I picked Lily up and gave her a big hug while thanking her for her help, but then I had to scold her for stowing away and putting herself in such terrible danger. Her attempts to go with us when we leave the house are becoming habitual, and I don\u2019t think she understand the danger. I\u2019m not sure my admonition really stuck with her, though. If this sort of behavior keeps up, I might have to punish her more severely so that she learns. She is a bit like a child, and it won\u2019t do for her to become spoiled. I wonder how that aspect of motherhood fits into her outlook as a femininity spirit?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Friday, August 6th<br /> <br /> -Taken care of. Going home.<br /> <br /> -Not all banged up this time.<br /> <br /> -My family is a sight for sore eyes.<br /> <br /> -May be going clubbing tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> -Hanging with Karen &amp; Doc &amp; Spooky &amp; Carl (Karl?)<br /> <br /> -Well aren\u2019t they just cute?<br /> <br /> -I have been promised a massage and I shall not be kept from it!<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, August 7th<br /> <br /> -Gloom Cookie First Class Natalie reporting for duty, Sir!<br /> <br /> -First (and second) crying fit talking to Sara about tonight. They won\u2019t be the last.<br /> <br /> -But she is going to join us! Yay!<br /> <br /> -Karen will be pleased (better not be too pleased)<br /> <br /> -Alexia will be also, and Chandra, quite a party!<br /> <br /> -Simon won\u2019t. Ah well, no big surprise.<br /> <br /> -Maybe he and Doc can braid each other\u2019s hair and have boi talk.<br /> <br /> -I think Jasmine will be happier not being asked.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -I hate sudden, out of nowhere crying jags.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s time for a John Hughes-esque makeover, but in reverse.<br /> <br /> -Well I have my outfit!<br /> <br /> -As done Karen. Rawr.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me has a little more going on up front then I do and I am not sure how I feel about that.<br /> <br /> -No I won\u2019t wear the outfit I had on leading the girl around on the leash in the S*G picture but thanks for asking Mini Me X-O<br /> <br /> -The internet is a dangerous thing.<br /> <br /> -Questions about Karen and leashes are not going to be answered. Doubly so if they are about which end I am on.<br /> <br /> -OK Sara is here, surely, the embarrassing questions are over.<br /> <br /> -Maybe.<br /> <br /> -I will be kind and let Karen apply some of Sara\u2019s make up, give her a chance to look in her eyes a bit. This will appear on my sainthood application.<br /> <br /> -Well Alexia is all dressed like a boi!<br /> <br /> -And this may be the second time I have seen Chandra in a skirt.<br /> <br /> -Well, I know how THEIR relationship works.<br /> <br /> -I am pretty sure Sara can put on her own lipstick, Karen.<br /> <br /> -Mini Me is gorgeous. Unless the girls are good at judging ages I won\u2019t have anyone to talk to at Gotham Citi.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear I am actually almost worried about that. x_x<br /> <br /> -OK no time to panic here we go!<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alexia\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Author's note: the letter below came in an envelope attached to the<br /> top of a large package.<br /> <br /> Opening the package reveals a complicated and expensive insulation<br /> surrounding two halves of larges cakes. One half is decorated with<br /> white icing and elaborate candy doves, the inside is filled with<br /> layers of fluffy vanilla cake and strawberry cream spread. The other<br /> half is decorated with dark chocolate icing with chocolate shavings<br /> artfully sprinkled on top, the inside is layers of chocolate cake with<br /> a creamy rich peanut butter spread in between.<br /> <br /> Inside the envelope is also two pictures. The first of a black cat and<br /> a rag doll giving the camera the most convincing looks of innocence<br /> while both of them are sitting in the middle of the kitchen floor,<br /> covered in white flour, with a mass of chaotic kitchen mayhem<br /> surrounding them. The second is of three women: Chandra, Alexia, and<br /> Sara between them. All three have huge smiles on their faces and both<br /> Alexia and Chandra are holding two fingers up behind Sara's head.<br /> <br /> The letter is hand written on orange stationary decorated with cute<br /> little halloween ghosts (more like Casper and less like Sadako) in the<br /> corners. There are cute little hand drawn pictures of rag dolls and<br /> kittens (similar to the ones in the picture) all playing together<br /> across the bottom of the letter.<br /> <br /> &quot;Dear Gwen,<br /> <br /> The Cracked Cook and I can't agree on what your favorite kind of cake<br /> is, so we're sending a half of each. We are all doing well over here.<br /> Sara, the cute girl with the awesome tattoos from the Flesh Fair,<br /> stopped by and she's currently staying with us. I've enclosed a<br /> picture in case you can't remember her. And the picture of our two<br /> kitchen trouble makers was too adorable to not send. So, I'm not good<br /> at this whole letter writing stuff, but suffice to say that I really<br /> miss your driving--so much confident adrenaline filled fun terrifying<br /> rides is only achieved when you are behind the wheel, I do bow down to<br /> your mastery of automobileness. We hope you are doing well, and<br /> Chandra and Tavia and Jasmine and Lily and oh *in this space the word<br /> &quot;hell&quot; has been crossed out with &quot;heck&quot; written above it* everyone<br /> says 'hi' -- be sure to have lots of fun and don't be a stranger.<br /> <br /> P.S. Drop us a line to say which cake half you liked better so I can<br /> prove that I'm right.<br /> <br /> Yours Truly,<br /> Alexia&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVII</i><br /> <br /> My my wasn\u2019t that adorable?<br /> <br /> The final battle was interesting, and raised more questions then answers. Just what happened? Will it happen again?<br /> <br /> Past that was mostly roleplaying. Getting Sara integrated, showing her the House. I'll try to have some Sara info soon my &quot;working on games&quot; time has been swamped by various projects.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time if you would. It should be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:17:36-08:00","id":16975,"title":"","content":"With the immediate threat of Candle Cove gone, our protagonists settle in and get acquainted. A little more variation this time given the clubbing split (Natalie/Alexia/Sara went one place, Jasmine another, Doc/Simon another) but eventually they come back together. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Sunday, August 8, 2010<br /> <br /> Rose came to talk to me before everyone left tonight. She still has some glimmer of misplaced hope that I will do more than just hook up with Deirdre. But while she managed to skirt that topic this time, she did want to ask a favor. She wants to take Karl hiking which is great but she wanted the two of them to trek through Sleeping Giant State Park. She needed my help as she wanted me to ask permission from Ildefonso, likely through Deirdre. I told her I would, but not until tomorrow given they would likely be getting ready to go out tonight as well. I also told her I couldn\u2019t promise anything. I like Karl; I know he\u2019s not trying to do anything but enjoy his time with Rose. However he is still a Brineborn and I don\u2019t know how the Uratha are going to take to that.<br /> <br /> After that rather awkward discussion, everyone headed out. Snowflake and I went out planning to be a little naughty in Alchemy. When we got there, those plans go more than a little altered. The hipsters that somehow managed not to find the Foreigner-Eating Bedroom at our party there, which was a pity. Also in attendance were Clarissa and Deanna, as well as nine dead Chinese people, including the vampiric Sheriff, all at the pool tables. After a brief conference between ourselves, Snowflake and I took a seat near the tables. With extra issues in using Boneyard and really not wanting to be recognized as always being around strange events, our night seemed greatly dampened. We did notice that Clarissa was making some ambitious shots and Deanna would whistle a little Star Wars-esque tune every time. Her insistence on Clarissa \u201cusing the Force\u201d is both amusing and annoying, but as Clarissa seemed okay with it, we didn\u2019t get involved. Besides, sometimes Deanna was wrong and Clarissa just made a nice shot. Then we got a break when Pilot Light and a very curvaceous friend came in together. I didn\u2019t recognize her but Snowflake did. He explained Lauren was an AMC student, but he had no idea what she was doing with Pilot Light. All I could tell was she was very enthusiastic about her alcohol.<br /> <br /> Our new plan, after our hopes of hustling hipsters were dashed, was for me to keep watch on the hipsters, just in case. Snowflake would be keeping tabs on the \u201cBloody Beijing\u201d contingent. Alchemy has already been blown up once, and with Murder Ballads still harboring the Beast of Bethlehem, we didn\u2019t want another supernatural flare up. Like I said, Pilot Light and Lauren were a break for us as he challenged Clarissa to a game. By that point, the \u201cBloody Beijing\u201d Contingent has moved to the dance floor. Snowflake winked at me before explaining to Pilot Light that beer was his Zen. Then he leaned a chair against the wall while I stood by him and watched. It all looked so cliche but it was fun. Clarissa didn\u2019t \u201cuse the Force\u201d too much and Snowflake didn\u2019t push the envelope either. Eventually though, our \u201cyoung Jedi\u201d won so Pilot Light challenged the hipsters. For that, I got another round of drinks.<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, Snowflake dropped his Boneyard and just encouraged Pilot Light for that game. As we hadn\u2019t been out for long, I was a little surprised when I got the call from Nightshade. They were coming by to join us. When I got off the phone, I found Lauren chatting up Snowflake. That was a little unexpected but she did make it clear very early on, she was only friends with PIlot Light. When the ladies arrived, I learned that Bella Donna had a good time but was unfortunately (in theory) \u201ccute\u201d to any of the women she seemed interested in. Nightshade seemed fine, but Karen was still somewhat unhappy with the night. I took Karen out to dance and try to calm her down. Apparently the groupies Nightshade had at the party showed up to Gotham Citi. In general this was okay as Bright Eyes went home with one. But one of them, who shall remain nameless for her own benefit, was actively interested in Nightshade. I knew where this was going after that. I\u2019m really glad Karen and I are friends, even if we aren\u2019t that close. She seemed to level out after a moment of awkward conversation. Fortunately, the groupie in question didn\u2019t follow them, or there may have been blood. Then I danced with Bella Donna for fun and to make sure no one tried anything stupid on the dance floor. If she was bothered by not getting picked up, she didn\u2019t seem like it with me. And I\u2019m no expert, but teenagers are usually terrible about hiding disappointment.<br /> <br /> By just after midnight, it was pretty clear Snowflake was not coming back to the Bluffs. Gently making an excuse to pull me to the side, he remembered about the whole wingman issue. Knowing that Tavia would want an answer as to why he wasn\u2019t home, Snowflake came up with a plan. His friend Julian called and asked him to come back to Providence. He needed Snowflake to properly make fun of a local poetry reading. I pointed out that it would be easy to check his phone for call records and Tavia was nothing if not thorough. He sent a text to Julian to have him call so the records would match and also so Julian knew what the deal was. I did point out that this would involve me trying to convince someone of something. That was almost a joke, but trying to convince Tavia... really a bad idea. Even still, Snowflake went home with Lauren. So I rode back with Nightshade, Bella Donna, and Karen.<br /> <br /> When we got home, Tavia came out of her studio expecting to find Snowflake. So I dutifully told my tale. I knew as soon as I stopped talking, she was not buying it. Tavia looked coldly even and said she understood before stalking off. I felt sick knowing I\u2019d just lied to her face like that. Nevermind that she knew slipping in and stabbing me in my sleep wouldn\u2019t help, I\u2019d just broken her trust. Trust in the sense of family I\u2019d enjoyed building. It felt dirty and I wanted to go after her and apologize. But I knew that wouldn\u2019t help. The worst part is, I don\u2019t know what will. This better be worth it for Snowflake. I can\u2019t do that ever again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1315 Hours, Sunday, August, 8, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation this morning took an hour, but it felt much longer. I knew it was because of how wrong I felt last night. Tavia was nowhere to be found when I came down, but to be honest I didn\u2019t try to find her. There\u2019s no way I couldn\u2019t look her in the eye again. I kept to myself until Nightshade came to me and was obviously upset. She was taking Bella Donna leaving very badly. I tried to be comforting and remind her that this was only a first visit. There was nothing that I knew about that would keep her from coming back again. I knew that Snowflake had some interesting thoughts and beliefs about Matron X, but I was trying to keep this from escalating emotionally for Nightshade. We all enjoyed Bella Donna\u2019s stay and approved of Nightshade being a part of her life. Privately Karen and I both think it\u2019s a bad idea for Nightshade to dive right into full time parenting, but that isn\u2019t something we needed to bring up either. I let her sob for a bit and just reminded her of all the positive things I could think of to help soothe her pain. I knew she\u2019d miss Bella Donna, but that\u2019s a good thing. Once she was mostly stable again, she went to get cleaned up before Bella Donna stumbled out of bed.<br /> <br /> I fired up my laptop and tried to find various junk yards online throughout Connecticut. Around 1130 Hours, I sent Snowflake a text letting him know things went as well as expected and that I was looking up junk yards. After that I went outside to tend to my somewhat neglected Death Garden. Snowflake apparently had clothes in his car as he came home around 1200 Hours already dressed in his suit and went straight to the graveyard. No one wants to disturb him while he pays his respects to his parents, so I came in to write this. We\u2019ll have to talk later though.<br /> While I want to be there for him and be a part of the family, I can\u2019t help but see Tavia as part of that same family as well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, August 7, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Alexia showed me the most adorable pictures of Fu and Lily! They had gotten up to some mischief in the kitchen while she was baking a cake to send to Gwen. The trouble-making pair were covered in flour and looked very pleased with themselves. It was the cutest thing, though I\u2019m going to have to give Fu a bath now, and he doesn\u2019t like that.<br /> <br /> Before everyone parted ways for their evening engagements, I cornered Doc and asked if he was still friends with Deirdre, the werewolf. He said he was, so I asked if he would please ask her for permission for Karl and me to go hiking in Sleeping Giant State Park. Normally, it wouldn\u2019t be a problem, but they might not like Karl being there, so I want to warn them before we drop in.<br /> <br /> I also went to the spa run by my Taiwanese friend Xuebing for a manicure and pedicure in preparation for my date. Tavia asked if she could go with me, and of course I said I\u2019d like that, even if I was a bit anxious about how she might behave. I\u2019m never quite comfortable around her, knowing how quickly she can turn psychotic. But we had a pleasant time, and I found the trip relaxing. I don\u2019t think Tavia had been to a spa before; next time Alexia and I go for a full spa treatment, we might have to take Tavia.<br /> <br /> Saturday, August 7, 2010, Night<br /> I had a wonderful date with Karl tonigh! First, we went to the fancy Italian restaurant I recommended to Mongler and Gretchen. The food and service there are wonderful, and the atmosphere is classy and inviting, perfect for a romantic date. Karl was such a gentleman, though I could tell he was very nervous. Once we were seated and were giving our orders to the waiter, he started stumbling anxiously over the etiquette until I gently placed my hand on his. That small bit of reassurance seemed to calm him.<br /> <br /> Dinner was fantastic. We had a nice conversation and learned more about each other. He thinks I\u2019ve been good for him, as I\u2019ve encouraged his literary interests and helped him expand his horizons beyond fishing. I learned that enjoys reading about history. Something about the antiquity of things appeals to him. He is fascinated with old relics. There are plenty of those around the mansion, but I suggested that we visit some quality antique shops and see what treasures we might find. Of course my father owns an antique shop in Taiwan, so I grew up around old things, and can very much understand Karl\u2019s interest.<br /> <br /> I asked if Karl would be interested in hiking at Sleeping Giant State Park. I\u2019ve been wanting to hike there for awhile, so I was glad when he said he\u2019s love to do that. I\u2019m quite excited about it.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I blundered badly then. I mentioned that hiking was something Richard and I enjoyed doing together, and the memory of Richard brought a pang of sorrow and guilt that must have shown in my expression, because Karl became uncertain and anxious again, and there were several moments of tremendous awkwardness between us. I regretted bringing up Richard immediately, and apologized, trying to change the subject quickly. We soon returned to more pleasant topics, and my sadness passed quickly, but I think the damage was done. The Bride, however, assures me that it\u2019s quite all right. My sorrow over Richard will never be completely quelled by a new love, and she says that it\u2019s better that Karl become accustomed to my melancholy turns now at the beginning of our relationship rather than later. If our relationship blossoms, though, I don\u2019t want Karl to feel like he\u2019s competing with a memory, even if he really is.<br /> <br /> After dinner we went to Barnes &amp; Noble and browsed, chatting lightly about the books we wanted to read. We each picked up a new book, and Karl was kind enough to pay for mine and for my coffee when we settled in at the store\u2019s coffee shop to continue talking. I quite enjoyed our bookshop stroll. It felt very pleasant and intimate. It was pleasant to be seen as a couple too, even if I did have to glare at a few people who were gawking unpleasantly at Karl.<br /> <br /> Then we returned home and found a movie to watch on Netflix while we snuggled on the couch. Only Tavia was home, and she stayed elsewhere in the mansion, so we had the TV room all to ourselves, which was nice for a change. I did have the impression that someone was watching us at one point, though. I suspect Lily was up to her usual mischief.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, August 8, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> My meditation this morning was amazing. I felt so wonderfully centered; I wonder if my happiness with Karl had anything to do with it?<br /> <br /> Not everyone returned home last night. Doc, Natalie and Karen came home quite late, but Simon stayed out, allegedly having visited Julian in Providence (though I suspect he was elsewhere and that Doc was lying to placate Tavia). Our guest, Sara, did not return either, and Karen sadi that she had gone home with someone she met at a club. I was surprised to find that Alexia was also absent, but I think she and Chandra simply decided to spend the night at Chandra\u2019s place instead of the mansion.<br /> <br /> After Alexia came home, I helped her with some gardening. Sara returned well before noon and helped us, so we were able to chat a bit. She\u2019s settling in nicely, it seems. Somehow Lily came up and we explained to Sara as best we could what Lily really is and the dangers she poses. Doing so reminded Alexia of some of the horrors she saw in Sansbury Hall, so I tried to change the subject quickly. I hope we haven\u2019t frightened Sara off, but she seems to be made of sterner stuff.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes<br /> </u><br /> <u>Doc and Deirdre</u><br /> <br /> I think I put Doc on the spot a bit when we were talking about Deirdre. I asked if he still had any sort of relationship with her, and commented that the two of them seemed good together. I supposed I must have pushed him in that direction a bit, which made Doc a bit uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not encouraging him to be unfaithful to Natalie, insomuch as that\u2019s even possible given their odd relationship. And I know that Natalie needs Doc and the support he offers her. But the relationship between Doc, Natalie, and Karen just isn\u2019t working out. Doc and Natalie care deeply about one another, but any time Natalie needs any sort of romantic or sexual companionship, she immediately turns to Karen, and Doc is more often than not left out. It\u2019s unfair and hurtful and I feel bad that he has to put up with such neglect. I want him to be happy, and I don\u2019t think he can find that with Natalie, not as long as Karen (or anyone else, for that matter) is also a part of the picture.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s why I\u2019d like to see Doc find romance elsewhere, with someone who will be willing to devote her attention to him like he deserves. I don\u2019t know if Deirdre is the right person for him, but they seem to like each other quite a lot, so maybe there\u2019s some potential there. And even if there isn\u2019t, it\u2019s a start.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Date Ideas</u><br /> <br /> I\u2019m trying to keep a list of possible date ideas. I need to ask Karl if he has any ideas as well.<br /> <br /> - Hiking at Sleeping Giant: I do hope Deirdre and Ildefonso are amenable to this.<br /> <br /> - Amusement Park? Not so sure this would be good, since Karl might be a bit big to fit comfortably in rides, and I\u2019ve always found amusement parks to be a bit annoying.<br /> <br /> - Movies: I wonder if there is any theatre in the area that shows classic movies on some nights? Surely in a college town like this there must be something like that.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Theatre: I should find out whether Karl would like to go see any stage plays.<br /> <br /> - Graveyard Walk: I find this to be a very romantic idea, but Karl may not. And of course visiting the cemetery where Richard is buried would be a bad idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> - Gallery: There are always a few art museum exhibits or gallery showings we could visit, but I\u2019m not sure that Karl would find that very interesting. He likes literature, but I don\u2019t know how much he enjoys visual art.<br /> <br /> - Poetry Readings: I know Karl likes to read, but I don\u2019t know if he would like to attend a poetry reading. I understand that Simon performs in a poetry reading somewhere in Providence from time to time. Perhaps I should ask him about it.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets<br /> </b><br /> Saturday, August 7th<br /> <br /> -Quite a crowd quite a crowd!<br /> <br /> -Karen and Sara are getting along well, good thing I am not a jealous person.<br /> <br /> -OK so Mini Me is \u201ccute\u201d that is good and bad for her.<br /> <br /> -I remember when I was \u201ccute\u201d it got me no girls and only creepy guys.<br /> <br /> -Sara is hitting it off with\u2026Eve I think her name was.<br /> <br /> -Well those two are a good team. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -And it is Tatum. Looks like I have someone to talk to.<br /> <br /> -I could just eat her up!<br /> <br /> -\u2026but not with Mini Me here.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear Karen is looming.<br /> <br /> -Gimme a break I\u2019ve been watching you flirt with Sara for a couple hours now &gt;_&lt;<br /> <br /> -I am pretty sure Karen has the hots for me and Tatum. This is easily solved.<br /> <br /> -Oh maybe Karen wants to a jerk. OK. Whatever.<br /> <br /> -Stanley chooses to intervene.<br /> <br /> -Much like Mr. Carp and the Giant Fish who was overfed, Stanley can just walk in and solve everything. The hell.<br /> <br /> -Well Karen is grumpy but quiescent<br /> <br /> -Oh my, looks like Sara and Eve are taking off<br /> <br /> -And Alexia and Chandra are picking up Deirdre.<br /> <br /> -Looks like I am the one not getting laid tonight. Oh well. I\u2019ll manage.<br /> <br /> -Got contact info for Tatum at least.<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s see if Doc is having a better evening.<br /> <br /> -Goddess Goodness Simon is flirting with a\u2026healthy young woman.<br /> <br /> -Apparently they have been helping pilot light play pool?<br /> <br /> -Maybe I can talk to Clarissa without Karen getting all jealous. Think so?<br /> <br /> -OK Karen has not totally lost her mind.<br /> <br /> -Well Doc hasn\u2019t picked up any ladies.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m\u2026not sure Simon is making a good decision.<br /> <br /> -How would he feel if Tavia started taking a massive interest in someone\u2019s chest, I wonder?<br /> <br /> -Not my business. He seems to have convinced Doc to lie for him. Bad idea.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d bug Doc not to do it, but I am sure he would do it out of loyalty and be worried about me being cross with him too. So\u2026yea.<br /> <br /> -Let\u2019s go home. Mini Me is having a sleepy.<br /> <br /> -Tavia\u2019s talking to herself after talking to Doc. Whelp, time for me to go upstairs!<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday August 8th<br /> <br /> -Oh damnit. This is not a good start.<br /> <br /> -Can\u2019t\u2026stop\u2026crying.<br /> <br /> -I gotta pull myself together before Mini Me wakes up. Fuck.<br /> <br /> -Oh Goddess can you pull together for five fucking minutes Allison?<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m not Allison anymore. Allison would have been a good mother.<br /> <br /> -No she can\u2019t leave not yet. No. Not gonna happen. We can cancel her flight.<br /> <br /> -Please please please make something happen so Natalie will stay with me\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Sorry to end on a depressing note.<br /> <br /> The session was mostly roleplaying. The main thing that was not reported was Deirdre actually managed to pick up Alexia and Chandra, and Tavia and Lily spent the night spying on Jasmine and Karl while they were on their date\u2026with a few exchanged described with them arguing and fighting over a pair of binoculars. Also, Doc\u2019s roll to lie to Tavia was terrible, and she saw right through it.<br /> <br /> For Natalie things went downhill that night when Tatum (one of the girls from the party) showed and Natalie flirted with her. The next day it\u2019s the impending \u201closs\u201d of her daughter making her crazy.<br /> <br /> Getting Sara integrated has been fun and gone well. I am quite pleased. More forthcoming, comments and questions welcome. Join us next time where Natalie attempts to fight off a nervous breakdown, and Simon is told something that changes everything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:21:06-08:00","id":16976,"title":"","content":"Journal time! Mostly this deals with Simon and Natalie\u2019s personal problems (and to a lesser degree, Jasmine and Doc\u2019s) rather then advancing the overall plot, but should make a good read. Drama is always interesting. If you usually skip Doc\u2019s or Jasmine\u2019s each has info the other doesn\u2019t. Anyway let\u2019s go\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXIX</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Monday, August 9, 2010<br /> <br /> The tension and silence in the House was a serious issue last night. Nothing much else happened, but I still stayed home from patrol, just in case. With Tavia and Nightshade both on edge, I didn\u2019t want to take any chances.<br /> <br /> Meditation was a little easier on the inside this morning, but it still took about an hour. When I came down for breakfast, Karen was already up and wanted to talk to us in general. She was worried about Nightshade in a big way. We all knew that Bella Donna\u2019s departure would have an impact on Nightshade, but Karen actually described it as small animals fleeing the coming earthquake. That was not how I wanted this day to go. Karen was so worried Nightshade was heading for huge breakdown that she broke several unspoken, and some spoken rules. Apparently Nightshade broke one of her own rules, and had stockpiled enough heroin in the Bluffs to be a major problem. This was an issue with Snowflake too as I\u2019m pretty sure Nightshade and he had agreed on that rule when we moved in. The other rule that she broke was to move the stash from Nightshade\u2019s hiding place. I knew that would get her in trouble when Nightshade found out, but right at the moment I was pretty sure Karen would have some backup. I said as much, and Snowflake stated, in a rather unquestionable manner, that he had a house and she wouldn\u2019t have to suffer very much for this indiscretion. The other concern Karen had was that Nightshade would just try to grab the kid and run. Now this one specifically gnawed on me as we had just talked about how Bella Donna was certainly coming back and/or we would go see her soon. Getting mad about Nightshade being emotionally distracted is a really bad idea for me, so I tried to just let it roll off...but it was hard. Seeing Karen as worried as she was wasn\u2019t helping given that Nightshade had kept most of these idea from me already. I might have felt a little jealous of Karen but she was so worried, I couldn\u2019t really wish myself in her place right then. I say that knowing damn well I\u2019m just as worried now so I don\u2019t know what kind of macho bullshit I\u2019m attempting to pull on myself. The truth is Karen and I make a good team and I like that. When things with Nightshade get really bad, we have each other. I know Karen has no interest in me, and that\u2019s okay. She\u2019s about to turn 20, even if she did like guys, I\u2019d not be the one. We just form our own support group when we need it.<br /> <br /> The conversation kept going until something about Tavia came up and we all realized that she was still not down for breakfast. Karl, not entirely pleased to be delivering the news, noted that she was under the House. A brief moment of OH SHIT looks moved around the table until Snowflake announced that he would need to speak with her. I offered to come too, mostly because I still wanted to apologize. Karl spoke up quickly then that Simon should go alone. He very gently suggested that Tavia was naked when he noted she was communing with the sea. Rose pulled Snowflake into the kitchen for a private discussion before he descended into the caverns below. While we still had Karen and I was thinking about it, we discussed setting up a \u201cthe next time\u201d visit to help stabilize Nightshade. This was also determined to probably be on the boat. A day down and a day back on the Saturnine Dreamer does not sound like a horrible way to visit coastal North Carolina. If I remember right, they are about four hours out from Camp Lejeune and really this would not be the time to visit any of my friends in the service. But we do have some ground work laid so hopefully Karen and I can use that to our advantage with Nightshade.<br /> <br /> Snowflake came back up around 1000 Hours, it was visibly shaken and seemed very strange, even for him. When I asked if things were alright, he said yes but then mentioned that things would have to be \u201cdealt with as a couple\u201d several times. I wasn\u2019t completely sure he was sober, and as we were getting everything ready for the airport trip, I told him we\u2019d have to talk after I got back. He said that sounded like a good idea. No part of that conversation seemed good to me, but I had other obligations right then. For now, I\u2019ll have to let it go as we\u2019re about to leave so Bella Donna has enough time to get through TSA and still make her flight...with a little extra time for goodbyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2200 Hours, Monday, August 9, 2010<br /> <br /> Well today has been ...interesting? eventful? emotionally draining? Take your pick.<br /> <br /> Nightshade, Bella Donna, Karen, Bright Eyes, Cupcake, and I all went to the airport to send Bella Donna back home. Things were a little more quiet than I expected on the way, but Nightshade kept it together without any visible problems. We made it through luggage and everything, no problem. We all told Bella Donna goodbye with smiles and hugs. I told her we would see her again, hoping that Nightshade might pick up on that. Mother and Daughter held each other for a bit, then Bella Donna headed down to board. That was when Nightshade began shaking. She turned and walked away, so Karen and I fell in flanking her back to the car. We made it about that far before Nightshade broke down into tears. She was trying to talk through the sobbing but not much was coming out. I understand something about my baby a few times. Cupcake drove home.<br /> <br /> Back at the Bluffs, I gently suggested Nightshade might want to have company around, to let her feel it was her idea and not have her knee jerk reactions. Karen was a bit more direct in ordering Nightshade stay with us. I gave her one of my service looks and she backed off. Fortunately Nightshade saw the upside of not being alone and pulled Karen and I into the TV Room. Nothing kinky, because I read that and thought the same thing at first, just people there to comfort her. Rose came in after she finished training Jean. She meant to be supportive, but in her usual awkward style, was accidentally unhelpful. Realizing this quickly, Rose tried to be comforting for a moment then headed out. I knew things were really serious, even with us there for Nightshade, when I glanced down and saw Elphaba circling through her mistress\u2019 feet and not in Karen\u2019s lap.<br /> <br /> Probably a little after 1300 Hours, I noticed Rose half carrying Snowflake into the kitchen from outside. I asked if I could get drinks for the anyone and Nightshade told me to bring her the girliest drink to ever girl or something to that effect. When I walked into the kitchen, Cupcake shoved ice cream at me while I was explaining our current situation. Snowflake was possibly more drunk than I have ever seen him. They were giving him black coffee to help. I was a little annoyed when I told him our little talk would have to wait until later. Bright Eyes offered to come with me when I mixed the drinks. But before we could leave, Nightshade and Karen came in. Nightshade declared that she needed to be around people. She then pulled Bright Eyes into the hall for a private conversation. They came back in shortly and no one looked worse than before. That\u2019s when Nightshade made the grabby hands at the ice cream I was holding. I had a rare flash of insight and whispered an offer to massage Nightshade\u2019s feet while Karen fed her ice cream. I didn\u2019t know how she might react, but being dragged back into the TV Room was a good clue she was interested. Karen might have been more surprised than Nightshade, but if she minded me taking over foot duties, she didn\u2019t show it.<br /> <br /> Things seemed to calm significantly then. Karl came back in from the caverns a little before dinner so I slipped out to talk to him. He\u2019s part of the family too and may become a more lasting part if Rose can get over her own emotional trauma and let herself love again. I also don\u2019t really want to piss off the Brineborn. So I asked about Tavia to make sure she was going to be okay. I still have to apologize and I said as much. While I don\u2019t think Karl is happy his cousin is upset or that I so blatantly lied to her, he doesn\u2019t seem outraged with me. He said Tavia was okay but gave me a very serious warning. He said that going down to see Tavia, especially right now was not a great idea and he would strongly recommend against it. I had a brief flash to C-3P0 saying, \u201cLet the Wookie win.\u201d I took his advice and thanked him, then walked away knowing somewhere Ronin was very amused without knowing why.<br /> <br /> Just before dinner, I called Deirdre. Last night, things were just too tense and the conversation would have been more awkward than I expected it to be anyway. I realized immediately this was not a talk to have over the phone. She enjoyed my bizarre attempts at secrecy but agreed to meet me at Lulu\u2019s at 2000 Hours. Thankfully dinner was almost normal for us. I did tell Rose that I would be asking the favor. She was very grateful.<br /> <br /> When I arrived, Deirdre was already there and dressed to get my attention. I don\u2019t want to sound overly confident, she made it pretty clear \u201cthe girls\u201d were happy to see me. Once we had coffee and a table as far away from other people as we could, I explained the favor I needed to ask. I was really happy it was only Deirdre. I got the feeling she tensed more than she usually does so Eris would have killed me on the spot. There were a lot of issues all the way around, none of which related directly to Rose and Karl going hiking in the park. I mostly expected this, but the conversation turned more toward explaining things to me. I thought I understood before I got there, but I was wrong. It\u2019s about so much more than just territory, at least the way they look at it. We talked about Noriko and the Colony, the name they use for that group. They actually are an infection, like the old stories of lycanthropy. I think that\u2019s why Malard was okay with her being around. But Dierdre said the Brineborn always spawn true, which is apparently not something the Uratha do. This led to the mention of Karl and Rose having kids. Before I thought, I said that if Karl could get far enough to get Rose pregnant, I\u2019d shake his damn hand. The look I got from Deirdre reminded me I didn\u2019t think about that comment. I was just glad Ronin didn\u2019t come along at that point. In the end, we agreed to discuss things. Me with Karl, to let him know he may be asked (forced) to agree that he and any \u201cspawn\u201d will not overrun the packs. Plus he will have to swear alliance against the Pure if they were ever to invade. That last part I\u2019m not worried about, as if the Pure come back, my whole Krewe will be on the Uratha\u2019s side in that fight. Deirdre will talk with Ildefonso after I get an idea of Karl\u2019s stance. She plans to couch it in terms of a controlled element which will be a weapon against the Pure. We\u2019ll see how this goes.<br /> <br /> Now, I think I\u2019m going to get a strong drink and draw until I think I can figure out how/when to discuss this with Rose and Karl.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, August 9, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> Over breakfast this morning, Karen informed us that Natalie was on the verge of a breakdown over Younger Natalie\u2019s impending departure today. Having reuinited with her daughter, she is not handling their separation well, which is understandable. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s much we can do to help her, though Doc and Karen will stick with Natalie to help her out. I know I won\u2019t be able to do any good, so I\u2019m going to try and stay out of the way. I honestly think that things would be much better if Natalie would reconcile with her own mother, as it would seem less like Younger Natalie was being taken from her again. But she seems stubbornly resistant to that. Indeed, Natalie seems to cling to her fears much more strongly than is healthy, but also lacks the conviction to truly carry though with overcoming them when she decides to do so. At least she\u2019s trying, but her psychological scars are so severe that she is bound by them in ways I cannot understand and, frankly, find a bit frustrating.<br /> <br /> Sara was quite concerned. She seems a very caring sort. I was worried we might be burdening our guest unnecessarily, but she said she prefered to help out if she could. It\u2019s nice to have someone about who is good with people and not completely mired in psychological trauma.<br /> <br /> Simon noticed that Tavia was not at breakfast, which likely meant she must be upset over his indiscretions of Saturday night. Naturally, we were all worried she might be plotting a killing spree, but Karl assured us she was in the cave beneath the house. Simon resolved to go see her, but before he left, I drew him aside and reminded him that I was there for him, and that I could try to talk to Tavia about his need for freedom if he wanted me to, since she likes me for some reason.<br /> <br /> Simon confessed that freedom was something he very much desired, but even if Tavia weren\u2019t so obsessively possessive, he might have difficulty finding that freedom. If he does not marry Tavia to continue the his family line, then Tzipporah might step in to take over the family, and we simply cannot allow that. I assured him that the krewe would do all we could to defeat Tzipporah, and that the threat she posed should not influence his romantic decisions.<br /> <br /> Simon thanked be for my advice and then went to see Tavia. I hope all is well. Now I\u2019m off to train Jean while Alexia, Sara, and Doc take the two Natalie\u2019s to the airport. I hope Our Natalie will be okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 9, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Natalie broke down a bit on the ride back (or so Alexia tells me), but she is actually okay, more or less. That\u2019s good to know. Doc and Karen have kept her company and refuse to let her retreat to her room, which I suppose is for the best.<br /> <br /> Simon, on the other hand, may not be. I\u2019m quite worried about him. When I returned to the house this afternoon, he was nowhere to be found, but Karl informed me that he had gone to seek solace at his tomb. Normally I would not bother Simon there, as I know it\u2019s his sanctuary, but I was teribly worried about him, so I ventured to the mausoleum.<br /> <br /> I think Simon was happy be able to unburden himself, and we talked for a long while. We discussed his freedom from the shackles of familial obligations, but he seemed worried that freedom from Fishborne expectations would also break the chains of his responsibilities to the family, and though he fears becoming a scion of the household like his father before him, he also feels it is important to maintain his grasp over the family\u2019s power. Given the alternatives, I agree with him.<br /> <br /> He wants to be happy, but he is burdened by his fears. In confidence, he revealed to me that Tavia is pregnant. I was quite shocked, and honestly a bit dismayed. The presence of a child should be the occasion for happiness and celebration, but I fear that this child is gambit. Certainly Simon\u2019s ill-advised coupling with Tavia was his own choice, and the child is the consequence of that choice, but I strongly suspect that Tavia informed Simon of her preganancy in order to prevent him from telling her that he did not wish to be with her anymore. She\u2019s using her child to trap him, and that disturbs me terribly. It would seem that Tavia is not just an eccentric woman with psychotic tendencies, but also deeply manipulative. She is reinforcing the Fishborne shackles that Simon so desperately wants to escape.<br /> <br /> And the worse part is that Simon has decided to give in after all. He even told me that the pregnancy has resolved the whole issue of freedom because his unborn child has made the choice for him. It concerns me that he seemed relieved to no longer have to struggle with the issue; he was practically giddy over having the burden of choice removed from him. I\u2019m terribly worried about him.<br /> <br /> Simon also revealed other worries to me. Apparently, when he died and returned as a sin-eater, he was overcome with a murderous fugue in which he attempted to shatter the bonds of his family once and for all by killing his parents. He did not come out and say that exactly, but I was able to infer it from what he did say, and I think he wanted me to know his secret.<br /> <br /> I hardly knew how to react to Simon\u2019s chilling revelation, but I could tell that he felt tremendous remorse. I never realized that Simon was so troubled, for he hides it well. And now he fears that his own child will grow up with same issues and will someday try to kill him in turn. He\u2019s terrified of it, in fact. I assured him that his child would grow up in a different environment that he did. The krewe is here to help, for one thing. But despite my assurances, I\u2019m also worried. The child\u2019s very birth is something of a trap for Simon, and if Simon throws away his freedom for the expediency of doing what his family expects of him, then he may well be creating an oppressive environment for his child. How can I say whether or not the child will follow his father\u2019s path?<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I encouraged Simon to look after his own happiness as well. He cannot simply become a tool of the family. He must seek his own well-being too. He seems as chained to the remorse of who he once was\u2014the young man who killed his own parents\u2014as he is to his familial obligations. So I encouraged him to seek out and be responsible for the man he wants to be, not the person he regrets.<br /> <br /> After our long talk, I helped a very drunk Simon to the kitchen to get sobered up. Karl had been down to see Tavia by then, and said she was disturbingly serene. That\u2019s never a good sign.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Karl, I sought a bit of comfort in his company later, and shared some of my worries over Simon. I did not mention anything regarding the child or Simon\u2019s murderous history, but I tried to express my concern for his happiness. Karl was sympathetic, which was really all I wanted.<br /> <br /> Karl informed me that he would need to return to Cold Harbor for a few days to gather some of his possessions and put things in order so that he can move into the mansion on a more permanent basis. I was quite happy to hear that, though I will miss him for the next few days.<br /> <u><br /> <br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Updated To Do List</u><br /> <br /> Alexia and I spent some time comparing notes on what we needed to do as a krewe.<br /> <br /> 1. Investigate and deal with the outsider taint creeping into Glenwood.<br /> <br /> 2. Visit the Athenaeum to learn more about the Strix. Then use that information to gain the assistance of the local vampires in accepting Chandra and learning who really owns Murder Ballads so that we can deal with the Beast of Bethlehem there.<br /> <br /> 3. Help the nuns in the Underworld Chapel at St. Mary\u2019s deal with \u201cGarlize\u201d<br /> <br /> 4. Deal with Dwayne Franklin\u2019s ghost, who is now a geist. This is a priority only after we have reoslved the threats against Officer Clevon Norris, for we will need his help in resolving Franklin\u2019s anchors (if that\u2019s even possible). Thus, we will need to visit the Athenaeum first to gain leverage with the vampires.<br /> <br /> 5. Meet with Uncle Guang. He will need to approach me first.<br /> <br /> 6. Find out more about Shatina and her disappearance. There is nothing we can do about this right now, so we might as well let it go until something else happens. Mongler and his people are keeping an eye on it.<br /> <br /> 7. Deal with Anders Mother, the blood-bathing immortal. Again, there is little we can do right now, though if we get a chance to direct our efforts toward helping Anders, that might change.<br /> <br /> 8. Resolve Marjorie, the hitchhiking ghost. As she doesn\u2019t even realize she\u2019s dead, this might be a bit challenging right now, and there are more urgent problems.<br /> <br /> Alexia and I decided the krewe should go see what we could do for the nuns in the Underworld Chapel next. I for one feel far more comfortable dealing with ghosts than with anything else, so this is certainly the most appealing option for me. I also feel personally responsible for helping them, as I was the one who agreed to do so.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>What Am I Doing?</u><br /> <br /> All of the talk with Simon and my fresh insights into Tavia\u2019s purpose have left me feeling anxious about my relationship with Karl. He\u2019s wonderful, intelligent, strong and caring. The fact that he has the blood of an ancient fish-god running in his veins and can become a monstrous fish-creature doesn\u2019t bother me that much anymore. But his family does bother me. I\u2019m frightened of the Fishbornes, all the more so because of Simon\u2019s fears and Tavia\u2019s behavior. I know the Cold Harbor branch of the family is quite different, but from what I do know of them, I don\u2019t really feel any more comfortable about them.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t tell Karl any of this, for I don\u2019t want to upset him. It\u2019s terrible of me to look at his family with such fear and discomfort, but I can\u2019t help it. If our relationship grows deeper, I don\u2019t know if I want to become a part of the Fishborne family. The Bride shares my worries, though she is far more willing to excuse them in favor of romance. Perhaps she is right, and love does conquer all. Or perhaps my melancholy disposition has jaded me just enough to worry that the adage may not be true.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday August 8th<br /> <br /> -Ah, there is my big girl.<br /> <br /> -The hot tub is niiiiiiice.<br /> <br /> -Maybe the hot tub will make mini me want to stay?<br /> <br /> -Karen is watching me with her concerned face.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s vain, but I am glad Mini Me turned out so pretty.<br /> <br /> -I wish this moment could last forever.<br /> <br /> -Time for bed, time for tears.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday August 9th<br /> <br /> -Help<br /> <br /> -Can\u2019t stop crying.<br /> <br /> -Please someone stop this.<br /> <br /> -Please<br /> <br /> -Please<br /> <br /> -Goddess<br /> <br /> -Managed not try cry where she could see me, or even in the airport. Small victories.<br /> <br /> -She\u2019s gone.<br /> <br /> -Goddess<br /> <br /> -Pain<br /> <br /> -Karen and Doc\u2026where would I be without them.<br /> <br /> -She\u2019s gone.<br /> <br /> -Need to not drink too much.<br /> <br /> -Surrounded by people who want to comfort me. It\u2019s not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> -They do know how to pamper a poor gothette.<br /> <br /> -Need sleepies.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -OK, I need to have a little talk with Miss Smith.<br /> <br /> -Damnit.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXIX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add here. Tavia and Simon have largely made up. The only thing really missed was Tavia expressing worry about Chandra, one of her closest friends. The issue being Chandra, being a Penanggalan, had an urge to feed on (and transform) pregnant women (most having been turned at this time, Chandra being an exception as her sire was obsessed with her, though hardly the only one). Tavia was with it enough to realize that could be a danger. <br /> <br /> It was also noted a number of little signs had come up Tavia was pregnant (no guarding the paintings during her period recently, knitting regularly, Chandra had commented on her smelling nice and she is drawn to feed on pregnant women). Right now only Simon and Jasmine know Tavia is pregnant.<br /> <br /> Natalie has done well on her Resolve rolls so far (4 Resolve will do that for you) so has remained fairly stable.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add mostly a drama session. And there may be more next time. Whee! Oh, if you are interested, started a new game of Deadlands: Lost Colony involving Simon\u2019s and Sara\u2019s players (and me, of course) that can be followed <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?658087-Deadlands-Lost-Colony-The-Shadow-Valley-Colonial-Rangers\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>. I\u2019ll see you in two weeks. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:23:45-08:00","id":16977,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time again for hearing from the old Geist Krewe. Lots of things being sorted out, and they do a little exploring. And make some friends. Sort of. I\u2019ll let them explain.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXX</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1115 Hours, Tuesday, August 10, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation went really quickly this morning. It was almost like I knew exactly what mental path to take to find peace. I felt determined and ready for the day in a way I haven\u2019t in some time. Rose opened her eyes around the same time and for a moment I thought she looked surprised to see me also rousing. Then we went back to our rooms to get ready for breakfast.<br /> <br /> Karen was already downstairs when I came to the kitchen. I asked how things were, knowing I didn\u2019t hear anything last night. She said Nightshade was extremely pissed last night, but they got the fight over and done with and were better now. I was relieved and I think she appreciated the concern. Once the others assembled for Cupcake\u2019s crepes, Rose told us that Karl had returned to Cold Harbor last night. For a split second, I was afraid something had happened but then she explained he needed to get things in order at home before coming back here for a more extended stay. Karl being gone meant I had a little longer to figure out how to explain the whole \u201chiking\u201d situation. I think I really need to talk to Karl away from Rose for things to work out the best. Then Rose announced she and Cupcake had revised our scheduled tasks for the next few weeks. Karen instinctively patted me on the shoulder as I took another bite. Apparently I broadcast some sensation when this happens. The others think it bothers more than it does. I mean it is a good idea to know what is most pressing to deal with...just maybe not on a near daily basis. But it gives Rose a sense of structure and I know the merits of structure all too well. Anyway, I reminded everyone that tomorrow was Karen\u2019s birthday and she perked up. Said that Nightshade was taking her away tomorrow for her birthday. She didn\u2019t know where but thought we should now since we were making plans. I had forgotten I didn\u2019t have a present for her yet. I knew immediately I had to fix that. Also thought Snowflake might like in too. I had an idea then. The stompy boots really get Karen excited and she is more than just slightly interested in our style of occult. I needed to talk with Snowflake first before I mentioned anything otherwise.<br /> <br /> Karen said something about Leslie and off we went on an information dump about Tzipporah. I don\u2019t think Karen wanted to know all that, but Tavia dotted the exclamation point by saying just how much the woman needed to be killed permanently. Nightshade came down about then and began alternating between mine and Karen\u2019s shoulders. When she heard we were thinking about dealing with the nuns and Beckoning Initiate, she noted she had some more information about Garlize. It was either a Neverborn or a rogue Kerberos. While the idea of Kerberoi going rogue is terrifying, I don\u2019t think the alternative is any better. None of us really knew so Nightshade explained a Neverborn was an unknowably ancient being that never lived. The rumors are that if such a creature exists, it dwelled in the time before creation in the Shadow of nothingness. Chances are good that if that\u2019s at all true, it will attack us on sight. The only experience it could have had with Sin-Eaters would be hostile. And I\u2019m not immediately interested in learning if the earliest Middle Shadows were notably more powerful or not. No matter what, the possibility exists that Garlize was forced out of a Dead Dominion, which means there was something there more powerful than it. That means the nuns are officially in more trouble than we realized. So we planned to go scout the Underworld and investigate the problem for the nuns.<br /> <br /> Before we all scattered, I made sure to get Karen\u2019s shoe size. That surprised her as she didn\u2019t really expect me to ask. Then I managed to catch Snowflake so we could talk. I told him I was sorry, but I couldn\u2019t treat Tavia as anything less than family if I was going to treat he and Karl that way. And lying to her the way I did made me sick to my stomach. He told me that he understood but there were much bigger things than last weekend going on now. I asked him what he was talking about, but he answered with his own question. He asked if he told me, could I act surprised later? I reminded him we were in this situation in part because I couldn\u2019t lie for shit. He nodded and just said everything was good. I knew that was a lie too, but I wasn\u2019t sure where to go with it from there. Snowflake said that talking to Tavia would be okay now as she wasn\u2019t plotting the death and downfall of all women in New Haven. I found that comforting. I should have known better.<br /> <br /> Tavia was in the TV Room knitting. She was still a little distant, but was willing to hear me out. I apologized for lying to her; let her know how much I hated doing it. She made it clear that it hurt her feelings and told me very assertively not to do it again. I was too wrapped up in trying to earn contrition to realize that was odd. Eventually, she accepted my apology and even let me hug her. I thought we were good and things would actually go back to normal. Then I saw how...no, that isn\u2019t sufficient. As I turned to leave, I saw two things that disturbed me like very few things ever have before. From the corner of my eye, I saw Tavia\u2019s smile spread so wide and sinister, it reminded me of the old Grinch cartoon. But it was not at all silly, much more horrifying. And in that same split second, my sight fell on what she was actually knitting...<i><b>baby clothes!!!</b></i><br /> <br /> I have witnessed war, death, and Underworld demigods. NOTHING has ever seemed that malevolent. Nearly in shock, I went to work then. The day has thankfully been pretty calm in the shop so far. I know Nightshade will be getting things together so I doubt she\u2019ll be by for lunch. Not being able to share this horror makes it seem worse, but I\u2019m not sure I would yet even if I could. I don\u2019t even know what or how to talk to Snowflake about it. Tavia being pregnant and somehow completely, maliciously in control terrifies me like nothing I can describe. I\u2019ve been drawing like usual today, but so far everything keeps turning into some kind of Tavia Beast with that smile and knitting needles for claws.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1915 Hours, Tuesday, August 10, 2010<br /> <br /> I managed to get myself together and calm down a little before coming back to the House. I still didn\u2019t know how I could tell Snowflake, but I knew I had to. Someone\u2019s life depended on it, of that much I was certain. Before I could think about it too much, Nightshade came to me before dinner. She wanted me to know that she was taking Karen to San Francisco for her birthday. This was a major surprise since Karen had never been and really seemed interested in seeing the places Nightshade use to haunt. As this was an intimate getaway, Nightshade was leaving her smart phone, but did have a track phone just in case of emergency. She gave me the number and just talked for a little bit.<br /> <br /> I forgot what it was like to feel so trapped, so helpless...just like I did when I was stuck in the wheelchair. Talking with Nightshade freed me again, just like she did before. I think I might have fallen in love with her all over again in that moment. The weight of Tavia\u2019s horror just fell away and I forgot anything but the moment. Then it was time for dinner. Spaghetti cures all ills. Tavia seemed completely normal...well normal for Tavia. We all just made small talk since Nightshade and Karen were still there. Nightshade was a little worried about us going into the Underworld without her, but I very specifically pointed out that we were just going scouting. I had no interest in trying to deal with something that came from the bowels of the Underworld without everyone present and fully prepared. Now I need to go get my mapping gear just in case.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0230 Hours, Wednesday, August 11, 2010<br /> <br /> We\u2019re getting a lot of dolls lately. I\u2019m going to have Puppet Master nightmares if this keeps up.<br /> <br /> After getting the grave dirt together, I explained to Bright Eyes how the ceremonial travel worked. Since she was new, Bright Eyes opened the Gate and I did my thing. We walked the bone path and all popped out in the crypt at St. Mary\u2019s. The Beckoning Initiate was already there and looked pretty much exactly the way Rose described her before. She gently felt our faces then led us inside. Cupcake was a little skittish when she saw all the skeletal nuns so she stayed back on the stone bridge. Bright Eyes felt bad for Cupcake, so she stayed outside as well. The rest of us entered the chapel hewn from the black stone of the Underworld. The nuns all spoke Latin so Snowflake translated, more directly this time. The nuns found us odd and just stared for a while before Rose introduced us. The Sisters of the Black Water (my name for them) told Snowflake they were no longer able to baptize people because Garlize has tainted their water. I had no idea what kind of taint they meant, so we asked. Apparently instead of bringing a spirit into the order, the person was racked with pain and red scorpions would start fighting their way out of the ghost. It sounded like a very unpleasant and fatal problem. And anything that can kill a ghost is bad news. Since we were last here, the creature has been coming almost into the chapel. It was horned, had skittering claws that clicked on the stone, and always seemed to splash when it moved. Probably not as friendly as Xerxes by the sounds of it.<br /> <br /> After a bit of discussion, Rose got ready for a recon mission. I reminded her that we had no idea what we were dealing with, so not to take any risks. She turned invisible and assured me she would be fine. I hate it when she does that. After way longer than I was comfortable waiting without any news, Rose came back to the chapel. She was carrying a water bottle filled with...well black water. She held it up to one of the torches and it was almost like someone turned on a black light. While she was exploring, Rose found an intersection in the tunnels. She heard a bipedal creature moving to the right. The Sisters said that was the Box Man. He was not dangerous but didn\u2019t like them. They said he found coffins and fixed them for some reason. I am still not entirely sure how that works. Anyway, back to the left, Rose said she heard the monster. It must be able to slip through small spaces and even though she was invisible, it could follow her. Rose wasn\u2019t sure if maybe it could sense life or maybe detected Geists. Either way, it didn\u2019t attack, but she could hear it tracking her from above. With a little chatter, we learned from the nuns that Box Man spoke English. That was at least helpful for most of us, so we decided to meet this Box Man.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes came in with Cupcake, who basically closed her eyes all the way through the chapel, before she used her Pyre-Flame Caul to light the way. As we moved through the tunnel to the right, everyone could hear a banging. It got louder as we continued until we found the ghost of an older black man, roughly 6\u20192\u201d and thin, dressed all in white. I greeted him and he stopped hammering on the coffin in front of him. The Box Man had been around a while, but still seemed pretty with it. He said that he fixed coffins to trade with the Ferrymen. Something about the coffins make them useful in the Dead Dominions. Box Man has a special one he sleeps in that keeps him from being pulled down the river. That was fascinating and I think we\u2019re going to look into what makes those coffins special, but for now, we needed intel on Garlize. Box Man said the beast couldn\u2019t attack anyone that had crossed one of the rivers. He said the nuns had a priest but he got mauled by Garlize. I asked if we could see any of his coffins, mainly because I couldn\u2019t think of anything else to ask. He led us down a narrow side tunnel until he got to a locked side door. He opened the door and showed us the ghost of a little girl. The girl\u2019s eye sockets were empty, her lips were gone, and her skin was blue-green. When she said hello, brackish water poured from her mouth. Even still, she seemed pretty happy all things considered. Then he showed us the coffins in another room off that same locked area. I examined them and they seemed very similar to the items I destroyed with my ceremony to bring into the Underworld. Box Man said they came through the ceiling sometimes, but he didn\u2019t want to show us where. That was his trade after all and I\u2019m pretty sure he didn\u2019t want to lose his only way to make a profit.<br /> <br /> We thanked him and then returned to the little girl. Box Man told me he was keeping her here to be safe from Garlize. Said Garlize couldn\u2019t get into his tunnels. We asked if she, or Box Man, needed anything from the other side? The girl wanted some new clothes and maybe something to play with. She told us her family burned all her toys and then her body when she appeared to them in water\u2019s reflection. That sent her here. Bright Eyes and Cupcake looked like they might cry and I was very glad Nightshade wasn\u2019t with us. We all gave her hugs and she seemed very happy. Rose pulled Lily out of her pack and asked if they\u2019d like play? I couldn\u2019t believe Rose was encouraging Lily to run around like that. Lily surprised the little girl, who told us her name was Naomi. Naomi Williams. But they played together for a few minutes while we \u201cgrown ups\u201d had a talk. Rose wanted to take Naomi back to the surface with us. With us didn\u2019t sound like a terrible idea, but she would need a new anchor and we didn\u2019t know very much about her. Plus I pointed out that we didn\u2019t know if she wanted to go back. It sounded like her family had scared her almost as much as she did them. But I agreed that we should ask.<br /> <br /> Calling Lily and Naomi back to us, we asked if she would be interested in going back to the living world with us. I also asked Box Man if he would be okay with us taking her. When she said yes, he said it was fine by him. Rose asked where she lived before and we got an address on the same street as Trinh. They pointed out that she might be related to Stephen Williams. When I looked confused Snowflake looked at me and explained they meant Pilot Light. Box Man mentioned quietly to me that Naomi died during or near the end of World War II. She described the river she drowned in and I recognized the spot in Sleeping Giant. Then several of us realized where she went to school. Rose asked Cupcake to make a doll in a blue dress when we got back so we could bind her to it. Then she asked if I would help her come back with us. Commanding and controlling ghosts is Nightshade\u2019s thing, but I know how. Thinking about it for a second, I cut my hand and dripped a little of the blood around Naomi. Then I just told her to come with me. I was pretty sure the girl couldn\u2019t have left my side for the rest of the night even if she wanted to. Fortunately, that didn\u2019t come up. We said goodbye to James, the Box Man and headed back through the tunnels to the chapel. Snowflake let the nuns know that we\u2019d have to come back with more people and information, but we would be back. I think they would have had more of a problem with this, except that Rose told them the same thing before and came back with most of the Krewe.<br /> <br /> Since the Beckoning Initiate keeps the Gate open at St. Mary\u2019s, I just had to perform the ceremony to get us back to the Bluffs. Tavia was waiting for us when we got back. I tried not to think about what she was knitting as we walked back upstairs. Cupcake got started on the doll before we headed off to the old school building. It was condemned and had closed before I would have gone, but I realized Cupcake actually went there as a little girl. Somehow that made everything seem better, even as she picked the lock to go in. Snowflake checked out the area with Boneyard and let us know that a few teens were urban exploring. Apparently Bonnie Lynn had a thing for Ben, the guy in the group, while Bright Eyes was newly familiar with Eve. The others were at our party, but I didn\u2019t recognize the names or descriptions. Using his illusions, Snowflake made sure the kids got out before stumbling onto us. By the sounds of it, they will have some stories to tell when school starts again. Rose then got down to business. She pulled together old desks and chairs and made an altar. Then she sacrificed burnt offerings to bind Naomi to the doll. I remember thinking that this would be an interesting scene to stumble on, if those kids did come back. We made sure to write Thanks Ben XOXO on the board where they were before heading out.<br /> <br /> Now I think everyone is ready to crash. I\u2019m hoping I don\u2019t regret bringing Naomi back. I\u2019m not sure which is more wrong though. Letting her stay with us or letting a little girl who died without knowing life fall into the Dead Dominions. I guess I\u2019ll learn the answer soon enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 10, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Alexia and I discussed the krewe\u2019s plans and priorities with the others over breakfast, and we have decided to investigate the Underworld Abbey and help the ghost nuns there against \u201cGarlize.\u201d Natalie did some research on the Twilight Network for us and learned that Garlize was the name of a Kerberoi or a Malfean driven from the Deep Dominions. We are likely dealing with a very powerful entity, and need to learn more if we can before we face it directly.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Natalie, she seems to be dealing with Younger Natalie\u2019s departure relatively well now, and will be taking Karen away for a couple of days to celebrate Karen\u2019s birthday. I hope they have a good time.<br /> <br /> Tavia is also going to be researching the Outsider problem at Glenwood, though we certainly aren\u2019t letting her go to the place on her own to do any sort of ritual investigations. It\u2019s far too dangerous. I\u2019m still very worried about Tavia and Simon. I can\u2019t shake the feeling that Tavia is far more calculating and manipulative than she lets on. I said something to that effect to Alexia, but she brushed it off.<br /> <br /> After training with Jean this morning, I stopped by Lulu\u2019s at the normal time to have a cup of mocha latte and chat a bit with Stanly. We talked about our boyfriends a little. His relationship with Adam seems to be going well, which is good to hear, and I told him a bit about Karl.<br /> <br /> We are going to head to St. Mary\u2019s through the Avernian Gate after dinner. Natalie and Karen have left, so this is going to be a simple reconnaissance trip, but it could still be dangerous, so we are approaching with caution.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 10, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Our trip to the Underworld was very eventful, and it appears the threat posed by Garlize is much more urgent than we thought. Lily tried to stow away again, and this time I decided to let her come with us. Doc seemed shocked by that, but I don\u2019t want to tell Lily \u201cno\u201d all the time, and I didn\u2019t think it would do any harm to let her join us this time. She\u2019s not going to cause as much of a stir in the Underworld as she would if someone noticed her in the living world.<br /> <br /> I opened the gate to the crypt at St. Mary\u2019s and Doc performed the ritual to allow us to travel quickly to it through the Underworld. The Beckoning Initiate was still there, passing in and out of the Underworld to keep the gate open, and I introduced her to my companions. She was gentle as before, and urged us to go to the Abbey inside. Sadly, Alexia\u2019s fear of skeletons forced her to wait on the bridge outside, but Sara stayed with her to keep her company. Sara is such a caring person. I envy her.<br /> <br /> The Abbey was as I left it, a stone church built into the rocky tunnels of the Underworld across a long stone bridge leading from the gate to St. Mary\u2019s. The nuns there grew excited at our approach. Since Simon speaks Latin, he did all the talking and translating.<br /> <br /> The nuns were upset because Garlize was becoming more aggressive and trespassing closer and closer to the Abbey. It even appeared once at the cavern entrance visible from the back of the church, and was lurking in the tunnels just beyond and below. I don\u2019t know exactly what keeps it away at all, but the nuns were convinced that it would not remain at bay for much longer. We probably only have a week or so to face the threat.<br /> <br /> The beast is lairing around the large subterranean pool from which they gather the Black Water, and its presence has tainted the water, and they can no longer baptize people so that they will join the nuns when they die. Since no mortals can really reach the Abbey easily right now, I don\u2019t know that it\u2019s really had much of an impact, but the nuns had assumed we were there to be baptized in the Black Water. We assured them that we would find another way to defeat Garlize.<br /> <br /> I offered to scout the caverns beyond the Abbey to see if I could get a look at Garlize or work out where the beast was. Doc wasn\u2019t eager to let me do it, but he agreed. The nuns told us that Garlize would probably hide from the large group of us instead of attacking, so it was important for me to go alone and unseen.<br /> <br /> I donned my Stillness Shroud and took on the feline aspect of my Primeval Caul to improve my senses, and made my way slowly into the pitch darkness of the caverns. Even though I couldn\u2019t see anything, my sharpened senses allowed me to perceive my surroundings fairly well. When I arrived at a split in the tunnel, I could sense a clawed beast moving in a passage above me. It seemed to follow my movements. One split of the passage led to the lake of Black Water, and I heard a sharp hammering coming from the other. Though curious about the hammering sound, I decided to investigate the pool instead, and made my way carefully down to the lake, following the damp smell of the water and the sound of it lapping against the shore.<br /> <br /> Garlize followed me out into the open cavern that held the lake. The passage it was in must have also opened into the lake cavern. I could hear it crawling across the ceiling, quietly searching for me. It could sense roughly where I was, that much is certain, but it couldn\u2019t actually see me, which is no doubt very fortunate.<br /> <br /> I emptied one of my water bottles and took a sample of the Black Water, then retreated back to the Abbey with Garlize following me as far as the split. I handed the water sample over to Simon and explained to everyone what I had encountered. The nuns told us that the hammering sound was probably made by someone they called the Box Man, a man who roams the caverns digging up empty coffins that seem to sink into the Underworld earth from some unknown place above, possibly even the living world.<br /> <br /> We decided to go talk to the Box Man to see if he knew anything that might help us against Garlize. He turned out to be a rather plainly dressed African-American man named James, and he is a ghost who makes a sort of living in the Underworld by excavating coffins and trading them to others, especially the boatmen who ply the rivers. We might be able to work out a deal with James to acquire a few coffins to pay for our own trip across the river when we decide to visit the Athenaeum, so this seems to have been a serendipitous encounter.<br /> <br /> We followed the Box Man back to a small shed that he was using to store his coffins and he told us a few things about the nuns that we didn\u2019t already know. They were governed by a priest, but he was mauled (and destroyed, I think) by Garlize not too long ago. Also, the Black Water has changed the nuns so that they can remain in the Autochthonous Depths without eventually being pulled into the deeper reaches of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> The Box Man was also protecting a little ghost girl named Naomi Williams. She had apparently drowned, for her eyes and lips had been eaten from her face by fish, and each time she spoke, brackish water spilled from her lungs, making it difficult to understand her at first. She was a bit frightened of us at first, but warmed up to us quickly enough. We asked whether we could bring her or James anything from the living world, and in the process of that discussion discovered that Naomi was going to be drawn across the river soon into the deeper Underworld. She no longer had any anchors, for her family had burned them long ago when she haunted them, mostly by appearing in reflections on water. Poor thing\u2026all she really wanted from them were hugs and affection, but I suppose her fish-eaten appearance frightened them. I can identify\u2026or rather, the Drowned Bride can. There\u2019s a reason her wedding veil always covers her face.<br /> <br /> Naomi was terrified about passing deeper into the depths, and I don\u2019t think any of us wanted her to suffer that sort of long, slow descent. So the krewe decided to adopt Naomi, with the Box Man\u2019s blessing. Doc offered to use a ceremony to make himself into a temporary anchor for Naomi so that she could leave the Underworld with us, if she wanted. Once we arrived in the living world, I could use my own ceremonies to bind her to a new anchor. Naomi\u2019s favorite color was blue, so Alexia offered to stitch her up a nice rag doll in a blue dress to serve as an anchor.<br /> <br /> Naomi accompanied us out of the Underworld, with Sara and Alexia taking care of her. Sara was particularly doting, acting a bit like a big sister as she guided Naomi around and helped make her comfortable as she waited for us to get ready for the anchor binding ritual. It didn\u2019t take Alexia long at all to make the doll.<br /> <br /> In order to perform the ritual, we had to go to Naomi\u2019s old school. She died in the 40\u2019s, and her school was now condemned, but it was still standing. We broke onto the grounds and began searching for her old classroom, but first Simon scanned the area with the Boneyard to search for any hauntings or other activity. There were a few \u201curban explorers\u201d roaming about inside, and we recognized most of them. One was the boy Bonnie-Lynn had a crush on at Albertus Magnus, and another was apparently one of Natalie\u2019s crushes. I wasn\u2019t familiar with the others, though according to Simon, they were at our party, and one of them, a girl named Eva, was apparently Sara\u2019s friend.<br /> <br /> Simon took great pleasure from using his Phantasmal powers to spook the kids, and they lost no time in leaving, though one girl apparently knocked herself out after running into a tree. She wasn\u2019t hurt badly, though, and once they were gone, we were able to go into the school and bind Naomi to her new doll. Now she can remain in the living world as long as she likes. Maybe someday we can find a way to resolve her peacefully without sending along the long and arduous journey through the Underworld.<br /> <br /> We then returned to the mansion to install Naomi into a room there. I hope she\u2019ll be comfortable with us. Perhaps she\u2019ll be a good playmate for Lily and Fu, once Fu gets used to her ghostly presence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Absence Makes the Heart\u2026</u><br /> <br /> I was worried that Karl\u2019s short trip back to Cold Harbor might make me sad, but I\u2019m finding that I don\u2019t mind his brief absence. Perhaps that makes me a terrible person, but with my confused feelings over his family, exacerbated by my fears of Tavia. I think I can use a few days to sort things out in my head. I think Ill make time to go visit Richard\u2019s grave. I don\u2019t know whether being there will help me figure things out or just confuse things more, but it\u2019s something the Bride and I need to do.<br /> <br /> <u>Garlize</u><br /> <br /> According the nuns in the Abbey, Garlize is a huge beast that seems to be made of viscous black oil, yet it maintains a relatively consistent quadrupedal shape, with long, sharp claws horns. Though I was unable to see it, it sounded quite massive, and I think I heard a long tail slithering around behind it.<br /> <br /> According the to Box Man, Garlize was a Kerberoi who was driven out by other Kerberoi, and most importantly, it cannot attack people or ghosts who have been across the river. It seems to me that it might be wise for use to buy passage across the river and back before we go to defeat the beast, but I don\u2019t think it can wait until after our trip to the Athenaeum.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday August 10th<br /> <br /> -I am awake time to see if my girlfriend is talking to me.<br /> <br /> -So this is breakfast. How strange.<br /> <br /> -Hrm. Krewe is being very good about giving me my space, but going on scouting mission without me.<br /> <br /> -Shall I channel Doc and Gwen? Nah.<br /> <br /> -Just want them to be OK.<br /> <br /> -I want Mini Me to be here. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Karen is fine, apparently.<br /> <br /> -Time to talk to Sara about that, actually\u2026<br /> <br /> -Ok turning fun talk into business talk, no fair.<br /> <br /> -Fortunately Sara\u2019s eyes make her very forgivable.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is discussing secret stuff.<br /> <br /> -Sara is simultaneously wise and an ing\u00e9nue. Fascinating.<br /> <br /> -Wow I don\u2019t think Doc\u2019s chat with Tavia went well at all.<br /> <br /> -Er, maybe it did. She is fine.<br /> <br /> -Ah Sara and Karen. I could get used to hanging out with them together, I am just saying.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is scheming.<br /> <br /> -I miss Mini Me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Need to take Sara on a boat ride at some point.<br /> <br /> -I think Sara may be a playa.<br /> <br /> -In a good way.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -I miss Mini Me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Packing packing.<br /> <br /> -Have dinner, try not to be a mama and act all worried about the Krewe going off without me. They are big bois and girls; they can handle it.<br /> <br /> -And they are off!<br /> <br /> -hehe, Karen was not expecting that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Mmmmmmm\u2026now this is what I call an appreciative gi8hb89kin 999999999999999<br /> <br /> -Signing off.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> All\u2019s well that ends well\u2026I guess. And the group adopted another stray. That house will be so haunted.<br /> <br /> Not much to add to the obvious. The haunting of the group of students, with Simon using the Phantasmal Boneyard, was highly amusing.<br /> <br /> Tonight\u2019s session involved some running around between getting home from the school and the next trip out to the graveyard. Gretchen fans will be happy to see her show up, Lily mashes potatoes to cheer up Jasmine, and research is done. Also, the Tavia awkwardness continues. Join us then. In the meantime, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:27:51-08:00","id":16980,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on the Middle Shadows, and see what is going on with the spectral guardians of New Haven. Or something. Apologies for the delay it\u2019s been very busy here<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1115 Hours, Wednesday, August 11, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still not 100% sure bringing Naomi back into the world was the best idea, but I have admit I found myself at peace during meditation this morning without any problem. Interestingly, Rose was still deep in her own meditation when I was leaving. I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s ever happened before. I tried to very carefully leave so I would not disturb her any more than she already was.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was interesting this morning. Naomi and Lily were both there and playing like kids usually do. Otherwise things were pretty normal. Rose had her training to get to, Cupcake was debating if she needed to go to work, and I\u2019m not sure what Bright Eyes had planned for the day. Snowflake mentioned he\u2019d be interested in going to look for cars today. I also told him we should go together and look for ceremonial robes for Karen. He didn\u2019t see that one coming, but immediately agreed that it would be a good idea. I think I\u2019ll just close up a little early this afternoon so we can do that.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, I found a text from Nightshade. She was worried about not hearing from us last night. She asked that I let her know we were all okay when I got up. Given it was around 0900 Hours, I figured she hadn\u2019t gone to bed yet. I sent her a message back letting her know we were all back plus one. I figured she\u2019d understand once she got back. Then I headed off to work.<br /> <br /> Today has been a pretty good day. I drew without surprising myself with more Tavia Beasts and didn\u2019t even get too lonely when I realized Nightshade wasn\u2019t coming for lunch again. Hopefully it will stay this way til Snowflake picks me up.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1830 Hours, Wednesday, August 11, 2010<br /> <br /> Well it wasn\u2019t what I expected but we found a vehicle. Okay, I should clarify, we found the frame of a \u201861 Falcon Econoline. Snowflake picked me up around 1500 Hours and we hit several of the spots I found online. Pretty sure I heard the old guy at the junkyard say something about it being a station bus. I\u2019d never heard of it, but I did notice the engine was in the rear like a hippie bus. Restoring this charm will definitely teach Snowflake and I alot about automotives. I just hope I can not make a fool of myself with this idea.<br /> <br /> We bought the frame and had it hauled back to Dark Haven Bluffs on a flatbed before Snowflake and I pushed it into the old carriage house. We\u2019ll apparently be using that for our workshop. After we finished and caught our breath, we headed back out for Karen\u2019s birthday present. I already knew of a pair of stompy boots with chrome buckles down the side that she\u2019d like. But then I needed Snowflake\u2019s knowledge of ritual items to find the robes. What he showed me was that you don\u2019t actually go out and buy robes, but the cloth and thread so you can make it. Any special embroidery would be different but the original robes is just a hand stitched article. We bought a heavy black tapestry fabric and found some quality silver thread and cording. Now we\u2019re back and I need to get downstairs to dinner.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0025 Hours, Thursday, August 12, 2010<br /> <br /> Rose was very sad at dinner. Even Lily doing her little hand over hand dance couldn\u2019t completely cheer her up. She then let on that she visited her husband\u2019s grave. She may have actually mentioned why she thought this was a good idea, but I was too busy screaming <u><i><b>WHY?!</b></i></u> in my head to notice. Karl\u2019s been gone all of two nights and she\u2019s already lost hope again. I really need to not get involved in this. I also didn\u2019t realize I was quite this much of a romantic, but still. Chandra brought me back to the table when she asked if anyone felt anything different in the House lately? That was kinda weird, but we all tried to think if we\u2019d noticed something off. She said it may be nothing, but she\u2019d just been really hungry lately. Maybe it was because my mind needed to stop thinking of Doom Cloud floating over Rose, or maybe I\u2019m just getting faster on my feet, but I realized what was bothering Chandra. Tavia was pregnant and pregnant women are Chandra\u2019s favored feeding vessels. Oh shit. The conversation continued on with no one really knowing anything, but I was considering if maybe Alchemy could help us.<br /> <br /> After dinner, Snowflake pulled Tavia aside as Rose went to research Garlize in the library. I used the opportunity to grab Chandra before Cupcake attached at her hip. I made the offer to try and enrich blood for her somehow, to try and help with the odd cravings. I mentioned we could maybe get something worked out with a butcher, but she quickly informed me she never had to drink animal blood. The look of pride on her face told me I was probably missing something, so I let that go. Chandra was a little confused as to why I was concerned. I told her I didn\u2019t think it was fair to try and restrict her. I mean I certainly didn\u2019t refrain from eating meat. That got a very wry smile, but she didn\u2019t say anything about it. She did tell me that if I could manage it, she certainly wouldn\u2019t turn it down but she thought she\u2019d be okay. I could tell she was very appreciative of the thought though. I didn\u2019t mention Tavia\u2019s condition at all as no matter what was happening, that was not my place. When we came back into the entry hall, Snowflake and Tavia were walking back from the parlor. Tavia looked resigned and asked Chandra if they could talk. I had a pretty good idea what that was about, so I appropriated Snowflake about putting our skill in Alchemy to work. We discussed the fact that I had learned about Tavia on my own. Also what I saw when I talked to her. He seemed to absorb my story but had little to add. That worried me a little, but it was not the time for that conversation. Then we both headed into the Library.<br /> <br /> When we got there, Rose, Bright Eyes, and Gretchen explained that drowned people were drawn to Garlize in the Underworld, but they hadn\u2019t learned much else. Since Gretchen was in a helpful mood, we helped her research for a way to ritually cleanse the Nun\u2019s Black Water. With the extra assistance, Gretchen was rather quickly able to assemble a solution. The ritual would take about two hours, but required Garlize stay away. Since most of us were already in the Library, we discussed how to deal with our new situation. The plan eventually fell to move straight in. We were then left with the options of negotiate or fight. Not the best Plans A and B, but Kerberoi aren\u2019t known for their patience or kindness. Once the others headed back upstairs, I searched our alchemy tomes for a way to increase the potence or purity of blood. I really doubted I\u2019d find much, but to my surprise (or horror, not sure yet), there was plenty. The problem was, it really didn\u2019t work that way. Increasing the potency of blood was not the same as increasing the value of something. Lead into gold didn\u2019t work in this case. It had something to do with the inherently magical properties in blood. What I could do, with luck and some work, would be to add properties like flavor or drug effects to existing blood. For Chandra, it might then be possible to add estrogen to blood. I just don\u2019t know if that would help or make her want it more. If I was exceptionally lucky though, I might even be able to turn water into blood. But that\u2019s for another time.<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Karen return tomorrow. I\u2019m excited about that, but there\u2019s so much going on that she will need to know about. And I really hope Karen likes our gifts. I think I\u2019m going to try to sleep now. We\u2019ll see how that works.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Thursday, August 12, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation took about an hour like usual this morning, but I think I might have still been distracted from worrying about Chandra. I stayed up after my last entry trying to guess at some alchemical equations in my room. All I think I came up with was how to make blood taste like dirt or water. I\u2019m pretty sure neither one of those will be helpful.<br /> <br /> Chandra was super bouncy at breakfast and Cupcake was pretty beaming too. I\u2019m not really sure all the details but it\u2019s a safe bet they didn\u2019t sleep much. Bright Eyes and Cupcake were telling everyone that the party decorating was happening today so that it was together when Karen got back. I knew that would make Nightshade happy to see us make a big deal over Karen. But honestly, Karen is almost one of us at this point. After breakfast, I took the boots to Nightshade\u2019s room and tied a blood red bow around them before heading to work.<br /> <br /> I hope to have a good day at the shop and come home to find my girlfriend happy and refreshed. Here\u2019s to hoping.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1915 Hours, Thursday, August 12, 2010<br /> <br /> I got a text from Nightshade around 1300 Hours saying they were back. I hadn\u2019t realized how tense I was until I felt myself relax after learning they were home. My shoulders much have unclenched or something because I was alot more loose after that.<br /> <br /> I came home from work as quick as I could (without closing early again) so I could help Snowflake finish the ceremonial robes before the party. The maid of honor had no idea we were planning anything and I think she really had a good time. I think she might have even squeed a little when Cupcake rolled out the Goth cake.<br /> <br /> But now it\u2019s time to go back to work. With Nightshade back, hopefully we can deal with Garlize tonight and remove one more problem from getting worse. It will be interesting for sure.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 11, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve just finished training with Jean this morning. I\u2019m about to head to the cemetery to visit Richard\u2019s grave and work through some of the confusing feelings flooding my heart. I don\u2019t know if being at Richard\u2019s grave will help or hurt, but somehow I can achieve a sort of clarity when I\u2019m mourning.<br /> <br /> Doc seems quite focused today. He centered himself during meditation long before I did. I suppose I let my troubled state of mind interfere with my meditation.<br /> <br /> Lily and Naomi are getting along well. They seem to have found mutual playmates in one another, and are including Fu in some of their games (much to his chagrin, at times). Sara has taken it upon herself to look after Naomi, perhaps as a sort of \u201cbig sister.\u201d I suspect that in Gwen\u2019s absence, Sara might remain with us for some time. She appears to be comfortable among us. I know she has wandered about on her on since she became a sin-eater, but I wonder if she wouldn\u2019t like to join the Middle Shadows? Perhaps I should speak to thenothers about extending an invitation, especially if she performs well against Garlize.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 11, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I spent most of the afternoon at Richard\u2019s grave. I must have seemed a bit mad, the way I was talking to it as though Richard\u2019s ghost might answer, but I know his spirit has moved on; otherwise, I would have found it already.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m very fond of Karl. I think, perhaps, I might be falling in love with him. His presence alleviate\u2019s my loneliness and brightens my perpetual melancholy. And yet, there are things holding me back. I loathe the idea of becoming any more entangled in the fates of the Fishborne family than I already am. There\u2019s simply something\u2026wrong with the family. So I wonder if there is any real future for Karl and me. Certainly I\u2019m thinking too far ahead, but if we did fall in love and marry, what of our children? How could I justify bringing a child into this family, to be tortured by the dysfunctional madness that seems to grip its members? And I suspect that even now Tavia is plotting to have her child marry Karl\u2019s. I can\u2019t bear the thought of my child becoming consumed by a loveless, arranged marriage like Simon, and if Karl were to support such a scheme (and why wouldn\u2019t he? It\u2019s the way of his family, after all), I can only imagine how much it would hurt him for me to refuse.<br /> <br /> I poured all of these burdens onto Richard\u2019s grave, hoping for some sign, anything to help me decide what to do. I have a chance to find real love again, yet when I think about the future of my romance with Karl, I don\u2019t see happily ever after. I don\u2019t even see a normal, contented comfortable marriage. I just see something that frightens me, and I\u2019m not sure if the love I feel for Karl will be enough to make it all right in the end.<br /> <br /> As I sat there, leaning against Richard\u2019s grave and wishing he was there to hold me tight and whisper words of comfort, I broke down into tears. I miss him so much. Things were never this confusing with Richard. Everything made sense with him. And now that I\u2019m one with the Drowned Bride, I don\u2019t know if love will ever be so pure and beautiful again. I began to realize that maybe all of these worries about my potential future with Karl are just excuses, a way for me to justify prolonging my loneliness. The Bride and I are practically of one mind these days. And as much as we are devoted to the search for true love, we also represent the inescapable sorrow that comes with knowing your one true love is lost. It\u2019s hard to overcome that, and I suppose that a part of me\u2026a part of HER, doesn\u2019t want to overcome it.<br /> <br /> In the end, I wasn\u2019t able to resolve any of my feelings regarding Karl. I returned home in a state of abject melancholy. Sara isn\u2019t used my doleful moods since she\u2019s mostly seen me when Karl has been around or when we are on a \u201cmission\u201d (as Doc might put it), so she asked if I was okay. I forced a small smile and told her that I would be fine. I explained that I\u2019m a very melancholy person, and that she shouldn\u2019t worry about me if I seem sad from time to time. As I was trying to explain, Lily came along and, instantly sensing my mood, tried to cheer me up with some of her adorable antics. I almost broke down into tears right then and there, but managed to keep it together as I picked her up and gave her a big, appreciative hug.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 11, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> I was a bit detached during dinner, but when Chandra mentioned that she\u2019d been getting strange feelings of intense hunger lately, I began paying attention. I knew exactly what was causing her hunger: Tavia\u2019s pregnancy. Pennangalan like feeding off pregnant women. I looked rather fiercely at Chandra, but then realized that she meant no harm, and was completely in the dark about what was happening to her. She couldn\u2019t help what she was feeling. But we can\u2019t allow her to indulge her hunger either. I glanced at Simon and realized he understood the situation as well, and the look he gave me convinced me he would handle it. I presume someone will have to inform Chandra of the pregnancy.<br /> <br /> After dinner, I decided to spend my time researching Garlize. Sara accompanied me, which gave her the opportunity to meet Gretchen. The two seemed to get along well enough, and Gretchen behaved herself. Eventually, most of the rest of the krewe joined us, and by the end of the evening, we had managed to confirm much of the information we had learned from the Box Mon. We also learned that before it was driven from it\u2019s Deep Dominion, Garlize was a largely subterranean entity who lived in water. The ghosts of the drowned tended to be drawn to its realm.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, we couldn\u2019t find anything that might help us defeat it. Before it became too late, Sara and I left Doc, Simon and Gretchen to their research and spent the rest of the evening getting Naomi moved into her own room. We decorated a room on the third floor (next to the sarcophagus room) so that a little girl would feel right at home. Naomi seemed to like it.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, August 12, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Natalie and Karen have returned. They seem to have had a wonderful time, and Natalie\u2019s mood is much improved. After welcoming them home, I filled Natalie in on our plans to deal with Garlize, so we will probably deal with that either tonight or tomorrow. Also, Alexia and Chandra were in an extraordinarily good mood this morning. I can only assume they had a passionate night last night.<br /> <br /> Gretchen surprised me by coming to visit me at the pool during my training session. She simply wanted to be friendly, and was very pleased to see her. We chatted for a minute or so before she left. The poor girl was petrified that she would say or do something to embarrass me. I offered her a ride back to Darkhaven Bluffs when I was done training, but she told me that she has her own car! I had no idea, as it isn\u2019t usually parked at the mansion. Apparently Richard bought it for her (though she\u2019s trying to keep that a bit discrete). They must be quite serious. I\u2019m so thrilled that things are working out for those two.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 11th<br /> <br /> -Doc, can you please send me a message when you are up to let me know everyone got back OK? Thanks sweetie. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> August 12th<br /> <br /> -On the plane, headed home.<br /> <br /> -Girlfriend is very happy. This means I am very happy.<br /> <br /> -No sex on plane\u2026this time.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress has returned to you, her dear ones!<br /> <br /> -Looks like most of you got by without me OK. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Ah Connecticut. Not so damn hot here. Despite me liking hot, there is such a thing as too much.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jog.<br /> <br /> -Looks like the gang made a friend.<br /> <br /> -She is cute, for certain definitions of cute.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up<br /> <br /> -Looks like I will be off tonight for more do-gooding. Vacation Over!<br /> <br /> -A witch\u2019s work is never done.<br /> <br /> -Awww\u2026Party for Karen!<br /> <br /> -So Gothy!<br /> <br /> -Hehehe she likes being guest of honor.<br /> <br /> -My goodness this cake!<br /> <br /> -Can this, you know, last forever?<br /> <br /> -Seeing my Krewe being so nice to Karen means a lot.<br /> <br /> -Getting ready for tonight.<br /> <br /> -I miss Mini Me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Not a lot to go over. Heavy role-playing session. Chandra was eventually informed about Tavia\u2019s pregnancy and is trying to work out her hungers\u2026constructively. Like her girlfriend, she has the Gluttony Vice and that does not help.<br /> <br /> I apologize again for the delay. Hopefully next time will be closer to on time. Next session is considerably more eventful, dealing with the Garlize situation and a (formal) new addition to the Krewe. See ya then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:29:38-08:00","id":16981,"title":"","content":"OK, it is time to return to our Krewe, as they enter the Autocthonus Depths to deal with an ancient supernatural horror and prepare for the arrival of a rebellious mystically skilled manipulative teenager. Really, you could damn near summarize the kinds of things that happen in this campaign just with that. Anyway.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXII</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0250 Hours, Friday, August 13, 2010<br /> <br /> Tonight started off a little strangely as Snowflake had to bow out at the last minute. I didn\u2019t doubt he felt bad, but checked him out as I was concerned given our constitution against such things. I\u2019m not sure if the party tired him out enough to finally notice or if it just suddenly hit that hard, but either way, it seemed Snowflake had a 24-hour flu. Tavia was busily chicken souping him when we left.<br /> <br /> Nightshade was not wearing a skirt, which is normal when we travel to the Underworld. But she did put a bag over her hair to keep it from getting cave dank in it. I was forced not to laugh. My ceremony to get us there took 20 minutes and then another 20 for us to walk to the next portal. The Beckoning Initiate was there like normal and we all entered the Underworld after she felt our faces. Cupcake even managed not to scream as we walked back through the chapel filled with skeletal nuns. When this is over, I\u2019ll have to see if I can help her work through these issues. Anyway, once we got to the back of the chapel, we all prepared. Nightshade rather cheerfully asked if anyone would like to strangle her. The others were a little shocked and of course Rose disapproved. I immediately knew why she was asking but given my issues with Nightshade\u2019s asphyxiation fixation, I moved away after carefully declining. Bright Eyes looked a little confused but said she\u2019d help. I did not need to see that. I unlocked my Primeval Shroud, but that was it. I wanted to be protected just in case, but I had other plans than to jump headlong into a fight with a kerberos. After a few minutes, Nightshade came flying up to me as a spirit being to let me know the show was over. It was a little strange seeing her that way, as here she was as solid as we were. Once we were assembled, the Krewe focused on the task at hand. Bright Eyes lit up with her Pyre-Flame Caul and we moved in.<br /> <br /> The creature was on the back wall at a guess, so we (Rose, Bright Eyes, and I) headed that way. We could hear Garlize scuttling along the walls of the dark cavern before us while we carefully sloshed through the black waters. But as we moved closer, Garlize would scuttled back away from the light. Bright Eyes figured out first that it was intimidated by us and might even know what we were. Given that, I asked the ladies to back up so the light and our numbers would fall away. Rose was not thrilled with that idea but they moved back a bit. Then I called out to Garlize and tried to talk to it. That went about as well as talking to a creature from another realm of reality usually does. After that, I unlocked my Primeval Marionette and tried it again. After asking if it could understand me, the response for the others was no different, but I heard it ask why we were there. I explained that we were there to help the nuns in the chapel. Then I asked if it knew it had tainted the waters in this cavern. When it said yes, I asked why. Garlize rumbled that it had spoiled the water to make it a suitable reliquary for the Forgotten Scion of the Old World. There was an uncomfortable moment while I translated to the others. Anything with a name like that is either a self-important poseur or a tremendous bad ass. Given it had a kerberos working for it as a lackey, I knew which to expect. I decided to keep with the direct approach and asked who that was. Garlize stated that It was that which protected the kerberos. Yes you could hear the capital in the description. I translated again, more than a little worried this time. Nightshade thought for a moment before noting that this Forgotten Scion sounded like a Malfean but that they should not be this close to the surface. Also that we probably shouldn\u2019t speak its name out loud until we knew more about it. The possibility exists that it could also be a Neverborn, though that was as much legend as anything. Either way, something that powerful from the Underworld should be sick or weakened this close to Pink Side. Apparently It isn\u2019t, which is disturbing. I asked why it had come to this cavern, thinking maybe we could find something more suitable to help the nuns. Garlize said this place was chosen because it was big enough. I glanced around and noted the wide stretch of water reflecting Bright Eyes\u2019 light. Then, ignoring the sinking feeling in the pit of my stomach, I pressed the issue. Garlize said it could not find a better place and had traveled far already.<br /> <br /> I asked some of the places it had been before to get an idea of acceptable realms or Dominions and maybe places to which it could be sent back. A few moments past before it roared back to me the Forest of Screaming Ashes. Sounded like a cheery place. Trying to relate to it as much as possible, I asked how many Rivers away that was. It again thought for a moment before growling three. Three Rivers of the Underworld away and that was somewhere it had been long enough to remember. Granted that didn\u2019t sound like a very wet place where ghosts of the drowned would be, but I wasn\u2019t about to argue. Rose intervened in my questioning at that point and told me to state what we wanted directly and then ask if Garlize or its master would be willing to cooperate. That seemed like as good a plan as any, so I told the kerberos that we were here to help the nuns cleanse this pool. We needed it and its master to move, though we were willing to try and help find another place. I then asked if that was acceptable. It scuttled off through a hole in the ceiling to get an answer. I was beginning to think it just ran away when we heard a distant clicking of claws. The skittering grew louder before Garlize emerged and announced its master was \u201cwilling to entertain a pact.\u201d I really didn\u2019t like how that sounded. I asked if we were to negotiate through it, but Garlize simply stated for us to come with it. With that the kerberos darted back into the hole. We all looked around at each other before Rose sighed and took the climbing rope, impossibly scaling the side of the cavern. She attached the rope with our gear and we all started the climb, except for Nightshade who very happily flew.<br /> <br /> Even though it felt like Garlize ran off and left us, we could always hear the next tunnel to take. It was very hard to tell how far we moved, given the weaving stone corridors. At length, we came out onto a ledge over a huge, dank cave. Before Bright Eyes cleared the tunnel, the only thing I could really tell was the cave looked to be about \u2154 of a mile long. And at the bottom of that cave was something...something that covered the entire area. Then our current Ghost Lantern emerged and we saw ...It. I have seen a lot in my time and maybe I\u2019ll see more before it\u2019s over. But this was not something you can really get past without being affected. The entire \u2154 mile stretch looked like a partially formed fetus, made of partially formed fetuses. The surface was sheathed in a reflective black covering. Nothing was uniform including the writhing of the shiny black limbs or stumps or heads. I remember the whole scene almost like I was viewing it from outside my body. Bright Eyes stopped short on the ledge, gasped, and almost ran. The look of mind-shredding terror on her normally sweet face put the whole situation into perspective. Nightshade and Cupcake immediately flanked Bright Eyes and tried to comfort her. Cupcake didn\u2019t seem nearly as horrified as I expected, but that may have been because she could focus on Bright Eyes. Rose went rigid and cold. We all have our coping mechanisms, I guess.<br /> <br /> Once we were all assembled and Garlize had mostly moved under the ledge to avoid the light, we all felt an ability granted to us by the behemoth creature before us. If we wished, we could connect to Its mind and communicate. Cupcake and Bright Eyes were definitely not interested. I think Nightshade might have squeed if it would not have been terribly inappropriate. Strangely Rose looked interested, though not with the same intensity as Nightshade. I relaxed as much as I could and allowed the link to be established. It felt strange as if I was moving without any action, though I remained where I stood. An entity spoke into my mind and asked to know my intentions. I answered through thought as well, giving as much detail as possible. I realized very quickly that was unnecessary. The Forgotten Scion sifted through my mind more rapidly than a computer sorts data before continuing. It told me that It and Garlize were being drawn toward the sickness in the New World. I understood this New World to be Pink Side and the sickness was the Outsider blight that we detected growing in Glenwood. It was not at all happy that it was being drawn in such a way, but said it was being pulled like it was caught in the tide. It said it was afraid of becoming altered by the sickness. It told me the cleric was interested in destroying the sickness and purging it from the New World. After a moment, I realized the cleric was Nightshade. I knew that she considered herself a Necromancer, same as Snowflake, but I hadn\u2019t given the situation any thought until then. The Forgotten Scion was very much like an Underworld god and we were communicating with it directly. It told me that the sickness was affecting Garlize more than It, but that this was complicating using Garlize to accomplish anything. I asked if anything could be done other than destroying the sickness to reverse these effects. It responded that if either were to consume enough souls, somewhere in the thousands, that it could help. I realized that was not a great option so we moved to the next useful thought I could come up with. It gave me images of various surroundings from where It had been, though I had very little context for how long or how long ago this might have been. Getting glimpses into Its vast knowledge made me realize how truly insignificant we were to a being such as this. Thus the lack of context for random locations. It was similar to how we don\u2019t notice ants as we move through our daily routine. We couldn\u2019t determine exactly which blades of grass or blocks of concrete we had stepped on more than one or two steps, nor would it be important to us. At that moment, I also realized that I was able to communicate with this being so well because it was using my own memories and understanding of the New World to translate in my mind. The Forgotten Scion had no time for misunderstanding or confusion. I greatly appreciated this knowledge as it was very liberating. I then asked if we could find another place for It to go, would it have any criteria. I felt that helping the Forgotten Scion move away from Pink Side would be good for everyone and It seemed to agree. As a Gatekeeper, even one as bad at it as I am, this was unbelievably encouraging. It told me that it wanted water and it should be very deep, It did not care about how many Rivers away it might be. Though It did mention that if the cleric destroyed the sickness, then it would move away from the surface on Its own. Interestingly, I found that I wanted to help this being and make sure it was in a place that was suitable without endangering the rest of the Underworld. It told me that the cleric believed she could learn an invocation to contact It. That pulled me quickly from my revelry. Invocation was normally not something we dealt with given it involved loss of body control. I was immediately made to understand, probably through interactions with Nightshade and my own mind, that this was not a capital I kind of invocation, but more a connection like we had now. My concerns were greatly soothed with that knowledge and I realized I would also want to know this. I thought of how Snowflake would go crazy to learn such a thing, but It explained to me that only those that had had a connection to It could make such a call. He would be so sad. But with that, we ended our connection.<br /> <br /> The first thing I noticed was that I had not blinked the whole time we were connected. Nightshade was still in talks with the Forgotten Scion as she was still unblinking. Rose was already out and looked...sad? I didn\u2019t quite know how to process that so I just waited for Nightshade. When she finally began blinking again, we headed back through the twisting tunnels. On the way back, I noticed Garlize didn\u2019t follow us. Nightshade began talking once we were far enough away from Garlize to not be concerned. She thinks the Outsider is a Qliphoth. That\u2019s some kind of negative energy-type being. Somehow its drawing the Forgotten Scion Pink Side and she could only guess that it was for a sort of interdimensional possession. I do not want to think of something that powerful being used as a container. I\u2019m sure that ratcheted Glenwood up on Rose\u2019s list of things to do, not that I can blame her. It is our duty to deal with, after all.<br /> <br /> When we got back to the cavern, I was thankful I had learned the cleansing ritual alongside Snowflake. With Bright Eyes lighting the way, I performed the two hour ritual. While I was still chanting, I noticed Nightshade get something from her body then fly back through the tunnels. I kept going, but I did get a little worried. She came back with a bag filled with black fluid before I was finished without any signs of trouble. Finally, I finished and watched as the black water became less viscous and flowed like a normal lake. We got the nuns together and they seemed pleased as Cupcake and Rose tried to explain; neither speaking Latin and Cupcake not wanting to be near the nuns. Once they got the gist of it across, I started working on the ceremony to get us back home. It took half an hour to get access to the bone road, but it finally opened and we got back to the Bluffs almost an hour after I started.<br /> <br /> Tavia was still up waiting for us, knitting. But after what we\u2019d seen, that was nothing. Nightshade pulled Karen and I into her room for a private conversation. I was on the way upstairs for a shower, but it sounded important. Turns out it was, but in a very different way than I thought. After she closed the door, Nightshade looked to both of us and asked that we not get sexually involved with Leslie. I knew Nightshade didn\u2019t trust the incoming DeLaPoer, but I didn\u2019t think she had any reason not to trust us. My frustration must have shown as Nightshade immediately explained that Leslie was very skilled at manipulating people, especially through sex. That was a real concern for her as she did not want us to lose our own agency to someone in that manner. My frustration immediately melted away when I realized Nightshade really did see this as Leslie being manipulative and less us being ruled by our hormones. It probably still sounds bad to anyone that doesn\u2019t understand Nightshade like we do, but that\u2019s okay. When we were all clear, I asked Nightshade if I could talk to her about something. Karen immediately got up and headed out, closing the door behind her. Given that this was her room too, I felt pretty bad. But I got right to business and asked Nightshade how involved she got with the Forgotten Scion. She was connected with It for quite a while longer than I was. She assured me we were good. She was working on something to make Garlize more functional without consuming thousands of souls and destroying the sickness. That was it. That was much better news that I was afraid of, so I kissed her on the head and went upstairs for a shower.<br /> <br /> When I got out, Bright Eyes was waiting around in the hall. She told me she wanted to get everyone together to talk. I guess she was more comfortable with me, or she knew I was alone. Either way, it was cool. We all gathered after a few minutes in the kitchen. Rose poured tea for everyone before Bright Eyes made her presentation. And I don\u2019t mean to belittle her at all, it really was a presentation. She wanted to join the Krewe. She told us that since she\u2019d been with us, she\u2019d seen and done so much that she could have never done on her own. It was comfortable with us and she felt like when she was with her troupe. She just wanted to make sure that no one had any problems with her joining. I briefly thought about trying to call Ronin but I knew she wouldn\u2019t be available quickly enough to explain it. No one had any objections however so we agreed. We usually aren\u2019t very ceremonial with our Ceremonies, but it\u2019s not everyday that we bring another Sin-Eater into the Krewe either.<br /> <br /> Rose led us out to the graveyard where the rest of us stood in place of our Aspects. She sat with Bright Eyes in the center of our strange circle to meditate. Each of the Aspects held a small flame as we stood watch over our own. As the meditation ended, we each placed our flames between Rose and Bright Eyes. Then Bright Eyes drew her blade across her forearm and gave her blood and Plasm to the pyre. Slowly I became aware of The Virgin Sacrifice as a satellite of the Aspect of Mercy. The Sacrifice symbolized Mercy within the Middle Shadows by willingly casting herself into the flames to save those she loves from the Darkness. I witnessed The Angel watching over the process from his winged vantage in silent acknowledgement. A single tear of crimson fell from his dark and hollow eye.<br /> <br /> I realized after a moment that we\u2019d all become enveloped into the power of the moment. The pyre had gutted itself and Bright Eyes asked to keep the ash for scarification. I suggested she might want to keep some of it for use in a later tattoo. I think she planned to do both. She mentioned something about getting the Krewe symbol tattooed by incorporating her initiation scar. It\u2019s not my thing but I\u2019ll make sure it doesn\u2019t get infected and then see about getting her inked.<br /> <br /> But now, it\u2019s late and I\u2019m drained. We have company coming today and I still have to work. Time for sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, August 12, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> The Krewe has returned from the Underworld, and we seem to have resolved the problem with Garlize, for the time being.<br /> <br /> We returned to the Underworld church through the gate at St. Mary\u2019s. Unfortunately, Simon was feeling unwell, and given his frail constitution, we thought it better that he stay behind and get well. Sadly, that meant we had no direct way to communicate with the ghost nuns since no one else speaks Latin.<br /> <br /> We did our best to convey that we were going to drive off Garlize and then delved down into the tunnels behind the abbey, heading toward the subterranean lake of Black Water. I was a bit worried about Alexia making it through the church, given her phobia of skeletons, but she proved her mettle and hurried through without giving in to the terror she must have felt.<br /> <br /> As we descended toward the lake, we all unlocked our manifestations. Doc cloaked himself in the Dog of War and Alexia grew her extra arms. Natalie left her body comatose in the church, watched over by the nuns while she projected her spirit with the Cold-Wind Oracle. Sara ignited her pyre-flame to give us light. I donned my Primeval Caul and Shroud, and felt myself become one with my primal nature in a deeper way that I ever have before. It was magnificent! It is fortunate that I ultimately had no need of the speed and power I felt, but if it had come to a fight with Garlize, I would have been more ready that I\u2019ve ever been before.<br /> <br /> Garlize was in the lake cavern, but he kept his distance from us. Doc drew upon his own primeval insights and spoke to the creature in the beastly language it understood. And that\u2019s how we negotiated with it.<br /> <br /> Doc learned that Garlize serves a thing (probably a Malfean) known as The Forgotten Scion of the Old World. It protect\u2019s Garlize, and in return, Garlize is searching for a place where the Forgotten Scion can rest, which much be somewhere quiet and with a great deal of water. That is why Garlize was tainting the Black Water; it was trying to prepare it to hold the Forgotten Scion.<br /> <br /> The discussion hit a snag when Doc\u2019s roundabout way of questioning Garlize was met with the creature\u2019s reluctance to meet us halfway in the negotiation, so Sara suggested that Doc simply ask it directly if we couldn\u2019t meet with its master. Doc was able to convince Garlize to take us to meet the Forgotten Scion so that we could negotiate with it. I was quite anxious about meeting the thing in person. It seems that it has strayed far from the deeper depths of the Underworld where it belongs, and according to Natalie, communing with Malfeans risks madness. Nevertheless, we had a chance to gain the good will of a powerful Underworld being and to save the nuns without a fight, so we had to take it.<br /> <br /> We followed Garlize until the tunnels opened onto a ledge looking into a vast cavern. The Forgotten Scion rested there, and though we could only see part of it in the darkness (which was illuminated only by Sara\u2019s brilliant pyre-flame), it gave the impression of an immense fetus made of countless smaller fetuses. It was one of the most disturbing sights I\u2019ve ever seen, and it was too much for Sara, who gasped and almost fled. She did withdraw slightly from the ledge so that she wouldn\u2019t have to see it, though the dank, fleshy smell of the thing was still overwhelming for all of us.<br /> <br /> Natalie and Doc communed with the Forgotten Scion, entering a trance-like state in which they interacted with it psychically. Doc negotiated a way to help the Malfean while keeping him away from the Black Water lake. Natalie, on the other hand, must have been discussing a great many other things with it, for she communed with it long after Doc was finished. I\u2019m worried about her. Her manic interest in communing with the thing was unsettling and a bit psychotic. Natalie\u2019s frequent obsessive mood swings are difficult for me to understand and always set me on edge, though I know she means no harm.<br /> <br /> I also communed briefly with the Forgotten Scion, though. It only took a few moments for it to answer my question, and I wouldn\u2019t have dared commune with it had I not been compelled by the weight of emotions that have flooding my heart lately.<br /> <br /> In the end, Doc was able to arrange for the Forgotten Scion to withdraw from the Black Water lake so that we can purify it and return it to the nuns. In return, we must try and help the Forgotten Scion find a safe, comfortable place to rest. We hope to do so while we are in the Athenaeum; perhaps while there we can learn something to help the Malfean, and if we can, then we will have secured a potent ally.<br /> <br /> Doc also learned that the Forgotten Scion is drawn to this area because of the tainted aura infusing Glenwood. Natalie thinks the aura is created by an Outsider known as a qliphoth, a Hebrew term referring to a dark and entropic entity. So, before we can move the Forgotten Scion elsewhere, it must be freed from the taint that\u2019s drawing it toward the area of the Underworld church. We will have to cleanse the taint in Glenwood, which means we will need to find its source soon.<br /> <br /> With the deal struck, we returned to the lake. Doc performed a long and intensive ritual to purify the water. Then we made our way back to the church. Natalie reunited with her body and Alexia and I tried as well as we could to explain to the nuns that we had freed them from Garlize. Then we headed home, no worse for the wear, but with a greater challenge ahead of us. All in all, it was exhausting.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that exhaustion was why, after we returned home and got cleaned up, I found Alexia working in the kitchen and poured out my soul to her. I told her all my worries about Karl and the mixture of sadness and relief I felt when the Forgotten Scion confirmed that Richard\u2019s ghost was not in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Talking to Alexia was the best thing I could have done. Somehow, just talking about everything made it all fall into place, and Alexia made my worries about Karl\u2019s family seemed trivial. I wish I could explain what it was she said or how she swept aside my worries and made me see that all that matters now is how Karl and I feel about each other. Everything else will fall into place from there. And if we do continue to grow closer and, eventually, children become an issue\u2026then I\u2019ll have to deal with that when it comes up. But I have to believe in love and its ability to give me the strength to face these things. Even the Bride was encouraged, though I still sense a touch of reservation from her, and fear that she might not know how to overcome the melancholy of separation and death that she embodies. It\u2019s ironic that it is so hard for us to embrace happiness because of the lingering sorrow that defines us.<br /> <br /> As we were finishing our conversation, the whole household gathered in the kitchen, and Sara asked if she could join the krewe. She\u2019s been looking for a home, and she thinks she\u2019s found it. Of course I was happy to hear her request, and the krewe agreed immediately. Sara seems to fit in well, and she\u2019s certainly proved herself.<br /> <br /> I spent the next hour preparing the ritual, and when all was ready, we met in the graveyard. Sara and I sat with the rest of the krewe (even a rather ill Simon) surrounding us, and I ritually inducted her into the krewe. During the ritual, Sara\u2019s geist, the Virgin Sacrifice, presented herself to the rest of our geists, and she quietly settled into the krewe mythos as the Sacrifice, a compassionate extension of the Angel\u2019s Mercy.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Dangerous Liaisons</u><br /> <br /> Natalie was far too excited about the opportunity to interact with the Forgotten Scion. Despite its apparent willingness to work with us, it\u2019s dangerous, and I worry that Natalie\u2019s lust for occult power and knowledge is overriding her sense of caution.<br /> <br /> She is not the only one who communed with the Malfean (I did as well, despite myself), and the Forgotten Scion did not seem willfully malevolent, but Malfeans are beyond our understanding, so who can say what it\u2019s thinking? I agree that it\u2019s good to encourage a good relationship with the Forgotten Scion, but Natalie seems to think of the Malfean as one of the gods she worships, and I confess that makes me uncomfortable. I wonder if she isn\u2019t putting too much faith in its so-called divinity. Of course, I\u2019m Buddhist, so in my opinion Natalie is calling something a god when it is really just a very powerful Underworld entity. She is knowledgeable about these things, so perhaps I am worrying for nothing. It\u2019s just that her obsessive attitude toward the opportunity of communing with the entity was a bit unnerving.<br /> <br /> I suppose I\u2019m worrying for nothing. Surely Doc will keep an eye on her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Ship</u><br /> <br /> I communed with the Forgotten Scion for one reason only. Natalie said he was a font of Underworld, so I decided to ask about the ship on the Underworld coast beneath the mansion, the one that bears Richard\u2019s name in an implied promise to take me to him. My concerns about my relationship with Karl have tempted me to board that ship and find out whether Richard really is there or not.<br /> <br /> So I communed with the Malfean only long enough to ask it if the ship really could take me to Richard. It\u2019s answer was what I suspected. The ship could take me to an illusion of Richard, but it wouldn\u2019t really be Richard, and by the time I realized that, it would be too late.<br /> <br /> I must abandon any thoughts of boarding the ship in the faint hope of finding my lost love again. In a way, it\u2019s heart-breaking to have that hope stolen from me. But I find that I\u2019m comforted more than depressed. It means that Richard isn\u2019t really in the Underworld. He didn\u2019t have to suffer through this dark and somber place. He returned to the karmic cycle, like it should be. And even though it means he really, truly is gone, it makes me happy to know that his soul is where it should be, not lost and alone without me.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> The Virgin Sacrifice</u><br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s geist, the Virgin Sacrifice, has settled into our krewe mythos quite comfortably. The binding ritual placed them within the Freedom axis of the krewe wheel, and her geist represents the selfless and compassionate qualities of Sacrifice. She has become an extension of the Mercy represented by Gwen\u2019s Angel. And, in Gwen\u2019s absence, she has become a fitting replacement for Gwen. I can only assume that some greater fate is at work here.<br /> <br /> As part of the krewe binding ritual, I performed an I Ching divination, as I did for all of us when we formed the Middle Shadows, and from that original divination, I found a hexagram to represent each of us. The hexagrams are closely tied to the krewe fates and roles of our geists, and Sara is no different. She is represented by Hexagram 15, Humbling, which implies not only humility, but also the idea of success and growth through sacrifice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 12, 2010<br /> <br /> -OK Radio Silence<br /> <br /> -Home again, home again jiggity-jog.<br /> <br /> -I miss Mini Me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Tasty as Karen\u2019s smooches are, I need to talk to her and Doc.<br /> <br /> -I feel like a total ass.<br /> <br /> -Doc is so sweet when not chewing foot.<br /> <br /> -I am so not good at this.<br /> <br /> -Looks like there is noting wrong, and I am not being a bitch. Yay!<br /> <br /> -Oh oh Karen\u2019s been sent out am I in trouble?<br /> <br /> -No naked power grab goes unpunished it seems.<br /> <br /> -Where\u2019s the fairness?<br /> <br /> -Eh, Doc is not too sore.<br /> <br /> -All back together.<br /> <br /> -Could have gone so much worse.<br /> <br /> -OK just have to talk to Sara.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is dispensing advice.<br /> <br /> -Always a source of wisdom, me.<br /> <br /> -Hehehe. Hehehehehehehe. Hehe.<br /> <br /> -Up to no good, me.<br /> <br /> -All Karen\u2019s fault.<br /> <br /> -Right, back to smooches.<br /> <br /> -Or not.<br /> <br /> -Yay!<br /> <br /> -We accept her! One of us! Gooble-Gobble!<br /> <br /> -OK damnit. Now the smooches!<br /> <br /> -Mmmmm\u2026smooches\u2026.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> First off, I will note that Simon\u2019s player had to miss\u2026hence no Simon. We all missed Simon, and more then that his player.<br /> <br /> I also wanted to mention the word Qlippoth is being thrown around in a Kabbalistic sense, not as specific game term, though it is being applied to the Abyss.<br /> <br /> Natalie was attempting to bargain for the Stygian Key. However, she has considerably more work ahead of her to get it, based on the information in the Book of the Dead. Speaking of Natalie, to clarify (since Doc kinda implied otherwise at first) Natalie stressed she did not want to limit Doc or Karen as far as partners normally (so long as they were tested before having sex with her if they slept with a stranger) she was making an exception in terms of Leslie. So it wasn't &quot;you guys are gonna cheat on me&quot; so much as &quot;I don't normally want to tell you who you can't sleep with, but this is an exception.&quot;<br /> <br /> And Sara is in the Krewe now, so yay for that\u2026they did Krewe Binding at the end of the session. Now Natalie can give her dice, and she gets other general Krewe benefits.<br /> <br /> Whelp, game tonight as the Krewe deals with it\u2019s new houseguest and considers how to deal with the Abyssal Intrusion. Or maybe they will do something totally else, I try not to assume anymore. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> See you next time, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:33:31-08:00","id":16983,"title":"","content":"Time to get back with the Krewe. The last session was\u2026eventful, and so we have a lot to cover. Doc\u2019s player was absent, so his journal will have little connection to the other two\u2026if you normally read just his you may wanna check Jasmine\u2019s. Oh yes, in addition to the usual suspects, we get something from Sara. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0730 Hours, Saturday, August 14, 2010<br /> <br /> The day had been so nice. Yesterday that is. Nightshade came over for lunch like usual and it was great. Then about 20 minutes after she left, a cabbie ran into the shop looking a little scared. He had a crumpled note in one hand and kept calling out for Doc. When I came around the counter and asked if I could help him, his English wouldn\u2019t come. But I caught a word of Arabic slip and asked him what I could do for him that way. His eyes went wide and then he nearly broke down. He said a woman was wounded on the street before dawn. He was scared but he stopped anyway and tried to take her to the hospital. She refused so he took her to a cheap motel that didn\u2019t ask questions. There she scrawled out the note he carried and sent him with money for help. Then he handed me the note.<br /> <br /> My shop\u2019s address was scribbled in what looked like Ronin\u2019s handwriting. It was fairly short and to the point, but what else would I expect from Ronin.<br /> <br /> Was tailing something. Found it. Wish I hadn\u2019t. Need you.<br /> <br /> Her writing was never neat to start with, but this looked like she wrote it while her fingers were broken. That\u2019s when I noticed the browning smears of old blood. She never did clean blood off her hands well. I grabbed my medic bag and put up the emergency closed sign, remembering ironically that Leslie was arriving today. Then I locked up and jumped in the cab with Shabazz. I called the Bluffs to let them know as much as I knew and then got off the phone. This was not how I planned today to go.<br /> <br /> We drove north for about a half hour before we took the exit for Durham. 10 minutes later, I gave another $60 for the trip and told Shabazz he saved a life today. I didn\u2019t bother to explain it might have been his. The motel was pretty sleazy but it would do. No one notices a brown man walking into a questionable motel anyway. The cabbie told me she was in room 23 so I went and knocked on the door. I heard a stumble and the familiar click of Ronin cocking the hammer of her pistol. Yes she did it alot. I stepped back from the door and let her know it was me. There was a pause before some shuffling and fumbling with the locks. The door opened a crack and then the shuffling moved away. What I saw next simultaneously terrified me and boiled my blood.<br /> <br /> I walked in and found a woman with blood matted in her hair. Black and purple ringed her eyes, though one was swollen completely shut. At a guess, the same impact had broken her nose. The bruising around her throat suggested something huge had held her off her feet. Her face was dirty from whatever she\u2019d landed on or in. One cheek was either burned or ground raw and there seemed to be a cigarette burn just under her clavicle. The pistol was still pointed at me when Ronin croaked to shut the door. Pushing the door closed and locking everything available before wedging a chair under the knob, I turned back and opened my mouth. But nothing came out...the rage was closing off my windpipe.<br /> Before I could regain my voice, Ronin finally released the hammer and set the pistol next to her on the floor. She tried to smile before cringing in pain. That snapped me back into medic mode. I tried to help her onto the cot in the corner. I thought she was going to pistol whip me before she finally allowed me to help her over to the wobbly bed. At least I knew this was definitely a memeber of my Krewe...what was left of her anyway. I helped her clean up a little before I actually checked her out. Major bruising both internal and external. A broken nose, cracked ribs, twisted ankle, crushed fingers. I couldn\u2019t be sure without an MRI, but I suspected she\u2019s ruptured something based on the pain in her abdomen. Of course, she refused to go to the hospital and reminded me that was what I was there for. I told her that that meant we\u2019d have to do this the hard way. I helped her undress, which led to more jokes about me getting an eyeful than I ever got in the service, before properly cleaning her up. She had more lacerations and contusions present and she was understandably very tender.<br /> <br /> I got out the whiskey, told her that she needed to drink heavily, and if she knew what was good for her not to argue. After she was starting to get a little tipsy, I got the leather strap out and told her she needed to trust me...also not to shoot me. I hated how bad this would hurt, but I knew she would get pneumonia if I didn\u2019t get her ribs set. Taking care of ribs would be so much easier if moving them around didn\u2019t cause intense pain. I gave her the strap and told her to bite down; we didn\u2019t need her to start screaming. Even if it was a cheap motel, those kind of screams would eventually get noticed. She only punched me once before I got her ribs wrapped, though I thought she might bite through the strap for a while there. And that\u2019s about the time she started coughing up blood from the punctured lung. Without a hospital and a lot of time, this was not going to work. I knew I\u2019d have to use my ceremony.<br /> <br /> The problem was that she was so injured that it wasn\u2019t so straightforward this time. Her wounds did not want to heal, either because they were as stubborn as Ronin or from some other influence. I had to alternate between my normal holistic approach and healing with the ceremony as I could. It was not a fast process and it really took it out of both of us. During all this, we talked about the new events since she left and also talked about Bright Eyes. Ronin make some stupid joke about replacing her already and I nearly lost it. Maybe it was because Bright Eyes came at just the right time or maybe the others didn\u2019t see it as that big of a deal, but I\u2019d thought about it a few times. It seemed strange that losing Ronin hadn\u2019t affected anyone, other than me that is. I missed Ronin but I knew that we couldn\u2019t keep her around if she had a lead. I just really snapped when she suggested we had moved on. I shouldn\u2019t have taken it out on Ronin...and she basically told me to chill the fuck out. I apologized and told her I missed her. Things aren\u2019t the same without her there. We both just let that trail off. No point in starting that one. Instead we talked about whatever it was that did all this to her. It was as big as some of the werewolves we\u2019ve met, but either she didn\u2019t get a great look at it (given the shape of her face when I found her, that was possible) or it was something else. It apparently had claws but it also had cigarettes and a lighter. It was fast enough that even though Ronin knew something was nearby, she couldn\u2019t get a shot off before all hell broke loose. We laughed as she described how surprised it was when she rolled over and stabbed it with thousands of invisible shards of hate. If I had to guess, I\u2019d say that was probably why it finally left her be.<br /> <br /> Around 0300 Hours, I finally managed to get Ronin mostly back together. She had long since gone to sleep so I sat with her until about 0400 Hours. I must have dozed off after that. I woke up a little bit ago and found Ronin up and around. She\u2019s still limping, but she doesn\u2019t look like a domestic violence victim after a car wreck. We\u2019re going to make sure she has a proper emergency kit and get some food. Three hours sleep is more than enough, right?<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1245 Hours, Saturday, August 14, 2010<br /> <br /> DAMN IT! If I hadn\u2019t just spent the last 23 hours putting her back together, I could kill Ronin right now!<br /> <br /> After we went to doughnut shop down the street for food, Ronin and I stocked up on supplies she\u2019d need to keep herself healing from this time and a proper medkit for whenever the next time is. It was slow going as I was tired and she wasn\u2019t really running any marathons yet either. I really expected the limp to go away by tomorrow. But that\u2019s beside the point now. We got back here about 1200 Hours and she laid down for a while. I watched her sleep for about 20 minutes and finally felt like she was going to be okay. Since I was still wearing the same clothes from yesterday (which I learned still had Ronin\u2019s blood when we went to breakfast) and felt kinda gross, I decided to take a shower. When I came out, Ronin was gone. She took the whiskey I keep for my medical bag and left me another note.<br /> <br /> Doc,<br /> <br /> Thanks for the assist and the whiskey. Best of luck to &lt;Bright Eyes&gt; and give my love to the Krewe. Miss you guys.<br /> <br /> &lt;Ronin&gt;<br /> <br /> Now I need to get another cab back to the Bluffs and figure out how I\u2019m going to explain all this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, August 13, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> Meditation was very good this morning. I think my talk with Alexia and the harmonious induction of Sara into our krewe helped me feel more centered. I know I shouldn\u2019t be so dependent upon external influences when achieving a proper meditational state, but it seems that lately I cannot help it.<br /> <br /> Training went well. Jean is nearly ready to compete. I\u2019ve already entered him into a few collegiate competitions during the upcoming semester, so he will get a chance to prove himself soon.<br /> <br /> Leslie should be arriving any time now, so I should head home. Doc will not be there, unfortunately. He got an emergency call from Gwen and sped off to find her without giving us much more information than that. I do hope that Gwen is all right.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 13, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> It has been an interesting afternoon. Leslie arrived safe and sound, and seems willing enough to behave herself. Gretchen made sure that she wouldn\u2019t get any ideas, though. As soon as Leslie walked in the door with Natalie, Sara, and Alexia, Gretchen stormed up to her and threatened her with her boyfriend, Mongler, if she tries anything nefarious. She made it very clear that she believes Leslie is working for Tzipporah. I have no doubt that Mongler will deal with Leslie in short order if she tries to do anything to Gretchen, but Leslie seemed as surprised as the rest of us by Gretchen\u2019s threats, all the more so because she didn\u2019t even know that Gretchen was still alive.<br /> <br /> In the aftermath of that rather shocking confrontation, I drew Sara aside and we had a bit of a chat about all the things the krewe has been dealing with. I told her about the Fishborne family and werewolves, and explained what Gretchen was going on about. I told her to talk to Doc about the vampires, and I tried to catch her up with all the problems we\u2019ve dealt with and informed her of the problems we have yet to resolve. I didn\u2019t realize just how much there was to tell until I started, and as the afternoon wore on and we moved on to other things, I kept remembering things Sara needed to know. Still, I think she\u2019s mostly informed on krewe business now. She\u2019ll be going to meet Malard tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Everyone decided we should go down to the yacht to celebrate Leslie\u2019s arrival, so that\u2019s where we spent the afternoon. While we were enjoying ourselves, however, Chandra proposed to Alexia! I think Alexia and I may have been the only ones who were shocked by it. It was quite sweet, really, though I\u2019m not sure how it\u2019s all going to work out, a sin-eater and vampire. Still, if it is true love, it will find a way. I am happy for them. I do regret that Chandra and I don\u2019t get on well anymore. I tried to show her my support for her romance by complimenting her on the proposal, since I know she likes being a \u201ctake charge\u201d kind of woman, but I\u2019m not convinced she really understood my intentions.<br /> <br /> With Simon and Tavia, Alexia and Chandra, and Natalie and Karen all enjoying the company of their paramours, I began feeling a bit lonely and wished that Karl were there. Tavia tells me that he called the house and is planning to return Saturday evening. I\u2019m looking forward to welcoming him home\u2026though I suppose the mansion probably doesn\u2019t feel exactly like home to him. Instead of letting my melancholy turn disrupt the festive atmosphere, I decided to go swimming, and disappeared into the depths for about an hour to meditate and commune with the sea. I felt better afterward.<br /> <br /> I should also mention that Sara can\u2019t swim! I was quite shocked to learn that, so I insisted she allow me to give her swimming lessons.<br /> <br /> After our time on the yacht, but before dinner, Simon and Alexia took Leslie to Malard\u2019s house to introduce her to him. After all, she might be trouble, so it\u2019s best to let him know she\u2019ll be here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 13, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> The night has seen its share of excitement. Over dinner, we decided that as a member of the krewe, Sara needed to see the Fish God that protects the mansion, so we took her down into the caves below to see it with her own eyes. Simon and Tavia showed us an easier way to enter the cave (so we didn\u2019t have to take Sara through the treacherous, half-submerged tunnels leading in from the sea). Needless to say, Sara was as awestruck as the rest of us were when we first saw the thing. I hope she isn\u2019t overwhelmed by all that we\u2019ve revealed to her in just one day. I don\u2019t think she regrets her decision to join us\u2026she seems too strong to shy away now.<br /> <br /> When we went back up, we found that Leslie was anxious and shaken. Moments before we emerged from below, she had seen a burnt, skeletal face peering in at her through the second-story window of her room. We immediately recognized the description as Pup Pid, the mysterious pirate ghost or spirit that haunts the nearby beaches. As he had only just fled, I decided to try and find him before he got too far away, so after telling the others I was going to track him down, I hurried to another room, opened the window, and flew out as a flock of crows. I flew over the grounds as far as the beaches below the cliffs, but saw no sign of him, so I landed and, since I was still enjoying the heightened senses of my Primeval Caul, I tracked him from the mansion down to the cliffs, where I could see that he had jumped to the beach below and then fled into the ocean. He was long gone.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Alexia communed with the window through which Pup Pid had been peering when Leslie saw him. Apparently this is the first time he\u2019s approached the mansion like this, and he seems to have simply walked up the wall to reach the window. Simon and Natalie believe that something about Leslie, or something she did, must have drawn Pup Pid here. Perhaps she tried to summon local spirits?<br /> <br /> While I was out looking for Pup Pid, I caught sight of Marjorie\u2019s ghost wandering the road by the mansion, trying to hitchhike home as usual. Since my search for Pup Pid was a dead end, I decided to go talk to Marjorie. She still doesn\u2019t realize she\u2019s dead, and that doesn\u2019t seem like it\u2019s going to change any time soon without some help.<br /> <br /> So I shed my Caul and approached Marjorie to see if she needed help. I normally get along well with ghosts, but she seemed nervous around me, and I quickly realized that the T-shirt and shorts I was wearing must have seemed a bit scandalous to her. Still, I decided to just be blunt and explained to her that she had been shot and killed, and was now a ghost. The reason she could never find her way home was because she was bound to her blue dress, and she could not move very far from it.<br /> <br /> Of course she didn\u2019t believe me at first, so I cut my hand a bit with my keys and flicked some of my blood onto her to make her more lucid. Once I did that, she seemed to realize what she was. She calmed down a bit, and allowed me to lead her back to the mansion, where I promised that my friends and I could help her come to terms with being a ghost.<br /> <br /> The rest of the krewe was surprised when I walked in with Marjorie in tow, but I quickly explained that I felt bad for her wandering the road each night, and had decided to take steps to help her out. We sat her down to talk in the TV room, away from anywhere Leslie might see (I believe Karen kept her occupied), and Alexia went to fetch Marjorie\u2019s dress anchor.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, once Marjorie came to terms with being dead, she asked what had happened to her killer. The woman who murdered her is my friend Stanly\u2019s great aunt, and Stanly is very fond of her. But she got away with the murder, and I suspect that for Marjorie to pass on, we are going to have to resolve the lingering crime somehow. I fear what that might mean, but I\u2019m willing to do what we must.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t tell Marjorie the her killer was still alive and free, as we weren\u2019t sure how she would react. She isn\u2019t a vengeful spirit, and we hope that she won\u2019t become one. While Sara looked after her, the rest of us discussed what to do, and on Natalie\u2019s suggestion, we simply told Marjorie that we would look into what happened to her killer. That seemed to satisfy her for now. She became very tired after that, and faded away to sleep in her anchor.<br /> <br /> Then we all retired for the night. I spent some time before going to sleep working on my Keats\u2019 translation while Naomi and Lily played in my room and Fu dozed contentedly on my lap. It was quite precious.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, August 14, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> Meditation this morning was good but empty. I\u2019m looking forward to Karl\u2019s return this evening. Over breakfast the krewe decided to go to Glenwood tomorrow to investigate the outsider presence there. I hope we can end the taint quickly, though I suspect it will be rather more involved than that.<br /> <br /> We invited Mr. Malard and his pack-mate, Angelique (who appears to be living with him much of the time now) over for lunch while Karen and Chandra took Leslie out shopping. We introduced Sara to him. He was pleasant as always, and I think we had a very nice meal together. We also informed him of the problems in Glenwood. At first, I think he thought we were asking for his help, and he was quite willing to give it, but Simon quickly assured him that we could handle it. We simply wanted him to be aware of the trouble since it was taking place in territory belonging to the Pure (werewolves who disagree with Malard\u2019s philosophy toward spirits, as I understand it). We suspect that the taint might be caused by something leaking from the Abyss or by something that went to the Abyss and returned, changed and corrupted.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve been relaxing a bit after lunch. In a few minutes, Sara and I are going to the Albertus Magnus pool to practice to swimming. I think she will be a fast learner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Another Fish Born<br /> </u><br /> As I was meditating in the depths far beneath the yacht, I briefly thought I caught sight of Karl swimming about down there with me. Then I realized that the fish-person I glimpsed was much smaller and more slender than Karl, and it dawned on me that it must be Tavia. She\u2019s finally managed to transform into her fish form. I can only assume her pregnancy has something to do with it. I\u2019m happy for her, though I do hope this means she\u2019ll become a bit more stable.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>American Culture and Idioms</u><br /> <br /> <u>\u201cBugbear\u201d</u><br /> <br /> Simon used the term \u201cbugbear\u201d to refer to the issue of Marjorie\u2019s murder and my worries over exactly what me might have to do to help Marjorie pass on. I had no idea what he meant, as it sounded like some for of bizarre creature to me, and I seemed to recall hearing the term in reference to European fairy tales. But Simon explained that saying something is the \u201cbugbear\u201d means that it is the central or troubling issue of a situation, something not easily dealt with or resolved.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Comfort of Ghosts</u><br /> <br /> I must confess that dealing with Marjorie\u2019s ghost was like a breath of fresh air for me. Perhaps that\u2019s why I decided to force the issue. We\u2019ve been dealing with Malfeans and outsiders, vampires and werewolves, and stranger, undefinable things like the Puppeteer for so long that it seems like ages since we\u2019ve just helped a ghost pass on comfortably into the karmic cycle. But helping ghosts like that is appealing and comforting for me. Yes, we adopted Naomi, and we did help the nuns, but that\u2019s not the same as peacefully resolving a ghost. I think I needed to deal with Marjorie to remind myself why I\u2019m really doing all of this. I\u2019m a Mourner, after all. It\u2019s what I should be doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 13, 2010<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s a day in da-dake. The water is blue and the Natalies are awake.<br /> <br /> -Friday the 13th!<br /> <br /> -Friday the 13th is lucky for Scorpios.<br /> <br /> -Fortunately Your Mistress is a Scorpio.<br /> <br /> -Guest coming! Alexia and Simon has gone to get her, along with Owlish housemate.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Sara still has some eyes. <br /> <br /> -Better than the alternative!<br /> <br /> -Looking out over fourth floor the balcony at the ocean getting a foot massage from my Goth slavegirl, I realize my life could really be worse.<br /> <br /> -I still see myself as a sort of modern Mercedes de Acosta, and I now know who is my Garbo. I just hope it ends better.<br /> <br /> -Mischief girl, take two<br /> <br /> -Well, that was unexpected!<br /> <br /> -Librarian girl has some \u2018tude!<br /> <br /> -Boat time!<br /> <br /> -@NAREK is all about a boat ride.<br /> <br /> -Ah my lovely parasol to preserve my lovely pallor. And strawberry scented sunblock!<br /> <br /> -Strawberry Deathcake lives!<br /> <br /> -Hmmm\u2026it seems @NAREK is also Strawberry Deathcake.<br /> <br /> -I suppose there are worse things than being asked \u201cWhen can WE get a yacht.\u201d<br /> <br /> -Oh the excitement of one woman proposing to another. I am glad to live in a civilized state.<br /> <br /> -I just wish I lived in a civilized nation\u2026<br /> <br /> -They will stop kissing, eventually.<br /> <br /> -Some people are swimming, your mistress is enjoying the romantic ambiance with her favorite Gloom Cookie.<br /> <br /> -Was not expecting Owlish Housemate to swim.<br /> <br /> -That was fun!<br /> <br /> -Sending Leslie to meet crazy neighbor, then have to show Sara what\u2019s in the basement.<br /> <br /> -Radio Silence<br /> <br /> -Undead Pirate Peepers? What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Oh, and back.<br /> <br /> -Spooky reminds us there is no such thing as overextension.<br /> <br /> -That was fun, but it is time for necking in the Jacuzzi.<br /> <br /> -Strawberry Deathcake signing off.<br /> <br /> <br /> August 14, 2010<br /> <br /> -Morning comes. Bedmate is warm. No wanna get up.<br /> <br /> -PM is for waking up. AM is not.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m as hard to hold as Quicksilver when I kiss and run away\u2026<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Sara gets to meet crazy neighbor.<br /> <br /> -gotta admit, crazy neighbor\u2019s lay is crazy hot.<br /> <br /> -Is she speaking up because she is nervous, or because she is taking more control of his life I wonder\u2026<br /> <br /> -Yay crazy neighbor!<br /> <br /> -Well that went well enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Missives</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> It seems you were right, that I wouldn\u2019t keep wandering forever. I managed to find a whole troupe of folks who are touched, like me. They don\u2019t travel around, but there seem to be plenty of things to handle in this area anyway. I think Gran would have approved of them, for all that they are country people. <br /> <br /> I met them at a large gathering of similar folk, and they invited me to stay in their house if I was ever passing through. And man, is it ever a house! It\u2019s bigger than most hotels we ever stayed at, four whole floors - I think its kitchen is bigger than our old trailer. It\u2019s got gardens and its own cemetery, as well as a library. It\u2019s right next to the ocean, and even has a yacht. Well, I guess the house doesn\u2019t have a yacht, but Simon, the man of the house, does. He\u2019s a little younger than me, but has been the head of one of those old families for some time. He\u2019s quite handsome, a fairly quiet, serious man, though he has a bit of a mischievous streak on occasion. He is a most polite prankster however. A few of his cousins are also staying in the house, and apparently this family only comes in attractive. Well, one of his cousins is not really my type, more of a ruggedly large, but 4 out of 5 isn\u2019t bad.<br /> <br /> The other man in the house is Doc. I kinda presume that\u2019s not his real name, but it\u2019s what he was introduced as and goes by. He was a soldier doctor, over in Iraq, until he got injured really badly. He\u2019s a very secure presence, and reminds me a little bit of Emcee. A little bit more with it, maybe, but a strong rock for the troupe. He\u2019s also a tattoo artist, and even knows a bit about scarification and the like, which is nice and convenient. He\u2019s an honest sort, the likes of which you rarely see, with no front or persona other than himself. Or else he\u2019s a really, really good liar, and I just haven\u2019t been around long enough, but I\u2019m usually a bit better with reading people that that.<br /> <br /> His girlfriend is Natalie. She reminds me a lot of home, and you guys. A passionate woman, beautiful, and an actress to boot, I think she would fit right in with the troupe. Which has been nice, when things take a turn for the new and frightening, to have someone who seems so familiar. She and her girlfriend Karen have also made much of me, which was balm to a lonely girl on the road, and promises nice things for a happy girl in a new troupe. She's something of a priestess for the troupe, in a complicated way that's, well, complicated. We're something of an eclectic bunch.<br /> <br /> Jasmine is a bit of a contrast to Natalie, being much like you warned me about the outside world when I left. She is lovely woman (Gretchen, one of Simon\u2019s cousins, asked him once what he\u2019d done to get so many beautiful women to come to the house. Whatever it was, it seriously worked.) but very uptight and proper. She is actually being courted by the ruggedly large cousin Karl, which is fairly adorable. Within the troupe, she reminds me a bit of you - she\u2019s in charge of making sure we keep on track, and that we don\u2019t forget our gigs and back-burner projects. She has also been very diligent in making sure I get up to speed, as they deal with a lot more serious situations and folks than I\u2019ve been able to on my own.<br /> <br /> The last touched member of the troupe here in the house is Alexia. She runs a bakery, as a regular job, but she cooks everything amazingly. It\u2019s pretty fun just to watch her work, in the gigantic kitchen, fixing meals for all of us. She\u2019s even let me help out a little, which mostly involved not letting the cats get anything more than covered in flour. She also tends the gardens I mentioned before. Her girlfriend Chandra proposed to her while we were out on the yacht earlier - after she managed to get the wind back to say yes, Alexia\u2019s joking comment was that the only thing she regretted was now *she* couldn\u2019t propose to her. Also, I think it left Karen wondering about precedents...<br /> The other touched member of the troupe is Gwen. She is actually the first of the troupe I met - at the large gathering I mentioned, I had sought her out as a teacher, and she introduced me to the others. She used to be a cop, and is currently chasing down a lead from one of her old cases, I believe. She had to leave suddenly shortly before I arrived, which leads a little to a feeling of fatedness in my arrival. <br /> <br /> I had planned to only stay awhile, but managed to get caught a bit of a whirlwind of activity, and everything going on has been telling me that this is a place where I'll belong and people I'll be able to belong with. So, I am safe and sound and no longer traipsing about on my own. If the road ever takes the troupe near Connecticut, let me know, and perhaps I can stop by. <br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Well that was both fun and exciting wasn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> As a reminder Doc's journal did not happen in game. It was what his and Gwen's player worked out, and I OKed.<br /> <br /> Jasmine covered a goodly part of what happened. Tavia\u2019s \u201csecret passage\u201d had been taught to Simon before (when she fled downstairs after he slept with a college student he used it to find her)<br /> <br /> One thing that came up repeated OOC near the end is Uratha are not supposed to sleep with each other, and the obvious sexual connection between Malard and Angelique was problematic. More of that will be coming up soon.<br /> <br /> One funny running theme was Jasmine early on decided to explain to Sara about other supernatural creatures (after Gretchen vividly threatened to have Grin eat and shit out Leslie). She hit the high points, but as the game went on other critters kept coming up to discuss, like Pup Pid, or the Black Shuck, or Tavia mentioning Wookalars.<br /> <br /> Of course there are no such things as Wookalars. What a silly thought.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, Happy New Year","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:36:12-08:00","id":16987,"title":"","content":"New Day, new post. Time to follow up on the Middle Shadows and their activities.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1330 Hours, Saturday, August 14, 2010<br /> <br /> I just got back to the Bluffs a little while ago. Rose and Tavia were the only ones around when I came in. They were very concerned for Ronin as I updated them. For once I\u2019m also pretty sure Rose and I are in complete agreement that Ronin was stupid today. But I\u2019m also still mad she vanished. After seeing what she got herself into, I really didn\u2019t want her leaving again. Rose explained what I missed with the grand return of Leslie. And as usual, I missed all the fun.<br /> <br /> As soon as she came through the door, Gretchen ambushed her cousin with what sounded like a long overdue berating. I don\u2019t really know what has happened between them in the past, but given Rose\u2019s difficulty in relating the \u201cconversation,\u201d it sounded littered with profanity and threats. The short translation was that if Leslie did, tried to do, or was suspected of doing anything to Gretchen she would have her boyfriend eat her whole and shit out her corpse. Now I don\u2019t doubt that Mongler could do that, but that seemed pretty brutal. Coming from Gretchen, it must have been pretty surreal. After that (I think Rose used the term aftermath), Bright Eyes was given an update on what we\u2019ve done and some background on the other supernatural beings we call neighbors. Then they decided to take everyone out on the yacht. And if that wasn\u2019t enough of a party, Chandra proposed to Cupcake while they were out there! That was one hell of an afternoon.<br /> <br /> The rest of the information kind of ran together. Bright Eyes met the Fish God while Pup Pid peeped on Leslie? Rose tried to track the pirate but found Marjorie instead? Then they bled on and brought her into the house (that one I understand). Now she knows she died and there was some fight about killing Stanley\u2019s aunt? I know Rose is smart but I was failing to understand. I had to pause there to go change clothes and get some sleep.<br /> <br /> Now that\u2019s what I\u2019m gonna do until somebody needs me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0340 Hours, Sunday, August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> It ended up that everyone felt like I should sleep, so I woke up just before dinner. I felt better too.<br /> <br /> Everyone came to dinner and it was pretty normal. Well except that we didn\u2019t talk about \u201cbusiness\u201d with Leslie there. We apparently don\u2019t want her knowing exactly what we are, so there was a gag order on dinner. Once that was finished, we decided to go to Murder Ballads. Even Tavia went this time, though she wore this giant black Elvira wig. Rose stayed home as she hates clubbing but also Karl was supposed to return. That was a much better reason to stay home so we didn\u2019t give her a hard time.<br /> It was busy like usual on a Saturday night, but we saw several people we knew. I spotted Neon and Rebecca right off. Then I saw Sonia light up when she saw Nightshade come in. I tried to ignore her and have good time anyway. Snowflake and I noticed with a grin that Pilot Light was showing around a friend. And though Karen didn\u2019t seem pleased by it, I noticed a few of Nightshade\u2019s groupies from the party as well. Since we had new people with us and it was something fun, Nightshade showed us around the VIP rooms under the stage. I knew she had a VIP pass but I\u2019m not sure I even knew there was anything under the stage, much less a set of sound dampened lounge rooms. After that, everyone started splitting off. Bright Eyes was taking it all in, so I gave her a bit of advice. I was happy to introduce her to my vampiric friend, but I wanted to her to know how bad of an idea it might be to get involved with either Rebecca or Neon. That love square is not worth the issues, plus I don\u2019t want Truman to have to deal with more internal trouble. Once she was made aware, Bright Eyes and I went over and talked with the Carthians. I mentioned seeing the Sheriff at Alchemi and Rebecca explained that he did indeed make it a point to hustle on the weekends. This could be invaluable information the next Boys\u2019 Night Snowflake and I go on. Bright Eyes seemed much more interested in Rebecca, even if just for casual conversation so when we all moved to dance, I asked Neon. I also felt like it was a safer bet. Eventually we moved our way through other parts of the club, parting on good terms and making more friends for Bright Eyes. Then Nightshade and Karen joined us and we talked and flirted a bit. Then Nightshade and Bright Eyes decided to dance together in the cage. That stopped quite a few people in their tracks. I had just enough brain working to grab my phone, which Nightshade insisted have a camera in it, and take a picture. Karen and I agreed that was probably the hottest thing we\u2019ve ever seen in Murder Ballads.<br /> <br /> When they were finished and we could all blink again, I walked over to actually speak to Leslie. She seemed at least moderately happy to see me, given we aren\u2019t close. But with the reception she\u2019s received already, I thought it might be good to have a positive face in the crowd. Also I wanted to make sure she was still willing to work in the shop. That seems like it won\u2019t be a problem once we get her class schedule. I should talk to Trinh and Elsie as well. We talked about her summer and random pleasant things until Pilot Light and his friend came over. It was very obvious who he was there to see so I made myself scarce. While I doubted that Leslie would have much interest in him, I also knew that Pilot Light would get nowhere with her she didn\u2019t want to go already. John, surprisingly Elsie\u2019s date and Pilot Light\u2019s friend, looked bored out of his mind until Bright Eyes came over and started talking to him. Bonnie Lynn would have been so proud to know he was very upfront with Bright Eyes about having a girlfriend. Somewhere in the night, Ronin just groaned and has no idea why.<br /> <br /> We got back to the Bluffs around 0100 Hours and most of the couples split off. Karen and Nightshade were talking about the jacuzzi so I knew I was not needed. That left Bright Eyes and I to our own devices. Before I could really think about my situation too hard, Rose came in and told us that Karl was home before she went to bed. She was obviously tired given the time, but she seemed so happy. It happens so seldom that it stands out. I went to talk but he told me he needed to speak with Snowflake and Tavia about a private matter. I let them know I\u2019d be around if they needed me. Not sure what\u2019s up with that, but it can\u2019t be good.<br /> <br /> They let me know that later today we are going back to Glenwood so I decided to hit the Library. I realize that Snowflake and even Tavia probably already know how to deal with all this, but I don\u2019t really know anything about handling Abyssal taint. When I came down to the main research table, I found a large box filled with bars of soap. I have no idea why it\u2019s in the Library or on the big table. Setting it down and out of the way, I got to work. After about two and half hours, I had a better idea of what might have caused the taint. Based on the research, there could be a gateway to the Abyssal Plane opening, which would be catastrophic, but the signs aren\u2019t really there for that. What seems more likely, if equally terrifying, is that someone or something has returned from the other side. I assume that things not of that plane eventually have to return, given the reading. The problem is that anything that returns from that terrible place isn\u2019t right anymore. And that includes far more insidious changes than simple insanity unfortunately. But because of these changes, whatever it is no longer belongs in this plane either. If this is the case in Glenwood, then the taint is coming from the being or object \u201ctrailing\u201d energy from the Abyss. To cleanse the taint, we\u2019ll first have to find the source. And after that, I hope Snowflake has a plan. I don\u2019t mean that to sound lazy, I mean I can find no way to remove Abyssal taint or deal with energy from the Abyssal plane.<br /> <br /> And with that cheery thought echoing through my skull, I\u2019m going to go lay down. Tomorrow will be a big day.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Sunday, August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, I think the concept of a fight settled my nerves after dealing with Ronin\u2019s injuries. I went into the Meditation Room just as Rose was settling in as well. In what seemed like a blink, I found myself at peace. My eyes snapped open to see Rose still with me. This almost never happens so I was shocked. But in my calmed state, I silently nodded and left her to her own journey.<br /> <br /> Cupcake made waffles for breakfast though the younger residents, namely Leslie and Karen, were still sleeping. Tavia took the opportunity to discuss the issue Karl brought to her and Snowflake last night. Apparently all is not well on the shores of Cold Harbor. The mayor is Henri Fishborn. He is a Brineborn cousin but also is well liked for being the driving force in modernizing the community as much as it has. The issue is that just before Karl left, Henri approached him with what sounded like orders for Tavia to return alone. Karl noted it was suspiciously right before he left, leaving no time for him to talk with anyone else in Cold Harbor about the situation. This sounded like a terrible idea for Tavia and then she explained why. When Tavia was still living in Cold Harbor, Henri left subtle hints that he was interested in her in more than just a citizen or cousin. Also the mayor has never hidden his displeasure that the Fishborns of Dark Haven Bluffs were separate. He felt they thought they were better than their family. Snowflake seemed to silently agree with this assessment, but did not comment. Tavia believed that Henri wanted to take her as his own and either through this or in addition to it, claim control of the House. Apparently even Karl was unaware of these events. Snowflake was not silent in his opposition to either of these options and Karl immediately asked if Henri had ever acted inappropriately toward her. While seeing Karl\u2019s posture nearly ripple into a protective and angry stance was intimidating, I had the same thought. Brineborn or no, no one would be claiming Tavia against her will while I was breathing. Tavia quickly assured Karl that nothing had happened, but woman\u2019s intuition had previously told her all she needed to know. Karl informed us, possibly noticing my similar shift in posture, that Henri was taller and wider than himself in both human and hybrid forms. That was a sobering thought. Tavia continued that she was suspicious of Tzipporah\u2019s possible involvement, even though it had been weeks since the would-be matron travelled through Cold Harbor. We really can\u2019t discount the possibility, but we also don\u2019t have anything to go on. We decided that when Tavia goes back, at the very least Rose will be going along. I think we should all go, so Snowflake can take the yacht and we can initiate a Hearts and Minds operation for the people of Cold Harbor. That will weaken Henri\u2019s powerbase and reconnect Snowflake with the people that might otherwise stand against him. We don\u2019t want to have to fight them and if we can somehow use this to our advantage in gaining strength against Tzipporah, all the better.<br /> <br /> I just reread that and yes, I realize how very paranoid it sounds. But just because you\u2019re paranoid doesn\u2019t mean they aren\u2019t out to get you.<br /> <br /> So that was breakfast. Now we\u2019re about to hit the Haunts before trekking back to Glenwood. This promises to be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> Saturday, August 14, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Doc returned this afternoon. He reports that Gwen had run afoul of something rather terrible, though she wouldn\u2019t say what it was, and was badly injured. He patched her up, but before he could get any more details from her, she snuck away. I am very worried for Gwen, and a part of me is quite angry with her, though, for going off on her own and endangering herself like she is. After the lecture she gave me on the subject, you\u2019d think she would be smarter about it, but apparently the leads she received on her missing brother have unhinged her already tenuous grasp of wisdom. Of course, I\u2019m also angry about it because I miss her and wish she were still here with us.<br /> <br /> Almost everyone else took Leslie out clubbing to Murder Ballads. I personally think it is a bad idea to introduce that girl to somewhere so ripe for her wiles, but I suppose she would find it on her own anyway. Chandra and Alexia stayed at the mansion, but have disappeared into Alexia\u2019s room. I stayed home as well, of course. I\u2019ve been enjoying having the house mostly to myself while Lily and Naomi keep each other occupied. It\u2019s given me a chance to catch up on some reading, with Fu curled up in my lap. I expect Karl to arrive within the hour, and I\u2019m excited to see him again. I needed a bit of time away from him to sort things out in my head, but now that I\u2019ve done so, more or less, I can\u2019t wait for him to return.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, August 15, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> We are currently preparing to go to Glenwood and investigate the outsider disturbance there. I have a little time to write, so I have decided to record the events of last night and this morning.<br /> <br /> Karl arrived home last night, tired but glad to see me. I\u2019m certain the rest of the krewe would have enjoyed seeing me rush into his welcoming embrace as he stepped over the threshold. While he settled in, I cooked him a nice dinner, and as he ate, he shared with me some troubling news from Cold Harbor. The mayor of the village, a brineborn named Henri, has insisted that Tavia come back to see him. The mayor made the request just as Karl was leaving, and Karl thinks he timed it so that Karl wouldn\u2019t have a chance to ask around any before coming back to the mansion. However, he is certain that Henri wants to claim Tavia for himself so that he can gain control over Dark Haven Bluffs. Karl said he would talk to Simon and Tavia about it when they returned home later, and that they could decide what to tell the rest of the krewe.<br /> <br /> After dinner, however, we tried to put all of that out of our minds and enjoy our time alone together. We retired to the TV room to relax, cuddle, and watch Funny Face (one of my favorite Audrey Hepburn films) and The Maltese Falcon, neither of which Karl had ever seen. I don\u2019t know if he enjoyed Funny Face very much (though he did enjoy snuggling with me during the film), but he seemed to like The Maltese Falcon. I think he has a penchant for film noir. The others returned home after midnight, just as The Maltese Falcon was ending. They seem to have had a good time, and once everyone had welcomed Karl home, I excused myself to go to bed and let Karl chat with Simon and Tavia.<br /> <br /> This morning, over breakfast, Simon brought up Karl\u2019s news with the rest of the krewe, and Tavia filled in a few more details. Henri has never approved of the separation of the different branches of the Fishborne family. Simon\u2019s branch is much better off, and Henri envies that, even though he is quite powerful in Cold Harbor and is single-handedly responsible for modernizing the village. Tavia agreed that he was likely trying to take her as his own (I hesitate to call it marriage) in order to get the mansion, and feared that he might use his powerful supernatural pheromones to make her more pliable to his will. The whole idea of it was disgusting, and I would rather Tavia not return to Cold Harbor, but Simon believes that ignoring Henri\u2019s request would be very dangerous. It might even drive into collusion with the de la Poers. We\u2019re not sure when exactly Tavia will go to see Henri, but when she does, she won\u2019t go alone. At the very least, we\u2019ve agreed that I will accompany her, and will invisibly attend her meeting with Henri to make sure no harm comes to her.<br /> <br /> I think we\u2019re ready to go to Glenwood now. Hopefully, next time I write, I\u2019ll have something good to report. I\u2019m not optimistic, though. I wish Karl could accompany us, but it\u2019s not a good idea to take a brineborn like him into territory belonging to the Pure werewolves.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 14, 2010<br /> <br /> -New Vlog up. That is two, which is better than one.<br /> <br /> -Seekrit project going well.<br /> <br /> -Doc back, but nasty.<br /> <br /> -Aha the old shower trick I\u2026may have done that.<br /> <br /> -Clubbing tonight, serious stuff tomorrow.<br /> <br /> -I will be at @Murderballads tonight.<br /> <br /> -Sara is in danger coming in my room like this\u2026<br /> <br /> -Someone may get her.<br /> <br /> -Mmmm hmmm<br /> <br /> -Murder Ballads is hopping!<br /> <br /> -Time for the tour!<br /> <br /> -I love power. Absolute power is kinda neat.<br /> <br /> -OK bois and grrls, if you miss this dance, you are either totally gay/straight, or about to be full of remorse.<br /> <br /> -Mmmm Hmmmm<br /> <br /> -Now getting away from Sara before something bad happens in public.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jog.<br /> <br /> -Spooky is with Karl, how nice.<br /> <br /> -Girlfriend is a damn firecracker\u2026also nice.<br /> <br /> -Back to the hot tub TTFN.<br /> <br /> <br /> August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> -Sorry no Vlog last night, stuff got out of hand.<br /> <br /> -OK, looks like there may be a coup in the making. Not good.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Back in the dressing room\u2026sadly not for clubbing. QQ.<br /> <br /> -Maybe later!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXIV<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add to this one. It was good to have them re-encounter old friends while clubbing. I had a whole pool of NPCs for such encounters to come and go, then they largely stopped clubbing. I found it amusing no one mentioned to Jasmine Leslie's interest in Pilot Light...I doubt she would approve.<br /> <br /> Tavia seemed sort of smug about Henri's interest in her on telling, almost bragging about it. Not that she was interested, but she noted Simon had &quot;serious competition&quot; for her and implied Henri was not her only other admirer.<br /> <br /> I want to thank everyone who gave feedback for their Geist feedback. Most was in PMs, but still very much appreciated<br /> <br /> Had a request for pics of the members of the household. Lily, Naomi and Marjorie do not have pictures\u2026. that is likely to change for Marjorie; Lily only if I find a good one. Doing a GIS for drowned little girl sounds not safe for the soul, so unlikely for Naomi. If there is a NPC (or several) you want to see I have pictures for most of them, even a lot of minor ones.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Tavia3_zps2a50caff.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Tavia Fishborn</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/chandra2_zps415fb6f6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Chandra Maharajapuram</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/KarenSmith_zpsa7811b83.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Karen Smith</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Karl_zps7d74b912.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Karl Fishborn</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Louise_zps6e24daa9.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Gretchen DeLaPoer</a><br /> <br /> I have other pics for Chandra and Tavia but those are my favorite. I\u2019ll note when they first saw Chandra detaching her head I showed them the pic on page 72. Magical pic that. I am still a little surprised they both let her live and let her live in their house.<br /> <br /> OK hope you enjoyed those. Game last night was exciting as the PCs discovered\u2026some rather frightening things, and I got to let my imagination go wild with Abyssal Intrusions. Also, they found something the house could not fight. I am sure you will want to read all about it in two weeks. I\u2019ve already gotten a journal from Alexia! See ya then, and comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:40:25-08:00","id":16989,"title":"","content":"OK, it\u2019s time for our Krewe\u2019s latest adventures. Note last update has a number of pics of those at the house, including Tavia and Chandra among others. I being El Genius forgot the requested Sara (and her Geist) before, so they are included at the end of this entry. Also, this time we get an Alexia journal, huzzah! Anyway, I got to play merry hell with them last session so here you go, enjoy.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1845 Hours, Sunday, August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> I knew there were worse places than I have experienced in war. What I\u2019ve seen and heard about in the Underworld proves that. But knowing it and witnessing something from those worse places are not the same thing. I\u2019ll try to make this make sense by starting at the beginning.<br /> <br /> Snowflake drove Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and myself while Cupcake rode with Rose on our merry trip to Glenwood. We (read I) were very specific in our mission perimeters. Recon and surveillance only. I was very clear that we had no idea what we were dealing with and therefore we should not in any way engage our target. I got the look from Rose, but we all agreed. That\u2019s how I should know things are going to be far worse than what I expect.<br /> <br /> After the hour it took to drive out, Cupcake called and told us to stop. She said there was a dead body in the window of the pawn shop we just passed. This was on Main Street so we figured that would stand out. Snowflake pulled into a parking spot next to Rose and we all got out. Sure enough, there was a body sitting in a chair, on display in the pawn shop window. It was male, dressed casually, and based on decomp, it had already been there awhile. The pawn shop was open so we went inside. None of us could see the body after we walked in. Rose and Cupcake went back out to direct as Bright Eyes tried to touch the body. They saw the body move from her actions, but Bright Eyes never felt anything. After a few minutes, the teenager working the register called out to us that the chair did not have a dead body in it. He sounded just like it was something said all the time. There is no dead body in the window. Watch your step. No pets allowed. There is no sex in the Champagne Room. We asked him about it and he sighed before telling us \u201cthe weird trick of the light\u201d started about a week ago. That\u2019s not good. I walked back out to check, but the body was still there, just in the floor now from Bright Eyes\u2019 pushing. Then I noticed the body had no Death Marks, which was my first sign the kid was right. I went back in while Cupcake investigated the chair itself, which was not for sale. Bright Eyes, with Rose instructing outside, moved the body out of the window and it was gone. The kid told us we were wasting our time. It would just be back tomorrow. Cupcake learned that there was not a dead body in the chair. Next she used her object reading on the window and that\u2019s when we hit the jackpot. The window told her we could see things because \u201ceverything is broken.\u201d We figured out that the Outsider must have returned a week ago and the taint must have been more of a blast radius at first. The outside of the window was affected but not the inside, which meant it wasn\u2019t completely pervasive...yet. The kid was pretty apathetic, even for a teenager. We decided we had to move a little faster. Rose found a watch that could be a charm while the kid talked to someone on the phone about us. Given the discussion, it was probably the owner but the kid was not inclined to exert himself. She bought the watch and we left. I just couldn\u2019t get a thought out of my head. Everything is broken. It was so simple but so profoundly terrible.<br /> <br /> Rose unlocked her Primeval senses and immediately realized we needed to go to the abandoned strip mall down the street. We didn\u2019t want to attract attention so we parked along the street and walked through the empty parking lot. Cupcake picked the lock while we prepared. I didn\u2019t want to overreact, so I only unlocked my Pyre-Flame Shroud for protection and so we could see without alerting anything that we were coming. Inside it looked just like any other cheap strip mall except it was deserted. The space felt big and dusty. Shelves and fixtures stood empty and the escalators were turned off. The only way to describe it was desolate, like something out of an apocalypse movie. We came to something next that was bizarre at first, then mind numbingly scary. In the center of the mall, under the large skylight were dozens of manikins standing around as if they were real people in a still image of the mall in its prime. That\u2019s when the terror hit. It was like something had tried to recreate a normal scene after forgetting what normal actually was. The cheap Greek statue reproduction didn\u2019t help make anything better. Cupcake object read the statue then jumped. Her face contorted in horror at first, then she shook her head like she\u2019d been dazed. She turned to us with no emotion on her face or in her voice and said she\u2019d seen the Outsider. She couldn\u2019t remember anything but eyes and teeth. She thought it was her mind protecting itself from things it shouldn\u2019t know. She then moved to one of the manikins to ask it if they could move without help. She blinked then asked why they weren\u2019t moving already. Her eyes widened just before the mall sound system started playing muzak. She quickly backed away while telling us that they could all move, we were just still too close to the doors. Under the terrible music, I started hearing an odd scraping as things were obviously moving toward us. Nightshade grabbed my arm and almost ran for the door. I managed to stay on my feet and moved with her, shotgun ready. As we retreated, I noticed not only were the manikins moving, but there were also dead people with pipe driven into them attempting to shamble after us. The escalators turned us as we ran by, but I was not interested in waiting for what came up. I covered our flank until everyone made it back to the door. The manikins were at least as slow as zombies from the movies so even Snowflake managed without trouble. Rose determined that we needed to see the rest of the place in case the Outsider was still here. I looked at her like she was nuts but I realized she was right. I told her I was coming with her, but she reminded me she could be invisible and I\u2019d be the only target. She had seen the dead bodies too, so she knew what was at stake. I did not like it, but I agreed. As soon as she vanished and we backed out, all the manikins turned back.<br /> <br /> I stood at the door planning how best to destroy the building for about 15 minutes before Rose walked around the corner of the building. She said there was a Goblin Market in the basement. It was closed until Monday, so she couldn\u2019t go in. Of course it was. What respectable Goblin Market opens on the weekend? The guards showed Rose a secret passage to get by all the manikins and come in easier. Unfortunately, she also found the First Aid Station was being used to make the zombie manikins. The signs of struggle and blood meant they were bringing live bodies in; probably the local homeless. I said we should firebomb the whole place, but the rest of the Krewe looked at me like I was crazy. The consensus was that the property damage wasn\u2019t worth it. I don\u2019t understand that, but whatever.<br /> <br /> We moved on to another abandoned building that Rose sniffed out on the same street. It was 1.5 stories with no signs or anything special. Looked like a few of the shops I thought about before finding my free standing building. Cupcake picked the back door and inside we went. We were immediately met with the stench of water and filth. It was obvious this use to be a druggie hangup due to all the needles on the floor. I cautioned everyone to be very careful with their footing and not to touch anything. Rose noticed something strange about the pile of trash in the floor. Bright Eyes confirmed what I suspected was a danger symbol, used by homeless people. We stuck together because splitting up was not an option here. Rose heard it first as we took our first few steps. The droning hum of some kind of machine upstairs. We started to move forward when Cupcake stated as fact that no we would have machine men instead of manikins. I stopped and looked back at her, my head filled with images of new Cybermen. When we got to the stairs, I could hear the humming too. That\u2019s when Rose stopped short and I think she almost shivered. When she looked back to us, she let us know with a look of disgust that the sound was actually flies. The sheer number of insects needed to make that much noise \u2026 I don\u2019t \u2026 I can\u2019t. Nothing natural could deal with that. Snowflake recommended we go back outside and let him investigate less directly. We propped him up on a few cinderblocks and listened as he described the scene. The upstairs was just as dirty and scattered as downstairs, except for one room. We could see it from outside, but there was a heavy curtain over the window. Actually Snowflake corrected us, as that room was covered on every surface with black flies. Walls, floor, window, everything. In the center of the Room of Flies, a man sat with his legs crossed. He was also covered in flies. Because of that, Snowflake couldn\u2019t tell anything about him, including if he was still alive. He suggested we try to communicate. I didn\u2019t like the idea as that could lead to confrontation, but no one was physically going in so I didn\u2019t have much to argue. Snowflake created an illusion to speak with the being. He looked up when the illusion appeared and seemed happy for the company, though he was obviously insane. He thought the illusion was just another hallucination. Snowflake learned from this man that Louisa, a member of his lodge, despaired after another member of the lodge, Stephen, sacrificed himself to banish an Abyssal creature back to its plane. His noble sacrifice was in vain thanks to Louisa using some kind of relic or artifact to summon Stephen back, her love for the man blinding her to the damnation she invited. I realize this is a little dramatic. I\u2019m paraphrasing the words of a madman spoken to an illusion. Work with me here. Anyway, Snowflake got the address of the lodge along with a warning. Any contact with Louisa or what once was Stephen would be terribly dangerous. After learning about how this man could not go on with the eggs in his belly or the flies crawling out his eyes and his ass, Snowflake empowered his illusion to strike at the man\u2019s mind, granting him release.<br /> <br /> I have never believed in the idea of a mercy killing...until this afternoon.<br /> <br /> Before we could investigate the lodge, we had to do something about the Room of Flies. We walked back down the street to the hardware store on the corner. We found several heavy duty bug bombs and duct tape. Rose and Bright Eyes used their reflexes to break the window, throw in the bombs, and seal up the hole with the duct tape without the horde of flies attacking. After a few minutes the black curtain fell away from the window. Millions of dead flies filled a room surrounding a desiccated body, a happy smile on its face.<br /> <br /> We drove past the lodge on the way back to the Bluffs. It was a two story storefront in what might have been the nicer section of town. Other stores around it were open and everything seemed fine. There was a Closed for Renovation sign out front, but no store name. After what we found at the last two businesses, I don\u2019t think any of us were eager to look inside that one. The minor discussion on the way home got me thinking. The possibility exists that these people in the lodge are hedge mages, but this is a power beyond anything I\u2019ve even read about. I\u2019ve seen rumors of true mages before while we were researching. Could that be what they are, or were? No one really wanted to talk about that so I let it go. We came back home and Cupcake ordered pizza.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been thinking about what to do with the strip mall. The UPS store, much like the Goblin Market, is closed so I can\u2019t buy enough packing peanuts. When I mentioned it, Snowflake looked confused so I explained how to use the peanuts to make an effective, if low grade, Napalm. He thought about this for a moment before wordlessly pouring me a drink. I thought maybe we should call Jerome for Dragon\u2019s Breath rounds. I was reminded it might be better to wait until tomorrow. Now why a black market arms dealer cares about it being Sunday night, I\u2019m not sure but I\u2019m going to take the hint and let it go for now. And with the pizza guy here, I\u2019ll leave off.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2130 Hours, Sunday, August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> Well something good happened today at least.<br /> <br /> After we ate dinner, we all split up to deal with what we learned in our own way. I was still fuming about that First Aid Station being used to kill people, so I eventually found my way to the Exercise Room. I know it was stupid, but I had a Ronin moment and needed to exert myself. I loaded almost all the weight we had for the press and was lifting without a spotter. Snowflake came in just to make sure I was okay. When he saw what I was doing, he actually stopped and (for the first time I can remember) scolded me for doing something that could get me hurt. I stopped and blinked for a second then realized he was right. I started to ask him to spot, but he made it clear he couldn\u2019t do anything with that much weight either. Cupcake came in just as he was leaving and asked if she could talk to me. I figured I was probably done working out anyway, so I agreed. Then she floored me. She sat down next to me and reminded me of how I found her before the Krewe was consecrated. I was looking for something to cheer Rose up and went to a bakery for anything sweet. When I saw another Sin-Eater behind the counter, I almost freaked out. No way that was coincidence, so I drew her into our fledgeling group. Well because of that and some apparently serious rift in her family, Cupcake wanted me to give her away at her wedding to Chandra. There was no way I could refuse, given she said she considered me the reason she was part of the Krewe. Wow...that\u2019s all I got.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0530 Hours, Monday, August 16, 2010<br /> <br /> When your Drill Instructor kicks your bedframe to wake you up, you remember it and react accordingly. When the bed itself tries to throw you out, you have to think about what\u2019s going on. About 0400 Hours, the House woke me up by throwing me around in the bed and slamming my window open and shut. When I sat up, the door opened and I knew something really bad was happening. I ran across the hall and grabbed my shotgun from the armory before heading toward the noise upstairs. I stopped short when I got to Leslie\u2019s room. The door is locked with her calling from inside. That was a good sign that she didn\u2019t do anything. I told her to stay put and she\u2019d be fine. When I got upstairs, I noticed the rest of the Krewe was there already. Gretchen\u2019s door had been ripped off its hinges and a trail of blood led to the Library. My mind raced with all the things Gretchen had feared would come for her as we moved on the Library like a front line strike team. Before I cleared the entryway, I heard Rose scream Karl\u2019s name and my blood ran cold. The massive man was cut to ribbons, huddled against the wall in a puddle of his own blood. He was stable but in bad shape. When we tried to tend to him, he stopped me and told us there was something here for Gretchen. It was mostly intangible and he couldn\u2019t stop it. I stood and chambered my shotgun while I possessed the Dog of War. When I turned, the others were also assuming their Geists\u2019 visage. The beast looked like a gorilla with a short snouted alligator head. I unlocked my Primeval Shroud and we moved in. Bright Eyes and Rose attacked but it didn\u2019t seem to slow down. I ordered it to stand down or we would tear it apart. No response. Snowflake and Nightshade both used their own powers, but I have no idea what they did. Then Cupcake jumped in and hacked into it with her cleaver hands. That did some real damage. Bright Eyes tried to light it up again but missed. Rose got slammed into a shelf but countered with a claw attack of her own. I tried to slam the but of my shotgun into its head, but missed also. Snowflake tried to run it through with his saber. I was impressed but that didn\u2019t seem to hurt it much. Then Cupcake slammed her bladed hands into it again and took its head. The being disappeared in a flash of light.<br /> <br /> We ran back to Karl who had stopped bleeding, but was really no better off otherwise. I realized we needed to warn Gretchen like NOW, but I had to get Karl to the Infirmary. Rose called Mongler as Snowflake and I got Karl to the table. At first I was just going to get him cleaned up and take care of him like I would any of us. Then I got a good look at his wounds. If he had been human, he would have been gone already. Given his natural healing abilities, I didn\u2019t know how to help. Eventually I got him prepped and used my ceremony. I couldn\u2019t heal everything. I managed to close about half the claw wounds, but I still needed to use Nightshade\u2019s Deathmask. Even if I had burned all my Plasm, I\u2019m not sure I could have made him whole in one go. And given what we\u2019re planning to deal with, I couldn\u2019t afford to do that. I\u2019ll have to look after him and let nature and my medicine do whatever it can. These are the decisions I hate myself for. I\u2019m just glad Karl understands. But the Great Good be damned, this sucks.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, August 15, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Our excursion to Glenwood to find out more about the outsider taint there was useful. We know where it came from, if not how to cleanse it. But it was an awful day. Some of the things we encountered in Glenwood were terrible, and I only hope my dreams tonight aren\u2019t haunted by the memories.<br /> <br /> Simon drove Natalie, Doc and Sara in his car. I drove Alexia in my car, and we had a nice chat along the way. Once we arrived in Glenwood, I opened my senses with the Primeval Oracle. Last time I had done so, the strength of the taint was almost palpable, so I thought the Oracle might help me track down sources of the taint this time as well, and I was right. As we drove around Glenwood, I sensed that the town\u2019s abandoned shopping mall positively seethed with the taint, as did a nearby shop on a vacant block close to the meager downtown area.<br /> <br /> But our first encounter with a symptom of the taint was a small pawn shop. As we were driving by, we noticed a dead body sitting in a chair in the shop\u2019s large front window. At first I thought my eyes must be playing tricks on me through the window\u2019s security bars. We stopped to investigate, and discovered that though there appeared to be a body in the shop\u2019s window, there was absolutely nothing sitting in the chair once we entered the shop to have a look. Doc and Sara spoke to the rather listless teenage clerk, who explained that the body had appeared in the window a week or so ago, and had been causing quite a stir in the neighborhood. Sara experimented with manipulating the non-existent body, and was able to move its image in the window by touching the empty space where it should have been inside the shop. And when Alexia used her own Oracle to commune with the window glass, she learned that it was broken. Not physically, but spiritually or supernaturally. There was no body. It only existed in the window.<br /> <br /> There was little else we could do there, and we felt that cleansing the taint from Glenwood would probably \u201cfix\u201d the window. So we moved on to the abandoned mall. Alexia picked the door locks so we could enter through one of the department stores, and we began exploring the place. It had been largely cleaned out, though there were still many fixtures\u2014shelves and clothing racks mostly\u2014whose empty presence deepened the sense of desolation that haunted the place.<br /> <br /> As we moved into the mall concourse, however, we saw that it was populated by mannequins, which were positioned around the mall like shoppers as though the place had been frozen in the middle of a day\u2019s business. It was quite chilling. Before we moved off to explore any deeper, Alexia communed with one of the mannequins using her Oracle. At first, her expression flickered briefly to horror when she asked what had placed the mannequins there. She later told us that she had seen the abyssal entity responsible for the taint, but her mind could not accept the sight and blocked it out immediately. All she remembered were malevolent, hungry eyes and jagged, needle-sharp teeth.<br /> <br /> Shaking off the brief terror of the half-remembered visage, Alexia asked the mannequins if they could move about on their own, and was surprised when they answered that they could. So she asked why they weren\u2019t moving then. The mannequin answered that it was because we were still too close to the door.<br /> <br /> Alexia went pale when she realized what that meant, and quickly told us what she\u2019d learned. Doc and I simultaneously told the krewe that we needed to retreat carefully but quickly, and we withdrew toward the department store and the way out. The mannequins reacted and began shambling toward us slowly but inexorably. Doc kicked one over as it lurched at him. It had trouble standing until two others helped it up, proving that the things were clumsy at best. And as we neared the door, I saw something horrible. There were corpses among the mannequins, dead people who had metal rods shoved into their limbs and were animated by whatever power gave the life to the mannequins.<br /> <br /> We were nearly out of the mall, when I decided that we needed to find out more. The outsider had obviously been very active in the mall, and we had no way of knowing whether it was still there or not. Perhaps the mall was its lair and the mannequins its guardians? So I told the others that I wanted to go back in and finish our search if I could. Doc growled and checked his guns. He didn\u2019t want me going in alone, but I gave him a sharp look and he realized that I could move about alone and unseen more safely than I could with him backing me up. The others weren\u2019t happy about me going back in alone, but we all agreed it was necessary. So I cloaked myself in my Shroud and crept invisibly back into the mall.<br /> <br /> I did not find much to further our investigation, though I found a first aid station hidden away off the concourse, and it was obvious that the mannequins had dragged people there in order to kill them and turn them into the animate corpses I had seen. No one was alive there anymore, though there were bodies, and the stench was unbearable.<br /> <br /> There was no evidence that the outsider was still in the mall or even that it laired there, though it had obviously spent quite awhile there, perhaps using the mannequins to study the forgotten habits of humanity (for we later learned that the abyssal thing had once been human). I did, however, find several bear traps and barricades placed around the door to the basement. I crept around them and descended into the dank space beneath the mall, and discovered a goblin market! I didn\u2019t know exactly what I was looking at at first, but the place was filled with ramshackle, colorful stalls that, were they open, would have been selling all manner of wondrous items. The whole place seemed to be hung with thorny vines that seemed completely out of place in the basement of a mall, but that\u2019s how I realized I was seeing changeling things, perhaps an entrance to the Hedge.<br /> <br /> There were two large, wart-covered green men (who I realized were hedge creatures) guarding the closed market with shotguns, though they seemed to be commanded by a feisty, green-skinned punk girl with pig-tails. I made myself visible so that I could speak with them, and though they were initially shocked and tried to warn me away, I was eventually able to have a nice conversation with them. They didn\u2019t know anything about the outsider or the mannequins, except that they tried to keep the mannequins out of the market. The market was closed on the weekends, but would be open Monday through Friday, and they invited me to come back to visit if I wanted. I promised I would.<br /> <br /> They also told me about an easier way in and out of the mall through a shaft that led to the roof. I had seen it on my way to the basement, and it leads almost directly from the door to the basement to the roof of the mall, bypassing all the mannequins. When I left, I escaped through the shaft and found that it was a simple matter to get in and out that way.<br /> <br /> I shared what I\u2019d found with the rest of the krewe and then called Mongler (I suppose I should call him Grin, since that\u2019s really what he prefers to be called by his friends). Grin didn\u2019t know about the market, but promised he\u2019d let other changelings know. He also gave me some good warnings and advice about shopping at goblin markets.<br /> <br /> We moved on then, to the empty shop near downtown, which was not far from the mall. The place was in poor shape, and filled with debris and garbage, including cast off drug needles. Sara said it had been used by homeless squatters, and pointed out a mark they left warning others away because of some sort of danger. It was then that I heard a faint humming sound. I concentrated on it, and realized it wasn\u2019t so much a hum as a persistent buzzing. I crept carefully to the stairs that led to the second floor. The buzzing was coming from there, and I recoiled as I realized that it was the sound of thousands of flies closed away in one of the upstairs rooms.<br /> <br /> Simon sank into a Boneyard trance and discovered that the room was filled with flies covering every surface. And in the middle was a man, still alive, who sat in the center of the room, flies covering him so that Simon could barely make out his outlines.<br /> <br /> Simon manifested an illusory image to speak to the man, and discovered that he was quite mad. He had been a member of some sort of mystic order of mages who seem to master powers beyond those that Doc, Natalie and Simon have explored through their hedge magic. He told Simon that another member of his lodge, a man named Stephen, had sacrificed himself to drive an outsider entity back to the Abyss. His lover, another member of the lodge named Louisa, had foolishly used some sort of artifact to summon Stephen back from the Abyss, but he was changed by that unearthly place. He is now the outsider we are hunting, and must be destroyed or driven back. Louisa, of course, has also been driven mad, and is likely hiding away in the lodge\u2019s meeting place, a nondescript building in a quiet area of downtown.<br /> <br /> Simon killed the madman after he had learned what he could. He said it was bad\u2026very bad, and death must have been a welcome mercy for the ruined mage. I hope that Simon is okay with what he had to do. I worry about him.<br /> <br /> We got several bug bombs and used them to kill the countless flies in the room, then decided we needed to head home and try to wash away the day\u2019s horror and disgust. The fly-covered madman had left us all feeling unpleasant, and the Bride encouraged me to retreat for now and seek some solace in the arms of my lover, so I was anxious to get home to Karl. On the way home, however, we drove by to have a look at the lodge so that we could plan our next steps. It was a nondescript building on the edge of the run-down downtown area of Glenwood, certainly not the sort of place that would attract attention.<br /> Getting home and cleaned up was wonderful, and I spent the rest of the evening with Karl, trying to forget the horrors of the day. Now I\u2019m about to go to bed, and I\u2019m glad Lily and Fu are here with me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 16, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I nearly lost Karl last night. I\u2019ve been sitting up with him in Doc\u2019s infirmary trying to make sure he\u2019s comfortable and okay while Doc uses his ceremonies to do what he can to heal him. I was frightened for him, but I know he\u2019ll be all right. Now I\u2019m simply furious at Tzipporah, because we are almost certain she is responsible.<br /> <br /> We were all awakened from sleep at about 4:00 a.m. when the house shuddered as though hit by an earthquake. I was almost flung from my bed, and Fu let out a terrified yowl. I immediately realized that was trying to warn us of something, so I sprinted out into the hall, where the rest of the krewe was emerging from their rooms. There was some sort of disturbance coming from the end of the hall where Gretchen\u2019s room is, and as we collected ourselves and hurried there, the house locked Leslie, Tavia, and Karen in their rooms to keep them safe. I\u2019m sure they were terrified, but it was best to keep them away from danger.<br /> <br /> Gretchen\u2019s room had been ransacked, and splashes of blood led toward the library. We followed them there, unlocking our manifestations in preparation for any danger me might find. Alexia grew her extra arms and revealed her knives and cleavers, while Doc cloaked himself in the fierce visage of the Dog of War. Sara blazed with pyre-flame, and I opened myself to my feline Primeval Caul and Shroud and grew spectral claws.<br /> <br /> Karl lay crumpled and bleeding against one wall of the library. He had been mauled by a horrid beast that resembled a reptilian gorilla. It was unthinkbale that he could be hurt so easily, but he never stood a chance because the creature seemed to become incorporeal at will. We all possessed our geists so that we could face it. As the Bride\u2019s wedding veils draped me, I felt the fear and terror of losing Karl take hold of me, and I became cold and determineds. I leapt toward the beast, but Sara was faster, and slashed at it with her knife. I dodged around behind it, slashing its leg so deeply that it stumbled and collapsed to one knee. Alexia gracefully attacked it from the other side, her cleaver biting deep into its neck. Sara and I struck again, as Doc roared out threats to keep it off balance and Simon cursed it. The beast raked me with its vicious claws, but I buffered the gashes with plasm. Then Alexia struck again, chopping its head from its body. The thing\u2019s corpse decayed into nothing and was gone, proving that it had been summoned.<br /> <br /> We believe that Tzipporah tried to kill Gretchen. I\u2019m so glad that Gretchen stays with Grin on the weekends. I don\u2019t know what we\u2019ll do to guarantee her safety now. If Tzipporah finds out about Grin, she could send something to him home to attack Gretchen. Mongler may be strong, but as far as I know he can\u2019t handle something that\u2019s partially incorporeal any better than Karl! But for now, Gretchen is safe. I called her to make sure she was okay and let her know what happened. She was not as shaken by the news of the attack as I would have expected, but I suppose she\u2019s become accustomed to the thought that someone or something is planning her demise.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve spent the rest of the night and morning with Karl. Doc has done a lot to help him heal, but the wounds inflicted by the beast\u2019s claws are vicious and terrible and Karl can\u2019t heal them quickly on his own like he can most injuries. It was a very close call. I almost lost him, and we haven\u2019t even really been able to explore our love for each other yet. I can\u2019t imagine what I would have done if he had been killed, and I don\u2019t want to think about it.<br /> <br /> And yet I can feel the Bride\u2019s fear that it is only a matter of time before we lose another lover. Her fear is tinged with the certainty of conviction, and it bothers me, because deep down inside, I know that the fear is my own.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Lily the Ninja</u><br /> <br /> Before we headed off to Glenwood, I tried to find Lily to say goodbye and give her a hug before I left. I wanted her to know that I\u2019d be home safe later that night. I couldn\u2019t find her, though. Naomi didn\u2019t know where she was, and Tavia had not seen her.<br /> I found her lurking in the trunk of Simon\u2019s car. She was trying to join us on our excursion. I wanted to be cross with her, but I know she only means well and is concerned about it. It\u2019s not as if she can\u2019t take care of herself, and besides, she had disguised herself as a ninja by wrapping a black bandana around her head and taping a shuriken to her back. It was absolutely adorable.<br /> <br /> So it broke my heart a little to have to tell her to stay home and look out for Karl while I was gone. I know she wants to useful, but I worry about her. Still, maybe we can talk about it and work something out. I want to encourage her and help her feel wanted and loved and useful, so perhaps allowing her to join us on an excursion every now and then will be good.<br /> <u><br /> A Dead Man\u2019s Watch</u><br /> <br /> At the pawn shop, I noticed an old watch from the 70\u2019s. It resonated with death, so I bought it. I fashioned it into a Cold-Wind charm by etching the Chinese for \u201cair\u201d into its face and removing the watch band and adding a small chain to attach it to my charm belt.<br /> <br /> <u>Shopping at Goblin Markets</u><br /> <br /> Grin (that is, Mongler) warned me that goblin markets could be dangerous. You can find many wondrous things for sale there, including things you would never think could be sold, like lost innocence, or forgotten memories. Money is no good there; you must always trade something away, and sometimes the price is too great.<br /> <br /> At the time I didn\u2019t really think about it, but as I sit here writing this diary entry, I wonder if it is possible to buy back anything I lost when Richard died. And if it is possible, I wonder how high the price would be and whether the purchase would be nothing but illusion. Hope inspires me to see an opportunity in the market, but prudence dims that hope.<br /> <u><br /> Maria</u><br /> <br /> I think Maria might be a mage like those from the lodge, though I doubt she is part of the same group. She is the college student who was calling the shots when I was spying on Trinh and she was obviously exploring the ley lines of the mansion when she was there for the party. I would like to find out more about her. Indeed, she might be very useful in helping us resolve the problems in Glenwood. I wonder how we might contact her and share information? After all, she was very evasive last time we spoke, though she certainly suspects that we are more than we seem.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 15, 2010<br /> <br /> -Awwwwwwwwwwwwwww that was romantic<br /> <br /> -Doc is, for the record, on my side. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -He always gets in the back seat so he can crowd me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Doc is touching me! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -OK, here. Outer Nothipenoughtobeseeninolia.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Creeeeeeeepy.<br /> <br /> -Wow El Guapo here is certainly\u2026uh\u2026dull?<br /> <br /> -OK the mall. This won\u2019t be creepy right? (yes it will)<br /> <br /> -Yep, I am psychic.<br /> <br /> -Creeeeeeeepy<br /> <br /> -That was so not good, on so many not good levels.<br /> <br /> -And Spooky\u2019s going to go back in. And leave me fretting.<br /> <br /> -OK Spooky is back.<br /> <br /> -I am not going to type it. You would not believe me if I did.<br /> <br /> -Oh, are we gonna harvest another bumper crop of nightmares? I did not need that whole sleeping all morning thing anyway.<br /> <br /> -This place reminds me of a place I slept in LA for a few weeks while I was homeless.<br /> <br /> -Part of my brain still looks at the needles for how dirty they look thus how unusable they are. Bad.<br /> <br /> -I feel cold.<br /> <br /> -Oh, flies, great.<br /> <br /> -Heavens to Murgatroyd, exit stage left.<br /> <br /> -Simon is Boneyarding, better him than me.<br /> <br /> -Be glad you aren\u2019t here sweetie.<br /> <br /> -OK we learned enough, going home.<br /> <br /> -I need enough Cognac I don\u2019t remember my name, stat.<br /> <br /> -Short Vlog tonight, your Mistress is not having a good night.<br /> <br /> -Backrub then sleep. Actual sleep, not \u201csleep\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> August 16, 2010<br /> <br /> -Hahahahaha sleep.<br /> <br /> -Goddamn it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alexia\u2019s Ramblings</b><br /> <br /> Dear Diary,<br /> <br /> You know, my life could be less interesting, and I\u2019d be cool with that.<br /> I mean, I know that I\u2019m not destined for boredom behind some cushy desk, and that I help a lot of people/entities and with my \u201cinteresting\u201d existence, but sometimes I wouldn\u2019t mind a bit of boredom--just a smidge.<br /> <br /> Yesterday\u2019s latest \u201cinteresting\u201d happenings currently seems to be the result of *spoiler alert* a girl\u2019s non-existent ability to cope with the lose of a loved one. So, imagine if you will, a lodge of happy little mages (note: mage is just a theory but a good theory) all going about and doing great deeds of heroicness in their happy little community of Glenwood. Then one day, some big scary creature comes along, and to put that creature \u201cto rest\u201d the mages have to open a portal to the abyss. Opening the portal was all fine and good until they realised that someone would have to sacrifice themselves and fall into the abyss in order to defeat this creature and force it into the abyss. So, a sparkly dashing mage from the lodge steps up to the challenge, and pays the ultimate price so that the world can be rid of this nasty scary creature thing. Problem is, this dashing mage has a lover who is also a mage in the lodge. And this lover is so upset at losing her dashing mage, that she decides to summon her dashing mage back into our world and out of the abyss -- note: Diary, this is never a good idea. So, as anyone who\u2019s heard a good story knows, what comes back from the abyss isn\u2019t the dashing mage that sacrificed himself to save his loved ones. No, what comes back is something different, something not nice, something dark with teeth and angry eyes and features that no human was ever meant to see. And this is why Glenwood feels so wrong and is broken: because the things that should not be have come out to play.<br /> <br /> So, anyways, we went to Glenwood yesterday on a more or less information gathering mission. First, we discovered the \u201cbroken\u201d front window of a pawn shop. I say \u201cbroken\u201d because that\u2019s what the window told was wrong with it -- on a conceptual level, the window was broken a week ago, and this broken state causes the viewer who stands outside the pawn shop to see a dead body sitting in the chair that is inside the front window. This dead body is not actually there, and I know this because I talked to the chair and it told me that there was nothing sitting in it. We could poke the illusory body and make it fall over, but as soon as we moved the illusion out of the view of the window glass, it disappears. The teenager behind the register says that the body will be back in the chair tomorrow, and that the chair is not for sale because when the chair isn\u2019t there, the illusory body stands up and that is much worse. The poor guy was having a tough time managing the store, so I bought Chandra a chain necklace to make up for all the trouble we were causing at the shop.<br /> <br /> Next we decided to explore an abandoned mall that was giving off these wicked dark vibes. It seems that an abyssal entity put manikins and other humanoid statues inside the mall, and let them run around and play. I say abyssal entity because when I asked the greek statue that was standing still in the middle of floor surrounded by his manikin companions (also standing completely still) what it was that put him there in this place at this time, I was given a vision of a face my conscious brain could not cope with and all I remember is lots of teeth and eyes. I then talked to a manikin and discovered that the reason all the manikins were standing still was because we were still too close to the door for them to completely trap us. It was after announcing this bit of information to the group that the manikins decided it was time to try to get us, but they are slow like zombies in those all those modern movies. Jasmine turned invisible, went exploring and found that the manikins make other manikins by taking live humans to the infirmary and sticking metal pipes into their limbs. She also found something called a Goblin Market, which has something to do with Changelings, but I\u2019m not really certain about the details. Suffice to say that after going into the Hedge, I\u2019m fine with not going to visit any more Changeling locals unless we have our friendly neighborhood dinosaur. Unfortunately, what Jasmine didn\u2019t find was the source of all the wrong brokenness. <br /> <br /> So, then we saw a nondescript abandoned store with spooky vibes, and we made that our next stop. Inside there was a nifty symbol made of garbage that was a warning to all homeless people that the store was not a safe place for hanging out. Then Jasmine heard the buzzing of flies upstairs, but not just a couple of flies -- thousands of flies. Happily we made the correct decision to go outside and let Simon do his thing and astrally project himself into the upstairs. This is where he met the man who had previously been a member of the lodge and who told him the backstory on what happened to Glenwood. Simon used his projection to kill the man and end his mortal pain, but not until he told us where the lodge was.<br /> <br /> Then, as this was an information gathering quest (and not a solve all problems in one go quest), we drove by the lodge so that we would have an idea of it\u2019s physical appearance and dimensions, etc. Surprisingly there was no obvious dead bodies in the windows or anything physically weird, and it was even surrounded by open businesses (shocking). There were also no voices telling us to come inside or spooky music, so we agreed to come back later after we talked to a girl we know who we suspect is a mage.<br /> <br /> That night, after much pizza and chocolate was consumed, Chandra gave me a mission: to decide who would give me away at our wedding. My parents, who are militant vegans, disowned me a long time ago because I was spreading the evils of egg and milk consumption to the public through my successful pastry shop. Discovering the magic that eggs and milk can make in the kitchen as a teenager is where my obsession for cakes and other sugary delights comes from. It was a hard decision, but I finally decided to choose Doc because my family now is my crew and Doc was the one who found me and brought me into the fold of this group of amazing people.<br /> <br /> Much later, in the middle of the night while I was sleeping in our bed, and Chandra had gone hunting, the Fishborn house began shaking our beds, slamming our bedroom doors and windows, trying to wake us up, and locking the more mortal household members in their rooms to protect them. We all ran around trying to figure out what was going on, when Jasmine discovered that Carl was not in his room. We ran into the open door of the library to find Carl a shredded mess, and talking about the invisible summoned creature that had been sent to kill Gretchen. Luckily, Gretchen was staying at her boyfriend\u2019s place that night and was not around to be hurt by the thing. We all possessed our geist companions and the fight began! The creature was an ugly cross between an ape and a crocodile, and Diary, I totally kicked its ass into oblivion, it was so amazing!<br /> <br /> Afterwards, we went to check on people, and discovered that Chandra had come home while we were fighting to find the house in a state of alarm. Not knowing what was going on, she raced through the air in her awesome head form, and was lucky enough to be in the hallway when the house decided the danger had passed, and unlocked the door to Leslie\u2019s bedroom. Leslie was hiding under her bed when me and Simon found her, but he was able to smooth things over and explain the nature of Chandra\u2019s current state of existence. <br /> <br /> And with that, I leave you, Diary, to contemplate the nature of the universe (or whatever you do when I\u2019m not writing in you).<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Was that not fun all around?<br /> <br /> The Abyssal stuff was not taken directly from but heavily informed by Summoners and Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss for Mage: The Awakening. Sommoners is, for the record, a really good book, and even not running Mage I have gotten a lot of mileage out of it.<br /> <br /> The critter they fought was an interpretation of a Dimensional Shambler. Its ability to shift into and out of twilight made it impossible for the House and for Karl to fight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here is our good friend Sara Rowan, the newest member of the Krewe, and her Geist, The Virgin Sacrifice<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/GeistCharPort2_zpsd468d78e.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Sara Rowan </a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/GeistGeistPort2_zps1dbe558f.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">The Virgin Sacrifice</a> (Note: Artistic Nudity)<br /> <br /> If there is anyone else you would like to see I am happy to take more requests. Comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T00:43:33-08:00","id":16993,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on the Krewe and their wily ways. Some Werewolf stuff here, that I may or may not have totally screwed up; I wrote parts of that almost three years ago.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Monday, August 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Surprisingly, meditation went pretty well this morning. Given the madness of last night, I think centering in an hour is more than reasonable. Nightshade was up when I can down for breakfast, which was unusual but definitely a welcome change. Hearing the anguish in Rose\u2019s voice when she screamed out Karl\u2019s name really reminded me of what we still have to lose.<br /> <br /> I stopped in to check on Karl before I left. He was still as stable as I left him a few hours before. I expected as much, but just because my patient is a Brineborn doesn\u2019t mean I can be lax in my physician\u2019s duties. He was tired and stiff, but given that he should have been dead I think we were both satisfied with his condition.<br /> <br /> Work started out like a normal Monday. Quick dusting of the shelves from the weekend, people rushing in to get their loose tea for the week on the way to work, kids skipping school and hoping to find a head shop, and then more normal customers. Then I got a surprise. Zed, from Malard\u2019s pack, stopped by. When I saw him, I knew he must want to talk about why we had some kind of throwdown with a spirit last night. I apologized immediately and assured him we weren\u2019t responsible for that. He blinked for a minute then shook his head. That wasn\u2019t why he was here and I felt pretty stupid. There was an issue with Ol\u2019 Man Malard, one that could be a really problem. Deirdre's story about old werewolves going crazy immediately sprang to mind. Apparently Malard and Angelique are together now, which is not okay by Uratha law. There had been some speculation about that before but apparently it\u2019s not a secret any more. Actually Zed said Malard was flaunting this situation, deciding that that particular edict didn\u2019t apply to him. I asked why this was an issue by Uratha law, not really knowing more than it was frowned on. The Cahalith explained children that resulted from such a coupling could be completely normal, not even a werewolf. Sometimes they did become Uratha, but there were obviously no hard and fast rules for that. Unfortunately they could also turn out as spirit beings. This was because as Zed put it, Uratha are already half-spirit, half-flesh. But the worse case, and what all Uratha wanted to avoid is the possibility of the child being some kind of insane monster (note this is a werewolf describing something as an insane monster). Another part of this problem is that Angelique likes to be the bad girl. She is they pack mystic and calls herself a witch. The pack has worried about her darker style but until now they\u2019ve never had any evidence she was anything more than a goth. I knew Nightshade would have issues with that part of the story. Since we were both sharing and being concerned about Malard, I asked if the information we had passed to the elder Uratha managed to filter out to the others. They all knew about Karl but Lily, Leslie, and Glenwood were all news to Zed. We agreed that this was not something the Krewe needed to get directly involved in, but he wanted us to know since we were in the immediate area. Zed said he felt a responsibility to keep us informed. I know that feeling. We traded cell numbers so we could keep in touch. He left feeling like he had given us fair warning and I felt like we had someone we could trust if things got bad.<br /> <br /> Happy Monday, Doc.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1405 Hours, Monday, August 16, 2010<br /> <br /> My girlfriend is so hot. Nightshade came by for lunch like normal, but she was wearing what she called her Little Black Riding Hood outfit. She had no idea about Zed coming by earlier, but the whole Big Bad Wolf idea took on a whole new meaning when I saw her. I didn\u2019t really get into it very much over lunch since I knew it would come up during dinner. We just had a relaxing lunch. I think I\u2019m going to have to piss Karen off and claim Nightshade for myself for a few nights very soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0345 Hours, Tuesday, August 17, 2010<br /> <br /> When I got back to the Bluffs after work, Gretchen was home but she was so very drunk. Snowflake was not as far gone as she was thankfully, but he was drinking with her. The Scottish Fishborn ranted about getting everyone mauled or killed or worse and how selfish she was. We talked her down a little before I got some coffee for Snowflake. She was rightfully worried about her presence putting other people in danger. We did point out we were probably better suited to deal with something like this than almost anyone else she could find. Mongler was another story. While we knew he could become a dinosaur, that wouldn\u2019t help him anymore than being a shifter helped Karl if another of these things attacked. Eventually I got more coffee for Gretchen and convinced her she should try to sober up for dinner so we could discuss it as a group there. I\u2019m not sure when I because the Krewe Dad, but whatever. She seemed willing to go along with it so I went to get cleaned up.<br /> <br /> Over dinner we had alot going on. I went over the Werewolf Update and as expected Nightshade felt like Angelique was getting a raw deal because of preconceived notions and not real evidence. Rose thought the younger Uratha was using Malard, though I\u2019m not so sure about that one. I may just being paranoid, but after hearing a separate pack voicing concern for just this sort of thing, I\u2019m more willing to consider the threat. Snowflake hadn\u2019t spent his day drinking but instead researched the creature that Cupcake put down last night. It was called a Supernal Hunter and camed from an Astral Realm. I\u2019m not sure how many realms exist in the pure Light, but we know of several in the Darkness so it\u2019s not entirely unthinkable. This particular creature was a dimensional traveller and actually had trouble remaining in the physical state. Gretchen talked to the whole Krewe about leaving and everyone else said the same thing I had. She\u2019s willing to try and stay if she can convince Mongler to come here while she\u2019s with him. Rose has apparently been talking to Lily about going out with us during some of our less dangerous trips. I\u2019m really not happy about this. I mean I don\u2019t think Lily is intentionally looking to screw us over, but if she gets out of that doll we don\u2019t know what she might do. Rose thinks this will strengthen her sense of responsibility and loyalty to us, which are good things. I just hope she knows what she\u2019s doing. We ended dinner on a much lighter note with Cupcake and Chandra explaining their wedding plans. Nightshade will be officiating, Snowflake will be Chandra\u2019s Best Man, Rose and Bright Eyes will be the Bride\u2019s Maids, I will give Cupcake away, and Lily may even get involved. I\u2019m going to have to let Ronin know about this and hope she can get back for it. Don\u2019t know how that will work out.<br /> <br /> After dinner, Snowflake and I went to research Warding. It was a strong 20 minutes of study. Now I think we have some pretty good guidelines. We\u2019ll know more when we have a chance to learn it and try it out.<br /> <br /> We had a pretty quiet night after that, but I was still keyed up from worrying about Malard so I went out on patrol. It felt good but I could tell it had been awhile. I didn\u2019t stop anything but there were more people on the streets in West Haven tonight that normally wouldn\u2019t be out when I came by. I\u2019ll have to keep them guessing. But now, it\u2019s time for some sleep.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, August 16, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> Given Karl\u2019s situation, I had to cancel my training session with Jean this morning. I had trouble with my meditation, so I went outside to the cliffs and performed some deeply meditative tai chi exercises. It was quite settling. I do routinely train in the martial form of tai chi, but it has been awhile since I\u2019ve taken the time to perform the slower, more tranquil exercises. Perhaps, while the warm weather lasts, I should get up earlier and move my morning meditations outside. I should also ask if Doc would like to join me. Perhaps tai chi would be good for him.<br /> <br /> Monday, August 16, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> Karl is doing much better thanks to Doc\u2019s healing touch. He is still injured, and it will take him awhile before he\u2019s fully recovered, but Doc shifted a great deal of his plasm into the ceremony he used to assist his medical treatment, so the worst of it is over. I should find a way to thank him.<br /> <br /> I called Trinh early this afternoon to see if she could put me in touch with Maria, as we believe Maria might know something about mages that could help us in dealing with the situation in Glenwood. It was nice talking to Trinh again. Unfortunately, she couldn\u2019t put me in touch with Maria directly, but told me that she\u2019d have Stephen (the young man known as Pilot Light) call me since he knows Maria much better. Trinh doesn\u2019t really care for Maria, in part because of the way she bosses Stephen around. Maria also has R.L. and Jimbo wrapped around her finger. There\u2019s something odd about those two\u2026<br /> Maria has also been feuding with Barry Teasdale. I\u2019m not even sure I recall who he is, but if our suspicions about her are true, then it\u2019s possible Barry has some supernatural ability as well. Of course it\u2019s not inconceivable that their rivalry is purely mundane; I\u2019ve come to realize that my lifestyle has made me a bit detached from mortal life, so I suppose I jump to extraordinary conclusions more often than I should.<br /> <br /> Gretchen also returned to the mansion this afternoon. She immediately spoke with Simon, and later with the rest of the krewe, announcing her intentions to leave. The attack last night convinced her that she must not endanger us or Grin any further. Naturally, we all argued with her and insisted she stay. Gretchen can be quite stubborn, and her concerns about Grin\u2019s safety when faced with a beast like the supernal hunter are quite valid. But I don\u2019t think any of us are willing to let her march off to her death. We were eventually able to convince her to stay. She\u2019s far safer in the mansion than anywhere else. Grin\u2019s safety is a worry, but Simon and Doc suggested that Grin might move in with us until we\u2019ve resolved this issue. Gretchen hasn\u2019t decided exactly what she\u2019s going to do, but at least she agreed to stay another day and think it over so that we can discuss it again once she has a clearer head.<br /> <br /> Monday, August 16, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been spending the evening babying Karl, and he\u2019s dozing a bit right now, so I thought I\u2019d take the moment to write a diary entry.<br /> <br /> Over dinner, Doc brought a potentially troublesome situation to our attention. Zed, one of Mr. Malard\u2019s werewolf pack, came to speak to Doc at his store earlier in the day. He\u2019s worried because Malard and Angelique, the fetching young woman who is currently living with Malard, are in a relationship. Malard is apparently quite a catch for his age, given his strength as a werewolf, but intimate relationships between werewolves are forbidden. There are several reasons for that, but perhaps the most compelling is that the offspring of such a relationship can become quite dangerous.<br /> <br /> Zed and the rest of the pack are concerned about this. Angelique is a sort of werewolf mystic (I believe Doc used the term \u201cwitch,\u201d to which Natalie responded with a bit of cautious indignation). I gather that it is especially taboo for her to be involved in this sort of relationship. Also, if Malard is flaunting this breach of werewolf society, what other rules will he decide to break? Zed is worried this could be the first sign of a dangerous instability in a werewolf of Malard\u2019s age.<br /> <br /> Zed wasn\u2019t expecting us to do anything about it, but since Malard is our neighbor and a touchy situation may be brewing, he thought we should know. I, for one, worry that Angelique is using Malard, manipulating him to her own ends. The impression I\u2019ve gotten of her is that she is cunning, sly and perhaps a bit arrogant, and though I am of course jumping to conclusions about her character, I wonder if she isn\u2019t just toying with his affections to get what she wants. If so, then by all means she should be stopped. Using love to such manipulative and selfish ends cannot be allowed. I hope I\u2019m wrong about her.<br /> <br /> Dinner conversation soon turned to a more pleasant topic: Alexia and Chandra\u2019s upcoming wedding, which is scheduled for early next month. They asked us all to participate, and I became quite excited about it as we discussed it. Weddings are, after all, ideally the most romantic occasion in anyone\u2019s life.<br /> <br /> Natalie will be performing the ceremony thanks to her status as a priestess of sorts, and Chandra and Alexia aren\u2019t looking for a denominational wedding in any event. Sara and I will be Alexia\u2019s bride\u2019s maids. Simon is Chandra\u2019s best man, and Doc, as the \u201cfather\u201d of the krewe and the one who brought Alexia into it, will be giving Alexia away. There was talk of Lily being a flower girl, which would be wonderful as long as no mortals are present. Alexia has planned a magnificent rainbow-colored cake to celebrate the same-sex marriage, and the wedding is to take place on the scenic cliffs behind Dark Haven Bluffs, overlooking the sea. I think it will be lovely!<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 16, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> Stephen called, a bit late, but well before my bed-time. He was a bit surprised for me to ask for his help, but was willing to do what he could since Trinh asked him on my behalf. He promised to have Maria contact me, and I told him to mention the mansion to her in order to pique her interest. I hope it works, and I hope Maria isn\u2019t as cagey or antagonistic as she was the first time I tried to probe her knowledge of the supernatural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Supernal Hunter</u><br /> <br /> Simon researched the entity that attacked the mansion in search of Gretchen last night. It is called a supernal hunter, and is an otherworldly creature that excels at hunting prey. Simon says that it has some difficulty remaining material in our world, which works to its advantage, as it can shift into Twilight when it wishes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Mother\u2019s Little Helper</u><br /> <br /> I spoke to Lily about the possibility of allowing her to accompany me on some of our outings if she behaves well. She was quite excited about the possibility of coming along and helping out. We were able to make a deal: I\u2019ll ask her to come along sometimes, when it\u2019s not too dangerous for her, but in return she mustn\u2019t try to sneak off with us, and must be a good little girl and stay home when I ask her to. She was a bit disappointed that she can\u2019t try to sneak off with us (I think she enjoys the \u201cgame\u201d), but she agreed and we made a pinky promise to that effect.<br /> <br /> I explained the deal to the rest of the krewe. I think that most of the krewe was satisfied with the arrangement, though as usual, Doc had his concerns. He is quite legitimately worried that if Lily accompanies us, then she is more likely to have her doll-body damaged, which would free her and possibly make her quite dangerous. I argued that it would be better for us to have more control over when she comes along so that we will be better able to make sure she\u2019s safe, and Doc grudgingly agreed.<br /> <br /> I believe that she\u2019ll be good, and I hope that her time with us gives her a better sense of responsibility so that even if she is freed from her doll body, she won\u2019t cause too much trouble. And excluding her from everything isn\u2019t good for her. She desperately wants to contribute, and I think that allowing her to express herself in a constructive way is better than deepening her frustrations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Cupid\u2019s Arrows</u><br /> <br /> Trinh and Stephen are childhood friends, and quite close. I\u2019ve figured out from observing them that they have serious feelings for one another, but they\u2019ve been friends for so long that they have certain assumptions about each other that are keeping them from exploring romance. Stephen assumes that Trinh isn\u2019t interested and Trinh seems shy about confessing her feelings for Stephen, and thinks he\u2019s only interested in well-endowed party girls.<br /> <br /> Perhaps it was presumptuous of me, but I was sad to see the potential for true love go unfulfilled, so the Drowned Bride and I decided to gently nudge things in the right direction. While I was talking to Trinh, I asked about her feelings for Stephen, trying to get her to admit them to herself. I encouraged her to stop ignoring them.<br /> <br /> When I spoke with Stephen, I tried to casually comment that I was surprised he wasn\u2019t dating Trinh\u2014after all, I\u2019d seen the way she looks at him. He honestly didn\u2019t think she was interested since\u2019s she\u2019s only ever dated Blacks or other Vietnamese, but now that her grandmother\u2019s ghost has been resolved, I\u2019m certain she\u2019ll be more open to a relationship with Stephen. Of course, he has no way of know about that, so I hope my gentle encouragement gets things moving.<br /> <br /> Of course, I was probably much more heavy handed and blunt about the whole thing than I meant to be. I seem to lack Natalie\u2019s skill at being subtle. But I\u2019ve come to accept that, and if it helps make Trinh and Stephen happy, then I\u2019ll have accomplished something good.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 16, 2010<br /> <br /> -Up early! Black Witch needs sleep badly!<br /> <br /> -I has a sleepy.<br /> <br /> -Uh, Chandra does not know what a bachelor party is.<br /> <br /> -I think I summarized it nicely.<br /> <br /> -Lunch with Doc<br /> <br /> -Naptime!<br /> <br /> -Naps are not long enough.<br /> <br /> -Your mistress will be conducting a wedding. Been a few years.<br /> <br /> -Something tells me this will be less Wiccan.<br /> <br /> -Oh don\u2019t give me that Wiccans are not so bad<br /> <br /> -Mostly.<br /> <br /> -Glad this is a lazy day. My sleep schedule is FUBARed<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up, sleepy edition.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s not easy to be a coquettish lady of mysterious ways when you haven\u2019t had enough damn sleep. :-/<br /> <br /> -Remember we are people too and it\u2019s not easy to pretty up all the time.<br /> <br /> -Seriously, I know a lot of cool Wiccans.<br /> <br /> -If Karen keeps that up zzzzzzzzz<br /> <br /> -Dinnertime!<br /> <br /> -Well that is more not good stuff I can\u2019t do anything about. Huzzah!<br /> <br /> -Poor Gretchen.<br /> <br /> -The wedding bells in Karen\u2019s head are so loud even I can hear them.<br /> <br /> -Mischief time!<br /> <br /> -Mischief is fun!<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Chatz!<br /> <br /> -Please maybe let me sleep tonight?<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXVI<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Mostly just people going about their day. Some plans being made, however. Still, the session was wall to wall IC play, with some excellent roleplaying, as always. The characters personalities really are interesting enough with or without anything else.<br /> <br /> I damn near killed Sara\u2019s player with Gretchen\u2019s IC ranting by making her laugh to death. It was pretty funny though. Jasmine\u2019s \u201cI care about her but I can\u2019t stand to hear her talk\u201d relationship with Gretchen remained awesome.<br /> <br /> Now I just need a good plot to throw Mummies at them. Or put them in the middle of a Mummy-related conflict.<br /> <br /> We have passed 101,000 views between the two sites these are posted on in just under three years. Thanks folks. Glad you enjoy looking in on our little gang so much. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:00:12-08:00","id":17006,"title":"","content":"ime to check back on the Krewe. I can promise Drama!<br /> <br /> Also, there are some Egyptian Immortals that come up this time. They are not Mummies. They were written before Mummy came out. The timing is coincidental, as it was when the PCs decided to seek one out.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Author\u2019s Note: The discussion of Napalm in this entry is an uneasy balance. We play the game for ourselves and to have fun. But we also recognize we interact in a purely fictional world. We do not condone or suggest anyone in the real world making, having, or using homemade Napalm or any other toxic substance. It is understandably illegal in most municipalities. It is extremely flammable and highly unstable. It can kill, maim, and destroy.<br /> <b><br /> PLEASE DO NOT ATTEMPT THIS AT HOME! </b><br /> <br /> You will not come back with lower Synergy. You just won\u2019t come back.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0940 Hours, Tuesday, August 17, 2010<br /> <br /> I found a note in the Meditation Room today instead of Rose. She said she was on the Bluffs and I was welcome to come join her. When I found her, she was practicing Tai Chi. It was a scene from Karate Kid with her standing on the rocks with the ocean crashing down below. She noticed me standing there and offered to help me. That was another way she could meditate. It was different with the wind, but the sun was warm and the sounds of the sea more than made up for the lack of music. We went through different katas for about an hour. It was different but I was able to slip into a peaceful state. I then slipped into the shower again so I wasn\u2019t soaked. I was never very good at Tai Chi. I\u2019ve learned today that was because I was doing it wrong, and it\u2019s hard. Now I have to look in on Karl and run to work.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1415 Hours, Tuesday, August 17, 2010<br /> <br /> I was a little surprised when Bright Eyes asked if she could come to work with me this morning, but she said she wanted to see how things worked and maybe see if she could help out. I\u2019m in no position to turn away willful help so we rode over and I showed her around. I explained the normal routine as I went through opening.<br /> <br /> The morning rush went smoothly and Bright Eyes took a few questions and grabbed a few things to keep things moving. It was pretty awesome actually. After things died down again, she dropped a nuke in my lap. When she asked me, I think my brain seized at first. I went numb. All I could feel was a wall in my mind getting slammed into. I didn\u2019t understand what was happening. The wall was getting hammered more and more, while a pressure was building like panic, but I wasn\u2019t afraid or in danger. I had to ask her what? several times to make sure I understood everything correctly.<br /> <br /> Would I be upset or uncomfortable, on any level, if she slept with Nightshade and Karen?<br /> <br /> As the full meaning of the words seeped into my mind, I realized the wall was the blinder I built to keep me from looking too closely at the arrangement we had for a relationship. The wall that had hidden what I knew was an issue. In that moment, that wall was destroyed by the raging realization that Nightshade didn\u2019t have any problem with the idea of sleeping with someone other than Karen or I. She never stated or inferred that this would be strictly monogamous, I just assumed that since she had both of us, she would have everything she needed. This simple and honest question had just laid bare my naive little idea that we would be all that Nightshade wanted... and shined the cold light of truth down on it like a prison spotlight.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes had no real idea what to expect, though I doubt she could have known what was going through my head. I opened my mouth several times but shut it quickly as I felt the anger flowing up my throat. I clamped down, knowing abstractly that she was trying to do the right thing. She did not deserve the flames of rage that ravaged my chest and howled for blood like a pack of rabid wolves. When I finally leashed the beasts, I told her that I\u2019d have to get back to her as I couldn\u2019t functionally answer that question. I needed to talk with Nightshade to figure out what was going on. I turned to look at her when I could actually speak and she saw my face for the first time. She immediately retracted the question and apologized. It wasn\u2019t her responsibility to apologize, but that made me feel bad. I knew my anger shouldn\u2019t be directed at her and I\u2019m pretty sure she understood my emotional state without me having to explain.<br /> <br /> I stayed quiet for a while before Bright Eyes started talking to me about my tattooing equipment. I knew she was trying to change the subject but I didn\u2019t care. It let me not dwell on how stupid I was or how hurt I felt. It was easier to talk to her after a few minutes and she was seriously interested in tattoos. We talked until Nightshade got here. She brought lunch like usual, but seemed surprised to see Bright Eyes when she came in. She apologized for not bringing food for three, but Bright Eyes politely excused herself and I guess headed back to the Bluffs. I hadn\u2019t...no I couldn\u2019t think about what to say when I saw Nightshade so I had no clue how to go about this. She knew something was up as soon as Bright Eyes left. I tried to stay very calm because I know it bothers Nightshade when I get angry or she thinks I get angry. We had meaningless conversation without really saying anything. I don\u2019t remember ever being this awkward with her even when I was still in the wheelchair. I could tell she was trying to help but she doesn\u2019t really understand what\u2019s wrong. And if I\u2019m being honest, that is exactly what the problem is. Nightshade is not a jealous person...as in doesn\u2019t really grasp the concept. To her, jealousy seems like greed because you want someone all to yourself. Her anti-objectification goes that deep. She doesn\u2019t get that there are some things a couple share, that are degraded when more than just the couple share it. Yes I\u2019m now objectifying emotions, feelings. Love.<br /> It was a little weird to think about sharing Nightshade with Karen at first. Then it was a little easier because Karen and I never tried to compete with each other. That made it seem more ...stable? It never seemed normal, but I never believed that it would be. I guess that\u2019s my way of coping. I just decided that Nightshade had us both and that was all she wanted. If she was only okay with us being with her, that would have made sense. But given she pushed me and encouraged Karen to get involved with other people, \u2026. I don\u2019t think I\u2019m a genius, but I must be a complete idiot or utterly delusional for this to make any sense. I need my punching bag so I don\u2019t slam into the counter and scare anymore customers. That old lady almost knocked the loose teas off the shelf when she jumped.<br /> <br /> Nightshade eventually left after we had eaten. I started drawing almost as a reflex and wasn\u2019t even thinking about it. Then when I walked back to the counter after helping a customer I realized I was drawing something that looked disturbingly like the Rose Bride. I\u2019ve tried to get away from that image and the frightening concepts it brings up.<br /> <br /> I just want to beat the bag until my arms are numb. I need to think through this but thinking is so hard without realizing how stupid I\u2019ve been. That just makes me think about things all over again. FUCK! Dinner is going to be special tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2230 Hours, Tuesday, August 17, 2010<br /> <br /> When I was still in the Sand, we put our pain, loss, sadness, and whatever other emotions were in the way aside so we could finish the mission. When I came home to the Bluffs, that\u2019s what I planned to do again.<br /> <br /> The first thing I noticed was that Nightshade was singing and playing piano. She was upset. My first response was to check on her to see if she was alright. Then I realized, half a second later, she was upset because of us. Some part of me thought maybe she understood. But the rational part of me, that was slowly taking back ground in my mind, shouted that idea down. Nightshade was upset because she realized she was in a real relationship and that meant she felt trapped. It wasn\u2019t an angry thought or malicious at all. Just a statement. Likely factual. That didn\u2019t make me feel any better so I headed upstairs until time to eat.<br /> <br /> Rose brought our board meeting to order with new information on Marie Smith and her apparent rival Barry Teasdale. They are both something called Reborn. Apparently Reborn are ancient beings that live in various cycles. They are not mages, though they do have some form of magic. Rose thought it might be similar to the hedge magic Snowflake and I practice. Regardless, Barry informed her that they were rivals and went out of his way to assure her they did not want to get us involved. It was blatant that Barry was afraid of us and that he at least knew what we were. Referring to us as Ghost Walkers, he said we were, in his experience, never afraid to up the ante. Also that we had buttons that should never be pushed. I laughed and immediately thought of Ronin. None of us could argue his point however. Unfortunately that again left us without any assistance in dealing with Glenwood.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re not really decided on Plan A though we did consider using the DeCastro Box. I need to come up with a better name for that thing. The Frozen Onyx Dungeon maybe. Anyway, that is one option though we\u2019ll have to work up a ritual just for that. Plus I suggested that Snowflake might need to find a ritual to bind the Outsider. He almost lost it and made me tell him I wanted him to do this out loud so there was no mistake. This was payback for the Doomponies, I\u2019m sure. But I did specify we were looking for temporary binding until the ritual to lock them in the Onyx Prison could pull it/him in. Plan B was a controlled burn of the lodge. We\u2019re not sure how good or bad that might be, or even if it would have any effect. Tavia suggested using fire or a bucket of lye to crack the shell to get to the Abyssal candy center. The worse part is, this is all just for learning how to deal with it. We aren\u2019t going to have a lot of time or chances. I told them my plan for using homemade Napalm. I was terrified when it was agreed that was a good idea. Cupcake said she could get the containers, Snowflake volunteered to get the gas (Nightshade had a moment about getting gas on her hands), and the others were going to get the packing peanuts.<br /> <br /> With that as decided as we could make it, Cupcake stated she wanted to play Life for Game Night. Rose was the first one up from the table. We played through and Snowflake won. Nightshade was feeling a little better and tried to play with me a little to make me feel better. Unfortunately it didn\u2019t help. Actually it just ripped open what little bit of a scab I had managed to work up. I had to get away. I didn\u2019t want anyone else to see me as upset as I knew I was going to be.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m back up in my room. I feel like I should go back on patrol, but I\u2019m afraid of what might happen. I think I may hang the bag and hope I have enough tape to keep it from ripping open. I just can\u2019t deal with people that I care about right now.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 17, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I have not been keeping up with my regimen of tai chi exercises, so this morning, instead of meditating in the meditation room, I decided to go out to the cliffs behind the house and perform several tai chi routines in order to focus and center myself. It was a good choice, and I felt quite good throughout the rest of the day.<br /> <br /> I left a note for Doc in the meditation room, and was pleased when he came to join me. He was somewhat familiar with tai chi, but still had a lot to learn, so I helped him through some routines. It seemed to be a good change for him too.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 17, 2010, Early Afternoon<br /> <br /> After my training session with Jean this morning, I was in my office going through some e-mail when a handsome young man stopped by. It wasn\u2019t until he introduced himself as Barry Teasdale that I recognized him, recalling that he was allegedly involved in some sort of college feud with Maria Smith.<br /> <br /> Barry was there for a reason, and he wasted no time in getting right to the point, which instantly improved my opinion of him. He is aware that I\u2019ve been trying to get in touch with Maria, and he wanted to warn me that might not be such a good idea. He and Maria have reincarnated time and time again since they first died in ancient Egypt, which is why when I look at them, I can see that they are very much alive, yet have died many times. Barry says they are called \u201cReborn.\u201d<br /> <br /> Barry claims that he was originally a very bad person, and that Maria was bound to him as a sort of eternal consort. Both of them are powerful sorcerers, though I gather that the magic at their disposal is more akin to the kind of things that Doc, Simon and Natalie do with their hedge magic than it is to the sort of power wielded by the mages in Glenwood.<br /> <br /> Several centuries ago, Barry tired of his wicked ways. If he is to be believed, he turned over a new leaf and has since redeemed himself. Part of doing so, however, was releasing Maria from her mystically enforced servitude to him. She was far from grateful, however, and has spent the centuries since doing all in her power to make him suffer. Neither wants to kill the other, since they are still soul-bound, and if one dies, the other always follows soon after. But within the limits of her current incarnation, Maria ruthlessly works against Barry whenever she can. Barry thinks she\u2019s currently trying to implicate him in a bit of academic fraud.<br /> <br /> Barry was also quite open about the fact that he knows what I am\u2026and that he knows what sin-eaters are capable of. Maria certainly knows as well. They call us \u201cghost walkers,\u201d a term that I find far more charming than \u201csin-eater.\u201d They had a run-in with our kind a few centuries ago, and learned that we are capable of wielding great power, and, in his words, are \u201calways willing to up the ante.\u201d He must have been dealing with a third tier krewe then, because he seems to believe that ghost walkers can call in a lot of reinforcements. I got the impression that he and Maria are actually quite frightened of us, and would prefer we not get involved in their affairs, which suits me just fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 17, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> After returning home, I sought out Simon and spoke with him about Barry and Maria. He shared my amusement over the idea that these millennia-old beings were frightened of us, and we are both glad that for once, this is not something we need to concern ourselves with. Simon also quite liked the term ghost walker.<br /> <br /> After we talked about that for a bit, Simon opened up to me again about his romantic life. It seems I am the only person he can really talk to about these things. I\u2019m the only one who seems to understand, because to some degree, we have similar outlooks toward love and romance. Indeed, I think we both enjoy our talks, and personally, I\u2019m just flattered that Simon feels comfortable sharing with me, and will do whatever I can to help him.<br /> <br /> He has decided that he really does want to be with Tavia. I was a bit surprised by that decision, but after Simon explained more, I found that I could support him in it. He says that he realized that he felt trapped by Tavia not because he lacked feelings for her, but because he felt that marrying her would be giving in to the oppressive demands of his family. He\u2019s been trying to free himself from his parents\u2019 shadow, and so some of his \u201cindiscretions\u201d have been expression of rebellion. But Simon claims that after thinking about it for some time, he realizes that if it is his choice to be with Tavia\u2014if it\u2019s what he really wants\u2014then he doesn\u2019t have to rebel against it.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s more to his decision, of course. After what almost happened to Gretchen, Simon fears for the safety of any \u201cnormal\u201d lovers he might have, which is a legitimate concern. Even were danger not at hand, the strange life we lead would certainly make romance with a normal person rather challenging, I would imagine. The only reason Karen and Natalie have worked so well is because Natalie and Doc have made an effort to bring Karen into our lives.<br /> <br /> So Simon has decided to be with Tavia, and since that seems to be what he really wants, I gave him my blessing. But I still think Tavia has worked to trap him, and I remain unhappy about that. Nevertheless, I decided to make peace with Tavia by telling her about some of my worries and also to give her my blessing on her romance with Simon. We chatted a bit in her studio, and it was, for me anyway, an awkward conversation because I realized about halfway through it that I had come to apologize for things that Tavia knew nothing about, namely my suspicions about her trapping Simon. So I ended up simply giving her my support in her relationship with Simon and apologizing for nothing, really. In the end, the conversation took a more whimsical spin, and somehow I admitted that I could turn into animals using my Primeval Caul, which led to Tavia asking me to turn into a monkey. I refused. I also refused to turn into a panda for her amusement, though I did briefly entertain the idea.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, August 17, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> I was so distracted by my encounters with Simon and Tavia that I didn\u2019t really notice the dismal atmosphere of the rest of the household until almost dinner time. Natalie spent the greater part of the afternoon in the music room playing the piano, and that\u2019s almost always a bad sign. She played beautifully, but there was a helpless, melancholy character to the notes that belied her feelings. I know better than to pry into Natalie\u2019s mind, though. Doc and Karen are far better suited to that.<br /> <br /> Doc seemed upset, angry even. I can only assume that something happened between him and Natalie. Even Sara seemed more reserved than usual, though I have no idea how she might have been involved. At least Alexia and Chandra were as chipper as ever.<br /> <br /> Despite the prevailing atmosphere of discomfort, we enjoyed a nice dinner. Simon and I brought up my encounter with Barry, and then we discussed our plans for tomorrow. We will be visiting the mages\u2019 lodge to have a look about, so I\u2019ll be going in under stealth with Simon or Natalie supporting me with their boneyard. Tavia believes that the outsider is cloaked in human flesh, and that in order to trap it or destroy it, we will have to ruin its mortal body, so Doc has us gathering supplies to make some homemade firebombs. Right now, we\u2019re planning to capture the entity in the Obsidian Box, but we will have to develop a ritual to do so, which is why we are conducting reconnaissance first.<br /> <br /> Tuesday is game night, and it had been some weeks since we had enjoyed a game, so we played Life after dinner. I confess that did not enjoy the game. There was little if any skill involved; it seemed to be pure luck, which made it a bit boring for me. Simon won, with Doc and Natalie close behind. Natalie tried to make light of things during the game, but I could sense that there was indeed an emotional wall between her and Doc.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>The Reborn</u><br /> <br /> I learned quite a bit about the Reborn from Barry. They are created through an ancient ritual. Shortly after they die, they are reincarnated into a new body. The reincarnation cycle of the Reborn seems different from that of most \u201cnormal\u201d people in two ways:<br /> <br /> -First, karma doesn\u2019t seem to have any impact on it. I believe the ritual used to create a Reborn freezes the karmic cycle for that individual. They can no longer improve their karma, and thus they become trapped, living one incarnation after the other with no hope of transcending the karmic cycle.<br /> <br /> -Second, they recover all of their memories (recalling who and what they were in previous lives) upon reaching puberty. This must be the trade-off for trapping themselves in the karmic cycle, though if you ask me, it\u2019s not worth it.<br /> <br /> The Reborn are powerful sorcerers, but their powers are limited. They can improve their powers by drawing upon ley lines and other places of power. Dark Haven Bluffs is the sort of nexus they can use, but Barry and Maria are far too frightened of \u201cghost walkers\u201d to try and take it from us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Not the Same</u><br /> <br /> The hardest thing about talking to Tavia is that she seems so earnestly taken with me that she makes me feel like I\u2019m betraying her with my suspicions that she\u2019s far more maliciously devious than she seems. She claims that I\u2019m her best friend, and I simply don\u2019t understand why, given that I\u2019m usually so cold to her. I asked her about that during our conversation, and she told me that she and I are very much alike. We\u2019re both rather quiet and distant from others, except when we\u2019re among close friends. We both feel socially awkward, and we have both dedicated our lives to our passions\u2014hers for art, and mine for swimming\u2014at the cost of social isolation.<br /> <br /> But I don\u2019t think I\u2019m anything like Tavia. Yes, those similarities do exist, but we\u2019re very different people. Certainly she understands that, doesn\u2019t she?<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but remain suspicious of Tavia. I wonder if her friendly overtures aren\u2019t simply a ploy to win me over. I wonder if she doesn\u2019t know that I suspect her of being a horribly manipulative person, and this is her way of either alleviating my suspicions or causing me enough guilt that I begin to doubt myself.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d like to think that she really is what she seems most of the time, so for now, that\u2019s how I\u2019ll choose to see her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Chandra</u><br /> <br /> The Tavia is very insistent that I make up with Chandra. We used to be good friends, but since our misunderstanding over Trinh, we barely speak to each other. The root of the problem, really, is that I essentially called Chandra a monster and forbade her from creating more penanggalans. To Chandra, that sounded like I was ashamed of her and I may as well have been forbidding her from having children.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean to sound so harsh and offensive. But I don\u2019t believe she should make more penanggalans. And she is a monster, but so am I, and I wouldn\u2019t wish my life as a sin-eater on anyone. We aren\u2019t mortal anymore, and the world we now occupy is dark and dangerous. I don\u2019t think it\u2019s right to bring others into this world against their will.<br /> <br /> Chandra has made a fine life for herself as a penanggalan, but her circumstances before her transformation very much inform her outlook on it. Others won\u2019t see it the same way.<br /> And when you get down to it, I really don\u2019t think I want to bring any children into this life. How can I subject such innocence to this twisted existence?<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> My psychiatrist, when I had one, told me writing things out sometimes helped perspective. So I am writing things out. Here, alone, in my own townhouse.<br /> <br /> If there is one thing I have learned in the school of hard knocks that is life, it is that I am terrible at relationships. In trying to make it as difficult to screw up as possible, I have still, apparently, managed to screw up and piss people off anyway.<br /> <br /> I can easily blame Karen for this, she sort of pushed, but it is not fair. I\u2019ve made clear that I am open to Doc and Karen exploring their sexualities as we see fit. I\u2019ve even been wingman for Doc. I let him make out with that cat girl (though I was a bit worried about her hurting him) and when Karen took a shine to Sara, I supported that. Granted, it was not me being saintly and unselfish, Sara is cute. It got more complicated when Sara joined the Krewe, but I like Sara as a person and if not getting any play with her is the price to pay for keeping her around as our friend, I am all for it. I genuinely like Sara on a non-physical level as well as physical.<br /> <br /> Doc is upset with me. I can on an academic level understand. He is not taking anything out on me, which is good, but apparently my loophole for my own sanity is not a loophole. It\u2019s a trap.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know what to do about Doc. Fucking him makes me panicky sometimes, enough I need heroin to calm down, and I have had issues ever since, despite my telling him I never, ever want anything but hands on my neck (which he does not want to do, which is fine, I don\u2019t think he should have to) he got something in his head then kept talking about the damn silken strand he wanted to use, even after I reminded him that I did not want anything artificial around my neck. I am scared enough of being with a guy anyway without having a damn artificial object chocking me, why he wants to use an object with a much higher chance of damaging my throat I will never understand. But it really, really, really scares me when guys don\u2019t take a direct \u201cno,\u201d though I avoided putting myself in a situation where he would use it. Already going through difficult issues I\u2019ve not perhaps been as involved since.<br /> <br /> My hands are shaking. Oh God.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not his fault either, of course. I can drag that little bit of why don\u2019t you listen up, or how he charged crazed killers in Africa and put us all at more risk, but I don\u2019t. No one needs a litany of their sins, and as his girlfriend I should be supporting him if he will let me. But I think his not actually hearing what I say but instead what he wants to hear is the biggest problem. Because eventually reality happens. The reality is I don\u2019t want something artificial around my neck when I say I don\u2019t want something artificial around my neck. The reality is when Jasmine says she has it handled she has it handled (thank goodness they are not dating, between that and the Candle Cove thing). The reality is I specified we were part of a relationship and, as I made abundantly clear, we have options. This was clear when I suggested he hook up with that werewolf, he flirted some, I helped, and he did not seem confused.<br /> <br /> But it is not Doc\u2019s fault I suck at relationships. All that sounds like I am blaming him and he has not been evil. If he was truly callus with me I\u2019d dump him in a heartbeat. He is trying his best, and sometimes his best is making me more crazy. Like now, definitely now. I don\u2019t wanna crucify him here. He is a good person, if apparently also bad at relationships. Rough combination.<br /> <br /> Karen wants to get married. She knows I want, on some level, to marry her. She does not understand how afraid I get when she pushes it. She does not realize how it makes me want to run away, but she is in my house. With the wedding between Chandra and Alexia, who I am happy for, she has been more jittery than before. I am glad the wedding stuff will be done next month and back to normal, though I wish them the best, of course.<br /> <br /> She also does not seem to realize why I don\u2019t want her as an employee. That\u2019s not a good thing in a relationship. One should not have real world hire fire power over someone they are involved with. That is one sided and seriously bad news.<br /> <br /> TRAPPED<br /> <br /> So what should I do now?<br /> <br /> Doc is upset and cannot be easily approached. He is not yelling, he is not violent, but he is in his cave. If we are going to talk, he needs to listen and not fill the gaps with what he wants to hear. If that means he is going to dump my ass he should dump my ass. I don\u2019t honestly think I am the best woman for him anyway. But if I am not stopping him from meeting whoever Mrs. Right is, I am fine with making him happy, if I am making him happy and not making him miserable. I don\u2019t honestly think right now breaking up with him would make him feel any better. But this stuff worries me. Did he expect I would try and get him laid and Karen laid and not take an interest in any other women? This fight is nothing compared to if he had tried to use his silken strand on me, though. Man I forget him much that scared and angered me till I wrote about it. It makes me shake.<br /> <br /> Karen I can talk to, but she may turn on the water works. I really don\u2019t want that. And she is so goddamn fucked. I am her world.<br /> <br /> I feel trapped. Both Doc and Karen are making me feel trapped. I thought I had options. This is really upsetting. I thought I had set up a situation where we could do as we liked but had each other to rely on. I don\u2019t feel that way now. Karen\u2019s wedding stuff was already fucking with me. I don\u2019t need this right now.<br /> <br /> Maybe I should end my relationships. That might be best for Doc. Maybe he can find someone less damaged than me. Fuck if I know what to do about Karen though. She left her parents behind to be with me, and does not have a home or a job. If I break things off with Doc but not her, I am pretty sure Jasmine at least will hate her. Doc might hate her. No idea about Simon or Alexia. Sera should be alright if this does not get out.<br /> <br /> Goddamnit, This isn\u2019t want I wanted. I wanted to try to have a relationship with two people who really seem to care. I tried to carefully set it up where I would not be trapped. Fuck if it worked. I\u2019m more scared of Doc than I was when this started, and now I feel rotten for wanting what I have tried to help my lovers get. I am clearly terrible with relationships. Why did I even do this? I don\u2019t even care about sleeping with Sara now, I just feel trapped.<br /> <br /> I can barely type. If it were not for spell-check this would be unreadable. My hands are shacking. I feel like I can\u2019t breathe.<br /> <br /> Maybe I need to get away, to escape. I\u2019ve thought about just vanishing for California, and never getting into a relationship again. Would totally fuck over poor Karen and possibly break her mentally. She is kinda dependant mentally at this point I think. And Sara would never forgive herself. Doc might never forgiven himself. And\u2026my daughter. My Natalie.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t go. Karen relies on me now, and in a way I rely on her. Maybe I sort of have these past three years. She would be jobless and rapidly homeless if I left her. And I die a little inside when I think about leaving her. DAMNIT WHY DID I LET HER IN? I can\u2019t leave where my daughter has found me. I love her. I can\u2019t, I won\u2019t, abandon her again.<br /> <br /> But this is crushing my brain. I feel trapped. I don\u2019t know what to do. I need heroin. Yes, I need to stop thinking for awhile. Heroin then bed.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know why everything has to nber all fucked anyway whybn I I don\u2019t wannn hurt nobody I kont lcar whi\\\\<br /> <br /> Dosnt<br /> <br /> Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu uuuuuuuuuuujnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn nnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnnn89n<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXVII<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Drama Drama Drama Drama Drama<br /> <br /> OK, not much needs commenting on. As noted Barry and Maria are Reborn, as per WoD: Immortal. The term Ghost Walkers was my invention, supposedly a medieval name for Sin-Eaters (given they keep adding and subtracting from their nomenclature) and their willingness to escalate a situation was reiterated. This and the name \u201cghost walkers\u201d was popular at the table.<br /> <br /> Also, Tavia and Jasmine arguing about Monkeys vs. Pandas was random and hilarious. Jasmine\u2019s ambient suspiciousness of Tavia and Tavia\u2019s apparent innocence is an interesting dynamic. How much of a schemer is she?<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:02:58-08:00","id":17008,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to revisit the Middle Shadows. This time they set aside some of their drama to deal with the Qlippoth, and it is\u2026not a happy thing.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1320 Hours, Wednesday, August 18, 2010<br /> <br /> Today has been different. Not good different but not exactly bad either. Yes that\u2019s confusing but that\u2019s kinda how I feel right now.<br /> <br /> I went out to do Tai Chi with Rose again this morning. Being active, even if it was a slow active, was apparently good for me. I found myself centered in about a half hour. Rose was still going so I went in and took a shower. I came down to what was a pretty light breakfast. Sliced fruit, toast, and some of Cupcake\u2019s homemade jam. Not a bad start to the day.<br /> <br /> I got to work without any issues and it was a normal Wednesday. Normal is almost new right now. Bright Eyes didn\u2019t ask about coming with me today and I didn\u2019t think about having Leslie come. I lost myself in work and drawing until my stomach started howling. When I looked up, it was already after 1300 Hours. I\u2019m not surprised, but it looks like no lunch with Nightshade today. Just as well. I think I still need some time to get my head around how I want things to be before I try to express anything.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still hurt but I\u2019m not as angry anymore. I think I\u2019ve worked through the confusion now too, which helps with the anger. It\u2019s weird but I almost wonder if that\u2019s why Ronin was so much better with using the Rage Manifestation. Even when she was happy, she still had all her anger just beneath the surface, sometimes not so beneath, whenever she needed it. I think I need to get better at bottling up my anger like that until I need it. Make my body stronger and strengthen my control. Reading over this, I\u2019m writing it like it\u2019s just that simple. The truth is I\u2019m no Incredible Hulk. But looking at it from the same standpoint might actually help me. Granted none of this may make any difference if things go poorly tonight.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s a whole different can of worms. I\u2019m still reeling from the decision to make the Napalm.<br /> <i><b><br /> Who the hell uses Napalm on a Recon mission?!?</b></i><br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1850 Hours, Wednesday, August 18, 2010<br /> <br /> I came home to find all my requested components for Napalm waiting. Cupcake had picked several baskets of vegetables from the garden, which reminded me that I had been neglecting the Death Garden. She was using some of her bounty in dinner, while I mixed everything together away from the House just in case. Once I was satisfied everything was as stable as I could make it, I cleaned and sealed the containers, then packed them in a box with more of the peanuts.<br /> <br /> As we ate, the plan was laid out and agreed upon. Snowflake and/or Nightshade would Boneyard to keep surveillance at all times. Rose would go in invisibly with the Napalm. The rest of the Krewe would be nearby outside with ear curls, ready to come in as backup. I really hate this plan, but I don\u2019t have a better one to suggest. We don\u2019t have experience as a Krewe dealing with live situations like this enough for me to be comfortable sending in one person. But Rose is the only one that can move invisibly. We need this to go very smoothly or it has the possibility of going very badly. Yes I always say things like that, but this is Outsiders. With Napalm.<br /> <br /> Anyway, they are ready to leave so I\u2019m out for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> We all made it back, but I\u2019m not sure we\u2019re all the same as we were when we left.<br /> <br /> We got into Glenwood about 2000 Hours with Cupcake driving Snowflake\u2019s car and Bright Eyes driving her own. Rose rode with Cupcake and Snowflake which left Nightshade and I with Bright Eyes. It probably would have been more awkward if we weren\u2019t so anxious about other things. The body was still in the window at the pawn shop as we drove by. I imagined the same kid in there being despondent at whoever might be shopping. Deeper into Glenwood, we parked on Main Street. We weren\u2019t hiding very well given no one else was around, but I had to hope no one was expecting us. Rose got out and vanished as Snowflake dropped into his Boneyard. Cupcake and Bright Eyes stayed behind the wheel and make sure the cars were ready for a quick escape.<br /> <br /> Since Rose was actually inside, she didn\u2019t speak very much. This left all the intel up to Snowflake. He immediately noticed it was unusually dark and there was no furniture or well anything. It was barren. The first signs of light was from an old oil lantern in a room toward the back of the building. There was someone slumped onto the table, staring at the flickering light. When Rose got to the entrance, she whispered that the man was dead from all his organs vanishing. She also noted that it took longer to move through the hallway than she thought was normal. There was another room off from that one and it had signs of life. Snowflake told us there was a woman, naked and dirty from not cleaning herself for possibly a few months, singing to the doll she cradled like she was trying to rock it to sleep. The doll was wrapped in rotting human skin and she was singing You and Me and the Devil make three. Nothing unusual here. He also noted there were three other dolls in a crib nearby. They were all wrapped in skin as well. There were two more rooms opening off of this one. One was pitch black and even Snowflake couldn\u2019t see into it. The other had another lamp. There was a single table with a flower on it and what looked like an old-style trap door into the cellar. Snowflake told us the whole place had this oppressive silence to it that was just not right. He looked upstairs and found a hole in the ceiling which let in the moonlight. There was blood everywhere, still no signs of any inhabitants, but the shadows were more natural. That was also when he realized there were windows on this floor, but not on the first. That was weird because we could see them from the street. It also seemed bigger downstairs than the structure should be. Being bigger on the inside might explain while Rose felt disoriented in the hallway. Since I didn\u2019t see any blue phone boxes, I was pretty sure nothing good was going to come from that. When Snowflake tried to look back downstairs, he found an empty house, one that looked like the one we saw on the outside. He had to pull his perceptions back out and go through the first floor to find this strange extradimensional space. Once we had a better idea of where everyone was, Rose decided to open the cellar door. Given the reaction Snowflake had, there must have been a horrible stench. Snowflake said there was the buzzing like in the other building and it was also pitch black. It apparently smelled if feces and \u201cother\u201d things they couldn\u2019t immediately identify. I had a few ideas, but given how sick Nightshade looked just from hearing about it, I decided to keep those thoughts to myself. Rose asked for a distraction to help her get out with less cost to herself. This didn\u2019t go as well as we\u2019d hoped. The illusion didn\u2019t fool Louisa as she called out for Stephen. The description I got was that a very well dressed human shaped man emerged from the blackened room. There was black light shining from his eyes. He opened his mouth, which also shone with the same black light, and some terrible sound happened. We couldn\u2019t hear it from outside or over the ear curls. But from Snowflake and Rose\u2019s descriptions later, it was not only not human, but not of this earth. Louisa seemed to understand and so did the dolls, as they were all moving by themselves. She said something about a Beverly and thought maybe she was jealous of Louisa for having more children. Then she said they might need to kill her. That was about the time Rose decided learning as much as we could and getting the hell out was the only option remaining. She threw Napalm on each of the figures in hopes of finding what we needed. Stephen seemed to burn away, leaving a shadow creature which glowed with that odd black light. Louisa started to burn from the chemical reaction as well, but she did something to regenerate. Rose said later she may have cast a spell or whatever mages actually do as the wounds just started to repair themselves even as she kept burning. Neither really reacted to the pain or damage to their bodies like people. Even ghosts usually react to pain. But when Stephen did finally react, it was in a big way. Just like when he spoke before, no one outside could hear. Snowflake was effectively inside however, so when Stephen screamed his ears immediately started bleeding. He jerked in pain that I could see from our car and I took a second before he could respond. I was getting ready to get out when the rear passenger door to Snowflakes car opened and Rose declared she was in. Just as both cars took off, Nightshade got a text. Karen noted that something had just happened to Tavia. She was hit with some kind of migraine and thought Snowflake was in danger. She then flipped out somehow. We sent word back that something had happened but everyone was mostly okay. It seemed like a good lie to me. After that, the news was that she was going to lay down.<br /> <br /> Cupcake took the long, confusing way back home just in case anyone was following us. Bright Eyes was following her anyway, so that made it as safe as it could be. I think we were all happier to see the House and the safety it provided than ever before. I asked Snowflake if he needed me to check out Tavia. He said he wanted to see her first. I let him go and went to get my bag just in case. When he came back down, Snowflake was definitely freaked out, but he was calm. We went back up together and I checked her as thoroughly as I could. The weird thing was that she was in much better shape than the last time I checked on her. She was definitely pregnant, as if I was not certain already. I told her that her vitals were improved but I couldn\u2019t explain it. She said that was a discussion for another time. She didn\u2019t react when I hinted at her being pregnant. No matter what, when I mentioned that I didn\u2019t see anything that would explain what happened, she noted that she and Snowflake were spiritually linked. Snowflake silently let me know he had no idea what she was talking about, but Tavia seemed very happy about everything. With that I left them to whatever it was they were going to do from there.<br /> <br /> I came back to my room and put my bag away while I heard the showers going for both Nightshade and Rose. I\u2019ve just been writing this since then. I think I\u2019ll head back down in a bit to make sure everyone else is doing okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0215 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> I found myself standing outside the Music Room listening to Nightshade play piano and sing Andrews Sisters. Most everyone else was there enjoying the music. I knew what I was hearing was Nightshade sobbing on the inside. I couldn\u2019t find any fault in that. We had experienced things, even if it was second hand, that no one should have to deal with. That it\u2019s our mystic duty doesn\u2019t make it any more bearable. I just couldn\u2019t bring myself to go in and be social yet. I felt out of place. Then Rose saw me and slipped out to talk. I braced myself but at first she only asked if she could help with any research I might do. I wasn\u2019t really thinking about it yet, but she reminded me that, in the absence of Snowflake, I was the one that should be looking into things. I told her I\u2019d let her know when I was ready. Then she paused and stood next to me as I stared into the Music Room. I could feel the question in the air before she managed to ask. Her polite but direct way of asking if Nightshade and I were okay was less painful than I expected. When I said no, she started to probe a little more, but I stopped her before she hit a nerve. She seemed to understand and said she\u2019d be around. Bright Eyes came out a few minutes after and didn\u2019t ask anything this time, just offered to help research. I took that as a hint.<br /> <br /> We moved to find Rose, but when I found her, she was sitting on the Bluffs with Karl. I couldn\u2019t make Karl whole and I couldn\u2019t explain the answers to Rose she wanted, so figured it be better to just let them have their moment together. About the time we started to the Library, Gretchen came by asking about celebrity asses. All I could gather was something about a website and she wanted us to see. I might not have been as polite in telling her how not helpful that was as I should have been, but she agreed to help us research anyway. With the two ladies helping, I started off by looking into what the hell Stephen was. It took us about 10 minutes to find out. Pretty damn efficient, if you ask me. Apparently Stephen is something called an Urperson. That\u2019s the result of when a person is taken apart and put back together, either as punishment or as a way for said person to deal with very bad things. They then act on memories of the world and their life, but they don\u2019t actually have much chance of properly interacting with the world anymore. From all the intel from Snowflake and Rose, my best guess is that we could use some piece of Louisa as a link to Stephen, or at least whatever is left of him. The Qlipoth is actually inside Stephen the Urperson. I suspect that Stephen will have regenerated or rebuilt himself by the time we get back to Glenwood so all this is good to know. Next we moved on to finding a binding ritual (or at least where to start to build one) to use for the Onyx Prison. After an hour without much in the way of progress, I decided we needed Snowflake\u2019s expertise. Bright Eyes went off with Gretchen to look at ass while I searched for Snowflake. I didn\u2019t find him up and about so I decided to let it go for tonight. There were other things on my mind anyway.<br /> <br /> After going back to my room, I considered something about myself. I have a tendency to assume others can\u2019t handle things. I don\u2019t mean discrimination exactly, but both medical and military service has reinforced the idea that normal people...can\u2019t handle the truth. We are taught by some of the older instructors that our service to our country is not just to fight and die, but to save the civilians from the horrors of war. It is our sacrifice that allows others to know peace. Given the pain, loss, and nightmares many of us endure, I know this to be true. I feel the same sense of service is due to the mortals. My sacrifice as a Gatekeeper allows them to remain ignorant of the horrors left by the Darkness and the Others. My problem has been that I have tried to protect my Krewe from those horrors as well. With the exception of Ronin, none of them knew what it was like to experience war. At least not until the Ivory Coast. I was angry when that was ripped from them. And now with the Glenwood lodge, more innocence and peace has been stolen from all of us. My bizarre sense of responsibility says that that shouldn\u2019t have happened. That is why I don\u2019t like Rose going in places alone as well. But tonight forced me to accept something.<br /> <br /> This is their duty as well.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t keep jeopardizing our missions because I\u2019m afraid something will scar or kill my Krewe. We are a unit. We all share the same burden to sacrifice ourselves. It can\u2019t just be me anymore. We each have our own specialties. When they are useful, I have to learn...no, I already know, I have to accept, that they are needed and get out of the way. I\u2019m still not going to let us walk blindly into situations, but I will stop being overprotective while in the field. Now I\u2019m going to bed.<br /> <br /> Oh and apparently The Middle Shadows of Dark Haven Bluffs are who the hell uses Napalm for a Recon mission.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> It was much harder to center today. I felt like I should be alone, so I let Rose do her Tai Chi while I meditated inside. My decision last night must have really been hard to get around as it took about an hour before I found peace.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast, Tavia informed us that the Qlipoth can be used as a gate since it is a link to the Abyssal Realm. The \u201cbad\u201d news was that someone else could try to use the gate to bring something through for protection. If you want to call it good news, we can apparently destroy the gate. After that fabulous news, I went to work.<br /> <br /> Thankfully today has gone fairly smoothly. I\u2019ve just been drawing during the downtime. I\u2019m starting to get better with some of the more tribal images and my shading on more detailed work is almost what I\u2019d call good. I don\u2019t expect I\u2019ll see Nightshade for lunch again, so I guess I better start thinking about what to eat. Delivery or nuke something in the back. Do I even have a phone book here? Oh wait, I have the laptop. One day I will fully embrace the Information Age.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 18, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I chose to meditate with tai chi again this morning; it was very refreshing, and I\u2019ve been nicely centered all day. Sadly Doc did not join me this morning.<br /> <br /> Karl is continuing to recover thanks to Doc\u2019s skilled healing. He is still not back to full strength, but he is getting there.<br /> <br /> Training with Jean went well this morning. Afterward, Sara and I went to get the packing peanuts for Doc\u2019s firebombs, while Simon got some gasoline. Then Sara and I joined Alexia outside for some gardening. The weather is still quite hot, but it won\u2019t be long before it cools off, so I suppose we should try to enjoy it while it lasts.<br /> <br /> Alexia is making spaghetti with tomatoes fresh from the garden, and Doc is making our firebombs. After dinner, we are going to investigate the lodge. I hope all goes well.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, August 18, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We have investigated the mages\u2019 lodge, and taken a step toward ending the taint in Glenwood, but it seems we still have a long way to go.<br /> <br /> We arrived around 8:00. Simon remained in the car with the others and sank into a Boneyard trance to support me. Armed with a satchel of three firebombs, I cloaked myself in the Cold-Wind and absolute Stillness so that I could pass unseen in the lodge, and moved to the rear of the building so that I could enter through the back door.<br /> <br /> I phased through the doorway and found myself in a long, almost empty room. As I moved through it, it seemed to lengthen, so that it took me a great deal longer to reach the door on the opposite end than it should have. I knew it was either a magical enchantment laid by the mages or the effects of the outsider\u2019s taint, and tried to adapt to the distortions of my surroundings as I searched the building.<br /> <br /> There was little in the back room aside from a flickering oil lantern resting on a table along one wall. A dead body slumped in a chair at the table. I could sense that he died when his organs simply vanished, and chose not to look too closely at the corpse. It had obviously been there for awhile, and would tell me little.<br /> <br /> There were no windows, even though there should have been, judging from the appearance of the place from outside. Simon found this curious, and as he maneuvered his consciousness through the building, he found that it was not the same on the inside as it was on the outside. It was larger inside, and the rooms were different. By withdrawing his consciousness and entering again through the upstairs, he found that he could roam through the building as it really was, not the extra-dimensional chambers I was exploring. The \u201creal\u201d building was apparently quite empty. I confess that I felt a bit disconcerted by the strangeness of it.<br /> <br /> I passed through the inner doorway into a central chamber, and the sight that greeted me there was terribly disturbing. A nude woman smeared with her own blood and filth cradled a doll wrapped in human skin, singing quietly to it as though it were a real child. Similar dolls lay scattered around the room in makeshift cribs, and the cluttered place was lit only by a single oil lamp glowing near the woman\u2019s feet. The stench was unbearable, a mixture of offal and charnel decay. When the woman began muttering about the babies she had with her boyfriend, I realized that she must be Louisa, the one who had summoned Stephen back from the Abyss and caused the trouble in Glenwood to start with.<br /> <br /> Two rooms opened from the central chamber. According to Simon, one was filled with inky, impenetrable blackness, and I avoided it. Instead, I passed through the wall into the other, which was lit by yet another lantern and held a trap door into a cellar area. I opened it and instantly regretted doing so, for the stench that rose from it nearly made me retch. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever smelled something so awful. There was also the sickeningly familiar buzzing of thousands of flies. I quickly closed the trap door and retreated from the room.<br /> <br /> However, moving through so many walls and doors was rapidly draining my plasm, so I asked Simon to create a distraction so that I could open the door to get out without being seen by Louisa. He created an illusion of the man covered in flies to draw her attention. Louisa did not seem impressed by the illusion, and called out for her \u201cboyfriend\u201d Stephen. A being clad in fine clothes emerged from the pitch dark room. He seemed remotely human, but blackness poured from his eyes and mouth. He screamed with the squeal of tearing metal. It was the Qliphoth.<br /> <br /> We had come to destroy its physical shell so that it could be defeated, so I threw two of the firebombs at it and another at Louisa\u2014she was so far gone that I felt death would be a mercy, whether she agreed or not. But she used some sort of magic to heal herself even as she burned, and I think she probably survived. The Qliphoth\u2019s body did not, and as it\u2019s stolen flesh burned away, leaving the darkness within exposed and vulnerable, it shrieked with an unearthly sound that tore at my soul and left my ears bleeding. Simon suffered the same, and withdrew his consciousness as quickly as he could.<br /> <br /> I retreated quickly, phasing through the wall. I was relieved to find myself outside in the real world and not in some sort of extra-dimensional limbo. I quickly rejoined the others at the car and filled them in on what had happened. Then we returned home. I was eager to shower away the taint and filth of that place, and it took a long while before I really felt clean. Natalie seemed more upset by it than I was even though she was nowhere near the place, but I think she is fine now.<br /> <br /> Tavia was incapacitated by a severe migraine, which started at the same moment that Simon and I heard the Qliphoth\u2019s screams. I have no idea what that means, but there is obviously some sort of mystical connection between them. Simon is attending to her.<br /> <br /> Natalie spent the evening playing piano again. I realize that doing so is therapeutic for her, so I hope she continues if it helps her heal. But it always makes me uncomfortable because I simply do not know how to deal with Natalie or her issues. It\u2019s probably best if I simply avoid her, since I doubt I can do anything to help anyway.<br /> <br /> I was surprised, however, to find Doc standing outside the music room, listening but keeping his distance. I asked if things were all right between him and Natalie, and he said no, they were not. He did not want to talk about it though. I didn\u2019t know what to do, or even if I could do anything, so I changed the subject and asked if he wanted my help researching the things we encountered tonight. He told me he would find me if decided to do any research later.<br /> <br /> So I went to unwind and try to forget about the evening by spending some time with Karl. He\u2019s strong yet gentle, and his presence is comforting and protective, but not stifling. We went out to the gazebo and sat there, enjoying the night air and each other\u2019s company. It was quite late when I went to bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, August 19, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> Doc and Gretchen did some research last night. Doc didn\u2019t fetch me to help. He must not have wanted to bother Karl and me, which was sweet of him. Of course, they didn\u2019t really need my help, and managed to learn quite a few things about the things in Glenwood, which we discussed after breakfast.<br /> <br /> They believe that the Qliphoth is going to behave according to a warped version of what it remembers about humanity. The bad news is that its presence acts as a gate, allowing other things to come through from the Abyss. There is some other creature there at the lodge, in the cellar. It must be the monster Alexia saw when she communed with the mannequins in the mall, and it probably came through the Qliphoth gate.<br /> <br /> We must destroy or seal the Qliphoth to close the opening between this world and the Abyss. That is our priority. And once that it done, we will have to find out more about the other thing and destroy it as well. Also, Louisa may try to draw other outsiders through the Qliphoth to help defend herself and her \u201cboyfriend,\u201d so we will need to deal with her as well. That likely means killing her, but she is beyond help, and her death would merciful.<br /> <br /> Simon, Tavia, and Sara are spending the day developing a ritual to bind and seal the Qliphoth in the Obsidian Box. I hope they work quickly, because I think we need to end this as soon as possible, before Louisa does more damage.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Hopeless Duty</u><br /> <br /> I will be glad to resolve the Abyssal threat in Glenwood so that we can return to our true calling, helping ghosts.<br /> <br /> No, that\u2019s not true. Dealing with outsider threats is an important part of our krewe\u2019s true calling. It is one of our core mandates, in fact. It\u2019s just not something that brings me a great deal of fulfillment. When we help a ghost resolve her anchors so that she can pass on peacefully, I feel like I have accomplished something. I feel a bit more complete. I do not feel the same way when we deal with Abyssal creatures. There is not the same sense of pleasant fulfillment, the same feeling of having truly helped someone, even though we are keeping many people safe by eliminating outsider threats. It just feels like we\u2019ve completed a dirty job, and I just want to forget about it as soon as it\u2019s over. But I can\u2019t because I know that it\u2019s only a matter of time before another horrid thing emerges. Victory over the outsiders does not bring the same sense of hope that helping ghosts does.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s day two, and time to move on. I want to be there for Doc regardless of what our relationship is, but that will have to happen when he wants to talk.<br /> <br /> Doc left me alone today and kept his distance. I have, I think, mostly pulled together. I say mostly as going to Glenwood has seriously fucked with my equilibrium. It is filthy<br /> <br /> Filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy filthy<br /> <br /> I was not Spooky or Simon and did not have to deal directly with the dirty, filthy rooms, but hearing about it was enough. I cannot even imagine how filthy those rooms are. How many showers did Spooky need I wonder. As bad as those places apparently smelled there must have been filth in the air, on the ground so filthy and gross. The filth sticks to you skin. I can\u2019t stand filthy, I don\u2019t like filthy I have to be clean.<br /> <br /> Filthy<br /> <br /> I still felt gross so had to take a very long shower but I spent some time after with the Andrews Sisters and felt better.<br /> <br /> Karen has been close at hand, not talking much but trying to be there for me. What the hell would I do without her? I am seriously wondering what the points of those walls between us I keep building are. Is it helping anyone?<br /> <br /> Perhaps I, a comet passing through space, need to accept that when I flew so close to planet Karen, when I surrounded myself in her atmosphere, I really was drawn into her gravity. Sure, Natalie comet could tell itself it could fly back into cold iciness of space, that the reason it kept it\u2019s route deeper into the atmosphere was it was warm and pleasant. It was. Maybe Natalie comet needs to acknowledge that now, in the gravitational pull, it can no longer leave, and soon will collide with planet Karen and no longer be two separate things. Perhaps it will see the beautiful, majestic mountains and peaceful, inviting valleys and realize after traveling through space\u2019s icy darkness it has finally found a place to finish its trip? That it can never return? Am I there? I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> And right now, when she could be anywhere, she is across the room, playing with her phone, pretending she is busy, waiting to see if I need her help.<br /> <br /> Fuck pretending I don\u2019t. Fuck it forever. I am going to go talk to her right now.<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXVIII<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Well, that was both fun and exciting.<br /> <br /> I spared few details with the corrupted room, and may have given a couple players heebie-jeebies a bit. The pervasive disgusting nature of it was stressed, the inescapable dirtiness, like mold you just can\u2019t seem to completely scrape away. It seemed effective.<br /> <br /> And drunk Gretchen talked about asses. That was funny.<br /> <br /> Anyway, most of the session was spent on the mission, so not much more to add. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:04:25-08:00","id":17010,"title":"","content":"Unusual case today, two Journals, and only one directly covers game events. Jasmine\u2019s player was under the weather, so we came up with what Jasmine would be doing separately. So look to Doc to recap the session Jasmine to cover what she was up to.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXIX<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1830 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> When I got back to the Bluffs, Snowflake, Cupcake, and Bright Eyes were off on a shopping trip. I was told they were looking for a night vision camera and a beekeeper's suit. I laughed til Tavia looked confused at me. So I asked how that would help us kill the Qlipoth. Apparently I was mistaken before as Tavia\u2019s eyes went wide. She explained that it was the thing in the cellar, a Gulmoth, that we could kill without leaving the horrible taint on the world. So the Qlipoth will go into the Onyx Prison. Nightshade let me know that they intended to paint the Qlipoth into a picture to bind it. I knew this was on the list of really bad ideas, but I asked if Rose knew yet. Surprisingly, she knew but wasn\u2019t home right now. At first I thought maybe she had car trouble and asked if we needed to go get her. Nightshade said she was in Taiwan investigating a teenage vampire sighting. I forgot that Nightshade knew how to open a Sepulchral Gateway too. Anyway, Rose is looking into the sighting. Jiang Shi I think she calls vampires. But I figure it\u2019s probably related to her uncle. Before much else could happen, Chandra started getting images of beekeepers\u2019 outfits on her phone. That was hilarious.<br /> <br /> Talk then turned to Leslie as I was going to ask to her about getting started in the shop. Nightshade and Karen apparently got her tickets to a concert to keep her out of the way so the Krewe could talk about the Gulmoth. Now we\u2019re just waiting for the others to get back. I didn\u2019t ask how Rose was getting home. Hope they figured that out before she left.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1945 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Snowflake and Bright Eyes came in wearing the beekeeper suits, but they were trying to sneak. They failed. When I asked why the hell we were going to go look at this thing, Snowflake explained that it was easier and quicker to bind the Outsider if Tavia could already have it painted. This way, we could give her a reference image and she could make the portrait before we went to the lodge. Then she could very quickly bind it once we were there. I was of course concerned about going back into the lodge, but Snowflake pointed out that this was more Recon. Tavia being at the lodge seemed like a really bad idea, but not really any worse than the rest of us being there. Snowflake was very proud of the new video camera though. He went through all the options it had that would help us and concluded it was completely anti-Blair Witch. I wasn\u2019t sure if he meant that as a joke or not, but the humor and irony of the statement hit me pretty hard. I managed not to laugh. Cupcake pointed out from the kitchen that Paranormal Activity was a better film. It\u2019s surreal moments like that that I never see coming.<br /> <br /> Snowflake, Karen, and I all cast Luck Magic while the others were getting ready. Snowflake and Tavia have some special resistance to going crazy from seeing horrors from beyond, so he made sure his ability to be sneaky was boosted. Not having that \u201cbenefit\u201d of the blood, Karen and I made sure that Nightshade and myself respectively were better able to handle mind-shattering horrors. But now we\u2019re loading up. Cupcake is driving Bright Eye\u2019s car with Snowflake riding shotgun. Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and I were in the back. I will be keeping my shotgun hidden in the back with us. I remember thinking earlier when Snowflake called this Recon, that we had moved from Recon to DefCon. I hope I\u2019m just paranoid.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2330 Hours, Thursday, August 19, 2010<br /> <br /> That worked better than I expected. And we all made it back as sane as were when we left.<br /> <br /> It was a dark and stormy night in Glenwood. Cupcake make sure we could bolt at a moment\u2019s notice. Bright Eyes and I flanked Nightshade as she used Boneyard to cover Snowflake\u2019s entrance. I didn\u2019t realize that she could make it easier to sneak around with her Stillness Boneyard. It never really comes up with Rose going in invisibly. The other beekeeper\u2019s suit was in the back as Bright Eyes and I were first responders if anything went wrong. Nightshade put Louisa to sleep as she was knitting. She couldn\u2019t find the Qlipoth so Snowflake would have to take his chances sneaking. He managed to get past the horrible babies and into the cellar without any problems. Using the camera to see, he managed to get to and film the Outsider but couldn\u2019t look at it and keep the image in his mind. With the main goal accomplished, he slipped back out again. It doesn\u2019t take long to write, but Snowflake had to move slowly and carefully. When he made it back to the car, I checked the camera to make sure he got what we needed, so we could go back if we needed. I will not be drawing this, but the Gulmoth had a big, pasty body. A human face with a fly\u2019s mouth lolled on top of the blob of torso and a huge pair of fly\u2019s wings spread from the back. The whole thing was covered in disgusting hair covered in eggs filled with some kind of slimy goo. That was all terrible enough but Snowflake zoomed at one point and I noticed the translucent eggs had what looked like human embryos floating in them. I\u2019m sure I\u2019m going to regret being able to keep that image in my mind without going insane. No, scratch that. I already do.<br /> <br /> Before Snowflake could get back in the car, we had to find a way to get all the flies off him. The beekeeper\u2019s suit worked but even the rain didn\u2019t force the buzzing cloud away. Nightshade called on her own magic and really made the sky open up. The storm winds and rain was enough to finally let Snowflake take off the suit without being swarmed. It didn\u2019t do anything to keep the rain out though, so he was soaking wet all the way back to Dark Haven Bluffs. We made it back around 2300 Hours and Cupcake immediately produced waffles and ice cream from the kitchen. Snowflake put his suit in a tray of bleach before joining us. He declared that all the recording he had to do covered TV Night and no one argued.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0250 Hours, Friday, August 20, 2010<br /> <br /> After everyone was cleaned up and dried off, Nightshade and Karen headed off to the townhouse together. I tried not to let that bother me, but it didn\u2019t work. Instead I went to the Exercise Room and worked out for a while. No one had heard anything from Rose yet either.<br /> <br /> After maybe an hour, Snowflake came and offered to share the Plasm in the House with me. I took him up on it, but he was only in so much of a mood to talk and I can\u2019t expect him to suffer through all the doubts and insecurities in my head. So around 0100 Hours, I got ready to go on patrol. I didn\u2019t think I was a danger to anyone but I had to do something besides stare at the walls. I met Leslie on the way out. She was just coming back from her concert. I asked about coming to the shop while I had the chance. She glanced at her watch and I realized she was about to crash for the night. I told to stop by after lunch and she seemed much less panicked.<br /> <br /> From there, I walked the streets of New Haven as much for solitude as anything. Granted that might make me more of a concern, but right now it doesn\u2019t matter. I came back in a little earlier than usual so I could recover from the stress of the lodge. Now I\u2019m going to sleep.<br /> <br /> Oh...I hope someone thought to go get Rose.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, August 19, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> At least once a week, I spend a little time scanning through online Taiwanese newspapers, just to keep up with what\u2019s going on at home. This afternoon, I encountered an article about some teenagers who claim they were attacked by some sort of ghoul or vampire. They described what seemed to be a jiang shi. The newspaper treated it like a hoax, but I\u2019m convinced that they really did see a jiang shi, and that it was my Uncle Guang.<br /> <br /> I need to get to Taiwan to investigate this. Doc\u2019s away at work right now. But Natalie is here, and I think she knows the Sepulchral Gateway ceremony. I believe I can get to Taiwan, spend a few hours looking around, and then get back in case I\u2019m needed in Glenwood.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve arrived in Taipei. It\u2019s the middle of night, almost opposite the time on east coast America.<br /> <br /> Natalie was quite willing to help me get here, and kindly provided the Sepulchral Gateway for me. I still have a quite a few Taiwanese dollars, so money won\u2019t be a problem for the short time I plan to be here.<br /> <br /> Natalie and I had a important chat before I left, though. We discussed her relationship with Doc. I can tell something has happened to put a wall between them, and Natalie seemed open to talking about it. She didn\u2019t go into detail about what exactly happened, but that\u2019s not important because whatever it was, it only brought to light existing issues. Natalie says that she cares about Doc, but is also frightened of him, or at least his dark moods and the anger that seethes beneath the surface. She also seems upset that she and Doc can\u2019t see certain things the same way. She\u2019s concerned about her friendship with Doc, and wants to preserve it, but doesn\u2019t know what to do at this point.<br /> <br /> I decided to give Natalie my honest opinion on the situation. I told her that I thought she and Doc were the closest of friends, more like a brother and sister than boyfriend and girlfriend. I told her that I didn\u2019t think she and Doc were right together as lovers because Natalie is obviously uncomfortable with the relationship and is much, much more in love with Karen.<br /> <br /> I think Natalie was surprised when I told her that I thought she and Karen belonged together. I pointed out how any time she needed emotional support, she ran to Karen. Whenever we go out to have fun, like on the yacht, she usually does so with Karen. Doc is practically neglected in the relationship, which says a lot about where Natalie\u2019s romantic affections really lie.<br /> <br /> But of course Doc is very important to her. He really is an extraordinarily close and loyal friend, and his friendship is valuable to her. He has been helping her heal in more ways than I can really fathom.<br /> <br /> I was a bit surprised when Natalie agreed with everything I said. She too thinks that she needs to break up with Doc, but she doesn\u2019t want to hurt him. She fears that ending their relationship will be a bad blow to his ego and self-confidence. I don\u2019t know what to do about that, but Natalie didn\u2019t want me saying anything to him about it, so I won\u2019t. I did advise her that Doc seems to be having similar doubts right now, though, so it might be a good time to discuss it with him. Then again, it might be a terrible time. He\u2019s angry right now, and might react poorly. I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> It was nice to talk to Natalie like that, even if the subject was troubling. But after our conversation, we went to the basement and she opened a Sepulchral Gateway for me. I traveled through it and emerged in one of the haunts I tracked down when I was in Taipei a couple months ago, the Buddhist shrine haunted by the ghost of a priest who hanged himself. I also took the time to absorb the shrine\u2019s plasm, since I\u2019m still quite drained after my efforts in Glenwood.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m off to see if I can\u2019t track down Guang.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Very Early Morning<br /> <br /> I spent the dark hours before dawn exploring the area where the jiang shi attacked the teenagers, but I haven\u2019t found anything particularly useful. I was hoping for some clue that might help me track down Guang, but I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be able find anything without talking to people in the area who might have seem something, or whose superstitions might lead me in the right direction. Fortunately, this is not the neighborhood where I grew up, so it is extremely unlikely that I\u2019ll run into anyone I know.<br /> <br /> The others are probably getting ready to go to Glenwood as I write this. I thought about heading back, and then realized that I have no way to get back without Natalie\u2019s help since I don\u2019t know the ceremony to create a Sepulchral Gateway. I don\u2019t know how we both overlooked that when she agreed to send me here. I\u2019ll need to call her and get her to come fetch me. But I suppose I should ask around a bit before I do that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I asked around the neighborhood, and even managed to talk to the teenagers who saw the jiang shi. Their fear was real, and I have no doubt that they saw <i>something</i> strange. They showed me photographs they took with their phones, but they were blurry and indistinct. According to Doc, that\u2019s how vampiric things show up in photos, so I\u2019m now certain that they really did encounter a jiang shi. I still don\u2019t know whether it was Guang or not, but I have a feeling that it was.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, I didn\u2019t find him. What I did do, however, was write several signs like those I\u2019ve placed around the mansion. They read \u201cUncle Guang, I want to speak with you. It\u2019s safe. Please visit,\u201d and I signed them with my name (Xiaomei, not Jasmine). I posted them on telephone poles and bulletin boards in the area. I think Guang probably hasn\u2019t returned to the mansion because he\u2019s frightened to go there, so perhaps the signs will convince him that it\u2019s okay, and that I want very much want to see him.<br /> <br /> I should return to Darkhaven Bluffs. It\u2019s very late at night there, and my absence has either kept the krewe from going to Glenwood, or they\u2019ve gone without me, and I hope it\u2019s not the latter. I suppose it\u2019s time to give Natalie a call. I hope I don\u2019t wake her.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>The Glenwood Plan<br /> </u><br /> There was some discussion of the Glenwood plan. I\u2019m not really happy with it, as it involved sealing away yet more horrid entities in the house, and keeping so many terrible things imprisoned there makes me anxious.<br /> <br /> Simon is right to be worried that any attempts to fight the Qliphoth and Louisa will draw the attention of the Abyssal entity (another gulmoth, we think) that lurks in the lodge cellar. So he wants to seal it away first. He and Tavia came up with a plan. If someone sneaks into the cellar (clad in a sealed bee-keeper\u2019s suit or something to keep the flies away) and takes a picture of the gulmoth with a night vision camera, then Tavia can paint it, and use that to seal it away.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m unhappy with the idea. I would rather destroy the beast. And I certainly don\u2019t want another cursed painting lying around, threatening to unleash horrors every new moon.<br /> <br /> But the rest of the krewe decided that\u2019s what they wanted to do, and if I don\u2019t go along to infiltrate the lodge, Simon is going to do it with Natalie\u2019s boneyard supporting him. I can\u2019t let him endanger himself like that. I\u2019m not sure why Sara wouldn\u2019t be the one going in, though I don\u2019t know how subtle she can be. So I\u2019ll help, even though I disapprove.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> It was fun messing with people with the Qlippoth again. I can\u2019t have that stuff happening too much or I will have too much fun. :P<br /> <br /> I was surprised they went for Tavia\u2019s idea, but the lack of Jasmine to reign them in may have made them bolder. Either way while even with help Simon was no Jasmine, the usage of Stillness Boneyard really helped, if Plasm hungry.<br /> <br /> Not much else to cover. Comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:06:07-08:00","id":17011,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s a quiet evening in a Fishborne house. Jasmine returns, preparations are made to deal with the Qlippoth, and more wedding plans. Here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Friday, August 20, 2010<br /> <br /> I got up still feeling anxious from last night. Everytime I think I\u2019m getting over things, ...nevermind.<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t find Rose in the Meditation Room or out on the Bluffs. I was more than a little worried that she was still in Taiwan, but no one had asked me for help so I had to force myself to assume everything was under control. Unfortunately, this did nothing for helping me center myself. After an hour and half of searching for peace in vain, I gave up and went down for breakfast. Because I meditated so long, I was running behind. Breakfast was almost over when I got downstairs. Only Cupcake, Chandra, and Bright Eyes were at the table however. No one knew anything about Rose as they had all gone to bed as well. Before we could really get too worried, Rose came hurrying down the stairs. She grabbed a piece of toast, waved, and rushed out the door. Obviously I wasn\u2019t the only one running late.<br /> <br /> Before I could head out for work, Bright Eyes asked if she could come again. I was only half joking when I asked if she had another question for me. She took it in good spirits, but assured me she only wanted to help out. Because she drove me, I didn\u2019t have any problems getting in and opening on time. We\u2019ve been here since and she is very helpful to have around. Having someone around to just talk to about normal things is incredibly relaxing. Now let\u2019s see if Leslie remembers to come to the shop.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1730 Hours, Friday, August 20, 2010<br /> <br /> Score one for the teens. Leslie showed up just as Bright Eyes and I were talking about ordering lunch. Once we got our delivery for all three of us, I started showing Leslie around. When she seemed surprised that I didn\u2019t sell pot labelled oregano, I had to make fun of her a little. She took it pretty well. After that, I showed her the ropes. Once it looked like things were in hand, Bright Eyes headed out. I don\u2019t know if she had something else to do or just didn\u2019t want to be around Leslie or what.<br /> <br /> Around 1400 Hours, Snowflake called with some updates. He and Cupcake had talked with Malard about Deirdre coming to the wedding. He said she could come but not for anything other than the wedding and reception. He was also pretty clear that she was okay to show, but not any of the others. I was impressed with that, but then Snowflake reminded me that we should probably check in with Zed to make sure the rest of the pack knew what was going on. We had pieced together that our situation with Erin at the Date with a Ghost party was due to Malard not passing information along. Since we now had direct lines, we wanted to make sure that didn\u2019t happen again. I don\u2019t think Erin crashing Cupcake and Chandra\u2019s wedding will be taken lightly. The call to Zed went very well. He is very accommodating given the situation and was happy to see we were living up to our end of the bargain. I almost laughed at that, but I didn\u2019t want to explain the in-joke while Leslie was here. That was taken care of and Zed sent his congratulations.<br /> <br /> Once I got off the phone with Zed, Leslie asked about her schedule. At first I just said we could try this and that, but then she reminded me that classes start Monday. Man that didn\u2019t take long. Summer\u2019s almost over. We worked out that she will come in from 1600 to close for this Monday and 1300 to close regularly on Tuesdays and Thursdays. I\u2019m really going to have to get in touch with Trinh and Elsie if I want to get this together. I just hope they are interested and have the time.<br /> <br /> The day finished in the shop pretty smoothly. I showed Leslie how to clean up and close up and still get out quickly. Then she was nice enough to drive me (she has a car?) back to the Bluffs. We came in and the first thing I see is Gretchen waiting just inside the door. She was cleaned up and wearing a slinky black dress and heels. She didn\u2019t even snipe at Leslie, who quietly blinked and let her be. I was stunned because she was so pretty and then she spoke. That pretty well snapped reality back into focus. She was waiting for Mongler to come over. I had forgotten the deal with him coming for the weekend. At that point, I started thinking about relationships and that didn\u2019t take long to spiral into a black place in my mind, so I came upstairs. I feel like a teenager being so awkward about my feelings right now. I know it will hurt and I\u2019m beginning to suspect that things are done with Nightshade and I. I don\u2019t think either of us can start the conversation right now. And while I\u2019m rational, like now, I can think that way. But then I get angry and I feel like something was taken from me. That\u2019s why I try to keep my distance.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019m just going to get cleaned up before trying to go to dinner and be around everyone.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2030 Hours, Friday, August 20, 2010<br /> <br /> Dinner was very nice. We had to use the real dining room because Gretchen, Mongler (should we call him Grin?), Karl, and Leslie all came to the table. Cupcake made authentic quesadillas for a battalion so there was plenty and it was so good. I hadn\u2019t thought about home, other than this place, in a long time until tonight. Those were good quesadillas. Rose took some food up to Tavia just before we sat down to eat. She was still in some kind of fugue state, working nonstop on the painting, so we weren\u2019t yet ready to go back to Glenwood. I don\u2019t like that this painting controls her mind like it does, but I don\u2019t think anyone was in a hurry to deal with what we know is in Glenwood yet. Rose didn\u2019t find her Uncle Guang while she was in Taiwan, but she did put more signs up around the neighborhood there. She said that she hoped he would show if she wasn\u2019t in the house. To make that less awkward, Karl was taking her to the movies. They were still working on which movie to see. I felt so bad for Karl when Rose mentioned Charlie St. Cloud was out. When I noted that Inception had opened, I was really surprised when Rose decided that sounded like fun. After dinner, Snowflake went up to stay with Tavia. He didn\u2019t like her being alone and dealing with everything without company. Cupcake and Chandra were excited to get dressed up for 80\u2019s Night at Gotham Citi. Nightshade, Karen, and Bright Eyes were all going to Murder Ballads. And why I didn\u2019t think they were hiding anything, I didn\u2019t feel like I was invited. Or maybe I\u2019m just being a grumpy baby. Gretchen almost dragged Mongler into the Library so if I had wanted to research anything, that was probably out. And my mood was shot with everyone else in the house splitting off into romantic groups. I think Leslie went out too, but I know she was going out to prowl. She\u2019s about to start college and a teenager. That is the thing to do.<br /> <br /> I went back to my room. Xerxes was there and he didn\u2019t want to be with anyone else so that really helped. I think I\u2019ve let him just be for too long in the House. I played with him for a while which cheered me up and then he laid down, apparently content with his efforts. I love that dog. After that, I decided to put the laptop to good use and look up options for setting up the van. I need to learn something about that wreck at some point. This seems like a great time.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I did all I could in Taipei, so in the afternoon (well after midnight in New Haven), I called Natalie. She was awake, and agreed to come fetch me. Then I waited for her on the warped wooden stairs of the abandoned temple. The place was dead, and to most I suppose it would seem rather forbidding, but I thought it was quite tranquil. Even the occasional hoarse cry of a crow and the waxing and waning chirps of the cicadas seemed peaceful. When Natalie finally arrived, she startled me out of a bit of a reverie.<br /> <br /> On the way home, Natalie updated me on what I\u2019d missed. Much to my chagrin, the others did go to the lodge again without me, but it all seems to have gone without incident, and now we have photos for Tavia to work from.<br /> <br /> Natalie also seemed rather excited about something, almost giddy in fact, but refused to tell me why. I have some suspicions, of course, but I suppose I will have to be patient until she feels comfortable sharing with the rest of us.<br /> <br /> We emerged from the mansion\u2019s Avernian gate at around 4:00 in the morning. I quickly showered and then went to bed to get a few hours sleep before going to train Jean. I hadn\u2019t thought about how long I\u2019d been awake until my head hit the pillow, and then I was out. I forgot to set my alarm, but Lily woke me up at bit after 9:00. I had just enough time to grab a piece of toast and say hi to the others at breakfast before leaving to meet Jean. I didn\u2019t even have a chance to meditate, but I did apologize for leaving them to return to the lodge without me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> My day has been uneventful, but the others have been busy. Alexia went with Simon to invite Malard to her wedding and get permission to have Deirdre for the ceremony. As I understand it, Malard is allowing Deirdre to come, but she mustn\u2019t stay any longer than necessary.<br /> <br /> Gretchen is excited because Grin is coming to stay the weekend. Unfortunately, she has big plans about making love to him in the library, and I find her lack of subtlety rather distressing. I asked Simon why he couldn\u2019t just forbid them from getting up to anything in the library, but her room is above his, and I think he\u2019d rather not be bothered by the noise they are likely to cause. Hopefully Grin has more discretion than his girlfriend.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, August 20, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> We all had a nice dinner in the dining hall since Grin was joining us. It was pleasant to enjoy a meal with the krewe and many of our friends, and despite some of the tension in the room between Natalie and Doc, or Gretchen and practically everyone, I think we all had a nice time.<br /> <br /> The only notable absence from dinner was Tavia. She has been in some sort of trance painting the gulmoth all day. I went up to take her some food after dinner, and got a glimpse of the painting. The creature is horrifying, a twisted fusion of hairy beast and fly and maggot. I feel sorry that Tavia has to paint the thing, and I can only imagine what sort of nightmares she\u2019ll have when she\u2019s done and finally gets some sleep.<br /> <br /> For now, though, most of us are going out for the evening. Alexia and Chandra are going to Gotham Citi, Natalie, Karen and Sara to Murder Ballads, and Karl and I are going to see a movie. We talked a bit about what to see. I want to see Charlie St. Cloud, and Karl wants to see Inception. We\u2019ve decided on Inception. Doc doesn\u2019t feel like going out, and Simon wants to stay with Tavia, so they will be staying home.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 19th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I can\u2019t believe this night happened. I am walking in a dream.<br /> <br /> -Gotta get Spooky<br /> <br /> -Can\u2019t tell her. Can\u2019t tell anyone yet. Omigod.<br /> <br /> -Play it cool, act normal<br /> <br /> -OK Spooky rescued, back to the townhouse.<br /> <br /> -Sleep (Maybe).<br /> <br /> <br /> August 20th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Oh man, I am going to be a little tired today.<br /> <br /> -What\u2019s up at Chez Satanique I wonder?<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Music? Nah, maybe later.<br /> <br /> -Spooky apparently does not need sleep.<br /> <br /> -Bad little witches, however, do.<br /> <br /> -Bad pillow, stay still!<br /> <br /> -Gretchen all dressed up nice.<br /> <br /> -Din dins!<br /> <br /> -Need to put things forward with the club.<br /> <br /> -Looks like tonight is a clubbing night. Alexia and Chandra\u2019s idea.<br /> <br /> -Hitting Murder Ballads!<br /> <br /> -Karen takes this whole thing seriously. ~*Love*~<br /> <br /> -Mistress is so cruel ~*Love*~<br /> <br /> -OK, well, now I feel watched.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m a what?<br /> <br /> -I hope Sara knows that\u2019s a vampire.<br /> <br /> -Oh does Karen want two personal bitches tonight? Fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Will pout nonetheless, as is the way of my people.<br /> <br /> -Three and I get grumpy!<br /> <br /> -Well, much worse places to be then here now\u2026.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Shorter journals this time.<br /> <br /> Little to add, really. Role-played through Jasmine\u2019s return. Some discussion, and eventual looking up, of what movies were out on that week in 2010. I can barely believe this game used to be in the future.<br /> <br /> One bit of the night\u2019s festivities were not really covered in any journal. Alexia saw Shatina at Gotham Citi acting very odd and like a puppet, so she followed her, as did an unknown Changeling. Alexia attempted to confront Shatina, did poorly, and wound up being pulled away by the Changeling, who never identified herself, but was a friend of Grin. Wound up calling Grin for advice and leaving Shatina to be followed by the Changeling.<br /> <br /> This will be very important, as tonight\u2019s session was mostly Changeling stuff; well that and some initial GMC type discussion, at least about rules changes.<br /> <br /> But that is a different story, I will see you then. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:08:31-08:00","id":17012,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s about time to check in on hour Geist group. Let\u2019s see how things are going.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXXI</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0945 Hours, Saturday, August 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Xerxes and I stayed in my room last night til I fell asleep. I don\u2019t remember getting tired, just looking at forums and how to videos for working a van like I have rusting outside. Then I woke up when I shifted and hit the laptop with my cheek on the table. Meditation after sleeping in a chair all night isn\u2019t the best thing, and it took me about two hours to find peace.<br /> <br /> I came down a little later than usual but breakfast was still going. Nightshade, Karen, Tavia, and Leslie were all missing, but that\u2019s only unusual for Tavia. Mongler was draining the OJ when he suddenly stopped short and started apologizing for ... enjoying orange juice? I finally had to tell him to relax. Karl also pointed out that Cupcake was going to feed him a lot so he should get use to it while he was here. From one really big guy to another, that was amusing. Cupcake did mention that she met another Changeling last night, though she didn\u2019t get a name. This was while she and Chandra were following Shatina\u2019s Fetch, which apparently flipped out in Gotham Citi. The small woman was originally crawling across the ceiling in the club before vanishing into an air vent. She then grabbed Cupcake and hid her in a tree when our unstealthy chef confronted Shatina-Fetch. Grin (Changeling stuff now, might as well identify him that way) heard the description and said that was Agnes the Creeper. But more importantly, if Shatina-Fetch is short circuiting, that is a sign that the real Shatina may be back. Grin and Karl went to hang out and get Grin\u2019s axe while we waiting for the others to wake up or come back. Once we\u2019re properly assembled, Rose and Cupcake can try to use Shatina\u2019s hair in the Finding Ceremony.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1215 Hours, Friday, August 20, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a hell of a day!<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Karen came back right after Grin and Karl got in. I couldn\u2019t see the axe, but I could tell Grin was carrying something big just based on his stance. With everyone back, we got the maps and hair to figure out where we might be going. Snowflake and Bright Eyes were driving again and had the cars ready. Rose, Cupcake, and Grin rode with Snowflake while Nightshade and I rode with Bright Eyes. We didn\u2019t think to give Grin an ear curl but I\u2019m not sure if it would fit since what I can see of him is an illusion. Don\u2019t ask. Anyway, Snowflake led and we followed. We started heading north toward the edge of New Haven. We weren\u2019t really out of town when these two huge dogs jumped at and on Snowflake\u2019s car. Rose announced through the ear curl that they were not normal. Something about Spider Dogs. What is it with Changelings and spider hybrids? Anyway, one missed and Bright Eyes had to swerve to miss it. The other landed on top of Snowflake\u2019s car. I put up my Primeval Shroud while Rose called out driving instructions to dodge invisible webbing. I should also note that Snowflake stomped it so the one on top was really just hanging on. Then Cupcake screamed into the curl that we had to get out as she saw a really tall guy with three more of those dogs on a leash. Bright Eyes floored it just to keep up with Snowflake. Meanwhile Rose decided she had had enough of these motherfuckin\u2019 dogs on the ...roof. She climbed out the window just like when the Scarecrow spirit tried to get to Tanya. The spider dog didn\u2019t fare any better against Rose than the spirit. I hope this isn\u2019t a habit we\u2019re developing. Rescue another fledgeling supernatural creature, have enemies try to kill or capture them from the roof of our cars. Back to what happened. The dog that missed apparently managed to web Snowflake\u2019s car, but they was driving so fast the inertia was more than the dog could handle. Instead of stopping the car, the car ripped the dog off its feet. This was especially interesting for us that couldn\u2019t see Changeling things. All we could see was this huge dog fly past us and then swing behind Snowflake\u2019s car...until it almost hit us. Bright Eyes jerked the wheel at just the right moment and missed the dog hurtling toward us. It let go after bouncing on the asphalt. I watched the dogs fade into the distance through Bright Eyes\u2019 rear window. So when Snowflake stopped, I was a little surprised. Grin and Rose got out and started tearing invisible web off the back of the car. Cupcake got out, but just got in the front seat carrying the map. Grin thought the tall man was actually a Gentry. He was keeping an eye behind us as we talked about it. He thought the Gentry was probably also looking for Shatina so we needed to hurry. Cupcake still had the Finding ceremony working so we loaded up again.<br /> <br /> Just a few minutes outside of North Haven, we stopped at an old barn. Snowflake put up a Boneyard to see what we could find. Rose slipped around back to keep Shatina from running. I hated to surround someone that had just escaped enslavement, but I didn\u2019t have a better idea or time to explain. Bright Eyes and I walked to the barn and tried to talk Shatina out. Before we could finish, I suddenly felt myself relax even though I was tense from worry. This was very helpful considering Grin announced that \u201cthey\u201d were coming. Shatina came out of the barn wearing what was once a black evening dress. It was more shredded black ribbons now. She was effectively nude given how badly everything was ripped. Even still, something about Shatina struck me. This was easily the most beautiful woman I had ever seen. I hated myself for thinking it, but I knew I wanted her even before I realized she was uncovered. Thankfully I was able to keep my shit together enough not to leer at her. When Grin made his announcement, I told her that we had to go because the people that took her were coming back. I realized as soon as I said it, that was the wrong thing to have spoken. The look in her eyes was of pure terror and the only reason she didn\u2019t panic and bolt was the odd calming effect around us. We got Shatina in the car and Cupcake drove for Bright Eyes. Then we took the long way home.<br /> <br /> Shatina sat in the back between Nightshade and Bright Eyes in the back. Someone draped a jacket over her shoulders but when I looked back, I found I couldn\u2019t help looking at her. Shaking my head a little, I pulled my shirt off and offered it to her. She was confused at first, then looked down and realized just how undressed she was. Bright Eyes looked like she might cut me, but we\u2019d have to deal with that later. I wanted to help this girl and help her to not be afraid. Being stared at from all sides with looks of sexual hunger was not going to help that. I asked if there was anything else we could do for her, as we would get her someplace safe. She said she needed food as she put my shirt on. She seemed a little less timid at that point. Snowflake went to McDonald\u2019s while we took Shatina back to Dark Haven Bluffs. It is easily the safest place we know. When we got inside, I went upstairs and got a part of gym shorts. I knew they were too big, but the draw string would help some. I was pretty sure Shatina wouldn\u2019t fit in any clothes the other women in the House might have.<br /> <br /> Grin went to talk with the Changelings as soon as we got back so they could be ready. The newest Changeling wondered if she couldn\u2019t just go home. We carefully explained, as best we could, that a Fetch might be at her house. Rose tried to help when the poor girl seemed confused by the word Fetch. Unfortunately I was trying to be delicate and avoid some of the details, and Rose didn\u2019t think about that. She stated rather plainly that a Fetch was a construct that took her place and lived her life so that no one would realize she was missing. I pointed out quickly that I was trying to avoid that to Rose and she suddenly realized why that made the situation worse. Snowflake and I excused ourselves while Shatina ate to find out exactly where Shatina-Fetch was. We went down into one of the rooms I had never been to before. The walls were lined with mirrors of all shapes, styles, and sizes. This was obviously the Mirror Room. I had to admit to Snowflake this was a lot of mirrors. He didn\u2019t really want to talk about that, so we got to work on the compact Rose took from Shatina-Fetch. In just a few moments, I saw a clear picture form in the mirror of Shatina-Fetch in what I eventually recognized as Yale-New Haven Psychiatric Hospital. I couldn\u2019t hear anything, but it looked like she was just in a room staring out the barred window. She drummed her fingers impatiently as if she were waiting for something...or someone. But she was not acting unnatural or bizarre in any way. I knew this meant she had been taken in for 24-hour evaluation. By the look of it, this was not a voluntary admission. At least she\u2019ll be in good hands while she stays there. Before we left, Snowflake mentioned that this room was private. I had to smile as if I would ever go into rooms I\u2019m not welcome in this House. But I agreed and we headed back upstairs.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re just waiting....Fuck. Gretchen just got a call from Grin. He said we should stay alert. I gotta get the shotgun.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, August 21, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> Karl and I had a wonderful night last night. After the movie (which was intriguing), we went out for milkshakes and then returned home to Dark Haven Bluffs, where we changed into our swimwear and went out for a swim in the ocean. We descended deep beneath the waves and played a bit before things became a bit more romantic. We cuddled for awhile, cradled in the night-dark depths lit only by Karl\u2019s gentle bioluminescence, and things got a bit steamy.<br /> <br /> I performed tai chi meditation this morning on the bluffs. Later, over breakfast, Alexia told those of us who were awake about a shocking encounter she had at Gotham Citi last night. She and Chandra were enjoying themselves when they noticed Shatina\u2019s fetch acting oddly. It was jerking around and moving strangely, causing quite a stir in the club. Bouncers came and escorted it out. Alexia also noticed a strange figure clinging to the club ceiling, hidden by the lights. The figure followed the fetch out through a vent in the wall, and Alexia gave chase as well.<br /> <br /> Once she was outside, she almost approached the fetch, but was grabbed and pulled back into the camouflage of a nearby tree by the small, spindly figure she had seen in the club, who turned out to be a changeling named Agnes the Creeper. The figure told her to be quiet and stay safe, and they watched the fetch wander off. Agnes said that approaching the fetch at that moment was too dangerous.<br /> <br /> Alexia contacted Grin, and he\u2019s looking into things. He believes the malfunctioning fetch indicates that the real Shatina had escaped from the Hedge and is nearby. Alexia and I suggested that we perform the Finding ceremony using the bits of Shatina\u2019s hair we collected some time ago to try and find her again. And this time, we\u2019ll be taking Grin with us to make sure we don\u2019t wander into the Hedge again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, August 21, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Simon use her mirror-viewing ceremony to spy on Shatina\u2019s fetch, and found that she was being held for observation in the Yale medical center\u2019s mental hospital. So for the time being, she won\u2019t be doing any har, I hope. Meanwhile, Alexia and I cooperated to perform the Finding ceremony, and got a strong lead on Shatina. We loaded up into two cars. Alexia, Grin and I rode with Simon in his large car, while Natalie and Doc rode with Sara in her station wagon.<br /> <br /> We drove as quickly as possible, following the erratic pull of the finding pendulum. Then, without warning, two monstrous creatures that resembled a tortured mixture of spider and dog ambushed us. Except for Grin, the others saw them only as huge dogs, so we knew that they must be creatures from the Hedge. They leapt toward the car. One missed landed on the street in fornt of Sara\u2019s car, but the other landed on the roof of the our car and clung there. Simon accelerated and began swerving to throw it off, but it held on. I don\u2019t know what happened to the other, but I think Sara managed to avoid it and keep going.<br /> <br /> I tossed the finding pendulum to Alexia so that she could maintain the ritual, then rolled down my car window and activated the beast form of my Primeval Caul. I leaned out of the car, grabbed the spider-dog by one leg, and tore it from the roof, flinging it to the asphalt. It scraped and rolled over the pavement for a moment before righting itself and spitting a strand of thick webbing at us.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the car was going so fast that it couldn\u2019t stop us. Instead, it was pulled along behind us. It quickly decided to let go, and I cut the remaining webbing.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, our troubles weren\u2019t over. We caught sight of a tall, lean man emerging onto the street from between two buildings. He appeared to be made of the vast expanse of the cosmos wrapped into human form, and despite the terror he projected, there was something deeply and carnally inviting about him. He led three more leashed spider-dogs, and Grin yelled that it looked like one of the Gentry. We decided to flee.<br /> <br /> Simon and Sara put as much distance between us and the Gentry as we could, and following Alexia\u2019s guidance, we found Shatina in a barn just outside of New Haven. She was terrified, clad only in a badly torn dress. She looked different from her fetch, at least to me and Grin: extraordinarily beautiful with star-filled eyes and lustrous silken-black black hair. Doc was obviously smitten the moment he laid eyes on her, and the other members of the group also seemed taken aback by her charms.<br /> <br /> Doc, Natalie, and Sara went in to calm her down and convince her we were friends. I don\u2019t know what Natalie said, exactly, (I was behind the barn to make sure Shatina didn\u2019t try to flee), but whatever she said, she made an impression. Shatina decided to place her trust in us, and we hurried her to the car and drove back to Darkhaven Bluffs, taking a circuitous route to avoid running into the Gentry again.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re trying to make Shatina is comfortable, safe, and fed. Doc has given her some of his clothes to wear (she\u2019s rather too well-endowed for any of the krewe\u2019s ladies\u2019 clothes to fit her), and Grin has gone to get some reinforcements and to try and find out more about the Gentry we spotted. Otherwise, we\u2019re simply trying to make sure Shatina is comfortable and feels safe.<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> Grin just called. He says we need to be prepared. The Gentry must have been able to track us here...<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes<br /> </u><br /> <u>Second Base<br /> </u><br /> Karl and I got to \u201csecond base\u201d last night. At least, I believe that\u2019s American expression for the sort of affectionate petting we got up to. Karl can be very tender and affectionate, and even if he was a bit unsure of himself, it only made him all the more endearing. There is something very intimate about exploring each other, and faltering a bit is a part of that intimacy. Afterward, we just held each other an drifted there in darkness until we were ready to return to surface.<br /> I\u2019m so glad that Karl understands my need to be close and intimate without rushing into things sexually. Not that I have a problem with sex (though many of my krewe-mates seem to think I do). Karl and I are certainly becoming more intimate, and it fills me with an odd mixture of affectionate anticipation and fear. I need to be with someone, to be with Karl, but the frozen knot inside me keeps saying that sleeping with Karl would be a betrayal of my memories of Richard. I know that isn\u2019t true, that Richard is gone and that I should move on, but it\u2019s hard to rid myself of that fear.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Primeval Changes</u><br /> <br /> I think the primeval beast-from I adopt when I unlock my Primeval Caul is changing a bit. I noticed during the fight against the spider-dogs. My did not become as feline as it usually does. My fingers grew long and thin but still incredibly strong, tipped with fearsome claws and sporting a soft smattering of thin scales. I even felt different\u2026a bit less like a prowling cat and more like a stalking shark, moving with cold purpose, gracefully and calmly approaching my prey until I struck with terrible ferocity. Perhaps something in me is changing a bit, altering the way I manifest my caul. Or perhaps it is responding to the way I\u2019ve been using it. Maybe my deepening connection to the sea is shaping my caul into something more appropriate. It\u2019s intriguing. I suppose it might make me uneasy except that it feels quite natural.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 21st, 2010<br /> <br /> -Holy hell, last night was AWESOME<br /> <br /> -I love Karen Smith<br /> <br /> -lovelovelove ~*LOVE*~<br /> <br /> -I feel good.<br /> <br /> -Back to the house. Act normal.<br /> <br /> -New Plan? New Plan!<br /> <br /> -Faerie stuff scares me. Seriously.<br /> <br /> -Time for magic.<br /> <br /> -Karen makes me so hot I can\u2019t think straight.<br /> <br /> -Focus<br /> <br /> -Time to get the real girl this time.<br /> <br /> -Meep!<br /> <br /> -MEEP!<br /> <br /> -Radio Silence<br /> <br /> -@Nerak Sweetheart, tell folks at home to get ready. We are bringing a very scared girl there. Very fast.<br /> <br /> -So\u2026none of our cloths are going to fit her, are they? No.<br /> <br /> -Bah Doc lacks any sense of humor<br /> <br /> -LOL Sara will be even more upset I think at him.<br /> <br /> -OK we are here. Not sure if we are safe<br /> <br /> -Awwwwwwwwwwwwwwwwww<br /> <br /> -Nasty.<br /> <br /> -Delay in Vlog, will be up later<br /> <br /> -Good to be back with my\u2026Karen.<br /> <br /> -Shatina\u2019s shaken, trying to be here assisting.<br /> <br /> -I miss when Doc and I were friends and I could talk to him. And wasn\u2019t afraid of him.<br /> <br /> -Those were good times.<br /> <br /> -Looks like her fetch was put in the hospital<br /> <br /> -That\u2019s is never any fun.<br /> <br /> -\u2026uh oh.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Well it was a good session, and the investigation of changeling business quickly took precedence. The car/driving stuff was pretty awesome. I had people make a lot of hard rolls, and Simon was rolling five dice Sara three. Sadly Gwen was the one with High Performance Driving from <i>Midnight Roads</i>. Willpower was spent like water.<br /> <br /> If you are wondering, Shatina is a Telluric/Shadowsoul Fairest, no Court yet. As for the fetch, well we will have to see. I have certain had some very friendly, and very treacherous, fetches from my time running <i>Changeling</i>.<br /> <br /> Natalie also got 9 successes on a roll to get Shatina to calm down and come with us, which was impressive.<br /> <br /> Some discussion of GMC. We are adopting a wait and see attitude.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome. Stay tuned for next time when Jasmine makes a friend, Doc shoots a Spider Dog, Alexia makes cupcakes, Simon makes a plan, Natalie puts on a top hat and tails, and Sara gets a text from a vampire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:10:05-08:00","id":17013,"title":"","content":"to see it resolved.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1315 Hours, Friday, August 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was ...something. Sorry, I\u2019m a little edgy as it reminds me of Kabul. Ambush of our home base, even with reinforcements. Fuck, I think I might be sick. This the first time I\u2019ve thought about that in months or longer. I think it\u2019s safe to say I officially have a standing kill order for Gentry now.<br /> <br /> Let me try to start over. We were on high alert after Grin\u2019s call when a Jeep and a big van pulled up. I was at the front door and counted 17 of the most ragtag bunch of people get out, before Grin finally rolled out of the back. This was our army! I lowered my shotgun and went out on the front porch. There were more Changelings here than I even realized were in town. One of the guys I didn\u2019t recognize announced that they were here to kill our monster. I let them in and they filled the entrance hall. I could tell by the way some of them moved, they were much bigger than they seemed to me. A slender girl carried what I knew to be a rifle case and headed upstairs. The rest stayed with Grin and I on the first floor. Rose was on the Widow\u2019s Walk as she could see Changeling stuff and acted as lookout. After about 10 minutes, she called down to Bright Eyes through the ear curl to find Lily. After a moment, Bright Eyes reported she couldn\u2019t find the doll. Snowflake informed us she was \u201csafe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Just a few minutes later, Snowflake told us there were dogs coming. One on either side of the House and one in the back. Rose noted Rita had the one in the back. I split the room to head to either end of the House. Two motley crews darted in their ordered directions. As I sat down to release the Dog of War, I heard that rifle go off from above. As the Dog of War stood I grabbed the ear curl and shot gun before running to the left, shoring up the lesser numbered group. I arrived to see one of the dogs, already in the House, bite Grin. I took no mercy and opened fire. Grin followed up with a swing of his invisible axe. Before the others could move, I shot it again and it slumped in a very disturbing heap. I ordered our group to converge with the other. On the way, Snowflake announced that we had Malard Incoming! He was apparently charging the battle in full werewolf form. I alerted the Changelings because Friendly Fire might be an issue. There was another shot from above and then a wolf howl rocked the area. I couldn\u2019t move. No one could. I knew where I was and that I was with friends, but everything else was pure fear. I don\u2019t know how long we were like that, but when we could move again, the Changelings demanded to know what the fuck that was. I told them I thought it was Malard. He confirmed it a few minutes later when he entered the House in human form.<br /> <br /> Malard stayed for cupcakes while I went around playing Medic to the bites and cuts. Grin and two others had some minor wounds. Once people were more together and combat nerves were easing off, we had Bright Eyes bring Shatina up. Before they got to us, I moved through the room and talked to a few of the women about getting some normal clothes for her. I figured they would have a better time of that. No one thought this was weird so I didn\u2019t feel so creepy asking about it. After a few minutes of talking, they made sure we were okay with her leaving. I thought that was interesting. I mean we obviously knew what Changelings were, but they didn\u2019t want us to worry about Shatina. They have a whole community that can help her and make her comfortable. We of course asked her if she was okay with it. That was really what was important. She said she thought it was a good idea, so they all piled back into their cars. Well not Grin. Gretchen took him to get his car, and god only knows what else.<br /> <br /> We need to replace two of the windows on either side of the House, but the Changelings took care of the dogs before they left apparently. Now we just need to regroup and figure everything out.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1630 Hours, Friday, August 21, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s pretty empty in here compared to what we\u2019ve just had. It\u2019s so quiet, it\u2019s like the House is resting after taking the wounds to the windows. Snowflake and I have already covered the wounds and we\u2019ll be replacing the windows soon. The House protects us, I will be the medic for it as well.<br /> <br /> The Krewe gathered and we decided that we need to have dinner out tonight. That led to the most amusing show of Foodie Elitism from Cupcake I\u2019ve ever seen. We determined that there would be 13 of us going and it was not far to Cupcake to have to get everything together on such short notice. So someone suggested Olive Garden and several more agreed. The look of ... well almost revulsion by Cupcake was so obvious, Nightshade had to ask what was wrong. This led to everyone learning how low on the totem pole of restaurants Cupcake ranked Olive Garden. She relented mainly because she got embarrassed by how everyone was looking at her after her mini-rant.<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, Nightshade pointed out that we really needed to learn if all werewolves could do that howl thing. If we ever had to deal with one again, that is something we have to plan for. That will probably be a question for Deirdre and Zed, separately.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2030 Hours, Saturday, August 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Dinner was not nearly as traumatic for Cupcake as I feared. There were breadsticks for all and great time was had. Afterwards, we went Plasm gulping before returning to the House. Karen and Nightshade got incredibly dressed up to go to a play. Karen had on an evening gown that made her look absolutely stunning. Nightshade was wearing a top hat and tails. She looked gorgeous too, of course, but it was very obvious what she was going for. Cupcake and Chandra were going back to Gotham Citi for a more relaxing evening than last night. Karl and Jasmine were going swimming again, which I suspect may have interesting consequences. I wish them both luck. Gretchen and Mongler were well, everyone else is leaving, so they were going to be loud. Snowflake, Bright Eyes, and I decided to go to Murder Ballads for drinking, finishing off the Plasm gulping, and people watching. Tavia decided she would come to. I think it was the people watching that got her.<br /> <br /> Now let\u2019s see how things go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> Saturday, August 21, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> The threat of the Gentry has abated, for now at least. With the help of Grin\u2019s fellow changelings, we were able to protect Shatina.<br /> <br /> We knew that the Gentry was coming for Shatina, so Doc set about preparing defenses and assigning everyone posts in the mansion. Leslie, Chandra, and others who couldn\u2019t fight took shelter in the basement while Natalie and Sara stayed with Shatina to guard her in case anything got into the house. I went up onto the widow\u2019s walk atop the house to stand watch, since I am ensorcelled. I unlocked the Primeval Oracle to enhance my senses, and remained alert. Alexia took position in one of the turrets in the front of the house to provide a second set of eyes.<br /> <br /> I was a bit worried about Lily, though. I called down to Alexia through my ear curl to find out where she was, but Alexia couldn\u2019t find her. Simon was safely ensconced in the basement, where he was monitoring the mansion and it\u2019s surroundings with Boneyard, and he assured me that Lily was safe. I found out later that she was perched above the door to the widow\u2019s walk, ready to pounced upon anything that tried to get through to attack me. She\u2019s such a dear, even though I do worry that she will get in over her head one of these days! Still, I think it\u2019s important for her to feel useful.<br /> <br /> Soon after I arrived on the walk, a van arrived and a nightmarish array of changelings piled out with Grin leading them. I noticed Tommy Knocker among them. Doc went out to greet them and began giving them orders, splitting them into two groups to defend both ends of the house. He sent one of the changelings up to where I was, though. She was a thin young woman with pale, slightly bluish skin that always seems to be wet. Her large mouth was full of sharp, piranha-like teeth, which gave even her friendly smile a disturbingly predatory edge.<br /> <br /> She began assembling a rifle, and as she did so, we introduced ourselves. Her name was Rita, and she seemed a very sweet girl. During her imprisonment in the Hedge, she was made into a siren who seduced and then ate her lovers. The rifle she was using had belonged to her brother, but he was taken by the gentry as well, and she hopes to one day get him back. I tried to encourage her, and told her that if we survive the Gentry at hand, then I would do what I could to help her retrieve her brother.<br /> <br /> Then the Gentry came. I did not see him directly, but his spider-dogs converged on the mansion from all sides. I saw the first, creeping stealthily through the cemetery in the backyard, and called it out to Rita, who quickly aimed and fired. She hit it, badly injuring it, but then it leapt onto the mansion walls and clambered onto the widow\u2019s walk. I unlocked my Primeval Caul, and as I focused to do so, I felt a surge of strength, and my caul completed its transformation from something feline to something altogether fish- or shark-like. I moved between the spider-dog and Rita, and when it lunged at me, I stepped to the side, deflecting its blow, the broke two of its legs before shoving it over the railing to fall to its death four stories below.<br /> <br /> Rita didn\u2019t seem to have much confidence in her abilities as a marksman, but she seemed quite capable to me. We made a good team. I called out targets and kept Rita safe by dealing with any who made it onto the walk, while Rita did the bulk of the work from afar with her keen aim.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Doc and the changelings had their hands full fighting the few spider-dogs that made it past Rita\u2019s aim. Two managed to break into the house, but they didn\u2019t make it much farther than the window before Doc and Grin crushed them. When Doc is ready for combat, he can be quite fearsome.<br /> <br /> The fight was nearly over when a massive white werewolf\u2014Malard\u2014 charged from his yard into ours, unleashing a monstrous howl as it did so. The howl was fearsome enough to rattle almost everyone present, though I managed to keep my wits about me. Rita was taking aim at the last of the spider-dogs when the roar startled her, and then Malard pounced on her target and tore it to pieces before bounding off to search for any remaining foes. By that time, though, the Gentry, if he had ever been there in the first place, had disappeared.<br /> <br /> With the battle over, everyone retreated into the mansion to celebrate. Malard returned home to change back into human form and into some clothes, and then came to join us. Grin believes the Gentry will not return, at least not immediately, since it appears that retrieving Shatina will be too dangerous. While Alexia fed everyone and we all congratulated each other, I got to know Rita a bit better. I think we were both impressed with each other during the fight, and I sensed a kindred soul. Indeed, Grin later told me that he thought I\u2019d be a good friend for Rita, one who could perhaps help her deal with some of her problems. I do hope I can. I quite liked Rita, and hope we can develop our friendship more. We shared phone numbers, so that we can stay in touch.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, August 21, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> After the changelings and Malard left, we all decided to relax. The krewe, along with Karl, Grin, Gretchen, Chandra, Tavia and Leslie, went out to eat at Olive Garden, though Alexia expressed some disdain for the restaurant. Her gourmet tastes have spoiled her toward food that the rest of us would consider quite satisfactory.<br /> <br /> Afterward, most of the others went clubbing. Natalie and Karen went to see a play, and they were dressed quite nicely, though Natalie was dressed in a very masculine fashion. Karl and I returned to the mansion, and decided to go swimming again\u2014for us, enjoying the depths together is always beautiful. Karl showed me a gorgeous hidden submarine grotto, where we enjoyed each other\u2019s company for a time and allowed ourselves to become a bit intimate like we did last night. It was nice.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Moment of Perfection</u><br /> <br /> When I unlocked my Caul with the Primeval Key in preparation for the fight against the Gentry\u2019s minions, I felt at first as though something was restraining me, like the key wouldn\u2019t turn smoothly in the lock because I was twisting it the wrong way. I focused, attempting to open myself as fully as possible to my primal connections and instincts, and felt a surge of newfound strength as the Caul overcame me. Before, I noticed my caul changing, becoming a bit more fish-like. This time, that change came fully, and felt both natural and empowering.<br /> <br /> I became sleek an strong\u2014more so even than usual, and my fingers lengthened and grew claws. Webbing grew between them, and I felt my mouth widen slightly and my teeth grow ever so slightly sharper. A sparse pattern of faint, blue-white scales appeared on my skin, and I was told later that my eyes changed, blackening completely like the eyes of a shark. The most striking thing for me, though was the way I could taste my surroundings. I could feel the approaching spider-dogs simply by tasting the air, and I could sense Rita\u2019s excitement and fear mixed with the bitter discharge of gunpowder. It was bewildering and exhilarating all at the same time.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve never felt such raw physical power and awareness when activating my caul.<br /> <br /> Later, I talked to Karl about it, and he seemed to understand. In fact, he seemed happy and excited to learn of the change\u2026which made me happy as well. I still worry that the fish-god is involved, but I can\u2019t tell Karl that. I do hope that I am worrying too much about it. After all, given my past as a swimmer and my ever-growing connection to the depths, this change may well be completely natural.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Dangerous Instincts </u><br /> <br /> During the celebration after the battle, Rita and I chatted a bit. She belongs to the changeling\u2019s Autumn Court, just like Grin. She seemed comfortable enough with me to share some of her fears. She\u2019s scared that the predatory instincts that defined her during her \u201cdurance\u201d may still have a grip over her. She is quite lonely and would like to find a lover, but she fears that she will lose control of herself and revert to her old habits, killing him should they become intimate.<br /> <br /> I did my best to encourage her, and I hope that I can help her overcome her fears. And, if they are grounded, I hope I can help her overcome those predatory impulses. I don\u2019t know her well, but I think I have a good sense of who she is, and a sweet girl like her deserves to be happy, especially after all she must have gone through.<br /> <br /> I did notice, sadly, that she seemed mildly saddened when I introduced Karl\u2026seeing my boyfriend must have made her feel the absence of one of her own more keenly. But fortunately it did not seem to harm the growth of our friendship in any way.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 21st, 2010<br /> <br /> -Can\u2019t chat, stuff going on.<br /> <br /> -OK, that was kind of scary.<br /> <br /> -Man the house is full!<br /> <br /> -Owlish Housemate is being a good hostess.<br /> <br /> -Sweet Cuppin cakes.<br /> <br /> -Aaaaaaaaaaand empty.<br /> <br /> -Hmmm\u2026Owlish Housemate wants Olive Garden<br /> <br /> -Oh just look at Alexia looking down her nose at the food we mere mortals eat.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is having Olive Garden!<br /> <br /> -Big group here but good times.<br /> <br /> -We are almost like a family, but awesomer.<br /> <br /> -Is that a word? Spellcheck says no.<br /> <br /> -Spellcheck also says Spellcheck is not a word, so what does it know?<br /> <br /> -Noms.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Hm! Playing dress up.<br /> <br /> -Waiting downstairs for my date.<br /> <br /> -My my my. Now this is a lady.<br /> <br /> Uh oh, perhaps she is no lady!<br /> <br /> -To the theater!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> That moment of perfection was because Jasmine\u2019s player got a lot of successes activating her Caul. Ten actually, though amazingly Jasmine only rolled three initially\u2026and seven from the Willpower point.<br /> <br /> There was actually more stuff that happened at Murder Ballads and Gotham Citi, but that spilled massively over into the next session, so will be discussed next time since it constituted the bulk of the session.<br /> <br /> Will catch up with you then, comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:12:33-08:00","id":17014,"title":"","content":"Last journal left us with our protagonists out clubbing. A lot happened, and we should probably address that. <br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0245 Hours, Sunday, August 22, 2010<br /> <br /> If I didn\u2019t know Luck Magic, I\u2019d swear I was cursed. ...I should probably try that again without all the bitter getting in the way. Bright Eyes is a serious pick up artist. But that\u2019s the end, the means was actually pretty fun for all of us to start with, then got a little thorny. Rose would not approve.<br /> <br /> When we got to Murder Ballads, the place was packed. Right off the bat, I saw Trinh with one of Nightshade\u2019s fans, Elsie with some of her friends, and Pilot Light with Lauren. Since Tavia was with us, I decided not mentioning Lauren was the best plan for everyone. So I did the smart thing and headed over to Trinh and Cindy. I talked to her about maybe working in the shop and she seemed at least mildly interested, though her point of reference was that I was connected to Nightshade. That was a little depressing, but she got past that and gave her her contact information. After a bit, I broke off to let them enjoy their night.<br /> <br /> When I got back to our table, Snowflake had decided that Trinh and Pilot Light needed to be together. I didn\u2019t realize he\u2019d had that much to drink while I was gone. But I figured that playing a little matchmaker would make Tavia happy and could be entertaining. We were in a large club with lots of people so things could only go so badly. Tavia dubbed the mission a \u201cMeet Cute,\u201d which is apparently something they do in the movies. Snowflake sent Nightshade a text and arranged for a private room to be opened for us. I procured the super sweet strawberry liqueurs which Nightshade seemed to know would be helpful. Bright Eyes was in charge of keeping Lauren distracted...and also not in a private room with Tavia. Snowflake, Tavia, and I would be in the private room with Trinh, Cindy, and Pilot Light. It was noted that between the Cursing and Boneyarding Bright Eyes and Snowflake were doing, I would need to be present in case something got out of hand. I realized that far in that this was no simple game of matchmaker but Nightshade\u2019s horrific nightmare of lost agency run berzerk. And I was going to be, until right then, a willing participant. This...could have gone worse? I went by Trinh and mentioned hearing about a bottle of the strawberry liqueur in the private room. That led to her almost dragging Cindy to get in. I don\u2019t honestly know how they managed to get Pilot Light to come in. I know that Bright Eyes met Lauren outside the door and very gently let her know how dangerous Tavia might be. That seemed to work without much issue. I talked with Cindy just in general, learning what some of her interests were. We were having a decent conversation when the culmination of Nightshade\u2019s nightmare bore its hideous fruit. Glancing over, Trinh had pushed Pilot Light into a chair, straddled him, and that\u2019s about the time I looked back to see Cindy turning red and storming out. Snowflake was drained and basically turning to a puddle from Tavia playing with his ear. I gently interrupted the chair dance which broke the mood, at least for that moment. I turned around so they could get mostly decent. Pilot Light was very confused but didn\u2019t seem too upset. Trinh on the other hand was mortified. She told me once they were presentable that she needed to talk to Cindy and Pilot Light. We cleared the room but when Trinh got to the door, one look at Cindy told her that was probably a talk for later.<br /> <br /> While Trinh and Pilot Light talked things out a little without the damning power of lust controlling them, Bright Eyes and I felt bad for Cindy. I didn\u2019t think I would be a good person to approach her given I felt guilty for having distracted her in the first place. Bright Eyes didn\u2019t seem too concerned about that so she went to talk and try to smooth things over. Snowflake was still completely caving to everything Tavia wanted. Talking to them briefly, I could tell Tavia needed to take Snowflake home. Glancing back, it was also obvious that Bright Eyes wasn\u2019t coming home with us again. I let her know we were heading out and apologized to Cindy for the issues. So once again, everyone around me is taking someone to bed. Me, I\u2019m writing my log.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019ll go workout assuming no one is making out in the jacuzzi.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Sunday, August 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Given the last few days, I wasn\u2019t surprised when it took an hour for me to center this morning. Rose was out by the Bluffs doing Tai Chi, but I still needed to be alone. I\u2019m not going to do or say anything that could hurt anyone on purpose, but I like to be at peace before I start just in case.<br /> <br /> I came down to breakfast and learned that Cupcake and Chandra met a normal psychic at Gotham Citi. She was looking into a missing brother for a friend. It wasn\u2019t related to Shatina or Rita as best we could tell, so apparently New Haven is really not a great place to be a brother. This psychic was the real thing as she immediately noted the girls were a Sin-Eater and vampire respectively. Apparently even used the word Sin-Eater. Still not as impressive as Ghost Walkers, but it was interesting that she knew about us. So we may end up with a new contact.<br /> <br /> It was about then that Rose noticed Bright Eyes wasn\u2019t coming down for food. I gently tried to gloss over her being out, but that just led to Rose getting worked up about Bright Eyes sleeping around. I didn\u2019t want any part of this lecture and fortunately a very perky Tavia swooped in to save me. Before Rose could reload, Tavia offhandedly mentioned that Trinh and Pilot Light got together last night. I do not know how she can be so smooth when she\u2019s so awkward other times, but I was in no position to complain. As the excitement for Trinh died down a little, Rose mentioned school and we all collectively realized that we have to move Leslie onto campus today. We\u2019re getting things loaded into Snowflake\u2019s car now, so I need to go. I have a feeling I\u2019m going to get another workout this afternoon.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, August 22, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I performed my tai chi meditations on the bluffs again this morning, and managed to get Karl to join me. He was a bit awkward, learning the proper stances and motions, but he took it seriously. We had fun, though. At one point when Karl made a particularly awkward mistake, he sort of smiled and laughed at himself, and I laughed too. Then he stopped, drew me close, and kissed me.<br /> <br /> I was not at all displeased with the kiss. I quite liked it. But I was surprised, so I asked Karl what it was for. And he said it was because I laughed. He liked it, and said I should do it more often. My heart melted a bit then, even as I realized that he\u2019s right. I don\u2019t laugh much. I can\u2019t even remember the last time I laughed before this morning. Richard used to make me laugh quite a lot. And when I\u2019m with Karl, I feel like I can laugh again. I suppose this must be love.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, August 22, 2010, Late Morning<br /> <br /> Over breakfast, the others discussed their clubbing adventures from last night. Natalie and Karen weren\u2019t at breakfast, so I don\u2019t know how their play was, though I imagine they had a wonderful time. Sara did not come home last night either, so I assumed she was with her girlfriend Eve, but apparently she left the club with someone named Cindy. Which is quite distressing, as I would hate to think the Sara was sleeping around and being unfaithful.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though, the others report that Trinh and Stephen have finally acknowledged their feelings for one another! They \u201chooked up\u201d at Murder Ballads last night! I\u2019m so glad that they finally listened to my encouragement and opened up to one another like that. I hope\u2026I think\u2026they\u2019ll be very happy together. And I\u2019m very happy for them. I will have to call Trinh and congratulate her!<br /> <br /> The other interesting bit of news is that Alexia and Chandra met a psychic at Gotham Citi. Her name is Catherine Callahan, and she was there searching for someone\u2019s brother. His name is Richie Abrams\u2014so it\u2019s not Rita\u2019s brother she\u2019s looking for, though that was my first thought. He used to frequent Gotham Citi before he disappeared. Alexia has invited Catherine to meet with Stanly since he probably knows Richie and tends to keep up with people fairly well, and she wants me to be there. We will go see him tomorrow during his daily visit to Lulu\u2019s Caf\u00e9.<br /> <br /> At the conclusion of breakfast, I reminded everyone that we had to move Leslie into her dorm today. I could tell from their reactions that everyone else had completely forgotten about it. The boys\u2014Doc, Karl and Grin\u2014made some manly grumbles about getting a workout this afternoon, but really, we\u2019re not moving any real furniture, just a a couple dozen boxes of Leslie\u2019s things, so I don\u2019t think it will be as strenuous as they\u2019re making it sound. Then again, Leslie seems quite a bit more materialistic than I am, so perhaps I\u2019m wrong.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 21st, 2010<br /> <br /> -Hm! What are the others up to?<br /> <br /> -Well, best not to ask. Best to demand answers tomorrow when I don\u2019t risk talking them out of it.<br /> <br /> -That was fun!<br /> <br /> -Mmmmmm toes\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> August 22nd, 2010<br /> <br /> -Man that was a hell of a night.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Time to interrogate Sara.<br /> <br /> -Ahem.<br /> <br /> -Wow Sara gets the ladies.<br /> <br /> -Sara and I are awesome.<br /> <br /> -Oh yes, taking Leslie to school.<br /> <br /> -Ah Albertus Magnus. Pretty campus.<br /> <br /> -Found all the buildings for @Nerak\u2019s classes.<br /> <br /> -Grin and Karl chumming around is hilarious.<br /> <br /> -I guess it isn\u2019t a surprise to anyone Karen isn\u2019t going to be living on campus\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> C\u2019mon Doc, only half the group was getting laid that night.<br /> <br /> The meet cute they set up was very much focused on the Passion Key, which has been snowballing somewhat as since Sara arrived both Simon and Natalie have picked it up. Once they got Pilot Light (Stephan is his real name) into a room with Trinh and Cindy, Simon used Passion Boneyard on the room and Sara used Passion Curse on Cindy, which combined to get people frisky (hence Tavia getting frisky with Simon). The Nightmare mentioned being Natalie\u2019s general aversion to supernatural mind control. Pilot Light rolled exceptionally well, with bonus dice, while Trinh\u2019s dice to resist were highly penalized and did poorly, so he did pretty well. As for Cindy, she went home with Sara, so despite her \u201cnot date\u201d going poorly (Trinh has, since dating Natalie, had a tendency to date women while not admitting it is a date or that she is less then straight according to Cindy). And Simon got Plasm from the exceptional successes and willpower spent, which was gravy for him. Passion Boneyard is crazy.<br /> <br /> As Simon has slept with Lauren, she was distracted from going in by pointing out Simon\u2019s violently jealous girlfriend was with him. As Tavia has something of a crazy look to her she followed.<br /> <br /> As an aside, it is fun for me how popular Pilot Light has been. A fairly minor NPC, he has been something of a surprise hit with the players, similar to Gyula V\u00e9g, The Sheriff in my <a href=\"http://forums.white-wolf.com/default.aspx?g=posts&amp;t=57061\" target=\"_blank\">Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a> Vampire: The Masquerade game. The picture is zany, and the character\u2019s tendency to notice supernatural horror and react simply in shock has been a staple. He\u2019s even shown up in a game I am playing in run by Simon\u2019s player (no AP yet), which rocks.<br /> <br /> So God Machine. The first ~hour was spent discussing this. It was quickly and unanimously decided we were not going to use beats or aspirations. Conditions got some discussion, but we decided given how long the game had gone it would be a big change. On the other hand, I think everyone was enthusiastic about changing Virtue/Vice to the new system, as the whole Virtues/Sins thing was never popular across the board. Though that does screw up mechanics for Tavia\u2019s paintings a little.<br /> <br /> We are tentatively looking at trying the new Combat and Social Combat systems, and systems for Spirits. Mostly people are self-policing on powers getting them in line with the new system. Also, discovered the stats for M1A1 pistol vary wildly between books, and by some systems Natalie should be unable to fire it accurately. This was fixed by making Nataliebane a new gun with essentially the same stats (it exists). Now we just have to see about how to adapt powers.<br /> <br /> Whelp, that is a whole lot of commentary right there. Your comments and questions are welcome too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:14:03-08:00","id":17016,"title":"","content":"pologies for the delay, here is our accounts of the last Geist session. It was a dangerous one!<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1600 Hours, Sunday, August 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that wasn\u2019t nearly as bad as I was afraid it might be. Granted having Karl there to help with the big lifting and stairs was great. I didn\u2019t notice Leslie getting any odd looks or anyone seeming to recognize us. In a weird way, that gave me hope for her. No preconceived notions, no shadowed reputation, just a teenager starting college. And one with local family to help her out. I\u2019ll be the first one to remind her that she\u2019ll dig her own hole if she does something supernaturally stupid, but that doesn\u2019t mean she can\u2019t make normal mistakes. It\u2019s just nice to see that she might get a fair shake without being swallowed by Ziporrah\u2019s shadow.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re getting ready for our final push into Glenwood. The town is suffering from a blackness it didn\u2019t create. And it\u2019s our responsibility to lead it out of that darkness. That\u2019s what hope is about. And this time, I don\u2019t intend on coming back until hope has returned to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0030 Hours, Monday, August 23, 2010<br /> <br /> When our Krewe was founded, we all knew, to our very soul, that we must protect the World from Outsiders. Not one of us has ever doubted this. It is not just the right thing to do, it is our sacred duty. Never have I been more positive in this than tonight.<br /> <br /> Because we are paranoid, we agreed as a Krewe that Snowflake should stay behind to make sure the Gentry didn\u2019t make another move on the House. With Snowflake at the helm, the House is a battleship anyway. Because of this, we taught Bright Eyes the binding ritual so someone else would know how to deal with things if I went down. Chandra insisted on coming as just her vampiric head, but we did not need to take Lily. With that agreed, we made our plans.<br /> <br /> Nightshade would handle Boneyard duties to help with sneaking and dulling perceptions. Tavia and Rose would sneak down into the cellar to bind the Gulmoth into her painting. Cupcake, Bright Eyes, and I would be waiting for the signal to come in through the front and lay waste to the abominations of Outsider taint within. Because Nightshade and I would be leaving our bodies in state (I was going in as the Dog of War), Chandra stayed in the car to act as our protector. Once inside, we decided Bright Eyes would initially handle casting the binding ritual to trap the Qlipoth in the Onyx Prison. Depending on how things went, I could assist or take over as needed. That left me to destroy as much of the other things inside as possible unless or until I was otherwise needed. Rose would also make sure Tavia was either safe or could get out with the painting. That covered as many possibilities as we could anticipate. Nightshade and Bright Eyes drove so we could carry everyone, Chandra\u2019s head, the painting, and Tavia\u2019s easel. We left just before 2100 Hours.<br /> <br /> We drove over to Glenwood without any trouble. Once we got into town, we saw two different places with downed power lines, both near the lodge. When we got out, we noticed it was also very windy. It was very dark everywhere, either because of the taint in the area or because of the power lines we weren\u2019t completely sure. That only served to remind us that everything around us had been affected but the Outsider, even the light. Tavia and Rose get their gear while Nightshade slipped into her trance. I moved between buildings and unlocked my Phantasmal Marionette. I\u2019m not sure if it was because of how serious the problem was, how bad I needed a fight, or if the Dog of War just approved, but when my consciousness flowed through the plasm into the Dog\u2019s form, something was different. We were more in sync and connected than I remember. It wasn\u2019t as taxing on me to do it, first of all, but also I realized I was able to boost myself, stronger, faster, tougher. I could feel the plasm surge through my muscles, tightening like steel. When I unlocked my Primeval Shroud, there too, I found my protection to be that much better. I came back from the side of the building carrying my body and crouched behind the cars with the others. Even on our fours, I was taller than the vehicles but I slid my body into the seat and took the ear curl. Now I was ready.<br /> <br /> We waited outside while Tavia and Rose slipped into the cellar. I wasn\u2019t sure how long Tavia might need for the painting so we needed to be prepared. After about 10 minutes or so, I could tell Rose was dealing with something. After a moment of heavier breathing, Rose informed us that the Gulmoth was trapped in the painting. They were securing Tavia and then told us to be ready to enter in 30 seconds. I moved to the door and silently counted down. When I hit 30, my foot shattered the door like toothpicks and we rushed in. I heard a crashing sound somewhere toward the back of the house. The hallways were weird and sound moved oddly, but we charged in at top speed. When we found Rose, she was dealing with three of the skin dolls. Cupcake hacked into one of the dolls attacking Rose with her cleaver. Louisa was on her knees next to a desk. She looked like she took a shot to the head, so I focused on one of the two dolls still in the crib. My anger at this blasphemous house ignited as I threw my hand like a major league pitcher. The white hot ghost flames of my rage incinerated the doll on impact. Based on the sudden flailing, I guessed that Nightshade had blinded Louisa. Before I could move to finish her, a zombie tore through the wall. Easily not something we expected, but zombies aren\u2019t really shocking to us. Unfortunately, all the noise roused the Qlipoth. The last doll in the crib launched itself at Rose, but missed and hit the wall like something out of the Muppets. Bright eyes got her stuff arranged and began casting the ritual while all three of the other dolls managed to flail at Rose. Louisa did something and started to heal herself. That was not good. Cupcake chopped one the dolls on Rose in half, assumedly killing or dispersing whatever animated it. I lit Louisa up and did more than a little bruise. I wasn\u2019t sure how she was healing, but it was a fair guess that searing burns would slow that down. Another of the dolls missed Rose as did the zombie. Then the Qlipoth did something and I could feel an odd shift in Rose. I wasn\u2019t sure what it was but I didn\u2019t like it. I started to move toward Rose when another of the dolls sailed past me. I growled, clearly not in the mood. When I glanced back, Rose had managed to use Tai Chi to get a hold on Louisa and slammed her head into that same desk. I heard the crack of her skull before the woman collapsed into a limp pile. I knew immediately her life was slipping away. There was no way Rose was going to deal well with this, no matter how certain she was of her actions. I didn\u2019t have time to think about it any longer as the three dolls suddenly behaved more like frenzied animals. One threw itself at Rose, though she was able to slap it aside. Cupcake sliced into another one, drawing some of the attention herself. I sent whipped a flame lash into the Qlipoth, trying to keep its attention off Rose. Unfortunately, one of the dwindling dolls did manage to catch Rose. I couldn\u2019t really tell how bad it might have been because right after that, the Qlipoth screamed. It was like rending sheet metal, the terrified screams of frightened children, the firing of jet engines, and the moans of the dying all meshed together. I felt my determination weaken, which was not something I was use to being aware of. Rose called over the ear curls that she might have to leave if that kept up. Another of the dolls missed as she said as much. I realized that without her determination, I\u2019m not sure how much of herself Rose could be. I blasted another doll and charred its form, but it still fought on. Cupcake sliced into that same one and finished it off. One of the other dolls jumped off the desk next to which Louisa lay, but Rose snatched it from the air and smashed its disturbing ceramic head on the desk. Another doll latched onto me, though my Shroud armored me from all but a minor bruise. I did realize that this damned things had jagged teeth though. They were biting Rose whenever they attacked. That was not good. Nightshade offered to deafen Rose through the ear curl to help in case of the scream. She agreed just as the zombie mimicked the dolls and launched itself at Rose. Her reflexes and Tai Chi helped the corpse go wide. The zombie found itself impaled on the well used writing desk. The humor of the moment was ripped away as the Qlipoth screamed again. Again I felt my resolve crack, but not break. I hurled another fireball into the Outsider, searing it. Cupcake missed her target as the doll rolled aside to face Rose. This was the last remaining doll and it meant to end Rose. Nightshade deafened Bright Eyes to help protect her from the screams as well. The doll managed to bite Rose, but it couldn\u2019t break the skin. Apparently Bright Eyes had gotten somewhere with the ritual as even after lighting it on fire twice, the Qlipoth tried to do something. Fortunately, it didn\u2019t seem to have any effect. I pointed at the zombie and watched as my ghost flames flared on its dead flesh. Cupcake brought her cleaver down on the scored flesh and left a wide space from the shoulder to the third rib. Rose and the final doll entered what can only be described as a brawl. They traded punches and bites respectively, with Rose keeping the upperhand. Just then, Tavia ran in carrying the painting...but she was different. Her thin frame was elongated, her skin darkened to pitch and seemed to be slippery. I realized that she had become a Brineborn and resembled a Viperfish. That realization had only entered my mind when the huge cloud of black flies followed her into the hallway. She paused as she saw our combat, but Rose ordered her to flee. The zombie tore itself from the desk and missed Rose again, almost punctuating her command. Tavia wisely retreated.<br /> <br /> By that point, I realized the madness inherent in the ritual as well as that caused by the Qlipoth was taking its toll on Bright Eyes. I abandoned my assault to go and help her. The Qlipoth was still trying to affect her but it didn\u2019t seem to work that time. As the sound of the final doll being crushed on the Desk of Doom echoed behind me and Tavia\u2019s exit from the front door signaled the all clear, I began the ritual as well. Unfortunately, I didn\u2019t notice the zombie flailing at me, so he thumped me in the back. Not really any damage other than a sore spot, but Cupcake drew its attention with another chop of her cleaver. The cloud of flies that chased Tavia out buzzed angrily back in and dove into Bright Eyes. She was covered much like the man in the shop. Her chanting and cast was stifled by flies flying into her eyes and down her throat. I knew there was nothing I could do for her so I continued to cast the ritual. After all, if we failed to trap the Qlipoth, flies would be the least of our problems. As if realizing the same thought, the Qlipoth opened itself in an attempt to pull everything into the Void. Cupcake struggled to resist the strength of the pull, but managed to grab the Desk of Doom at the last moment. Nothing, including the zombie was pulled in. Either we were entirely lucky or this was a really terrible Gate. Rose turned into a murder of crows to devour the flies and try to help Bright Eyes. I didn\u2019t really want to find out if the Qlipoth could do that again or not. I felt the zombie miss me again but when I turned to look at it, I saw Cupcake chop her cleaver the rest of the way through. Sans zombie. Sadly it was finally all too much for Bright Eyes. As I returned my concentration to the ritual, I heard her to the side make a squeak, flailed a little, and then puked flies. I could have done without that, but it\u2019ll be better for her later. There was something building in the air as I continued the ritual. It was like a pressure change mixed with static charge. I had no way of knowing if that was a good thing or not, but the Qlipoth seemed to have stopped so I kept going. Then the cloud of flies started to disperse. Before I could think about it very hard, the Onyx Prison opened one of its drawers and the Qlipoth was sucked in.<br /> <br /> After a moment of everyone looking around to make sure we were all still here and nothing else was coming for us, I allowed myself to exhale. Rose reformed as herself and Bright Eyes ran outside. Rose and Cupcake decided to take the Desk of Doom with us as it must surely be a charm. I took the Onyx Prison out to the cars then went back in. With the desk out, nothing remained of any usefulness. The bodies didn\u2019t need to be examined for our own benefit and no one needed to see those dolls. Louisa\u2019s body, and her state of filth before we got involved, added another layer of Charlie Manson to the scene. I looked around and found a piece of the shattered door big enough to touch both the inside of the house wherever it stood and the outside which was still in Glenwood. Using my Pyre-Flame Rage, I lit the fragment and made sure both houses started to burn. Then I stepped over the flames and slowly walked back to the car. I didn\u2019t need to see the fire consume the house. It was made of my anger. I knew what I\u2019d see.<br /> <br /> Cupcake and Nightshade drove home. Bright Eyes was visually disturbed while Rose stayed very quiet and distant the whole ride back. It was right around midnight when we got back to Dark Haven Bluffs. I knew that both my Krewemates had suffered psychological trauma. I also knew that Rose would need time before she could even realize something was wrong. In the meantime, I took a bottle of peroxide up and knocked on the door to Bright Eyes\u2019 room. I didn\u2019t mess with small talk. I just held out the bottle and told her to gargle. Eventually that and time might help. But it was a small gesture to remind her there were others there if she needed us. Now I\u2019m going to go and see if I can find Karl. He\u2019ll need to be prepared for what\u2019s to come.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, August 22, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really feel like writing right now, but I cannot sleep, so I think perhaps it is best that I record the events of tonight while they are still fresh in my mind<br /> <br /> I killed another person tonight.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been involved in situations where other krewe members have killed people: the Ivory Coast, our fight against the werewolves. And I have killed supernatural entities before. But I have never personally killed another human being. And even though it was necessary, I\u2019m still quite shaken.<br /> <br /> The krewe went to Glenwood to deal with the Abyssal threat there tonight, though we decided that Simon should remain at the manor in case the Gentry or his servants decided to show up again. We arrived at the mages\u2019 lodge with Tavia and her painting. Natalie remained in the car and entered a Boneyard trance in order to muffle the perceptions of those in the lodge so that Tavia and I could sneak in to trap the pestilential beast in the cellar. Then we would deal with Louisa, the maddened mage and the Qliphoth.<br /> <br /> Tavia and I were able to slip through the house, past Louisa and her dolls, and into the cellar, though Tavia had some difficulty even with Natalie\u2019s help. Fortunately, I was carrying the painting, which was rendered invisible by my shroud of Stillness.<br /> <br /> Simply being in that pitch dark, fetid cellar was enough to leave one sickened and weak, but we both sensed that somewhere in the lightless chamber there lurked the horrible beast we had come to trap. It was bad enough seeing Tavia\u2019s rendition of it; I had no desire to see it in person, so I was thankful for the darkness.<br /> <br /> I stood ready to intercept the beast as Tavia began her ritual, and when it realized that she was there, it lurched from the darkness toward her, only to encounter me instead. I blocked its approach, and over the next few moments, we fought, though I was simply trying to distract it. The heightened senses granted by my Primeval caul helped me avoid most of its blows, for I couldn\u2019t see anything, and the tattered veils of my shroud protected me when it did land a blow.<br /> <br /> I only had to distract the beast for a few moments, and then Tavia and her painting did their work. With a buzzing moan, the beast was torn from this world and imprisoned in the painting.<br /> <br /> Tavia and I moved back upstairs, and I told her to remain safe with the painting in the room above the cellar while the krewe dealt with Louisa and the Qliphoth. She agreed, and I let the others know that I was moving in to deal with Louisa so they would be ready to attack.<br /> <br /> Still invisible, I moved into the filthy room in which Louisa sat at a small writing desk, surrounded by her skin-swaddled dolls. I gave her absolutely no warning as I suddenly grabbed the back of her head and slammed her face into the desk, breaking her nose and leaving her stunned.<br /> <br /> The dolls were immediately alert, but they had no one to attack until I swept Louisa\u2019s chair out from under her and twisted her into the floor. The bones of her arm cracked as I twisted it behind her, but in the process, I became visible again. The dolls threw themselves at me, trying to tear my flesh with their gnashing teeth, and though I tried to move in harmony with their attacks, a couple of them still hit me. My shroud protected me, but I knew I would not be able to withstand the dolls indefinitely.<br /> <br /> Fortunately Doc kicked open the lodge\u2019s front door then and destroyed one of the dolls in an eruption of fire as he unleashed his Pyre-flame Rage upon it. Alexia and Sara followed him in. Sara quickly cleared a portion of the floor and began setting up the binding ritual, while Alexia rushed in and began hacking away at the dolls with her cleavers and knives.<br /> <br /> Natalie did something to strike Louisa blind, which might have kept her from attacking me with her magic, but it did not keep her from healing herself. I could hear the broken bones in her arm knitting, and she started to force herself to her feet, so I pulled her from the floor and smashed her against the wall next to the door to the back room. That\u2019s when the door burst open and a corpse clawed its way into the room. It was the body slumped over the table in the back room\u2014the one I noticed when we first investigated the place. It tried to strike me with its rotting fists, but I easily twisted out of the way as I flung Louisa against the writing desk, where she fell to her knees.<br /> <br /> She struggled to get up, but then Doc blasted her with more fire and she screamed in pain, falling again to her knees. That\u2019s when the Qliphoth emerged. It\u2019s all-encompassing darkness began to drain the light from the room, and as I glanced at it, I saw something in the endless void inside it that unnerved me. I felt my resolve slipping, but stubbornly steeled myself and returned my attention to Louisa. We had to end this, quickly, before the Qliphoth unhinged our minds completely.<br /> <br /> Again I grabbed Louisa\u2019s still-healing arm and wrenched her shoulder out of joint as I slammed her head into the corner of the writing desk. This time, I heard the sickening crunch of breaking bone, and when I released her, Louisa\u2019s body slumped limply to the ground, dead.<br /> <br /> It was not until later that the impact of that moment hit me.<br /> <br /> Doc attacked the Qliphoth to draw its attention, but it quickly realized that Sara was the real threat. The thing began screaming, and each of its metallic shrieks sent a bone-chilling wave of uncertainty through us, weakening our will. I could tell that Sara was losing her mind, and I realized that if it screamed just once more, even I might not be able to keep my wits about me. Thankfully, Natalie caught on to our distress and used her Boneyard to deafen Sara and me so that we could no longer hear the soul-shattering screams.<br /> <br /> The dolls continued attacking me, though they were largely a nuisance, and I was also easily able to avoid the zombie\u2019s clumsy blows. Alexia came to my assistance, and together we destroyed the rest of the dolls. Doc worked with Alexia to lay the zombie to rest as well.<br /> <br /> As the ritual neared completion, the door to the cellar burst open and Tavia ran out with her painting. She was in her fishgirl form, and though I had seen her like that before, the others were surprised. She was pursued by a cloud of flies. When Tavia saw how much we were struggling against the Qliphoth, she hesitated until I shouted at her to flee. Fortunately, she listened.<br /> <br /> The cloud of flies swarmed around Sara, though, trying to fill her nose and mouth and eyes in order to stop the ritual. She was coughing and gagging, barely able to finish the binding incantation. I was scared that the flies might get the best of her, so I did the only thing I could think to do. I transformed into a flock of crows and began fluttering throughout the room, eating as many of the flies as possible. Several of my crows landed on Sara, delicately snatching the flies directly from her face and eyes. The experience was unpleasant for both of us, but it granted Sara the respite she needed to finish the ritual.<br /> <br /> The Qliphoth screamed a terrible scream that left our ears bleeding as it was drawn into the Obsidian Box. Poor Sara spent the next few minutes retching. Alexia went to comfort her, and as soon as the flies dispersed, I returned to my human form to help get Sara back on her feet and out to the car. Meanwhile, Doc set the lodge aflame both inside and out. The place was so tainted that it needed to burn. Before we left, though, Alexia and I took the writing desk and stowed it into the back of her car. It may sound cold, but the desk is now infused with death and could become a charm, largely because of how Louisa met her end. Perhaps it will help me find some deeper meaning in killing her.<br /> <br /> We returned to the mansion and spent a good, long time cleaning up, then went our separate ways to occupy ourselves for the evening. I\u2019m certain that everyone was eager to forget the events of the day. I found my will restored by our triumph. The fact that we did not back off even when it seemed our minds were at risk gave me a confirming sense of accomplishment, and has done a bit to help me come to terms with the fact that I killed someone.<br /> <br /> Rationally, I know that Louisa had to die. She was too far gone, too tainted, and too dangerous to let live. But I am still haunted by the sound of her skull cracking, by the sight of blood oozing from the side of her head, pooling in the floor like a twisted halo. I feel cold and dead inside, or rather, I feel like a part of me has died.<br /> <br /> The worst of it, perhaps, is that I know that I could do it again. I\u2019ve tried to steel my resolve so that if necessary, I can take measures like these. I\u2019m fulfilling my fate as the Resolution of Death within the krewe. But that doesn\u2019t make me feel any better. Indeed, it makes me feel even colder. I\u2019ve lost the last vestiges of my innocence. I don\u2019t\u2026like this part of me.<br /> <br /> I retired to my room after cleaning up. I didn\u2019t even go see Karl. He came by awhile ago, but I sadly told him I\u2019d rather be alone. He seemed worried, but left me alone without any argument. I don\u2019t mean to hurt his feelings, but I don\u2019t want to be with anyone right now. I simply feel so wretched.<br /> Lily wanted to cheer me up, but I told her I wasn\u2019t in the mood. Still, I hugged her tightly as I curled up on my bed and tried to sleep. Wrapping her in my arms gave me something to hold on to, something stable to keep me from going a little mad over what I\u2019ve done and what it means for me.<br /> <br /> I suppose I should try again to get some sleep.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Power Down</u><br /> <br /> On our way to the mage lodge in Glenwood, we noticed two power lines down. I don\u2019t know if that is significant or not; hopefully it was simply a manifestation of the increasing distortions in that place, which we have now cleansed. I have no desire to visit Glenwood again any time soon.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> August 22nd, 2010<br /> <br /> Oh Goddess are we doing this tonight? Ick.<br /> <br /> -I guess so<br /> <br /> -Odd<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up<br /> <br /> -Heading out, to adventure.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Cindy is messaging Sara? Already?<br /> <br /> -She did not try to hook up with ME the very next night. Hrm.<br /> <br /> -I am not sure how I feel about this.<br /> <br /> -Eyes on the prize!<br /> <br /> -Radio Silence<br /> <br /> -Ew. Ew EW EW EW EW ew ew ew EW<br /> <br /> -I did not even go in there and I still feel awful.<br /> <br /> -Spooky and Sara are really quiet.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t think most of us feel good.<br /> <br /> -Something fishy with Tavia<br /> <br /> -(rimshot)<br /> <br /> -Is Sara off for a booty call after that??<br /> <br /> -Gotta say something to Karen, then going away for the night.<br /> <br /> -Goddess\u2026I don\u2019t want to see anything when I sleep<br /> <br /> -clean<br /> <br /> -sleep<br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Simon\u2019s player had to miss, hence the (admittedly odd) decision to leave him at home.<br /> <br /> Stillness Boneyard proved incredibly helpful, both for boosting Tavia\u2019s stealth and the blinding and deafening abilities. The Qlippoth was able to drain willpower to attack minds directly, and only that kept Jasmine (who spends Willpower like water) and Sara from going mad. It could do an all affecting drain of one or a resisted targeted drain of successes.<br /> <br /> Sara did pick up a phobia of flies.<br /> <br /> The GMC combat rules held up. Jasmine is a beast under them, and were it not for the magic attacks could possibly have held her own against most of the room herself, and pretty much anyone who got hit had the armor to reduce everything to a Bashing level. Sin-Eaters are clearly immensely tough under GMC. We are working on Virtues/Vices. Some, Doc for example, are staying mostly the same. Looking at a new Virtue for Jasmine (to represent her steadfastness) and Alexia (for her optimism) and Vice for Natalie (to represent her need to be needed and have attention paid to her).<br /> <br /> We will get it settled when we have Simon\u2019s player there. In the meantime, missed the session last night due to I not being in town, so no new session journal in 2 weeks. Will see if I can have something, but no promises. In the meantime comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:16:13-08:00","id":17018,"title":"","content":"There was no Geist last time due to vacation related hijinx. However, I do have a small something to tide you over until the next full update in two weeks.<br /> <br /> <b>Relationships</b><br /> <br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Oh hey mom<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Hey Natalie, how goes<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: OK, they want me to go to school or something.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: I know right? When is your first day?<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Next week.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: cool, cool<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: So I wanted to tell you something. We have not announced it, so you are hearing early.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Cool!<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Karen has proposed, and I accepted. So we will get married<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Awesome!<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: So now I have 3 moms!<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: I am kinda scared<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: No you have one mom. Me. I am your mother.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: and a dad*<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: you have a mother, a stepmother soon, and a grandmother. But I am your mother.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: OK, OK<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: No one can take that from me.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: I will be invited right?<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Of course.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: You wearing a gown<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Yes<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Is Karen<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Undecided. She keeps changing her mind. I am fine either way.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: So when will the announcement be? I wanna know when to say something.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: I do not know. When Doc can handle it without getting upset.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: What is wrong with Doc?<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: He is upset. I sadly can\u2019t really help him.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Is he upset with you?<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Sorta, not really. He is not angry with me exactly.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: But you are worried enough about him to wait.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: Yes.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: He means that much to me.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: OK<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: I don\u2019t know how to follow that up.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: It will work out. I really want to heal my friendship with Doc, but I don\u2019t know how.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: I am sure you will think of something.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: I hope so. But this will wait. Karen knows. She knows how important Doc is to me.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: I guess she is not crazy about it.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: No but she understands.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Good<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: But you are OK mom?<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: I am\u2026at peace. I will be better when Doc is better<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Good<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: You know, you should talk to grandmom.<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: She wants to talk to you.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark: What?<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Talk to mom<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: Grandma*<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: She wants to talk you.<br /> WhiplashGirlChildintheDark has left the chat<br /> <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#3975564f5c74407456565d40791d1d031717177f4c5a52\">LoveMyMoody@$$:...Fuck</a><br /> Itsmejulie has joined the chat<br /> Itsmejulie: Hello?<br /> Itsmejulie: Allison?<br /> LoveMyMoody@$$: She left mom<br /> Itsmejulie: I love You Allison<br /> Itsmejulie: oh<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Will see you in two weeks. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:17:53-08:00","id":17019,"title":"","content":"So the last bit to finish up the Glenwood stuff has been this session. Let\u2019s see what the Krewe has been up to<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1645 Hours, Monday, August 23, 2010<br /> <br /> I felt better this morning than I have for a while. I knew getting the Qlipoth out of Glenwood was an absolute must. Going out with Snowflake after everyone else was settled in to grab a little Plasm didn\u2019t hurt either. But when I prepared to center myself this morning, I had no idea how<br /> simple it would be. It was as though I had a well tended garden to walk through. Wonderful babbling brooks on either side, daisies and petunias lining the banks, all leading me to an open circle in the center of a silent grove.<br /> <br /> When I opened my eyes, I was so at peace I could have had a debate with Erin about the concept of boundaries and jurisdiction. Okay, that peace wouldn\u2019t last long, but I was in a much better place. I came down to breakfast much earlier than usual and found Snowflake there as well. He said he wanted to ask about coming to work with me today, but was a little concern at the connotations it might have. I told him as long as he didn\u2019t have anything important to ask me, I was probably fine. The nervous tension in the room broke at that point and everyone was amused. Snowflake said he\u2019d like to come and learn about some of the herbs I sell, as today is Study Day in Dark Haven Bluffs. I was more than okay with that so again, I didn\u2019t need to call a cab or walk. Since I knew he wasn\u2019t interested in working in the shop, I mainly went over what occult properties I knew for my various offerings. When I had customers he would quiz himself on what I had explained and ask questions once I returned. He also helped me figure something out that has annoyed me for a while. Two different times with different people, a guy came in and in the lamest attempt at being sneaky ever, asked about \u201cbuying \u2018herb.\u2019\u201d This happens at the beginning of every semester and occasionally other times, but always right when school starts. I knew it was dumb college kids, and I always very politely explain I don\u2019t sell illicit or controlled substances...the first time. If they push it, I either sell them an ounce of Mexican Oregano from the back at 400% mark up or throw them out. Snowflake asked why I didn\u2019t just sell what I had on the floor to them, and I explained the secretive behavior and the margin increase. He was notably impressed I think. He also suggested that maybe it was a fraternity hazing ritual. I had never considered it before, but it all made perfect sense. Fortunately for them, I don\u2019t know which frat it is. When we were slow, I drew again while Snowflake used one of his memorization techniques to keep track of all the herbs. Leslie came in at 1600 Hours so I went over the closing with her again. Having Snowflake there probably didn\u2019t hurt, but she really seemed okay with everything that needed to happen. If I hear interest back from Elsie and Trinh, I\u2019ll hopefully only need to come in a few times a week just to make sure the ordering is maintained. Part of me is excited to get this new free time. Another part of me is scared to let go. With all that in my head, Snowflake took me back to the Bluffs. We talked about our Krewe\u2019s very unique methods and dubbed the recent use of Napalm a tactic of our own Aggressive Reconnaissance, or Agg Recon.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m just waiting for dinner and hopefully a good report from Leslie.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1945 Hours, Monday, August 23, 2010<br /> <br /> After Leslie finished dinner, we shifted conversation back to business. Rose was more irritated about this than other things she wants to be finished. I suspected that her reactions to last night were slowly beginning to manifest. I\u2019m glad I already talked to Karl about this. But the plan is to get everyone plus Tavia and her painting back out to the Puppeteer warehouse. There we can get set up and be prepared before we let the Gulmoth out of the painting. We still have a little while before time to leave, but this is the best option we have. Hopefully I\u2019ll still feel that way when we get back.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2330 Hours, Monday, August 23, 2010<br /> <br /> That was a very different fight than we were expecting. It went well, so no complaints I guess.<br /> <br /> When we arrived, a man who was very drunk and really unwashed staggered over. In an incredibly garbled soliloquy, he told us the place was very bad. Then he nodded sagely and shambled off. Snowflake decided not to waste another opportunity to Boneyard. He said he couldn\u2019t see anything, but there was a bad resonance, even beyond the evil taint of the Outsider. Nightshade checked for spirits and did not like what she saw. The place was crawling with spirits. The bulk of them were either Child spirits or Death spirits. At least a few seemed to Nightshade to be both. But spirits are not our department and being inside a hostile werewolf pack\u2019s territory is not the place to branch out.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes did not want to have to see the human fly so she carved open her arm and bled out a homunculus. Nightshade animated Clyde to make sure someone was between her and the Gulmoth. Rose fell into a column of spiders which then webbed up the entire area so that no flies could come to assist. Bright Eyes blindfolded herself to keep from crumbling in terror during the fight. Bright Eyes\u2019 little blood self and Clyde would take the painting into the main room and wreck the image. The webs would keep out the flies. Then we would move in and destroy the Gulmoth.<br /> <br /> Rose took on her Shark woman form after reassembling all the spiders, while I unleashed the Dog of War again. Once little Bloody Bright Eyes and Clyde were ready, we got started. Clyde chopped the painting only twice with the fire axe before it vomited out its festering contents. Bright Eyes changed her Caul and her homunculus collapsed into a puddle. Nightshade opened with pistol fire which the Gulmoth had very little protection against. We all then took a turn beating, tearing, chopping, and clawing at it. We didn\u2019t get very far for a while and even as slow as it was, it was still able to attack us once it realized what was happening. Rose was the first to be hit, though it was only a bruise. Snowflake did something terrible as the Gulmoth suffered unseen damage and seemed to almost start to drop pieces of itself off. Though blindfolded, Bright Eyes used the sounds the creature made to pinpont her target and stabbed its fleshy folds with her dagger. Clyde turned his axe skills on the Outsider as Nightshade shot it again. I managed to slice into it with my own claws, but still the human fly continued. Then Cupcake came from behind and buried her cleaver in its head, somewhere around the stump. At that moment, the Gulmoth just faded out like fog at night. It is finally over. For now.<br /> We\u2019ve just gotten back home and I\u2019m sure there will be ice cream for celebration. Now maybe we can actually get this wedding planned, since it is coming up in a few weeks. Oh, and Snowflake and I can work on the van.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, August 23, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> I slept fitfully last night, and woke earlier than usual. Lily was a bit distressed, and even Fu seemed unhappy. I went to the cliff to try and center myself through meditative tai chi, but found it difficult. A sense of unease borne from my actions yesterday has followed me all day. Jean noticed during our training session, and asked if I was all right. I told him I was fine, just tired. What else could I say?<br /> <br /> After breakfast this morning, we discussed our plans to finish the Abyssal thing trapped in Tavia\u2019s painting. I insisted that we summon and destroy it tonight. Perhaps I was a bit pushy; the others were not in such a hurry to get rid of the beast, though they certainly agreed on the necessity of doing so soon. But I wanted to put the troubles in Glenwood behind us. I\u2019m still coming to terms with the fact that I killed someone, and though I know I can accept it as a part of who I am now, I am troubled by the coldness overcoming me. We all deal with these things in different ways. Doc nurses a deep anger because of the carnage he has seen and inflicted. Simon analyzes his own guilt over the murders he has committed. And I grow cold and distant.<br /> <br /> Karl is concerned. I know he feels helpless, but he is giving me my space. He truly is a wonderful, sensitive man, and I\u2019m grateful to have him. But I can\u2019t bring myself to confide in him yet.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 23, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> I visited Stanly with Alexia and her psychic friend Catherine Callahan. Stanly was quite happy to see us, though he did not know much about Richie, the young man Catherine is trying to find. Stanly could only tell us that he saw Evan Callum spending time with Richie. Evan is John Callum\u2019s older brother (and John Callum is the boy Elsie was interested in and is now dating). Stanly did not know whether Evan and Richie were a couple or just friends, but at least we were able to provide Catherine with another lead.<br /> <br /> Stanly could sense that I was deeply troubled. He did not ask what was wrong, but as I sat beside him during our conversation, he quietly placed a comforting hand on mine. It is amazing how the simple touch of a friend can make such a difference.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, August 23, 2010, Late Afternoon<br /> <br /> It is done. The foetid beast from Glenwood is dead.<br /> <br /> We decided to summon and fight it in the abandoned warehouse where we first fought the Puppetmaster, as the location is isolated, quiet and unlikely to attract much attention. As we prepared, the others kept discussing and planning how we were going to handle the fight, and I confess that I became quite impatient with them. I simply wanted to get it over with, and it felt as though it took us hours to finally settle on a confused plan and then depart for the warehouse. I suppose my mental state is to blame for my agitation. I\u2019m normally much calmer about these things, though my sense of resolve does sometimes make me impatient.<br /> <br /> As we approached the warehouse, we were accosted by a half-mad homeless man who warned us away. He seemed spooked by something, and so Simon allowed himself to sink into a Boneyard trance, where he saw that the warehouse had become the haunt of numerous spirits, all of them mournful, child-like things. The place is spiritually corrupt, and our actions tonight cannot have helped. But the spirits did not interfere with us, so we went ahead with our plan.<br /> <br /> Before we released the beast, I donned my Primeval Caul and transformed into a swarm of spiders. I crawled through every crack of the building, sealing every last hole and opening with thick webs so that the Abyssal beast could not summon clouds of flies to plague us. Any who arrived would be trapped, and indeed, my webs were full when we left the place. Once that was done, I returned to my normal shark-like Caul form in preparation for the fight.<br /> <br /> Natalie animated her zombie servant and Sara constructed a sort of doll made of her own blood. Together, the two of them destroyed the painting, releasing the beast and distracting it briefly while the rest of us surrounded it and attacked. Most of us were able to shake off the mind-wrenching horror of its appearance, but Sara chose to blindfold herself, fearing the effect its fly-like features would have on her fragile psyche after yesterday\u2019s fight.<br /> <br /> I will say little about the battle except that it took nothing short of the entire krewe to best the beast. It was not exceptionally dangerous to us\u2014not with the defenses we could muster. But it was very tough, and it took everything we had to kill it.<br /> <br /> I had hoped that killing the beast and ending the plague on Glenwood would give me a sort of solace, but it did not. I was relieved to be done with the outsiders there, and I just want to forget it all as soon as I can. But I\u2019m still troubled by the things I\u2019ve learned about myself in all of this. I need time, I suppose, to come to terms with it. Fortunately, there is little demanding the krewe\u2019s urgent attention right now, and the semester has just started, with new classes to teach, so maybe we can take a break for a few weeks. I think I need that.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes<br /> </u><br /> <u>Wedding Date</u><br /> <br /> Chandra and Alexia\u2019s wedding is set for Saturday, September 25th. Natalie will be performing the ceremony, Lily is to be the flower girl, and Alexia has asked me to be the Maid of Honor. I\u2019m quite touched. I believe that Doc will be giving Alexia away, as Alexia is estranged from her parents. I\u2019m very excited, and I hope that such a happy occasion will do much to lift the krewe\u2019s spirits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>New Schedule</u><br /> <br /> Albertus Magnus College has renewed my contract to train Jean professionally, so I will continue to work with him for a few hours each day. He has entered a few upcoming college swim meets, one of which is only a couple of weeks from now, so I will likely be spending extra time getting him ready.<br /> <br /> I also have two other classes to teach on Tuesday and Thursday afternoons, keeping me on campus until almost 5:00 on those days. I shall be quite busy over the next couple of weeks. I do hope I have good students this semester.<br /> <i><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</i><br /> <br /> August 23rd, 2010<br /> <br /> -Feel like hell, must get ladyfriend to school.<br /> <br /> -This is both oddly fun and a little creepy, taking your girlfriend to school.<br /> <br /> -School=College<br /> <br /> -Jeez<br /> <br /> -Gonna nap in case people get ambitious.<br /> <br /> -Ah good, people are here. Need to talk to Sara.<br /> <br /> -She said almost exactly everything I was afraid she was going to say.<br /> <br /> -Damnit<br /> <br /> -Sigh<br /> <br /> -I do not know what to do that will not make this situation worse.<br /> <br /> -I feel like I should do something<br /> <br /> -Mind powers are bad.<br /> <br /> -She did not lie to me, that counts for something.<br /> <br /> -Maybe<br /> <br /> -I\u2019d be less hostile if they had not involved me.<br /> <br /> -Certain people are already a little nuts without having their minds played with.<br /> <br /> -Hrm.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Of course, even after last night\u2019s trauma, people want to go fight the last monster<br /> <br /> -Of course<br /> <br /> -Even Sara, which is odd.<br /> <br /> -Doc and Jasmine less so.<br /> <br /> -RISE FROM YOUR GRAVE<br /> <br /> -Power Mwa ha ha ha ha!<br /> <br /> -Sara\u2019s behavior would be more intriguing if I did not know she had just the other day tricked me into helping her do bad things to people\u2019s minds.<br /> <br /> -So not working. Not tonight.<br /> <br /> -OK here we go<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -ooooooooooooooooooooookkkkkkkkk<br /> <br /> -OK radio silence<br /> <br /> -Well, that could have gone worse\u2026.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> End Session LXXXV</i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add. The fight was not easy, but manageable. Their reactions to the bum were a nice tough. Natalie was not so much super effective as it turns out the critter was ill prepared for guns.<br /> <br /> Not much to add. Something of a time jump, just under a month. and then we begin the wedding week for Alexia and Chandra. We\u2019ve been doing light research on Indian wedding traditions, and it should be something of a fusion of that and American traditions.<br /> <br /> See you then. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:21:34-08:00","id":17021,"title":"","content":"There was a bit under a month between the last journals and these, as school started and people adjusted to the schedules of it, especially Jasmine and Natalie. Eventually, however, the time drew close for Alexia and Chandra\u2019s wedding, and some of the traditional Indian wedding celebrations began. Let\u2019s rejoin our heroes (?) there.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXXVI</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Tuesday, August 24, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s an odd thing, waking up to find the world exactly like you left it after removing something that never belonged in it to start with. Everything dies, that\u2019s part of the Natural Order so I guess that\u2019s why all the creatures from the Underworld don\u2019t bother me as much.<br /> <br /> I got up and meditated like normal but there was a tension missing that I hadn\u2019t even realized was there before. It wasn\u2019t necessarily any easier to get center as much as it felt more natural. Everything today has felt more real and more normal. But then I guess that\u2019s how I know we did something important. I\u2019m not sure that Bright Eyes would feel that way, but she lost a piece of herself to that wrongness. I just hope we can help her fill that void.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was much more calm than usual. It was more like a family breakfast and less like a military briefing before a major offensive. There was still a lot going on with the wedding plans and figuring out who will do what and by when to pull this whole thing off. But in a surreal way, it was like the end of a movie. The ones where my character would just sit back in his chair and smile up to the camera as it pulled back and away, overlooking everyone like the chaos of the morning was the most normal of things. Not perfect, but like it should be.<br /> <br /> I look forward to seeing the rest of the day. Everything feels, not different....just right.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1645 Hours, Tuesday, August 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was unexpected. Elsie just came by and wanted to talk about the job I offered. She left me her number and her class schedule so I can actually start working this out. It is a good day.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Thursday, August 26, 2010<br /> <br /> I had a day off! And I didn\u2019t have to close the shop.<br /> <br /> Well, I had a day off from the shop. Snowflake and I started the process with the van for Work Day yesterday. Leslie and Elsie were both very quick studies and I think Leslie even realized how bad an idea it would be to mess with Elsie. The van is not as trashed as it looked. But it will be a learning experience for us. The body is slag, but the Internet tells me that I can do lots to it through custom van sites. Now if I can just get Nightshade to stop suggesting the NeverEnding Story as a theme...but at least she\u2019s talking to me about silly things again. Karen doesn\u2019t tense up when I make sudden moves anymore either, so that\u2019s a plus.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s almost lunchtime and....<br /> <br /> Wow. Trinh came in and said she\u2019d like to work here too! Her schedule is perfect. This is great. I realize that something terrible is coming, but I\u2019m just going to enjoy it while I can.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1330 Hours, Monday, September 6, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation went well, if long this morning. That might just be because I\u2019m sore as hell from moving the new engine. Wait, has it really been that long?<br /> <br /> The girls have basically taken over the shop, cleaned it up, and even reorganized things a little. It looks better, smells nicer, and they are getting it done. It\u2019s hard to believe they have all been there together for about a week.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, I\u2019ve been working on the van. It definitely feels like mine now. Everything that was missing or damaged is being a pain in the ass to fix, but once I finally have it working, it works great. The engine and transmission have been overhauled, mostly by me and Snowflake. I think it\u2019s safe to say, we\u2019ve learned a ton about cars. Also about tools and how arcane that seem. I\u2019m pretty sure Snowflake enjoys that part of it. I mean when you say oil filter wrench, I don\u2019t automatically think of something that looks like a clamp from some kind of bondage device. But as it\u2019s Study Day, I\u2019ve been watching online videos for everything I can find. Right now, I\u2019m taking a break for lunch and to write this.<br /> <br /> Nightshade got up and came around while I was still eating. I asked if she wanted to join me. It was a little awkward, given our previous lunch engagements, but we eventually started joking about my van and all the crazy ideas for the Bachelor Party. It felt good to be able to talk to her again with nothing requiring us to be together. Karen was at school so that probably helped a little. Anyway, back to the videos before sticking my hands back in the grease pit.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0300 Hours, Saturday, September 11, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a long day. We were all in the TV room tonight night when someone changed the channel and the news popped up. A teenager in the midwest committed suicide on Thursday after being bullied at school for being gay. Nightshade blinked a few times and went silent. I could tell she and Karen were both shocked, we all were. But when Nightshade stood up and announced she was going to the apartment, I knew things were bad.<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t believe those assholes pushed someone that far. That goes beyond the old argument that kids are just kids. That is bullshit. I just can\u2019t unload how pissed off about this I am because I need to stay calm for Nightshade. Whenever she comes back. She won\u2019t let Karen come with her so I know what she\u2019s doing.<br /> <br /> Given what today is, I should be a wonderful ball of nerves myself. Just have to save it for the punching bag.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2215 Hours, Thursday, September 16, 2010<br /> <br /> FOR FUCKS SAKE!<br /> <br /> Karen sent a text early in the day. Another gay teen committed suicide after being bullied in school on Monday.<br /> <br /> Nightshade is in bad shape. Karen, Bright Eyes, and I have all been with her for the past several hours. Karen isn\u2019t even twitchy about my presence so I guess she knows I\u2019m only around for Nightshade. That we\u2019re all trying to remind her that she\u2019s proof it gets better can\u2019t hurt. It\u2019s just so hard to reach her right now. The drugs are muting her, but I can feel just how angry she is. I know it\u2019s not just the gay bashing, but also the fact that it\u2019s teenagers. Little Nightshade could be any one of these kids...and Nightshade <b>was</b> one of these kids. Violence is not the answer, but I will definitely have to beat on something once we can get her stable again.<br /> <br /> Almost time for my shift with Nightshade, so I have to keep calm. I\u2019m signing off.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0830 Hours, Friday, September 17, 2010<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t sleep until she was too exhausted from sobbing to keep going. Well I should say she didn\u2019t sleep. That was about an hour ago. I reminded her that she is supposed to sleep in the AM as she was fighting it. That made her giggle before drifting off. Hopefully she\u2019ll be a little more even when she wakes up. I promised Karen I would text her with news so she would go to school. Should probably do that now.<br /> <br /> Oh god. I just realized the wedding ceremony starts tomorrow. I have got to get Nightshade\u2019s system clear as she is a part of almost every piece of this thing. The plan, as I know it, is as follows:<br /> <br /> Bridal Party Groomsmen\u2019s Party<br /> <br /> Sat. Sept. 18 Anointing in Oils<br /> <br /> Sun. Sept. 19 Making Garlen Decorating &amp; Prep (Yacht)<br /> <br /> Mon. Sept. 20 Making Wreaths \u201c<br /> <br /> Tue. Sept. 21 Bridal Shower (Spa) Bachelar Party (Yacht)<br /> <br /> Wed. Sept. 22 Finishing Garlen/Wreaths Clean Yacht<br /> <br /> Thur. Sept. 23 Henna Party (Yacht) Prep Ceremony Space (Gazebo)<br /> <br /> Fri. Sept. 24 Rehearsal<br /> <br /> Sat. Sept 25 Wedding<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really just writing that down so I can keep up with it in my head. Tavia is so happy with all this she can barely stand it. That at least is really cute.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019m going to text Cupcake about sending breakfast up. I\u2019m starving and Karen will stab me if I leave.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1830 Hours, Saturday, September 18, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation took forever, but it usually does after I go several days without. And I have totally not been centered.<br /> <br /> We had the Anointing in Oils ceremony today about 1300 Hours. Nightshade was enough like herself again to go and participate. Though I don\u2019t think she enjoyed being around all the oil and how much it went everywhere. I tried to be as respectful as I could and used the oils to give each of them a traditional foot massage. I got some weird looks, but no one objected. Snowflake heard the word ceremony and took it as a solemn duty to make sure everything was perfect on his end. Bright Eyes on the other hand was giggling and tickling and generally having a good time. That helped lighten the mood, though I think I saw Nightshade shrink just to avoid oil splatters.<br /> <br /> When the ceremony was complete, Nightshade asked several of us to visit the 27 Club. It was more ready to open than I realized. Snowflake, Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and I all went to take a look. It was very different from the one time I had seen it before. There was a main stage and a much smaller side stage for... well I\u2019m not sure if it was for announcers or single performers. The amplifiers and various speaker equipment were causing some problems as Nightshade was telling us about needing more generators. I suggested that maybe she could also put solar panels on the roof to help offset the power drain from the rest of the club. I had seen something about it online while researching my van. She seemed impressed that I had a suggestion so I was happy. All in all, it was a cool place. The murals of the \u201cmembers\u201d of the 27 Club were up and watching over the stage. I think they will be proud.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re back at the Bluffs waiting for dinner.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> [Excerpts from Jasmine\u2019s Journal, Aug. 24 - Sept. 18, 2010]<br /> <br /> Friday, August 27, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I met Rita for coffee at Lulu\u2019s this afternoon, and introduced her to Stanly. We sat and chatted for a few hours - I completely lost track of time. It felt good to just sit and talk with a friend. I don\u2019t mean to imply that my house mates aren\u2019t friends, it\u2019s just that I don\u2019t always feel comfortable around them, and I don\u2019t think they feel comfortable around me. That doesn\u2019t bother me, but it did feel nice to relax and open up to Rita a bit. She\u2019s very charming, if insecure, and I do hope I can help boost her confidence and possibly find someone to love. And of course there is her troubling predatory instinct, but our conversation today remained too light-hearted to dwell on such worries.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Karl and I remain a bit distant. We still spend time together, and I do love him, but I don\u2019t know how to talk about what is troubling me. How can I share my fears with him? How would he react to my worries that I am a killer at heart? I want to talk to him, but I can\u2019t bring myself to do so. He is keeping his distance, when what I really need is for him to take control, hold me, and quiet my fears.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, September 4, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Jean competed in his first semi-professional swim meet today, and his performance exceeded my expectations! He was in top form, and placed first in the 200 and 400 meter freestyle, 100 meter backstroke, and 200 meter butterfly events! This was a big step for him. The recognition gained today is already opening doors, and I\u2019ve been able to schedule him for some professional tryout competitions. If he continues to perform like he did today, it will be easy to obtain sponsorships. I have confidence in him. I\u2019ve seen his ability. He has more potential as a swimmer than I ever did. I\u2019ll do whatever I can to make sure he fulfills that potential.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, September 14, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Natalie is extremely upset over the gay suicides that occured over the past week. The news hit her hard, and she\u2019s escaped to her apartment. I don\u2019t like it when she runs to her drugs like that. I hope she will be okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, September 18, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> We had the oil anointing ceremony today, which begins the week of wedding festivities. It began formally enough, with me helping Lily be the first to pour a bit of oil on Alexia, but it soon became quite chaotic.Tavia, Chandra, Sara and Gretchen ended up flinging oil all over the place while Natalie and I retreated to cleaner rooms.<br /> <br /> Saturday, September 18, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> After the day\u2019s festivities had died down, I felt myself growing a bit morose. I suppose it\u2019s simply my natural response to the waning spirits of a happy day. I sat with Karl to watch a movie, but I was acutely aware of the distance between us, so I excused myself to go up to my room. I ended up changing into more rugged clothing and headed to the Avernian gate in the basement to enter the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Of course, this isn\u2019t the first time I\u2019ve visited the Underworld over the past few weeks. I haven\u2019t really told the rest of the krewe because they would say that it\u2019s too dangerous to go alone and would insist on accompanying me. But I know the local Underworld fairly well now, and a part of me feels drawn to it more and more, like I belong there. I suppose I should be worried about that, but I\u2019m not. The Bride is not happy about it, but she doesn\u2019t complain either. I think she understands the echoes of melancholy that make both of us feel at home there.<br /> <br /> As always, I made my way to the diner and took a seat at the bar. I ordered my usual milkshake, paying with some colorful key chain trinkets I picked up last time I visited the mall.<br /> <br /> Janice was there as usual, and we chatted for awhile. She\u2019s very easy to talk to, though I get the sense that she has done some very bad things in the past. Perhaps she used to harm or prey on other ghosts. Whatever she did, she feels tremendous remorse now, or so it seems. I think that\u2019s why she lingers in the diner, trying to help other ghosts. She certainly helped me tonight. I gave her a few trinkets as gift, and then found myself sharing my fears with her. I told her about how killing Louisa has made me doubt myself. It\u2019s made me feel like a cold-hearted killer, and that scares me.<br /> <br /> I told her that I hadn\u2019t been able to talk to my boyfriend about it, and that he was keeping his distance even though that\u2019s the last thing I need. Janice encouraged me to talk to someone. If not Karl, then someone else, someone alive. And that\u2019s when I realized that I should talk to Simon. Of all my friends, he\u2019s the only one who struggles with the same doubts.<br /> I found Simon once I returned home, and we had a long conversation. He told me that I might always wonder whether or not I can be a good person again, having killed someone. He wonders the same thing all the time and still spends a lot of time trying to atone for the murder of his parents. Simon feels that worrying about it shows that I\u2019m not a killer at heart. It bothers me because it should bother me. The remorse shows that I\u2019m not taking it for granted. Yes, I may have to kill someone else in the future. I\u2019m prepared for that. But I will never do so lightly, and there will always be regret, because at heart, I\u2019m not a killer.<br /> <br /> Thank you Simon. I hope you find as much solace in your advice as I did.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Wedding Schedule</u><br /> <br /> Chandra and Alexia have decided to have an extensive wedding celebration, including both Hindi and western traditions during the ceremony and throughout the week leading up to it. Here is the schedule:<br /> <br /> Sat., Sept. 18 - Oil Anointing Ceremony<br /> <br /> A not-too-serious ceremony during which Alexia is anointed with aromatic oils by the other ladies in the household.<br /> <br /> Tues., Sept. 21 - Bridal Shower/Bachelor Party<br /> <br /> As Alexia\u2019s Maid of Honor, I am arranging the Bridal Shower. I\u2019m very excited about it, and certainly thrilled to have the opportunity. I\u2019ve arranged a spa date at Harmony, the local spa we go to occasionally. I\u2019m friends with the Taiwanese owner, so I was able to get us a good group discount. We will have several nice hours at the spa and then we\u2019ll have dinner and give presents in a private room at Ibiza, an upscale Spanish restaurant not far from Yale.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know anything about the bachelor party except that it will be held on the yacht, but I gather that Simon and Doc are planning to make it truly scandalous. I\u2019m quite happy to be kept in the dark about what might occur.<br /> <br /> Thurs., Sept. 23 - Henna Party<br /> <br /> A party for the ladies of the household, which will be held on the yacht (after the boys have done a thorough job cleaning it following the bachelor party). We will decorate each other with Henna in preparation for the wedding.<br /> <br /> Fri., Sept. 24 - Wedding Rehearsal<br /> <br /> The rehearsal is especially important since we are mixing western and Hindi traditions, and many of us have no idea what to expect.<br /> <br /> Sat., Sept. 25 - Wedding!<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Bridal Shower - Invitation List</u><br /> Tavia<br /> Karen<br /> Gretchen<br /> Deirdre<br /> Stanly (&amp; Adam)<br /> Karl (not attending - too awkward)<br /> Grin<br /> Gwen (not attending - can\u2019t get in touch)<br /> Natalie (attending bachelor party, not shower)<br /> Sara (attending bachelor party, not shower)<br /> Rita<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Henna Party - Invitation List</u><br /> Tavia<br /> Karen<br /> Gretchen<br /> Deirdre<br /> Natalie<br /> Sara<br /> Marjorie (ghost)<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Study<br /> </u><br /> I\u2019ve been spending quite a bit of time in the library, particularly since I\u2019ve been spending less with Karl. Mostly I\u2019ve been brushing up on my Underworld lore. I already know a great deal about the occult, and since I\u2019ve become a sin-eater, I\u2019ve been particularly drawn to myths and legends having to do with the enigmas of ghosts and the Underworld. The resources in our library have done a great deal to fill in the gaps in my knowledge.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> September 18th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Chin up, stay strong Natalie.<br /> <br /> -There is a wedding, a lesbian wedding, dependant on you. Can\u2019t let how these people are being treated get you down.<br /> <br /> -Living proud and not letting others define your mood is part of the point, right?<br /> <br /> -Any GLBT youth reading this stay strong! Stay alive! Things will get better. We will make it better!<br /> <br /> -I want a day when I can watch the news and not want to reach for my Heroin, though. Not this month, though.<br /> <br /> -OK, but oil party today<br /> <br /> -People are excited!<br /> <br /> -Putting away phone while I get sloppy.<br /> <br /> -OK, OCD did not like that, but people had fun.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t like getting my hands dirty.<br /> <br /> -Some of these people, though, don\u2019t mind getting dirty.<br /> <br /> -Could not handle an Indian wedding, would not be able to sit there without screaming.<br /> <br /> -But it was good times, am just crazy.<br /> <br /> -To the club!<br /> <br /> -Clubs require a lot of power.<br /> <br /> -Doc and Sara approve! Yay!<br /> <br /> -Good feelings all around.<br /> <br /> -I needed a day like this\u2026.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s issues stem from the rash of GLBT suicides in September 2010. There was weighing whether a serious real world issue would get even cursory mention in a campaign for fun, but in the end I decided we must not ignore such a tragedy, especially in a group with a PC GLBT activist and where half the PCs are GLBT themselves. It\u2019s not major plot point, but the inclusion is done with respect, and not done lightly.<br /> <br /> The Indian oil anointing ceremony is of course, a real thing, and you can read about it on the interwebs or at your local library.<br /> <br /> Only other note is much of the session was spent OOCly discussing downtime and working out bachelor party, bridal shower, and henna party guest lists, as well as wedding guest list. Some interesting discussion of gender roles and roles in the wedding and stuff like the bachelor party and bridal shower. Chandra takes the more masculine role in she and Alexia\u2019s relationship and is the groom. She is also getting a bachelor party not a bridal shower. Natalie and Karen don\u2019t have defined \u201croles\u201d in their romance, but Natalie elected to go to the Bachelor party being the randier one in the relationship, though both will be at the henna party.<br /> <br /> OK well there you go. Comments and questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:41:24-08:00","id":17027,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for the bridal shower and bachelor party, and one of the two groups is up to no good. It is kinda predictable which one.<br /> <i><br /> Session LXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1500 Hours, Tuesday, September 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Snowflake does not mess around when he wants to throw a party. We\u2019ve been cleaning and prepping the boat for the past two days. The bridal party has been working on garland and wreaths for the wedding, so not just sitting around talking. But we have moved so many pillows onto the boat, it looks like something out of an old Sinbad movie. Today is the Bridal Shower so we\u2019re still waiting for them to get back from the Spa.<br /> <br /> Later tonight is the Bachelor Party. I\u2019m equal parts excited and terrified of that. Think we are planning to load up around 2000 Hours and shove off about 2100 Hours. The guest list is a little nuts and I don\u2019t know almost half of these women. But from the view on the dock, I think Chandra will enjoy herself.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2030 Hours, Tuesday, September 21, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m on the docks doing a little bit of greeting party with Snowflake. Noriko was one of the first to arrive. She\u2019s wearing a short kimono and wiggled a little more than usual when she walked by. But then, she probably knew I was looking. There are tons of friend of a friend of Nightshade\u2019s here tonight.<br /> <br /> I need to make sure I have my yarn, just in case.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0025 Hours, Wednesday, September 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Never a dull moment.<br /> <br /> Zed, Snowflake, and I are the only men on board tonight. This is interesting to say the least. That most of the women here are at least bisexual and willing to come to a lesbian bachelor party speaks to being friends with Nightshade . Still, the view from the deck is beautiful.<br /> <br /> Sadly, we can\u2019t even take a boatload of beautiful women out on a yacht for the Penanggalan\u2019s lesbian bachelor party without something supernatural turning up. I started the night mingling with the crowd. I didn\u2019t want to make anyone uncomfortable so I tried to make a good impression. Zed was having a very good time and he didn\u2019t have much to say otherwise. Chandra was not expecting the girl to pop out of the cake and her night only got better from there. As I was moving through the crowd psuedo-hosting while Snowflake ran the bar, I noticed a woman that I didn\u2019t recognize. With a minor inspection, I noticed that she had some strange energy source that I couldn\u2019t place. Even the Dog of War noticed something. As I was smoozing anyway, I introduced myself. Elizabeth was happy to take a drink so I alerted Snowflake and Nightshade before returning to deliver the drinks. Elizabeth didn\u2019t have loads to say, but she was polite. When I glanced back, Nightshade had some very big eyes and motioned for me to come back. Nightshade more of a skilled mystic whereas I\u2019m more of a scholarly occultist. What she noticed, even from the DJ booth, was that Elizabeth had died an untold number of times and had an illusion covering everything. I assumed that mean even mystically. Nightshade said she was also very powerful. We weren\u2019t sure but we thought maybe she was like the Reborn we met before. It was at that point the body shots started so the dance floor got a little chaotic.<br /> <br /> Snowflake learned of our information and asked that I take over the bar. He had a few maudlin characters stationed there, but nothing too hard to keep up with. He of course went over to talk with Elizabeth. She was much more chatty with him than with me and even gave him her number. Noriko was almost prowling around the bar for a while but moved back to the dance floor once she knew I was paying attention. Snowflake returned and snapped my focus. Apparently Elizabeth is playing coy about wanting an artifact that she knows is in the House. This cannot be good, but she\u2019s willing to play nice so we\u2019ll see where it goes.<br /> <br /> I am going to have a talk with Rose when I get back to port. There was a far amount of green thread in my pocket when I reached for my yarn. The yarn was there too, but the thread was lower, meaning it was placed there well before we left.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, Sept. 19, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Alexia, Tavia and I have been busy most of the day making wreaths and other decorations for the wedding. It was fun spending time with them and chatting as we worked, even if Tavia can\u2019t carry on a conversation without taking off in odd directions. I usually find it frustrating, particularly since the others seem to become easily distracted by her antics, but today I didn\u2019t mind it so much, and Alexia\u2019s cheerful disposition helped.<br /> <br /> Tuesday, Sept. 21, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> The bridal shower was a complete success. At least, I think everyone had fun. Alexia certainly seemed pleased, and we all enjoyed being pampered a bit at the spa.<br /> <br /> The shower began in the early afternoon at Harmony, my friend\u2019s spa. We were treated to a wonderful time in the sauna, refreshing massages, manicures, pedicures, and facials. I always feel so good after a day there. For the most part, Rita, Deirdre, Karen, Tavia and I chatted while Adam and Grin, being the most masculine of the guests, bonded a bit talking clumsily about fantasy football, though I confess I have no idea what that is even after catching bits of their conversation. Stanly and Gretchen talked amiably in low voices when they could (when the ladies and gentlemen were together at the spa, such as during the manicures/pedicures). I didn\u2019t hear much of what they talked about, which is fortunate and intentional, as I got the distinct sense they were telling rather raunchy stories to one another. I had no idea Stanly could be such a lewd man; he always seemed so polite and charming, but I suppose everyone has a darker side. Alexia enjoyed their conversation and laughed at their stories until they became too obscene even for her.<br /> <br /> Of course, Alexia spent time with all of us, and particularly enjoyed Deirdre\u2019s company. I\u2019m glad Deirdre is a friend of the krewe. I don\u2019t know a great deal about her, but she\u2019s nice and seems like she\u2019s good for Doc and Alexia.<br /> <br /> I think Rita had fun. If nothing else, I enjoyed spending time with her. She and Deirdre seemed to hit it off well too, though I noticed that they were on guard toward each even though they seemed drawn together. Thanks to my Primeval Key, I quickly understood that their predatory souls felt a subconscious rivalry that neither really understood. So as Rita and I were driving from the spa to the restaurant for dinner, I explained what was going on. She was quite relieved, as she liked Deirdre but didn\u2019t know what to make of her, and we agreed that it would be okay to let Deirdre know that Rita is supernatural as well.<br /> <br /> When we arrived at Ibiza, the 5-star Spanish gourmet restaurant I\u2019d reserved for dinner, Rita and I drew Deirdre aside and explained the situation to her. She seemed relieved, and I could sense the tension between them evaporating now that they both understood what they were feeling. I think they\u2019d like to hang out again, and they shared e-mail addresses. There was some talk about going to a club together with me, and though I\u2019m not normally very eager to visit clubs, I think I might enjoy it with Deirdre and Rita, as long as it\u2019s not a dark, fetish-ridden place like Murder Ballads.<br /> <br /> I also bragged a bit about Jean\u2019s recent success at the swimming competition. Rita seemed quite interested in meeting Jean after I described him, so I think I might be able to arrange a date. In any event, I\u2019ve invited her to campus next Monday morning to swim, which will give me to opportunity to introduce the two of them. Of course, there\u2019s still the matter of Rita\u2019s predatory instincts getting the best of her, but I think that meditation will help her achieve a greater degree of self control, so I\u2019ve also invited her to learn tai chi and meditation with me. Hopefully it will help.<br /> <br /> After dinner we shared gifts. Tavia, Karen, Grin, Gretchen and I all went in together on a set of very fine china, which is something Alexia has said she\u2019s wanted for awhile now, as she is quite opposed to using the antique Fishborne china. Stanly got her a nice toaster, which I thought was a rather dull and inappropriate gift, but there was apparently some sort of inside joke going on which I didn\u2019t understand. Alexia appreciated it, though, which is all that matters.<br /> <br /> The boys are out on the yacht with Chandra and who know who else right now, enjoying their bachelor party. I do hope things don\u2019t get too out of control.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u> A Bit of String</u><br /> <br /> I happened to overhear that Noriko had been invited to the bachelor party. Every since I encountered her in her werecat form and learned what she was about, I\u2019ve liked Noriko, though I don\u2019t really know her well. She seems fun and uncomplicated (aside from her supernatural activities), which is why I\u2019ve always thought she and Doc would be good together. Of course, I also think Doc and Deirdre would be good together, but he doesn\u2019t seem interested in pursuing that relationship, and Deirdre is a bit promiscuous, so perhaps that\u2019s for the best.<br /> <br /> Doc has not been the same since his relationship with Natalie fell apart, and though I couldn\u2019t be happier that he ended things with her (for reasons I\u2019ve explained at length in this diary already), I think he seems lonely, and a bit of romance is just what he needs. I remembered how he almost got in trouble before when he flirted with her using a piece of string to tease her like a cat, and decided that getting \u201cin trouble\u201d with her now is exactly what he needs.<br /> <br /> To that end, I made sure to sneak a length of string into his pocket earlier today. I\u2019m hoping he finds it during the bachelor party and decides to use it to rekindle Noriko\u2019s interest.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add. Technically the Bridal Shower ran before the Bachelor Party, but I ran them concurrently so I would not extendedly fixate on one group then the other. The parties did finish, Doc just ended where he could have last gotten to his log\u2026.<br /> <br /> It was a lot of fun, even if non-ideal to split the group up.<br /> <br /> More next time. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:43:36-08:00","id":17028,"title":"","content":"Back to wedding preparations when everything gets sidetracked! Everything is coming up vampires!<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Wednesday, September 22, 2010<br /> <br /> The yarn was incredibly useful. Noriko is as acrobatic as I could have hoped; we spent the night out on the boat together after slipping away from the party. I\u2019d probably still be laying around except I could hear the others when they were getting their things together. I got her number before she got dressed to leave. All things considered, I had a pretty damn good night.<br /> <br /> Snowflake raised an eyebrow when I followed her out, but didn\u2019t say anything. Once all the guests were gone, I walked back up to the railing he was leaning on. I wasn\u2019t sure if I needed to give an explanation, but when I turned to look at him, Snowflake merely nodded approvingly. We spent the next few hours cleaning up so the other ladies could have the yacht tonight. We\u2019re just taking a break for lunch (breakfast) now.<br /> <br /> I am so glad I hired the girls for the shop.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1730 Hours, Wednesday, September 22, 2010<br /> <br /> The yacht is spotless, refueled, and fully restocked. Snowflake, Nightshade, Bright Eyes, and I went over the whole ship. We didn\u2019t scrub it with toothbrushes, but it was in great shape when we were finished. It felt good to spend that much time on the water again. I didn\u2019t realize how much I\u2019d missed it. Maybe I can find more reasons to go out again.<br /> <br /> Nothing really exciting happened so we\u2019re just getting ready for dinner now.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2345 Hours, Wednesday, September 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Tonight has definitely been interesting. And exciting.<br /> <br /> Around 2130 Hours, Bright Eyes found me to ask a favor. Apparently her vampiric date from a while back called and sounded like she needed help. Now we all knew this Lynne was a vampire as soon as we saw her, but she didn\u2019t know anything about us. Thus it was odd she would call Bright Eyes for help, but our girl not being born last night, asked for backup. I didn\u2019t mind at all so I agreed to go along.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes knocked and was let in. I came in behind and a somewhat ...feral looking little woman stared at Bright Eyes and stated that she needed to feed. That didn\u2019t seem right to me. Lynne didn\u2019t look hurt, but her clothes suggested she might have been recently. When I brought attention to myself, she demanded to know who I was, but the feral edge never left. I had an idea of what was happening, but even if I was wrong, I knew this was not a good situation. I adjusted my posture slightly to be less confrontational and tried to verbally present myself as a friend. I didn\u2019t move far away from Bright Eyes though. Lynne again stated that she needed to feed. This time Bright Eyes agreed, though I did note that she would need to be careful. Lynne almost launched herself at Bright Eyes and fed for far longer than I was comfortable. Though paler than normal, Bright Eyes seemed to still be okay. When Lynne drew back, she had obviously sated her Beast and was shocked to see me standing there. She became very nervous and paranoid, which seemed much more natural to the situation. Together, Bright Eyes and I calmed her down. I made sure to use language that proved I knew about vampires, which didn\u2019t really help her relax but made her more comfortable with me. She asked me several times if I was a ghoul, or failing that, if I wanted to be. I found that be to somewhat cute, considering she should technically kill me for knowing what I do. Eventually we got her to explain why she called for help.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s where the night started going off the rails. Lynne managed to steal something from the Nosferatu of the Ordo Dracul. Yes the same Nosferatu that have the alchemy lab. According to Lynne, she got away clean but they still somehow managed to figure out she was the thief. So they are as mystically inclined as we thought. From there, they called in a boon with the Prince, even though that group and the Prince aren\u2019t on good terms. Good to know, but not helpful in this situation. The Prince sent the Sheriff to ... well I\u2019m not completely sure what they were supposed to do. I have to assume they were trying to get the something back, but beating Lynne into torpor seems to be the point of her story. Either way, she tangled with the Sheriff\u2019s people, likely some of the same group that Snowflake and I saw playing pool. By the fact she was still mobile indicated she won, but also explained the state of her clothes. It also helped me to understand her hunger. Once we got all that explained, it was clear that Lynne needed to lay low and also that we were being called into something that would complicate our bargaining with the vampires at large. Given Bright Eyes trusted Lynne enough to let her feed, I knew she wouldn\u2019t abandon her to the Sheriff. That meant I needed more information. Without mentioning Truman, I convinced Lynne to let me call a vampiric friend of mine to see what they could suggest.<br /> <br /> I stepped out into the hall hoping she couldn\u2019t just listen from where she was. Then I called Truman. I explained as generically as I could and asked what would be best to do. Truman is always in the know about something and asked if I meant Lynne. When I said yes, the first thing he told me was to stay away from her as she was crazy. Not the way I wanted to learn this. Especially not after I just left Bright Eyes alone in the room with her. Ignoring that, Truman said that she would die if we brought her there. It was also clear that Truman did not want to have this on him. That I more than understood. But it was about that time when I heard several cars pull up and lots of people jump out. I told Truman they were here and hung up. I ran back in and interrupted what looked like an intimate moment in the making to tell everyone we had to go. Before we could get any further, a Chinese accented voice yelled up the stairs that anyone with Lynne should, \u201clay down and you won\u2019t get shot.\u201d That settled that. I looked out the window and saw the fire escape then asked Lynne how far she could fall as we were climbing out the window. She said she could take it, so before anything else was said, I grabbed the five foot nothing woman and threw her over the railing. Bright Eyes looked at me like she was angry but before she could speak I barked, \u201cUP!\u201d We ran up the fire escape to the roof. Bright Eyes seemed to be trying to understand how we were going to get away, but I tried to calm her down. We weren\u2019t getting away, Lynne was. Before I could explain, the Sheriff and four of his closest friends walked out on the roof. I had no desire to ruin our chances at being on good terms with the vampires of New Haven, but if things went badly I was also aware that the two members of our Krewe skilled in the Pyre-Flame Key were both standing with their backs to a five story drop. There was really only two ways this could go. Sheriff Lang asked the obvious questions, though he stared at both of us when we answered. I have to guess he was trying to see if we were lying. But we didn\u2019t know where Lynne was. We could see she wasn\u2019t in the alley I threw her into, so we had no idea where she went. The Sheriff didn\u2019t like our answer but knew we couldn\u2019t help him. He did warn us that if he found us in the wrong place like this again, he wouldn\u2019t be so polite. We could hear other people moving below us. Based on what we could see, four other of the Sheriff\u2019s people were working through Lynne\u2019s apartment and her things. The Dog and I were both tense and ready, but this was not our fight...yet. We watched as they planted something on Lynne\u2019s car. Then they left.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes looked like she wanted to act, but hostility with vampires is not what we needed. We waited there on the roof for a while to make sure they were gone. Coming back down, we saw Lang didn\u2019t really mind making his presence known. They left Lynne\u2019s door open. Her apartment wasn\u2019t turned over exactly, but I could tell things were gone through. Holding my finger to my lips, I signaled to Bright Eyes that we weren\u2019t through. We went back through Lynne\u2019s apartment ourselves and though I didn\u2019t find anything, Bright Eyes pointed out three bugs. Looking them over, I realized we could speak. These weren\u2019t microphones, but location trackers. One in Lynne\u2019s boots, one in a purse, and another in a coat pocket. This was probably the same thing they put on her car. Grabbing a brush and a small compact, I felt like we were done. With that, we went back to the House.<br /> <br /> When we got back, Nightshade was singing Sweet Dreams in the Music room. I hated to interrupt but she being one of the others in the know about vampires, I thought we should include her. I made an effort to give Karen an excuse to leave. She didn\u2019t understand but eventually it was explained that what we were going to discuss was grounds for her to be killed. She moved a little closer to Nightshade but said she wasn\u2019t going anywhere. Not like I wouldn\u2019t try to protect her just like any other part of the family. Anyway, I explained what we had gotten into. I was more than a little angry because I\u2019d brought Truman into something that had nothing to do with him. Given the reaction we had at Lynne\u2019s, I assumed they were tapping Truman\u2019s phone for some reason. Now I knew they would be tracking my calls and we couldn\u2019t think of any reason they wouldn\u2019t be looking at Bright Eyes\u2019 phone as well. I wanted to include Snowflake but Nightshade thought we should gather the Krewe. I went to each and suggested we meet in the basement. I didn\u2019t think the vampires would come in the House, but they might be hiding by the windows. Yes I was that paranoid. Rose was sitting with Karl out on the second floor veranda. It was a beautiful night, but they were somewhat awkwardly staring at the ocean. I don\u2019t need to get involved in another couple\u2019s issues, so I just let them know we needed to discuss something in the basement. Cupcake was in the kitchen and didn\u2019t understand why she had to leave her experiment, but I eventually convinced her. The others assembled in the Dwarven Throne Room without issue for us to explain the horror.<br /> <br /> Rose was instantly confused about who Lynne was. Nightshade and I tried to help Bright Eyes by suggesting she was dating. But she absently waved that idea away. We both just sighed to each other as Rose became flustered about how many partners Bright Eyes has. Nevermind that it\u2019s none of her business, it didn\u2019t matter to this topic. Eventually I stepped in and pointed out that right now, we needed to decide what, if anything, we wanted to do about this. We all agreed that this could be a roadblock for our negotiations with the vampires of the city. Bright Eyes tried to give everyone else a way out, saying this wasn\u2019t something the Krewe should suffer through. I knew that wouldn\u2019t work. Rose championed going to the Athenaeum as a more pressing issue. Once it was settled that we would help Lynne, we gave a brief thought to feeding. Rose strangely volunteered that she could most easily deal with the damage, but that she was not interested in doing so unless it was a last resort. I spoke up and pointed out that that should not even be considered given she wasn\u2019t completely okay with it. But I was not at all interested in keeping Bright Eyes healthy through the kind of blood loss Lynne had already inflicted. We left the others at that point, so I could see just how badly she was injured. I dropped the brush and mirror off with Snowflake on the way out. He looked confused at first but understood as he handled the items.<br /> <br /> Lynne had taken enough blood that most people would have gone unconscious at the time and possibly become anemic for a while assuming they didn\u2019t have other complications. My irritation was rising, but I was trying not to be harsh with Bright Eyes for wanting to help someone. I knew I could heal the damage, but as I realized how extensive it was, Bright Eyes made a joke about knowing how to fix it but she\u2019d need a lighter. She and Nightshade share the ability to \u201cdie\u201d in relation to their elemental aspect to take on a spiritual form. The side effect is that any damage they suffered beforehand would be healed. I winced as I realized a much less intensive way to heal Bright Eyes. I went up and got a robe from one of the guest linen closets and told Bright Eyes to strip before walking back out. We then walked into the backyard with the people-sized oven, as Tavia calls it. I apologized as Bright Eyes slipped out of the robe. I had to be there to kill the flames. She didn\u2019t seem to mind. As I lit the gas, I closed my eyes. I have already seen myself and others on fire, I have no intention of watching as someone else close to me burns to death. Fortunately, it took only an instant before Bright Eyes was engulfed and fell to ash. After a few minutes I carefully pulled the cooling grate out so she could come back without issues. A few moments later, a healthy and nude Bright Eyes seemed to jump from the cremated remains. I wrapped her in the robe and made sure she was better. Everything checked out, so we headed back inside to check on Snowflake. We picked Nightshade up along the way, though honestly a happily nude Bright Eyes will almost certainly summon Nightshade. She went to get dressed before we walked down and knocked on the door to the Mirror Room. Rose opened the door which surprised me. Finding her and Cupcake inside was startling, but Snowflake sat in his chair looking pensive. He carried the mirror out, closed the door, then placed the compact in a wooden curio box away from the Mirror Room before speaking to us. The irritation on his face was a sign something wasn\u2019t right. He explained that Lynne has an animate reflection. They had a discussion with this reflection and learned a few things about Lynne. The reflection, I decided to call her Ennyl, claims she is a piece of Lynne\u2019s humanity. Something about a remaining part of Lynne from before she was Embraced. Ennyl is very jealous of Lynne, but not enough to want to harm her. She was the one that actually stole the item but Snowflake sensed that he should not trust her. Thus we left the mirror in the box while he performed the Distance Voices ceremony to contact Lynne. We informed her to get a new phone and text the number to Nightshade\u2019s number. We were all confident that the vampires could not tap a phone they knew nothing about. In the meantime, we took the mirror out and locked it in the cooler under the gazebo.<br /> <br /> Nightshade, Snowflake, Bright Eyes and I are staying up to make sure things are handled. Now it\u2019s just time to wait.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Thursday, September 23, 2010<br /> <br /> Lynne eventually sent Nightshade a text around 0130 Hours. We gave her the address of the Firehouse Church and said to meet there. Nightshade opened the Avernian Gate in the house and then we spent the next 40 minutes dealing with the ceremony and the walk to the Firehouse Church. While we were casting, Bright Eyes gathered her ashes from the oven and grabbed a change of clothes to take with us. We had a plan.<br /> <br /> I came out first with Bright Eyes behind then Nightshade, wearing her Deathmask. I kept the Gate open as the Beckoning Initiate showed us so we could just get back without issue. Lynne hugged and kissed Bright Eyes and was genuinely happy to see her. She was a little confused when we told her she had to change into clothes that did not belong to her. Bright Eyes staged the scene fairly well. Lynne\u2019s clothes were filled with the ashes and dropped to seem as though worn. These were placed such that the lower windows of the Firehouse would hold the first rays of the dawn sun. And presto! We had a vampire death scene. Next I rather gruffly gave Lynne instructions on how to walk the Bone Path. I tried to keep myself even but the more I considered the collateral problems on the way back, the madder I got. Snowflake had arranged a room in the basement while we were gone, which was impressive. We introduced Lynne to Snowflake as it was his house she was taken refuge in, then settled her into her new bedroom. The questions started immediately after that.<br /> <br /> According to Lynne, the artifact was from Rome and turned up in Fort Hale Park, the same place we found the Strix. It was some sort of theatrical mask that can control a Kindred\u2019s Beast. She thought the Strix led the Ordo Dracul to it but she didn\u2019t think anyone should have that kind of power, given the political and physical dangers that posed. She also mentioned that the Strix were thought to be somehow involved in the fall of Vampiric Rome. Definitely need a trip to the Athenaeum. Anyway, Ennyl stole the artifact as part of some deal with Lynne. Then four of the Sheriff\u2019s boys came for her in Murder Ballads. Four on one didn\u2019t sound like odds I wanted, granted we had 9 on 2. They made the mistake of splitting up. Apparently she left two in torpor before running away. I had to let that sink in for a minute. I knew that vampires were way stronger than they looked sometimes, but that was still pretty impressive. Lynne is apparently a Carthian with ties to something called the Circle of the Crone. She said it was like a mystic order. Otherwise, she said the artifact is well hidden. She didn\u2019t want to tell us where in case the Sheriff tried to compel us. I know Rebecca has mentioned something like that before. We decided not to push it. We also told Lynne about having a Penanggalan living here. As we didn\u2019t want a contest of Beasts in the House, I felt it wise to keep the surprises to a minimum. I also made it clear that at NO point was the rest of the city to learn of this. We\u2019ll have to talk to Chandra about it later since she\u2019s not sleeping here due to the wedding.<br /> <br /> I was more than a little verbally aggressive with Lynne. The others could tell it as well. When all was said and done, I apologized for being so hard on her. I was concerned for us and felt responsible for whatever trouble Truman is or will be in. I stopped short of saying that it was her fault, but I\u2019m pretty sure she was aware. That being the case or not, it will be up to me to keep Truman from paying for something he wasn\u2019t involved in until I pulled him in.<br /> <br /> I stayed up til breakfast so I could inform the Krewe of our status. Either tonight or tomorrow, we\u2019ll have to deal with feeding. This is not going to end well for someone. My goal at this point is to make sure it\u2019s not one of the Krewe.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to bed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, September 22, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> I was sitting quietly on the second story veranda with Karl this evening, enjoying the evening air and sipping lemonade when Doc called out to us, insisting that the krewe meet in the basement. I thought it odd, meeting in the basement, but I assumed Doc had a good reason.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Doc\u2019s summons interrupted my thoughts. Now that I\u2019ve made peace with the fact that I killed someone and may do so again on behalf of the krewe, the cold distance that has grown between Karl and me has become a lonely ache, and I want to overcome it. But poor Karl has a hard time reading me, and I\u2019m not very good at being warm and inviting. We still spend a great deal of time together, but it hasn\u2019t been the same as it was just before we dealt with Glenwood. I\u2019m ready to bridge the gap get our relationship moving again, but I\u2019m having a difficult time figuring out how. Simply talking about it might make my intentions clear to Karl, but it wouldn\u2019t do anything to heat things up, so I\u2019d like to find some other way to share my wishes with him.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I had to put those thoughts aside to see what Doc wanted.<br /> <br /> It seems one of Sara\u2019s friends has gotten into some trouble. Doc, Natalie and Sara are primarily involved, so I only know the situation second-hand, and for the most part they seem content to keep me, Alexia, and Simon out of it unless necessary.<br /> <br /> It seems that Sara\u2019s latest lover is a vampire named Lynne. And Lynne has stolen something from the cabal of nosferatu vampires known as the Ordo Dracul, the order whose hideout we discovered some time ago. I gather that whatever she stole is best kept out of the hands of the vampires, but the theft did not go unnoticed, and now the Ordo Dracul and the vampires\u2019 sheriff are out for Lynne\u2019s blood. According to Doc and Natalie, it seems like a strange alliance, altogether to convenient. They suspect there is something larger at work, which is all the more reason for us to head into the Athenaeum to gain the leverage we need to strike a deal with the vampires.<br /> <br /> Doc and Sara managed to protect Lynne from the sheriff without resorting to violence, but she\u2019s far from safe, and Doc and Sara wish to provide sanctuary to Lynne in the mansion. I was not particularly happy about that decision, particularly once I learned that Lynne was just another casual lover to Sara. After all, we don\u2019t really know anything about this Lynne or the trouble she is in. But Sara is a member of the krewe, so I agreed to help when she assured me that she trusted Lynne. And Lynne seems quite attached to Sara. She was actually planning to turn her into a vampire!<br /> <br /> After we agreed to help Lynne, Doc and Sara left to make preparations for secretly bringing Lynne to the house, while Alexia and I followed Simon into a basement chamber that I\u2019d never entered before.<br /> <br /> Apparently it is something of a private space for Simon, which I did not realize at the time, though he raised no objection to use entering.<br /> <br /> The room was filled with countless mirrors, each labeled with a name. I recognized the mirror I had stolen from Mr. Malard\u2019s house, as well as the mirror from Shatina\u2019s room. And then I realized that this was where Simon went to perform his mirror-reading ritual, to spy on people through the mirrors. It was a bit spine-chilling, and if I didn\u2019t have such trust in Simon\u2019s discretion, I might have found the room far creepier than I did. Perhaps I\u2019m being too generous as it is. The comfortable chair and bottle of brandy suggested that Simon has spent a lot of time in the room in the past.<br /> <br /> Sara and Doc had retrieved a mirror from Lynne\u2019s things, and Simon attempted to use his mirror-reading ceremony to find out where Lynne had fled. But he did not receive a vision of Lynne, not exactly. Instead, a spirit that looked exactly like Lynne appeared in the mirror and confronted us. Simon was even more surprised than I was.<br /> <br /> The spirit was a bit acerbic, but fairly cooperative. She explained that when Lynne was turned into a vampire, she left a piece of her soul behind, and that piece, her shadow, became a doppelg\u00e4nger that inhabits mirrors. She is bound to Lynne, so she has a vested interest in Lynne\u2019s survival, but she also seemed bitterly envious of Lynne.<br /> <br /> Apparently, the mirror ghost was the one who actually stole the artifact at Lynne\u2019s behest. She seemed interested in helping save Lynne from the trouble she is in, so for now it seems the mirror ghost is an ally. I am chilled by the idea that she can freely travel through any mirrors she wishes, so I hope her powers are not so widespread.<br /> <br /> Doc, Natalie and Sara rejoined us after the mirror ghost had retreated into her mirror realm, and we explained what had happened. They were as impressed as we were. They have decided to sneak Lynne into the mansion by inviting her to the firehouse church, which we now own. Doc will then fetch her through the Avernian gate, so there is no way the vampires will be able to track her to the mansion.<br /> <br /> I suggested that they might take some ash from the furnace behind the house and leave it piled inside Lynne\u2019s clothing in the church basement. I felt that might convince Lynne\u2019s pursuers that she had burned to death from sunlight pouring into the basement, or at least confuse them.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m off to bed now. Doc and Sara don\u2019t need me to help fetch Lynne or explain the house rules to her, and Simon is using his Boneyard to gain complete mastery of the house and arrange a basement room for our guest as well as rearrange furniture elsewhere. As a result, the hallways look like a scene from the Sorcerer\u2019s Apprentice, and Tavia is absolutely giddy over it. It\u2019s altogether too much for me though, and tomorrow\u2019s going to be a long day.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Promiscuity</u><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve only just realized how shamefully promiscuous Sara is. I thought she was with a girl named Eve, and was happy that she had found love so soon after joining us. But then I discovered that she was with someone named Cyndi, and wondered what happened to Eve. I honestly thought Sara was cheating on her girlfriend. And now she seems to have become serious with a third girl, Lynne. I don\u2019t know what to think, and Sara herself doesn\u2019t seem committed to any of these \u201crelationships,\u201d leading me to understand that she\u2019s sleeping around for fun.<br /> <br /> I disapprove, but it\u2019s hardly my place to tell her what she can and can\u2019t do. I have the impression, however, that some of these girls are quite attached to Sara, and wonder if she isn\u2019t hurting them. That would be quite cold, I think, and I\u2019d rather not believe that Sara could be so callous. Perhaps it is simply part of the culture they espouse; after all, Natalie wasn\u2019t really any different until recently. Or maybe she feels she can keep her relationship with each girl secret from the others. Whatever the case, I find it sordid and confusing.<br /> <br /> <u>The Mask</u><br /> <br /> The artifact Lynne stole is an ancient Roman mask, allegedly created during a great political upheaval among the vampires. It apparently allows a vampire to control the feral, predatory spirit of other vampires, which would give one of them a great deal of power over others of his kind. I think it\u2019s best to keep such a thing out of the hands of the vampires, for their own good. Anyone who would use such an artifact can\u2019t possibly have good intentions.<br /> <br /> The artifact is safely hidden away. Lynne hasn\u2019t told us where, though I suspect it is trapped inside the mirror realm occupied by Lynne\u2019s reflection. Fortunately, Lynne doesn\u2019t seem to have any desire to use the artifact herself; she claims she simply wants to keep it away from other vampires. I hope that is the truth.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> While it is never said outright, as the PCs don\u2019t really follow the terminology for these things, Lynne is a Hollow Mekhet, as described in their Clanbook. This was not Lynne\u2019s first appearance; Sara encountered her a couple times in the past and passing reference was made I think in Doc\u2019s log but I could be mistaken. Her picture is adorable.<br /> <br /> There were some Ennyl jokes, due to a character in a different game run my Simon\u2019s player, Karen who has a mirror monster called Nerak. Karen/Nerak is a whole different kettle of fish though. Journals for that game are not presently up but hopefully that will change in time, we have some good ones. Anyway.<br /> <br /> I should also mention vampire defenestration was mentioned a few times, and the group was amused by. Again crossing games over, it was noted the Prague Vampire group should be the ones defenestrating people.<br /> <br /> More on this next time, as one more vampire gets into the mix. At least. Comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:45:15-08:00","id":17029,"title":"","content":"Well now, just when you thought things could not get any more complicated, it is time for one of those on the periphery to take the stage, and we get some more Requiem eye view information on the city. Here we go<br /> <br /> <i>Session LXXXIX<br /> </i><b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Thursday, September 23, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a short day, but that does happen when you sleep until 1530 Hours. Once I was up and aware, I took the mysterious string and went to find Lily. She was very busy being cute in the Dining Room. I asked her about the string and she immediately raised her hand, letting me know she put it in my pocket. Got it in one. I gave it back and asked her to put it on Rose\u2019s desk, where she\u2019d see it. She bounded off happily and I walked outside shaking my head.<br /> <br /> Tonight is the Henna party so I went out to help Snowflake get prep the boat. We worked on that until just before the party started. Snowflake has always been peculiar about certain things, but this whole major event has him completely OCD about the tiniest details. We might as well have swabbed the deck with a toothbrush for how perfect things were before he was satisfied. Once they shoved off, I got cleaned up and went down to wait for Lynne to wake up. I was leaning on a column in the Dwarven Throne Room when she came out. She asked if I was supposed to be her jailer. That hit me pretty hard. I tried to immediately assure her she was not a prisoner, but she waved me off. Apparently she was trying to be funny and I was just being too sensitive. I don\u2019t take well to the idea of holding innocents against their will and from where I stand, Lynne is actually innocent. She has unintentionally complicated the fuck out of our plans, but she is still innocent. Anyway, she asked if she could watch TV. There was no way she could understand why I thought watching TV on TV Night was so funny. I directed her to the TV Room as I knew Snowflake would be up there, but suggested she try to avoid the windows. Because I\u2019m paranoid.<br /> <br /> They flipped channels a bit and I struck up a conversations about the Strix. Lynne is either full of shit and great with a story, or she has done some real research. She said that that Gangrel have stories about how vampires actually came from the owls. Somehow they were vampiric Beasts without bodies. I didn\u2019t immediately recognize Gangrel, so she explained they were a Clan. She was Mekhet, Winton and Neon are apparently Daeva. This led into a rough breakdown of New Haven by territory, which Snowflake found most interesting. According to Lynne, anytime you find big houses and rich people, the Lancea Sanctum controls that area. She said there were five vampires from the Lancea Sanctum in control at AMC, but they all disappeared about a year ago. Snowflake and I shared a look at that. Normally the Lancea Sanctum are fairly powerful because they have money, power, and magic learned from early Roman Church. Yale is technically off limits to political power plays because it\u2019s too important for a vampire to control. But Lynne did say that the Circle of the Crone has a weird worship dungeon somewhere under Yale. Snowflake wondered aloud if we should be worried about that. I thought about it but decided that it was Yale, we don\u2019t deal with Yale. If the Skull &amp; Bones Society wants to track down and piss off a vampiric cult of mystics...we don\u2019t deal with Yale. Everyone else in any position of power in the city is Invictus, if Lynne is be believed (and I don\u2019t know why we wouldn\u2019t at this point). She has been sifting through the DVDs for a bit now. Also something important to note, vampires don\u2019t do well with history. Lynne says they get things confused that happened a long time ago. That\u2019s why no one really knows what to do about the Strix even if they were around when Rome fell. That is so odd to me. But then most people think it\u2019s odd I can talk to animals and start fires with my mind, so who am I to talk.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2200 Hours, Thursday, September 23, 2010<br /> <br /> I think I understand how confirmed addicts can O.D. and why vampires get so jaded. If you experience something enough times, it loses impact. I think I\u2019m getting that way with exciting events.<br /> <br /> The others came back in around 2130 Hours and Rose announced them, so the vampires could get their internal turf war settled gently. Snowflake and I led Lynne into the main hall. Chandra never took her suddenly very cold eyes off Lynne, but her words were fairly soothing as she kept telling Lynne that it was okay. Lynne still seemed to shrink a little. Chandra was obviously the dominant vampire in the house from that moment on. Then Rose was possibly the closest to rude any of us have ever seen while dealing with Lynne. I know that she isn\u2019t pleased with the situation, none of us are, but she really made it clear Lynne was not welcome as far as she was concerned. That point was made so finely, Snowflake actually noted that guests of his home would be welcomed as he saw fit. Rose wasn\u2019t there for it, but his words carried a punch. I was impressed and I\u2019m pretty sure Lynne was fully aware of how things fell out after that.<br /> <br /> Nightshade helped smooth things a little by asking about Murder Ballads. Lynne seemed to know without thinking about it that the club was run by the Circle of the Crone. We were happily discussing that when both Chandra and Lynne turned and snarled down the hallway. I heard sounds of someone running. The someone ran into Gretchen and she called the someone Ken. I jumped up and moved between the hallway and \u201cour\u201d vampires. We called down the dark hallway to see if Gretchen was okay. Rose had returned at the signs of trouble by that point. The thick Scottish-accented response that it was the green, hairy monster confused everyone but Rose. When she started running for the hallway, I fell in right behind. It wasn\u2019t until she called out to \u201cUncle Guang\u201d that I understood. The humanoid creature half cowered at our approach. They spoke in Mandarin and Rose seemed completely at ease. I went back to calm the other vampires ready to pounce in the TV Room while Gretchen, Rose, and Guang went to the Library. Snowflake went to investigate at that point, leaving me to entertain. Bright Eyes stayed with Lynne which made things at least a little less awkward. It was strange seeing Chandra so definitely in control though. Knowing about the predatory test of wills and watching it play out are very different than I expected.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Friday, September 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Eventually Rose and the others brought Guang in to meet the growing vampire contingent. Chandra not only remained dominant, but Guang seemed to fall into the Omega position, which I think pissed Rose off. I bowed and tried to greet Guang in Mandarin, but I knew as soon as I spoke I didn\u2019t really get the words right. I\u2019m sure I looked as embarrassed as I felt. Guang bowed in returned however and Rose made proper introductions. She also got to introduce Karl to her uncle, which was really special for her. Unfortunately, Guang forgot himself. A Jiang Shi that smiles at a Brineborn is still a vampire with jagged fangs. Karl tightened at first, I guess thinking some kind of challenge was made. That fact that Guang speaks no English did not help this situation. Eventually Karl realized Guang was trying to be friendly.<br /> <br /> Once that little bit of excitement was over, Rose sent Guang back to the Library with Gretchen and called the Krewe up to the Armory. Once we were there, Rose\u2019s face tightened as she relayed her uncle\u2019s tale of betrayal and enslavement. Apparently a powerful sorcerer sold the ambitious occultist a ritual for immortality. Guang soon learned however that instead of eternal life, he was cursed with unlife. Worse, the ritual placed Guang under the control of the sorcerer, who has collected 8 Jiang Shi so far. Only because Guang was an occultist, he was able to bind himself to Rose as a sort of anchor. I was trembling with rage when Rose finished telling us her uncle\u2019s torment. I tried to fight it down, but Nightshade saw the fires burning in my eyes and immediately shifted away from me. Before I could say anything, Karen came in. This was not a room I was expecting her to come, but she let us know Lynne\u2019s stolen artifact was actually a Deathmask. Karen showed Nightshade\u2019s mask to our guest and she noted they shared similar properties. But I didn\u2019t have the patience to think about that right then and split off to hit the Library. Thinking about it now, this is probably a Primeval Deathmask. Definitely useful, but it would be even more difficult to be on good terms with the vampires if they knew we had that. I guess we\u2019ll have to save that discussion for later.<br /> <br /> I knew I couldn\u2019t just leave for Taiwan without some prep but I had to do something to moved us closer to really kicking this sorcerer in the nuts. I asked Gretchen to help me find a way to track him, preferably using his mystic link to Guang to lead us right to him. I may have been a bit overzealous. After only about fifteen minutes it was obvious to both of us and Guang that this line of thought wasn\u2019t going to work. But as I glanced at the legal pad on the table, I realized I had another option. Running out to grab my sketch pad, I came back and had Gretchen translate. Then I spent the next two hours making a target sketch of the sorcerer. Now we\u2019ll know who we\u2019re dealing with when we get to Taiwan.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, September 23, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> The henna party went off quite well this afternoon. Everyone had fun, I think, though Gretchen\u2019s invasive questioning scandalized Marjorie a bit. Gretchen and Tavia both seem sincerely concerned that Marjorie doesn\u2019t have a boyfriend, though that doesn\u2019t seem to matter so much to Marjorie. After all, she\u2019s a ghost, and ghosts are driven by different passions than we are. Some of them, like the Drowned Bride or Bonnie-Lynn, do seek companionship. Others don\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Marjorie was worried about Naomi hearing Gretchen talk, but I assured her that they didn\u2019t encounter one another often, and I have a feeling Naomi wouldn\u2019t really understand most of what Gretchen says. I certainly don\u2019t, and that\u2019s fine with me.<br /> <br /> Sara did most of henna, and it all turned out beautifully. I keep admiring my hands, which are covered with the most fanciful designs. Poor Tavia nearly went mad waiting for the henna to dry; being unable to use or even move her hands too much while the henna soaked in was hard for her.<br /> <br /> During the party, I spoke to Natalie briefly about reigniting things with Karl. I felt uncomfortable talking to her about it, but I trust her enough now to know that she is sensitive to my needs and would do her best to give me good advice. Also, I like it when she calls me Spooky. I never had nicknames when I was younger, and I appreciate the affection the name implies.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Natalie suggested going somewhere that Karl and I were close\u2014somewhere were felt the passion that I would like to recapture. Perhaps surprising Karl there will send the right message to him and let him know that I want to heat things up again.<br /> <br /> The undersea grotto is perfect. It\u2019s Karl\u2019s special place, and he goes there often to be alone and think. Since he showed it to me, it\u2019s become a place I we both associate with our steamy romance. If he finds me waiting for him there next time he goes, he\u2019ll understand.<br /> <br /> I asked Tavia to let me know next time Karl says anything about going down to the grotto.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, September 23, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> It has been an exciting night! And Uncle Guang is here, finally!<br /> <br /> First off, I met Lynne tonight when we brought Chandra in to make introductions. There was an uncomfortable moment when the two vampires seemed to be struggling with their predatory instincts, but they got it sorted out soon enough, and Chandra took a very dominant attitude toward Lynne.<br /> <br /> I spoke to Lynne only briefly and made sure that Doc had explained the rules of the house to her. I suppose I wasn\u2019t very nice, but I wanted to make sure she wasn\u2019t going to cause any trouble.<br /> <br /> While everyone was getting to know one another, the two vampires perked up. I could sense their predatory instincts again, and then Gretchen or Tavia said something about Ken and a fuzzy green monster. I was confused, but we all realized that something was going on in the library. Doc, Sara and Natalie stayed with the vampires to keep them calm while Alexia, Simon and I ran downstairs to see if we were in danger.<br /> <br /> There in the library was my uncle. He didn\u2019t look at all like I remembered him. Instead, I recognized the ghoulish thing I had chased across campus some months ago. His features were the same, but his pale skin was drawn and gaunt and covered with a very fine layer of gray-green hair, a bit like the fur on a cat\u2019s nose. I immediately recognized the tell-tale marks of a jiang shi.<br /> <br /> My uncle was shocked to see me, and he seemed frightened and timid. He calmed down once I began speaking to him, but even then he remained uneasy and a bit feral, as though it had become his natural state. The nearby presence of two other vampire wasn\u2019t helping. It made me sad to see him like that. The Uncle Guang I remember may not have gotten on well with the family, but he was always confident in his occult pursuits.<br /> <br /> Guang and I spoke at length with Simon. Guang doesn\u2019t speak English, but he does understand Latin, so Simon could communicate with him perfectly well; he just couldn\u2019t follow when Guang and I were speaking Mandarin.<br /> <br /> Guang was anxious about what had happened to me. He had been quite frightened when I transformed into a flock of crows to chase him down before, so I explained how I had died and come back as something more. He was upset to learn that I had died, but happy that I came back. I asked how it was he had become a jiang shi, and he told me his sad story.<br /> <br /> He attempted a ritual to gain immortality. The ritual was sold to him by a powerful mystic, but it was a trap. The magic turned Guang into a jiang shi under the sorcerer\u2019s control. All would have been lost except that Guang was able to leverage his occult knowledge to bind himself to me. He knew I was in Connecticut, and therefore as far from the sorcerer as possible. Since I now serve as his anchor, he is able to escape the sorcerer\u2019s direct control by fleeing Taiwan and spending as much time as he can in America. The sorcerer can still command him, but not if he keeps his distance.<br /> <br /> Guang isn\u2019t the only jiang shi the sorcerer has acquired this way, and the sorcerer is quick to destroy any who defy his will. Guang has nearly been destroyed at least twice, and only his connection to me saved him.<br /> <br /> I am extremely angry about this. So is Doc, who always reacts badly to any form of slavery or occult deceit. Natalie is frightened of Doc\u2019s rage, so she\u2019s keeping her distance from him right now. As soon as we can, however, I think we will venture to Taiwan and try to find out more about this sorcerer. We must track him down and destroy him, not only for my uncle\u2019s sake, but also to keep him from victimizing anyone else with his promises of immortality.<br /> <br /> I was surprised to learn that Guang has been visiting the house for some time now without our knowledge. He has befriended Gretchen, after a fashion, and she has been allowing him to use the library to research ways he might break free of the sorcerer\u2019s control. Apparently, he introduced himself as \u201cKen,\u201d a character from some TV show, so that\u2019s what Gretchen has been calling him. I wish I had know that he\u2019s been here before now, but I can understand why he was frightened of me after the last time we ran into him. We seem to have gotten past that now, though. He never saw the signs I left in Taipei, though, and says that he has been feeding here, not in Taiwain. That means the jiang shi attack I investigated a month or so ago wasn\u2019t him. It must have been one of the sorcerer\u2019s other jiang shi victims.<br /> <br /> We have arranged a room in the house for Guang\u2014Bonnie-Lynn\u2019s old room. Jiang Shi aren\u2019t harmed by sunlight, but they are paralyzed during the day. My uncle prefers to remain active as much as possible, and since he can transport himself to any of his anchors, he\u2019s been moving back and forth between here and Taiwan a lot, trying to stay wherever it is night. This way, though, he can stay safely out of the sorcerer\u2019s reach even during the day.<br /> <br /> After everything had calmed down, we introduced Guang to the other vampires so that they could sort out their predatory status. He seemed frightened of the other two, which is awful. But then I introduced him to Karl, and I think it made him genuinely happy to see me with someone. He never got to meet Richard; I\u2019m glad he can meet the other man who has become so precious to me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, September 23, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> After things had settled down in the house, Doc, Simon Gretchen and Guang disappeared into the library to research Guang\u2019s problem with the sorcerer. I wanted to help, but felt that I would only be in the way. Nevertheless, I was feeling restless, and decided to venture into the Underworld again. I\u2019m feeling drawn to it more and more, and I need to work on arranging a retreat there, somewhere safe and comfortable that I can make my own. Somewhere I can leave some things and go to for a day or two at a time when the need takes me. Also, I felt that it might be useful to have such a place ready in case we cannot sever the sorcerer\u2019s control over Guang and are forced to hide my uncle somewhere.<br /> <br /> I went to the diner, as usual, and chatted to Janice about it over a strawberry milkshake. Specifically, I asked about a lighthouse I had seen along the coast of the Underworld sea below the cliffs. I thought it would make a nice and picturesque home away from home if I could claim it.<br /> <br /> Janice says that the lighthouse is kept by some sort of powerful thing, which I suspect to be a geist of some sort. Its large eye shines with a bright light, and her description brought to mind images of the vulture-eyed old man from Edgar Allen Poe\u2019s \u201cTell-Tale Heart.\u201d The Lighthouse Keeper asks visitors if they have a reason for disturbing him, and if they do, he might let them stay a night. If they don\u2019t, they disappear forever.<br /> <br /> The lighthouse is surrounded by luminous crabs that can take the plasm right out of you, so ghosts stay away. Furthermore, there is allegedly something dark and sinister in a shipwreck just off the coast. It is some sort of coral monster, and Janice thinks that it and the Lighthouse Keeper might be enemies.<br /> <br /> I think I might be able to negotiate with the Lighthouse Keeper. Perhaps dealing with his enemy in exchange for a claim on the lighthouse. I would prefer a place all my own, but having the Keeper there to watch over things and keep it safe when I\u2019m not around might be nice. I won\u2019t know, though, until I visit the place and talk to him.<br /> <br /> Of course, I\u2019m not going to do this before the Alexia\u2019s wedding, and I\u2019m certainly not going to do it without the rest of the krewe. Exploring the local Underworld on my own is one thing. But approaching something powerful and potentially dangerous like that is not something I\u2019m going to do by myself.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>The String</u><br /> <br /> I found the string that I placed in Doc\u2019s pocket on my the desk in my room when I returned from work today. Lily seems to have had something to do with it, and I think Doc asked her to return it to me. His way of saying \u201cthanks\u201d I suppose. I do hope this means he got on well with Noriko.<br /> <u><br /> Cults and Masks</u><br /> <br /> Natalie discovered from Lynne that vampires do own Murder Ballads. The ones who own it are from a vampiric group known as the Cycle of the Crone or Cult of the Crone\u2026something like that. I didn\u2019t really catch it all, as I was not directly involved in the conversation, but it sounds as though they worship an archetypal goddess figure.<br /> Also, the relic mask Lynne stole is actually a death mask. That\u2019s bad business.<br /> <br /> <u>Mandarin</u><br /> <br /> Doc did introduce himself to my uncle in halting Mandarin. I think Doc was embarrassed by his lack of skill with the language, but I told him that my uncle appreciated it. People from Taiwan, and many other Asian nations, for that matter, respect it when people really try to communicate in our language, even if they aren\u2019t very good at it. It\u2019s something Americans don\u2019t really understand.<br /> <br /> Doc is even more interested in learning Mandarin now, so I suppose I\u2019ll be working with him on that.<br /> <br /> <u>Underworld Exploration</u><br /> <br /> As I was leaving the Underworld in the early hours of morning, I ran across Sara leaving Lynne\u2019s room in the basement. We were both somewhat surprised. Sara was curious about what I had been doing, so I told her that I have been going into the Underworld more frequently of late, exploring a bit and simply spending time there.<br /> <br /> Sara seemed excited by that, and asked if she could go with me next time. She hasn\u2019t been to the Underworld much aside from the time we helped the nuns beneath St. Mary\u2019s, and she wants to become more familiar with it. I suppose she must feel drawn there like I do.<br /> <br /> I agreed to let her know next time I\u2019m going. I should instruct her to bring some colorful trinkets as gifts and currency as well.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> September 23rd, 2010<br /> <br /> -New day, new day.<br /> <br /> -Henna party tonight<br /> <br /> -Will be attending, but not getting decorated.<br /> <br /> -Karen and I are gonna have to make time for Tatum when this is all over.<br /> <br /> -Bah I don\u2019t like not having Karen around during the day.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -OK, things with the 27 Club are nearly go.<br /> <br /> -First bookings done. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -That\u2019s a good feeling.<br /> <br /> -Need to talk to Cindy about what her band/not band status is.<br /> <br /> -Karen home! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -To the boat!<br /> <br /> -I wish I were not such a clean freak sometimes.<br /> <br /> -Chandra and Alexia are having a good time.<br /> <br /> -Aw Spooky, lay it on me.<br /> <br /> -Poor Spooky<br /> <br /> -I hope I helped!<br /> <br /> -Gretchen! What the Frimple???<br /> <br /> -I watched the feminine mystique as it slowly expired on the floor\u2026<br /> <br /> -Oh goddess she is not going to ask Jasmine?<br /> <br /> -Apparently not. Whew.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jogg<br /> <br /> -Oink?<br /> <br /> -Right, Lynne, I nearly forgot.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear.<br /> <br /> -The\u2026fuck\u2026?<br /> <br /> -Gretchen is officially insane.<br /> <br /> -Ok, so. Well. That was weird.<br /> <br /> -Interesting.<br /> <br /> -The vampires seem to be happy, or what passes for happy among vampires.<br /> <br /> -seekrit meeting<br /> <br /> -Huh<br /> <br /> -Oh goddess Doc could you not scare me so much? Please?<br /> <br /> - <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -People are talking, but can\u2019t focus Doc\u2019s rage will eat me.<br /> <br /> -Goddess I need to get out of here.<br /> <br /> -Oh, Karen, interesting.<br /> <br /> -Ok, well, that makes sense, sort of.<br /> <br /> -Where is that crafty lady o\u2019 mine?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LXXXIX<br /> </i><br /> The initial meeting of the vampires ran that way as Chandra has Blood Potency 5, Lynne 3, Guang 0. Guang Sung actually does have a Blood Potency rating, just one of zero. You can see Jiang Shi in Night Horrors: the Wicked Dead for more information. Living Anchor, a Merit that Jasmine fulfills for Guang, is there too.<br /> <br /> Guang Sung actually referred to himself as Ken Malansky when he met Gretchen. Ken Malansky was a character from the Perry Mason TV movies, and Guang is something of a Perry Mason fan. Gretchen did not catch the reference, but she was aware \u201cKen\u201d was being less then truthful but, as a green hairy monster, probably had an unpronounceable name. Guang was trying to access the library to learn how to break the effect, and coincidentally meeting Gretchen (who could communicate with him in Latin) convinced the <span style=\"color:green\">House </span>that Guang was OK.<br /> <br /> The Lancea Sanctum actually controls a very specific wealthy area, but Doc\u2019s comments are a logical understanding of what Lynne said.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t repeat the particular question Gretchen asked Natalie, just say it was health/beauty related and stopped the game for a few moments.<br /> <br /> Jasmine hit Psyche 6, and several characters are leaning that way. Thus the interest in Underworld headquarters.<br /> <br /> Tell me if anything needs clarification. Otherwise, catch you in two weeks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:46:32-08:00","id":17030,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to haunted Connecticut and check on our monsters in the Middle Shadows. Its time we had a little wedding\u2026love is in the air!<br /> <i><br /> Session XC</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Friday, September 24, 2010<br /> <br /> I went to bed fairly early last night to keep myself from stalking around the House and terrifying anyone. It really seemed to help. I got up like normal and was able to meditate without issues. That was important given how angry I was last night. After only about a half hour, I came down to breakfast.<br /> <br /> Plans for the next few weeks were discussed, given Chandra and Cupcake are leaving for Paris for two weeks. Rose informed us that she had been sneaking off to the Underworld lately. Not the safest move, but people don\u2019t bitch at me for going on patrol, so I\u2019ll just keep my mouth shut. Anyway, she found a place she wants to claim for herself. It\u2019s apparently a lighthouse out by the Sea of Darkness. If the geography holds, it should be close to Lighthouse Park. Fitting at least. If I had to guess, I think that Rose and the Drowned Bride have grown so close they have to spend time Greyside now. I know that The Dog and I have discussed it before, just not something that comes up all the time. But this lighthouse already has something inhabiting it. Something that sounds like a geist. She wants to try and either flush it out or make a deal with it. Part of the agreement would be to find some way to handle the glowing crabs on the beach. From what Rose says, the crabs each Plasm and can destroy ghosts. They are somehow tied to a sunken ship at the seafloor leading to the lighthouse. Visions of my own Black Pearl came to my mind unbidden. I realize it was completely selfish, but I immediately signed on to this idea when she mentioned the sunken ship. There was even talk about taking supplies down to build something into the Bluffs on the other side for Snowflake. This would need some scouting and we also needed some preliminary reconn on Taipei. Rose told us about the abandoned Buddhist Monastery she was travelling to and thought it might be useful as a base of operations in Taiwan. Guang\u2019s house may still be available, though the sorcerer is certainly keeping watch there. We mentioned trying to get it in order so Rose can move Guang back into his home when this is over. Between investigating our own locations in the Underworld and setting up our own Krewe base in Taipei, it sounds like we\u2019re going to be busy while the honeymooners are gone.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve come back to the shop to check in. I need to order a few things and make a cheat sheet on the herbs so the girls don\u2019t have to stumble through questions, but otherwise they have done a fantastic job while I\u2019ve been gone. I did notice there were more college guys in than usual, but I also know why that is too. It\u2019s kinda of relaxing to be back here again.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2200 Hours, Friday, September 24, 2010<br /> <br /> I got back to the House around 1500 Hours and got a text right after I walked in from a TigerKittyMeltdown asking, \u201cAm I your girlfriend?\u201d I realized immediately that I was an idiot. I hadn\u2019t talked to Noriko at all since she went home Wednesday morning. I\u2019m not that kind of guy, so I called her right then. She answered quickly and I apologized for not calling. I didn\u2019t want to sound lame, but Wednesday night was vampires, Thursday night was vampires, and the wedding was going the whole time. So instead of sounding like a player with bad excuses, I asked her if she would like to be my girlfriend. Listening to myself say the words, I thought of junior high, but she was so quick to answer I lost that train of thought. I couldn\u2019t think of a good reason why a woman who could easily take care of herself shouldn\u2019t go out with a guy who\u2019d seen some things. I asked if she wanted to come over and I think she jumped and grabbed her stuff before getting off the phone.<br /> <br /> She made it to the house about twenty minutes later. I smiled when I opened the door and started to greet her, but she pounced on me and kissed all over my face. I got the very real impression it might have been awhile since she had been safely involved with anyone. Once she was standing on the floor again, I gave her the tour of the House. I didn\u2019t just unload all our secrets on her, but I did give her the \u201cWhat you need to know to safely visit Dark Haven Bluffs\u201d speech. We wandered the House talking and enjoying each other\u2019s company until Snowflake came to herd the Krewe to the rehearsal. Noriko watched the proceeding and didn\u2019t even laugh at all the weirdness. Rose was incredibly warm and happy. It was a little surreal but I guess it was the wedding and Noriko being here. Either way, Rose was positively giddy. Snowflake on the other hand was the most authoritative and demanding I had ever seen him. He was his normal gracious self with Chandra and Cupcake, but with all the rest of us, he was nearly a tyrant. I chalked it up to being nervous and wanting everything to be perfect for the wedding. Lynne came up after dark and watched for a while, but based on the looks from Chandra and Rose, she stayed at the back and didn\u2019t say much. At one point, I walked back and sat with Noriko while some of the others were going over details. She was staring at her phone which seemed to constantly get messages. She looked up at me with a blank stare and said she should have never mentioned me to her mom. She showed me the phone and I blinked a few times before admitting to her that I didn\u2019t yet speak Japanese. Noriko snapped out of her fugue and blushed a little. Getting the translation was like hearing a laundry list of things her mom expected of any man that she went out with. I asked about her parents and learned that they were still in Japan. Snowflake ushered me off before I could get much more conversation going.<br /> <br /> When the rehearsal was (finally) over, I scooped Snowflake up like in the movies and rushed into the bar. Then I put him down and handed him a bottle of scotch. He was catch off guard and wasn\u2019t sure what was happening until the scotch arrived. Then he shrugged and poured a drink. I laughed until I turned around and saw Tavia standing in the doorway behind me. There was no kindness in her large eyes and her features were equally unwelcoming. When she saw Snowflake intact and happy, she half nodded as her expression became more normal. Afterward, she soundlessly turned and walked away. ...That was creepy. Now I\u2019m going to put this away and get to know my new girlfriend better.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1315 Hours, Saturday, September 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I woke up early this morning after sharing hours with Noriko last night. It was nice to talk and kiss and touch like that. There was something about that it just felt...innocent? Anyway, I slipped out of bed to go meditate around 0600 Hours. Centering was again a fairly simple affair as I seemed to glide along the mental path today. When I found myself awake and centered by 6:30, I decided to be a decent housemate. After getting cleaned up, I went out and get breakfast for whoever eventually stumbled out of bed. I left a note back in my room to let Noriko know I was running errands for the wedding. It\u2019s probably clich\u00e9 but when I went in, she was catnapping. I saw an eye peeking out from the covers before her hand slid out and reached for me. I sat next to her and kissed her before whispering what I was doing. She nodded and rolled over. Noriko is adorable.<br /> <br /> Quietly, I got my Service Dress Blues to be pressed and I headed out to get a regulation haircut. I got back around 1100 Hours and found Noriko staring at her phone again. She blinked a little when she saw me, but she didn\u2019t seem upset with the haircut. She asked me about the wedding and I realized it was only a few hours away and she only had the shorts and t-shirt she came over in last night. I asked if she wanted to go shopping for something to wear, but she said she had something, she just needed to go get it. I went to talk with Chandra to make sure it would be okay to add a +1 to the ceremony. I think Chandra was a little surprised, but didn\u2019t mind the added guest.<br /> <br /> Snowflake and I mounted cameras around the wedding venue and on the widow\u2019s walk to record the whole ceremony from any angle we could think of. The plan is to edit all the best shots together to have a proper video without having a normal person here to freak out at the ghosts, living doll, etc. Honestly I think we did it so we could both give it to the happy couple and send a copy to Ronin, since she\u2019s still MIA.<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Snowflake were both visibly nervous about their speaking parts when I came back down. Snowflake was assembling images and recordings of speeches so I knew what he was about to do. Thinking it might help, I offered to give Nightshade a little luck with her oration. She immediately jumped at the chance and the three of us headed down to the GMC Room.<br /> <br /> Now we all need to get dressed so Snowflake doesn\u2019t get a whip.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2200 Hours, Saturday, September 25, 2010<br /> <br /> As weddings that last a full week go, this one was quite beautiful. After the meticulous rehearsal last night, the ceremony was actually very smooth. Nightshade officiated and did a wonderful job, if I do say so myself. Snowflake gave a moving Best Man Speech at the reception and then the dancing started. As I gave away the bride, I got the first dance. Cupcake just seemed to drink in the moment and everything about the day. Then I danced with Chandra as it seemed like the only fair thing to do. Nightshade danced with me next, though she danced with the everyone present in the Krewe except for Rose. And that\u2019s about the time I realized that my dance card was going to stay full. Being professionally trained means everyone wants to dance with you, even if I\u2019m not a professional. After Nightshade, I danced with Noriko and showed off a little, but just enough to make her dance feel special. Then I danced with Karen because she likes to dance at any occasion. Next I danced with Marjorie because I didn\u2019t want her to be left out of something I knew she understood. There was a break in the dancing for a few minutes and I explained why it was a big deal that Snowflake and Tavia were dancing together for a third time. This was clearly a new concept to her, but she nodded and watched the various couples move on and off the floor. She danced with other people as well. Next up for me was Bright Eyes, then Dierdre. I did notice Noriko watching seemingly uninterested and realized just how catlike she really is. Before things wound down, I danced with Grin as well, as he seemed up for it but was turned down by Karl. There were a few cheers as we headed to the floor, but I wasn\u2019t too concerned. We were there to have a good time. Lynne even joined the party. Bright Eyes danced a few times with her, but they also just sat and talked a bit. I noticed that Rose and then Karl disappeared before Chandra and Cupcake announced that they were going to take the yacht out. We all cheered and threw flower petals or blew bubbles at them as they left. The Krewe and all our various +1s had pitched in together to get a full set of china for the shower since Cupcake didn\u2019t have any. We also got a full set of silverware to match as a wedding gift. While Snowflake and I were mounting the cameras, we talked about making a new cabinet to keep all these presents in.<br /> <br /> When things started calming back down, Noriko informed me that she was happy I was her boyfriend. I think that about sums up my day, so I\u2019m going to end here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, September 24, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I had a particularly good meditation this morning. The Bride and I are very much in tune with one another, no doubt because of our excitement over Alexia and Chandra\u2019s wedding.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast, the krewe discussed our plans and how Alexia and Chandra\u2019s two-week honeymoon would affect them. I mentioned my recent trips to the Underworld and I explained my wish to establish a retreat there where I can go and stay when the urge strikes me. To my surprise, the others understood immediately. I had expected them to scold me unnecessarily about going to the Underworld on my own, but I was pleased to find that my forays didn\u2019t distress them at all. Indeed, the others must also be starting to feel the pull of the Underworld, because Doc and Simon began a lively discussion of the ways they might also establish their own private getaways.<br /> <br /> We also decided that we would spend much of next week in Taipei, preparing things there. It will give me the opportunity to introduce my friends to my father. Unfortunately, it means Jean will be on his own for training next week, but I have confidence that he handle himself for awhile. I considered getting Rita to fill in for me\u2014she is an excellent swimmer\u2014but she and I both decided that she wasn\u2019t quite ready to be left to her own devices with a handsome man like Jean.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, Karen drew me aside to ask if I was okay. She and Natalie have both been worried that I\u2019ve been especially distant and melancholy of late, and after hearing me talk about needing to spend time in the Underworld, she was afraid I had some sort of supernatural sickness. I assured her I was fine, that my dark mood had mostly passed, and that the pull of the Underworld was a manifestation of my deepening connection to the dead, which, all in all, is not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, September 24, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Karen and I went shopping for matching dresses to wear at the wedding. Alexia didn\u2019t want us to bother with formal bridesmaid dresses, but we wanted something that would look good and compliment the bride\u2019s clothing. Since Alexia is wearing mostly red (this being an Indian wedding), Karen and I found charming, simple white dresses with red trim. I can\u2019t really speak for myself, but Karen looks very nice in hers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, September 24, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> The wedding rehearsal went quite well tonight. There were no major problems, though Natalie seemed more nervous than I expected. I felt like everything was a whirl of activity, and I was rushing here and there trying to make sure everything was just right. But my efforts paled in comparison to Simon\u2019s. He was almost a nervous wreck as he managed every detail, intent on making sure that the wedding will be flawless. And yet whenever he spoke to Alexia and Chandra, his whole demeanor changed. He seemed calm and collected, as if that would assure them that they need not worry about a thing. More than anything, Simon wants the couple to be happy on their wedding day. It\u2019s terribly sweet, even if Simon has been frighteningly manic over the past day or so.<br /> <br /> Noriko showed up to hang out with Doc this evening, so she was there for the rehearsal. I greeted her warmly, glad to see that she and Doc have hit it off so well. I\u2019m so happy to see that he\u2019s involved with someone who really appreciates him.<br /> <br /> Lily and Naomi were very good during the rehearsal. Lily did a fine job as flower girl, and was quite well behaved, and Naomi managed to sit still and not get into any trouble (which is hardly surprising, as most of the trouble she gets into is Lily\u2019s fault anyway). So after the rehearsal, I took both of them into the kitchen for a little treat. Lily got a bright new pink bow barrette for her hair, and Naomi got a tasty cupcake. I had to rely on Doc\u2019s help to destroy the cupcake earlier in the day with a ceremony that would transform it into a ghostly object that Naomi could eat, but it was worth it to see the look of delight on her face as she munched away. I should get Doc to teach me that ceremony in case I want to make another treat for Naomi in the future. I hate to bother him with it with everything else he is working on, like his shop and the van he has been rebuilding.<br /> <br /> I spent the evening after the rehearsal helping Alexia cook for the wedding tomorrow. And now I\u2019m off to bed, though it may be hard to sleep. I\u2019m almost as excited tonight as I was the night before my wedding to Richard!<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, September 25, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> What a wonderful wedding!<br /> <br /> The wedding today was beautiful, full of joy and roses and the closeness that comes from being a family. The whole household was there, including Karl and Gretchen, and Deirdre, Mr. Malard, Angelique and Grin joined us as well. It was small but intimate. Alexia was gorgeous in her gown, which was a fine reward for all the hours we spent helping her get ready. It\u2019s a good thing I was there, because Karen, Tavia and Natalie would have lost everything from hairpins to stockings if I had not kept up with it all. Chandra was dashing as well, though I think she would have looked much better in a nice dress rather than the more masculine clothing she chose.<br /> <br /> Doc was very handsome as he gave Alexia away, and Natalie performed the ceremony with dignity and poise. What she lacked in gravitas, she made up for in warmth, which was probably more fitting for a wedding like this anyway.<br /> <br /> I suspect that Simon was out of sorts making sure everything was just right before the wedding, but once the ceremony began, he became a sea of tranquility, and seemed to enjoy the event as much as anyone else. Tavia was at his side the whole time, which I\u2019m certain helped.<br /> <br /> During the reception, there was a lot of laughing and dancing. Even I laughed quite a lot, which is rare. Lily was energetic, and I think she enjoyed the atmosphere of romance. I danced twice with Karl, and during our second dance, which was slow and romantic, I laid my head against his chest. It was nice to hear his heart beat, and I could sense him relaxing and enjoying the moment. I also danced with Mr. Malard and with Grin. Natalie asked me quietly if I\u2019d like to dance, but I politely refused. I don\u2019t really feel right dancing with another woman like that, though I was certainly pleased to see most of the other women at the reception enjoying dances with one another.<br /> <br /> Tavia danced tree times with Simon, and made something of a show if it. She obviously intends to marry him soon, though I think most of us assumed that was coming, so her antics were not surprise. However, Natalie and Karen also danced together three times. It was very touching and gentle announcement of their intentions toward one another.<br /> <br /> After the reception, Alexia and Chandra departed to the yacht to spend their wedding night there, and the rest of us departed, many to spend time with lovers. Before she disappeared with Simon, Tavia found a chance to tell me that Karl was planning to visit the undersea grotto once night fell, so I resolved to go meet him there.<br /> <br /> Once the sun set, I donned my swimsuit and slipped out of the house. I felt a bit like a teenager sneaking out to meet her boyfriend. I dove into the sea and swam down to the grotto, where I waited for Karl.<br /> <br /> When he arrived, the warm look on his face told me that he understood. Even if we could have spoken underwater, we didn\u2019t need words. We swam together and embraced. As our hands caressed and explored each other, we recaptured the passion that has been lost these last few weeks, and for a time, the world no longer existed. We had found each other again. We made love, and it was simply amazing. I had forgotten how incredible it could be with someone you really love.<br /> <br /> The Drowned Bride is aflutter with excitement and love and wonder and a thousand other wonderful emotions that I can barely explain. But as usual, her feelings echo my own. I\u2019ve taken a big step toward what we both want\u2014need, even. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s ever been this content before.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Karl and I realized that we had to return to the house. Even though neither of us wanted to, we decided to go to bed in our separate rooms. We didn\u2019t want to make a spectacle, not on Alexia\u2019s wedding night and especially not with Tavia\u2019s almost obsessive interest in our relationship. And I think both of us are a little scared to move too quickly. But I think I will sleep well tonight, cozy in the warm afterglow.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Krewe Plans</u><br /> <br /> We took the time Friday morning to make our plans for the next few weeks:<br /> <br /> - Before Alexia and Chandra go away on honeymoon, we will scout out the lighthouse and other Underworld spots along the coast. My talk of establishing an Underworld refuge in response to my urge to visit there more often has encouraged Doc and Simon to think about what they will do once the Underworld calls to them as well. As a result, they want to see if there is anywhere they might claim or carve out a niche. Doc was particularly interested in the sunken ship off the coast from the lighthouse, and wants to see if he can raise it and turn it into a retreat for himself. I suppose there is a romance to that, though the Bride cannot fathom why anyone would want to spend their time in the hulk of a ghost ship, not after she languished for ages in the sunken wreck within which she died.<br /> <br /> - While Chandra and Alexia are away, we plan to visit Taipei to prepare our attack against the sorcerer who trapped my uncle. Among other things, I suggested that we might be able to establish ourselves in the abandoned Buddhist temple haunt near my old neighborhood. I\u2019ve used its Avernian gate to go back and forth a time or two (thanks to Doc or Natalie). Doc and Simon also felt it would be a good idea to check out Guang\u2019s house and to make sure it is still in good shape, with rent and utilities up to date, so that Guang will have a place to live when this business with the sorcerer is done. I\u2019m glad they thought of that.<br /> <br /> <br /> - After Alexia and Chandra return, Natalie\u2019s 27 Club will open and then we will try to establish a refuge in the Underworld lighthouse and go to Taipei to rid my uncle of the sorcerer who deceived him.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Taoist Magic</u><br /> <br /> I woke especially early the morning of the wedding so that I could check on my uncle before the sunrise paralyzed him. I must try to get him some more interesting videos to watch during the day, as Tavia\u2019s choices aren\u2019t always to his liking. Perhaps something to help him learn English.<br /> <br /> I also asked a bit about Taoist magic. I know he is a skilled practitioner of the Taoist arts, and I would like to learn. He says that his books (and much of his occult paraphernalia) were willed to me. I wonder why I never received them? I must ask my father about it when I return to Taipei next week.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XC</i><br /> <br /> Main thing to report that was never directly mentioned was Natalie, in fact, contacted Noriko and told her to contact Doc. Noriko had been waiting to see if he would contact her after sex or not, and Natalie figured since he had not mentioned her he had too much on his mind and did not want Noriko giving up on him/getting mad at him.<br /> <br /> There was some amusement that Gretchen, who still calls Guang \u201cKen\u201d (and refers to him as a fuzzy green monster) decided to show him <i>The 10th Kingdom</i> during the day since he was paralyzed. Unfortunately, in her excitement she forgot he does not speak English, and has little understanding of Western Fairytales, so the whole thing was utterly baffling and incomprehensible to him.<br /> <br /> So that\u2019s the wedding then. Stay tuned for next time when another engagement is announced, Lily continues to scheme, and Jasmine gives relationship advice. See you then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:49:39-08:00","id":17031,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check back on our gang of walking dead up Connecticut way. Unfortunately, we are shorter on journals this time due to Doc\u2019s player having to miss and writing commitments preventing a Natalie journal, but we have a longer then usual Jasmine journal to cover the session. But you may still have to do some real work this hour if reading at work, sorry about that. Doc and Simon\u2019s players were missing this session, and we will discuss this a bit after the journals. But lets get rolling.<br /> <br /> Edit: Doc's Log has been retroactively added to this post.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCI</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc's Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Monday, September 27, 2010<br /> <br /> It was a busy weekend. Today was just as busy, but very different.<br /> <br /> Cupcake and Chandra left for Paris this morning. I helped them load the taxi for the airport while most of the others were still in bed. I\u2019m sure they will have a great time...but just in case I made sure to do a little investigative web searching for larger cemeteries around Paris. The maps really helped in the event I need to go get them.<br /> <br /> Once Snowflake was up and moving around, we discussed how we could spend the day. It\u2019s Study day so he was planning to learn what he needed to make the china cabinet for Cupcake\u2019s new China. We looked over that together and made sure we had all the materials on hand. He even showed me how to mark the wood before making cuts with the bandsaw. That led us to the other part of the day. I\u2019ve been realizing that when a fight starts, I tend to be very obvious with my attacks. And while I\u2019m okay with that, even Rose is more subtle than I am when we really have to throw down. Thus I asked Snowflake about Curse. I haven\u2019t learned a Manifestation in a while and the Dog of War isn\u2019t any more subtle than I am. I just wanted to be useful without always tipping our hand. Snowflake was surprised but seemed more than happy to teach me. We share a Key so that helped but also learning from Snowflake seemed natural. Maybe it was just the way things should be on Study day. While the others got things ready for our trip to Taipei, I learned the subtle art of curses.<br /> <br /> Now I need to get my stuff together too. We\u2019ve worked out the times so we can leave just after midnight to arrive a little after 2000 Hours Taipei time.That will work out for Guang with the daylight issues and allow us to have dinner with Rose\u2019s dad.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, September 26, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> This morning seemed brighter than any morning I can remember since Richard died, and the early autumn chill was invigorating and inviting when I went out to perform my Tai Chi meditations. Memories of last night lingered pleasantly, bringing an unbidden but welcome smile to my lips. I could hardly wait to see Karl at breakfast.<br /> <br /> Of course, I had to get inside and sort out breakfast myself, since Alexia and Chandra were enjoying the morning of their honeymoon, but I didn\u2019t mind. Karl joined me in the kitchen shortly before the rest of the household made it downstairs, and it was nice having a quiet moment with him before the day really began.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, September 26, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I made a trip into the Underworld to investigate the Lighthouse today. Doc and Simon were elsewhere, but I asked Sara, Natalie and Alexia to join me since it might be dangerous and I didn\u2019t want to risk going alone. I led the way; I\u2019ve grown so used to the Underworld that I have little trouble finding my way around, and I\u2019ve managed to learn much of the area around our Avernian gate.<br /> <br /> We stopped by the diner first. Poor Alexia chose to wait outside; I think she\u2019s worried that she might be too tempted by the Underworld\u2019s food. But Natalie, Sara and I went inside and had a nice chat with Janice over milkshakes. At least, the chat was nice until Natalie asked about Janice\u2019s last name. Janice bristled at that, and informed us that she would rather not discuss it. I told her it was okay, and Natalie helped calm her down, so there was no harm done. I personally suspect that Janice did some very bad things and is trying to make amends for her past by helping other ghosts. But she\u2019s my friend, so I\u2019m willing to respect her privacy.<br /> <br /> I led the way to the sea from the diner. The Underworld ocean always strikes me as ominously beautiful: a vast sea captured in a cavern so large that the opposite walls are lost in darkness. The faint luminescence of a moonlit night illuminates the sea, and something like stars sparkle here and there in the cavern ceiling overhead, all the way to horizon.<br /> <br /> The Lighthouse stands upon a rocky outcropping over the sea, tall and dark, with its pale, ghostly light stretching gently across the waves. We made our way toward it, unsure of what we would find.<br /> <br /> Janice had warned me about the soul-drinking crabs. They were clustered in small groups on the beach around the Lighthouse, glowing softly. Some of them were quite large, easily the size of a dog, and as we approached, they began to scuttle hungrily toward us. I suggested that I should hold them off while the others made for the Lighthouse, but Sara had a better idea. She shifted into her Pyre-Flame Caul and burst into ghostly flame. The crabs fled from her as she ran toward them and did not seem interested in harassing us any further.<br /> <br /> I knocked on the Lighthouse\u2019s door, and a man in a faded yellow fisherman\u2019s coat and hat answered. He stood well over two meters, and he had only one huge eye that beamed with light. His large mouth was filled with shark-like teeth. I suppose he might have been terrifying if we weren\u2019t used to dealing with such otherworldly beings, but the way he was forced to stoop beneath the house\u2019s low ceilings made him less impressive than he might have been otherwise. He was simply called the Lighthouse Keeper.<br /> <br /> The Lighthouse Keeper was very gracious and polite, and even offered us tea after I explained why we had come. I told him that I was looking for a place to stay, an Underworld retreat that I could come to when the need struck me. I asked if we might have a tour of the Lighthouse, and he guided us through the house, though we did not go into the lighthouse tower itself.<br /> <br /> The entry room is rather small, with raincoats and other gear hanging on pegs on the wall or stacked neatly on a bench. A bare light bulb sways constantly in the center of the room. It wasn\u2019t exactly inviting, but the rest of the house was cozy enough, and I\u2019m certain that I can make it more so. Everything was quaint, attractive, and well-kept. There are a few rooms with beds in them, all attached to a central kitchen and dining area. The wooden walls are painted in a faded, dull red, and the wood is slightly warped, as though they had been water damaged at some point in the past. In fact, most of the furniture looks somewhat water damaged, though it\u2019s clean and functional. I suspect that the Lighthouse must have fallen into the sea, which is how it\u2019s echo came to rest in the Underworld. I should research and find out more about it.<br /> <br /> I asked about the entity lurking in the shipwreck off the coast, and the Lighthouse Keeper explained that it was Pup Pid. He is a pirate skeleton made of coral, and he commands the monstrous creatures and the drowned dead of the sea. His victims become drowned things under his power; I suppose I\u2019ll call them the Drowned. I think the crabs also belong to Pup Pid.<br /> <br /> The Lighthouse Keeper operates the lighthouse in part to keep the horrors that lurk in the sea from coming ashore. His efforts keep Pup Pid in check, which is a good thing.<br /> <br /> In the end, I was able to make a deal with the Lighthouse Keeper. He will allow me to move into one of the rooms in the Lighthouse and share the place with him whenever I visit. He rarely comes down from the tower in any event. In exchange, we must try to deal with Pup Pid. The Lighthouse Keeper also asked that I apprentice with him when I\u2019m there and learn how to operate the Lighthouse. That way, there will be someone else to keep it going should he need help.<br /> <br /> Now we just have to go out to sea and deal with Pup Pid. I\u2019m a bit worried about how my krewe mates will fare with that. I\u2019m at home underwater for many reasons, but they aren\u2019t, and I fear they might have a difficult time of things down there.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, September 27, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> Last night, after we returned from the Underworld, I spent the afternoon with Karl. We watched some movies when night fell and snuggled happily on the couch. It was very cozy and romantic, though I did have to shoo Lily off. After the movies, our cuddling became a bit more intense and we went upstairs to my room to make love again. We spent the night there together, and it felt so good to wake up next to someone I love. Karl is so gentle and kind and sweet in his awkwardness, but most of all I can feel the depth of his passion for me when he holds me. I had forgotten what it feels like to be loved like that. The memory had become more like a dream, but now the dream is reality again.<br /> <br /> Everyone was up early today, though, to see off Chandra and Alexia. They\u2019ll be spending the next two weeks in Paris on honeymoon. Alexia studied to become a chef there, so she knows the city well. I\u2019m certain they will have a marvelous time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, September 27, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve taken the week off so that we can set things up in Taipei. I think we will head there tomorrow to get started. I\u2019ve called my father to let him know that I will be arriving tomorrow along with some friends, and assured him that he didn\u2019t need to pick me up at the airport.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve spent a portion of the day acting as counsellor to Gretchen and Grin. They are very much in love, but Gretchen is becoming too clingy, and it\u2019s making Grin feel uncomfortable. When he goes back home during the week, she feels terribly depressed and lonely for a day or two, and wants him around all the time. But he needs his space. Gretchen is still convinced she is going to die, and feels that she needs to give Grin as much time as possible before that happens. Her fatalistic attitude upsets Grin, of course.<br /> <br /> I tried to convince Gretchen to give Grin his space. Since she becomes depressed on Monday and Tuesday after he\u2019s left, I suggested that she should spend less time in the library on those days and more time around the house with the rest of us, because what she really needs is company. I also recommended that they arrange dates on weeknights instead of just getting together all weekend. Fortunately, she knows Grin loves her, so at least she\u2019s not afraid they\u2019re going to break up.<br /> <br /> I spoke to Grin as well, and we both agree that the real problem is Gretchen\u2019s fatalism, which is really a symptom of her fear. We won\u2019t be able to convince her that she isn\u2019t doomed unless we deal with Tzipporah. Unfortunately, I have no idea how to approach that problem. We need to rely on Simon\u2019s guidance for that.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Another Engagement</u><br /> <br /> There was more good news this morning. Natalie and Karen have become engaged as well! It was quite considerate of them to wait until after Alexia\u2019s wedding to make the announcement. We are all happy for them, though Natalie does seem a bit out of sorts over it all. In a good way, I think.<br /> <br /> They will have two weddings. One\u2014the real one\u2014will be a private wedding for us. But since Natalie is something of a local celebrity, they will have another public affair for the GBLT and Goth community. I think the latter might take place at Natalie\u2019s club once it\u2019s up and running, though I\u2019m not sure.<br /> <br /> When we were in the Underworld, I noticed that Natalie\u2019s engagement ring glowed warmly, signifying how much it means to her. I believe that what she and Karen share is real after all, not the same sordid or confused romances or immature infatuations she has had in the past. The Bride and I are very happy that she has finally found her own true love.<br /> <br /> <u>Birth of a Geist</u><br /> <br /> I think Janice is on the verge of becoming a geist. I\u2019ve honestly become so familiar with her that I hadn\u2019t bothered to notice until Natalie mentioned it after we left the Underworld diner. But when she said something, it seemed obvious to me. I do wonder what motivates Janice, but I dare not harm our friendship by pestering her about it since she obviously wishes to keep her past a secret. Still, perhaps if I knew, I could help.<br /> <u><br /> Low Ceilings</u><br /> <br /> During our tour of the Lighthouse, I commented that I would like Karl to come there with me sometime once I\u2019ve made it into a home away from home, but I was worried that he would be uncomfortable there because of the low ceilings. Natalie said, quite cattily, that she\u2019s sure the two of us could find some way to deal with it. The way she smiled at me when she said it told me that she had figured out Karl and I had made love. She\u2019s frighteningly good at reading people. I must have turned bright red, because she immediately apologized. I was embarrassed, but really, I didn\u2019t mind. So I gave her a small smile and told her it was okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Pup Pid</u><br /> <br /> The Pup Pid in the Underworld doesn\u2019t sound like the same thing as the one in the living world. I wonder if the Pup Pid we have seen in New Haven is a spirit. But a spirit of what? Pirate Legends? I hope the two are unrelated. Otherwise things could get messy.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Christmas</u><br /> <br /> The only day of the year that the Lighthouse Keeper does not man the light is on Christmas, and he says that day is very dangerous because Pup Pid and other sea bound horrors roam free then. He asked that I promise to keep the Lighthouse lit on Christmas in his stead once he\u2019s trained me.<br /> <br /> He claims that family comes to visit on Christmas. I got the unnerving impression that his family is just as monstrous as he is, if not more so. I suppose I will find out eventually.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XCI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> That pretty much covered everything except the coke orgy in Natalie\u2019s club. And, you know, no need to go into detail on such things. The downtime was not completely covered; we covered some this time, and will also be covering some next session. Nothing with Taipei was covered this time. That will probably be the main focus of the downtime we cover next session, then we will get everyone to the same place in the timeline.<br /> <br /> Changeling fans may want to note Grin did some discussion of fear, it\u2019s nature, and how it relates to Gretchen. He is Autumn Court, after all. It\u2019s also worth noting discussion of \u201cChristmas\u201d was generally deemed hilarious.<br /> <br /> OK, so this Autumn is going to be very busy for our gaming group. A good sort of busy, but the sort of thing that will affect games and journals.<br /> <br /> Simon is MIA and won't be back for awhile. His player is hard at work on his doctoral dissertation, and it will be defended in the Spring. Simon WILL be back, his player has lost no interest in the game, but this has to come first. If he reaches a point where he feels comfortable coming back sooner then that he will.<br /> <br /> Sara's player is working on her doctoral dissertation as well, due same time, but does not think she will have to miss. It may impact her journaling, but she is not journaling in this game. Don't expect anything from Sara journal-wise before Spring though. Hopefully she will continue to not be affected, but she may have to miss a session or two.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s not being present is due to illness. I am expecting him Sunday. However, he will also be having a break this Autumn, also for chaotic short term but good long term reasons: He and his wife will be having a baby in late October/early November. They both game a lot with us, but she is not currently in <b>Geist </b>(Gwen's player). Doc similarly will be returning when everything settles down. That one will be harder to predict when, but you will be kept updated.<br /> <br /> I am hopeful they will at least be able to pop back in for session 100, and both should be returning once baby stuff calms down/dissertation is in hand full time. If you are following my other games on this forum they will be impacted (Diego/Eleanor in <b>Masquerade</b> and Nemi/Phaedra in <b>Scion</b>) eventually as well.<br /> <br /> If Sara\u2019s player has to miss a few sessions when Doc and Simon\u2019s both do, we may decide to do a short hiatus depending on what is going on. It is the nature of Sandbox that we can get by with fewer players then an adventure game, as it is easy for missing players to blue book or just discuss what their characters are doing. It will depend on what is going on when at half-staff. If this happens it will not be indicative of <i>Balance of Shadows </i>ending. All this will be sorted out come Spring. I am expecting no long term negative impact on the game. But now you are aware.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:51:56-08:00","id":17032,"title":"","content":"interruption.<br /> <br /> Hey, unfortunately not many journals again this time, but we do have Jasmine\u2019s as per. Everyone but Simon was there, though, and she should cover it. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> Edit: Doc's Log has been retroactively added to this post<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc's Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2300 Hours, Tuesday, September 28, 2010<br /> <br /> The plan for tonight (this is marked local time) was to meet Rose\u2019s dad for dinner. It was very traditional and T\u01d4zh\u00ec (my name for Rose\u2019s father) was an excellent cook. I was glad I had already started working on learning Mandarin. T\u01d4zh\u00ec doesn\u2019t speak English so it was a little slow during the introductions. I felt bad for Karl. Not only could he not speak Mandarin, but T\u01d4zh\u00ec treated him just like every father treats his daughter\u2019s first dates. With everyone else, T\u01d4zh\u00ec was very warm and inviting. To Karl, he was distant, stern, and questioning. Karl is usually nervous around new people, but he looked almost frozen by T\u01d4zh\u00ec\u2019s stone gaze. I have to admit that I would have been a little intimidated by T\u01d4zh\u00ec so I can\u2019t say Karl handled things badly. Rose translated everything except for my broken attempts at short phrases. T\u01d4zh\u00ec seemed very surprised when I thanked him for inviting us to dinner. At least, I hope that\u2019s what I said.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow we\u2019re going to search Guang\u2019s house for the occult information he left behind. Rose, Karl, and Bright Eyes are starting to fade. Nightshade and I are still okay, but suspect she will turn in soon. The time difference isn\u2019t so bad, but there is still a little jet lag from a 20 minute walk that transports us to the other side of the world. Fortunately, the temple has already had the utilities reconnected. Nightshade has still grumbled about the lack of a bidet, but that just means she\u2019s feeling okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1430 Hours, Wednesday, September 29, 2010<br /> <br /> Our visit to Guang\u2019s house was exciting. Guang gave us specific details (through Rose\u2019s translation) of where everything in the house should be. To keep him safe from the sorcerer\u2019s reach, we were going in without Guang. We discussed it before leaving the temple and decided we should plan not to destroy any Jiang Shi we found as they were probably duped just like Guang. Also because that would alert the sorcerer that something powerful was coming. This left Bright Eyes and I at somewhat of a handicap, but I thought we\u2019d figure something else out if the time came. Being that we were going during the day, none of this should have been an issue. Unfortunately, that didn\u2019t matter.<br /> <br /> Nightshade scanned the house through her Boneyard and declared it clear. Karl remained outside and down the street with Nightshade while the rest of us went to investigate. We entered Guang\u2019s house without any issue and carefully moved toward his meditation chamber. As we walked down the hallway, white smoke flowed from the vents in the ceiling. This smoke solidified into three Jiang Shi, which immediately attacked. Rose, Bright Eyes, and I were all hit before we could react. We each had our own white smoke rising from the wounds at that time. Rose was quick enough to wrap herself in Cold Winds before we were struck again. Bright Eyes was able to duck the strike, while I was just able to shield myself with my Phantasmal Shroud. The Jiang Shi that struck Rose howled in pain as his hand iced over for his efforts. The claws which impacted my Shroud left little more than a bruise and allowed me to make good use of my time sketching the sorcerer. Drawing on the power of my Shroud, I warped their perceptions of me to appear as their sorcerous master, then commanded them to stop in Mandarin. All three Jiang Shi ceased their attack, but we weren\u2019t sure if they were obeying or simply confused. Rose coached me on how to tell them to go away. I awkwardly did so and we waited to see what would happen next. At first, they seemed to be deciding how to react. Then one of the three screamed as if terrified and fled. I turned to see Nightshade standing in the door. She must have used one of her Passion powers. The other two Jiang Shi thought about their options for a few seconds longer until Karl charged into the hallway in all his Brineborn glory! The lumbering monster and the terrifying goth joining the fight was more than the remaining Jiang Shi bargained for. They simply vanished, leaving us standing alone in the hallway. With Karl\u2019s hulking form standing near a window, I realized that these Jiang Shi had not only been able to move, but attacked freely in daylight. They were never directly struck by daylight, but Guang was paralyzed at dawn each day. This should not have happened. I looked over our wounds but they were nothing to worry about. I realized as I joked about it, these wounds would have crippled or killed anyone living without a Geist. It was entirely less funny after that.<br /> <br /> Once I was sure we were all in one piece and nothing else would try to eat us, we found the books and scrolls Guang and Rose were looking for. The chamber still smelled of burnt hair from the ritual which transformed Guang. With a little looking and checking, we figured out that Guang had a Taoist alchemy lab installed over a Nexus, similar to Dark Haven Bluffs. Rose rearranged the rooms to give Jiang Shi bad Feng Shui. She also taught me how to properly say, \u201cReturn to your anchor\u201d in Mandarin. Hopefully I won\u2019t have to try and fool the Jiang Shi again, but if I do, knowing how to give them orders will be helpful. We\u2019ll have to ask Guang if he knows how these Jiang Shi could move during the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2345 Hours, Sunday, October 10, 2010<br /> <br /> We have traveled back and forth to Taipei several times over the past two weeks. The temple is now completely operational as a forward outpost. I haven\u2019t completely decided if it would be necessary or worth it to outfit the grounds with a weapons cache.The ghostly monk anchored there speaks less English than I Mandarin, so I don\u2019t know if he would realize keeping them hidden was important. There has been very little else going on. Well other than the work on Cupcake\u2019s china cabinet, but that was only Snowflake and I while I was in country. I have learned a better grasp of Mandarin now, but I still sound more like a child. I can at least get my point across most of the time. And I haven\u2019t been a terrible boyfriend either, so I\u2019ve spent some time with Noriko while I\u2019ve been home.<br /> <br /> We\u2019re expecting the newlyweds to return tomorrow. Hopefully there will be lots of pictures and stories. Knowing Cupcake, there will probably be more recipes than either. Wednesday will be a major party as Nightshade will hold her grand opening of the 27 Club. Then I think we\u2019re heading back to Taipei to actually deal with the sorcerer. For now, I\u2019m going on patrol. Maybe I should talk to Noriko about going out together for patrols now? That\u2019s something for later though.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2000 Hours, Monday, October 11, 2010<br /> <br /> Cupcake and Chandra are home! I missed them and based on the hugs, I think they might have missed us too. Cupcake couldn\u2019t wait to get back into her kitchen, though Tavia and Rose did have to admit they ruined one of the pots. Cupcake froze for a second but before she could freak out, Rose let her know they replaced it with the same thing. Chandra was amused.<br /> <br /> Once everyone was back and our honeymooners were rested, we gathered to talk to Guang in more detail about the sorcerer. They never met in person until after Guang had transformed into a Jiang Shi. The ritual Guang used was sent through the mail in a series of PO Box style interactions. The whole process was just shady enough to seem legitimate. I suggested that the Krewe minus Rose could try to pose as occultists as well. Perhaps gain the attention of the sorcerer and work back that way. Rose let us know that she had crafted a half dozen prayer strips. This led to another option to reach the sorcerer being to use Guang as bait. We could kill him if the sorcerer took control and he would come back to his grave later. We would just have to not use fire. Given that several of the Jiang Shi have seen most of us, using Guang is likely the best shot. This is going to be a busy week.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to get all the fun stories from Paris.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0915 Hours, Tuesday, October 12, 2010<br /> <br /> I shouldn\u2019t go without meditating as often as I do, but I made up for it today. I was centered and ready for anything in about a half hour. Then I came down for breakfast. The usual suspects were already at the table while Cupcake gleefully peddled stuffed crepes to any willing plate. Rose\u2019s vacation is over so we can\u2019t go back to Taipei for any extended trips for a while, but it sounds like we planning to go and hit hard on Thursday.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, it\u2019s Game day so I\u2019m not sure what I\u2019ll do. Maybe check the prices on some of the interior pieces for the van. I think Snowflake and I might actually be able to get things together before the end of the year. Then I just have to learn how to drive.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1945 Hours, Tuesday, October 12, 2010<br /> <br /> So apparently Rose pissed Stanley off today. He called to make one of their coffee dates and surprised Rose by introducing his favorite Aunt Phyllis. The same Phyllis that killed Marjorie over a man and shoved her corpse in a lock box. On the surface, this could have been a great opportunity to learn more about a potential target and not tip our hand. Unfortunately, only Rose is less subtle than I am. If I understand the situation correctly, Rose based made a comment about how she has outlived all her competition for attention. It might not have been that direct, but it was still obvious enough that Phyllis immediately became suspicious. Stanley, who loves his aunt for not turning her back on him when he came out of the closet so long ago, was very confused and more than a little irritated that Rose suggested something about his aunt. When Rose made her admission, it was Cupcake who became disgruntled and chastised Rose for her poor judgement. Her words were hard, but her expression and tone were almost cartoonish they were so exaggerated. She instantly covered her mouth after realizing she actually said what she was thinking. I watched carefully while enjoying my Duck Confit to see where this might go. Rose took the verbal dressing down seriously until Cupcake covered her mouth and squeaked. At that point, the tension and frustration must have finally gotten to be too much. Rose began laughing and holding her face in her hands. The rest of the table was silent as we all looked around trying to remember the last time Rose was this emotional. With the exception of the funeral, I couldn\u2019t think of any other time. Eventually she recovered and we started clearing the table while considering how to deal with a much more guarded Phyllis.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0715 Hours, Wednesday, October 13, 2010<br /> <br /> It felt good to get back into my meditation routine. I was quickly at peace again this morning. Which was good considering today might be very awkward and stressful. Tonight is the grand opening of the 27 Club and I have offered to help get things ready. In general, this should be fine. In practice, I\u2019m going to be around Nightshade, Karen, Bright Eyes, and several of their various girlfriends while we get everything setup. But I know she needs the extra hands, so after breakfast, I\u2019ll plan on doing heavy labor in the club.<br /> <br /> I just hope we get a chance to get cleaned up before I need to pick up Noriko.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1930 Hours, Wednesday, October 13, 2010<br /> <br /> Thankfully we got everything into place the way Nightshade wanted it and still had time to get cleaned up. It sounds like the whole Krewe and all our various attachments are planning to attend (short the vampire contingent, but that\u2019s understandable). Getting ready to leave, so I\u2019ll end here. This would be a good time to have the van ready. Oh well.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday, September 28, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> We have arrived in Taipei and begun getting things arranged here. We\u2019ve started the process of purchasing the haunted temple and its grounds and we have put in the order to have Guang\u2019s utilities reconnected and paid.<br /> <br /> We went to my father\u2019s home this evening and found a nice traditional Taiwanese meal waiting for us. He has always been a good cook, but I suspect that one of his neighbors, perhaps Mrs. Liu, helped out.<br /> <br /> My father was very hospitable toward my friends. He was perplexed by some of them, like Natalie, who was dressed in decorative black with a great deal of lace. But he was very friendly and I think it warmed his heart to see that I do, in fact, have such close friends. I was quite busy translating for him, though.<br /> <br /> The only person he was not openly friendly toward was Karl. I think he was a bit shocked by Karl\u2019s appearance. Karl is nothing like Richard, and he looks a little rough around the edges. Though I adore him, he does look the part of the bully. Of course I know better, and I find the sheepish gentleness underlying his rough looks quite charming.<br /> <br /> But my father adjusted to Karl\u2019s presence quickly enough, and treated Karl to a series of stern, appraising looks over the course of dinner. He was trying to make sure that Karl understood that dating me was serious business, and that he would not stand for it if Karl were to hurt me in any way. Poor Karl thought my father was angry with him, but I simply explained that it was just his way of looking out for me. Once he\u2019s made the impression he wants, father will warm up to Karl; that\u2019s how it happened with Richard, anyway.<br /> <br /> It was a nice evening. Karl went back to the hotel with the others, and I\u2019m staying at my father\u2019s home tonight. I do hope Lily isn\u2019t getting into too much trouble while I\u2019m away.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, September 29, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> We went to Guang\u2019s house to search for some occult tomes he might find useful as well as his Taoist alchemical texts, in which I am personally interested. He has a rather normal house, though it is filled with all manner or curiosities. The basement contains his occult library and ritual chamber, and that is where we found what we were after.<br /> <br /> In the process, however, we were attacked by three jiang shi. They materialized out of smoke and immediately attacked. I quickly summoned the cold winds to enshroud me, and when one of the jiang shi attempted to strike me, he shrieked in pain as his hand was frozen. Sara and Doc looked like they might summon flames of protection and rage, but wisely chose to avoid using any fire. It might be our most potent weapon against the jiang shi, but we don\u2019t want to reveal too much of our powers to the sorcerer. Furthermore, these jiang shi are probably his victims as well, tricked into becoming his undead servants just like my uncle, so it would be best if we can avoid hurting them for the time being.<br /> <br /> Doc brought the fight to a standstill with a brilliant manifestation of his Phantasmal Shroud; he changed himself to look like the sorcerer, or as close as he could get from Guang\u2019s descriptions. The disguise was convincing enough that the jiang shi stopped attacking when he commanded them, though they may have been confused more than compelled since his Chinese was a bit off. Then Natalie created an intense fear effect that forced them to flee in terror. Karl ran in then, having heard the sounds of a fight. He had transformed into his fish man form, which did only terrified the jiang shi even more. All three of the vampires burst into wispy clouds of vapor and disappeared entirely. They almost certainly returned to their graves or their master.<br /> <br /> I took some time to rearrange some things in the house, adjusting the feng shui so that it would be more difficult for the jiang shi to operate there. It will not keep them away, but it might help. I also taught Doc how to say, \u201cReturn to your anchor\u201d in Mandarin so that if he used the same illusory disguise trick in the future, he could be more convincing. If we have time, I\u2019ll teach him some other useful phrases as well.<br /> <br /> One thing troubles, me, though. It was daytime when we went to the house, and jiang shi are supposed to become inactive during the day. The sorcerer must have some sort of magic that allows his jiang shi to remain active when the sun is up, which is a frightening prospect. We will need to find out how he is doing it and stop it. If we can learn the secret, then perhaps we can give my uncle the same ability. I\u2019m certain he would appreciate that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, September 30, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> My father took Karl and me out to a very nice dinner tonight. It was a chance for him to get to know Karl better, and I\u2019m glad the two of them had the chance to become more comfortable with each other. My father was no longer the stern, disapproving parent (though I know now where I get that side of my personality). Instead, he was warm and interested in knowing more about Karl and his family. Karl was very diplomatic about the Fishbornes, essentially telling father that his family was old and influential in certain parts of New England, but his particular branch of the family was not as posh as the main branch, which owned the mansion we live in now. My father was still impressed.<br /> <br /> By the end of the evening they seemed to be getting along fairly well, even if I did have to translate everything for them. Honestly I think my father feels better about me being in America now that he sees me becoming happy again.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, October 11, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Alexia and Chandra returned today. They had a rather warm homecoming, and it seems they had a wonderful time on their honeymoon. Alexia was a bit upset to learn that we had ruined one of her favorite pans, but it was okay since we replaced it with an identical piece. I suppose we didn\u2019t have to tell her, but I\u2019m certain she would have noticed the switch anyway.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, October 12, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Stanly invited me to coffee at Lulu\u2019s today, and I was caught off guard to find that he intended to introduce me to his Aunt Phyllis, a woman he treasures since she has always been supportive of his lifestyle. Unfortunately, we also happen to know that she killed Marjorie and left her corpse locked in a trunk.<br /> <br /> It was interesting to put a face to the name. Phyllis is a charming old woman, and Stanly\u2019s affection for her is obvious. But I really had only one thing on my mind during our conversation: bringing peace to Marjorie. I suppose that is why I tested Phyllis by making what I thought was a subtle comment to the effect that a charming woman such as she is fortunate to have outlived all of her romantic rivals.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, it does sound terribly awkward, but I\u2019m absolutely impossible when it comes to being socially subtle. Stanly picked up on the remark, and Phyllis positively bristled. Our coffee did not last long after that.<br /> <br /> I mentioned the encounter to the others, and they criticized my approach rather harshly, though I agree that I deserved it. Phyllis will be more on guard now. Alexia was quite cross with me. I was honestly shocked at the depth of her disapproval, and tried to defend myself, though ultimately her kittenish frown and petulant admonitions undermined her disapproval and somehow the whole situation seemed absurd. I actually started laughing. Not just a quick giggle, but actually laughing. I cannot remember the last time I really laughed, and from the look on the rest of the krewe\u2019s faces, neither could they.<br /> <br /> My odd fit aside, I really did make a mistake, and I hope that I can somehow salvage it. I don\u2019t want Stanly to hate me, but it may be too late for that. I should know by now that I don\u2019t do well trying to be subtle in social encounters, so I should just keep my mouth shut.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 13, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Tonight was the opening of Natalie\u2019s club, the 27 Club. We all turned out to wish her well. Alexia catered, and of course Natalie, Karen and Doc were busy all day preparing. I\u2019ve never seen Natalie so full of nervous energy, though I didn\u2019t really see her much until the opening itself. She even summoned a thunderstorm using her hedge magic, so there was a nice rumbling over the club throughout the evening, not that you could really hear it over the loud music.<br /> <br /> I suppose the opening went well, though I was a bit distracted. Stanly was there, and he beckoned me over to talk. He wanted to know what had happened between me and his aunt. I tried to brush it off, but he saw right through me, and I couldn\u2019t bear the disappointment in his eyes, so I told him what I could. I explained that I suspect his aunt knows something about a mysterious death that happened some years ago, and that my group of paranormal investigators are currently investigating the death. I promised that I meant his aunt no harm, but that we needed to find out what happened.<br /> <br /> I suppose I was a bit untruthful, since I am prepared to kill Phyllis if she is unrepentant and there is no other way to resolve Marjorie. But I sincerely hope it will not come to that. I do feel a great sense of injustice on Marjorie\u2019s behalf though. It seems wrong that Phyllis has enjoyed such a long and fulfilling life after she sentenced Marjorie to languish as a poor, lost shade.<br /> <br /> Stanly was very upset, but he offered to see if Phyllis would be willing to talk to the krewe. I tried to comfort him, but I could tell he was angry. I don\u2019t blame him. I\u2019ve all but accused his dear aunt of murder. I fear I\u2019ve ruined my friendship with Stanly, and that makes me very sad. It was difficult to enjoy the rest of Natalie\u2019s opening night, so Karl and I left as soon as it was polite to do so.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>The Plan</u><br /> <br /> We have discussed how to deal with the sorcerer, and I think we have settled on a risky but rather direct plan. I prefer things to be more direct, so I\u2019m satisfied with this plan even though it does put my uncle at greater risk. He is quite willing to help us, though.<br /> <br /> The plan is simply to take Guang back to Taipei and then follow him when he feels the sorcerer\u2019s summons. Just in case we somehow lose him, I\u2019ve collected a lock of his hair to use in a Finding ritual. Our hope is that Guang will lead us right to the sorcerer, and then we can deal with the problem at its source.<br /> <br /> The biggest challenge, of course, will be avoiding the attacks from the jiang shi while we deal with the sorcerer. As far as we know, they are all relatively innocent victims of the sorcerer\u2019s schemes, and hopefully they will be peaceful and relatively harmless once their master is dead. With my uncle\u2019s help, I\u2019ve crafted several paper exorcism charms. They should paralyze the jiang shi if I can place them on their faces, but the vampires are very quick, so I will have to be even quicker.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XCII<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Jiang Shi are, as always, in <i>Night Horrors: Wicked Dead</i> for <b>Requiem</b>.<br /> <br /> A lot of the drama of course centered on Jasmine, and she covered most of it. There was madness focusing around Natalie getting ready for the 27 Club to open, and that went well, though we will be taking up with that tonight. Sara hung around Tatum the whole time, pretty much (Tatum is working there now) and Doc took Noriko while Simon and Tavia, Gretchen and Grin, and Jasmine and Karl went.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s weather control came from <i>Second Sight</i>; she is a Witch, as Doc and Simon are Ceremonial Magicians.<br /> <br /> Phyllis actually has the same model as Marjorie, Sylvia Sydney. I used older Sylvia Sydney for Phyllis and young for Marjorie.<br /> <br /> I think that covers everything, let me know if you have comments or questions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:52:52-08:00","id":17033,"title":"","content":"Please note, the last two entries have been updated to have Doc's Log entries there to flesh them out. Feel free to reread them with his POV added.<br /> <br /> OK, it\u2019s time to visit our gang of dead men and women walking. Today they meet a very odd person. But it\u2019s my game, so that is nothing new. Please enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0600 Hours, Thursday, October 14, 2010<br /> <br /> It has been awhile since I woke up in a strange bed at dawn. Having Noriko purring against me made the bed seem much less strange though. Last night was certainly an experience.<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Karen came back to the club before the rest to be there at open. I picked up Noriko about 2030 Hours and we came in about the same time as the rest of the Krewe. Stanley and Adam were already there. Rose was beckoned over almost immediately. Cupcake and I followed just to be supportive and to drag Rose away if necessary. Based on his tone and choice of words, it was obvious that Stanley knew something was wrong. Rose tried to explain that everything was fine, but Stanley being very astute, disbelieved. They moved off for a private conversation. I decided to keep Adam company and learned what kind of drink Stanley liked. After a moment, I excused myself and returned with a drink for both gentlemen. Rose and Stanley returned shortly thereafter so I handed him his drink and patted him reassuringly on the shoulder. He thanked me for the drink but was very distant. I could only imagine how well that conversation went.<br /> <br /> Outside of that, the grand opening seemed to be a huge success. Nightshade addressed the crowd at midnight and it was as though she were addressing a lover. They were attentive, wanting, and ready for anything Nightshade suggested. Rose and Karl left soon after, but I stayed until Noriko was ready to release some tension. Time was a little unimportant at that point, so here I am.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1315 Hours, Thursday, October 14, 2010<br /> <br /> Noriko had to work so I didn\u2019t really get to do the breakfast date like I planned. I ran by the shop and helped out until around lunch before getting out of the way. When I got back to the House, Nightshade gathered us all for an announcement. Apparently Karen\u2019s parents are trying to bring Nightshade up on multiple changes. They claim that Nightshade became sexually active with Karen when she was 15, as well as claiming that Karen has been brainwashed into her relationship with Nightshade. I\u2019m not really sure what prompted this, but apparently it was known before now. Nightshade just didn\u2019t want anything affecting the grand opening ceremony. I happen to know Karen was older than 15 when they met so that charge is utter bullshit. As far as brainwashing goes, I will be happy to remind them under oath that they kicked Karen out of the house when they learned she was in a lesbian relationship. I can probably even nail down a date if I look back through my journals. This has left me in an incredibly shitty mood. But I need to hold on to that anger. It makes Nightshade nervous when I get angry and we\u2019re going out hunting soon anyway.<br /> <br /> Chandra was unhappy that we recommended against her going with us. It was just more logistics than we could safely handle. No one knows if this sorcerer could affect a panagallen or not. And we did not want Chandra turning on us. She reluctantly agreed, but I could tell she was not pleased that Cupcake would be going without her. While we were gathering supplies, Gretchen mentioned that this sorcerer might be some kind of necromancing mage. Because that\u2019s what we need. Rose did make a rather dark joke that we just needed to bring the writing desk. I decided it wasn\u2019t a good idea to take a chance, so I\u2019ve loaded up my shotgun and the Winchester. Now I need to get everything together for the gateway ceremony.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0500 Hours, Friday, October 15, 2010<br /> <br /> We arrived in Taipei around 0200 Hours. Rose performed a Taoist ritual to increase her speed, but we convinced her that renting a car for the rest of the Krewe would be best. That way we could also keep up (should we need to follow Guang or others) and hide our weapons. Once that was handled and we explained why our Jeeps with Connecticut plates would stand out to Cupcake, we returned to Guang\u2019s house. Nightshade surveyed the area with her Boneyard while Rose prepared to follow her uncle in. Inside something waited and it was likely there for us. The creature had three eyes in a triangle pattern, a horn on its head, long claws, and shaggy red and yellow fur. Rose went in invisibly behind Guang while the rest of us waited. Nightshade could tell the creature, I heard oni and demon alternately, could sense Rose but not where she was. It sniffed in that direction but stayed hidden in the closet. Guang seemed unchanged when he entered the house and the demon seemed uninterested in him.<br /> <br /> The arrival of a Jiang Shi caught Nightshade\u2019s attention. The old woman climbed down the chimney. Rose let us know that the old woman told Guang that he should follow her as there was someone coming for him. The odd looking Jiang Shi claimed she could protect Guang from danger. The demon was aware of the old woman as well. Nightshade warned Rose that it was creeping up on them so she prepared for a fight. What happened next I\u2019m not entirely sure as we didn\u2019t get a description. Rose impacted with something and Nightshade told us to move. We rushed the house only to find Guang and a strange old woman Jiang Shi staring as Rose snapped the neck of the demon. It apparently tried to attack Ms. Po. With that, we all moved back to our car. Ms. Po seemed very interested in riding. She directed us to cave on the outskirts of town, near the temple. There she admitted that she was Manchurian and we made proper introductions. And speaking of proper, Rose and I both felt like Ms. Po was very old indeed. Rose has never worn anything revealing since I\u2019ve known her, but Ms. Po threw a robe over her at Guang\u2019s house when I entered. The ancient Jiang Shi seemed to believe I was Rose\u2019s suitor and thus instructed me on what needed to be corrected. That I understood almost none of her accented Mandarin was lost on her.<br /> <br /> Ms. Po did know many helpful things however. The sorcerer we sought was called Bone Dry. The Jiang Shi noted that she could not attack him directly but neither could he control her. As a powerful necromancer, Bone Dry was capturing Jiang Shi for nefarious purposes according to Ms. Po. Rose asked if her prayer strips would work. After looking over the calligraphy and nodding, Ms. Po showed me how to improve Rose\u2019s brush technique. While she was talking to me, I noticed Ms. Po\u2019s head was hollow and a faint blue glow came from within. I got the impression her internal organs were somewhere else. There was a ritual stone with four bound ghosts nearby that Ms. Po knew to be a place of power for Bone Dry. We decided that this was a good time to investigate. The ritual stone was actually a magical nexus attuned to Bone Dry. There were four ghostly monks who reminded me of the Shaolin, only they were wearing all white robes. Rose pointed out that white is the color of death and ghosts in Taiwan. Also it seems that Rose has become a Taoist magician. The monks were bound to the stone feature in the small park before us. I asked Nightshade if she could lock the ghosts down long enough for us tamper with the nexus? The plan evolved slightly as Rose managed to speak with the ghosts and learn more information. They were bound by Bone Dry but not loyal to him. If freed, they would have no duty to the necromancer and actually welcomed their freedom. However if we were to enter the area directly around the stone, they were compelled to attack. Nightshade solved both problems but forcing them away from the stone. This allowed Rose to change area enough to channel the nexus differently. After that, we returned to the temple to rest. Our goal will be to find Bone Dry at the ritual stone then kill him if we can or follow him back to his lair.<br /> <br /> Either way, there will be a reckoning.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, October 14, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> We are off to Taipei tonight. Of course, it\u2019s already Friday there. Gretchen has blessed my uncle with good fortune, and our current plan is to try and get the sorcerer to notice Guang so that my uncle will be drawn to him. Then we follow him to the sorcerer and deal with the problem at its source. We plan to rent a car once we arrive; fortunately, I\u2019m actually Taiwanese so the rental place won\u2019t have to check anyone\u2019s passports.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, October 15, 2010, Early Morning<br /> <br /> It\u2019s quite early in Taiwan\u2014before dawn\u2014and we have made a good deal of progress toward finding and defeating the sorcerer, though our plans haven\u2019t worked out as we thought they would. They never do.<br /> <br /> After arriving and getting a car, we drove to my uncle\u2019s house and parked a few blocks away, assuming it was being watched by the sorcerer. We hoped that Guang would feel the summons there, but that is not what happened. The house seemed empty, but Natalie peered into the house with her Boneyard and sensed a large, ape-like Chinese demon covered in shaggy reddish fur. It had a single horn and three bulging eyes, and was hidden in a closet, folded up into an impossibly small bundle in order to remain unobtrusive.<br /> <br /> Guang entered the house and busied himself as though looking for something, but he never felt any summons. I performed a Taoist ritual to increase my agility, hoping it might give me an edge against any danger we might encounter. I also transformed myself into my shark-like mein with the Primeval Caul and donned the Shroud of Stillness, cloaking myself in invisibility. I followed my uncle inside, watching over him unseen.<br /> Natalie reported that the demon seemed to be able to smell me, but could not determine exactly where I was. Its attention was mostly focused on my uncle, though. I moved to stand between my uncle and the beast so that I could intercept it if it crawled out to attack him, but then Natalie reported something else strange. An ancient jiang shi woman crawled down the chimney and into the house. She hopped into the same room as my uncle, and began speaking to him. Her limbs moved oddly, bending the wrong way and flopping around a bit like a stringless poppet, and I eventually realized that her body and spirit were separate, and the part of her that I was seeing was little more than a shell through which she was projecting her consciousness.<br /> <br /> She spoke with a think Manchurian accent, and insisted that my uncle should come with her if he wanted to stay safe. She claimed that she could protect him. Of course, my uncle was wary, but I when I wear the Primeval Caul, my instincts are sharp, and they told me that we could trust the old woman.<br /> <br /> Natalie whispered through my ear curl that the demon was creeping from its hiding spot to ambush my uncle and the old woman. I waiting for it to pounce and then tore it from the air, slamming it into the wall with the crunch of bone. I\u2019m afraid I left quite a dent in the house. It was surprised by the sudden attack, and once I appeared, so was the old woman. I quickly wrapped an arm around the demon\u2019s neck while forcing it\u2019s arm painfully behind it, and after a few moments of struggle I snapped its neck, leaving it dead on the floor.<br /> <br /> By that point, Doc, Sara, Alexia and Natalie showed up as well, and we introduced ourselves to the ancient jiang shi. She introduced herself as Miss Po, and insisted that we leave quickly, so we followed her directions to a hidden cave in the mountains on the edge of the city, not far from our temple.<br /> <br /> <br /> Once at the cave, we were able to talk to Miss Po at length, and learned a great deal about what we are facing. She is an elder jiang shi, and possesses powers far beyond those of my uncle or the sorcerer\u2019s other servants. I quite liked her, actually, despite the fact that she constantly chided me for not being a perfect lady, though of course her views on feminine qualities are quite old-fashioned.<br /> <br /> The sorcerer is named Bone Dry, and he might be a true mage rather than a simple hedge magician. After all the trouble caused by Louisa in Glenwood, this is not good news. Miss Po would like to oppose Bone Dry, but cannot do so directly because he is heavily warded against jiang shi. However, she knows of a ritual stone located in the mountains outside of Taiwan. Doc believes the stone is a mystical nexus, which strengthens the sorcerer\u2019s magic. The sorcerer uses it for his rituals, and its power spikes during the full moon and new moon. There is a full moon in a few days, so we believe Bone Dry will try to use the ritual stone then.<br /> <br /> We plan to ambush him there.<br /> <br /> In order to do this, however, we will have to do something about the monk ghosts he has guarding the nexus. We are currently on our way to the stone to see what can be done about that.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, October 15, 2010, Early Morning<br /> <br /> We are heading back to New Haven now, and I think we have done as much as we can to prepare for our fight against Bone Dry.<br /> <br /> We visited the ritual stone, which was a large, flat stone polished on one side and engraved with Chinese characters describing the dragon lines that converged there. The stone sat upon a hillside clearing in a forest of bamboo, facing away from Taipei and hidden from the city by the bulk of the mountain. The road leading there was unpaved, and we parked the car some distance away and made our way to the stone on foot.<br /> <br /> Four ghostly monks clad in white robes guarded the stone. They did not attack immediately, though they might have if Natalie had not used the power of her Stigmata to intimidate them.<br /> <br /> Even though I\u2019m awful at talking to people, the dead seem to find me more charismatic than the living, so I spoke to the ghosts. I asked if they wanted to move on. They did, but they were bound to the stone by Bone Dry, and could not disobey his will. In the end, we promised to help them once the sorcerer was destroyed and they were freed from their slavery. But until then, we had to prevent them from interfering, so Natalie warded the ritual area, forcing the ghosts away from it. They will not be a problem for us when we face the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> I spent some time rearranging things in the ritual space\u2014moving some of the stone lanterns (with Guang, Doc and Sara\u2019s help, of course) and other objects so that the feng shui was disturbed. The flow of chi is now diffuse and unfocused there, so the sorcerer will not be able to draw power from the site when we face him.<br /> <br /> Now we simply need to wait for the full moon.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Taoist Training</u><br /> <br /> Over the past week or so since we recovered my uncle\u2019s texts from his home, I have been studying Taoist alchemy with him. I\u2019m not terribly good at it, and I fear I never shall be. Some of its intricacies are honestly beyond me, but I have managed to master the basic skills of internal alchemy. Since I died, I\u2019ve not had any trouble manipulating my plasm, which is related to my chi, but now I\u2019ve begun to learn how to focus and shift my chi as I do plasm. The effects are less powerful and more subtle, but in time perhaps I can do more.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve also begun studying the art of feng shui. I already know the basics, but there is so much more to it, and my uncle is helping me understand the complexities. Studying my native occult again is quite engaging.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Legal Trouble</u><br /> <br /> Natalie is in trouble with the police because Karen\u2019s parents claim she was sleeping with Karen when Karen was still a minor, and also that she has brainwashed Karen. All the evidence shows otherwise, so I don\u2019t think there will be any lasting trouble from it, but Natalie is still anxious about the situation, and for good reason. It all came about because she was trying to make peace with Karen\u2019s parents so that they would attend the wedding, but they are so closed-minded that all they can do is blame Natalie for their daughter\u2019s choices.<br /> <br /> Simon, Karen and Natalie\u2019s lawyer are trying to get things sorted out while we are in Taipei taking care of the sorcerer.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Old-fashioned Sensibilities</u><br /> <br /> Miss Po was quite old-fashioned. She had never ridden in a car before and was excited to have the opportunity to do so when we drove back to her cave.<br /> <br /> Of course, my first indication of her outdated perspective on the world was her dismay at my \u201crevealing\u201d clothing. I was wearing a charcoal gray turtleneck, a black vest, and a pair of black jeans, which is often the sort of thing I wear when we are on a \u201cmission.\u201d But apparently my clothing hugged my curves a bit too tightly for Miss Po\u2019s tastes, and I was surprised when she threw a robe around me when Doc showed up after I\u2019d killed the demon.<br /> <br /> She keeps instructing me on ways to be more lady-like. I have been nothing but respectful toward her; she seems to appreciate the way I call her \u201cHonored Grandmother.\u201d And I find her constant worrying over my modern habits quite amusing, though it does not do my confidence any favors to have her criticizing my brazen fashion sense or sloppy calligraphy.<br /> <br /> She has figured out that everyone else in the group is married or engaged except for Doc and me (she seems to think one of Sara\u2019s rings implies an engagement or marriage of some sort), and believes that the two of us are a couple. Among other things, this means that she keeps instructing him on ways to train me to be a better wife. It would be insulting if it weren\u2019t so amusing. I\u2019m honestly surprised that Natalie isn\u2019t having fit over. I should not be surprised by Miss Po\u2019s attitude, though. There are still quite a few older people in Taiwan who still think a bit like she does.<br /> <br /> When we returned to New Haven, I told Karl that I had a another suitor now, so he\u2019d best be careful. It was a joke, of course, but it made Doc nervous nonetheless. I don\u2019t think he wants to tangle with Karl, and for good reason. We quickly explained the situation to Karl. I suppose we will have to clear up the misunderstanding for Miss Po eventually as well, but for now it seems simpler just to let her keep believing what she likes.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Doc\u2019s Mandarin</u><br /> <br /> Doc is trying very hard to improve his Mandarin, and he is making progress, but right now it\u2019s still quite awkward. He stumbled through a few phrases with Miss Po, and I can tell that he pays close attention whenever I\u2019m translating. I suppose Chinese must be a difficult language for Americans to learn. But Doc is trying, which means a great deal to me. And he is learning very quickly. If he keeps it up, then he will be holding conversations in no time. Perhaps I should start speaking to him only in Mandarin? After all, the best way to learn a language is through immersion, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCIII<br /> </i><br /> <br /> Miss Po, by design, is a character with serious and comedic elements. She is more powerful then a typical Jiang Shi, mad as a hatter, and fairly powerful. The demon was just a sort of generic summoned creature.<br /> <br /> Of course Simon\u2019s legal involvement was partially just to explain his being missing due to player responsibilities, as noted above.<br /> <br /> Jasmine has picked up Taoist Alchemy from <b>Second Sight</b>, so everyone but Alexia is a hedge mage now. I don\u2019t see her planning to get any hedge magic anytime soon. It may also be worth noting at this point Jasmine and Natalie both have Psyche 6. I think Sara may be picking it up soon.<br /> <br /> Well, that should cover things. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:55:10-08:00","id":17034,"title":"","content":"As it turns out, we only have a Jasmine journal this time. Gwen\u2019s player had her baby on Friday a week ago, and that has forestalled a Doc\u2019s Log. Still Jasmine covers events pretty well. Let\u2019s give it a look.<br /> <br /> Note Sara\u2019s player had to miss. This was a temporary issue; she should be at the game tonight.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, October 15, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> This afternoon, once I\u2019d returned home from work, we discussed our plans for the sorcerer, Bone Dry. We are going back to Taipei tomorrow to deal with him, and plan to ambush him at the ritual stone. I will be invisible and will attack Bone Dry directly when he arrives. The others will hide themselves and ambush the sorcerer when the time is right. Doc will most likely assist me against Bone Dry, and I\u2019ve given Alexia the exorcism charms I made, so she and Karl will attempt to slow down or stop the jiang shi. Natalie will remain some distance away, watching over the area with her boneyard while Sara protects her.<br /> <br /> Karl has asked me out this evening, so we will be going out for dinner and a movie, then maybe a romantic walk on the beach at night. It\u2019s going to be wonderful.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, October 16, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Our attempt to deal with Bone Dry was not successful, though I suppose it isn\u2019t a complete loss, as we learned a great deal about him. Nevertheless, I like direct and rapid results and feel as though I have let Guang down a bit.<br /> <br /> We prepared our ambush at the nexus. The night mists covered the mountain and the moon shone bright and full overhead. At about midnight, six figures approached: Bone Dry and five jiang shi. Bone Dry was not what I expected. He was only half Chinese, and styled himself in a manner that would not go amiss at Murder Ballads. He certainly stands out. However, I also noticed that he was dead, and quickly realized that his body was a corpse, preserved and animated by his spirit. It had taken on his true appearance, but his real body and the anchor for his soul lay elsewhere. If we defeated him here, it would only inconvenience him. The best we could hope for was to free the jiang shi.<br /> <br /> I quietly shared my observations with the others via our ear curls, and Natalie confirmed it. Even though Doc had Bone Dry in the sights of his rifle and was ready to take the shot, we decided not to attack. Instead, I would follow him and his jiang shi back to their lair, hoping they would lead us to the real Bone Dry.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Bone Dry is quite sharp and noticed both Alexia and Karl hiding. It\u2019s fortunate his jiang shi did not get a good look at Karl when we encountered them before at Guang\u2019s house. He demanded they explain their presence, but Alexia seemed so hapless that even when he saw through her lies, she seemed more sheepish than dangerous, and he must have concluded that she and Karl were drawn there by the mystical energies of the nexus. Supernatural things are often drawn to such places, so it\u2019s not an illogical conclusion.<br /> <br /> He eventually told Karl and Alexia to leave, but then he spoke to the air in a language I could not understand. I realized he was talking to a spirit. I possessed the Drowned Bride and saw two wraith-like death spirits, one of which glided after my lover and my friend. I considered following them and eliminating the spirit when we were out of sight, but it was becoming more and more apparent that Bone Dry was on guard, and Doc cautioned me against doing anything that might make him more paranoid.<br /> <br /> Then Natalie reported that her Boneyard had been dispelled. So it seems Bone Dry can cancel our plasmic manifestations as well. That does not sit well with me at all, and Bride is very agitated about it.<br /> <br /> Bone Dry examined the ritual site as his jiang shi began repositioning stone lanterns and replacing stepping stones to clean up the feng shui I had ruined a few days ago. He eventually decided that caution was the best course of action and left with his jiang shi in tow.<br /> <br /> I followed, of course, while Doc, Natalie and Sara remained at the ritual site.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t have to follow far. The unpaved road down the mountain led to a small suburb neighborhood, and Bone Dry entered a rather normal-looking house there. I followed, but as soon as I crossed the threshold, I could sense something amiss, and Bone Dry knew I was somewhere inside. He could not see me, though, as I was still invisible, and as his jiang shi spread out to search for me, I transformed into living shadow and slid across the walls to search the house. I tried to make my presence fade from Bone Dry\u2019s memory, but he seemed a bit too keen for that.<br /> <br /> The house was, in a word, boring. There was very little of interest there, and certainly nothing to suggest that it was a mystic\u2019s lair. The real Bone Dry was not present. The sorcerer was growing increasingly anxious, though, since he knew I was there yet could not find me, so he drew a small crystalline spider from his robe and cast a spell upon it. It began moving about and then faded from view, though I could still sense it skittering about, sometimes dangerously close as it searched for me.<br /> <br /> Bone Dry was spooked by my unseen presence and decided to flee, so he cast another spell and opened a portal into some other realm. It was not the Underworld, and all I could see through the glowing purple gate was darkness. For the briefest of moments, I considered following him into that realm, but with no idea what lay on the other side or how it might affect me, I decided it was too dangerous and let him go. Besides, Doc would have been extremely cross with me. So would Gwen, if she were still around.<br /> <br /> Instead of following him, though, I slid past him, becoming solid again so that I could pluck a few hairs from his head to use in a Finding ceremony. He was startled but continued into the portal. Then the crystalline spider, perhaps responding to its master\u2019s distress, reappeared and jumped at the spot where I had been standing mere moments before. It split into dozens of copies and swarmed the area but when it could not find me, it reabsorbed all of its copies and disappeared again.<br /> <br /> It may not have been able to find me, but I found it. I waited, listened, and followed its invisible presence. The auspices of my Primeval Oracle guided my senses, and as it scurried close to me, still searching, I struck and shattered it with one rapid blow. I gathered the pieces in a zip lock bag from Bone Dry\u2019s kitchen to take back to the others. I also searched the house in more detail since it was now vacant, and found an assortment of books and art from the 19th century, many Dutch in origin. I suspect Bone Dry is actually very old and has used magic to extend his life. He may even have been born in one of the Dutch colonies in China.<br /> <br /> I rejoined the rest of the group after reporting Bone Dry\u2019s escape. We decided that Alexia should eliminate the death spirit that was following her, but when she possessed the Cracked Cook and turned to attack it, it was gone, perhaps summoned away by Bone Dry before he left.<br /> <br /> We went to visit Miss Po and tell her what had happened. It seems as though there is little else we can do in Taipei for now, which I find quite frustrating. Miss Po has agreed to keep an eye on things and to let us know if Bone Dry returns. We have installed an old-style telephone in the temple that she can use to call us. For now, though, we are heading back to New Haven.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Mystical Espionage</u><br /> <br /> We were all shocked when Bone Dry command the Cracked Cook to tell him what Alexia was up to, though only Bone Dry and Alexia could hear what he said. Whatever excuse he gave, it seemed to satisfy Bone Dry. Still, it\u2019s disconcerting to think that the sorcerer might be able to exercise some control over our geists. We must be especially careful in opposing him, and I am glad that he seems to lack the power to pierce the veil of my Stillness Shroud.<br /> <br /> Of course, we have our own advantages too. Bone Dry doesn\u2019t know the size of our krewe or who exactly is in it. He doesn\u2019t think Alexia or Karl are connected to us, and as far as we know, the only ones his jiang shi have seen are me, Doc and Sara. And if he tries to track us, he will have a great deal of trouble since there is no way he can possibly follow us back through the temporary paths Doc and Natalie have been forging through the Underworld to get us to and from Taipei.<br /> <br /> Still, Bone Dry may be more dangerous and challenging any foe we have faced before.<br /> <i><br /> End Session XCIV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> At the very least until Doc\u2019s player is back there should be a Natalie journal to go with Jasmine\u2019s each time. This happened a little sooner then expected. Both Doc and Gwen\u2019s players are well, however.<br /> <br /> Bone Dry is a Mage, I will leave it at that for now.<br /> <br /> Unrelated mostly to anything above, I was playing <i>Bloodlines </i>and I kinda think <a href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=YX_kez_xwJs\" target=\"_blank\">Smaller God by Darling Violetta</a> that plays in that game is a pretty good <b>Geist </b>song. The imagry works especially well for Jasmine but works in general for <b>Geist</b>.<br /> <br /> Well more to come, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-24T01:56:22-08:00","id":17035,"title":"","content":"Hey, had a quieter session last time as we kinda kicked back a bit from the big adventure fighting the mage\u2026and it was time for mini golf. So mostly rping. More below.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, October 16, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> The krewe does not have much on its plate right now. We need to help Marjorie, though she seem content right now, largely thanks to Tavia. We need to head to the Athenaeum, but our vampire troubles seem to have receded for the time being, and we aren\u2019t quite ready to dive into the Underworld sea to fight Pup Pid.<br /> <br /> In any event, Doc and Simon became involved in their own projects this evening, so the ladies of the house (Natalie, Alexia, Chandra, Sara and Karen)decided to go out for a ladies\u2019 night. Tavia stayed home to help Simon with whatever he was working on, and we invited Karl to join us since he would otherwise be on his own and I certainly felt it would be nice to have him along. We also invited Deirdre and Rita.<br /> <br /> We started the evening with dinner at a really upscale Italian restaurant. Alexia insisted that the gourmet cuisine there was top notch, and she wasn\u2019t wrong. I understand now why she has such disdain for Olive Garden, though it\u2019s still quite amusing. The restaurant was also very expensive at $60 a plate, but she paid for it all. It was easily the most expensive meal I\u2019ve ever eaten.<br /> <br /> We had a good time. Deirdre and Rita have struck up a nice friendship, and I enjoyed chatting with both of them. I\u2019m afraid poor Karl might have felt a bit isolated in our conversations, but I\u2019m glad he was there, and tried to include him as much as possible.<br /> <br /> After dinner, we spontaneously decided to play miniature golf, which brought out my competitive side. I suppose I can\u2019t give Alexia too hard a time about being a food snob when I get so wrapped up in competitive games. Alexia seemed quite exasperated with me. We split into two groups. Alexia, Chandra, Karen and Natalie played against one another, and Karen and Natalie seemed to have quite the competition going. Deirdre, Rita, Karl. Sara and I were in the other group, and it turns out that Rita and Sara are good competition. We tied at mini-golf, but we couldn\u2019t let that stand, so we moved on to skeeball and then foosball. In the end, Rita and I remained tied, while Sara lost her focus when playing foosball. I really enjoyed foosball, and even suggested we get a foosball table for the house. It\u2019s also nice to have strong competitors like Rita and Sara to really challenge me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, October 17, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve spent much of the day studying my feng shui and helping Alexia with the yard, mostly raking leaves. Over dinner we discussed the situation with the missing Richie Abrams, whom we suspect fell victim to one of the Gentry. I believe we are going to speak to his friend Evan Callum to see if he knows anything.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Tavia the Anchor</u><br /> <br /> It appears that Tavia has become a new anchor for Marjorie. I\u2019m not sure exactly how that happened, and I\u2019m not sure it\u2019s a good thing, as it will make it a bit more difficult to help Marjorie pass on.<br /> <br /> Tavia asked if it were possible to help Marjorie learn new numina. I really didn\u2019t have an answer, but then I learned that she wanted Marjorie to control the security system at a local art museum so that the two of them could go in and have a look around after hours. I was appalled, and told Tavia that she could not just trespass in the museum after it\u2019s closed.<br /> <br /> I also told her that she had to be responsible for Marjorie since she\u2019s one of her anchors now. I have no idea how she will interpret that, but at least she seems fairly sincere.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Shadowing Rita</u><br /> <br /> Rita has a date with Jean! He asked her out! I\u2019m so happy, and I do hope they hit it off. There\u2019s just one problem. Rita is still very worried about her predatory instincts, and fears that she might do something awful, like attack and eat Jean when her passions are aroused. I\u2019ve been helping her try and gain better self-control through meditation, but she\u2019s not confident.<br /> <br /> So she asked me to shadow her on her date. She knows I can move about unseen, and wants me to follow the two of them and make sure she doesn\u2019t do anything she will regret. It\u2019s a very awkward situation\u2026and I would prefer to put my trust in her. But she insisted, and for now, at least, she\u2019s probably justified in her fears. Hopefully knowing that I\u2019m nearby will give her the strength to deal with her unwholesome urges, and I won\u2019t have to intercede. If I intercede, then there will be a lot of awkward explaining, and I don\u2019t want to put Jean through that. Besides, if Rita can get through the evening without attacking her.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Saturday October 16th 2010<br /> <br /> -Back from getting Chinese<br /> <br /> -What to do what to do?<br /> <br /> -Girl\u2019s night out? Girl\u2019s night out.<br /> <br /> -And Karl. We can put a wig on him or something.<br /> <br /> -Oh wow, have not had food like this in awhile.<br /> <br /> -Noms!<br /> <br /> -It does taste better then \u201cnormal\u201d food, just not sure it tastes enough better to justify the costs.<br /> <br /> -Hmmmm\u2026golf?<br /> <br /> -My gang has odd issues with bowling.<br /> <br /> -heh mini-golf<br /> <br /> -A wager?<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is winning.<br /> <br /> -Mmm-Hmmmm<br /> <br /> -Mmmmmmmm-Hmmmmmmm<br /> <br /> -Heh heh heh.<br /> <br /> -Poor Karen<br /> <br /> -Jasmine is facing down Sara and Rita.<br /> <br /> -Aha Diedre is leaving with Alexis and Chandra.<br /> <br /> -I may be a little busy myself. cracks knuckles<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jog<br /> <br /> -Oh yea. Oh hell yea. Heh heh heh heh<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, October 17th 2010<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s a good morning. How Do I know? I slept through it and it is afternoon.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -^-^ o_o O_O X-P<br /> <br /> -Thanks Gretchen\u2026.I always wanted to be asked that.<br /> <br /> -Greaten appears to assume certain elements are mighty prevalent in my love life. Far moreso then is the case.<br /> <br /> -Oh goddess I turn 30 in ten days. I feel like Grover trying to build a wall to keep you from the end of the book.<br /> <br /> -Evidently gardening is popular.<br /> <br /> -Vlog numbah two is up!<br /> <br /> -Psychic lady is back, so back to that search I think.<br /> <br /> -Ah the great sacrifice up clubbing. It is rough.<br /> <br /> -Rough, I tell you.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCV</i><br /> <br /> <br /> We had a roll off to handle the mini golf. Of course Jasmine went well. More Willpower was spent then absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not going to repeat Gretchen\u2019s question, but it involved Natalie walking away singing \u201cla la la la\u201d with her fingers in her ears, and Sara answering the question then telling her to not ask anyone else.<br /> <br /> Next session we cover a date being chaperoned by Jasmine. Also, things begin to pick up as we introduce new plots which leads to the phrases \u201cOh so we are doing a contract killing for a demon\u201d and \u201cwhat is a hotel without an axe murder, really?\u201d We will see you then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br /> Transcription Note: DONE! Holy crap! *collapse*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank