:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-06T09:24:11-08:00","id":24394,"title":"","content":"*Tentatively nibbles a little window/hole into the upper-left corner of this thread: very close to the Reload Button on the browser; for those that may try to stab him with their mouse pointer. (May you efforts always be maddeningly fruitless, by-the-by.) Only portions of either his eyes or his mouth can be seen at any one time; but frequently enough to be a long-standing audience-member*<br /> <br /> I must say, dear Baron: I enjoy this thread more than I care to elaborate on. (I might shame the author of War and Peace, after all, with the sheer volume of content.) But to say the very least; I adore your Troupe and the work you do.<br /> <br /> *A section of his hat can be seen through the tiny hole, tipping in the other's direction*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1219-shake","name":"Shake","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1219_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-09T02:04:35-08:00","id":26377,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. We put a lot of work into the journals and are glad people are enjoying. Hope to have a new post up in about a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-15T12:25:19-08:00","id":30518,"title":"","content":"Here is your two weeks overdue session update for Geist. I apologize for not giving you anything two weeks ago, but you have some meaty story here. Enjoy.<br /> <i><br /> Session XCVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, October 18, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I went to AMC early today to meet Rita so that we could meditate with some tai chi in the gym. I\u2019m still teaching her the basics, but she\u2019s taking to it very well. She\u2019s quite athletic.<br /> <br /> She then joined Jean and I in the pool while we were training. It\u2019s obvious the two of them are quite smitten with each other, and unfortunately her presence became rather distracting. I was pleased to see both of them happy, so I didn\u2019t say anything about it today, but if it becomes a recurring problem, then I will have to ask Rita to stay away while we are training.<br /> <br /> As the morning wore on, I noticed a strange old man watching us. He sat on one of the pool side benches, and he was quite large even though his build did not seem extraordinary. I could sense that he was making the other swimmers anxious, but more importantly, I could see that he was neither living nor dead, so I confronted him quietly.<br /> <br /> I believe he is a Chinese ox demon wearing the guise of a human, and he meant no harm, but he was quite interested in me. He spoke in cryptic stories and questions, making him difficult to understand. Had we not been speaking in Mandarin, I think I might have lost the thread of his words. But I was able to piece together that he was interested in me because Bone Dry is interested in me, and he therefore thought I might be an ally against someone who is under Bone Dry\u2019s protection.<br /> <br /> There is a bad man, a rapist and murderer who preys upon young women in the clubs of Taipei. He particularly prefers blondes. He should be dead, his soul suffering its just punishment in the Chinese Hell of Being Skinned Alive, but Bone Dry has placed a protective charm on him that keeps him from dying. The ox demon simply wants to collect his soul.<br /> <br /> The demon claims that he has an ointment that can be applied to the lips. If those lips are then used to kiss the bad man, it will remove Bone Dry\u2019s protection and he will, presumably, die. He promises to give me the ointment if I visit his shop, called the Road to Hell, in Taipei.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m inclined to take the ox demon at his word. Chinese demons are not given to lying, though they might prevaricate a bit. They deceive, but their deceptions are more illusory in nature, and I have little reason to doubt that the ox demon is being as honest as he needs to be. When I asked why I should help him (aside from the fact that the murderer should be brought to justice), he pointed out that Bone Dry relies on this man for his financial assets, and he will suffer from the loss. This might force the mage\u2019s hand and lead him into a situation where we can strike against him.<br /> <br /> When I returned home, I discussed all of this with Alexia, Sara and Natalie. Doc and Simon were still cloistered away with whatever they\u2019ve been busy at lately. We decided to head to Taipei tomorrow (arriving in Taipei late at night). Sara and Alexia will both pose as blondes to try and attract the bad man\u2019s attention, and once they are alone with him, will kiss him to free his soul. I will follow them, hidden and invisible, to make sure that the man\u2019s bodyguards do not cause any problems after he\u2019s dead. We\u2019ve decided that Doc and Simon should stay behind and continue the search for Evan Callum, which is what Sara and Alexia have been up to lately. We still need to find out what happened to Richie, after all. I have a feeling, however, that Doc isn\u2019t going to let us ladies go it alone. He is chivalrous to a fault.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, October 18, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> Rita and Jean had their date tonight, and as promised, I followed them, invisible and unseen, to make sure that Rita did not succumb to her predatory instincts.<br /> <br /> The date went fabulously. They really are quite smitten with each other, and I could tell how deep the attraction was by the way their eyes met with a sort of shy intensity, and the tender way they held hands across the table while waiting for their dinner. It was very romantic, though I felt terribly awkward being a voyeur.<br /> <br /> After dinner I followed them to a movie, and then they stood talking for awhile in the parking lot, postponing the moment when they would have to part ways for the night and return to their separate cars to go home, their dreams buoyed by the afterglow of the romantic evening.<br /> <br /> And that\u2019s when things began to go wrong.<br /> <br /> Rita had eaten quite a lot over dinner and snacked throughout the movie. I got the impression that she was trying to forestall her instinctual hunger, but she seemed to be fighting a losing battle. As they were about to sweetly part ways for the night, she began to ask Jean back to her apartment. Even if a part of her weren\u2019t planning on devouring him once they arrived there, inviting Jean home for the night after a first date is certainly moving far to fast, so I quietly tugged a few of Rita\u2019s hairs to remind her that I was there and to help her refocus her resolve.<br /> <br /> It worked. She and Jean sat in his car and made out for a bit, and then parted ways for the night. Rita returned to her car and I slid into the passenger seat beside her and dropped my Shroud so that she could see me again. The look she gave me then was frightening. It was the hungry look of a ravenous beast ready to spring on its prey. She told me to leave, but she needed the support of a friend, so instead I shifted into my Primeval Caul, hoping that my sharkish features and deep black eyes would discourage her from attacking me.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s when all of the stress and overeating of the night hit her. She opened the car door and vomited up much of the food she had eaten while I held her hair out of the way, rubbed her back, and tried to soothe and encourage her with what paltry words I could find to do so.<br /> <br /> I drove her home and made sure she was all right, then had Sara pick me up and take me back to Darkhaven Bluffs. I had not been home more than thirty minutes when Rita called me. She sounded terribly drunk, and told me that she had decided to reveal what she really is to Jean.<br /> <br /> Rita was not in her right mind, and we needed to talk. At the very least, she needed a friend to look after her. So I drove back to her apartment.<br /> <br /> Poor Karl. The first night after we moved into the same room together and I\u2019m not even there to enjoy it with him. I felt absolutely terrible for abandoning him like that, but I was afraid Rita might do something foolish.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, she wasn\u2019t going to any thing foolish at all, because she was passed out drunk on the floor. At least she had showered. I got her into bed and covered her up, and now I\u2019m curled up on her couch, where I hope I\u2019ll be able to get some sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, October 18, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> I woke up before Rita, and manage to scrounge up breakfast for her. Her hangover was unpleasant, but she was in a much better frame of mind this morning.<br /> <br /> She wants to continue seeing Jean, and they plan to go out again tonight. She\u2019s feeling a bit more confident, and we sat and meditated to help her center herself and deepen her self-control. I\u2019m still worried about her, but I also think that she learned some things about herself last night and has a better handle on her limits. Unfortunately, I will be in Taipei, so I can\u2019t keep an eye on here. I\u2019m seriously considering asking Natalie or Simon to watch over her with the Boneyard, but if Rita did lose control, I\u2019m not sure what either of them would be able to do do about it. I suppose I simply have to trust Rita.<br /> <br /> We also discussed whether she should tell Jean that she is a changeling. I cautioned her to take things slowly. I agree that she should not wait long because if she does, Jean might feel betrayed by the secret when she does tell him. But I\u2019m not sure that now is the right time, because it could also scare him off. I feel they need to get to know one another a bit better first. Furthermore, if she reveals what she is, then I may need to let Jean know that I\u2019m supernatural as well, and I have no idea how that\u2019s going to turn out. He and I have known each other for some time now; it might help him accept Rita\u2019s true nature if he learns that I\u2019m not entirely mortal first, but I\u2019d rather not invite him into the dark, occult world in which I live.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Sexual Harassment</u><br /> <br /> It seem there has been an awful misunderstanding between Gretchen and my uncle. The two of them spend a lot of time together in the library, and there has apparently been a bit if flirting between them. This gave Uncle Guang the wrong idea, and he has a big crush on Gretchen, so much so that he was very forward with her. He backed off when she made it clear she wasn\u2019t interested, but not before making a fool of himself and making Gretchen extremely uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Gretchen told me this in secret, but I promised to speak to my uncle about it. She\u2019s not really angry with him, just distressed by the situation. She certainly doesn\u2019t want to be around him again for the time being. My uncle is mortified. He really thought there was a spark between them, and I suppose he is a terribly lonely man. Now that the misunderstanding has been cleared up, he\u2019s giving up on Gretchen.<br /> <br /> There is one major problem, though. He was largely feeding from Gretchen, so now he must either go out to hunt or rely on someone else from the household to feed. I offered, because as I understand it, I can recover from the ill effects of losing that much blood simply by immersing myself in water while wearing my Tear-Stained Caul. But apparently the act of feeding is rather pleasurable, and that would be extremely awkward for both of us.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Blonde</u><br /> <br /> While we were discussing our plans for Taipei, it was briefly suggested that I dye my hair blonde to try and attract the attention of our mark. I quickly discarded the idea, of course\u2014I\u2019m much better off shadowing my krewe-mates, and I told the others that I would look terrible as a blonde. Natalie replied that I would look good not matter what color my hair was, and I was touched by the compliment. It was very sweet. Still, I\u2019d prefer to keep my hair its natural black.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Moving in Together </u><br /> <br /> Karl has been spending most nights in my room lately. Even when we aren\u2019t intimate, he likes being with me, sleeping in the same place I am, surrounded by things that remind him of me. It\u2019s very endearing. So I suggested today that I move into his room instead. His room is twice as large as mine, so there\u2019s plenty of room for both of our things. He was quite open to the idea, and eagerly volunteered to help me move my things this afternoon.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still storing some of my things in my old room; it\u2019s still mine, after all, and the extra closet space is nice. But most of it has been moved into Karl\u2019s room\u2014our room\u2014now. I feel very cozy and comfortable. I think this is the right thing for us at this point in our relationship.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Haunted Hotel </u><br /> <br /> Sara updated me on a new haunting Natalie dug up thanks to her friend Becky Franklin, the reporter who helped us when we were investigating the Puppeteer. I\u2019ve never actually met Becky, but apparently she is rather fetching and has caught Natalie\u2019s eye, which infuriates Karen.<br /> <br /> There is a haunted hotel near New Haven, and it is allegedly full of ghosts, including some unpleasant ones. It certainly sounds like something we should investigate. At the very least, I\u2019d like to help the ghosts there pass on peacefully. I don\u2019t know much about the hotel yet, though Natalie and Sara did a bit of research on it. It is currently closed after the latest death there, and in the pictures they found, there was something odd about the building, though none of us could put a finger on what was wrong with it. There have been a few murders and other deaths there, including the following:<br /> <br /> 1923: Sandra Taylor was murdered with an axe, but the murderer was not found.<br /> <br /> 1940: Wynona Watts was murdered with an axe. Another would-be victim, Thomas Windham, was badly injured by the axe-murderer, but did not get a good look at the killer. A man named Marvin Tommelson was caught and accused of the murder and later hanged, though it is likely that he was a convenient scapegoat and not the real killer.<br /> <br /> 1962: Albert Finnigan simply dropped dead in the hotel, though the mafia was suspected to be responsible for his death.<br /> <br /> 1968: A maid named Molly supposedly died or killed herself in the hotel.<br /> <br /> Also, there is the ghost of an old man who talks about the Great War. However, there is no record of the man dying in the hotel.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all we know for now. I suppose we will investigate it once we\u2019ve taken care of a few other things.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday October 18th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I am a needful thing.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s pitiful, Karen goes to school I get all mopey<br /> <br /> -Awww Sara will look after me.<br /> <br /> -Showed Sara the Craft!<br /> <br /> -It is good to have friends who love you!<br /> <br /> -Jasmine has the weirdest stuff happen to her. Seriously.<br /> <br /> -OK, this is just absolutely bizarre. I mean, it makes sense, but wow.<br /> <br /> -Karen\u2019s back!<br /> <br /> -Spooky is off to chaperone. Sort of.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress, her Fianc\u00e9e and her dear friend are clubbing!<br /> <br /> -Oh boy.<br /> <br /> -Well, Karen still does not like Becky. Did the temperature of the room drop or is it just me?<br /> <br /> -Emo everywhere!<br /> <br /> -Well this is interesting.<br /> <br /> -Best take Karen home, will leave Becky with Sara.<br /> <br /> -Huh. Something went wrong with Jasmine\u2019s friend, I think.<br /> <br /> -Mmm\u2026my presence is required.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday October 19th 2010<br /> <br /> -I wish every night were like last night, wow.<br /> <br /> -Of course, now Karen is off to school again. And it is Tuesday thus worse<br /> <br /> -Ah, but your Mistress has research of her own to do!<br /> <br /> -Interesting.<br /> <br /> -Nothing like a few axe murders to keep everything fun.<br /> <br /> -This could be interesting.<br /> <br /> -But of course tonight we have to carry out a contract killing for a demon from hell. What?<br /> <br /> -I haven\u2019t done anything like this since LA.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCVI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> One minor point of Clarification: Karen\u2019s dislike for Becky is less that Natalie finds her attractive and more that Becky wants a serious relationship with Natalie for herself, and Karen knows Becky has traits Natalie likes in a woman.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox is inspired somewhat by the character with the same name in Vampire: The Masquerade Bloodlines. I\u2019m actually planning to lift one \u201cquest\u201d straight from the game, a simple matter for Sin-Eaters. He was originally to be Mr. Horse, given the types Demons, but I realized people would invariably query him as to how he felt \u201cabout that fall\u201d or similar. If no one else did I probably would.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox spoke in terms of stories. He never identified himself, but after noting people were asking questions, not to him but which he could not answer, he wanted to investigate and seemed satisfied with his investigation. He would speak of stories he knew, and the need for a hero. He never directly asked Jasmine to do anything, or even confirmed his story was true. Still, he has little apparent reason to lie, though having an NPC answer questions by laughing evilly and making no comment then the PCs deciding he is legit is a new one. Not saying he isn\u2019t, mind.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox is a deliberate moral quandary. His purpose, assuming he is not misleading the PCs, is to torment souls in a hell of sorts. How do the PCs feel about helping such a dark entity? One thing I told them OOC is cooperating with Mr. Ox is NOT required to forward the Bone Dry plot. It will however make it much, much easier to deal with. None of his requests has threatened their Synergy though\u2026yet. Not that it matters to Mr. Ox. Temptation is not his job.<br /> <br /> The hotel ghost story is based on a dream. It\u2019s not really inspired by the Ocean House in Bloodlines (Good lord, play that if you haven\u2019t. Best haunting area ever in game not about hauntings) as keeping it true to that story the Sin-Eaters would be able to crush the ghost out of hand. No this matter is far, far more complicated, but should be fun. It\u2019s not a conventional situation. There\u2019s a\u2026complicated subsystem with it I can\u2019t reveal just yet. Suffice to say dealing with the ghosts helps ultimately solve it, and their vices could cause them to make unfortunate decisions.<br /> <br /> Doc should be back this next session, and huzzah for that. Almost to session 100. Not every game has one of those. Anyway, see you in two weeks. Comments and Questions Welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T14:57:27-08:00","id":33437,"title":"","content":"Considering what her uncle looks like now. I suddenly have this image of him playing the Grinch.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-19T16:35:12-08:00","id":33526,"title":"","content":"Heh, sadly in world too early in the year to make that reference, but still amusing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-30T01:28:41-08:00","id":39244,"title":"","content":"Hey folks.<br /> <br /> The good news is Doc\u2019s player is back! The bad news is it will be a bit longer for Simon\u2019s player, he still has work to do. Still, we will have Simon eventually, and we have some good stuff going on with the Chinese Demon plot. Let\u2019s look in on the Krewe, shall we?<br /> <br /> Note: Doc\u2019s Log is catching up to current, so longer as it is sort-of covering 3 sessions of time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCVII</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1700 Hours, Saturday, October 16, 2010<br /> <br /> The real issue with globetrotting through Avernian Gates is that you really lose a concept of dates. When we left Taipei, it was Sunday morning. Now we\u2019re back in New Haven and it\u2019s Saturday afternoon. This is not the way to do time travel. At least, we didn\u2019t have to stay overnight. The jet lag from walking twenty minutes can be ridiculous. I\u2019m coping by just not sleeping until I can get my body tuned to where we are.<br /> <br /> Anyway, the girls are all talking about having a night out since Snowflake and I are discussing applications and techniques of the Curse. The plan is to compare our various Keys and look for strategic overlap. Oh ... Rose apparently talked Karl into going out for Ladies\u2019 Night. That should be awkward for him. Right, so other than work on mystic strategy, Snowflake and I may investigate some Alchemical experimentation. I would enjoy tinkering with the properties of wood to give it the hardness of steel, while maintaining normal weight. Should be fun to see how we do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Sunday, October 17, 2010<br /> <br /> Curse is nothing to play with. Also Snowflake is a bad man. It\u2019s taken me most of the night to get back upstairs. Because I didn\u2019t want the others to get the wrong idea, I have tried to stay very quiet as I struggled up from the basement to my second floor room. Now that I am safely in a chair, I can better describe my ordeal and the exercise that led me here.<br /> <br /> First of all, I should note, Snowflake has not betrayed me. We agreed on this experiment together and he told me what to expect. I think its fitting that the Curse he used would be the one that in theory I\u2019m most skilled with. Anyway, we talked it over and decided that the easiest way for me to learn more about using Curse would be to remove one. Unfortunately, I\u2019ve had a very hard time doing much more than standing since. There are three ways to remove a Curse before it has run its course: The hexslinger could just remove it, another Curse could overwrite it, or a victim could break it themselves. Being that I needed a fuller understanding, we decided to go with the last option. Now that I\u2019m here, I can try to break the Curse.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1415 Hours, Monday, October 18, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been over 24 hours and I still haven\u2019t broken the Curse. I knew Snowflake was good at what he did, but I\u2019ve never had to attempt to under it. Well, outside of social situations anyway. I felt the effects loosen but then take hold again. This is an all or nothing process I\u2019m finding. I can walk slowly without too much trouble, so I came to the shop in hopes I could focus more. Pretty sure Leslie thinks I\u2019m drunk. I\u2019d tell her the truth except I don\u2019t want her to try and help. She\u2019s probably better at this than I am. So far, nothing has changed. I\u2019ve pulled up the laptop to do some research. Maybe I\u2019ll stumble on something that helps me get that final push.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2245 Hours, Monday, October 18, 2010<br /> <br /> I did it! It took me about 48 hours, but I finally figured it out.<br /> <br /> Most of my day was spent in research, but all I was finding suggested I find a way to make the hexslinger lift the Curse or find some component to help break it. One wasn\u2019t an option and the other isn\u2019t how our powers work. But then I read something from a completely non-Occult article that said many curses (small c) were nothing more than psychological warfare and if you wanted to break a curse like that, all you had to do was focus on your successes. Basically I needed to ignore the negative energy and generate my own positive vibes. Yes this is incredibly useless from a mystic perspective, but it did give me some hope.<br /> <br /> I knew exactly how the Curse was laid upon me, I knew the hexslinger, and I knew this was a test. But I also knew that I was highly skilled in three other Manifestations, had the support of The Dog of War, and I would not fail. With that in mind, I gave myself a little luck when concentrating and started from scratch. I closed my eyes and envisioned the chains wrapped around me. Those chains led back to what I assumed The Little Prince looked like, sitting upon his throne of lies. His staff of authority tied those chains to me and the smug look of control he exuded stirred something I haven\u2019t remembered in a while. While The Little Prince and The Laughing Lady hold aspects of Control in the Krewe, The Dog of War is one of the aspects of Freedom. Specifically together we are the aspect of Freedom through Conflict. As that realization washed over me, I felt the Dog bristle. With a shared growl, we struggled against the dark steel chains of Snowflake\u2019s Curse. The Little Prince\u2019s smug demeanor shifted to disbelief in my mind as the links of the chain began to warp. With a final surge of determination, we grasps our bonds and tore them from the staff. With that we were free and the Curse was broken.<br /> <br /> Needless to say, that was a mentally exhausting experience but it was vital as I now have a much greater and more personal understanding of a very useful Manifestation. It also gave me a better sense of confidence in myself. The Dog of War is proud of me as well. All in all, I pretty good evening. Now I think I\u2019m going to get cleaned up and go out on patrol.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0945 Hours, Tuesday, October 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation took an hour, but after my epiphany last night, the peace that came to me was sublime. After breakfast, Rose caught me up on the latest situation Taipei. Apparently there is an ox demon working with us to oppose Bone Dry. They talks in stories but Rose things he\u2019s on the level. This is a Chinese demon so we\u2019re not talking about the western thought of \u201cdeals with the devil\u201d here. Anyway, the story they heard was about a man who raped and murdered blonde women. This man was protected by Bone Dry mystically from dying as his soul belonged in the Hell of Being Skinned Alive. Seemed fitting to me. The plan was to dress Bright Eyes or Cupcake up in a wig and let them try to lure him out. I suggested we check with Noriko to see if she\u2019s met her monthly quota. They hadn\u2019t given that any thought but Rose thought it was a great idea. I called and told Noriko what was going on. She had not yet found her target for the month, so she was all about this. She did ask that we go shopping before we had to flee the country though. I promised as that was only fair. And because she was adorable in her request. Cupcake and Bright Eyes took her wig shopping here before we left. I noted to the others that Taipei would now forever be known for its Murder Tourism. We are a dark group.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010 (Taipei Time)<br /> <br /> I\u2019m going to have to label my logs this way to keep from confusing myself on dates.<br /> <br /> I opened the Sepulchral Gateway in about 20 minutes but oddly it only took 10 to walk into Taipei. We noticed the Road to Hell shop near the temple when we arrived. I couldn\u2019t remember seeing it there before, but Rose led us in anyway. It immediately smelled familiar but I couldn\u2019t tell why. The Dog of War grew restless and said the scent reminded him of something from long ago, but he couldn\u2019t place it either. Before we could discuss it in my head, Noriko glanced at the oddly serene man behind the counter and freaked out. She bolted from the shop babbling in Japanese. Before I could ask what the shopkeeper did, she ran back in and dragged me outside. When I finally got her speaking English again, she told me to stay away from Mr. Ox because he was Evil. Yes the say she said it, the e was capital.<br /> <br /> I stayed outside to calm her down. The rest of the Krewe joined us after a few minutes. I made some Mogwai reference and turned to look back but there was only a fish shop. The whole store front vanished. I guess it really was a curio shop. Rose confirmed we had the salve necessary to end the man financially supporting Bone Dry so I made good on my promise to take Noriko shopping.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re all getting ready to hit the club. Noriko has her wig and skimpy kimono on, but her makeup and presence when not relaxed it very different than usual. I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s slipping into the bait character she uses to lure bad men away from crowds. Anyone with an innocence fetish should really watch out.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2215 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010 (Taipei Time)<br /> <br /> We hit the club about 2130 Hours and it was interesting. Not much different from Alchemy or Gotham City, only decidedly not so gay-friendly. I knew I would stick out here and planned to stay near the door unless things went badly. But as soon as we were in, something changed. Noriko did something and I was so drawn to her, needed to be closer, that I couldn\u2019t let her get more than about 10 feet away. I was able to keep it together but it was a primal attraction and I was not prepared. Not long after, a local in a white suit and expensive jewelry walked up. I noticed three bodyguards among the others in the crowd. I also noticed I was growling once he approached Noriko. For her part, Noriko played the innocent foreigner like something out of an erotic fiction novel. Our mark was hooked almost from the moment he walked up. She strung him along until she had him just inside a mostly blind hallway. That\u2019s when he couldn\u2019t take it anymore. Our mark grabbed Noriko and kissed her deeply. My increasing growl was cut short when he stepped back with an odd look on his face. Then his skin began to violently peel off in long bloody strips. His screams increased until he exploded into a shower of gore. What hit the floor was a skeleton in a pristine suit. Blood went everywhere, some places that shouldn\u2019t have even been possible, like the back wall of the bathroom, which was behind another wall and a door. The main blood splatter on the front wall looked like an ox.<br /> <br /> That was all fascinating but I realized something had changed. Looking around, Noriko was missing. Before I completely lost it, I got a text from her that said she was outside. The three bodyguards were still in shock like most of the crowd, so we decided to leave them alone. That was about the time people started screaming and realizing this wasn\u2019t some kind of joke. We slipped out with the suddenly large number of patrons no longer interested in a good time. Once we were clear, I checked with Nightshade to make sure she was okay. I knew her issues with gore, not blood. She was \u201cmostly\u201d okay but was spared some trauma by not being in the line of fire.<br /> <br /> I noticed the Road to Hell along the nearby store fronts. That is terrifying and interesting all at once. Rose stomped in with her bag to clean up. I looked around and realized most of us were not able to do that here so I got a few plastic trash bags from Mr. Ox to save the car seats. I do not want to explain blood stains to a Chinese rental agency. When I came back in with a mostly sedate Noriko, it was story time again.<br /> <br /> According to the story, there is a shop on Hollywood Road in Hong Kong that is always closed. But it is near a cemetery with a very lovely view of the lake. Inside, books are printed on special paper. This bookshop is important to Bone Dry, which makes me suspect they produce the information that transformed Guang. Mr. Ox called it a bad luck farm. It is guarded by a pair of Jiang Shi. If \u201csomething\u201d were to happen to this shop, especially after Bone Dry\u2019s now imminent financial collapse, it was be very hard to replace. I realized this might be our best chance to get the information used to damn people and maybe find a way to reverse it or at least release the Jiang Shi from Bone Dry\u2019s control. Then there was another story, one that made less sense to our situation. The eyes of Lin the thief, a man which stole a gem for the local mafia but then let his eyes become very greedy, were preserved in the Red Dragon restaurant. The mafia, having killed the thief for not being them the gem, had his body in the freezer. Mr. Ox wanted the eyes. Should be doable, but not tonight.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1245 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade opened the gate for our trip back home. We arrived about 1030 Hours. Karen was waiting for us, which meant she probably missed at least once class. Rose went to work while the others went to sleep. I went home with Noriko. She\u2019s sleeping now and I might snuggle up next to her for a little nap soon too.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1415 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes caught me as I was getting back to the House. Apparently while I was dealing with my Curse, they learned about a haunted hotel through Becky. I\u2019m sure that makes Karen very happy. Anyway, Bright Eyes showed me a picture and asked if I could see anything wrong. There was supposed to be something off about it, but I didn\u2019t see anything.<br /> <br /> Once we were all together again, we discussed going for the eyes Thursday. I need to get a pair of extractors and a pair of large marbles, but that shouldn\u2019t be too hard. We also talked about the karmic debt we were earning for helping a demon. That was Noriko\u2019s take on things and I promised her I would mention it to the Krewe. Rose dismissed this idea at first, claiming that we do enough good for other people to offset the debt. But unlike when she usually brushes an idea off, she didn\u2019t sound so convinced herself. So long as we aren\u2019t being used as unwitting pawns by a supernatural creature that finds our involvement entertaining, I think Nightshade and I will be okay. But if we learn that we aren\u2019t actually working against Bone Dry or are causing more harm than good, then we\u2019ll be quite pissed. I guess we\u2019ll just have to see.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0450 Hours, Thursday, October 21, 2010 (Taipei Time)<br /> <br /> It was another short walk to Taipei tonight, but not everything was so cut and dried.<br /> <br /> Nightshade handled the Red Dragon guards through her Boneyard while Rose, Cupcake, and I slipped in. I don\u2019t normally go along on our B&amp;E parties, but I didn\u2019t want anyone else in the Krewe trying to perform surgery, even if it was on a dead guy.<br /> <br /> We got to the freezer and I got to it. Lin was obviously killed by shotgun wound to the chest, close range, and probably didn\u2019t have a chance to defend himself. But his eyes were completely intact. With the extractors, surgery went very smoothly and the marbles fit very nicely. That was just a touch I thought of to keep the mafia from realizing something had changed about his eyes. Never know when they might notice sunken sockets. But as soon as I held both eyes, I knew that Lin\u2019s eyes held a connection to his spirit...I\u2019m not even sure it was a connection to a ghost. It didn\u2019t feel like an anchor, but similar. I also immediately knew, somehow, that Lin would feel anything that happened to his eyes. This is not just a snatch and grab and Mr. Ox has some questions to answer. But we were able to sneak out again before the opening shift came in. I explained to the others what I felt. We aren\u2019t really sure why Ox needs the eyes now. But the big question I have is simple.<br /> <br /> Why isn\u2019t Lin\u2019s soul in the Hell of Gouged-Out Eyes already?<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s time to talk to a demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> Tuesday, October 19, 2010, Night (Wednesday in Taipei)<br /> <br /> I told Doc and Simon about the ox demon and our plans to help him retrieve a soul bound for the Hell of Being Skinned Alive. Simon took it in stride, but Doc was predictably concerned and insisted on accompanying us. However, he had a brilliant idea. Noriko is well-practiced in attracting the wrong kind of attention from the wrong kind of men, so he called her and invited her to serve as our \u201cbait.\u201d Since she\u2019s a werecat and must kill a morally corrupt person each month, she readily agreed. Alexia and Sara found a blonde wig for Noriko to ensure that she draw the eye of our prey.<br /> <br /> Noriko was less enthusiastic when we arrived in Taiwan and found the Road to Hell, the ox demon\u2019s shop. It was a cluttered curio shop full of strange and mysterious items hidden among cheap antiques, and Noriko must have been able to see the ox demon for what he really was. She was frightened, and though she agreed to go through with the plan, she suggested that we not deal with the demon anymore. However, she doesn\u2019t quite see the whole picture.<br /> <br /> The ox demon gave us the balm we would need to sever our prey\u2019s soul from his body, and we were off to a club. I remained invisible as we went inside, shadowing Noriko closely. Something she did made me want to follow her, to watch her. It put me a bit off guard, at least as far as she was concerned, but it did not interfere with my job.<br /> <br /> We found our mark fairly quickly. He was a young, handsome Chinese man with a wolfish, predatory look in his eye and charming smile that hid a sinister purpose. Noriko used her charms to draw him in, simultaneously leading him on and playing hard to get until she could lure him into a small hallway on one side of the club. There, she got him to kiss her, and as soon as he did, his flesh began to boil off his bones and then exploded as though he had been torn apart from a hundred directions at once. The blood spatters covered everything nearby, including me, and even managed to phase through the walls. It was\u2026gruesome, to say the least.<br /> <br /> The club froze for long moments as the guests tried to reconcile what had just happened, and then chaos erupted. Noriko and I quickly made our escape, and the others, who had been watching from nearby, careful not to draw attention, filtered out with the crowd.<br /> <br /> Once we were outside, I noticed the Road to Hell around the corner nearby. The place has a convenient way of being where it needs to be. I was a little annoyed at being covered in blood and gore, but I had brought extra clothing. Doc tossed me my bag and I strode to the shop and inside, and demanded to use the ox demon\u2019s bathroom to clean up and change.<br /> <br /> Once that was done, the others had joined me inside the shop. The ox demon was pleased with our results, and offered us two more \u201cstories\u201d as payment. The first was a particular interest. It seems that the there is a shop on Hollywood Road in Hong Kong. It\u2019s always closed, but inside, Bone Dry\u2019s servants prepare manuals on special papers, manuals that claim to teach the secrets of immortality but instead transform one into a jiang shi bound to Bone Dry\u2019s will. Manuals like the one that tricked Uncle Guang.<br /> <br /> The shop is located conveniently near a cemetery, and the ox demon described it in enough detail that Doc thinks he can find it with his sepulchral gate ceremony. We plan to go deal with the place soon enough, but chose to wait until another night.<br /> <br /> The second story involved a jewel thief named Lin who stole a priceless gem for the local mob, but his greed got the better of him and he decided to keep the gem. The mob tracked him down and murdered him to retrieve the gem, and his corpse was, at that moment, being stored in a freezer in a large restaurant known as the Red Dragon. I was familiar with the place, as it\u2019s a fairly well-known restaurant, though I had always heard rumors that the mob ran it.<br /> <br /> The ox demon wanted Lin\u2019s eyes, claiming that they were perfect for the Eye-Gouging Hell, which holds the most avaricious sinners. He did not insist that we follow up on the story; he simply offered it with the implied promise that if we brought him the eyes, he would share another story that would help us hurt Bone Dry. I think the ox demon has even darker designs on Bone Dry than we do.<br /> <br /> For now, however, we are returning home. I\u2019m looking forward to getting some sleep for the first time in my new room with Karl there beside me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 20, 2010, Night (Thursday in Taipei)<br /> <br /> Sara made arrangements with Becky to get in touch with her aunt so that we can gain access to the Haunted Hotel sometime soon. Sara seems quite interested in Becky, so I suspect she will attempt to bed her soon and add her to her steadily lengthening list of conquests.<br /> <br /> We decided to go after the thief\u2019s eyes, and so we headed back to Taipei in the afternoon so as to arrive late in the dark hours of night. Natalie and Sara remained several blocks away. Sara watched over Natalie\u2019s body as Natalie allowed her mind to wander her Boneyard. She had a look throughout the restaurant and caused the two guards to fall asleep.<br /> <br /> Alexia, Doc and I made our way inside. I donned my Cold-Wind caul to become as insubstantial as the air, but did not become invisible. Alexia used her mastery over machines and electronics to disable the security system and any cameras, with Natalie warning us of anything we might have missed. We almost triggered a laser trip-wire. I walked right through it, but did not set it off thanks to my ephemeral state, and Alexia noticed it in time to keep herself and Doc from crossing it.<br /> <br /> It took some time to locate the right freezer, as there were several. Alexia worked the locks and got us inside, and once we found the body, Doc went to work with some sort of medical instruments he brought along. They seemed the perfect tools for removing one\u2019s eyes, though the task was made more difficult because the eyes were frozen.<br /> <br /> I had been bothered all along, wondering why Lin\u2019s spirit was not already in the hell where it belongs if he really was so greedy. So while Doc worked, I touched the body and opened my eyes with the Stillness Oracle. I fetched glimpses of the thief\u2019s life and death, and found that he was not especially greedy, though it was greed that led to his demise. From what I saw, I could not tell whether he truly belonged in the Hell of Gouged-Out Eyes or not, but it was enough to make me doubt our purpose.<br /> <br /> We all noticed that the thief\u2019s spirit seemed to reside in his eyes, and though they remained inanimate, they seemed to respond to us, as though they could feel and see us. There was something odd about that, and Alexia suggested that the ox demon might wish to use them as some sort of ingredient for one of his concoctions, or perhaps he planned to trade them to someone else who could find a purpose for them. In either case, his interest in the eyes, and in the thief\u2019s soul, might be selfish rather than an attempt to right a karmic imbalance.<br /> <br /> So I decided to confront the ox demon about it, and ask him why Lin\u2019s soul isn\u2019t in the Hell of Gouged-Out Eyes if it already belongs there, and why he wants the eyes. We are heading to the shop now.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Shen</u><br /> <br /> The ox demon is a potent supernatural entity, but also a natural part of the supernatural world. Like all Chinese shen, he serves his purpose. Demons like him often try to take advantage of mortals, so I\u2019ve been a bit cautious around him, and will continue to be for as long as we deal with him. However, I realized that he is not treating me like a mortal, but rather as a fellow shen. Which means he is dealing with me from a position of respect and equality instead of trying to take advantage of me. Knowing that made me feel more confident, and I hope the demon does nothing to upset that confidence.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Sally Fields</u><br /> <br /> I spent a portion of the afternoon translating for Alexia as she invades a Taiwanese confectionary and worked out an arrangement with the owners: she would teach them some new tricks about western desserts if they would show her a thing or two about some of their traditional confections. It was interesting to see her work, though I think the confectionary employees were a bit bewildered by the whole thing, sudden as it was. I suppose it didn\u2019t help that Alexia introduced herself as Sally Fields.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Rita\u2019s Conscience </u><br /> <br /> I was concerned about Rita\u2019s date with Jean, which was happening while we were in Taipei with Noriko. I couldn\u2019t be there to make sure she did nothing foolish, so I asked Simon to stay behind and watch over her with his Boneyard. He readily agreed, and promised to make Rita see a small illusion of me on her shoulder, acting as her conscience, should things get out of control. I called Rita when we returned, and all is well. She kept her urges in check, but she\u2019s more eager than ever to tell Jean who and what she really is. I hope he takes it well, but I worry that Rita\u2019s heart may be broken.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Questionable Activities</u><br /> <br /> We spent some time discussing whether or not we were doing the right thing by helping the ox demon. I was a bit concerned about the karmic impact of our actions. Noriko thought that helping him was bad karma through and through, and she might be right. But I think it\u2019s more complicated than that. I believe we were helping to right a karmic wrong by freeing the murderer-rapist\u2019s soul to be claimed by the hell where it belonged. Now it can be cleansed and returned to the karmic cycle.<br /> <br /> Even if it is bad karma to work with the ox demon, I think we do enough good and generate enough good karma to offset it. We are the Middle Shadows, which implies that we walk the line between good and bad, light and dark, and as long as we are helping the karmic cycle and its balance, I think we are doing the right thing.<br /> <br /> Natalie, Doc and Sara are pagan, of course, and they believe in serving minors gods anyway. As far as they are concerned, that\u2019s exactly what the ox demon is, so they are far less troubled by the karmic consequences of our actions than I am.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Tuesday October 19th 2010<br /> <br /> -Getting ready for tonight.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up. Very short one.<br /> <br /> -New plan?<br /> <br /> -Psycho killer qu'est-ce que c'est\u2026.<br /> <br /> -And they are off!<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 20th 2010<br /> <br /> -Back from a faraway land.<br /> <br /> -That was only mildly traumatizing.<br /> <br /> -One week till my birthday.<br /> <br /> -I need to be held.<br /> <br /> -I need a nap.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -My Fianc\u00e9e is, admittedly, mildly crazy.<br /> <br /> -I will, however, be spending the evening with her.<br /> <br /> -Movies and ice cream? Movies and ice cream!<br /> <br /> -@nerak smells so nice.<br /> <br /> -Wheeeeeeeeeeeeeeee<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday October 21st<br /> <br /> -My 20s are running out so fast!<br /> <br /> -If I build a wall someone will still turn the page\u2026<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Eventually things will settle down.<br /> <br /> -OK it\u2019s go time.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> End Session XCVII</i><br /> <br /> My players threw me for a bit of a loop bringing Noriko in, but nothing I cannot handle. As a reminder, The Colony are in War Against the Pure if you are unfamiliar with them. They are plenty screwed up.<br /> <br /> As I had hoped, a lot of discussion and consideration on how to proceed. This was intended to be a little morally questionable, and I was not disappointed. That tension was good.<br /> <br /> Lots to do for next time. I am ready for them if they hit the hotel, but they may keep messing with the Demon. We will see. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-13T02:06:57-08:00","id":48018,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the start of the hotel story. Our posse begins their investigations. Woo.<br /> <br /> <i>Session XCVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1800 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t say exactly that paranoia is a negative trait when you are knowingly working with demons. But apparently, we were over suspicious this time.<br /> <br /> Rose and the others went into the Road to Hell first to discuss our concerns with Mr. Ox, while Nightshade and I stayed in the car with the eyes. After a few minutes, Rose came for us with the demon\u2019s explanation. It was still a little cryptic, but the gist of it was that if Mr. Ox were to mettle in the affairs of the soul, then he too would have his own Hell to visit. I trust Rose\u2019s judgment in these things so we took the eyes inside. Mr. Ox looked, not nervous, but not as certain of things as when I saw him last. The demon examined the eyes of Lin the Thief, then settled himself into a more composed expression. Nodding to Rose, he confirmed that Lin\u2019s soul was in the Hell of Gouged-Out Eyes. As we handed over the eyes, Mr. Ox admitted he did not yet have another story, but make sure we were aware there was another one owed to us. Once we knew things were as we hoped, I made sure to be exceptionally polite and respectful. As we took our leave, I bowed deeply and never turned my back on Mr. Ox. He seemed to take note of the respect, but I couldn\u2019t have hoped for any sort of response. That\u2019s not how these things work.<br /> <br /> With our soul trafficking concluded, Nightshade opened the gate and we headed back home. It occurred to me as we walked along the bone path that we had acted as agents of an Underworld god and that of the Karmic cycle while also opposing the will of what amounts to a demigod. There were myths about people doing similar acts throughout the history of man. The Balance of Shadows now stands with an elite collection of heroes. This led to me planning out a new drawing. Images of this collection of heroes standing together, waiting with the Krewe ascending the treacherous stairs to meet them. We stepped through the Avernian Gate into Dark Haven Bluffs just as my mental image of the drawing formed.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re going to get changed, cleaned up a little bit and go to dinner before meeting with Becky to discuss her haunted Hidden Hillside Hotel.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2300 Hours, Wednesday, October 20, 2010<br /> <br /> We met Becky at her house around 2000 Hours. Rose had never met her but seemed to have already decided that Nightshade had designs on bedding our host. I knew better but it was slightly fun to watch Rose dig a hole. We made introductions then Becky handed over a set of three keys: front door, master room key, and employee only areas. She had a computer setup with a large monitor and microphone so we could contact her aunt. This Brenda did not seem convinced we weren\u2019t charlatans but Becky was certain we were the paranormal investigators she needed. Before we called Brenda I tried to play the part a little, but also get useful information. Brenda\u2019s ownership of the hotel was neither new nor unusual since it had been in the family since sometime in the \u201840s. Sometime during the \u201840s there was an axe murder and by all accounts an innocent man was convicted and electrocuted for being black. There had been nothing strange about the hotel other than the ghosts and murders. Once Becky gave us the broad overview, she called Brenda over Skype. Brenda was an older woman but not frail or withered. I could see a slight family resemblance between aunt and niece. Becky introduced us all by first name, which is still a little jarring to hear, before Brenda gave us specific details about the most common ghostly encounters. Troy Donovan seems to be the most connected to the hotel. He was born in 1899, the year the hotel was built and stayed there at multiple points throughout his life. A travelling salesman by trade, Troy got around but always seemed to find his way back to the Hidden Hillside. Brenda even met Troy when she was a girl. Oddly, Troy did not die in the hotel nor did he die of anything other than old age. Troy is connected with the longest running sightings. There is even a room named for him. Nightshade was pleased to learn this was the Troy Donovan Music Room. It was also noted that Troy found it amusing if you suggested he was a ghost. Daisy was a young teen during the \u201820s. She was also a prostitute within the hotel where she stayed on the first floor. She hanged herself in the room. Sondra Taylor was an actress during the \u201820s. She was a confirmed victim of the axe murderer. Another actress, Wynona Watts, is most often found in the bar. She also fell to the axe murderer, but in the \u201840s. Thomas Wyndham is somewhat of a mystery to us except he stayed in the hotel during the \u201840s and was attacked from behind in the hedge maze. He was badly injured, but survived the attack. Marvin Tomilson was the arrested in the \u201840s as the only suspect in the axe murders. As a black man with no reason to be there, he was convicted by the highly dependable justice system of the post-depression era without any known evidence to connect him to the murders. He was sentenced to the electric chair and died an innocent man, at least as far as anyone can tell today. Molly Hatcher was a maid during the \u201860s and was noted for being terrified of the ghosts, which were already a known phenomenon at the time. She allegedly committed suicide by throwing herself down the grand staircase. And finally Yvette. She stayed in the hotel in the \u201860s. No one named Yvette died or reported any attacks in the hotel so she is a mystery as well. Brenda noted that she often spoke of the Kennedy assassination. Many of these individuals were sighted in the bar, music room, or the hallways near their rooms. Troy seemed to be an exception to this as well as he seemed to pop up in any place a guest may be. Brenda added a strange piece of information as well. She said that Troy seemed to manifest during different periods in his life, with knowledge connected to that age and time. He did not remember meeting Brenda when she met him as a ghost however.<br /> <br /> Brenda then stated that she didn\u2019t see a reason to pay us until we were completed with our investigation. I was shocked...I had no idea we were being offered payment. Becky stepped in and made more acceptable arrangements, including securing expenses for us. We could buy supplies on the way and actually get reimbursed for it. This was really new for me. Brenda got off Skype at the point, leaving Becky to give the rest of the details. We would need to get into the basement to turn on the power and water. There was a generator that should handle this, but there had been a collapse of the basement access recently. The workers hired to fix the damage were what sparked the latest round of sightings. She also let us know that the elevator was turned off to keep the shaft as a safe entrance into the basement. Brenda apparently thought Becky should go along with us but we found this to be unnecessary.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re back in our own haunted House. Cupcake is gathering our caving gear and some food supplies from our own stock. I suggested that we all contact our significant others as the hotel was up on the mountains and would likely take us a few days to deal with, longer if the weather decided to be difficult. Now I\u2019m just writing this until Noriko gets here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2000 Hours, Thursday, October 21, 2010<br /> <br /> This place is weird.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes and Cupcake both drove so we could load all of our equipment and supplies. We arrived about 1800 Hours and nothing seemed out of the ordinary. I looked around outside but there were normal bird and insect noises, the wind rustled through the trees, you know - normal. As soon as we moved inside however, we met Troy. He was very pleasant man, looking to be in his early 40s. He told us during our conversation that it had been 10 years since he had last been here. Looking at him, he was a physical ghost, but he was a ghost. He died of a heart attack, but this was not the age of his death. Bright Eyes began chatting him up and learned that Wynona was here but Sondra had died \u201cseveral years ago.\u201d Cupcake walked in with her Death Mask on while she looked the place over for illusions. This completely weirded Troy out. While Bright Eyes talked her way through that, I used the distraction to really look around. The room felt weird or off somehow but I couldn\u2019t tell why. That this was the room in the picture I\u2019d been shown before, it make it more ominous. Troy left to find the desk clerk but said he\u2019d be back to help with our luggage. Just as Rose came in, Troy returned and sure enough he helped us carry our luggage to the second floor where we decided to take rooms. Rose asked him about \u201cnews from the war.\u201d Her Asian features threw Troy for a moment, but he recovered as she explained she was half Kiwi. I\u2019m not sure if he knew what that was or not, but he certainly knew how to stay in a conversation. He mentioned that FDR hadn\u2019t gotten us into the war yet. He also noted that Tommy was on our hall so we might meet him soon. We could only assume he meant Thomas Wyndham. Once we had our gear in the hallway, he told us his room was in the West Wing on the second floor as well before walking off again.<br /> <br /> Cupcake took Rose, who brought Lily for some reason that I canNOT fathom, and went room to room checking for anything. Nightshade took her things into a room as Bright Eyes suggested we head to the basement to restart the furnace. We managed to get back to the first floor and open the elevator shaft when we heard a woman scream upstairs. It was not one of the Krewe so we raced back up the stairs. When we reached the room Rose and Cupcake were looking in, we met Molly. She was at least as concerned about police showing up as she was about the ghosts. And she was very afraid of ghosts. The story we gave her was that we were hired by the owners to investigate. I even gave her my room number to report anything she thought was unusual. This seemed to calm her a little, but she was still very nervous. We left the room and Nightshade met us in the hallway. She informed us that she had sweeped the rooms ahead of Rose and Cupcake to keep any surprises to a minimum. Molly wasn\u2019t there until they opened the door. She also couldn\u2019t find Troy through her Boneyard. We all got our ear curls after that.<br /> <br /> Moving back to the basement, we managed the 10 foot drop without issue and the dark was no match for her flashlights. But there was something wrong here. The Dog was restless and eventually I was able to pinpoint the sensation of being drawn, almost like the pull of a magnet. I didn\u2019t notice it on the first floor and I got the impression the pull would get stronger if I could somehow move below the basement. Nightshade began a conversation with who was eventually realized was Thomas Wyndham but that went without incident. By this point, Bright Eyes just warned me to shield my eyes and lit up her Pyre-Flame Caul. I flung just enough blood from a scratch on my hand to pull my Stigmata Shroud close around me. The red light at the end of the basement was more than a little disturbing until we realized it was the emergency light for the furnace. I turned off my flashlight and turned it around so I could use it as a club. This was quickly becoming a scene from a horror movie.<br /> <br /> While we carefully picked our way through the basement by Bright Eye\u2019s ghost light, Rose and Cupcake found another guest. This one was not at all happy with a room inspection. Nightshade stopped us for a moment as she noted the woman had two pistols, matched silencers, and ammo in the nightstand. She said the guns were made for someone not strong enough to fire larger weapons with precision, similar to Nightshade\u2019s own weapon. This gave us a strong suspect for the murderer. Once Rose left the room, Nightshade described how she became a red silhouette of herself then disappeared, as if phasing out. Bright Eyes flipped the switch and the furnace rumbled to life. That also fired up the generator. With the hotel back in operating order, we went to check out the cave-in. There was plenty of rubble blocking the rest of the basement but then I noticed the blast marks. This was no cave-in. Someone detonated a shaped-charge to collapse the floor on purpose. Bright Eyes and Rose decided to switch groups so we called down the elevator. It was decided that no one needed to be alone at this point. Nightshade met us on the way to the top floor. The pull felt weaker like on the first floor, but was still there. The others noticed it once we mentioned it as well. Rose and Lily came back down with me while Nightshade joined Cupcake and Bright Eyes. When we got out on the first floor, a woman\u2019s voice called out to me from the Music Room. Though she called me Pedro, I knew she meant me and I also knew by the concern in her voice that she was not being funny. I turned to see a woman that would be lovely in any decade, but was obviously from the \u201820s. She looked at me for a moment before realizing I was not her friend. She apologized and I struck up a conversation as she seemed very concerned for a friend. Pedro had been in a car accident and was confined to a wheelchair some time ago. She was confused as she did not realize her friend had healed so well. Her story was an eerie mirror to my own injuries and her considerate stance toward myself and her Pedro was notable for her time given the delicate white complexion of her face. Once Sondra Taylor returned to the Music Room as we bid her goodbye and I tried to focus again. The odd similarities between myself and Pedro were unexpected. Rose and I climbed down the shaft after I sent the elevator back up and noted through the ear curl not to send the elevator for the first floor while we were down. Rose noticed the pull here as well and she liked it even less. She decided to phase through the rubble to see what she could find. After a few minutes she called through the curl that she found the plasm, but very little else. There was enough plasm to justify all the ghosts here however. We\u2019ve come back up now so I could write this down and to get away from that pulling sensation. This will be a long few days.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 20, 2010, Afternoon (Thursday in Taipei)<br /> <br /> I confronted the ox demon about the thief and his eyes while the others waited outside. He was quite elusive about it, speaking in half truths that were beginning to infuriate me when he relented somewhat and admitted that he could do nothing that would harm a soul\u2019s place in the karmic cycle. To do so would be to sentence himself to the same punishments he inflicted on others. In the end, I suppose the demon might use the eyes for occult purpose, but the thief\u2019s soul belongs where it is in the Hell of Gouged-Out Eyes. I simply hope his suffering ends soon so that his karma will be cleansed and he can be reincarnated to try again. Perhaps his experiences now will help subconsciously inform the choices he makes in his next life.<br /> <br /> The ox demon promised to give us more information once we were finished with Bone Dry\u2019s publishing house in Hong Kong. He might be a bit sketchy, but he is not a liar, and he has been true to his word, so I am certain that when we need the information, we will find him.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 20, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Sara had scheduled a meeting with Becky to discuss the haunted Hidden Hillside Hotel, so upon returning to New Haven, we went to meet Becky and Skype with her aunt. There was a spot of confusion on my part regarding Becky and her relationship to Natalie and Karen. I thought Natalie was carrying on with her somehow, or leading her on, which would explain Karen\u2019s attitude toward the situation. But I should have had greater faith in Natalie, as she has been quite firm in rebuffing Becky\u2019s flirtations.<br /> <br /> The visit went well enough, and we learned enough to get started on our investigation of the hotel. Becky\u2019s aunt Brenda was quite forthcoming. The ghosts in the hotel aren\u2019t like other ghosts\u2014they aren\u2019t mere shades hidden from view by the veil that separates Twilight from the living world. Instead, they move about and interact as though they are normal people, and seem \u201creal\u201d enough to those who encounter them.<br /> <br /> Oddly, the hotel\u2019s basement collapsed recently, though the rest of the hotel was undamaged. Neither Becky nor Brenda knew how or why it had collapsed, though.<br /> <br /> It seems our best approach is to go and stay at the hotel for a few days, seeking out the ghosts and trying to find out why they linger so that we can resolve them.<br /> <br /> I think I\u2019ve made notes on the hotel ghosts before, but it won\u2019t hurt to collect the information again along with what we learned from Becky and Brenda.<br /> <br /> Troy Donovan (the Salesman; lived 1899 - 1976): One of the more significant ghosts in the hotel. Troy was a traveling salesman who stayed at the hotel frequently over the years. Strangely, he manifests in different clothes and hairstyles that correspond to the various decades in which he stayed at the hotel. He was born in the same year the hotel was built, and he is the only one who knew the other ghosts, or rather the people they were, in life. He may well be the lynch pin to whatever is going on in the hotel, though by all accounts he seems quite friendly, and not at all malicious. The music room was named after Troy after his passing.<br /> <br /> Daisy (the Young Girl): Daisy was a poor orphaned girl in her early teens who lived at the hotel. Sadly, she prostituted herself to guests, and it must have been too much for her, because she hanged herself in her room sometime in the 20\u2019s.<br /> <br /> Wynona Watts (an Actress): Wynona was an actress who often stayed in the hotel and spent much of her time in the bar.<br /> <br /> Sandra Taylor (an Actress): Sandra was also an actress who stayed frequently at the hotel and was killed there in the 20\u2019s by the mysterious axe murderer.<br /> <br /> Thomas Wynham: I don\u2019t know much about Thomas, but he was injured by the axe murderer in the hedge maze behind the hotel. He only survived being struck in the back with an axe because the murderer left him for dead.<br /> <br /> Marvin Tommelson (the Scapegoat): Marvin was an African-American man connected to the hotel, and he was accused unfairly of committing the axe murders. He was executed by electric chair despite his probable innocence.<br /> <br /> Molly Hatcher (the Maid): Molly was one of the hotel maids. She was terrified of the hotel\u2019s ghosts and is often seen in the Music Room. She died when she fell down the hotel\u2019s long grand staircase. It was called a suicide, but it was probably either an accident or a murder. Indeed, I think it must have been a murder, because I cannot otherwise guess why the hotel management would have claimed it was a suicide instead of an accident unless they were anxiously trying to cover something up.<br /> <br /> Yvette (a Young Woman): Yvette stayed in the hotel during the 60\u2019s and is often seen in the Music Room or in and around her room. No one by her name ever died in the hotel, so her presence there is a bit strange.<br /> <br /> There aren\u2019t any other sorts of ghostly manifestation\u2014strange sounds, things moving on their own and the like\u2014aside from the appearance of the ghosts themselves, which is also odd. We decided to go to the hotel this weekend, starting Thursday after I\u2019m finished with my classes. To that end, we\u2019ve spent the afternoon getting plenty of equipment, food and water together for our investigation.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, October 21, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Karl and I and a wonderful night together last night. It was only the second we\u2019ve spent together in our room, but it already feels like home, all because Karl is there, I\u2019m sure. I really wanted to put aside this hotel business and spend a few more days with Karl without running off to Taipei or anywhere else, but the others were quite eager to explore the hotel, and I confess that I do relish the opportunity to help some ghosts. It\u2019s been a long time since we\u2019ve really been able to do so, and I always feel most like I\u2019m fulfilling my purpose when we help ghosts pass on peacefully. While we are away, Karl is going back to Cold Harbor to visit family and take care of some things. I hope he has a nice trip, and I\u2019m glad he won\u2019t be lonely in the mansion without me.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, October 21, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We arrived at the hotel, settled into rooms on the second floor and began our investigation this evening. The situation here at the hotel is considerably more complex and mysterious than we thought it would be. Lily wanted to come with us, and I thought it would be a good opportunity for her to help out a bit and feel useful, so I invited her along, much to Doc\u2019s chagrin.<br /> <br /> Troy greeted us in the lobby, and he was just and friendly as Becky told us he would be. He even helped us carry some of our bags. He seemed surprised that I had an American name, so I explained that I\u2019m half Kiwi. I got him talking a bit about \u201ccurrent events,\u201d and he certainly seemed to think it was sometime in the late 30\u2019s. Meanwhile, Alexia walked in wearing her wooden death mask and shaking around a few of our charms in order to awaken her Phantasmal Oracle so that she could examine the place for illusory or hidden things, but I don\u2019t think she saw anything out of place. Troy seemed to think her antics were a bit odd, but she didn\u2019t care. Sara took over talking to Troy and learned that he was staying in room 2N on the west wing of the 2nd floor. She asked about the actresses, but he said that Sandra had died some time ago. Then, once he had helped us get our bags to the second floor, he disappeared.<br /> <br /> After we settled into rooms on the main wing of the second floor, Lily and I followed Alexia around as she continued to scan the rooms with her Oracle. We did not find anything hidden by illusion, but when we opened room 2L on the east wing, we startle a maid there: Molly\u2019s ghost. She was very nervous, so we told her we had been hired by the hotel owner to look into things at the hotel. She didn\u2019t quite believe us, and might have feared that we were with the police. Natalie had remained in her room and was having a look around with her Boneyard, and she told us that the ghost simply appeared in the room as soon as we entered. I began to get the sense that these ghostly manifestations were being controlled by something else. They seem to be ghosts as far as we can tell, but there\u2019s something not quite right here. I would wonder if they were illusions except that Alexia is certain they are not.<br /> <br /> Doc and Sara went downstairs to find a way into the basement and discovered that it was caved in and almost completely blocked off. They were able to reach the generator room and restore electricity, but the deeper they went, the edgier the Dog of War and Virgin Sacrifice became. The geists felt a pull, firm and insistent though far from overpowering. Once Doc mentioned it to the rest of us, we could feel it as well. It was weak but present, like the beginnings of a headache. The Drowned Bride was practically wringing her hangs in agitation.<br /> <br /> Natalie was visited in her room by Thomas Windham\u2019s ghost, and had a bit of a chat with him, though I don\u2019t gather anything came of it. Alexia and I moved on to the 3rd floor and encountered yet another of the ghosts in room 3B. This time it was Yvette, and she seemed very nervous. She didn\u2019t want us looking around her room, but we bullied our way in anyway and asked her if something was wrong. Ultimately Alexia and I did our best to distract Yvette while Lily sneaked in to have a look around. She discovered a gun in the bedside drawer and a body bag hidden beneath the bed, as though Yvette was planning to commit a murder.<br /> <br /> I decided to test a theory, so I made excuses to leave the room and then cloaked myself invisibly in the Shroud of Stilness. I then crept back into the room while Alexia apologized for the intrusion and left. I wanted to see if Yvette\u2019s ghost would disappear once there were not witnesses present, but she did not. Instead, she went through the motions of checking her gun and summoning the determination to kill another person. But then she seemed to get stuck, like she did not know what else to do. I have a feeling that whatever presence is commanding these ghosts could sense me. It must have known I was still there, and tried to keep up its charade, but it didn\u2019t know what to do without someone to interact with. Natalie was watching through her Boneyard, and when I finally left by phasing through the wall, she saw Yvette fade into a reddish silhouette and then disappear completely, along with her gun and body bag.<br /> <br /> By that time, Doc and Sara had checked out what they could in the basement, and Doc was certain the basement had been collapsed intentionally with explosive charges. Whatever was down there, someone wanted it sealed off. We decided that Sara and I would switch places since I could phase through the rubble choking the basement while Sara and Natalie teamed up with Alexia to investigate the attic.<br /> <br /> The attic was filled with various articles of hotel furniture, all in storage, but Sara\u2019s keen eyes noticed a case filled with newspaper clippings. The clippings were all about the people who died in the hotel: Sandra, Thomas, Daisy, and others. There was an article about a man named Albert Finnigan, a teamster informant who allegedly died of appendicitis but was probably killed by the mob. Molly had something to do with his death; she might have sold him out or perhaps delivered poison to him with the room service. Yvette cared for Albert, so it\u2019s possible that her decision to kill someone was connected to his death.<br /> <br /> Also of note was the fact that Daisy\u2019s remains were stolen, and no one knows where they ended up.<br /> <br /> While Doc and I were on our way back down to the basement, Sandra\u2019s ghost appeared from the Music Room and called after him. She mistook Doc for a Latino friend named Pedro who had been badly injured, and she was surprised to see him up and about. Doc had a nice conversation with her even after she realized she had mistaken his identity, and she seemed to be a charming woman. There were some odd similarities between her friend and Doc.<br /> <br /> Once we bid Sandra goodbye, we returned to the basement, which involved climbing down the elevator shaft. There was little left down there, honestly, but I phased into the rubble, looking for a room beyond it or anything else that might be significant. I found only that the debris filled almost the whole space. Only a few empty pockets remained, and there was nothing of interest there. Whatever secrets still lie in the basement are beyond us for now. I was, however, able to track down the spot where the haunt\u2019s plasm gathers, and since no one else could reach it, I absorbed it.<br /> <br /> We are taking a break now to discuss what we\u2019ve learned and what steps to take next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Room Assignments </u><br /> (2F) My room.<br /> (2G) Alexia\u2019s room.<br /> (2H) Natalie\u2019s room. Thomas Windham also appeared here.<br /> (2I) Sara\u2019s room.<br /> (2J) Doc\u2019s room.<br /> (2L) Molly appeared here.<br /> (2N) Troy Donovan\u2019s room.<br /> (3B) Yvette\u2019s room. She appeared here and seemed to be plotting a murder.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCVIII</i><br /> <br /> No Natalie log, as she was able to tweet for very little of the session; the parts in China and the Hotel she could not.<br /> <br /> Looks like they have something rather interesting they have gotten involved in. The hotel mystery should keep them busy for a little while. I should note while I have pictures for everyone, Troy Donavon is represented by John Goodman. That should give some idea of how strange a character Troy is given some of Mr. Goodman\u2019s roles.<br /> <br /> I also have a handy map of the hotel, created by Jasmine\u2019s player. Here you go:<br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/HiddenHillsideHotel1stFloor_zps434742d6.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">1st Floor</a><br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/HiddenHillsideHotel2ndFloor_zps420a081d.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">2nd Floor</a><br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/HiddenHillsideHotel3rdFloor_zps69903cca.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">3rd Floor</a><br /> <br /> Let me know if you have any comments or questions. Hope you enjoyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-27T16:57:20-08:00","id":59279,"title":"","content":"Time to continue the investigation of the Haunted Hillside. Lot happened.<br /> <i><br /> Session XCIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Friday, October 22, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m surrounded by liars, smugglers, assassins, and murderers; all being controlled by an unknown entity. That\u2019s what we have in this hotel. Hidden Hillside Hotel my ass. More like the Hideous Highway to Hell.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m angry so this probably doesn\u2019t make sense. But it\u2019s because I\u2019m angry that this place needs to burn.<br /> <br /> Let me try again.<br /> <br /> Back up on the 1st floor, Rose, Cupcake, and I ran into Molly again. She didn\u2019t remember us at first, but after we talked to her for a few moments, recalled having met upstairs. She warned us not to go to the bar as it was filled with ghosts. She continued, almost conspiratorially, that the hotel was dangerous at night. We convinced her we were here to try and help some of that and she calmed down a little. She apologized and mentioned a fog in her head so I offered my services as a doctor. She looked around for a moment, then opened the nearest unoccupied room and we all went inside. Rose stayed by the door so Molly wasn\u2019t alone, keeping the security concerns down. Even in the \u201860s, running off into a room alone with a man you just met wasn\u2019t always a wise idea. I checked her vitals, pupils, and reflexes. It was odd as she was as solid as any of the Krewe but stranger yet were the very real signs of hypertension and stress. I wasn\u2019t sure why, but for her age Molly was under a huge amount of stress. When I asked her about it, she was gently evasive, which was not unusual. She just said she had some problems at home. Rose suggested I bleed on her through the ear curl. I sliced my finger out of Molly\u2019s line of sight and dripped a few drops on her back. I wasn\u2019t prepared for what came next.<br /> <br /> Molly\u2019s eyes flew wide in obvious panic. She began screaming through the realization that she was dead. But before I could calm her down, she turned her head sharply as if she saw something we couldn\u2019t and with a look of sheer terror on her face, screamed \u201cLET GO!\u201d She was visibly pulled away from me and seemed to vanish into a scarlet silhouette before fading entirely. She was gone without a trace. But as I looked around the room I realized an important detail. The pull on The Dog of War weakened when I bled on Molly.<br /> <br /> I asked Nightshade through the ear curl if she could sense anyone or anything else looking around through her Boneyard. She couldn\u2019t find anything but suspected a similar possibility that the entity could sense the hotel. It might be a leap, but I think somehow the ghosts trapped here were empowering their jailer. When they are removed from its control, the entity grows weaker. Rose began to have the same thoughts as we moved to the pool. As soon as we crossed the line in the hall where renovations took place, the pull on our Geists disappeared. I realized just how much it annoyed me once the pull was gone. We declared the pool as a safe room and theorized that if we could lure some of the ghosts in, we might be able to temporarily free them from their prison. Then we moved on.<br /> <br /> The Laundry Room was clear so we moved next to the Music Room. It was empty of ghosts, but there was a piano and large windows streaming in moonlight. There was a stage for a small band to one side. It looked like something from Casablanca. This \u201840s style lounge was perfect for any number of movies or dates. I asked Nightshade to play something from the \u201840s after I had an idea. I almost immediately recognized Apple Blossom Time, even with the piano being a little out of tune. Nightshade always favors the Andrews Sisters anyway. Shortly after, Sondra came to the doorway and watched without trying to draw attention away. After a short reminder of our previous meeting, I coaxed the actress into conversation. Then I unlocked the Stigmata Marionette, binding her to me for a while. She seemed a little more alert, but didn\u2019t seem to notice a change. Through our small talk, I learned she was from Santa Monica, Troy sells booze hidden with his travelling sales supplies, and that he apparently has a hiding place in the hotel. For her, we were discussing bootlegging during Prohibition, so I felt like we were making progress. Eventually I steered the conversation toward her career, which Nightshade thankfully helped me with over the ear curl. I introduced Sondra to Nightshade and between us, we convinced her to sing along with the piano. Rose came in and watched for a bit, then cut her own hand so she could subtly bleed on Sondra. They shook hands after her song was finished. Much like Molly, Sondra panicked. She started trying to run, even with us offering to help her. We finally managed to make out, \u201cHe\u2019s coming!\u201d as she tore herself away from Rose. Moving quickly to catch up and try to protect her, I asked who? The name name screamed back over her shoulder, chilled us.<br /> <br /> \u201cTroy!\u201d<br /> <br /> I tried to lead Sondra to the pool but she pulled herself away again, desperate now to escape an unseen pursuer. Before I could get her to the hallway, she red phased and vanished. We gained much information in those next split seconds. Unfortunately I became part of the experiment. Seconds after Sondra vanished, I was flooded with pure anger. From my very core, I could feel the searing flames of rage engulfing the me. The walls of my inner restraint first smoldered, then I felt the conflagration of take hold. Deep wounds, forgotten or ignored, blistered to the surface of my senses.<br /> <br /> Glancing around as my fists tightened into iron, I spotted a target for my wrath. Bright Eyes wanted me to share Nightshade with her, when she was mine! But a flicker of movement from the piano pulled my attention. It was Nightshade that invited others into her bed, it was she that made me fall in love, it was HER that hurt me. And was her flight which flared my inner flames. Bright Eyes noticed something was wrong and shifted between me and the door while Rose tried to distract me. She claimed to know what it was like for me. She had no idea what my life was like. The first gouts of inner flames lashed out as I cut her off, letting her know she actually had no idea what it was like. But my flames also light up the darkness in my mind. I clamped down and bit back the hurtful words I was about to spew at the others. While I still had some control of myself, I roughly told Rose to stay away from me and that I was going to the pool. With that, I jumped up and ran for the designated safe room.<br /> <br /> This was less the sanctuary I was hoping for and more a comfortless dead end, as cold and silent as a tomb. I knew Nightshade ran as soon as she recognized my anger. The others seemed to sense it this time as well. But here I expected the flames to bank and die down once I cleared the hotel. Unfortunately, I was left with the sickening knowledge that I had terrorized Nightshade and caused my Krewe to question if they could trust me. Trembling with norepinephrine and fire in my veins, I forced myself down on the uncaring concrete and tried to meditate. Clarity came quickly, focus and control not so much. I was still struggling to find my center when Rose came in very quietly. My anger had slowly faded but was still a warm glow in the center of my chest when she approached. I guessed it had been about 15 minutes before she came to check on me. By that point, I was far more angry with myself than anyone else. That was an old familiar discomfort so I knew it was safe for me to speak with Rose. I knew she came to check on me, both to see if I was okay and to see if I was a danger to the others. I asked her how Nightshade was, dreading the answer. Rose can\u2019t lie any better than I can, so when she said Nightshade was shaken up but better since she went to lay down, I had to believe it. I asked her to apologize for me. I knew that Nightshade didn\u2019t need to see me for a while.<br /> <br /> After that, I tried to use my time for something other than feeling sorry for myself or stewing on old memories. What had happened to me before? It felt like my inner rage was awakened and amplified by something. I knew the something to be the entity, but not how. That it could just tap into my own negative traits and focus them through my perspective was very important information, if incredibly uncomfortable to think about. I still needed to cool off, but that\u2019s why we had the heavy bag in the House. I\u2019d need to figure something out here. Then I remembered when Cupcake and Rose were looking through the kitchen, they mentioned old storage bags. I headed over and found everyone except Nightshade. I asked Rose for several canvas storage bags then I went out back and filled them with dirt. There was an old clothes line in the Laundry Room which was all I needed. I set up a line of makeship speed bags at the back of the pool area.<br /> <br /> I was just about to try the gambit I made, when I suddenly felt the effects of whatever was making me angry vanish. It felt similar to how the pull weakened with Molly and Sondra. I ran out to find the Krewe. I didn\u2019t get far as everyone but Nightshade was at the end of the hallway already. They found a \u201820s version of Troy and Rose bled on him. Instead of panicking or breaking down, Troy reacted with anger and awareness. Apparently his fight reflex comes complete with ungentlemanly language as well. The red silhouette came for him, but he fought it off several times, even seeming to fight back before finally being dragged into the nothing. But before he let go, Troy manifested like a normal ghost and warned the others to get away. They said he seemed to know what was controlling him as if he had possibly broken free before. Either way, it was obvious that Troy was a powerful ghost. It was also suggested that Nightshade was in danger from Troy given his serial killings were linked to those who were actresses or stage performers. I went up to stay with Nightshade after that while the others went to call Becky on the land line phone.<br /> <br /> Nightshade was more calm than when I last saw her, but it didn\u2019t take long for me to recognize the signs of heroin use. I didn\u2019t react as I was just glad she didn\u2019t try to run away. Once I was sure she was okay with me being there, she fell into another Boneyard and I guarded over her. A little while later, Nightshade found Yvette and Molly arguing on the 3rd floor. We all heard as Nightshade called the play by play. Molly blamed Yvette for killing Albert, while Yvette claimed she found him dead already. The argument got more heated as Molly mentioned Yvette was holding a gun when she spotted her with Albert. Molly was backing up even as she pressed her assumed advantage. She stepped too far and lost her footing at the top of the stairs. Molly fought wildly to right herself as Yvette rushed forward, then coldly stopped reaching for her at the last second. At that point, I ran out of the room to try and get to them. I found Molly at the foot of the stairs with Rose leaning over her. Molly had tried to say something to Rose, but slipped away before she could get it out. So there was a \u201cdead\u201d ghost which Rose picked up and carried to the Pool Room. Surprisingly, it didn\u2019t disappear or anything else. Rose used her Oracle powers to learn what she could from the \u201ccorpse.\u201d As far as Molly knew, Yvette killed Albert because she broke into his room and Molly found her standing over the body with a gun. She was also so stressed, other than because of the ghosts, because her mother didn\u2019t want her to marry a gentile, which her boyfriend, Nathan Long, was. That would explain the problems at home. We knew Albert wasn\u2019t killed by gunshot, but due to acute untreated appendicitis, leading to perforation and eventually death. Our suspicions were that Albert was hiding from the mob and thus couldn\u2019t safely go for treatment. Rose bled on Molly inside the Pool Room and she awoke, though she was gruesome. The back of her skull was cracked open and her neck was twisted in a disturbing angle for someone that was still moving. She had another mild panic attack, but we calmed her more easily this time. She was still in pain from reexperiencing her death but she tried to give us more information. She remembered that James Gibson came to investigate Sondra\u2019s murder. We were unsure who that was, but it was noted. Molly was also certain that Yvette pushed her. Nightshade confirmed that, at least in the tableau she witnessed, that was not the case. The pain was growing for Molly so I used my healing powers on her. I\u2019d never tried to heal a ghost before, but since she was effectively made flesh, it seemed to make sense. There was certainly plenty of blood to utilize. I didn\u2019t want to burn myself out, but I managed to close the gaping wound on the back of her head and properly set her neck again. She was grateful as this alleviated a far amount of the pain she was enduring. Molly was very clear that she did not want to be a ghost and had issues with being trapped. We talked with her about Nightshade making it where she had to stay in this room so the entity could not reach her. She agreed so the ceremony was enacted.<br /> <br /> Based on what we learned, our blood snaps these ghosts out of whatever fugue state the entity inflicts on them. This alerts the entity, however, as it seems not to have omniscience within the hotel. Most of the ghosts aren\u2019t experienced with their condition, with the exception of Troy, who exhibits a ghostly variation of my Rage Manifestation. When we cut them off from the entity, they relive their death, usually in their own minds, before becoming aware of the present. Only Troy seems to hold any memories from after death not made since we arrived. Making myself an anchor with the Stigmata Marionette does not give me any ability to keep the ghost manifested if the entity tries to recall them. Cutting the ghosts off from the entity seems to weaken it, based on the reduced pull on our Geists from the basement. The new addition of the Pool Room is safe from the entity\u2019s control, but does not undo any effects already in place. And finally, the entity possesses some form of ability to unlock our dark passions. Seven hours in and that\u2019s what we know.<br /> <br /> Whatever this thing is, it\u2019s keeping an ever growing number of ghosts as slaves for an unknown morality play of some kind. Spectral slavery, forced interaction with the living, and fucking with my emotions are only some of the reasons I will see the end of this thing. Now I\u2019m not sure if we\u2019re sleeping in shifts or what.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Thursday, October 21, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> We spent the afternoon and evening continuing to explore the house. Alexia led us on a very organized survey of the entire place, floor by floor, using her Phantasmal Oracle to peer through any illusions we might encounter. There were none, however.<br /> <br /> We encountered Molly again. She warned us about ghosts again, and complained of disorientation and fogged recollections. Doc offered to examine her medically, and though she was hesitant, she agreed. He reported that she was exhibiting symptoms of severe stress, among other things. I quietly suggested that he bleed on her to make her more lucid, hoping that would grant us more insight into what\u2019s going on.<br /> <br /> When he flicked a few drops on her, she began screaming \u201cLet go!\u201d at the empty air, and then, with a horrified look on her face, she exclaimed \u201cNo! I\u2019m trapped here too!\u201d Then she seemed to be pulled away, leaving only a reddish silhouette that persisted for an instant before fading. However, when Molly became lucid, we all felt the pull on our geists weaken a bit.<br /> <br /> Doc suggested that the trapped ghosts strengthen whatever is keeping them here. When they are freed from its control, even briefly, it becomes weaker. If we can help to resolve and free the ghosts here, then perhaps we can draw out and destroy whatever is holding on to them. Troy seems to be a linchpin of sorts, and we discussed the very real possibility that he was the entity behind all of this, though our later experiences seemed to prove otherwise.<br /> <br /> We made is significant discovery when we entered the swimming pool room. It was a large, spacious chamber with large windows to let in plenty of sunlight. The pool itself was very old fashioned, and not large enough to swim regulation laps, but it seemed like it would be suitable for a bit of relaxation. Of course, it was empty now. More importantly, however, we all felt the pull on our geists disappear entirely when we entered the room. The pool is of much newer construction than the rest of the hotel, so it appears that the entity trapping all the ghosts is confined to the physical space of the original building. This is good news, as it means we have a safe haven to retreat to if necessary.<br /> <br /> I recommended that we try to bring a ghost into the room. If necessary, and if whatever is trapping the ghosts keeps pulling them away from us, we might use a ceremony to capture a ghost in a vessel long enough to get them there. Natalie volunteered to use the Spectral Captivity ritual to accomplish that, and we might also have a few other options.<br /> <br /> After the pool, we searched the laundry room and music room. There was little of interest in the laundry room. In the music room, however, Doc suggested that Natalie play something from the 40\u2019s on the piano (which was a bit out of tune, I gather). He was hoping to draw one or more of the ghosts out so that he could try binding them to himself as a new anchor. He reasoned that doing so might prevent whatever is trapping the ghosts from tearing them away from us, or at least give them a better chance of resisting the pull.<br /> <br /> Soon enough, Sandra came in search of the music. She was a bit tipsy, and said that she couldn\u2019t sleep. Doc quietly used Stigmata and became a new anchor for Sandra. Drawn to him, she struck up a conversation. It seems she\u2019s from Santa Monica, and the hotel is a getaway for actresses like her. It\u2019s quiet, and nearly as far from California as you can get and still be in America.<br /> <br /> We asked her about Troy, and she seemed charmed by him. She also told us that he would sometimes smuggle things about, using his job as a traveling salesman to do so without drawing much attention. Since she was alive during the Prohibition, she said he mostly smuggled alcohol, and suggested we talk to him if we needed any.<br /> <br /> Doc eventually got her to sing along with Natalie\u2019s music, a popular tune from the 20\u2019s, I think, and she was quite good. While she sang, Sara, Doc, Alexia and I agreed to see what would happen if we made her more lucid like we had done with Molly. So I cut my hand and intercepted her as she left Natalie and the piano. I smeared blood on her as I shook her hand to compliment on her singing, and then she became lucid.<br /> <br /> Like Molly, she immediately began to freak out. She started screaming about Troy; she was terribly frightened of him, and it seemed obvious that he must have been the axe murderer who killed her. At that point, we were even more convinced that Troy must be the entity keeping the other ghosts in the hotel. We tried to maneuver Sandra to the pool room, which was no easy task given her hysterics, but before we could reach it she turned into a red silhouette and was torn away like Molly. It didn\u2019t matter that she was anchored to Doc\u2014his bond to her was severed as soon as she disappeared.<br /> <br /> Then something odd happened. Doc became extraordinarily angry. He\u2019s prone to a temper anyway, but he usually keeps it in check. It frightens Natalie terribly. This time, however, we could all sense the fury simmering inside him, and he turned to look at Natalie with something approaching hatred. Sara and I both put ourselves between Doc and Natalie, but Natalie turned and fled, dashing out of the hotel. Doc stormed stiffly to the pool area to try and calm down.<br /> <br /> We all went out to check on Natalie. She was shaken but okay. She knows that whatever came over Doc had more to do with the hotel than with her, but she is terrified of Doc\u2019s temper. Sara and Alexia helped her go up to her room to lie down for a bit. I went to check on Doc.<br /> <br /> I found him meditating in the empty pool. He was still angry, but he was calmer. Unfortunately, the pool didn\u2019t help calm him like he hoped. Whatever got into his head set him off and that was enough; the rest was all Doc. The entity behind all of this must have some way to draw out our dark sides. It\u2019s a frightening thought; I can only imagine the dark, depressing places my own mind might go if the hotel turns its influence on me. I tried to encourage Doc, but I wasn\u2019t really helping, so I left him to find his center on his own.<br /> <br /> Alexia, Lily and I continued to explore the hotel while Sara sat with Natalie. We didn\u2019t find much in the kitchen aside from a few empty bottles we can use for the Spectral Captivity ritual should we need it. Doc briefly came in looking for large, empty flour sacks or other things he could use to make a punching bag, and once he had what he needed, he left again. Hopefully the makeshift punching bag will help him work out the rest of his anger.<br /> <br /> Lastly, we went into the bar, and found it positively full of ghosts. There was a 40\u2019s-era bartender, 20\u2019s-era Troy Donovan, Wynona Watts, Thomas Wyndham, and Marvin Tommelson. Alexia can be a bit odd at times, and lately she doesn\u2019t seem to care much what ghosts think of her activities, though I suppose the same is true of her attitude toward living people as well. She began rummaging around in the bar while the bartender looked on, a bit put off until he asked her what she thought she was doing. Meanwhile, I struck up a conversation with Thomas Wyndham. He was a very handsome, charming fellow. We talked a bit about the war, and he was of the opinion that Hitler was not the real threat. Our so-called ally Stalin was the truly dangerous one. We chatted a bit about it, and I told him that if Stalin kept supporting the Chinese like he was, things would go poorly in the long run. Eventually I turned the conversation to Thomas himself and asked what he did for a living. He was a bit evasive, but eventually admitted that he worked for the IRS, though he was at the hotel on vacation.<br /> <br /> Sara came down to join us about then, and struck up a conversation with the bartender, Bertrand Stanley. He told her that he had been there forever. She asked about Wynona, and he said she had become fascinated by the hotel after learning about Sandra\u2019s murder, and ended up spending a lot of time there, mostly in her room. She had been spending more and more time there during the late 30\u2019s and early 40\u2019s because she was on the out in Hollywood.<br /> <br /> He did tell Sara something curious, as though he knew more than he really should. He told her that some of the people at the hotel really needed help. \u201cHeaven rewards good deeds,\u201d he said. Perhaps he knows more about what\u2019s going at the hotel, but if so, how and why?<br /> <br /> Alexia and Sara also struck up another conversation with Troy, who was charming as always. They decided to test him a bit, and the conversation turned to talk of the basement. He didn\u2019t seem to know much about anything down there, but agreed to go with them to check it out. He was apparently surprised to find it caved in, and did not seem comfortable with the elevator. He did not behave strangely in the basement, and that was our first sign that he might not be the entity behind this haunting.<br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Lily</u><br /> <br /> Sara asked Lily if she felt the same pull our geists did. Whatever is keeping the ghosts here seems to affect only the spirits of the dead, not spirits like Lily. I\u2019m glad; I wouldn\u2019t want my little girl to be here if something was threatening her like that.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Trauma </u><br /> <br /> Natalie is terrified of Doc\u2019s temper. I\u2019m not really sure why. As far as I know, he\u2019s never done anything to hurt her, even when he\u2019s angry. I can only assume that there is some history of abuse in her past. I don\u2019t think her father was abusive, but I know she\u2019s been raped before, so I suspect some boyfriend or other person in her past traumatized her. It\u2019s probably a good thing she doesn\u2019t talk about it, because if she did, Doc, Sara and I might hunt the bastard down and end him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Troy Donovan</u><br /> <br /> Troy may not be the entity responsible for the hotel haunting, but we are fairly certain he is the axe murderer. It seems clear that he killed Sandra, at least. He was at the hotel enough to have been involved in the other murders there, and if he was a serial killer, he might have killed others along his sales route. Sara called Becky and had her look into that for us. Becky was also able to clear up a few other things.<br /> <br /> For one, Thomas might have been investigating Troy for some sort of smuggling, which would explain why Troy tried to kill him even though he doesn\u2019t quite fit the profile of Troy\u2019s other two victims (Sandra and Wynona)<br /> <br /> Bertrand Stanley worked as the hotel\u2019s bartender for decades, from the time he was a young man until he died there in the 1970\u2019s when he was over 90 years old. If he is haunting the place, he may be a benevolent presence. It\u2019s hard to think he would have devoted his life to the Hidden Hillside Hotel and not feel some sort of responsibility toward it in death.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session XCIX</i><br /> <br /> <br /> As discussed previously, the ghosts seem real and solid. There has been no spectral activity. Nothing from Natalie as she cannot tweet from there.<br /> <br /> Next time is session 100, which also takes place within the hotel. It\u2019s been a fun ride. Hope you keep going along with us. Take care now. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphi