lways Baron, I'm immensely looking forward to the next post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-05T17:15:22-08:00","id":66093,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. This has been fun to run so far.<br /> <br /> Session 100 in a few days!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T17:06:37-08:00","id":67485,"title":"","content":"This may be the longest forum I ve ever seen and also a really cool plot but still pretty long","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T02:34:09-08:00","id":68921,"title":"","content":"It has been going awhile. How many readers have followed us 100 sessions I wonder? We began in the winter of '10 (when the game was set in the<i> future</i> by a few months!) and it has been a strange trip. Glad you are enjoying it though.<br /> <br /> Session 100! It is time to see what the Krewe has uncovered at the Haunted Hotel.<br /> <br /> <i>Session C</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1445 Hours, Friday, October 22, 2010<br /> <br /> We decided not to leave any one of us less rested than the others and simply slept in our rooms. I suspect Bright Eyes and Nightshade stayed together all night, but after Nightshade\u2019s trauma from yesterday, that is not unusual. What I did find unusual was that I was actually relaxed. I knew it wasn\u2019t anything about the sleep, the hotel beds aren\u2019t that special. But it was almost like I had a plan for how things needed to be. This was further backed up by the fact it was very easy to get centered this morning. Meditation took about half an hour, though I did go to the pool for security.<br /> <br /> When I came back into the kitchen, Cupcake was raving worse than usual with the Cracked Cook. She was having some kind of argument about eating herself into a stupor. I asked what was wrong, since she had to have woken up the others with the screaming. She launched into a fit about The Shining before getting a hold of herself. Something had provoked an idea with the Cracked Cook and he wasn\u2019t willing to let it go, though it seemed to me like he was trying to look out for her in his own demented way. The Dog of War was more relaxed this morning than yesterday as well. I usually have to get into a fight for him to get that calm.<br /> <br /> <b>Mysteries of Death are not always about violence Sadeeuk, but there will always be conflict.</b><br /> <br /> That isn\u2019t at all ominous. Anyway, Cupcake made bacon biscuits for breakfast but Bright Eyes and Nightshade didn\u2019t come down throughout all of the meal. Eventually I got nervous and went to check on them. Nightshade called back from behind the door that everything was fine. They both came down together a few minutes later. Nightshade looked a little flustered but Bright Eyes looked down right hungry, and I don\u2019t think her meal was on the table. While it\u2019s not at all a problem for beautiful woman to pay attention to me, it was weird that Bright Eyes was so openly flirty. Once the Krewe was assembled, we made plans to check out the maze and below the basement if possible. Rose wanted to just splinter into a pile of spiders and look for a way down, but we have so little information and no way to get to her if things went bad, that was just too risky. I wasn\u2019t the only one to think so for once either. While the others got ready, I went to the third floor balcony and sketched the maze. It wasn\u2019t very involved but neither was the maze honestly.<br /> <br /> When I came back down, Bright Eyes suggested we split into groups to solve the maze and investigate anything we could. Even Rose could tell that wasn\u2019t why Bright Eyes wanted to be alone with Nightshade. It was weird given she is normally so considerate about things like that. Cupcake was trying to ignore the obvious when she mentioned that she had string to use like Theseus in the Labyrinth. With Bright Eyes attached to Nightshade, it was obvious they would be a group. Rose and Cupcake decided to move together for safety but also for their strength in investigation. That left me to travel with Lily. Rose strapped one half of a pair of cloth sheers to Lily\u2019s right hand before putting her on top of my pack. She shifted around until she was straddling my pack with her back against my neck. It was informed that she was now watching my back. She could slip down into my pack of those that wouldn\u2019t understand came out, but still have freedom to move and help. Now my best day of picking teams, but for what I was doing, I could have done worse.<br /> <br /> Lily and I started off based on my sketch of the maze and were making pretty good time when a little girl that might have been ten stumbled out of the hedge. She was wearing a ridiculously short skirt, even by today\u2019s standards, and was sloppy drunk. I knew this had to be Daisy and she quickly confirmed things as her introduction was also a pick up attempt. I offered her my coat since she was showing so much skin it made me cold (and a little sick). I suggested we go to the pool in an attempt to play along. She didn\u2019t know about a pool, having died in the \u201820s, but she was willing to keep walking...well stumbling with me. The pull in the maze and right out of it was no different than inside so I knew the pool was my only shot. Lily was confused as to why I was acting interested in what was blatantly a helpless little girl. I could feel the grip of her sheers pressing into the back of my neck, I guess to get my attention. I tried to mumble over my shoulder for her to trust me a few times, but that didn\u2019t work very well. The churning in my stomach from what I was doing wasn\u2019t getting any easier to deal with either, so I can\u2019t really blame her. I scooped Daisy up and carried her since she was almost falling every few steps from all the cheap booze she\u2019d had. Things got very difficult when we got to the pool. Daisy panicked when she saw it, given that it should exist for her. I reached back and had Lily cut me so I could bleed on the ghost, but that didn\u2019t go as I\u2019d hoped. Daisy got very quiet as she relived everything from life in her mind, then called me a pervert and fought to get free. She wanted nothing to do with the pool. My gag reflex was tightening so I set Daisy down. I couldn\u2019t bring myself to force a ten year old to go somewhere with a stranger that she thought was going to molest her. She bolted as soon as her feet were down. I called after her but she red phased as soon as she hit the edge of the woods. I gave a brief recap to the others through the ear curl as I continued to the woods. There I took out the curl and puked in the trees. I don\u2019t care if it would have been for her own good, that little girl had experienced things that no child should ever know. I couldn\u2019t be a part of that even for a moment. Once I was able to stand again, I explained things to Lily. She was happy to know that I was still the person she thought I was, but then she was sad that Daisy had to live like that. For once, we were in complete agreement.<br /> <br /> Once the queasy feeling in the pit of my stomach was settled and Lily didn\u2019t want to stab me anymore, I put the ear curl back in. Rose and Cupcake were talking to someone but I couldn\u2019t figure out who. Bright Eyes came over the curl to let me know it was Troy, since I missed the start of the conversation. She seemed more focused now so hopefully we won\u2019t have any more uncomfortable issues. They were leading Troy from the maze back to the pool. Once I was a little more aware of what was happening, I realized Troy felt something strange with the pool. They convinced him to come inside just before Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and I got to the pool entrance. The ghost was immediately alerted to something being different, even though I could tell this was \u201840s Troy. Probably felt the changes from Nightshade\u2019s trapping ritual, but also seeing Molly there could have done it. For her part, Molly moved to me almost immediately as Troy tried to talk to her. She was obviously afraid, as if she\u2019d seen a ghost. Rose bled on Troy to bring him back to us, as it were. There wasn\u2019t the same change for him as with the others. But when we tried to ask him questions, he became evasive and suspicious. I thought I could see what was happening, so I sent Molly to go talk with Rose in the other corner of the pool area. Then I took Troy to the side and explained that I knew. I was a little worried that he might become violent, but instead he admitted to me what he\u2019d done. More importantly however, he told me how it happened. Much like my sense of rage drove me to get away from my Krewe, the entity had incited Troy after some slight by Sondra and later Wynona. He explained about how he hated it but after they were dead, it was like all his cares were lifted. He relaxed and was happy with his life (outside of being a murderer). Troy had even tried to stay away from the Hidden Hillside after Sondra was killed, but he said it was just completely natural for him to come back. He had attacked Wyndham in the maze after Thomas witnessed his murder of Wynona. However he had no idea why Wyndham accused Marvin Tomilson, as everyone knew he was innocent. There was a very real sense of remorse from Troy, for committing the murders, attacking Wyndham, and for Tomilson\u2019s unjust execution. There was no attempt to explain why these things had to happen, no rationalizing, nothing that suggested the type of personality that could take another life on purpose. We moved back to the others and Troy agreed to be bound in the pool room.<br /> <br /> After giving Molly some reassurances, Cupcake and I went to get some tables, chairs, cards, and really anything else we could to help make for a more comfortable prison. While we were away from the pool, Nightshade shared her suspicion that Sondra was lesbian. At first I was confused as to why that would matter until Nightshade pointed out Sondra was more likely to follow her back to the pool. I realized there is a certain trust among compatriots of which Nightshade was looking to take advantage. That same trust could probably exist between Marvin Tomilson and myself given our backgrounds. Given that idea, we decided to split up again, as we tended to meet ghosts in smaller groups. Cupcake announced that she had found a typed letter in the bar, since she could finally go through it properly. It was from Bertrand according to her Oracle vision. The letter was written after she left the bar last night. It had only a single line.<br /> <br /> They need your help.<br /> <br /> We don\u2019t know what\u2019s special about the bartender, but he definitely knows something. Nightshade, Rose, and Lily went to look for Sondra while Cupcake and Bright Eyes came with me to search for Tomilson. Before we could get to his room, Rose began a characteristically awkward conversation with what turned out to be Yvette. Nightshade stepped in to make things less uncomfortable and they convinced Yvette to follow them in search of Molly the maid. We managed to all get back to the pool within a few moments of each other, and Yvette became incredibly suspicious as soon as she came in. Yvette panicked and drew her pistol. Rose locked down her arms, while Troy snatched the gun away. Nightshade was feeling a bit prickly as she put her own pistol to Yvette\u2019s head. Probably unnecessary but it immediately took the fight out of her. It was more fear than anything else from them on. That was amplified when Molly saw who we brought back. She flipped out, pointed like a Hangin\u2019 Judge from the movies, and shouted about her killer. Molly got so worked up that I had to catch her before she attacked Yvette. Eventually I talked her down while Troy positioned himself directly between the two women. Bright Eyes stepped up for her turn to donate. When blood was applied, Yvette calmed into a notably depressed state and listened without struggle. She seemed to accept this fate and agreed to be bound to weaken the entity. When Rose let go, Yvette collapsed and sobbed her wish to end it all....again. Before anyone else could offer comfort or even a pat on the shoulder, Troy moved to stand in front of her. Looking down with an expression of pained truth, he pointed out to Yvette that they both had debits to pay before things could be set right. She could only nod and sniffle.<br /> <br /> Now if we can keep Molly and Yvette from killing each other again, I think our plan might work. Each time we bind a ghost to the pool, the pull in the rest of the hotel fades. But we still have at least six ghosts, and that\u2019s assuming no others show up. We also still don\u2019t know what to make of the bartender. But after this, I think most of us could use a drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, October 22, 2010, Noon<br /> <br /> It took be awhile to meditate this morning, in part because Alexia was making quite a fuss arguing with the cracked cook about the movie The Shining. When I finally made it down to breakfast, I found that Doc and Lily were already there, but not Natalie or Sara, and eventually Doc had to go up to fetch them. Sara was acting peculiar. She had a sultry, wanton look in her eyes and was practically clinging to Natalie all morning. She\u2019s normally a bit more discrete about these things.<br /> <br /> Over breakfast, we discussed what steps we should take in the hotel. It might be possible for me to perform a more thorough investigation of the ruined basement by turning into a swarm of spiders, but the others were worried about me being alone down there. So our main plan at this point is to get as many of the ghosts as possible into the pool area so that they would be free of the entity\u2019s influence. Then, hopefully we can draw out the entity and destroy it. To that end, we needed to search the hedge maze behind the hotel, as some of the ghosts occasionally appear there and it is where Thomas was attacked. So we split up to do just that. Natalie and Sara headed off together while Alexia and I accompanied one another. Doc took Lily. I disassembled a large pair of sewing shears and gave her the blades so that she would have a weapon of sorts of use if necessary, and we taped one of them to her right hand. She looked very brave riding on Doc\u2019s backpack. I don\u2019t think Doc was happy to be baby-sitting Lily, but he handled it with good grace.<br /> <br /> Doc and Lily were the first to encounter something. They found Daisy\u2019s ghost wandering the maze, drunk. Daisy was a young girl, no more than ten or eleven, who sold her body to make ends meet in the early days of the hotel. Doc tried to lead Daisy into the pool area by pretending to be interested in her services\u2026and it made us all very uncomfortable, most of all Doc. According to Doc, Lily disapproved very strongly and nearly stabbed him because she didn\u2019t understand that he was simply trying to get Daisy to safety.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Daisy didn\u2019t remember the pool; it was built after her time, so she thought Doc was trying to take her somewhere she didn\u2019t know. It spooked her, and she started to panic. It didn\u2019t help when Doc asked Lily to cut him so that he could bleed on Daisy. When he did that, she became very quiet as though remembering all the horrors of her life and suicide, and then she fled as fast as she could. I almost transformed into a flock of bird to follow her, but Doc reported that she disappeared when she hit the edge of the yard, leaving only a momentary red silhouette like the other ghosts.<br /> <br /> Not long after that, Alexia and I encountered 40\u2019s-era Troy. He offered to walk with us, and we cautiously guided him back toward the hotel. While we were still in the maze, though, he stopped as though something <br /> were bothering him. He said he had a chill, so we looked around and could sense the deathly residue in that spot. Someone had been killed there, probably in the 20\u2019s, though I don\u2019t know who. Was Sandra killed in the hedge maze?<br /> <br /> Troy was a perfect gentleman, though, and as we approached the outdoor entrance to the pool, he got a bad feeling about something and told us to wait while he checked it out. He seemed honestly concerned for our well-being. Despite his misgivings, however, we got him into the pool, and then he realized that something was off. He became very defensive, ready to lash out at us if necessary, but I approached him as calmly and gently as I could and took his hand after leaving a little blood on mine. He calmed down as he realized that he was safe there in the pool. All the while, Molly looked on anxiously.<br /> <br /> Doc, Natalie and Sara soon joined us. Once Troy realized he was safe, he was more talkative. He didn\u2019t know what was going on in the hotel, but he knew that something there was trying to control him and the other ghosts. As far as he knew, it was the hotel itself. The entity seems to be fed by people dying there, but Troy didn\u2019t know why people who didn\u2019t die there, like Yvette, were also trapped.<br /> <br /> Troy asked to speak to Doc privately out of earshot of the ladies, but thanks to the ear curls, we could all listen in. He confessed to Doc that when he was alive, he had killed Sandra and Wynona, but he didn\u2019t know why. Something bad would happen, or they would do something he didn\u2019t like, such as turning down his earnest advances, and then something in his head would take over. Anger blinded him and he killed them. Afterward, he felt relieved; all of his anger and tension and frustration just melted away. He tried to stay away form the hotel but always ended up coming back like it was the most natural thing in the world. He seemed to feel sincere remorse over what he had done. After what happened to Doc yesterday, it\u2019s easy to believe that Troy would not have become a murderer if the hotel weren\u2019t fanning the flames of his wrath. Troy seems to be unique among the ghosts because he fought against the entity\u2019s influence even while he was alive and was at least somewhat aware of it power. Perhaps that\u2019s why he is so strong against it now.<br /> <br /> Then the entity started to pull at Troy even though he was in the pool. It must have a strong influence on him. Troy started to flicker a bit, but fought against the pull long enough for Doc to bind him with Stigmata. Then Natalie performed her ceremony to seal him into the room. The ceremony severed the entity\u2019s pull, so Troy is safe for now.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Sara tried to encourage and comfort Molly, who is still scared out of her wits. The rest of us went to get a few things for the ghosts to entertain themselves. A card table, cards, some books and magazines and other things. I filled the pool and got it ready for swimmers.<br /> <br /> Our next step is to split up and try to draw out the ghosts, as they seem to appear more easily when we are in smaller groups.<br /> <br /> <br /> Friday, October 22, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> Alexia decided to go back to the bar after we had things arranged in the pool. She did not get much of a chance to search behind the bar last night because the bartender, Bertrand, ran her off. This time, however, she found a typewritten note that simply said, \u201cThey need your help.\u201d I recalled seeing an old typewriter in one of the offices yesterday, and Alexia activated her Oracle in order to read the note\u2019s past. She discovered that Bertrand had typed it last night after meeting us.<br /> <br /> Whatever he is, he knows more than the other ghosts. But is he a guardian spirit or a trap?<br /> <br /> We split up to wander the hotel in search of more ghosts. Doc, Sara and Alexia split off into one group. Natalie felt that she could probably get Sandra to follow her to the pool, as she believes Sandra is attracted to women and felt that would help her gain Sandra\u2019s trust. I accompanied her along with Lily. If we encounter Sandra, I can excuse myself and then become invisible in order to keep an eye on Natalie without making Sandra feel uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> We ran into Yvette, not Sandra, though. She was a bit anxious to run into us again, but Natalie soon put her at ease. Yvette said she was looking for Molly, so I kindly offered to help her find the maid. I suggested that I had a complaint about my room, and needed to speak to Molly anyway.<br /> <br /> Natalie and I led her into the pool. As soon as she saw Molly there, she knew something was wrong. She opened her eyes wide and drew her pistol. I was on her in an instant, immobilizing her arms while Troy took her gun. Natalie put her own pistol to Yvette\u2019s head, which was a bit excessive but got the point across. Faced with her \u201ckiller,\u201d Molly screamed incoherently and tried to attack Yvette, but Doc held her back and eventually calmed her down.<br /> <br /> Sara bled on Yvette to grant her clarity, and then we explained the situation. Both Molly and Yvette seemed to accept that if we could keep them there in the pool long enough, we could defeat the force that has bound them to the hotel so that they could pass on. Yvette collapsed to the floor when I released her and moaned that she wanted to die and end it all again. She apparently feels a lot of remorse over the things she did.<br /> <br /> Troy stepped in at that point and told Yvette that they both have debts to pay, and they will only feel better once that\u2019s done. Yvette seemed to accept that bitter truth.<br /> <br /> So now we have three ghosts. Now we just have to collect the rest. We should be fine as long Yvette and Molly don\u2019t attack each other, and I don\u2019t think that\u2019s going to happen. Not with Troy in there, anyway.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Hats</u><br /> <br /> The Drowned Bride has decided that Karl would look good in a hat, something with more class than the flat cap he often wears. I discussed it with Natalie a bit while we split off to search the hotel. I\u2019m not sure if a fedora is right for him, and certainly not a trilby. Natalie says that trilbies are fashionable among arrogant hipsters, whatever that means, and that Karl doesn\u2019t want to make that sort of impression. I don\u2019t think there\u2019s much threat of that. I get the feeling that these hipsters tend to be rather dapper sorts, and as much as I love Karl, he\u2019s a bit rough around the edges to be considered dapper.<br /> <br /> Still, perhaps a bowler?<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Troy\u2019s Guilt </u><br /> <br /> Troy did kill Sandra and Wynona, and he tried to kill Thomas Wyndham. But he was extremely upset that Marvin Tommelson took the fall for the murders. Thomas accused Marvin, and Troy didn\u2019t understand why since he thought Thomas had seen him when he attacked. Maybe Thomas made a mistake. Maybe not. Next time we run into Thomas, we should find out. In any event, Troy was very upset that an innocent man took the fall for his crimes, though obviously not upset enough to step forward and confess his crimes before the man was executed. Or perhaps he was away and did not find out about the conviction until afterward.<br /> <br /> Troy claims that he did not kill Albert Finnigan or Daisy, and I believe him.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Our Darker Selves</u><br /> <br /> The hotel entity seems to be able to draw out a person\u2019s darker self, causing our inner demons to take over. That\u2019s what happened with Doc\u2019s rage yesterday, and I suspect something along those lines might have been happening this morning with Sara and Natalie. It\u2019s how the hotel got Troy to commit murder.<br /> <br /> Our geists are quite aware of this possibility as well, and I caught Alexia arguing with the Cracked Cook about her own vice. He\u2019s worried she will give in to her gluttony while we\u2019re here and stuff her face until she\u2019s sick. But I know Alexia is very careful about how much she eats. She\u2019s very sensitive about her love of food, which is one reason the Underworld makes her so anxious. I do feel a bit guilty, though, because it was the Drowned Bride who put the idea into the Cracked Cook\u2019s head in the first place when she realized how the hotel was affecting some of us\u2026<br /> <i><br /> End Session C</i><br /> <br /> Several notes here<br /> <br /> First, was a good session 100.<br /> <br /> Second, being session 100, the first hour was spent with the PC\u2019s Geists RPing a conversation through the channel. Everyone described and played their Geist, which was quite exciting. That\u2019s where the whole \u201chat\u201d note in Jasmine\u2019s journal came from.<br /> <br /> Third, Sara\u2019s behavior was due to the Entity empowering her vice, much like Doc\u2019s was the previous session.<br /> <br /> I will also note there was some confusion regarding Yvette\u2019s behavior. She drew her firearm when she saw Molly, with clear intent to fire. Jasmine wrestled the gun away, Troy interposed himself, and Natalie put a pistol to her head, which made her calm down.<br /> <br /> The Krewe is putting together the mystery of the hotel. Next session they add 2 more ghosts to their little \u201cfamily\u201d, discover a powerful Memento, and have an unexpected visitor arrive at the hotel. Come back in two weeks for the continuation of the story. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T22:54:04-08:00","id":69646,"title":"","content":"Quite enjoyable. I like the role-playing their geists. As for Karls' hat. What about a greek fisherman's hat?<br /> <br /> Does lily not understand the concept of lying? Also, Are you guys updating to GM?<br /> <br /> Herr Baron, I am an attempting film major. So I am officially calling dibs on turning this portion with the hotel into a film at some point. The dibs has been stamped and notarized.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T01:35:26-08:00","id":69695,"title":"","content":"Heh, probably not a bad plan.<br /> <br /> Lily being a Spirit, and does not &quot;get&quot; things all the time. She sort of does, the femininity/fertility spirit side is a human spirit so it has some basic familiarity, but misses nuances. She also thinks in terms of reproduction, romance, and femininity, so she misread Doc. She DOES understand lying, but not reliably. She was sufficiantly unsure what was going on to not actually hurt Doc, but was confused and put off.<br /> <br /> We have adopted some of GMC. We are using the combat system and virtues/vices. Jasmine's vice is now melancholy, for example, while Doc's is still Wrath. Sara still has Lust, Simon Greed and Alexis Gluttony, but Natalie's is now Attention-Grabbing. The Beats system had a very lukewarm response, certain players strongly dislike it, others are neutral. So not using it.<br /> <br /> Sure go ahead as far as film. ^_^. The players seem quite into the story, so it seems to be going well. I generally put this up for Geist game inspiration but hey, inspiration is inspiration, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-11-2014, 05:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-11T02:35:30-08:00","id":69715,"title":"","content":"Indeed Herr Baron <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T00:34:09-08:00","id":75469,"title":"","content":"Doc's experiences were in my head when I watched Donnie Darko for the first time last week. &quot;Is Sparkle Motion making anyone else uncomfortable? Oh good it not just me.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-20T02:12:03-08:00","id":75485,"title":"","content":"LOL noted. I will pass it on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-23T14:34:15-08:00","id":77829,"title":"","content":"The hotel saga continues. More ghosts recruited, more drama to deal with. It\u2019s session 101, holy crap!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1715 Hours, Friday, October 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Things just get better and better around here. It\u2019s more like Dark Shadows here than back at Dark Haven Bluffs. I really hate that Snowflake isn\u2019t here. He could get some great context from this place.<br /> <br /> Once we got Yvette settled in, the Krewe gathered to determine our next move. Before we could get very far, Troy told us he knew of something that might help us against the hotel. He said there was a shed on the other side of the hedge maze. Buried under that shed was the axe he used to kill Sondra and Wynona. This brought our conversation back to who died in the maze. James \u201cJimbo\u201d Gibson vanished investigating Sondra\u2019s murder, but Troy swore he was in Indiana at the time. Gibson was either FBI or a Marshal so it seems odd that no one else would come looking for him. But then we don\u2019t know how the bartender got here either. Daisy came up next and Rose mentioned maybe trying to be a matronly figure to try and draw her in. Troy said that was a very bad idea. Apparently Daisy does not like women. The way Troy described it, I suspect she was either abandoned or abused by her mother or a mother figure. Given her age at death, this made the depravities Daisy endured all the more disgusting. I can only hope the people that did this to her have all found a particularly violent Dark Dominion to spend eternity. If not, I may have to track them down and help them move.<br /> <br /> We followed Troy\u2019s directions to the shed and there it was. Wiping the dirt away, I lifted what I knew to be a very powerful piece of Memorabilia out of the ground. The bloodstained fire axe, Troy Donovan\u2019s Axe, was a Passion Charm, but also made chopping wood or targets much easier. The nightmares it guaranteed were more than a fair price to pay, though there was more to this glorious blade than that. If Troy was enraged at any target that had not died while wielding his axe, the damage would be devastating. It\u2019s also telling that other Sin-Eaters would see this as some awesome bling, while normal mortals would be creeped out being anywhere around it. Either way, I want it. Rose locked the axe in the shed next to a mattock and other normal maintenance tools before we headed back.<br /> <br /> When we got to the pool, Troy was leaning in the doorway waiting for us. He said there had been an incident after we left. Apparently Molly attacked Yvette and couldn\u2019t be trusted not to try again, so he tied her to a chair with the pool divider rope. Once we had been informed, Troy stepped aside and allowed us to see into the pool area. Molly was still screaming at Yvette but she was certainly not going anywhere. There was no other signs of struggle so I was mostly fine with this. Rose tried to calm Molly while Cupcake suggested she make cookies. Troy was very supportive of the idea. I spent a few minutes making sure we had enough supplies for the ghosts in the pool and then generally talked with Troy. Then we heard some kind of feral roar out in the hotel proper. Cupcake was calling for me from the kitchen as she was terrified. Rose and I bolted out to find an incredibly angry Mr. Ox immobilized in the lobby. Whatever the entity is, it\u2019s more powerful than we thought. Mr. Ox could not move at all other than to speak. Rose picked him up as he was no heavier than he looked and carried him outside. There the pull was lessened at least to the point he could walk, though he described it as though moving through thick mud. He also addressed me by my real name. That was mildly disturbing. Then he assumed a more true form. The eight foot tall black furred ox man stood with fire for eyes and horns that could gore several men each. There was something that told me there was more to his appearance but that same sensation led me to not to look. Madness lies beyond the illusion of our world. Cupcake immediately turned and mumbled about cookies as she nearly fled the area. Mr. Ox expected Rose to be at her pool and intended to give her another story. As things did not work out that way, Rose gave him her number to more easily contact her. In return, Mr. Ox pulled a doll\u2019s head from the folds of his robes. He handed it to Rose with the instruction to pull the doll\u2019s hair when we met the entity. It would scream immobilizing anything not us for a minute. This would affect incorporeal beings as well. Mr. Ox said that one was on the house, then mumbled something in Mandarin about how he owed it one. Rose and I thanked him before he disappeared. We shared a look before heading back to the pool.<br /> <br /> Once we explained what happened to the others, Cupcake, Bright Eyes and I went looking for Tomilson. Troy said he was staying on the second floor, so we headed up. We got to the entrance of the wing when we heard someone fumbling with a door. Turning the corner, we found an incredibly drunk Wynona Watts. Her key (no longer keyed to her door) couldn\u2019t open her room and she was very confused. She stumbled when she tried to stand upright and I moved to catch her. She thanked me then shifted her weight so she was leaning on me. When she asked if I could help steady her I thought Bright Eyes was going to laugh. We helped her downstairs so she could talk to the people at the front desk. When we could find no one at the desk, I suggested we try down the north wing (pool) as we thought we\u2019d seen Molly down that way. By that point Wynona was hanging on me, completely on her own. Once we were in the pool area, Bright Eyes bled on her from behind just as she was realizing something wasn\u2019t right. Then the screaming started as the memories flooded back into her mind. Then after just a moment, she became very calm and actually fairly blas\u00e9 about being dead. A few moments of conversation after that and it because clue she also had no clue about how to be social. Troy pulled me to the side and said that the problem with her was that \u201cthe miner didn\u2019t wanna go to work\u201d and she laughed at him. I nodded because, really what else is polite when a ghost explains why he murdered someone over sexual dysfunction? Though I could easily see how Wynona was wholly unable to communicate normally. It was similar to Gretchen with less disturbing outbursts. But in this case, I thought I could help by giving Wynona some context. I took her to a table and we talked about how she could try to relate to others without constantly upsetting them. I learned very quickly that Wynona was born rich and died rich, so she never really had to consider others. As a result, she was very bad at it. She also talked about how bad of a Catholic she was, as obviously her mother hadn\u2019t been to able to pay her way into heaven.<br /> <br /> I left Wynona to marvel at her new reality while trying to keep others from listening to her. Molly and Troy were both at least mildly offended by the actress before I spoke with her. I moved to Molly and asked what her favorite flowers were. I needed something for her to focus on because her constant fear. Once she told me, I drew her a vase full of daffodils which did get me a smile. Once we got Wynona bound and safe, Nightshade, Rose, and Cupcake went back out to drag the net. When they came back, Nightshade was leading Sondra Taylor. As soon as they were safely into the pool area, Nightshade pulled Sondra into a deep kiss. Wynona\u2019s eyes and smile both doubled in size before Sondra completely flipped out. My guess is that Nightshade had blood in her mouth. Troy was trying to remain as out of the way as possible but even he was not expecting the kiss. His presence was not lost on Sondra however and it took several minutes of calming words, gentle hugs, and explanations before she seemed unlikely to go hysterical again. Nightshade then almost seemed to shut down after that. I knew something was up when she pulled Sondra into the kiss without warning, so I had my suspicions the entity had struck again.<br /> Wynona tried to speak with Sondra as the elder actress was something of an inspiration, but this went less well than Wynona expected. Instead she just dove into the pool, fully clothed, and relaxed.<br /> <br /> I called a Krewe meeting in the corner as I had a few ideas. I wanted everything to be more careful when we go out of the pool. We needed to be aware that the entity may appear soon as we have several of its ghosts. That is not a situation we need to be in unprepared. The other option is that we may run out of ghosts and still not find the entity. If that happens, we\u2019ll have to go looking for it and that could be even more dangerous. The others seemed to understand and appreciate the weight of my concerns, which was good. I don\u2019t need something to be angry about later. Rose went out to the shed and brought the Axe and a few mattocks in to hide behind the front desk. That way they are centrally located and we can hopefully get them and Troy together quickly. After that, Nightshade and Rose suggested we try to nap. We may not going to get much more sleep here until this is over so everyone agreed. I was in no place I could actually sleep being so early, but I did meditate in my room. Surprisingly, I was centered in only a half hour. I felt more in control than I had been and that was the kind of reassurance I needed.<br /> <br /> We met back at the pool after a couple hours and Wynona nearly ambushed Nightshade. She was very gleefully asking something while Sondra hid her face in embarrassment. I\u2019m not sure what that\u2019s about, but the younger actress scurried over to me grinning after that. I can\u2019t complain about her flirting, but she is just a half step out of sync with any of the social norms I know. She is very interested in her current state however. I\u2019m not really sure that she wouldn\u2019t be happy to remain a ghost for as long as possible. Troy gave us a status report which was mostly okay, though Yvette was depressed, Molly was still seething, and Wynona continually asked horribly insensitive questions. Nothing new here. Nightshade decided to explain an option to Troy of how we could take him into battle with the entity. She wanted to bottle him and take him with us. Then we could just smash the bottle when the entity appeared or we found it and have instant Troy. He agreed so they got to work on the ritual. Why that was happening, I asked if I could get anything else to make the others more comfortable. Wynona asked if ghosts could get drunk as she had been sober since we bound her here and that might have been the longest she\u2019d ever gone. I reminded her that she was drunk when we found her so she asked me to bring Scotch. I don\u2019t think she understands.<br /> <br /> The problems between Molly and Yvette could be a problem without Troy given Wynona and Sondra aren\u2019t likely to intervene. Thus Rose went to Molly while I grabbed two chairs and told Yvette to come with me. I took my ear curl out and we moved away from the others. I set Yvette with her back to Molly so she couldn\u2019t watch her stare angrily for a few minutes. I tried to be very gentle with Yvette but I needed to know what she was feeling. It became very apparent that Yvette had PTSD, something I was not expecting a ghost from the \u201860s to have. I guess that\u2019s my own assumptions getting in the way. I explained to her that she didn\u2019t have to despair every second of her existence. Something in my words triggered a realization and Yvette sat up with a surprised smile on her face for the first time since we arrived. She was in the body of her 21 year old self. The fact that she remembered having children, living to her 50s, and still looking like she did in what I suspect she calls her prime, brightened Yvette noticeably. She was actually very pretty in that moment of happiness. That moment passed as she then explained that she was terrified of Molly doing something to her. She was not a killer, though she couldn\u2019t make Molly believe that. I tried to explain that Molly had some right to be angry, and I knew what it was like to be angry. But as we talked, I realized that Molly could very well have trouble moving on if she continued to hold to this rage and hatred. I didn\u2019t want that and I knew that Molly really didn\u2019t either. So I promised Yvette that I would make sure Molly left her alone if she promised not to give up hope. She nodded and I stood and stabbed Molly\u2019s attention with my gaze. I walked over not looking at all pleased and while I didn\u2019t have it in me to be really upset with Molly, I needed her to understand me.<br /> <br /> When I got over to her, she seemed almost ready to flee. At least I had her attention. I explained to her, less politely than I had been before, that if she kept obsessing on this need to hurt Yvette, then she\u2019d be more likely to become something else. Something we\u2019d have to hunt and put down. My brief definition of an angry ghost played up how she would lose herself and be nothing more than a ghost that wanted to hurt people...forever. The look of abject terror in Molly\u2019s eyes told me everything I needed to know. Rose shot me her own withering look, but I was done. I nodded once to Yvette then left them to whatever they were doing. Then I put my ear curl back in and started writing this.<br /> <br /> I think Wynona may have asked Troy if he enjoyed killing her, though not in a spiteful way. For her, I think it was similar to asking what it felt like to fly or get drunk. There is a kind of innocence in her obliviousness that is refreshing, but I have to look really hard to see around the annoying parts. Not to say that Wynona is a pure flower as I\u2019m sure she\u2019s had her share of sins...Actually everyone here has. Maybe that\u2019s why Mr. Ox was trapped as well. Maybe this entity has trapped these souls by somehow using their sins to shackle them here. Since we are only part ghost, the pull isn\u2019t as strong. Because Mr. Ox is a demon and therefore all spirit, that might be what held him. And also why our vices (I can only assume that was what triggered Nightshade and Bright Eyes) can be manipulated. This thing is Nightshade\u2019s worse nightmare. No love lost from me either. Slavery, mental or otherwise, ghosts forced to have interaction with the living...this thing has to go. The more violently the better at this point.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, October 22, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> After getting Yvette calmed down and secured in the pool room, we were going to break up into groups again to resume our search for more ghosts when Troy said he knew where there might be something that could help us against the hotel. It was the axe he had used to murder Wynona and Sandra, and we found it just where he said it would be, buried next to a tool shed beside the hedge maze.<br /> <br /> The axe is a powerful memorabilia. Doc seemed very impressed by it, and I think he plans to carry it on combat missions from here on out. He is\u2026very well armed. With his shotgun, Stanton\u2019s rifle, and this axe, he\u2019ll be positively covered in weapons. It seems a bit excessive to me, but then again, I fight unarmed. In any event, for the time being we are allowing Troy to wield it against the hotel entity if it comes to that.<br /> <br /> After retrieving the axe, we returned to the pool to find Molly tied to a chair screaming, mad as a meat axe. Apparently she attacked Yvette. Sara seems to have taken to Yvette, so she went to comfort her while I spoke to Molly. I was very stern at first, telling her that she was out of line and needed to calm down and let us work so that we can free her from the hotel. Then I softened my approach. I took a more motherly attitude as I tried to convince Molly that the best thing she could do was to calm down and bear with things while we worked. I reminded her that Yvette will get her just punishment once we free everyone from the hotel and the ghosts pass on to whatever awaits them beyond death.<br /> <br /> My stern-then-soft approach worked fairly well, and Molly promised to behave, so I untied her. Meanwhile, Sara learned more about Yvette\u2019s history. She really was sent to kill Finnigan, but he was dead of appendicitis by the time she got to him. She had hoped her mobster boyfriend would respect her more if she committed the murder, but it didn\u2019t work out that way. It rarely does.<br /> <br /> Once things were calmer in the pool room, Alexia and I headed to the kitchen to arrange some refreshments for our guests, but we were interrupted when we heard a tremendous roar from the lobby. I rushed in to see what it was, fearing that the hotel entity had revealed itself at last, but instead I found Mr. Ox standing rigid just inside the entrance. A furious expression contorted his normally placid face. The hotel was trapping him there. I was able to drag him outside the front door, and once he was on the lawn, he was more-or-less free of the hotel\u2019s pull, though it still weighed on him. He discarded his human guise, however, and became a hulking ox demon. I didn\u2019t want to look too closely at him for fear of seeing beyond even that monstrous visage, for I sensed that his true appearance was even more terrifying. Alexia fled.<br /> <br /> It seems that Mr. Ox teleported to me with more news of Bone Dry\u2019s activities. He expected to find me at the AMC pool, but instead found himself in the hotel. I explained the matter to him and he was satisfied, but chose to leave instead of sticking around to discuss things further. Once we are done at the hotel, I will have to search for his store so that he will find me and tell me what he knows.<br /> <br /> After that, we split up to search for more ghosts. Doc, Sara and Alexia found Wynona shortly thereafter, drunk and fumbling with her key as she tried to enter her room. We all gathered again in the pool room to get her settled in. Sara bled on Wynona and we found that once she was lucid, she was a rather odd person. She was obsessed with Sandra\u2019s death and seemed more fascinated than distressed by her own demise. She wasn\u2019t even frightened of Troy. Indeed, she was a bit insensitive toward him. She also has all sorts of strange impressions about her state, given that she was trying and failing to be a good Catholic when she died.<br /> <br /> Wynona is rather outgoing and irrepressible. She is obsessed with death, which isn\u2019t really that odd among our social circles, but for some reason Wynona\u2019s brazen personality rubbed Alexia the wrong way. I think it\u2019s because the two of them are a bit more similar than Alexia would like to admit. Sara, on the other hand, seemed quite amused by Wynona\u2019s antics.<br /> <br /> Once Wynona was secured in the pool room, Natalie, Alexia and I went out searching for Sandra. Predictably, we found her in the music room, and once she and Natalie struck up a conversation, Alexia and I excused ourselves to give them some privacy. I hid myself in the Shroud of Stillness and returned to keep an eye on the two, and was rather puzzled to find that Natalie was being quite forward with Sandra. She lured the actress back to the pool room, and once we were there, Natalie smeared blood on her lips and passionately kissed the ghost. She was certainly right about Sandra\u2019s sexual orientation. I wonder if the hotel wasn\u2019t exerting a bit of its influence over Natalie.<br /> <br /> Of course, once Sandra became lucid and remembered her death, she began screaming hysterically. Natalie held and calmed her. After Sandra was over the initial shock, Doc explained the situation to her. His resemblance to her friend Pedro was a benefit, and I\u2019m still rather curious about the uncanny similarity between Natalie/Doc and Sandra/Pedro.<br /> <br /> Eventually, as evening approached, we discussed what to do once the entity appeared. We assume that it won\u2019t let us keep stealing its ghosts much longer before it takes more aggressive action against us. I got the axe and a mattock (in case we need to dig into the basement) and placed both behind the front desk so that they would be in a nice, central location should we need them. We decided we wanted Troy\u2019s help fighting the entity, and he certainly deserves a chance to avenge himself. To that end, we convinced him to let Natalie seal him in a bottle so that we could summon him and give him his axe when the entity appears. Then we decided to rest a bit for the remainder of the afternoon before heading to the hotel bar later tonight to capture more ghosts. I have a feeling the entity might show itself then.<br /> <br /> We were a bit worried that Molly might attack Yvette again since Troy was no longer in the pool room to keep the peace. Quite frankly, the other ghosts aren\u2019t really very reliable, so I don\u2019t think we can expect Wynona or Sandra to help, and Wynona might even get a perverse thrill out of more fighting.<br /> <br /> Doc and Sara went to talk to Yvette and make sure she is okay because the poor girl is terrified of Molly. Meanwhile, I sat with Molly again and tried to help calm her and remind her that revenge against Yvette simply isn\u2019t worth it. She\u2019s not a violent or angry person, and the longer she holds onto her anger, the more it will become a part of her ghostly persona. If she keeps on like she is, she could become a vengeful ghost, and then she won\u2019t be able to pass on or find peace once we force the hotel to release its hold on her. She doesn\u2019t want that, and I think that by the end of our conversation, she understood that she needs to let go of the anger and try to move beyond it. Besides, anything Molly might do now would only pale in comparison to whatever punishment awaits Yvette when she passes on.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d just managed to calm her down and help her stabilize her emotions when Doc came over and practically threatened her to stay away from Yvette! It didn\u2019t take him long to choose sides. I was a bit mad about that. Of all people, he should understand what it\u2019s like to be angry. More to the point, Molly\u2019s anger is partly based in her fear, and intimidating her isn\u2019t going to help.<br /> <br /> In response, I resumed my motherly attitude and gave Molly a bit of a hug. I told her that I trusted her not to do anything foolish while we were out, and she agreed. I think she\u2019ll be fine.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Death in the Maze</u><br /> <br /> It occurred to us that James Gibson, the federal agent who was investigating Sandra\u2019s murder, might have been the one who died in the hedge maze and left the death mark that Alexia and I perceived earlier in the day. There\u2019s no sign of his ghost, though.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Murder Axe</u><br /> <br /> Troy\u2019s murder axe is a powerful piece of memorabilia. It can be a powerful weapon and it echoes with the Passion key. Because it\u2019s a memorabilia, it should impress other sin-eaters, but its haunted atmosphere will probably spook mortals. The axe could be especially potent in Troy\u2019s hands if he is enraged.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>The Doll\u2019s Head</u><br /> <br /> To express both his appreciation of my efforts on his behalf and his displeasure toward the hotel entity, Mr. Ox gave me a severed doll\u2019s head from his shop. Were it on a doll\u2019s body, it would be a very cute Chinese doll, but decapitated and with tangled hair, it looks altogether very spooky. If I tug at its hair, it will scream just once before losing its power, but that horrible scream will terrify and stun anything within earshot except for our krewe. Mr. Ox asked me to use it against the hotel entity when it reveals itself, and that seems like a marvelous plan to me.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Troy Donovan\u2019s Axe is, as noted, Memorabilia. It gives the +5 bonus to attack, has the Passion Key attached, and the usual bling benefits for Sin-Eaters. It also has the usual drawbacks with mortals on social rolls and with nightmares.<br /> <br /> Additionally, if wielded by Troy at someone he is enraged at, it does aggravated damage. However, it does not do aggravated damage to those who have died, even temporarily, so it has no special effect on Vampires, Mummies, Sin-Eaters, Ghosts, Prometheans, Revenants, or Zombies. Troy not being a Sin-Eater also does not get the +5 to attack.<br /> <br /> This session it was Natalie\u2019s turn to be afflicted by the entity. Natalie\u2019s vice manifests itself in a need for attention; so she was acting to put herself front in center and in Sara\u2019s crosshairs (Sara being one of the two she most wants attention from and the one that she is not afraid of). Natalie does not have Sara\u2019s lust for sex (though she does have quite a libido) as much as attention, so more flirting less seducing.<br /> <br /> I am aware Catholicism does not work as Wynona suggested. She has an odd idea of Catholicism, being completely out of touch with most people. She is also completely unused to not being drunk (which makes her somewhat suspicious and morose) and barely knew how to behave.<br /> <br /> I described Mr. Ox as a monstrous Ox-man demon, but noted they were, essentially, seeing what their minds would let them, and sort of clouding over his horrific form. I noted they could try and focus past the rationalization to see his true form, but would have to make checks to see if they developed derangements at the unhinging sight. Everyone elected not to try. And what could Mr. Ox have wanted? Questions, questions\u2026<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-24-2014, 01:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-11T16:55:30-07:00","id":89120,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for the latest chapter in our story, in which our heroes almost do bad things. Sorry about the delay...the ice storm did not cost us the session but made things a bit inconvenient for us.<br /> <br /> <i><br /> Session CII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc's Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2015 Hours, Friday, October 23, 2010<br /> <br /> After I finished my last entry, I shared my concerns about sin and vice with the others. It wasn\u2019t much, but it was at least an idea to start from. The Krewe had a few other thoughts on the matter, so we weren\u2019t convinced yet. Also Rose was not agreeable to my insistence that the entity suffer. She predictably tried to tell my why it was important to just do what needed to be done. But I was not in any mood. And while I doubt I frighten her, she backed down while we could still talk jokingly about it.<br /> <br /> The next step was to visit the bar again. That seemed to be the most likely place for us to find our remaining ghosts. Our plan was to split up depending on who we found based on our previous discussions. Bertrand was behind the bar, Marvin Tomilson was alone at table in the farthest corner, Thomas Wyndham was at a table near the bar, and a new face had his own table in the center. Everyone here was dressed appropriate to the \u201820s so we had an idea of who the newcomer was. Cupcake headed straight for the bar and immediately struck up a conversation. Or rather I guess Bertrand started talking to her. Rose sat with Wyndham as I walked back and mentioned how quiet it was in this corner to Tomilson. At first he seemed a little worried but I asked if he would mind some company. For emphasis, I glanced back at all the white people in the room. Only the pretty Asian lady was different. Tomilson smiled a little and nodded at that. As I sat and made introductions, I saw Bright Eyes and Nightshade had engaged our unknown ghost and had his attention well in hand. It was then that I felt the entity trying to affect me again. My anger never rose, at least not outwardly. Marvin and I were just beginning to have a relaxing and casual conversation when Cupcake started speaking louder and louder about \u201cthe flesh will come back, but why do I know it will come back?\u201d She wasn\u2019t talking to Bertrand anymore but to the bar. And the talk of flesh was getting the attention of the other guests. About that time, Bright Eyes called out to me and nodded at Rose. When I looked, she was weeping into her hands while Wyndham tried to find something to say that might comfort her. She shook her head then left the bar. Bright Eyes took Nightshade and followed Rose, leaving the unknown man in an utter state of confusion. I took a chance on Marvin being a decent person and asked him to help me get \u201cthe crazy lady back to her room for her medicine.\u201d I knew the look of fear in his eyes as he stumbled through an excuse but I assured him I was certain it would be better for us to help than for her to go crazy in the bar. And I didn\u2019t even have to pretend to lie about that. Marvin followed my lead, but he let me do all the direct interaction. I gently took Cupcake\u2019s arm as she was practically screaming now and \u201creminded\u201d her that we met in the hall and I knew about her medicine. Marvin got swept up in doing the right thing and forgot to worry about what people would think about him being around a white woman. He made sure all the doors were open as I directed Cupcake back to the pool. Bright Eyes came in behind and bled on Marvin just as he realized we walked into a pool that shouldn\u2019t be there. Cupcake was able to fight off the entity at that point, cheering that she was free. I gave Tomilson the short explanation and told him what we needed to do as we led him away from the door. Nightshade was able to bind him fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> Cupcake gathered the Krewe once our current selection of ghosts were accommodated. Bertrand talked with her before the entity triggered her hunger in a way she never considered. He said that there were eleven ghosts and that he must be last. He knew we were removing the other ghosts from the entity\u2019s control. When the time came, Bertrand said he might not remember but we were to say to him, \u201cIt\u2019s Time to Bring the End.\u201d Bertrand promised that at that point he would remember everything and help us finish this. Something happened when we took Troy that made the bartender lose part of his hold on what was real. We might have gotten more information but that was about the time Cupcake decided that eating one of us would be okay because \u201cthe flesh will come back.\u201d This was more than a little disturbing but at the same time, it seemed like a warning I\u2019d heard somewhere before. The Dog was restless about it as well. Neither of us were okay with eating another member of the Krewe, much less anyone else.<br /> <br /> That is the path to destruction. Partaking of the flesh is the first step, muhaarib. The next is to consume the spirit. Your Krewe is spirit and flesh knit together. This cannot be tolerated.<br /> <br /> Makes sense to me. It\u2019s even creepier when you say it like that, but this isn\u2019t supposed to be something anyone considers okay. Anyway, Bright Eyes shared what she learned before chasing after Rose. The unknown man that was very happy to talk to her in the bar was James Gibson. He claimed to be with the police, but Bright Eyes knew he was lying. At that revelation, Nightshade left us to speak privately with Sondra. She came back shortly and stated that James might be involved with the Mob. Then it was Nightshade\u2019s turn to make a hypothesis. She suspects Bertrand killed James as that would put everyone here having killed, been murdered, or otherwise died due to a connection to this hotel. This made sense to the Krewe and it still worked with my sin theory.<br /> <br /> We decided to try our luck again since we knew we were almost there with only five more to go. Cupcake needed something to eat to take her mind off the lingering hunger, so we headed to the kitchen to grab some snacks. Something seemed to called Cupcake as she kept looking at the oven. Finally she just jerked open the oven door and then shrieked. We all rushed over as the smell of something very nice filled the kitchen. But when I looked in the oven, my blood ran cold and my rage boiled hot. There in a large roasting pan was Daisey. She had been prepared like any other roast with basting and vegetables. Cupcake ran out of arm\u2019s reach as I very carefully removed the pan from the oven. I could see Daisey\u2019s Deathmarks so we knew she had died by hanging, but this explained why the body disappeared. We may never know who did this, but it does stand to reason that the guests may have been served the body for dinner. I tried to keep my voice in check as I wanted to scream. I wanted to heal her as I had with Molly, but the tissue damage was extensive. It would take most of my plasm reserves plus Daisey would awaken with all the memories again. But first we had to get her back to the pool before the entity pulled her away to suffer more agony later. Rose left and came back with one of Molly\u2019s laundry carts. We put the ghost corpse in the cart so we could take Daisey through without causing a complete panic in the pool. Rose also noted that James had spotted her and seemed interested in what we were up to. She suggested we act more suspicious to possibly lure him into the pool. Everyone agreed so we moved with far more dramatic sneaking movement than was necessary.<br /> <br /> Along the way, Bright Eyes, who had suffered several cuts by this point, asked that someone else bleed on Daisey. I nodded but before I could offer to help, she continued that we didn\u2019t have a people oven here like back at the Bluffs. I stopped short and felt my stare freeze as I turned. She realized what she\u2019d said as soon as she saw me, but it was too late. Even Nightshade looked at her oddly as Bright Eyes blushed brightly and apologized. I went back to the bar at that point with Nightshade for alcohol. I\u2019d need some to heal Daisey, Nightshade needed the bottles, and I was tired of Wynona asking for Scotch. This time the bar was empty so Nightshade grabbed two bottles, both full, as well as one or two from the trash. I got the Scotch and we headed back. I poured Marvin a drink before Wynona grabbed the bottle. Rose looked at me disapprovingly, but that\u2019s become a comforting sensation at this point.<br /> <br /> There was much discussion made over what to do with Daisey. I was adamant that we could not leave her like this or allow her to awaken in this state. No one wanted her to suffer that pain on top of the Hell that was her life. Then Rose came up with an idea we just hadn\u2019t thought of before, likely because we were distracted by the fact some asshole cooked a dead 10 year old. We would just put Daisey in a bottle for now to keep her from the entity and then we could help her when we have more time and plasm. I have to assume she can\u2019t wake up while held in the bottle so I\u2019m okay with this idea. The less suffering or even knowledge Daisey has of what happened to her after death, the better. Rose cleaned Daisey very carefully before Nightshade cast her ceremony. Bright Eyes and Rose then went to \u201cstand guard\u201d to be more suspicious. Rose was invisible of course, but she planned to get the drop on James if he got close enough to the pool. Through the ear curl, Rose requested Sondra scream to lure James in, but Nightshade offered to take care of it, given her movie roles were usually to be the girl that gets eaten. As Rose gave Bright Eyes a play by play of James\u2019 movements, it sounded like something from a spy film as he crept toward our position. I herded everyone else to the far corner of the pool to reduce the risk of friendly fire. Then Nightshade screamed. It was as if time stopped and images of horribly butchered body parts lept into my head. At that moment, I ignited my Pyre-Flame Shroud to absorb any stray shots and positioned myself between the door and our \u201csurvivors.\u201d James burst through the door with a pistol in one hand, a shotgun in the other. Rose pounced, becoming visible just as James seemed to expect her and tossed her off like we might while playing with Lily. At that point, he widened his coverage of the room and ordered no one to move. For our part, the Krewe was stunned that Rose was completely ignored. Then Sondra ran in front of everyone, including Rose who was still lying before the gunman, and shouted, \u201cWilliam! Stop it!\u201d James turned a frightened pale as he stammered out that he thought she was dead. Sondra was much more in control of the chaos then we were, explaining that they all were dead. At that point, our would-be assassin dropped his weapons. Rose bled on him and his demeanor changed from cautious and controlled to that of agony. The rush of pain from the shot to the back of the head which killed him left the man staggering. I poured William, as James was some kind of alias, a drink while Nightshade bound him. Rose picked up the weapons and handed them over to me before I gave the explanation speech again. William seemed to settle in fairly easily once the pain subsided. He took up with Marvin surprisingly quickly as well.<br /> <br /> We headed back to the bar but found it was still empty. Just before walking in, Nightshade announced the entity was trying to affect her. Of course we all turned to look, which made her blush for a moment. In trying to fight off the urge to grab attention, she had instead grabbed attention. Still that\u2019s better than suddenly having the urge to beat down a close friend for a slight that was based on my own assumptions anyway. ...There was a tangent. Anyway, since the bar was a bust, we headed over to room 1I to check on Finnegan. Nightshade knocked but there was no answer. So we did what any TV ghost hunter would do. We used the Master Key and went in anyway. And just like every other lame ghost hunter depicted on TV, we found nothing. I for one felt a little dumb.<br /> <br /> We decided to split up then, after Nightshade had to explain the concept of missing her girlfriend to Rose. Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and Cupcake all went down to the one phone on-site to call back to the Bluffs. I went and got the mattocks from the shed before meeting with Rose at the elevator. We went down into the basement and I stood with a mattock on each shoulder while Rose dissolved into a million spiders. She canvassed the whole floor, crawling and creeping in all the dark spaces. She found a few chunks of the floor shattered from the explosives. Beneath our current floor was an older surface with what looked like some kind of ritual markings. This wasn\u2019t the entrance to a monster\u2019s lair I was hoping for, but it was a clue. It also meant we were probably dealing with something not from our realm...again. Before we could explore any further, the others came down after the phone call. Apparently Noriko was taken to lunch by Tavia and Gretchen wants to talk to me for some reason. I\u2019m certain I will not enjoy that conversation, but at least Noriko is being made to feel welcome.<br /> <br /> Now I think we\u2019re just going to call it a night.<br /> <b><br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Friday, October 22, 2010, Night<br /> <br /> When night fell, we all went to the bar to see what ghosts we might rescue there. The plan was for Alexia to speak to Bertrand, the bartender, while I spoke to Thomas Wyndham since I had already established a rapport with him. Doc would talk to Marvin if he was there.<br /> <br /> We were pleasantly surprised to see that James Gibson, the investigator who was asking around after Sandra\u2019s death, was also in the bar. He disappeared mysteriously in the 20\u2019s, though Alexia and I suspect it was his death mark we sensed in the hedge maze earlier in the day. Sara volunteered to speak with him.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Gibson\u2019s appearance was the only pleasant surprise we faced. No sooner did I sit down to speak with Thomas than I felt the old, familiar weight settle in my heart. The loss, loneliness and heartbreak I\u2019ve suffered over the past nineteen months welled up inside me and I felt so utterly hopeless that even the thought of Karl did little to comfort me. Richard\u2019s death felt as fresh and terrible as it did the moment I found out he had killed himself, and I lost all will to go on. I buried my face in my hands and began to sob. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve cried openly, when others were around, since Richard\u2019s funeral\u2026but I was so depressed I couldn\u2019t help it. I think that Thomas was trying to speak to me, but the only thing that pierced my morose fog was some other disturbance in the bar involving Alexia. I looked up at her with tear-soaked eyes and she looked back, and I could see that she was also taken by some strange urge and wanted nothing more than to carve me up then and there. She was muttering to herself more and more loudly until at last she was shouting \u201cThe flesh will come back, but how do I know it will come back?\u201d Everyone\u2019s attention was focused on her\u2026but I didn\u2019t care. I just wanted everything to end. Even knowing what might lie in store for me beyond the threshold of death, I just wanted to die. But Alexia\u2019s insane shouting was helping her fight her urges, so I couldn\u2019t rely on her to kill me. I knew I would have to end it myself.<br /> <br /> So I pushed myself up from the table and slowly staggered from the room, barely able to set one foot in front of the other. All the while, the Bride was pleading with me. She kept reminding me that I\u2019ve found love again, that Karl is waiting for me to return to him. She practically screamed at me to stop what I was planning, but all I could think about was how much I missed Richard and how ironic it was that the Bride, who represents the Resolution of Death in our krewe mythos, would be railing against my own deathly resolve. And for some reason I forgot that as a sin-eater, I would come back if I did manage to kill myself. Or perhaps I simply planned to kill myself again and again until I couldn\u2019t come back anymore.<br /> <br /> Then Natalie was there with her arms around my shoulders. She said she would help me. In my depressed state, I thought she was promising to help me end it. She guided me toward the pool room, and I thought how fitting it would be to drown, like I did the first time when I should have stayed dead. But once we were in the pool room, Natalie looked me in the eyes and reminded me that I had to have hope. And as she said that, she did something to me that counteracted the hotel\u2019s influence. My depression lessened until it was nothing more than the melancholy that has haunted me since Richard died, and then even that faded. I remembered Karl and how sweet and wonderful he is, and I felt good again, so sad at all.<br /> <br /> It still took me some time to get my bearing again and shake off the last shreds of sorrow, but before long I was back on my feet again. I stayed in the pool room a bit anyway, though just to make sure.<br /> <br /> Once I came to my senses, it was clear that the hotel had been manipulating me. And I wasn\u2019t the only one. Alexia had fallen under its sway as well. She had a terrifying urge to kill and eat someone and struggled with the chilling idea that slaughtering and eating another sin-eater would be okay because we would come back, so she really wouldn\u2019t be killing us. Fortunately, she managed to fight against the urge until Sara and Doc helped her to the pool. Doc, being a clever man, managed to get Marvin\u2019s ghost into the pool room as well by asking him to help guide Alexia there. Natalie sealed him in the room in short order, so that\u2019s one more ghost captured.<br /> <br /> We asked Marvin if he knew why Thomas had accused him of Wynona\u2019s murder. Marvin had no idea, but Wynona suggested that it was because Marvin had been stalking her. He flatly denied it. I\u2019m more inclined to believe him than her, because her judgment of things has proven decidedly suspect. Given Thomas\u2019s opinions on Hitler versus Stalin, I wonder if he isn\u2019t especially racist? Then again, he did not seem particularly averse to me.<br /> <br /> Marvin was surprised to learn that Troy was the murderer.<br /> <br /> We discussed what to do next. Natalie thought that James might be involved with the mob. Perhaps he was a hit man sent to kill whoever murdered Sandra, in which case she too must have been involved with the mob somehow. Natalie suspects Bertrand might have killed Gibson in order to protect Troy, but if so, he must have known more about what was happening at the hotel even then. It\u2019s quite mysterious. I can\u2019t help but remain suspicious of Bertrand and his connection to the hotel.<br /> <br /> Friday, October 22, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We once more ventured from the pool room to find more ghosts, though really Alexia wanted to visit the kitchen to whip up a few snacks so that if the hotel targeted her again, she would have something to eat in order to help stave off her darker cravings. She felt drawn to the oven, and that is when we made a terrifying discovery. Daisy\u2019s corpse was inside the oven, curled up and cooked like a gruesome roast. It was sickening. But it does explain why her remains were never found.<br /> <br /> We have no idea who did that to her, but I suspect it was someone who was victim to the same vice as Alexia.<br /> <br /> Despite the horrifying condition of her corpse, we had the perfect opportunity to get her to the pool room. But we did not want to upset the other ghosts with the horrifying vision of her cooked flesh. She was quite unconscious, effectively \u201cdead\u201d as a ghost. Doc wanted to try and heal her, but doing so would have drained his plasmic energies to almost nothing, so I suggested that we take her into the pool room in a laundry cart, covered with some spare towels. Then, once there, we could shield her with one of the folding screens we had brought in while Natalie sealed her in a bottle. That way we wouldn\u2019t have to worry about her waking up or suffering any more until we were finished with the hotel, and the other ghosts wouldn\u2019t have to see her gruesome state.<br /> <br /> While we were gathering the laundry cart and then moving back to the pool room, Sara and I realized that James Gibson was watching us furtively from the music room doorway. He seemed suspicious of us, and we both had the impression that he planned to follow us to the pool to see what we were up to. So Sara and I hatched a plan. She followed the others to the pool room and made it a bit obvious so that Gibson would know where we had gone. Meanwhile, I cloaked myself in my Shroud and disappeared. I quietly followed him as he crept carefully and silently toward the pool. He seemed unsure of what to do once he was outside the door, so I suggest through the ear curls that he needed a little motivation to get him into the pool. So Natalie did her best damsel in distress scream, and in response Gibson burst into the pool, drawing a gun in each hand and ordering everyone inside to freeze.<br /> <br /> Our ploy worked, and we had gotten him into the pool room, but he was still dangerous, so shifted into my Tear-Stained Caul, then reappeared and grabbed him from behind. He recovered from the shock quickly, and I must confess that he got the best of me. He threw his weight forward and threw me off balance, shrugging out of my hold quite handily. I quickly recovered, of course. He leveled his shotgun at me, but with my Shroud on I was not too concerned, and made a move to shift his arm out of the way and lock him in another hold. Before I could do that, though, Sandra ran up and forced herself between the two of us.<br /> <br /> She knew James Gibson, but not by that name. She called him William. He was so shocked that she was still alive that he dropped his guns to the floor and put his hands on her shoulders. Sara said we should bleed on him to help him remember, so I cut myself and smeared some of my blood on his back.<br /> <br /> He remembered being shot in the back of the head, but not by whom. He told us that he was sent by the mob to kill Sandra\u2019s murderer, and we explained his current situation to him. He seemed quite taken with Yvette. I think her short skirt made an impression on him. I was also flattered when he asked if I was a professional. \u201cIt\u2019s been a long time since anyone\u2019s gotten the drop on me like that,\u201d he said. I assured him that I was, in fact, a professional, and then complimented him as well. It\u2019s been a long time since anyone\u2019s been able to shrug out of one of my holds like he did.<br /> <br /> We left Sandra and Gibson to catch up, and headed back out to see what else we could accomplish. Doc asked a few questions of Yvette about Finnigan. It seems he was good with numbers, and fixed accounts for the mob. While he was on the run, he was supposed to be well-armed. We stopped by his room on the first floor, but there was no sign of his ghost. I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve seen him at all yet.<br /> Natalie, Sara and Alexia went to call their girlfriends using the hotel\u2019s land line. I think that after all we have been through, they really needed to hear Karen and Chandra\u2019s voices. I would have spoken to Karl, but he\u2019s not due back from Cold Harbor for another day or so. It\u2019s probably best that I stay on task right now anyway.<br /> <br /> While they were doing that, Doc and I went to the basement to explore more there. We were out of other avenues to investigate, so I transformed into a swarm of spiders to have a closer look at the collapsed chamber below the hotel. As a collective of spiders, I was able to crawl into cracks and crevices I couldn\u2019t reach before, and I discovered that the concrete floor had been laid over an older floor. On the original floor, I could see remnants of an occult circle. What pieces I could find looked like a summoning or binding circle to me, but a few fragments looked like they had been damaged before the newer floor was laid over the original. I suspect that whatever entity is trapping the ghosts here is an outsider that was summoned decades ago, perhaps while the hotel was being built. The burnt fragments of the binding circle imply that something went wrong with the summoning, which would explain the entity\u2019s presence in the hotel.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow, we plan to do what we can to dig out the basement and have a closer, less obstructed look at the occult markings down there. They might be the key to undoing the influence of the hotel entity. For now, though, I\u2019m going to take a bath, heal up a bit, and get some sleep. Since the hotel has proven adept at influencing all of us, we have decided to alter the rooming arrangements. Natalie, Sara and I will lock ourselves in a room together since we know our darker sides aren\u2019t going to hurt anyone else, and so that we can all keep an eye on one another to make sure we don\u2019t do anything foolish. Doc and Alexia, who have proven to be a bit dangerous when the hotel gets to them, are locking themselves in their own rooms so that they won\u2019t be around anyone else. And if they do come for the rest of us, the locked door should prove a nice deterrent and give us some warning of their approach.<br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Theories</u><br /> <br /> Before going to the bar Friday night, we discussed the nature of the entity haunting the hotel. Doc suggested that it anchored spirits through their vices - Troy\u2019s anger, Molly\u2019s fear, and so on - but that doesn\u2019t all add up. Perhaps it\u2019s the ghosts\u2019 connection to deaths in the hotel that tie them to the place. I suppose we may never know the whole truth, but that doesn\u2019t matter as long as we can free the ghosts and destroy the entity.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Bertrand</u><br /> <br /> I was in no shape to think about our investigations when we first went to the bar and I fell under the sway of the hotel\u2019s influence. I\u2019m still rather annoyed by that, and frightened of what I almost did had it not been for Natalie. I was not until later that I learned from the others what Alexia had discovered. Bertrand, the bartender, is losing track of things now that Troy\u2019s stabilizing presence has been removed. He won\u2019t be aware of things for much longer, so he told Alexia that he should be the last ghost we capture. And when the time comes for that, she can make him understand what we need by telling him \u201cIt\u2019s time to bring the end.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia also learned that there are eleven ghosts in total. Molly, Yvette, Troy, Sandra, Wynona, Daisy, Marvin and William (a.ka. James Gibson) make eight. Finnigan, Tommelson and Bertrand are the other three, so we only have a few left to go.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Manipulation </u><br /> <br /> Natalie saved me, and for that I am extremely grateful. She apologized for manipulating my mind like that, but there was no reason to ask forgiveness. She was helping me, not using me. I tried to make her understand that, but I think she still felt uncomfortable exerting her powers over someone else\u2019s mind. Oddly, she seems to draw a line between using supernatural powers to manipulate someone and doing so merely with honeyed words and charm. In my opinion, though, they are both simply different means to the same ends, even if one is more potent than the other. If you are going to judge one harshly, you should judge the other harshly as well. I think that if Natalie comes to realize this, it will help her understand herself better, and ultimately make her a better person. I don\u2019t really know how to tell her what I think, though. Not without upsetting her or botching it all.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> Molly and Lily </u><br /> <br /> Molly was worried about me when she saw me distraught under the hotel\u2019s influence. I tried to put her mind at ease once I was feeling better, and in the process I discovered that she was frightened of Lily. So I decided to put her mind at ease and asked Lily to join us and dance a bit. It\u2019s absolutely adorable when she does the Mashed Potato or the Twist, and Molly agreed. She seemed more comfortable with Lily after that.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CII</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Exciting, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Everyone had to make a roll on Resolve + Composure. Jasmine, despite having a die pool that dwarfed anyone else\u2019s, rolled no successes at all. Natalie and Alexia were addled, rolling enough successes to avoid acting our their vices but still reevaluating them in small ways, or so went the theory. Sara and Doc cleaned house. Alexia went a little overboard, but it was OK, she did well on escalating things.<br /> <br /> Natalie used Passion Marionette on Jasmine, which hit her like a hammer. Her near instant recovery was because she would have been dancing on the roof if not addled.<br /> <br /> The other main thing from a story perspective was Jasmine got to make a clue finding roll with a penalty but was unable to, so one tidbit in the basement was never found. It\u2019s OK, all was revealed tonight.<br /> <br /> On phone Natalie and Sara talked to Karen, and generally bonded with her. Alexia spoke with Chandra, and found the girls had taken Noriko out and had lunch, which aside from Gretchen asking \u201csomething disturbing\u201d went well. Noriko and Tavia seemed to bond, which is always scary.<br /> <br /> Finally as an aside, James was not going to be two-gun kid-ing with a pistol and shotgun. He had them both out when he saw how many people were in so he could cover more directions at once. Not the best plan but it all happened quickly.<br /> <br /> We finished the story tonight, so next time should have the conclusion of the hotel story, and we can return to the usual Real World: Death storyline. See you then, comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T01:18:43-07:00","id":89337,"title":"","content":"To be concluded? Oh you tease.... Did that come off weird?<br /> <br /> I have come to the conclusion the krewe need a dispassionate third party to tell them the things they don't want to hear. That and a bracing drink would probably do them some good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-12T02:45:51-07:00","id":89362,"title":"","content":"Quite possibly.<br /> <br /> This story was designed to mess with them, however. I gave consideration to how each one could have their vices used either to cause discord directly or make them vulnerable, and the players went along with it marvelously.<br /> <br /> And yea, next session is the resolution of the hotel story...mostly. They still have a handful of ghosts to deal with at the end. I will say at least one area of discord was, at least in theory, closed in the resolution of the storyline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-24T16:50:34-07:00","id":97874,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the delay. Here is the climax of the hotel scenario. Enjoy!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CIII<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Saturday, October 23, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation would probably be a good idea here were it not for the fact that in the middle of centering my mind, The Entity could come along and wave the red flag in my mind. Because of that and because everyone has to be constantly on guard outside of our rooms and the Pool Room, I skipped it. Plus I\u2019m pretty focused on finishing this without being centered.<br /> <br /> Cupcake made pancakes for an army in the hotel\u2019s kitchen. If it weren\u2019t for the whole \u201ccraving the other other white meat\u201d she might really enjoy it here. While we ate, ideas were considered for what to do today. After a few options, we settled on splitting up. Rose, Nightshade, and Cupcake planned to look for Albert Finnegan again. If they could find him, they figured he would be more trusting of women since the Mob thought so poorly of them in his day. Not that the Mafia is an enlightened institution today, but still. We also wanted to get a look at what actually happened in the basement. But to do that, Cupcake needed to be able to touch the area. Bright Eyes and I are heading for the basement so we could get to work clearing the top layer of concrete. We all have our ear curls this time.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1630 Hours, Saturday, October 23, 2010<br /> <br /> While we were breaking rocks, the rest of Krewe found a surprised Finnegan in his room. They convinced him that not only was Yvette after him, but she had called in backup. Once they had spiked his paranoid meter, Nightshade promised to lead him to safety. It really sounded like a scene from a Bogart movie. Cupcake \u201cmade sure the coast was clear,\u201d or hid Yvette so Finnegan wouldn\u2019t bolt from the Pool Room. Once he was in, Nightshade cast her ceremony and the explaining began. Cupcake also brought Yvette out from the changing curtain once Finnegan was up to speed. That seemed to go a little better than it did with Molly.<br /> <br /> With no more immediate ideas, Rose came downstairs and unlocked her Primeval Caul. The hulking shark-woman was able to heave the larger sections of concrete aside while we cleared the more manageable debris. Nightshade brought drinks periodically as we basically turned all the heavy lifting over to Rose. It still took us all morning and most of this afternoon, but we did finally clear most of the new floor and rubble from the explosives. Then it was Cupcake\u2019s turn. Bright Eyes pointed out that she could do some similar investigating of the explosion, so we stepped back and let our postcogs work their magic.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes finished up first and gave us more information on the people that set the charges. Three men and two women entered about the time we knew the cave-in was reported. One of the men was a priest and didn\u2019t seem to be a full member of the group. He seemed to know why he was there and what was going on however. One of the women was dressed very femininely but carried a machine gun. The other woman dressed in fatigues and carried herself in a more masculine manner. She apparently also had a buzzcut. Why Bright Eyes looked at me while explaining this, I\u2019m not sure. Anyway, they set the charges in very specific locations along the wall while the priest paced in the center of the room. Once the charges were set, they all left. Apparently the charges were set either on a timer or from a remote detonator as they blew up well after everyone was gone. I wondered if maybe this was another Krewe but nothing they did seemed to suggest they were Sin-Eaters. Very knowledgeable mortals seemed to be the prevailing theory.<br /> <br /> Once we had that information, we turned to Cupcake and brainstormed what we wanted to know about the Evil Magic Circle (TM). Apparently Cupcake was very in tune with the hotel as she learned volumes of information. We thought it might be wise to know what the ritual space was intended to summon as well as who was responsible for it. The man responsible was tall and very intellectual looking, with a well-trimmed beard. We never got a name but that was less important. His target was a plant-like female creature that reminded me of a dryad. It wasn\u2019t like the Ancient Greek nymphs thankfully. This was more tied to plant life, so the female features were likely a representation of fertility. What the bearded man actually summoned was a dark tree-like Thing (TM) with multiple faces in its bark and branched tendrils which ended in disturbing pods. We tried to determine what went wrong with the summoning. We never figured out what about the ritual was done incorrectly, but we did learn more about one of the ghosts. When the bearded man summoned The Entity, he knew immediately that it was wrong. He tried to banish the creature and undo the terrible mistake he\u2019d made. While he was trying to banish the thing from this world, a very young Bertrand ran into the basement. The boy screamed at the sight, distracting the bearded man\u2019s spell. The Entity impaled the bearded man and absorbed his soul while Bertrand ran away. As the caster\u2019s soul was destroyed, The Entity became more powerful. We needed to next find out what happened to this Entity. It was still here, as we well knew, but a series of explosions cut it off from its roots. These roots had The Entity immortal, so now it could die. Cupcake also mentioned how it howled in pain from the explosion. I knew that pain and as much as I wanted to hurt it even more, I felt badly for just a moment. The caster was trying to summon the plant creature to grow magical fruits and plants throughout the hotel. He wanted to have magical healing and other components of magic to sell and become very rich. So he ultimately broke laws of the universe to sate his greed. I don\u2019t know if that had something to do with why The Entity works as it does or not, but it stayed with me. The bearded man\u2019s impaled body was found by police eventually, but they were unable to determine anything else about the murder. The group of mortals came to the basement once before they blew it up. One of the men was able to use object reading to find where the roots were. That was why they placed the charges where they did. I was somewhat confused by the fact that they never returned after the explosion. As well informed and apparently capable as these mortals were, I couldn\u2019t understand why they wouldn\u2019t come back to make sure it had worked. The last thing Cupcake learned was that the faces in the bark were not ghosts it controlled, but souls it absorbed. Only the caster\u2019s face was recognizable of the many she saw.<br /> <br /> After that information dump, we decided to rest up a bit. We still have two ghosts left and then we need to be ready. The blight on this place ends tonight.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2200 Hours, Saturday, October 23, 2010<br /> <br /> A Krewe of Sin-Eaters that know (mostly) what they are dealing with are not something to ever be trifled with. I\u2019m still a little keyed up. Let me try this again.<br /> <br /> We headed back into the bar around 2000 Hours. Wyndham and Bertrande were both there, thankfully. Rose went to speak with former while Cupcake moved straight to the bar. I could tell she was nervous but this was the time. Rose tried to convince Wyndham that the bar was so empty tonight because of a pool party. Since he didn\u2019t know about it, Rose wanted to take him herself. As off the cuff bullshit goes, that one flowed pretty well. Wyndham was no fool however. A beautiful foreign woman inviting him to a pool party to which he was completely unaware set off some warning bells for a man in the \u201840s. He was hesitant to say the least, but eventually he agreed to take a look. Nightshade followed behind them at a distance to ensure things worked out. Rose was fairly quick to bleed on the ghost once in the pool. He completely freaked out, so there was a few moments of soothing the melted into the explaining.<br /> <br /> I noticed immediately that Marvin Tomilson and William Gibson perked up when we brought in Wyndham. The two men had bonded somewhat since being trapped in the Pool Room. While refreshing, I found that odd for a mobster. When I could be sure Wyndham was stable, I asked Tomilson about things. He was not happy that Wyndham was responsible for him going to the electric chair but had no plans to vent that displeasure. He noted that Gibson was a man of honor and felt it was wrong that Wyndham cost a man his life without any real consequences. I understood but I asked if he could keep Gibson from doing anything \u201ccounter productive\u201d while we were gone. Tomilson agreed but I got the feeling there was more to Gibson than I was aware. I stopped and spoke to the hitman next. He was definitely unhappy an innocent black man was killed because Wyndham made an assumption. William also believed Wyndham when he said he\u2019d made a mistake and apologized to Marvin. He noted that the man was stupid but not racist. Then he explained that his family had a maid while he was a boy that took care of him. Something happened to her that was equally unjust and apparently made a very deep impression on him. I explained my position and he agreed this was not the time. We shook hands and I left him at his word.<br /> <br /> Once Thomas Wyndham was secured, we met Cupcake back in the bar. She looked to Bertrand and with only a little hesitation told him \u201cIt\u2019s time to bring the end.\u201d Bertrand looked confused for a moment, then pulled a shotgun from behind the counter. I started to get involved, but then he pulled a bottle of Scotch from a different counter and poured a double. The bartender downed his drink, then picked up the shotgun. Rose quickly bled on him to keep the potential of things going badly down. Bertrand immediately shook his head and realized we were ready. He told us the group of investigators fought with The Entity as well, but only the woman with the buzzcut, Cindy, survived. She fled after The Entity shoved a bulb down her throat. The rest were turned against each other. Somehow Bertrand was able to move about on his own some of the time, possibly because of the damage from the explosion, so he rescued some of the notes from the dead investigators. Sondra had been ordered to burn the information. Bertrand just got to it before they all went up. We could summon The Entity if someone were to die or be killed based on a vice. There were several other ways that involved vice and death with multiple people. Those were all he could save from the fire, but he knew where they were burned. So we moved to the fireplace in the Troy Donovan Music Room. Cupcake object read the bricks. What we learned immediately made my blood run cold. Not because of untold horrors or otherworldly rituals, but because it hit too close to home. Two people must bury the hatchet over a vice-related grievance. I was controlled by The Entity through my anger. I was still holding the pain and rage I felt toward the breakup with Nightshade inside. An event that was every bit my doing based on an issue that only I had. And to make it even more ridiculous, I had already found another loving relationship without the kinds of problems that led to my issues to begin with. Not only was that unhealthy and dangerous, it was completely stupid. Nightshade was just as uncomfortable as she didn\u2019t want anything brought up. Rose started to suggest we talk when Nightshade mentioned we could call Chandra and they could make up. That wasn\u2019t fair, though it was amusing (now). I told the others to get ready for a huge fight. At first, I think everyone thought I was joking about Chandra. Then they realized I was preparing for war. Once my Stigmata Shroud encased me in my scarlet armor, I walked to Nightshade. I apologized for letting my own issues get in the way and be projected on our relationship. I admitted to her and myself that she was free to love who she wished, the way she wished, and I should have never thought I had a say otherwise. Leaning over, I kissed her on the forehead then shook Bright Eyes\u2019 hand as I apologized to her for getting her involved in my problem. It was a strange feeling to have my emotional turmoil splashed out in front of everyone and laid bare in such a way. But before I could think about the embarrassment, we heard and felt a terrible roar coming from the lobby. We rushed in to find a dark tree creature stooped over in the three floor opening. The beast was massive with eleven damaged pods hanging from the tendrils. I spotted the four faces of the investigators Cupcake described molded into the bark. It was time to bring the end.<br /> <br /> Before The Entity could attack, Nightshade smashed the bottle freeing Troy while Rose held the doll\u2019s head up and ripped on her hair. Physically, nothing happened other than a very scary scream tore through the hotel. In my mind however, I got the image of every nerve in The Entity\u2019s body being shredded horribly and healed over and over, every second. We wasted no more than that split second in attacking the creature. The Krewe unleashed Hell.<br /> <br /> I remembered the anguish I caused Nightshade when The Entity tried to turn me against her. The flame ignited inside and filled my chest with malice. The blaze of my emotions exploded from my hand as a gout of wicked Pyre-Flame hatefire. But my rage was my own this time and my fire ravaged The Entity\u2019s soul as well as its form. Strength, flexibility, and endurance all burned away just like its wooden body. I followed with Stigmata Rage and forced its boiling, tar-like sap from every crevice. But I also hinder its mind from the agony. After three more blasts of my damning Pyre-Flame, The Entity broke free of Mr. Ox\u2019s Gift of Spite. It was not finished yet, but a sickening burnt smell filled the hall and it was covered in wounds. The first attack came to me as The Entity lashed out to impale me as it had the bearded man. The impact on my chest hit like a fallen tree, but it only managed to slide me backward from the force. The others continued with their attacks. I had lots more anger to throw. The sap continued to pump from its wounds thanks to my Stigmata Rage so I continued twice more with my Pyre-Flame assault. The gunshots and other mystic attacks had more trouble damaging it. But a creature made of wood will not stand against the rage of a Pyre-Flame. Rose and Bright Eyes combined the final strike to finish it. The Entity shrieked then started to vibrate as its bark seemed to rip apart into itself. Something inside was effectively consuming the outside. When it was over, all that was left was a burnt husk in the odd shape of a tree that was pulled out of the living realm. I wrapped my Shroud tighter around me and stepped into Twilight where the tree fell and proceeded to pummel the trunk to smoldering bits. Rose and Nightshade shouted and snapped me out of my fugue of vindication.<br /> <br /> Molly was calling for us so I ran to the Pool Room and phased back in. Bertrand seemed distant but allowed Molly to speak. She thanked us for keeping our promise. Then she turned and walked out the back door. As soon as she crossed the threshold, she vanished. Yvette, who had quietly sat watching behind Molly, stood and followed. She also vanished at the threshold. Troy staggered in about the same time, but most of the other men were gone. Bertrand asked if the hotel would be safe and made me promise that it will go on. I told him that the new owner hired us so that she could reopen the Hidden Hillside Hotel. Once he knew that, he smiled and took on a more peaceful expression before walking out the door as well.<br /> <br /> Wynona noted that \u201call the boys got Raptured.\u201d Looking around, only she and Sondra remained other than Troy who basically collapsed. We had miscalculated when to open the bottle so he was affected by Mr. Ox\u2019s gift as well. Once we are sure that nothing else is lingering, we\u2019re done. After that, we just need to clean up, rest up, load up, and go home.<br /> <br /> I still don\u2019t know exactly what this thing was, but I do know one thing: It fell to the Middle Shadows of Dark Haven Bluffs.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, October 23, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> This morning, Alexia and I were the first up and about. Fortunately, there were no further incidents during the night; I did not become suicidal, and Alexia\u2019s unfortunate cravings did not surge again. After meditating, I joined Alexia in the kitchen to prepare a spot of breakfast, and eventually the others joined us.<br /> <br /> We decided to check Finnigan\u2019s room again before returning the basement to begin clearing the a path through the rubble. Natalie, Sara and I went, since we thought he would be less threatened by women. Finnigan was there this time. I kept my distance and let Natalie and Sara do all the talking, and they managed to convince Finnigan that Yvette had brought in backup and was coming with some mob goons to kill him. They promised to lead him to safety and we got him into the pool room. I flicked blood on him to make him lucid and we explained what had happened to him. When he finally saw Yvette, who had been hiding behind the folding screen, he managed to hold it together well enough.<br /> <br /> We spent much of the rest of the day clearing the rubble and debris from the basement so that Alexia could get to the remnants of the summoning circle. When we finally cleared away enough, Alexia crept in and examined the circle with her Industrial Oracle while Sara performed a ceremony to read the emotional resonances left by the people who demolished the basement recently. Together, they discovered quite a lot about what happened here.<br /> <br /> Long ago, when the hotel was being built, a distinguished-looking man with a dark beard attempted to summon a benevolent, plant-like feminine spirit, probably in an attempt to turn the hotel into a sort of garden-house to grow strange fruits with miraculous supernatural qualities. However, something went wrong with the summoning (as it so often does), and instead he summoned a terrible outsider that resembled a gnarled, twisted tree with tentacle-like branches. At that moment, a young Bertrand interrupted the ceremony, and the outsider broke free of the summoning. It became a part of the hotel, twisting it into a trap for those who die under the effects of their vices. The bearded man\u2019s soul was devoured by the outsider.<br /> <br /> This does explain Bertrand\u2019s strange connection to the place, as well as his loyalty to the hotel throughout the years. He seems to have understood what he had inadvertently caused, and was trying to take responsibility for it.<br /> <br /> More recently, a group of people who worked together like a close-knit military squad came to investigate the hotel. One of them used some sort of ritual or power to locate the tree-outsider\u2019s hidden roots, and then the group set explosives to destroy them. They succeeded, and that is what collapsed the basement. With its roots destroyed, the outsider could finally be killed, so the group fought it in the hotel yard. They were not prepared for its influence, however, and they fell to jealous in-fighting as it slaughtered them all save one, a woman named Cindy. It planted some sort of seed in her, forcing it down her throat and allowing her to escape alive. Sara seemed quite disturbed by the strength of emotion that lingered from the confrontation.<br /> <br /> Alexia did note that the face of the summoner was formed in the gnarled bark of the outsider\u2019s trunk amidst many others. Sadly, there is little we can do for him now.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve just drawn a bath, so I suppose it\u2019s time to drown myself a bit in order to recover some of my plasmic energy and then heal and rest until night falls.<br /> <br /> <br /> Saturday, October 23, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> We went to the bar again at night to find the last two ghosts, Thomas and Bertrand. I was responsible for luring Thomas into the pool room, so I sat and talked with him awhile in the bar. He was quite charming as always, though I\u2019m beginning to get the impression that he\u2019s too charming, if that makes any sense. I eventually convinced him that there was a party for guests going on at the pool, and expressed my surprise that he hadn\u2019t received an invitation. He was more than happy to accompany me to the party, however, and once we arrived in the pool, I took his hand and bled on him. Naturally, he was horrified to realize the truth of his current state, particularly when he saw Marvin\u2019s ghost. Though he had survived the axe blow that nearly killed him, it had paralyzed him from the waist down, and he still blamed Marvin, which convinced us that he really did believe Marvin killed Wynona. Not only had he encountered Marvin in the hedge maze just before he was attacked, but it also seems that Wynona thought Marvin had been following her. She had expressed her worry to Thomas, which is why he assumed Marvin was the murderer. Marvin denied ever stalking Wynona, and I\u2019m more inclined to believe him than her, as she has a rather egocentric and warped view of reality.<br /> <br /> Thomas had a hard time believing that Troy was the culprit, but eventually accepted it. Natalie sealed him in the room with the others. Then Alexia and Sara returned to the bar to gather Bertrand. Alexia used the code phrase Bertrand told her: \u201cIt\u2019s time to bring the end.\u201d He immediately understood and solemnly joined us in the pool room, where we bled on him and then sealed him inside as well.<br /> <br /> There was an odd moment of quiet disappointment then. I think we all expected the outsider to appear in a huge show of force once the last of its ghostly captives were torn away from it, but there was\u2026 nothing. Bertrand told us that the group who had fought it before kept notes on the beast, but once they were killed, it used Sandra to try and burn them. He was, however, able to rescue a few fragments, and they revealed a few means by which the weakened, vulnerable outsider might be summoned. Unfortunately neither method sat well with us.<br /> <br /> First, if someone dies under the effects of a vice, then the outsider will manifest in a spiritual reflection. Second, if people act very strongly in accordance with their vices, it will appear.<br /> <br /> Neither of those prospects were very appealing to us. We\u2019ve all had quite enough of our darker sides, and I for one don\u2019t want to kill myself in order to draw out our enemy.<br /> <br /> I suggested that Alexia examine the fireplace in which the notes were burned. She might be able to gain glimpses of the past in which she could see more fragments of the notes before they were claimed by the fire. Bertrand showed us the place and Alexia unlocked her Oracle again, and she found that there was yet another option.<br /> <br /> If two people earnestly overcome some sort of vice-ridden conflict between them, then it will anger the outsider, causing it to manifest. We all looked at Doc and Natalie at that. It\u2019s no secret that their doomed romantic relationship and Doc\u2019s tendency to be possessive of Natalie has made their friendship very tense of late, and the trouble has only fueled Doc\u2019s frustration and anger to the extent that Natalie is honestly frightened of him.<br /> <br /> Doc sighed and nodded, realizing that he finally needed to put aside his anger and come to terms with the fact that he and Natalie are close friends and nothing more. It was a touching moment. Doc\u2019s apology was heartfelt and true, and I could sense the simmering fires of his rage subside. He even admitted that he had no reason to be angry anymore. He\u2019s happy with Noriko and he still cares deeply for Natalie, and she for him. Natalie apologized for her selfishness in everything. Yes, her emotional issues are partly to blame, but she had to take some responsibility for hurting Doc, and I for one was glad to hear her do so. I know it was hard for both of them, but as they finally forgave each other and embraced, the hotel shuddered and there was a terrible groan from the lobby. It sounded like the roar of a hundred creaking trees. The outsider had arrived.<br /> <br /> We rushed out to face it. Doc tossed Troy\u2019s bottle against a wall and Troy swirled out of it, rapidly coalescing and ready to fight. Then I snatched Mr. Ox\u2019s doll head from my belt and tore at its hair. It unleashed a bone-chilling scream, and the outsider shuddered as though every part of it was struck with utter agony. Unfortunately, Troy reacted the same way. He fell to his knees paralyzed by pain. I felt bad about that. We should have waited to smash the bottle, I suppose. In any event, we took advantage of the outsider\u2019s distress to attack it brutally. The creature was immense, filling all three stories of the lobby. Heavy, cocoon-like pods grew within each of its tentacle branches, and we could tell that each pod held the essence of one of the hotel\u2019s ghosts. Countless faces screamed with wooden groans from its trunk. Natalie sank into the earth with her Grave-Dirt Boneyard and began throwing chunks of rubble from the basement at it, denting its tough, bark-covered hide. Sara flitted about like pyre-flame in her Caul, stabbing deeply the remnants of its roots. Chips of bloody, wooden flesh flew away as her knife plunged again and again. Clad in my Primeval Caul and Shroud, I leapt into its branches and slashed at them with my fierce claws, but the thing\u2019s bark was so tough that even with my great strength, I struggled to pierce it. Doc unleashed his fiery wrath on the thing, blasting it with fire and using his Rage to tear open its bark so that its thick blood ran free. Alexia, however, was most impressive. She was clad in her Phantasmal Caul and wielded heavy cleavers in each hand. Her many arms hacked away at the beast\u2019s trunk, carving deep wounds.<br /> <br /> The outsider managed to shrug off the effects of the doll\u2019s head far sooner than we expected, but by then it was too late. It lashed out at us, but to little effect, as we literally tore it limb from limb. Its body fell apart and disintegrated, leaving only a shriveled husk in Twilight. Doc took care of that by stepping into Twilight and hacking at the husk with Troy\u2019s axe until it was nothing more than splinters. Even then he kept at it. It was cathartic, I think, and Doc needed an outlet for his anger. I hope that he\u2019s a bit calmer after this.<br /> <br /> Troy recovered from the paralyzing effects of the doll\u2019s head and accompanied the rest of us to the pool room to check on the ghosts. I apologized for putting him through such agony, but he shrugged it off. He understood, and the important thing was that the outsider had been destroyed.<br /> <br /> The back door of the pool room was open, and a soft light shone from it. Only Molly, Yvette, Sandra, Bertrand, and Wynona remained. The others had already departed though the door as soon as the outsider was killed, and I slightly regretted being unable to say goodbye to William. Molly came to thank us for helping her as we entered, and after she did that, she turned and walked calmly through the glowing doorway. Tears of joy welled in her eyes as she turned to walk out, and I was glad to see that there was no more fear lurking in her eyes.<br /> <br /> Once Molly left, Yvette sighed as though a great weight were lifted from her, and she too walked out the doors and disappeared into the light, no longer shackled by guilt. Bertrand lingered a bit longer. He was concerned about the hotel, but we assured him that it would reopen now that the horror was over. He seemed satisfied, and then he too passed on.<br /> <br /> Troy, Sandra and Wynona, however, made no move toward the door. Wynona seemed frightened of it, honestly. She seems to think that eternal damnation awaits her if she passes through it, and she may be right. At the very least, her she has a bit of karmic cleansing to undergo, and her next incarnation probably won\u2019t be so posh. Troy, on the other hand, just seemed comfortable where he is. I don\u2019t know what, if anything, is holding him here. Maybe nothing. But he doesn\u2019t seem ready to pass on yet. I\u2019m not sure what will become of him, but we need to discuss it before we leave the hotel. And as for Sandra, I\u2019m afraid she\u2019s too attached to Natalie to move on now, and that\u2019s not good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <u>Spreading Seeds </u><br /> <br /> I fear we need to find Cindy quickly. The outsider was certainly trying to create another of its kind by planting its seed pod in her, and we fear that it will germinate inside her and grow a new terror elsewhere if we don\u2019t stop it. It may already be too late.<br /> <br /> <u><br /> No Prejudice </u><br /> <br /> William Gibson was quite upset to learn that Marvin had been wrongly accused, and I almost feared he would attack Thomas. So while Doc checked on Marvin to make sure he was okay, I spoke with William. He and Marvin has struck up a friendship, and seem to be getting along famously. William told me that he respects people of other races. He was raised by a black nanny, and she was as much a mother to him as his biological mother. He learned from her that racial differences exist only in the mind, and we\u2019re all people just the same. It was pleasant to hear that someone from his time held such a view. Having suffered a bit of prejudice when I was younger in Taiwan because I\u2019m half Kiwi, I found William\u2019s outlook quite pleasant and refreshing. I think I would have liked William very much when he was alive, and I regret that we couldn\u2019t spend more time together. The Bride seemed quite taken with him as well. He\u2019s no Karl, though, and I do look forward to getting back to Dark Haven Bluffs and my boyfriend again.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CII</i><br /> <br /> The Creature was not actually an Outsider, though Jasmine\u2019s believing that is understandable given her past. It was a powerful Underworld tainted Spirit which had been summoned and took control of the hotel. <br /> <br /> Beyond that, my comment is 5 armor is incredibly powerful under GMC rules. Those with high Shroud were Juggernaught, shrugging off a great deal of damage like nothing, even this thing which could all but one shot normal people. Granted, paralyzing it for five turns while they wailed on it helped, but in the battle Doc took 1 Bashing from damage his armor stopped and that is it. I generally prefer GMC combat to the original New WoD combat but I am unsure if I will use it in future Geist games.<br /> <br /> Still some loose ends but all in all a fairly satisfying ending. Let me know if you need clarification about anything.<br /> <br /> Last night\u2019s session was a little shorter, as Doc\u2019s player was late and Jasmine\u2019s player was sick so we waited to start till Doc\u2019s player arrived. We still covered Sunday, and some general settling back in. Expect some journals about that in two weeks, including at least one major personal milestone for a member of the Krewe. See you then, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T03:32:33-07:00","id":98238,"title":"","content":"I admit, I wasn't expecting a plant. Good job Herr Baron.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-25T16:55:56-07:00","id":98774,"title":"","content":"Well, it was a metaphoric thing for growing stronger on the dead. Ultimatly, the look of the spirit was less critical than the story of dealing with the ghosts. Once they worked their way through helping the ghosts and facing their vices, the battle and spirit was really a capstone, not the climax.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T02:12:44-07:00","id":99030,"title":"","content":"I see. Would Lily have been able to tare the dolls hair? When I read Doc's log I misread that part and thought she had. It was an interesting image.<br /> <br /> Unrelated question: What is the longest thing you've written?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-26T12:41:27-07:00","id":99425,"title":"","content":"I am not sure if she would have. Probably with effort and a little use of simple tools.<br /> <br /> The longest thing I have written was probably my Pathfinder for Graduate School.. The Longest thing I have written professionally is my part of Mortal Remains at about 20K words, but I am just getting started.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-27T16:33:51-07:00","id":100459,"title":"","content":"Maybe if she grabbed with both stumps and braced with her legs?<br /> <br /> That certainly sounds intimidating. Any tricks or advise on how to write something that long?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:52:43-07:00","id":107093,"title":"","content":"Omenseer: Not really, beyond don't write it at once and, if possible, have other pairs of eyes go over it behind you.<br /> <br /> Quiet session. Jasmine\u2019s player was under the weather, so Doc\u2019s log has the actual events of the session. It was short regardless, Jasmine and Simon both being missing and Doc\u2019s player was delayed getting there. Still, enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0145 Hours, Sunday, October 24, 2010<br /> <br /> We canvassed the rest of the hotel before finally deeming it safe. Then everything was loaded up, including our three new friends, and we headed back to the Bluffs. We got here around 0100 Hours and the whole house emptied to help us unload.<br /> <br /> Gretchen managed to ambush me as I came in with my last load. I hadn\u2019t forgotten she wanted to ask me something, but this didn\u2019t bode well. And as usual, Gretchen lived up to her reputation. Her question, cleaned up enough that I will dain to write it, regarded if Asian women were...situated differently than caucasian women. I blinked for longer than usual trying to keep from laughing or getting pissed off. I opted for a different approach and asked if she had ever been with another woman before? She hadn\u2019t, which honestly surprised me a little, so I told her to get back to me after she had. Then I walked away.<br /> <br /> While Rose gave our new tenants the grand tour, I went to my room and called Noriko. She should be here soon, which will be very nice. Assuming Gretchen doesn\u2019t say something incredibly unfortunate.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Sunday, October 24, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s incredibly relaxing to be home again. I left Noriko in bed around 0800 Hours and went to meditate. That was long overdue. After several false starts, I was finally able to center myself after about an hour. Then I went back to coax the sleepy purring woman out of bed and down to breakfast.<br /> <br /> Hopefully today continues on this way. I don\u2019t know of anything we need to do before we talk with Becky later. Plus I get to hang out with Noriko and be lazy all morning.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1500 Hours, Sunday, October 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Around 1400 Hours, Bright Eyes came to ask me about getting some tattoos. Noriko didn\u2019t really know I could do that, so we all sat down and talked through the process. I knew that Bright Eyes used tattoos and body modification to mark major events in her life so I was interested in helping. I was a little surprised at what she told me however.<br /> <br /> My acceptance of the split between Nightshade and I removed a huge weight I didn\u2019t realize I was carrying. And after we killed the creature that tried to wield my anger like a weapon, I noticed how much easier it was to keep the edge off of my rage. I also realized how dramatic I get when I\u2019m writing about a fight after reading over my entries from the hotel...but that\u2019s an issue to work on for another time. The point is, I don\u2019t feel the constant blade of white hot rage searing against my nerves all the time now. So when Bright Eyes came to me with the idea to use the Mpatapo to represent the events at the hotel, I was pretty impressed and a little moved. The African knot was a symbol of reconciliation, of peacemaking after strife. This she wanted on her forearm. The other request came with pictures for reference. She wanted three rings, all linked. These she wanted on her upper left arm. The forearm was where she remembered important ghostly events, but the upper arm was for major personal life events. It was then that I realized one of the rings was hers. She admitted to me that she, Nightshade, and Karen had handfasted last night and planned to have a formal marriage ceremony sometime in the future. That was a very big deal and I was honored both that she told me and that she wanted me to ink the tattoo. I immediately got my sketch pad out and marked off a space to size my template. Once I was satisfied with my sketches, I showed them to Bright Eyes. Noriko took the whole process in with interest but said very little. I\u2019m a little bit of a perfectionist so it took a little longer than it could have, but Bright Eyes was very happy with my work. I don\u2019t think Noriko realized I could draw.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1945 Hours, Sunday, October 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade called Becky, much to Karen\u2019s irritation, around 1500 Hours to setup a meeting at her townhouse. We met at 1800 Hours and confirmed that there were no more ghosts in the Hidden Hillside Hotel. She said that she would talk to her aunt and that after some time went by with no more hauntings, she would pay us. Six months sounds like forever for payment, but I can understand the desire to be sure.<br /> <br /> We came back and I informed the Krewe that I had a plan for a new picture, one that I wanted to give to the hotel. I plan to sketch each of the ghosts which had been trapped there separately with room to include their names under the image. The images would go from left to right with the \u201820s first, then \u201840s, and finally the \u201860s. Of course, Troy would be in the center of all the images. In this way, the ghosts that were the most closely tied, by choice or otherwise, could always be remembered. They could keep the picture at the front desk so everyone could see it at check in and check out. Everyone thought this was a great idea so I\u2019ll need to look into getting a proper drafting board and any other equipment I might need to do this the right way. Then I\u2019ll ask Snowflake for a custom frame before I donate it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, October 24, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> It is wonderful to be back home again. I\u2019m pleased that we were able to resolve things there so handily, though I do still worry that the seed pod the outsider planted in that woman is germinating somewhere even now. I suppose we will have to try and track her down somehow, though I haven\u2019t the foggiest notion how we might go about that. Perhaps Becky might be able to help. Sadly, Karl is not back from Cold Harbor yet. He should be getting back in a few hours, and after everything I\u2019ve gone through over the past few days, I\u2019m looking forward to a good night\u2019s sleep with him beside me. I suppose I am feeling a bit lonesome right now, but aside from that I\u2019m simply elated over helping all of the ghosts who were trapped in the hotel. It\u2019s not often I feel this content and\u2026happy\u2026though the feeling is becoming more common now that I\u2019m in love with Karl.<br /> <br /> We did not return to Dark Haven Bluffs alone. Troy, Sandra and Wynona all returned with us, as they were the only ghosts who did not pass on. We couldn\u2019t exactly leave them at the hotel since we had promised to rid the place of its haunting, but I confess that I am unhappy about adopting them all. Despite that, it somehow fell to me to show them around the house and get them situated in their new home.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really mind Troy. He is earnest and charming, and I like him immensely despite myself. It would be best if he would move on and return to the karmic cycle, but his company is welcome, and I think it will be nice to have another man in the household.<br /> <br /> Sandra and Wynona are another matter. Wynona is eccentric and amusing, but she easily annoys me. Even a large house like Dark Haven Bluffs can become crowded, especially when it is full of so many bewildering personalities. Thanks to Tavia, Gretchen, and Chandra, things are already frustratingly chaotic and distracting at times, and I fear\u2026no, I know\u2026that Wynona will only make things worse.<br /> <br /> Sandra is a completely different matter. I\u2019m upset that she is moving in with us because she should have passed on already when we destroyed the outsider. Unfortunately, her blossoming interest in Natalie has anchored her here, or so it seems. I know that Natalie did not intend to awaken such feelings in Sandra, but she did, and now Sandra\u2019s lingering on pointlessly. I feel sorry for her, and I am annoyed with the situation, but since Sandra is drawn to Natalie, there\u2019s very little I can do about it. I can only hope that Natalie takes responsibility and helps resolve Sandra soon.<br /> <br /> I prepared rooms for our new guests and helped them settle in, a process that included all the standard warnings and an extensive explanation of the rules, which I\u2019m sure Wynona found quite tiresome. If she ignores what I said and wanders into something dangerous, she only has herself to blame. Anyway, I put all the ghosts in rooms on the fourth floor. Troy occupies a room on the west wing, across the hall from the Foreigner Eating Bedroom. Sandra and Wynona are in the east wing, Sandra in the back of the house with a room that opens onto the small widow\u2019s walk there, and Wynona across the hall in the front of the house. Hopefully they will be comfortable there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -I am no longer alone, physically, spiritually, or emotionally.<br /> <br /> -I am happy.<br /> <br /> -&lt;3<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CIV</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add here. Should have Jazzy back tonight. Sadly still no Simon for awhile but he still plans to be back when he can.<br /> <br /> WoD fans should note I am starting a Changeling: The Lost campaign \u201cMalibu Dream House\u201d and putting backgrounds up. Session 1 journals go up on Saturday, link for the campaign is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\">here</a> . Also as a reminder, for those with an appetite for both there is a Masquerade game going on, &quot;The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora&quot;, with APs, link is <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-06-2014, 05:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T02:53:07-07:00","id":116426,"title":"","content":"Back on track with Geist. This session was largely planning, but still, let\u2019s check in on the Middle Shadows.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Monday, October 25, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation went well this morning and I was on my way only half an hour later. After breakfast, I went into the shop to confirm everything was on schedule for Nightshade\u2019s birthday present. I guess with everything that\u2019s been going on I forgot to mention it. I located a foundry that was willing to custom forge to my specs. So I have a silver-plated athame with a poison ring well in the pommel. Shifting the cross guard will allow whatever is in the pommel to reach the blade through channels in the hilt.<br /> <br /> Now that I\u2019m satisfied the shipping dates are accurate, I\u2019m going to clean up the tattoo stations for Bright Eyes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1950 Hours, Monday, October 25, 2010<br /> <br /> Cupcake found something called Craig\u2019s List today. She was trying to find ways online to track the mysterious Cindy. I\u2019ve heard of Craig\u2019s List, but it\u2019s not something I would have any reason to deal with. Nightshade was working on getting some leads as well, but she is more accomplished online so she has gotten a little farther.<br /> <br /> I brought up the Underworld trip that needs to be pending. I think I surprised Rose with that. But after all that\u2019s happened at the hotel, The Dog and I are feeling closer. Maybe not much more in sync, but closer. I\u2019m very interested in checking out this pirate ship in the Underworld too. Rose mentioned that she needed to talk with Mr. Ox. I think she plans to burn some Hell Money with a message for him tonight. Then tomorrow she is going to purchase our scuba gear. I suggested that she get 10 sets. She looked at me like I was nuts, but I pointed out that we could possibly want to take friends with us for non-mission based events. Things that involve fun. She took the joke quietly but agreed to arrange for 10.<br /> <br /> Chandra approached me just after dinner. She told me that she wanted a navel ring and asked if I could do the piercing. I told her she just needed to pick out the stud and whatever she wanted to use once the piercing healed.<br /> <br /> With scuba gear coming and Nightshade\u2019s birthday in two days, I realized that I need to get the van together ASAP.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Tuesday, October 26, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m really not sure where the night went. I guess I just fell asleep like normal people do.<br /> <br /> I can tell we\u2019re back home again though. Meditation took an hour this morning. Complacency breeds contempt, I guess. Everyone is falling back into their routines now too. It really feels like we were away for weeks, but it was only a weekend.<br /> <br /> Chandra found me after breakfast and asked about the navel ring. We agreed to meet here after she can Cupcake get back from shopping for the stud and final piece. Until then, I\u2019m going to be getting some detailing and fine tuning down on the van.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1745 Hours, Tuesday, October 26, 2010<br /> <br /> I was crawling over, around, under, and through the van until late this afternoon before Cupcake and Chandra got home. I got cleaned up then we headed over to the shop. She was surprisingly nervous for someone that can remove her own head. Since they were out all day, we brought home take out for dinner.<br /> <br /> Rose had more news and it wasn\u2019t good. Mr. Ox is looking out for us again. He let us know that Bone Dry has summoned four very powerful spirits of vice and bound them into bodies. After what we just finished, more vice creatures almost gave me flashbacks. To make it worse, these are made more dangerous for having bodies. These aren\u2019t normal spirits and Mr. Ox said that it was both difficult and risky for Bone Dry to deal with them. That suggests that he is no longer underestimating us and is looking for a fight. They also have magic summoning circles in several locations to which they can simply teleport if contacted. The four spirits don\u2019t know everything, so if we kill communications first, then damage the circles, they will have to learn something is wrong, then travel like everyone else. Not perfect, but it buys us some time to wipe out the book shop. That has easily taken priority over the Underworld trip for now.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll need to send Rose in invisibly to damage the circle, while we cut any other forms of communication, then level the place. I definitely want one of the books to study before we torch everything, but then we have to get the hell out<br /> <br /> Another interesting note from Rose today is that she found a little girl that can see the truth, or at least, can see what people are. She ran up to Rose after Mr. Ox left and told her not to go near that man as he was made of people. That was pretty terrifying and I\u2019m glad I didn\u2019t look any harder. Still, I know how hard it is to be a kid and see things that no one else can. Her mother is a student at AMC and apologized for her daughter\u2019s imagination. Rose tried to convince her that she should listen to her child when she says things like that. Unsurprisingly, the mother led her child away from the woman suggesting monsters were real. Rose really has no business speaking to normal people.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so our week looks mostly full. Today was get the scuba gear. Tomorrow is Nightshade\u2019s birthday so we will be celebrating her life for most of the day, as well as some basic scuba training. Then once everyone has recovered, we\u2019ll have more in depth training and a book burning of sorts on Thursday. But it will probably be Friday in Hong Kong so that just jumbles everything up. Now I need to see what everyone else is doing tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Monday, October 25, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> I called Rita last night while I was waiting for Karl to get home. She and Jean are doing fine, and are positively giddy about being in love. She seems to be in control of her urges now, which is good, but I suggested that we continue meditating with tai chi in the mornings.<br /> <br /> Karl was surprised to see me home already, but very pleased. It was nice to spend a night at home snuggled up with him in our room after all we\u2019ve been through lately. I think it\u2019s the soundest sleep I\u2019ve had in weeks.<br /> <br /> When I went in for Jean\u2019s training session this morning, I found that he was just as happy as Rita about their relationship, though there is one thing that worries him. Rita keeps trying to work up the courage to tell him what she really is, and she\u2019s hinted that she has something to talk to him about, but never gets around to it. I think it\u2019s probably good for her the ease into things, but Jean\u2019s becoming anxious about whatever it is she has to tell him. I told him not to worry. Rita\u2019s a wonderful girl, and she\u2019ll tell him whenever she\u2019s ready. I don\u2019t think it helped, but maybe he\u2019ll at least be patient with her.<br /> <br /> Since Natalie\u2019s birthday is on Wednesday, I went out after work to pick up a nice collection of sheet music from the 20\u2019s and 30\u2019s that I think she will like. She enjoys playing piano pieces from that era, so I hope she will find it comforting. Afterward, I returned to campus to see if I couldn\u2019t research Cindy, the hunter in whom the tree outsider from the hotel implanted a seed pod. She seemed to be ex-military, but I didn\u2019t have any luck searching through recent newspapers. Perhaps the others will know of a better approach.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, October 25, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> Karl and I went out swimming this evening. It was wonderful. We ended up in our secret undersea grotto and spent some time there enjoying one another\u2019s company and making love. We were a bit late getting back for dinner, but Alexia wasn\u2019t cross with us.<br /> <br /> Over dinner, the krewe discussed our next plans. Doc is eager to sort things with Pup Pid in the Underworld. I already have my arrangement with the Lighthouse Keeper, but the others need places to stay as well. Alexia seemed to assume she could stay at my place in the lighthouse whenever she reaches the point when she needs to spend time in the Underworld, and I certainly don\u2019t have a problem sharing with her. But I can\u2019t really host everyone, particularly since my deal with the Lighthouse Keeper applies only to me. Doc seems very eager to resurrect Pup Pid\u2019s sunken pirate ship and turn it into a haven, and I would like to rid the seas of the pirate creature, if only to make things easier on the Lighthouse Keeper.<br /> <br /> To that end, I\u2019ll be purchasing SCUBA gear for all of us tomorrow. I have experience SCUBA diving, so I\u2019ll need to give the others a bit of training if they are going to use the equipment to explore the Underworld shipwreck. We will take care of that this week.<br /> <br /> I also needed to get in touch with Uncle Ox, so I performed an ancestor honoring ritual and burned some hell money in order to summon him. I suspect he will show up some time tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Tuesday, October 26, 2010, Afternoon<br /> <br /> If I didn\u2019t know any better, I\u2019d think Uncle Ox likes seeing me in my swimsuit. He showed up at the Albertus Magnus swimming pool again today, patiently waiting for me to finish working with Jean. I went to speak with him, and he shared some very important information with me.<br /> <br /> Bone Dry has summoned four powerful spirits to defend his assets. They represent various sins, and are violent and dangerous. They can kill people to become more powerful for a time, so if they know we are coming, they will murder as many people as they can to prepare. We cannot allow that. Fortunately, the spirits are not omnipresent. They move between Bone Dry\u2019s various operations, so if we are careful, we can avoid them, at least for the time being. However, Uncle Ox warned me that there is a mystic circle in the warehouse in Hong Kong where Bone Dry is publishing his false immortality manuals, and the four spirits can transport themselves to the circle very quickly if there is trouble there. That means we will need to damage and deactivate the circle before we attack and find a way to interfere with or cut off any phones that are there so no one can call for help.<br /> <br /> If the four spirits are beaten, they will return to shadow and must be summoned and bound again if Bone Dry wishes to retain their services, and Uncle Ox assures me that is not something that is easy for Bone Dry to accomplish. The fact that he summoned them in the first place implies that he is scared and desperate. And while it is possible to destroy Bone Dry\u2019s control over them, that would free them to rampage throughout the world, and we cannot allow that either.<br /> <br /> I asked how we would know the spirits when we saw them, and Uncle Ox simply told me that we would know. They reek of death and though they look mostly human, they will be unmistakable.<br /> <br /> After Uncle Ox left, a little girl approached me. Her name was Lucy Johnson. She warned me that the man I had been talking to was a really a scary monster. I was shocked that she could see him as he really was, or at least something close to it, and even more shocked that the girl was handling it so well. I suspected that she must see things like this from time to time, and my suspicion was confirmed when her mother, Alice, arrived and apologized for her daughter\u2019s vivid imagination. I tried to tell Alice that some people see things others do not, and that she should listen to her daughter when she speaks of the things she sees. That really wasn\u2019t the right thing to say, and Alice hurried Lucy away. At least Lucy seemed to trust me. If she ever sees anything really scary, I hope she\u2019ll find a way to let me know.<br /> <br /> I discussed Uncle Ox\u2019s information with the others over dinner, and I think we\u2019ve decided to eliminate Bone Dry\u2019s publishing house in Hong Kong before we go to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Surfboards </u><br /> <br /> Sara and I went to the SCUBA and surf shop to pick up our order of SCUBA gear this afternoon after I returned from work. We took her station wagon since my Beetle doesn\u2019t have room for all the gear.<br /> <br /> While there, I talked to the clerk about surf boards. I used to surf quite a bit in Taiwan, often with Richard. Both my board and his are in storage at my father\u2019s home, but I thought it would be nice to get Karl a board so that he and I can go surfing at Green Bay or Daxi or any of the other good surf beaches in Taiwan. I spent about an hour discussing the details and placed an order before I left. I told Sara to keep it a secret; I plan to surprise Karl with the surfboard as a gift! I know he has surfed before, but only a little. He seemed eager to give it a try when I suggested we should go surfing some time, though, so I think he will appreciate having a board of his own.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -Tonight I broke a promise to a gun. Keeping a promise to two wonderful women who mean more to me than life itself, and a man who is so very important to me, was much more important.<br /> <br /> -&lt;3<br /> <i><br /> End Session CV</i><br /> <br /> The creatures summoned are Vice Spirits. I am playing a bit fast and loose with some of the rules in Book of Spirits and Inferno to create potent and useful Antagonists here. They are not connected with the Abyss.<br /> <br /> I think about covers it. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T09:24:34-07:00","id":116539,"title":"","content":"Broke a promise to a gun?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T12:21:37-07:00","id":116627,"title":"","content":"Natalie bought the pistol to shoot herself on her 30th birthday so she would not get old, something she fears greatly. It's part of why early on especially she was looking for the Codex to not age. She was not quiet about this, but noted she was reconsidering.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 04-20-2014, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-20T20:01:25-07:00","id":116809,"title":"","content":"Oooh, o.k. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-04T13:24:04-07:00","id":125319,"title":"","content":"We return to our Krewe, in which they pause to celebrate a birthday and deal with fallout from matchmaking..<br /> <br /> <i>Session CVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc's Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Wednesday, October 27, 2010<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t go out on patrol last night and I didn\u2019t call Noriko over because I needed to be available at midnight just in case. Today is Nightshade\u2019s 30th birthday. Though things got a little tense, nothing happened that they needed medical attention to correct, so I call it a win.<br /> <br /> Once I felt things were as normalized as it could be, I went to bed. Today is a big day after all. I was up by 0700 Hours and meditation was a breeze. By 0800 Hours, I was downstairs to make sure no one needed help with anything. We were all assembled by 0900 Hours and the birthday party started. It was surreal that Nightshade was willfully awake at that time of day on her birthday, but she seemed in good spirits.<br /> <br /> Cupcake made the Strawberry Birthday Breakfast as part of her present. Tons of crepes and strawberries with everything you can think of to add if we wanted. I even \u201cinvented\u201d a new Strawberry Shortcake character. The happy morning conversation was mostly directed to and about Nightshade and Strawberry Deathcake came up. Someone mentioned a doll with batwings. I declared that the gothic character would have to be Blackberry Tart, in full \u201ctraditional\u201d goth gear with the batwings and all. This I think set the tone for the day.<br /> <br /> My present is in a black faux wood box with a crimson bow tied around it. I think everyone else is getting their presents and bathing suits together. We\u2019ll be shoving off in about an hour so I guess I should gather up my own clothes for the party.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2245 Hours, Wednesday, October 27, 2010<br /> <br /> The party\u2019s being going all day and everybody is happy. Hopefully things continue that way, but the phone call Rose got has kind of threatened that. But that happened last so I\u2019ll get to it.<br /> <br /> Once we got out on the yacht, the party actually started. Before the dancing and the drinking started too much, Cupcake handed everyone a tall, fluted champagne glass. Inside was a blood red mixed drink that smelled of strawberries. We learned that she had made a Chocolate Strawberry margarita. So long as Nightshade approved, it would be named after her and sold in Cupcake\u2019s shop. That was pretty awesome and Nightshade happily approved after drinking it. The rest of the presents and several of the bathing suits came out after that. I gave my present and Nightshade\u2019s eyes got wide. I\u2019m pretty sure she liked it. Also pretty sure Karen wanted to steal it. That just means I did good. Tavia and family got her some custom made black leather thigh high boots with stylized symbols running down the side. Bright Eyes had been working on several herbal teas recently as she\u2019d gotten several things from my shop. Different teas were for different things. That and teas are classy. Rose found some \u201820s sheet music on piano. I honestly don\u2019t remember the titles but it made Nightshade happy, so that\u2019s all that matters.<br /> <br /> Presents opened, everyone who hadn\u2019t changed into their bathing suits already, did so. Scuba practice began with Rose fighting not to chastise the alcohol consumption as she helped everyone understand how the gear worked. We learned how to wear the equipment as well as how to maintain it. I quietly noted that Rose made sure it took a little more than half an hour to explain all this. I didn\u2019t mention it, but I was amused that she still followed the 30 minutes after food before swimming rule. Once she was satisfied with our understanding of the tanks, we hit the water. Rose was being overly cautious, sending us down in pairs, but it did highlight that she was a good teacher and paid attention to details. Screwing this up for normal people can kill them. I had some very rudimentary scuba experience from the Navy, but it had been years and I never got the chance to practice. This was very helpful and we were glad for Rose to show us how it all worked. The party continued as different people took turns going back down and others just partied on the boat. No one got more than tipsy since Cupcake planned to take us out for dinner as well.<br /> <br /> We got back to Dark Haven Bluffs around 1700 Hours to clean up. Our reservations were for 1900 Hours and it was Italian that was Cupcake approved. I called Noriko over and let her know that we were getting a little dressed up for dinner. Having another beautiful woman in the party didn\u2019t upset anyone, and we had enough room so I think Cupcake assumed she was coming anyway. The food was great and the company excellent. About midway through the third course, Rose got a call from Jean. She was trying to be nonchalant about it, but we all realized that something was wrong. When she got off the phone, Rose apologized and said she had to leave. I knew she was going to check on Jean, so I assumed it had something to do with Rita. I asked if they needed any help. Rose knew immediately I was offering first aid, but said she\u2019d call if things were bad. I haven\u2019t heard anything but Rose still isn\u2019t bad either. I\u2019m going to get back to the party now, but hopefully I\u2019ll know more soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Thursday, October 28, 2010<br /> <br /> Well in good news, Nightshade made it through her birthday without any overt breakdowns or suicide attempts. Her party was fun and she was surrounded by what she calls her family. She even talked to Belladonna at one point. In that respect, today was a smash hit.<br /> <br /> The bad news is that Rita went all Jaws on Jean. If that were the only problem, then things would just be awkward. Jean is alive and will even keep his leg, thanks to some kind of healing bear from the Spring Court. The problem is, he\u2019s in shock and from all the descriptions I\u2019m hearing, is too terrified of the situation to run. I mean to learn that your girlfriend is a shark monster while having sex, have most of your leg eaten off, have your Olympic swim coach come and tell you everything will be okay, then have a bear some and use magic to heal your leg. Rita and Rose were worried that he would want to break up with her. I don\u2019t understand why he hasn\u2019t run screaming (literally or figuratively) into the night. I mean, okay. There is a chance Noriko could snap and do something like that, but I knew that going in. Rita did this because she had sex. She told us that was her concern from being a Siren back in the Hedge. And Jean was just a normal guy, not a Sin-Eater, not a vampire, not a nothing. Jean Q. Mortal. This is why we shouldn\u2019t let ghosts and humans mix. If she had told him beforehand and enchanted him like Grin did to Rose, that would be on him for still going along with it. Karen knew what she was getting into when she came into the house, but we at least taught her to use magic. I was (and still am) not happy about all this, so I called Grin to get an opinion from someone that\u2019s dealt with it before. He told me that Jean was strong willed and that was a good sign he\u2019d be fine as long as Rita didn\u2019t eat him. I just stared at the phone for a second before handing it to Gretchen while she and Tavia were banging pans.<br /> <br /> I had to walk away after that. Noriko came with me so I asked her if I was the one who was crazy. She knew I wasn\u2019t joking or happy so she thought about what to say for a few seconds. Finally she said I was crazy but as someone who goes crazier the longer they go without killing bad people, she might not be the best person to ask. I sighed and hugged her. That was fair. I just have to remember that every single Changeling is completely insane and work from that baseline. After that, I found some string and decided I\u2019d had enough bullshit for the night. Now I\u2019m going to use that string and not think about Changelings or anything else other than Noriko for a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Thursday, October 28, 2010<br /> <br /> When she finally opened one eye the morning, Noriko purred good morning. I was already up and about to go meditate. She opened the other eye and asked me how meditation worked. I wasn\u2019t expecting that, so I took her to the Meditation Room with me. I\u2019d never led a meditation before so that was I a little awkward but after about an hour, we both found our center.<br /> <br /> We got cleaned up and came down for breakfast. We were later than usual, but no one was upset. I learned from Rose that Jean was still alive, even after he spent the night with Rita. Now I\u2019m going to spend the rest of the morning and early afternoon waxing and polishing the van, then stocking the minibar. Once everyone else is home or awake, we\u2019ll go back out for more intense scuba training.<br /> <br /> Rose stopped out in the carriage house while I was working to let me know Jean was \u201cbetter.\u201d I don\u2019t think she understands why I\u2019m not pleased by this. Especially since she said now that Jean knows about Rita, he wants to protect her from her Keeper. That boy has completely snapped and has no idea what he\u2019s suggesting. Rose is just thrilled that true love has prevailed. She was not at all amused when I mentioned Stockholm Syndrome however.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Jasmine\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 27, 2010, Evening<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s birthday was today, and we all went out to celebrate with a party on the yacht. Since Natalie likes strawberry things, Alexia made her a special alcoholic strawberry cocktail, which she plans to serve in her restaurant as a regular item named the Natalie Knight. Alexia is very sweet and thoughtful, though I didn\u2019t know her pastry shop had a liquor license. Doc gave her a beautiful custom-made ceremonial dagger that he had a hand in designing. Sara gave her a collection of hand-made herbals teas. Compared to all of those gifts crafted with loving care, my own gift of sheet music seemed rather pathetic in comparison.<br /> <br /> We spent some time practicing SCUBA diving while we were out on the ocean. Karen was quite good at it. We are getting ready to visit one of Alexia\u2019s upscale Italian restaurants for dinner. Karl and I are good to go, but of course, Natalie and Karen are taking a very long time getting ready, so I suppose we will have to wait a while longer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Wednesday, October 27, 2010, Late Night<br /> <br /> At dinner, I got a call from Jean. He sounded shaky, and told me that he had injured himself and wouldn\u2019t be able to train for a couple of days. Of course I immediately suspected that something had gone wrong with Rita, and my fears were confirmed when I got her on the phone and she explained that she had lost control and bitten Jean\u2019s leg rather badly. I excused myself from dinner with a quick word of explanation to the others and rushed to Rita\u2019s flat.<br /> <br /> Rita had not just bitten Jean, she had eaten a large chunk of his thigh. She was quite apologetic and was doing everything she could to make Jean feel comfortable and to keep him from sliding further into shock. I simply wondered how she had managed to eat so much of his leg without Jean beating her off. I did what I could for Jean\u2019s injury, and Rita assured me that she had called other help, a changeling who could perform miracles of healing. I asked if the damage could be completely repaired, because it was so extensive that any normal healing would leave severe muscle damage that would ruin Jean\u2019s professional career as a swimmer. Rita thought it would be as good as new.<br /> <br /> With that out of the way, the matter of their relationship remained. Jean understandably frightened of Rita, but he didn\u2019t want to leave her, and she certainly didn\u2019t want him to leave. I think she felt that if he left and was able to think through things without talking them over with her, he would become even more frightened and leave her. I wanted to point out the fact that she had nearly killed him. It all seemed like a terrible situation and I worried that I had made the wrong decision by introducing them to one another.<br /> <br /> But I chose not to say anything at the moment. I always seem to muddle things up when I start talking to people who aren\u2019t ghosts, and I didn\u2019t want to ruin things between Jean and Rita if they weren\u2019t ruined already. After all, Jean was obviously ensorcelled and could see Rita as she really was, and yet he still seemed attracted to her, so my geist and I felt we had no choice but to put our faith in true love, which was much easier for the Bride than it was for me.<br /> <br /> Once the healer arrived and all seemed well, I left with a few words of warning to Rita. However, I was concerned about Jean. I worried that he was only staying because he was frightened that Rita wouldn\u2019t let him leave. I returned to the manor, where I was greeted by Doc and Sara, both of whom were quite worried about the situation. I explained what had happened, and immediately realized that was a bad idea. Doc was furious, and made it quite clear that he was inclined to kill Rita because she was too dangerous. I tried to tell him that she has been struggling very hard to overcome her problems and has been making very good progress, the night\u2019s setback notwithstanding. Perhaps my faith in true love is misguided, but I wanted to give Rita and Jean a chance. But, Doc was rightly concerned that we might be gambling with Jean\u2019s life, so I decided to return to Rita\u2019s flat unseen to spy on her and Jean.<br /> <br /> It seems I needn\u2019t have been worried. Jean was healed as good as new, and he and Rita were in bed together, so I quickly left them to it. The Bride chided me a bit, all but saying, \u201cI told you so\u201d as we drove home.<br /> <br /> <br /> Thursday, October 28, 2010, Morning<br /> <br /> I called Jean this morning to make sure everything was okay, and he sounded fine. He was still a bit dazed and confused, though I got the distinct impression that had more to do with an amazing night of passion than any further mishaps. I suppose I should trust Rita. She is my friend, and I need to be supportive of her now even more than before. She\u2019s finally happy, which means a lot, so long as Jean is safe. And Jean seems to have accepted what Rita is and all that entails. Indeed, Rita says that it\u2019s all she can do to convince him not to go marching into the Hedge to protect her from her Keeper. He\u2019s so gallant!<br /> <br /> I reported everything to the others over breakfast. Doc still thinks Rita\u2019s too dangerous, but he\u2019s not planning anything drastic, thank goodness. It did occur to me, however, that Doc and I are similar in a way. We both have triggers that make us willing to kill. They may be different\u2014he is more likely to kill for the living, and I for the dead\u2014but we are more alike in that resolution than I think either of us would like to admit.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, of course, that I need to set up a meeting with Stanley\u2019s aunt soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <u>Footnotes</u><br /> <u><br /> Secret Identity </u><br /> <br /> Now that Jean knows about the supernatural, I think he should probably know that I\u2019m not what I seem. After all, he knows I\u2019m involved somehow. Doc, however, has a different opinion. He questioned why I wanted to \u201cout\u201d myself when in fact there\u2019s no reason for Jean to know anything about what I really am. It should be enough for him to know that I\u2019m a paranormal investigator with a few clever tricks up her sleeve. I suppose Doc is right. I do seem to have a hard time separating my supernatural life from my mundane, mortal life, which may be the root of my problems dealing with normal people. I\u2019ll take his advice for now.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CVI</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add. Changeling problems man.<br /> <br /> Focus was not as good on this session. Probably tired people\u2026it\u2019s the end of the semester and all, and a good chunk of the extended group are either college professors or staff, college/grad students, or school faculty\u2026very nearly the entire Geist group is.<br /> <br /> Well without much to comment on, I will just say I hope you enjoyed, and comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T01:41:17-07:00","id":142161,"title":"","content":"Just one journal this time. It\u2019s a doozy though. Let\u2019s check in.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CVII<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0015 Hours, Friday, October 29, 2010 (Hong Kong Time)<br /> <br /> The extended scuba lessons were put on hold in favor of shutting down Ye Olde Book Shoppe of Damnation. We didn\u2019t want to let Bone Dry get any more occultists tricked into becoming Hopping Vampire slaves before we could get things moving. The revelation of the vice spirits coming in as backup left a bad taste in everyone\u2019s mouth. As such, we left around 1130 Hours New Haven time. I brought a cheap plastic gas can as we all walked out from the wall of a very detailed mausoleum wall. An emaciated blonde vampire was reading in the solitude before we arrived. After watching people walk through a burial wall, she bolted. I tried to call after her in Chinese, but I realized that my limited Mandarin was really unhelpful in a place where they normally speak Cantonese.<br /> <br /> Once we walked out of the mausoleum, we could see the factory used for the book shop just down the street. Before we could walk very far, Rose stopped short and looked up into a tree on the sidewalk. She took a pair of keys from the lower branches. I couldn\u2019t read the script, but she translated for us. Bad Luck Farmer. Mr. Ox\u2019s handiwork. At least we know we can count on him.<br /> <br /> Nightshade scanned as much of the factory as she could through her Boneyard. There were four Jiang Shi and what looked like a prostitute with a cell phone spread between the two main rooms. The prostitute actually posed the greatest risk because we couldn\u2019t cut a line for her cell phone. Rose left us the keys then phased through the wall invisibly to finish scouting the shop. In a basement concealed by trapdoor, was the summoning circle. While she was looking, Bright Eyes and I realized we could solve all our problems with Pyre-Flame. We couldn\u2019t curse the prostitute until we saw her and that was too long to wait, but we could curse one of us. That would kill the lights, the cell phone, and any security systems we couldn\u2019t see. My Pyre-Flame Shroud would still allow us to see in the blackout and we could move from there. The major downside to this was that the ear curls would also be cut out. Rose also noted that the prostitute had two Deathmarks. They were both signs that she had been drained of blood but that was odd. Either way, we all made sure we knew the plan before our communication channel went down. Bright Eyes would curse Cupcake just before we entered while Rose would tackle the vampire with the cell phone. We could then come in the front door and deal with the Jiang Shi with our full group. Rose got in position in the basement so we could cut the phone line as she disrupted the circle. Then Bright Eyes cursed Cupcake and we rushed the door.<br /> <br /> The sounds of crashing water greeted us as we moved. When we got in, there was no prostitute but a purple winged monster flapping in the air. Three of the Jiang Shi were wet and on the far side of the room. I announced in my broken Mandarin to surrender or die, as we were still hoping to save as many of the Jiang Shi from slavery as possible. With that, I hurled a ghost flame fireball into a wooden chair. It sparked but fizzled due to the curse. That was enough for the three Jiang Shi though. The look of terror in their eyes told me they were in full frenzy as they bolted for the door. The purple thing turned out to be a shape changing Filipino vampire called an Aswang. I must have read about them while researching Chandra or something. Anyway, she didn\u2019t seem impressed with my little spark as she literally shrugged. The fourth Jiang Shi arrived but wasn\u2019t able to get to us. The Aswang decided that I was annoying or a threat or just didn\u2019t like my aftershave because she swooped in and hit me with some wicked claws. It stung a little, but I returned the favor by lighting her hand on fire for touching me. She shrieked as the Jiang Shi missed Bright Eyes. Rose rushed in and turned into her Shark Woman form. Thankfully Cupcake had grabbed the cell phone as Bright Eyes ended the curse. Nightshade immediately reported over the ear curl that someone was coming. Bright Eyes turned and ran for the door. I missed the Aswang with my hatefire just as a woman screamed something in Cantonese from outside. Rose translated that someone was rigged to explode. After that the ear curls went dead again but a rough and disturbing voice came to all of us that we could understand anyway.<br /> <br /> \u201cBlowing the place up? Let me help!\u201d<br /> <br /> Nothing happened immediately but the Aswang looked incredibly pissed off and flew through a window to escape. I flared up another spark to make the last Jiang Shi frenzy, then I headed outside. Rose was talking to the blonde vampire. Apparently the vice spirits had somehow controlled a random patsy to come here and kill us. The man wore a long coat to conceal 26 sticks of dynamite and a detonator. According to Nightshade, he hit the button after the voice came from his oddly open mouth but when nothing happened, the patsy was released. The poor man ran screaming down the street, ripping dynamite off as he went. I have since gathered that up for later use. I think I know of a great housewarming present for Bone Dry now coincidentally. I walked back inside and shoved the TNT into a duffle bag before joining them again.<br /> <br /> The vampire that helped us seemed just a little off and I suspected she was Nosferatu. Her name was Rotten Lily, which added to my suspicion. She told us that someone that sounded like one of the vice spirits killed all twelve Elders in a meeting he arrived, then named some nobody from Taiwan as Prince. I asked in my bad Chinese where the Sheriff was for all this, but she said he was one of the ones killed. It occurred to me that we could further weaken the vice spirits and Bone Dry by removing their hold on the local vampires. We agreed to go to Elysium and check it out, but not until we were finished here. I went back in and investigated the shop to make sure we weren\u2019t going to miss anything. I found three complete books and a box of various children\u2019s clothes. Looking at the box a moment longer, I realized that all the children were killed while they still wore the clothes. Downstairs, there were 16-30 round clips for an AK-47 waiting on a table next to the summoning circle. Those also went into the duffle bag. Then I told everyone to get out.<br /> <br /> I threw gas on all the equipment and all the walls before pouring a trail to the center of the floor. Then I turned the can over and let the gas pool. As I walked to the door, I struck a match and dropped it. Rotten Lily\u2019s eyes grew wide when my shadow came through the door with a wall of flame rising behind me. I\u2019m not sure if anyone else was aware, but my buttons had been pushed. The vice spirit double crossed the Aswang as she was obviously an outside merc, but more importantly, it tried to blow us up. I have died that way once. That was a very special moment, and not one that I will allow to be repeated. Now it\u2019s personal.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0200 Hours, Friday, October 29, 2010 (Hong Kong Time)<br /> <br /> We stashed the duffle bag back at the mausoleum then went with Lily to Elysium. That was an interesting word to translate. I wonder which dialect of Chinese the Sheriff back home speaks? Anyway, we spotted a woman in a similar trench coat as the man at the shop. She was standing in front of the main door trembling with a look of terror in her eyes. We decided that Lily should hide until we came back for her. With that taken care of (and her not responsible for what we were about to do with the Masquerade), we decided that play time was over. Rose changed back into Shark Woman, Bright Eyes ignited her Pyre-Flame Caul before cursing herself, then I armored up. The lights, elevator, even cars in what looked like about a 60 yard radius just stopped. We walked up and ripped the dynamite off the woman who screamed and ran away. Then up to the 7th floor. Cupcake moved to the heavy steel door and spoke to it with her Industrial Marionette. Just as the massive lock slid back, we heard a window break inside. Rose moved so fast I almost didn\u2019t see it. In what was almost one fluid motion, she dove through the window on our side of the door. As she floated amid the shards of broken glass, she shifted into a murder of crows that then spiraled around the building. I didn\u2019t say anything at the time, but that might have been the most bad ass and gothic thing I have ever seen. About 10 minutes later, she came back up the stairs with a vampire in a arm bar. Bright Eyes dropped the curse again so we were all aware that we would be playing Good Cop, Bad Cop, Worse Cop. Guess which one I got. Apparently Rose changed back into her human form while in the air and landed on him like something out of the Crow. I could hear Nightshade\u2019s pulse quicken. Rose and I could both speak to him while Bright Eyes was basically just trying to be intimidating. We didn\u2019t ask for a name at first, but we did learn that he was only about 40 years old. I may have made a comment about him living beyond tonight would depend on how useful he was. Definitely on the weak end of the scale for Prince, given that worked. I think Lynne and Truman called them Neonates. Anyway, he told us the vice spirit he answered to called himself Mr. Smile but there was another one that always wore a red suit. We got the phone number for Mr. Smile, but then I barked enough Mandarin to get a list of all the businesses owned by Bone Dry in Hong Kong. Yang Gong seemed more than ready to do anything we asked at that point. Before we could capitalize on that realization however, he burst into flames in the chair which Rose planted him. Bright Eyes and I almost cursed him to put the flames out but realized it had to be Bone Dry\u2019s supernatural powers, so Rose just grew her claws to put him out of his misery. There was a very pitiful look on her face as she ripped out the flaming vampire\u2019s throat. We\u2019re not very accustomed to mercy killings. But we didn\u2019t have time to think much more about it either. Nightshade got our attention after we made sure the vampire\u2019s corpse didn\u2019t set the rest of the building on fire. From her vantage point at the broken window, she could see the Road to Hell was now one of the shops on the street below. Now that I\u2019m done writing, we\u2019re all going to go down and see what Mr. Ox has to say.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CVII</i><br /> <br /> I am not sure what the situation will be with Jasmine journals for a bit. The player is burned out on doing them right now. We should have some Natalie journals picking up some of the slack, and maybe something from Sara, her player is considering options.<br /> <br /> I was struck while double-checking rules how incredibly little damage falling and explosives do in New WoD. The bomber originally had a couple sticks of dynamite, which would have done nothing to the PCs if they went off. It\u2019s not a complaint really, but the very rapid healing times (moreso than even much more gonzo games like Scion) and low damage from falls and explosions is somewhat boggling. But then, I am no expert on how damaging explosives really are in the real world.<br /> <br /> I was working with the Aswang from <i>Wicked Dead,</i> which seemed more sophisticated than the <i>Antagonists</i> ones.<br /> <br /> I will see folks next time, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:12:04-07:00","id":149740,"title":"","content":"*Plays a certain computer game* So... Which one of the krewe is the best Bad Luck Farmer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:19:07-07:00","id":149745,"title":"","content":"Well Jasmine is at the center of the &quot;Bad Luck Farmer&quot; stuff, so I'd say her.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:31:24-07:00","id":149757,"title":"","content":"A malkavian would have harvested bad luck today but a glitch not in his head happened and he couldn't get int the Blossom. Trying again later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T15:50:14-07:00","id":149763,"title":"","content":"Heh I am sorry. I think you might need a different quest to get in there and do that one...the one to rescue Kiki maybe? If you are looking for Bloodlines references by the way, It's not been made explicit but in Changeling Gawain lives above Trip's Pawnshop, and the Surfside diner has come up (though I am not sure it was mentioned in journal). Mr. Ox is a great character, and seemed a good twist to add some moral greyness to a black and white storyline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-26T22:31:11-07:00","id":150043,"title":"","content":"Very nice. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T03:10:08-07:00","id":150166,"title":"","content":"Now that i've had time to brain some more. Does that mean the events of Bloodlines occurred in your continuity, but presumably with the old world to new world conversions? What creature group then plays the part of Kuei-Jin? It is also implied that Balance and Dream House occur in the same continuity. Not surprising, but not really something you think about until a connecting element pops up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T11:45:45-07:00","id":150630,"title":"","content":"Mostly not. None of the people/places used in my games have been Vampires* or Ghouls, and that is a deliberate choice. I have used Mortal NPCs (well, only Trip so far) but nothing with Vampires (Asylum has not come up at all, and is not likely to. Plenty of real clubs in Santa Monica) so no, Bloodlines has nothing to do with my game really. Just someone (in <b>Changeling</b>) wanted a semi-crappy apartment in Santa Monica, and having it above the pawnshop seemed a fun reference. I do plan to have a reference that is a ship arriving without crew, but the events related to that are <b>Changeling-</b>specific, not <b>Vampire</b> specific...no vampires have anything to do with it whatsoever, unlike Bloodlines.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox is never actually fully explained what his deal is in Bloodlines. He is not Kuei-Jin, he is definitely not human or Kindred. I have an explanation for him in <b>Geist</b>, which is semi-New WoD specific. He is sort of a <b>Geist</b> thing. Sorta. Nothing specifically like him is discussed in <b>Geist</b> but...ah I'm not gonna give it away.<br /> <br /> The exception to this rule is my Vampire game, which is a different continuity than my New WoD games (<i>Balance of Shadows, Malibu Dream House, Brand New Key, Beyond the Sea</i>, the latter two of which never really got journaled). <i>The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</i> assumes Bloodlines happened. If it ever comes up, it assumes my Tremere Anarch playthrough of Bloodlines happened. Of course, <i>Conspiracy</i> is set in Prague, so there is no major impact from the game, though Nines Rodriguez is currently visiting the local Anarchs he is not a huge plot point, just a background thing in a city that is a major diplomatic hub.<br /> <br /> The major reason <i>Conspiracy</i> is a different continuity is <b>Requiem</b>-specific Vampires and terminology occurred in <i>Balance of Shadows, Malibu Dream House</i> (well, not yet but it will) and <i>Beyond the Sea</i>.<br /> <br /> Does all that make sense?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-27T14:13:33-07:00","id":150785,"title":"","content":"I think it does, but then again I think a lot of things <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-01T01:11:41-07:00","id":155541,"title":"","content":"Time for your regular update for Balance of Shadows. This time we have an entry for Doc and Sara, with a word from Sara\u2019s player on her journal. Natalie was planned but (dealt with) health issues got in the way so no journal from her this time.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Thursday, October 28, 2010<br /> <br /> I hate international time zones. We left this afternoon and after about 7 hours of Black Ops and interrogation, we came back tonight. Alaska would not do me any favors.<br /> <br /> But I might just be a little jumpy. Let\u2019s start again.<br /> <br /> We left the smouldering corpse, headed down to street level, and into The Road to Hell. There we found a serene Mr. Ox waiting as usual. After the honorifics and my broken attempts at greetings, Mr. Ox let us know that he was both happy and concerned. While we were shaking down Bone Dry\u2019s publishing shop, Mr. Ox was running reconn and intel for us. What he found surprised me. Bone Dry was reaching towards powers that were even unsafe for him. He didn\u2019t know we could reach his operations in Hong Kong and he is having one hell of a time trying to learn who we are. This is good because he if finds us, we\u2019re not going to enjoy it. But at the same time, it\u2019s bad because now he\u2019s afraid. According to Mr. Ox, the mage has learned what we are which we knew, but he has also learned what we are capable of. I don\u2019t know how do found that out exactly, but I really don\u2019t like it. If I find out who or what squealed on us, we may have a discussion.<br /> <br /> But things were more complicated than that. Mr. Ox placed an ornate prayer strip on the counter. As soon as I saw it, I felt weird and the Dog snarled. The others had a similarly negative reaction. It seems our quarry has constructed this prayer strips and hidden them throughout Taiwan. He doesn\u2019t know that we have any idea about them so they aren\u2019t everywhere and we can probably avoid most of them. The problem is that if more than one or two of these things catch us in what amounts to a mystic laser grid, it will boil the plasm inside us. If that doesn\u2019t kill us outright, it will definitely leave us without a way to use our powers. We talked for a moment about ways we could remove the strips but ultimately, we need to keep Bone Dry in the dark by avoiding them. The less we tip our hands, the more likely we are to catch him by surprise.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox gave us a final bit of wisdom before we left. He noted that Bone Dry was now aware of our powers, which meant they would be much less helpful. However I believe the way he put it, \u201cHe cannot make napalm cease to burn him.\u201d That little koan made total sense to me. Why use magic, when a dagger will do the job.<br /> <br /> Rotten Lily was waiting for us when we walked back outside. Each time the door to The Road to Hell opened, I could see the struggle to avoid frenzy in her eyes. Much like Noriko, Lily warned us that that was a very bad place. Once we convinced her we knew, she seemed to snap out of it and remembered why she came. Mr. Smile and the rest of Bone Dry\u2019s fleshbound lieutenants were searching the far side of Elysium. Lily told us a way to get back to the mausoleum that didn\u2019t take us near the vice spirits. I thought we might need to take her with us, but Rose was not pleased with adding another vampire to the house. I was worried about protecting her, but the Nosferatu felt sure that she could hide well enough. Once she was out of sight, we made for the Avernian Gate. Half an hour later, we were back at Dark Haven Bluffs.<br /> <br /> I almost caused Karen to pass out when I patted the duffle bag filled with dynamite. Everyone else moved into the kitchen to have an ice cream party. I was too preoccupied with a persistent thought. If I couldn\u2019t use my powers, I would still be able to fire a weapon. I took the dynamite and properly secured it in the Armory. I set the detonators aside so I can learn more about how they work later. Then I got my cleaning kit out and fieldstripped the Model 1873 I received from Stanton Marshall. The trigger had some kind of special attachment so I was very careful about handling it. Somehow I managed to miss that this was as special as it was. I knew it was a charm and I knew Stanton had it modified somehow, but I didn\u2019t see the markings on the barrel before. It was engraved with very elegant scrollwork. In calligraphy just before the rear sights was the phrase, \u201cOne of One Thousand.\u201d I didn\u2019t know what that meant so I brought in my laptop and looked it up. Now I understand why Stanton\u2019s rifle is so special. Something about the barrel was better than average when it was test fired during production. This barrel was given a special finish and the gun was assembled with a set trigger. The barrels were actually being made just for that model so no one is sure how many were used, but this was one. My charm rifle was once one of the best of the best. I took extreme care in cleaning it and making sure everything was pristine when I was finished. Then I wondered about finding a scope that could work. With that thought dancing in my head, I pulled out the Mossberg and started working on it as well. No revelations there, but I knew that one was as average as they come.<br /> <br /> Now I think I might see what the others are doing before I turn in.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1730 Hours, Friday, October 29, 2010<br /> <br /> I sometimes forget how much Nightshade enjoys weapons. Today has been fun and interesting.<br /> <br /> So after fieldstripping and cleaning my weapons last night, I mentioned to the Krewe that I might go look for a rifle scope. Apparently Nightshade and Bright Eyes had discussed the need for Bright Eyes to acquire \u201csomething\u201d as well. The need to \u201cpoint and click\u201d came up again, which I have always felt oversimplifies the process of properly firing a weapon, but I let it go. They determined that the two of them would accompany me this morning. Karen was definitely not coming along but then she really dislikes firearms or most other non-bladed weapons.<br /> <br /> I was able to find my scope and I\u2019m pretty sure I can attach it to the existing sight without damaging the sights or the barrel finish. While we were shopping, we found some surplus Winchester Model 1897s. The 12-gauge has been a reliable shotgun for pretty much all the branches and even has the option for a bayonette from back in its trenchgun days. They were fairly inexpensive, but I also asked the gunsmith about any specialty stocks. I didn\u2019t want to sound like a sexist ass, but I don\u2019t think either of the ladies with me could fire a 12-gauge twice due to kickback. I didn\u2019t really need to worry though. Nightshade had dressed for the occasion and her high heels and stockings were commanding the attention of the whole store. She moved through discussing various types of pistols with Bright Eyes while the various outdoorsmen present stepped aside and gawked. As luck would have it, they had some stock mods that did exactly what I wanted. A recoil absorbing stock for all three (yes I got one as it was a much better weapon than my Mossberg), my scope, ammo for all three weapons, a sling trap for skeet shooting on the yacht, clay pigeons, as well as various Airsoft replicas for Bright Eyes and I to train with were rung up. It was not a small bill, but we were prepared. And best of all, it was all legal.<br /> <br /> We came back and moved most of our purchases to the Armory where I showed Bright Eyes where everything went, how to secure it, and how to open the secret panel. I don\u2019t think anyone told her about the Armory and she was definitely not expecting a hidden room filled with various weapons and ammo. After her tour in the Armory, we took the Airsoft out to a field in West Haven, near the Patch. Nightshade came along but she was not interested in our wargames. The heels would not allow that kind of mobility. We\u2019re back now and about to clean up for whatever we\u2019re having for dinner. It seems great, whatever Cupcake is cooking.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> <i> [Sara has been writing regularly to Sasha, both letting her know about her personal life and talking about the more supernatural aspects of things. However, as Sasha is not particularly clueful to the supernatural stuff, Sara\u2019s presented that part as stories she\u2019s told to pass the time on long business trips, using the other PCs as characters for fun.]</i><br /> <br /> Last we left our intrepid adventurers, they\u2019d just got done interrogating a fairly pathetic excuse for a vampire, only to have him burst into flames. The lovely Natalie had been keeping an eye on the street and managed to spot their contact\u2019s magical shopfront below. And so we go...<br /> <br /> Jasmine took the lead going into Mr. Ox\u2019s shop, The Road to Hell. After the customary greetings were exchanged, Mr. Ox congratulated the team of bad luck farmers, as he called them. Your quarry is frightened, he told them, and calling upon powers possibly beyond his reach. He would be watching carefully, Mr. Ox would, for the mistake that such arrogance virtually demanded. But until then, he had a warning.<br /> <br /> The demon laid down a prayer strip. It left an uneasy feeling in the minds of the team, raising Doc\u2019s hackles and getting a crinkled nose from Alexia. Jasmine\u2019s stare grew colder, looking at it, and Sara moved closer to Natalie. She moved even closer when the demon explained that, should the energy given off by enough of these prayer strips intersect, it would boil the very magic from their veins. This might even kill them, and if it did not, they would be without their powers for some time.<br /> <br /> Of course, the sorcerer is unaware of that the heros have such an ally as Mr. Ox. He will expect to take them unawares, lying a trap like a spider lays their web. But the clever fly - the forewarned fly - can avoid the web, flying through its cracks and above its reach. Even if the fly would rather take a flamethrower to the web. Sometimes the subtler ways are best.<br /> <br /> For now, the sorcerer sits in his lair. He does not know where the mages live, or how to reach them directly, though, Mr. Ox warned, he does have some newly acquired knowledge of their abilities. He is frightened, and desperately searching for something to shield himself with. As a final warning, Mr. Ox reminds them that even if they avoid the web, the sorcerer has his ways of restricting the flow of magic, leaving them without their own. However, he mentioned with twinkle in his eye, he cannot make napalm stop burning him.<br /> <br /> The team left The Road to Hell to find their vampire friend, Rotten Lily waiting anxiously for them outside. She was disturbed not only by Mr. Ox and his shop, fearing them on a level she did not even understand, but also by a group of the strong evil spirits that had converged on the lair of the former Vampire King of the city. Her warning was well-received by the heros, who prudently decided to leave by a slightly circuitous route. It was returned, as the mages reminded her to keep a low profile, not wanting any harm to come to the vampire simply because she had aided them.<br /> <br /> And so the heros left, secrecy and patience as their watchwords. Mr. Ox had promised to send swift word as soon as the sorcerer made a misstep, but until then - or until they had discovered their own way to strike a blow against them - they were to keep a low profile, allowing themselves time to build up in power and skills so that they could face him and end his threat.<br /> <br /> That\u2019s all I have now for you. The trip didn\u2019t take very long, so I got to leave it on a bit of a cliffhanger. I\u2019m not really sure what\u2019s going to happen next, but it will have to be suitably spectacular for sure, with such a buildup. Bone Dry\u2019s a bad one, but I\u2019m sure the team will find a way. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Outside of story-land, we\u2019ve had a fun, relaxing day after our last business trip. It was a bit of a rough one - things were way out of balance and some folks don\u2019t appreciate our work. But we made some strides, so we all felt good about that. Jasmine felt good enough to want to celebrate with ice cream, so us girls had an ice cream party while Doc went off and did... boy things, I guess. Cleaning his guns, I think (not a euphemism, as far as I know <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />) and plotting - I\u2019ll get to that more later.<br /> <br /> Karen was glad to see us home again, of course. She always gets nervous when we head out, especially when she hears about folks not appreciating our presence, even when yours truly saves the day. It does usually mean some extra cuddles, so between that and the ice cream (lemon sherbert, my favorite <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> of course), it was an awesome night.<br /> <br /> So, about Doc and the guns - it occurred to me on the trip back that having a gun and knowing how to use it could be a sight more useful that Dad\u2019s old balisong in a serious emergency type situation. Dad did his best to make sure I could take care of myself, but while his usual tactic of \u201chold them off until I can run away\u201d does fine for just me, it doesn\u2019t work quite as well in a group. There\u2019s also a lot less worry about differing state laws, and customs bullshit with my line of work now. So, I asked Doc to teach me to shoot.<br /> <br /> He was all for that, right away, and immediately started quizzing me about what gun I wanted. At first I said pistol, since, being small and everything, it seemed like the easiest. So he started in on what kind of pistol, and how fast did I want it. I just kinda stared wide eyed until Natalie took pity on me and suggested a shotgun. That apparently took care of the \u201chow fast\u201d kind of questions, and I escaped from the rest to the ice cream party.<br /> <br /> The questions started up again Friday on the way to the gun store until I just said I\u2019d take whatever he recommended. Natalie was \u2018helping\u2019 by showing me some pictures of her doing... interesting things with a massive handgun. They did not help me focus on Doc\u2019s questions. Ostensibly, they were my first gun safety lesson, as each picture was proceeded by Natalie telling me I should never do that with a gun, nor that and especially not that. She also gave the guys at the gun shop something of a show. She was dressed up way more girl-y than usual, high heels and everything, making far to much of a show running her fingers down the guns\u2019 barrels. Of course I, being incorrigible, joined her, asking if they had any bandoliers that wouldn\u2019t chafe on bare skin.<br /> <br /> At the firing range, things weren\u2019t much different. I mean, I did fire a couple of shots to test out the gun Doc picked - the add-on he\u2019d gotten put on mine seemed to help a lot with the kick of the gun. But mostly I just stood wrong so that Natalie had to correct exactly where my arms were going. Doc sighed and added a few Airsoft guns to the tab, so we could get some actual, safe practice. I hit a lot of everything-but-Doc in those fields, but it was kinda fun, even if Natalie didn\u2019t join in. I don\u2019t think her heels would have fared well anyway.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CVIII</i><br /> <br /> The session was somewhat abbreviated due to some focusing issues, but we got some good play in. Not a great deal to add to the above, though.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s gun related Suicide Girl shots have come up before, but heck if I recall the journal number. Sara's format is still a little experimental...her player is trying to find the best way to record events and still keep to the character's history and background. So it may change a bit, we will see. If anything is confusing let us know.<br /> <br /> We are discussing how to apply Shroud in GMC combat. 5-6 armor is very very powerful in GMC, and since converting over no one with Shroud has taken more than one level of damage from a hit, even from an extremely dangerous tree-monster.<br /> There has been talk of having Shroud apply 1/2/3 Armor at levels 1/3/5 keeping the +1 for a successful roll. That is the current favored method anyway. It\u2019s still under discussion. Any suggestions?<br /> <br /> Should be a bit more substantial next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T01:39:02-07:00","id":171501,"title":"","content":"I apologize for the delay. It's been a rough few days, hell a rough month. But it is time for journals. Jasmine's player is taking a short hiatus, so not present in this journal but will return in a couple sessions.<br /> <i><br /> Session CIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc's Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Saturday, October 30, 2010<br /> <br /> Apparently I was smelling whatever Tavia was making for dinner. Cupcake and Chandra had plans to take the psychic out for a \u201cbusiness dinner.\u201d The way they were dressed, I wasn\u2019t sure how much business would be discussed, but I guess we\u2019ll hear about it tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Nightshade, Karen, and Bright Eyes invited Noriko and I along for the secret blasphemy of Olive Garden before actually getting to enjoy the 27 Club. It was a good time, but before it was over, Nightshade had two other of her followers ready to go. With five hot and bothered women pawing at each other, Noriko decided a) lesbians are weird b) we should go explore my room for dangers.<br /> <br /> Now she\u2019s about to pounce on my pen as it\u2019s keeping me from paying her attention.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Saturday, October 30, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s a wonderful thing I don\u2019t need as much sleep as most of the Krewe. I woke up about 0830 Hours and asked if Noriko wanted to meditate with me. I took her flinging the covers over her head as a no.<br /> <br /> It took longer than usual to get centered today. I\u2019m not sure if I was that tired, or if something else was distracting me, but it took about an hour and a half. None of the others were either home, awake, or moving yet, except for Tavia who was making toast with honey for breakfast. She shared some toast, but I didn\u2019t chance the honey. I think I\u2019m going to study the road sign\u2019s book from the DMV, at least until Noriko wakes up.<br /> <br /> Now that the van is finished, I need to get insurance and finally get my license.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1400 Hours, Saturday, October 30, 2010<br /> <br /> Rose was out at a swim meet with Jean so she and Karl weren\u2019t around when the others started stumbling in. It was about 1300 Hours when I heard Cupcake and Chandra come in. They were still wearing their dinner attire with their new friend in tow. I will call her Mouse. Mouse is very nervous and slightly timid but from what we know, she is a very skilled psychic. Not long thereafter, Nightshade, Bright Eyes, and Karen staggered in as well. Once everyone was comfortable, Cupcake asked for some backup on an information gathering meeting with an informant named Raindancer. Nightshade perked up at the name. Raindancer was a prominent and vocal member of the local LGBTQ community. She worked covertly as an information broker, easily disguised as a gossip in a salon. Rumors suggested that her deceased brother was important with several local gangs as well. This explained how she remained as well connected as she seems to be, but also why she strongly distrusts any kind of police presence. Nightshade explained that while her own aversion to police was warranted, she recognized that she did not hate them. The same couldn\u2019t be said for Raindancer. This was the problem originally as Mouse was worried she would be linked to the police or at least suspected. Nightshade called a very large poet and mutual friend we\u2019ve run into in the clubs before. The Poet was happy to help look for Ritchie Abrams. He confirmed that Ritchie\u2019s boyfriend was often blamed for the disappearance and as such was fairly well shunned from social events. Because we were friends of Nightshade, the Poet agreed to meet Cupcake and Mouse at the salon to give a proper introduction. The rest of us would go and wait outside in case of trouble. Now it\u2019s time to leave. Hopefully we\u2019re know something when we get back.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1800 Hours, Saturday, October 30, 2010<br /> <br /> That definitely proved enlightening. We arrived in two cars and met the Poet at 1530 Hours beside Shear Delight salon. Bright Eyes convinced Cupcake to get bakery-inspired nails before going in. It took just over an hour for them to finish but once we were all back together and at the Bluffs, Cupcake and Mouse filled us in.<br /> <br /> According to Raindancer, Ritchie\u2019s boyfriend didn\u2019t have any part of Ritchie\u2019s disappearance. He was not welcome at most gay-friendly locations because of suspicions and him being absent has only allowed the rumors to grow. I felt genuinely sorry for the kid. Normally the gay community takes care of their own in New Haven, but this time they were shutting him out when he needed them more than ever. Next we learned about a disturbing trend had been happening at Gotham Citi for a while, which may have something to do with Ritchie. Rich, attractive, \u201cstraight\u201d men are coming to the club on Saturday (Gay night) looking for young men to \u201cwork on their roof\u201d or \u201chelp with their plumbing.\u201d If questioned, they were always \u201csurprised\u201d it was Gay night and were only \u201clooking for workers.\u201d Cupcake saw a picture of a man in a horrible bowtie which Raindancer knew to be one of these recruiters. She said there was a woman who had similarly disappeared but resurfaced some time later telling friends not to ask questions. This Carol Jameson stormed into Gotham Citi and berated the Bowtie Man for trying to lure boys away, at least until the cops came and removed her. At the very least, it sounds like these men are taking advantage of teen boys which I\u2019m not okay with. Though Nightshade suspects that the recruiters are doing so for someone else. And the overall feeling is that there could be some vampiric connection. That area is controlled by the Invictus based on what Lynne told us and that still falls within the MO. I don\u2019t want to call Truman on this one, at least not yet since the situation with Lynne likely caused him some issues.<br /> <br /> The Poet called Nightshade after we were well into our discussions. Apparently Raindancer felt very protective of Cupcake and asked him to shadow her. He wanted to pass the information along and also determine if he should or not. Thankfully Nightshade told him no. The Poet if a very nice man, but we do not wish to see him trying to deal with anything that plans to move on us. It did remind me to speak with Mouse about getting a brush or other personal item from Ritchie\u2019s so we could try to track him using our abilities. She said she could go tomorrow and expect to get anything like that we would need. Bright Eyes and I shared the Plasm in the House while the others were getting ready. Then I went to clean up and call Noriko. We\u2019ll see how this goes.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2300 Hours, Saturday, October 30, 2010<br /> <br /> Well we didn\u2019t find the Bowtie Man, but we did meet up with Carol Jameson. It was strange because even though she was alive, she was not aging. It was like she was frozen in time. Bright Eyes will likely have some interesting observations for us about Carol, but not until she gets home. I dressed appropriately for the club which was much more clean cut and less gothic than my normal club gear. Noriko was a little surprised, but she looks good wherever we go. I spotted Carol at the bar as soon as we walked in. She was a little surprised that I recognized her description before becoming incredibly suspicious of my intentions. I knew lying was out so I very delicately (and quietly) told her we were looking into Ritchie\u2019s disappearance and I thought she was on the same side. She told me to let it go and not get involved. It was immediately obvious at that point that she was trying to protect me by not telling me anything. Without giving too much away, I explained that I would be okay but if she needed some help, I\u2019d be happy to try. After a few more failed attempts to persuade her, I apologized for ruining her mood. Carol left for the bathroom at that point and I suddenly realized how Rose must feel when she talks to people. I turned to ask Noriko a question, but she was locked on Carol like a cat stalking her prey. She mumbled something about how Carol smelled guilty. I eventually had to snap my fingers a few times to get her attention again. I also asked that she please not eat people we needed for information. I noticed that Bright Eyes had caught up to Carol and was getting a much better reaction. That was my cue to take Noriko out on the dance floor.<br /> <br /> Before it was over (and it was over fairly quickly), Nightshade had snatched up a girl whose entire presence was dominated by her massive amounts of hair. I still don\u2019t know what her face looked like. Bright Eyes left with Carol, Chandra had an unspoken dominance challenge with a gorgeous vampire over Cupcake and Karen picked up someone that Bright Eyes didn\u2019t have time for on the way to catch Carol. I was vaguely glad Noriko drove. Unfortunately Carol left a lasting impression on my girlfriend. Noriko thinks that Carol has killed people or otherwise has blood on her hands from something. She told me to make sure I hear from Bright Eyes tomorrow because she went missing, Carol would be her next target.<br /> <br /> Hopefully it won\u2019t come down to that. But to distract Noriko and because I realized just after we got home that it\u2019s Devil\u2019s Night, we\u2019re going out on patrol together. I have no idea what we might get into but hopefully it will help. She was of course all for this, so we\u2019re about to leave.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> October 29th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Cheffy Housemate is off on \u201cbusiness,\u201d So Doc, Sara, Karen and Noriko are going to Olive Garden.<br /> <br /> -So Sinful. She would not approve.<br /> <br /> -I never thought eating at the Olive Garden would be rebellious, but there you go.<br /> <br /> -Speaking of Sinful, going to 27 Club tonight with the gang. =-D<br /> <br /> -Yay My club =-D<br /> <br /> -Our Club. Karen. Ahem.<br /> <br /> -Time to go mad with power!<br /> <br /> -powerpowerpower.<br /> <br /> -Sara has a better idea: Go mad with ladies.<br /> <br /> -ladiesladiesladies? Does not sound as good.<br /> <br /> -Oh what am I getting myself into?<br /> <br /> -Hehehehehe<br /> <br /> -You know what is awesome? Going out and having fun with Doc without tension is awesome.<br /> <br /> -Doc is great.<br /> <br /> -ladies are great<br /> <br /> -Tonight is great! Wooooooooooooooooooooooooooooooo!<br /> <br /> -^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> October 30th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I am absolutely doing that again sometime.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jog.<br /> <br /> -Hmmmmm\u2026there is a name I have not dealt with in awhile\u2026<br /> <br /> -Stephan to the rescue!<br /> <br /> -Ok, this works, time to roll out peoples.<br /> <br /> -Oh man I am not sure what Alexia and Chandra did but this poor girl is SWOONING.<br /> <br /> -High fives would be both appropriate and inappropriate, I guess?<br /> <br /> -Okay, Stephan, Miss Callahan and Alexia are going in.<br /> <br /> -Stephan gives the clear sign. Time to pester Sara and Doc.<br /> <br /> -Looks like it was productive<br /> <br /> -Clubbing tonight!<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress will be at Gotham Citi tonight. Feel free to come and pay tribute<br /> <br /> -Just not\u2026too much tribute. I\u2019m a little sore.<br /> <br /> -Heading out<br /> <br /> -Looks like one of the people we were looking for is here.<br /> <br /> -Poor Doc :-/<br /> <br /> -Sara will try.<br /> <br /> -Maybe not<br /> <br /> -Oooh, Ok you are on<br /> <br /> -YES! Wooo! You go Sara.<br /> <br /> -Ahem<br /> <br /> -Ok, so splitting up tonight, is cool. I think Karen is going to interrogate the girl Sara blew off.<br /> <br /> -For, uh, important investigative reasons.<br /> <br /> -Speaking of which\u2026I\u2019m gonna solve a little mystery myself\u2026<br /> <br /> -Oh wow\u2026okay, someone\u2019s roommate did NOT like seeing me show up here.<br /> <br /> -Wonder if it is because I am me, female, or a lay?<br /> <br /> -Oh to better, more intriguing things!<br /> <br /> -Oh\u2026well\u2026that is interesting\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> No new story this time. Our latest job is in town, so no long trips to fill. Our new job has certainly been plenty of fun, so far. Though really, it\u2019s not new. It\u2019s the job with Catharine, with the missing guy Richie. She\u2019s another paranormal investigator and we kinda stumbled onto her gig a bit back. She\u2019s been tracking down leads while we were out and about and now that she found one, she got in contact again for our (technically the rest of the troupe\u2019s, but I made myself useful) local expertise and contacts. Plus, I think Catharine might have become a bit ensnared by the lovely Chandra and Alexia.<br /> <br /> You see, they were really the ones who stumbled into their case, and Chandra took advantage of Catharine\u2019s new lead to take her out on a date (with Alexia as well, of course) to one of the fancy French places Alexia prefers. They showed up back at the house *after* we did the next day, so I assume they had plenty of fun. The rest of us capitalized on Alexia\u2019s absence to slum it at Olive Garden, as it offends her chef-ly sensibilities. Then we went to the 27 Club. Jasmine went home herself, hopefully to spend time with Karl - surely it bodes well for a case to start off with everyone well and truly laid.<br /> <br /> For our part, as soon as we made our grand entrance and Natalie had a look around, she looked at me with a wicked twinkle in her eyes. \u201cI think we have an important meeting tonight, don\u2019t you?\u201d I was certainly all for it, even just assuming she meant a most certainly non-managerial meeting with the adorable Tatum. I was also not displeased when she let Cindy know she was expected as well. It was a very stimulating meeting, where we all worked assiduously to make sure all parties were satisfied.<br /> <br /> Tatum does continue to be adorable. She is convinced Natalie is some kind of supernatural creature, like a vampire or an avatar of a goddess instead of just a paranormal investigator. She asked if I \u2018had been elevated\u2019 and kept trying to get me to confirm her suspicions. I was very noncommittal. Maybe it's mean, but it\u2019s far too much fun to speculate with her. Besides, she probably wouldn\u2019t believe me.<br /> <br /> After we\u2019d all dragged our asses back to the house and Alexia had fixed up a light lunch, making sure the kitchen was still her domain, she and Catharine and Chandra told us about this new lead. There was an information broker, named Raindancer, with ties to the local GLBT community who might know something. At first, Alexia was just hoping we might loiter nearby as backup, but Natalie was familiar with Raindancer and did one better. She called a friend of hers, Stephen-who-writes-plays, who is a giant biker of a man, and who knew Raindancer better than Natalie and was willing to give an introduction, since she was a bit leary of cops and anyone who might be connected with them.<br /> <br /> The meet went well - we got a strong suspect with a potential pattern of abductions and a name of someone who might have been abducted by the same group. Also, Alexia got *adorable* nails. She was just going to get her hair done, since that\u2019s how it works - you visit Raindancer at her salon, ask your questions and tip her based on the information she gives you. She\u2019s a genius with that fancy nail art stuff though, so I convinced Alexia to get a bakery themed deal, with cupcakes and cookies and pie, all with smiling happy faces.<br /> <br /> More pertinent to the case, she told them there were a few regulars at Gotham Citi\u2019s gay night, rich \u2018straight\u2019 men who need the occasional strapping young man to \u2018work on their roof\u2019 or \u2018help with the plumbing\u2019. Richie had gone off with one in particular (who we have dubbed \u2018Bowtie Man\u2019, since Raindancer didn\u2019t know his name, he had on an awful speckled-y bowtie and he\u2019s too much of a potential villain to be \u2018Incredibly Handsome Man who can Totally Wear Whatever Bowtie He Wants as Long as He Doesn\u2019t Kidnap Me\u2019). To make things worse, a girl named Carol had gone missing a lot like Richie but she had come back eventually and threw a fit when she saw Bowtie Man at the club, telling him to stay away from those boys.<br /> <br /> Which means we had a bunch to keep an eye out for when we went to Gotham Citi. Mr. Bowtie Man didn\u2019t show, so I didn\u2019t have to go stumbling drunk to get a few hairs. Ah, the wonders of sympathetic links. It was a little bit of a shame, but not too much of one, since Carol was there. Doc went to talk with her first and hit a total brick wall. She knew just what he was talking about when he said he was looking for someone and told him to leave it alone. That was pretty clear from her body language, and from Doc\u2019s side of the conversation over the ear curls, things seemed to go downhill from there. She certainly seemed to have some kind of trouble, but kept turning aside his offers to help. She also didn\u2019t respond well to him claiming that surely she was on our side, since she had confronted Bowtie Man. She eventually brushed him off, so I tagged in, going for a bit of a long con, to coax it out of her. And if that meant I had to seduce the tall, striking mysterious woman, well then, so be it. It did mean leaving my new friend Tracy on the dance floor, but there was something there - I felt it. I\u2019ll be able to find her again, I'm sure.<br /> <br /> As it was, I spent the night at the... well, before living at the Bluffs, I might have called it the palatial estate of the mysterious Carol. It was a big place, when not compared to the Bluffs, especially since she lived there all alone. There was no lingering... talk once we\u2019d woken up - I\u2019m writing this at a cafe nearby waiting for Doc or someone to pick me up - and she seemed a little reserved once hormones weren\u2019t quite so much in control, so I didn\u2019t push on the case or anything. She did say she hoped to do this again, so I\u2019ll have another chance.<br /> <br /> We'll have to move carefully on this one, especially since it's on our home turf. Bowtie Man is rich and powerful, with rich and powerful friends. Carol herself is certainly well-to-do, at the least. That surprised me a little, since I had been thinking of her as a victim of whatever scheme this is. Which is not to say the rich never victimize each other, or give their victims gifts, so they feel tied to them, as if they should be grateful. That maybe accounts for some of her guilt earlier. Anyway, with any luck, we\u2019ll be able to help this kid Richie, and maybe give Carol a little bit of peace too. Even without getting into what Carol knows, we've got a couple of lines of questioning to go down for a bit.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CIX</i><br /> <br /> Compared to last session\u2019s lack of focus, this session was very solid. A lot of good RP took place, and the PCs had lots of fun I think.<br /> <br /> Stephan came up in session 1 (he gave Natalie a play to read) so is a major blast from earlier in the campaign when I expected him to be a slightly more important character. Raindancer is a transwoman who working on a picture for her lead me to realize how unfriendly Google image search is to finding decent pictures of transwomen, particularly black transwomen like Raindancer.<br /> <br /> Interesting anecdote, when Sara went to talk to Carol, I had a picture ready for Tracy which I tossed down, and Sara\u2019s player gave me the most awesome \u201cfuck you\u201d look ever as Sara had to blow her off. I am a terrible person.<br /> <br /> Not much else to cover. I was worried my dental pain would keep me from having the session, already delayed a night, but after three hellish days I got it under control, and the session went better than I expected. Not quite as on task as this, but pretty good and a lot of good RP and discussion. You will be getting that in two weeks. In the meantime comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:26:15-07:00","id":171514,"title":"","content":"Glad you're feeling better.<br /> <br /> Transwoman? Male to female or female to male? I am unclear.<br /> <br /> You're story made me think of a villain idea. A man who hunts young gay men for his blood rituals because they are easy targets. Normally for motivation one would expect an anti gay sentiment, but he only chooses them for their easiness. That would be the turn around, but that got me thinking which would be the worse or more angering motivation from the heroes perspective? The anti sentiment or the opportunistic because they're easy sentiment?<br /> <br /> Or heroes as vessels for the reader perspective. If that makes sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-17T02:40:26-07:00","id":171516,"title":"","content":"Raindancer is a MTF Transwoman.<br /> <br /> Part of this is examining something that does sometimes happen in places. I knew a guy who ran into some of those people even down here. So yea, that exploitation happens. People get in over their head, and young gay men can be especially vulnerable to exploitation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-29T13:10:03-07:00","id":183984,"title":"","content":"New Geist journals. I am swapping the order of Natalie and Sara\u2019s journals to have Natalie last again. This is due to the oblique nature of her journals; they make more sense in the context of other journals. If we get Jasmine journals again at some point we will position them between Doc\u2019s and Sara\u2019s, about where they have been. Speaking of which, Jasmine\u2019s player was on hiatus this session also, so no Jasmine this time. I anticipate one more session without Jasmine after this one, then she will be back. In game, Jasmine is away for the weekend, so the PCs are left to their own devices. Anyway, enough exposition, let\u2019s move on.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0900 Hours, Sunday, October 31, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s almost as peaceful as a cemetery around here this morning. Just about everyone is either still out, still asleep, or off to themselves in quiet contemplation.<br /> <br /> After our rounds on Devil\u2019s Night, which was fairly uneventful, Noriko came back to Dark Haven Bluffs with me. We didn\u2019t get much sleep, but that\u2019s okay. She\u2019s under the covers in my bed still and is very cute unless you try to wake her up. I got out of bed around 0730 Hours to meditate.<br /> <br /> Things were easy to put in place today as I was able to find my center in about half an hour. I\u2019ve just been hanging out since. I\u2019ll probably study the DMV book some more until I\u2019m needed or until people start crawling in.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Sunday, October 31, 2010<br /> <br /> So that was unexpected.<br /> <br /> Nightshade was up and around earlier than normal. She pulled me to the side and I thought I\u2019d upset someone. Instead I learned that Noriko was developing a major attachment to me. I didn\u2019t know if she meant that in a bad way or not. When I asked, Nightshade clarified that she was seriously in love with me. That explained the question of what I wanted in our relationship the other night. But honestly, I was pretty surprised. I told Noriko at the time that I was happy and enjoying us. I hadn\u2019t put any long term goals down or anything as I was just enjoying the moment. I could tell at the time that wasn\u2019t exactly the answer she was looking for, but it didn\u2019t seem to upset her either. Nightshade and I talked about it and we think that Noriko hasn\u2019t ever had a serious relationship. Supernaturals have that problem sometimes; not that I can throw stones. The running theory right now, since I didn\u2019t think it was my place to ask, is that since Noriko was \u201cturned\u201d by the Colony, she has been mostly alone. That makes our relationship mean that much more as she doesn\u2019t have to hide or lie or anything like that. Nightshade thought I should know where things stood as she didn\u2019t think Noriko was talking to me about it. And she was right. But now we\u2019re gathering for lunch, so I don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be discussing it just yet.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Sunday, October 31, 2010<br /> <br /> During lunch, we discussed Carol\u2019s disappearance never made waves because she was over 18 and everyone thought she, \u201cran off to California.\u201d This was assisted by her being seen with someone before vanishing. Her parents, William and Karen, were loaded but we got the impression from Nightshade\u2019s research that they believed they\u2019d lost their daughter before she disappeared. Strangely it seems like Carol inherited their fortune when she returned, but we don\u2019t know much else about them. That doesn\u2019t help us find Ritchie, but it does keep the focus on the north side. The more we learn, the more circumstantially these disappearances seem tied to the Invictus. I wish I knew a way to contact Lynne. I don\u2019t want to bring any more heat down on Truman than I think I already have, but I need some inside information. Everytime we go to one of the clubs where these kids are being lured away, I see the vampire that Chandra stared down last night. I don\u2019t know her but she\u2019s obviously well off and in all the wrong places to be a coincidence. I just can\u2019t risk ruining our chances to leverage the Prince if we can ever get to the Athenaeum. Otherwise, I could have been less pleasant with the Sheriff. It serves me better for now though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Nightshade had news about the girl we privately referred to as The Hair. I\u2019m still not sure I\u2019ve ever seen her face. I now know her real name but I\u2019ll stick with The Hair for now. She seems to be somewhat in the know as she asked Nightshade to assist her in finding a special heirloom. The Hair said some other things that led Nightshade to believe there was more to her than just copious amounts of hair. The Hair\u2019s roommate also made an impression. She all but cornered Nightshade and stated in what was meant to be a warning that she \u201cwas into girls, but The Hair was not.\u201d We weren\u2019t sure if she was just jealous, being protective, or if something else was going on. In theory, we\u2019re about to find out as The Hair is coming over for an interview with our merry band of paranormal investigators.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1500 Hours, Sunday, October 31, 2010<br /> <br /> The Hair is apparently from a long line of Irish Hairs. All jokes aside, she said that all the women in her family were long lived, had lots of hair, and tended to keep it naturally dark until advanced age set in. It was partially because of these traits that the family heirloom was a bone and silver comb. The Hair told us the story of the comb. Her grandmother gave it to her along with the family warning. Never give or let a man take the comb, else she would be compelled to marry him. If she had already married, she should still not give the comb to her husband as this would give him power over her. I\u2019m not an expert but that reminded me of Irish folklore. This whole situation came up because someone had stolen the comb. Afterwards, The Hair began having dreams of men\u2019s faces. I grabbed my sketch pad and tried to quickly get down the descriptions. The sketches weren\u2019t my best work, but we gained a rough image of the thief, the middle man, and the final owner. The Hair went on to say she now feels pursued. Her mother gave the comb back to her own mother as she was too afraid to keep it. That was why The Hair received it from her grandmother. The comb was stolen just after school started and the dreams began soon thereafter.<br /> <br /> The Hair confessed that she could see our death aura, which really opened up most of our doors. She noted the blonde woman Cupcake and Chandra were talking to last night had a different death aura. We told her to be careful with that woman and anyone else with that kind of death aura. Vampires might find The Hair a bit more intriguing than would be healthy for her. We explained that we were working on a missing person so we couldn\u2019t devote all our effort into the search. She understood but she also said that she felt betrothed, which I never realized was a feeling, but didn\u2019t think it was polite to mention. Given that, I reluctantly offered to cast a spell to help protect her from \u201cunwanted advances.\u201d I don\u2019t want it to be a habit for people we just met to have everything thrown on the table, but I could tell she was scared and likely in danger. I spent the next half hour preparing the GMC room with images and symbols of resistance and will. When I was done, Nightshade accompanied The Hair down into our casting chamber. As our Krewe priestess, Nightshade blessed me with a bit of the power she can draw from our Channel. It was a welcome boost. The Hair was rightfully nervous but I did all I could. My magic is only so powerful but it\u2019s better than going unprotected. She left with a new group of friends to watch over her and as much luck as I could lend.<br /> <br /> When I joined the rest of the Krewe, Cupcake and Bright Eyes recognized a local pawn shop owner as the middle man, so apparently the sketch wasn\u2019t so rough. Bright Eyes was talking about trying to sweet talk her way into learning about the comb. Something about dealing in stolen goods came up and I smiled. Well at least inside I smiled. Apparently I was a little more intimidating on the outside as Bright Eyes looked at me and declared that they were bringing me to talk with the Pawn shop owner. He should keep records just in case of something like this, but I also intend to \u201cclue him in\u201d that the kid he bought the comb from was fencing stolen goods. If he didn\u2019t take that hint, I was pretty sure I could be more blunt about his involvement. But now, we\u2019re going costume shopping for hijinx tonight.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1900 Hours, Sunday, October 31, 2010<br /> <br /> Sometimes I forget that Snowflake, Karl, and I are three of the luckiest men on the Eastern Seaboard. I remembered today.<br /> <br /> Cupcake decided that she, Chandra, and Mouse needed a group costume. They were a vampire, werewolf, and victim respectively. Bright Eyes found a sexy Leprechaun outfit complete with platform boots and a cane. Nightshade was just her normally gothic self, while Karen was more an S&amp;M Bitch (their phraseology, not mine) or just Karen. For Noriko, we found an Underworld style outfit that put Beckinsale to shame. I was an Undead Pirate. Now that we\u2019re back and everyone is getting ready, we are a sight to behold. I may have to get pictures.<br /> <br /> The plan for now is to hit Murder Ballads and enjoy the atmosphere. Being that it\u2019s Halloween, we\u2019ll see what else we get to deal with. I know one thing though. Tonight the ear curls are on.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> When it rains, it pours, I suppose. Not that I\u2019m complaining, mind - I harbor no ill will towards any job that requires working closely with a beautiful young woman. And after the somewhat... hectic out-of-town jobs lately, I don\u2019t really mind staying at home for a bit. Gods, but that still feels strange to type - home. Especially it being a stationary place, a house even.<br /> <br /> The new job will get back burnered, for now at least, since a missing person is a more urgent situation that a missing heirloom, even if that heirloom likely has some kind of mystical influence on our new friend Sarah. The warnings her grandmother had passed down - to not lose the family comb, since if a man got possession of it she\u2019d be compelled to marry him - reminded me right off of some of the water spirits of the old country: bean sidhe or night, mermaids, water hags, that sort of thing. The warning apparently had some kind of teeth, as her mother had returned it to her grandmother with some distress.<br /> <br /> If that were all, of course, we would be unlikely to have been called in, but she had, in fact, lost it. Had it stolen, to be fair, from her dorm room. Ever since then, she\u2019d felt an odd sense of foreboding, a feeling of being betrothed. She\u2019d also had dreams, first of a young college-aged man, then of an older man that Alexia and I recognized as a local pawn shop owner. Recently, she\u2019d been seeing a different man, probably in his late 30s, who presumably bought the comb from the pawn shop.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019ve got a decent lead to start out with. And, may I say, it is a wonder to be part of a team for this sort of thing. Alexia and I were discussing speaking with the pawn shop guy and I mentioned that since it was a case of stolen goods, we had every reason to speak with him, even not mentioning any paranormal stuff, but he\u2019d be under no obligation to share. Working on my own, I might have gotten somewhere with a damsel-in-distress routine, but lots of folks in his situation are a bit prickly about things. Doc caught my eye though, and gave me just enough of his grumpy face to make it clear his plan. And even if he\u2019s immune to a pretty face, I pretty sure pawn shop guy will be thrilled to help us out.<br /> <br /> First though, we need to find RIchie. In the meantime, Doc gave Sarah a bit of luck, for the purposes of staving off unwanted advances. While he set that up, Natalie and I made some totally wanted advances - purely to avoid awkwardness, of course, since Natalie had gone home with her last night. She kept looking at me like I\u2019d drop kick her for that any second, so it was pure kindness really, to show there were no hard feelings. She\u2019ll hopefully be at Murder Ballads tonight for Halloween hijinx.<br /> <br /> We did talk some about Richie\u2019s case, it hasn\u2019t been all new cases, pretty girls and holidays. Okay, it was mostly pretty girls, even still. I shared what I had learned at Carol\u2019s place and Natalia shared what she\u2019d learned online. Natalie was able to answer my main question - if Carol\u2019s so well-to-do, how did she go missing without more of a hue and cry than I\u2019d gotten the impression happened? Apparently, the police thought she\u2019d run off with someone to California and her not being a minor, that was that. Other than that, however, and Noriko\u2019s bad feeling about her, we don\u2019t have much more. I left her on good terms though, and the rest of the team has another local contact who might know something.<br /> <br /> But now it is holiday time. Natalie will be performing a rite to send us off this Halloween night. We\u2019ve already made a special trip for costuming - not much has made me curse the jealousy of country people more than Doc\u2019s dashing pirate get up. He and Noriko do make an adorable couple though. She\u2019s been following him around like a second shadow, or a kitten set to pounce all day.<br /> <br /> Speaking of pouncing, Karen\u2019s just passed by, and I think I need some practice... maneuvering in these boots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> October 31st, 2010<br /> <br /> -Ah, poor Noriko. Must be hard being crazy.<br /> <br /> -I will be little Ms. Helpful, though. ^_^<br /> <br /> -Okay, convo with Doc went well, I think.<br /> <br /> -Hopefully I am not meddling.<br /> <br /> -Okay, time to see Sarah.<br /> <br /> -I just have to not call her \u201cThe Hair\u201d<br /> <br /> -Simple, right?<br /> <br /> -Ok, meeting not too uncomfortable all things considered.<br /> <br /> -Hrm, that is unexpected.<br /> <br /> -Very unexpected.<br /> <br /> -If she turns into a Mermaid, I am not sure what I will do.<br /> <br /> -Sara is on a roll.<br /> <br /> -Doc wants to help with Magic. Cool.<br /> <br /> -I am so bad ^_^<br /> <br /> -Sara makes me bad. S\u2019not my fault.<br /> <br /> -She is a baaaaaaaaad influence <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -I think we can help this girl<br /> <br /> -Of course, it sounds non horrible now, so of course there is horrid monsters somehow.<br /> <br /> -They are shopping, your Mistress must prepare for the night.<br /> <br /> -Happy Halloween!<br /> <br /> -Solemn Pagan Rituals are Solemn<br /> <br /> -I feel powerful. I like that.<br /> <br /> -Heading to Murder Ballads<br /> <br /> -Wow that did not take long<br /> <br /> -Helpful info for Alexia maybe?<br /> <br /> -Funtime!<br /> <br /> -Once again, Happy Halloween!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CX</i><br /> <br /> So well over a year ago Sarah\u2019s pic started appearing among Clubgoers, and she developed a sort of reputation OOC as \u201cThe Hair\u201d. The pic is of a girl with a good deal of hair. The dominant theory held by Jasmine and Simon\u2019s players was that the girl\u2019s body is a puppet and the hair drives her around. Simon\u2019s player used the pic in a short lived game as a background NPC we never spoke to and the theory came up there as well. However, as it turns out she is not, in fact, sentient hair puppeting around an emo girl\u2019s body. I hope they could contain their disappointment.<br /> <br /> Not much else to report on, the session was largely role-playing. We did RP some at Murder Ballads\u2026that will be covered in the session notes in two weeks. I\u2019ll hope to see you then, in the meantime comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 06-29-2014, 06:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T02:40:58-07:00","id":184677,"title":"","content":"Is the pawnshop the part where Doc starts throwing rings the owner stating that each is a life he helped end? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-06-30T11:32:17-07:00","id":184965,"title":"","content":"Heh we have not gotten to it yet (most of last night was dealing with Richie and a rather...odd...discovery by Sara) but I am sure his player will take it under advisement ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T14:24:01-07:00","id":196554,"title":"","content":"One more session with Jasmine away filling out the weekend. We do actually move a bit into Monday but it is okay. Come along and enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXI</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Monday, November 1, 2010<br /> <br /> Tonight was interesting in ways I wasn\u2019t expecting.<br /> <br /> Murder Ballads was filled to capacity and I don\u2019t remember there ever being that many incredibly attractive women in attendance before our Krewe arrived. I\u2019m sure the costumes helped. Carol was there among many other familiar faces but no Bowtie Man. I had to keep drawing Noriko\u2019s attention back to me as she was staring at Carol more than was healthy for anyone. I asked her if she was okay once but she just said she was \u201cthinking about dinner.\u201d Eating the people we need to pump for information is really not helpful and I keep needing to remind Noriko of this lately. Eventually I just pulled her out to the dance floor. That kept her focused on me at least.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Cupcake decided that she should use her business as an inroad with Carol to meet this mysterious benefactor Mariah Williams. The plan was to attempt to go for a catering job for the parties Mariah threw for the upper crust (the ones where young boys go missing afterwards). That went about as far as getting the name out before Carol looked like she was going to search Cupcake for a wire. It bombed so badly that Cupcake stopped and said she heard someone calling her before walking away. I\u2019m sure Rose had the sudden thought in her hotel room, \u201cI hate \u2018clubbing\u2019 and Murder Ballads is just not my style,\u201d but had no idea why.<br /> <br /> Once we were sure things were smooth, we hit the Plasm for the week and split off for the night. I took Noriko home as it seemed like the house would be a little empty again. Now if I don\u2019t close the journal and put the pen away, I may get dragged into bed by a werecat with thinning patience.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0600 Hours, Monday, November 1, 2010<br /> <br /> Okay that was different.<br /> <br /> I was just contacted through my dreams. I was cuddling with a giant tiger curled up around me when I realized something else was watching me in the dream. My mental landscape fell away and I was standing in a dark space. I didn\u2019t see anything except myself standing in this blank area. There was something trying to make contact with me. I expected Garlize or may even the Forgotten Scion of the Old World itself. Instead I got Timmy, the boy with a magic dream house. Timmy (who does not like to be called Timmy) was the brother of Tracy, the girl Bright Eyes left the club with. That immediately put me on edge and I asked if she was alright. Timmy said she was fine but that she was there in his dream house. They had never had visitors that were alive before so he was confused. Also he had never tried to use the phone before. I couldn\u2019t hear Bright Eyes but Tracy also could talk to me and they relayed messages to Bright Eyes. It was a strange conversation and I think it was done mainly to see if they could do it. I\u2019m not even sure when it happened. Now I\u2019m going to curl back up with my tiny tiger because I can.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0900 Hours, Monday, November 1, 2010<br /> <br /> I got back up around 0800 Hours and went to meditate. Seems dream communication helps focus the mind. I was able to center myself in about a half hour. That was useful since I had a text from Tavia waiting for me when I got back.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing happened I couldn\u2019t handle, be back in afternoon <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u201d<br /> <br /> That\u2019s not terrifying at all. I think I\u2019m going to work on my katas. I immediately thought of my guns when we learned our Manifestations couldn\u2019t be trusted against Bone Dry, but I have other ways of attacking. And if I\u2019m in close, that big rifle is going to hurt more than help me. My martial arts can\u2019t just be turned off because I\u2019m dealing with a mage.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1445 Hours, Monday, November 1, 2010<br /> <br /> For the record, Bright Eyes was fine but really surprised by the siblings with magic white dream houses.<br /> <br /> We all got back together around 1230 Hours for lunch and to discuss the plans for the day. Breakfast really didn\u2019t happen as such, so this was the first chance we found. Bright Eyes was going to hit the library and research Carol Jameson\u2019s family. Nightshade was going along as well to help speed the research along. Cupcake was convinced we needed to speak with Crowley so her and Chandra\u2019s time was filled wine shopping before searching the alleys of New Haven. Given the pallor of Cupcake and Mouse\u2019s face, Chandra had enjoyed herself last night. Thus I planned to head to the shop to mix up something to keep Mouse\u2019s anemia in check. We scattered to the four winds but kept our ear curls so we could actually update everyone.<br /> <br /> Because we all were getting the information at the same time, I don\u2019t remember who found out what now, but the end results pissed me off. Carol is a Blood Bather. This came out due to the mysterious Mariah Williams being almost guaranteed to be the fabled Mariah Winthrop. It almost sounds like she\u2019s built a cult around her this time. And they are not subtle as the disappearances have drawn the attention of a European group of vampire hunters. They are apparently not just Christian, but devout followers of Jesus. In general, I would have little issues here minus the vampire hunter part, but they don\u2019t seem to be the \u201cTurn the other cheek\u201d sort of followers. This isn\u2019t just a bunch of book-toting occultists either. They have apparently tracked Carol to Gotham Citi fully loaded for a fight. They were packing so much heat, the club threw them out and called the police. Carol wasn\u2019t lucky enough to slip past them though as they managed to drive a stake through her heart before escaping. That was apparently a few days before I tried to talk to her. Explains why Carol was so paranoid. But to top off everything else, the hunters have set camp in the Firehouse church. We own that church and I pushed to have Ephraim setup to stay there. It is not meant to be used by squatting vampire hunters. Nightshade is sounding nervous, so apparently I\u2019m getting angry.<br /> <br /> We have a plan. We use the hair we got from Mouse to track Ritchie. Then we covertly rescue him as long as he\u2019s still Ritchie the kid. Then we sneak in and curse one of the hunters during the day (so they can\u2019t blame vampires) with an image of Jesus come to send them on a mission. This way it looks like the hunters (that have the vampires all wound up and pissed off thanks to the Blood Bathers being sloppy) left after saving Ritchie, which was obviously what they came for. Then no one else needs to know we were involved or that someone other than the hunters is on their trail. This sounds like a Napalm Recon Mission if ever there was one.<br /> <br /> Oh no. Tavia came in just a bit ago to inform me she \u201chandled\u201d Leslie summoning a spirit to her party last night. She wouldn\u2019t elaborate but she did smile like a shark. On the way out, she mentioned that Leslie probably wouldn\u2019t be coming into work today either. I wasn\u2019t even thinking about when I was at the shop. One of the girls was working so I just kept working on my elixir. I\u2019ll have to ask them about it later. At least I know I can count on them to keep the shop running. I will definitely need to speak with Leslie...maybe with bandages.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1800 Hours, Monday, November 1, 2010<br /> <br /> The plans changed.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes, Nightshade, and I accepted our mission and headed to the Firehouse church. Because we\u2019re dealing with religious fanatics, we decided that all of them should bear witness to the Word. Yes we\u2019re terrible people, but trust me I could have been so much worse before we were finished. I would set a trigger for the curse to take effect and then they would be visited by Jesus directly. Everyone would see the same thing. We just had to hope I was good enough to pull it off.<br /> <br /> Nightshade used her Boneyard to find four hunters sleeping with a fifth on watch. She made it easier for me to sneak around, but I still had to be careful. I\u2019m no Rose. I stepped over the bear trap just inside the door and then almost hit a tripwire. My heart stopped for a beat. I traced it back and found the wire led to tin cans. I felt better as that was something to alert them, not blow up intruders. Pretty smart low-tech idea. Unfortunately low-tech was not the order of the day. When I came to the basement staircase, they had barricaded half of it with furniture and pallets to narrow the passage. At the head of the stairs was a laptop on a table. Nightshade told me she couldn\u2019t read the screen but described it enough for us to figure out it was some kind of monitoring software. I looked around at how everything was setup and realized it was using infrared beams, two ahead of the laptop and two more across the staircase. Who the hell keeps that kind of tech just on them? Made me realize this was part of something larger and that making sure they left without suspension was suddenly our top priority. I went back out and got some of Nightshade\u2019s mirrors. Next we fashioned a sort of brace on my leg at the right spots for the most MacGyver\u2019d countermeasures ever. Thankfully it worked. The laptop was in Cyrillic but I couldn\u2019t say what language for sure. But at least I knew we were dealing with Eastern Europeans for a point of reference.<br /> <br /> I made it down the stairs and avoided another can tripwire. In the basement, things got harder. There were two more laptops setup around the space. One had another set of sensors but I didn\u2019t have to deal with that one as I could see all five of the hunters. They had more firepower and weaponry around them than we do in the armory. The problem came when I got a good look at the second laptop. The chair was sitting on was lashed to the wall shelf. At the bottom of the chair was a shaped charge, set to take the legs out from under anyone that hit the tripwire. I felt my pulse double and the red started closing in around the edges of my vision. They had constructed an IED in my church!<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how many seconds I stood there fighting the urge to finish them all or to reset the charge before I realized I was hearing Nightshade\u2019s worried voice through the ear curl. She talked me back down and I stuck to the plan, mostly. While I\u2019m no master like Snowflake, I\u2019ve gotten pretty good at curses. I burned a chunk of my Plasm but I think it will be worth it. After we rescue Ritchie, Nightshade will return and strike them all blind with her Boneyard. That will trigger the Phantasmal Curse I laid on each of them. Jesus will appear to them and explain how Scientology is run by vampires in Clearwater, Florida. Obviously this is a much larger problem than the issues here in New Haven. \u201cFollowers\u201d would be sent to handle things locally so they could leave. \u201cBody Thetan Tests\u201d were being used to test blood for nutrients under the guise of Scientologist beliefs. But the Lord will be displeased and also inform them, \u201cBring Not Weapons of Mass Destruction into My House.\u201d Then the Savior will leave them with a final decree to spread His message to all that they trust. They will all believe these edicts as ... well gospel, for almost a week without question. After that, I\u2019m hoping we set the situation up well enough that their belief won\u2019t allow them to doubt and follow through anyway. With my mission accomplished, I used my countermeasures and escaped without leaving any sign of my passing.<br /> <br /> I might have scared myself a little bit now that I\u2019m calm. I had to convince myself not to kill five people on the spot or sabotage things so they killed themselves. I am usually the first to realize violence is not the first option. I will have to steel myself for the possibility the next time I have to go in.<br /> <br /> Goddamned explosives.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> So, Natalie says I shouldn\u2019t sleep with anyone new until we\u2019d actually completed some of our jobs, which seems totally unfair since she picked up the one before last. Though, I guess, to really be fair, she said *we* shouldn\u2019t. :-) I think I might make an exception for Timothy though, since we\u2019re already working for his sister (and technically him) and it has been a bit of time since I\u2019ve been with a dude, after Doc got all grumpy and everything. And besides, Timothy\u2019s a pretty cute guy.<br /> <br /> So, Halloween was good. I did in fact find my new friend Tracy again and after we\u2019d enjoyed a stimulating Halloween celebration at Murder Ballads, we snuck off to her house to become further acquainted. All in all, a very good time - I even dreamed about her that night. Apparently, in my dreams she has a brilliantly white house on a stunningly bright island, and despite my state upon arrival, she usually doesn\u2019t have beautiful naked women showing up there, which is just a shame really.<br /> <br /> I met her brother (Timothy) that morning, seeing as he shares the house with her. Like I said, he\u2019s pretty cute. He\u2019s the younger one, and seems to live in her shadow a lot. It would really be cruel to leave him all alone. Besides, I'll be seeing him again anyway, since he and his sister had a job for us. It would just be teasing at that point. The job's nothing I can really talk about right now, though mostly because it\u2019s really puzzling and we don\u2019t have a lot that\u2019s concrete at the moment. However, it doesn\u2019t seem to be immediately dangerous, so again, back burnered.<br /> <br /> Especially since things with the Richie case have heated up. Alexia got in touch with a contact she thought might be able to help and between that and the research Natalie and I got done, we have a good idea what\u2019s going on, if not a good way to deal with it. It\u2019s some serious shit. Nothing I would think about taking on by myself. See, there\u2019s a, let\u2019s say, cult, a real conspiracy theory type thing, that a different troupe nearby had dealt with before. We figured out the Carol\u2019s family had ties to them, going way back. Also, Alexia had been approached by another man who knew about the disappearances, and the name he gave her was similar to a leader of the cult, near enough that an incredibly vain villain might think it made a good cover identity. All the pieces fit together, so most likely, that cult\u2019s pulled itself together and has gone back to abducting kids for their rituals.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s bad news, for certain. Unfortunately, Carol is almost certainly a part of the cult, based on her conversation with Doc. With any, well, luck, I guess, she was blackmailed into it, coerced somehow, and I might be able to convince her to help us out. Of course, that means bad things happening to her, almost surely, but... this is seriously bad news and can\u2019t be allowed to continue. I just hope I can, as Doc said, \u201cfuck her into saying yes\u201d to helping us, as opposed to having to threaten or kidnap her somehow.<br /> <br /> Anyways, to make things more complicated, there\u2019s a different flavor of cult/gang also in town that\u2019s gotten stirred up. Not so much because they have anything to do with Carol\u2019s cult, but because the gang\u2019s rivals have showed up, thinking that Carol\u2019s cult is actually the gang because of the way they\u2019ve tipped their hand. So the gang is getting twitchy, and so is Doc, cause the rivals have set up their territory in his. Specifically, in an old church that the troupe technically owns, I think, but mostly appears to be abandoned.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve worked out a decent plan though. We need to get Richie out of there, and fast, if he\u2019s still around to be gotten out - the cult\u2019s into blood magic and just, bad shit. Even so, we\u2019re not set up to go head to head with the cult yet, and if we show our hand, it\u2019ll likely go to ground again. So, our immediate plan is to go for a snatch and grab, getting Richie out of there by any means necessary without showing our faces. Then, we make it so the rival gang skips town. Hopefully, the cult assumes that it was the taking of Richie that stuck a bee in the rival gang\u2019s bonnet, and since they were gone, the threat had passed.<br /> <br /> The best part is going to be setting it up so that the rival gang will leave. You see, the gang is very... Jesus oriented, as our informant put it. So we\u2019re going to arrange for the group of them to each have a personal visitation. Since mostly we just want them out of town, we\u2019re going to give them a new mission. These guys will be receiving word from on high that the Clearwater headquarters of Scientology had been infiltrated by the gang they were after, which is clearly far more important than whatever was going on here. I believe Doc made some last minute alterations to the set up, since as he was going down to rig up what we\u2019d need to convince these guys, he came across a tripwire bomb, a shaped charge no less. Doc is... not very alright with explosives and things, from being in the war and all, so he made sure they\u2019d never bring bombs into a church again. It seems fair to me.<br /> <br /> Our last piece of the plan before we get down to action is finding out precisely where Richie is and doing some surveillance. Ideally, finding all the snipers. I like the idea of finding *all* of them. So, wish us luck?<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 1st, 2010<br /> <br /> -Well that was a fun night.<br /> <br /> -I have never had a more\u2026thorough\u2026interview.<br /> <br /> -Man what a crazy weekend. I can\u2019t do every weekend like that anymore.<br /> <br /> -Damnit.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jog<br /> <br /> -Did you have a good Halloween? I had a good Halloween.<br /> <br /> -Sara has the weirdest things happen to her.<br /> <br /> -No seriously. I could try and explain but\u2026no I don\u2019t know where to start.<br /> <br /> -Scheming, but a good kind of scheming.<br /> <br /> -Chandra looks like the canary that ate the cat.<br /> <br /> -Okay so I think we have a plan.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -Reading Reading<br /> <br /> -Not that, you know, Sara is distracting or anything.<br /> <br /> -Oh that is so not good, on so many not good levels.<br /> <br /> -Well, we know what we are up against :-/<br /> <br /> -Time to Huddle.<br /> <br /> -Well there is Karen, bout time she showed up ^_^<br /> <br /> -Yaaaaaaaaaaaay! ^_^<br /> <br /> -Okay Owlish Housemate scares me.<br /> <br /> -Focus now, planning and stuff.<br /> <br /> -Man Doc is angry.<br /> <br /> -\u2026Redundant, I suppose.<br /> <br /> -Man I have a sacrilege problem.<br /> <br /> -Okay, cursing and such time.<br /> <br /> -Not the usual way.<br /> <br /> -Tune in, turn on, drop out.<br /> <br /> -Odd.<br /> <br /> -Okay, that is done. Back to base for phase 2.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXI</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Jeez 111 sessions already?<br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s journal, as usual, is oblique. The \u201cJesus oriented\u201d gang is of course Vampire Hunters. The stirred up gang is the local Kindred and Carol\u2019s \u201cgang\u201d are the Blood Bathers. Hopefully the other journals put that in context but there you go.<br /> <br /> The \u201cMagic Dream Island\u201d Tracy and Timothy have has no apparent explanation\u2026for now. But I wanted to go ahead and introduce it. Tracy was the one I was tormenting Sara\u2019s player with previously. One thing Sara did not mention directly was dead relatives of theirs sometimes come and give them messages. But then one day they all showed up at once for Tracy, became zombie-looking, and tried to pull her into the sea. They have not appeared since, in normal or undead form, but it was recently and no relatives have died since then.<br /> <br /> Had the Candle Cove story come up on rpg.net and I gave a bit of a recap. Good times.<br /> <br /> Jasmine returns this coming session. Simon\u2019s player is still dealing with his Doctoral Work so is not back, but I <i>hope</i> to have him back by the end of the year. Comments and Questions are welcome as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-13T20:22:54-07:00","id":196645,"title":"","content":"Can't these gangs just solve their problems with the power of dance? You know like all the gangs of '82?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 07-13-2014, 11:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-14T02:02:51-07:00","id":196658,"title":"","content":"Well of course that is how *I* would do it, certainly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-30T01:26:06-07:00","id":213279,"title":"","content":"Apologies for the delay, totally my fault I did not realize Doc\u2019s player had sent his log in much earlier, or I would have had this earlier. Jasmine is back and life is good for the Krewe\u2026of course a good life means mysteries, and they have those a-plenty.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> When I finished my last entry, I came down to find Rose and Karl were back. We had dinner with most of the Krewe like normal and it felt good. We filled her in on the events of the weekend minus the copious number of sexual encounters by pretty much everyone and Leslie\u2019s event, though honestly I still don\u2019t know much about that myself.<br /> <br /> After dinner, we split up. Bright Eyes drove Nightshade\u2019s care while Cupcake cast the Finding ceremony on Ritchie\u2019s hair. Rose went along for protection and support. Once in the area, Nightshade claimed her Boneyard and the search began. Meanwhile, Tavia drove me to go shopping for supplies and also to have me closer without the entire Krewe being identified randomly. The ear curls kept us all in communication just in case.<br /> <br /> Nightshade found Ritchie and another girl in the target house with two women dressed as maids. It was an upper class ranch with an addition built specifically for housing their victims. A single door led in from the main house with no exterior exits. The windows were all rigged with alarms and the door on the inside of the detention area was made up to blend with the wall. Both of the prisoners seemed high. On the plus side, Nightshade found the security cameras but did not see any snipers. I picked up ski masks for the whole Krewe as I doubt this will be the last time we need to be seen but not identified. Then I found fatigues and a few other pieces based on what I saw of the sleeping hunters. We also stopped at TruValue and I found some planting stakes. Rose waited until they were far enough away then turned into a flock of birds to double check the area for snipers or anything else we might not be expecting. Once she had moved back through the area without finding any shooters, she phased into the house to determine the state of the kids. I keep saying kids, but I\u2019m pretty sure they are over 18. Either way, they were under the influence of something.<br /> <br /> Invisibly, Rose talked to them and determined that they were still alive and aging normally, but they were both very high. She posed as the \u201cFriendly Neighborhood Wallaby\u201d and learned that they were probably being fed the drugs with meals but had otherwise not been harmed. They were so high that Ritchie had never even noticed the door in the wall. When Rose pointed it out, he moved over and tried to open it, but found it was locked. I tuned out of that conversation when someone suggested that we get something from the hunters to leave behind when we assaulted the house. Thus I had Tavia take me over the the Firehouse church. It was well after dark by this point so the hunters were all gone. Thankfully so were their laptops. I found three stakes and their sleeping bags but I decided not to take their stuff for fear of alerting them. Instead I gathered up hair from their sleeping bags to leave for physical evidence at the house. Then we met the others back at the Bluffs.<br /> <br /> I handed out the masks and fatigues then got the guns ready. We took Nightshade and Bright Eye\u2019s cars due to number of people. When we got close, Nightshade used her Hedge magic to summon a thunderstorm. It would help cover us and also make her uses of Cold Wind Boneyard easier. Rose went invisible and I activated my Phantasmal Shroud just to I could make myself unrecognizable regardless of the mask. The plan evolved a bit since the storm provided so much assistance. We\u2019d use thunder to cover the shotgun blast to open the front door. Then we would not speak while I took care of the maid. Once I knew where she was, I brought a black cloth bag to pull over her head then use a chair to lock her in a room. As I dealt with her, Cupcake and Rose the invisible wallaby would deal with the prison door. Since we knew the place at security cameras that didn\u2019t display anywhere in the house, we wanted to make sure they got a look at both me and Cupcake. But then Nightshade realized she could blow a transformer with her lightning and make the whole area blackout. That made things even easier. Hard to blame supernatural influence over your cameras when a whole neighborhood goes dark. The plan worked perfectly. We got in after blowing the door open without any problems. Nightshade waited until I had the maid locked down and moved to join my accomplice before zapping the lines. Cupcake had the lock picked by the time I got to that side of the house and Rose convinced Ritchie and his cellmate to come with us. I dropped the hunters\u2019 hair by the cell door and by the door to the maid\u2019s room. Then we bolted.<br /> <br /> The storm made driving a little harder, but it also mean fewer people on the roads and less chance of anyone spotting us. On the way back to the Bluffs, we learned Ritchie\u2019s cellmate was Lindsey Davis. They were both still very high. We arrived back home without incident to find Tavia, Karl and Chandra waiting just inside the door. Tavia\u2019s knife was on the end table next to her while Chandra had a bat on her lap. It was obvious they were prepared in case trouble tried to follow us. I was kind of glad Ritchie and Lindsey were high right then. Tavia took our guests upstairs to find a room while Cupcake called Mouse. Rose drove me over to the shop so I could gather my ingredients for a cleansing tea in the morning. Then we gathered Plasm from AMC before coming back. The storm was and is still going strong so I think we\u2019ll get a pass on suspicion leading to us this time. I was very impressed with how well we managed this mission. No direct ties to us, completely framed another group, and no one got hurt. I really want us to get in the habit of using these tactics more often. Openly being Paranormal Investigators is one thing, covertly ruining plans of much more organized and paranoid groups is another entirely.<br /> <br /> Now I think I\u2019m going to practice my katas until closer to time for me to sleep.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> I might have worked myself a little harder than I thought last night. I got up around 0700 Hours but it took an hour to meditate. Retraining muscle memory is stressful when the body isn\u2019t prepared for it.<br /> <br /> We all gathered for breakfast around 0900 Hours, including Ritchie, Lindsey, and Mouse. They kids were mostly sobered up but I gave them each some cleansing tea to help get the trash out of their system. I also gave Mouse more tea to keep her system from getting run down. I\u2019m not sure how much blood Chandra took, but I didn\u2019t want any surprises or accidents either. Then we had breakfast and got info from our rescuees. I asked each of them what they remembered before last night. Ritchie was unconvincingly vague at first. Lindsey made some reference to being with a woman and I stated that we weren\u2019t here or able to judge people. Lindsey was with Carol when Jenny came. Jenny was Carol\u2019s ex or something and they had had a fight. Then Jenny looked at Lindsey and basically said \u201cCome to me!\u201d with her eyes. This worked better than Lindsey could understand and she woke up in the cell with Ritchie. She said that here Jenny was called Mariah, but she was sure her named was Jenny. Blushing a little, Ritchie then admitted that he went home with John. It was the Bowtie Man. They had no idea how long they\u2019d been missing and Ritchie freaked out when I pointed out he was gone a month. When I told Lindsey what day it was, she said she\u2019d been gone for two weeks. I noted that Mouse would take them home but first, they should probably figure out what they were going to tell their families. I also told Ritchie that he needed to clear Evan\u2019s name. I made it a point to note that the people who took them were very protected so trying to send the police after them would not be a great idea. I wanted to vomit as I said it because I wanted nothing more than to watch these people rot behind bars. But proving to remember who was behind their kidnapping would eventually prove fatal for those unprepared and/or unable to fight back against the money and influence. I also gave them both my number and told them if they ever needed help, they could always call me. Then Mouse took them home.<br /> <br /> Nightshade waited until they were gone to state that she thought Lindsey was taken to leverage Carol back in line. I wasn\u2019t sure that Carol cared, given that she was prowling when she picked Bright Eyes up, maybe a week or so later. But we had more to do and timing was important. So while Bright Eyes goes to invite Carol for coffee so we could see if she was worth dealing with, the rest of the Krewe is headed to the Firehouse church.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1145 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade used her Boneyard in the car and after just a few minutes she sat up and declared that Jesus had entered the building. We left the hunters to their vision and headed to Lulu\u2019s for coffee and Blood Bathers.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes and Carol arrived separately and Carol looked very much on edge. If I had to guess, I\u2019d say she was packing. She didn\u2019t seem surprised to see me, but she didn\u2019t look pleased about it either. We tried to be as honest with her as possible, given we needed her to do the same. I talked more than usual, probably because we weren\u2019t trying to hide anything. We learned that Jenny was the mysterious Mariah Williams, but that Mariah Winthrop was behind her sudden burst of influence. Jenny came from a family that worked for a living and actually her father worked for Carol\u2019s family. That was how they met. They were just friends at first, then lovers. But Carol said that Jenny always wanted to be part of the elite. They eventually had a fight and broke up over how close Jenny was getting to Mariah. Then after some time passed, Jenny called Carol claiming to have found a way to let her live forever. Carol said she met with Jenny intending to break off everything...then things were a blur and she didn\u2019t really want to talk about it. She said that Jenny was different after that and she believed that Mariah was controlling Jenny somehow. The description made me think more of possession and we know better than to put anything past Mariah. I also suspected that while Jenny believed turning Carol into a Blood Bather was a favor, Mariah\u2019s plan was to groom and prepare two new bodies to help her go unnoticed for longer. Carol agreed to bring a ring which matches one Jenny has from Mariah. Jenny never seems to be without it and she wanted Carol to wear it as well. Carol says she\u2019s only had the ring on once, but not for very long. It has some sort of red liquid inside and is heavy. We suspect this ring is magical and I think it may be linked sympathetically to Mariah Winthrop. If so, we might finally have a led on how to stop her.<br /> <br /> Now I think I\u2019m going to ask Nightshade to help me with the driving part of the license test.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Well, things have certainly moved quickly. Once we set up things so we could run the rival gang out whenever we needed to, it was about time for Jasmine to get back, so we swung round and picked her up. We took time for dinner and to get Jasmine all caught up, then we started right up after Richie. Alexia\u2019s really good at the tracking kind of sympathetic magic, and since Katherine was working for Richie\u2019s family, we had everything we needed. So we knew exactly where he was in just a couple of hours.<br /> <br /> The set up was a bit strange. He (and another girl) were being kept in a house on the good side of town, not mansion-land or anything, but a good neighborhood. Most of the security, such as it was, came from the fact that there had been an addition to the house somewhat recently, 3 rooms or so, that had only one door and even that just led into the house. Still, there were windows in the addition, probably with alarms or something, but nothing making it more secure than a regular house not used for storing kidnapped college aged kids. There weren\u2019t even any guards, just a couple of maids. The only reason the kids couldn\u2019t just get out themselves was they were being kept drugged.<br /> <br /> I don't mean to sound like I'm complaining or anything, because breaking them out went really smoothly and that's always good. Natalie and I stayed back in the car - Natalie for surveillance and me to keep the engine running, so the other three got suited up, pretending to be members of that rival gang. One be-closeted maid and a few moments of lockpick jiggling later, and I was off with 5 adults in fatigues/sneak suits and 2 drugged out college kids in my station wagon. Typical Monday, right?<br /> <br /> As an aside, Jasmine has an absolutely horrendous American accent. I pray to all the gods who watch over beautiful women that we never need to all pretend to be American ever, cause that is just an affront to the hotness that is her usual accent. I\u2019m telling you, if this whole supernatural vigilante thing doesn\u2019t work out, I\u2019m moving to New Zealand. Like, yesterday.<br /> <br /> Anyways, it was pretty late, and the rescuees were drugged to the gills, so we left them parked in front of a TV, figuring we\u2019d talk with them in the morning. Jasmine and Doc went for a bit of erranding, including getting some cleansing herbs for our guests, while I spent time with my ladies. The roof of the house is an amazing viewpoint, by the way. It\u2019s almost like being suspended (especially when doing handstands on the peak). It\u2019s a bit lacking in the fire aspect, but the idea last night was to get more in touch with the air aspect anyway. I\u2019ll have to go up next time we have a lightning storm, see how the balance works then.<br /> <br /> The kids were much better this morning. Richie was a bit cagey about the last thing he remembered before getting all drugged up, at least until Lindsay (the other girl who we rescued) started talking about how the last thing she remembered was getting seduced away from her kinda girlfriend Carol by a hot lady named Jenny. When we didn\u2019t respond poorly to any of that, Richie admitted he\u2019d gone off with Mr John I-didn\u2019t-get-his-last-name Formerly-known-as-bowtie-man. That was about what we\u2019d figured, and he didn\u2019t remember much else, but Lindsay\u2019s story was intriguing, as her kinda girlfriend Carol was in fact the same Carol we\u2019d been keeping an eye on. Jenny was a new name, which at the time we figured was a more creative pseudonym for the cult leader. Turns out we had it all mixed up, but that comes later.<br /> <br /> Lindsay\u2019s story worked like this though - she\u2019d been with Carol at her place when Carol\u2019s ex, Jenny, showed up. Carol was upset that she was there in the first place, and Jenny\u2019s response was to seduce Lindsay away from her. This Jenny has some serious mind whammy stuff going on. Lindsay said she couldn\u2019t think clearly when she was around, and everything was kind of surreal, even before the drugs. Even so, looking back, she was pretty sure Jenny had only done it to piss Carol off, as the two of them (Carol and Lindsay) were pretty serious. Lindsay wasn\u2019t really comfortable calling her her girlfriend, I think largely because of class differences, and also because the last time Lindsay had seen Carol she\u2019d left with her ex, but there was something there anyway.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s theory (and all of us agreed) was that Lindsay had been taken to get leverage over Carol. Calling it Carol\u2019s cult (while the safest way to describe it for you) was probably unfair, as from the sound of it, she\u2019d gotten out, or become estranged. And cults generally don\u2019t like that. So, we figured we needed to get to Carol as soon as possible, since we had no idea what the cult might do now that they\u2019d lost their leverage. The trap still needed to be sprung, to get the rival gang out of town, so the others went to do that while I went to go lure Carol into a meeting somewhere where there would be less likely to be sniper retaliation. At least that\u2019s what I talked us down to after starting at storming Carol\u2019s house and confronting her all together.<br /> <br /> Carol was surprised to see me, but did let me in. She was extremely suspicious, which seems fair for someone being pursued by a crazy cult. I eventually got her to trust me enough to meet me somewhere, mostly by talking about saving Lindsay, and emphasizing that we wanted to stop people from being kidnapped and needed her help. She does really care about Lindsay, and for her part, had no qualms about calling her her girlfriend. I did manage to avoid tying us to the other troupe, the one that had dealt with the cult leader before - that's probably our biggest goal, to not be associated with them until we are in a place to do something for good. And if it had turned out that Carol was working with them willingly, all she would have known is that we wanted to stop the kidnappings.<br /> <br /> I really don't want to believe she was though. Not because I'd slept with her. Well, not just because I'd slept with her. It's not like I haven't had sex with douchebags before. It just didn't seem to fit. She had an air of sadness and fear and everything seemed to point away from her being evil. Probably I'm just being silly and a pretty face will get me killed someday. I did warn Carol about Doc. Not because I thought he'd do anything to her, or even be too particularly threatening, but mostly because this was a 'lay (almost) all your cards on the table' kind of moment. Doc does have something of a hammer problem sometimes, and I was worried that if she noticed him looking at her like a nail, she'd get spooked, and it would be worse since I said my friends were safe. It all worked out anyway.<br /> <br /> As it turns out, Carol hadn't been inducted very deep into the cult. She participated in one of their rituals, which we'd known - there are signs of that sort of thing - but she didn't know any of the details, having been kept in the dark by the cult leader, who was using Jenny as a face for the cult, setting her up as the wealthy woman I spoke of before, who ran 'parties'. Carol was strongly tied to them however. Jenny was Carol's ex, as Lindsay had mentioned, and the cult leader was an old friend of her family. Carol had always had something of a crush on the cult leader, but the cult leader had always preferred men, until she met Jenny. Now, we're pretty sure she's still just interested in men, at least sexually, and Jenny's being groomed as, well, something like a successor, rather than a romantic partner.<br /> <br /> To that point, Carol said Jenny had changed, a lot, since she took up with the cult leader. Things like the way she smiled, and an extra added coldness to her eyes. Also, things like stealing away Lindsay just because she could. Not to mention the fact that she could in the first place, that Lindsay couldn't think clearly when she was talking to her, that Carol got talked into joining the cult. Something about their blood magic clearly speaks to manipulation. Still, Carol was very persistent in trying to get us to promise to try and save Jenny from the cult. Alexia and I promised to try, and Doc wouldn't even go so far, probably fairly. With any luck though, there will be some sort of focus we can deal with to break the cult leader's hold over Jenny. Really, our luck will be with us if she has any kind of supernatural hold over Jenny, and not just the more mundane tools of jealousy and greed - even according to Carol, having been born the daughter of a servant in her house, Jenny always had something of a chip on her shoulder. And now, as part of this cult, she has more wealth and power than Carol ever did.<br /> <br /> So, there was good news and bad news. The good news is Carol absolutely does not want to be part of the cult, even though her participation in the first ritual could mean her death if she does not continue. Also, she has some jewelry that Jenny gave her, that might provide enough of a sympathetic link to learn more. The bad news is, we still no absolutely nothing more mystically about the cult or where the leader might be holed up. We knew before that they use a particularly nasty variety of blood magic, but the possibilities within that category are close to limitless. And each one has a different counter.<br /> <br /> We do have a few leads to go on. She did tell us where Jenny's actual house is, which is where the ritual took place, at least for Carol. So we can check that out. The jewelry might turn out to be helpful. Lastly, though I think I'll have a fight on my hands, if Jenny is watching over Carol, and stealing away anyone she gets close to, then, well, I might just need to spend some time with a beautiful woman (the horror). Admittedly, that's as likely to get us another bolthole like we found Richie and Lindsay in as anything useful, but it might get me in physical contact with Jenny or even the cult leader. And that has some possibilities. No one liked that very much, especially Doc, so that's off the table until we have nothing else to check, I imagine.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 1st 2010<br /> <br /> -Awwwight, now we\u2019s got Spooky back, we\u2019s unstoppable.<br /> <br /> -Explaining everything to Spooky.<br /> <br /> -Well, almost everything.<br /> <br /> -Lady\u2019s gotta have her secrets.<br /> <br /> -Dinner then rescue mission<br /> <br /> -Power Mwa ha ha ha!<br /> <br /> -Ahem.<br /> <br /> -Okay radio silence<br /> <br /> -Well, that could have gone worse.<br /> <br /> -Hmmm\u2026your Mistress needs to snuggle with her spouses and get an emotional recharge.<br /> <br /> -Yay Sara and Karen. ^_^<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m so happy\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> November 2nd, 2010<br /> <br /> -\u201cBreakfast\u201d went as well as could be expected.<br /> <br /> -Catherine is taking the kids home, time for scouting. And cursing.<br /> <br /> -Whee cursing!<br /> <br /> -Sara was successful with her project.<br /> <br /> -Yea, yea this is gonna be awkward.<br /> <br /> -Pretty awkward.<br /> <br /> -Uh boy.<br /> <br /> -Well, it certainly could have gone worse\u2026<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Twilight Network Report:<br /> <br /> Hey Guys and Ghouls, sorry to have a second report so soon, and still not about my spending my Halloween smothered in beautiful women. That report will have to wait. No no, this is relevant to your interests. Your other interests, ghoulfriends. What is it with you people and my love life anyway?<br /> <br /> Ok serious time. The number of Blood Bathers in the area has ramped up to three minimum. They are all connected, and are part of the Winthrop Problem. Names of two are Jenny Chambers and Carol Jameson. Jenny may be under the control of Mariah Winthrop. Well, she sort of is but may be being possessed or directly controlled.<br /> <br /> They have been culling their victims from the local gay community, though now that we have freed two would be victims that may or may not continue. Hopefully the quietus has been put on that tool. Because Winthrop is involved they may be alert to Sin-Eaters. Not rousing the other Krewe quite yet, and not looking to have Bound creeping in yet. If I need help, I\u2019ll sound the red alert. Right now we are handling it.<br /> <br /> If I abruptly go off the grid, I\u2019ve encoded both Jenny and Carol\u2019s addresses. We are probably captive if this happens. Usual contact at the usual number can answer questions.<br /> <br /> Whiplash Girl Child in the Dark signing off.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXII</i><br /> <br /> So Jasmine is back. We spent some time updating her player with what went on. They had kept up with journals, of course, but it was good to give a breakdown of the past few days in game.<br /> <br /> Not much mechanically to go over here. Of course Mariah is not limited to just Blood Bather powers, but she is not a Mage or anything.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s player had to miss the next session due to unexpected family needs, but the session went well, and we will have, at least, something for Natalie and Sara. Some developments with Natalie and Jasmine\u2019s personal issues and pushed the plots forward a bit. Do join us. Comments and Questions welcome in the meantime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T14:28:21-07:00","id":222459,"title":"","content":"Question Herr Baron: Is Dark Haven an actual town or one that you came up with? Also, in either case do you have a link to info about the town or am I being silly and there is a post in the way beginning of this journal with the information I am seeking? I ask because I am going to be running a part-time gods game for my Dad and roommate and I was hoping to set it in Dark Haven.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T16:47:16-07:00","id":222564,"title":"","content":"The game is set in New Haven, Connecticut, most famous for Yale, which is real. Dark Haven Bluffs is a fictional location in New Haven where the Fishborn house (also made up, obviously) stands.<br /> <br /> Most clubs/bars mentioned in the game are real. Gotham Citi is real, Alchemy is real. Lulu's is real. The exception is Murder Ballads, which is not real. The name was taken from a club in Providence I think (which is no longer wherever it was), though I could be misremembering, but the Club itself takes inspiration from a lot of sources, including the classic Succubus Club from <b>Chicago by Night</b> and the standard &quot;Dark Cathedral Nightclub&quot; stuff, such as Confession in<i> Bloodlines </i>(though Confession itself did not inspire it initially as I created it about 3 years before I played <i>Bloodlines</i> the first time). Of course The 27 Club is not real, but somewhat inspired, both IC and OOC, by CBGB. All the parks (like Sleeping Giant) are real. All the Universities (Yale, Albertus Magnus) are real and the dorms mentioned at Albertus Magnus are real. Hopefully less haunted though. The history of how some Dorms were sort of absorbed from old buildings in the area is true. The mentioned lighthouses are real.<br /> <br /> I can't promise how accurate my portrayal of New Haven is. Only one of all 7 of us have been to New Haven (Simon Fishborne's player) and he stopped by a place or two while driving through a few times. One other player has been to Conneticut once for a wedding (Jasmine's player) but did not stop in or drive though New Haven as far as I know, and it was well over a decade before the game regardless. I consulted with another player not in this game (but in <i>Malibu Dream House</i>) who is from Connecticut (but not New Haven) when I was first working on the game, but it was mostly a &quot;does this sound like stupid bullshit to you&quot; conversation. I used <a href=\"http://www.clubct.com/newhaven.htm\" target=\"_blank\">This Website</a> when researching the game in 2010 but it looks different now, some clubs added some gone. Also sites for state parks and the universities, and Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> Hope that is helpful","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-08T17:01:36-07:00","id":222569,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Thanks you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-11T02:03:00-07:00","id":224939,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to return to our group in New Haven. This session\u2019s journals will be strange, as only Sara will really be describing events that took place in play. Doc\u2019s player had to miss due to a last minute family emergency (everyone is fine now) so his log deals with what Doc was doing during the game time, and Natalie\u2019s journal is a vignette showing events which took place off camera during the session. As a reminder in that, Natalie\u2019s birth name (Allison) is used in the vignette. Anyway, here we go.<br /> <br /> As a note, Natalie\u2019s section may be disturbing or disquieting to new parents, expecting couples, or couples trying to have kids.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> Before I could talk with Nightshade about helping me with driving, the Krewe met for what we might as well call a Working Lunch. All the cards were put on the table so we could figure out the best way to handle things. Bright Eyes still wanted to \u201cgo in\u201d as bait to get close Jenny and Mariah. This was thankfully shouted down by more people than just me, but I\u2019m not sure I like the alternative any better. I\u2019m not sure when we found out there would be another party on Friday, but Nightshade and Bright Eyes are going as a couple since Nightshade feels sure she can use her status as a local sex symbol to get in. For what is ostensibly a sex party, that should do it. Rose, Cupcake, and I will be staked out nearby for if and when the SNAFU hits.<br /> <br /> Carol was apparently bringing the ring to Bright Eyes after lunch so she and Cupcake could give it a full object read and occult inspection. I\u2019m pretty sure we could charge $999.95 for that and make a killing, but anyway. Once we know their results, we\u2019ll have a better idea what can be done with Jenny.<br /> <br /> Since I\u2019m not useful in any of this, I\u2019m going to snatch Nightshade away to make sure I know what I\u2019m doing behind the wheel.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1700 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> Driving is harder than it looks. I mean I think I have a pretty good handle on it, but I was surprised at how much you have to constantly consider. I have no idea how Ronin could do the things she did while driving. Nightshade gave me a good lesson on three point turns and parallel parking. Apparently they are very particular about getting that right on the test down in North Carolina. And I have to admit, it took a few tries to get either one right. I\u2019m just glad I didn\u2019t scrape the curb or scratch Nightshade\u2019s wheels. I think the extra height I\u2019ll have in the van will help, but not having a rear view mirror will not. If I have too many problems with it, I\u2019ll see about getting one of those rear view backup monitors. I\u2019m sure Snowflake and I can figure out how that is supposed to work.<br /> <br /> I got the Cliff Notes version of what happened with the ring after Nightshade and I came back around 1600 Hours. I wasn\u2019t too far off from my theory about the Blood Stone rings. The ring didn\u2019t make you love someone, like Jenny hoped. Instead it makes the wearer easier to control. And there was something that I didn\u2019t get all the details on that would allow Mariah to suck away the wearer\u2019s life force. I assume this is to somehow keep her alive or healthy or amused. Something. Either way, they wouldn\u2019t let me smash the rings nor were they ready to try to use sympathetic magic to strike at Mariah.<br /> <br /> They were ready to visit Rose\u2019s dad in Taiwan however. Yeah, that felt like a jump to me too, but I wasn\u2019t there for all the details. Apparently there was blood in the ring Cupcake and Bright Eyes studied. Because we\u2019re dealing with Blood Bathers, this is even more important to get. Rose\u2019s dad had the right kind of jeweler\u2019s tools at his antique shop to get to the blood without ruining the ring. So Nightshade offered to pop her over for a visit. They plan to head over sometime after dinner so that the times line up a little better. Given we aren\u2019t pressed for time (yet), I think Rose is hoping to spend time with her dad while there. Also probably have more of those awesome buns and potstickers without having to share. Maybe I\u2019m just hungry. Lucky for me Cupcake will have dinner ready soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Tuesday, November 2, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Rose got off without any problems about an hour ago. With them gone, I caught up with Karl a little bit until Chandra announced that she and Cupcake were going to watch a movie. We knew what that meant, but Bright Eyes didn\u2019t. She and Karen were apparently having their own date night. Karl and I moved out of the TV room to continue our discussion of the effects shifting forms has on hand-to-hand combat. He gave me some examples of how your center of gravity has to shift when your opponents are smaller than you that I would have never considered. About fifteen minutes into our happily uninterrupted conversation, Bright Eyes and Karen walked out of the TV room. I figured the movie must have been interesting if it took Chandra that long. Karl smirked at me but was too classy to comment. I\u2019ve missed getting to hang out with the big guy.<br /> <br /> Eventually I left Karl to a book he was looking forward to reading. I started to work on a few of my katas, but then remembered that I haven\u2019t contacted Sebastian in some time. When I called so early, Sebastian answered quickly and seemed surprised it was me. I apologized for not staying in touch and wondered if he was still up for teaching me more dance steps. I figured why stop now? Sebastian was little reluctant to commit this time though. I asked if I could make it up to him as I thought he was pissed that I just stopped coming to practice. Instead he admitted he was little afraid to stick around so late as there had been an armed robbery down the block from the studio. So I thought if a different reason for us to meet. I asked if Sebastian would like to have coffee and talk about a different proposal. I really hope he doesn\u2019t think I\u2019m asking him out. I want to ask if he\u2019d like to train in martial arts, given how I\u2019ve started getting back into it. Training someone would only help to get me back into the mindset faster. We\u2019ll see what he thinks.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0230 Hours, Wednesday, November 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I got really lucky when I found Sebastian. I doubt many dance instructors would be nearly as open to my bizarre ideas.<br /> <br /> I met him at the studio just as they were closing up and he took me to a coffee shop many of the dancers frequented. It wasn\u2019t as friendly as Lulu\u2019s but they didn\u2019t kick me out or anything. The robbery had shaken many at the studio because it was one of the other teachers that got robbed. She was okay, but the whole experience left her feeling very vulnerable and violated. Sebastian pointed her out but said she was really not dealing well with strangers right now. I thought was fair. I asked if any of the instructors had ever studied martial arts, since I knew some routines utilized similar movements. He smiled at my question but said he didn\u2019t think so. Then has asked if I wanted to trade. I laughed but that wasn\u2019t my idea. I told him that I would be happy to teach him as it would also help me get back into practice. However I wouldn\u2019t do it instead of paying his fee. Then if he wanted to teach the others when I thought it was safe, he could help them out. I told him that he had to credit me if he worked any of our moves into a routine though. We both laughed and finished our coffee. I walked several of the instructors back to their cars, before they left for the night. Sebastian agreed to meet me again tomorrow night.<br /> <br /> But I was just getting started for the evening. Once the studio instructors had all gone home and the coffee shop closed, I started my patrol. There were only a few people out after 2200 Hours and even less that were obviously sticking around. Sometime after 2300 Hours, a couple of guys that might have been 18 \u201cstumbled\u201d into me but they found they couldn\u2019t pick empty pockets. When I didn\u2019t actually fall from them running into me, I held up a five and asked if that was what they were looking for? I looked back and forth between them as they tried to decide what to do next. Before things turned ugly, a light shined on us. I lowered my hand so it didn\u2019t look like a drug deal. The police asked if everything was alright. I smiled and told the faceless light that we were fine. The boys looked less calm but nodded along with me. I heard the driver say something about that being Doc and they chuckled before wishing us a good night. I turned back to the boys as the light switched off and the cruiser pulled away. We had a very frank discussion about how I would be watching these streets at night and they should probably let their friends know that people in their line of work were going to have it a lot harder. There was another calculated silence. I heard the cruiser turn the corner behind me when the boy on the left decided they could take me. The punch was telegraphed but it would have shattered my nose if I hadn\u2019t stopped it short by catching his fist. When the other boy swung at my open ribs, I threw a left to counter and drove my knuckles into his inner forearm. The force of movement pulled the first boy into the other and they fell into a heap on the curb. I stood over them and repeated that I would be watching these streets. It took a few seconds for them to stop stepping on each up and scramble away. The rest of the evening went smoothly. Tomorrow night should be interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Wednesday, November 3, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation took a little longer than normal this morning. I\u2019m sure it\u2019s because I\u2019m nervous. Hopefully I\u2019ll get my license today.<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Rose got back this morning so they talked about visiting the pawn shop owner over breakfast. I really wanted to go along for that, but I knew Bright Eyes and Nightshade could get things done. Besides, I needed to ask Karl or Tavia to take me to the DMV so I could take my test. Hell maybe even Snowflake, but I don\u2019t know if he\u2019s up yet. Wish me luck.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1630 Hours, Wednesday, November 3, 2010<br /> <br /> I had to wait a little while before I could get a ride as Tavia had to remove a few things from her car. Which really wasn\u2019t so bad considering the Three hours! Three! To wait in line so I could take my test.<br /> <br /> I passed! But everything is not yet happy. They let me take the written test but said I needed some form to show I had insurance before I could take the driving test. I have no idea why my insurance company didn\u2019t think to tell me that when I added the van before. And given the time, there is no way I can get the form and get back in time for anything to happen. Damn it!<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0330 Hours, Thursday, November 4, 2010<br /> <br /> I stalked around the House for a while trying not to be grumpy at anyone. I did learn that Nightshade only had to sniffle a few times before the pawn shop owner gave up the name of the guy who bought Sarah\u2019s comb. I may stop by at some point to get the name of the kid who stole it in the first place, but that will be for later.<br /> <br /> The rest of the time, I spent trying to stay loose and well hydrated for tonight. I got the studio about 2100 Hours, which is still late but not past the time several people are around. Sebastian had a smaller room prepared and was happy to see me so early. We worked on the basics for about two and half hours. Then I decided to break so he could train me. We worked on a tango until about 0100 Hours. Then I walked him to his car. He laughed and said people really would think we were a couple if I kept doing that. I told him I wasn\u2019t worried about what people thought, but I was worried about keeping people safe. He shook my hand and then went home. I spent another two hours walking the alleys around the studio. Nothing happening tonight so now I\u2019m going to bed and hopefully I\u2019ll have my license tomorrow.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1030 Hours, Thursday, November 4, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation went fine today but I\u2019m still nervous. I still haven\u2019t told the Krewe what I\u2019m up to because I want to surprise them with the news. That made breakfast a little harder, but I think we\u2019re just getting ready for tomorrow. Sounds good to me.<br /> <br /> I was going to ask Karl if he could take me to the insurance company and then to the DMV, but when I came down Tavia was already standing with keys in hand. Karl was there too. He told me that Tavia insisted he come with me to make sure everything went smoothly. I had to laugh at that, given I wasn\u2019t really looking to intimidate the DMV. I went back up to get my things and write this<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s to hoping.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1715 Hours, Thursday, November 4, 2010<br /> <br /> Today was a test of my patience more than my driving skills. I had to fill out so much paperwork at the insurance company. I thought they had already taken care of it.<br /> <br /> An hour and a half later, I had to wait in line at the DMV again. How many damn people drive in New Haven? This time I had my form from the insurance company, all my proof of ID, and the paper from yesterday saying I had passed the written test. That was a problem because the people working today didn\u2019t know they could do that. After another thirty minutes of that, I just told the lady to give me the written test again. Then I had to wait for them to grade it and find someone that could go out with me for the driving test. Karl kept shaking his head at Tavia when another delay came up. That was keeping me focused as I couldn\u2019t let myself rage out if I was afraid she would do something we\u2019d all regret later. Finally, a very unimpressed looking lady came up to me and asked if I was ready. Tavia handled me her keys and wished me luck. The DMV lady blinked at Tavia and Karl for a moment then seemed happy to walk a little faster outside.<br /> <br /> But I did it! I have my license and all the bullshit paperwork complete to make me and van a legally matched pair. I swear it\u2019s like getting married. But I did it! And I think Tavia is as proud of me as my Mom would be. Now I get to share the news.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Well, we certainly have a plan now and the more specific we get about it, the less copacetic I get. It is a good plan, don\u2019t get me wrong. And It\u2019s much less dangerous than my bait idea. But with that one, I just have to submit and keep my wits about me to help fate along. This new plan is much more, well, active, I guess? I\u2019m backup! In case a fight breaks out! I\u2019m much better at running away than helping out, though I do have a few tricks that work well with the troupe here. I just have to keep reminding myself that it is highly unlikely to come to a fight and Doc, Jasmine and Alexia will be right outside if it does. Plus, it does mean being the personal guest of a sex symbol/internet personality at a hoity-toity sex party. What\u2019s not to love, aside from rumors of certain \u2018guests\u2019 being disposable so that no one can out any of the rich bastards as gay.<br /> <br /> Anyways, the ring Jenny gave Carol was super helpful, especially since Jenny has one just like it, from the cult leader. Alexia\u2019s got a slightly different slant to her psychic abilities and we complement each other nicely. With our powers combined, we found out that Jenny thought the cult leader had placed a love spell on it, using both her blood and Jenny\u2019s, so that Carol would come back to her. Actually, it makes the wearer... suggestible, magically speaking, to the cult leader herself. Also, over time, it would allow the cult leader to use the wearer\u2019s life energy in an incredibly destructive way. Way bad juju.<br /> <br /> What we learned did give us some level of hope of saving Jenny for Carol. She\u2019s not quite as deep in it as we might have thought - she didn\u2019t understand the ritual taking place in front of her and didn\u2019t seem to be in any sort of romantic relationship with the cult leader, much less in her confidence. Natalie and I have a goal for the aforementioned sex party on Friday - to get Jenny\u2019s copy of the ring back and hopefully remove the mystical influence the cult leader has over her. Whether or not that will truly redeem her is still questionable, as the picture Carol\u2019s painted of her is not very nice, despite her assuring us that Jenny\u2019s not that bad. But \u2018not very nice\u2019 and \u2018evil blood magic\u2019 aren\u2019t really the same thing, and if it\u2019s just back to \u2018not very nice\u2019 that\u2019s Carol\u2019s lookout.<br /> <br /> So we\u2019ve had ourselves a bit of downtime, since we don\u2019t want to do anything on that case to scare folks off before Friday. Jasmine and Natalie took a day trip to visit Jasmine\u2019s dad. He runs an antique shop and had the kind of gem cutting equipment we needed to really deal with the enspelled rings. So Karen and I had something like a date night. It started out being a double with Alexia and Chandra, watching a movie at the house. Apparently, to those two, \u201cwatching a movie\u201d means something slightly different, so Karen and I wandered off. I wound up telling stories about life with the old troupe until we \u201cwatched a movie\u201d ourselves.<br /> <br /> We also got some foot work done on the heirloom comb case while we were waiting, once Natalie and Jasmine were back. The pawn shop guy gave us a name for the guy who bought it from him, saying he was a collector of some kind, and a regular there. It nearly took Natalie bursting into tears at the thought of losing \u2018the comb her gran had used when she was a young girl\u2019, but he gave in after only a sniffle or two.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Natalie\u2019s \u2018gran\u2019, she\u2019s reconciled at least somewhat with her mom, which is awesome. I\u2019ve felt a little bad here as she works through it, cause even though Natalie\u2019s probably the country person I understand the most, of all I\u2019ve met, I can\u2019t really wrap my head around her family situation. I mean, intellectually, sure, I know that my family situation is not the norm or anything, but in my heart, it is difficult to consider. Some of the stuff Natalie\u2019s figured out recently, along with what she\u2019s found out talking to her mom, makes things make more sense at least. For example, Natalie\u2019s mom is touched, a little, like the rest of us, and she had thought she\u2019d seen Natalie die, on one of her close calls. That explains why her mom was so against Natalie\u2019s daughter coming to visit - she thought Natalie had to be an impostor. Also, it explains why she never checked up on her. Dad would have moved heaven and earth to find me, no matter how we\u2019d left things, but if he thought I was dead, well, that would have been different. But anyway, we might get to meet Natalie\u2019s mom, which will be awesome. From what Natalie said, her mom\u2019s a lot like her, more even that Natalie realized. We just have to deal with an evil blood cult first. Yay?<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> <b><div align=\"center\">Calling Home</div></b><br /> <br /> \u201cHello\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHello Mom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026Allison?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYea Mom, it\u2019s me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI love you Allison. I still do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026love you too Mom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you all right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes\u2026I was just thinking. It was time to call.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m happy to talk to you Allie\u2026about anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou knew I died\u2026didn\u2019t you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAllison, I don\u2019t know how you are still alive\u2026and honestly, I am not sure you really are.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am. It\u2019s complicated. Why did Natalie not know?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI got my visions first. It always happens that way. I\u2026drugged her on the night she would have seen it. She was too out of it to remember and may have thought it was a bad dream, if anything.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am not sure how I feel about you drugging my baby.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry Allison\u2026it would have shattered her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI see. How are you, Mom?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am well\u2026I\u2026hope you are.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to ask you something.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay baby.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy did you have me Exorcised if you had what I had? Why put me through that hell? Why did you let them hurt me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI had visions and I did everything in my power that you would not suffer as I did. I saw my brother die and talked to him on the phone before he passed away knowing it would be my last conversation, trying to talking him into being careful. I got pregnant three times Allison, only to see a vision of my unborn baby dying in my own womb\u2026It drove me nearly mad. I saw your sister die, your sister you\u2026well\u2026took into yourself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI figured.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI did not want you to ever deal with that. Ever. Too many deaths. Too many awful visions. You and I are so much alike\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow are we alike?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cI never told you I was a groupie, did I Allison?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026What?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI traveled with several bands in my early twenties before I met your father. I slept with several musicians. I drank, did pot, LSD\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No, no that is not possible\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe booze nearly killed me, Allison. One afternoon I woke up from alcohol and I don\u2019t even know how many pills and what kind. I was in a bedroom I did not recognize with a man I did not recognize in a city I did not recognize, and only my underwear was in the room. I went home after that. Found a good man and put that life behind me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve wanted\u2026needed\u2026to tell you that for a long time. Over a decade. I should have when you were eighteen before you left. I am not asking you to do what I did, even if I think you should. Well, the stopping drugs and following musicians thing. But what I really want is to be a part of your life.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026you will be, Mom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you sweetie.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you crying?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes I am Allie\u2026but it\u2019s okay, it\u2019s a good sort of crying.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know about Karen\u2026Sara\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes I do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not the life I would have chosen for you, Allison, but it is yours. I will support you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2026I saw you die, yes Allison. I for years believed you were gone, that I had failed, that you died to the life I escaped, that I had not done enough. I was skeptical about your contacting Nat, but when I glanced in at the Skyping\u2026that was you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou dyed your hair. Dyed out the blonde streaks?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was sort of looking forward to seeing my daughter have more grey hair than I did.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry honey\u2026you just have your father\u2019s hair color\u2026mostly.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry, so how have you been?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell Mom. My life is under control. I am happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI am so glad to hear it Allie\u2026should I call you Natalie?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo Mom. Call me Allison.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThank you Allison. Now, tell me about Karen and Sara\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXIII</i><br /> <br /> Jasmine and Natalie had a long discussion of Jasmine\u2019s issues with Carl, focusing on her guilt at being unsure about integrating with the Fishbornes or having children. This conversation triggered Natalie\u2019s realization her mother must have known about her death and had powers like her. Despite this, she regained composure and gave Jasmine some suggestions and urged her to not let it color her interactions with him for now. She also attempted to offer some counterpoints, but things like not realizing how much Jasmine dislikes Tavia (despite Tavia\u2019s fondness for her) sort of mucked that up.<br /> <br /> This game is going to see little impact from it, but I am going to be at Gen Con this year. If you are coming to Gen Con, I will be at the Onyx Path booth much of the time, and would love to meet some of those enjoying the APs. Sadly none of the players will be there. Still, feel free to come say hi. Because of the dates journals go up and such, neither sessions nor journals should be affected.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome, but may be very tardy during Gen Con. Feel free to comment nonetheless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/