"avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-12T12:24:35-07:00","id":226198,"title":"","content":"Fair niff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T02:04:30-07:00","id":241181,"title":"","content":"Ok we are way late getting you this installment. I can\u2019t blame Gen Con anymore, so I blame Doc\u2019s Log being late and moving. Okay, here we go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1930 Hours, Thursday, November 4, 2010<br /> <br /> Tavia kept my secret during dinner but I could tell she was expecting me to make an announcement. Instead we made plans to contact our pawn shop buyer. Just based on the name along, I immediately thought of a Russian mobster. The pawn shop owner said he was a collector of some kind and a regular in his shop so fencing didn\u2019t seem completely out of the question. Since we also had a number, Cupcake made the call to setup an appointment.<br /> <br /> A woman with a slight Japanese accent answered and in so many words or less said, if you can come while we\u2019re ready, come now. If not, we\u2019ll have to get the traps in place first, so come later. The appointment was in two hours. This only added to the paranoia I felt building. I warned the others that we should look at this in one of two ways.We either go in as professionals, possibly those that keep muscle in view at all times, or we go in as clueless people looking to ask for stolen goods back. One would likely establish that we were a little more (or less) than professionals while the other could be disarming enough that things don\u2019t get out of hand. No one else really wanted to go in with the intent to flex muscles we didn\u2019t want to use, so Rose and I will be the guards on the wings. Bright Eyes, Cupcake, and Nightshade will be the face. I know that Nightshade will be carrying her pistol but the others have asked that we not go in making a show of that kind of power either, so I\u2019ll keep things out in the van.<br /> <br /> Oh yeah, and I plan to tell everyone about my license before we leave so I can drive. I\u2019m a little excited.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0330 Hours, Friday, November 5, 2010<br /> <br /> I think I might have been a little cheesy with my declaration that I was driving, but it was fun.<br /> <br /> We loaded up into the van with no problems of space. Everyone had a comfortable seat and we still had a section behind the couch for storage, just as Snowflake and I intended. I do think Bright Eyes was a little overly nervous when I holstered the shotgun in the velcro sling next to the driver\u2019s seat belt, but it will pass. And either everyone was at least a nervous about this meeting as I was, or no one cared about the custom hardwood floors Snowflake and I put in. The Krewe symbol in the center I thought would at least get Rose\u2019s attention, but no one mentioned it. They may have also been nervous about me driving, which was fair. Nightshade is the only one who\u2019s ever ridden with me before.<br /> <br /> We arrived about 2100 Hours, dressed for what looked like either a funeral or a mob meeting. Lots of black. So normal for us, but we had on suits and dresses. Then we knocked on the door of what looked like an office attached to a warehouse on the edge of the nice section of New Haven. A stone faced Japanese vampire answered and led us to a man standing in a large mostly empty room. A large table stood in front of him and six brass statues towered over the conference area. Each one held some form of medieval weapon as it stared blankly at the center of the table before it. The Dog and I both got a bad feeling about those statues. The man, I\u2019ll call him The Collector, invited us to sit. Rose and I stood behind the chairs while the other three sat, given the visual that we were guards. Lucille, the vampire, stood similarly behind and to the side of our host. Before we could begin, The Collector noted that he didn\u2019t expect Sin-Eaters. We all blinked in shock. He was completely alive and had nothing affecting him that would allow him to know that. Rose and I stood a little more tensely after that. The whole room now made me twitchy. I wasn\u2019t worried about Lucille so much as how I would deal with six brass golems or whatever those statues were. Thankfully I wasn\u2019t the one elected to speak so I could recover in silence. The Collector knew what the comb was, at least as much as we did, and claimed he bought it in hopes of protecting whatever legendary being to which it was connected. He stated his moral code dictated him to ask if we planned to control the woman to whom the comb belonged so openly that I had to remember to be suspicious. We were quick to refute any attempts at control which earned us the opportunity for a fair trade. The Collector informed us that he was part of an ancient order that studied various relics and artifacts which held power. It was through these studies that he learned of Sin-Eaters and that he would like to watch us create one of our relics of power in exchange for The Hair\u2019s comb. He clarified that he wanted us to make him a charm. Rose agreed once Cupcake attached the condition that the charm would not be used against us or other Sin-Eaters. The Collector admitted that his organization would likely dislike him giving up the comb, but that the knowledge they could gain from our charm should offset the matter. But if certain of his group decided to push the issue, he would make sure we were alerted beforehand and given time to prepare. This group would kill us and The Collector if we learned who they were, so we agreed to just leave it for now. I suspect I will learn who this group is just through future research, but we\u2019ll see about that when the time comes. When asked how he knew were were Sin-Eaters, he mentioned something about some of his mysterious preparations as he was not supernatural himself. Since he was so forthright with us, I offered to create a second charm so that he might study two different processes. This was meant to keep in the good graces of The Collector should we (likely) ever need to consult with him again. He happily agreed and another appointment was made for tonight at 2200 Hours for him to bring an assortment of items that might be suitable for our magic. He made some joke about taking Lucelle to the club run by vampires, though Lucelle remained just as stone faced with him as with us.<br /> <br /> In the van on our way back to The Bluffs, Rose told us that The Collector was so honest that she trusted him implicitly. And she felt like he would have been happier just giving us the comb but his organization would not have suffered that insult. Nightshade told us she was able to Boneyard and that The Collector was actually standing on a trapdoor with a remote control in his hand. Now that is my kind of precaution.<br /> <br /> Once we got back and the van was unloaded, I headed out on patrol. I didn\u2019t park near the studio just so I could walk like always. Sebastian was happy to see me. We worked out our new deal with me training him while he trains me. I walked him to his car and then stuck around after the studio was closed. There were a few people around on the streets but no one that seemed the type to cause a problem. I headed out after about an hour. I\u2019d like to think everything is fine now, but I know better. We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Now sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1700 Hours, Friday, November 5, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation went well, but it took me about an hour this morning. After that, it was a pretty smooth day considering that we\u2019re going into a Blood Bather\u2019s lair with a standing No Kill order. That\u2019s going out the fucking window if things turn ugly, but upfront it\u2019s no guns blazing.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting ahead. We didn\u2019t just coast through the day. Well most of us didn\u2019t. Rose got another visit from Mr. Ox. And as with most of his visits, Mr. Ox brought with him another story. The story seemed a little close to home for him though. Rose\u2019s telling of the tale indicated there may be a reason why Mr. Ox is so very determined to end Bone Dry. This was a tale of two women, the best of friends, who fell madly in love with the same man. Prudence and Radiance competed fiercely for the man, and eventually Radiance won his heart. But in their struggles, the women lost their innocence and their compassion for one another. Prudence tended a cold flame of revenge while Radiance gave birth to a son, fortuitously named Mischievousness. That was the final straw for Prudence, who then put her plan in motion. She wooed Radiance\u2019s widowed father, marrying him and keeping herself close to her former friend and lover. Next Prudence used a slow poison on both her husband and Radiance, murdering her way into the arms of the man she still loved.<br /> <br /> Radiance was not content to allow Prudence to win, even in death however. When she found herself in one of the Chinese Hells, she bribed a young jailer new at his post to allow her to return to the cycle. She was even able to convince him to let her keep her memories. These sins paled in comparison to her final request. She asked to return as the daughter of Prudence and her coveted husband. All these things were granted but the inexperienced demon, who was surprisingly never named. Though Rose noted that Mr. Ox smiled a smile that suggested responsibility. Thus Radiance returned to the world and grew with hate in her heart for her mother. But she had not forgotten her love for the man she lost. And it was convenient that her half-brother Mischievousness shared his father\u2019s eyes. Radiance eventually poisoned her mother, as Prudence had done to her, then sealed her soul within a gemmed amulet. Prudence\u2019s husband soon died of a broken heart from his loss, while Radiance married Mischievousness to finally have what she had been denied. They had twelve children and many years together.<br /> <br /> Mr. Ox did not so much end his story as start a new one. He told Rose of a spiritually sacred place in Taiwan which Bone Dry used to draw much of his power over spirits. He then noted that he had a certain amulet with a gem as black as the darkest heart. Mr. Ox said it was a reminder of how we can all make mistakes. When we looked at the Shadow Stone, all the Sin-Eaters at the table could see a screaming woman\u2019s face pressed against the inside. He asked that we release the spirit inside the sacred place. Prudence\u2019s mere presence would taint the area, however Mr. Ox was suggesting to free her so the spirits which would come to end the taint would also devour her soul. Prudence would be completely destroyed but the corruption to the spiritual area would be absolute. And somehow, this link to the area and the corruption by Prudence\u2019s destruction would shatter much of Bone Dry\u2019s power over spirits.<br /> <br /> We talked about that one for some time. Rose is all in, which terrifies us considering she is agreeing to destroy a ghost. Several of us are against this and not just because our Geists are far from happy with the thought. I am not okay with permanently corrupting a spiritual nexus. There has to be other options that accomplish the same or similar goals without so much collateral damage. Plus I\u2019m not sure I like the direction Rose is taking with her concept of resolution here.<br /> <br /> In a totally different line of thinking, Nightshade had discovered someone on the Twilight Network that wants to come and observe how an established Krewe does things/solves problems. She goes by Coffee and she\u2019s new. We talked about that a little bit and I was surprised at how guarded our Krewe became at the mention of it. I mean I don\u2019t mind us using caution, but it was almost paranoid fears. Now to be honest, it is a little weird that another Sin-Eater just asks to come watch. But I guess we\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Since we had an early dinner, we\u2019re free to get ready for the party now. I am already getting edgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> We have a little bit of time left before we have to head out for the fancy sex party, so I thought I\u2019d go ahead and write something to you to keep me from bothering anyone too much. I\u2019ve already been clinging to Karen most of the day, Natalie is getting herself all super-prettified and I don\u2019t want to put Doc and Alexia and Jasmine *more* on the edge. Good gods the number of guns he put in that van... Anyways, so, writing things out it is. We have actually managed to find a couple of things to occupy us these last few days, including making some interesting and very attractive contacts, so it\u2019s not like I don\u2019t have anything to talk about.<br /> <br /> Firstly, Doc got his license! It was why he was a little scarce these past few days, between secret driving lessons with Natalie and standing in line at the DMV. He was suitably dramatic about the reveal, ordering us to \u201cStop!\u201d as we were walking out the door, following it up with \u201cI\u2019m driving.\u201d as he flourished his new license. So we got to take the van to go speak with Janus, the man who had bought Sarah\u2019s comb from the pawn shop.<br /> <br /> We were playing it very professional all told, especially since we got a bit of a mob-ish vibe, between Alexia\u2019s phone conversation, and to be completely honest, his name. Not fair perhaps, but at least we weren\u2019t thinking it before the conversation. Or, I wasn\u2019t. I oughtn\u2019t speak for the others. We were met at the door by a smoking hot Japanese lady, Lucile, who led us to a big nicely appointed conference room. Sadly, a sense of humor was not among her charms, at least not one that meshed particularly well with the boss man\u2019s, though watching him try was amusing all by itself.<br /> <br /> All in all, the interview went much better than we all expected, I believe. Janos is a curator, of a sort, of mystical knowledge - I rather hope to stay in touch after we resolve this, for more than just his handsome face, though that doesn\u2019t hurt either of course. He works for a super secret organization, a he-could-tell-us-the-name-and-then-he\u2019d-have-to-kill-us kind of secret. Or really, from the sounds of it, someone else would have to come kill us *and* him, to be fair. But after introductions were made, and it was established that he knew we were touched and not just investigators and also that we knew what we were looking for, his first question was whether we intended to use it to control Sarah. He is very set against any sort of binding-type thing, which is automatic bonus points. That plus his knowledge and forthrightness meant that we all felt pretty good about taking his deal, which was that we\u2019d let him watch while we used some of our abilities, so that he could learn about what makes us touched. It helped that he could foot the bill for any materials we needed. I even kinda got the idea he wouldn\u2019t mind just giving us the comb a long as it got back to its owner, except his organization would not be pleased. He did promise to shield us as he could if they did not consider this a sufficient trade and warn us if he couldn\u2019t shield us. I had a pretty good vibe from him though, I think that will all turn out ok.<br /> <br /> We arranged to meet him at Murder Ballads once he\u2019d gotten hold of the materials we needed. It would definitely be a change of scenery. Janos\u2019 place was almost a supervillain lair - giant brass armed statues lining the walls, a gigantic conference table and a trapdoor with a remote. To be fair, the trapdoor was under him, so it was more of an escape route than a shark pit or something. Would expecting that be racist too, or would it only be if he\u2019d been Japanese and I\u2019d expected alligators? I\u2019m not really up to date with my supervillain racial stereotypes, obvs. Anyways, it was pretty badass. And a meeting at Murder Ballads means I have a new mission: get Lucile to loosen up enough to dance with me.<br /> <br /> That was all yesterday. This afternoon, before we started finalizing plans for the party, we moved the Mr. Ox story on a little bit.<br /> <br /> After a time, Jasmine was yet again approached by Mr. Ox. He had another story for her, he said. There was once a pair of young women, he began, called Prudence and Radiance. They were the best of friends, he continued, until they fell in love with the same man, as has happened so many times. This time, neither would give way for the other, and in their pursuit, they both went too far for forgiveness. In the end, or perhaps the beginning, Radiance won. She and the man lived their lives together and had a son, Mischievousness. But Prudence... she was not one to take losing lightly. She married Radiance\u2019s widowed father, and, when the time was right, she used a slow poison to kill her former friend, her current rival, and then to kill her own husband, leaving her free to marry the man that was the original cause of this strife. They had their own child, a daughter, and were happy, for a time.<br /> <br /> But, he told her, this was not to last, as the natural order of things was disrupted when Radiance bribed one of the young, new to his post jailors at the hell she was sent to. She convinced him to let her return to the cycle, remembering her old life, and not only that, but specifically to come back as the daughter of Prudence and the prize husband. The demon telling the story smiled wide, without humor.<br /> <br /> He continued, saying so their daughter grew up, nurturing hate in her heart, aimed at her mother. And there was something else in her heart - love for her half-brother, her son, who had inherited his father\u2019s eyes, the eyes of the man she loved and wanted so much. And so, Mr. Ox concluded, Radiance poisoned Prudence, as Prudence had her, and trapped her soul in a magical amulet. Her husband died soon after, of a broken heart, and Radiance married Mischievousness and had many children.<br /> <br /> The demon changed the subject after this. He knew of a place in Taiwan, a sacred place that the sorcerer drew considerable power from. If this place could be corrupted, he would lose his hold over some of his most powerful servants. It just so happened that Mr. Ox had in his possession a particular amulet, a reminder, he said, that we all can make mistakes. The amulet gleamed in a well placed shaft of light, a screaming woman\u2019s face pressed up against the inside of the black gem, for those with the sight to see. He placed the amulet in Jasmine\u2019s hand. He had hoped, he said, that some bad luck farmers might find a way to release the spirit trapped within at the place of power.<br /> <br /> The mere presence of the ghost in that sacred space would weaken it, reducing the power Bone Dry would have over his servants. To truly break his power, the spirits of the place would have to consume the corrupt soul, destroying her utterly and transmuting their own essence entirely. The heroes discussed their options, unable to reach a true consensus...<br /> <br /> Another cliffhanger, I know, but we got a bit sidetracked with an interesting discussion about what everyone felt our heroes should do with the amulet. Jasmine felt strongly that the price was worth it, as far as the corruption went, and that Prudence deserved her fate after what she\u2019d done. Alexia was largely swayed to agree with Jasmine by her expertise in the matter, and by her strong assurance. Natalie was perturbed by the thought of destroying the sacred space, as it would not truly be able to recover from the full corruption. I myself agreed with Jasmine that destroying the sacred space was an acceptable price, as Bone Dry had already corrupted in it some way, if not spiritually, but I was not at all comfortable with the heroes destroying the very soul of a person, regardless of what that person might have done. Doc was not comfortable with what it would require to fully break the sorcerer\u2019s power, for the land and the soul\u2019s sake, and he focussed on finding alternatives, within the context of the story.<br /> <br /> Figuring out how the story should go is the task of another moment however. I believe it\u2019s now time to head out. I\u2019m not sure I ever expected to be this nervous to attend a high class sex party. I\u2019m sure it\u2019ll go fine, no problems, or anything like that, but, Sasha, if you don\u2019t hear from me soon, just, well, avoid Newhaven. Someone will deal with these guys, fate\u2019s not going to let her keep going this way, I have faith in that, but until that happens, it\u2019s a bad scene. Of course, I\u2019m being silly and you\u2019ll hear from me tomorrow if not again tonight. So, talk to you later.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Alright, I\u2019m back. Got out of that house alive and everything. It wasn\u2019t even that bad. Once I put on my performing face, I was able to hold it together pretty well, I think, *and* I got to make out with yet another incredibly hot lady. So, points for the sex party, creepy or no.<br /> <br /> Natalie was doing the heavy lifting anyway, and I was just backup, like I mentioned. So Natalie made a beeline for Jenny (really, Jenny made a beeline for her) and had her wrapped around her little finger in no time. I got to make socializing rounds while trying not to think of Doc and the arsenal he had loaded in the van nearby and hoping that they wouldn\u2019t need to use it. It wasn\u2019t that hard, like I said, once I started playing my part, though a familiar face that clearly recognized me didn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> Well, she didn\u2019t help my mood right at that very first moment, though here\u2019s hoping that her being there will be super useful in the long run. See, she\u2019s part of the local gang, the one whose lives got a bit disrupted when the rival gang came into town looking for the blood cult, because the rival gang thought the blood cult was the local gang. Gods, that\u2019s confusing just to write down. Anyway, the local gang had figured out that the blood cult was the reason the rival gang was in town and they were not well pleased. So we might very well have allies in this. Naturally, she told me all this *after* she insisted we go back into one of the private rooms, something I was really hoping to avoid, despite how out of character that might seem, as whenever I started imagining anything nice with any of the pretty people there, the word \u2018disposable\u2019 popped back up into my head.<br /> <br /> Of course, being in a private room with a very pretty lady I was fairly certain was an ally, there was no reason not to take advantage of the relative privacy. I would have just fretted the night away and possibly had to deal with the less friendly pretty people out there. Besides, Elizabeth was *very* persuasive. And if I paid more attention to not-her than was properly polite, I think she understood.<br /> <br /> Nothing happened anyway, no covers blown, no emergencies to be dealt with, just a plan that came together well. I did appear to have made an impression, or maybe just shown more nervousness than I\u2019d hoped, as Elizabeth stayed close, especially when Natalie and Jenny came back from the back and Jenny came to speak with me. Natalie let me know she had succeeded in getting both the ring away from Jenny and Jenny to agree to come talk after, at Murder Ballads. It is nice being able to get a private room at a popular club whenever you need it. I let Elizabeth know it was alright, and she shouldn\u2019t freak out when I stayed behind after, and off we went.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 4th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Doc is a driver now. Huzzah!<br /> <br /> -He probably drives better than I do, I have for years.<br /> <br /> -Anyway, time to talk to Mr. Scary.<br /> <br /> -Well, here is Ms. Scary.<br /> <br /> -Mr. Scary is only sort of scary.<br /> <br /> -Statues give him at least a 6/10 though.<br /> <br /> -This might not even come to blows. Fancy that!<br /> <br /> -Lucille?<br /> <br /> -Okay, I think we have come to an arrangement.<br /> <br /> -Seriously, Lucille?<br /> <br /> -Mr. Scary raises my hackles a bit, but it should work out.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -Lucille.<br /> <br /> -Witch needs TLC badly.<br /> <br /> <br /> November 5th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Okay, my big day.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019ll be the prettiest girl at the ball!<br /> <br /> -Or something.<br /> <br /> -Ohboy, Spooky has been talking to her \u201cUncle\u201d<br /> <br /> -Spooky\u2019s \u201cUncle\u201d scares me.<br /> <br /> -Um, okay, yikes.<br /> <br /> -This deal is getting worse all the time.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m not crazy about this.<br /> <br /> -Okay, made Coffee\u2019s request. Lukewarm, but not too bad.<br /> <br /> -Okay, time to get ready.<br /> <br /> -Alright, here goes pretty.<br /> <br /> <br /> November 6th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Out safe Karen.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXIV</i><br /> <br /> We touched on three plots that game, which was cool. All three got some advancement. Interest in the Mr. Ox plot is quite high, and folks seem to be enjoying the Blood Bather storyline.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t have much to add, but comments and questions are welcome. Next time we advance the Blood Bather and Comb story further.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T23:55:28-07:00","id":242059,"title":"","content":"Did you make the tale of Prudence and Radiance yourself or did you grab it from somewhere else? I rather liked it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-27T00:04:39-07:00","id":242062,"title":"","content":"Made it up myself, actually. Well, unless I read it in my Chinese studies, forgot, and dredged it up to accidentally plagiarize. But pretty sure I made it up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-07T12:53:25-07:00","id":251666,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to recap our previous session. First one in the new game room in the new house was successful, I think, but enough of that, here are Doc and Sara. No Natalie this time, but she should be back soon enough.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0330 Hours, Saturday, November 6, 2010<br /> <br /> Tonight went better than I expected. I\u2019ll just hold on to this badge for another time.<br /> <br /> The plan for the party was fairly well put together. Nightshade went in with the intention of seducing Jenny as necessary to get the ring off. Once that\u2019s done, Jenny would be told how she\u2019s been controlled then attempts would be made to bring her over to our side of this issue.<br /> <br /> For my part, I was prepared to make a big hole in the door before making similar holes in people if things went badly. I was more on edge than normal because Nightshade and Bright Eyes weren\u2019t wearing ear curls, but they were wired.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, our plan seems to have worked. We were only going to give this one shot, after which we were marking Jenny\u2019s name off the Save List. Also Nightshade had Troy ready to chop off Jenny\u2019s hand to get the ring if things did not go according to plan. Because the clientele at the party would absolutely not want anything to do with the police or being identified, I called our friendly neighborhood arms dealer with a request. If I came in with a shotgun and bodyguards shoot me, no one would blink. But if I came in with a shotgun and a badge, the waters would part. The New Haven badge arrived about two hours into the party. But it will be useful someday.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes made a new friend while Nightshade was removing the ring from Jenny. The rich blonde vampire we\u2019ve been seeing around is apparently named Elizabeth and was trying to crack her way into the Blood Bathers too. She wanted political power as the vampires were trying to figure out what to do with the mess.<br /> <br /> The party ended with a contented sign instead of a bang, so we all met in a private room back at Murder Ballads. I figured out very quickly that all of Jenny\u2019s best assets are on display at these parties. She is all wrapping and no prize inside. She tried to put ambition in place of intelligence but never quite understood why it wasn\u2019t working. The fact that she was whiny didn\u2019t endear her to me either. Jenny firmly believes that being rich either makes you a good person or makes it easier to be a good person. Bright Eyes and I tried to explain that has nothing to do with it while Cupcake texted Carol. We weren\u2019t making much progress with the work hard and earn your status, so Bright Eyes pointed out she could just marry into money. I stopped and looked at her like I had been looking at Jenny. Fortunately for her, I knew better than to think she was that...well shallow. Still bothered me that she would suggest it to someone who was obviously morally bankrupt. And right after we heard the story of Prudence and Radiance too.<br /> <br /> Carol showed up much faster than any of us expected, blowing off the bouncer that was keeping the private rooms private. Nightshade smoothed that over as Carol and Jenny reunited. I still don\u2019t understand what Carol sees in Jenny, but I guess she keeps some hope that Jenny can figure out why she\u2019s not being successful. That Jenny is unbelievably stupid only adds to my confusion. But back to the reunion. Nightshade explained what the ring was actually used for and we learned that Jenny had lost some time at different points and even woke up once with a new scar that healed strangely. With Carol and more facts than she could ignore, Jenny agreed to cooperate with us to stop the Blood Bathers. Nightshade arranged a \u201cclothes-on private room\u201d session for them to be alone. Then she got out her disguise kit. I always forget she has that. Someone arranged for a hotel room and Tatum would take Jenny and Carol and come right back. I asked that the two of them try to work out what actually happened during the ritual so we could figure out what they did. Once I know that, I can try to determine more about their condition and requirements, but more importantly I can try to figure out if it can be reversed or if there are any loopholes we can keep in mind.<br /> <br /> The two women left with purple and green hair, punk make up, and fetish dresses that pretty much guaranteed anyone looking for them didn\u2019t notice their exit. With that handled, we headed back to the Bluffs. Once we were back, I texted Leslie and told her to be at the Bluffs before dawn. Then I went to the Library to start working on the Hopping Vampire book around 0200 Hours. Surprisingly, a motorcycle roared up the drive not long afterwards. I met Leslie on the porch and suggested we go have a private discussion. Once I was sure Gretchen wasn\u2019t in the Library and Tavia wasn\u2019t lurking, I told Leslie about the possible threat of Mariah Winthrop because of her connection to Tzipporah. She was completely unaware and I could tell she was honestly thankful that I let her know. Then I asked about what Tavia did. I was more than a little unhappy to learn that Tavia had basically sworn her to secrecy on pain of whatever injury she had already inflicted if she talked about it. We discussed our deal again and I realized that I would have to talk with Tavia if I am ever going to keep up my end of the bargain. Leslie was doing something questionable, but still not something Tavia should have been involved in by the sounds of it. When we were as clear as possible on the situations at hand, Leslie took me for a ride on her motorcycle. That was interesting.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1345 Hours, Saturday, November 6, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation was a little harder this morning, but I\u2019m fairly sure I was concerned about talking with Tavia. She and I were one of the first ones up and about as Rose was either sleeping in or already gone. I used the time before everyone started moving around to discuss Leslie. I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve ever heard the phrase, \u201clittle bitch mouth\u201d so many times in my life. Tavia has no patience or intention of dealing with double talk or insults, as she has no mind for metaphor or tolerance for her cousin. The role of matriarch has definitely grabbed Tavia and that leaves no room for question. That she and Leslie are basically the same age (and being reminded of this by Leslie) really only served to infuriate Tavia. From what I could coax from the deadliest Fishborn, Leslie was hosting a party where she was summoning ecstasy spirits to play with those in attendance. I still don\u2019t know how Tavia found out, but she surprised her cousin by showing up and what sounded like scolding her in front of this collection of friends and hangers on. I can\u2019t imagine why that didn\u2019t go over well. When Leslie \u201cused her little bitch mouth\u201d to voice her displeasure, things went south quickly. I had to very patiently explain to Tavia, without any sarcasm or metaphor, how this made it very hard for me to keep my word to Leslie and how there are different ways to deal with said cousin. In the end, we agreed that if Tavia felt like Leslie needed to be talked to, it would be better if we both were there. Though she was very concerned about the possibility of me not being able to keep my word, Tavia was not at all remorseful or concerned at all about Leslie\u2019s wellbeing. I gathered that Leslie had made fun of her while they were growing up, or recently for all I know. It\u2019s all the same thing to Tavia. Either way, Leslie is more of a modern woman while Tavia is not and expects all women of the Fishborn family to follow the traditions of the House. That Tavia has the advantage of her Brineborn legacy is just a point that makes her smile. I\u2019m worried about Leslie but I think making me go against my word will at least slow Tavia down.<br /> <br /> I hope.<br /> <br /> Things were fairly quiet for a while since it was the weekend and we were going out tonight. Lunch was a group planning session. We\u2019re meeting The Collector and Elizabeth separately at Murder Ballads tonight. Hopefully we can make the charms for him without issue and maybe come away with one of them, if they are useful. My understanding of Elizabeth\u2019s meeting is to combine our forces to work against the Blood Bathers without involving the rest of the vampires of the city. I know what she\u2019s trying to do, but I can\u2019t say that I mind having wealthy and attractive help in this situation, even if she is only helping to directly gain an advantage. Hopefully, neither meeting runs into problems as we don\u2019t need to have anything flashy erupt in Murder Ballads.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont. from last time)<br /> <br /> As it turns out, Jenny is a piece of work. To her credit, she does seem to sincerely care for Carol, though even that was tarnished somewhat by her self-pitying, hero-worship-esque belief that Carol is a better person than she could ever be, solely because she \u201cwas born to it\u201d, as if you have to have money to have morals. She blamed her attempt to \u201crise above her station\u201d for all her recent problems and failings. Doc tried to convince her that rising above your station is not a problem, if you did it by trying and working hard. I think I annoyed him when I piped up that the hard work bit was even optional, she could marry into it or something, as long as it didn\u2019t involve murder. I had been thinking about Carol in particular, but I still think the idea of marrying up offended his sensibilities, a little.<br /> <br /> We did manage to drive the point home that the cult leader was bad news, despite whatever money she has. Trust to Jasmine to cut to the point - we all started off with \u201cshe\u2019s not very nice\u201d and before Jenny could even get very far in her \u201cbut she helped me so much\u201d speech, Jasmine corrected us, saying she was a \u201chorrid evil bitch\u201d. True, and probably even fair. I told Jenny what the ring could do, pulling details out of the ritual she was involved in that I\u2019d seen in my object reading vision for verisimilitude. The threat to Carol finally got her attention and she was fairly well convinced when we confirmed she\u2019d lost time.<br /> <br /> About then was when Carol showed up. I\u2019m not sure how she knew where we were and that Jenny was here, but she came straight to the back, trailing a protesting bouncer and threw herself at Jenny. Natalie headed the bouncer off, and arranged another room for them to have a private, clothing-on conversation. Natalie also gave them a serious makeover, and arranged for Tatum to give them a ride to a local hotel, to get them out all clandestine-like. So far, the plan is for them to lay low while they do their best to remember details of the rituals they were involved in, in between the clothing-off conversations. Until we figure out their ritual style, we\u2019re flying a little too blind for any of our likings, so our part is just going to be reconnaissance, for now.<br /> <br /> I wanted to get this out so you wouldn\u2019t worry (too much). That done, I believe I hear the first guests arriving for Natalie\u2019s not dangerous-in-a-bad-way sex party. After all, we have worked very hard, and we - well, Natalie really - had to leave it at a tease earlier. We clearly deserve it. Plus, gotta give Tatum some extra incentive to leave the cult-ish lovebirds be.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Tonight was meeting night, apparently. I had totally forgotten that we were supposed to meet with Janos tonight when I made plans to meet with Elizabeth. We discussed splitting up so we could meet both at the same time, which would have broken my heart, but in the end, Elizabeth was perfectly fine meeting a little later, so it all worked out.<br /> <br /> I did fail Natalie\u2019s challenge to dance with Lucille, but it was for a good cause, as Doc beat me there. And got her to go from reluctant to dance at all to asking permission to leave her post to have a second dance, so he did something right, for sure. I did promise to take good care of Janos while she was gone. I debated, but held off on asking for a dance myself - Lucille seemed a lot more comfortable with Janos in the back room and after Doc got her to relax a little, it seemed a shame to stress her out again.<br /> <br /> I think our showing off went well too. Janos certainly got a glimpse of a variety of styles - Jasmine\u2019s Feng Shui centered work, Doc\u2019s very correspondence focused, symbolically practical methods, and my flashy show. I might have pulled out a bit more showmanship than my usual. Comes from having an audience, I suppose. :-)<br /> <br /> Even better, my bit was to do some psychic object reading. I asked if he had an item on him with a known history that he wouldn\u2019t mind sharing, and he gave me the comb. It seems the reason the bean sidhe influence over Sarah is largely dormant is because she hadn\u2019t bled on the comb itself. Good to know for Sarah, certainly, and interesting to Janos as well. I probably wouldn\u2019t have thought to do that without his asking, so it worked out well.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXV</i><br /> <br /> So yea, we ended still at Murder Ballads. Between Jenny and Tavia Doc\u2019s player got to spend a lot of time playing Doc\u2019s frustrations with people.<br /> <br /> So there is some cast related news. Jasmine\u2019s player has been burning out on playing Jasmine. They feel like a lot of her story arc has been completed, and have not really been as into the sessions of late, hence the lack of journals on Jasmine\u2019s part and the hiatus, which they were hoping would get them back into playing Jasmine. It did not, so much.<br /> <br /> So the new plan is they will be introducing a new character. Jasmine will not be totally vanishing, but moving into the background a bit. She will still be especially playing a strong part in the Mr. Ox story, a storyline everyone is enjoying a lot and will see completion. But Jasmine may be starting a branch of the Krewe in Taiwan as things go on, involving the main Krewe in further dealing with Bone Dry.<br /> <br /> The new character, Alice Campbell, will be introduced in the session tonight. Next weekend I will post a short teaser story Doc\u2019s player wrote to introduce her, and in the next \u201cdowntime\u201d between sessions will post her background.<br /> <br /> In other cast related news, or lack thereof, no word on Simon Fishborne as yet. His player still has every hope of returning to the game, but things are really crazy right now as he tries to finish his Doctorate and a lot of issues are coming and going, and he is really still not gaming right now. What happens when he gets his degree, and if he stays in the area, will determine if Simon returns. I know we all certainly hope so.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions are welcome. Teaser in about a week.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T13:00:59-07:00","id":256201,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week for Geist, but I wanted to put up a brief teaser for the upcoming Krewe member. The below was written by Doc\u2019s player on a lark, but Jasmine/Alice\u2019s player really liked it, so we decided to go with it as something that happened, and essentially began playing the scene as soon as the fictlet ends about an hour into the game. Jasmine/Alice\u2019s player edited it a bit to make it more forum-presentable, and here it is. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <b>Interlude</b><br /> <br /> &quot;The chase is nearly over. Like something out of a slasher film, the stranger stalks her prey through the litter-strewn alleys of the warehouse district. Her face is hidden behind a wooden skull mask, and she grips a well-used wood axe in one hand, eager to bury it in her quarry's flesh.<br /> <br /> The slasher's prey scrambles through an open window and into the cover of a warehouse. He thinks he has escaped. He thinks he is safe. He is not. As he stops to catch his breath, a shadow falls across his face, and she is in front of him. He flees. He twists and turns through a maze of shipping crates, but no matter where he goes, she is always right behind him, moving slowly, deliberately thorough the clutter of the abandoned building. And then there is nowhere left to run. He is trapped in a corner, surrounded by stacks of heavy containers.<br /> <br /> The stranger steps into view only a few feet away. Her axe is ready. Predator and prey both pause, breathing heavily as they stare intently at one another. Then, just before hefting her axe to deliver a fatal blow, the stranger spots a pair of green cat's eyes reflecting in the rafters. She pauses; the eyes are far too large to belong to any normal cat, but when she looks again, they are gone.<br /> <br /> The stranger raises her axe. Her muscles tense, but just as she begins to bring it down on her prey, it stops. She turns her head and follows the hand gripping her axe handle until she meets Doc's steely gaze.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not Jerome's time yet. And now you have our attention.&quot;<br /> <br /> The owner of the green cat's eyes blocks the exit, her notable nails silhouetted in the light of a passing vehicle. The spectral aura of the stranger's Shroud sizzles as Doc's ghost flames lick at her axe.&quot;<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Journals going up usual time next week. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T15:40:01-07:00","id":256312,"title":"","content":"Oh my... (Now we just need some Two Steps from Hell music playing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-23T15:55:34-07:00","id":264213,"title":"","content":"Okay it\u2019s time to check back with the Middle Shadows. In this episode, we meet the newest PCs. Doc\u2019s player had a technical malfunction with his journal, so has to re-write it almost from the top. That will probably appear along with next sessions journal\u2026we did not want to wait further on putting this out.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> (cont. from last time)<br /> <br /> The meeting with Elizabeth went similarly well. Much less relaxed though. She started off the sharing first. It was mostly stuff we\u2019d known before - the whole mess with the out of town rival gang and everything. She did know (well, could find out easily) where the cult leader had bought her ritual supplies and, even better, what precisely those supplies were. She remembered a treated silver scalpel, and is going to figure out the rest for us. Elizabeth\u2019s people had mostly been handling this in a hands-off kinda fashion, since they didn\u2019t want to play their hand in front of the rival gang. Her people mostly cared about their cover being blown, though she claimed to not care for blood magic as a general sort of thing, so bonus points to her? I think the others warmed up to her a little bit as she was so open, but I know it didn\u2019t help Doc\u2019s estimation of me re: beautiful people.<br /> <br /> Doc filled her in on some of what we knew, about her kinds of rituals and how they work, as well as letting her know we\u2019d dealt with the rival gang, at least for now. I warned her about the kind of weaponry the cult leader (hopefully) no longer had at her disposal, as unfortunately she has the means to get more. We did figure out that stealing Carol and Jenny from her probably means her inner circle (as much as she had one) was gutted. That\u2019s still presuming a bit, but based on the way the rest of the troupe describes her, it\u2019s at least a reasonable presumption.<br /> <br /> Then came the exciting bit, brought about by yours truly being really dumb. Sarah had been at the same club, you see, that we\u2019d been having all these secret meetings at, so I thought it would be nice for me to let her know that we\u2019d gotten her comb back, and to arrange a meeting for tomorrow to explain all we\u2019d learned about it. I wasn\u2019t thinking about the fact that I had the comb, and that apparently ancient faerie magic is more progressive than some parts of this grand country we live in, and so it didn\u2019t even register that I needed to avoid Sarah while I had it. The look in her eyes when I moved to meet up with her on the dance floor sure reminded me though. I mean, usually it\u2019s pretty great when a pretty girl looks at you like that, but... knowing it wasn\u2019t really her kinda puts a damper on that kind of thing.<br /> <br /> I tried to send Natalie to head her off, but she was more than a little fixated. I managed to get to another private room before she jumped me, and I tried to head everything off by giving the comb back to her first thing, but that didn\u2019t really change anything. Neither did pointing out that it was just the comb\u2019s influence, and that she hadn\u2019t felt that way about me just a few hours ago. Natalie had to dampen all the emotions in the room for her to come to her senses. We explained about the whole bleeding on the comb thing - I just hope it sunk in. I\u2019ll probably want to check up on her and talk about it more later when she wasn\u2019t under one influence or another.<br /> <br /> I was a little surprised Natalie was so willing to bring out the emotion changing stuff. I mean, I think it was totally justified, mostly just counteracting someone else\u2019s manipulation, but she\u2019s usually pretty hard-line about that. And the whole extended metaphor about souls, and how mine was bound to hers, while she and Sarah\u2019s souls had just high fived in passing, and mine and hers were buying a house... well, I think it got out of hand a bit at the end there. She mentioned afterwards that she\u2019d actually been feeling jealous, in the midst of all that. She decided she didn\u2019t like it, for the record, which was good to hear certainly. But after all that, I didn\u2019t feel so much like dancing, so we\u2019re just chilling out, she and Karen and me, watching movies. I think the others are around - Jasmine and Alexia are in bed at this point and Doc is researching, maybe?<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> So... I apparently left off yesterday\u2019s email a bit early, considering the night was not yet over. Doc gave us a call shortly after I hit send - well, gave Natalie a call. He\u2019d found another person who was touched, and found them trying to kill a friend of his, so, not so great feelings all around. He stopped her, with no one getting hurt, but he was considerably upset (understandably) and still feeling very violent (understandably, I guess, but not quite as cool). There were lots of plans made around \u201cif she doesn\u2019t do things exactly the way I want her to down to the second, she dies\u201d which just seems like a recipe for falling down the same slope as her.<br /> <br /> See, I haven\u2019t talked too much about us touched, just talked around the edges of things, but I have mentioned that it\u2019s not an easy road. There\u2019s a call we all feel, a sense of purpose bestowed on us when we\u2019re touched. There\u2019s also a sorta different kind of conscience that comes with it, a shoulder angel, if you will. Or a shoulder devil, as the case maybe. All of us have gone through things, and not come out of the other side intact. This new touched, Alice, is maybe, *maybe* less intact than us. But she\u2019s asking for help, and Doc even acknowledged that she was pretty pitiful as she did so. I got pretty lucky with my own particular shoulder angel, for the most part, and even then, when I was alone, it got hard sometimes to keep my own counsel and to remember who *I* was. Alice wasn\u2019t so lucky, and I think if she loses herself, it could be really bad, for a lot of people. And if that happens, I will help Doc deal with it. Until that happens, I will stand in front of the scary man and argue for mercy.<br /> <br /> Well, that got dark. On a lighter note, Jasmine looks absolutely adorable in her nightgown when she\u2019s just been woken up and Gretchen is getting squirted with a Super Soaker every time she starts to talk about her sex life in front of Tavia. Last I checked, her clothes were soaked through.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Thanks being sent to all the gods watching over beautiful women, Alice called Doc at 11AM sharp, just like he asked, and showed up at Lulu\u2019s even a few minutes before the arranged meeting time of 1PM. It was mostly just us touched there, as well as Doc\u2019s girlfriend, since she was there last night, to meet her, as Natalie at least was not comfortable with Karen being introduced to the serial killer before she was vetted. Same with Tavia (in addition to not wanting to scare Alice off) and Chandra.<br /> <br /> When she got there, I stood up to make sure she noticed the table we\u2019d gotten, and if I sat down in a different seat, so that both Natalie and I could sit next to her, then surely no one would begrudge me. She was, after all, and extremely beautiful redhead, tall as the day is long, with bright blue eyes and a tough girl leather jacket. According to Doc, she nearly wrenched his arm out of its socket trying to get her weapon away, so it wasn\u2019t just a tough girl act with the jacket, though her smile was shy.<br /> <br /> I was all prepped to go to bat for her before, if I had to, and she wasn\u2019t obviously morally bankrupt past the point of redemption. At this point, I know Doc\u2019s going to chalk it up to the fact she\u2019s pretty (and I guess I didn\u2019t help with my reaction to her statement of having not expected to be embraced with open arms) but hopefully he does respect the fact that I have made a living reading people. Even barring a living, you don\u2019t have a life anymore on the streets if you can get taken in by *every* pretty smile.<br /> <br /> She definitely wasn\u2019t morally bankrupt. She was thankful Doc stopped her, and acknowledge that what might have truly began as a hunt for justice had gone too far. Her drive towards the hunt as an end unto itself, ignoring the justice bit of it had overwhelmed her. Which is why she was looking for help, for a troupe that could make sure that true justice was being done, and that it wasn\u2019t only being used as an excuse. No one was ready to invite her into the troupe right off the bat, cause none of us are quite that foolish, even me, even with how pretty she is, but we did offer to be a sort of outside conscience, for now.<br /> <br /> We also offered to let her stay at the house while she was here, after consulting amongst ourselves for a bit. We\u2019d sent her away so we could, and when she came back, she was all shyness and nerves, which is fair, it\u2019s rough going for a 30 minute walk down the block while people who hold your very life in their hands debate whether or not they like you enough to help you out. She was touched, in a non-supernatural *or* literal way, by the offer, so much so that the poor dear started crying. She\u2019d just been asking if we knew any good, cheap places to stay, or where she could get a job, she really didn\u2019t expect we\u2019d offer to let her stay, even if it was (on some people\u2019s part) largely just to keep a close eye on her.<br /> <br /> I think most of us warmed up to her at least a little. She was very sincere and direct with what she said, which was a plus for Jasmine. Natalie was a bit harder to read, but she took the lead in negotiating, and offered everything I might have wanted to, so I guess she believed in what Alice was saying. Speaking of which, Alice certainly is country people, with a little more emphasis on country than the phrase usually has anymore. I don\u2019t think I heard her curse, not once, and there were plenty of \u2018darn\u2019s to go about. She also didn\u2019t know quite how to respond to my aforementioned reaction to the whole open arms concept, though I\u2019m not sure if it was a \u2018not used to flirting with girls\u2019 or \u2018not used to flirting\u2019 or even a \u2018why the fuck are you flirting while we\u2019re having a discussion that might make the lot of you decide to kill me?\u2019. Further exploration will be required. Mine is a hard life.<br /> <br /> Doc and Alexia were still a bit on the fence if not on the other side of it, but they did agree to help and have her about, so I\u2019m not going to rib them about that. It\u2019s not as if I discount what she\u2019s done. I just think that intentions matter, and she originally meant to do good. That she\u2019s fucked that up is not in question, by her or us, but she\u2019s trying to fix it. And now we are too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t mean to get involved in a hunt so soon after arriving in New Haven. I haven\u2019t even found the Middle Shadows yet, but there he is, the ghost of Warren Ross, crying out for vengeance on the gang banger who killed him. He was in the wrong place at the wrong time. A mugging went badly, and Warren tried to play the hero to protect his fianc\u00e9e. It didn\u2019t end well for him.<br /> <br /> <i><i>There are bad people. They deserve to die.</i> </i><br /> <br /> I shouldn\u2019t get involved, not without a krewe to back me up.<br /> <br /> <i><i>We don\u2019t need a krewe for this. I know you feel the hunt calling.</i> </i><br /> <br /> I try to deny it, but the Huntress is right. A man is dead, leaving a young woman with nothing but broken dreams to comfort her as she cries herself to sleep at night. Justice must be done.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The man who shot Warren Ross to death is named James Leonard. It didn\u2019t take long to track down one of his gang buddies. A few tricks of the trade and he was well and truly spooked. He told me pretty much everything I wanted to know after a phantom phone call. It\u2019s amazing what people will do when they think they\u2019re being haunted by a vengeful ghost.<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s a problem. James was picked up by the cops not long after he shot Warren. He\u2019s in jail now, awaiting trial. They aren\u2019t letting him out until the case has been settled. That pretty much puts him out of my reach.<br /> <br /> <i><i>Our reach is long. Walls cannot keep us from our prey. Nothing can.</i> </i><br /> <br /> The Huntress wants me to risk it anyway. I can be invisible, walk through walls, evade surveillance cameras. It wouldn\u2019t be hard to kill James even in a jail cell. But it would be messy. It could cause problems, and maybe send the wrong message to the Middle Shadows. I can\u2019t risk it.<br /> <br /> <i><i>The challenge calls to us.</i> </i><br /> <br /> I shake my head to clear the Huntress\u2019 voice. It doesn\u2019t quite work. It\u2019s harder to push her whispers to the back of my mind than it used to be. I stand in front of the mirror in the bathroom of my cheap motel room, staring at myself as I will her to go away. I don\u2019t <i>want</i> to hunt anyone, not until I have a krewe to help me keep my perspective.<br /> <br /> <i><i>You </i>do<i> want to hunt. We crave it.</i> </i><br /> <br /> No, I don\u2019t. And James is going to be punished for his crime. They\u2019ll find him guilty, and he\u2019ll go to jail for a long, long time. That\u2019s what matters. I start to feel better, more sure of myself. I run some cold water into the sink and splash it on my face. I expect the Huntress to try and convince me that jail time isn\u2019t enough. That James need to die. I\u2019m prepared to ignore her.<br /> <br /> Instead, she hits me with a different approach.<br /> <br /> <i><i>How many other killers will there be? As long as they have their guns, they will grow like blossoms after a desert rain.</i> </i><br /> <br /> The gang banger who told me about James also told me where he got the gun that killed Warren: an arms dealer named Jerome. He is an eccentric man who wears colorful suits. It would take some effort, but I could probably track him down if he\u2019s local.<br /> <br /> <i><i>How much blood is on his hands? How many murders have been committed with the guns he sells? To stop the killers from blossoming, we must prevent the rain.</i> </i><br /> <br /> As far as I know, Jerome hasn\u2019t killed anyone. But he sells the tools others use to kill. He is an enabler. He\u2019s dangerous.<br /> <br /> <i>The hunt will be a welcome challenge.</i><br /> I stare hard into my own eyes reflected in the mirror. I can see pale echoes of the Huntress\u2019 grasping hands flickering around my head and shoulders, and I wonder if my reasoning is too tenuous. Is my perspective skewed, or does it make sense to kill Jerome? Is he really responsible for all the people his guns have killed? There\u2019s no question he deserves to be punished for selling illegal arms, but does he deserve my particular brand of justice? I can\u2019t even tell anymore.<br /> <br /> <i><i>He knows what his guns will do. If you don\u2019t kill him, many others will die.</i> </i><br /> <br /> That\u2019s all it takes. Suddenly, it seems clear as day. I have to kill the arms dealer.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> It takes me some time to track down Jerome, but I finally manage to catch up to him after he meets with some of his clients in New Haven\u2019s run-down warehouse district. I stalk him, running him to ground. His terror grows as I slowly follow him through a labyrinth of alleys and shipping containers. As I close in for the kill, he pulls out a pistol and empties the clip at me. Some of the shots fly wild. Others hit me, and each impact creates a small cloud of dust as the bullets shatter against my Grave Dirt Shroud. I barely notice.<br /> <br /> Finally, I corner him in an abandoned warehouse. In these final moments, I do what I always do. I explain why my prey must die. I tell Jerome that he is an enabler. The burden of all the deaths his guns have caused is his to bear.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m about to strike the killing blow when I feel something watching me. I catch a glimpse of cat\u2019s eyes for a moment, and then they are gone. My conviction wavers. Something isn\u2019t right. I shouldn\u2019t be doing this.<br /> <br /> <i><i>End the hunt.</i> </i><br /> <br /> I raise my axe, and then it stops. Someone has grabbed it. I spin around and see an angry Latino man. A sin-eater like me. He is wreathed in ghost flames that lick my axe where he holds it in an iron grip.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot Jerome\u2019s time yet. And now you have our attention.\u201d<br /> <br /> There is another here as well, a hulking cat-thing. I recoginze the eyes I saw before. I know I should be terrified of it, but my attention is fixed on the angry man before me. I know, beyond a doubt, that he is one of the Middle Shadows. And I\u2019ve probably ruined my best chance at getting the krewe to help me.<br /> <br /> I yank my axe away from the man\u2019s grip. My strength seems to surprise him. I try to explain why Jerome has to die, but even as the words leave my mouth, they feel hollow. Then the man tells me that blaming Jerome for Warren\u2019s death is no different than blaming a liquor store clerk when a drunk driver causes a fatal accident. I don\u2019t exactly agree with the comparison, but his point rings true. My resolve dies, and I let my Caul and Shroud fade away. I thought I was doing the right thing. A sense of hopelessness descends upon me as I realize that my footing is still far from stable, my perspective still horribly skewed by the voice that will always be a part of me.<br /> <br /> All I can do is ask the angry sin-eater for help, even though I know he wants to kill me on the spot. Right now, he is my only hope for redemption.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I bury my face in my hands and cry. I can\u2019t help it. I\u2019m simply overwhelmed by the Middle Shadows\u2019 generosity. I\u2019m sure some of the other people in the cafe are staring, wondering what\u2019s wrong with me, but I don\u2019t care. After my encounter with Doc last night, I thought I had destroyed any hope of finding a home here, but this krewe has proven me wrong. They\u2019re going to help me get control of my life again. They\u2019ve even invited me to stay in their house. Sure, partly they just want to keep an eye on me, but that\u2019s okay. That\u2019s what I <i>want</i>. It\u2019s what I <i>need</i>.<br /> <br /> The man I met last night is called Doc. He\u2019s still pretty angry with me. Jerome the arms dealer is a friend of his, and I\u2019m pretty sure that if I hadn\u2019t been cooperating so nicely, Doc would be trying to end me about now. Maybe he and I have more in common than he\u2019d like to admit. After all, he wasn\u2019t just out for a pleasant evening stroll last night with his werecat girlfriend. They were hunting too.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t even know there was such a thing as werecats. Werewolves, sure. I ran into them in Oregon. But not werecats. Still, she seems really nice. Her name is Noriko, and more than anyone else I\u2019ve met, she seems to really understand what I\u2019m going through. I don\u2019t necessarily understand why, but she\u2019s made me feel more comfortable and hopeful than I\u2019ve felt in a long time. She\u2019s really cute too. It\u2019s too bad she\u2019s spoken for. Then again, I\u2019m still trying to wrap my head around the idea of dating someone who isn\u2019t another sin-eater. I honestly never really thought a relationship would work with someone who hadn\u2019t been through the same thing I have. Besides, the last thing I should be thinking about right now is romance.<br /> <br /> Even so, I\u2019m pretty sure that Sara was flirting with me. She\u2019s really pretty, and she\u2019s also been really sweet and understanding. So far, Sara\u2019s the krewe member who has made me feel the most welcome. I\u2019m kind of confused, though. It seems strange that she would flirt with me, given the circumstances. And I\u2019m pretty sure she and Natalie are together. I can\u2019t believe she would flirt with another woman right in front of her girlfriend. I must be misinterpreting something.<br /> <br /> Along with Sara, Natalie was the other krewe member arguing most strongly in my favor. Natalie is gorgeous too, but I\u2019m not sure what to make of her. She seems kind of vain, but alos caring and motherly. She\u2019s definitely one of the krewe leaders, alongside Doc. At least, that\u2019s the impression she gives. I wonder if she\u2019s the one who posts on the Twilight network. If so, she\u2019s pretty much the reason I came to New Haven looking for the Middle Shadows.<br /> <br /> The other two krewe members are Jasmine and Alexia. Jasmine\u2019s an Asian woman and seems really serious. When she looks at me, she seems to be peering right into my soul. I get the feeling she can read me like book. Whatever she sees must satisfy her, though, because she seems willing to help me out.<br /> <br /> Alexia isn\u2019t quite as inviting, but she still seems nice, just cautious. I don\u2019t think she likes me very much, but I can\u2019t blame her. I doubt she cares for the whole killing thing. I gather the krewe hasn\u2019t had a Reaper before, and I\u2019m not sure Alexia\u2019s comfortable with what I do, even when it\u2019s for the right reasons. Still, that could be a good thing. If I\u2019m right about her, then she could be exactly the kind of person I need to help me regain my perspective and keep the Huntress at bay.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Eventually, I manage to stop crying. Sara\u2019s arm around my shoulders is nice. It\u2019s the first real human connection I\u2019ve felt in a long time.<br /> <br /> The Middle Shadows are going to show me their home next. They say\u2019s its really big, so I don\u2019t know what to expect. I\u2019m anxious about it. Things seem to moving really fast, but maybe it\u2019s for the best. This is what I came for, after all.<br /> <br /> <i><i>You can\u2019t escape your calling. This is all a mere distraction.</i> </i><br /> <br /> I tell the Huntress to shut up.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVI</i><br /> <br /> And that introduced the new character. We sort of ran with assuming the fictlet Doc\u2019s player wrote happened, and started at that point.<br /> <br /> Nothing much else to add, comments and questions welcome<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T11:18:43-07:00","id":265591,"title":"","content":"Hey, Alice is kind of like me. Except for being lesbian and killing people... But I don't curse, though I use dang instead of darn... O.k. never mind.<br /> <br /> A Demon game? Curious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T16:02:35-07:00","id":265777,"title":"","content":"Yea Alice is a cool character, but then they are all cool characters.<br /> <br /> I am planning to put up her background Saturday. Sometime after Sunday, when I am done getting Changeling stuff up, initial Demon stuff will go up for <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"