26T00:57:54-07:00","id":266041,"title":"","content":"Fair enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T01:24:02-07:00","id":267258,"title":"","content":"It's the off week. Let's meet Alice<br /> <br /> <b>Lost Footing</b><br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <b><b>Alice Campbell</b></b><br /> <b><b>Threshold: </b></b> Prey<br /> <b><b>Archetype:</b> </b>Reaper<br /> <b><b>Virtue: </b></b> Just<br /> <b><b>Vice: </b></b> Relentless<br /> <br /> <b><b>LOST FOOTING</b></b><br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how long I\u2019ve been repeating that to myself.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s so much blood. It\u2019s all over my hands and arms. I\u2019m pretty sure it\u2019s splattered all over my face too. The carpet is soaked in it, and I\u2019m kneeling in the puddle because I can\u2019t stand. All the strength has drained from my body. I guess I\u2019m in shock.<br /> <br /> Arizona State House Representative George Powell lies dead on the floor in front of me. His body is twisted awkwardly, one leg bent painfully under the other. One of his forearms is nearly severed. I can see the pale white bone peeking out of the ragged flesh. His stern blue eyes are staring at the ceiling, wide open with surprise. There\u2019s a wood axe planted deep in his chest. My axe.<br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I never imagined my life would turn out this way, but I guess there were signs all along. I was born and raised in Casa Grande, Arizona, on my parents\u2019 small dairy ranch. I was the youngest of three children; both my elder siblings were brothers, Jacob and Ethan, and they picked on me a lot, so I learned to be tough. When push came to shove, though, they always looked out for me.<br /> <br /> The ranch work wasn\u2019t easy, but that never really bothered me. I don\u2019t mind hard work. I helped take care of the cattle, making sure they were fed and milked. When the cows got sick or were injured, I tried to take care of them. I didn\u2019t like to see them suffer. Sometimes the sickness was incurable or the injury too great. In those cases, I still did my best, and somehow my presence seemed to help the poor beasts die more comfortably. Maybe even more quickly.The same thing happened when my grandfather passed away. He had terminal cancer, and was in a lot of pain. In his final moments, I held his feeble hand and all the anguish drained from his face. He died at peace, with a gentle smile and a soft, contented sigh. My mother said I had a gift for bringing peace to people and animals that were about to pass on, like a little redheaded angel. I always felt more like an angel of death.<br /> <br /> My family was pretty religious. Church on Sundays, prayer before meals and bed. I had a harder time with my faith than they did, though, especially once I became a teenager and discovered that I had no interest in boys. In fact, I developed a serious crush on another girl in my class that lasted through high school. I never acted on it, though. I was terrified that my family and classmates would discover that I was a lesbian. To this day, my parents don\u2019t know. My brother Jacob does, but he\u2019s cool about it, and he helps me keep the secret from the rest of my family.<br /> <br /> We never had a lot of money. It was all we could do to keep the ranch going, but in the end it wasn\u2019t enough. By the time I finished high school, we were in debt and forced to sell our land and cattle. The family moved to Phoenix after I graduated, and I got my own apartment. I made ends meet working as a waitress. Compared to the farm work, it was a breeze, and the tips were pretty good. I used to dream about saving enough to attend university, but even then I knew that college was a futile hope. As it was, I spent most of my disposable earnings on camping and climbing equipment. Whenever I could, I\u2019d head out into the desert or the canyons to go rock climbing, caving, kayaking or just camping with my friends. Phoenix was great and all, but I never felt more alive than when I was scaling a sheer rock face or exploring a twisting cavern.<br /> <br /> In Phoenix, I was more open about my sexuality and even dated a few other women. It was nice to be myself for a change, even if none of the relationships worked out. And then I met Katherine Powell.<br /> <br /> She walked into the restaurant where I worked. It wasn\u2019t an expensive place, but it was trendy. She was there with her friends, and I was their server. As soon as I laid eyes on her, my heart skipped a beat. She was beautiful, with gorgeous brown eyes and a great body. Her mouth turned up slighly at the corners of her lips, giving her this confident, cat-like smile that just made me melt. Her friends called her Kitty. It was love at first sight.<br /> <br /> But of course I couldn\u2019t say anything to her. She probably wasn\u2019t into girls, and I didn\u2019t want to embarass myself. When I found out she was the daughter of George Powell, an influential conservative politician, I figured I had zero chance with her. But it wasn\u2019t like that at all. She was really alternative and open-minded. She came to the restaurant about once every week or two to eat with her friends, and I ended up serving their table most of the time, so we sort of got to know one another a little. I think one of her friends picked up on the fact that I was crushing on her pretty badly and must have said something, because one night Kitty started flirting with me. The next thing I knew, we were dating.<br /> <br /> Those were some of the best weeks of my life. Even now, knowing how it all turned out\u2014knowing what a sham it all was\u2014I still can\u2019t help but remember my time with Kitty fondly. I was in love.<br /> <br /> We had been going out for a few months when we decided to go caving. Kitty had never been before, but she was always eager to try new things. She was athletic and enjoyed camping and spending time outdoors, so one weekend we headed to a cave I\u2019d been wanting to explore. We had all the right equipment and took all the right precautions. But sometimes tragedy strikes, and there\u2019s nothing you can do about it.<br /> <br /> I was scaling a deep shaft in the cave, trying to see if there were passages at the bottom. It was rough going. Kitty was managing my safety rope, but something went wrong and the rope came loose. I should have been fine, anyway; I\u2019m a good climber. But I made a mistake and lost my footing. I fell thirty feet down the shaft and landed badly on the uneven rocks at the bottom.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know exactly how bad it was, but it was pretty bad. I broke my back, one of my legs, and several ribs. I had severe internal injuries. Each breath was excruciating. I was dying.<br /> <br /> Kitty frantically screamed down to me. I could barely manage to call out to her. I told her to go find help. She couldn\u2019t do anything for me by herself, so she ran out of the cave. That\u2019s the last I saw of her before I died.<br /> <br /> If she had brought help, she could have made it back in time to save me. I didn\u2019t expire quickly. I lay there for over a day. Every moment was agony, punctuated by brief, blissful blackouts. And then I died.<br /> <br /> <i>* * * * *</i><br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> I know I should stand up, leave the house. Flee before I\u2019m discovered. I\u2019ve taken my revenge on the man who killed me. Justice has been done. The hunt is over.<br /> <br /> <i><i>The hunt was good.</i> </i><br /> <br /> Her voice echoes in my head. My shock starts to give way to a sort of determined conviction. It wasn\u2019t easy getting this close to Mr. Powell. It took weeks of investigation and waiting before I found the right moment. The Huntress encouraged me, guided me. She\u2019s done this before. And it all paid off. Powell was an evil, unscrupulous man. And now he\u2019s dead.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I woke up slowly. I felt like I had been dreaming. In my dream, a strange woman came to me. She looked like a Navajo witch. Grasping arms reached from the shadows behind her, clutching at me, at her and at things they could never reach. I somehow knew that she was called the Grasping Huntress. She told me that Kitty wasn\u2019t coming back. She had abandoned me. Her father made her leave me to die, and no one would ever be the wiser. Unless\u2026<br /> <br /> As I woke, I realized that I was no longer in pain. I could move again. My spine was whole, my leg unbroken. I could breath without effort. I knew then that it wasn\u2019t a dream. I\u2019d made a deal. The Grasping Huntress brought me back so that I could make Representative Powell pay for leaving me to die.<br /> <br /> I free climbed out of the shaft and found my way out of the cave. It was the middle of the night, and the desert was bathed in moonlight. I had to hike several miles to the closest highway and hitchhike back to Phoenix. I didn\u2019t want to believe that Kitty had really abandoned me, and my phone had a little charge left, so I called her.<br /> <br /> When she answered the phone, her voice was trembling. She never expected to get a call from me. My voice was dry and it must have sounded strange, but she recognized me.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice? Oh my god, Alice! Are you okay? How did you\u2014?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy did you leave me to die?\u201d I asked, quietly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t want to\u2026but it was too late! I couldn\u2019t do anything. And if it came out that I was involved\u2026my father said it would ruin us!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRuin you? His political career is worth more than my <i>life</i>?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo\u2026it\u2019s just\u2026I didn\u2019t know what to do! So I just did what he told me!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice? Are you still there?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow could you leave me? I thought you loved me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2026I\u2019m sorry. I\u2019m not really into girls. I was just curious and you seemed nice. I guess I was just rebelling against my dad. He\u2019s always so concerned about his political reputation. It\u2019s annoying! He hated that we were together! He thought it was a stain on our family. I mean, he couldn\u2019t <i>stand</i> the fact that I was dating a lower income lesbian.\u201d<br /> <br /> The torrent of her words swept through my heart and broke it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s why you were with me? Rebelling against your father? I love you, and you don\u2019t feel anything at all?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m so sorry, Alice! I shouldn\u2019t have used you like that. I was going to tell you\u2026but\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou killed me,\u201d I whispered.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know why I said that. I think I was angry because I knew that she really <i>had</i> killed me, more or less. Ultimately, though, she was just a scared twenty-year-old. It was her father\u2019s fault that I died. But I was angry and heartbroken. I wanted her to know what she\u2019d done, and that was all I could think of to say.<br /> <br /> Kitty was silent. I could sense the terror rising in her as she realized she must be talking to a ghost.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice?\u201d She could barely get my name out past her fear.<br /> <br /> That was the last thing I heard before my phone died.<br /> <br /> <i>* * * * *</i><br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> <i><i>Only what you had to. </i></i><br /> <br /> I slowly struggle to my feet. I feel sick, but manage to keep from vomiting. It\u2019s time to leave. I turn to the door\u2026and Kitty is standing there, staring in horror at the corpse of her father. At the axe planted in his chest. At the blood-splattered girlfriend that she never loved. She\u2019s in shock and can\u2019t even speak. She doesn\u2019t believe what she\u2019s seeing.<br /> <br /> <i><i>She left you to die. </i></i><br /> <br /> All the anger and betrayal and heartbreak fills my head. I grab my axe and wrench it from Powell\u2019s chest. It makes a horrible wet cracking sound as it pulls free. I grip the axe with both hands and take two long strides toward Kitty. She screams, but the scream is silenced when my axe digs halfways through her neck. She falls to the floor and another puddle of blood begins to blossom beneath her.<br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> <i><i>Only what you promised. </i></i><br /> <br /> I collapse to my knees again and break down into sobs. My tears mix with Kitty\u2019s blood, leaving bitter streaks that run down my face. The Huntress tries to comfort me, to justify what I\u2019ve done.<br /> <br /> <i><i>There are bad people. They deserve to die. </i></i><br /> <br /> I realize in that moment that I\u2019ve committed myself to this murderous path. I\u2019m only alive so that I can bring justice to those whose crimes deserve death. I feel my innocence shatter like glass, its jagged shards slicing at my heart and leaving scars that will never heal. This brings on a new round of sobs.<br /> <br /> Eventually, I collect myself. Now that I\u2019ve killed Kitty, it will be easy for the authorities to connect the murders to me. I\u2019ll have to mask the evidence, and the Huntress shows me how. We find a pistol hidden in a closet and I use my plasm to conduct a ceremony that makes it look like Kitty shot herself. The police will think it\u2019s a murder-suicide. I have to leave my axe behind, but I can get another one easily enough.<br /> <br /> Before I leave, though, I notice Kitty\u2019s bracelet. It\u2019s Navajo, made of silver and turquoise. I gave it to her not long before I died. I\u2019m surprised she\u2019s still wearing it. Maybe she did have feelings for me. Or maybe she felt guilty and kept it as a reminder of her mistakes. Either way, I\u2019m flooded with remorse when I see it. Kitty didn\u2019t deserve to die.<br /> <br /> Inwardly, I scream at the Huntress. It\u2019s all I can do. But she\u2019s silent.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I left Arizona as soon as I could. I just emptied my bank account, got in my jeep and drove. I ended up in Portland, Oregon. I still didn\u2019t completely understand what I\u2019d become. I knew that I\u2019d been brought back from the dead for a reason. I knew I could sense death and see ghosts, and I decided it was my duty to help them seek justice against their killers. That definitely seemed to be what the Huntress wanted.<br /> <br /> As far as I knew, there weren\u2019t any others like me. I didn\u2019t know the term sin-eater. The Huntress always referred to us as skinwalkers, but that made me uncomfortable because I remember hearing Navajo legends about skinwalkers when I was a girl, and they were always portrayed as evil witches. That description might\u2019ve applied to the Huntress, but I didn\u2019t want to think of <i>myself</i> as evil. Still, one of the first Keys I learned to use was Primeval, which seemed a lot like skinwalker witchraft to me.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t too long before I ran into other sin-eaters, though. A little girl had been murdered, her body thrown into the Columbia River. The police hadn\u2019t been able to track down her killer, but I heard her ghost still wandered the river banks, so I went to talk to her. That\u2019s when I ran across the Dead Judges. They were a young krewe of sin-eaters dedicated to making sure that dangerous ghosts were eliminated, imprisoned, or destroyed to pay for their crimes. Of course, they did it mainly to protect the living.<br /> <br /> The krewe only had three members. Jonathan Marshall was a handsome thirty-something Stricken Advocate, joined to the Crying Woman. He was the krewe\u2019s leader, and used to be a lawyer until he died of cancer. Then he gave up his practice in order to serve the dead. Cassidy O\u2019Rourke was an angry Torn Gatekeeper, and she was tied to a geist called the Red Hood. She\u2019d been raped and murdered by a man possessed by a psychopathic ghost and was determined to make sure no one else had to suffer her fate. And then there was Randy Goddard, a Forgotten Bonepicker who used to be a P.I. until his fascination with the paranormal discredited him. His geist was the Plank Walker. In the krewe\u2019s mythos, Jon was the Judge, and Randy and Cassidy were the Jury.<br /> <br /> I ended up joining the krewe, and the krewe binding gave me a new mandate. The Dead Judges had always just focused on dangerous ghosts, leaving living killers to the mortal authorities. But that wasn\u2019t enough. I became the Executioner. If someone needed to die to avenge and resolve a wronged ghost, I was the sin-eater for the job. I\u2019m not proud of it, but I took to it easily enough. That still scares me. I could blame the Huntress, but it wasn\u2019t just her. Something inside me needed to seek justice.<br /> <br /> <i>* * * * *</i><br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a long time since I\u2019ve caught myself thinking those words.<br /> <br /> <i><i>He was worthy prey. </i></i><br /> <br /> The body of a park ranger lies sprawled on the ground before me, bent uncomfortably over moss-covered tree roots. His eyes stare at the sky, wide with fear. His shotgun rests on the ground nearby, its shells spent. Blood stains the moss red and soaks into the moist earth. It drips from the head of my axe.<br /> <br /> Rain begins to fall.<br /> <br /> Somehow, this doesn\u2019t feel right. This wasn\u2019t a just kill.<br /> <br /> <i><i>The hunt was good. That\u2019s all that matters. </i></i><br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I liked being a part of the Dead Judges. I felt like I belonged for the first time since high school. For a few years, we did good work helping ghosts and making sure that monsters, both living and dead, wouldn\u2019t hurt anyone again.<br /> <br /> Cassidy and I fell for each other and we ended up in a relationship. She had a hard time with men since she died, and we shared a desire to see justice done. We were good for each other, and I think she understood me better than anyone. Probably still does.<br /> <br /> I could go on and on about the things the krewe did, like the time we destroyed a geist who had grown into a huge ghost tree, or the time I stalked and killed a thrillseeking cult of rich college kids who got their jollies from drugging and burying homeless people alive in homemade coffins. I could describe the time we investigated a haunted mine and helped free the ghosts of several miners. But those days are past, and I don\u2019t feel like reliving them.<br /> <br /> In the end, I screwed up. I lost my footing. My perspective became skewed. I killed some people who didn\u2019t deserve it. An alcoholic who killed a family of three in a drunken car accident. A young woman whose marital indiscretions led her husband to commit suicide.They\u2019d made mistakes, sure. They were selfish idiots who deserved punishment. But they hadn\u2019t set out to do wrong. They didn\u2019t deserve to die. The other Dead Judges became worried about me, Cassidy especially. We started arguing a lot. She was afraid of what I was becoming. She warned me that the Grasping Huntress was leading me astray, but I refused to see it.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> \u201cOh fuck me,\u201d Randy exclaims, out of breath from running through the forest. Cassidy and Jon are standing there too, staring at the ranger\u2019s corpse and my bloodied axe. The look in Jon\u2019s eyes is cold and hard. He\u2019s angry. Maybe angrier than I\u2019ve ever seen him.<br /> <br /> But Jon\u2019s angry look is meaningless compared to the mixture of rage and hurt on Cassidy\u2019s face. The rain has plastered her straight blonde hair to her forehead, but she\u2019s still beautiful. It\u2019s over between us, though. I can tell.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat the hell, Alice?\u201d Cassidy shouts. \u201cWhy the fuck did you kill him?\u201d<br /> <br /> <i><i>He was dangerous. He was a challenge. The hunt always ends in death. </i></i><br /> <br /> I close my eyes and shake my head, trying to clear the Huntress\u2019s voice from my mind. I reach up and tear my deathmask from my face as I begin to argue. \u201cHe shot that camper. He killed her! Her ghost is suffering!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was an accident! He didn\u2019t mean to shoot her! The gun just misfired. You <i>know</i> that!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe didn\u2019t deserve to die, Alice.\u201d Jon says. There is a chill in his voice. \u201cYou were there when we made that judgement.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut the camper\u2019s ghost is crying out for revenge! We can\u2019t just let her linger on in anguish. How else are we supposed to help her?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat girl\u2019s ghost is confused and angry!\u201d Cassidy is screaming at me now. \u201cShe\u2019s just furious that her life was cut short. She doesn\u2019t care about justice. That\u2019s <i>our</i> job Alice. That\u2019s what <i>we</i> do. And this?\u201d Cassidy gestured angrily at the ranger\u2019s bloody corpse. \u201cThis isn\u2019t right! It\u2019s just cold-blooded murder.\u201d<br /> <br /> Cassidy turns her back on me, wrapping her arms around herself as if to stave off the cold. \u201cYou\u2019re a monster,\u201d she says.<br /> <br /> As soon as the words leave Cassidy\u2019s mouth, I know she\u2019s right. I\u2019ve lost my footing. I\u2019ve fallen and I don\u2019t even know where I\u2019ve landed. The Grasping Huntress has ahold of me, and I\u2019m losing my mind. I lower my eyes and see the ranger\u2019s corpse.<br /> <br /> What have I done?<br /> <br /> \u201cYou went too far this time, Alice,\u201d Randy says, shaking his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s been going too far for awhile now,\u201d says Jon. His voice is like stone.<br /> <br /> Cassidy begins walking away, her back still turned. Randy and Jon share a look, and I can tell they\u2019ve talked about what comes next.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re too dangerous, Alice. You have no idea what justice is anymore.\u201d Jon hesitates, then sighs deeply before continuing.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t belong in this krewe. The executioner can\u2019t be judge and jury too. I\u2019m sorry, Alice, but we\u2019re done.\u201d<br /> <br /> Randy and Jon turn and follow Cassidy into the forest.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t want to go on living after I got kicked out of the Dead Judges, but I\u2019m a survivor. I had to move on. I was angry at the Grasping Huntress, but I couldn\u2019t lay all the blame on her. We\u2019re a part of each other now, even if we both want different things. Somehow, I have to find a way to live <i>with</i> her without <i>becoming</i> her. I need to regain my footing, get back to solid ground, and figure out how to do my job as a Reaper without losing perspective again.<br /> <br /> I thought about making a go of it alone, but that\u2019s a bad plan. I can\u2019t do this by myself. If I\u2019m alone, the only thing I have to guide me is my geist, and I know exactly where that road leads.<br /> <br /> I need a krewe. And preferably one as far from Portland as possible.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-28-2014, 04:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T02:27:25-07:00","id":268109,"title":"","content":"The OP has been updated! Characters who updated their Virtues/Vices for GMC have had them updated, and behind a spoiler block is the new Krewe Wheel and thumbnails on Sara and Alice, with pictures. Check it out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-06T01:39:29-07:00","id":273532,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to continue the tale of the Middle Shadows, and their newest recruit. Let\u2019s check in on them. Note that Doc\u2019s Log is long as it covers the past two sessions not just 117.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2245 Hours, Saturday, November 6, 2010<br /> <br /> I came home early to get some work in on Bone Dry\u2019s book of damning spells. But we had a lot going on tonight.<br /> <br /> We arrived slightly early to Murder Ballads to arrange the rooms and make sure we weren\u2019t being setup. Or maybe I was just being paranoid. Nightshade led The Hair away before The Collector and Lucille arrived. We didn\u2019t want any incidents to occur willingly or otherwise with that. I greeted the unlikely couple before asking if Lucille would like to dance. I meant it as a way to relax a bit but she declined. Then something odd happened between her and The Collector in that he almost seemed to gently order her to go. I noted politely that she was not required, I was only trying to be polite. Lucille came with me but she was extremely nervous. Realizing that I had no idea if she could dance or not, I gently asked if she had a style preference. She admitted that she was \u201cfamiliar with late 19th Century Western dance.\u201d Great so I put her in an incredibly awkward position. I stopped by the DJ booth and requested some symphonic metal as we moved to the dance floor. I knew enough about the dances she was familiar with to fake it given the musical choices and she was able to keep up for the same reason. When we finished our dance they were ready for me to craft my Charm for The Collector. Lucille gave me a genuine smile and seemed to be glad she came. She noted before we entered the private room that she was very thankful for the dance and thought that she might enjoy dancing again later. I felt like I had made someone happy that hadn\u2019t been happy in a very long time. We both entered the private room looking pleased.<br /> <br /> The Collector brought a silver sacrificial dagger with a blade of strange black stone. I didn\u2019t need to be told that the dagger had killed many times as the death energy flowed in waves. I got my gear together and acid etched blood rivulets into the grip to match the grooves on the blade. Then I fully attuned the Charm to the Stigmata Key. Rose took a Cat\u2019s Eye marble and converted it to more of a bracelet attuned to the Primeval Key. I was surprised when she handed it to me. Lucille seemed very interested in dancing again and The Collector was interested in watching Bright Eyes object read, so we slipped back out to the dance floor. When the others came back, I used my incredibly weak Japanese to say goodbye. She responded in a way that I didn\u2019t understand, but she looked very pleased. I\u2019ll have to ask Noriko what that means.<br /> <br /> After the mystic work was done, we switched to a different private room to meet Elizabeth. She arrived shortly after The Collector left. Elizabeth was obviously looking to use this situation to get a leg up in her community, which wasn\u2019t surprising, but did annoy me a little bit. It\u2019s a bigger problem, but I kept my mouth shut. We are after all, planning to do the same thing to them on a larger scale. The vampires knew that there was some magic that involves draining people. Someone sent pictures of the drained bodies to the hunters. Elizabeth suspected it was servants of Mariah as they weren\u2019t considered real people anyway. But the most important bits of information was that she had seen and could get more information about the ritual. A ritual scalpel which Mariah ordered had some kind of special treated silver coating. Also Elizabeth said she could find out where the supplies came from. We got her contact information and agreed as a group that we could coordinate our assault, whenever that would be.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m actually going to work on decrypting this book.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0115 Hours, Sunday, November 7, 2010<br /> <br /> It was 2300 Hours before I get everything ready in the Library. I got a good two hours of research in but I didn\u2019t feel like I\u2019d gotten very far. Then Gretchen came in and asked one of her special questions. I had to tell her that I, in fact, didn\u2019t know why guys don\u2019t just buttfuck people all the time. The rational answers that started to form in my head were shouted down by the need not let her ask follow up questions. I called Noriko after that and we decided to go on patrol together.<br /> <br /> Here\u2019s to hoping that works out better.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0400 Hours, Sunday, November 7, 2010<br /> <br /> I have no idea where this restraint is coming from but I can tell you it is damn well wearing thin quick. Logically I knew if I killed her, she\u2019d just be back at dawn, but what the fuck!?!<br /> <br /> Let me back up, I\u2019m really pissed and out of sorts.<br /> <br /> Noriko and I went on patrol. I gave the streets near the dance studio a break and we headed for rougher areas. We had just gotten started when I saw a flicker down a side street of what I realized was a chase. We cut through some back alleys and caught up when I realized the one running away was Jerome. I didn\u2019t know the girl but I could see she was a Sin-Eater. The axe on her back left very little confusion as to what was happening. I looked at Noriko and she nodded. We moved in quickly and as quietly as I could manage. Noriko moved into the shadows of the building and started stripping. I didn\u2019t understand at first and then she shifted. As I moved into the condemned shell, I unlocked my Pyre-Flame Shroud to keep down the surprises and also make sure I had some tricks ready, just in case.<br /> <br /> Noriko was already in the rafters and made it easier for me to see where to go. When I got to them, Jerome was pressed into a corner and the Sin-Eater was looking up where Noriko had been moments before. She threw the axe over her head and I had to bust my ass to grab it. This girl must be really into her kills because she didn\u2019t notice the room brighten or hear me or anything. When the axe stopped, she noticed. When my ghostflame started sizzling around the handle, she ripped the axe away and damn near threw me to the side. I told her it wasn\u2019t time for Jerome to die yet, but that she definitely had our attention. Noriko stood in the doorway, her silhouette falling over the room like a blackout cloak and her claws leaving wicked grooves in the pale street light. And that\u2019s about the time things got weird.<br /> <br /> I told Jerome to go home while staring at the redhead. She was pretty, even covered in sweat and grime from the chase. She tried to protest that Jerome was a bad person and needed to be punished. Somehow she figured out that he was a gun runner. Because of that, she then decided that he was responsible for deaths caused by guns. Now in general, that might hold some weight, but given that Jerome was picky about his clients, I didn\u2019t bite. I asked her if she knew how bat shit crazy that was or if she went around killing liquor store clerks after DUI accidents too? As the words left my lips, it was like they formed a hand that slapped her. The strange new Sin-Eater shook her head like she was coming out of a fog and was obviously confused. Jerome ran behind me and outside. He screamed a little and kept running. Noriko came back in dressed after that. Proper introductions were made after that. I will call her Axe, both to protect her and because I\u2019m an asshole. Noriko rode with her and we went to Alchemy for coffee and story time.<br /> <br /> Axe has problems. Major problems. Geist has at least as much say about what is right and wrong as you do problems. And she was pitiful as she asked for help. Noriko was incredibly sympathetic and I know why, but I didn\u2019t meet her until after she was in control. I also didn\u2019t meet her trying to kill one of my friends and contacts. Axe originally came to New Haven to find the Middle Shadows. She needed a Krewe and pieced together that Nightshade was in the area. I felt sorry for her, but I also didn\u2019t trust her. I gave her my number to call at 1100 Hours. We\u2019ll see if I go on a hunting trip after that. I called Nightshade and gave her the short version as I was driving over to the motel Axe was staying in. I needed to make sure she didn\u2019t just play me.<br /> <br /> I got back to the Bluffs without issues once I spotted Axe\u2019s Jeep in the parking lot. Nightshade and Bright Eyes had already assembled the Krewe so I explained things to them. Bright Eyes was very bothered by how \u201cfinal\u201d I was planning to be if Axe didn\u2019t follow the letter and spirit of our agreement. She wasn\u2019t wrong, but I didn\u2019t care. A mass murdering Sin-Eater with no way to tell accident from intent will have to be put down.<br /> <br /> Okay sleep is really a joke at this point. I\u2019m going to go setup the hanging bag and work off some tension.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Sunday, November 7, 2010<br /> <br /> Very little sleep, nerves over whether I would need to hunt down another Sin-Eater, I\u2019m impressed that it only took an hour to find my center. The rest of the Krewe gave me a fairly wide berth this morning with the exception of Bright Eyes. For someone who really doesn\u2019t like to fight, she was damned on the spot about pressing me to be merciful if Axe were to fuck this up.<br /> <br /> Fortunately (for Axe), the call came in right at 1100 Hours. I almost asked Nightshade if she had some way to trace the call, but I knew Bright Eyes would go off on me for that one. Axe agreed to meet us at Lulu\u2019s at 1300 Hours so the plan is set. We\u2019ll see why she thinks we can help her and then decide what to do with her.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1430 Hours, Sunday, November 7, 2010<br /> <br /> I may yet live to regret this, but even I have to admit that we made the right choice. And I\u2019m getting ahead again.<br /> <br /> We arrived at Lulu\u2019s just before 1300 Hours to get a table. Axe arrived shortly after we did, still before 1300. Bright Eyes almost swooned when the now cleaned up redhead walked in and I nodded to her. In an instant I knew she was lost to any negative comment I might make, it was a little disturbing. Bright Eyes got up and let Axe sit between her and Nightshade, for no reason of course. Then we had Axe tell her story again. There were a few more details than the version Noriko and I heard, but it was obviously the same story. I will say without any attempt at sarcasm that Axe\u2019s life has been shit since she came back. Any bright spots have been blotted out by problems with The Huntress. I\u2019m pretty sure I like the Laughing Lady a whole lot more now. And I know for a fact that I have a whole new respect for the Dog of War.<br /> <br /> After we learned how Axe was homeless, friendless, and directionless, Nightshade suggested that she take a walk while we discussed options. Killing her was off the table as she was obviously not in control of her actions in the way normal people, even normal Sin-Eaters would be. She had asked for a good, cheap place to rent so we could help her get her footing in terms of learning to balance the wishes of The Huntress with not being a mass murderer. When it was said and done, it took us a half hour to decide that she needed to stay with the Krewe. We could keep an eye on her and she could be with people that understood her particular kind of crazy. When Axe came back and we told her the news, she broke down and cried. I admit I felt like a horse\u2019s ass, but I still didn\u2019t want to believe she was that lost. Noriko rode with Axe again and made sure she got back to the Bluffs.<br /> <br /> If I were a sadistic asshole, instead of just an asshole, I might have felt a bit of glee at just how overwhelmed Axe was when she first saw the House. That followed by \u201cThe Rules\u201d discussion and I think she was almost ready to bolt. Tavia made a production of getting the room ready and I managed to pull Lily aside and gain an extra set of eyes. Lily has no time for anyone that is dangerous to the Krewe so she was fully on board.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not sure how it came up now, but in the various conversations Karen mentioned how the House keeps watch sometimes. I pressed a little because the rest of us didn\u2019t know what she meant. Apparently Karen has felt like she was being watched while alone in her room multiple times. If Axe thought I was just playing the protector card to be pissed at her, I\u2019m pretty sure she learned otherwise at that. I don\u2019t know who or what is spying on Karen, but I will. And it or they should hope that a very good explanation is available for me.<br /> <br /> For now, I\u2019m actually going to bury myself in research and see what secrets I can learn about Bone Dry\u2019s magic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1900 Hours, Sunday, November 7, 2010<br /> <br /> Four good hours of research and I\u2019m on the verge of something big. I can feel it! But now we\u2019re getting everyone together to go clubbing. I think Nightshade wants to show off the 27 Club, and why not? She should be proud of it. But ultimately we\u2019re heading out to introduce Axe to Murder Ballads. Who knows what we\u2019ll get into this time.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, that our long tall Alice hasn\u2019t run off screaming into the night is a strong testament to her tenacity, for certain. She\u2019s taking it fairly well, all told - a bit overwhelmed, to be sure, but so was I when I showed up, and I was there as an invited if not looked for guest, not as someone on probation from a death sentence. She\u2019d barely had time to step into the house, an awestruck look on her face, when the introductions started. She took it all in stride at first, given Tavia\u2019s occasionally startling intensity (I think Noriko gave her a little bit of a heads up, as she didn\u2019t even blink at Natalie calling us a triad, and Noriko made a small \u201cyes!\u201d motion to herself). But as more and more of the broader troupe was mentioned, and more and more warnings - about the house, the city, various not present housemates - were given, I could see the panic rising in Alice\u2019s eyes. So I called a pause, and most of us headed over to the TV room to relax a bit, while Alexia made a delicious lemon meringue pie (Alice\u2019s favorite) and Jasmine, Doc, and Tavia got Alice\u2019s bedroom ready.<br /> <br /> We did manage to get her to relax a little, especially once Alexia brought out a pair of super wonderful pies. Eventually, we finished up the tour, and even with the break, and the pie, it wasn\u2019t too long before she started regretting everything all over again. Not really, I hope, but it was a whole lot to take in, even once I started trying to talk about some of the cool things about the house and how we helped people too, not just about all the spooky stuff and the stories about all the messed up situations we\u2019ve run into.<br /> <br /> We ended the tour at her new bedroom, and I may have lingered behind a bit - to make sure she didn\u2019t need anything, of course. She did ask that I be sure and let her know when we headed out, as she was looking forward to getting some fresh air. Not one to leave an opportunity at the wayside, I offered to stand as escort, if she wanted to take a walk along the bluffs - not precisely the rock climbing, spelunking and camping she said she enjoyed, but it sounded like it might be better to get her settled than staying in the \u2018Addam\u2019s family mansion\u2019. There is a State Park nearby - I haven\u2019t had any reason to go visit yet, but I might try and make sure we get a trip in for Alice between cases.<br /> <br /> We talked a little, as we walked, but there was plenty of quiet as well - this was to let her decompress after all. We had plenty to talk about, as we\u2019ve had very different paths to walk to get to where we are, she and I, the farm girl from Arizona and the dancing girl from everywhere. But we could both commiserate about driving through the Midwest, and we\u2019re both touched, so there\u2019s common ground as well. I spoke some about the attack, and she, well come to think of it, she didn\u2019t tell me much about what happened to her, but she opened up a little. She did talk more about her old troupe, specifically someone that I vaguely reminded her of. Well, someone I share certain aspects with. The \u2018reminding\u2019 bit might be simple wishful thinking, as I\u2019m pretty sure this Cassidy was a lover of Alice\u2019s, even if she didn\u2019t come out and say so.<br /> <br /> Speaking of such things, she is remarkably tightlipped on such topics. Though, to be fair, I do understand my particular upbringing and even current surroundings are unusual, so perhaps she is merely as tightlipped as is normal, but at this point, I\u2019m not sure how to make my intentions more known other than by complimenting her shoes, and I get the feeling she wouldn\u2019t appreciate the crudeness. I was hoping to ask for a dance while we were clubbing, as my seduction skills go as follows, in order from descending effectiveness: (1) my eyes (2) my dancing (3) the rest of my face (100) my pick up lines, and my eyes are just not getting it done with this one. Sadly, I did have to ask for another rain check, as Tracey was in trouble.<br /> <br /> I mentioned before that Tracey had an interesting problem for us, but that we\u2019d backburnered it as it wasn\u2019t dangerous. That changed, a few nights ago. Unfortunately, we don\u2019t know a whole lot more than we did before. She\u2019s had disquieting dreams, dreams where she\u2019s been attacked, and the night before last, when she awoke, she had marks on her wrists and ankles, where she\u2019d been held, in the dream. The dream she\u2019d been attacked in was a recurring one, though the attack element was new. Another element of the dream had changed, a runner on the beach that had gotten closer than ever this past week, and was the only reason she was able to escape her attackers, when they showed up.<br /> <br /> Tracy pulled me aside right as we walked in, happy I chanced to come in, as she had lost my card sometime recently. Not because of carelessness either, according to her - she felt it had disappeared suspiciously. It\u2019s an odd thing, but I have no idea how it might be connected to the whole dream attack. Though if I find out the good Mr Timothy absconded with it (and hasn\u2019t called me yet), I shall be quite cross. I might even pout.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, I gathered up the krewe and Alice. Poor Alice - I was perhaps a little flippant describing the recurring dream bit, trying to recall a happier time for Tracey, and Alice was fairly certain we were putting her on. But we got that all cleared up and everyone up to speed and put together a plan. It meant a sleepover, of the non-sexy kind, unfortunately, where I attempted to go with Tracey into her recurring dream setting, like I somehow managed to do last time I spent the night with her. Natalie was along to keep watch so she could wake us up, should things go badly, and Alice and Doc were along to keep an eye out for outside forces that might be intruding.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday November 7th 2010<br /> <br /> -Okay first meeting went well. We will see where things go from here.<br /> <br /> -Giving the grand tour.<br /> <br /> -Sara may be crazy.<br /> <br /> -I mean, I love her anyway.<br /> <br /> -Yea that is enough tour for now, did not finish bottom floor.<br /> <br /> -So much to chat about.<br /> <br /> -Okay, gonna relax a bit before tonight.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up!<br /> <br /> -My what a lovely club I\u2019ve got<br /> <br /> -Lovely, lovely<br /> <br /> -Sara has SUCH a crush on Tatum.<br /> <br /> -I am a terrible person.<br /> <br /> -Ah look it is Murder Ballads, hello Murder Ballads<br /> <br /> -Ah Sara, you do make friends.<br /> <br /> -Hmmm Tatum is acting up. In a good way.<br /> <br /> -Poor thing gets so spacey when I show up.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear<br /> <br /> -Meeting Meeting<br /> <br /> -Friend Tracy has a problem<br /> <br /> -What do you mean the internet won\u2019t tell me everything? It\u2019s the Internet.<br /> <br /> -Sin-Eaters need a Wikipedia.<br /> <br /> -Quick change of plans.<br /> <br /> -Bah, will have to paddle Tatum later.<br /> <br /> -You hear that my dear? I will get you next time! ^_^<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVII</i><br /> <br /> So never a dull moment I suppose.<br /> <br /> Alice's player did not have time for a journal this time, but I believe plans one for next if possible.<br /> <br /> For those who enjoy my games, I have begun a Demon: The Descent game. First journals go up in a week, so far some introductions and a couple backgrounds. Night Train Detective Agency can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\">here</a>. Feel free to drop in and check it out. With Malibu Dream House it makes for a trio of New WoD games being covered. I just hate we did not really get that many journals for Beyond the Sea or Brand New Key, my old Changeling: the Lost and Geist games, respectively. Regardless, I am optimistic Night Train Detective Agency will be fun, so drop by if you have interest.<br /> <br /> Anyway, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T12:55:17-07:00","id":286862,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look into the Krewe. It seems our good friend Tracy\u2019s issues have come up again, and she needs some help\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Monday, November 8, 2010<br /> <br /> So apparently Murder Ballads has instituted a new rule. If Doc leads a deadly Japanese woman to the dance floor, chaos ensues. I\u2019m not sure if the bouncers know yet or not. Come to think of it, maybe the Universe has made some new rules given what Nightshade had to deal with. I\u2019m getting ahead again, but only a little.<br /> <br /> We made our first stop at the 27 Club, which was doing good business. We didn\u2019t stay long enough to see the performance, so I can\u2019t say how that went. Nightshade\u2019s manager, I\u2019ll call her Tantrum (both because I think it would thrill her to have a craft name and because of her admittedly curious actions tonight) was introduced to Axe. I\u2019ve met Tantrum several times now, but something was different tonight. At first I just thought she was checking Axe out, which is fair. But that wasn\u2019t really it. She wasn\u2019t looking interested when Nightshade absently offered to bring Tantrum with us to Murder Ballads, given she was working. After we left, Nightshade got some texts that didn\u2019t do her any good mood-wise.<br /> <br /> Walking into Murder Ballads like we owned the place about 2000 Hours, Axe got a firsthand view of how most of us are when relaxed. As I led my girlfriend to the dance floor, Tracy appeared out of the crowd and pulled Bright Eyes aside. This wasn\u2019t new but she looked scared. We danced until Bright Eyes motioned for me to head to the private rooms. Tracy had a major problem and it wasn\u2019t her explosive crush on Bright Eyes. Axe giggled at first when we started talking about the Magic Dream Island, but the looks she got cut the humor short. Tracy had been attacked before she could even realize she was in trouble while at the White Beach. There were marks on her arm in the shape of grasping hands which looked like exposure. This time the Runner had converged on her position and saved her by screaming the howl of terrifying winds. There were so many questions that Tracy didn\u2019t know the answer to, but we did learn that recently the Runner had been getting closer and closer while she was on the Magic Dream Island. Also this happened two nights ago and Tracy hadn\u2019t slept since then. Not good, but Tracy\u2019s young enough that that particular problem can be fixed by sleeping in once.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes assured Tracy we\u2019d help her but we needed to go home and gear up first. Nightshade was still distracted by her texts, but she agreed we could keep track of what was happening and try to learn more once we got to Tracy and Timothy\u2019s. When I got back, I got my ritual gear. I knew I could do very little with the dream itself, but I could look for any sympathetic connections made during the sleep and try to track that backwards. It wasn\u2019t much, but it was all I had. Before we left, Nightshade let us know that Tantrum was going crazy but that didn\u2019t give us much details.<br /> <br /> We all loaded up the van with our various occult equipment and headed out. I actually got to meet Timothy as I cast my ceremonial circle. He stood by protectively as I painted sigils on his sister. We talked in general terms to see if it might be helpful if I went to Timothy\u2019s room and entered his dreams. The Krewe agreed I was needed out here but Timothy got so dreamy eyed and then embarrassed that even Nightshade laughed. Bright Eyes is right about one thing, he is really adorable. Unspoken compliments aside, we got down to business. Nightshade used her powers to both put Bright Eyes to sleep and to monitor both her and Tracy\u2019s auras for signs of trouble. Tracy was so tired that just laying next to Bright Eyes was enough for her. They had been asleep for less than two breaths when Nightshade pulled them back almost in a panic. Apparently when Tracy takes someone to her Magic Dream Island, they aura becomes subsumed into hers. Once we heard that, I understood entirely why Nightshade was nearly panicking. Everything was okay though, so we tried it again.<br /> <br /> I concentrated on all the various connections in the room that made this part of Tracy, so that anything outside that would stand out. Her feelings for Bright Eyes meant that didn\u2019t really get in the way either. While nothing outwardly changed, a few minutes in I noticed that something both familiar and very different seemed to connect to Tracy. It wasn\u2019t here but seemed to connect directly to her dreams. I was still trying to trace where it was coming from so I could use the sympathetic link against it, when they woke up again. Tracy looked terrified and Bright Eyes looked surprised. The Runner had arrived and Bright Eyes engaged him with her powers. She learned that the Runner was actually tied to the twins as it was their great great great great great grandfather. However, when she looked into the ghost with her Manifestation, the Runner stopped. Actually he walked to them, which nearly woke Tracy up on her own until Bright Eyes smoothed things over. According to the Runner, Tracy and Timothy were still awaiting their powers. The Magic Dream Island was but a relic of the realm he almost completed before he was \u201ccast down.\u201d The Runner claimed that the family had been cursed by his enemies, though we could break those chains with \u201cthe church we\u2019d taken.\u201d Bright Eyes was about to pump him for information when he turned back to the ocean as if he could sense something, then ordered them to leave. Tracy woke up immediately which ripped Bright Eyes out as well.<br /> <br /> Tracy had no idea what was going on, but Timothy knew more about the family history. Apparently they had an ancestor that was a preacher. A following gathered and helped as he built a \u201cladder to Heaven.\u201d Then one day, the preacher and all his people just disappeared. Timothy, who was apparently the brains of the Psychic Wonder Twins, said that there was a book that told the whole story that he\u2019d get for us. But then he also offered up some very important (for me) information. He said that they might be the only ones in the family with their powers because they were born on the autumnal equinox. I know that means September, but given the implications, might try to get their exact time and date of birth later so I can get a star chart worked up. Astrology isn\u2019t my strongest suit, but I think it will play directly into this situation. Anyway, they were also the seventh generation of their family. Twins, born on the autumnal equinox, into the seventh generation of a family with a legacy of power. Yeah there\u2019s something up here.<br /> <br /> While I was getting my ritual tools together, Tracy went to sleep. Timothy seemed very confused about Bright Eyes\u2019 card being missing when it came up. Axe used her Oracle to become a bloodhound. She sniffed out both the twins, their parents, and us, but then there were signs of a woman without a scent. She was sure she could detect the women she couldn\u2019t smell if she didn\u2019t smell her again...I don\u2019t know. I\u2019m sure if you have Oracle that makes sense.<br /> <br /> The Firehouse Church was everyone\u2019s first thought about the church we\u2019d taken. I considered the Underworld chapel back in Glenwood, but that seemed odd given we had negotiated to free that one. We hit up our property first as it was a) ours and b) close. On the way, Nightshade and Bright Eyes elaborated on the issues with Tantrum. I\u2019m having to guess about part of the details, but I think she suddenly felt threatened by Axe. But not for her safety, for pecking order into whatever supernatural cabal Nightshade obviously was building. I don\u2019t think, no, I know Tantrum doesn\u2019t actually know what Nightshade or any of us are. I figure she suspects at least Nightshade of being a vampire, which works for Nightshade fairly well. Somehow, Tantrum seems to think that Axe has leapfrogged ahead of her in line to receive her powers. That would be cute if it wasn\u2019t so earthshaking to Nightshade\u2019s calm. Axe was of course completely clueless as to what was happening.<br /> <br /> Ephram was there and though he didn\u2019t know anything about that church in relation to our problem, but he did remember the preacher we were talking about. That alone was terrifying. The preacher was what our spectral friend called a Charismatic. We don\u2019t refer to them that way much anymore, but at the time they were those that believed strongly in the signs of the Lord in all things, or emphasized the gifts of the Spirit. Or I completely misread the situation and the preacher was just a good con man. Either way, this man had the voice of an angel they said. He built his ladder in Glenwood of course. So now the plan is to go back to Glenwood, birthpalce of all evil in Connecticut later today. Seriously if Mariah Winthrop came from Glenwood, I would not be the least bit surprised. Thankfully we aren\u2019t going tonight.<br /> <br /> More drama was explained on the way back to the Bluffs. Tantrum was also rejecting the concept that Nightshade had to cut off conversations tonight due to \u201cwork.\u201d Even given that Bright Eyes sent a separate text to reassure her. I hope no one took this as a joke when I suggested that it sounded like Bright Eyes or Nightshade was cursed. We go back to continued our discussion of Glenwood. That just added more problems as Karen then flipped out and forbid Nightshade to return that pit of evil and other words that I had to stop hearing. I knew that Karen was very upset the last time we went to Glenwood, but this triggered a full on fear attack. Fear that Nightshade would never return.<br /> <br /> At some point, the crying and wailing stopped. Nightshade left so I don\u2019t imagine things have gotten any better. I\u2019m not going out tonight. I need to figure out what kind of a curse can do this, and how I can reverse it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> The Middle Shadows must stay pretty busy. I\u2019ve only just met them, and they\u2019ve already pulled me along on one of their cases. Something involving a girl named Tracey and her brother. The siblings have some sort of dream realm that\u2019s being invaded by ghosts. Whatever it is, it\u2019s not like anything I\u2019ve ever encountered before.<br /> <br /> Natalie, Doc and Sara are busy talking with Tracey and her brother, Timothy. I don\u2019t really feel like it\u2019s my place to butt in, so I stand back and examine their small house. There\u2019s not much to it, and it\u2019s a bit cluttered, but it looks cozy and comfortable. Tracey\u2019s bedroom looks like a college girl\u2019s bedroom. It\u2019s not very spacious, though, especially with all seven of us milling around in here.<br /> <br /> I end up standing next to Alexia. She doesn\u2019t seem to have much to add to the conversation with Tracey either. I think she\u2019s warming up to me, and she cooks a darn good lemon meringue pie. That\u2019s my favorite dessert.<br /> <br /> I hesitate for a few minutes, but finally gather my resolve.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmmm\u2026can I ask you a question? About Sara?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure,\u201d Alexia answers cheerfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026I know she\u2019s in a\u2026thing\u2026a triad with Natalie and that other girl back at the mansion. But I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s been flirting with me constantly since we met, and, uh, I don\u2019t really know how to react.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d Alexia responds, \u201cIt\u2019s kinda weird. They\u2019re all basically married, but they\u2019re all cool with each other hooking up casually with other people. As long as it\u2019s not serious. They sleep with other people all the time.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReally? That seems complicated\u2026and potentially messy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I agree. It\u2019s pretty odd,\u201d Alexia nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t get me wrong. Sara\u2019s very pretty. She\u2019s really sweet, and I\u2019m flattered by her attention, but I\u2019m not really comfortable with the idea of sharing my lover like that. It\u2019s just\u2026weird to me. I guess I\u2019m not really into casual sex.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know what you mean,\u201d Alexia agrees. \u201cI have Chandra, and we\u2019re happy together. That\u2019s enough for me.\u201d She pauses for a few moments. \u201cThough Chandra is pretty adventurous. I think Natalie has been a bad influence on her. She wants to sleep with other people sometimes, but only if I\u2019m a part of it. We have a good friend we invited to bed with us once, and it was pretty fun.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t exactly know how to respond to that, so I just clam up. I still don\u2019t know how to react to Sara either. I guess I\u2019ll have to tell her that I\u2019m not the kind of girl who is comfortable sharing lovers like she does. It\u2019s really too bad because otherwise I think we might hit it off.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Tracey and Sara went to sleep together to enter Tracey\u2019s dream realm, and they learned a lot about a ghost there who screams like a hurricane. He is one of Tracey and Timothy\u2019s ancestors, some sort of preacher. The Middle Shadows are going to follow up on his history. They seem to know of a couple of old churches to investigate.<br /> <br /> Then Tracey mentioned something about Sara\u2019s card going missing. Sara gave her a business card before so that she could contact the Middle Shadows if she needed them, but the card is gone. They searched for it, but it\u2019s nowhere to be found. Timothy is positive they didn\u2019t throw it out. Something seems suspicious.<br /> <br /> I ask how many other people have been to the house since Tracey got the card. They tell me it\u2019s just been the two of them and of course the Middle Shadows. Their parents stopped by recently, but that\u2019s it. I\u2019ve gotten the impression that the krewe is trying to hide the true nature of their abilities from the siblings, so I look to Doc to make sure it\u2019s okay to use my powers to investigate. He gives me the nod.<br /> <br /> I become the skinwalker. I don\u2019t change much, just enough to heighten my senses. My eyes become cat-like, my teeth lengthen a bit, that sort of thing. It\u2019s still enough to spook Tracey and Timothy, though. More importantly, it\u2019s enough to let me catch the scents layered throughout the room.<br /> <br /> It takes me minutes or two. I kneel periodically and focus on one scent and then another until I\u2019m sure. Someone else has been here. Someone who isn\u2019t Tracey, Timothy, or their parents. Whoever it was probably stole Sara\u2019s card to keep Tracey from contacting us.<br /> <br /> <i>We have the scent. The hunt begins.</i><br /> <br /> The Grasping Huntress purrs the words into my mind with a great deal of pleasure. She sees an opportunity here. I do have the scent. If I encounter it again, I\u2019ll know it. And whoever stole the card is probably responsible for the attacks on Tracey\u2019s dream realm. They might be worthy prey.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> We are all in Doc\u2019s van, driving toward an abandoned church that might be connected to Tracey\u2019s ancestor. The others are discussing the church. It\u2019s a place they\u2019ve been before. I gather that they own the property, and that some vampire hunters were squatting there recently.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m distracted. The Huntress keeps talking to me, encouraging me to follow up on the scent we discovered. Sara gave Tracey some more cards. It\u2019s possible whoever stole the first one will come back.<br /> <br /> <i>We should be watching the house.</i><br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but agree. It would make sense for some of us to stake out Tracey\u2019s house. We could also go back to the club, and maybe try a few other places Tracey spends a lot of time. Whoever stole the card might be a regular at one of those places. I might be able to catch the scent again.<br /> <br /> <i>Our prey is trying to hurt Tracey. Our prey is dangerous. Our prey must die.</i><br /> <br /> I find myself agreeing with the Huntress. Now that I have the prey\u2019s scent, I don\u2019t want to let it go.<br /> <br /> Then Sara puts a hand on my arm. \u201cAre you okay?\u201d she asks. \u201cYou seem tense.\u201d<br /> <br /> I suddenly become aware of the dark path my thoughts are following. I tell Sara that the Huntress is pushing me again. I\u2019m focused on whoever stole the card from Tracey. Now that I have the scent, I feel compelled to track it down. It\u2019s always hardest in situations like this, because to some extent, the Huntress is right. We do need to follow up on the person that stole the card. But she wants me to take it too far, and I can\u2019t risk getting caught up in that again.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, Sara seems to understand. We briefly discuss splitting up so that some of us can keep watch on Tracey\u2019s house, but we decide against it. Until we know what we\u2019re facing at the church, we should probably stick together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> The plan, overall, went well. After stopping by the house to get geared up, we all piled into the van. Tracey was back by the time we got there, of course, good naturedly sniping at Timothy. He was giving as good as he got, but was clearly concerned for his sleep-deprived sister and eager to help. He was even willing to fall asleep with Doc (the horror!). His shy smile when Doc suggested that had Natalie giggling, which had Timothy blushing, cranking the adorable level in the room to 11.<br /> <br /> However, we decided against that plan, if nothing else because it would be difficult to watch two groups of sleepers. Instead Doc prepared the room and then Tracey and I headed off to her magic dream house. Natalie immediately woke us up. I was bad, I confess - my first assumption was that she\u2019d had a problem with the way my aura looked as I teased Tracey about the fact that I always show up naked in her dreams. I guess the thing with Sarah is sticking with me way more than it should - Natalie had actual good reasons for her reaction then, it wasn\u2019t just about control. And she had good reasons this time too. She was watching our auras, keeping an eye out for mortal terror that would indicate we needed waking up. When we fell asleep, and I entered her dream, my aura got subsumed by hers, as if I became just a small part of Tracey\u2019s mind. Understandably disconcerting.<br /> <br /> She was prepared for it the second time, and as Tracey was rummaging around for some clothes for me, we heard a disturbing howl, like the wind of a bad storm. The running man Tracey had described was close again. We headed outside, clothes be damned, to see if I could get a look at him. He was a ghost, and a powerful one, my Sight showed me. I called to him and he slowed and came back around. He was an ancestor of the twins, their 5 times great grandfather and was there to make sure they came into their powers, his legacy. He believed me when I said I was there to help the twins and explained that they had been cursed by an enemy of his and that this island was a piece of a realm he had almost created before being cast down. We could break the chains, he said, if we went to the church we had taken. He may have gotten a little oracular there for a bit.<br /> <br /> He had begun to ask more about me when he turned towards the ocean, ordering us to leave. Tracey quickly obeyed, and I got pulled out as well, shortly thereafter. Alice\u2019s hands moved quickly to her axe as we shot up, but relaxed when we assured her we were ok.<br /> <br /> After that, we had a little bit of a powwow. Tracey thought she recognized the ghost\u2019s voice, but couldn\u2019t place it. Timothy had an idea who it might be - a preacher who built a \u201cladder to heaven\u201d who, along with a collection of his followers, disappeared mysteriously one day. He knew of a history book with the whole story and is getting it for us to look through. Timothy also put forth that they might be the heirs as opposed to anyone else in the seven generations of family tree between them because they were born on the autumnal equinox. Though, having laid it out like that, it might be because of them being of the seventh generation. If the autumnal equinox is important though, that might give us a little bit of insight into what kind of thing we\u2019re dealing with here. I did obviously let them know they were heirs to some kind of power, probably related to their dream island. The idea went straight to Tracey\u2019s head, while Timothy immediately warned her to be careful. They\u2019ll make good foils for each other, I think, when they do come into their power.<br /> <br /> With all that done, however, Tracey needed sleep, and more than fifteen minutes of it. Neither of them liked running away from their island, as it was supposed to be their safe haven, but she really did need that sleep and for now at least, it wasn\u2019t so safe. Hopefully she got to another dream quickly enough.<br /> <br /> Before we left, we warned Timothy about the missing card. He double-checked, but it was in fact missing, and he was pretty sure she wouldn\u2019t have tossed it. He was doing his best to look all menacing at the thought of someone taking her stuff, which is difficult when you are that adorable. Alice did some looking around, and did find traces of someone not us who had been there recently, a woman, from what she could See. She\u2019d recognize the traces again, if she was using her Sight, so for now we\u2019re just keeping our eyes peeled.<br /> <br /> Our biggest lead is the \u2018church we\u2019d taken\u2019. There were actually two that fit the bill, and we decided to check up on the in-town, not-super-scary one first. It, naturally, was not the right one, though the conversations on the way there and back did give me a couple more opportunities to flirt with Alice. She is also super adorable when she blushes. Plus, the troupe\u2019s ghostly friend at the church knew a few more details about the ladder to heaven guy. He was a traveling Charismatic, it seems, with a voice like an angel\u2019s (or Satan\u2019s, depending) who could talk anyone into anything. Dangerous powers for the twins. The sweet talking man built his ladder in Glenwood (the scary town with the other church in it) so that\u2019s the plan for later today.<br /> <br /> In less work related news, poor Natalie had to deal with something of a meltdown from Tatum. She didn\u2019t appreciate having their flirty conversation cut short by work - well, really, it was that she didn't believe it had been cut short by work, no matter how many times I back Natalie up on it. See, she know Natalie is \u2018special\u2019 (she thinks she\u2019s a vampire, or something crazy like that - to be fair, Natalie does cultivate something of an image) and she thinks I \u2018cut in line\u2019 to be made something special as well. With Alice showing up, and getting a job and going clubbing with us right off the bat, Tatum got worried about getting passed over again. Natalie let her know that I was already touched, before I showed up, and that it wasn\u2019t something Natalie could give out as a prize. It was a difficult conversation, from the sound of it.<br /> <br /> The fact that we have to go to Glenwood and that Karen was upset by this didn\u2019t help matters. I convinced her we\u2019d be careful, so that wasn\u2019t a crisis or anything, just a thing, I guess. But I think we\u2019re all ready to head out, so let\u2019s go get this visit over with.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -Um, Tatum, what\u2019s wrong honey?<br /> <br /> -Er, um<br /> <br /> -Okay. The fuck?<br /> <br /> -My Mistress is being weird.<br /> <br /> -Okay at chez Tracy<br /> <br /> -I do know her brother! Well, I have seen him.<br /> <br /> -Seems nice enough.<br /> <br /> -Sara is all girl crazy.<br /> <br /> -Ok, radio silence, busy stuff.<br /> <br /> -Back around.<br /> <br /> -Sweetheart, seriously, what has gotten into you?<br /> <br /> -Okay, have plan for helping Tracy; Sara\u2019s heart is not broken, huzzah.<br /> <br /> -Time to go to church.<br /> <br /> -I have fond memories of this church.<br /> <br /> -Hey it\u2019s my ghost buddy! Or something.<br /> <br /> -Oh Goddess. Seriously?<br /> <br /> -I never wanted to go back there. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -@Narek I\u2019ll tell you in person.<br /> <br /> -Okay, gonna try to deal with Tatum.<br /> <br /> -Okay this is going poorly. Going offline.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, November 8th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t remember Tatum being this crazy.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jogg.<br /> <br /> -Bah must we go today? I need a mental health day.<br /> <br /> -Glenwood is not good for mental health.<br /> <br /> -My wife is telling me what I want to hear, and commanding me in a great tone, but I suspect I will still have to go. My Krewe will overrule me.<br /> <br /> -Bah Sara treachery?<br /> <br /> -More Cognac. Need more Cognac.<br /> <br /> -Lots more Cognac.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Tracy and Timothy seem to be popular NPCs.<br /> <br /> The ghost at the Firehouse Church was Ephraim Yarborough, who they had dealt with when they first visited it.<br /> <br /> Having been pleased with how Aspirations were working in Night Train Detective Agency, I decided to add them to Balance of Shadows and Malibu Dream House. Given those games do not use Beats, I am rewarding a Willpower point for completing an Aspiration. Less useful in Geist, with it\u2019s Vanitases, but will be more use in Malibu Dream House and not all the Middle Shadows have a Vantias. Only a couple were added in 118, but people are figuring some out. I like the tangible role-playing reward for going out and doing something, very useful in a Sandbox game. A Plasm reward did not really make meta, or internal, sense to me. I may allow fulfilling a long-term Aspiration to restore a spent Willpower Dot, but undecided at this time.<br /> <br /> Not much else to cover, but if you have comments or questions I will be happy to answer them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\