"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T16:53:19-07:00","id":286996,"title":"","content":"I don't know if this has been asked but have considered bringing in a changeling for the dream exploration?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T21:12:17-07:00","id":287231,"title":"","content":"It's come up, but they have not elected to try it. IC they do not know just how powerful Changelings are in dreams.<br /> <br /> Session went well tonight, well, except the 18 angry werewolves. But you know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-19T23:10:56-07:00","id":287282,"title":"","content":"Throw them some rawhides and some kibble. It'll be fine. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-02T02:39:07-08:00","id":299879,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check on the Krewe, and their harrowing trip to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1200 Hours, Monday, November 8, 2010<br /> <br /> Today started out well. I got up around 0800 Hours and was able to find my center while meditating in only a half hour. And that\u2019s about where the day stopped going well.<br /> <br /> At breakfast, we decided that we\u2019d need to do some research as we knew next to nothing about Tracy and Timothy\u2019s family. Bright Eyes did fill in the family name of Lowe, though that could have easily changed through seven generations. St. Mary\u2019s sounds like our best bet just because they will likely have some records dating back far enough to help us. Unfortunately that means that we\u2019re all about to go back to Glenwood. Karen is fuming and no one else is thrilled with the idea either. But now I need to go and help load the van.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1605 Hours, Monday, November 8, 2010<br /> <br /> I hate Glenwood. I hate Glenwood. I fucking <b><i>HATE</i></b> Glenwood!<br /> <br /> I need to call Rawl. I need to fix my van. I need to fucking bomb Glenwood off the face of the goddamn map.<br /> <br /> This isn\u2019t helping.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1635 Hours, Monday, November 8, 2010<br /> <br /> I need to replace the hanging bag.<br /> <br /> Things did not go anything resembling well in Glenwood. But not how we expected.<br /> <br /> Axe was very confused as to why we were all so gloomy about going to this Glenwood place. The first part of trip was then explaining our history to the town. Then she told us more about what she can do as a Sin-Eater. We got to St. Mary\u2019s around 1300 Hours and were met by a nice lady who made sure we had everything we needed in the records room. I\u2019m not sure if she sold us out or if Glenwood just has an entity like Dark Haven Bluffs that can feel our presence and hates us. I\u2019m getting ahead of myself and my blood pressure is spiking again. Let\u2019s try this more logically.<br /> <br /> In the first hour, everyone helped me research and I was able to piece together the family history and draw a line directly from Tracy and Timothy back to Israel Smith. Israel was around Glenwood in the 1880s and by most descriptions was a charismatic man more and a Charismatic Preacher less. He was involved in what he called building a Ladder to Heaven. Israel seemed to want to live up to his namesake, at least one definition of it. Wrestles with God. Israel saw a dark and dangerous void between Heaven and Earth. Some accounts use nautical descriptions as though he thought this void were a dark ocean. Thus he set out to build a shining island or some form of vessel to cross the \u201cabyss.\u201d Based on what the twins have in their dreams, he accomplished at least the island. The various articles gave me the impression that Israel was somehow siphoning off the life force of his assembled followers to generate the spiritual power he needed. The people that went to help were reported to slowly waste away by uninvolved family and friends. My first thoughts were that Israel was yet another crazy mage or possibly an incredibly powerful Sin-Eater, but I can\u2019t figure out how he managed to do it. There was a plot twist we didn\u2019t see coming however. Israel had an enemy just as charismatic as he was, only prettier. Star Jameson had her own following, not a small feat for the 1880s. She was described as having exceptionally long, luxurious dark (or black) hair. There were rumors that she was a witch and that she once strangled a man using her magic animated hair. Many accounts alluded to Star\u2019s beauty directly or otherwise. We all sort of paused at that point as those descriptions nearly painted a picture of The Hair and her family\u2019s specific brand of special. We don\u2019t know where The Hair\u2019s family comes from, but it doesn\u2019t sound good. We also talked about how The Hair may have been the mysterious woman that Axe can\u2019t identify. This was just random discussion but the more we talked the more distant Axe became. Finally she just stood up and said she needed to get some fresh air. Bright Eyes immediately volunteered to keep her company, and given where we were, I couldn\u2019t even make a joke.<br /> <br /> The rest of us continued our research and pulling various bits of information together. Israel and Star came into conflict, likely by poaching followers from one another. This led to accusations of witchcraft from both sides ...because when you find yourself in the Atlantic Northeast, that\u2019s how you win. Things escalated as conflicts between cults often do before there was finally a face off. Star led her followers to Israel\u2019s HQ. There was the requisite Sharks and Jets issues, but by the end a huge \u201cconflagration\u201d erupted and burned down the church. There was never any signs of the people involved and by the next day, even the ashes were reported to be very cold. Building fires don\u2019t generally cool off for days, so this was very odd. There were some random sightings of both Israel and Star afterwards, in England and Florida respectively, but nothing definite.<br /> <br /> That was all we could dig up at first, but I figured that was more than enough. I did want to find out where the old church was. We did our group huddle for pulling multiple sources and I sorted it all out. When I got it all together and referenced a map, it felt like I was suddenly very empty inside. I laughed, the sound dull even to my ears, before I dropped my pencil and announced, \u201cFuck.\u201d<br /> <br /> It was the Outsider Mage Lodge we had burnt down several weeks ago.<br /> <br /> The one that took you to another place when you walked through the front door, but not if you Boneyarded in through the windows. The place that felt thick and otherworldly, with strange sound distortions like it was underwater. The place an Outsider seemed quite happy to use for a lair.<br /> <br /> I had just explained all that to Cupcake and Nightshade when the latter received a text from Bright Eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cWerewolves outside the cemetery.\u201d<br /> <br /> We were done researching right then. Normally I would put all my research back where I found it. That\u2019s polite and it\u2019s expected. But today, we grabbed our notes and ran. Cupcake and Nightshade took my keys and headed for the van while I went around the side to attempt to talk down any violence that might be avoided. This was an incredibly stupid idea.<br /> <br /> <i>You do a disservice by placing blame upon yourself where none is deserved, Ghazi. Do not fault yourself for following peace before war. For when peace fails, you do not falter in your pursuit of war.</i><br /> <br /> I can\u2019t argue that and I do plan to revisit this little incident. But I\u2019m getting ahead again. Five guys that looked like they lived under a bridge were in what I guess was near human form. They were really agitated and pacing like tigers in a cage around the exits of the cemetery. By my best guess, they had some spirit ban against entering and this made them even more pissed to have to be here. There was something else about them too, something not right. I knew that Rawl was a Predator King also, but something he said hit home when I saw these guys. He said that the Predator Kings from around Glenwood were crazy, even by Predator King standards. The Pure, I had been informed by Malard, were all insane to start with, so no part of this would end well.<br /> <br /> I started talking to the men, trying to get and keep their attention in as non-threatening a manner as possible. Unfortunately, Axe and Bright Eyes were prepared to defend themselves and were unlocking Manifestations while in the graveyard. When Bright Eyes used her fiery speed to blur past on her way to the van, that was the final straw. Two immediately shifted into their war form. I tried to keep them focused on me, but then Axe grew into her cat-like war form and all bets were off. When she ran for the van, the other three shifted and one gave chase. Then something surged over me from the parking lot. It felt like fear. I was very hopeful this was Nightshade trying to convince our attackers to go away. I kept trying to be a distraction, but they all ignored me and ran for my van. It was about then I heard another vehicle and Cupcake screaming that we were blocked in. Her orders for everyone to get in the van convinced me to give up trying to talk down the Predator Kings and get the fuck out. I put up my own Primeval Shroud and moved for my van.<br /> <br /> Pouring Plasm into my Shroud, I boosted my speed and blurred past as well. Unfortunately by the time I got there, we were facing a total of eighteen fucking werewolves, some of which Axe had chopped into Death Frenzy and other just in regular frenzy. On my way to the van, I was ripped open twice but bulwarked it as my plasm continued to steam from my wounds. Cupcake had to use her powers to drive the van since one asshole or another had forced the engine to die with one of their powers. Multiple werewolves attacked the vehicle as we drove away at top speed. I\u2019m pretty sure we drove over at least one of them as we had to swing around their damn pickup. I looked around as huge claws rent wide gashes through the sides and roof of my van. While her Boneyard was still up, Nightshade warned Cupcake about a strange white man with pure white eyes wearing all white walking slowly down the street in our direction. Bright Eyes had Axe in a deep kiss and Nightshade rubbed my shoulders as Cupcake drove us to safety. The white man was neither alive nor dead and didn\u2019t stop us or try to follow. He just continued to walk slowly toward the werewolves. We were not prepared to deal with that, so I\u2019ll have to file that one under WTF.<br /> <br /> Now that we\u2019re back and everyone is okay, I\u2019ve had time to look over the van. After months of work and learning how to build this wonderful vehicle, it is damn near ruined after four days of having my license. If I had to guess, I\u2019d say it\u2019s about 60% fucked.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m packing silver the next time we go to Glenwood. I should call Jerome.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> The others are still inside the church, researching the past and discussing the future. All except Sara. She decided to accompany me outside for a walk in the cemetery. It\u2019s nice to have her company. The weather is clear, if a bit too chilly for my tastes. I don\u2019t really care for cold weather, which I guess comes from growing up in Arizona. Still, it\u2019s a nice day. I don\u2019t really see what\u2019s so bad about this Glenwood place. Maybe the Middle Shadows really did fix it before.<br /> <br /> I explain to Sara why I had to step outside and get some fresh air. The krewe was making plans based on their research, but a lot of the planning was wrapped around conjecture and educated guesses. It felt awfully familiar, and then I realized that sort of reasoning was exactly the kind of process that led me down the wrong path in the first place. The Middle Shadows are more cautious. I guess it works for them, but I still felt like the banshee they were talking about needed to be put down since she\u2019s likely the one who stole Sara\u2019s card. I can\u2019t afford to think that way or make those judgments based on so little information. So I had to get out.<br /> <br /> Then I notice the men prowling around outside the cemetery. No, prowling isn\u2019t the right word. Stalking. Like caged beasts spoiling for a fight. Sara notices them too and we both stop. My instincts tell me that the men will attack as soon as we leave the cemetery.<br /> <br /> <i>We will NOT be prey. Not again.</i><br /> <br /> I hear an unfamiliar edge in the Huntress\u2019 voice and some of her memories flicker through my mind. Memories of the night she was surrounded by five Apache men who raped her, beat her and left her for dead. I remember Sara telling me about her own death. It wasn\u2019t that different. We are not going to let that happen again. Not to us, and not to Sara.<br /> <br /> I move protectively in front of Sara and lock eyes with one of the men, challenging him with my gaze. He and his companions grow more agitated and start to change. Werewolves. I thought the Middle Shadows were on good terms with the local werewolves. What\u2019s going on here?<br /> <br /> I unlock my Primeval Shroud. I\u2019d rather cloak myself in Grave Dirt, but I don\u2019t have my axe, so I need the claws. The day grows brighter behind me as Sara blazes with Pyre Flame.<br /> <br /> \u201cI texted the others. We need to get to the van, fast!\u201d Sara implores.<br /> <br /> \u201cGo,\u201d I reply.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re running too, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot until you\u2019re safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nods and bolts. She moves like flickering flame, so fast the werewolves can\u2019t move quickly enough to stop her. I\u2019m right behind her, guarding her back, and as I spring over the cemetery gate and across the parking lot, I shift fully into my Primeval Caul. The werewolves can\u2019t help but notice; I\u2019m not too different from them now, or maybe more like Noriko, a woman with a mountain lion\u2019s features. They also unleash their inner beasts, shifting into hulking wolf forms as they charge after us. It occurs to me that I\u2019ve never actually fought werewolves before. The Dead Judges were on good terms with the werewolves in Portland and the surrounding territory, or at least we stayed out of each others\u2019 way. Strangely, though, I\u2019m not afraid. I have to protect Sara and the other Middle Shadows.<br /> <br /> Alexia and Natalie bolt toward the van and reach it at almost the same time Sara and I do. Doc walks boldly toward the werewolves, hands outstretched in a peaceful gesture. He wants to talk them down, but my instincts and the charging bundles of fangs, fur and fury tell me it\u2019s too late for that.<br /> <br /> Sara calls out to me and then tosses me my axe. I feel a sense of calm determination come over me as I grip its familiar wooden handle.<br /> <br /> <i>Kill them.</i><br /> <br /> I stand my ground just outside the van. If the werewolves want to get to Sara or the others, they\u2019ll have to go through me. And that\u2019s exactly what they try to do. The next moments are a blur. I hack one of them into a bloody mess. He should be dead, but he just keeps coming! I fend off a second one, leaving him with a deep wound that would kill most normal people, but he\u2019s still standing too. Their claws rend my flesh but I let my plasm fill the wounds. I\u2019m splattered with blood, but I\u2019m used to that.<br /> <br /> More and more werewolves are coming. I don\u2019t know how many there are, but there\u2019s no way I can fight them all off. Where the heck is Doc?! We have to get out of here!<br /> <br /> Then, thankfully, Doc races past me, dodging around the frenzying werewolves. Natalie pulls him into the van. I start to back into the van too, but then Sara\u2019s arms are around me and she pulls me in. As Doc slams the doors shut and Alexia speeds out of the parking lot, Sara pulls me onto her lap, wraps her arms around my neck, and kisses me, deeply. I close my eyes and succumb to the warmth of the kiss.<br /> <br /> Then the moment is over.<br /> <br /> \u201cWh\u2026what was that?\u201d I ask, confused.<br /> <br /> Sara is embarrassed. Her blush is adorable. \u201cUmmm\u2026you saved me. Thanks.\u201d<br /> <br /> I can\u2019t help but smile.<br /> <br /> Then I notice the tall man walking down the street toward us, or rather, toward the werewolves. He is clad in a white suit and his eyes are blank, milky orbs. I can tell from the gasps and exclamations around me that the Middle Shadows have noticed him too, and they can see that this man is neither living nor dead. Even the Huntress is at a loss to explain him. Alexia swerves around him and keeps going. And then it\u2019s all behind us: the strange man, the werewolves, and Glenwood. We\u2019re on our way back to the mansion.<br /> <br /> The drive is awkward. Sara is still embarrassed, and I still don\u2019t know how to react. Doc is fuming over his damaged van, and Natalie is trying to comfort him. But everyone is okay. That\u2019s what matters, for now.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, I may have just put my foot in it, though really I shouldn\u2019t be worried about my poor wounded pride, considering the actual wounds Alice and Doc came away with. We\u2019re all fine, mostly bruises and scratches, but Glenwood has not risen in anyone\u2019s estimation on this trip.<br /> <br /> It started out well enough. The roughly hour long ride gave us some time to get Alice up to speed, and to get a more solid idea of her gifts, She has a strong connection to nature and stillness. She\u2019s more earth oriented then fire, despite her hair, but we do share an affiliation with air. We also share a talent for curses, and she has powerful Sight, as I mentioned last time.<br /> <br /> We knew exactly where we were heading, so there was no sightseeing - we all wanted to get in and out, quickly. The church, St. Mary\u2019s was open, so that was good. Natalie and Doc spoke fluent Catholic, which was good since I speak Catholic like a dog speaks English - I can repeat specific phrases, and I do it to get people off... wait, that metaphor went nowhere good. Anyways, they got us permission to go through their historical records, so we all sat down and got to it.<br /> <br /> Poor Alice was crazy out of her element, but she stuck to it like a trooper until we found some solid information. It wasn\u2019t great: Israel Smith, the travelling Charismatic of note, had in fact been trying to build a ladder to heaven, though it might have been better termed a boat. He had a vision of a dark and dangerous sea, separating Earth from Heaven, and was inspired to create something - a realm, a boat, a magic dream island - that could traverse this sea safely. To do so, as best we could tell from the ~120 year old records, he pilfered psychic energy from his followers, leaving them wan and listless.<br /> <br /> A woman in town, Star Jameson, did not care for this. She was almost assuredly the enemy we were looking for - each had accused the other of witchcraft and when the negative effects of his construction made themselves obvious to the community at large, she and her followers confronted he and his. The building was consumed in a fire and no trace of the forty or so people there was ever found. To add to the mystery, the next morning, the ashes were cold, not just as if it had happened days before, but colder. There were reported sightings of the two instigators, Star in Florida and Israel in England, but nothing definite.<br /> <br /> It was Star\u2019s description that resonated the most with us. A number of the chroniclers waxed rhapsodic about her about her beauty describing it as otherworldly, and going into great detail about her long, thick, dark hair. It was strongly reminiscent of our local bean sidhe, Sarah. The thought of her being somehow behind the twins\u2019 troubles was unsettling, but it did (selfishly) make me feel a bit better about the card going missing. She was a little... fixated on me for a bit after the whole comb thing, so maybe it was nothing more than a romantic rival thing, and not me being targeted as someone who could help. Though that does bring up the question of why she was there in the first place.<br /> <br /> The other bit of troubling news was how closely this tied into our other Glenwood adventure. The site where the building that had been burned down around Israel and Star had more recently been home to a lodge of demon summoners, until we burned that down around their heads.<br /> <br /> Doc, Natalie and Alexia filled us in on that later, as at that time Alice and I were enjoying a lovely afternoon stroll in the graveyard. We\u2019d done a lot of speculating in our brainstorming, and those kinds of assumptions and logical leaps were part of what led her down some of the darker paths she\u2019d been on recently. So she needed some air, and I offered to keep her company, honestly without ulterior motive, either personal reasons or to keep an eye on her for the troupe. Glenwood is just not the place to forget the buddy system.<br /> <br /> And so it wasn\u2019t today, A local gang, one that knows about the touched, and is superstitious enough, with a particular bent, to think we are unclean, showed up, at first casually guarding the exits to the cemetery. And when I say a gang, I mean the whole damn thing - 18 big rough and tumble folks showed up by the end of it. Someone called in reserves, or something. The five that were there at the first were scary enough - they were all armed and once they noticed that we noticed, they were no longer casually so much as menacingly prowling around the entrances to the cemetery.<br /> <br /> Alice was totally my knight in shining armor. She could have gone toe-to-toe with them and gotten out, but she wouldn\u2019t until I took the opportunity Doc made with his distraction to get the fuck out. I managed to stop cowering the van just long enough to get Alice her axe. That let her and Doc pull off a fighting retreat towards the van. We pulled them inside and Alexia drove like a bat out of hell, with the entirety of the gang tearing out after us. She managed to lose them on the highway, despite the number they did on the van.<br /> <br /> I may have gotten a little carried away with the joy at escaping. When I said \u201cwe pulled them inside\u201d, what I meant was Natalie helped Doc hop in, while I pulled Alice into my lap and kissed her. So... the rest of the ride was a little awkward. She did seem to enjoy the kiss though, so there\u2019s that. :-)<br /> <br /> Anyways, Natalie set us up a meeting with Sarah - we want to get confirmation of our assumptions before we go much further. If it turns out Star is not Sarah\u2019s ancestor, we\u2019re a little back to the drawing board, with a few more details to work on. If she is, we\u2019re all gonna set down together - us and the twins and Sarah - and hash this out. Hopefully Natalie and I aren\u2019t completely wrong about her, and we can get this sorted out happily for both families.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday, November 8th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Dum dum dum on the way to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t like Glenwood.<br /> <br /> -Glen must be punished.<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress would sooner be going to the dentist than where she is going.<br /> <br /> -I suppose I am dissin\u2019 on dentists, I mean they provide a needed service.<br /> <br /> -Here we are<br /> <br /> -Reading Reading<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t think Alice is a Reader<br /> <br /> -I am Reader, thanks to LeVar.<br /> <br /> -He is a nice guy.<br /> <br /> -Okay, conclusions<br /> <br /> -Fate is a fickle mistress at best.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear.<br /> <br /> -Radio silence, this is bad.<br /> <br /> -Leaving Glenwood, qui<br /> <br /> -Um, okay, that was unexpected. Anyway.<br /> <br /> -Things went south<br /> <br /> -We are okay. Mostly.<br /> <br /> -Poor Doc<br /> <br /> -Quick thinking on Lexi\u2019s part though.<br /> <br /> -Can\u2019t wait to be home.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXIX</i><br /> <br /> Well that was exciting. Some research, some battling Werewolves.<br /> <br /> But they have begun to put a picture together. Something happened many years ago, and it affecting the decendents of those involved. How innocent is Sarah? We will find out soon.<br /> <br /> Sat down and chatted with Simon's player last night. He really hopes to get back in sometime. We looked at some of Simon's notes. We will see what the situation is in January.<br /> <br /> Had a Halloween one shot, <i>Malibu Scream House</i>, with characters from several games, including <i>Balance of Shadows, Malibu Dream House, Night Train Detective Agency,</i> and my old <b>Changeling</b> game <i>Beyond the Sea</i>, as well as a couple from other folks games. <i>Balance of Shadows</i> had Natalie and Sara show. It went pretty well, if we get any journals from any of the 13 who showed I will post them.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"