voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-17T00:29:26-08:00","id":314306,"title":"","content":"Back to the Banshee mystery, a little bit more light is shown into the dark.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Tuesday, November 9, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019m mentally exhausted.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think everything would be cake and ice cream when we dealt with The Hair, but fuck me the rabbit hole is deep.<br /> <br /> Nightshade let us know around 1930 Hours that the meeting with The Hair was set for 2030 Hours at Murder Ballads. We had all healed up from the trip to Glenwood and I had looked online for some panels to replace the sides of the van. Nightshade had been suspicious missing since we got back, mainly because Karen sent her to their room. The level of Dom/sub that goes on there is a little baffling to me sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, we got to Murder Ballads a little early to make sure we handled any unexpected complications before meeting The Hair. Right as we walked in, a complication came up. I will call the complication Jaggling as I don\u2019t think she has her own Craft Name. Jaggling is The Hair\u2019s roommate, confirmed lesbian, more than mildly jealous, and moved to unwise actions. Jaggling reached from the random people in Murder Ballads and grabbed Nightshade\u2019s wrist to confront her. Given the earlier events of the day, I felt my verbally aggressive response in taking control of the situation was far more calm than other ways. I mean as far as we could tell, Jaggling was about to attack Nightshade and I didn\u2019t even strike her. Nightshade ran into conflict with Jaggling after The Hair took her home.<br /> <br /> Instincts and being on edge had me ready to destroy the girl where she stood, because I take care of my own. Logic screamed loud enough to get my attention however and we learned that Jaggling was also a Hedge Witch. More importantly to us, she knew that The Hair\u2019s family were and are Banshee. Because she has an affinity with spirits, Jaggling was aware of a Darkness spirit following The Hair. This spirit was incredibly weak but was sent to keep watch over The Hair without her knowledge. The spirit was apparently loose lipped with the witch as she knew the family line was dwindling and The Hair had to be preserved to pass on her birthright. Jaggling was fully convinced of this \u201ctruth,\u201d which at least partially explained her opposition to Nightshade \u201cinterfering\u201d with The Hair\u2019s legacy. I guess because I had originally placed myself between Nightshade and Jaggling, I was allowed to do most of the talking. That or Nightshade just enjoyed seeing how Jaggling shrank away from my anger. I suspect I know which one it was. Eventually, I gave Jaggling my card and told her to call me if she needed research assistance, basically giving her an out to ask for help, as she clearly jumps in over her head with things she didn\u2019t know anything about. Then I ran interference for her when The Hair showed up so Jaggling could get away unseen.<br /> <br /> I directed The Hair to the private rooms to meet the others, then headed over to the bar to ask for a steak knife. The bartender looked at me for a moment and asked if I planed to kill anyone. I decided against making the joke that I didn\u2019t need a knife for that and promised not to make him regret helping me. Then I walked back into the private hallway behind the Krewe, cut my hand to pull my Stigmata Shroud around me, and walked directly into Twilight. The little wingless bat with red beady eyes jumped when I stepped into its reality but I found it could speak to me directly. English is not usually available to such minor spirits so I was sure something had meddled with the tiny Darkness spirit following The Hair. The others were keeping tabs on me and stalling The Hair while I argued with Vlad the Informer to give us some privacy. Finally, I just grabbed it with the intention of walking out of the room and continuing our argument. Sadly, it started shrieking like some horrible invention that did not just drag fingernails down a chalkboard, but fired real nails across a chalkboard the length of a football field. I still left the room, but Vlad never stopped screaming. I didn\u2019t want to hurt the spirit but after about ten minutes, my head was splitting. Before I could lose my temper however, the Vlad stopped screaming. It was strange because something was still screaming almost as loud. I glanced down and realized that while the spirit had been afraid I would eat it or whatever, it was now terrified. I ran back into the private room and stepped back through to our plane of reality. The Hair was floating, her mouth was big enough Nightshade could have crawled in, and she was unquestioningly Keening! Axe looked at me funny before I realized I was still holding the tiny Darkness spirit. I apologized and let go, instantly sending it back into Twilight. It stayed across the room from me after that, but seemed to be okay with me otherwise.<br /> <br /> It hit us that The Hair must have bled on the comb since she was a real Banshee, thus she was screaming because someone was about to die. She had taken no breath since I arrived and did not seem aware, while her hair was thrashing around as if she were in gale force winds. Axe ran out to see if she could find out who was dying. Nightshade went to go handle the bouncers and ease the terror growing in the club. Eventually The Hair collapsed, though her hair with, assistance from Bright Eyes, caught her before she hit the floor. Axe came back in with a mirror fragment from the car accident outside. Apparently there was a t-bone crash and the passenger of the struck vehicle \u201cwas turned to paste.\u201d Axe has a way with description, though based on the wreckage I saw later, her assessment was probably closer than I originally thought. The mirror fragment will make a nice charm necklace.<br /> <br /> Once The Hair came to, she seemed nearly high or possibly more drunk on power. She became very dominant of Nightshade, a fact that Karen did not miss. They moved to the dance floor while Axe, Bright Eyes, Karen, and I all headed to the bar so I could return the knife. We took our seats as the bartender mixed our drinks and talked to relax like normal people. Karen and I don\u2019t get to hang out very much due to schedules and interests so tonight we talked more about her mysterious watcher. She has only ever noticed the sensation at night and only while on the second or third floor. Never the first floor for sure. The more I hear about this the less I think there\u2019s anything innocent going on. The first floor of the House is very easily navigated and also heavily utilized at most times of day. The upper floors are murkier as people are occasionally around but not usually awake at all times. Plus it would be harder for us to know exactly where to go right away if we heard a disturbance. Before this, I didn\u2019t worry too much as the House has always protected us. I don\u2019t think there is a physical intrusion because of that. That makes me more worried that someone is scrying on Karen specifically. That opens up many possibilities since we know it isn\u2019t through a Boneyard. I don\u2019t like unknown possibilities when it comes to our home. I had a mental image of Ronin flipping out because the sanctity of our sanctuary has been defiled.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t get very far into my own personal rabbit hole before Nightshade needed Karen. I was right beside her so I couldn\u2019t help but hear the fact Nightshade was asking permission to leave with The Hair. I could feel Karen stiffen at first, but then she turned on her barstool, stood as high as her platform boots could go and, while staring directly down at The Hair, grabbed Nightshade by the hair and kissed her ...savagely? I don\u2019t know if The Hair got the telegraphed message, but I heard the psychic scream of \u201cMY BITCH!\u201d loud and clear. After Nightshade could breathe evenly again, she left with The Hair. Karen sat back down at the bar, but the time for conversation was over. I left after a while as I still had work to do back at the Bluffs.<br /> <br /> Around 2300 Hours, I settled into the Library to finally get back to decrypting Bone Dry\u2019s book of damnation and slavery. I read back over all my other notes as I poured over the occult Mandarin tome for a third time. I had just finished the last section describing the final ritual as the massive grandfather clock struck midnight when the answers came rushing into my mind. It was satisfying, but also slightly disturbing, given the situation. I double checked my information against the various vampiric information I knew and had available in the Library. My epiphany seems to hold up. Sadly there is no way I can find to unweave or reverse the spell, which is disappointing but not surprising.<br /> <br /> I already knew but confirmed that a Jiangshi could become a more traditional (to my Western sensibilities) vampire through consuming the soul of another vampire. Though I did learn that this would apply to any other type of vampire, Penanggalan, Aswang, etc. Useful to know for other situations I guess. The next option, from most unhelpful down, is have another mage try to take control of the Jiangshi. This would, for the mage, simply be a contest of wills with Bone Dry. But even if the new mage won, we would have have to trust that she would then release her new slave. I hate to judge groups of people unfairly, but my track record with mages is not really making it easy for me to assume they are sane, much less trust one. Option 3 is to send the Jiangshi into a truly holy site. Once there, Guang would have a chance to throw off Bone Dry\u2019s control. Unfortunately there is almost an equal chance that he, or any other Jiangshi, would burst into white flames due to the power of the holy site.<br /> <br /> In the Chinese culture (and many others), 4 is the number for Death. That works out to be favorable to a Sin Eater blessed with Luck Magic. Option four seems to be the most likely route to freeing Guang. My research indicates that if a Jiangshi can drink the blood of another type of vampire, enough to spiritually represent her strength of will, she can try to throw off the bonds in which Bone Dry has mystically bound her. Assuming the might of blood and force of will is strong enough, the Jiangshi will shatter the bonds and serve no other master. If not, the Jiangshi can drink twice that amount of vampire blood and try again. Should she fail again, she must drink a frighteningly large amount of vampire blood and make a final attempt. I have to guess that the three tries option stops there because of the risk of Vinculum, though I\u2019m only peripherally familiar with that concept. Still, this seems like our best bet and I believe we could call enough enough favors with individual vampires to make this possible. The rest is simply up to Guang. Though, thinking about it, I can grant him fortune in pursuing his freedom once we have the rest together.<br /> <br /> Either way, we now know there is hope for Guang plus I know how to free the Jiangshi slaves of Bone Dry. His days are numbered and the pendulum swings back toward the light.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0915 Hours, Tuesday, November 9, 2010<br /> <br /> I went to bed last night feeling pretty good about what I\u2019d learned. Maybe it was still that same intellectual high that helped me meditate this morning. I centered in half an hour and felt great.<br /> Nightshade was still out when I came down for breakfast, but the rest of the Krewe and Axe were there. I briefly explained the ritual we could use to free Guang. Surprisingly, Chandra volunteered to let Guang drink from her. Cupcake was a little concerned but her wife was fairly determined that she would help the man tricked into becoming a hopping vampire. I also got the point from her wording that she was willing once. If Guang failed after the first attempt, we\u2019d need to find additional blood donors.<br /> <br /> We really are lucky to have Chandra around, most of the time.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Tuesday, November 9, 2010<br /> <br /> Right after breakfast, I got a call from Jaggling. She sounded rattled but dutifully delivered a message for Nightshade. The Hair said that Star was alive and that she wouldn\u2019t be around for a while. That message, given what we knew of The Hair\u2019s family, was ominous enough. But Jaggling added that it was not like The Hair to not say goodbye. This time she just hung up abruptly. I immediately felt my hackles raise and went to find Nightshade and gather the Krewe.<br /> Jaggling hesitated when I asked if there was anything else. Finally she said that she thought she saw The Hair, but then it wasn\u2019t her. Given the control of the Darkness spirit, I immediately instructed Jaggling to come to Dark Haven Bluffs.<br /> <br /> Jaggling arrived shortly after we got off the phone, but she seemed incredibly frightened and not just of the House. She said as she started walking up the steps that she thought something had happened. The shadows had been playing tricks on her. Worried that more than just paranoia had affected Jaggling, I commanded her to halt. I think that might have temporarily made her more afraid of me. Then I gave her a brief warning before calling for Lily. The doll happily ambled down stairs and looked the young woman over. Then she frustratedly tried to tell me something before Nightshade knelt beside her and whispers in the strange spirit language I can\u2019t seem to understand. Jaggling had been marked by a spirit according to Lily\u2019s findings. This did not soothe Jaggling nor did it lower my state of alert. I turned to Bright Eyes and told her to get the twins here before taking Jaggling into the TV room. I knew the others could fill in Timothy and Tracy once they arrived while I tried to stabilize Jaggling.<br /> <br /> I say stabilize as the poor girl was almost hyperventilating by the time we moved away from the Krewe. We turned on all the lights so that she was mostly away from any shadows before I could ask what else happened that she hadn\u2019t told me. After several deep breaths, Jaggling explained that after she thought she say The Hair, she turned to speak to her roommate like normal. The problem was that when she turned, it was not The Hair standing next to her, but someone else. Someone that looked surprisingly similar to The Hair. Then in the next moment as Jaggling realized this, that person was no longer there either. From that moment until she arrived at Dark Haven Bluffs, she continually saw things out of the corner of her eye. Always in the shadows, always outside of her directly line of sight. She kept saying things and shadows when I finally just asked if she meant she was seeing the shadows move. She said no, it was more like the shadows were becoming something else. It then that I spoke without realizing I was thinking aloud. The shadows were becoming locks of black hair moving to grab her when she wasn\u2019t prepared. Jaggling could only nod, lip trembling as she fought to hold back the sob of terror she so obviously felt.<br /> <br /> Apparently it\u2019s time to have a discussion with a Banshee Queen.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, the good thing about getting attacked by a gang of very large, very angry folks is that the gods have bequeathed hot tubs to mankind and bequeathed me with beautiful women to fill them with. The bad thing about hot tubs is when one of the previously mentioned hot women tell me they\u2019re not that kind of girl and don\u2019t much care for sharing. A sad day indeed. Not that I am pining - there are more paths to the comfort of physical contact than sex, and Alice was feeling a little tense after the altercation, something a purely platonic back rub did wonders for. Plus, I get Karen all to myself tonight, as Natalie is off being naughty.<br /> <br /> Alice did open up a little more, telling us what happened when she was touched. It had been caving accident, and left some wicked scars, even if she had gotten out. She also talked more about what had led her down the dark path she was one - her girlfriend had abandoned her there to die, and the influences on her after she was touched drove Alice to take revenge, on her girlfriend and her girlfriend\u2019s father, who was the one truly responsible. So I really have no place complaining. It was a far more emotionally taxing hot tub soak for Alice than for me. She did seem less tense after all the discussions, so that\u2019s good.<br /> <br /> Natalie had arranged for us to meet Sarah at around 8:30, so we showed up at Murder Ballads a bit before that to get the private room arranged and to scope out the place. It was fairly dead, being a Monday night and everything. We did get accosted by Marie, Sarah\u2019s roommate. Well, Natalie did. We almost had a fight on our hands until Doc intervened. I tried really hard not to grin too big, but Natalie was adorable, standing on her tiptoes to not look smaller than the other girl. Marie did have some interesting things to say, as it runs out she is a witch herself. She\u2019d intercepted a darkness spirit that was tailing Sarah, set up protect her by her ancestor. Marie was largely upset with Natalie, it seemed, for \u201cturning her gay\u201d because then Sarah wouldn\u2019t have any children to continue the bloodline, as the bean sidhe are a dying breed. Honestly, any sort of pressure to \u2018continue a bloodline\u2019 is a little creepy to me, regardless of how many of what are left in the world.<br /> <br /> Though, to be fair to Marie, Sarah had been acting awfully strange recently. To be fair to us, it was entirely because of the comb. Between the temporary obsession with me, and the fact that she bled on the comb and unlocked her heritage, there was enough to make anyone paying attention worry. Doc did make her apologize for throwing around accusations of mind-control though.<br /> <br /> Marie was really worried about being spotted by Sarah, so she split as soon as Sarah showed up. Doc headed Sarah off, since she\u2019d caught something of a glimpse of Marie anyway, and I gathered folks up, warning them not to talk about the twins until Doc had dealt with the spy. That took a moment, so there was some awkward stalling talk, but once he had, we got down to business. Alice had used her Sight to confirm that Sarah was the one that had stolen my card. The comb again - she\u2019d still been in its grip and had been super jealous. Alice got a little tense when Sarah was talking about having wanted to hurt Tracey, but since she hadn\u2019t, and we\u2019ll hopefully be getting this curse thing dealt with, I don\u2019t think there will be any justice needed.<br /> <br /> Sarah did agree that the sins of the great ... grandfather had no place being visited on the twins, so once she and Natalie disentangle, she\u2019s going to talk with her grandmother about it. We\u2019re thinking that Star is actually her great-grandmother with no steps being left out, so the family history might be a bit less buried. The interview was cut short slightly a bit after that when she spaced out and then began shrieking. There was no question about her bean sidhe heritage after that, as she kept shrieking without breathing for minutes, stopping and collapsing only after the passenger in the t-boned car just outside the club took his last breath. I managed to catch her, with her hair helping, grabbing onto the nearby chair with a life of its own.<br /> <br /> That cut our plotting short - Sarah dragged Natalie out to the dance floor, feeling a little high after her shrieking fit, while we caught poor Doc up. He had something of a headache, as the spying spirit was something of a shrieker itself. When Alice got back from helping out at the crash, I claimed my rainchecked dance. Platonic or not, it is a true pleasure in life to dance with someone so graceful and athletic. Doc, Karen and I had a few drinks at the bar before heading home, while Natalie went home with Sarah.<br /> <br /> An eventful day all around. I can say I hope tomorrow\u2019s not anymore exciting than facilitating a meeting between two families that have been feuding for generations without jinxing it, right? It's not like that will be a walk in the park or anything...<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> It seems the answer is no. As stressful as facilitating a meeting between two families that have been feuding for generations sounds like, I\u2019d take it over having one party disappear and another show up jumping at shadows, having been marked spiritually by some unknown being any day.<br /> <br /> Marie called Doc a little after breakfast, since he\u2019d given her his card, and she needed to get a message to Natalie from Sarah. It seems that not only is Star Jameson Sarah\u2019s great-grandmother, but she\u2019s still alive - that women in her family live a long time is almost an understatement. In addition, Sarah said she\u2019d be unreachable for a bit, but that she wasn\u2019t in danger. She hadn\u2019t said goodbye, just hung up abruptly, which started Marie down the worrying path.<br /> <br /> Doc told Marie to head on over, so we could get more details and figure out where we need to go from here, and by the time she arrived, she was scared out of her skull. Apparently, since the call, she\u2019d been seeing.. things, always out of the corner of her eye. Once, she\u2019d thought it had been Sarah, but when she looked at it straight on, it clearly wasn\u2019t her, and then it clearly just wasn\u2019t. As soon as we heard that, I contacted Timothy, asking him to keep in touch, and to stay close to his sister. Once we figured out that Marie had been marked by something, I asked both of them to come over too. It seemed a decidedly hostile move. If it was made by the bean sidhes, then Timothy and Tracey were also in danger. If it was made by their ancestor, then maybe we could work together to counteract it.<br /> <br /> Once the twins showed up, we got them up to speed while Doc tried to get Marie calmed down. Tracey... Tracey is a dear, but I\u2019d be much more worried about their bloodline\u2019s power if Timothy were not around. She\u2019d not malicious, or even stupid, just a little careless and prone to asking dangerous questions without thinking. The two of them together should be fine. They were both worried and upset about Sarah\u2019s disappearance, despite some awkward history - Sarah had misread some intentions, and so had been a bit surprised when Tracey came in for a kiss. Still, they did know each other, and there were no hard feelings. So a reunion and team-up seemed promising, provided we could get Sarah back in one piece.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 8th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I have been sent to my room, by my Mistress.<br /> <br /> -Mistress is worried about me, I know.<br /> <br /> -Still, Sara was not sent to her room. I did not transgress more than her.<br /> <br /> -Mistress loves me. &lt;B<br /> <br /> -Okay off to Murder Ballads.<br /> <br /> -The bitch is back.<br /> <br /> -I did not get to clock her. Sad.<br /> <br /> -Sarah is here!<br /> <br /> -Poor Doc.<br /> <br /> -Huh, wow. Poor Doc, and Alice I guess?<br /> <br /> -This may be going badly.<br /> <br /> -Okay this is odd.<br /> <br /> -UMMMMMMM<br /> <br /> -Crap. Crap Crap Crap Crap.<br /> <br /> -Damn It!<br /> <br /> -<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Okay, we can salvage this.<br /> <br /> -Oh shit.<br /> <br /> -That was surreal.<br /> <br /> -I..wow.<br /> <br /> -Natalie is going to put away her phone now and pay attention to me. \u2013Sarah<br /> <br /> <br /> November 9th, 2010<br /> <br /> -That was\u2026something.<br /> <br /> -Sarah is back to her old demure self, which is probably a good thing, if a little disappointing.<br /> <br /> -Karen is not happy with me.<br /> <br /> -Ow.<br /> <br /> -Useful information from Doc<br /> <br /> -We have a plan I think.<br /> <br /> -My Mistress has plans for me after the group plan. &lt;B<br /> <br /> -GODILOVEITWHENKARENGETSALLDOMINANT<br /> <br /> -&lt;B<br /> <br /> -Uh oh.<br /> <br /> -Sarah may be missing.<br /> <br /> -This is bad.<br /> <br /> -This is really bad.<br /> <br /> -Doc\u2019s favorite people are here.<br /> <br /> -They really are adorable. I think Sara wants to keep them both.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear, I hope Sarah is alright.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXX</i><br /> <br /> Not a whole lot to add; mostly was a social session. Doc\u2019s struggle with the Spirit was interesting; it was bound and it\u2019s options limited, so it had no way to consensually comply with leaving even if it wished to. The result was a rather comedic struggle.<br /> <br /> As a Reminder, Natalie has the Hedge Witch Spell of Spirit Speech, hence was able to speak to Lily directly.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-11-30T13:30:22-08:00","id":326256,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to look in on our Krewe as they unravel the tangled mystery going on with the old grudges.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1600 Hours, Tuesday, November 9, 2010<br /> <br /> I did not see today going the way it has. Nothing says it can\u2019t go nuclear tonight, but for the moment we feel pretty satisfied.<br /> <br /> Before we left to confront Star/rescue The Hair, Cupcake insisted that we bring sweets to the old women. Her thought was that it worked with Mallard so it should at least win us points. I reminded her that we were about to leave so we didn\u2019t really have time to bake a cake. I went to ask Tavia is she could look after the twins while we were gone, but Karen seemed to be perfectly happen to keep them company. When I came back, the decision had been made. We had to stop at Sweet Surrender before heading for The Hair\u2019s grandmother\u2019s house. We were also taking Jaggling with us as she actually knew the way. I realized as we were heading out, and looking at my van, that I still needed to call Rawl. That also reminded me I needed to be a better shot before my next trip to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> We didn\u2019t lose too much time waiting for Cupcake at her shop before we were back on the road, cookies and various pastries in tow. The Hair\u2019s family home was very unassuming, though it was definitely well maintained. The group of us went to the door expecting to meet an elderly woman. Thus when a woman that may have looked like an exquisite 35 answered the door knowing that we had come to speak with The Hair before we admitted it, we were surprised. When we learned this woman of incredible beauty was actually Star, we were all silent for a moment. Whether that moment was spent in appreciation or not, depended on the Krewe member in question. Which is to say, FUCK Star is hot!<br /> <br /> She invited us in and seemed very grateful for the sweets. Apparently The Hair\u2019s mother is Star\u2019s daughter. She said this daughter was actually taking a nap, so I offered for us to keep our voices down so as not to wake her. Star made some amused joke about offering us doilies before leading us into a sitting room. She was going by Rhiannon these days. Thankfully, she both had an idea of what we were and had no interest in conflict. She told us up front that The Hair was having trouble returning to human form and thus did not want to be seen, but was absolutely there. She also apologized to Jaggling and noted that she probably suffered from shock after seeing The Hair while unprepared. Her opinion was that The Hair was doing fine but that the stress of frightening Jaggling was distracting her. We asked how she knew what we were as she too called us Ghostwalkers. Rhiannon told us as far as she knew, Banshee actually came from the Lower Depths. Her understanding was that perhaps a Geist or Kerberoi managed to return to the living world and spawned children. She even mentioned she knew two of our Keys, though she demured when we asked which ones. I think Nightshade almost swooned given the situation. Of course, that could also be because of the many sidelong glances Rhiannon sent her way.<br /> <br /> While we were all taken with Rhiannon\u2019s beauty, at least a few of us were still focused enough to want to see The Hair. Since Nightshade and Bright Eyes were specifically concerning to The Hair, Rhiannon allowed me to go back and see her. Given her current image problem, I intentionally waited around the corner and spoke to The Hair until she agreed it was okay for me to look at her. My medical background seemed to calm her fears of rejection. The Hair\u2019s features had become gaunt, almost skeletal with a deathly pallor, but she was still clearly the same person I knew before. If there was any question, her personality guaranteed her authenticity. I assured The Hair that neither Nightshade nor Bright Eyes would shun her for her appearance, and that she should know that all of us could look much worse depending on our powers. Rhiannon made some comment suggesting that Nightshade would possibly enjoy it. While I agreed, I kept that to myself. She was very concerned for what happened with Jaggling. I assured her that things would be okay. We also included her in the invitation made to Rhiannon to meet with the twins to help solve this unintended curse complication. After that, I confirmed to the Krewe that The Hair was alright and that we would see her when she was ready. We thanked Rhiannon for being so willing to help and make sure we could all keep in contact. We needed to speak with the twins before a meeting could be arranged.<br /> <br /> Before sending her on her way, I stopped Jaggling and showed her the Library. Then I asked if she had any questions. I could see volumes of queries flow over her blank eyes before she admitted she didn\u2019t know where to start. I gave her an incredibly short crash course on what a Sin Eater is, so she would have some context and that seemed to satisfy her, or overwhelm her more, I\u2019m not sure which. But either way, I think Jaggling, The Hair, and possibly Rhiannon could make great contacts for our Krewe. Finally, I sent Jaggling home after promising to let her know about any meeting that took place.<br /> <br /> By the time I joined the rest of the Krewe, they were explaining the situation to the twins. I drew a sketch of Rhiannon while we discussed the situation. Tracy was probably more interested than she should have been. Around 1500 Hours, the twins confirmed that they were willing to meet the Banshee Queen and try to work out at least a compromise. Neither of them were interested in killing people for power, even if they did awaken their inheritance. Since the Krewe was mediating, I suggested we meet at the Firehouse Church. Everyone agreed and the time was set for 2030 Hours.<br /> <br /> Once that was settled, I called Jaggling per my promise. Then I asked Timothy to walk with me. The look I got from Nightshade suggested she thought I was up to something, but I didn\u2019t have time to consider that. If one or, more likely both, twins would awaken as mages, I wanted to speak with the more thoughtful and informed of the two. Timothy was duly impressed with the implications of what lay before him, but I couldn\u2019t help but feel like he knew than he was letting on. I gave him what I think can be summed up as the \u201cJust because you can, doesn\u2019t mean you should\u201d talk. Given the level of his potential powers, I noted that I couldn\u2019t stand against him directly and that seemed to surprise him. Almost like he knew he would have powers but not on a level that could affect me. That at least assured me that he wasn\u2019t making too many contingencies. I hate myself for this, but I\u2019ve already thought of several ways to take both twins out should it become necessary. Hopefully it will never come to that and they will become the first mages we\u2019ve encountered that are neither insane nor need to be put down.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s nice to hope.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Ok, I admit it - that was not quite how I expected that to go. Of course, Natalie might be right, the beautiful bean sidhe matriarch might have been lying through her teeth, but even Natalie didn\u2019t really believe that. It is something to keep in mind though. If anyone can pull one over the lot of us, it would be the mysterious faerie woman. If she can be taken at her word however, this whole situation is looking much brighter.<br /> <br /> Alexia had the right approach from the beginning. She made sure we stopped off at the bakery to grab a collection of her best stuff, to make it look likes less of a castle storming, and also got each of us a treat. The eclair she got for Marie worked wonders. In hindsight, that\u2019s probably round about when she started \u2018getting better\u2019. See, it turns out the jumpiness was just from shock. Her initial \u2018hallucination\u2019 had been Sarah contacting her using her new bean sidhe powers, which, as Marie was quite unprepared, was startling, to say the least.<br /> <br /> Rhiannon, as Star is calling herself these days, apologized for that scare when we found her at Sarah\u2019s grandmother\u2019s house. She also apologized for Sarah\u2019s absence from our discussion, but she was dealing with the aftershocks of awakening her powers, and didn\u2019t feel up to seeing Natalie in particular. Doc did check up on her though, and everything did check out - she was fine, just a bit shaky. He said he didn\u2019t understand what all the fuss was about, but after her roommate's reaction, it\u2019s not that odd.<br /> <br /> As far as the twins' situation, it turns out the curse is far more protective that vindictive, though there was something of a gleam in Rhiannon\u2019s eye as she described it. Its main problem for the moment seems to be that it was described rather broadly, and that Natalie and I are too damnedably sexy. See, the curse stated that if Israel\u2019s descendents attempted to follow in his footsteps, then the protections Israel had set up would crumble. So the tainted ancestor spirits (according to the bean sidhe) are a result of his work, and their bindings are, in fact, loose at the moment. What was meant by \u2018follow in his footsteps\u2019 was harder to pin down. It had two parts and one was easy: it would be satisfied if they came in contact with a significant amount of death energy. That is, if they, I dunno, had sex with someone(s) touched by death, like maybe me and Natalie, for example.<br /> <br /> The other half, that they used their ancestor\u2019s power, was trickier. Rhiannon wasn\u2019t familiar enough with his power to say what that would be. It seems like the transgression was fairly innocent - Tracey had found some place in the dream sea \u2018interesting\u2019 and, all unknowing, tried to move the island towards it. Apparently it moves quite fast, when she puts her mind to it.<br /> <br /> Now that you are all caught up on the business portion of this whole deal - good lords and ladies above and below, Rhiannon is gorgeous. Yes, some might consider it gauche to go immediately from a definitely non platonic, somewhere on the other side of making out session in the hot tub (which almost assuredly has not improved Alice\u2019s opinions of my relationship habits) to gushing about another woman. Thankfully, I am neither speaking (typing?) nor married to anyone of that nature. Tracey is a wonderful, lovely and quite talented woman, but when you\u2019ve had at least seven human generations to perfect a human guise, well, it shows. Not to mention the accumulated power and knowledge. She herself was quite intrigued by the flock of lesbians we presented her with. Well, the flock of women who like women anyway, not to leave myself out. She was particularly intrigued by Natalie, having gotten quite a description of her from Sarah it seems. I also managed to put a bug in her ear as I was setting up the meeting for tonight - she felt Murder Ballads would be too distracting for a business meeting, but regretted that it had been so long since she had been dancing. With any luck, there will be a decidedly non-business meeting later.<br /> <br /> Also with any luck, this business meeting will result in a solution that works for everyone. I am more inclined to trust the bean sidhes at this point, quite honestly, so perhaps we can get some new strictures set in place, fully laid out so there\u2019s no accidental triggering. I think Israel is likely to be as much a danger to the twins as the rest of their dead relatives, should they come into their power. But we need time to confirm that and learn more about him. Hopefully, Rhiannon can help us with that.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 9th, 2010<br /> <br /> -We are off to grandmother\u2019s house.<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s like a fairy tale.<br /> <br /> -We need more Goth Fairy Tales.<br /> <br /> -<i>Lady Spiderweb and the Old Mill</i><br /> <br /> -Awkward car ride is awkward.<br /> <br /> -<i>Prince Velvet and the Magical Bridge</i><br /> <br /> -<i>Three Billy Goats Goth</i><br /> <br /> -<i>Snow White</i><br /> <br /> -<i>Littlest Witch in the Woods</i><br /> <br /> -I\u2019d try to come up with Pagan Fairy Tales but that is pretty much all of them.<br /> <br /> -Zing!<br /> <br /> -Okay here we are.<br /> <br /> -Wow. Also. Wow.<br /> <br /> -Quite lovely, and checking me out. Awesome.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple? I am not going to reject someone for looking Banshee like!<br /> <br /> -A I am not that superficial and B HOW GOTH IS THAT.<br /> <br /> -It shits bats, that\u2019s how goth it is.<br /> <br /> -If she doesn\u2019t stop looking at me like that\u2026<br /> <br /> -Okay this is all very surreal.<br /> <br /> -Doc to the rescue. Maybe.<br /> <br /> -Seemed to go well. Back home now. Jiggity Jog<br /> <br /> -<i>Little Black Riding Hood</i><br /> <br /> -<i>The Prince and the LARPer</i><br /> <br /> -What\u2019s Doc gonna talk to crazy roommate about I wonder?<br /> <br /> -Boots. Oof.<br /> <br /> -One big happy party coming up.<br /> <br /> -Apparently Sara can resist no longer. Not sure what Doc is doing this time.<br /> <br /> -If it turns out all these secret side conversations are Doc building a harem I will laugh.<br /> <br /> -I mean, I will be really surprised, but I will laugh.<br /> <br /> -Firehouse Church tiem. I like the Firehouse Church.<br /> <br /> -Hate the van is all busted up, oh well.<br /> <br /> -<i>Rose Dead</i><br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXI</i><br /> <br /> Note on Terminology: What Doc and Rhiannon/Star referred to as \u201cLower Depths\u201d was the Dead Dominions, not Lower Depths in a Mage sense. Doc was not inaccurate in his recording of the wording, though\u2026Rhiannon used that name. There is some question as to precisely what Sarah and Rhiannon\u2019s ancestor is or was, but Rhiannon seems to possess Keys, and it seems genetic, though whether the comb was always key or if it was worked in later is obscure.<br /> <br /> Mostly a social session. Not really much to add. As noted the Bean Sidhe here are not Gentry, they are basically similar to Geists or Kereboi (though I tend to use human type stats most of the time for major characters, so Rhiannon and Sarah have Attributes and Skills).<br /> <br /> That\u2019s about it for now, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-09T19:41:00-08:00","id":335709,"title":"","content":"Doc building a harem? He's not you Natalie <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-10T05:11:36-08:00","id":335996,"title":"","content":"Heh Sara has Natalie edged out for harem. But she has a solid #2.<br /> <br /> Doc's player was the one who noted OOC his side conversations probably looked bad, but of course Doc was not thinking that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 12-10-2014, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T14:29:32-08:00","id":340224,"title":"","content":"\u2019s time to look in on the Krewe, as they manage affairs with Banshee and Werewolves<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2145 Hours, Tuesday, November 9, 2010<br /> <br /> WOOHOO! Mark one point for Hope!<br /> <br /> We just got back from what I think was the most productive meeting of supernaturals we\u2019ve ever attended. The twins came with us and then we went to work. They had never seen the Firehouse Church and since we had to prepare, they got the grand tour. Rhiannon accompanied The cloaked and cowled Hair as they arrived right on time. Cupcake set up her refreshments table while I organized the most fair wait to have the seating arrangements.<br /> <br /> Ironically, when I was finished we had what looked like the last supper with the Krewe around me in the middle. We were meeting in the sanctuary and once together, I made introductions. Tracy looked terrified and refused to let go of Bright Eyes. I was afraid I\u2019d have to amputate later. Timothy was as impressed as everyone else when he saw Rhiannon, but otherwise remained fairly calm. For her part, Rhiannon was very gracious. Jaggling sat next to The Hair. She tried to make up for panicking and going into shock earlier by asking The Hair if there was anything she needed, about every 15 seconds. The Hair was there, even though she couldn\u2019t rebuild her face yet, to show how important this was and I think everyone appreciated the effort.<br /> <br /> I intended to act as moderator, though it turned out that, other than prompting Tracy a few times, everyone was happy to speak in turn. The Banshee Queen made it clear she had no desire to harm the twins, so long as they were not following in Israel\u2019s footsteps. While thankful not to be marked for death, Timothy did voice his frustration at having a sword hanging over his head without a clear idea of what would cause it to drop. The problem here is that the original curse was met for Israel, therefore very little effort was put into clear boundaries, as mages will find ways around them. However, this is now a more delicate situation. Possibly more pressing is that Rhiannon is very concerned that awakening the twins\u2019 powers will actually summon Israel, who may simply absorb them before unleashing his plans all over again. I planted the seed with the Krewe that maybe we could summon him. It\u2019s not like we\u2019ve never had to bind an incredibly powerful ghost before. Or dealt with mages for that matter. Rhiannon warned us that her attempts to summon Israel have always failed. We\u2019re hoping that we have stronger methods we can bring to bear.<br /> <br /> Because there is so much grey area, we concluded the meeting on a high note. Tavia and Gretchen were offered as stewards of the library for either side to try and find more information. I was a little confused as to why Nightshade left me out of the equation, but also suggested that we all keep in contact and share information as we find it. Everyone left happy.<br /> <br /> Tracy and Timothy took Bright Eyes home, while The Hair went back to her apartment with Jaggling. I came back to The Bluffs to write this. Now I think I\u2019m going online to look for van parts.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0300 Hours, Wednesday, November 10, 2010<br /> <br /> I started finding what I needed for the van pretty quickly, everything being on the Internet like they say. But before I clicked the Checkout button, I realized I was doing it wrong. Several thousand dollars worth of parts were exactly what I needed, but the chance something else would rend my van next week, gave me pause. I needed to find the cheapest replacement parts I could for the van. Then put my alchemy to good use. First I\u2019ll greatly improve the quality of the cheap parts, then I\u2019ll lace the panels with silver. Let those bastard Predator Kings fuck with my van again. Surprise asshole!<br /> <br /> Buying remarkably cheaper parts with malicious intent got me thinking about other contingencies. It occurred to me that when it comes to spirits and most anything else in the Shadow, we were almost fighting blind. With two tribes of Pure putting us on their list as well as the random spirits we may have to deal with in relation to Bone Dry, I felt it was time I ripped off the blindfold. I hit the Library like Titan and came out three and a half hours later with a spell that will let me summon and command spirits. I\u2019m not thrilled about the fall out I could have for commanding spirits, but my naive assumption is that if I\u2019m issuing commands that tie to their influences, it shouldn\u2019t have as bad of a backlash later.<br /> <br /> I even have my first target, but I think it\u2019s probably better not to summon a spirit at 0300 Hours and order it to teach me things. Bed for now.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1015 Hours, Wednesday, November 10, 2010<br /> <br /> I woke up pretty easily this morning around 0800 Hours. Meditation took about an hour but I was very much a peace when I finished. Nightshade came home while we were finishing breakfast so I pulled her to the side before she slipped off. I\u2019d be worried about her. This whole issue with Tantrum left me thinking that I might be able to help, but only if I wouldn\u2019t get in the way. I suggested that I could \u201cbring her in\u201d to something by teaching her my ceremonial magic if she thought it would help. I could tell by the look on her face that Nightshade was not interested in the idea, but she explained that right now she was still trying to keep Tantrum protected. But the \u201cnot yet\u201d told me Nightshade had looked at the future possibilities as well. She also thanked me for trying to look out for her. It was nice.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to mind my own business and try to salvage as much as I can on the van before I get the parts in.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1445 Hours, Wednesday, November 10, 2010<br /> <br /> So much for the warm fuzzies Nightshade and I were sharing. Wait...I\u2019m jumping all over. Damn werewolves are getting me all out of sorts.<br /> <br /> Okay so I spent about three hours tearing out ruined sections of the van and making sure the good pieces weren\u2019t going to be damaged from exposure before I could put the new parts in. That was a decent exercise for not forgetting everything Snowflake and I learned while we put the van together. But when I got finished, I was still thinking about what happened and realized I\u2019d never tried my only contact in Glenwood.<br /> <br /> About 1330 Hours, I called Rawl with a little hesitation. I didn\u2019t think he was the type that would lead a war party into New Haven, but I honestly didn\u2019t know him that well. He figured out who I was fairly quickly and seemed as eager to talk about things as I was. I told him what happened from our viewpoint, which must have been fairly amusing. He told me that he wasn\u2019t there, like I expected, though that he was with his nephew playing mini golf was not what I expected. I asked why we were attacked when we had only come to do research on something else as horrible as the last thing we came to Glenwood about? That was a long, very informative story that pissed me the fuck off.<br /> <br /> Rawl explained that there are people werewolves call Claimed. They sound like Shadow versions of Sin-Eaters, except the people are subsumed by the spirit. The Pure don\u2019t really mind these creatures but others, like our friends around here put them down. Something about spirits keeping to their duties and not interfering with humans. I\u2019m just a Gatekeeper so I don\u2019t know anything about that. But this time, a nasty group of these Claimed were working for a Balehound. More explanations got me to up to speed. Werewolves have a name for vice spirits, not just the little ones, but the Vice Lords. Those more powerful vice spirits are called Majin. These are the spirits that some humans refer to as demons. So a Balehound is a werewolf that actively works for these Majin. The Claimed work for the Balehound but may also be in league with the Majin, something about being vice-ridden and pledging to a Vice Lord. Either way, given our experience with vice spirits during our stay at the Hidden Hillside Hotel, I was not pleased to be compared to such creatures. To make it worse, this particular group of vice-ridden were targeting the Predator Kings kin.<br /> <br /> This all ties back in to us, but not really. Apparently when Xavier and his Ivory Claws got their asses handed to them, he very loudly announced that a group of Claimed with strange powers were in New Haven. It was after our run in with the Ivory Claws that this group of Claimed started their rampage through Glenwood. So when it comes right down to it, the Predator Kings were acting on an honest case of mistaken identity. That still doesn\u2019t excuse that Mustachioed fuckwit Xavier from, well anything, as not even the Predator Kings like him. Rawl did clue me in on some of the Ivory Claws issues as Pure though. They don\u2019t like us because they believe that death is the end of pain; that your suffering stops once you die. And yet, he ran away instead of ending his pain when he fought with us. Anyway, Rawl also said that the Predator Kings haven\u2019t had a fight like we gave them in a long time. They revelled in it as they are hunters and we gave them a challenge. This came up as I tried to gather a concept of truce. These werewolves may or may not believe that we are not vice-ridden, but ultimately they may not care. Rawl believes me, but like he said before these Predator Kings are crazy, even for Predator Kings. Fucking Glenwood.<br /> <br /> After that enlightening conversation, I called Zed. Rawl heard rumors that the Balehound was operating out of New Haven and that made me think about Malard and Angelique. I apologized even as I suggested it, but Zed let me know very quickly that it was something they thought of too. He said that couldn\u2019t prove anything and Angelique got incredibly pissy if people tried to go through her personal stuff. Funny had that works. But while Zed told us we should go for it if we wanted to investigate, there wouldn\u2019t be anything to keep either Malard or Angelique from ripping us to shreds if we were caught.<br /> <br /> So now I know that because the Ivory Claws are cowards, an entire tribe of werewolves in Glenwood attacked us. Because we are fairly competent, those same morons want another piece of us. Also because of Xavier I had to learn about something else in werewolf culture that makes me suspicious of one of our most powerful allies. And all this led me to glance outside where my devastated van sits like a wounded soldier laying in a hospital bed. There will be no quarter for these vice-ridden. And there will be no mercy given to the Ivory Claws ever again. Now I have to tell the others what I found out and try not to smash anything while I tell them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well that went well, I think. How anything catered by Alexia could go poorly, I\u2019m not sure, but the balance between phenomenal cosmic power and itty bitty living space is a tricky thing. And while Israel is capable of influencing things, itty bitty living space it kinda needs to be.<br /> <br /> Primarily, we established that Rhiannon has no desire to hurt either of them, and the twins had no desire to consume people\u2019s lifeforce to make a mad dash for godhood, even if the word \u2018godhood\u2019 perked Tracey up a bit more than it ought have. There was some frustration on Timothy\u2019s part - Rhiannon doesn\u2019t know much about their kind of powers, except that they can be dangerous. It seemed to him (and I agree) that it shouldn\u2019t be that everything they can do is automatically harmful, to them or others. Very few powers in this world are purely evil, or purely good, but instead depend on who wields them. Which means we need to deal with Israel, as soon as we can.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Rhiannon doesn\u2019t know any acceptable ways to make him manifest (and her unacceptable one truly is). We touched have a few more tricks up our sleeves though. Also, a badass library. The lovely librarian duo have been set upon the task of figuring out alternate mentoring sources for the twins.<br /> <br /> We exchanged contact info before we went our separate ways. Tracey and by extension Timothy had my card already, as did Sarah, for reasons, but I made sure Rhiannon got one as well. Sarah had in fact shown up, cloaked and cowled since she hadn\u2019t yet mastered \u2018putting on her face\u2019. She went back to her own place with Marie, who was all apologies and consideration, with the great grandmother\u2019s hope that being in a familiar place would help with that. I went home with Tracey. At first that was looking like an inevitability, but I did eventually have something of a choice, as by the end of the meeting the Jaws of Life were no longer required to pull us apart. The poor dear was pretty terrified going in to things. I think she was on a more even keel after everything, even if we didn\u2019t get to linger comfortably on the dream island, and when she came to pull me out of there, I didn\u2019t wind up going to wherever she was.<br /> <br /> For now, it is a lazy day about the house. Alexia and Alice baked some perfectly delicious pumpkin cookies last night, which I believe require musical tribute, even if our guitarist has absconded with Alice for a shopping trip. Natalie is around here somewhere, I bet I can wrangle up some piano...<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> People and their feuds are weird, sometimes. Also, if I hadn\u2019t mentioned, angry Doc is fucking scary. I was this close to joining Natalie under the piano, and not in a fun way, except I\u2019m pretty sure he\u2019d chew a box of bullets before he\u2019d hurt one of us. Still. Brr...<br /> <br /> See, Doc had managed to track down a... friend, I guess, in Glenwood. Someone from before I showed up. He has ties to the gang that attacked us at the church, which is kinda more like a family, if you know what I mean. Anyway, they managed to put together why they attacked and it wasn\u2019t cause the death touched are unclean. *sigh* This is going to be complicated...<br /> <br /> A while ago, a particular clique in this family made trouble for a pal of Doc\u2019s (funnily enough, the same one Alice was caught making trouble for. And a similar kind of trouble.) So, Doc was a little pissed, to put it mildly, and, as opposed to Alice, these thugs decided to escalate things, and the clique got torn a new one. Shortly thereafter, some seriously bad news mystical types started going after the civilian element of the family. There weren\u2019t any witness to that, and our mysticality was, I guess, just enough like the bad guys\u2019 that they kinda conflated the two incidents. So it\u2019s kinda understandable, as to why all the stops were pulled out and such.<br /> <br /> To complicate things, there\u2019s a branch of the family in Newhaven that does not get along with the branch in Glenwood and the bad news from above is technically another far divergent branch of the family that no one likes. Well, at least the bad news is allied with someone like that. Even better, the divergent one might be undercover as our next door neighbor. It\u2019s lovely. However, as bad as all this sounds, it\u2019s not precisely pressing. The family can generally take care of themselves and they do have ways to get in touch (with Doc) if they need a hand. So, here\u2019s hoping that doesn\u2019t explode somehow.<br /> <br /> On a lighter note, Doc\u2019s angry voice saying Mr. Mustachio-Fuckwit is kinda hilarious, and Alice would totally rock a Red Riding Hood outfit. You know it\u2019s true. :-)<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> The Grasping Huntress has been quiet for the past day or so. Just a week ago, I could hardly have a thought of my own without her whispering in my head. But now she\u2019s silent. Maybe she\u2019s angry, or maybe she\u2019s just calculating how to respond to our new situation. She doesn\u2019t like the Middle Shadows. I hope she changes her mind, though. It\u2019s going to be better with the Middle Shadows. We can hunt real prey, prey that deserve final justice.<br /> <br /> <i>All this krewe does is talk. There is no hunt here, only unsatisfied anger.</i><br /> <br /> Ah, there she is. I should have known her silence was too good to last.<br /> <br /> <i>You have fallen in with scholars, diplomats and whores. They aren\u2019t hunters like us.</i><br /> <br /> Maybe not, but they seem to be giving me the balance I need. Let\u2019s face it. I\u2019m a weapon. Maybe that\u2019s a pretty awful way to look at it, but like any weapon, I can kill for the right reasons or I can kill for the wrong reasons. The Middle Shadows seems to be able to give me the right reasons, and\u2014.<br /> <br /> <i>All they DO is reason. They do not act.</i><br /> <br /> \u2014and when they DO unleash me as their Reaper, it will be justified. At least, that\u2019s what I keep telling myself.<br /> <br /> <i>We don\u2019t belong here.</i><br /> <br /> I keep telling myself the Huntress is wrong, but I have to admit that I feel like a fish out of water. So much of what this krewe does is foreign to me: research, negotiation, mediation. I\u2019m on the sidelines. But that\u2019s okay. They\u2019re helping me, and I\u2019ll have an opportunity to prove myself eventually. Heck, I\u2019ve already proven myself, haven\u2019t I? When we fought those werewolves. Sara might have died if I hadn\u2019t been there. So I shouldn\u2019t worry.<br /> <br /> Now I know why it\u2019s so easy for the Huntress to manipulate me. When I don\u2019t have a purpose\u2014when I\u2019m not on a hunt\u2014all I do is doubt myself.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I\u2019m at New Haven\u2019s biggest shopping mall with Natalie\u2019s wife Karen. She\u2019s treating me to a small shopping spree, courtesy of the krewe. I tried to politely refuse their charity until Alexia assured me that they had loads of money thanks to a fortuitous windfall during one of their investigations.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Alexia, she\u2019s really warmed up to me. I think she was worried I was some sort of psycho at first, but now that she\u2019s gotten to know me, she\u2019s sort of taken me under her wing. She takes the time to explain things, and she lets me help in the kitchen, which I gather is her sacred territory. She\u2019s a real sweetheart.<br /> <br /> So is Karen, for that matter, but she\u2019s a lot more serious. I was surprised she asked me to go shopping. We haven\u2019t spoken more than a few words to each other since I arrived, but I guess she wanted to get to know me better and do her part to make me feel welcome. I\u2019m just glad she isn\u2019t scared of me.<br /> <br /> And I have to admit, it will be nice to get some new clothes. All I have is what I brought with me form Portland: mostly jeans, t-shirts, tank tops, hiking shoes and steel-toed boots. The krewe wants me to have some more options: nicer clothes and stylish shoes for professional meetings, sexier clothes for clubbing. Alexia said that if I was going to be a part of the krewe, I needed to look the part. I don\u2019t think my black jeans and Children of Bodom tank tops look bad at Murder Ballads, but I don\u2019t mind kicking it up a notch. So I picked up some sleek leather pants, nicer jeans, and a couple of leather bustier tops. Now we\u2019re shopping for a pants suit, button-down blouse, and some classy but sensible flats to go with the suit.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should get a pencil skirt too, to go with the suit jacket,\u201d Karen says.<br /> <br /> \u201cReally? I don\u2019t know about that. I can\u2019t remember the last time I wore a skirt.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeriously? As tall as you are, with those nice long legs? You\u2019d rock a pencil skirt.\u201d<br /> <br /> I must be blushing, because Karen gives me an appraising look.<br /> <br /> \u201cSorry,\u201d she says. \u201cI wasn\u2019t flirting with you. I know Sara\u2019s been a little\u2026forward. If it makes you uncomfortable, I\u2019ll talk to her about it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s okay. I like Sara. She\u2019s really made me feel welcome, and the flirting is flattering. But I get the impression she\u2026gets around a bit. And she seems really committed to you and Natalie. I\u2019m not really\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not really willing to share your lover. I remember you saying that in the hot tub the other day. It\u2019s cool. I mean, most people wouldn\u2019t be comfortable with the way things work for Sara, Natalie and me. I totally get it. But you\u2019re into girls, right? Are you looking for a relationship?\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m pretty sure I\u2019m blushing again. \u201cWell, I haven\u2019t been with anyone since my last girlfriend left me in Portland.\u201d The memory of Cassidy turning her back and walking away in the rain tugs at my wounded heart, probing scars that still have yet to heal. I hesitate before continuing, and Karen thinks she\u2019s upset me.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I didn\u2019t mean to pry,\u201d she says. \u201cI just wanted to know if I should introduce you to people you might like. You know, when we go out clubbing. I\u2019m not trying to play matchmaker or anything. But it doesn\u2019t hurt to make introductions, right?\u201d Karen smiles encouragingly.<br /> <br /> I smile back. \u201cThat would be good,\u201d I say hesitantly. Then, more confidently, \u201cYeah, I\u2019d like that. But the pickings must be pretty slim. So far, just about every young woman we\u2019ve meet seems fatally attracted to Natalie. I can\u2019t compete with that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you kidding?\u201d Karen replies. \u201cYou\u2019re gorgeous, and despite what you\u2019ve seen so far, there are plenty of lovely ladies out there who aren\u2019t caught up in Natalie\u2019s orbit. Or Sara\u2019s for that matter.\u201d<br /> <br /> I laugh a bit at that, and it feels good. I had no idea the Middle Shadows would welcome me so warmly. I certainly don\u2019t deserve it. But I\u2019m grateful.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Doc is fuming again. I think his calm moments must be the exception, not the rule. This time, he\u2019s perfectly justified, though. More importantly, it looks like I might have a target, and this will be a very challenging hunt.<br /> <br /> <i>A challening hunt indeed. This is a bold opportunity for us. Perhaps I was wrong about this krewe, perhaps not. We will see whether they embrace the hunt or just talk about it.</i><br /> <br /> The Huntess\u2019 whispers are laced with derision, but I can also sense her aniticpation. I\u2019m also eager for this hunt. The prey is a Balehound, a corrupt, dangerous werewolf that uses evil spirits to do his bidding. His spirits possess people, giving them supernatural abilities that force others to indulge their darkest vices. Their powers might be a bit different, but otherwise these \u201cPossessed\u201d aren\u2019t that different from sin-eaters. At least, the similarities were enough to convince the Pure in Glenwood that we are working with this Balehound, and that\u2019s why they attacked us at the church a couple of days ago. It was a misunderstanding, but it\u2019s probably too late for reconciliation now. I mean, I almost killed two of them., and they aren\u2019t likely to forget that.<br /> <i><br /> It was us or them.</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress is right, and I don\u2019t regret my actions. Still, it\u2019s going to be hard tracking down this Balehound if we can\u2019t move around Glenwood openly. I could do it alone, invisible and unseen. And if werewolves did come for me, I could get away by merging with the winds or turning into a flock of birds. But I can\u2019t speak for the rest of the krewe, and I don\u2019t think they\u2019re keen on letting me investigate Glenwood on my own.<br /> <br /> Apparently there\u2019s something fishy going on next door too. The elder werewolf who lives there has a gorgeous young girlfriend named Angelique. She\u2019s also a werewolf\u2014some kind of mystic. Doc says it\u2019s a major taboo for werewolves to sleep with each other, and the krewe is considering the possibility that Angelique is the Balehound.<br /> <br /> I tell the krewe that this Balehound sounds like worthy prey, and definitely someone who deserves to die. Doc is the first to agree with me. The others notice a predatory glint in my eyes, but this time they approve. Natalie even says something about Red Riding Hood taking the fight to the wolf, I guess because I\u2019m a redhead. I kind of like the idea, but it reminds me of Cassidy. Her geist, Red Hood, was basically a victimized but still defiant Red Riding Hood. Then I notice the look on Sara\u2019s face, which suggests she has something altogether kinkier in mind when she thinks of me as Red Riding Hood. I blush again and forget all about Cassidy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 9th 2010<br /> <br /> -Time for our meeting.<br /> <br /> -Meeting is 4 kids, an ancient Banshee, and us.<br /> <br /> -Good times.<br /> <br /> -Doc takes charge!<br /> <br /> -Seems to be going well.<br /> <br /> -Hrm<br /> <br /> -Okay that could have gone worse.<br /> <br /> -ooooh <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Okay that conversation I have had before <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Oh Sara, you big silly.<br /> <br /> -For now, though, Karen and I are seeing Ms. Pouty.<br /> <br /> -I even got to walk out of the house before Karen collared me this time.<br /> <br /> -Mistress is kind &lt;3<br /> <br /> -Awww Tatum is dressed like a boi.<br /> <br /> -Karen and Tatum keep eating off of my plate. I am a growing girl.<br /> <br /> -Back home.<br /> <br /> -Such tasty boots\u2026<br /> <br /> <br /> November 10th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I got phone privileges back! Yay!<br /> <br /> -Now if I can get clothing privileges back we can go home.<br /> <br /> -I am not doing a Vlog in the altogether.<br /> <br /> -Karen will be hanging out with Alice.<br /> <br /> -Or maybe Karen will just leave me here without privileges.<br /> <br /> -Uh oh\u2026<br /> <br /> -Okay finally back at the Twilight Zone.<br /> <br /> -Tatum needs to remember I am not a bendy toy. I like to think I am flexible but I have limits.<br /> <br /> -In other news ow, my shoulder.<br /> <br /> -Vlog is up.<br /> <br /> -To the music room!<br /> <br /> -Yay Sara in the music room!<br /> <br /> -Karen is back! Jam Session!<br /> <br /> -Doc is unhappy.<br /> <br /> -Poor Doc<br /> <br /> -Damn Werewolf Problems\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXII</i><br /> <br /> Some of the Bale Hound stuff comes from <i>Predators</i>. Other stuff from <i>Book of Spirits</i> and <i>Inferno</i>.<br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add beyond that. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T19:48:47-08:00","id":340376,"title":"","content":"#Werewolf Problems? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-30T15:01:33-08:00","id":355159,"title":"","content":"The Krewe continues investigating this whole Bale Hound thing, and makes some discoveries about the girl next door. Doc\u2019s player had to miss, but that should be a pretty temporary thing. Let\u2019s move on to Sara and Alice\u2019s accounts of the session.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, I have a new project. It\u2019s going to be rough - it will require some serious smooth talking and precise timing, which I have in spades of course, and some intense self-deprivation, which is not something I\u2019m good at. Though maybe, when it\u2019s all said and done, I can convince them into a threesome. And good lords and ladies above and below, what a threesome. Especially if I can get that Red Riding Hood outfit for Alice. You know, the one Katie wears when we\u2019re at a not-so-family friendly venue, where she does the thing with the knife?<br /> <br /> Believe it or not, this does follow directly from what I was writing about last time. Remember I mentioned that a divergent element of an old family might be undercover as our next door neighbor? Turns out, she\u2019s not, or at least, if she is, I have *completely* lost my touch at reading people. She\u2019s also totally into Alice, but I\u2019ll get into that later.<br /> <br /> Her boyfriend is also not one of the bad guys, which is really good, as he\u2019s one of the old guard of the family. Tangling with him would likely be fatal, to us. We went over, ostensibly, to introduce Alice to him, as he is... protective of his territory. You can tell by the warning shot he fires over the head of anyone who sets foot in his lawn, darn kids or no. We came around with Simon and some of Alexia\u2019s heavenly cookies, so there was only the one shot.<br /> <br /> He actually brought up Doc\u2019s beat up van unprompted, so we told him what had gone down, and tried to size up his and Angelique\u2019s (that would be the smoking hot brunette with excellent taste in redheads) reactions to the whole thing. They passed muster, thus, the conclusion that they were on the up and up. They offered to help even, an offer Angelique reiterated when she stopped by to return the tupperware the cookies had been in.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s in a particular place to help out, since her mentor, unbeknownst to her until the end, was one of these undercover turncoats. She\u2019d gotten run out of town, sort of a \u2018sins of the father\u2019 type thing. I\u2019m convinced, personally, that she didn\u2019t know what was up with him and also that she was hiding something from us. Probably that along with her mentor, this turncoat had also been her lover. Which also might have something to do with her getting run out of town.<br /> <br /> See, these guys don\u2019t really like keeping it in even the mostly metaphorical family. Relationships like the one Angelique has now, and the one I figure she had with her mentor, are definitely verboten. Now, our neighbor is powerful enough to pretty much tell the others to go fuck themselves when they make a big deal about it and get away with it, and normally I\u2019d be all about it. Any rule that says there\u2019s something wrong with two (or more) consenting adults making a meaningful connection (and having all sorts of fun doing it) is no rule for me. In this particular case though, leaving aside their personal prejudices, I\u2019m not sure this is a great relationship for Angelique. Not every connection is a personally uplifting one and from some of the things she said, I think this one is chafing and setting off some negative instincts that it\u2019s important to listen too. And if my purely speculative assumption about her old relationship is correct, it sets up an unfortunate pattern.<br /> <br /> Plus, she was totally digging Alice and Alice was *definitely* into her. Alice could hardly keep her eyes off her. (And her hair. And her legs. And her eyes. And her legs. She has nice legs, is what I\u2019m saying. And a hot nature, to judge by the length of her shorts this fine November evening.) Alice might take some convincing even so, being even less copacetic than me about breaking up an already in place relationship and much less ok with exploring the fact that Angelique\u2019s description of said already in place relationship was just this side of vaguely open. Alice did invite Angelique to go hiking, all unprompted. (At the time. Karen might have left a seed of an idea there earlier.) Sadly, thanks to family politics, she can\u2019t. :-(<br /> <br /> In other news, Tatum\u2019s parents have no problem flirting outrageously with the married women their daughter is sleeping with, and offering them pot. They sound absolutely brilliant. I might have to actually swing that invite next time.<br /> <br /> Also - also - teenagers + telekinesis with Hulk-like strength (emotional triggers included) = holy shit what the fuck? Natalie got an emergency text from a friend of a client\u2019s who had gotten into a fight with said client - the client Clarissa's boyfriend had gotten a little fresh with the friend Deanna and Clarissa got it in her head that it was Deanna\u2019s fault, as one does, when one is young and foolish. Of course, one usually doesn\u2019t then get to respond by telekinetically throwing a car at the offending friend.<br /> <br /> So we headed over to see if we could defuse things. Alice immediately grabbed her axe, mostly just by habit, I think, but it did leave me with this awesome mental image of Alice standing there all tuff, having just chopped the car that had been flying towards us into two pieces in mid air, while the two pieces go barrelling harmlessly past. OK, that looks a little silly now that I\u2019ve written it out, but it was a wonderful image at the time.<br /> <br /> Natalie managed to talk Clarissa down without too much trouble and Alice got to be all protector-y over Deanna. Clarissa\u2019s not a bad kid or anything, just emotionally volatile, which is dangerous paired with burgeoning psychic talent. The display wore her out though, since throwing cars is pretty far past her usual capabilities. She passed out shortly after she calmed down. She does need to do something, and probably pretty damn soon, to get her emotions under control a little. The poor kid. 17 can be a hard enough time as it is, it can\u2019t help to have physics take a hike whenever you get upset. And on a less personal note, there\u2019s only so many Wookalar attacks/freak localized tornadoes that can happen in a neighborhood before the mundanes start getting suspicious. This time however, one of the policeman left it absolutely convinced that some kind of pig man ghost thing called a Wookalar was loose, and the other left convinced it was absolutely anything but that.<br /> <br /> With all that, Clarissa hadn\u2019t done any damage to their friendship, so we left Clarissa in Deanna\u2019s concerned care. Everyone was ready for a night in, And Alice likes scary movies, so we decided on Hellraiser. I too like scary movies, provided a pretty person to hide behind during the, you know, scary parts. And I had my pick there, even if I didn\u2019t want to interrupt Chandra and Alexia\u2019s make out time. There was even a Tatum, as she stopped by to apologize to Natalie for something her mom said and got roped into staying the night.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which, I am the luckiest girl.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> Alexia, Simon and Sara have taken me next door to meet their neighbor, Mr. Malard. They say he\u2019s a terrifying elder werewolf, and though I believe them, it\u2019s hard to reconcile that with the doddering old man munching cookies in front of me. Honestly, though, my attention isn\u2019t on Malard. It\u2019s on the gorgeous woman sitting beside him. Her name is Angelique, and there is an outside chance she might be the Balehound we\u2019re hunting. That\u2019s why I\u2019m watching her so carefully. I\u2019m looking for a tell, something to let me know if she really is the Balehound or if we\u2019re barking up the wrong tree.<br /> <i><br /> Is that really the reason you keep staring at her?</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress knows me too well. She\u2019s right. I\u2019m watching Angelique because she takes my breath away. She\u2019s enchanting, with beautiful, dark eyes, silky hair, and shapely legs that make my heart skip a beat. Sara wasn\u2019t kidding when she told me Mr. Malard\u2019s werewolf girlfriend was a knockout. I sure hope she\u2019s not the Balehound, because I\u2019d hate to have to kill her.<br /> <i><br /> Hate is such a strong word\u2026</i><br /> <br /> As if on cue, Alexia mentions the Balehound to Malard and Angelique. Sara and I both study Angelique\u2019s reaction carefully, and I\u2019ve even unlocked my Oracle, so my hunter\u2019s instincts are sharp. She becomes interested, intrigued, but there\u2019s no hint of guilt, no sudden sense of fear. Much to my relief, Angelique isn\u2019t the Balehound. I\u2019m sure of it. I share a glance with Sara and can tell that she\u2019s come to the same conclusion.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m able to relax a little after that and converse more freely with Angelique. She offers to help us with the Balehound situation. I gather she\u2019s something of an occultist among her kind, and she might know things that can help us. Her interest isn\u2019t wholly innocent\u2014I get the impression that she\u2019s drawn to power. But I do think she means well, and I\u2019m not exactly in a position to throw stones.<br /> <br /> We finish our conversation and get up to leave when Angelique reiterates how much she would like to help us and writes down her email address in case we need to contact her. I step forward a bit too eagerly to take the slip of paper, and I cringe inwardly. I mean, sure, Angelique was making eyes at me too, but her old boyfriend is right there, and I\u2019m sure I look like an idiot. The fact that Sara gives me a sly smile on the way out of the house doesn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Apparently my misstep with the email address earlier didn\u2019t leave a bad impression with Angelique. At least I hope not. She\u2019s come to visit us now. We all settle into the TV room, and Angelique begins telling us more about herself. It strikes me as odd that she\u2019s dressed in shorts and a t-shirt here at the end of November. That might fly where I\u2019m from, but I\u2019m freezing in this New England chill. Angelique doesn\u2019t seem bothered, though, and I\u2019m not really complaining. The shorts do show off her gorgeous legs. I wish my legs looked that amazing.<br /> <br /> I also can\u2019t help staring at her enchanting eyes, or the coy way the corners of her mouth turn up with the hint of a smile as she talks. Or the way she absently brushes her hair over one ear and then, as if remembering that she\u2019s supposed to be mysterious, brushes it forward against so that it shades part of her face. I think she knows I\u2019m watching her, and I think she likes the attention.<br /> <br /> Angelique tells us that the reason she\u2019s so interested in this Balehound is because she was trained by a Balehound. She didn\u2019t know it at the time, but her mentor, another older werewolf like Malard, was a Balehound and was secretly training her to become one when he was found out. His pack destroyed him and drove Angelique away, fearing that she would follow in her mentor\u2019s footsteps. She managed to find a place with Malard\u2019s pack, but most of the werewolves around here don\u2019t trust her. She\u2019s tainted by her mentor\u2019s corruption. I sense that she\u2019s scared that some part of her wants the power of a Balehound, and she\u2019s worried about what would happen if that dark desire were to take root. I can identify with that. Sounds like we have a few things in common. At least Angelique\u2019s mentor isn\u2019t whispering into her head constantly. Thank god for small favors.<br /> <br /> I think Angelique can tell that I\u2019m sympathetic, but I\u2019m not sure because I\u2019ve gone all sheepish again, which happens when I\u2019m around a woman that I find really attractive. I\u2019m darn sure Angelique has noticed that I\u2019m into her, and I think she\u2019s into me too. But she and Malard are an item, and I\u2019m not in the habit of butting into other people\u2019s relationships. I definitely don\u2019t want to be a part of any cheating. Still, I ask about her relationship with Malard, hoping that the krewe has misunderstood the whole thing. But no, she says that she and Malard are lovers, though they do have a bit of an \u201cunderstanding.\u201d I get the impression that it\u2019s a little bit like the understanding Natalie, Karen and Sara have. Sadly, that\u2019s not really going to work for me.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, werewolves aren\u2019t supposed to take each other as lovers. It\u2019s taboo for some reason. Of course, no one in the krewe cares about that taboo, but for some reason I can\u2019t shake the feeling that Angelique\u2019s relationship with Malard is bad for her. It would probably be in her best interest if she were out of it.<br /> <br /> Wait, what am I thinking? Am I seriously considering breaking up a happy couple just because I\u2019m developing a crush on this woman? I\u2019m a terrible person. And so is Sara, apparently, since she keeps encouraging me with her sly glances.<br /> <br /> And yet I still ask Angelique if she wants to join Sara, Karen and me for hike in Sleeping Giant State Park on Friday. I\u2019m really hoping she\u2019ll say yes. But\u2026she can\u2019t. A different werewolf pack holds that territory, and they aren\u2019t keen on other werewolves intruding on their turf, especially ones they despise, like Angelique.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s okay, though. Angelique knows how to sniff out signs of Balehound activity. All we have to do is point her in the right direction. So if we can find some place we think the Balehound has been active, it will give me an excuse to call her up and\u2026and what? Ask her out? I can\u2019t do that. She\u2019s with Malard.<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or are all the really amazing ladies in this town are already spoken for?<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXXIII</i><br /> <br /> Not a great deal to add to this. Mostly an RP session, and ran just a bit shorter as we were down Doc\u2019s player.<br /> <br /> The Officers Tart and McReedy showed up again, which was the first time inna while. Tart you may recall was the Wookalar obsessed one who Simon created an illusion for him to fight while dealing with issues at Albertus Magnus, while McCreedy was the skeptic and anti-psi.<br /> <br /> So, if you enjoy these sorts of stories, I was sent by a reader of the <b>Geist</b> game a link for the Youtube series <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLbvYWjKFvS5rX2yv-k5AJ8oxPoZ9zHcpe\" target=\"_blank\">Carmilla</a>, which has no Sin-Eater types but maps pretty close to the sort of stories I tend to tell, so if you enjoy this, you may enjoy that. Also, it has a <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AObdNbNYoiQ\" target=\"_blank\">Christmas Episode</a> that takes place post series. Contrary to the description, it does not seem to be as much based on the novella as inspired by it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Happy New Year, update in about 2 weeks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-31T18:38:11-08:00","id":356162,"title":"","content":"Don't worry Alice. Wolves like sheep.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-12T02:47:41-08:00","id":367174,"title":"","content":"Ready to check on the Krewe? They are ready for you. Sudden combat this time. No Doc's Log as his player has a lot going on atm.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> I need to come up with a cool superhero teacher name. And a catchphrase. The X-Men have those, right? We\u2019ll have appearances to maintain, after all. You see, Alexia has had an awesome idea. She\u2019s been worried about Clarissa, and the whole problem with suppressing emotions because they\u2019re dangerous, especially when you\u2019re a teenager. Also, we actually know a number of young, not supernaturally experienced touched, as well as a couple of safe, smart, very experienced supernatural folks. So... why not get them together? Let the inexperienced ones have a core group of folks like them, who they can be themselves around and also a collection of mentors. Even if we aren\u2019t all touched in the same way (none of them are death touched, for example), there are enough touchstones and baselines between us that we could do them some good. Deanna\u2019s on board and thinks she can talk Clarissa into it, as long as there are cute boys involved. Priorities, you know. But it seems like a good start, and a good plan. The whole discussion did lead us to a compare/contrast session concerning the Hulk philosophy versus the X-Men philosophy. Which is how I know Karen has a serious crush on She-Hulk. Which is hilarious. And adorable.<br /> <br /> As to other projects mentioned before, either I\u2019m so good it\u2019s scary or I\u2019m entirely extraneous. Me being me, you know I prefer the former. Corrupter of Maidens, they call me. Well, they call me that somewhere, I\u2019m sure. ;-) Of course, the less than overt nature of my influence on the situation, and the fact I may or may not have had any influence over it at all does make it difficult to angle for the \u2018thanks for hooking us up\u2019 threesome. Still, I am nothing if not full of hope.<br /> <br /> At this point, you have probably sussed out that my two unattainable lovelies, Alice and Angelique have, to all appearances, hit things off quite well, despite my being called away to sadly pressing errands. Angelique was ostensibly over to get caught up on our sleuthing, so perhaps I ought start with that. It\u2019s how our day started as well, so doubly appropriate. Alice has latched on to this investigation hard, and not just because it gets her closer to Angelique, unless I miss my guess. I get the idea it\u2019s sorta more in her bailiwick than some of what we\u2019ve done so far. To be fair, we do a very different kind of thing than I did on my own too, but my bailiwick is performing in front of a different audience each night, so the fish out of water experiences aren\u2019t really comparable. I do wonder if her old troupe just focused on these particular kinds of jobs, or if they kept her in a box, like a sharp tool they pulled out when necessary. I wonder if they are puzzled at the fate she found.<br /> <br /> ...That is unkind and unfair. We do what we can, when we can, and I don\u2019t know a whole lot about how things were there. And regardless, I for one am glad fate led her here. She was amazing today at the Red Robin we met our contact Raul at. He\u2019d been followed by some minions of the baddies, sort of spiritual suicide bombers. Well, the suicide bit isn\u2019t really right - it was maybe more like a spiritual deadman\u2019s switch? Anyways, I got the wind knocked out of me when the first one went (they dogpiled Raul and we jumped in to help) so Alice kept trying to shield me, bodily, from the rest. I kinda screwed up her heroic gesture by moving around her to finish one off instead of letting them try to rip into her again. Not that she got anything more than bruised herself. Lords and ladies, she\u2019s tough.<br /> <br /> So, she was awesome, Alexia and Doc were pretty damn badass themselves, Natalie was on overwatch and Raul held up his end like a boss considering he got torn into himself. The videotape he was bringing us even came out of it completely intact. It was a surveillance tape of the first attack, the one on the civilians of the family, so between that and the attack on us, we\u2019ve got more of a clue than we had this morning. The fact that Raul was followed at all was telling, as he didn\u2019t even let anyone know he was going but us. Alexia used her Sight to check if his phone was bugged, which it wasn\u2019t, so that seemed to suggest that it wasn\u2019t actually a traitor in the family. It\u2019s not hard proof though, as he did ask for evidence, so he might have been being followed on general principles, even without knowledge of this particular meetup. It could also have simply been bad timing, and they were waiting for someone expendable to leave town to stir up trouble. Alternately, as Alice pointed out, the attack might have been staged for our benefit and Raul is the traitor. I hope not. He was kinda cute, in an incredibly acerbic way. Emcee would *love* him. Way old school jester schtick.<br /> <br /> Alice was super adorable when we got home. She called up Angelique right away, just to keep her updated, naturally. When Angelique said she\u2019d be over to \u2018consult\u2019 in ~15 minutes, Alice quickly let us know and rushed off to freshen herself up for her lady. After hearing what we had, Angelique had an idea of what the baddies end goal might be, slightly beyond \u2018cause trouble\u2019, but she needs to Look things over before she could say for sure. There was some serious flirting going on there - I have never before been so intrigued by a \u2018scouting mission\u2019, that required tuff girl \u2018protection\u2019. Between Angelique\u2019s smolder and Alice\u2019s blushing awkwardness, there was enough heat to warm even that big old house a few degrees.<br /> <br /> So here in a bit, we head back to Glenwood. Karen is not happy, but I believe Natalie and I have \u2018earned\u2019 clothing privileges back. I teased her a bit about leaving without them, but sneaky reconnaissance mission and hot naked girl don\u2019t generally go so well together. With any luck though, that will be a simple look-see, and we will have no pressing issues that get in the way of our hiking trip tomorrow. Alice owes Karen and I some gossip, I believe.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> Angelique is here again, at the mansion. We invited her over to update her on our hunt for the Balehound. As Doc and Sara explain what happened outside of town at a Red Robin restaurant, I realize that there\u2019s some serious chemistry forming between Angelique and me. The way she keeps cutting me looks with her bedroom eyes just makes me melt, but I try not to let it show.<br /> <br /> Not that she isn\u2019t focused on what we\u2019re telling her. She listens carefully as Doc explains how we met his contact, Rawl, at the restaurant, but the meeting was interrupted when we were attacked by three of these \u201cClaimed\u201d or \u201cPossessed\u201d or whatever they\u2019re called. We made pretty short work of them, and it felt good to unleash my axe against some victims\u2014I mean enemies\u2014who really deserved it.<br /> <br /> <i>If justification is all you need, then I\u2019m sure we can find plenty of that. </i><br /> <br /> The Huntress is trying to make me doubt myself, since she knows that my self-doubt puts her in control. I try to ignore her. It\u2019s easier than it used to be now that I\u2019m surrounded by friends. And it helps to be able to focus on Angelique.<br /> <br /> Sara was hurt badly in the encounter with the Claimed, but Doc fixed her up nicely. I tried to protect her, but this time she wasn\u2019t having it. She\u2019s brave, I\u2019ll give her that. The rest of us fared much better, though. I ended up on fire when the Claimed exploded as we killed them, but it wasn\u2019t all that bad. Mostly it just burned away the grave dust of my Shroud, and Natalie summoned some rain to quench the flames. Sara was concerned, but on the way home I told her it wasn\u2019t the first time I\u2019d been on fire. Some victims are surprisingly resourceful. When I said as much, Alexia got pretty upset. I tried to explain that the victims I was referring to had deserved it, but she didn\u2019t want to hear it. It really bothers her when I talk about killing. I envy her sensitivity.<br /> <br /> It doesn\u2019t take Doc long to finish recounting the day\u2019s events to Angelique, and we decide to head back to Red Robin later on tonight to let Angelique look for anything important that might help us track down the Balehound. We have a few hours to kill, so Angelique asks me for a tour of the mansion. I\u2019m more than happy to oblige, though I warn her that I\u2019m a newcomer here too, so I don\u2019t really know it all that well myself. That doesn\u2019t matter, though, because I know what she really wants is some time alone with me, and just knowing that makes my heart soar.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> This thing with Angelique is moving fast. Really fast. I\u2019ve never been in a relationship that\u2019s moved this quickly, and this isn\u2019t even a relationship! Yet. I guess that\u2019s how things work around here. But I\u2019m not sure what to do. All during the tour of the mansion, I want to take Angelique\u2019s hand. I get the feeling that she wants me to take her hand, but then I remember that she lives with her boyfriend next door, and I doubt myself. I don\u2019t want to be a home-wrecker.<br /> <br /> <i>Her \u201cboyfriend\u201d is not someone with whom we want to tangle.</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress\u2019 warning rings true. I try to rein in my feelings, but it\u2019s hard when Angelique keeps looking at me with smoldering eyes.<br /> <br /> We reach the library, and Angelique\u2019s interest in me is temporarily distracted by her fascination with the wealth of knowledge there. I\u2019m both relieved and envious. I\u2019m also a little nervous. I\u2019m not really the academic sort. What if Angelique realizes that and loses her interest in me? I really don\u2019t want that to happen. Or maybe I do. I mean, getting involved with her is a bad idea, isn\u2019t it? At least as long as she\u2019s with Malard, anyway. I think about testing the waters with some comment about how I don\u2019t really spend any time in the library, or maybe some line about being lost when it comes to research. But I think better of it. Even though I rationally know I shouldn\u2019t get involved with Angelique, I can\u2019t bring myself to close that door.<br /> <br /> After the library, I end the tour at my room. I wasn\u2019t really thinking about it, and as soon as we arrive and step inside, I realize that I\u2019m probably sending the wrong message to Angelique. Or the right one. She glances about the room and then her smoldering bedroom eyes fix on me again.<br /> <br /> Definitely the right message.<br /> <br /> I sit down on my bed and say something about how the room\u2019s a lot bigger and fancier than anything I\u2019ve ever had before, but at least the bed\u2019s comfortable. Immediately after the words leave my mouth, I inwardly cringe. Without even meaning to, I\u2019m coming on as strong as she is! There\u2019s no doubt about it, I\u2019m completely losing my head over this girl. Angelique takes a cautious step toward me, and realize it\u2019s now or never.<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, Angelique, I am seriously into you. I can\u2019t even describe the effect you\u2019re having on me. But I\u2014.\u201d<br /> <br /> I had intended to say, \u201cbut I don\u2019t want to break up your relationship with Malard,\u201d but I don\u2019t get that far. As soon as she hears me say I\u2019m into her, she\u2019s on me and we\u2019re kissing, caressing, stripping each other. All my reservations dissolve in the face of Angelique\u2019s wild and unrestrained passion. It\u2019s obvious that she doesn\u2019t really have any experience with other women, but it\u2019s equally obvious that she\u2019s been bi-curious for a long time. It feels so real and right and amazing.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Afterward as we lay in bed cuddling, I remember that I haven\u2019t told Angelique about my past. She doesn\u2019t know about all the people I\u2019ve murdered. I think she\u2019ll understand, but I don\u2019t want to tell her just yet. I don\u2019t want to ruin the afterglow.<br /> <br /> <i>You\u2019re more worried about how she\u2019ll feel about your lack of education than about the fact that you are a cold-blooded killer. What does that say about you? Or her? Where does your heart really lie, dear Alice?</i><br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Natalie should be reporting again starting next time, in theory. Ditto Doc<br /> <br /> This time they went up against so Inferno-esque Possessed, who did\u2026okay given what they were up against. I really was not expecting a close fight, and did not get one.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add. Comments and Questions Welcome<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T02:39:36-08:00","id":382831,"title":"","content":"Okay, new session, new journals. First off it\u2019s the Doc Countdown as his player catches us up to the present. Doc covers several sessions right off, then he, Sara and Natalie cover the last one. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2300 Hours, Wednesday, November 10, 2010<br /> <br /> I have got to keep my temper at least hidden better.<br /> <br /> When I went in earlier to tell the Krewe what I learned, Nightshade took one look at me and dove under the piano. I must have reacted poorly to that because Bright Eyes moved between us then looked like she might join her.<br /> <br /> Once I got everyone out from hiding, I explained what I learned. Axe reacted with her all guns blazing approach before I shot her a look, but I softened it by letting her know the next time we went to Glenwood, I would be packing silver.<br /> <br /> About that time, the doorbell rang and I found Tavia speaking with the delivery driver, who trying to escape back to get the parts for the van. I signed for everything then helped him bring everything into the carriage house. Snowflake and I wired some ballast lighting in there so that took most of my evening. At this point, the van is mostly back to 100%, if only with shitty parts. I\u2019ll wait to try and use my alchemy on things when I haven\u2019t worked for multiple hours beforehand.<br /> <br /> I came back in to find Tantrum, Axe, Bright Eyes, Nightshade, Cupcake, and Chandra all watching Hellraiser. Well, Cupcake and Chandra were watching as much as they watch any movie when they have the perfect opportunity to make out. Bright Eyes was doing more \u201chiding\u201d behind Tantrum than anything. Really Axe was the only one watching the movie.<br /> <br /> I think I should probably get a shower and find something to use for comparison when I enhance the van to be less shitty.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Thursday, November 11, 2010<br /> <br /> I got up this morning planning to call Rawl for more details before discussing a scouting mission with Axe. The day has kind of sprinted from there. I came down for breakfast to find the Krewe seemingly looking for something to do.<br /> <br /> Last night while I was out working on the van, lots went down in New Haven. Our friendly neighborhood psychic teen raged out and threw a car over an imagined betrayal, Angelique has decided to either trust us completely or is using us to draw all of Connecticut into a downward spiral of depravity, and it seems her and Axe have \u201ca thing.\u201d I blame Bright Eyes.<br /> <br /> So when I came down and mentioned calling Rawl again, I got a list of questions Axe nearly demanded to know.<br /> <br /> \u00b7 Where did the attacks on the families happen?<br /> \u00b7 Who was attacked?<br /> \u00b7 What did the Claimed look like?<br /> <br /> I knew that I wasn\u2019t going to get anywhere with where they happened because that would be telling us where their families lived or frequented. I\u2019m not super paranoid and I wouldn\u2019t do that. But I asked when I called anyway.<br /> <br /> It was around 0930 Hours when I called. It was pretty obvious that he was just getting up and almost obvious that he was hung over. He explained that he\u2019s had a long night out \u201cwerewolfing\u201d and I knew how these things went. The things he was mumbling under his breath and the sounds of garbage rummaging suggested he didn\u2019t know where he was right at the moment. However he was very aware of my requests. Rawl said that he knew his Tribesmen were dumb but no so dumb as to not have any security. He would happily dub a copy of the VHS tape which had surveillance footage of the Claimed. For obvious reasons, he asked that we meet in neutral territory, which was more than acceptable to me. Checking Google Maps, I found a Red Robin about an hour away which would be about half way and in no territory that either of us cared about. He gave me his email address, <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#fc958f88949d888f95908a998ebc9b919d9590d29f9391\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"e188929589809592888d978493a1868c80888dcf828e8c\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a> just in case. I also tried to reassure him that if anyone attacked him for any reason, they would answer to me. With that, I got off the phone.<br /> <br /> When I turned back to the Krewe, Cupcake quickly informed me that she was starting a school for the \u201cgifted\u201d (read supernatural) and wanted to run it out of the Firehouse Church. She began listing off all the wild or new powered (mostly young) people we knew just in the area. Then she noted several of the more established people that we could trust which could possibly help as teachers or mentors. It wasn\u2019t the worst idea I\u2019d heard but we had more pressing issues at hand.<br /> I knew better than to think the Predator Kings would just let Rawl go off with film identifying their families without a guarantee that no further harm could come from it. That meant I was fully expecting an ambush. I told the others as much and the whole Krewe got up to come with me. My Krewe is awesome.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1515 Hours, Thursday, November 11, 2010<br /> <br /> Well went about as well as I expected, but for very different reasons.<br /> <br /> When I got to the Red Robin I left the rest of the Krewe in the van and walked in keeping an eye open for any slightly familiar scowling faces. What I found was Rawl looking...wrong. As soon as he caught my eye, he shook his head very slightly then looked at another open table. The vibe was just bad all the way around. I wasn\u2019t sure what was happening but I took the empty table and tried not to seem to interested in my contact. I very carefully related the situation back to the Krewe through my ear curl and told Axe to hold her position. I could just see her in my mind\u2019s eye grabbing her namesake. After a few minutes Rawl stood without speaking and walked past. I glanced back to see him counting down on his fingers as we made his way to the door. I unlocked my Primeval Shroud and followed. But I didn\u2019t have to go far. As soon as he hit the door, three separate columns of heat haze appeared in front of Rawl. By the time I cleared the door and my Krewe made to over, the haze had solidified into a young caucasian couple and an older black man. All their hands ended in long yellow claws that didn\u2019t look natural or healthy. Rawl responded by shifting into his warform. The three apparent Claimed all moved to attack the werewolf as the diners all screamed and panicked.<br /> <br /> Axe flew into attack, finally getting to jump into a fray. Her attacks left the older black man with wounds that gave off heat and the same haze as before, much like we leak Plasm-smoke from our wounds. I had sworn anyone who attacked Rawl would answer to me and I intended to make good on that oath. Turning toward the woman, I thrust my hand out then ripped it back, feeling the blood within her body obey my Stigmata Rage. Her facial expression fell slack after she felt the massive hemorrhage. Blood flowed from her ears, nose, and dulled eyes. Before she could even fall her corpse exploded. The flames were a surprise, washing over us and setting our clothes and hair on fire. I wasn\u2019t armored against flames so this would be a problem before the fight was over. More importantly, Rawl was being hit with the flames as well as the vicious yellow claws and already didn\u2019t look well. Before I could move, lightning struck the younger man attacking our werewolf associate. Cupcake drew the black man\u2019s attention so I charged the last Claimed and hurled him backward with my Plasm-enhanced strength. Before I could reach him again, a cold rain poured from the sky, quenching the fire still burning on each of us. Bright Eyes darted around Cupcake and stabbed the black man. The explosion lit the fires again, but I had target and a personal grievance. Beyond my promise to protect Rawl, I had not yet consciously understood why I was so angry. It was not until I drew my arm back and felt my Rage channelling down my arm that it hit me. These Claimed were nothing more than spiritual suicide bombers, laying a trap to confuse and terrify. The similarities to my own personal death triggered a part of me I generally keep buried around the others. My fist slammed into the Claimed with all the force of my Rage, rupturing his vessels and organs. The fiery explosion wrapped around me like an unwanted lover and I took a disgusted step back before brushing the embers out. Plasm flowed into me from the deaths as I silently returned to my Krewe. Rawl, Axe, and Bright Eyes cut off the escape of one of the fire spirits in Twilight. If the Balehound expected information, he\u2019d be waiting for a while before that particular spirit could talk again.<br /> <br /> Rawl\u2019s wounds had not healed completely, but oddly they looked more like another werewolf had slashed him. It was then that I realized this was a setup. Rawl confirmed that we had dealt with vice spirits and that those were some of the Claimed which attacked his people. Axe stood by looking very suspicious while the werewolf explained that he realized something was wrong before I arrived. Cupcake object read his cell phone but found nothing unusual. That meant there could still be a traitor among the Predator Kings. That was not a good situation for any of us.<br /> <br /> Cupcake went back into the kitchen and made us all some food while Rawl called for a ride. Axe surprised me with her quick thinking to trash the security system. There were still some customers cowering under tables, but they wouldn\u2019t remember what happened later. And since they stayed inside, they weren\u2019t injured. Axe noted that the police must hate this place. We all looked around and realized that no officials had arrived. Once we knew Rawl was safely back with his people, and I had moved my van out of sight, we loaded up and headed back home before we pushed our luck.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Thursday, November 11, 2010<br /> <br /> We are about to leave for Glenwood again. I\u2019d say we were crazy, but wait it gets better.<br /> <br /> We got back and made sure everyone was properly patched up, then while Karen \u201chad words\u201d with Nightshade and Bright Eyes, Axe called Angelique. That led to another visit and more discussion. I learned that Angelique\u2019s tribe is called the Bone Shadows and that she is either nuts incredibly brave. I realize she needs to stop the Balehound for personal reasons, but she wants to go with us back into Glenwood (knowing we\u2019re on a watchlist already) to investigate the Claimed. I know it\u2019s rude, but I\u2019m not going back without packing silver. Hope she doesn\u2019t get too upset.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0245 Hours, Friday, November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a night of firsts.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes and I went around gathering Plasm while Cupcake rented a passenger van for the weekend. Angelique noted that she would need to keep a low profile, which I already understood, but that put Axe on edge. I saw an opportunity to keep Axe focused and also be awesome. Which her Primeval attunement, I tasked Axe with being lookout. We needed someone that could keep watch in Twilight so we didn\u2019t have any surprises. The look of sheer determination in her eyes told me she could do it.<br /> <br /> We stopped first at the Red Robin. With a short investigation, Angelique noted the Claimed came through the Shadow. She could still see the marks from their passing. I didn\u2019t know exactly what that meant, but seemed fair enough. Axe did a great job of keeping watch of Twilight. The problem came while Nightshade was searching through her Boneyard. The sudden and violent deaths combined with the terror involved for the customers inside caused a temporary Avernian Gate in the door to the restaurant. I studied the door a moment and determined that anyone that lit any source of fire before walking over the threshold would actually enter the Underworld. I don\u2019t remember who asked now, but it was asked if we could just close the door. I was immediately sorry I tried to answer after the words left my mouth. I knew that to permanently close a Gate, we would need at least three different fluids that affirmed life. Menstrual blood, spit, and seman being the most likely sources, we would need a cyathus worth of each. By my estimates, that would be a shot glass filled the rim. But we didn\u2019t have that on hand and ignoring Cupcake\u2019s happy diatribe about how we could just all \u201cstore it up,\u201d Nightshade and I led the charge to simply put up a sign. No smoking within 15 feet of entrance. If they decided to be assholes since you aren\u2019t supposed to smoke inside anyway, then that is on their head. We\u2019ll just have to come back about once a week and check for bodies or something. Actually I\u2019ll probably come back more often than that with food and water to get people out. Hopefully I don\u2019t find anything.<br /> <br /> We moved next to the mage\u2019s lodge. Axe stopped us before we made it out of the van. In Twilight, she spotted a pair of what seemed to be velociraptors patrolling the area. We weren\u2019t sure what specifically they were looking for, but I was sure they were stupid. Using my Phantasmal Curse, I changed their view of reality to make squirrels seem like Claimed. Angelique helped with the proper descriptions. Then I made Angelique seem like an actual squirrel and that our Krewe were simply not important. Additionally, I made sure the speedy watchdogs were unable to move very well. With that bit of mental treachery in place, Axe became a dray of squirrels. While the raptors found themselves falling on their face, we looked through the husk of the lodge. The interdimensional space had been severed from our reality, but was still there. The best assessment is that the pocket reality is still anchored to our world, but not currently open. I didn\u2019t say anything but it occurred to me that Tracey and Timothy were probably the anchor. Axe mentioned odd feelings of being disconnected in the basement, as she wandered off to investigate. I suggested that the door to the pocket reality may be down there, but given the time frames and the bad feelings the lodge still conveyed, Angelique got twitchy about staying and walked out.<br /> <br /> We made a brief stop at the fly house. Nothing had changed, but Angelique did note that the location was a minor nexus. Knowing what I do about the location\u2019s history, I wouldn\u2019t recommend using it. We moved on as there was nothing of use here and my tricks on the raptors would have definitely worn off by now. What we intended to be our last stop was the abandoned mall where the mannequins came to life. Nightshade fell into her trance for Boneyard but Angelique noted there was definitely a werewolf glyph here. She said it roughly translated as \u201cWarning of Bad Thing.\u201d I was confused as the Predator Kings didn\u2019t generally show that much restraint. Nightshade cleared that confusion right up. She saw what she could only describe as a Hamburger Man walking around the mall. The mannequins were gone so whatever this thing is, it can\u2019t be a pushover.<br /> <br /> Before we could really debate much more than wondering if it were something Changeling, Nightshade got a mystic message. Something was wrong with Elphaba. A text with Karen later found that Nightshade\u2019s familiar was definitely distressed and it had something to do with Chandra. The problem was that Chandra\u2019s body was locked in the freezer. That meant she was in trouble while hunting. We decided the mall wasn\u2019t our problem right then.<br /> <br /> Two hours later, we were on AMC campus following Cupcake\u2019s Finding ceremony. I didn\u2019t see which dorm we walked to as it was from the back. ANd honestly, we didn\u2019t care. From the ground all I could see in the moonlight was briars surrounding four second floor windows. I was just about to mention that that was an old village protection against Pennangalan, when Cupcake jumped from the van and ran to the wall. Chandra\u2019s detached head appeared then, all tangled in the thorny vines. Between Cupcake and Axe, they got her untangled without waking any of the four girls in those rooms. Then we headed back home.<br /> <br /> I made some very awkward introductions back at the van between Angelique and Chandra. The last thing we needed was for some misunderstanding to cause a fight. Back at Dark Haven Bluffs, Angelique excused Chandra, Cupcake, and myself so our vampire could collect herself. I stopped her before we rejoined the others. She was as confused about why those old protections were up as we were. What bothered me more was that she was completely unaware those vines were there until she was caught in them. This could cause real issues later.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow we\u2019re gonna need to talk to Grin.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Quick update, since there was Glenwood-exploring involved with the end of my last email and that's never a good thing to leave things hanging on. However, as a wonder, it was pretty much a simple look-see. Alice found it much less wondrous, but I, unlike some unnamed medics of my acquaintance, understand that she is simply more action oriented. And tonight definitely would have been left out of the action movie version of my life. It would totally work for the romance movie version though, which is my favorite version, naturally. Alice and Angelique were down right adorable, holding each others\u2019 hands whenever one of the got worried/nervous, and generally making with the significant looks and sidelong glances.<br /> <br /> More dishing will come tomorrow, with our nature hike, but for now, onto our non-action packed adventures in Glenwood. We hit all the low points there, but we started with the Red Robin we\u2019d met Raul at. Angelique used her Sight to discover that the folks who attacked us actually arrived before he did, rather than following him, which lends some credence to Alice\u2019s suspicions of Raul and makes the alternative even more concerning, because then how the hell did the bad guys know where to ambush Raul at and/or why were they watching that Red Robin. To make matters worse, the conflict weakened the wall between this world and the world of the dead, enough so that someone could find a way through. We\u2019ll have to deal with that, but it requires materials - semen, menstrual blood, birth fluids, life-creating stuff - that we don\u2019t have on hand, apparently because my country folk troupe mates are awfully squeamish. We did what we could to make it less likely anyone would go through by accident, as a stopgap measure.<br /> <br /> We showed Angelique all the sites in Glenwood of mystical significance that we know of. One of them was in fact desirable to practitioners like those in her family, traitors included. Shockingly, it was tainted for any of their purposes, but potentially cleansable. The local family had sussed that out as well - I just hope our efforts to distract their sentry didn\u2019t have any problematic consequences, either by letting the bad guys in after us, or sending our erstwhile allies on a wild goose chase. We\u2019ll have to check with Raul. We at least went to some effort so that they wouldn\u2019t, enough so that Alice got a bit anxious as we talked it over and over. Alice did try to distract herself from her anxiety by asking if Angelique wanted to go out some time. So. Adorable.<br /> <br /> One other place in Glenwood was of some interest, but not enough to go to so much trouble, by Angelique\u2019s estimation. The mall had... something. But it was something that the violence oriented, bruiser types that make up the Glenwood branch of the family had decided to put up a warning about, instead of beating up themselves. So to Alice\u2019s great dismay, we left whatever it was be until we knew more. Lords and ladies above and below, Glenwood is fucking horrible.<br /> <br /> We did have one bit of actual trouble, which, despite my last sentence, had nothing to do with Glenwood, since we gave the mall a miss. Natalie\u2019s familiar Elphaba had let Karen know something was wrong with Chandra and she passed it on to us. That let us intercept her before she got jumped. The timing didn\u2019t work out so that we had any idea who meant her harm, but there was an indication that she specifically was targeted, as opposed to a random mugging. So, another mystery to work with. Plus, Chandra owes Elphaba many head scritches.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll say this - this troupe of mine is never dull. I do believe it will feel strange spending a day just hiking and gossiping with one of my wives and a new girl friend. Almost... normal. :-)<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 11th, 2010<br /> <br /> -My Sara is curious\u2026<br /> <br /> -Okay moving out.<br /> <br /> -Seriously, Sara needs to pay more attention to me, less to Alice.<br /> <br /> -I can be an adult about this\u2026you know if I choose to.<br /> <br /> -Or I could focus on the mission, but who wants to think about Glenwood?<br /> <br /> -I wonder what Karen and Tatum are doing. Not the obvious, I think they both need to recover.<br /> <br /> -Sadly the weekend is coming and we have to let Tatum leave the house so she can go to work for us. It\u2019s been a fun few days though.<br /> <br /> -Maybe we can adopt her. She seems mostly housebroken. Only requires the rolled-up newspaper once in a while.<br /> <br /> -Apparently Karen is showing Tatum stuff on Youtube.<br /> <br /> -Here we are. Exciting exciting.<br /> <br /> -Okay, we did not find anything menacing, except a door to the Underworld Alexia is freaking out about.<br /> <br /> -I expected Doc to be the one with more issues about this.<br /> <br /> -Man, sorry I brought that ritual up at all.<br /> <br /> -Okay I can hide in the van!<br /> <br /> -How are you doing girls?<br /> <br /> -Oh my, I seem to have fallen in love with my girls again. This always happens.<br /> <br /> -Shucky darn.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m not sure if they are going to go with one of their disquieting ideas or not, but if I don\u2019t bring it up maybe they will forget.<br /> <br /> -I am not going to tell you two what they are talking about. Because I love you, you see.<br /> <br /> -Stop two: Dinosaurs. Because Dinosaurs.<br /> -I really did not think we would be dealing with that many dinosaurs over our career.<br /> <br /> -My Krewe has some awesome plans.<br /> <br /> -Squirrel!<br /> <br /> -I think things are, what, an acceptable amount of not okay here?<br /> <br /> -Somehow we got away without anyone saying Non-Euclidian.<br /> <br /> -No, we did not fight the dinosaur.<br /> <br /> -This building reminds me of when I was semi-homeless. In a more bad way than it sounds like.<br /> <br /> -I want a needle every time I get near it. I have not used needles in a long time. That was rock bottom.<br /> <br /> -No Karen, I am not using any needles. Nor have I since we met.<br /> <br /> -I did not even go in. Just minimal Boneyarding.<br /> <br /> --Okay next spot seems clear, toyshop is all quiet.<br /> <br /> -Okay, mall and we can go home.<br /> <br /> -Um. Um\u2026um\u2026UM<br /> <br /> -So we are not going in the mall. Holy shit.<br /> <br /> -Glenwood is so fucked up.<br /> <br /> -Okay, set some Cognac in my room and have Tatum ready to be cuffed, we are on our way back.<br /> <br /> -What is Elphaba doing?<br /> <br /> -Hrm-passing it along.<br /> <br /> -Okay, change of plans.<br /> <br /> -Yes I think Chandra needs our help.<br /> <br /> -Lexi has the right ritual.<br /> <br /> -Well this is unusual. And here I thought I got up to weird shit in college.<br /> <br /> -Chandra is okay, heading back.<br /> <br /> -Okay, not far now, if you would be so kind as to cuff Tatum, preferably while she is off guard, I would appreciate it.<br /> <br /> -Thank you ever so much.<br /> <br /> -&lt;3<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXXV</i><br /> <br /> We spent some time deciding how to deal with the dinosaur-spirit. Many plans were discussed, most involving squirrels. The determination that we could not actually summon squirrels put a crimp in them. Eventually we settled on Doc and Alice making it crazy. Also, how about that monster in the mall eh? Can\u2019t have anything to do with the trod.<br /> <br /> Next time Karen, Sara, and Alice go hiking, Doc breaks up a fight and Alexia starts plans for their \u201cgifted youngsters\u201d class. See you then. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-27T23:39:57-08:00","id":384017,"title":"","content":"Is it I wrong that I had the terrible idea of someone slipping Chandra Gangrel Dhampir blood?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T15:00:55-08:00","id":398086,"title":"","content":"Okay, time to check in on our Sin-Eaters. A couple went on a nature hike, and a couple remained back at the house. Nonetheless, stuff happened, and they were kept busy, more with Drama than plot, but hey, Drama is always interesting (when you are not in it).<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc's Log: 1030 Hours, Friday, November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> Our interesting night didn't seem to slow anyone down this morning. I found my center after about an hour of meditation then followed the smell of breakfast into the kitchen. Cupcake was very much into explaining more about her plan for a school. Nightshade put her foot down that no one would be sleeping with anyone they mentored. Bright Eyes was visibly nonplussed by this, but she went along with it without much grumbling.<br /> <br /> I think Rose is going to call Grin to ask him for assistance in setting up the club. As covers go, Underwater Story Weaving is pretty good. Cupcake wanted to make sure that if someone outside our group were to overhear our discussions, we could easily wave them off since we were OBVIOUSLY talking about fantasy writing. Not only is that a well thought out guise, it's also something college students would join.<br /> <br /> With that in the works, I agreed to call Jaggling as I knew nothing good would come from Nightshade speaking to her. That she will likely need to help mentor Jaggling was nothing less than ironic. I was not expecting the conversation I had once I explained what we intended to do. Jaggling, for all her seeming naivet\u00e9 was seriously concerned about outsiders finding out about the group. She seemed willing enough to join but I had to almost talk her down from a ledge that wasn't there in regards to our security. She finally seemed satisfied when I promised that only those directly involved would actually know anything about what was going on. She doesn't realize what contacts we have in the AMC administration nor what precautions we can take to keep things a secret. If things were really suspicious, we could just gather in Twilight or the Underworld. But Jaggling is in and that means I can start working in the Alchemy lab to finish work on the van.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc's Log: 1530 Hours, Friday, November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was not what I expected to have to deal with.<br /> <br /> I was about three hours into what will be a five hour process to convert the shitty panels I installed on my van. Using my Alchemy, I'm keeping the light weight but increasing the tensile strength of the composite panels to match the rest of the body. At the very least, this will make future repairs reliably less expensive and not sacrifice any of the structural quality. Which is all great and all, but then Gretchen came into the Carriage House. She was speaking very clipped as if she was trying to keep herself together without messing something up when she asked if I could come to the Library. When I asked what was wrong, I was led in.<br /> <br /> Angelique was on one side of the research table in what I would call direwolf form, while Noriko was in full on Kill a Bitch form on the opposite side. It was obvious they were facing off in a not happy way. I inserted myself into the mostly not English conversation and at length talked Noriko down. The problems started when Angelique showed up, based on a previous invitation, to research in the Library. Noriko didn't know that, but took the opportunity to voice her opinion on what Angelique was doing to/with Malard. We moved away from the Library where Noriko assured me that Angelique was a bad person, she could tell. Also that she was manipulating Malard. I reminded her that Angelique's pack had never found anything to suggest she was doing anything wrong and that she was helping us. Then I mentioned, not realizing how badly this would go, that Axe and Angelique were being more than friendly. I have never seen Noriko more agitated as she began wildly gesturing and frantically pleading for me to save Axe. Though I was pretty sure Axe didn't want saving, I eventually gave up trying to reason with Noriko as she was too far gone to accept my logical responses. Scooping her up into my arms, I carried her upstairs to more directly distract her.<br /> <br /> Reading back over that, I feel like a Neanderthal now but I was out of ideas. I'm sending Bright Eyes a text to let her know we need to talk about some things when they get back from hiking. Now I'm going back to using magic to get better performance out of my van.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc's Log: 1800 Hours, Friday, November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> JESUS! And I thought I had Shifter Musk aftershave!<br /> <br /> When Bright Eyes, Karen, and Axe got home, I pulled the Sin-Eater aside for our talk. It was most enlightening. I info dumped what I dealt with and learned on Bright Eyes before she let me know that Eris and Axe hit it off VERY well. Eris claimed that Axe &quot;smelled new&quot; and after what sounded like wildly inappropriate, animalistic sex, Eris publicly invited Axe to hunt in her territory. I'd swear that was a euphemism if it were anyone but Eris.<br /> <br /> I came back to find Noriko sobbing on Axe's shoulder. Given her mellow mental state before I walked away, I wasn't sure what Axe had said to upset Noriko again, but I dragged her into the drawing room while Bright Eyes led Noriko into the kitchen. She was not concerned about my girlfriend but was completely embarrassed when I mentioned Eris. I was not in the mood to dance around niceties so I just told her, it came up from talking to Bright Eyes, I wasn't trying to spy on her love life. However that was a concern given how badly Noriko was reacting to the thought of Angelique being involved. I explained what Noriko's issues with Angelique were and told her to be careful.<br /> <br /> Now I'm hoping we can get through dinner without someone else being upset about Angelique.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Whew! I think I dodged a bullet this time. I have to remember that who\u2019s sleeping with who is not always an acceptable topic for musing on out loud. But Alice isn\u2019t actually mad at me, despite the stink-eye she gave me when Doc started in on her. Poor Little Red. I have not, as Natalie teasingly accused, fed her to two wolves, though it\u2019s a good enough description of her two feral/predatory, primally Touched paramours. No, it\u2019s apparently just that Alice + powerful hot woman + bed = sexy times.<br /> <br /> To back up a bit: hiking, obviously, was awesome. Even the drive up there was fun. We talked about family and growing up - Karen and Alice both have older brothers, though it couldn\u2019t have been a more different situation otherwise. Alice was kinda one of the gang, while Karen was treated like a porcelain princess, things like being relegated to the boring paddle boats while the boys went kayaking. Of course, since I haven\u2019t ever been kayaking either, we\u2019re going to have to fix that. Or perhaps try out white water rafting or some such. I\u2019m sure it\u2019ll involve Sleeping Giant park, anyway.<br /> <br /> We also got Alice to dish about Angelique. Apparently she was quite enthusiastic, if inexperienced. With girls at least. Alice is still super worried about the relationship thing. She doesn\u2019t like being the \u2018thing on the side\u2019 and to be fair - Angelique is attracted to power and strength and Mr. Malard has both in spades. There\u2019s no way I\u2019d try to sneak around him. Even if Angelique\u2019s thoughtful look meant she was considering breaking up with him, I\u2019d still be nervous,. I do still believe it would be for the best.<br /> <br /> Speaking of relationship things, Karen\u2019s been on a name change kick. She apparently has the forms just sitting around, waiting. Where I am now though, I\u2019m not giving up Rowan. Even more than the physical things they left me, it\u2019s my connection to my family, to Dad and Grandma. I\u2019m not claiming any grand legacy - I wouldn\u2019t be surprised to find Grandma picked it out of an herbal. But it\u2019s ours, the three of us. Karen\u2019s latest tactic does have slightly more traction though. Rowan-Knight or Knight-Rowan. Very high fantasy (or Ren Faire, if you\u2019re made of cynicism and eyeshadow). I told her I\u2019d think about it.<br /> <br /> But I have gotten *way* off topic. So there we were, right, relaxing and enjoying our hike. Alice was way in her comfort zone, and even opened up a little more. She seems kinda surprised we didn\u2019t kick her out immediately and we tried to reassure her that (1) Doc is a giant teddy bear (2) he\u2019ll come around like pretty much the rest of us (3) that we didn\u2019t need another over thinker in the troupe. I think we succeeded at (2) and (3), but not so much at (1), which is good cause even I don\u2019t believe that, and I\u2019d worry about Alice\u2019s gullibility.<br /> <br /> Anyway, so there we were, standing near the waterfall, not yet thinking about having sex under it (I will find someone willing, dammit, November temperatures be damned), when some friends of the troupe, more of the family Angelique belongs to, came up to check on us. They\u2019re guardians of the place, and since they recognized us, wanted to check and make sure we weren\u2019t looking for them.<br /> <br /> Have I mentioned they breed them hot in that family? I mean, the redneck types in Glenwood didn\u2019t precisely trip any triggers, but that may have been the intent to do harm. Rawl\u2019s a handsome fellow though. Barrett\u2019s not really my type, but neither am I his, so it works out. He has a friend that might be more my style, but I\u2019ve yet to meet him. And Deirdre and Eris, from Sleeping Giant, are both crazy hot. So there at the park, there was plenty of flirting going on and Eris and Alice really hit it off. She hardly had a coherent thought for the rest of us, but she made an effort for our Little Red. See, Deirdre told us later, Eris is a foundling, something of a grown up feral child. Deirdre arranged for the two of them to have a moment alone and even then was kinda surprised when the howling Eris was doing made it clear someone was having fun. Apparently, I was the only one not surprised when two hot women, who were clearly attracted to each other and were given privacy and a bed, started having sex. Country folk...<br /> <br /> Anyhow, Alice was, of course, horribly embarrassed. Plus now, since Alice seems intent on only having one playmate, she has to choose, the poor duck. Eris seemed pretty serious. She said she liked her and *everything*. That \u2018see you again\u2019 sounded an awful lot like a promise and lords and ladies is she intense. She\u2019s even going to try to stop from losing her phone. On the other hand, Angelique is slightly more with it, pretty intense herself and super hot. And even aside from the innate difficulties in choosing between two incredibly hot options, family politics are sure to make this interesting.<br /> <br /> That has already thrown something of a wrench in the happy home life, kinda. Noriko is a friend of Mr. Malard and knows enough about the family to know that his and Angelique\u2019s relationship is verboten. That, plus probably the age gap, has Noriko convinced that Angelique is just manipulating Malard for something. So when Noriko found Angelique in the library... well, it was almost a lot less pretty. Doc intervened and talked Noriko out of anything hasty. He did mention Angelique and Alice hooking up, which had her in another tizzy. So now Noriko (and Doc) are both souring on the idea of Alice and Angelique.<br /> <br /> Not that it hasn\u2019t been hard enough trying to convince Alice she hasn\u2019t made a mistake either. Making a connection with another person, strengthening the ties that hold us together, especially in such a joyful, pleasureful way, is never a mistake. Holding on until those ties become bonds and the pleasure becomes bitterness - that\u2019s a mistake. Weakening the joy with lies can sometimes be a mistake. But making the connection, never. I dunno if I convinced her though... Ah well. I certainly don't envy her the fate she's chosen for herself. I mean, aside from the fact it probably includes a hot lady. That is the best kind of fate.<br /> <br /> So aside from Alice\u2019s love triangle? 3 sides of a square?, Alexia\u2019s school idea has really taken off. Since all of our prospective students attend AMC, we\u2019re gonna try to get it set up as a club there. Alexia came up with the name Underwater Story Weaving, which is adorable and awesome, and gives the perfect cover (fantasy writing) for us to be discussing being Touched, magic, the Sight and its like. And given AMC\u2019s Catholic leanings, a cover is sadly necessary. We settled on a regular rotating seminar type thing, with a one-on-one mentoring setup for practical aspects. I\u2019m not allowed to mentor Tracey (and hopefully eventually Timothy) since we\u2019re sleeping together. It seems a bit overboard to me, since there\u2019s no grades or evaluations to bias, and it\u2019s not like it\u2019s the other way around and I was using my position as a mentor to coerce her. Though to be fair, as I mentioned earlier, two hot women, clearly attracted to each other and given privacy, might not always be on task, if the task in question is anything but sex. Even if there\u2019s no bed involved. After all, that\u2019s Karen\u2019s fetish. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019re on our way to Sleeping Giant State Park, and I\u2019m more excited and relaxed than I\u2019ve been in months. Even though it\u2019s shockingly cold out there, I can\u2019t wait to hit the trails. It\u2019s been too long since I\u2019ve been out hiking, and I\u2019m hoping the park can become a regular retreat for me. It\u2019s too bad Angelique can\u2019t come with us, though.<br /> <br /> As we drive, our light-hearted conversation turns to kayaking. I ask if Sara or Karen have ever been, but they haven\u2019t. They\u2019ve never been white water rafting either. I need to get them out on a river some time. Karen laments that her brothers have gone kayaking, but they didn\u2019t let her join in, so we start talking about our families.<br /> <br /> Karen doesn\u2019t get along well with her parents, but things are a little better with her brothers. Even so, she was always the pretty princess. Not because she wanted to be, but because that\u2019s how her brothers treated her. She never got to do things like kayaking or roughhousing. They were too protective and always treated her like a fading flower. That sounds miserable to me, and Karen agrees, so I talk a bit about my own older brothers, Jacob and Ethan. They picked on me a lot, but they also looked out for me. And unlike Karen, they didn\u2019t treat me like a fragile doll. I often tagged along on their adventures, and I guess when you get right down to it, they are the reason I\u2019m