look in them. If she\u2019s a werewolf, I get the sense that she\u2019s more wolf than woman, but she is DEFINITELY a woman. Sara introduces her, and Deirdre points out that she\u2019s a little crazy, which is why they named her after a goddess of chaos when they found her wandering naked and alone in the forest. Somehow, that all just makes her more interesting.<br /> <br /> Eris seems very interested in me. She says I smell new, so as we begin walking toward a camping area with the rangers, Sara explains that I\u2019ve only recently begun hanging out with the krewe. I guess Eris also senses something primal in me. She instantly gauges that I\u2019m predator too, and this seems to impress her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou hunt?\u201d she asks. She\u2019s not talking about hanging out in camo with rifles.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. It\u2019s kind of what I do.\u201d I respond with smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can come hunt with me in my hunting ground,\u201d she says. She\u2019s very focused and seems very serious when she says it, but I think she\u2019s flirting with me. The other two werewolves seem shocked, but then Deirdre and Sara share a sly look. I should probably be worried, but I\u2019m too intrigued by Eris to care. We continue to talk, and she tells me a bit about the park. She has a lot of love for the place, but she\u2019s so intent on the conversation that it\u2019s hard to pick up on that at first. Still, I realize that she\u2019s trying to share something meaningful with me. She\u2019s also trying to make a good impression, but it\u2019s like she\u2019s not used to putting forth that kind of effort. The things Deirdre and Barret say lead me to believe that Eris isn\u2019t normally this talkative. I\u2019m flattered.<br /> <br /> We eventually arrive at some cabins. They\u2019re unoccupied in the off season, and Eris offers to show me around. It\u2019s a thinly veiled excuse to get some time alone with me away from her friends, but I don\u2019t mind. Honestly, I\u2019m very attracted to her. I guess I\u2019m just as drawn to her primal, predatory spirit as she is to mine. We wander into a cabin, and even though I\u2019m pretty sure she\u2019s going to try and seduce me, I don\u2019t really know what to expect. I don\u2019t want to lead her on, though, so I decide that if she does put the moves on me, I\u2019ll have to tell her I\u2019m already in a relationship.<br /> <br /> But almost as soon as the cabin door closes, she turns to me with a startlingly intense look in her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cI really like you,\u201d she says, simply.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re quite a surprise yourself. I like you too,\u201d I say with a smile. I\u2019m about to head off any further come-ons by telling her I\u2019m already involved, but she interrupts me.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you want to mate?\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m completely flustered. I have no idea what I was about to say.<br /> \u201cI\u2019m very direct,\u201d she explains.<br /> <br /> I recover just long enough to stutter, \u201cI like direct,\u201d and then Eris pushes me onto the bed and I find myself in a situation very similar to the one with Angelique the other day. This must be a werewolf thing, and I\u2019m starting to feel like Little Red Riding Hood. Eris is completely inexperienced, but she\u2019s intense and passionate and instinctual and my god is it incredible. The howling is a bit weird, but I can deal with it.<br /> <br /> Of course, even through the bewildering passion of the moment, I\u2019m still wondering how the heck this is happening to me for a second time in less than a week! I\u2019ve never been the sort of girl to sleep around! Maybe Sara\u2019s been a bad influence on me, though I\u2019m sure she would insist she\u2019s been a good influence. Or maybe I just miss Cassidy more than I realize and I\u2019m desperately trying to recapture what I had with her.<br /> <br /> <i>Those are mere excuses. Look deeply within yourself, dear Alice. You are turning to sex to satisfy a craving that can only be fulfilled with your axe.</i><br /> <br /> Inwardly, I scream at the Huntress to quiet her voice. I try to drive her from my mind by focusing on Eris and succumbing to the heat of the moment.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Afterward, we lay cuddling for awhile before returning to the others.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like this,\u201d Eris says. I\u2019m not sure whether she\u2019s talking about the sex or the cuddling, but I think she means both.<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d I respond. I love cuddling in the pleasant afterglow after sex. It might be my favorite part of the whole thing.<br /> <br /> All too soon, we get up and rejoin the others. Sara\u2019s grin makes me feel sheepish and embarrassed, and it\u2019s clear that everyone could hear Eris howling, which only makes things worse. Deirdre and Barret seem a little shell-shocked. I guess this kind of behavior is completely new for Eris.<br /> <br /> But as we hike with the rangers toward the park entrance, Eris says that she really likes me and that she will see me again. It\u2019s a statement more than a question. Deirdre promises to get her another phone so she can call me if she promises not to lose this one. Eris seems motivated, so expect I\u2019ll get a call from her soon. I\u2019d like that. It\u2019s nice that someone is so unreservedly attracted to me, and not only is Eris really sexy, super intense and very direct, but she seems uncomplicated and honest. That\u2019s really appealing. And I really don\u2019t think she\u2019d care about the things I\u2019ve done in the past. I hope not.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not until the drive back that it really hits me how much trouble I\u2019ve gotten myself into. How serious is Angelique? I thought maybe she was thinking of breaking things off with Malard for me, but she\u2019s really mysterious about her intentions. And I\u2019ve already asked her out, sort of. She\u2019s intelligent and classy, which is really attractive but also intimidating. Eris, on the other hand seems really serious, and I\u2019ll admit that an uncomplicated relationship with a passionate, smoking hot blonde is really enticing right now. I do have a thing for blondes. That said, I suppose that Eris is strange enough that it\u2019s probably wishful thinking to say that a relationship with her would be uncomplicated. For one thing, it would be difficult for her to visit us at the mansion, given werewolf territory issues.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my god. I am so screwed. I have no freakin\u2019 idea what to do.\u201d I say to no one in particular.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> When we get home, Noriko greets me. She\u2019s obviously upset, so I ask what\u2019s wrong, and that\u2019s when the floodgates open and it all comes out.<br /> <br /> First off, she\u2019s worried about me and Angelique. I guess she found out we were together, though she doesn\u2019t say how. She doesn\u2019t trust Angelique, and she feels protective of Mr. Malard since he\u2019s always been kind to her and allowed her into his territory. As far and Noriko is concerned, Angelique is a bad person who is up to no good, and she doesn\u2019t want the werewolf digging her claws into me. I try to tell her that Angelique isn\u2019t like that, but Noriko is doesn\u2019t believe it.<br /> <br /> Then she starts to cry about Doc. At first I\u2019m worried that Doc has done something to hurt her, and I\u2019m ready to go give him a piece of my mind, but then she explains that she\u2019s worried about ruining their relationship. She\u2019s really in love with him, and she wants things to work out. But I guess she doesn\u2019t think she\u2019s worthy of him, and she\u2019s worried she\u2019ll do something to screw things up. I tell her that\u2019s impossible. Everyone makes mistakes, but she and Doc are good together, and I can\u2019t imagine her doing anything that would seriously mess up their relationship. Not if Doc really loves her too. And if he doesn\u2019t, then maybe HE\u2019S the one who isn\u2019t worthy of HER. But honestly, I don\u2019t think that\u2019s the case, and I told Noriko as much.<br /> After a good cry on my shoulder, Noriko seems comforted and more sure of herself, so hopefully I helped restore some of her confidence. Doc had better be good to her. Noriko\u2019s quite a catch, and she\u2019s my friend, so I\u2019m not going to be happy if he hurts her. Not that I think he will. Honestly, as far as I\u2019m concerned, Noriko\u2019s worried for nothing, and I hope I at least helped her see that.<br /> <br /> As if on cue, Doc comes striding into the TV room looking for me. He is surprised and a bit perturbed to see that Noriko is upset, but he doesn\u2019t get a chance to talk to her because Sara guides her out of the room. I think he suspects I had was the one who upset his girlfriend, but if so, he puts it aside long enough to tell me that Angelique and Noriko almost came to blows in the library earlier. I\u2019m disturbed to hear that, but Doc goes on to warn me that Angelique is bad news, and romancing her is going to cause problems, and not just with Noriko. He makes it pretty clear that while he\u2019s not trying to tell me what to do or who to be with, he doesn\u2019t think a relationship with Angelique is a good idea. He encourages me to be careful.<br /> <br /> Then he lightens up a little bit and tells me that he is surprised, amused and kind of intrigued by the fact that I hooked up with Eris. I\u2019m annoyed that he already knows about that. Sara has loose lips, and it isn\u2019t really any of Doc\u2019s business. I\u2019m not really mad, I guess, but I am embarrassed. And I still don\u2019t know what to do about the whole Angelique/Eris thing. Doc has an opinion on that, though. He says that it\u2019s not like Eris to show the sort of affection and attachment she was showing toward me, but he thinks it\u2019s probably good for her. He seems to think I\u2019d be better off with Eris than Angelique.<br /> <br /> Is it just me, or are people are conspiring against Angelique? I feel pretty rotten about that. I think we ought to give her chance. I mean, the krewe is giving ME a chance. Angelique deserves the same.<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t help me make a choice, though. Sara thinks I can date both of them until I figure out who I\u2019m really falling for as long as I\u2019m honest with each of them about it, but that still feels like cheating to me, and I don\u2019t think I would appreciate being the \u201cother girl\u201d if I were in their shoes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve managed to get myself into a bit of trouble. I\u2019ve had Tatum working as manager at The 27 Club for awhile now, and while inexperienced she does a decent job. Karen and I look after her. It\u2019s good experience and can help her get a job in entertainment management later; all is well.<br /> <br /> Except that when I hired her, I was supposed to be being good and not sleeping with anyone but Doc or Karen. Doc and I broke up, and Karen pretty much planted her flag. Sara got involved, but then Karen planted her flag there too. We are all bound as wives, and all is good. Except Sara\u2019s soul seems to be affecting mine, as I am back to my skirt chasing ways\u2026admittedly not looking for Ms. Right, as there is no question my Ms. Right is found, twice over. But Sara does not mind, and Karen is accepting if there is not attachment. Because Sara\u2019s soul is affecting hers too, of course.<br /> <br /> I had had sex with Tatum one time before when she was hired, and I had no plans to do so again, but then Karen expressed interest in her as well, so we had sex with her in the VIP room one night after working on getting the place ready and took her back to our townhouse. We have been fucking her since. Even Karen is kinda attached to her, which is kinda amazing, she does not get attached easy, except to me.<br /> <br /> Now Tatum has spent a few days at the Addams Family House here and is quite happy. I\u2019ve spent a lot of time with her. We are all pretty luvy-duvy, which is okay, complicated but okay, except that she is still my and Karen\u2019s employee. We write her paychecks. We decide on her performance. She is decidedly under our control in terms of her livelihood. That\u2019s bad for a relationship. There is a major difference of power.<br /> <br /> The problem is I don\u2019t know what to do. I don\u2019t want to stop sleeping with her. Nor, for that matter, does Karen. Sara doesn\u2019t, though she is not technically her boss like Karen and I are so less an issue. So not sleeping with Tatum is off the table, very off the table.<br /> <br /> I could let her go, but she does not have other work and anything she found would pay notably less and not offer her the same experience and not be as helpful on her resume. I would be doing her a disservice, if not shooting her in the foot, letting her go even on her own terms.<br /> <br /> I could hire someone just to manage her, but that would be a money sink. And they would still be beholden to me, with just a step in between.<br /> <br /> Sara thinks I am overthinking it. She agrees it can be an issue, but the fact we are not abusing it (she has made it very clear her relationship to us is consensual) means no one is being hurt. Karen is happy with the situation, but admits she enjoys having power over her lovers and being in charge, so her control over Tatum kinda gets her off. She does not abuse her power, though, and while technically Tatum\u2019s boss I, not Karen, make the decisions on her, unless Karen overrides me because that is how our relationship works; she is my domme after all. Of course, she is also twenty, which is close to Tatum\u2019s age but slightly younger.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know. I will talk to everyone about it a little more. It does not sit right with me, but maybe I am overreacting.<br /> <br /> Tatum having to head off to work sucked too, since she is going back home not coming here. At least my sweethearts will be back from hiking soon. I hope they had fun.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Not much to give commentary metagame wise, it was mostly a Drama session.<br /> <br /> Sara sort of referred to it, but some of what she was discussing involved Barrett talking about enjoying sex under waterfalls, Sara being intrigued, and Karen making it clear she does not do such things in November in freaking Connecticut. She also noted while Natalie had a church fetish and Sara apparently now has a waterfall fetish, she has a bed fetish; they are warm, soft, and hikers/petitioners rarely wander in and interrupt you.<br /> <br /> I could sell this to HBO. Hell, I could sell all 3 of my New WoD campaigns to HBO honestly.<br /> <br /> As a side note on the subject, the esteemed Mr. Ox has made an appearance in my <b>Demon: The Descent</b> game <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\">Night Train Detective Agency</a>. It has 3 common players with <b>Geist</b>, so feel free to check it out if you want to see some Demon Neo-Noir action.<br /> <br /> That looks like about everything, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 02-08-2015, 06:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T16:57:35-08:00","id":416979,"title":"","content":"Time to check in with the Krewe as Alice settles into an acceptable level of Drama<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1845 Hours, Friday, November 12, 2010<br /> <br /> Didn\u2019t have to wait all the way til dinner.<br /> <br /> Since Cupcake had to finish cooking, Axe decided that she needed to talk with Angelique right away. I stayed back in the hallway figuring that I\u2019d catch Angelique on the way out. I had a question I intended to ask, but she came out much sooner than I thought. The Bone Shadow was already in tears when I tried to ask what was wrong but she was struggling to keep herself that much together. She wanted to be left alone and made that clear. It occurred to me that pushing an emotionally distraught werewolf was not how I wanted to end my evening, so I got the hell out the way. Axe came out shortly and was also not happy. I was still shocked from Angelique rushing out, so I didn\u2019t really think about it before I started talking. I asked what Axe did to Angelique. The look of hurt and frustration on Axe\u2019s face brought me up short. I tried to ask if things were okay, but that was a fairly silly question. I apologized and left Axe to her thoughts. I found Noriko and found that I still hadn\u2019t finished swallowing my foot. It was at that point that I declared I was just going to stop talking. Noriko was more understanding, not always being able to get her words together fast enough normally.<br /> <br /> Once I was less flustered, I told Noriko I thought I was ready if she would be willing to teach me Japanese. Her eyes got huge and she squeaked out that she would try. She seemed very surprised and more than a little nervous about trying to teach me. I doubt it will be an issue. It was something I\u2019ve been thinking about, but I\u2019m ashamed to admit I also had another reason to ask her. I intend on summoning a spirit of Language using the evocation spell i learned and commanding it to teach me First Tongue. My research suggests that I might be able to strengthen the spirit and therefore make it more inclined to help me. Actively learning an additional language could only serve to help me more. And I thought it might be a subtle move to assure Noriko that we were doing okay.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Saturday, November 13, 2010<br /> <br /> I have got to think my relationship plans all the way through before I try to be smooth again. It\u2019s hard for me to remember that Noriko hasn\u2019t been able to have a relationship before we started dating, at least since she was turned. I also just realized, I still haven\u2019t ever sit down and talked with her about that privately. It seems like the kind of thing we should share. Hopefully it\u2019ll remove one more burden on her mind. But there was a whole night that happened before all this.<br /> <br /> Mouse showed for dinner tonight. It was pretty obvious she was there to fawn over Cupcake and Chandra, but she had news as well. Carol and Jenny were in hiding but stayed in touch with Mouse. They also apparently eloped after the Bowtie Man found their hotel room, held under assumed names. I suspect I\u2019m going to have a discussion with him at some point. I may or may not earn some Plasm from that conversation. But I digress. Mouse had a thumb drive of information as well as skin, hair, and blood samples for my sympathetic rituals. Sadly they still couldn\u2019t piece very much together about their own ritual, but this is a big step in getting back to Mariah.<br /> <br /> After dinner, I slipped down to the GMC room to call a spirit. I had never experienced this kind of summoning before. It was almost like part of me reached out into Twilight until I found something that matched what I was looking for, then pulled it back. At the conclusion, an interesting spirit appeared. It looked like an open book with a flowing scroll circling around as it floated in front of me. I issued my command to teach me First Tongue and it accepted with the condition that I sacrifice a book written several languages. I hadn\u2019t expected that, but as it happens Snowflake and I had a few mechanic guides in the carriage house which had English, French, and German instructions, so I agreed. Once I ritually sacrificed the book, my spirit mentor taught me the very rudimentary basics of First Tongue. It also explained that I would have great difficulty using the language as I was never meant to utter those sounds. Understanding is my prime goal, though I suspect when I possess the Dog of War, I should have little trouble. Once the spirit was satisfied with my progress, it dematerialized and I went to find Noriko.<br /> <br /> She wasn\u2019t any less nervous about teaching me her native language, but I did my best to keep up with what Noriko was telling me. During a break to grab some water, I walked back into my room and out of nowhere, Noriko noted, almost casually, that I had some space in my closet. Of course I have space, we have two deep closets in our \u201cservants\u2019 quarters\u201d that just short of walk-in anyway. But Noriko went back to trying to explain polite tenses without any other mention of it. Now that she\u2019s asleep and I\u2019m writing this, I realize she wants to move in. In any \u201cnormal\u201d relationship, this would be incredibly too soon.<br /> <br /> See previous comment about Noriko and relationships.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t want to send her mixed signals after asking to learn Japanese, but I don\u2019t think it\u2019s a good idea to move this fast either. Nightshade and I already lived in the same place, so we never had to consider this. I think I\u2019ll need to think of a good middle ground to keep her from thinking she messed something up. For now, I\u2019m going to cuddle up with her and go to sleep. I suspect I\u2019ll be awake early in the morning.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Saturday, November 13, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation seems to be my best answer to most problems outside of a firefight. I sat up just as the clock flipped over to 0600 Hours and headed to the Meditation Room. It took an hour, but not only did I find my center, I also found my answer. I knew the others would really not appreciate the sound of the bandsaw pre-breakfast, so I marked off all the lumber for cutting and pre-drilled all the screws, then found a stain to match the rooms. By then, Cupcake had food ready and I was happy for breakfast. Once we were finished with breakfast, I didn\u2019t feel as bad about cutting the wood. I built closet inserts for both closets in my room. I\u2019ve just finished sanding and staining the finished product. It looks like I just doubled the amount of space in each closet. Once Noriko wakes up, I\u2019ll install the inserts and invite her to stay with me off and on as she likes.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1500 Hours, Saturday, November 13, 2010<br /> <br /> Thinking. It really is one of my better options. Noriko was really happy to find the renovated closets when she came back up. When I asked her about staying, she squeed and pounced me so I think I did okay. Karen saw the inserts as I was bringing one in so I asked if she needed more closet space since they were basically sharing the space between all three of them. The gears in her head immediately started turning, but she simply asked if I could without it being a problem. That girl has way more going for her than she lets on. After I installed our inserts and laughed at Noriko bouncing around the room for a bit, I started working on a slight modification for Karen. Nightshade, Karen, &amp; Bright Eyes all have clothes but a big storage issue for Karen is her (very tall) boots. So I did the right closet insert with mostly shoe storage, taking her styles into account for height, while the left was more hanging storage, with two swiveling hanging rods on each side of the center shelf. The rods lock into place when not being used, but give eight total racks and gently swing up or down to access each rack.<br /> <br /> By the time I finished installing those, Karen had organized an 80\u2019s clubbing party that most of the women in the house were involved in. So I should probably get cleaned up and be ready to go clubbing soon.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Ah, Alice. Apparently the \u2018wolves\u2019 I\u2019ve been accused of throwing our Little Red at are as territorial as their metaphorical namesake. On the plus side, Angelique didn\u2019t blame Alice for sleeping with Eris, since they weren\u2019t in a \u2018serious relationship\u2019 at the time, which is awful magnanimous of her. She was, however, hurt that Alice hadn\u2019t been giving their potential \u2018serious relationship\u2019 the same brain time that Angelique apparently had and therefore needed time to think things over. Especially since things include Angelique possibly moving in, at least temporarily , as breaking things off with Mr Malard might mean losing his protection and their relationship is not the only prejudice against her.<br /> <br /> I by no means can or will begrudge Angelique her pain, but I do wish I could convince Alice it\u2019s not her responsibility nor does she have any guilt in it. Unless my ability to read people is fading with my advancing age, she had and has no intentions to hurt her. They only thing she\u2019s done is not made a significant life decision without knowing her own heart. And had sex with two hot women who were totally into her. But I\u2019m not entirely sure she respects my relationship advice, even if we\u2019re not that different on a number of points. Hopefully Natalie\u2019s talk with her helped some.<br /> <br /> Case in point re similarities: she was honest with Angelique and tonight we're headed off to Murder Ballads to come clean with Eris and see if her insights can help Alice find her heart. Hopefully not literally... but Alice will have plenty of backup in case Eris takes it poorly. She was even an absolute darling and got Deirdre to agree to bring Ildefonso, one of the few unattached interested dudes that apparently have all been in hiding or something. One of these days I\u2019ll convince the troupe to introduce me to Anders, one of the folks in the other death-Touched troupe. Karen will just have to believe that I won\u2019t let him steal me away, despite his single occasion of precedent. Anyhow, I promised I\u2019d keep Ildefonso distracted from the drama right up until/if the \u2018wolf\u2019 turned on Little Red, at which point he\u2019d be further back up.<br /> <br /> Of course, Karen heard the word \u2018clubbing\u2019 and so it became a Thing. It has been an 80s makeover moment all afternoon, despite Natalie\u2019s insistence that since Karen could not remember the 80s, the idea was not allowed to bring her so much joy. To be fair, I\u2019m given to understand a true 80s makeover moment would involve more teased hair and legwarmers. It did involve more revolutions though our wardrobes than entirely necessary in order to show off/ arrange things on Doc\u2019s new closet insert things he built us.<br /> <br /> So it will be a true event, with all of the troupe, all four of the park rangers and Catharine, who showed up yesterday with news of our cultists friends. On positive relationship news, she, Alexia and Chandra are downright adorable. She looked in absolute heaven at dinner. Also, Carol and Jenny eloped! John the Bowtie Man had found them out - after a few days, so probably mystically - so they split and decided to split in a direction with a little white chapel. Karen, of course, immediately began planning them a proper ceremony. They had passed on some info to Catharine, including a few likely addresses. They still didn\u2019t remember much about the ritual, but she did bring some skin, hair and blood samples, so possibly Doc\u2019s sympathetic magics can get us somewhere.<br /> <br /> Alright, I think my break from being Barbied is up. And since I already got my reward of getting to watch/help with Alice and Noriko\u2019s Barbieing, I better be good.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> I pause outside the library doors and take a deep breath before opening them. I\u2019m not looking forward to this, but it\u2019s the right thing to do. My parents raised me to be honest and do right by others. Sure, I\u2019ve messed up a lot, even if I\u2019ve always tried to be just. But Angelique deserves for me to be upfront with her.<br /> <br /> It takes me a minute or two to find her hidden among the maze of shelves. I\u2019ve always thought that old libraries like this are creepy. I can\u2019t shake the feeling that dark things lie behind each shelf. In THIS library, it\u2019s probably closer to the truth to say that the dark things reside ON the shelves. Who knows what ugly secrets these books hold.<br /> <br /> Angelique looks like she\u2019s in her element when I find her, though. For a brief moment, I\u2019m able to admire her focused look and the absent way she toys with a lock of her hair as she reads, then she notices me and looks up from her studies, and a smile brightens her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice! How was the hiking trip?\u201d she asks. The question is an arrow that pierces my heart.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was\u2026uh\u2026good,\u201d I say, trying to smile as warmly as she is.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad. Hey, listen, I wanted to talk to you about something,\u201d she says, standing up and stepping toward me to take my hands in hers.<br /> <br /> \u201cSure, but I\u2026\u201d I try to stop her, but she plows ahead. I guess I\u2019m not really very assertive when the situation doesn\u2019t involve my axe.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, I like you, Alice. A lot. I did a lot of thinking last night. About you. About us. It\u2019s all I could do. I want us to be together, if that\u2019s what you want. And if it is\u2026then I\u2019m prepared to break things off with Malard. I can talk to him tomorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s\u2026wonderful,\u201d I say, sincerely. Regardless of what happens between me and Angelique, she needs to split up with Malard. It\u2019s not a healthy relationship on so many levels. I wish I had the liberty to break up with MY \u201cmentor.\u201d<br /> <i><br /> You need me. You OWE me. What would you be without me? Nothing but a pile of bones forgotten in a desert cave.</i><br /> <br /> \u201cThe only thing is,\u201d Angelique continues, \u201cif I\u2019m not staying with Malard, I might not have his protection. I have a lot enemies. People who misunderstand me. You know that. I\u2019ll need somewhere to stay. Someone to watch my back.\u201d She looks at me hopefully. When I don\u2019t respond immediately, she quickly continues. \u201cI\u2019m not saying the two of us should move in together or anything. I know that\u2019s moving a bit fast. I just wanted you to know that I might need some help. I don\u2019t know if I can move into the mansion, but I\u2019m anxious about my safety if I were to stay somewhere else\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I shake my head to dispel her worries. \u201cDon\u2019t worry about that, Angelique. If you need protection, I\u2019ll make sure you\u2019re safe. I\u2019ll ask Simon if you can move into the mansion. We have spare rooms. But, um, there\u2019s something I need to tell you first.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique looks at me expectantly. I take another deep breath and inwardly cringe as I see a look of anxious caution creep into her eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, I didn\u2019t really know what was going on between us. I didn\u2019t know how serious you were, and well, when we were out hiking, we ran into some of Karen and Sara\u2019s friends, and I really hit it off with one of them. We\u2026kind of hooked up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique takes a step back with a stricken look on her face. She drops my hands and I instantly regret the loss of her touch. It symbolizes the distance that has suddenly forced its way between us.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t mean for it to happen. I\u2019ve never slept around before. She was just really aggressive and I\u2026I don\u2019t know what to say. I\u2019m sorry Angelique.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2026you don\u2019t want me then,\u201d she says, softly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? No! I do! I mean, I really, really like you. I want to be with you. And you need to get away from Malard. It\u2019s just, I really like this other girl too. And\u2026I just met you both and\u2026\u201d I sigh deeply. \u201c\u2026I don\u2019t know what I want right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique is quiet for a few moments, thinking. She turns away from me, and I\u2019m reminded of Cassidy turning away in the rain the last time I saw her. Unlike Cassidy, though, Angelique turns to face me again after several awkward moments. I can see the hurt plainly etched on her face and it breaks my heart. I just want to take her in my arms so that we can comfort each other and smooth away the pain.<br /> <br /> \u201cI spent all night figuring out what my heart wants,\u201d she says. \u201cNow you need to do the same. You don\u2019t have to tell me right now\u2014.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight now, I know what my heart\u2019s telling me,\u201d I say, foolishly, as I step toward her to take her hand again.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. That\u2019s not your heart, and that\u2019s not what I want,\u201d she says, stepping back again and gently pulling her hand away. \u201cI love you Alice. I want to be with you. But I want it to be the right thing for you too.\u201d Angelique begins to tear up and I feel like the most horrible person in the world.<br /> <br /> \u201cTake time to think about it. I\u2019ll be waiting. And when you\u2019ve decided where your heart lies, I\u2019ll leave Malard to be with you, if that\u2019s what you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> I nod, at a loss for words momentarily, and then manage to say, \u201cThank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique hurries past me and disappears around a tome-lined shelf. I hear a stifled sob as she disappears from view and her footsteps fade.<br /> <br /> I sink into a chair at a table strewn with the books she was studying and let my face fall into my hands. At least she took it better than I feared she might. Still, I feel awful. The last thing I wanted to do was hurt Angelique, but I screwed up and now I\u2019m paying for it. Sometimes I feel like my whole life is just a procession of unpleasant consequences. And now I have to do this again with Eris. But Angelique\u2019s right. I need to figure out what I want.<br /> <br /> Another set of footsteps approaches. Heavier, more masculine footsteps. Without looking up, I know it\u2019s Doc. Great, I think sourly.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, what\u2019s going on?\u201d Doc asks. \u201cAngelique just ran by me crying. What did you do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI told her about Eris, and she\u2019s upset.\u201d I say, miserably.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh,\u201d Doc responds. Then, after a pause, \u201cSo, I should leave you alone, shouldn\u2019t I?\u201d<br /> <br /> Wow. Doc isn\u2019t as dense as I thought.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that would be good,\u201d I say, perhaps a bit more curtly that I intend. Without another word, Doc departs and I\u2019m left alone with my guilt.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> <i>Emotional stress is exhausting,</i> I think as I collapse into a chair in Natalie\u2019s room, where she, Sara and Karen are hanging out, listening to music, and painting toenails. I\u2019ve never actually had much use for painted toenails. I don\u2019t wear a lot of shoes that show off my feet. I think feet are kind of a thing for Natalie, though.<br /> <br /> \u201cI called Deirdre and arranged a meeting with Eris at Murder Ballads tomorrow night. I have no idea how Eris is going to react when I tell her there\u2019s another girl and I\u2019m trying to figure out where my heart lies. Neither did Deirdre. This is totally new territory for everyone, I guess.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want us there to back you up?\u201d Sara asks.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that would be good. I\u2019m not worried about Eris freaking out and trying to kill me. I can probably handle that. But I feel worse right now than I\u2019ve felt since my last krewe dumped me and I realized I\u2019d gone off the rails. Your emotional support would be nice. I haven\u2019t had a lot of that lately, but you girls have been really good to me since I arrived.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you know we\u2019re here for you sweetie,\u201d Natalie says with a sympathetic smile. I like it when she calls me \u201csweetie.\u201d It reminds me of my mother, which is probably part of why I tend to think of Natalie as the krewe mom despite all her sexual quirks. She might not have grown up on a farm like I did, and she\u2019s run a long way from her rural upbringing, but deep down, we\u2019re both country girls.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow did things go with Angelique?\u201d Karen asks.<br /> <br /> \u201cAwful. But it could have been worse. She\u2019s thought a lot about what she wants with me over the past few days, and more or less decided to break up with Malard to make that happen. She\u2019s really serious about it. But she understands that I haven\u2019t sorted out what I want yet, and she\u2019s willing to give me time to do that. Still\u2026she\u2019s hurt that I haven\u2019t spent as much time thinking about \u2018us\u2019 as she has. I don\u2019t blame her. Heck, I\u2019ve been in love only to realize that my lover didn\u2019t feel the same way I did. It was one of the worst moments of my life, and I never wanted to cause Angelique that pain.\u201d<br /> <br /> Without realizing it at first, I begin touch Kitty\u2019s bracelet. I can still see her enchanting brown eyes and cat-like smile as though she were standing right before me, but almost as soon as her memory springs to mind, her eyes widen in terror and her smile turns to a scream. The sensation of my axe nearly severing her head still haunts me.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s voice drives away the memories. \u201cWell, I think you\u2019re doing the right thing. If you\u2019re meant to be with Angelique or Eris, you need to get to know them better. It\u2019s the only way you\u2019ll be able to find your heart.\u201d Sara and Karen voice their agreement.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re right. As awful as I feel, I know I\u2019m doing the right thing now. I\u2019m worried about Angelique, though. She\u2019s worried that if she breaks up with Malard, she might lose his protection. She asked if I would help her out, and I think she\u2019s hoping to move into the mansion.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course, she\u2019s welcome here,\u201d Sara says. \u201cPending Simon and Tavia\u2019s approval, of course. But I can\u2019t imagine they\u2019d object.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I already talked to Simon and he was fine with it,\u201d I say. \u201cBut the reason I\u2019m worried is because if I don\u2019t choose her, I\u2019m afraid she won\u2019t break up with Malard, even though I can tell she knows the relationship is bad for her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s look becomes instantly more stern. \u201cDid she try to blackmail you with that? You can\u2019t let her hold that over you in order to get what she wants.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d Sara agrees, \u201cThat kind of thing will poison a good relationship.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, it\u2019s not like that,\u201d I respond. \u201cAt least, I don\u2019t think she was trying to manipulate me. If she\u2019s going to be with me, she really wants me to want the relationship as much as she does. It\u2019s just that old habits die hard, and if she doesn\u2019t have a good reason to break her bond with Malard, I don\u2019t think she\u2019s going to be able to bring herself to do it. She needs to get away from him, though. I want to make sure she does.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, that\u2019s good, but don\u2019t hook up with her just because of that,\u201d Natalie tells me. \u201cHopefully, even if things don\u2019t work out between the two of you, you can at least be friends, and you can still convince her to get away from Malard.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, I\u2019d like that,\u201d I say, even though I seriously doubt that Angelique will want to be friends if I choose Eris instead. Assuming, of course, that Eris wants anything to do with me after I come clean with her too.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Almost all role-playing, little to add.<br /> <br /> If it seems like less is occurring, it is mostly as these sessions have been very role-playing intensive, lots of IC conversation and such. This is good thing, it brings out personalities a lot.<br /> <br /> Hope you are enjoying the drama. Stay tuned for next time where Alice talks to Eris, Sara meets Ildefonso, Chandra has a surprise presentation to the prince, and Alexia gets into some awkward conversations.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:30:21-07:00","id":433122,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s Lycanthrope night as our heroes go to Murder Ballads. But it is not just Werewolves there.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0200 Hours, Sunday, November 14, 2010<br /> <br /> This was a fun filled and enlightening evening.<br /> <br /> After a rather glamorous assembly for dinner, we hit Murder Ballads like Titans...and then stopped short. After spending some time up there and realizing the vantage it gives, I tend to scan the catwalks when we go in. Tonight, I spotted the Sheriff, Rebecca, Elizabeth, and another vampire I didn\u2019t recognize. I grabbed Axe and pulled her in front of Chandra, blocking as best I could while I let the others know what was happening. I knew that Chandra was potentially in danger since she still wasn\u2019t introduced. After a little discussion, Chandra decided to stop hiding. Thus I accompanied her (as a friend, I knew better than to think she needed my help) up as a nervous vampire I didn\u2019t know came over to address us. I was asked to stay behind. Out of some unnecessary need to be taken seriously, I stood at parade rest while Chandra met with the Prince.<br /> <br /> When it was over, she was formally accepted. We both expect the Prince will be calling on Chandra for special assignments since she told him the truth about being a Penanggalan. But that left us free to enjoy ourselves. Well for Chandra anyway. I went to the bar to watch as Axe and Bright Eyes went to meet the werewolves. Eris and Axe moved to the side for an uncomfortable conversation while Bright Eyes and Ildefonso paired off on the dance floor. I noticed Axe turn bright red and figured that was a good sign but then Eris became ...upset? Confused? Her normal lack of focus was replaced by an intensity like that of a caged animal. That intensity never left, it just changed focus as Axe and Eris kissed, then danced for a while. After that, they sat down to talk, but the werewolf was still noticeably upset. I stopped watching after that as it was apparent that Eris wasn\u2019t going to flip out on anyone.<br /> <br /> I led Noriko out to the floor and danced like I wanted the attention of a woman with cat-like reflexes. Some nights you have it, some you don\u2019t. Tonight, the crowds parted and I danced with my werecat like the end was coming. I was happy. We got to enjoy a night mostly like any normal couple. Somewhere through the haze of sweat and stage lights, I noticed Axe leaving with Eris and Tanya. Deirdre didn\u2019t seem to be interested in dislodging from Chandra, Cupcake, and Mouse. I don\u2019t honestly know where or with whom Karen and Nightshade went. But it was a night that put me a peace. I was not a supernatural creature, I was just some dude dancing the stress and the stupid of the world off in the waves of music.<br /> <br /> We got home and I led Noriko to my room. I wanted to keep going with my night of normal, but there was a question that had been bouncing around in my head. I needed to know how Noriko was turned. It seemed almost an intrusive question, but something told me I needed to hear it from my girlfriend, not from some book. The Colony is odd, even for shifters. Noriko was turned while on a trip to America. She was almost raped by a mugger when something ripped the guy apart. Then it attacked her. She woke up to a different world than the one she passed out in. Unfortunately I also learned that not only does she have her monthly killing quota, but she also has to find someone else to turn every decade, or she suffers the non-gentle insanity. Her first decade as a werecat is almost up. I think Noriko expect me to be revolted or send her away. When I didn\u2019t, she pounced me then and there.<br /> <br /> She\u2019s been suffering with this knowledge for a while now. She won\u2019t have to deal with it alone anymore.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, that was certainly the night of honesty, drama and debauchery that was promised. Ildefonso was just as handsome and twice the charming gentleman the others made him out to be. He also smelled like heaven, in an earthy, natural sort of way. We danced - a lot - and I could scarcely turn down his offer to \u2018while away the rest of the evening in quieter circumstances\u2019. His place is super swanky. If I hadn\u2019t been living in a manor for the past however many months, I might have felt more insecure about it - lots of (real) gold, statuary and some absolutely beautiful art pieces. He wore the class of it well too. Conveniently, Alice also spent the night with Eris in Sleeping Giant, and even drove, so the ride home is handled, provided I can pry her and Eris apart.<br /> <br /> We were not the only happy pairings, though I guess some of the others were more grouped than paired. Doc and Noriko had more than a few dances,and Doc was killing it on the floor. Chandra, Alexia and Catharine got pounced on by Deirdre, who certainly seemed woman enough to take on all three of them. Poor Alexia seemed somewhat flummoxed, though, I think, more from her round of conversation with the prospective students for her school. I was... quite distracted but I did glance over at least once to see Timothy with a wicked grin aimed at Tracey and Alexia looking sternly at him.<br /> <br /> I think that was after they introduced Clarissa and Deanna to the twins. At least, it was after the text Natalie sent me asking if it was ok to, which was confusing... I mean, it\u2019s not like I\u2019m a gatekeeper to either of them and they\u2019ll meet when the school thing gets off the ground anyway. I\u2019ll have to ask Natalie how that went though. Hopefully well - those four are a large portion of the prospective students.<br /> <br /> Anyways, other than our assignations, the headliners of the evening were of course Alice and Eris. That went... interestingly. Like I mentioned, Alice came back to Sleeping Giant with Eris, so that counts as good in my book. It was touch and go for a bit - the rangers were certainly worried. The still distress we could see from across the way didn\u2019t match up with her usual states of either manic or asleep. Alice was being heart meltingly comforting, so it seemed under control to me, but I don\u2019t know the wild eyed woman as well as the others.<br /> <br /> To be fair though, apparently they didn\u2019t know her as well as they thought. As soon as the pair got back to us, Eris asked for help figuring out who she was (presumably responding to a \u2018wanting to get to know you better\u2019 speech). This kinda floored the others, who hadn\u2019t realized Eris didn\u2019t remember anything from before they found her. Hell, she didn\u2019t remember being found, just waking up in Deirdre\u2019s house. According to Eris, the fact you have serious amnesia is the kind of thing you only tell your mate. I can\u2019t even imagine having a gap like that, not knowing where I came from. I hope we can help her figure it out, regardless of where Alice plants her flag.<br /> <br /> We did try to go through what she did remember some, but it mostly just upset her. Alice got her to calm down a little by having Eris focus her attention on her, though calm down maybe isn\u2019t accurate. Distract sounds better, considering Eris\u2019 subsequent announcement that she should stop looking at Alice like that unless they were going to mate. After that Alice worked on finding common ground with who Eris is now, even if she doesn\u2019t remember who she might have been. I missed what was assuredly an adorable conversation, as I was dragged out onto the dance floor after I missed the conversation change thanks to being in brainstorming mode. Not that I\u2019m complaining. I mentioned Ildefonso is to die for, right?<br /> <br /> All in all, it was nice to have a night out, with regular human interest drama being all that\u2019s on the card. There was something of a minor political-type standoff right when we got in, which was tense in a \u2018not your night off\u2019 kinda way, but it was resolved positively and fairly quickly. That will come back up later, I\u2019m sure, but for now, all I have in my forseen future is a ~45 minute long car ride to gossip with Alice.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> We walk into Murder Ballads like we own the place, which I guess is more or less true given Natalie\u2019s influence. The krewe is a pretty good-looking bunch, so we draw some attention when we enter the place. I catch sight of Deirdre and Eris across the floor, but before I can head that way, Doc grabs me and pulls me in front of Chandra. I\u2019m bewildered until I realize he\u2019s using me to shield her from the view of some people on the catwalks. Good thing I\u2019m fairly tall.<br /> <br /> Doc explains that the guys on the catwalk are vampires, and Chandra is sort of trespassing on their territory. It could be trouble, But to her credit, Chandra decides to meet it head on. She\u2019s going to present herself to the Vampire Prince, who I gather is one of the vampires above us. Doc and Alexia go with her, thoug Alexia keeps her distance. Doc asks if I can jump up there if things go south. I assure him that won\u2019t be a problem. I wish I had my axe, but I suspect my Primeval claws might work better against vampires anyway.<br /> <br /> I gotta say, it feels good to have Doc relying on me for backup. It makes me feel like part of the team.<br /> <br /> I text Deirdre to let her know that we have a situation and that I\u2019ll head over to join them as soon as it\u2019s resolved, then I pick a spot at the bar with a good view of the catwalk and hang out with Sara until Chandra\u2019s done or something goes down.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Fortunately the vampires didn\u2019t get violent. The Prince seems more intrigued by Chandra than angry with her. Somehow I\u2019m not sure that\u2019s better. Anyway, now that\u2019s settled, the hard part begins. I have to talk to Eris. I take a deep breath, and Sara wishes me luck and follows me over to the shadowed table where the werewolves are gathered. Deirdre and Eris are there, of course, and there\u2019s another blonde woman I haven\u2019t met. I assume the suave-looking guy is Ildefonso. Sara seems to like what she sees, and wastes no time sliding into the booth next to him.<br /> <br /> Eris is happy to see me. She\u2019s not quite as disheveled as she was yesterday, and she looks ravishing in her clubwear: loose-fitting black pants and a sexy, midriff-baring bustier top that I\u2019m pretty sure Deirdre had something to do with. There\u2019s a hungry, passionate look in her eyes as she gazes at me. It makes me melt.<br /> <br /> Still, I stay resolved and after introductions and small talk are over and Sara starts chatting up Ildefonso, I ask Eris to step aside with me so we can talk. We find a quiet corner not too far from the rest of her pack.<br /> <br /> I try to be as gentle as I can. I tell Eris that I\u2019m totally into her, but I also met someone else recently, and I\u2019m not sure where my heart really lies. I hold my breath, waiting to see if she\u2019s going to freak out and attack me. I don\u2019t really think she will, but I\u2019m not quite sure how she\u2019s going to react.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo should me and this other girl fight?\u201d Eris asks. \u201cDo you want us to fight over you? I\u2019ll fight for you.\u201d She\u2019s deadly serious, and her gaze as she stares at me is intense and determined. God, she has gorgeous eyes.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo,\u201d I quickly stop her. \u201cNo, it\u2019s not like that. I don\u2019t really know either of you very well, but I\u2019d like to get to know you better. That\u2019s the only way I\u2019ll be able to figure out who I should be with. I mean, I\u2019m really into you, but I barely know you. So let\u2019s get to know each other better.\u201d I give her a smile that I hope is sweet and encouraging.<br /> <br /> Eris freezes and stares at me like a deer in headlights, and then she starts to panic.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know how to do that,\u201d she says, sounding desparate and pitiful. \u201cI don\u2019t know anything about myself. I don\u2019t know how to make you know me better.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m shocked to notice that she\u2019s actually so anxious that she\u2019s trembling.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know how to make you like me!\u201d she almost wails. \u201cI want to win, but I don\u2019t know how!\u201d<br /> <br /> I feel terrible. I don\u2019t know whether this is better or worse than how things went down with Angelique. And I thought Eris would be less complicated\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, listen,\u201d I move forward and place my hands on her shoulders, trying to comfort her. \u201cDon\u2019t worry, I\u2019ll help you! We just need to spend more time together. You know, talk about things we like, that kind of thing. It\u2019ll be okay.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut I don\u2019t know what to talk about! I don\u2019t who I am. I don\u2019t remember.\u201d<br /> <br /> That catches my attention.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you mean?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t remember before Deirdre found me in the forest.\u201d<br /> <br /> Hmmm. I might need some backup here. I suggest that we go have a seat with her friends, and guide her back to the pack\u2019s table. The others, especially Deirdre, look worried and they might be getting a little angry at me, so I try to explain what Eris is upset about. They\u2019re as surprised as I was. The rest of the pack had no idea that Eris didn\u2019t remember anything from before she was found. Deirdre asks why she didn\u2019t say anything before.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s something you only tell your mate,\u201d Eris explains matter-of-factly. Well, regardless of how things play out between us, I guess it\u2019s good I came along to help her open up about her amnesia.<br /> <br /> Ildefonso, Sara and Deirdre start asking Eris about what she does remember. It\u2019s not much. She remembers being chased, bright lights and yelling, and a big red dog. She doesn\u2019t remember when Deirdre found her, just waking up later in Deirdre\u2019s house. The more questions they ask, the more panicked Eris becomes. I can tell that she\u2019s literally about to crawl right over the table and bolt, so I shoot them all a stern look and then take her head in my hands to gently turn her so that she\u2019s staring at me.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, it\u2019s okay, we don\u2019t have to talk about the past or the things you don\u2019t remember. That\u2019s not important right now. I don\u2019t need that to get to know you. Let\u2019s just talk, okay? Not about anything important\u2026just talking.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris calms down a bit. She\u2019s still agitated, but what I\u2019m doing is helping. She nods a little. \u201cOkay, but if I keep looking at you like this, we\u2019re going to have to mate,\u201d she says, with all seriousness. I feel myself turn bright red, and Sara takes the cue to invite Ildefonso out onto the dance floor. He\u2019s more than happy to oblige. Deirdre also gets up to give us a little more privacy, and heads over to talk to Alexia, Chandra, and Catherine. The other werewolf girl, Tanya, sticks around to keep an eye on us, but she seems pretty nice and keeps to herself.<br /> <br /> \u201cUm\u2026\u201d I try to cover my composure a bit, but Eris catches onto the fact that I\u2019m a bit embarassed.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can\u2019t mate until you choose?\u201d<br /> <br /> This is so weird. \u201cUm\u2026probably not. It would be better if we didn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d she seems disappointed but not upset.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, what kind of things do you like?\u201d<br /> <br /> She immediately becomes anxious again. \u201cI don\u2019t know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay, well, I\u2019ll start. I like hiking, rock-climbing and caving. I like being outdoors and active. How about you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris nods. \u201cI like the the park,\u201d she says, referring to Sleeping Giant.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do like about it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI like the trees.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMe too,\u201d I smile. I take her hand to try and comfort and connect with her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI like the sunrise. And the night air. And fireflies,\u201d she says, warming to the conversation.<br /> \u201cI love fireflies! Do you ever try to catch them?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris nods. \u201cI like cars with the top down.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou mean convertibles? I can take the top off my jeep. Maybe when the weather warms up we can go for ride sometime.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris smiles. \u201cYes, I want to do that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s way too cold for that right now, though,\u201d I say. \u201cHonestly, the weather here is way too cold for me. I\u2019m from Arizona. It\u2019s really hot and dry there. There\u2019s a lot of desert. I don\u2019t know if you would like it, but I kind of miss it. There\u2019s a lot of great caves and rock-climbing there. Not a lot trees, though. At least, not in the parts where I grew up.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris listens intently. She seems to be thinking about what Arizona must be like, perhaps trying to imagine the feeling of the hot dry air or the blazing sun.<br /> <br /> We managed to converse for some time, and I learn a bit more about her. She likes the outdoors as much as I do, and she reminds me that she wants me to hunt with her sometime, maybe tracking down some errant spirit or something. I\u2019m game. Eventually, she calms down and though she\u2019s obviously still a bit anxious, she\u2019s no longer panicked. Her eyes still smolder, though. Our conversation has not quieted her desire to \u201cmate\u201d with me. I\u2019m starting to lose my chaste resolve.<br /> <br /> I occurs to me that the Huntress has been very quiet tonight. Does that mean she approves of Eris? Or is she just tired of dealing with my love life? I don\u2019t know, nor do I care. For tonight, at least, she\u2019s giving me some privacy, and I\u2019m going to enjoy it.<br /> <br /> I ask Eris if she\u2019d like to dance, and she\u2019s pretty eager to get out onto the dance floor now that she\u2019s more collected. I quickly realize that asking her to dance was probably not the best idea if I want to avoid sleeping with her again. She knows how to dance. It\u2019s not practiced or even especially graceful, but she\u2019s intense and sensual. We dance close. And who am I kidding, I absolutely want to sleep with her again.<br /> <br /> As if she can read my thoughts, she tells me that if we keep dancing, she\u2019s going to mate with me. It\u2019s a statement, not a question. It only takes me a moment to decide.<br /> <br /> \u201cListen, if we hook up again, it doesn\u2019t mean I don\u2019t still have to figure things out. You understand that, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. But I still want to mate,\u201d she says. And then we\u2019re heading out to my jeep to drive back to her place at Sleeping Giant State Park. I catch Sara\u2019s eye on our way out so she knows where I\u2019m going. She gives me a smug thumbs up. Heck, even Alexia smiles approvingly at us on our way out. I think the krewe favors Eris.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Eris lives with Deirdre and a couple of the other werewolf rangers in a house at Sleeping Giant State Park. But I didn\u2019t really get a chance to examine her room when we first arrived. We were WAY too busy then.<br /> <br /> Now that we are snuggled up together on her bed, cuddling, though, I have a chance to look around. Her room is pretty spartan. It\u2019s clean but not tidy. The closet door is open, and she doesn\u2019t have much to wear other than her ranger\u2019s uniforms, a set of clubwear, and one or two casual outfits, one of which is haphazardly thrown across her big, soft chair. Some of her clothes might be hand-me-downs from Deirdre. There\u2019s a fuzzy rug on the floor and a few odds and ends on the nightstand, but otherwise she doesn\u2019t have much. I comment that her room needs some personal touches.<br /> <br /> \u201cDeirdre has a lot of things,\u201d she says. \u201cShe has pictures of rock stars all over her walls.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMaybe we should find you some things to decorate this place. You know, stuff you like.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I would like that. Especially if it will make you come here more.\u201d<br /> <br /> I smile. \u201cThat would be good.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad you\u2019re here.\u201d<br /> <br /> I think for a moment as I snuggle my head against her neck. \u201cYeah. I\u2019m glad we did this too.\u201d<br /> <br /> There is a moment\u2019s quiet, then Eris speaks again, confidently.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to win.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Saturday, November 13th, 2010<br /> <br /> -I am at Murder Ballads tonight<br /> <br /> -Oh dear, protective Doc time.<br /> <br /> -Not even the problem I was worried about.<br /> <br /> -Okay, time to see forever.<br /> <br /> -Oh yea, that\u2019s the ticket.<br /> <br /> -Things seem smooth with Chandra, which is good as in retrospect I don\u2019t think I can put Vampires to sleep.<br /> <br /> -Chandra in takes no guff stance is more than kinda hot. I am just saying.<br /> <br /> -Emergency #1 over. Huzzah.<br /> <br /> -Doc and Sara are watching Alice, Imma help Alexia.<br /> <br /> -Deanna may be crazy.<br /> <br /> -Perhaps sweet Alexia took the X-men thing too far.<br /> <br /> -Time to distract Deanna.<br /> <br /> -Deanna is pretty cute.<br /> <br /> -Is, is Deanna putting limits on me? The heck?<br /> <br /> -Weird.<br /> <br /> -I am not Deanna\u2019s lovestruck sycophant. She is unaware of this.<br /> <br /> -Alexia has clearly lost control of the situation.<br /> <br /> -It is sadly too hilarious for me to intervene.<br /> <br /> -Especially when Deanna does the batman voice.<br /> <br /> -@Nerak, you need to hear Deanna do the batman voice.<br /> <br /> -Okay, Alexia flees in shame and horror to the two pairs of bosoms over there.<br /> <br /> -Three. Make that three pairs of bosoms.<br /> <br /> -Damn girl!<br /> <br /> -\u2026Speaking of which, Alice just left with Eris. Unsure if that means things went well or poorly.<br /> <br /> -Am I seriously the only one in the Krewe not sleeping with a shapeshifter tonight?<br /> <br /> -How does that even happen?<br /> <br /> -Oh well headed to the 27 club for my slave girl then back home, were Deanna cannot smirk at me.<br /> <br /> -But it has been a good night for the Krewe.<br /> <br /> -I think.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Chandra met and negotiated with the Prince, Jackson Harvard. It is, I think, the first time the Prince actually has shown up in the game.<br /> <br /> Deanna James being Batman is largely due to how the whole special class was originally introduced to her. She was described as \u201chas no powers, but still special and part of the class\u201d by Alexia in previous conversation so Deanna, using her usual power of interpreting things in an interesting way, assumes she will be like Batman to the Justice League given the sort of X-Men vibe Alexia was describing. So having had time to let that percolate, she has decided she is Batman.<br /> <br /> Also, speaking of her superpower, since Natalie\u2019s flirting, even gentle flirting, sets up whoever she is flirting with as the pursuer, Deanna is now sure Natalie is clearly crazy in love with her, since she is Batman therefore awesome, so she has to totally play this thing cool while she decides if a Bi fling would kill or enhance her mystique.<br /> <br /> In other news, everyone loves Deanna.<br /> <br /> Finally it was determined that even counting Simon and Jasmine, it seems every member of the Krewe went to bed with a shapeshifter that night except Natalie. This was not planned, but there you go.<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T21:49:25-07:00","id":439367,"title":"","content":"Fantastic as always Baron, my thanks to you and your players <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> I almost died from cutesplosion from both Noriko and Eris in those two posts. Eris certainly gets my vote. So much nyawwwwww.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-12T23:15:28-07:00","id":439487,"title":"","content":"Cool. Their issues are not radically dissimilar but different. Alice is having to pick between the feral but naive Eris or the dark and mysterious yet issue laden Angelique. Not a planned thing, but it just sort of happened that way (Alice's player had no plans for her to get entangled with Werewolves either, it just sorta happened). I am glad you are enjoying and appreciate the comments.<br /> <br /> Next time the PCs buckle down and get back to some investigating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T14:26:32-07:00","id":440466,"title":"","content":"Maybe I am dense (Not outside of the realm of possibly), but it seems to me that between two baggage laden options, Angelique might be the lighter of two loads.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 03-13-2015, 05:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T20:18:01-07:00","id":440820,"title":"","content":"I tend to find that on the whole unplanned character developments or progressions are more enjoyable or interesting than planned ones. Of course, there is the potential for them to go horribly wrong or take the character far from what you wanted, but most of the time its worth the ride.<br /> <br /> @Omenseer, I can certainly see that point of view. I don't know whether its my time playing/running Werewolf (admittedly Apocalypse rather than Forsaken) or perhaps the influence of the other journals but I just feel there is something *off* about Angelique, from my reading she seems to clearly have too many possible ulterior motives like access to the house and its resources, being drawn to dark powers/actually a balewolf or seeking protection. That and it depends on how things with old man Malard go, he's certainly from what I remember of his description not someone that I would want as an enemy.<br /> Then again, Eris comes with an imperial fucktonne of baggage, being feral and the whole missing memories baggage, so I suppose it comes down to personal preference.<br /> <br /> Though I won't blame Angelique for violating the no-werewolf-on-werewolf romance rule, I've done that or been intending to do that with all my werewolf characters to date. It even worked out pretty well for my Silverfang Alpha and his Bone Gnawer-er beta, who were certainly an odd couple and miraculously the rest of the pack never actually found out...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1060,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","user":"Kale Fangblade","date":". 03-13-2015, 11:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1060-kale-fangblade","name":"Kale Fangblade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1060_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T21:40:54-07:00","id":440871,"title":"","content":"You didn't plan that? I always just assumed you were deliberately doing this sympathy thing going on with the other supernaturals through their Geists and their Keys.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2111-doeman","name":"DoeMan","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-14T14:54:13-07:00","id":441862,"title":"","content":"Maybe? I mean, Angelique was mentored by a Bale Hound, was in a relationship with said Bale Hound and may or may not be pledged to a Maeljin. She has areas she will be killed if she enters, she is distrusted by all but one local werewolf, and is in her second inappropriate relationship with a Werewolf who is sitting in his house hoping to fight a Great Beast that may or may not be describable as a God. Oh, and she might or might not qualify as a Bale Hound depending on how you define it. Also, her current boyfriend is crazy, and even if he logically knows to let her go Werewolves are not beings of pure logic.<br /> <br /> Eris has amnesia, very poor social skills, is not crazy about wearing clothes, and may or may not be hunted by some sort of organization that was able to keep her prisoner and presumably did some sort of experiments on her based on her mental state. She is feral enough she has issues with humans. One could also question her not telling her pack this.<br /> <br /> It's sort of a toss up, depending on what colors your red flags redder<br /> <br /> I do not ever plan relationships. I mean, I am not dumb, some things occurred to me as possible (Noriko and Doc, for instance, or Chandra and Alexia) because they began knowing the person of their preferred sex and had something of a bond with them. But I never <i>decided</i> they were getting together...neither Noriko nor Chandra made the first move (it would not have occurred to Chandra to do so). I will say Alexia's player made it clear she wanted Alexia to hook up with Chandra, so that was expected but not planned...though it made Chandra's revelation as a penanggalan more interesting. I confess given Chandra's horrific secret I kinda hoped that would happen. With Alice, Honestly the PCs decided to persue the Bale Hound, meet Malard, and go to Sleeping Giant more or less without my input. I did not direct them to any of that. Indeed, my expectation was they would continue after the Blood Bather; I was planning to deal with the Werewolf stuff more after Forsaken 2e came out, though I did not shy away when that was what they wanted to do, nor did I do anything to forestall it when they did some digging.<br /> <br /> Now, it was not accidental that the women took interest in Alice. When she met Eris I figured Eris would be attracted to her; she is right up Eris's ally and is not actually a Werewolf. Eris did put moves on Alice. When she met with Angelique I decided Angelique would be intrigued as she showed clear interest and is a pretty redhead. She also can clearly take care of herself. And true to Angelique's terrible taste in partners, she is a death tainted Claimed psycho. But when Alice came into the picture, I did not do anything to engineer her meeting Angelique or Eris. Indeed, Eris did not even come to mind, and pretty much everyone at the table finds Angelique's pic attractive OOC.<br /> <br /> Overall my strengths as a GM are in creating scenarios and reacting well to what the PCs want to do, and keeping things interesting. I am not so good at masterful plans where everything falls into place. I am a far better GM of sandboxes than tight narratives.<br /> <br /> I can't remember if I had mentioned, but most NPCs are either Hetroflexible or Homoflexible, or bi of course. In general unless it does not fit them, it is possible for a PC of either gender to become involved with an NPC...some involve more work or baggage. Chandra is really mostly gay, for instance. It would not have been impossible for a male to get involved with her, but it would have taken more work. Tavia is mostly straight, it would take a woman more work to get her in the sack. Karl is mostly straight, it would take more work for a male to woo him. Noriko and Tatum are pretty much bi. Either could easily go for either sex. Karen is a lesbian; it would not be possible for her to have a consensual relationship with a man, she is sort of an exception, but not the only one.<br /> <br /> That help?<br /> <br /> ETA: Don't take my comments about Alice as disliking her. Alice rocks. All the PCs are a little broken, but the broken toys are the most fun. I am just saying she has issues she brings to a relationship, but so do the others.<br /> <br /> ETA II: Okay, maybe Alexia is stable, but then she is the one happily married to a penanggalan so maybe not. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-14-2015, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T14:28:14-07:00","id":453150,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s that time again. The Sin-Eaters have been busy ,and are moving back to dealing with one of their older villains.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0930 Hours, Sunday, November 14, 2010<br /> <br /> Finally learning how Noriko \u201cjoined\u201d the Colony and helping her make peace a little more with her situation did good things for me. When I woke up, things just felt more in line. Meditation was both incredibly relaxing and quick.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t expect to see Cupcake for a few hours, so I headed downstairs planning to make food. Rose had beat me to it so we had eggs and fruit instead. We that actually made it home or stayed in last night were just finishing up breakfast when Chandra and Cupcake arrived. Rose gave Cupcake the look while Chandra pulled me to the side.<br /> <br /> While they certainly seemed to have enjoyed themselves with Mouse, Chandra had been thinking about her meeting with the Prince. She wanted me to set up an interview with Rebecca. The honest purpose was to find leverage on the Prince, but I warned her Rebecca wasn\u2019t likely to betray him. I knew she didn\u2019t expect Rebecca to tell her dark secrets but I pointed out that she wasn\u2019t likely going to do anything to further strain their relationship. We sat down and I told her everything I knew about Rebecca and her relationship with her Sire and as much as I could about Vampires in general. The consensus was that she should play the \u201cinnocent and ignorant foreigner\u201d for all it was worth but not to push too hard. We were both a little amused that I was the one to tell her these things. At least I hope she was amused and not embarrassed. I agreed to call Rebecca and try to set up a meeting later tonight.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1330 Hours, Sunday, November 14, 2010<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t understand how Axe can find the most unlikely actions to irritate me like no one else. I was happy this morning, after last night especially. I wasn\u2019t grumpy, I\u2019d had breakfast, I was helpful to Chandra. I even stepped back and watched while Karen decreed to Noriko that she planned to \u201cgoth you up.\u201d I wasn\u2019t at all upset with that idea, but it was amusing to watch Noriko decline in a polite but eventually firm way.<br /> <br /> And then, BAM! Axe runs into the TV Room obviously just in from a morning run and announces to everyone, including Tantrum, Mouse, and Karen that she just free climbed the Bluffs \u201cin five minutes!\u201d Everyone was speechless. Yes, it was an incredible feat and not one I think I could manage. But the Bluffs are at least 100 feet up, and she had no equipment. Worse, we had no idea she was going to do it. The peacock\u2019s aura of pride that surrounded her stabbed a needle into my nerves. I apparently became Mr. Buzzkill when I asked which one of the three mortals present she wanted to kill? I probably could have gone about discussing it with Axe differently, probably should have actually. But she acts like a teenager with no concept of judgement sometimes, and she can\u2019t always blame The Huntress. She tried to \u201creassure\u201d me that she was safe because of all her various powers. Still in front of Tantrum. I get that she is skilled and at least as powerful as any of us, but she takes unnecessary risks with no backup or even a plan B. And she doesn\u2019t given any thoughts to what she says around who. And now I just feel like a grouchy old man.<br /> <br /> Karen led Tantrum out of the room so we could discuss Blood Bather issue after that. Axe just sat next to Bright Eyes (who gave me a dirty look) and looked restless. I want to find a way to connect with Axe but she has no context for where I\u2019m coming from most of the time, and apparently I\u2019m in the same boat. Also, I\u2019m off topic. Mouse has been getting worried about the two turncoat Bathers, so we decided it was not wise to doubt the Psychic\u2019s intuition. We are all in agreement that we will have to do things to Mariah that none of us are normally comfortable with. Bright Eyes shot down my idea of taking the cut up pieces sealed in concrete into the Underworld. Her objection to having to then perform a Hero\u2019s Quest once we figured out how to permanently kill the Blood Bather was not without merit. The Underworld or any other realm is unstable enough that we might lose a piece or have it stolen and we never know until it\u2019s too late. That prompted the conversation about needing to plant a flag in the Underworld. Axe was unaware we were planning anything other than a long visit, so she perked back up again at that. We\u2019ll have to spend some time on cleanup and clear out duty soon, but the Blood Bathers are on the front burner for the moment. I didn\u2019t want to move on Mariah until we had some clue as to what this Soul Destruction power she came up with was all about. Bright Eyes and Gretchen came with me to the Library to figure out anything we could about a source for this power, any defense, or really anything actionable we could find.<br /> <br /> It was slow going at first, not least because we had to keep Gretchen from asking questions she already knew would get her cut to ribbons by my girlfriend. Then we decided to change course since we weren\u2019t finding anything about Blood Bathers and their spells that suggested this was even possible. That was about the time Nightshade came in to let us know she was sending Axe to spy on Mariah. I was far more jaded than I should have been but I was still annoyed with Axe from earlier. Nightshade tried to calm me down by reminding me that she needed to find her place in the Krewe and we didn\u2019t know what she could do. I resisted the urge to bring up the powers she listed off like groceries and agreed that Axe should be allowed to prove herself useful. I really hope whatever I said didn\u2019t come out sounded as much like an asshole as it looks written down here. I asked that she get an ear curl so we could help if she needed it. I didn\u2019t want Axe to learn the hard way that we were dealing with shit not even we can come back from just to prove herself worthy to me. I didn\u2019t say that, but given the looks I\u2019d gotten earlier and the dejected face Axe wore after I scolded her, I\u2019m pretty sure that\u2019s what she feels she has to do. I don\u2019t like being the old man on the mountain.<br /> <br /> Getting back to our research, we realized that the power Mariah is using likely comes from an artifact as thankfully this seems to be something she can\u2019t do without all the prep work. After about an hour and a half, the best thing we\u2019d come up with is that we needed an expert. I called The Collector to see if he could discuss possible objects that could create such a situation. Bright Eyes was very interested in hearing from The Collector and also feeling silly. Just as our expert answered the phone, she licked the back of my neck. I shot her a look before inquiring about a meeting. The Collector was actually in New York CIty and wouldn\u2019t be back until tomorrow, but agreed to meet sometime between 1400 and 2100 Hours. To be fair, it almost sounded like he was planning a museum heist, so I didn\u2019t ask for any details over the phone.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2000 Hours, Sunday, November 14, 2010<br /> <br /> Axe has been busy and it sounds like she\u2019s dancing on the razor\u2019s edge. Mariah has some kind of pheromones that are both sexual and apparently almost hypnotic. Axe can\u2019t be in the same room with her target without wanting to forget the mission and throw herself at Mariah. She has been watching from a distance, but Mariah is about to leave and Axe is going to follow her. I don\u2019t like it, but I wasn\u2019t given a say in what Axe was doing to fulfill her duty to the Krewe. I should be there backing her up. Not because she can\u2019t do it alone but because she shouldn\u2019t have to. We\u2019re going to have to have a talk when this is over. Anyway, Axe wants us to investigate the vanity mirror at Mariah\u2019s house. She said it didn\u2019t show Mariah\u2019s reflection when all the other mirrors did. She\u2019s going to text us the security code as soon as she gets it and we\u2019ll head out.<br /> <br /> If anything happens to Axe, I may be more enthusiastic with Mariah than I have any right to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> My wives, in case it is not already clear, are silly ducks. Karen, the sweetling, has a deathly fear of being tossed aside in favor of someone with \u2018boy parts\u2019. So I made much of her, and them, when I got back and they got downstairs. It was a nice relaxing afternoon to follow up a nice relaxing morning and evening. But that\u2019s not the silly part.<br /> <br /> It seems in my absence that they and Tatum decided that Goth Train (a Goth version of Soul Train you see) needed to be a Thing. What kind of thing - TV show/cartoon/band/album name - was unclear, but we were required to pick instruments. Ocarina is apparently not goth enough (triangle and cowbell were also discluded before it got to me) and just dancing on stage doesn\u2019t suffice, but I think I could handle bass guitar. It\u2019s been awhile since I\u2019ve played, but it\u2019s like riding a bike, right? We\u2019ll be too damn hot for anyone to care anyway. So far I think it\u2019s the four of us - everyone else turned them down, despite Natalie\u2019s sultan clap and Tatum\u2019s puppy dog eyes. We couldn\u2019t even get Noriko to play drums for us, and everyone loves playing drums. Maybe I\u2019ll claim them instead if she doesn\u2019t want them.<br /> <br /> We did gather quite a crowd, so everyone but Alexia and Chandra were in the TV room when Alice burst in super excited to tell us it only took her five minutes to scale the 10-story cliff to the beach! I was both impressed and happy - that sort of thing was really her element and she looked revitalized. That is, until Doc got grumpy at her for doing it alone. He had a point - I certainly don\u2019t want anything to happen to her - but the way her excitement just sort of drained out of her and left her kinda slumped was heart-breaking. I pulled her over to sit by me and promised I\u2019d go climb it with her next time, which is kinda terrifying, but I have to now, and not just because I said I would. If I go, I bet she\u2019ll promise to keep me safe again,and that\u2019s worth 20 storys of rock-climbing.<br /> <br /> She seemed a little better after that, between me promising Doc didn\u2019t think she was an idiot anymore than he did me, and the idea of rock climbing again and her date with Angelique tomorrow. Not that the last is pure happiness. She\u2019s planning on telling Angelique some about her past and is worried how that\u2019ll go over. I hope it goes well for her sake. A rejection for that would deal with her dating dilemma, at the cost of a big chunk of self-respect and confidence, I imagine. It\u2019s hard to grow past you old failings when they continue to control your fate. I also hope she doesn\u2019t get lured in either direction by simply being needed. It\u2019s a heady thing but not often enough to sustain someone. I think she gets that though.<br /> <br /> After a late lunch (bao ban! They were delicious. I think Alexia felt guilty about... something? re: Jasmine and so made her favorite), it was time to get back to work. Catherine,with her strong foreSight, was getting fretty about the lovebirds Carol and Jenny, which lights something of a fire for certain. We still don\u2019t know how to counter her personal blood magic thing, so containment and separation of certain... focal points of power is the plan. I argued against extreme separation, on the grounds of not wanting to have to go through a Hero\u2019s Journey once we did find the counter that would return her to the cycle of fate. That definitely rules out the Underworld, though other things do too. Bringing it up did lead to discussing our plans concerning answering its pull \u2013 all of us need to spend sometime there, with how connected we are with death. So we need to make it safe. I'm hoping to set up my own little beachside campsite \u2013 the RV might be a bit rough to get down there though. With any luck, we might even make it safe enough for visitors. I'm sure Karen will appreciate that. Just gotta convince Doc and Natalie...<br /> <br /> But, back on topic - Doc did want to figure out how to deal with the ring, so he and I hit the books, with Gretchen's help and undying interest in everyone\u2019s sex life. Alice decided, with Natalie\u2019s encouragement, to do some surveillance of the cult leader and make sure she\u2019s not up to anything involving the girls. It was a little distracting, but Natalie\u2019s right - she needs to feel like she\u2019s a proper part of things. Besides, like with the cliff, she\u2019s a big girl who knows the risks and is really good at that sort of thing. We even got a call a bit ago, after we spoke with Janus, to let us know the leader was going out and she planned to follow and there was something we should maybe follow up on at the house while she\u2019s out. We\u2019re waiting for the text that will include the security code and let us know she\u2019s gone now.<br /> <br /> In happier news, we did in fact get to call Janus (well, Doc did. I just listened over his shoulder). See, our research found that the effect on the rings likely came from an artifact and he\u2019s kinda our guy for that sort of thing. At least, he is if I have anything to say about it. We\u2019re even getting to meet with him again, but not until tomorrow afternoon when he gets back in town. The final conclusion of the call, other than the meeting, was that one should never touch or lick evil artifacts, the back of Doc\u2019s neck tastes funny, and Gretchen is not allowed to make out in the library. I think I heard Doc\u2019s phone beep though, so I\u2019m going to go poke him until he tells me our Little Red is safe.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> Now that Sara and I are back home at the mansion, I\u2019m trying to figure out what to do with myself.<br /> <br /> Back home at the mansion. I never thought I\u2019d say that. It still feels odd, and my room still feels too big and too empty. Eris\u2019 room was more to my liking, honestly. Still, if I\u2019m going to become a member of this krewe, I\u2019d better get used to living in a drafty, haunted mansion.<br /> <br /> <i>Don\u2019t become too cozy. You mustn\u2019t lose your predator\u2019s edge.</i><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t plan to. If we can hunt down this Balehound, or those blood-bathers we\u2019ve been talking about, I\u2019ll have work to do.<br /> <i><br /> Don\u2019t try to sound so reluctant. I know you want to hunt. And kill. How long has it been since our last? A month? Two? The craving is there. I can sense it.</i><br /> <br /> I take a deep breath to try and clear my head. Sure, I\u2019ve been distracted over the past couple of days, but I am getting impatient for a new kill. Someone who deserves it, of course.<br /> <br /> <i>Of course.</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress is being patronizing. I don\u2019t actually crave the kill as much as she makes out. At least, I keep telling myself that. Still, I would really like to take action against\u2026something. Something meaningful. Someone who really deserves my axe.<br /> <br /> I decide to deal with the tension by taking a nice, long jog. Even in the winter, the beach below the cliffs make for a nice run. By the time I\u2019m finished, my head feels clearer even if my lungs are burning from the frigid air. I\u2019m in better spirits. I stand on the beach and catch my breath. Now that I\u2019ve stopped running, the chill starts to sink. Even so, I don\u2019t want to go inside just yet.<br /> <br /> Without even realizing it, I keep staring at the cliff leading up to the mansion\u2019s yard. There\u2019s a stairway cut into it leading down the pier and dock, but I\u2019m studying the cliff itself. It\u2019s a rough, dark rock wall. It wouldn\u2019t be too hard to climb. There are plenty of handholds, plenty of little ledges where my foot could find purchase. I take a few moments to pick out a likely route up to the top. I\u2019m feeling energized from my run and it\u2019s been too long since I\u2019ve had a good climb.<br /> <br /> I run toward the cliff and leap for some low handholds. It\u2019s not hard to get a good grip even though my fingers are freezing, and the rest is easy. It doesn\u2019t take me long to scale it. It feels good. Now I\u2019m ready to head back in.<br /> <br /> I feel good. Flush with the thrill of the climb, I find the others hanging out in the TV room. As soon as I enter, I can\u2019t help but tell everyone that I scaled the cliff in under five minutes. I don\u2019t know why I expect them to be impressed, or to at least share in my triumph. Not that it was really much of a climb, but you know. It\u2019s the little things.<br /> <br /> Instead, Doc get mad. He starts scolding me. He asks me which of the people in the room might have died to resurrect me if I\u2019d fallen and killed myself. I try to tell him that I\u2019m an expert climber. I wasn\u2019t going to fall. He doesn\u2019t care, even when I point out that I can turn into a flock of birds just by thinking about it. I was never in any real danger.<br /> <br /> All I can do in the face of Doc\u2019s disappointment, though, is admit that I was being careless, even if I don\u2019t agree. What the heck is Doc\u2019s problem, anyway? <br /> <br /> I\u2019m crestfallen. I feel like an idiot again, and the only thing that makes it better is Sara\u2019s sympathetic hand on my arm and her promises that she\u2019ll scale the cliff with me again sometime, with the proper equipment. That\u2019s something to look forward to, at least. It\u2019s always fun sharing my passions for rock climbing. Sara looks a bit anxious about it, though, so I promise that I won\u2019t let her fall. Then she gives me a wanton look that makes me blush. I think she likes it when I get all protective.<br /> <br /> I want to stalk off to the shower and just forget about it, but it seems like I interrupted a serious talk about the blood-bathers. It seems like Alexia\u2019s new girlfriend, Catherine, is worried, so the krewe is discussing our next steps in dealing with them. Doc wants to do more research. Big surprise there. Sounds like he hopes to find a way to prevent the queen blood-bather from destroying us with some sort of magic. Fair enough, but how much does he expect to learn from the library? It\u2019s not like some sort of magic secret weapon is going to jump out of a book and up his butt, though if it did, maybe it would dislodge the bug stuck there.<br /> <br /> We need to get eyes on this woman and find out what she\u2019s up to. But there\u2019s no way I\u2019m sharing my opinion on the matter now. Doc\u2019s already humiliated me once. Maybe I\u2019ll bring it up to Natalie later.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> After a nice, hot shower, I flop onto my bed and decide to call Angelique. Maybe she\u2019ll be up for that date I asked for days ago. I feel a little guilty about it, have just spent the night with another woman, but I guess I\u2019ve been as honest as I can be without being hurtful. As the phone rings, I wonder if Angelique will even want to talk to me. She was pretty upset the other day. I she doesn\u2019t want a date, I guess that\u2019ll pretty much decide things for me. A part of me almost hopes she WILL make the decision for me, but that\u2019s not really what I want. Or is it? Maybe I\u2019ve already made a decision and I\u2019m just looking for justification.<br /> <br /> <i>If you deny Angelique now, it will make it much easier when we decide that she needs to die. It\u2019s inevitable, after all. You know the evil that gnaws at her heart. Her lust for dark power. She might not be a balehound now, but she\u2019s destined to explore that path eventually.<br /> </i><br /> You don\u2019t know that. She\u2019s trying to escape her past. Her\u2026lusts.<br /> <br /> <i>Ah yes, like you. But you aren\u2019t really escaping either, are you? You\u2019re simply stalling. Pretending. Looking for justification when all you really want is to hunt and kill.</i><br /> <br /> \u201cAlice?\u201d Angelique picks up the phone. She sounds hopeful.<br /> <br /> I hesitate, trying to get the Huntress out of my head.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm. Hi, Angelique,\u201d I begin, uncertainly. \u201cSo, I\u2019m trying to figure out what my heart wants, like you asked. But I can\u2019t do that unless I get to know you better. I mean, we only just met. I can\u2019t really commit if I don\u2019t really know you. So, I was wondering if you\u2019re still up for that date?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. I\u2019d like that very much,\u201d she replies readily. \u201cI\u2019m busy this evening though. Pack business.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTomorrow then?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, that would be good.\u201d<br /> <br /> I can tell from the sound of her voice that she\u2019s smiling, and even though I can\u2019t see it, it makes me happy.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I move carefully to the blood-bather\u2019s house. Her name is Moriah, and she\u2019s going to feel the bite of my axe, but not quite yet.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m still kind of amazed that Doc gave me the go ahead. I didn\u2019t even want to talk to him about this. That\u2019s why I went to Natalie first. She was hesitant, but she agreed with me. We have to find out more about what Moriah\u2019s doing. And I\u2019d like to know more about this particular victim before we try to kill her. There are plenty of things you can\u2019t learn from the library, like the layout of her house, whether she keeps any sort of schedule, or what sort of security she has.<br /> <br /> I become invisible well before reaching the house. Natalie dropped me off, but she\u2019s long gone now. I\u2019m planning to stick with Moriah as long as I can; I probably won\u2019t call for pick-up until tomorrow.<br /> <br /> Getting inside is easy. She has a nice security system, but I just phase through the back door. The house is nice. Upper middle-class, two stories. Clean and tidy. The kind of house that never looks lived in. It reminds me a bit of Kitty\u2019s house.<br /> <br /> Moriah is upstairs. She\u2019s taking her time getting ready to go out. She meticulously applies her make-up, styles her hair, and selects a ravishing dress. She has beautiful eyes and full, red lips. I want to be kissed by those lips. I want to get lost in those eyes. Why the heck am I trying to choose between Angelique and Eris when I could belong to this stunning beauty?<br /> <br /> <i>Your heart is not so fickle, Alice. You know better than to succumb to this witchcraft.</i><br /> <br /> Oh my god. I can\u2019t believe what I was just thinking! This is bad. Just being around this woman is intoxicating. Is this some sort of pheromone thing? And if it is, why is it triggering? She can\u2019t possibly have this going on all the time or she\u2019d cause riots wherever she goes. Maybe this only works on sin-eaters? Whatever it is, at least it hasn\u2019t tipped her off to my presence. She doesn\u2019t seem to know I\u2019m here.<br /> <br /> Even though I know it\u2019s unwise, I can\u2019t help but watch as she changes into her elegant dress for the evening. Her body is gorgeous. Her bed is right there. I\u2019m sure she would invite me into it if I revealed myself\u2026<br /> <br /> No! I have Angelique and Eris to worry about, and I\u2019m here to gather information, not get laid. We\u2019re going to kill this woman. I need to focus on that.<br /> <br /> <i>Yes, you do. Perhaps you\u2019d best kill her now while you have the element of surprise. I\u2019m beginning to doubt your ability to shrug off this witch\u2019s charms. She won\u2019t be able to seduce you with her magic when she\u2019s chopped into bits and her blood is strewn across the walls.</i><br /> <br /> I hate to agree with the Huntress, but she has a point. It\u2019s dangerous for me to stay close to this woman. Still, I have a job to do, and I\u2019m not going to screw it up. I need to show the krewe that I can do more than just fight. Doc and the others would kill me if I attacked Moriah now. And besides, I don\u2019t know what she\u2019s capable of yet. According to Doc and Natalie, those rings she\u2019s wearing could easily give her the power to strike me dead, permanently, even though I am a sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Then I notice something. Moriah\u2019s vanity mirror doesn\u2019t reflect her. I quickly examine the room\u2019s other mirrors and they bear her reflection like they should. There is something mystical about the vanity mirror. Maybe the others should break in and have a look when Moriah leaves for the evening. I\u2019d do it, but I have to keep tailing the witch.<br /> <br /> I need to get away from Moriah for a few minutes anyway, so I head outside to text Natalie and Sara. I report what I\u2019ve learned and suggest that someone comes to check out the mirror in about an hour, once Moriah has left for the evening.<br /> <br /> Then I find a blackbird foraging for seed in a neighbor\u2019s bird feeder and catch it. I break its neck and then use my knife to cut a chunk of meat from under its feathers with my knife. I grimace in disgust as I swallow the meat raw. It\u2019s gross, but I have to do it if I want to turn into a bird to follow Moriah\u2019s car when she leaves. I\u2019m definitely not going to ride along inside the car with her. Even invisible, she might notice, and I don\u2019t know if I could resist her mystical charms if I stayed so close to her for so long.<br /> <br /> I go back inside after that. Moriah has finished her preparations, and then, just before she heads downstairs, she stares into the vanity mirror and draws forth some sort of simulacrum from it. It resembles her, vaguely, but it\u2019s made entirely of blood. As Moriah strides gracefully downstairs, her hips swaying in the most hypnotic way imaginable, the blood simulacrum hides itself in a dim corner, waiting to ambush any trespassers. Fortunately, it doesn\u2019t see me at all.<br /> <br /> I follow Moriah downstairs, trying hard not to think about her hips, her eyes, her lips\u2026and I watch carefully as she inputs her alarm\u2019s security code. Once she\u2019s out the door and getting into the car, I text Natalie the code and a warning about the simulacrum. Then I follow Moriah outside.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, November 14th 2010<br /> <br /> -The Sun is not yet up yet we are out of wine.<br /> <br /> -I can\u2019t send the slave girl down for wine when I am the slave girl.<br /> <br /> -Bah.<br /> <br /> -Wine, Cognac, Vodka, woo.<br /> <br /> -What? Hot fudge cake?<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, November 14th 2010<br /> <br /> -Early.<br /> <br /> -Sometimes afternoon is early.<br /> <br /> -Goth train? GOTH TRAIN.<br /> <br /> -I still say a \u201cThe Craft\u201d animated series would have been good.<br /> <br /> -There are the people who agree with me and the people who are wrong.<br /> <br /> -GOOOOOOOOOTH TRAAAAIIIIIIN<br /> <br /> -Now we must recruit Sara into our band.<br /> <br /> -That was easy.<br /> <br /> -Okay lets check with some others.<br /> <br /> -Pah someday I will give Noriko an anti-makeover.<br /> <br /> -People not wanting to join rock bands I don\u2019t get it.<br /> <br /> -hrm serious conversation is serious.<br /> <br /> -Alice has that gleam in her eye.<br /> <br /> -Oh this might go badly.<br /> <br /> -Okay, not too badly.<br /> <br /> -Time for me to play go-between.<br /> <br /> -That worked, mostly.<br /> <br /> -Time to find us a bitch!<br /> <br /> -Goddesspeed, Alice<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jogg<br /> <br /> -Mmmmmmmmmmmmm hot fudge cake\u2026.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Now I want hot fudge cake. <br /> <br /> Not much to add about the session, except that Natalie may have been on cocaine for part of it.<br /> <br /> Janos, if you have forgotten, is the human artifact hunter who may be part of a certain secret society of such.<br /> <br /> Dramatic end point! Let\u2019s take up there next time. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-06T01:24:36-07:00","id":469957,"title":"","content":"Looking into the Mariah Winthrop affair has yielded fruit, and a couple well loved young women are in peril. Let\u2019s catch up!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Monday, November 15, 2010<br /> <br /> Breaking and entering is not my first choice in any situation. I\u2019m not experienced in it, I\u2019m not good at it, and I\u2019m not terribly thrilled to have to do it. But tonight, with the help of Cupcake\u2019s lockpicks and the weight of our Krewe Fate, I was able to circumvent an electronic alarm. Nightshade\u2019s manipulation of our Krewe Fate definitely put the odds in our favor. Once I dropped the security, Cupcake climbed in Mariah\u2019s bedroom window and interrogated the vanity mirror and the bed.<br /> <br /> The bed just showed that she slept with multiple men, though not always looking like herself. There were multiple faces we did not recognize, though Jenny\u2019s was one we could identify. Interestingly, Mariah never went to sleep wearing another face. We debated briefly is it was because she couldn\u2019t maintain the control while unconscious. The vanity mirror was much more informative (and horrifying).<br /> <br /> The mirror was enchanted somehow so that it could store blood samples, drain someone completely of their blood and \u201chide\u201d the body, as well as create a blood simulacrum to guard the mirror. Cupcake also learned that Mariah has the ability to drastically age someone with a touch. I\u2019m not sure if she can take that vitality into herself or just remove it from her target. Either way, touching Mariah directly is a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Before we could get too much further into our recon mission, Axe called Nightshade. Apparently Mariah isn\u2019t after Carol and Jenny, but Clarissa and Deanna instead. Their parents met with Mariah in secret under the premise of enrolling them in a finishing school. We met Axe at Clarissa's and took everyone back to the Bluffs. The plan right now is for us to keep the girls away from Mariah for as long as we can before the cops are called, then take them back. If something big were to happen, we are prepared to curse the girls into being forgotten This would temporarily protect them from Mariah\u2019s hunt for fresh bodies. While we have the girls safe, we fixed the problem of them being alone by binding Troy to Deanna\u2019s phone. Clarissa can handle herself if things got scary but Deanna could just vanish. Troy was not pleased that the Blood Bather was going around unchecked and actually volunteered for the duty. I added my number just in case Troy needed to call us and Deanna couldn\u2019t. Rose is performing the Fetter ritual While Mariah is busy waiting for the girls to show up, we\u2019ll cause a distraction va fire in her safe house. Axe can follow her again and see where she goes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, it seems like our psychic was right to worry, just not about the right pair of ladies. I\u2019m really glad Alice decided to go surveilling. It has moved our timetable up, which is better done on our terms than because Clarissa and Deanna went missing. This way, at least, we can have layers of backup plans.<br /> <br /> But I\u2019m getting ahead of myself. That call from Alice was to let us know that there was a strange mirror in the cult leader\u2019s room that didn\u2019t reflect her (all the others did) and that she was going out. Once she did, Alice sent us a text letting us know and what the alarm code was, and everyone (including Chandra) piled into the van and we made our way over to the cult leader\u2019s place. Natalie, Chandra and me were on lookout duty, which meant me and Natalie were not-making-out in the back of the van and Chandra was hiding in the bushes. Doc snuck in and turned off the alarm, then Alexia went in via the window in her bedroom.<br /> <br /> That let us get directly to the strange mirror, which didn\u2019t reflect Alexia either! It was a blood drinking mirror, a very strange artifact. It could produce a guardian spirit made of blood, store blood samples, and provide a non-messy way to exsanguinate someone and gather the blood, which is handy and not unexpected for a blood cult. Alexia\u2019s Sight showed her that one could make it mostly non-functional in the usual way one disfunctionalizes a vanity mirror, but to truly destroy it would require a very pure spirit, and would release a lot of energy. We did also find one of the powers she controls - the power to quickly age someone/drain their vitality. At least, Alexia got an image of the cult leader doing something that fit that description.<br /> <br /> Lastly for our part, Alexia used her Sight on the cult leader\u2019s bed. She has had many paramours recently, all men, and was not always looking like herself. Occasionally she looked like Jenny. So our thoughts about Jenny\u2019s lost time are correct (or, to be fair, the cult leader has some way of making herself look like her proteges). She never fell asleep looking like someone else though, which is good to note. Also of interest was that she would also arrange to get a small sample of blood from her lovers, occasionally as part of play, and occasionally by \u201caccident\u201d.<br /> <br /> For Alice\u2019s part of things, she followed the cult leader to a theatre, and managed to get into a place where her Senses let her eavesdrop. She met with a pair of well-to-do couples, who were interested in hiring the cult leader for etiquette/finishing school training for their daughters. Alice had only met Clarissa and Deanna the once, but eventually she realized that these two couples were their parents, and they were talking about introducing them tonight!<br /> <br /> Alice left the theatre and got to the girls as quickly as she could. She called us after getting them started moving, and we swung by to pick them up on the way home. Clarissa was greatly disappointed, as she\u2019d had a boy over. Deanna was less so, but then, secret disappearances and intrigue are far more interesting than playing lookout while your friend gets some. Deanna was keen to remind us she\u2019d been working on her boomerang skills, since she\u2019s going to be the Batman of the super team. I think I managed to impart on her that all good superheroes contact the Batcave/Justice League/home base before they attack their parents with boomerangs for trying to take them to finishing school. We also anchored a ghost of justice with a debt to repay into her cell phone. So if she forgets, or happens to get separated from it, we\u2019ll still get a call.<br /> <br /> See, we figured we had to take them back before their parents got the cops involved. So we put together a plan to distract the cult leader (by burning her house down. We should be able to cut down on collateral damage by cursing the fire away from neighboring houses at least. And she kinda deserves it.) Alice is going to keep eyes on her so that we know where she goes when she feels threaten. Then after we talk with Janos, we go for her. If the cult leader recovers from her distraction soon enough to pose a threat to the girls before we\u2019re ready, we want to be able to be on hand to curse the girls so that they become forgotten. It\u2019s rough, but the safest way to protect them with their parents affected the way they are.<br /> <br /> Poor Clarissa was not happy with the conversation, neither with the talk of arson, nor the idea of being forgotten like that. I can\u2019t say I blame her. She\u2019s got a good friend in Deanna though, even if I can see how she might ease her way under someone\u2019s skin. She did promise to protect Clarissa, and was incorrigibly cheerful the whole way home. She has no lack of self confidence, that\u2019s for sure. Now I just hope she doesn\u2019t wind up having to use that boomerang...<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, November 14<sup>th</sup> 2010<br /> <br /> -Steppin\u2019 Out.<br /> <br /> -Taking up position.<br /> <br /> -Sara better not get frisky back here.<br /> <br /> -Off without a hitch.<br /> <br /> -Or not?<br /> <br /> -Hrm, boyfriends. Of course.<br /> <br /> -Okay, ready for pick up.<br /> <br /> -LOL Clarissa.<br /> <br /> -Mmmm my hair.<br /> <br /> -Someone is sneaky.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jogg.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite She is pretty isn\u2019t she.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite You should be careful. I may get very jealous of Alice.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite You are kind to say.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite I am looking in your direction. Several People are there, including Clarissa.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Maybe I am looking at Clarissa. She is very pretty.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Oh I did not say which of you I thought was prettier, just that she was pretty.<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m being hit on by text from someone in the same room. Awesome.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Mmm hmmm<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Oh brave girl. I am impressed.<br /> <br /> -@Narek: Oh, no, feel free to menace her. It will be fun.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: I am sitting right here, feel free to try something.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Go ahead. I dare you.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Hm. Didn\u2019t think so.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite: Now, you need to focus on you and your friend. Your lives may be at stake. Other\u2026Pursuits are for another day. Seriously.<br /> <br /> -Time for phase two.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXX</i><br /> <br /> -Deceptively little said given the amount that got done.<br /> <br /> Alice has a similar build to Jasmine, so getting get in and about without detection was not difficult. Speaking of the latter, she made Deanna\u2019s phone a temporary Anchor with Bind Anchor for Troy Donovan, from the Hotel. Troy is keen to protect the girls as part of his redemption, and does have a lot of experience in attacking people with axes.<br /> <br /> Everyone seemed enthused about pulling Clarissa and Deanna into things. I mean, not that they were in danger, but making them part of the plot. It has been semi-seriously suggested Deanna should have a Vice of \u201cAwesome\u201d<br /> <br /> There was enough discussion of the particulars of arson that if my house were bugged I am sure someone would have been arrested for suspicion of something.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add. See you in two weeks, comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-19T01:29:26-07:00","id":485218,"title":"","content":"Geist journals! The Krewe was somewhat fragmented, and Doc\u2019s player had to miss, but the journals will cover what the PCs saw. Doc\u2019s player still has a journal, to cover what he was up to; however it does not break down at the table events. And on that note\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1600 Hours, Monday, November 15, 2010<br /> <br /> I was up by 0500 Hours this morning as I had terrible dreams of what might happen if Mariah were allowed to continue her plans. When I sat up covered in sweat the last time, I could still hear the phantom screams of my Krewe and those we hold close echoing in my room. I knew I had to do something and it had to be soon.<br /> <br /> Meditation went very quickly, which was good given how terribly my dreams were. At 0600 Hours, I called Jerome. I\u2019m certain that I woke him up, but he answered anyway. My money\u2019s always good and I keep crazy axe-wielding redheads from killing him. That might help.<br /> <br /> We met at 0800 Hours in a doughnut shop inside West Haven as it was probably the least likely to notice a pair of Black and Hispanic males having coffee as anything unusual. Also because Fuck Yale. I think I\u2019ve been around someone too long, I\u2019m just not sure who. Anyway, I knew what I wanted was legal but I didn\u2019t have time to find one and send up all the flags of paying in cash. Plus, I knew Jerome could get me the military grade configuration without any hold ups. Then there was the favor.<br /> <br /> I am not a master marksman, but I\u2019m trained to fire a standardized assortment of weapons. However firing a thirty two pound, four foot, nine inch weapon without prior knowledge is not going to produce satisfactory results. Or more bluntly, all I\u2019m going to do is bruise my shoulder while I blow a hole in a wall or the sidewalk. I went to the shop and surprised the girls. They had the place much brighter, organized differently (not sure what I think about that part), clean, and welcoming. I\u2019m starting to understand why my sales are going up.<br /> <br /> Jerome called back after roughly four hours. The price would have been triple for most people given how fast I needed it, but because he felt like he owed me, it was only double the legal selling point. Such is the cost of business, I guess. But that meant I was now the owner of a Barrett M107, aka Model 821A, aka .50 BMG. If the Krewe asks, I think I\u2019ll have to tell them it stands for Big Motherfucking Gun.<br /> <br /> As for that favor, well I needed a place where I could practice and get a feel for the handling of such a beast. Jerome found an old abandoned manufacturing plant of some kind that was set down in the ground about two stories. It was also far enough away from any residential areas that we weren\u2019t likely to disturb anyone. And damn does this thing do some disturbance. I emptied three clips and demolished two cinder block walls. I also spent a little time making sure the sights were zeroed and then I spent about two hours learning how to break it down quickly. I\u2019m sure there are active duty marksmen that can do it in a fraction of my time, but I\u2019m satisfied with what I\u2019ve learned today. Now I need to go find Nightshade or Bright Eyes and find out what I\u2019ve missed today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Alright, we\u2019re just waiting for the appropriate time now... but we\u2019ve been waiting all day. Our plan last night worked... better than expected? Definitely with more fallout. On one hand, the other group of Touched, the ones that dealt with her before, got felony amounts of cocaine planted on them and an anonymous tip called in. A number of them are well enough off to afford the kind of lawyer that gets a paid in cars/day though, so it\u2019s a rap they\u2019ll beat. So it\u2019s unfortunate, but not the end of the world.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Elizabeth\u2019s people noticed the fire and looked to capitalize on it. They unfortunately has some troubles with the cult leader\u2019s guardian, but managed to get it under control. They thought it was her, so they moved against Bowtie-Man. That served to distract her even more, so Deanna and Clarissa have been safe. They are even safer right now, as Natalie got permission from their parent\u2019s to have them come to chill at our house, under the guise of \u2018etiquette training\u2019, despite Clarissa being grounded for throwing their breakfast table at her mother.<br /> <br /> Getting Elizabeth\u2019s people\u2019s help wasn\u2019t purely good news. A number of them were hurt badly, either by the guardian, or by whatever saved Bowtie-Man. We still haven\u2019t figured that one out - the cult leader never left her other house, according to Alice, but there\u2019s no indication that he was able to do... whatever happened to the people following him by himself. We did what we could to help out our allies by dealing with the mirror, which was exciting since, you know, crime scene. But we managed to deal with it without causing a scene.<br /> <br /> So, there was all that, and mostly arranged over night. Today we also got allies in the form of Janos and Lucille. I dunno how Doc was gonna run it, but he was off acquiring high caliber weaponry, so I had to talk with Janos (the sacrifices I make ;-D). I went ahead and laid what we had on the table, about the cult, and the powers we\u2019d seen and everything. Janos is a way more than halfway decent guy, so he couldn\u2019t just leave it to us, knowing about what was going on.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, he didn\u2019t know how to counter that one bit of soul-destroying blood magic we knew about. He was fairly certain that it required an intensely intimate connection, so *fingers crossed* we\u2019ve broken the ones she had and it will take time to rebuild, which we won\u2019t give her. He was absolutely certain that given the checks and balances involved in that kind of blood magic, there must be a focal item, somewhere. The twins might be able to track it down, given a sympathetic link. Catherine might be able to as well, or possibly Janos himself. If we can find it fast enough, once we make sure she can\u2019t cause anymore trouble, we might be able to cut her off from her powers.<br /> <br /> For now, there\u2019s still the making sure she can\u2019t cause anymore trouble. Janos was impressed by everything I said she could do, which is a bad sign. Elizabeth\u2019s people are fewer in number than they would have been last night, but still more than we were expecting, if we can keep the peace between their leader and Doc (and me... I dunno if he likes me much - the leader, that is. Doc and me are fine). Having Janos along, and Lucille as well, is great. If we\u2019ve got a chance at doing this, we\u2019ve got the best one with this crew, I think. We haven\u2019t played all our cards, but she\u2019s better prepped for people like us, so our other cards (the other troupe of Touched) are best kept close to the vest.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve do have some things to look forward too. One of the protective rituals we\u2019re doing is very... pleasant. And I\u2019m pretty sure Elizabeth\u2019s not letting me off without seeing her again soon. And Alice will be back safe and sound and not on a stakeout. Soon, everyone will be safe and it will be time for fun.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Sunday, November 14<sup>th</sup> 2010<br /> <br /> -Kids are dropped off.<br /> <br /> -Deanna may be crazy.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Yes, I got the picture.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Oh?<br /> <br /> -Mission accomplished<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Now your getting warmer. Or maybe I am. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Oh dear. That was quick.<br /> <br /> -But that Domino was just sitting there, being all Domino-like!<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite not bad.<br /> <br /> -Okay, everything seems okay now with the other Krewe.<br /> <br /> -For certain admittedly stretched definitions of okay.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Oh you are adorable.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Hmmm\u2026that will get a response when I go upstairs.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite You are learning, young padawan, but take care lest you fall to the darkside.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Yea, I thought you might like that <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Signing off, hopefully nothing will explode while I catch some sleep.<br /> <br /> <br /> Monday, November 15<sup>th</sup> 2010<br /> <br /> -Okay, small explosions.<br /> <br /> -Sigh.<br /> <br /> -Well damage contained for now I think.<br /> <br /> -Some people have too much money.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite I\u2019d love to meet you after class. But I can\u2019t. I am trying to save you and Clarissa. Remember?<br /> <br /> -More sleep. Long night ahead.<br /> <br /> -Okay time to meet with Janos.<br /> <br /> -Well this is informative. So he has done pretty much everything eh?<br /> <br /> -Younger Most Interesting Man in the World I guess.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite I am going to pick you and Clarissa up. Be ready.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite I will talk Clarissa\u2019s parents into letting her go.<br /> <br /> -Okay, it seems quite an unlikely group is forming.<br /> <br /> -Now we wait for show time I guess.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite I suppose we can step out for a couple minutes. I will show you the cliffs.<br /> <br /> -Okay, so the warm feelings of safety and relief makes sense, as does someone feeling more secure right then. But (con\u2019t)<br /> <br /> -Someone crying after I kiss them is not something I hope to have happen again.<br /> <br /> -Even if it was adorable in retrospect.<br /> <br /> -But it officially never happened<sup>tm.</sup><br /> <br /> -Okay, time to move.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXI</i><br /> <br /> The Skull and Bones society had evidence planted in their homes and the police called\u2026it was determined that Mariah did not control the police so much as know how to arrange for badness for the Krewe that previously fought her.<br /> <br /> The PCs determined she likely reforms via the body of someone she had intimate contact with inside their bloodstream. This returns her original appearance, however (hence her considering a new body) and can only be truly foiled by destroying her tub.<br /> <br /> Elizabeth\u2019s people are of course Vampires. The Ordo Dracul were having a devil of a time dealing with the Blood Guardian, particularly because it could do nothing but try with all it\u2019s power to return to the wandering radius of the vanity mirror.<br /> <br /> Most of the session was thus preparation. Big throw down next time. Join us. Comments and Questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T01:15:43-07:00","id":502614,"title":"","content":"The Krewe squares off against Moriah. A lot goes on. This session was mostly combat prep and combat, but here goes.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Tuesday, November 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade caught up to me first and made the obligatory \u201cThat\u2019s a big gun\u201d comment. Then we met the others in the drawing room so I could be debriefed.<br /> <br /> Our distraction had triggered a series of events we hadn\u2019t anticipated. And people think I\u2019m too cautious. But \u201cI told you so\u201d doesn\u2019t help right now. More than half of the Sheriff\u2019s men were MIA or found in torpor and John the Bowtie Man was in the wind. The vanity mirror and the Blood Guardian which existed within were destroyed. Bright Eyes got some quality time with The Collector by the sounds of it. She learned that Mariah probably got her big scary magics from a \u201cdemon.\u201d The air quotes were emphasized so I assume they are important. And The Skull and Bones Society had all been arrested after an anonymous tip clued the police into a mountain of cocaine in their HQ.<br /> <br /> Tonight was a little more complicated as we weren\u2019t moving in alone. Nor were we going in as a full frontal assault. Sometime around 1930 Hours, Axe sent a text letting us know that there were three patrol cars and at least six cops trying to hide in the area. We were already en route but still good intel. We met the others at the local community center just after 2000 Hours.<br /> <br /> Dantaine stood apart from the Sheriff and his three goons. The Collector and Lucille were there, though it looked more than a little awkward and tense until we arrived. Chandra had detached and come with as did Troy. Dantaine was in rare form as we could see he existed simultaneously in Twilight and Pink Side. Dantaine was on hand because Elizabeth\u2019s investigation found Mariah was in league with the Strix. They were to be left to him on his own direction. He explained that to put down a Strix for us would require an attack that would kill the host instantly and still do enough damage to finish the spirit within. Bright Eyes glanced at me and I just nodded. I might know where a weapon like that could be.<br /> <br /> The plan was fairly tight, even if it did mean I had to trust the Sheriff with the safety of my Krewe. Chandra, Axe, and the Sheriff would go in invisibly to take up positions. Cupcake was on police detail, to scare them all away so we didn\u2019t have to deal with them. Nightshade was originally going to stay with me, but the only position with a proper vantage I could spot was up a tree. Instead she was hanging back with The Collector in a car nearby. I would cover the front, Troy would guard the back. He specifically asked to come, said he needed to help bring someone this horrible to justice. Lucille and Bright Eyes were going in as shock troops. Lucille with a katana, Bright Eyes with curses and fire. The explosives for both the greater house and the safe room would be disabled thanks to those wonderful Pyre-Flame Curses. Who the fuck booby traps their safe room?!?! Anyway, the Sheriff\u2019s flunkies were going in conveniently after Bright Eyes and Lucille \u201cto help contain,\u201d but I suggested that no one should look like Mariah or get between her and a window. I also made sure Bright Eyes and Axe knew to watch their backs around those three. I didn\u2019t want to take any chances on the Sheriff removing \u201cmasquerade breaches\u201d in an accident during the heat of battle. Nightshade would be keeping watch and adding support where she could, while Dantaine would keep his position outside the house unless the Owls were spotted inside.<br /> <br /> Troy conferred with Nightshade for a moment before nodding and running for the back of the house. The Krewe shared a glance and silent nod. Our eyes all said be careful before we turned and moved into position. I put up my Phantasmal Shroud and took on the appearance of Anders, just to make Mariah more confused if she or her followers did get a look at me. As \u201cluck\u201d would have it, I was the only one to have any police problems. I made for my perch in the copse of trees just as Officer Norris drove down the street. I could tell he saw something, but he must not have gotten a good look at me because even though he stopped, he never got out. Very carefully, I climbed the tree and assembled my weapon. Just as I got everything together and laid sights on the house, I heard Chandra scream. It seemed to come from much farther away than I knew she was. That sound will never not be chilling. I didn\u2019t have time to think about it as I heard something in the next stand of trees over and saw two black shapes fly out and dive into the ground. It looked like two huge owls. Then my senses were jerked back to the house as I heard the most determined and constant chopping sound from a large oak just behind the home. Troy must have found something. Dantaine was in position in front when a rotten corpse erupted out of the front yard and made for Cupcake. The police had not made it to us so she was still holding her position, which left her as a sitting duck. I didn\u2019t have a shot yet when I realized the shadows bubbling up behind the corpse became the Mekhet. With a single swing of his shadow khopesh, Dantaine left nothing but a corpse and a collection of shadow feathers. I only had a few seconds to relax my trigger finger before the chopping stopped and a massive crash rocked the neighborhood. Troy had chopped most of the tree down and then used his own powers to jump on it until it carried him into the previously warded house. The second corpse tore itself out of the ground, but before I or Dantaine could attack, the owl abandoned the body and fled into Twilight. I was getting a little concerned since all the intel I could gather was outside. But then a rifle reported from across the street. The Mekhet lurched slightly from the impact, turned in the direction of the attack, seemed to take a step, then vanished. The police all reacted to the gunshot so I returned my attention to the target house. An explosion from across the street suggested that Dantaine was perhaps still engaged with his attacker but I was no longer worried for his safety. The police were dispatched rather quickly as a giant fly creature met then from between two of the neighboring houses. I almost felt sorry for them considering I had seen the real creature before.<br /> <br /> The front door opened and I had a bead at head level of anything that walked out. Fortunately Axe shuffled out first. She was covered in gore and looked exhausted, but otherwise unharmed. I watched and counted as everyone exited the building. The Sheriff was the last to leave. I\u2019m almost ashamed to admit my crosshairs lingered on the bridge of his nose longer than they had any reason to. Bright Eyes was more blood sprayed than I would have expected when I had packed up and climbed down to meet the others. Dantaine returned about the same time. His suit was shredded by what I suddenly recognized as a grenade explosion. Cupcake was all but clinging to him verbally, which was beyond amusing. I gathered the shadow feathers as the others cataloged the viscera they collected in plastic bags for me. I still think the best way for use to find Mariah\u2019s tub is through sympathetic link. I just wanted the feathers as souvenirs and maybe parts of future charms. Once we were all clear, the Sheriff moved everyone back from the house. He and I had very little to say to each other from the start, but the fact that he came out with the final trick was a little annoying. He may have realized it or he may have just enjoyed what came next as he pressed the detonator and slow walked away from the exploding building.<br /> Probably should have shot him.<br /> <br /> After all that, we all loaded up and head back to the Bluffs. Axe had been on stake out for two days, she and Bright Eyes were covered in tainted blood, Nightshade was trying her damnedest not to retch from being close to them, Cupcake was still going on about how awesome Dantaine was, and Chandra was trying not to look annoyed. Once we got back and the van was unloaded, Nightshade pulled me to the side and looked concerned before I could leave the Armory. She wanted my opinion on something but first, she asked if I was okay with how things went down. I think she or someone was worried that I wasn\u2019t involved directly enough. I hugged her and told her I was glad we accomplished out mission without any friendly casualties. Besides, I still needed to help find the tub and I was pretty sure I knew something we could use to destroy it. Nightshade laid her hand gently on the case I kept my Barrett in with a smile that reminded me why everyone wanted her. Then she asked what I thought about Axe joining the Krewe. I knew that was a goal she set for herself, but it seems that the others are ready for it as well. Nightshade has always forced the best of me to the surface, so I told her what I thought. That being that Axe had proven herself at great risk to herself not to join the Krewe or to convince me, but because it was the right thing to do. Most of the work she did with tracking, following, and spying on Mariah was alone without any of us reminding her of anything. Nothing to counter the homicidal lunatic she is so unlucky to have inside her. Nothing but herself. As far as I\u2019m concerned, she\u2019s already part of the Krewe. ...I just might not tell her that. I think I\u2019ll leave that to Bright Eyes.<br /> <br /> Nightshade surprised me after that. She had other questions for me. We discussed which of our associates should help look for the tub. The twins are probably the most capable, but also the most at risk, from themselves and their ancestor. Mouse would have to experiment with her own powers and that could be painful, but I suggested we introduce her to the Sympathetic Magic Room. The Circle of dummies will be creepy, but it might be useful. Then before she left, Nightshade asked if I would lead meditation sessions for Cupcake\u2019s School for Supernatural Kids. I knew she was most concerned about Clarissa, but there are others that could benefit. And I\u2019ve gotten better with my meditation lately so I didn\u2019t see any reason not to agree. Now I think it\u2019s time for a snack.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> The time has come. The waiting, the watching, the <i>hunting</i> of the blood-bather, Moriah, is over, and I\u2019m ready to strike and end this.<br /> <br /> Doc, Troy and a few of our vampire allies are positioned outside to keep Moriah from escaping if she manages to make it out of the house. Chandra and the vampire sheriff are slipping inside, invisible like me. I\u2019m pretty sure they are here now, waiting for Sara and some other vampire girl named Lucille to burst in and get things started. Sara\u2019s using her Pyre-flame Curse to make sure Moriah\u2019s explosives don\u2019t go boom, so the blood witch should be easy prey. Alexia is outside waiting for the cops to arrive so that she can do her Beetlejuice thing to scare them off.<br /> <br /> And then it begins. A hot Asian vampire with a sword smashes through the door, and Sara\u2019s right behind her. Moriah spins to face her attackers. That\u2019s when Chandra\u2019s head appears, keening with a soul-shattering scream that makes Moriah falter and nearly fall to her knees. The vampire sheriff appears and stabs Moriah in the back with some sort of Asian short sword. Moriah\u2019s thumb clamps down on the detonator she\u2019s been carrying ever since she got to the house. Her eyes widen in shock when nothing happens. I detect a hint of real fear in her eyes. It even cuts her pheromones with the sharp tang of need, and suddenly I\u2019m overcome with the desire to protect this beautiful, sexual goddess from her attackers.<br /> <br /> For the life of me, I can\u2019t figure out why I\u2019ve been resisting her ambient charms for over two days now. She\u2019s the most gorgeous woman I\u2019ve ever seen. Clearly, the others are misguided! Moriah doesn\u2019t deserve this. How can she? And even if she does, is she really any worse than I am? We\u2019ve both killed innocents. I have to get her to safety. Maybe if I can drag her to the panic room she\u2019ll be safe long enough for me to talk the others down.<br /> <br /> <i><i>Foolish girl!</i> </i><br /> <br /> Derision drips from the Huntress\u2019 words like blood from an axe.<br /> <br /> <i><i>Look at you, wallowing in doubt, and I haven\u2019t even fanned the embers. I should let you deceive yourself, if only to teach you a lesson and drive a wedge between you and this krewe you inexplicably persist in courting\u2014but I want a kill. This has been a good hunt, and I need the satisfaction of murder to end it. Take her head! </i></i><br /> <br /> The Huntress\u2019 screams crescendo just as Sara does something to strike Moriah blind, and Moriah throws herself at my friend, clawing at her madly. Somehow it\u2019s all enough to break the blood-bather\u2019s spell on me. I have to protect Sara. I have to finish the hunt. Moriah and I are nothing alike. She deserves justice, and I am the executioner.<br /> <br /> I fade into view and with a swift and powerful swing of my axe, I cleave Moriah\u2019s head from her shoulders. It flies across the room and rolls to a stop against the wall. But I don\u2019t stop there. I keep hacking at her fallen corpse. Lucille and the sheriff follow suit, and Troy\u2019s axe joins the symphony of slaughter after he dispels Moriah\u2019s ghost wards by felling a tree onto the back half of the house. We don\u2019t stop until Moriah\u2019s body is a dismembered mess. Even then she proves herself dangerous when her ribcage cracks open and lashes out at me like some sort of macabre spider, but Sara flings it away and then smashes it into splinters.<br /> <br /> I help Sara gather some of the twitching remains so that Doc can work his ritual magic on them to find out where Moriah\u2019s tub is. We still have to end her for good. But for now, I feel like I\u2019ve done my job. I couldn\u2019t have done it without the rest of the krewe, though. Not without Sara to keep me grounded, or without Alexia to look out for the rest of us. Not without Natalie to provide support both moral and mystical. And not without Doc\u2019s planning (excessive though it might be sometimes).<br /> <br /> Heck, it sounds like even the vampires were crucial in this operation; they kept some sort of vampire bogeymen from interfering with our work. One of the vampires in particular, a tall, distinguished black man named Dantaine, apparently hunts these bogeymen professionally. He also caught Alexia\u2019s fancy. I thought she was a lesbian, but I guess she\u2019s bisexual, because she was very impressed with Dantaine. She can\u2019t stop talking about how cool he was. I think she might swoon.<br /> <br /> Speaking of the vampires, Lucille is really attractive, and very capable. She was nothing but grace and beauty while she wielded her sword. She\u2019s seems kind of cold, though. And the sheriff doesn\u2019t seem so bad to me. He is aloof but respectful and professional. He is handsome too, and if I were into guys, I\u2019d probably think he was pretty hot. I don\u2019t know why Doc has such a problem with him, but I\u2019m sure he has his reasons. My guess is that they\u2019re both alphas who don\u2019t like anyone else trying to exert authority over them.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> On the drive back, I feel a sort of post-hunt languor set in. It\u2019s always like this after a kill. The Huntress feels satisfied, and so do I. On top of that, it\u2019s been a long couple of days, and I haven\u2019t slept in over 48 hours. Sara seems to notice, and even though I\u2019m still covered with blood, she gives me a nice back rub. Natalie is staying as far away from me as she can get, though. She\u2019s pretty finicky about blood.<br /> <br /> Right now, I just want to get home, shower for at least thirty minutes, and then go to bed. Maybe I\u2019ll call Angelique and reschedule our date before I drift off to sleep. Yeah, that sounds good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Whew. Well, as Alice said, the hard part\u2019s over. And no one even got hurt! Seriously hurt, at least. Dantaine\u2019s suit looked like it had gotten mauled by a tiger but the armor he was wearing underneath it kept him from being similarly shredded. Alice got scratched by one of the cult leader\u2019s spiritual defense mechanisms, but other than that, we got off free and clear.<br /> <br /> Not that it wasn\u2019t tricky. Two wrinkles showed up just before go time. One was handled by our allies, specifically Dantaine. Turns out that Elizabeth\u2019s gang connections had more issues with the cult that just the fact they brought their rival gang to town. The cult leader had also allied herself with their spiritual rivals. Dantaine specializes in dealing with that kind of thing, so he kept that from being a problem.<br /> <br /> That wasn\u2019t where the mauling came from - that was because Bow-Tie John decided to blow himself up while standing rudely close to Dantaine. Alexia was devastated by how torn up he looked. I can\u2019t say I minded, once I knew he was alright - that suit had hung well on his toned frame, and the ragged tatters accentuated it just as nicely, while showing off a little more skin. But Alexia was at least a little bit in love with him, in part I think because of the neat, put together image of pure power he projected. We were all glad of that armor though.<br /> <br /> The second wrinkle was that someone had tipped off the police that someone in the cult leader\u2019s house might be attacked. So three squad cars were prowling the neighborhood. Alexia picked that up, using her illusory powers to frighten them off, unharmed.<br /> <br /> I made an ok showing myself. I managed to lay a curse on the cult leader, striking her blind. Unfortunately, I was one of the first to be revealed from hiding, so she tried to come after me. I was able to avoid her flailing for a moment, then Alice saved me! She and Lucille were both pretty amazing - I even managed to forget for half a second that I was in a fight and just watch how beautifully they moved. I got snapped out of it when that defense mechanism went off. I managed to \u2018repay\u2019 Alice by batting it aside, not that she was in any real danger from it...<br /> <br /> Once everything was done, we got what we needed for later sympathetic magics (still gotta find that bathtub) and got out of there. The others met us just outside, which meant Natalie was right there for me to throw myself in her arms. She and Doc had been a ways away, so he could use his big gun effectively, and she could be mystical backup. I held onto her for a few good minutes before I would get in the van. She mighta been the safest of us all, three blocks away with Doc right beside her, and I had Alice to protect me, but... I don\u2019t like fighting. On the ride back, I gave Alice a back rub, managing to avoid making out with her this time. Even without the saving bit though, she had been on a stakeout for two days. She deserved to relax.<br /> <br /> We all did. Alice opted for a shower, dinner and bed for herself. Natalie and Karen and I started making plans. for one of \u2018those parties\u2019, with the usual suspects and maybe Tracey. No Deanna, despite her adorable attempt to pick Natalie up when she drove her home (the old hand-on-the-knee, \u2018sure you just wanna drop me off?... I\u2019m Batman\u2019 trick). We also discussed adding Alice to the troupe officially and Doc agreed! Everyone else seemed more likely to be on board, so while we still have to poll the group, it seems likely our Little Red is here to stay. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Monday, November 15<sup>th</sup> 2010<br /> <br /> -Doc\u2019s here, final preparations are in order.<br /> <br /> -That is a big gun. Ahem.<br /> <br /> -Moving out.<br /> <br /> -Pretty quiet in the car.<br /> <br /> -Interesting bunch here. Scary group.<br /> <br /> -LOL tell him how you really feel Alexia<br /> <br /> -Alexia is amusing.<br /> <br /> -I am doing a great job of pretending I am not terrified!<br /> <br /> -Radio silence operation started.<br /> <br /> -Everyone is okay. More later<br /> <br /> -Not so bad for me, I just had to watch.<br /> <br /> -Now I need to plan a party.<br /> <br /> -It is like Alexia does not trust me or something.<br /> <br /> -Heh Deanna is amusing.<br /> <br /> -She has much to learn.<br /> <br /> -@Deanna-mite Stay Safe!<br /> <br /> -Actually, lets see about Alice.<br /> <br /> -Getting the difficult part over with.<br /> <br /> -Okay Doc is on board.<br /> <br /> -What hijinx should ensue now?<br /> <br /> -Ouch! Well, Karen has put her boot down. &lt;3<br /> <br /> -Oh boy &lt;3<br /> <br /> -Goodnight!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXII</i><br /> <br /> As has been mentioned, Dantaine is a Khaibit. I was using the 2e rules for Obtenebration as he fought the Strix. The combat was short, relatively speaking, but fun. Poor Alice was hindered by a pheromone attack, but I ruled she could get a chance to snap out of it when Sara was attacked, given that and her Virtue. Obviously, Moriah\u2019s abilities go beyond normal for a Blood Bather.<br /> <br /> While inside was very much combat, outside was more of an action scene, with largely NPCs fighting. It was rolled out, for the record, since Alexia was out there.<br /> <br /> For those who enjoy my Actual Plays, I have started a Crossover one set between 1920 and 1949 called <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/465832-world-of-darkness-the-golden-eagle-actual-play\">The Golden Eagle</a>. It should be taking place across Europe and the Levant, as a group of Supernaturals drawn togather by a strange artifact and mysterious patron work to survive in the post Great War era as Fascism and other dark forces rise. There is a Sin-Eater present, Wolfram Johann Ritter von Klingemann of Germany, a Forgotten Advocate. There will be certainly some ghostly elements to stories in this campaign. I expect most games will have their critters show eventually. There will be some pulp and noir elements worked in, so if you enjoy that sort of thing check it out. And don\u2019t forget to check out my Changeling (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\">Malibu Dream House</a>) and Demon (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\">Night Train Detective Agency</a>) games as well.<br /> <br /> Okay, well that covers this session I think. Comments and questions welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T17:26:18-07:00","id":506256,"title":"","content":"In yet a another odd question to add to the series of questions I have asked (hopefully they haven't got too annoying yet), how would a Claimed coming to the krewe seeking sanctuary fly? After all the krewe is a group of death duguthim who the local packs don't seem to mess with, right?<br /> <br /> Two Claimed come to mind. One is someone who merged with a love spirit and other is one who merged with a spider spirit. Both can approximate a human form when pressed and entered into the merger willingly. Out of a sense of love in the first Claimed's case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":490,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","user":"omenseer","date":". 05-06-2015, 08:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T22:42:07-07:00","id":506416,"title":"","content":"It honestly depends on them. I can't begin to answer for them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T23:53:16-07:00","id":506438,"title":"","content":"Fair enough <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. I'll be quiet now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-07T12:19:04-07:00","id":507090,"title":"","content":"Better question (Why do the better questions after one has already asked the silly ones?), how would the packs or the key members that we have seen react to this situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-08T00:57:13-07:00","id":507805,"title":"","content":"Well the PCs are being watched by the Sleeping Giant pack carefully...they have a lot of Storm Lords who hunt Claimed as their favored prey. They are already watching the PCs very closely...Dierdre is in fact a Storm Lord herself, who chooses a less aggressive way to keep tabs on the Krewe and monitor them.<br /> <br /> The closer pack depends? Malard is difficult to predict. He did not kill their pet spirit or the Brineborn...so maybe? Or maybe there is a line. The scary thing about Malard is how hard he is to predict.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T01:52:40-07:00","id":516880,"title":"","content":"Last game our heroes recovered from their ordeal and moved onto taking care of loose ends. There seem to be a lot of those.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0900 Hours, Tuesday, November 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation continues to go very smoothly. I seem to be centered in a half hour routinely now. I cleaned up and came down to Celebratory Breakfast! Cupcake had chocolate crepes, fruit, eggs, powdered sugar, sausage, I think she called the chocolate drizzle a gonosh... it was a feast. Nightshade even came to breakfast. That Karen was stealing her strawberries was noted by all. Rose was disapproving of all the sugar, but there were normal crepes and fruit for her so she had little to grumble over. Honestly she even seemed to be in a good mood.<br /> <br /> Nightshade mentioned that we needed to get everyone together today to discuss \u201csomething\u201d Krewe-related for Axe. Axe was unaware of something needing to be discussed so was immediately concerned. I offered that I\u2019d bring the rum and the rope. Because I like helping. We planned to gather with plenty of time for Axe to make her date with Angelique. 1300 Hours seemed like the easiest time, so we dispersed to do our own things. Axe and Bright Eyes were going for a run, Nightshade was probably going to bed, and I took the Winchester to the local firing range. I wanted to make sure I could built up my marksmanship without using a weapon that sends people scattering with one shot.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1445 Hours, Tuesday, November, 16, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was more involved than I was expecting. Once everyone was around and prepared, we moved our procession to the cemetery out back. I wore my ceremonial robes and brought the rum and rope as promised. It was the cheapest rum I could find on the way back from the range. Then I just grabbed one of my climbing ropes and headed out. Rose and Nightshade shared the Krewe binding ceremony, which was unexpected. I set Xerxes to guard the ritual area because I recalled a trance during our Founding.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t remember everything as we were in a Trance and only some of the Geists\u2019 conversation faded through the mystical haze of the Krewe Channel. I know that The Grasping Huntress was just as \u201cwell liked\u201d by our Geists as she was by us. For her part, she was resigned to joining because of Axe\u2019s intent, not of her own choosing. Then something happened and there was a shift in the Channel. The Drowned Bride became distant somehow and I could feel The Grasping Huntress assume the Mantle of Resolution. When the ceremony completed, Rose announced that she was moving back to Taiwan. She and Karl will be heading over soon, dependent upon his passport. I think it was safe to say that we were all sad, but she wants to keep doing good work with Mr. Ox after Bone Dry is dealt with. Also she plans to expand the Krewe once she\u2019s settled. I noted that since Axe was officially part of the Krewe now, we needed to drag her over to create a new Avernian Gate, specifically somewhere we can drive the van. Then we\u2019ll be able to help them move.<br /> <br /> Cupcake invited everyone in for lemon meringue pie, as that was Axe\u2019s favorite. She hadn\u2019t been in the Krewe an hour before Axe started questioning Nightshade about her intentions with Deanna. I didn\u2019t want to ruin the happy mood, but that was not a conversation that should have an audience. Nevermind the fact that it was none of her goddamn business. I mean I teased Nightshade with mock frustration about playing with Deanna, but I know she likes the attention. I also know she\u2019s never going to take away the agency of another, except in Necromantic rituals, and only then for the good of the group. So instead of snap at Axe, which is what I wanted to do, I decided to give them the privacy that conversation deserved. Which mean that will be a talk Axe and I have privately another time. She might be a country girl from out west, but there are some lines she needs to recognize. In most any other circumstance, that would have earned her a very unpleasant discussion with the very protective part of me.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to go find Noriko and see what she\u2019s up for. Channelling this frustration into something constructive sounds like a great way for me not to explode at Axe later tonight.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2330 Hours, Tuesday, November, 16, 2010<br /> <br /> So we went to \u201can annual event\u201d tonight. There was beer, boats, and lots of ignorance. But I exposed Noriko a group of people she normally wouldn\u2019t have to choose from, and I think she found several potential targets. Then we left the madness and had a nice dinner with far less noise. Now I think we\u2019re going to enjoy the rest of the evening in my room.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Wednesday, November, 17, 2010<br /> <br /> Meditation was wonderful and centering. I got cleaned up and headed down for breakfast and was surprised to find Angelique at the table with Axe. Well, I was surprised Angelique was staying for breakfast, the rest was not a shock. I was glad, just for that moment, that Noriko had to go to work this morning. Once we were all together, Angelique told us some very disturbing news. Her patron/mentor/Dom/whatever contacted her in a dream last night. I didn\u2019t get all the details, but the short version was that this woman tried to force Angelique to kill Axe. She fought off any control that may have been there and learned that a minion of the Bale Hound is coming and that \u201cshe will be working with them.\u201d This minion calls itself Bright Shadows, something about how fire leaves all things destroyed as one worthless collection of ash.<br /> <br /> While no one was particularly thrilled with that assessment, Bright Eyes and Axe turned to me for any ideas on how to help. Without any research and basing my idea on a total guess, my first suggestion was to try and create a cleansing rite of penance that involved silver nitrate in a low grade acid solution and careful application of a form to apply the solution as Angelique\u2019s auspice. Sort of a moon calendar with her symbol lining up across her waist and down her spine. The whole point of that would be to alter her physically enough to make changes to her True Name. That got me thinking about what little I know about the Pure. I remembered something about them having a rite that rips out a Uratha\u2019s auspice. That might be a better place to start and then redesign the rite with Angelique, given she is an Ithaeur. I guess I\u2019m due for a little \u201clight reading\u201d today.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, the wheel of fate has turned again. Endings, beginnings and the change in between all at once. The story of the cult leader has turned against her, our Little Red is now part of the troupe and Jasmine is going to be leaving us soon to go back to Taipei. Not leaving us really - we have some contacts out that way and it\u2019s more of an expansion. She\u2019ll always be a quick call away. It will be sad to not have her around but the quiet certainly she announced the news with and the import carried by the troupe binding ritual has the weight of fate.<br /> <br /> Other than those turns of fate, yesterday was a slow, relaxing, centering kind of day. Alexia made us chocolate crepes with smiling faces made of fruit, celebrating that everyone was safe. Karen \u2018helped\u2019 Natalie with her portion, of course, but I guarded mine with a knife and fork and got away with all of it.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, Alice invited me jogging. Well, she invited everyone but I was the only one who took her up on it. She offered to go three miles instead of her planned five, since I was out of practice and of course a nerd. I assured her I\u2019d just drop back and walk the rest of the way if I needed to. I think she was impressed when I made it the whole way, and threw in a few backflips and walked the last bit on my hands. She was at least an appreciative audience, even jogging backwards to keep watching.<br /> <br /> The troupe binding ceremony went off as planned, with Natalie assisting Jasmine so she could learn how to lead it herself, even if it was rather cold in the graveyard. Our Little Red doesn\u2019t like the cold - she was happy to get inside, and happier to find a lemon meringue pie waiting for her. And even happier (maybe I\u2019m projecting) - Doc was actually nice to her! I was touched, at least.<br /> <br /> Deanna has kept at it, btw. She asked Alice out, and apparently Natalie sometime after that. She\u2019ll hear the end of that from Natalie at some point, probably. Doc got silly about it, as if his own two eyes couldn\u2019t give him plenty of reasons Deanna might be asking. It\u2019s alright though - Alice is even more adorable when she blushes and Natalie even managed to make Doc blush, so... worth it.<br /> <br /> Alice was also concerned, not that she was asking period, but that Deanna might be deceiving herself about Natalie\u2019s intentions. She had an ex who loved the attention more than she loved Alice herself and was worried about Deanna being hurt the way she had been. Her ex was not upfront about it, however, so the difference is that Natalie has been as super clear as she could about how not serious she is. Leading someone on is not ok, but you can only be so responsible for the pain of someone who refuses to take your words at face value or anything close.<br /> <br /> That conversation chased everyone away, so once Alice left to prepare for her date with Angelique, I got to spend some time with my ladies. Most of which was spent teasing each of them in turn for the situation with Tatum\u2019s parents. There was another Tatum family dinner last night and there is no end to Karen\u2019s amusement with how much they want to sleep with Natalie.<br /> <br /> Especially after an \u201cAre they cute?\u201d, I was not allowed to come along (fair - i I totally would have taken Tatum\u2019s mom\u2019s offer to see her new tattoo) so I called up Elizabeth, since it was apparently date night. She picked me up in a limo (!), took me to a fancy dinner place (!!) and then, of lords and ladies, her house is gorgeous. And just generally impressive - for instance, we caught a movie in her home theater (!!!) which rivaled any public theater I\u2019ve ever been to.<br /> <br /> Things are picking back up today though - break time\u2019s over, I guess. See, Alice\u2019s date went well enough that Angelique stayed the night, so Alice got a first hand view of her disturbed sleeping. It seems the mystical power her turncoat mentor/lover had been working with is trying to exert an influence over her. On one hand, that\u2019s gotten us some intel on the turncoat causing problems here - they call themselves Bright Shadows and have cleaved themselves to the concept of fire as a destructive force that leaves everything lesser and homogeneous, which, speaking as a fire person, is the worst concept of fire ever.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the power was trying to get her to kill Alice last night, which is not ok (I\u2019m going for \u2018understatement of the year\u2019 with that one). Bright side, Angelique was able to resist the influence and because of what she is, has a good chance of being able to get free of it altogether.<br /> <br /> And we\u2019re going to help her with that. As Alice herself said, this seems like a job for some preliminary research, so I better go join Doc in the library.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> I\u2019ve done it! I\u2019ve proven myself to the Middle Shadows, and now they\u2019re making me one of them. They\u2019ve already done so much to help me regain my footing; now I feel like I actually have a chance at a life that isn\u2019t dictated by the Grasping Huntress.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve been excited about it since breakfast, when Natalie told me the krewe needed to have a talk with me about something important. At first, I was worried. Did I do something wrong? Then I noticed the ghost of a smile on Natalie lips, and Doc said he\u2019d bring the rum and ropes. I didn\u2019t really get what he was talking about, but his words carried the tone of a good-natured ribbing, and that\u2019s when I realized that they were ready to bring me into the krewe.<br /> <br /> So now I\u2019m kneeling with the others in the cemetery behind the house. The sky is overcast and gray, and it is bitterly cold out here. Even bundled up in a couple of shirts, a thick sweater, a warm scarf, a knit cap and my jacket, I\u2019m freezing. I hate cold weather, but it\u2019s worth it. Natalie is kneeling to my left, and Jasmine to my right. Doc\u2019s directly across from me. The others\u2014Sara, Alexia, and Simon\u2014complete the circle.<br /> <br /> Doc starts things off by slamming a bottle of rum down in the middle of our circle, and we all take a drink, all except for Jasmine, who is leading the ceremony. I gather she\u2019s got some sort of Chinese religious thing that keeps her from imbibing. Then Natalie solemnly recounts how I came to join the krewe and the things I\u2019ve done for them since I arrived. She says that she feels it\u2019s time for me to join the Middle Shadows, and then asks the others if anyone has a problem with me joining. Even though I know he supports all of this, I still halfway expect Doc to object. Instead, he just looks at me with his stern but accepting gaze and says, \u201cHell, as far as I\u2019m concerned, you\u2019re already a part of the krewe.\u201d I\u2019m touched, and it\u2019s a struggle to keep the tears at bay.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Memories of my first krewe binding flood my mind. The Huntress was content then. She was getting what she wanted. Jon was so serious as he performed the ceremony, and Randy was eager to get it done so we could go out drinking to celebrate afterward. I think he wanted to get in my pants back then, before he learned I wasn\u2019t into guys. Not that Randy wasn\u2019t a good guy. He knew more about what we were getting into than the rest of us did, after all, and he taught me a ton about investigation.<br /> <br /> I remember Cassidy watching me warily during the ceremony. She still wasn\u2019t sure about me. She didn\u2019t think I would be a good fit. Maybe she sensed the darkness inside of me. But, like the Middle Shadows, she gave me the benefit of the doubt. And eventually we fell in love. I miss her. I probably always will. I guess I\u2019ll always be haunted by the knowledge that I betrayed her faith in me, and by the pain I caused her. I\u2019ll never be able to make that up to her, but I can still learn from my mistakes.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Jasmine takes over the ceremony. Even though Natalie is basically the krewe witch, Jasmine seems to run a lot of the krewe\u2019s ceremonial maintenance: krewe binding, making charms, that sort of thing. Maybe that\u2019s why she doesn\u2019t get out in the field that much. I guess she\u2019s more about support than engagement. She runs us through a short litany that reminds us all of the krewe\u2019s mythos and responsibilities. Then each member of the krewe cuts his or her hand and spills blood upon the cemetery ground. Jasmine takes my hand and cuts it, then has me do the same to hers. Then she takes my hand so that our blood mingles before falling on the graves. I get the distinct impression that she\u2019s passing the torch, but I don\u2019t know why. Not at first, anyway.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> We enter a trance, and then each of us takes a back seat as our geists gather in a spectral graveyard of their own to welcome the Grasping Huntress. The meeting is tense. The Dog of War despises the Grasping Huntress, and makes it very clear that he will not put up with her blood lust if it threatens the krewe. The Virgin Sacrifice, normally reticent and submissive, similarly warns the Huntress to behave. The Huntress is arrogant and angry that she is being forced into the krewe, but she decides to make the best of things. She tells her fellow geists that she will serve the krewe well, but reminds them that she is Death and Resolve, and that her sin-eater is a Reaper. She tells them that we will do our job, and do it well. Though she doesn\u2019t say it outright, her words imply that the krewe needs us much more than we need them. But she\u2019s wrong. It\u2019s the other way around, and I just wish she would shut up and play nice.<br /> <br /> And then something strange happens. Jasmine\u2019s geist, the Drowned Bride, withdraws into the shadows and mist behind the Huntress. Barely visible, she whispers in a gentle voice full of longing and tells the assembled geists that she will leave the Resolution of Death in the capable, and perhaps more fitting hands of a killer while she and Jasmine move on to other things. And that\u2019s when I realize that the enclave of geists has shifted: the Huntress now occupies the Bride\u2019s place.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The ceremony ends. I\u2019m a part of the krewe. It feels good.<br /> <br /> But there\u2019s more to it than that. Everyone looks to Jasmine for some explanation of her geist\u2019s behavior, and that\u2019s when Jasmine explains that she\u2019s going to be leaving the krewe. Well, not leaving it, exactly. She\u2019s a founding member of the Middle Shadows, and she\u2019s still a part of the krewe. But she\u2019s going back to Taiwan with her boyfriend, Karl, to establish a new branch of the Middle Shadows. She\u2019s going to be working with some sort of Chinese demon she calls Uncle Ox to make sure that karmic debts are paid. I don\u2019t really get it, but she seems sure of herself, and the rest of the krewe is supportive. We\u2019re all sad to see her go, though.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Later in the afternoon, after celebrating, Deanna comes up in conversation. She\u2019s been flirting with me, and I finally had to tell her I\u2019m seeing someone else. Natalie, on the other hand, has been toying with the idea of a fling with the girl. That worries me, so I ask Natalie if she\u2019s sure she\u2019s doing the right thing. She assures me that she\u2019s made it very clear to Deanna that she\u2019s not interested in a relationship, and that if anything happens between them, it\u2019s merely fun. That\u2019s all well and good, but I\u2019m not sure Deanna really understands that. I mean, it\u2019s one thing to say it, but I know from experience how much it can hurt if two people don\u2019t have the same expectations in a relationship.<br /> <br /> I tell Natalie that I\u2019m worried because I was in relationship with someone who wasn\u2019t really in love with me and just wanted to be with me because she liked the attention. I tell her a little about Kitty, and how she used me. But even after hearing me out, Natalie still assures me that Deanna understands how things are. She also points out that she\u2019s not like Kitty; she\u2019s not trying to deceive Deanna. And she\u2019s right, that\u2019s a big difference. On the other hand, I don\u2019t think Kitty was maliciously trying to deceive me either. Maybe I\u2019m just being generous because I murdered her, but I think she just got carried away with herself and didn\u2019t think about how much it would hurt ME.<br /> <br /> Natalie still doesn\u2019t seem to understand that I\u2019m afraid the same thing might happen with Deanna. Natalie likes attention, and Deanna\u2019s giving her plenty of it. It\u2019s affecting Natalie\u2019s judgment, and I know from personal experience how easy it is to get swept up in a relationship and let hopes change your expectations. Deanna\u2019s very impressionable, and people tend to become VERY enamored of Natalie. I know Natalie doesn\u2019t mean any harm, but I think this is going to end in tears\u2014Deanna\u2019s tears, to be exact. Natalie says that a little heartbreak might help make Deanna less naive, and while that may be true, it still seems a bit cold.<br /> <br /> Still, I\u2019ve said my piece, so now I\u2019ll leave it well enough alone.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Angelique and I are finally on our first date, chatting over a meal at a fancy restaurant. It\u2019s been nice so far. Angelique is charming and sexy, and she is clearly in love with me. The intensity of her feelings is a bit frightening, actually. It makes what I\u2019m about to do all that much harder.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Angelique,\u201d I open hesitantly as I finish my salad, \u201cyou\u2019ve been up front with me about your past, so I think you should know a little about mine. There\u2019s a reason I understand you so well, and I think I should be open with you too.\u201d<br /> <br /> I take a deep breath before continuing. \u201cIn our krewe, I\u2019m a Reaper. That means it\u2019s my job to kill things that need to die, even people, if it helps resolve a ghost. The problem is, I used to be a part of a different krewe when I lived in Portland. And my geist\u2014the spirit inside me\u2014is a vengeful psychopath.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>And you are a \u201cjust\u201d psychopath. Is there much of a difference?</i><br /> <br /> I pause to try and quiet the Huntress, reminding myself that I am NOT a psychopath. Once I gather my thoughts again, I continue.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s all too easy to listen to her whispers and doubt myself, and when I was in Portland, I started to lose my footing. I went too far, and killed some people who didn\u2019t deserve it. I was well on my way to becoming a serial killer when my old krewe kicked me out. That made me realize I was heading down a dark path, so I came here looking for help from the Middle Shadows. I knew that if I tried to go it alone, I wouldn\u2019t be able to resist the Huntress\u2019s influence.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe krewe has helped me a lot, and they\u2019re still helping me. But the Huntress is always there, in the back of my mind, and she wants to hunt and kill. It\u2019s something I\u2019ll probably always struggle with.\u201d<br /> <br /> I take another deep breath and then look timidly at Angelique, who fixes me with her elegant eyes. I don\u2019t know whether to expect caution and revulsion or sympathy and compassion in her eyes, but I don\u2019t see any of those things. Instead, I see sadness and a hint of resignation. After a moment, she looks down at her plate as though embarrassed to meet my gaze.<br /> <br /> \u201cNone of that bothers me,\u201d she says. I\u2019m both relieved and worried with how easily she took the dark secrets of my past until I realize that something else is bothering her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong?\u201d I ask.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy demonic patron has contacted me in my dreams,\u201d she whispers, her expression a mask of despair and hopelessness. \u201cShe wants me to work with the Balehound. He\u2019s called Bright Shadow because, like a fire, he transforms things into useless dust and ashes. Figuratively, anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, maybe we can use that to help us hunt and kill this Bright Shadow,\u201d I offer.<br /> <br /> Angelique shakes her head, \u201cI\u2019m just\u2026I don\u2019t know if I can resist my patron. I don\u2019t know how much of a hold she has on me. I don\u2019t really remember what my mentor did to bind me to her, and if I contact the Balehound, I\u2019m worried my connection to the demon will become even stronger. I don\u2019t know if I can resist.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t say that. You don\u2019t belong to her. She\u2019s not your master. If I can resist the geist in my head, you can resist this demon.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wish I could be so sure.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNonsense. You know I\u2019ve got your back, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique raises her gaze to look at me with a glimmer of hope. The intensity of her gaze is startling. \u201cIf it weren\u2019t for you, I wouldn\u2019t know what to do right now. It\u2019s because of you that I was able to resist my patron when she spoke to me in my dreams.\u201d<br /> <br /> Oh boy. Angelique is really serious about us. It\u2019s scary, bordering on obsessive, and I\u2019m not sure I\u2019m comfortable with it.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell listen, no matter what happens between us, I\u2019m your friend,\u201d I try to cool things off a bit. \u201cI\u2019m here for you\u2014the krewe is here for you\u2014and we\u2019ll get through this, okay? We\u2019ll find out what to do about this demon and help protect you from her. I don\u2019t really know how right now, but we\u2019ll figure something out. I guess all Doc\u2019s research might come in handy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique smile softly and nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cPromise me one thing, Alice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat do you need?\u201d I answer warily.<br /> <br /> \u201cPromise me that if I become dangerous to others that you will kill me rather than let me hurt anyone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Somehow I knew that\u2019s what she was going to ask. I stop and stare down at my plate for several moments, thinking and gathering my thoughts. When I look up again, it\u2019s Alice the Reaper talking.<br /> <br /> \u201cUnderstand that if you ask me that, and I say yes, then I mean it,\u201d I say.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen you promise?\u201d Angelique insists.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I do,\u201d I say with a slight nod.<br /> <br /> <i>She wouldn\u2019t be the first girlfriend you\u2019ve killed.</i><br /> <br /> Without thinking, I give voice to the Huntress\u2019s thoughts in a terribly misguided attempt to lighten the mood. \u201cYou wouldn\u2019t be the first girlfriend I\u2019ve killed,\u201d I say quietly.<br /> <br /> There\u2019s an awkward silence after that.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The rest of our dinner goes much better once we put dark talk of demons and murder aside, and then we go to see a punk band performing at a local club. I have a lot of fun even though I\u2019m not really into punk. Angelique is, though, and she really likes the show. She also likes being with me, and seems to go out of her way to make it clear that we\u2019re a couple. She likes it when I drape my arm around her waist, but I get the feeling there\u2019s something more. Like she\u2019s trying to prove that she\u2019s mine and not the demon\u2019s. The problem is that she\u2019s not really mine. We\u2019re just dating, and I might be even less sure of how I feel about her now than I was before tonight.<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t stop me from inviting her home with me. I know I shouldn\u2019t sleep with her again, not when I\u2019m not really sure we\u2019re going to work out as anything other than friends. But she\u2019s gorgeous, and seductive, and she gives the strong impression that she NEEDS me.<br /> <br /> <i>Why aren\u2019t you this good at justifying your actions when there\u2019s a kill at stake? I don\u2019t know why you bother. You\u2019ve slept with that feral tramp Eris twice. It\u2019s only fair to Angelique to sleep with her again too.</i><br /> <br /> The sarcasm in the Huntress\u2019s cloying voice is so thick I could cut it with a knife, but it doesn\u2019t get in the way of my lovemaking. Angelique is an amazing partner, more confident and comfortable than she was last time. I lose myself in her. And then, during one incredibly intense moment, she breathlessly whispers, \u201cI don\u2019t belong to her. I belong to you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Later, as we\u2019re drifting off to sleep, I realize that it\u2019s not going to work with Angelique. She wants too much too quickly. The intensity of her feelings for me is frightening, the kind of thing I\u2019d expect from a stalker. I mean, I get it. She\u2019s desperate to escape her demonic patron, and I\u2019m the only thing she has to grab on to. But I clearly don\u2019t share her obsession with this relationship, and it\u2019s frankly making me uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> I wake up in the middle of the night to find Angelique standing on my bed in the form of a huge black wolf. She\u2019s staring at the wall as though she sees something I don\u2019t. I invoke my Oracle to see if I can sense anything more, but there\u2019s nothing. My heightened senses tell me that Angelique\u2019s heart is beating way too fast, though. I\u2019m wary of touching her, unsure whether she\u2019ll attack or not, but I gently call out to her.<br /> <br /> At the sound of her name, she begins to shudder and transform back into her human form. She collapses and I catch her, holding her gently. Her eyes flutter open and closed and her heartbeat begins to slow, but she\u2019s exhausted.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened?\u201d I ask.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy patron\u2026she visited my dreams again. She hates you. You\u2019re the only thing giving me the strength to defy her. She told me to kill you, but I resisted. I stood up to her\u2026because of\u2026you.\u201d<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think Angelique is TRYING to blackmail me into a relationship, but she\u2019s doing a darn good job of it.<br /> <br /> Then Angelique succumbs to her exhaustion and sinks into a deep sleep. I lay holding her, stroking her hair to comfort her until I drift off to sleep, wondering what the heck I\u2019m going to do about this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, November 17th 2010<br /> <br /> Let me write some here to get my thoughts on pixels.<br /> <br /> Okay, Deanna\u2026agh! Well, not Deanna, nothing here is her fault. Alice confronted me in a well-reasoned, polite tone about concerns I was taking advantage of Deanna. She had seen me having fun with Deanna\u2019s foibles, and flirting back and forth, and was worried I might hurt her. She was up front about her own biases, that her relationship with an ex- might be coloring her opinions. We had a discussion, like adults, and I pointed out yes, I was enjoying Deanna\u2019s attentions and yes, I was flirting with her. No, I did not have intentions to add her to my relationships. Yes, I was considering an adventure with her. Yes, I told her this. No, this did not seem to bother her. I was unsure if Deanna truly absorbed it or if she was approaching from a similar direction. I pointed out I had not slept with her despite two invitations (one of which I would not have taken anyway because timing) because I wanted to ensure I was not going to hurt her.<br /> <br /> Most of my early experiences, with men and women, were adventures, not relationships. I\u2019ve had relationships too, and I have had cases where my partner and I had different opinions of where things were going, and I have been mislead. But those adventures were good. They helped me learn about relationships. And Karen was an adventure that became a relationship, whereas Sonia was a case where we were both looking for a relationship. It was difficult to convey this, but Alice seemed to be listening, if hammering the point she felt like Deanna may not know what is going on a bit much. I promised to be clear and careful.<br /> <br /> While Alice\u2019s questioning me was a bit aggravating since it lingered on \u201cI know you told her what was going on but what if she did not listen?\u201d it was in good faith. I am not upset with Alice. Doc and Alexia, on the other hand, stayed long enough for Alice to ask about concerns I was taking advantage of Deanna and walked away. I thought that was assholish behavior. First of all, I stand up for Doc. Even when he is\u2026not quite in the right I am quick to point out the logic of his thinking. That his feelings about me in such a situation was \u201cMeh\u201d rather hurt. Neither stayed to hear my reasoning, or that maybe Alice misread the situation, they just left at the accusation. They also made a display of leaving at that point, between accusation and defense. Clearly they think I am some sort of manipulative slut or something. I am honestly kind of pissed with them. They would not even do me the privilege of explaining or defending, they just chose to walk away. Goddess it makes me angry with them. Apparently while I am willing to take up for them, Doc especially, the feeling is not mutual. It honestly hurts. I\u2019m not even pissed at Alice. She does not know me very well. She had limited information. While her questions might should have been asked in private, that was the worst she was guilty of. She actually stayed to listen, unlike them. Sara also stayed, which was good of her. At least she showed respect.<br /> <br /> Other than that, things have gone well with Alice. We got her inducted in the Krewe, and she performed well under the recent trials against Moriah. Her reactions with Angelique also speak well, as she has not been too swift to condemn her, even with recent stuff. I could give her insufficient credit and say it is because she and Angelique are sleeping together, but that would be selling her short, especially given she did kill one ex before.<br /> <br /> Jasmine is going to be headed to Taiwan. That makes me sad. Whatever our relationship has been, I\u2019ve always cared about Jasmine and wanted the best for her. We will never see eye to eye on a lot of things but she is family, and a dear friend. Maybe it is the fact that Doc and Alexia were willing to throw me to the wolves, but I feel sort of lonely right now and like I can\u2019t quite rely on people, Sara aside. Which is ironic that is bugging me with Jasmine since she would have disapproved of that whole conversation but eh, I never said I was always logical.<br /> <br /> Karen and Sara are going okay, outside the fact that Karen thinks Tatum\u2019s parents embarrassing me is somehow hilarious.<br /> <br /> So I am sort of sad, sort of Angry when I should be happy. It is not a good place to be, and I feel disquieted. Maybe I will talk to Karen or Sara. Or maybe I will just stay in here and cry again. It is a mystery even to me.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIII</i><br /> <br /> The torch passing thing was obviously planned, since Alice and Jasmine have the same player.<br /> <br /> Not a great deal else to comment on. The Ceremony was well played by the group.<br /> <br /> Largely a role playing session, not much else to add but if you have comments or questions they are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-17T04:23:28-07:00","id":516926,"title":"","content":"Would their Taiwan branch be a corporate or a franchise? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T13:00:34-07:00","id":535853,"title":"","content":"Alice\u2019s player had to miss, so we focused on the \u201cmagic island\u201d storyline here. Some research and prepwork. It was a shorter session, so shorter journals this time.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXXXIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1150 Hours, Wednesday, November, 17, 2010<br /> <br /> I went in a different direction than trying to find, steal, then alter a rite of the Pure. Something in my head told me that Mallard would somehow sense the taint and Angelique would suffer for it. Plus it would take Axe or Rose, or both, to ninja into Glenwood without backup and it\u2019s not worth all that.<br /> <br /> But I did hit on another idea as I entered the Library. I grabbed my sketch pad and made a really fast drawing of a cocoon. It was the most simple symbol of change I could think of quickly. Drawing in hand, I headed down to the GMC Room. I used the picture to focus my summoning of a Change spirit. The protean nature of the Uratha, wanting to alter an aspect of someone, and being a spirit of change, I figured this was a better option. Plus any rite made with the assistance of a spirit would be cleaner than bastardizing something from the Pure anyway.<br /> <br /> The spirit was incredibly helpful, whether because I wanted to \u201cdo something (TM)\u201d to an Uratha or because I was furthering its Influence, I\u2019m not sure. Either way, I was given a recipe of sorts for how to do exactly what I wanted. That\u2019s a little scary reading back over it. Anyway, I\u2019ll need to:<br /> <br /> -Summon at least 1 Lune Spirit, probably several<br /> <br /> -A powerful enough spirit could make the change itself<br /> <br /> -Control the change so that it only does what I want<br /> <br /> -Need Earth-oriented items for grounding to do this<br /> <br /> -Guide the spirit<br /> <br /> -Silver weapon (check) to make the mark, metaphorically cut out the infection<br /> <br /> -Be ready for Kuruth<br /> <br /> -Axe can help hold Angelique down, but we may need to investigate sleep magics, anchor chains, and bear tranquilizers<br /> <br /> From what I know, Lunes can only be summoned while the moon is in the sky at night and they tend to be hard to control. Based on what the Change spirit said and what I understand of True Names, the mark will need to be either on the forehead (nope) or between the shoulders at the base of the neck. That fits more in line with the lunar cycle tattoo I had in mind so that Angelique didn\u2019t just have some random and wicked scar. We can\u2019t always make healing beautiful, but there\u2019s nothing that says we can\u2019t try.<br /> <br /> All that was left was for me to build a ritual. I headed back into the Library and started working. It was hopeful going at first, but then I seemed to have almost lost the point. I either refocused well or just pulled everything along with me by sheer determination because then everything seemed to fall into place.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m finished an hour later and I can actually have lunch with the Twins to talk about finding Mariah\u2019s tub. As long as that goes well, I think I\u2019ll practice First Tongue after lunch to keep in shape for summoning the Lune.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, this has been a productive and enjoyable day. Well, productive and (hopefully) enjoyable for the other. Just enjoyable for me. I didn\u2019t *need* to sleep with Timothy to visit the magic dream island, but he is a handsome young man and I am a beautiful young woman and my bed is extremely comfortable. Natalie was \u2018distracting\u2019 Tracey, as I am sure I will hear no end to. Not that it was just for me - on the practical, incredibly non-romantic side, we wanted more than one set of experienced Sighted eyes on the magic dream island, just in case. On the just as pertinent side, well, Tracey is a beautiful young woman and Natalie is a beautiful young woman and Natalie\u2019s bed is extremely comfortable...<br /> <br /> To explain, seeing as our plans changed a bit since my last email - Doc handled the research, as he had some insight into what was required. He found just what he needed, and in roughly an hour! Maybe I should let him research on his own more often. He didn\u2019t fill us in, maybe cause the twins were about, but I\u2019m sure he will when we\u2019ve a moment.<br /> <br /> We did (obviously) manage to convince Doc that the twins were our best bet. Catherine risked burning out her Sight, if she tried. Janos was uncertain of his own abilities, which is terrifying in its implications. The \u2018risk\u2019 of the twins awakening to their own power is manageable. Besides, don\u2019t tell Doc, but I\u2019m kinda hoping they do awaken into their own on this quest. They will eventually, and fate is as much about the beginning of the journey as the end. If they awaken while doing their best to rid the world of a true evil, so much the better than awakening randomly, or when Tracey tries make herself live forever or they unwittingly try to travel to the Abyss. Plus, if they awaken while we\u2019re there, we might be able to stop their ancestor from overcoming them.<br /> <br /> So, after our pleasant afternoon and lazy evening, it\u2019s about time for our sleepover in the sympathetic magic room. Sleeping in a room surrounded by creepy faceless manikins and Ziploc bags full of viscera is not really how I imagined that cultural staple that is the sleepover. But one of my favorite people will be there with me and two that I am quite fond of. I\u2019ve fallen asleep in less pleasant circumstance and I have a magical dream island adventure to look forward to.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Wednesday, November 17th 2010<br /> <br /> -Discussing how to proceed. Looks like Doc is researching while we talk to the twins.<br /> <br /> -Sara seems pleased by this turn of events.<br /> <br /> -Looked at several options the twins seem like best bet.<br /> <br /> -Grim conversation is grim.<br /> <br /> -Okay I think we are on track.<br /> <br /> -Oh boy I am never gonna live this down.<br /> <br /> -Sara is certainly unstoppable.<br /> <br /> -Okay they are coming for lunch.<br /> <br /> -Oh Doc is showing up, cool.<br /> <br /> -Alexia sort of knows what is going on.<br /> <br /> -Not awkward.<br /> <br /> -Okay seems to be going well.<br /> <br /> -We will see how it works.<br /> <br /> -Tee hee<br /> <br /> -Signing off for now.<br /> <br /> -Dinner, now with vague awkwardness.<br /> <br /> -Tracy seems to be enjoying herself.<br /> <br /> -Pajama party?<br /> <br /> -Bah.<br /> <br /> -Yep, still creepy as hell.<br /> <br /> -Maybe I will be able to sleep. Maybe.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIV</i><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s research was not for an Uratha Rite proper, more an hedge ritual for altering the name. Will it do the trick? That remains to be seen.<br /> <br /> As I say, short session. But comments and Questions are welcome<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-14T02:30:40-07:00","id":554072,"title":"","content":"Hello there folks.<br /> <br /> I was out of town Sunday two weeks ago, and we were unable to schedule the game around it due to other vacations and obligations. So, no Geist journals today. However, Balance of Shadows will be happening tonight.<br /> <br /> I did want to take a moment to thank those of you who have been following this story the past five and almost a half years. We are having a lot of fun, and powering ahead with our storyline. I earnestly hope you continue to join us and enjoy. And those who stumbled upon this Actual Play I hope you have been enjoying it as well, and continue to.<br /> <br /> I do want to remind, as our story is plenty convoluted and you don\u2019t have access to the dozens of NPC pics we do, that if you need clarification, or just wanna see what someone looks like, questions and such are welcome.<br /> <br /> Regardless, tonight we wake the ghosts and dance with the dead once more. New journals in two weeks. Hope to have you back then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-28T15:17:49-07:00","id":571927,"title":"","content":"We missed a session but we are back in black!<br /> <br /> However, the oddities of the break, having missed Alice for a session, and other stuff meant time got rewound somewhat, and we actually technically wound up ending at the same point we did last session, just covering some stuff between dinner and islanding. So the timing seems strange, but it should work out.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2045 Hours, Wednesday, November 17, 2010<br /> <br /> Wow I\u2019m apparently a huge asshole. This might not be a major surprise to anyone other than me, but I didn\u2019t realize how much of a jerk I\u2019d been to Axe. Yes that\u2019s what I lead off with after several hours of First Tongue practice. And yes I\u2019m skipping things already.<br /> <br /> Axe came back in from what should have been an afternoon run about two coughs away from hypothermia. Bright Eyes hugged her while I grabbed a blanket from the coat closet to wrap her up. Cupcake had worked most of the afternoon on a locally sourced Bouillabaisse, which she was very proud of, so while Axe took a quick hot shower, the rest of us set the table. We filled Axe in on the plan for the ritual and what her role would be over fish soup. She was very happy to provide security and hoped that this would finally fix the issues with Angelique. The way she said that made me think something was up, but I decided not to be nosey at the table.<br /> <br /> When we were shuffling out, all content with the incredible food Cupcake made, Axe pulled Bright Eyes and I to the side. She wanted to let us know how relieved she was that we found an answer for the whole werewolf vice monster issue haunting Angelique. Actually it was more she was glad she could help the Bone Shadow and then move on. Apparently Axe isn\u2019t really as into Angelique as I thought. According to our Little Red, as Bright Eyes calls her, the werewolf has basically taken up speaking of herself as Axe\u2019s property and become unbearably clingy. Axe believes it\u2019s mainly to be free of her Patron, but that\u2019s still not okay. That veers deeply into the realm of using Axe instead of loving her in my book. Even Bright Eyes looked annoyed at that revelation. And then, things went pear-shaped. Axe started talking about how relieved she was because she wouldn\u2019t have to worry about her fear of keeping up with Angelique intellectually. I thought that was ridiculous, as if Angelique was that smart, she wouldn\u2019t be in the mess. But Axe took it differently and opened up on me with both barrels. She let me know, to my shock and shame, just how little she appreciated my not so subtle hints about how dumb she was. She listed, far more than I could bear to hear, the numerous times I\u2019d been snide or condescending about her common sense or intelligence. At one point, Axe reminded me of my comment to, \u201cread a book.\u201d The incident with free climbing the Bluffs left a particularly barbed memory for her as I felt her words cut and slice as she recounted my mockery in excruciating detail. The look of mortification on my face eventually (mercifully) stopped her. Stumbling through thoughts, struggling to find any string of words which may adequately work for an apology (and finding none), I staggered through the most uncomfortable and shame-filled attempt at atonement in my life. I remembered the book comment, but it was only ever meant as a jab as a way for her to pass the time. Not that that, given current context, helped anything. Eventually, with Bright Eyes standing by being incredibly helpful with her nods of, \u201cyes you did that,\u201d Axe finally ended her litany of justified grievances with an edict \u201cthat from now on, trust me to know what I\u2019m capable of and don\u2019t assume that I\u2019m an idiot.\u201d Obviously I agreed, but I did remind her, sheepishly, that the medic in me will always come out when people endanger themselves. That brought up another sticking point that Axe believed we were all academic scholars. When I told her that as far as I knew only Cupcake had ever finished (or attended) college, I really thought Axe might punch me. Her disbelief melted when Bright Eyes gave her the \u201chelpful\u201d nod.<br /> <br /> Before anything more awkward could happen, we were distracted by what sounded like a whispered argument between Tavia and Noriko in the hall outside the Music Room. The issue seemed to be whether or not Noriko was eavesdropping on our conversation. Once it was obvious we knew they were there, Noriko showed me a picture from her cellphone. An hour ago, a homeless squat was hit with what looked like a wall of fire which killed the three scorched bodies in the image. The image in the phone triggered a momentary flashback unlike I\u2019d had in a while. I immediately heard the screams, smelled the blood and burning flesh of the explosion. Just for those few seconds, I was dying again.<br /> <br /> Now that this is written, Axe, Noriko, Cupcake, Bright Eyes and I are going to find who did this.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0030 Hours, Thursday, November 18, 2010<br /> <br /> I will regret this, but I can\u2019t be as cruel as I should be in this case.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m out of order again.<br /> <br /> We drove out to West Haven in the van to what amounted to an abandoned construction site. Most of the exterior walls for a building long forgotten served as a temporary squatters\u2019 settlement. Noriko shifted into a housecat while Axe just turned invisible before both went in to investigate. The rest of us stayed at the van as the police line had already moved everyone else along. From where we waited, I could see one of the inner walls. The burn marks suggested there was no blast radius, or even a blast. Nothing continued to burn because it was so hot, everything turned to ash. The fire seemed to just move across the inside of the structure without any accelerant or really anything that is normal for a fire. Remote controlled is what I thought of first.<br /> <br /> Axe found a scent and followed it to a dead end. Other than the police and the dead homeless people, there had only been one person here that didn\u2019t fit. The scent was of a young caucasian male, who was oddly not sweaty given the heat needed to cause this level of damage. He walked to a car parked at the curb and left. We had a lead, but not a good one. But something else struck me. Officer Tart was the lead investigator on the scene. For all that Tart is crazy, he\u2019s probably also a sensitive. This was almost confirmed tonight. The whole time we were there, he continually walked an odd circuit around the perimeter, stopping exactly where Axe send our kid stood. I went to distract him on the other side of the building while our sensitives read the area. He opened up to me as I was a face he trusted. He told me that he probably wouldn\u2019t be lead on this case for long as his superiors didn\u2019t believe this had anything to do with Satanists. I suggested that maybe he not mention the Satanists without proof of Satanists. I don\u2019t think he\u2019d gotten that far in his procedure for all the paranoia. We talked for a while and I talked him up a bit about trying to keep from bringing up the \u201cother\u201d before finding evidence of it, because we needed decent cops to stay on the force. I was absolutely distracting him, but nothing I said was false. Tart is a good man, just doesn\u2019t understand what he\u2019s poking at. I got his card to give to Mouse. Maybe she can help me figure something out.<br /> <br /> When I made it back to the van, Cupcake led the debriefing. A pyrokinetic started the fire on purpose; stared at a lighter before forming the wall of flames that he then pushed through the structure. She got his license plate off the lamp post and his description of crimes from the spot Tart kept returning to. Bright Eyes noted that there was also a ghost around randomly scaring people. That set me on edge. A pyromaniac with his own juice is bad news, but not something we can\u2019t handle. A ghost that is scaring the hell out of the living is exactly what I\u2019m supposed to keep from happening. Bright Eyes used one of her ceremonies to track down any nearby ghosts. She found two, but one was a child so not the one they saw in the visions. Without any other leads we could follow on our arsonist, we tracked the ghost to a nearby townhouse that looked like it might be condemned in the next ten minutes.<br /> <br /> The door was unlocked so we called inside. No sense in walking into a homeless squat and causing even more disruption. That was not actually the case this time though. A woman\u2019s voice called from deeper inside. My senses said she was a ghost, but the sound wasn\u2019t in Twilight. When we walked in, we all felt that we were standing in a haunt. And the pretty woman in the white flowing gown was standing in the living room of a cheap Elvira-wannabe set. There were movie and band posters from the nineties as well as a plastic stack of skulls from either a Hot Topic or Halloween store. The Beetlejuice poster was displayed the most prominently. Though the perky ghost didn\u2019t look much like it right then, with her bright smile and bouncy attitude, I could see she died due to a combination of heroin overdose and starvation. Marcie, as she introduced herself, was not \u201cthe scariest ghost on the East Coast,\u201d but she obviously had aspirations. The talk of Scare Raids like in the Casper movie set me on edge. Marcie had faded back to Twilight for her own comfort but was happy to talk to us about the pyro. She thought he was from New York but noticed him around several buildings. There was also a coffee shop he went to that the waitress\u2019 like him. The two things that stuck out the most of me in her story was that our target wasn\u2019t afraid of anything. She had checked him since Fear/Terror was apparently one of her growing Influences. That was the other thing. Marcie was becoming a geist and very quickly. That our pyro was apparently a sociopath which explained his lack of concern for committing a triple homicide; well that and no proof that would stand up in mortal courts. But we had proof and he\u2019s not a normal mortal. Axe had tightened from the moment we heard the description of the fire and this time I can\u2019t really say I disagree. Only Bright Eyes seems to think there was anything but malice used in the fire. She also mentioned he was cute. I don\u2019t get that woman sometimes.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Marcie was very helpful but she continually talked about looking for people to possess or terrify. It was driving me nuts so I finally started asking about her life so maybe I could find out more and learn a way to help her move on. She had moved her body into one of the rooms so her main anchor was here. That was where things got really hard for me. Marcie has some pretty big dreams, if somewhat twisted by silly movies, to become the scariest ghost around. She can already sense the fears of those around her and wants to lead Scare Raids. That\u2019s a pretty creative thought for a ghost. However getting her to talk about herself caused her appearance to change. The more she talked, the less she was the pretty blonde in the flowing white gown and more the track marked, dirty waif in makeshift clothes. Her demeanor changed from excited and happy to tired and depressed. It was then that we could see exactly who had died, forgotten and alone. I could feel my guts tighten as for a split second I saw Nightshade\u2019s face instead of Marcie\u2019s. Nightshade and I have shared most of our nightmares and hardships. I knew the anguish and disgust she went through before. But things turned around for Nightshade. Marcie was a reminder of exactly what could have happened to one of my closest friends. What I should have said was that she needed to stop interfering with the living unless they interfered with her. It is my responsibility to stop that kind of activity. What I actually said, while fighting back tears of my own, was that I knew some people she might be able to work with to do her Scare Raids. I\u2019m going to call Grin and/or the rest of the Autumn Court. Marcie died without fulfilling any of her dreams. Maybe in death, I can help her become something more without losing what made her who she was. I realize this is basically experimenting with the creation of a geist but I can\u2019t bring myself to crush the glimmer of hope Marcie has finally gained.<br /> <br /> Marcie gave us her key so we could come and go to check on her. I\u2019m also going to use my ceremony to create some ofrenda and books so she has new context on the world since she died. Beetlejuice should not be the height of her goals. But first, we have to finish with the magic island sleepover.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s going to be a long night.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Alice was gone for most of the day, off trying to get her thoughts together with a walk on the beach. A long walk, and a cold one. But we took care of our Little Red when she got back, me with a hug for warmth and Doc with a blanket. A hot bath (alone, sadly) and a piping hot seafood stew later and she was good as new and confronting Doc about looking down on her.<br /> <br /> It didn\u2019t start out that way, naturally. It started out with her explaining what her gathering of thoughts had led to and why that had her particularly pleased at Doc\u2019s ritual. She\u2019s felt kinda uncomfortable at how intense, clingy and strong Angelique was coming on. Apparently it moved beyond \u2018U-Haul\u2019 into stalkery a bit ago. Probably when she had strongly implied that it was only her depth of feeling for Alice that let her resist her mentor\u2019s patron\u2019s commands. It might have ruined Angelique\u2019s chances with Alice, but it did make it so she didn\u2019t want to break it off so long as her mentor\u2019s patron was an issue. Which has my back up, and puts me solidly behind Alice\u2019s decision. Not that I wouldn\u2019t have been whatever her reasons, but... *shrug* \u201cYou have to be with me or I\u2019ll become a horrible murder-beast, starting with the people you care about\u201d is not that way to start things off, even if there is no malicious intent.<br /> <br /> But the Doc thing - Alice also mentioned being worried about keeping up mentally with Angelique. When Doc was confused at the idea, it all came out about how our Little Rd felt like Doc didn\u2019t think much of her intelligence or even common sense. With some of the the things he\u2019s said, it wasn\u2019t a huge leap, even it he didn\u2019t actually intend what she read out of it. My previous assurances that he fussed at everyone and that she wasn\u2019t, in fact, dumb, just cause she didn\u2019t like the books like the rest of us didn\u2019t quite cut it, I guess. Really, I ought have gone to him and told him how she\u2019d taken his comments, so they could have had this conversation and hashed it out before now. It needed to happen eventually, and should have sooner, probably.<br /> <br /> Thinking about it, I should go to talk to him now, as at least part of why I didn\u2019t was a feeling that he wouldn\u2019t have taken it seriously coming from me, especially since it\u2019s her, and he knows I think she\u2019s beautiful. I\u2019m not entirely certain he trusts my reads on people at this point. I was gonna say it\u2019s because of how many people I\u2019ve had sex with, but that\u2019s not fair. It\u2019s more likely because of *who* I\u2018ve had sex with. And because I insist on everyone\u2019s potential to do good, even the ones we catch doing bad things. Or maybe I\u2019m just imagining it. But I definitely ought to talk with him, before I let assumptions get in the way of the cohesion of the troupe.<br /> <br /> I did promise to kick him in the shins next time he puts his foot in his mouth. He wanted me to do it before said shoe tasting, but I\u2019ve yet to develop foot-in-mouth prescience, so he\u2019ll have to settle for after. :-)<br /> <br /> In other news, we\u2019re actually getting to help out a ghost! To be fair, it\u2019s sorta a side thing - Noriko told us about this very strange fire and we went to check it out, her, Doc, Alice, Alexia and me. Alice used her Sight (technically, I should probably say her Sense of Smell, but Sight is much more mystical sounding - I haven\u2019t forgotten all you\u2019ve taught me of showmanship) to find where the arsonist had stood and gone, and the Alexia and I used our Sight on those areas to get a glimpse of him. He was kinda cute, to be honest,a little on the preppy side. The others seem to have written him off though. He did kill 3 people, it\u2019s true. Conceivably by accident, though that is a stretch. But all we have of him is a single vision of one (admittedly, without context a pretty bad one) action and the word of a ghost that he is sociopathically not afraid of anything and from New York. Hopefully the others will at least humor me in attempting to see if there is anything redeemable or mitigating in the situation. Hopefully by talking to the supposedly cute barista that has a crush on him if nothing else.<br /> <br /> But the ghost - she also hung out at the newly burnt down building, acting out Beetlejuician jump scares on passersby. Hers was a sad story - a young runaway who died of a drug overdose and starvation. When I searched for her voice in the spectral howl, it even said she was still addicted to heroin. Which made it a little strange to find a bright, happy young woman, in a flowing white dress, surrounded by accumulated detritus, including wind chimes, movie posters, newspapers and plastic Halloween decorations, talking about being \u2018the Scariest Ghost on the East Coast\u2019. She was even planning on a scare raid, like the trio of ghosts from Casper. Casper\u2019s uncles, I think, or older brothers?<br /> <br /> The connections unfolded during our conversation. It became clear that she was well on her way towards a different kind of fate, where she will become a new thing, a conceptual being, instead of returning to the cycle. We mentioned this to her and she latched onto it, even the idea of losing her Self into whatever concept she will embody (something to do with fear, certainly). This bugged Doc particularly (as did her spooking habits) because, I think, he was as charmed by Marcy as the rest of us.<br /> <br /> A Self is a hell of a thing to sacrifice on your way to becoming, but it is a harder thing to sacrifice for some than others. Unfortunately, the Marcy we were charmed by was the result of her already having lost much of her living Self. When Doc discussed finding her body to give it a proper burial, and her old life was brought too close to the surface, she shrunk in on herself, looking gaunt and starved. Her flowing white dress became ragged barely-clothes and her ghostly arms were covered in track marks. She was clearly jonesing for a fix. I comforted her as I could, and we managed to get her a little stable, a little more like the Scariest Ghost on the East Coast.<br /> <br /> Doc was clearly conflicted between his dislike of the idea of sacrificing even one\u2019s own Self to become something greater and his desire to make it so ghost Marcy never hurt the way junkie Marcy had. We\u2019ll be seeing her again though, and helping her out one way or another. I think we\u2019re all agreed on that.<br /> <br /> So, after our pleasant and lazy afternoon and kinda hectic and heart-wrenching evening, it\u2019s about time for our sleepover in the sympathetic magic room. Sleeping in a room surrounded by creepy faceless manikins and Ziploc bags full of viscera is not really how I imagined that cultural staple that is the sleepover. But one of my favorite people will be there with me and two that I am quite fond of. I\u2019ve fallen asleep in less pleasant circumstance and I have a magical dream island adventure to look forward to.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> After Angelique leaves, I\u2019m fairly restless, so I decide to take a walk along the beach to gather my thoughts. My walk periodically becomes a jog, and I end up staying out for the next few hours even though it\u2019s ridiculously cold and there\u2019s a bone-chilling wind coming in off the ocean. I really hate this freezing winter weather. Even bundled up against it, it still gets under my skin.<br /> <br /> I miss Arizona.<br /> <br /> The weather\u2019s good for something, though. Thoughts of Angelique clutter my mind, and the cold helps give me a sort of clarity. Angelique seems so different now than when I first met her. I feel for her, and I\u2019ll do anything to help free her from the bonds forced on her by her late mentor, but being with her is making me increasingly uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> Maybe it\u2019s the cold, or maybe it\u2019s the stress over Angelique, but I really want to see Eris right now. I guess that means I\u2019ve made my choice.<br /> <br /> How the heck am I going to break the news to Angelique?<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> By the time I return to the mansion, I feel like a popsicle. I take the time to enjoy a long, hot bath before dinner, and I feel much better afterward.<br /> <br /> Over dinner, I learn that the others have been busy this afternoon, working out plans with the twins for finding Moriah\u2019s blood-bathing tub. And while I was out walking, Doc was cloistered in the library, looking for answers to Angelique\u2019s problem. He might have found them. He\u2019s developed a ritual that will help Angelique change her true name. It doesn\u2019t sound pleasant, but if it works, then hopefully it will sever her ties to her diabolic master. That is the best news I\u2019ve had all day.<br /> <br /> After dinner, I draw Doc and Sara aside to get more details of the ritual. It will involve branding Angelique with silver and weathering her werewolf death rage, but I\u2019ll be there to absorb her fury if necessary. With the right Shroud, I should be able to handle it for a short time at least.<br /> <br /> I thank Doc, and then begin to explain how relieved I am to know we might have a solution to the immediate problem. I explain that I don\u2019t think things are going to work out between Angelique and me, and that it will seriously help me break the bad news to her if she\u2019s not relying on me as an anchor against the lure of her demonic patron. But the discussion goes off the rails.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s scary how insistent and needy she\u2019s been. She\u2019s been saying the she belongs to me. It\u2019s creepy, almost like a stalker,\u201d I explain as Doc and Sara listen. Sara in particular seems troubled by Angelique\u2019s behavior. She\u2019s almost angry that my werewolf friend has been using her plight to make me hers, but I try to defend Angelique. I don\u2019t think she\u2019s maliciously forcing me into a relationship. She\u2019s just desperate. That doesn\u2019t make it any less uncomfortable.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not just that, though,\u201d I continue. \u201cWhen I first me Angelique, I liked the mysterious, coy, confident woman I saw. Even then, though, I was intimidated by her sharp mind. She\u2019s so intelligent and beautiful, a part of me worries that I can\u2019t really keep up with her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWait, why would you be worried about that?\u201d Doc interrupts.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m confused. What\u2019s he getting at? In the back of my mind, I start to feel defensive. Is Doc making fun of me?<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, you know. She\u2019s a lot smarter than me,\u201d I try to explain.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat?\u201d Doc replies. \u201cThat\u2019s bullshit.\u201d<br /> <br /> I\u2019m incredulous. I can\u2019t believe that Doc, of all people, is trying to compliment my intelligence.<br /> <br /> \u201cReally, Doc? Since I\u2019ve arrived, you\u2019ve made it abundantly clear that you think I\u2019m an idiot, and now you\u2019re trying to convince me that I can keep up with Angelique?\u201d<br /> <br /> Now it\u2019s Doc\u2019s turn to look confused. And then mortified.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh my god, Alice,\u201d he babbles, clearly flustered by his embarrassment. \u201cI don\u2019t think you\u2019re stupid. Far from it! You\u2019re smart, you\u2019re cunning, and I\u2019m glad to have you with the krewe. What the hell gave you the idea that I thought you were an idiot?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, let\u2019s see,\u201d I say with a hint of sarcasm as Sara cringes in the background. \u201cFor starters, the way you went off on me when I climbed the cliff. I know my limits, and I know what\u2019s safe and what isn\u2019t, but you didn\u2019t give me the benefit of the doubt. And for that matter, you also got upset at me for talking about our supernatural gifts in front of the normals, but you were the one who brought them up in the first place! And then there was the time you told me to \u2018go read a book,\u2019 when I was trying to suggest a plan of action that didn\u2019t involve getting lost in a library for a few hours. That\u2019s not all, but I don\u2019t even remember the other things you\u2019ve said or done that made me feel stupid and small.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc is shocked. Apparently, he didn\u2019t realize how he was making me feel. He glances at Sara and she nods with a \u2018she\u2019s right, you know,\u2019 look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice, I\u2019m so sorry!\u201d Doc says with sincere remorse. \u201cI had no idea\u2026I never meant to make you feel like I thought you weren\u2019t intelligent. You\u2019re a smart woman. I\u2019ve seen more than enough to respect that. I don\u2019t know what to say.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t have to say anything,\u201d I respond. \u201cJust, in the future, give me the benefit of the doubt, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc nods absently, still embarrassed. \u201cYeah. Look, I\u2019m sorry about the cliff-climbing thing, but I have a duty toward the krewe. Everyone here is my responsibility, and I have to make sure they are all safe. Especially the normals.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know. I get it. You\u2019re the Papa Bear, and I respect that. Sara and Natalie have both made it clear that you care about all of us, even me. I\u2019m glad. It\u2019s nice to be part of a family again. It\u2019s just that I\u2019ve been doing this sin-eater thing just as long as you have. With another krewe, sure. But I have experience and I know my capabilities and my limits better than you do. I\u2019m not well-educated, and I didn\u2019t go to college like the rest of you academic types, but I\u2019m not an idiot. All I\u2019m asking is that you trust that I know what I\u2019m doing. I can\u2019t guarantee I won\u2019t do something stupid from time to time\u2014.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc barks out a laugh that interrupts me. \u201cTrust me, we\u2019re all guilty of that,\u201d he says. Sara nods significantly again, and I get the impression that Doc\u2019s made his share of mistakes. \u201cLook, I\u2019m sorry. I\u2019ll try to trust you more from here on out. It\u2019s not easy for me, but I\u2019ll do my best. And Alice, you are an intelligent woman. Hell, you aren\u2019t the only one of us without a college education, like that should make a difference anyway. I think Alexia\u2019s the only one who graduated.\u201d<br /> <br /> It\u2019s my turn to be surprised. \u201cReally? You guys seem so academic and you all spend so much time in the library, I just thought\u2026I mean, didn\u2019t you go to medical school?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNah, I\u2019m just a field medic. Army training.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReally? Huh.\u201d<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Since I\u2019ve arrived in New Haven, Noriko has quickly become one of my best friends (along with Sara, of course). So when she asked for my help just after dinner, I was more than happy to oblige. Doc, Sara and Alexia tagged along too.<br /> <br /> Someone committed arson on the bad side of town, and it looks like it was supernatural. The flames killed three homeless people, so the arsonist is also a murderer. Sounds like the sort of person who deserves my axe.<br /> <br /> Ah, yes. Deserving prey at last. There\u2019s the Alice I love.<br /> <br /> The Grasping Huntress sighs like she\u2019s just taken a fresh drink of water after being stuck in the desert all day. I can almost feel her spectral hands stroking my head in what I assume is supposed to be a gesture of encouragement and affection.<br /> <br /> We spent some time investigating the building. Flames swept through it quickly, but there was no accelerant, no incendiaries, nothing to start the fire. Between my tracking and Sara and Alexia\u2019s ability to read the echoes of things and places, we were able to put a face to our arsonist. He\u2019s young man in his early 20\u2019s. Looks like a preppy. Sara got a glimpse of him in her visions, and says he\u2019s handsome. Worst of all, he\u2019s able to create flames just by thinking about it. He must be some sort of pyrokinetic.<br /> <br /> The homeless who perished in the fire didn\u2019t leave any ghosts, but our search did turn up a local haunt, and Sara tracked her down with a ceremony. I need to get her to teach me that one.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re in an abandoned, run-down house in the bad part of town, talking to a heroine-addict ghost named Marcie who is actually transforming herself into a geist of whimsical terror (it looks like Beetlejuice is one of her inspirations). Who knows? Maybe she\u2019ll succeed. I\u2019m all for it if it helps her escape the painful echoes of her shattered life.<br /> <br /> Marcie lyrically claims she\u2019ll someday become the \u201cScariest Ghost on the East Coast,\u201d and I\u2019m enjoying her antics and Doc\u2019s discomfort until we get down to the business of grilling her about our arsonist. She says she\u2019s seen him around. He\u2019s wandered through the neighborhood a few times, scoping out buildings, and he sometimes hangs out in a nearby coffee shop. There are a few people there who seem to know him, and Sara volunteers to talk to them. I get the feeling she\u2019s hoping to find out something to redeem the arsonist.<br /> <br /> Fire is a terrible way to die. He does not deserve redemption. Your friend\u2019s bleeding heart will not deny us our prey.<br /> <br /> I find myself agreeing with the Huntress. The others are more cautious, though. Maybe there\u2019s more to the story? Maybe this guy had a reason for burning the building or killing those homeless people. Then Marcie tells us that she once tried to use her ghostly powers to scare him, but it didn\u2019t work. There wasn\u2019t even a glimmer of fear in his eyes.<br /> <br /> Sounds like he\u2019s a psychopath.<br /> <br /> The best kind of prey.<br /> <br /> I can feel the excitement of the hunt building inside me, and this time I don\u2019t try to force it back down. I\u2019m already convinced this is a just kill, and I\u2019m eager to throw myself into the hunt.<br /> <br /> Then Marcie comments, somewhat timidly, that both my cat and I have killed a lot of people. She\u2019s referring to Noriko, of course, who is in her cat form. I\u2019m holding and petting her at the moment. We\u2019re both pretty amused by Marcie\u2019s confusion, but then the Huntress goes and ruins the moment.<br /> <br /> You realize that your little cat friend is competition, don\u2019t you? She\u2019s after the same prey, the same kill. Only one of us can end this pyromaniac, and it must be our axe that extinguishes his life. We need this hunt\u2026this kill, Alice.<br /> <br /> The Huntress is insatiable. We just killed Moriah a few days ago.<br /> <br /> Yes, and that was a worthy hunt. But we did not end her. She is not truly dead. It leaves me feeling\u2026unsettled. Unsatisfied. I know you feel the same. I can sense it. We need to bathe our axe in this firestarter\u2019s blood.<br /> <br /> I try to put the Huntress\u2019 insistent whispers out of my mind, but a part of me can\u2019t shake the territorial fear that she\u2019s right. Still, I suppress my doubts and tell myself that Noriko is not competition. She\u2019s a kindred spirit and an important friend. We\u2019ll hunt this pyromaniac together. End him together. And if the Huntress doesn\u2019t like that, then she\u2019ll just have to go sulk about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> I never met Marcie Hicks. Still haven\u2019t, technically.<br /> <br /> But she was still a ghost from my past. I lived on the street too. I did heroin on the street too. Goddess if I had been there I would have broken down and cried. I still cried after hearing about her. Can\u2019t let Tracy or Timothy see that, and can\u2019t be anything less than on task for a significantly dangerous supernatural experiment.<br /> <br /> Marcie Hicks, the Internet says, is a missing person from Tennessee, went missing in \u201996, said she was going to New York. Somehow she OD\u2019d and died in New Haven. There was apparently an appropriate amount of Missing White Girl Syndrome at the time; she is, Sara says, rather cute.<br /> <br /> I was on the street, did heroin, but I got lucky. Well, I got lucky because I was pretty enough to find a sugar daddy, and manipulative enough to keep him for awhile. But I only stayed off because I had some talent for marketing myself.<br /> <br /> Marcie did not get lucky. She starved, she OD\u2019d. I hear about her, and I think \u201cthat could have been me\u2026that was me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Stop crying.<br /> <br /> I need to get this out of my system before I meet her. I don\u2019t need to bring her down, I don\u2019t need to start crying, and I don\u2019t need to start acting like I am her mom. I got better, I survived. I am sorry she didn\u2019t. I should, must, help her as best I can. If that means helping her be \u201cThe scariest ghost on the east coast\u201d that is what it will take\u2026but I think I will start helping her with a better tagline.<br /> <br /> My life got better when I died. Maybe hers will too.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXXXV</i><br /> <br /> I am old, and forget people think of the movie Casper not the TV show or comics.<br /> <br /> And yea, as a reminder Tart is kinda the opposite of anti-psi. Psychics and ghosts get an extra die to use their powers when around him, and he does not count against them as a witness. Low Magic Practitioners don\u2019t gain a die, but they lose one less then they normally would (minimum no effect if they would not have lost any) and he does not count as an unbelieving witness there either. He can sense recent haunting or psychic activity, though he is unaware of this. His powers don\u2019t affect Spirits, God-Machine stuff, or anything with a Major Template. He still does not believe in Vampires though.<br /> <br /> Lotta good drama though, Marcie was popular, and we are back to where we were. We should be going forward tonight. See you in two weeks. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-12T14:21:09-07:00","id":588481,"title":"","content":"Back to Geist. It\u2019s been a crazy couple weeks with a lot going on, and Doc had to miss this particular session. He should be back at tonight\u2019s game, though, so fear not. Alice, Natalie, and Sara kept busy, and provided us with their own narratives, and of course Alexia was there as well. Let\u2019s dig in, as they say.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> A quick note to keep you updated, since I was off on a magical dream island adventure with unknown consequences at the end of my last email. After our very fruitful dreamy nap time, we have relocated to much less creepy environs. Sadly,Tracey and Timothy each have their own guest bedroom and are not keeping me company, but I will have a Natalie rewrapped around me soon.<br /> <br /> That is the way we woke up on the magic dream island. Naked, of course. Natalie refused to budge until she got some clothes, going so far as to give a maidenly \u2018eep!\u2019 when Tracey came in to get her some, pulling the sheet to her chin. Tracey did manage to will into existence a wonderfully low cut white dress for Natalie. It was downright delicious.<br /> <br /> But there was also a job to do. Timothy seems far more tuned into the sensory side of things to do with the island - he was able to sense the consciousness of the island sized thing that submerged shortly after they arrived. He also seems to have a handle on defense and wards, as he was able to keep it out and had to allow me and Natalie to leave later.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t have to keep out the big thing long, as Tracey started us moving at a quick pace. Once the big thing was left behind, and all that was left was a group of shadowy, more humanoid shapes, he joined her and we picked up even more speed. Unfortunately, the distance we put between us and our bodies left me at least feeling weaker,lesser, like I wasn\u2019t quite as existent as before. It was not a pleasant experience, or one I\u2019m rushing to have again. It was handleable though, and not too long after it became noticeable, we had arrived. By Tim\u2019s calculations, we were at the northeast seaboard, possibly just barely into Canada. Not bad, for 15 minutes of... floating?<br /> <br /> We used our Sight to peek over into the waking world. It wasn\u2019t but the work of a moment to get the street name, the nearest cross street, the state (Maine, at least based on license plates). It was a quiet suburban street, and the house at hand appeared to be occupied by a Sikh family. It was a little harder to confirm that the tub was actually there, but Natalie found it in a hidden basement room.<br /> <br /> So we popped back home and let the others know. Alice is gonna call Angelique first thing in the morning to make sure we can get that situation worked out soon, then it\u2019s time for a road trip!<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> When it rains, it pours, no? A lead, a complication and a detour, all in &lt; 24 hours. The lead, of course, was courtesy of the twins, who I thanked profusely again before they headed out this morning. The second I unwittingly mentioned last email, and the third was, as detours occasionally are, out of the blue.<br /> <br /> The complication is that things have progressed with Angelique\u2019s situation. Alice had hints that something was not right when she called with the good news before breakfast, and then proof after, when she called to lure her out to the woods, since the Angelique that would take more than a millisecond to say yes to a date with our Little Red was not the Angelique we all know and love.<br /> <br /> Out current plan involves going to Mallard with a slightly tailored story and getting her help. That, however is waiting 1) for nightfall, to lessen the amount of time for things to go pear shaped before the ritual could begin and 2) for Alice to get back. See, she had called Eris, to hear her voice, check in and maybe set up a date, but found out Eris had gone off searching for her past. Alone. With no way to be reached. Haring off alone is apparently a thing she does, but considering the imagery of what little memory she had, I cannot blame Alice for worrying about this particular adventure.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, our Little Red found Eris safe and sound and with a chunk of extra memories. Memories of being kept in a cage, but nonetheless, I imagine filling in any holes is a relief. The site where she was kept is a currently abandoned factory, that showed signs of having been raided, in a serious way. That, the few memories and a stash of medical files marked with a logo for Team Tomorrow Genetic Research was not a bad haul for a wild goose chase.<br /> <br /> Alice should be back soon though, and then it will be time to go talk to a powerful crazy old man with a shotgun about how his verboten girlfriend may be tainted by an evil spirit and we need his help abducting and securing her for a ritual that involves marking her permanently and painfully in order to change her true name. Piece of cake, right?<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> With the help of the twins, Natalie and Sara managed to find out where Moriah\u2019s blood-bathing tub is hidden last night, but at breakfast, the krewe decided to go ahead and do what we need to do for Angelique before we head off to finish Moriah once and for all. After all, Angelique\u2019s problem is a little more urgent.<br /> <br /> I pick up the phone and call her and make plans. When she picks up, I can instantly tell that something\u2019s not right. She doesn\u2019t greet me with her normal hopeful enthusiasm. It\u2019s almost like she\u2019s feigning interest in our conversation.<br /> <br /> Testing the waters, I tell her that Doc came up with a plan to help her, and we\u2019d like to go ahead and put it into action tonight.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot yet,\u201d she says. \u201cMy connection to my patron will help us track down the Balehound. I need to hold on to it for awhile longer.\u201d<br /> <br /> That doesn\u2019t sound like Angelique. The Angelique I know would be eager to sever ties to her personal demon. A sinking feeling settles in the pit of my stomach and puts me on guard. I try a different approach.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, if that\u2019s what you think is best...\u201d I say hesitantly. \u201cI\u2019d like to see you all the same. Do you want to come over and hang out tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique hesitates, and when she speaks her voice is clipped and impatient. \u201cNo, I have other things I need to do tonight. Important things.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, maybe I can help? I mean, I\u2019m worried about you, and I\u2019d like to see you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>You are one manipulative bitch. </i><br /> <br /> The Huntress loves pointing out my missteps. She\u2019s also prone to exaggeration.<br /> <br /> <i>One minute you\u2019re talking about how Angelique makes you uncomfortable, how you\u2019re going to break things off with her, and the next you\u2019re begging her to come over and play. </i><br /> <br /> Sometimes the Huntress is deeply unsettling and insidiously accurate with the slings and barbs she tosses at me, but right now she\u2019s just being petty. I don\u2019t think she cares much for Angelique. Of course, I am being a little manipulative, but it\u2019s for Angelique\u2019s own good. She\u2019s my friend, and I need to help her. Getting her out of that house against her will isn\u2019t going to be easy. Her elder werewolf boyfriend isn\u2019t likely to put up with us kidnapping his girl.<br /> <br /> Angelique hesitates before responding, and when she speaks, it\u2019s different. I can hear the real Angelique fighting through whatever has hold of her mind. She tries to warn me off, to let me know that something\u2019s wrong.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t call me, Alice. Stay away from me! Just\u2026just leave me alone!\u201d<br /> <br /> She hangs up.<br /> <br /> It looks like we\u2019re going to have to figure out how to kidnap a demon-possessed werewolf from under the watchful gaze of her ridiculously dangerous and arguably unstable boyfriend and force her into a soul-changing ritual against her will.<br /> <br /> If we can\u2019t do that\u2026well, I promised to kill her, and I keep my promises.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t think I\u2019d end up tracking down my missing girlfriend this afternoon, not when the krewe has plans to get Mr. Malard on our side and deal with Angelique tonight. But I wanted to talk to Eris and tell her how I felt, so I called Deirdre. She said Eris was missing. Honestly, Eris disappears from time to time for a few days, and according to Deirdre, it\u2019s not a big deal. In fact, she tends to get a bit snippy when people come looking for her. This time, though, Deirdre was pretty sure Eris was tracking down bits of her past, and given what little we knew, that sounded dangerous. I was pretty worried, and it didn\u2019t take much to convince Deirdre and Barret to help me find their errant pack mate.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re hot on her trail. The bitter cold of this New England winter doesn\u2019t bite as hard when you\u2019re tracking prey with a couple of werewolves. Deirdre and Barret dash through the streets of New Haven like wolf-shaped shadows, and I\u2019m pleased to find that I can easily keep pace once I\u2019ve unlocked my Primeval Caul. Between the three of us, it\u2019s not hard to follow Eris\u2019 trail, and we soon track her to an abandoned facility of some sort. It might have been a factory, but something\u2019s not quite right about it. The place looks like it was some sort of war zone a few years ago, with bullet-pocked walls and flame-scorched steel doors.<br /> <br /> The werewolves regain their human forms and we break into the abandoned building. It\u2019s hard to tell what the heck the place once was, but it\u2019s big, with lots of open rooms that look like they might once have held machinery or labs. I get the feeling this was some sort of research facility, and it sends a shiver down my spine. If someone was experimenting on Eris\u2026<br /> <br /> I call out for her and I\u2019m immensely relieved when a cinnamon-brown wolf runs out of an upstairs room and barks to us from the railing of the upstairs gallery that overlooks the building\u2019s main floor. Eris bounds over the railing and transforms into her human shape as she rushes over to greet us. The poor girl is naked again, and now that she\u2019s bereft of her thick, soft fur, she starts to shiver.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you okay?\u201d I ask, placing my hands on her shoulders and looking seriously into her eyes. \u201c I called Deirdre to talk to you and she told me you\u2019d gone off to look into your past. I was worried!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m okay. I go off sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, yeah, but not to look into your past. I thought\u2026I was worried that if you found something, it might find you. That you might get in over your head. I was scared something bad might\u2019ve happened to you. I\u2019m glad you\u2019re safe, though.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris nod and shifts uncomfortably. I don\u2019t think she knows how to respond to my concern, but she\u2019s clearly glad to see me.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd good lord, take my coat,\u201d I give her my coat and then wrap my arm around her shoulder to help her warm up. I\u2019m not sure how much it helps. I think now we\u2019re both freezing, but it\u2019s the thought that counts, right?<br /> <br /> \u201cYou called me?\u201d she asks. \u201cOn the phone?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, she called me because she wanted to talk to you,\u201d Deirdre says a little impatiently. \u201cYou have a phone now. We can give Alice your number, but you have to take your phone with you or else she can\u2019t call you and you can\u2019t talk to her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris nods. Deirdre doesn\u2019t seem convinced.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you want to talk to Alice, you\u2019ve got to keep your phone on you,\u201d Deirdre repeats.<br /> <br /> Eris nods again but she\u2019s having trouble focusing. She keeps glancing upstairs.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, you know this place?\u201d I ask.<br /> <br /> Eris nods excitedly. \u201cYes. I was here. I don\u2019t remember before, I just remember being here.\u201d She suddenly dashes off, bounding up some nearby stairs three at a time. The rest of us hurry to follow her. She stops in a large room. The floor shows signs of discoloration where industrial furnishings or some sort of machinery might once have stood, but now the room is almost empty except for bits of debris.<br /> <br /> \u201cI woke up here. I was in a cage,\u201d she says, pacing in a small circle in one corner of the room. I look around, my eyes narrowing at the thought of Eris being caged. The Huntress becomes very interested. She\u2019s caught the scent of a hunt, and this time I\u2019m right there with her. I don\u2019t know exactly what happened to Eris, but it was wrong, and the people responsible have to pay.<br /> <br /> \u201cThen I escaped from the cage,\u201d Eris says. She hurries out of the room, down a short hallway, and into another room with a big window. We follow. \u201cI jumped on a table here,\u201d she stands in front of the window, and then points at the glass. \u201cThen I broke out through the window and ran away. That\u2019s when the bright lights and the shouting and the big red dog happened.\u201d She turns to look at me, a mixture of fear and excitement on her face.<br /> <br /> Deirdre and Barret look around the room, taking it all in. We\u2019ve stumbled onto something big, and none of us quite know what to think.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you remember what they were doing here? What this place was?\u201d I ask.<br /> <br /> Eris shakes her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt looks like maybe some sort of lab,\u201d says Deirdre, giving voice to my thoughts.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah,\u201d Barret concurs. \u201cIt doesn\u2019t look like they left much behind, but let\u2019s look around. Maybe we\u2019ll find something.\u201d<br /> <br /> We spread out and begin combing the abandoned facility for anything that might be a clue: a company logo, old papers, leftover equipment. Unfortunately, whoever used to run the place did a thorough job of cleaning it out when they left.<br /> <br /> Then I notice a couple of folders full of papers wedged into a gap in the wall. It all looks medical to me, and it\u2019s well beyond the emergency medical training Deirdre and Barret received as park rangers. Maybe Doc will know what it means. Even if he doesn\u2019t, though, the papers give us a name: Team Tomorrow Genetic Research.<br /> <br /> What the heck was this place, and what did they do to Eris?<br /> <br /> We look around a little longer, but dusk is fast approaching, and I have to get back to help the krewe with Angelique. We head back to Sleeping Giant and it\u2019s completely dark by the time we arrive. Deirdre and Barret want to hold on to the papers to do a little research of their own, but they make copies for me to take back to Doc.<br /> <br /> Eris wants me to stay. It\u2019s hard for me to tell her I have to go, and Deirdre has to remind her why she can\u2019t go home with me. Before I go, though, I tell her what I\u2019ve been wanting to say to her all day.<br /> <br /> \u201cEris, I hate to go. I wish I could stay. Right now, nothing would make me happier. But someone else badly needs my help. Before I go, though, I want you to know that I\u2019ve chosen. My heart knows what it wants now, and it\u2019s you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris\u2019 face lights up, her gorgeous, exotic eyes widening with pleasure and maybe a hint of surprise. She wraps her arms around my neck and smothers me with kisses. I enjoy the moment as long as I can, but all too soon, Deirdre comes to my rescue.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s got to go, Eris. I\u2019m sure Alice will be back as soon as she can.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou bet,\u201d I say, smiling at Eris and kissing her once more. \u201cIn the meantime, I\u2019ll probably call, so keep your phone handy, okay?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d Eris says seriously. Maybe the advice will stick this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 17th 2010<br /> <br /> -Ugh that was exciting.<br /> <br /> -Real Sleep this time.<br /> <br /> <br /> November 18th 2010<br /> <br /> -Early.<br /> <br /> -Bitch betta not touch the flapjacky goodness.<br /> <br /> -Hya Hya! Back foul temptress!<br /> <br /> -Hmmmm that is not good.<br /> <br /> -Concerned about Werewolf lady.<br /> <br /> -Planning Planning<br /> <br /> -Alexia is a very, very strange person.<br /> <br /> -We make very strange plans.<br /> <br /> -I think there are few things more ominous not involving weapons than having a bag put over your head.<br /> <br /> -She was trying to help\u2026<br /> <br /> -Alice is going out to find her girlfriend.<br /> <br /> -Hope that ends up okay. Minimum of gnawing, etc.<br /> <br /> -Pinochle, anyone?<br /> <br /> -Yea me neither.<br /> <br /> -Do I actually WANT to go out and see Deathly Hallows tomorrow night? On opening weekend?<br /> <br /> -It does have the words \u201cDeathly\u201d and \u201cHallows\u201d in the title.<br /> <br /> -Alice back, safe and sound.<br /> <br /> -Now what?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXVI</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s probably not lost on some of you there is some crossover here with a certain group of Antagonists in Night Train Detective Agency. They <i>are</i> connected; however, the trails won\u2019t lead to precisely the same place; Balance of Shadows takes place (currently) about 4 years before Night Train Detective Agency. Both stories will play out within each game, though, and if you enjoy that kind of thing (hopefully) everything will be extra clear between games, though Team Tomorrow is a major story element for NTDA and a sort of single plot direction for BoS.<br /> <br /> And the island stuff is interesting, eh?<br /> <br /> But we have reached the point of wrapping this recap up. I should be feeling better tonight than last time, and we should have the whole Krewe\u2026well, short Simon as far as I know. I hope you will join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 07-12-2015, 05:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T16:41:34-07:00","id":605119,"title":"","content":"Tonight we deal with freeing Angelique, a step toward dealing with the Bale Hound. It\u2019s a sticky situation. It always is.<br /> <br /> Note Doc covers the previous session here as well as current.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log\u2019s: 0800 Hours, Thursday, November 18, 2010<br /> <br /> The girls managed to find Mariah\u2019s tub during the magic island sleepover last night with the twins. Nothing that Cupcake or I could sense tried to reach them so we feel like this was an unqualified success. But we\u2019re not finished putting out fires here, so no trip to Maine just yet.<br /> <br /> I have a long day of shopping ahead of me. We\u2019re going to perform the ritual on Angelique tonight so I need to gather my ritual components:<br /> <br /> 1 kg of medical grade Silver Nitrate<br /> <br /> 10 ft anchor chain<br /> <br /> smelting ladle<br /> <br /> horse tranquilizers<br /> <br /> We\u2019ll see how fruitful this works out to be. I have ideas about how to use some of this practically and then metaphysically during the ritual. I hope I\u2019m not missing the point.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1600 Hours, Thursday, November 18, 2010<br /> <br /> I couldn\u2019t find the horse tranqs anywhere that wouldn\u2019t look oddly at me for buying in cash without a vet\u2019s license. The anchor chain I couldn\u2019t buy in such a small length. Ended up having to hit an old shipyard and figuring out how to use a torch to cut one loose. For the record, that shit is HEAVY. The silver nitrate wasn\u2019t a problem, I just had to five different medical supply shops to get enough to do what I needed it to do. The smelting ladle was actually the easiest thing to get as I just went to Guilford Art Center and bought one of the blacksmith.<br /> <br /> After I got all that together, I came back to the Bluffs and borrowed Snowflake\u2019s carpentry expertise. We built the form for the moon cycle from Hickory so that it wouldn\u2019t just burn away as soon as the molten silver hit the sides. Then I went and set up my alchemy equipment. I really have to find a place to install a more permanent lab. Anyway, using a preparation similar to the Lead into Gold solution, I coated the iron smelting ladle on the glass and waited for the results. Luckily I used the right measurements and the alchemical reaction darkened the iron into tungsten. It happened quickly enough that there may be other qualities but the main need I have is to withstand the heat for the silver nitrate and act as an earth-oriented object to guide the Lune. Now I have to take the silver nitrate out to the people oven for smelting.<br /> <br /> Damn it! Bright Eyes has me saying it now.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log\u2019s: 2130 Hours, Thursday, November 18, 2010<br /> <br /> I need to find this Balehound. Guns, fire, fists, blades. Whatever I have at the time is fair game.<br /> <br /> Let me back up. I had a good day until the ritual. I should at least get that out before I rant about how I\u2019m going to fucking kill this asshole!<br /> <br /> The silver nitrate trick worked, but keeping it in liquid form did require I buy an acetylene torch. It was cheap enough that renting it would be dumb. Plus I\u2019m sure Snowflake and I will find other uses for a blow torch in the future. Once I have everything ready, Noriko and I headed out to a spot in the woods about 30 minutes into West Haven to prepare the grounds for our ritual.<br /> <br /> We had most things ready when Nightshade sent the text that they were going to get Angelique. That was probably around 1900 Hours. 20 minutes later I got a text from Cupcake letting me know that they were on the way. Unfortunately, Malard and the rest of his pack were also coming to watch the ritual. That was totally not what we planned. Something must have happened with Angelique. When they arrived, I learned that was an understatement.<br /> <br /> Apparently a Lust spirit or something similar had taken over our favorite Bone Shadow. She put the mind whammy on Malard and did more than that to Axe. Then when Cupcake came to move the pick-up process along, she interrupted. Not-Angelique tried to cut and run, but Cupcake when all Cowgirl Kali on her direwolf ass and had her hogtied in less than 8 seconds. This did led to a tense discussion with Malard about what was happening and how we needed his help to fix Angelique. From what I heard, he called Zed and said to meet or start running. Fortunately I didn\u2019t know any of this when they got to the ritual site.<br /> <br /> I got a little clue something was up when the pack didn\u2019t just show up but took up positions around the sacrificial rock I was using as a table. That\u2019s what it looked like, not what it was. But that did mean I didn\u2019t need to drag that big ass anchor chain out. They held Angelique even though she was knocked out at first. I unlocked my Phantasmal Shroud just in case and then looked at the grim faces of all the werewolves present. I was going to have to summon a Lune either way and I didn\u2019t need any extra handicaps, so I said fuck it. Letting my body fall to the ground, I unlocked the Phantasmal Marionette. The Dog of War stood well above anyone else as I walked back to my summoning circle. Erin did raise an eyebrow, but didn\u2019t move. It took about 40 minutes to summon the Lune, which just proved it wasn\u2019t something I did often. In First Tongue, and holding the tungsten smelting ladle, I convinced the spirit to help us. The only took about 15 minutes. The pack was pretty busy holding Angelique down so I don\u2019t know what they thought about things.<br /> <br /> Honestly, after that I don\u2019t really know what anyone else thought, did, or said. I took the form Snowflake and I made and positioned it at the base of Angelique\u2019s neck. Then I took the silver Noriko kept melted while I dealt with the spirit and poured it into the form. I knew that this would be very painful, but the medic in me blocked anything other than the fact this was for Angelique\u2019s health to realize what I would actually be doing. The only substance that can really wound a werewolf was being poured as molten metal onto bare skin and held there while a random moon spirit rearranged her soul. The Krewe was there to help save a friend and neighbor. The pack was there to see that a disease was cleansed from one of their own. But me? I was there to be the torturer of an accused witch. Molten metal poured over you when you can\u2019t get away is one of the most painful sensations the human body can endure. That I was dealing with a werewolf just meant that her body was fighting back harder than mine would to not burn. And to be woken by that pain was entirely on me. Amputation is never simple, clean, or easy to handle, and that\u2019s just from the medic\u2019s point of view. But this was unlike anything I\u2019ve ever had to perform. Torture to cure. I felt the strongest sense of self-loathing for what I had to do that I can remember.<br /> <br /> When it was finally over, Angelique was conscious but understandable exhausted. By all accounts, the ritual worked. I took the final precaution of thanking the Lune so that it would leave without incident. Then I let the Dog of War disperse like the floating embers of a dying fire. Axe helped Angelique stand before her pack came to her aid. As they moved to take her back home to rest, I caught Zed\u2019s attention. He came over and I confirmed that they would be hunting this Balehound. He assured me that they would be. I then told him that I will be there. He nodded and shook my hand.<br /> <br /> The ride home was celebratory but subdued. At least it was in the back. I was sick and fighting back tears. We got back to Dark Haven Bluffs around 2100 Hours. I set about unloading the van so the others were inside long before me. The cold night air helped me focus so I didn\u2019t fall apart. Then as I came back inside, Axe and Noriko came up to me almost giddily. Noriko said that they wanted to get matching tattoos, they didn\u2019t know of what yet, but they wanted me to do it. I had to smile at that. Axe said that they were going to be hunting partners so they needed something that represented them both. As a joke, I asked if she meant a scythe with a crossed claw mark over it. That didn\u2019t seem to amuse them so I said I\u2019d think of something. They thanked me then went with Nightshade and Bright Eyes to get in the hot tub. I went upstairs and cleaned off the ashes and blood that wasn\u2019t actually still on my hands. Then I threw up. Returning to my room after cleaning things up, I sat on the edge of my bed, looking at my hands. That was when the Dog of War decided I needed to talk.<br /> <br /> <i>Once again the guilt of another stains your heart as you strive to save others from themselves. Should this blame not fall entirely upon this foul creature of vice?<br /> </i><br /> That\u2019s pretty much what he said then too. It was about that time that the realization hit me. I wasn\u2019t trying to rationalize blame away when the tiny voice (that was mine) in my head said this was the Balehound\u2019s fault. That was my voice of reason trying to scream around my sense of responsibility. And with that confirmation of innocence came the tidal wave of anger that was so richly deserved.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to go and beat the heavy bag until one of us gives out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, that went... better? than I expected. Less violence than I expected, surely. More of Alice having things with a lust spirit go further than she intended/wanted. She promised she was alright though, and I think we got her fully clothed and standing upright before Mr Malard got a read on the situation, so trouble shouldn\u2019t come from that direction later. Hopefully.<br /> <br /> See, we\u2019d just got there when Mr. Malard went to find Angelique, who put on the lust spirit\u2019s sultriest voice to promise him the night of his life, if he shooed us away without listening to us. Alice did what she could to interrupt those promises, and wound up seducing her away/getting the hell seduced out of her. I think I\u2019m rubbing off on her. It did give Natalie, Alexia, me and Alexia\u2019s delicious cake pops times to tell our version of the story that didn\u2019t involve the distant past and managed to convince him something was wrong.<br /> <br /> There was a little bit of violence when Alexia went to go break up Angelique and Alice\u2019s compromising situation. Angelique did not appreciate this, but we managed to restrain her, largely due to Alexia\u2019s quick thinking when Angelique tried to bolt.<br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s state when I got there made me wish the spirit of lust wasn\u2019t on the other team. It took the whole car ride to the woods for her to be steady on her feet again. I was more worried than envious, of course, but she promised she was OK and even confided that she had said a bad word. I went through every nonstandard \u201cbad words\u201d I could think of, to cheer her up and admittedly, to see if I could coax her into saying it again, but our Little Red held out against my clever tricks. I do think I impressed her with my vocabulary though.<br /> <br /> Doc and Noriko had the ritual all laid out, waiting for us. Poor guy - he did not take his role in the situation well. The ritual involved marking her in a permanent and very painful way. Kinda like scarification, but in this case, not by true choice, not for the art of it. And the spiritual aspect of it made it even more painful. And, since Doc was the ritemaster, he was the one inflicting the pain. It wasn\u2019t easy on anyone, but her, Alice and Mr. Malard were the most affected. Since we got back home, Doc\u2019s been taking it out on the heavy bag while us ladies soaked in the hot tub. I think he\u2019s still going...<br /> <br /> Anyway, they were all prepared and Natalie was too. She\u2019d been dressed more normally for talking with Mr Malard, but she\u2019d stashed about seven extra layers in the Jeep. You\u2019d think with all that, plus me and a quilt draped over her, and an extra Alice under the quilt with us, she\u2019d be warm enough for an hour in the woods at night, but no... Karen didn\u2019t help. sending her pictures of her smiling beside a lit fireplace. I believe the retaliatory water gun was in fact filled with ice water, but Karen does seem to have let that lie as the final strike in our own Cold War.<br /> <br /> And in the end, it all worked out. Angelique is herself again, and currently recovering at home. The family has some questions for her, but they agreed that tonight, at the least, would be for resting. Alice is alright (she keeps assuring me) and everyone is safe. And warm. A hot tub is a lovely thing. All in all, a celebratory night\u2019s sleep is totally called for, if you ask me.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> Alexia knocks on Mr. Malard\u2019s door, and a moment later, the old man opens up. I\u2019m nervous. I wonder if he knows I\u2019ve been sleeping with his girlfriend, and I\u2019m more than a little scared of what he might do to me if he does. But if he knows, he doesn\u2019t seem to care. He greets us with a kindly smile and invites us in.<br /> <br /> Alexia hands over the cake pops. Mr. Malard smiles like a child whose mother has just given him a cookie before dinner, but before any of us can settle in and get comfortable, he goes to find Angelique. He disappears into the next room, where I can barely overhear a hushed conversation. Angelique isn\u2019t herself. She can be incredibly sexy when she wants to be, but the sultry tones I manage to pick out as she urges Malard to get rid of us don\u2019t sound like the girl I know.<br /> <br /> Sara, Alexia and I share helpless looks for a moment or two. We need to talk to Malard in private, and this isn\u2019t going so well. I shrug and take a deep breath. I might be taking my life into my own hands, but someone has to do something.<br /> <br /> I barge into the room, interrupting Angelique and Malard. She has her hand on the front of his pants and he has a lovestruck leer on his face that makes him look like a creepy old man. Angelique glances angrily at me, but if that were enough to intimidate me, I wouldn\u2019t be standing here.<br /> <br /> \u201cUmm\u2026Mr. Malard, sir,\u201d I say, reverting back to my country girl roots in the hopes he\u2019ll find it charming, \u201cI think Alexia wanted your opinion on those cake pops. And, uh\u2026we had something we kinda wanted to ask you about, if you don\u2019t mind. Also, I\u2019d like to have a word in private with Angelique, if it\u2019s okay with you, sir.\u201d<br /> <br /> Mr. Malard seems to snap out of a daze momentarily, and then Sara calls out something about the cake pops being darn good. He seems hesitant, but then Angelique waves him away.<br /> <br /> \u201cStay close,\u201d she says. \u201cAnd attend to me if I call.\u201d Malard nods as though he\u2019s in a trance and wanders back into the other room.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought I told you to leave me alone,\u201d Angelique whispers venomously as she turns to me. I do my best to look hurt.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, but\u2026I was worried about you. I really wanted to see you.\u201d I reach out to take her hand but she pulls away.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think that\u2019s a good idea. I have things to attend to. My studies of the Balehound\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey can wait. I want to talk to you. In private,\u201d I say suggestively. Angelique\u2019s expression wavers and I think I\u2019m getting through to her. I move closer.<br /> <br /> <i>Look at yourself. You\u2019re acting like a whore.</i><br /> <br /> The Grasping Huntress\u2019 accusation almost ruins my whole act.<br /> <br /> <i>This krewe has been a bad influence on you. You NEVER would have prostituted yourself like this before you met Sara and Natalie.<br /> </i><br /> A part of me knows she\u2019s right and wonders what the heck I\u2019m doing here. But it seems to be working. Angelique, or whatever is controlling her, seems confused. And besides, I\u2019m not trying to seduce her. Well, I guess I AM, but I\u2019m not actually trying to get her in bed. Just away from Malard\u2019s conversation with the others.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think talking in private is a good idea,\u201d she says.<br /> <br /> I move closer, our faces mere inches apart.<br /> <br /> \u201cPlease,\u201d I whisper, and with that single word, all of Angelique\u2019s inhibitions evaporate. I\u2019m not sure if that\u2019s a good thing or bad thing.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, the hell with it,\u201d she says, and as she touches me a wave of profound pleasure floods my body. I can barely keep my feet, much less keep track of what\u2019s going on around me as she whisks me to her room upstairs and seduces the heck out of me. I\u2019m not even sure how things go so turned around, but this has got to be the most intense sex I\u2019ve ever had. I think the Huntress is screaming at me, but her voice is just a far off echo.<br /> <br /> The next thing I know, Alexia is bursting into the room. She points at Angelique and tells her to stop and get off me. Angelique growls, a low, feral sound, and transforms into her dire wolf form to escape. I\u2019m still too out of it to do much other than pull the sheets around me, but Alexia is quick and clever. She sprouts extra arms and then pounces on Angelique, pinning her until Angelique passes out and transforms back into her human form.<br /> <br /> \u201cGet dressed! Malard\u2019s coming!\u201d Alexia commands as she snatches the sheets from me and uses them to wrap Angelique.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh shit!\u201d I exclaim as I roll out of bed and collapse. I\u2019m finding it hard to stand, but somehow manage to struggle into my underwear. I\u2019m halfway into my jeans when Sara arrives and helps me finish getting dressed. I\u2019m still sort of dazed, and when I tell her, with some embarrassment, that I just said a bad word, Sara laughs.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not going to let you live that down, you know,\u201d she says.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t really have time to get all the flyaway locks back into my ponytail, but I\u2019m more-or-less presentable by the time Malard thunders into the room. Fortunately, he\u2019s way too worried about Angelique to notice me. Thanks to my \u201cdistraction,\u201d the others managed to explain the situation to him, so he\u2019s on board. His pack is going to meet us at the ritual site, where I hope Doc and Noriko have the ceremony ready to go.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I\u2019m in no shape to drive to the ritual site, so Sara takes the wheel of my jeep. On the way, she prods me a bit, trying to get me to tell her what bad word I said. She keeps trying to guess, and her guesses make me blush several times. I don\u2019t even know what some of them mean. But I manage to hold out against her interrogation.<br /> <br /> I guess I shouldn\u2019t be so shy about profanity. I don\u2019t really care when other people use it. I don\u2019t know why I\u2019m averse to using it myself. I\u2019d say it was because of how I was raised, but my parents also taught me that murder was bad, and look at me now.<br /> <br /> Anyway, between Sara\u2019s good-natured ribbing and the bracing drive out into the woods, by the time we arrive, I\u2019m pretty much myself again.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> As soon as Doc begins the ritual and touches silver to Angelique\u2019s flesh, she awakens and begins thrashing and screaming. It breaks my heart, and I can barely watch. I would help restrain her, but the rest of her pack is here, and they seem to have it well in hand. It\u2019s better to let them handle it. So instead, I stand by as a little more than an observer, huddled under a blanket with Sara and Natalie in the cold November chill.<br /> <br /> As much as seeing Angelique in pain breaks my heart, I think it breaks Doc\u2019s more. He may be grouchy and angry, but he cares about people, and he doesn\u2019t like seeing them hurt, especially when he\u2019s the one inflicting the pain. The fact that it\u2019s necessary doesn\u2019t make it any more palatable. I\u2019d say something reassuring, but somehow I feel like this is all partly my fault even though I know it isn\u2019t, and I\u2019m worried Doc would just lash out at me. I mean, rationally I know that\u2019s not true, but I guess it\u2019s better to let Natalie and Noriko comfort Doc. Besides, a few comforting words aren\u2019t going to help.<br /> <br /> Once the ritual is done, I kneel down to make sure Angelique\u2019s okay. She\u2019s exhausted and trembling, but the look in her eyes tells me that it\u2019s really her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI feel better, \u201c she pants. \u201cIt\u2019s gone. Her presence is gone. I\u2019m free.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you going to be okay?\u201d I ask.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes,\u201d she nods. \u201cBut I\u2019m about to collapse. I need\u2026I need rest.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMalard will get you home. You rest there as long as you need to.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Alice. I\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s okay,\u201d I interrupt. \u201cYou just rest now. Put it all behind you. I\u2019ll see you soon.\u201d<br /> <br /> I realize as I see Angelique go that my words were referring to more than just her struggle with her demonic patron. I think I was also trying, in some way, to tell her that it\u2019s over between us, that now that she\u2019s free, she doesn\u2019t really need me anymore. Or maybe that\u2019s all in my imagination. Either way, I\u2019ll need to break things off with her soon, and I\u2019m not looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 18th 2010<br /> <br /> -Okay, operation please goddess let this work underway.<br /> <br /> -So far, so good.<br /> <br /> -Oh dear.<br /> <br /> -Alexia, not Sara.<br /> <br /> -hrm.<br /> <br /> -Tune in, turn on, drop out.<br /> <br /> -Okay, problem solved. I think.<br /> <br /> -Next step: The Ritual.<br /> <br /> -Cold<br /> <br /> -co;f<br /> <br /> -Cold Cold<br /> <br /> -Cold Cold Cold Cold<br /> <br /> -CoLD<br /> <br /> -It\u2019s cold enough to freeze your Winnebago.<br /> <br /> -@NAREK nlm<br /> <br /> -Thanks Karen. (Bitch)<br /> <br /> -SERIOUSLY COLD<br /> <br /> -How long have we been out here? Am I still alive?<br /> <br /> -vp;d<br /> <br /> -I am just going outside and may be some time.<br /> <br /> -COLD. Seriously.<br /> <br /> -I think one of my parts fell off.<br /> <br /> -These woods are lovely, dark and deep<br /> <br /> -But I have promises to keep<br /> <br /> -And miles to go before I sleep<br /> <br /> -And miles to go before I sleep.<br /> <br /> -Done yet?<br /> <br /> -Okay, next stage?<br /> <br /> -I think two of my parts fell off. Sara will be disappoint.<br /> <br /> -Nah she and Alice are keeping me warm.<br /> <br /> -We are a strawberry scented cute roll up!<br /> <br /> -Which is cold.<br /> <br /> -THANK PERSEPHONE WE ARE DONE<br /> <br /> -Er, I mean, good work Doc!<br /> <br /> -^_^<br /> <br /> -yes sweet heating<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity jog.<br /> <br /> -VENGANCE! HEHEHEHEHEHEHE!<br /> <br /> -Hot tub time.<br /> <br /> -Cold night. Warm bed. Happy Natalie.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Natalie and Alice are not fond of cold.<br /> <br /> So the Willpower drain on Stillness Boneyard is potent. That is what put Angelique down. I wound up HRing that it had a cost of two Plasm and could not be used on the same subject repeatedly, as it was far too potent otherwise. Also restricting it to living subjects. Because it straight put a Werewolf on her ass.<br /> <br /> Obviously some of the systems for Balehound stuff came from <i>Blasphemies</i> and <i>Inferno</i>.<br /> <br /> Alexia\u2019s player RPing an \u201cin your face\u201d attitude to the shenanigans was a delight and amused all present.<br /> <br /> I think that is all. Next time tub business, I think. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T13:06:44-07:00","id":613888,"title":"","content":"So, some of the players were talking, and we wondered if people had theories about who was playing which characters in the various WoD games I have up. So I figured we would offer a chance at discussion of it. In order to protect identities of players, I have not been in a habit of confirming links between players between games. But if you are curious and follow more than one game you can ask. Anything else you ask about will be up to the players if they want to answer. But I will confirm or deny common links between characters if you ask.<br /> <br /> Some facts<br /> <br /> In the four New WoD and one Classic WoD games there are 13 different players. 2 are/were in all five games. 1 is in four games, 4 are in three games, and 6 are only in one game each, at least of WoD games.<br /> <br /> I\u2019d rather you be nice\u2026I don\u2019t want to hear \u201cI think player A plays X and Y because they suck\u201d or anything, I am proud of my players. A number of them will be peering in to enjoy this too.<br /> <br /> Anyway, if you have any theories I would enjoy hearing them!<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-09T15:14:12-07:00","id":621658,"title":"","content":"So I have good news and bad news, Geist fans. The good news is Simon Fishborn\u2019s player returned this session to play Simon once again. That bad news is it is an extinction surge; as I post this Simon\u2019s player is no longer living in the area. But show he did, and was there for the end of the Mariah storyline. Let\u2019s go.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0800 Hours, Friday, November 19, 2010<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll give it to the heavy bag. It lasted a good long time last night. I did stop before I had to wrap it with tape. The girls were done with the hot tub for at least an hour when I finished. It was a great workout though. I feel more loose than I have in a while. I also noticed that I have more power in my strikes than I did while I was in the Navy. I took a shower as I was soaked then slipped into bed with Noriko. She immediately slid against me in her sleep. I drifted off feeling more like myself.<br /> <br /> I woke up at 0700 Hours this morning and found my center easily in about half an hour. Then I did a few katas to keep loose and remind my muscles that they are supposed to have memory. I think I\u2019m going to keep stretching until it\u2019s time for breakfast. If we have to do any real travelling, it will be good not to be stiff before I get there.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1030 Hours, Friday, November 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Well this is going to be an interesting Friday.<br /> <br /> Snowflake has been mostly keeping to himself lately, so it was a big deal when he came down for breakfast. Rose apparently chastised him for being antisocial or something. Over a large spread and one of my maps, we discussed our plans for the day. Mariah\u2019s tub is in a little bedroom town near York, Maine. A Sikh family unknowingly (we hope) lives above a terrible relic of death roughly three hours away. Axe invited Eris, Chandra is coming and so is Snowflake. In fact, we\u2019re taking his Fleetwood and the van just to handle all the people. Just to be safe, we\u2019re all packing an overnight. Just in case and because he still feels he has a debit to pay, I packed Troy. I think the cars are about ready so I\u2019m gonna leave off here.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1400 Hours, Friday, November 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that was an interesting trip. We wired the bluetooth to work like an intercom between the two cars. Chandra and Cupcake rode with Snowflake. Everyone else camped out in the van. I think I will probably need to completely restock the mini bar by the time we get back. So much cognac. But I may never get the smell out from that swill Axe calls beer. Axe almost caused Eris to have a panic attack along the way but offering to take her to the mall. Turns out, Eris had an \u201cincident\u201d in the mall back in New Haven involving a wishing well, public nudity, and mall security. We arrived about 1330 Hours and located our target before taking up positions in less obvious locations. Snowflake helped with that by wrapping my van in a illusion of the Total Electric company. His Fleetwood was parked a little farther away where he and Chandra \u201clooked at a map.\u201d Bright Eyes and I put on enough of an approximation of work clothes to pass as meter checkers.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re going to find out just much of this is a cover and how much is actually a secret.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1800 Hours, Friday, November 19, 2010<br /> <br /> Nightshade and Cupcake went to the door and served as distraction and backup to Snowflake\u2019s surveillance. We had to make an assumption that the family would not be home given the usual professions of the average Sikh. I hate making those kinds of generalizations, but most of the Sikhs I\u2019ve ever known were white collar if they weren\u2019t in the military. A caucasian woman answered the door. She was the housekeeper and was a little confused as she didn\u2019t know anything about any checks scheduled for this afternoon. We were moving around the side of the building when Nightshade began talking and I saw how she was shifting posture before we hit the corner. That poor woman had no idea what was coming. Axe found several trapped steps on the secret staircase so we knew to miss those. Once the house was clear, Bright Eyes and Noriko slipped in. I heard some issue over the ear curls and Bright Eyes came to get me &amp; Eris. We had to move carefully to dodge the traps, but even still I stopped short when I hit the basement.<br /> <br /> There were chains hanging everywhere, channels and drains in the floor, with pipes and tubes overhead, all leading to an old clawfoot tub at the center of the room. Inside, there was a thing made of congealing blood. It almost looked like a body, but not quite yet. Axe and Noriko were already covered in gore as apparently another blood simulacrum attacked. They finished it off while Bright Eyes ran for help. I sat against the wall and the Dog of War stood up as my Phantasmal Shroud wrapped around me. I was not dealing with mind control on top of everything else we expected from Mariah.<br /> <br /> It took all of us using everything we had to finally shatter that damn tub. Even with the vicious claws the Dog has, I only managed to crack it once. The sniper rifle probably could have handled it, but we were already pushing the bounds of a stealth mission. Once the clawfoot shattered, the blood form inside exploded. There was a shriek that seemed to come from outside, but that doesn\u2019t seem right now that I\u2019m thinking about it. Maybe it was going somewhere else. I just know that everyone hurt it so it wasn\u2019t a trick of Twilight. I gathered up the pieces of the tub because I\u2019m sure I can use them as reagents for something. The sheer power they helped create and absorbed means they will be useful someday. I tried to get some paper towels upstairs to clean up, but Nightshade rushed us back to the van. She might have pushed me to get the others moving, but she would have had to touch me. As bloody as I was, that wasn\u2019t going to happen. She, Chandra, and Cupcake rode back with Snowflake, while everyone else piled into the van. Once we were moving, Nightshade pointed out how likely the police were once the housekeeper thought about her situation very much at all.<br /> <br /> Now we\u2019re back and I\u2019m so glad we designed the interior of the van to be hose-friendly. Snowflake stopped for Fribbles so after showers, everyone will be happy.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, that\u2019s that and that is good. The blood magic cult leader is dealt with once and for all. Her focus is destroyed and her soul returned to the cycle, properly. And nobody even got hurt, except maybe the housekeeper\u2019s peace of mind. The aftermath wasn\u2019t pleasant - a three hour car ride covered in blood used in evil rituals is far from that and Alice\u2019s glee in the \u2018kill\u2019 is somewhat disconcerting, but we got hot showers , Fribbles and the satisfaction of saving people when we got home, so it all balances out.<br /> <br /> The three hour car ride up to Maine was much more fun. We had to take two cars because there were so many of us - all of the Death Touched (even Simon!), plus Chandra, Eris and Noriko. That made 9, which not even the van can hold comfortably, so Simon drove as well. We had phones set up so that we could chat though.<br /> <br /> I might have ridden with Simon, since he\u2019s been a bit reclusive of late, so it was a treat to have him with us, but Eris was new and exciting (and she and Alice are just adorable to watch) so I was in the van. Eris is an intriguing woman, and I know I\u2019m not the only one looking forward to our upcoming shopping trip, for many reasons. It seems Eris\u2019 (soon to be frequently occupied by Alice) living space is a little spartan and they wanna spruce it up a bit. A worthy project, even if we might have to avoid the mall. It seems there was an issue with Eris and the wishing fountain, back near the earliest regions of her memory.<br /> <br /> However, the best part of the ride was when Alice pretended like she thought I knew what shame was. The well stocked minibar in the van *may* have had something to do with it, but even so... an opportunity to volunteer to strip for a van full of seriously hot people? I was on that shit. See, Natalie was explaining how she kept her house in Malibu warm enough you could not wear clothes and still be comfortable, so Doc offered to keep the van that warm. So, clearly, he started it. To be fair, it sounded like an entirely perfect plan to me, and I was the only one that moved to take their shirt off...<br /> <br /> Anyway, all that was fun, so the three hours went by fast. We were in Maine in no time it seemed like., and pulled into the nice suburban neighborhood around 1:30. We were posing as electricians to explain the van and the loitering. We debated between that and exterminators, but apparently electricians are more metal, so there it was. Simon handled that. He\u2019s got a talent for illusions. I told you about his proposal, right? To have him for a show... that\u2019d be amazing. Anyway, it was very handy since we didn\u2019t have time to get decals made or anything.<br /> <br /> The ruse got us past the housekeeper, the only one there, without problems, though Natalie could make any cover story believable. And distracting. I was lucky I only heard her over the ear curls. If I\u2019d been hanging out with them, I\u2019m sure *I\u2019d* have been very distracted. As it was, I followed Alice down the stairs to the hidden basement to find the cult leader\u2019s focus.<br /> <br /> It was a disturbing place, with blood channels and reservoirs, chains and hooks, and a larval? pupaed? semblance of an adult human. And a mystical guardian, that I was utterly useless against, but Alice took down handily while I went for Eris. The focus was more durable than a bathtub had any right to be, but some concerted effort had it in pieces in not too long.<br /> <br /> All our efforts left us covered in blood, except for Natalie and Alexia, who were distracting the poor housekeeper, Simon, who was using illusions to mask us, and Chandra, who was guarding Simon. So they were the four in the car on the way back, while the van is going to need a damn good steam cleaning. After three hours, a shower was more than welcome, even if I did have to take it alone. Natalie took a shower at the mere thought of other people being dirty and Alice\u2019s shower doesn\u2019t fit three, not that that information was at all pertinent. Still, Simon got Fribbles for everyone, so I suppose I\u2019ll live.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> We\u2019re heading to Maine, but we had to take two cars. Even Simon came along this time, which is a nice surprise. He\u2019s in the other car with Alexia and Chandra. The rest of us are in Doc\u2019s van.<br /> <br /> The drive to Maine doesn\u2019t seem so long with Eris at my side. It was Natalie\u2019s suggestion that she join us, and I\u2019m glad she\u2019s here. She\u2019s excited and nervous and beautiful. I slide my arm around her waist and she reflexively leans against me. Sara, Natalie and Noriko are taking the opportunity to get to know her better as we chat. It turns out this is the first time Noriko has met her when she wasn\u2019t a wolf, but the two of them seem friendly enough, which is a huge relief. It\u2019s good when your girlfriend gets along with your best friends.<br /> <br /> Eventually, I ask her about shopping.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Eris,\u201d I begin, \u201cyou said before that you wanted me to help decorate your room a bit, right? And you also need more clothes. I mean, you\u2019ve only got what, two or three outfits aside from your park ranger uniforms?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris fixes me with her big, exotic eyes and nods.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I was thinking we could go shopping tomorrow or the next day.\u201d Eris\u2019 eyes widen and she tenses up. I can sense the now-familiar signs of panic rising in her. \u201cYou don\u2019t need to worry about money,\u201d I add quickly. \u201cThe krewe will cover it. But I\u2019m probably going to be spending a lot more time at your place now that we\u2019re together, I thought it would be nice to sort of make the place more cozy. So, what do you think? Are you up for it?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris is still anxious. I don\u2019t think money was the issue.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know,\u201d she says. \u201cIt might go all wrong again. I don\u2019t want to mess it up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are you talking about?\u201d I ask. \u201cI\u2019ll be right there with you. You\u2019ll be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut when I went to the mall with Deirdre I got in trouble. I saw money in the fountain and tried to get it because someone just left it there. And I didn\u2019t want to get my clothes wet, so I took them off.\u201d<br /> <br /> I pause, mouth open in mid-response as I process this. Sara and Natalie have bemused smiles on their faces, which doesn\u2019t help.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut\u2026you know better now, right? The money in the fountain represents people\u2019s wishes, and if you take it, their wishes might not come true. And, more importantly, you know you can\u2019t just take off your clothes in public places, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris nods. \u201cBut I\u2019m scared to go shopping. I don\u2019t want to make a mistake again and mess it up. Deirdre was mad. And the mall people won\u2019t let me go back there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t worry. I\u2019ll be right there with you. Just stick with me and you\u2019ll be fine. There are plenty of places to shop outside of the mall, I promise. It\u2019ll be fun! You\u2019ll see. Natalie and Sara and Noriko will go with us\u2026we\u2019ll have a blast. I promise.\u201d I give Eris a comforting look and a big smile. She still looks a little worried, so I lean in and give her gentle, reassuring kiss. Natalie rolls her eyes in mock disgust, but there\u2019s a fond smile on her lips.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I phase through the secret door and creep down the stairs. The people who own the house are away, and Natalie and Alexia are distracting the housekeeper. Simon and Chandra are outside keeping an eye on things with Simon\u2019s Boneyard, and Eris is prowling around somewhere in her wolf form. Doc is outside, ready to rush in as backup if things go south.<br /> I notice that the stairs are trapped just in time to stop myself from stepping on the wrong ones. Some of them are fake - insulation foam or something painted to look like wood. They are easy enough to avoid once I know what to look for, and I warn the others through the ear curls.<br /> <br /> The door opens behind me as Sara find her way in, and a dark shadow darts between her legs and joins our basement search. As Sara activate her Pyre-Flame and begins to glow, illuminating the macabre chamber at the bottom of the stairs, the shadow resolves itself into a sleek feline form: Noriko. Once she\u2019s downstairs, she shifts into her werecat form.<br /> <br /> Chains hang from the ceiling and basins and tubs rest around the room with channels and pipes leading to a central tub. It\u2019s a large antique piece, and quivering inside it is a half-formed figure, a vaguely humanoid shape made of congealing blood. When I was a girl, my big brothers once rented Invasion of the Body Snatchers, the one with Donald Sutherland in it, and I watched it with them. It terrified me, and I had nightmares for a week. The thing in the tub reminds me of the featureless, half-formed clones in that movie, and it evokes a similar sense of terror.<br /> <br /> <i>Let the terror fuel your fire. This is our kill. We\u2019ve worked for it. The hunt has been good, but when we struck her head from her neck, it did not satiate us, did it? No\u2026because we knew she wasn\u2019t truly dead. But there she is. She is ours, and we must end her!</i><br /> <br /> I find it hard to argue with the Huntress this time. I heft my axe and prepare to go to work on tub, but then there is a loud sloshing sound and a feminine figure made of boiling blood rises from a grate in the floor. It throws a spray of searing hot blood at us and I try to block it from hitting Sara and Noriko, who both recoil. The blood spatters against me but my Shroud protects me.<br /> <br /> Noriko and Sara both back away. They can\u2019t really attack the blood simulacrum without burning themselves. I step froward, getting in its face and keeping its attention on me. It lashes out again as I shift my Caul and my Shroud. Bitterly cold winds wrap around me and I strike the thing with an elbow, shoving it back and freezing its arm. It recoils, but I don\u2019t let up. Then a dark figure with long, blade-like claws and a sinister-looking top hat emerges from the shadows. At first, I think it\u2019s another one of Moriah\u2019s defenses, but then Simon mutters something about helping out, and I realize that it\u2019s just one of his illusions. All the same, it seems perfectly capable of hurting the blood-beast. Sara goes to get help, but by the time Doc and Eris arrive, Simon and I have turned the blood-beast into an icy red statue.<br /> <br /> We waste no time destroying the tub before the blood-beast thaws out. A blaring alarm sounds form the house above, masking the horrendous racket we make as we smash the tub into pieces. Sounds like Simon\u2019s got our back again. He should join us in the field more often, but I guess he doesn\u2019t like leaving the mansion any more than he has to.<br /> <br /> I hammer on the tub with my axe and manage to put a few big cracks in it. Doc assumes his Phantasmal form and lays into it with beastly claws. Eris tries to claw at it, but as a wolf, there\u2019s not much she can do. Like me, Noriko senses a kill, and Moriah is a worthy victim for her too. She needs the kill as much as I do, maybe more.<br /> <br /> <i>But she cannot have it! Moriah is our kill. WE stalked her. WE hunted her. WE struck her head from her shoulders. WE should be the ones to end this!</i><br /> <br /> I strike harder with my axe, aiming to strike the blow that destroys the tub and ends Moriah once and for all before Noriko or Doc can do it.<br /> <br /> Then Noriko\u2019s ferocity peaks and she cleaves through the cracks in the tub with her razor claw claws. There is a resounding crack as the tub shatters, and the thing in the tub explodes in a spray of blood. The frozen simulacrum shatters.<br /> <br /> For a moment, I\u2019m stunned. And for a moment, anger surges inside of me. Noriko stole my kill! The Huntress is seething and her rage flickers through me.<br /> <br /> Then the anger evaporates. I\u2019m not the Huntress. It doesn\u2019t matter who struck the killing blow. What\u2019s important is that Moriah is dead. She was the krewe\u2019s kill. The hunt was worthy and just, and I did my job as the Middle Shadows\u2019 Reaper. A sense of triumph settles over me.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> The drive back to New Haven feels a lot longer than the drive to Maine. Those of us in the van are covered in blood. I\u2019m used to it. It comes with the job. But I\u2019m not happy about it, and I\u2019ll be glad to get home and have a shower. Maybe Eris will join me.<br /> <br /> Blood aside, though, I feel good. There\u2019s a certain satisfaction that comes from a just kill, but it\u2019s more than that. This time, my target really did deserve to die. This is the first kill I\u2019ve had in a long time that felt right. The fact that the Huntress is still in a stew about Noriko just makes it even better.<br /> <br /> Sara keeps looking at me with a hint of worry in her eyes. I don\u2019t think she cares for the sense of satisfaction I\u2019m feeling right now, but she doesn\u2019t really understand. She probably thinks I\u2019m caught up in the afterglow of the kill like a junkie getting a fix. And I guess she\u2019s not entirely wrong, which, I confess, scares me a little. But honestly, the real reason this feels so good is that for the first time in ages, I really feel like I\u2019m back on the track. Like I\u2019ve found my footing again.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 19th 2010<br /> <br /> --Early<br /> <br /> -Simon at Breakfast. Hi Simon.<br /> <br /> -How can people talk and smile this early?<br /> <br /> -Those who are somewhat more accepting of their own filth need to make accommodations for those who want to be clean. Just because it is normal does not mean it is not gross.<br /> <br /> -Oh wow is Simon going with us?<br /> <br /> -He is!<br /> <br /> -Crap, need to be a good Yenta and be sure Eris is ready for a call.<br /> <br /> -Yenta Yenta<br /> <br /> -My good deed for the day is done.<br /> <br /> -I can go back to sleep.<br /> <br /> -Sleeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeep.<br /> <br /> -No sleep till\u2026Maine?<br /> <br /> -That is farther than Brooklyn.<br /> <br /> -Time to sing in the car!<br /> <br /> -Skinnamarinky dinky dink Skinnamarinky do...<br /> <br /> -Hey Sara is on MY SIDE<br /> <br /> -WOAH that definitely qualifies as my side.<br /> <br /> -hrgurflloortamaz<br /> <br /> -Alice and Eris are cool.<br /> <br /> -Hmmm those names sound too similar.<br /> <br /> -They risk becoming the dreaded cutsie lesbians.<br /> <br /> -Dreaded, I tell you.<br /> <br /> -Being an electrician seems to be more metal than being a plumber, I suppose.<br /> <br /> -POP QUIZ: Which is more metal, an electrician or plumber?<br /> <br /> -I never liked Massachusetts.<br /> <br /> -I mean it is almost like a cool place, I guess, except cold. And less cool.<br /> <br /> -I mean, it is not Delaware.<br /> <br /> -But where is?<br /> <br /> -Delaware, that\u2019s where.<br /> <br /> -I honestly don\u2019t even know where we are any more.<br /> <br /> -Haberdasher is metal just based on the name.<br /> <br /> -Um, no stripping zone!<br /> <br /> -At site, radio silence while I do some important work.<br /> <br /> -On the way back<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is in the non-messy car.<br /> <br /> -Computer repair is totally metal.<br /> <br /> -Pizza Deliveryman is many things, but not metal.<br /> <br /> -How does anyone, anywhere, not know who the Pixies are?<br /> <br /> -Fribbles make everything better.<br /> <br /> -Fribbles can be metal.<br /> <br /> -I guess how metal singing telegrams are depends on what is being sung.<br /> <br /> -Home again home again jiggity-jogg.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXXXVIII</i><br /> <br /> I noted previously Simon\u2019s player took a hiatus to work on his degree. He earned it, but never quite returned to the social circle. He has recently, but it has accompanied his getting a nice job out of state. He was kind enough to come by for a last session, which did not necessarily resolve Simon, but let him say goodbye to the character and enjoy the defeat of a major villain. Needless to say, we did a lot of catching up which lead to a somewhat shorter session.<br /> <br /> Natalie sledgehammered the poor housekeeper socially even without her powers. Meanwhile everyone finding the secret door and sneaking in was funny. There were some troubles slipping inside. Also funny was Eris and Noriko meeting in human form face to face.<br /> <br /> If you read this and other game journals, note the comments above about guessing about common players. We are curious what you think. Though comments and questions of other sorts are welcome as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-24T22:37:33-07:00","id":638819,"title":"","content":"Hey folks, I am running behind but I do have journals for the last Geist game. After that last big storyline had a quiet roleplaying session, leading into our next\u2026set of events.<br /> <br /> Fear the Turkey Day!<br /> <i><br /> Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log<br /> </b><br /> Meditation is becoming consistently more simple. I\u2019m not sure what snapped into place, but it\u2019s like my mind has developed something akin to muscle memory when it comes to finding my center. Since today was the big shopping trip, I moved from meditation straight to stretches and then katas.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t know how long everyone will be gone, so I\u2019m going to take the opportunity to really focus on my martial arts for a while.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1600 Hours, Saturday, November 20, 2010<br /> <br /> That was terrifying and insightful.<br /> <br /> Noriko came to me after the Great Shopping Trip 2010, and informed me that she is going to talk to Malard about Eris. They got back around 1300 Hours so I was still sweaty and practicing. Noriko\u2019s plans easily broke my concentration however. She reminded me that I could give her luck, then went to talk with Cupcake about cookies. I quickly scrambled to gather some pictures of Nightshade. If anyone was a useful image to illustrate persuasion, she was it. Once I gave Noriko as much of a blessing as I could bestow, I jumped in the shower. No way in Hell was I sending her over there alone for this. Noriko was dressed so adorably, it was like someone packaged a four year old in an adult, without being creepy. It\u2019s hard to describe but she must have distilled cute somehow. Anyway, we left with cookies courtesy of Cupcake after Axe left to redecorate Eris\u2019 place. She claimed not to be a U-haul Lesbian, but...whatever.<br /> <br /> After the required warning shot, Malard welcomed us inside. Taking the cookies, he led us into the den. I was going to be helpful and offered to check on Angelique as a medic. Malard informed us that she was being evaluated by someone that was not him and therefore not here at present. Given what we knew had happened, I thought that was fair. After that, I basically sat back and watched Noriko, whose accent was significantly thicker than usual, lay out a point for point argument for allowing Eris into his territory. A major point was that Lily would be leaving soon, and therefore no longer a threat. Noriko referred to her as something called a Host. It sounded more involved than just a possession issue. I had to guess that it had something to do with the spider spirit Malard warned us about when Lily came to live with us. While Noriko can always be persuasive, between the Luck magic, whatever planning she had put into this, and her absolutely disarming adorability, Malard completely agreed. The only \u201ccatch\u201d was that Eris had to respect his territory and bring him what I interrupted as tribute kills. Hunting trophies as an acknowledgement of sovereignty? I understood but spelling it out in English is harder without a strong understanding of werewolf politics. With that agreed, Noriko gave him a very sweet hug and we came home.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to wonder around the local tattoo parlors to see what the level of competition is and if I can get any ideas for making my operation better before it takes off. Nightshade calls what I\u2019m planning trolling, but I\u2019m not sure what that means.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Sunday, November 21, 2010<br /> <br /> Holy shit it\u2019s almost Thanksgiving!<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t stay out too late last night so I was up by 0700 this morning. Meditation was a breezy half hour before I headed down for breakfast. Because it would be a while before everyone was up and around, I went back to work on my katas. Around 1100 Hours, Nightshade and company resurfaced and announced that Thanksgiving was coming. Talk soon turned to bringing Bella Donna and Matron X up for the holidays. Noriko blurted out almost on cue that she hasn\u2019t told her mom that I\u2019m not Japanese. I was surprised by all these revelations. Then the conversation turned to family in general as Nightshade because obviously nervous about Matron X coming. This is always a touchy situation. Chandra and Cupcake aren\u2019t on speaking terms with their family, one for trying to destroy her, the other for disowning a non-vegan child respectively. Snowflake, Tavia, and Karl add a 4th dimension to any family discussion. It occurred to me again that I hadn\u2019t talked to Mom in months, which made my stomach tighten. Rose is in semi-regular contact with her dad again. Even Axe mentioned wanting to call her youngest older brother. He apparently is the only one that she has come out to. Jacob I think was his name. I noticed that Bright Eyes was unusually quiet for all this. I made a conscious decision that this is one of those times I should observe and not comment.<br /> <br /> At some point, the reminiscing turned to how we were (or weren\u2019t) connected to Death before the Bargain. This sparked Nightshade to remind folks about Bella Donna\u2019s \u201cability\u201d around mirrors, but that maybe Matron X didn\u2019t need the mirror. Nightshade believes that Matron X knew when she died without seeing her or even being on the same side of the country when it happened. The mood lightened(?) somewhat as Nightshade had to remind (demand) Bright Eyes not try to seduce Matron X.<br /> <br /> I need to call Mom and see what she\u2019s doing.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> A long day of shopping capped off with a night of dancing with Karen is just what the doctor ordered to recover from a day trip to Maine to deal with evil magic. In fact, a week(ish) of relaxing and making Thanksgiving preparations sounds like just the thing. Especially since Noriko got Mr. Malard to agree to giving Eris permission to visit (it\u2019s the weird family rivalry/territoriality thing), so Alice and Eris will be doing some of that relaxing over here.<br /> <br /> If we can pull them away from Eris\u2019 newly decorated digs, that is. The shopping trip was a resounding success. We stopped at Hot Topic first, of course. Natalie was involved, after all. But we wound up going the length of the mall, to an f.y.e., a little poster kiosk and REI, to name a few. All in all, she came out with a number of cute, loose fitting outfits in dark earth tones that complemented her coloring nicely, a stereo (I had to rescue them from Natalie\u2019s sharing of her expertise on speaker quality), some non-Ranger hiking equipment and a few things to liven up her room. We\u2019d figured out the night before that Eris\u2019 preferred music was electronica and techno, specifically with a heavy beat, but not such that she was too into band/album posters. That was fine though - she gravitated quickly towards the nature photographs, especially the night sky shots. The best catch of the day, in my opinion, was a very beautiful shot of the Arizona night sky, including one of the famous mesas our Little Red had actually climbed. The bamboo lamp Noriko found was a good one too.<br /> <br /> I didn\u2019t come away empty handed myself. I hadn\u2019t really intended on joining in on the purchasing things part of shopping, as there\u2019s not much I\u2019m in need of, but when we went by the REI, I got some proper hiking gear, and Alice picked up some appropriate climbing gear for the troupe. I am looking forward to trying that. I\u2019m sure it will be exhilarating(ly terrifying).<br /> <br /> But we\u2019re home now, and soon me and Karen are gonna leave for a night out at the 27 Club. Natalie will be going to a party as Deanna\u2019s date instead. I\u2019m sure that\u2019ll be fun and good for Deanna - I get the idea she\u2019s played second fiddle to Clarissa a lot, and having the prettiest girl in the room on her arm will surely be a pleasant change from that.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Not really much new on my end, just feeling a little homesick really. We\u2019ve been making Thanksgiving plans and between prodding Natalie to invite her mom and young Natalie (Alice was adorably awkward with her reaction to learning Natalie has a daughter), Alice\u2019s worries about coming out to her parents, Noriko\u2019s surety that her mom will begin wedding planning whenever she arrives in town, and Alexia\u2019s bitterness at the way her parents disowned her for not being vegan, I\u2019ve been feeling the absence of Dad and Grandma. And all you folks too. I don\u2019t suppose the troupe\u2019s off track and in New England, huh? :-)<br /> <br /> It sounds like it\u2019s gonna be a good Thanksgiving anyway. Even with just us (and girlfriends) we make a good crowd, and Natalie is still considering calling her family over, Doc\u2019s gonna call his mom, and Alice wound up inviting Jacob, the younger of her older brothers, the only one in her family who knows she\u2019s gay. So it\u2019ll be a party, full of people I love, who love me, and new people to meet. I wonder if Alice\u2019s brother is single...<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> I place the bamboo wood lamp on Eris\u2019 nightstand and Eris plugs it in. I twist the switch and the lamp\u2019s light filters through its off-white shade to fill the room with a soft, warm glow. Just so that we can really enjoy it, I step over to the door and turn off the overhead light. The room descends into a cozy half-light. Eris smiles.<br /> <br /> I sit down on the edge of the bed and Eris settles in next to me. We sit there in silence for several long moments as we look around the room and its new decorations, all things we picked up on our shopping trip today. A dark, marine blue hairbrush and matching hand mirror sit on the nightstand next to the lamp, and a deep forest green throw is draped haphazardly over the back of Eris\u2019 big, fluffy chair. A pile of climbing gear rests in the corner underneath a poster of a cool forest waterfall. The closet door is open, showing off almost a dozen new outfits for Eris as well as a few changes of my own clothes. There\u2019s even a brand new stereo and a small rack of CDs on the dresser. It turns out Eris likes electronic music, so we found her something to listen to along with a couple of my favorite albums.<br /> <br /> Our eyes settle on the big, framed photo print hanging on the wall next to the bed. It\u2019s a gorgeous shot of the Arizona desert at night, and it must have been taken during a meteor shower because a couple of shooting stars streak across the rich black sky. I recognize the place. I\u2019ve climbed those mesas. I\u2019ve stood atop them under the blazing desert sun and breathed in the warm, dry air. Maybe someday Eris and I will climb them together. Right now, though, all that matters is that we've made this room hers. Sure, she already lived here, but until today, she hadn't really made it her own.<br /> <br /> As if sensing my thoughts, Eris reaches out and takes my hand. Then she turns and looks at me, nuzzles my neck with her nose and a moment later we\u2019re all kisses and questing hands. But then I stop.<br /> <br /> \u201cHold on,\u201d I say. Eris frowns and looks disappointed. \u201cDon\u2019t worry,\u201d I continue with a mischievous smile, \u201cwe\u2019ll get right back to it. But first\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> I move to the stereo and select a CD, a mix of hair metal tracks that I made for myself ages ago. I\u2019m almost embarrassed to put it on. Hair metal isn\u2019t my normal fare. I\u2019d rather listen to classic, real metal like Testament and Judas Priest or melodic death metal like Children of Bodom. But I can\u2019t deny that I have a soft spot for Def Leppard and Motley Crue, especially their ballads. I guess they touch that sappy, romantic side of me that I don't really acknowledge that often.<br /> <br /> As Def Leppard's Stand Up starts playing, I slide onto the bed with Eris, and our lovemaking is soft and tender in a way it hasn't been before. I feel warm and peaceful, and for the first time in months, Motley Crue's Without You doesn't make miss Cassidy.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> I hadn't really been planning on calling my brother Jacob, but the krewe was talking about our plans for Thanksgiving this Thursday, and somehow he came up. It all made me a feel a little homesick, so I've decided to call and see if he happens to be in the area. After all, he's a long haul truck driver, and sometimes his routes bring him to New England. If he's close, maybe he can join us for Thanksgiving.<br /> <br /> Of all the members of my family, I'm probably closest to Jacob. He's three years older than I am, but he's always looked out for me more than my oldest brother, Ethan. And he's the only member of my family that knows I'm a lesbian. He's cool with it. In fact, he's always been really supportive. He doesn't know anything about me being sin-eater though. And he sure doesn't know that I'm a killer.<br /> <br /> The phone rings three times before Jacob picks up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Freckles!&quot; he says brightly, using the nickname he and Ethan gave me when I was just a kid. &quot;You've been out of touch for a while. What's going on?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Hey Jacob,&quot; I respond warmly. &quot;I've been busy lately, I guess.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Too busy to give me a call?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Look whose talking. When's the last time you called me?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Good point. So how's my kid sister?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm okay. I'm all settled in here in New Haven.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, you said you'd found a place to live. Any work yet?&quot;<br /> <br /> I hesitate, unsure what to say. Jacob's awfully understanding, but what am I supposed to tell him? That I run with a crew of paranormal investigators? Back in Portland, I had a job as a bartender to pay the bills. I don't want to lie to him, but I don't want him to worry about me either. I settle on the truth, or at least as much of it as I can share.<br /> <br /> &quot;Um\u2026not really. I mean, I've done some odd jobs since I got here. But nothing solid. I've still got some money, though, and I'm living with a bunch of friends. One of them owns the house, so I don't have to pay rent or utilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sounds like a good deal. You sure it's legit?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a little weird. But it's good. I mean, the house is big and old. It's like a mansion. The guy who owns it has a lot of money, and I think he just likes having us all around. It's in a good neighborhood. And I'm staying busy. Like I said, lots of odd jobs. There's a state park nearby and I go up there pretty often these days. I'm friends with the park rangers. In fact\u2026I'm dating one of them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah? What's her name?&quot; Jacob sounds honestly pleased to hear that I've bounced back from Cassidy. He still thinks I left Portland because we broke up.<br /> <br /> &quot;Eris.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Weird name.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, and she IS kinda strange. But she's wonderful and I love her.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I'm glad to hear that. Maybe I'll get a chance to meet her someday soon.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Speaking of that,&quot; I seize the opening, &quot;we're having Thanksgiving dinner here on Thursday. It's kind of a big thing, and, well\u2026I was wondering if you were going to be anywhere nearby this week. If you are, I was hoping you could come.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Seriously? I'd love to. And you're in luck. I'm making a delivery in Albany on Wednesday. I was actually kinda bummed out that I wouldn't be able to see Mom and Dad this Thanksgiving, but this is even better. It's short hop from Albany to Connecticut. I can probably be in New Haven sometime Wednesday evening.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Really?&quot; I answer excitedly. I'm sure Jacob can hear the smile in my voice. &quot;You just made my day! I'll text you the address.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I was thinking just the other day that it's been way too long since I've seen my kid sister at any sort of family get-together. This is perfect.&quot; Jacob pauses for a moment. I'm about to say something to break the suddenly awkward silence, but he beats me to it.<br /> <br /> &quot;But you know, Freckles, you really should find your way back to Phoenix sometime. Mom and Dad worry about you. I mean, you've only seen them what, maybe three or four times over the past few years?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know,&quot; I say softly, &quot;it's just tough for me to get away long enough to drive halfway across the country.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Listen, Freckles, I know you better than that. You're avoiding them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What? No I'm not.&quot; Even though I argue, I know Jacob's right.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, you are. And I know why.&quot;<br /> <br /> I experience a brief moment of panic. Jacob can't possibly know about the people I've killed. As far as I know, he doesn't even suspect that I killed Kitty. Does he? When I don't immediately respond, Jacob continues.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's because you're afraid they'll find out that you're into girls, right? You want to come out to them, but you can't bring yourself to do it. So you're avoiding them.&quot;<br /> <br /> I breathe a sigh of relief. Jacob doesn't know about Kitty or any of the other people I've killed. But my relief quickly gives way to a different sort of anxiety. He's right. I'm afraid of coming out to my parents. It may not be the only reason I've been avoiding them, but it's a big part of it. An awkward silence stretches for a few moments as Jacob waits patiently for my response. Finally, I speak.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. That's part of it,&quot; I say.<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I'm not going to push you one way or the other. It's up to you when and how you come out to Mom and Dad. But they miss you. You really ought to go see them.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know,&quot; I say sadly. &quot;Do you think they suspect?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;What, that you're a lesbian?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah. Alexia\u2014she's one of my friends here\u2014swings the same way I do, and she says her parents noticed things about her when she was growing up, so they weren't really surprised when she came out to them. I'm wondering if somewhere, deep down, Mom and Dad sort of know, even if they haven't consciously acknowledged it.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Wow, listen to you, getting all psychological on me!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm serious, Jacob! I'm worried about this!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know, I know. I'm sorry.&quot; He pauses and sighs deeply. &quot;Look, Freckles, I don't know if they suspect anything or not. But you didn't even look twice at any guys in high school, and you talked an awful lot about that girl in your class. What was her name?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Jamie,&quot; I say, filling in the name of my unrequited high school crush.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, Jamie. That's when I started to figure it out. So I don't know. Maybe, subconsciously, they kinda already know. Maybe not. Either way, they love you. And they miss you. It's not right avoiding them like this.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, I know.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Just think about it, okay? Maybe we can drive out to Phoenix together if my delivery schedule lines up right someday soon.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I'd like that,&quot; I say sincerely.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good. Look, I gotta go. But I'll see you Wednesday, okay?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;You bet.&quot;<br /> <br /> We hang up. Somehow, the phone call didn't cure my homesickness.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> -Shopping today<br /> <br /> -Going our with @Nerak, Sara, Alice, Eris, and Noriko<br /> <br /> -Not spending as much time in Hot Topic as anticipated.<br /> <br /> -What the frimple?<br /> <br /> -Poor Eris is overwhelmed.<br /> <br /> -Thomas Kinkade? Seriously Noriko?<br /> <br /> -Who would want the work of that hypocritical boozehound?<br /> <br /> -Bah.<br /> <br /> -Aha boots! Now you speak @Nerak\u2019s language\u2026and mine.<br /> <br /> -Nice nice shopping nice\u2026hmmm\u2026Alice and Eris wandered off again.<br /> <br /> -No wait, everyone wandered off!<br /> <br /> -Okay found them. Good thing too they were lost!<br /> <br /> -Back home! Trip successful!<br /> <br /> -Your Mistress is a date for a party tonight.<br /> <br /> -I have no idea what sort of party.<br /> <br /> -I do know I can fit lingerie into a very small space in my purse, and this phone is getting turned off for the evening. Sleep well. ^_^<br /> <br /> <br /> November 21th 2010<br /> <br /> -I had a wonderful evening and hope you did.<br /> <br /> -Huh, way to go Noriko<br /> <br /> -Planning planning.<br /> <br /> -People don\u2019t want to hear the truth about Thanksgiving but it needs to be said damnit<br /> <br /> -Uh oh.<br /> <br /> -Frozen.<br /> <br /> -Crap<br /> <br /> -Maybe?<br /> <br /> -I<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t know\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXXXIX</i><br /> <br /> Not much to add here. Good roleplaying all around.<br /> <br /> Next session, meet Doc\u2019s mom, Alice\u2019s sister, Natalie\u2019s Mom, and Natalie\u2019s (now 17) year old daughter returns. Come for the drama, stay for the hijinx!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-06T13:59:51-07:00","id":654370,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s family time. We begin the Thanksgiving Story. Note Natalie\u2019s journal is a short story (with important character moment) rather than usual tweets. Note in that story she is referred to as Allison exclusively, while Natalie Lousler is Natalie<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXL</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1215 Hours, Monday, November 22, 2010<br /> <br /> Sunday flew by as uneventful as anything can be when the main topic of conversation is everyone\u2019s family.<br /> <br /> Meditation today was simple and relaxing. There were many talks of ground rules for the families over breakfast. No outting anyone, no seducing family, be careful around mirrors, try not to left the topic of death come up if at all possible, no talk of magic, etc. I left breakfast feeling even more anxious than yesterday.<br /> <br /> Around 1100 Hours, I called Mom and asked what she was doing for Thanksgiving. She talked about some options she had, but mainly it just sounded like she was going to be alone. I am a terrible son. So I told her that I would buy her a round trip ticket to New Haven so she could spend some time with us over the holidays. She agreed, so I bought the tickets. But I\u2019m so much more nervous now that I was before she agreed.<br /> <br /> I love my mother without question, but she is a very ...I don\u2019t know how to describe her. She isn\u2019t domineering or overly controlling. But she does like certain things to be just the way she wants them. And I fall into that category. Unfortunately when I\u2019m being honest, I\u2019ve often felt like a disappointment to her. I mean I made something of myself in the military, before the attack, and now I\u2019ve become an important part of the Krewe. We may seem more like the Addam\u2019s Family than a detective agency, but we deal with things that no one else can. Sadly, I can never really share that with Mom. Partly because of that and because I don\u2019t like to endanger mortals, I haven\u2019t really kept in touch. I am a Gatekeeper and it\u2019s my job to keep the living and the dead apart. I\u2019m worse at that than I am at being a son. We have ghosts coming to Thanksgiving for Christ\u2019s sake. But that\u2019s all beside the point. I haven\u2019t seen Mom since I was still in the hospital and I haven\u2019t talked to her since I got out. That\u2019s been close to a year, if I\u2019m remembering all the dates right. I\u2019ve made many compromises in the name of keeping the peace when it comes to my place in the Krewe. But I\u2019ve made more sacrifices in the name of keeping those I love safe. And now that I have a wider perspective, I don\u2019t think I\u2019ve always made the best decisions.<br /> <br /> <i>Life must still be lived, even as conflicts arise. Your reluctance to enjoy life does you no service as a warrior. One must hold dear those who mean the most, lest our battles become nothing more than violence committed to fill the void of our existence.</i><br /> <br /> I know he\u2019s right, but that only makes me feel worse.<br /> <br /> Matron X and Bella Donna will arrive tomorrow night so we have, with Tavia coordinating, begun the prepping of the rooms. Mom will be here around 1500 Hours Wednesday and I\u2019m not sure if Axe\u2019s brother has said when or if he will be around. I haven\u2019t said anything about it, but I still haven\u2019t heard anything from Bright Eyes about her family. I know they travel, but I was hoping she would be able to have someone here as well.<br /> <br /> We have so much to do and I am so ....I think ashamed is the word I\u2019m looking for. Mom knows Nightshade from the hospital but the others don\u2019t realize how long it\u2019s been. I need a drink.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1100 Hours, Tuesday, November 23, 2010<br /> <br /> We spent the rest of yesterday making sure all the rooms were prepared and cleaned. Sometimes I forget just how big Dark Haven Bluffs really is. I was reminded as we moved room to room last night with linens.<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t even remember if I meditated this morning. Everyone is either stressed out or super excited about all the guests coming in. I\u2019m at both ends of that spectrum depending on which guest we\u2019re talking about. Nightshade was slightly annoyed that \u201csomeone\u201d hid her heroin. I applauded that someone even though I risked setting Nightshade off. Karen grinned like a naughty child.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2300 Hours, Tuesday, November 23, 2010<br /> <br /> Matron X and Belladonna arrived just before Cupcake put food on the table. Nightshade insisted on carrying her mom\u2019s bags, despite them being more difficult than she wanted to admit, and Matron X trying to help anyway. I grabbed Belladonna\u2019s bags after noting I didn\u2019t think she\u2019s mind someone helping her with the bags. For her part, Belladonna looked both uninterested (as is her teenage superpower) and cold. The nearly pointless mini skirt and midriff top was a ridiculous choice for Connecticut and Axe actually told her she must be crazy. Our executioner was bundled in multiple layers before the jacket and was still shivering. It was neither the Carolina coast nor the dusty flats of Arizona here. I made it back to the stairs as Nightshade was still arguing with Matron X while struggling with the suitcase. Sliding next to Matron X on the staircase, I winked before silently lifting the bags to help Nightshade make it up the steps. Matron X smiled conspiratorially as we moved up the stairs together.<br /> <br /> Once the rooms were designated and bags were in, proper introductions were made. A tour of the house followed, then our guests unpacked a bit before we all grabbed something to eat. Belladonna had quietly changed into something Matron X packed for her, that was much more appropriate to the weather. Wisely, no one mentioned this.<br /> We\u2019ve tried to all be as social as possible without overwhelming anyone or getting in the way of the obvious need for family reconnection. This is wonderful to see but it\u2019s making me even more nervous about Mom coming.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1030 Hours, Wednesday, November 24, 2010<br /> <br /> I am terrified and sick.<br /> <br /> Mom has never done anything for me to have abandoned her like I have. And I don\u2019t have any explainable reason to give her for vanishing. I am going to have to pull it together soon though. I want this to somehow be wonderful and fun and to show her that I\u2019m not some static living on the streets. I want her to see that her son is someone she can feel proud of. But I don\u2019t want to remind her again that he also sees dead people.<br /> <br /> Her flight gets here about 1500 Hours, but I\u2019ll be at the airport by 1300 to be sure. I\u2019m also going to get a haircut on my way in. I need to have the van professionally cleaned as I do not want Mom to accidentally find any questionable stains to ask about.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I need to leave soon. Need something to keep me focused and working until she gets here and ....I don\u2019t know. She loves me. I really don\u2019t know what it is I expect her to do. But I\u2019m more nervous than when Axe announces she\u2019s going out for a run.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2100 Hours, Wednesday, November 24, 2010<br /> <br /> Well that wasn\u2019t what I expected, but some part of me remembers this all too well.<br /> <br /> I got to the airport a little before 1300 Hours. The last thing I wanted was to keep my Mom waiting in the airport. Bumfuck, Illinois is plenty cold this time of year, but that doesn\u2019t mean I wanted her to stand around in a strange airport for any longer than was absolutely necessary. The van was spotless, my haircut was regulation, and I was dressed in a pressed, button down navy shirt with khakis that were so sharp, I could have shaved with the legs. I made my way as far in as I could without a ticket and grabbed an overpriced sandwich and some water. The arrival board showed Mom\u2019s flight was on time. I slumped into a chair and ate my stale sandwich.<br /> <br /> How had I let a year go by and not talked with Mom?<br /> <br /> She came to the hospital when I came back from the Sands. I don\u2019t know what sort of maiming she expected but she was not prepared for what the reality of it was. If Nightshade hadn\u2019t been there to help keep her spirits up before I woke up from the drugs, I don\u2019t know what she would have done. When you learn someone has been wounded in the service, I think most people assume gunshot wounds, or now missing limbs. I was whole, but still missing most of who I was as far as she was concerned. She sat with me for days, refusing to go home. After weeks and a real concern that she might lose her job, I had to promise her that I would call as soon as anything changed. I kept that promise but nothing changed until I was being released. It killed her to see me sitting in a wheelchair, when she last saw me standing almost a foot over her.<br /> <br /> It was like being stabbed in the heart watching the tears fall down her face as she left. I\u2019m not sure if I was projecting or if she honestly thought I would die from depression and boredom. Either way, she was sure I was doomed. She never said that, but I could see the sadness in her eyes. At least that was one accomplishment I could show her.<br /> <br /> Her plane touched down 15 minutes early. I sprinted to the closest spot to her gate I could wait for her. When she left the gate, I was standing at parade rest in the middle of the concourse. I\u2019m stronger, in better shape, and at least as flexible now as I was when I joined the Navy. Her eyes passed me for a split second before widening and jerking back, tears spilling down her cheeks before she could even blink. I broke rank and ran to hug my mother. Not even I could understand her thickly accented words through the tears at first. She held my face and kissed my cheeks before making me do a modeling turn to get a look at how I had healed. It was a little embarrassing, but I figured I owed her that much.<br /> <br /> I walked with her to the baggage claim and grabbed her luggage before she could reach for the handles. It felt good to show Mom that was finally whole again. She even made it to the van before she started to pick me apart. The ghost flames were something I thought of to test my abilities and held some meaning to our Krewe. Mom pulled up short and asked why I had to further the stereotype. I sighed and assured her that I was not furthering any stereotypes that I was ever aware of. We eventually got her luggage and her in the van. The mini bar behind the front seats caused another round of loaded questions and explanations. And by 1530, I was finally able to leave and head back to the Bluffs.<br /> <br /> Axe surprised me with her knowledge of Spanish. Mom surprised me by how warm she was everyone else. Her questions and remarks about the van, was I in a gang, did I sell drugs, was I working illegally (when she saw the house), really got to me. I was trying to keep my cool and not snap back at her, as that was just bad form. But damn it, she pushed all my buttons and then became sweet as agave when she met the others. Axe greeted her in Spanish which means that she got to hear all the jabs Mom threw at me on the way to her room. Not how I wanted that to go. I saved Noriko to last and introduced her as my girlfriend. I figured there was no point in trying to hide that, nor did I want to. Noriko greeted Mom in attempted Spanish. To her credit, Mom didn\u2019t even flinch. She did mention that Noriko could speak to her in English and it would be fine. Noriko looked so relieved she could have fainted. Mom made a big deal over Nightshade as usual, but getting to meet Matron X seemed to put a sparkle in Mom\u2019s eyes. Their rooms were next to each other, so who knows how that will go. As exasperated as I was, Axe\u2019s brother pulled up just as we got Mom settled in. It was rude to leave another guest in the cold so I escaped to welcome Jacob. He was a nice looking guy, good with his hands, and quick to pick on Axe. That was a little better. He seemed to recognize Nightshade too, but based on the look on his face, it was probably from the Internet.<br /> <br /> We all gathered for an informal meal once Jacob was settled. Axe\u2019s brother is apparently one for tall tales and that grabbed Bright Eyes\u2019 attention at least as much as his face. Matron X surprised me as she intentionally built a conversation that led to getting me to talk about what I do. The questions and responses made sure that Mom got to hear how I basically ran a free medical clinic for the uninsured (only slightly not true), a successful store front, a massage by appointment business (which Matron X has declared she will utilize), and general medic for the house at large. That was followed by Jacob being called on to tell some of his stories. Matron X gets that massage on the house.<br /> <br /> Now I need to convince Noriko that my mom doesn\u2019t hate her or whatever it is she is about to crawl under the bed about. I just know it\u2019s related to her being a ball of nerves over meeting my mom.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, everyone\u2019s here. Which means enough drama and pretty people to keep away the homesickness. Mostly, at least. It helps that all the family here is family I never had - moms, brothers, daughters. There is a Gran involved, but that\u2019s a... different situation.<br /> <br /> Bah, here I am, being all mopey and completely misrepresenting the last few days. They have been wonderful, truly, if a little stressful. Though personally, it\u2019s all been sympathy stress. Natalie was a bundle of nerves, barking out orders and laying down ground rules and being strung tight enough to snap. The ground rules bit was important. Most folks have not had the benefit of Gran\u2019s tutelage in the ways of the beyond and are less receptive to the concept of the Touched. So no spooky stuff around our little Red\u2019s brother Jacob, or Doc\u2019s mom Girasol. Natalie\u2019s mom Julie and daughter Younger Natalie are both somewhat Touched themselves.<br /> <br /> As far as other ground rules go, Natalie was preoccupied with lecturing me and Karen about doing anything with her 17 year old daughter and Doc was preoccupied with implying I in particular would do something tasteless in front of his somewhat prudish mom. Alice at least didn\u2019t assume I\u2019d try to hook up with her incredibly attractive brother. And aside from giving me some exasperated looks, she doesn\u2019t seem upset at the fact I\u2019m totally going to try to hook up with her incredibly attractive brother.<br /> <br /> He\u2019s a rough and tumble kind of handsome, a diesel mechanic who owns his own rig and makes deliveries across the country. He has lots of stories, apparently, and has promised he\u2019ll work up to \u2018the Bigfoot one\u2019. He\u2019s a good storyteller too - Alice did get him to tell one at dinner tonight, mostly to distract him from teasing her about her fear of needles. Their relationship is adorable, and it\u2019s great to see her as comfortable, relaxed and happy as she is with him around.<br /> <br /> Of course, she\u2019s stolen him away to the state park tonight. It\u2019s alright, I get to help give Julie and Younger Natalie a tour of the 27 Club. By which I mean I\u2019ll probably be helping Karen stay out of Younger Natalie\u2019s clutches. The waif has not only perfected the art of teenage apathy (she didn\u2019t even seem impressed with Alexia\u2019s cookies, except for the fact she had 3) but is damn smooth too. Sometimes I really regret that whole caring about other people thing. Natalie owes me anyway. ;-) And Karen is a saint for not bringing up the fact that she was 17 when first Natalie slept with her.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll live though. Natalie did manage to completely forget to make me promise to be a chaste angel around her mom. It is pretty easy to see where both Natalies get it from. She is very attractive, eyes from the devil and ears of a bat/super mom powers notwithstanding. (Natalie may have issues.) I\u2019m a little distracted by Natalie\u2019s distress - not at my flirting, that\u2019s mildly hilarious, but at the situation as a whole. I\u2019m still sure it will turn out all the best for all of us involved.<br /> <br /> Girasol is not so bad to look at either. Doc did give the right kind of warning beforehand - indicating she wouldn\u2019t be appreciative rather than that he wouldn\u2019t be appreciative. He had me a bit worried with that, but she hasn\u2019t batted an eye at the various relationships. She\u2019s batted, berated and harangued Doc though, so Alice likes her. She did do it mostly in Spanish, so the rest of us don\u2019t know what about. She does seem to approve of Noriko though, which is good - the poor dear was almost as nervous as Natalie. Girasol lightened up on Doc a little as Julie made it so he could brag about his shop and clinic without actually bragging.<br /> <br /> Well, it does seem like folks have finished getting ready for the rout - I can tell, cause Girasol has started thanking Alexia again. That makes three times, in English and I\u2019m sure I caught at least one \u2018gracias\u2019. It is a big thing, to be invited to cook something special in someone else\u2019s kitchen for Thanksgiving after all. So everybody's excited, happy and ready to be all family like by visiting a club/bar. Sounds right to me.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> It's not even Thanksgiving yet, but with all the family gathered around the long dining table for dinner the night before, it already feels like the holiday has begun. I'm probably happier than I've been in a long time. Natalie and Doc are excited, if nervous, to have their mothers around. They both seem to have a pretty tense relationship with their parents: Natalie because of the way she and her mother alienated each other when she was younger, and Doc because he hasn't kept up with his mom like he should have after he was killed and became a sin-eater. I can identify. I'm sure my parents are worried and upset that I don't talk to them that much these days. I'd be pretty anxious if they were here too.<br /> <br /> Natalie's mother, Julie, hasn't made the best impression on me. She's the sort of cold and proper woman you never want to visit because you're afraid to touch anything in her immaculately decorated and cleaned house. I feel like she's always judging everyone around her. She actually reminds me of Kitty's mother, not that I really got to know Kitty's mom. I've never really felt comfortable around people like that.<br /> <br /> Of course, just as I'm thinking that, Julie starts asking Doc about what he does, and it gives Doc an opportunity to brag about himself in front of his mother a bit. It's pretty clear to me that Julie's trying to make Doc look good on purpose, so I guess she's not so bad.<br /> <br /> Doc's mother, Garisol, beams a bit at hearing how well her son is doing. I like Garisol. She's the sort of no-nonsense, down-to-earth woman I grew up around, and it helps that I speak Spanish. You don't grow up as a farmer in Casa Grande, Arizona, without picking up a bit of the language, and I made an effort to master it when I was younger. I'm not really fluent, and I got a bit rusty in Portland, but I still speak it well enough to understand all the nagging jabs Doc's mom throws at him. I'll admit I've been enjoying Doc's discomfort, especially since he knows I understand just about everything his mother's saying. Still, it's clear his mother loves him, and I'm glad Julie's building him up a bit. It makes me a feel a little guilty, though. And it makes me miss my own mom.<br /> <br /> I ask someone to pass the salad, and Natalie's daughter\u2014also named Natalie\u2014sends the salad bowl my way. <i>Our </i>Natalie's real name is Alison, and I gather she took her daughter's name when she ran away from home. I don't really know all the details and frankly I don't want to. Natalie's past drama is a lingering emotional minefield that's already claimed enough casualties, and I don't want to become one of them, so I'm keeping my distance.<br /> <br /> Young Natalie seems nice enough, if a bit out of her element. She takes after her mother, or wants to, at least, but she doesn't have much common sense. When she and Julie arrived at the house, she showed up in a mini skirt and halter top and not much else. I was bundled up in a long-sleeved shirt, jeans, sweater, scarf, knit cap and winter coat and I was still freezing! I guess she was trying to make an impression, but it was largely lost on most of us. For one thing, she's just a teenager, and the way she tries to play it cool by feigning disinterest in everything is kind of a turn off. I like people who are more genuine, and I can't help but feel like young Natalie is trying too hard to be her mother and not hard enough to be herself.<br /> <br /> As I munch on my salad and listen to the conversations around me, I notice that Sara is flirting with my brother. Jacob seems interested, which is hardly surprising. He's pretty shameless. I shoot Sara a look that says, &quot;What the heck do you think you're doing?&quot;, but I can't keep the smile from my face, so she knows I don't really mind. Jacob's a grown-up, so he can hook up with Sara if he wants. I know for a fact that he picks up waitresses at trucks stops from time to time, so it's not like he's a paragon of virtue. And I just learned that he knows Natalie from her Internet photos! He's such a dog. But I still love him.<br /> <br /> It is pretty awkward, though.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> As Alexia serves dessert, Sara and I cajole Jacob into sharing one of his trucker tall tales. He has a host of great stories from the road, and he's a great storyteller. He swears that every last one of them is 100% true, but I figure he's probably exaggerating some of the details.<br /> <br /> &quot;So it's a long haul from California to Chicago,&quot; Jacob begins. &quot;I've been on the road for something like 8 hours since my last stop and going on 24 since I last slept, and I've just entered Nebraska. It's getting a bit late, the sun's going down, and all the sudden I realize I've missed my interchange and I'm heading to Topeka, not Illinois. Now, I'm pretty adventurous, so instead of turning around, I decide I'll just wing it and exit onto highway 36 because I know it'll eventually link up to some roads I can use to get back to I-80 East.&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone at the table is quiet, watching as my brother's gestures add weight to his words. Eris looks on with solemn, wide eyes, and it occurs to me that she'll probably take Jacob's story at face value. Sara's a different matter, and I see her eyes light up to match the twinkle in Jacob's baby blues as he gets into his story.<br /> <br /> &quot;So before long, I find myself in the middle if nowhere. There's just the highway and cornfields as far as the eye can see, and late afternoon is dragging on toward night. Now I don't know if you've ever been driving through Midwestern cornfields after dark, but it's creepy as hell, and it doesn't take much to get lost, so I'm starting to get worried that I'm going to run out of sunlight. I mean, if that happens, I'm up shit creek because road signs aren't exactly easy to find out there, and my GPS is suddenly telling me I'm on a road that doesn't exist. To make matters worse, it's getting darker earlier than usual because a storm's brewing, and winds are whipping around like they're trying to organize a tornado.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm about to get on the CB and ask if any other truckers nearby know this area when suddenly this dude in raggedy clothes just comes flying out of the cornfield right in front of me like the devil's chasing him! I barely have time to register what I'm seeing, much less do anything about it. I slam on the brakes and swerve, but there's just nothing I can do. I hit him. I see him fly off to the side, arms flailing, but it all happens so fast that I can't tell if he gets thrown free or caught up under the wheels.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jacob's eyes are intense, and his expression deadly serious. You can feel the mounting horror of what's happened, but I know that there's got to be a twist. Jacob wouldn't be telling this story if he'd really killed someone. Sara gets it too, but I can see that a lot of our other guests are pretty anxious to hear how the story turns out.<br /> <br /> &quot;So I've lost control, and I'm freaking out, and next thing I know, my rig is plowing through this cornfield. I struggle to regain control, and by the time I come to a stop, I've pulled a complete three-sixty and my truck is covered in corn stalks. I'm counting my blessings that my load didn't tip over. I mean, I'm carrying a bunch of canned lima and pinto beans, and all I can think is that this farmer almost had a field full of succotash.<br /> <br /> &quot;Then it hits me that I probably just killed someone. I start to freak out, right? But I grab my first aid kit and scramble out of my cab. I run back to see if I can find the person I hit, just knowing I'm going to find a mangled corpse. It's not easy making my way through all the flattened corn, but I finally make it back to the road just as lightning strikes in the distance, bathing everything in a white flash. And as the flash of lightning fades, I see it right at my feet. The body. It's not moving. My heart's pounding so hard I can't even think.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jacob pauses, letting the moment sink in.<br /> <br /> &quot;It's a scarecrow. A freakin' <i>scarecrow</i>! It must have been blown across the road by the storm winds or something! I fell on my ass in the corn beside it and just started to laugh.&quot;<br /> <br /> A palpable sense of relief washes over everyone at the table and most of us can't help but chuckle.<br /> <br /> &quot;Once I got done laughing, I got back in my rig, coaxed it onto the highway and drove off. I considered tracking down the farmer and putting him in touch with the company I was working for at the time, but by now it was dark and I had no earthly idea where the closest farmhouse was, so I just high-tailed it out of there. I was pretty shaken, though, so I didn't go much farther that night. I pulled into the first truck stop I could find, crawled into the back, had a couple beers and went to sleep.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;But here's the kicker. The next morning, when I get up, I turned on the radio and caught part of a local news program. And there's this news report about a crop circle that appeared in a nearby cornfield last night just off highway 36.&quot; Jacob pauses a moment to let that sink in. &quot;The locals are speculating about aliens and UFOs, but I know who's really to blame.&quot; Jacob smirks with a mixture of mischief and guilt. &quot;Took me forever to clean all that corn out of my truck.&quot;<br /> <br /> Everyone laughs, and Jacob basks in our amused smiles. Even younger Natalie cracks a grin. It's good to have my brother here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> <b>Homecoming</b><br /> <br /> Fifty-four may not be old, but Julie Lousler felt every year of it. With her granddaughter Natalie in tow, she walked through the Tweed New Haven Airport, scanning the crowd for a face she had not seen in person for a dozen years. Chastity Allison Lousler was eighteen when she left for California and never returned. Never called. Never wrote. She simply vanished. Almost three years ago, Julie saw her death in the mirror, and she had changed. Now Julie scanned the crowd for that face that had gazed lifelessly at her in that mirror.<br /> <br /> Allison had been her greatest failure, the one she could not protect. Now she was getting another chance. She would not fail again.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t miss her,\u201d Natalie said, staying close to her grandmother. For herself, she had only recently learned her \u201cmother\u201d was her grandmother and her \u201csister\u201d was her mother. But her real mother was basically a rock star, and never made her clean her room. That was all right with her. Using her name was a little weird, though. \u201cLook for the Burton film reject.\u201d<br /> <br /> Julie remembered the last says she saw Allison. They played over and over in her head, over the years. An unstoppable train that no matter how much she tried to push from her mind, were always there. When Allison applied to college in Los Angeles without telling anyone until she was accepted. The argument where Allison simply sat on the couch, arms crossed, glaring at her.<br /> <br /> Their last conversation before Allison got on the boat. Julie asked Allison to call when she arrived safe. Allison simply stared at her, her green and blue eyes void of any emotion, turned around, and walked away.<br /> <br /> \u201cGood bye! I love you!\u201d Julie had called out. Allison never replied, or looked back.<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t call your mother a reject!\u201d Julie chastised sharply. She shoved the memory out of her mind, as she had so many times, her voice like an evocation to dispel it. The harshness in her voice also covered for nervousness. She had not been this nervous since she was about to bear Allison Lousler thirty years ago. Maybe not even then.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere!\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger girl pointed at a blob of darkness at the bottom the escalator. Down there in pure monochrome, save her ruby lips and blue and green eyes, was Chastity Allison Lousler, now Natalie Caroline Knight, Mistress of the Dead. She leaned against a post nonchalantly looking around, but her fidgeting hands in her fingerless gloves gave away her own nervousness.<br /> <br /> Julie Froze.<br /> <br /> Julie saw Allison die in the mirror, just before New Years. She knew it would happen New Years Eve as she saw the ball dropping on television in the background. It was clearly a hotel room. White powder lay across the floor Allison laid on, staring lifelessly at the television. Eyes green and blue held no more emotion than they had when she parted at the boat. Once again, she didn\u2019t say goodbye. Julie pushed the memory away.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am going to maintain my poise,\u201d Julie thought. \u201cI am not given to emotional displays. It is time to kill the fatted calf. My child is home.\u201d She got on the escalator and stood still watching the apparition of the dark clad girl grow closer. Allison hadn\u2019t seen her yet. Beside her, her granddaughter considered how much her mom looked photoshopped into the tableau before her, her stark black white and silver hardly matching the world around her.<br /> <br /> Julie stepped off the escalator. Her heart tightened in her chest.<br /> <br /> Julie and Allison made eye contact. Julie walked toward her. What she wanted to say was \u201cAllison, it is good to see you! Allison, you look so much better than I feared! Allison, I am so sorry about what I did.\u201d But no words came from Julie Lousler\u2019s mouth. She wept. Allison wept. Tears fell, from eyes green and blue. They embraced. Julie held her daughter tightly as Allison, too, tried and failed to speak. Natalie cried too, and hugged her mother. For several minutes mother and daughter held each other, bawling, at the foot of the escalator.<br /> <br /> Natalie, for her part, soon disengaged to check her phone.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXL</i><br /> <br /> Heavily Roleplaying this session. Doc\u2019s player largely covered playing his mom, while I mostly handled Jacob, as per the wishes of the players.<br /> <br /> There was a rather amusing issue that came up I had not planned. The game has two players in common with <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, which has a major NPC named Julia. Julie kept being called Julia by accident, and once it got started it was hard to stop. Even one player not in Changeling called her Julia at one point. There was even a journal that accidentally had a Julia in it. So Julie. Not Julia. Very different person. Also, I slipped up and called Jacob (Jay-Kob) Jacob (YAH-kub) the PC from MDH once, but I was the only one guilty of that.<br /> <br /> There was the moment where Jacob started to ask Natalie where he knew her from, and Natalie quickly said \u201cSuicide Girls, 2001-2004.\u201d When he started to stammer she just asked him if he wanted a signed print. It was funny.<br /> <br /> Not much else to add. Lots of good roleplaying and family awkwardness. But if you want to know more, comments and questions welcome. See you next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-06-2015, 05:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T02:10:20-07:00","id":671734,"title":"","content":"ew Session. Alice\u2019s player could not make due to illness, so we let time drag a bit and mostly covered the outing Wednesday Evening, covering them taking the moms to several locations, more than was in the original plan. It got us some good roleplaying, so here we are. This means no Alice journal, and like before Natalie is a short story. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXLI<br /> </i><br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0100 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I have so many random thoughts in my head, I don\u2019t really know where to start. I guess I\u2019ll try to keep it all together the way I can remember it and hope that it still makes any kind of sense.<br /> <br /> After storytime, we all loaded up in the van and Nightshade\u2019s car. Well Axe, Eris, and Jacob headed off after dinner but the rest of us. Bright Eyes, Karen, Belladonna, and Matron X all rode together. When I asked, Nightshade mumbled something quickly about driving her family. Mom, Cupcake, Chandra, and Noriko all rode in the van. Mom was up front with me so the ladies had a very roomy ride on the sectional. If Noriko hadn\u2019t been so nervous, she probably would have stretched out. Mom did ask quietly in Spanish about the Bluffs being a lesbian commune, but it was mostly an observation type question. It didn\u2019t seem to bother her as much as surprise her. Probably because no one seemed to mind the few men we do have around. It was kind of funny now that I think about it, but I guess I was still a little nervous at the time too.<br /> <br /> My nerves went away once we got to the 27 Club. Matron X seems to have a keen sense for things that will catch Nightshade off guard without actually trying to trip her up. The many couches in the Champagne Room did not escape her notice. When Matron X asked about it, Belladonna unknowingly drove another nail in by mumbling something about there being a lot of couches. Bright Eyes decided to \u201chelp\u201d by then listing as many of the hot female acts Nightshade had booked as she could. As I didn\u2019t want to kick her in front of everyone, I decided to counter Bright Eyes\u2019 \u201chelp\u201d with other bands that were less likely to have \u201cutilized\u201d the Champagne Room in the same way. The bigger than names, the better as far as I could tell. I did give Bright Eyes a look. She grinned with a guilty shrug, but stopped tormenting Nightshade.<br /> <br /> While Mom, Matron X, and Belladonna were off to one side, Nightshade corralled us all together to ask for help. She remembered the first song she learned to play by ear, because it was one of Matron X\u2019s favorites at the time. She wanted us to put a band together so we could surprise everyone by playing Joe Jackson\u2019s Steppin\u2019 Out. I pointed out that I could move heavy things and possibly play the tambourine. Because I was helping and me and instruments still don\u2019t really mesh together yet. Nightshade swears she will teach me but we haven\u2019t made the time and I haven\u2019t considered what instrument.<br /> <br /> From the 27 Club, Matron X asked if she could see my shop. I was only a little surprised but definitely nervous as I don\u2019t know everything the girls have done to change the feel and flow yet. This was entirely my fault, but I was not about to turn down the request. When we arrived, I got to the door and gave the standard speech about my herbs. There was no marijuana in my \u201cherbs.\u201d Belladonna and Nightshade shared a look that I didn\u2019t entirely understand but no one said anything. The shop was mostly the way I expected it, though some things were arranged so that the whole place seemed brighter. The herbs were in rows based on cooking, medicinal, and ritual uses. I can\u2019t remember how I described that to not sound so occulty, but it seemed to work. Mom was immediately oooing and ahhhing over the Mexican Oregano and other seasoning herbs. Belladonna was searching for what I suspect was anything illicit that might be hidden after I mentioned that my employees were college students. Matron X was seemingly impressed with all of it, but didn\u2019t admit to anything. I gathered some of the more complimentary aromatics and gently slid them into an incense vial with the better quality oil before handing it to her. I suggested we could use it tomorrow before the cooking started so we had wonderful scents all day. Then I made a collection of herbs for Mom since I knew she\u2019d want to use seasonings she was familiar with while cooking. She immediately chastised me for ruining my bookkeeping until I showed her I was writing off the pittance of herbs I was giving her. Honestly I\u2019ve lost more from kids sneezing around an open bag than what I gave her. I talked a little about the massage practice next, though there was nothing but the table to see there. Then there was the tattoo discussion which I kept for the end. When I first moved to show the area, Matron X asked about any visible needles with a pointed glance at Belladonna. For a teen that doesn\u2019t like to react to anything, she paled fairly well at the thoughts of needles. But as a show of force, she declared that she would be fine. I asked if she had issues with the standard gun or the tribal tapping stick I had. I thought Belladonna was going to be sick, but she only wobbled a little before Matron X was behind her just enough that she couldn\u2019t lose her balance. I threw a towel over the tribal stick and kept the gun out without getting it close to anyone. This got Belladonna talking about what she wanted when she turned 18. She started with wanting an ankh above her ankle. I gave her more information that was a bit more elaborate, would take longer, have color, and represent something that wasn\u2019t just a clich\u00e9 symbol that everyone ignored. Nightshade looked at me briefly when I went into the more ritualistic side of things, but stayed quiet. I wanted Belladonna to know what could be available but I also wanted to test her resolve for being under the needle for that long and enduring the pain of it. Bright Eyes showed off a bit of the work I had done for her afterwards and that eased the tension slightly. Surprisingly, Mom looked on without any disapproving expressions.<br /> <br /> The next stop was to Sweet Surrender, which was actually still open. Cupcake\u2019s bakers and cookie makers were moving like medics after a firefight with all the customers wanting baked goods without taking the time themselves. Still, Cupcake being the Master Chef, many of them stopped to receive new orders. She didn\u2019t have any so they ran back to work while she pulled various goodies from the front case. None of our guests or the Krewe turned down anything that was offered, especially not the virgin drinks named after Nightshade.<br /> <br /> World of Wicker is always open and in walking distance from Sweet Surrender. Mom was most eager to investigate. I looked at Chandra before we went in and asked her just to tell me how bad it was. For her part, Chandra went into sales mode and it was a frightening thing. Her smile was a separate part of her face, her accent thickened, and she was more bubbly than the drinks at Sweet Surrender. I wanted to hide my wallet, but just looked on at the train wreck unfolding before me. Mom picked out a set of end tables and some really nice nightstands, but before I could do anything, she jerked out her checkbook. I opened my mouth to protest but Mom cut me off with a rapid fire reminder in Spanish that she was not here to mooch off her son, that she could use her own money how she wanted, and that she hadn\u2019t gotten so old that she had to be handled with mittens in public. Chandra covered by noting that the most expensive of the grouping was free, but as the manager, the rest was simply on sale. I paid for shipping separately so Mom wouldn\u2019t have to pay to fly the furniture back. Mom didn\u2019t seem to notice.<br /> <br /> We made it back to the Bluffs without any other issues. Belladonna decided that she was going for a walk up on the Widow\u2019s Walk. I tried not to grin at Nightshade, given how much she used to do that when the Krewe was just coming together. Realizing an opportunity, I nudged Cupcake after Belladonna and Nightshade both disappeared and suggested hot chocolate. That apparently was a cue for Matron X. She pulled me to the side and told me some things that I knew and asked me some things I didn\u2019t immediately know. She was here to try and mend the wounds between herself and Nightshade and not let new ones open between any of them and Belladonna. But she told me she thought maybe I had some similar issues to handle. Somehow this led to me admitting what a terrible son I\u2019ve been and how I wanted to try to make it up to Mom. About that time, we all heard Mom coming downstairs. The smile in her voice filled the stairwell as she asked if that was chocolate she smelled. I thought my chest was going to explode from the irony of how happy she sounded verses how guilty I felt. After the hot chocolate, Mom and Matron X went upstairs speaking Spanglish to each other cheerfully. I headed for the bar. I didn\u2019t know what else to do and bourbon sounded like an option, if not an answer. Before I made it that far, Noriko stopped me dead with an innocent question. She should dress up in her dragon kimono tomorrow or not? I forgot all about needing a drink, about how guilty I was (briefly), and that my Mom was in the house. After the description of this kimono, I was very focused on my girlfriend.<br /> <br /> And then of course, we had to \u201csneak out\u201d to practice. I think Matron X will enjoy the music and Mom will be amused and impressed with the talent tomorrow. Tonight, they are asleep (I hope) and I am going to find a piece of string and see how long I have to nibble on Noriko\u2019s ear before she either wakes up and pounces me or throws me across the room. Or both. I suppose both is an option<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, that was a productive night of showing off our lives. At least the troupe\u2019s lives. I was starting to feel a little bad, in that not really kinda way. I\u2019m not precisely mooching after all . I do my part in our more mystical existence. And the others\u2019 mundane businesses - Natalie\u2019s club, Doc\u2019s shop and parlor, Alexia\u2019s bakery and Chandra\u2019s store - are done as much out of love as necessity and I\u2019m far too much of a hedonistic vagabond to fall in love with a single job or place of business.<br /> <br /> I am getting back on stage in a couple of days, and that is about as close as I get. Music, not dancing, but still. Natalie still remembers the first song she learned by ear, a favorite of her mom\u2019s - Stepping Out by Joe Jackson. So as a treat, while Julie and Younger Natalie are here, we\u2019re going to perform it. Natalie is on piano and vocals, me and Karen have worked out a guitar and bass arrangement of the synth part and Noriko is handling the drums. We had a pretty good first practice, sneaking out after all the guests had gone to bed. It\u2019s gonna be great, and Julie will certainly appreciate it.<br /> <br /> I think we\u2019ve made a good impression already. She (and Garisol) were suitably impressed by the club, though Julie couldn\u2019t help but raise an eyebrow at the champagne room. I \u2018helped\u2019 by talking up all the hot lady bands that had played at the club. Doc tried to actually help by listing bands Natalie clearly wouldn't have been entertaining. To be fair, it did add up to an impressive list of acts Natalie\u2019s manage to get to come to the club, ignoring the implications that I totally didn\u2019t start. So, wins all around<br /> <br /> Next was Doc\u2019s shop. Younger Natalie was the most impressed there, especially with the Craft supplies and his tattooing equipment. Both Julie and Natalie enforced the rule of no tattoos until you\u2019re 18 though. Doc did make her an awesome sketch for her anticipated one. Garisol on the other hand was impressed by the cooking supplies, if not by her son\u2019s business acumen when he tried to let her take whatever she wanted for free.<br /> <br /> Chandra wasn't able to get away with that. To be fair, she does have the business acumen not to try. Garisol likes her wicker furniture. Her business acumen is kinda scary really - her \u2018saleswoman\u2019 persona can be flipped on like a switch and she\u2019s all bubbly smiles and a slightly thicker Indian accent. It was a little disconcerting, to be honest. She did manage to give Garisol one piece for free and the rest were conveniently on sale. Doc managed to pay for shipping the pieces back to his mom, but she was quick with the checkbook to pay for the pieces themselves.<br /> <br /> Alexia\u2019s shop was the only other one still open, since lots of folks wanted delicious baked goods for Thanksgiving without the work. Everyone there was hard at work with special orders, but Alexia got us all our favorite treats from the counter, plus virgin Natalies :-D for everyone.<br /> <br /> Yes, I think we made a good impression. I know I made an excellent one on Julie. She was certainly easy to pay attention to and enough like her daughter to enjoy it. It hasn\u2019t gone anywhere and probably won\u2019t. Natalie is so focused on making this work and so nervous about the entire situation. So is Julie for that matter. She feels fated to finally leave a painful past behind, and her words really resonated, for all her insistence that Christians have a monopoly on being led. Again, fairness, she was trying to make sure she didn\u2019t make us uncomfortable, but I mostly found it amusing. Anyway, I\u2019m not good at keeping this sort of thing secret so... it\u2019s probably best to leave it at the flirting. Still fun to think about though.<br /> <br /> Well, tomorrow is the proper festivities, with family and friends all around and plenty of food for all. I might have to get some almond M&amp;Ms - Karen spilled the beans about Tatum\u2019s... fondness for them to Alexia. That was a good night. Seems good enough reason for the treat to me, and it\u2019ll make Natalie squirm. And that's what the holidays are all about.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> <b>Homecoming II</b><br /> <br /> Natalie Lousler stepped out onto the widow\u2019s walk. She had been looking forward to going out on it in the evening again ever since her summer visit, but as she leaned against the railing to look out over the darkness and hear the sea, she was cold. She had not considered how much colder November was. Though she was still near the ocean, Connecticut was cooler than North Carolina.<br /> <br /> \u201cMind company?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie jumped. The light silhouetted the woman stepping through the door but she recognized her mother. Natalie Knight closed the door behind her and, dressed in her long coat, walked over to her daughter.<br /> <br /> \u201cNah Alli\u2026Mom\u2026you\u2019re cool.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie Knight walked over and put an arm around her daughter. Natalie Lousler instinctively moved closer to her mother, sharing the warmth. She smelled like strawberries. The teen rather liked strawberries.<br /> <br /> \u201cI wanted to be sure you were okay sweetheart,\u201d Natalie started, looking at her shivering daughter. \u201cYou are, well, distant compared to your last visit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry\u2026it\u2019s\u2026I was hoping to move here, you know. Get away from the island, like you did. I thought you wanted me here\u2026\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do,\u201d The older woman looked in her daughter\u2019s eyes. \u201cIt\u2019s\u2026more complicated than that. Assuming I am still living here when you are in college, I would like you to go to college up here. In your own dorm, of course, for that freedom, but nearby me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was hoping for sooner.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo was I,\u201d the elder girl sighed. \u201cBut it did not turn out that way. There are lots of arrangements that would need to be made. The house would need to be inspected and I doubt Simon would be okay with that. Also, by the time I could really arrange for you to move up here and get into a high school, you will be a senior, I think, and I would rather you spend your senior year with people you know not strangers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could hang out,\u201d the younger girl said, hopefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can. And in time, we will. I hope. But I would rather you be at an age where my strutting around your friends would not be a potential problem.\u201d Natalie smiled wryly.<br /> <br /> \u201cLooking for more people to invite to the \u2018totally not a Champaign room?\u2019\u201d her daughter returned the wry tone back at her mother.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a hospitality room, like I told mom. And I have a backlog of people as is,\u201d The elder smirked.\u201d I won\u2019t need help. I just don\u2019t want to feel bad about flirting.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo have you slept with any rock singers I have heard of?\u201d The younger girl ventured, curiosity in her voice. Her mom was awesome, and smelled like strawberries.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot there, but Yes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo who\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pregnant pause. Natalie Lousler eventually said,\u201d So you are not going to tell me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, one is not out of the closet at all and just got married. One is known to be at least bi but does not wish to confirm or discuss it. Two I will not admit to till my dying day. That\u2019s all I spent the night with anyway. The first couple you may hear when you are older. Did that answer your question?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess. So\u2026Did Doc get replaced by Sara or what?\u201d<br /> <br /> The elder Natalie froze.<br /> <br /> \u201cI mean, you were with Karen and Doc before, now it is Karen and Sara.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s complicated. Honestly, Doc and I are very good friends. However a relationship with him was not feasible. We were not, it turned out, as compatible as I hoped. But we care a lot about each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCool, I guess. Sara sure seems to want Jacob. Do you care?\u201d The younger girl looked at her mother. Natalie stroked her daughter\u2019s hair, \u201cHonest answer? I am not a very jealous person. Sara will stay with me, return to me. We belong to each other. Sleeping with Jacob is not the same. Sara can\u2019t be happy with a jealous person, we are good for each other.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow can it not bug you though?\u201d<br /> <br /> The older woman sighed, \u201cSara will stay with me or she won\u2019t. I can patrol and try and catch her messing around, or I can assume if she feels she no longer has the connection to Karen and I she will break the triad. I don\u2019t expect her to, but she has that freedom. If I did not give her the freedom to come and go as she pleases, am I simply pressing her to end things, if she desires? No, I will let her have her freedom.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow does it not bug you she can\u2019t be with just you two though? Most people only get one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause we like freedom?\u201d Natalie smiled at her daughter, \u201cLook sweetie, if it sounds crazy and does not make sense, than it is not for you. That\u2019s fine. You don\u2019t need to do it because I do. I do what makes me happy without hurting others as best I can. I recommend you do the same.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two were quiet for a time. A cloud moved and the moon shone silver light down on the pair. Natalie rubbed her daughters shoulders, and felt her relax as she leaned forward a little.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice is new,\u201d Natalie Lousler said after a time. \u201cWho is she?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlice is one of us, she came to us for help. We helped her. She reminds me a little of myself. Our struggles are different, but we both fought our dark sides.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s cute.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer girlfriend thinks so, yes,\u201d Natalie smiled somewhat feeling her daughter\u2019s shoulders stiffen a moment. The younger girl knew Eris was Alice\u2019s girlfriend of course, but she did not miss the implication of the reminder. After a moment, though, the older girl frowned; it was her mother\u2019s tactic to give reminders like that.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo is there a big lesbian magnet on the house or something?\u201d the younger girl broke the silence quickly to move on from the awkwardness.<br /> <br /> Natalie chuckled, \u201cWhy yes I had it installed myself. Seriously no, Sara is bisexual, Alexia is a lesbian\u2026as far as I know\u2026and I am as well. Doc is straight, Simon\u2026has never demonstrated not being straight. Jasmine is straight\u2026<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat happened to Jasmine?<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s moving to Taiwan, to do some work over there. Her dad actually lives in Taiwan,\u201d Natalie could feel her daughter was finally relaxing.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou two don\u2019t like each other, do you?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Goth laughed, \u201cActually, considering how few things we agree on Spooky and I get along amazingly well,\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger girl paused, \u201cSo\u2026why do you call her Spooky?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s a pet name, a mark of affection. It actually was something that helped break the ice. She took it as intended; my trying to reach out to be her friend,\u201d Natalie finished with her daughters shoulders and moved beside her, looking out with her towards the sound of the sea.<br /> <br /> \u201cSooooooo\u2026Noriko is Doc\u2019s new girlfriend? What\u2019s her deal? She is not one of you,\u201d The younger girl leaned on her mom once again. She would need a strawberry when she went inside.<br /> <br /> \u201cIn the sense she has not returned from the dead no. In the sense she is part of our spooky family, yes. I consider her to belong,\u201d The older girl said simply. \u201cShe makes Doc happy, and gets along really well with Alice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd she checks you out too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smirked, \u201cOf course not dear. It is your imagination. But even if she did, she and Doc are happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019d turn her down for him?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt will never come to that. Noriko would not do that. But I would do far more than that for him.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCool\u201d<br /> <br /> Another long pause. The moon went behind a cloud. The younger girl was really shivering now, but she had been looking forward to being on this widow\u2019s walk and hanging out with her mom here. She was not going to budge.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlexia has not changed.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older girl laughed, \u201cNo, no she hasn\u2019t. She is the same kooky Alexia she always has been. She is the stable one I think, in the sense of not changing too much. But it has only been a couple seasons. Who knows? It\u2019s been the most eventful summer of my life, regardless.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry I ran away from you last time. I was scared.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older girl blinked a moment at her daughter, than recalled the moment of her last visit, as she confessed her own feelings about Mary Magdalene. \u201cIt\u2019s okay sweetie. I should have told you right off. I won\u2019t hide anything like that from you now.\u201d<br /> <br /> The younger girl thought a moment, \u201cSo then\u2026how did you and Karen meet, anyway? You got flustered when it came up before. Is there more than at a concert?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie Knight began to stammer when the door opened.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know neither of you are actually cold, but Alexia made us all hot chocolate and I think it would be nice to drink some all the same,\u201d Julie Lousler smiled at her family huddled for warmth.<br /> <br /> \u201cOkay,\u201d the younger girl said, and walked inside hand in hand with her mom. Maybe she would grab a strawberry with her chocolate.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLI</i><br /> <br /> You are not old enough to hear the Almond story. It was based on something that (allegedly) really happened.<br /> <br /> So we got to have the players describe their businesses and kinda run their scenes. That was fun. Lots of chatter and RP, it was it good session.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions Welcome. Thanksgiving Day should be next session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:34:31-07:00","id":672293,"title":"","content":"So not only did I catch up on the journals recently, but in your fashion you continued to spark thoughts and ideas. That purified character idea has recently expanded.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-22T17:27:47-07:00","id":674694,"title":"","content":"Caught up at last!<br /> Congratulations to all of you on running or participating in such a long lasting and active game!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-23T02:22:12-07:00","id":675038,"title":"","content":"Thanks. It is a true pleasure. Hopefully the others will do so well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T16:11:07-07:00","id":688983,"title":"","content":"Time to check in on the Krewe! This session we cover the evening for Alice and move into turkey day. Due to a family crisis Sara\u2019s player was unable to attend. Let\u2019s see what the rest got up to.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXLII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1000 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> Thanksgiving.<br /> <br /> Not the first holiday you think of as being a big deal at Dark Haven Bluffs. Harder to say that now that we\u2019re in the middle of it. I\u2019m getting ahead of myself.<br /> <br /> We got back to the Bluffs late last night and to be honest, I drug Noriko to bed. Between the stress of everything and the talk of the kimono, I was done.<br /> <br /> This morning I went for meditation about 0800 Hours and easily found my center, even with Mom here. After that, I stretched and worked on my katas until now. I should probably get cleaned up, make sure Noriko is awake, and see what everyone else is up to. I also need to get things together for lunch.<br /> <br /> Cupcake doesn\u2019t know it yet, but MY tradition at Thanksgiving is to force the cooks to stop long enough to enjoy a more simple but decent meal at lunch. Given the number of people that need to be fed, I\u2019ll need to get a pretty big sandwich line going. So maybe I just get cleaned up and do that.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I am a terrible Gatekeeper. But I guess I make up for it by being a decent person. I stumbled into Nightshade, Belladonna, and Karen setting up the Ghost Dinner table upstairs. I was confused but Karen rescued me from Nightshade\u2019s anxiety long enough to say this was a family event now. Also that Matron X could see my death without mirrors. This was not part of the plan and I had to try very hard not to lose it in front of Belladonna. Instead I just helped them finish the setup, making sure to keep my reflection away from the youngest would-be Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> Now I\u2019m going to pick up the food I ordered for the sandwich line and pay a huge tip for the store getting it together for me at such short notice.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> The sandwich line was a hit. Chandra and I kept things under watch in the kitchen while everyone else ate. Then after about 30 minutes, Cupcake and Mom marched back into the kitchen and ran us out.<br /> <br /> My work mostly done, I grabbed a sandwich and my sketchpad. I opened up the laptop and looked up several nautical knots that I think I\u2019ll need to know how to handle if we can raise the ship in the Underworld. I only got a few done when Karen came to me to call in a favor I\u2019d offered, maybe last night? The days are running together. Anyway, she asked if I could get her brother here without her parents being involved. There was only a small joke about asking the guy with a van to kidnap someone. I think as retaliation she informed me that my girlfriend was showing Axe\u2019s girlfriend pictures of her (Karen\u2019s) wife. I had to think about that for minute. When it hit me, Karen giggled while I wondered where Noriko found pictures of Nightshade to start with.<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> So far, so good.<br /> <br /> Yes, having my mother and Natalie here has been stressful, but quite frankly I am surprised at how mom and I are getting along. It has been stressful and yes I am seeing disapproval in her eyes now and again\u2026but not like I feared. I think in part it is because I am older than the eighteen-year-old girl who turned her back on her twelve years ago. I\u2019ve also grown a great deal as a person. Fuck, this summer and autumn I have grown a great deal as a person. It is impossible to accurately describe how good this Krewe has been for me.<br /> <br /> Bad girl, ramble. Mom\u2019s been to my club now, though she was perhaps, ahem, a bit on the nose with noticing the intended purpose of the hospitality room. A gal has to explore who she is, and something it helps a gal explore who she is when she has a half dozen friends there to help. She did not say anything but to comment on the room, but I caught the \u201cI see what you are doing\u201d that was there. Still, otherwise things have been smooth. She has not asked about my religion, she has not said a word about me being poly, and she has not said a word about me being queer (though if younger Natalie is believed, that is somewhat true of her also, which blows my mind.)<br /> <br /> She wants this to work. She wants to finally put the past behind her. I want to that too. I just have to keep being a good host and maybe we will not only have a good Thanksgiving but I might actually go home for Christmas. We have had tea and sat and even laughed together. It was awesome.<br /> <br /> Things were rocky with my baby, however. She was upset with me. I think she had her heart set on moving up here and leading a party life. Like mother like grandmother like daughter I guess. But unlike us she does not have a dark closet full of regrets. Goddess, I want to do everything in my power to stop it. I don\u2019t want my little girl to suffer.<br /> <br /> But\u2026based on history, and my observations of her now, she will. I see it in her overconfident eyes and swagger. And I will be powerless to stop it. The harder I grasp, the more things slip through my fingers like sand. It kills me, savages my psyche\u2026to think of my little girl going through what I did sends me into a despondent rage. I\u2019ve already broken down once thinking about it.<br /> <br /> But I have seen with myself how trying to hard to shield her fails, and indeed drove me to a darker time than even my mother saw. And just as I see the pain in her eyes that she could not protect me I wonder if I will have it in my eyes when I look at Natalie. The worry is there, stealing my sleep and giving me crow\u2019s feet.<br /> <br /> But it is family time. Time to focus on what I have. I\u2019ve never been this happy. Everything is falling into place. This is the best Autumn of my life. Just don\u2019t fuck this up, Allison.<br /> <br /> You know, like you always do.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXLII</i><br /> <br /> Alice was very active this session. We covered her events Wednesday night as she and her brother had dinner with the Sleeping Giant pack. They got along marvelously, but she noticed her brother noticed something seemed off about them.<br /> <br /> They had a private conversation where he asked if they were in something like the military together. He noted they were in very good shape, kept an eye on each other (in a protective way) and sorted differences carefully. It reminded him of something military. Also, they took in a well built amnesiac. Alice admitted having noticed but dodged things after, though Jacob noticed her evasion.<br /> <br /> They all plan to go on a hike Friday. Both girls besides Eris flirted with Jacob a bit.<br /> <br /> That should cover it. We will be without Sara tonight for similar family related reasons, but the rest of the Krewe will be here. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-04T22:27:41-07:00","id":689315,"title":"","content":"Observant family members always complicate the lives of their supernatural relatives. I wonder what kind of troubles Jacob will attract? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T00:44:15-07:00","id":689399,"title":"","content":"We will see. We did not get to the hike this session, as we spent it finishing up Thanksgiving day. Was a lot of fun though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T12:37:51-07:00","id":692851,"title":"","content":"Natalie's lament reminds me of a thought I had a while back. Admittedly I am not a parent and haven't been close, but it seems to me that parenting often has an aspect of Greek Tragedy to it. One tries to prevent the disaster that befell them, but in doing so they end up causing it. This doesn't happen to every parent yes, but it does seem to be a common trend.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-07T23:46:55-07:00","id":693505,"title":"","content":"My father managed to avoid his difficulties of growing up with us, fortunately.<br /> <br /> That said yea, this is very much the case with Julie, Natalie Knight, and Natalie Lousler.<br /> <br /> Next session journals will have a much more upbeat fiction of a conversation between Natalie Knight and her mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-18T21:58:21-07:00","id":708133,"title":"","content":"Thanksgiving day has arrived, and the group has balancing to do. Let\u2019s check in. For related reasons to before, Sara\u2019s player could not make. They will return when the immediate Thanksgiving plot is over.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s journal like most of the last few is a short fiction dealing with her family. It did not happen at the table.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXLIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 2000 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I have a minute to write before I have to go \u201ccook\u201d dinner again so I wanted to get this down if I can.<br /> <br /> I had to rescue Karen from Matron X around 1700 Hours both to get Karen a break and to talk with Matron X. I know where Nightshade got her mischievous streak from. Anyway, once we got to the Game Room and away from the others, I apologized. She seemed annoyed that I knew she had seen me more than anything but told me I had nothing to apologize for. We talked about things openly (without me outing anyone or any other secrets not Sin-Eater related) for a while. Matron X is actually very content with her powers, which is not how I expected it. I also mentioned how I was trying very hard not to let my reflection get near Belladonna. She was perhaps more appreciative of that than if she hadn\u2019t seen my death wounds. She can also see ghosts in reflections it seems. Naomi bothered her a little, but she hadn\u2019t seen the fish so it could have been worse. I told her about the dinner later and that Nightshade had organized it. She might not have intended to, but Matron X was very proud of her daughter for caring for those that couldn\u2019t care for themselves. Especially this way.<br /> <br /> Once I felt like I had given Matron X as much info as she could safely understand and just talk without a wall of secrets, I let her get back to her vacation. Sadly, that meant going straight for Karen again. I would have tried to help a little more, but Noriko came back in from her walk with Axe, Eris, and Jacob. She immediately jumped up on my shoulders, which was funny for a lot of reasons, not the least of which was that she realized she was still wearing the kimono about half way through the air. We talked together for a while before everyone gathered just to wait for food. That became a little more uncomfortable as everyone watched Karen squirm form Matron X\u2019s line of questions. Eventually, I stepped in with the only helpful thing I could think of.<br /> <br /> Dancing.<br /> <br /> I led as many as were interested into the Music Room and put on Sarah Vaughan\u2019s Summertime. Then I offered my hand to Matron X, both to keep her involved and to put her in the spotlight for a little bit. The song works for a foxtrot and it\u2019s slow enough that I could lead without dragging Matron X around the floor. When we were done, we got an ovation and Matron X looked surprised, happy but surprised.<br /> <br /> Cupcake came in and announced dinner was ready. We all fell into the Dining Room to find enough food for a week. Mom made enough food to feed the entire gathering but it still paled in comparison to what Cupcake presented. She mentioned there were two types of everything when I realized that she and the Cracked Cook were competing again. I knew this was my chance to figure out which one was which. I got a small portion of everything, except Mom\u2019s cooking. The tamales and elote are not something I can get anywhere nearby, plus it was homemade! And I wanted to weep when I had some of the frijoles borrachos. It had been too long. But, I did get a taste of everything Cupcake had to offer and this gave me a good idea of both styles. Given I\u2019ve eaten Cupcake\u2019s meals alot, I was able to pick out hers from the Cook\u2019s. I made sure to compliment everything, but looked at Cupcake directly when I spoke of her dishes. All in all, I think Thanksgiving Dinner went very smoothly. I was a little surprised when Matron X announced that she was going to 27 Club tomorrow night, but that should be fine. Not sure what Mom thought about it, but should be okay.<br /> <br /> Now I have my own cooking to do.<br /> <br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1130 Hours, Thursday, November 25, 2010<br /> <br /> I am truly not a chef. Fortunately for our spectral guests, the food was made by an excellent one. I just had to bring it across. It took a half hour before I could get the ceremony to work, but it finally did and I was able to go up with Nightshade. We brought drinks and sat with our gathered deceased. Troy, Naomi, Marjorie, and especially Marcy had not seen a spread like we brought in a really long time, if ever. Having tasted of everything already, I could have normal conversation about it and not just awkwardly sit without eating. If anyone would have looked into the room, they would have seen Nightshade and I casually chatting with different people that weren\u2019t there in front of a table with nothing on it. Lucky for them, no one did.<br /> <br /> After both dinners were finished, everyone wandered into the TV Room. When we joined them, Axe convinced Jacob to tell \u201cThe Bigfoot Story.\u201d If someone else had been telling the story, I think Belladonna would have been less attentive, but she did a good job of not oooing and ahhing. I wonder if I can talk him into telling it again with Barrett around. Once he was done, I saw Matron X look toward Karen again and decided something else needed to keep everyone\u2019s attention. I invited everyone into the Music Room for dancing. Then I asked Mom to dance.<br /> <br /> I think she must have taken it more as a challenge than an invitation. I didn\u2019t know if Mom knew how to ballroom dance or not, but she kept up with me in a waltz easily. Nightshade and Karen followed with a pair of dances, strictly for showing off. A tango to the Addams Family theme and then a stylish recreation of the contest dance from Pulp Fiction. Mom was looking through the vinyl after they were done. She frowned and asked me why we didn\u2019t have any proper dancing records in Spanish. I knew she wanted to Flamenco, so I hit the laptop Nightshade wired into the sound system. It took a moment, but I found a decent quality traditional guitar and clap meant for Flamenco. Mom was apparently looking to prove that I wasn\u2019t the only one that could dance. She set fire to the floor in a way that I couldn\u2019t have imagined. The applause was fitting for the number in attendance. The smirk Mom gave me as she walked back told me she had won whatever challenge she thought was issued. Jacob asked Belladonna to dance and though she was obviously terrified, she accepted. He made her look good for not knowing a step and I think I saw Matron X pointing something out to Nightshade from the corner of my eye, but I\u2019m not sure what was happening.<br /> <br /> When he came back, Axe asked Jacob if he could show her and Eris how to dance. She looked very nervous but he agreed. What that went on, Nightshade and Karen danced more normally for them, and then it was a group dance. Everyone started pairing off, though I did start a Conga Line at one point. Once I was off the floor but everyone else was still dancing to whatever they could, Jacob appeared beside me as if on cue. I think it\u2019s the power of storytellers to always be in the right place at the right time. Anyway, he mentioned that no one was dancing with Matron X. I looked around and found her alone to one side. I think she was just watching the event but I took the hint. When I walked up, I asked if she\u2019d like to dance again. She smiled and asked if we could Shag. I\u2019m very glad I knew she was from the Carolina coast. I was not very good at that style dance, but she made it look simple. I can attest, it was not. Still, it got her confidence and maybe a little of that mischief up. She then marched over and called Karen out. That might have been the most awkward I\u2019ve ever seen Karen on the dance floor.<br /> <br /> As their set was winding down, I asked Nightshade if she\u2019d like to do something special. It was partly for me, partly for Mom, and if I\u2019m honest, partly to show off. I knew Noriko didn\u2019t know how to ballroom dance and was already nervous around Mom. So I asked if we could do a Pasodoble. I again used the internet for music and Nightshade as my cape. If Mom wasn\u2019t sure I could be Mexican enough, I think I proved my roots.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> <b>Homecoming III</b><br /> <br /> \u201cI feel wonderful, you have no idea,\u201d the older woman said. Julie Lousler was sitting on the couch with her daughter Allison. Allison\u2019s daughter Natalie, Julie\u2019s granddaughter, lay across their laps, fast asleep. Her mother played idly with her hair.<br /> <br /> \u201cI am glad mom. It\u2019s important to me you feel better. I do seem to have that effect on people,\u201d said Allison, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, it\u2019s you, it\u2019s the whole group. Karen, Sara, Doc\u2026they make me feel so welcome, and we have such interesting conversations. The older woman chuckled. \u201cI am almost afraid I will have to remind them I am not their age.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt doesn\u2019t matter, Mom. You are you, that\u2019s what matters. You fit in here.\u201d She paused. \u201cYou know, you could come here more often. I mean, I will see you on Christmas, but we should arrange to come here more times. You should come in what passes for warm here in the summer,\u201d the younger woman said, smirking at the last part.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do feel almost like I have been sleepwalking for quite awhile, I admit. Stepping away from work, housework, all that\u2026it\u2019s unreal,\u201d Julie looked a bit distant. \u201cSitting here with you\u2026I wonder if I am dreaming.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou aren\u2019t. I\u2019m here. You know\u2026if you have been \u2018sleepwalking\u2019\u2026maybe\u2026you should date again. Live life again,\u201d Allison chose her words carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know, I am a bit old, and I don\u2019t know if anyone would be interested.\u201d<br /> <br /> Allison pointed at her sleeping daughter, \u201cSomeone has suggested you get quite a bit of attention from men at church,\u201d Allison leaned closer, bringing with her the scent of strawberries, \u201cAnd you are related to me, so I know you notice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI do, but moving on is hard,\u201d The older woman sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat could be the title of my biography,\u201d Allison said. \u201cJust an idea. Not pushing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt WOULD be a man, you know,\u201d the older woman smirked at her daughter.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo? I am obviously not against such arrangements. Some of my best friends are in straight relationships,\u201d Allison gave an exaggerated grin.<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. That reminds me\u2026thanks for being okay with me saying grace I remember it was\u2026a point of contention before you left,\u201d her mother looked seriously at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cI was rebelling. I don\u2019t mind anymore,\u201d The younger girl looked serious as well. \u201cThose demons have been put to bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I appreciate it anyway.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u2018Thanks for giving me the option too. I demurred mostly for Sunny\u2019s sake. She seems to feel out of place as is.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older woman nodded. \u201cThat was good of you.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause, as Allison played with her sleeping daughters hair while Julie silently watched her. After a short time, Allison spoke again.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo besides Thanksgiving and Christmas, maybe you could come up summer, say July or something. You are off from teaching, and we can ride on the yacht and walk in the park without freezing anything off. Probably a little earlier since the other two are so close together.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy birthday is in June. How about that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt could work. I would be very happy to see you again,\u201d Allison smiled warmly. Her mother smiled back then looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is surreal. I was so sure I had lost you, and even if I hadn\u2019t, we weren\u2019t speaking. Just this Easter I would never have believed we would talk again. Yet here we are, full of turkey, sitting and talking like old friends. I\u2019m\u2026happy.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was another pause, but this time both women were smiling. After a moment, Allison spoke again.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what do you think of the others?\u201d<br /> <br /> Julia looked thoughtful, \u201cI really like Karen. She is a sweet girl, and I see in her eyes how she worries about you. Be good to her. She watches you the way a woman should watch her spouse. Sara is fun, and I am conflicted about whether I wish I knew her as a younger woman or not. I don\u2019t dislike her, but I am still making up my mind a little. Doc is very nice, and like Karen he cares about you. Noriko, Eris, and Alice I don\u2019t know what to make of. If you were not\u2026you\u2026I would be worried.,\u201d She looked down at her granddaughter, \u201cI trust you to keep Natalie safe with them around.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlexia and Chandra are a cute couple. I met some Christian Indians before but she is the first Hindu\u2026she is Hindu right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHonestly? No clue. We have not talked about it. She has said she is not Muslim.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe wears Hindu clothes. Anyway, Simon and Tavia are reclusive but nice. Much like Alice and company, I would worry more if\u2026well, you were not you,\u201d Now the older woman was choosing her words carefully.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess Jacob and Sunny are new to both of us. I like Sunny, she seems to be trying to keep her bearings\u2026working with young people it\u2019s been easier for me. Jacob is rather handsome, of course. Maybe you have noticed\u201d<br /> <br /> Her daughter smiled. \u201cMaybe,\u201d Then after a moment, \u201cI meant what I said, Mom. I really do want to keep seeing you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad,\u201d Julie smiled. \u201cAnd while it may be clich\u00e9 to say\u2026I am proud of you. You have good friends. You are taking care of a good woman, and from what I hear, you are doing good things. You have grown into a beautiful and confidant young woman, and you care for your daughter. Whatever was between us, I am proud of the woman you have become.\u201d<br /> <br /> Allison sat speechless. \u201cTh-thanks Mom,\u201d she said eventually. I don\u2019t know how to respond.\u201d<br /> <br /> The older woman smiled. \u201cThen don\u2019t. Relax and enjoy a compliment well earned.\u201d<br /> <br /> The still form laying across their laps stirred. \u201cI should go to bed, and take her upstairs too. I leave you to your night, Allison,\u201d Julie helped Natalie up, turned and smiled, then headed upstairs.<br /> <br /> Allison, Natalie to all save two, stood up and got out her phone, sending a text to Doc, Noriko, Karen, and Sara: \u201cTime to work on Mom\u2019s present.\u201d<br /> <br /> Then she smiled, and left to room to stillness, and a lingering scent of strawberries that soon faded with her passing.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLIII</i><br /> <br /> Pretty much an RP session. These stories are helping PCs flesh out their backstories and advance their character somewhat. I thus don\u2019t have a lot of commentary. There have been some genuinely emotional moments, well played out, and more than one comment of \u201cI am going go and hug my [Parent/Sibling] now.\u201d<br /> <br /> It's worth noting after Doc's initial Dance Natalie and Karen swept across the floor to the Addam's family movie theme.<br /> <br /> Smaller cast than usual next time as we finish up Julie, Natalie and Sunny\u2019s stay. Please join us. In the meantime comments and questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-01-2015, 04:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-19T10:28:20-07:00","id":708972,"title":"","content":"Interesting interactions between Doc and his mother, Julie and Karen and Doc and Julie.<br /> Doc seemed quite puzzled by his perception of his mother's attitude, and so was I. Did she feel he'd forsaken his roots?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-21T13:18:19-07:00","id":712946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=708972#post708972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting interactions between Doc and his mother, Julie and Karen and Doc and Julie.<br /> Doc seemed quite puzzled by his perception of his mother's attitude, and so was I. Did she feel he'd forsaken his roots?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Didn't you know? Doc used to be a redhead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:24:01-07:00","id":715064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anteros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=708972#post708972\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interesting interactions between Doc and his mother, Julie and Karen and Doc and Julie.<br /> Doc seemed quite puzzled by his perception of his mother's attitude, and so was I. Did she feel he'd forsaken his roots?<br /> </div> </div> </div> </div> I had a really well reasoned response and then it got eaten (edit: Twice). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Let me sum up. This is a common theme among non-native ethnicities between generations.<br /> <br /> Specifically between Doc and Sunny: he feels like he has failed his mother by abandoning her after he healed his death wounds. She feels like she did something to push him away. They are both wrong and both feel badly over things they could easily talk through. Neither of them are willing to consider that as an option, believing &quot;it&quot; must be solely repaired by them individually, whatever IT is. Doc's insistence on trying to take care of everyone else but himself is perhaps an inherited trait.<br /> <br /> Additionally, Sunny never danced or really did anything fun for herself after Doc's father died so her ability (and interest) in dancing was completely lost on Doc. Her unnecessary nagging/chastising is actually her being stereotypical to mask her own insecurities and to keep Doc distracted so she can be a little more herself away from his view.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T12:24:53-07:00","id":715066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=712946#post712946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Didn't you know? Doc used to be a redhead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>That was awful.<br /> <br /> /slowclap<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This is just my bright, shiny two cents.<br /> <br /> Here's the thing. I try not to argue in forums. It's like pouring concrete in a river. It doesn't get you anywhere in the short term and it poisons the environment long term.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2668-asmenedas","name":"Asmenedas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2668_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-22T14:00:28-07:00","id":715405,"title":"","content":"The family stuff in this story is awesome. Also heartwarming. It can't rain all the time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-01T01:55:49-08:00","id":746216,"title":"","content":"Somewhat strange session. Sara\u2019s player had to miss for personal reasons, and Alice\u2019s was under the weather. Doc\u2019s promised to be there, so I had it anyway, and for more than half we just had Natalie and Alexia. Doc skyped in a bit over halfway though, so we got the moms their last evening there so we could move on to getting dear Sara back.<br /> <br /> Because of the nature of the session and Doc missing half, Natalie\u2019s journal is just a recap of the session from an OOC perspective. Doc\u2019s Log covers events while he was there. We have an Alice\u2019s journal, but it actually records events from a couple sessions ago her player had been intending to record. So it is not covering the same session Doc and Natalie are. Nonetheless, strange as it may be enjoy the reminder of the Julie and Sunny appearance for their thanksgiving visit.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CXLIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 1300 Hours, Friday, November 26, 2010<br /> <br /> Last night worked out at least as well as everyone hoped, as best I can tell. Which is good because today is rainy as hell so we\u2019re all still stuck together. I don\u2019t think we\u2019ve ever had a night in of dancing. So that\u2019s something to remember as well.<br /> <br /> I rolled out of bed about 0700 Hours and enjoyed a simple meditation before stretches and several hours of katas. I don\u2019t think anyone planned to fight with Black Friday madness and my shop is closed so the girls can get a real break. I feel like I might be back to where my muscle memory was at this point. I don\u2019t know how my training would translate to other styles or training methods. I\u2019d like to continue so I\u2019m planning to look online to see if I can find anything. If nothing else, I guess I could call the Naval bases over in New London to see if they have any leads.<br /> <br /> I came down after getting cleaned up around 1100 Hours to grab a snack. The rain apparently postponed the hiking trip to Sleeping Giant so Jacob was trying to relax. I don\u2019t think he was doing very well with that.<br /> <br /> After lunch, there was talk of some board game that sounded ridiculous to me, so Noriko and I are going to work on teaching each other Spanish and Japanese.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0045 Hours, Saturday, November 27, 2010<br /> <br /> That went better than I was afraid it might. Most all the family are heading out later today but Matron X declared her intention to visit the 27 Club while it was open so we all put on the glitz.<br /> <br /> Everyone dressed up somehow. Cupcake went very feminine with a mermaid dress and Chandra matched with a top hat and tails. Nightshade and Belladonna dressed like goth twins, which was a little disturbing for me. Matron X dressed in a formal evening gown which got everyone\u2019s attention. Noriko put some extensions in her hair and wore a leather vest that showed off her navel piercing. I didn\u2019t go too crazy since I didn\u2019t want to freak Mom out. I wore a pair of black leather pants and a crimson silk shirt with some wingtips I could dance in, just in case.<br /> <br /> Speaking of, Mom seemed entirely too familiar and comfortable in that kind of setting for my brain to process. She didn\u2019t have anything particularly fancy to wear but at one point I glanced over and she looked like still shot from Casablanca or something. Posed, confident, relaxed; it was all very odd. I don\u2019t think I\u2019d ever seen Mom like that before. And I\u2019m not sure what I think about it either. I don\u2019t think anyone expected Matron X to be so fond of Tantrum either. She walked up in a full suit and immediately had Matron X\u2019s attention until she walked away.<br /> <br /> We had a fair amount of standard bar talk, which also included Belladonna trying to order whiskey. Then there was the sudden realization that I had made no plans with or even mentioned Christmas to Mom. This was followed by a sense of failure and panic that I was not expecting or prepared for. Honestly I thought I was going to be sick. Matron X realized something was up and tried to smooth things over, but it was for Mom and I to work out. After a few acts and a few hours, Tantrum came to our table and asked for Karen, Noriko, and I to meet with Nightshade. It was time for Matron X\u2019s surprise. We gathered on stage to more than a few catcalls and wolf whistles. But the performance was very well received. I moved heavy things and hit a tambourine very well. As a group however, we sounded way better than a few nights of practice should have. The others are very talented. Matron X smiled broadly as we started the song and managed to only tear up slightly when Nightshade finished with, \u201cI love you, Mom.\u201d That also drove the place nuts with applause.<br /> <br /> Now to figure out what or if I need to work out with Mom for Christmas. Talking to her should not be this stressful. I just feel like I should already know and because I don\u2019t, I\u2019m ...less attentive? I don\u2019t know. I should probably just sit down and talk with her on the way to the airport like a grown up. We\u2019ll see how well I pull that off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> It's the night before Thanksgiving, and I've brought Jacob to meet my werewolf friends at Sleeping Giant. He's a big hit. Jacob's always had a way with people. He's outgoing and charismatic. I kind of envy that about him. Even though he's just met Ildefonso, Deirdre, Barrett and Tanya, he's already joking around and telling stories like they're old friends. Tanya's flirting shyly with him, and Deirdre's encouraging them. I think Tanya and Jacob would get on well together.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, Eris and I are sitting together on the couch, watching the spectacle. I don't mind. I've always been more reserved than my brother in large gatherings, and besides, it's nice to snuggle up with my girlfriend near the fire place in the pack's cozy lodge.<br /> <br /> <i>Don't get too cozy. You sense it, don't you? The barely perceptible scent of your brother's fear?</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress has been blessedly quiet lately, and I grimace inwardly as her voice echoes in the back of my mind. Then I realize that she's not trying to start an argument or give me a hard time. She's merely curious. She's noticed something I should have picked up on sooner. Jacob is nervous. Not much, and he's hiding it well, but something is making him uneasy.<br /> <br /> As if to punctuate that thought, Jacob asks Ildefonso and the others, &quot;So, are you guys ex-military?&quot; They look at one another and shake their heads.<br /> <br /> &quot;No,&quot; answers Ildefonso. &quot;I mean, we're park rangers, of course, so we have law enforcement training, and we're experienced hunters. But we've never been military.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jacob doesn't probe any further, but now that the Huntress has drawn my attention to it, I can tell what he's thinking. He senses something predatory and dangerous about my werewolf friends. And I think he's realized, on a subconscious level, that he's more prey here than predator.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> When we arrive back at the mansion it's late. I tell Eris that I'd like some time with my brother, and she scurries off to bed ahead of me. Jacob and I head to the kitchen and I grab us a couple of Coronas from the fridge.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm glad you came, Jacob. It's really brightened my spirits.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Happy to oblige,&quot; he replies as we raise our beers in a lazy toast. &quot;I'll say this. You run with a strange crowd these days.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Stranger than my friends in Portland?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you kidding? Those guys were positively vanilla compared to the people here. It's good, though. They seem good.&quot;<br /> <br /> I can sense the tension hanging on the end of his words, like there's something else he wants to say but doesn't quite know if he should say it. I know what it is, so I give him a little push.<br /> <br /> &quot;What did you think of my ranger friends. They're a fun bunch, huh?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh yeah,&quot; Jacob smiles reflexively. A moment later, the smile fades. &quot;But are they okay? I mean, they seemed\u2026I don't know\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Dangerous?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, I didn't want to put it that way, but yeah. I guess so.&quot; Jacob sighs and takes another swig of beer. &quot;Look, Freckles, when you're on the road as much as I am, you get good at reading people, and you get pretty good at sensing when someone is dangerous. It's a kind of survival mechanism, I guess. Your friends back there tripped all the triggers.&quot; As he says this Jacob looks at me intently. I can tell he's worried about me, but is there more to it than that? Am I triggering his 'danger sense' too?<br /> <br /> &quot;I won't lie to you, Jacob. The guys at Sleeping Giant are dangerous, but not to you or me. They\u2026look out for people like us, I guess. Kind of like the police, in a way.&quot;<br /> <br /> Jacob gives me a dubious look. &quot;I'm just worried about you, Freckles. I know you've had it rough lately, and I don't want you running with a bad crowd.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;They aren't bad, Jacob. They're good people, and I'm not just saying that. I'd trust them with my life.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Just so long as they aren't going to attack <i>me</i> or anything.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Seriously? It's not like that.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;If you say so,&quot; he looks straight in my eyes and nods.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> It's Thanksgiving day, and the family drama is running high in the mansion. Doc's mother is a sweetheart, but Natalie's mom is even more manipulative than her daughter. I think she means well, but she really rubs me the wrong way. I'm trying to stay out of her way as much as possible.<br /> <br /> That's one reason I'm walking out into the freezing cold of the mansion's backyard cemetery instead of snuggling up in front of the fireplace with a cup of Alexia's amazing hot chocolate. The other reason is that Eris and Noriko are both out here somewhere.<br /> <br /> I find them both sitting in a tree, talking. Now that they've been formally introduced, the two of them are becoming fast friends, and Noriko helps bring Eris out of her shell, which makes me happy. As I approach, they wave.<br /> <br /> &quot;What the heck are you guys <i>doing</i> in that tree? It's freezing out here!&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh, it's not that bad,&quot; says Noriko. &quot;And besides, aren't we planning on going out hiking Saturday? It's still going to be cold then.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Well, yeah,&quot; I respond defensively, &quot;but that's different. We'll be doing something. Staying active will keep the chill off.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We're doing something, &quot; Eris says brightly. &quot;Come up and sit with us!&quot;<br /> <br /> I only hesitate a moment. Sure, I'm shivering from the cold, and sitting in the wind-blown branches of a tree does not sound the least bit fun to me right now. But Eris really looks like she wants me to join them, and if I'm up there, I'm with her. So I climb up and snuggle up next to her for warmth. We stay there, chatting, laughing, and freezing our butts off for about thirty minutes.<br /> <br /> Then Eris says, &quot;We should go in so Alice can thaw out.&quot; She turns to me and leans in close to nibble my ear lobe. It sends pleasant shivers down my spine. &quot;Thank you,&quot; she whispers. &quot;This meant a lot to me. How about we go in and warm up together in the hot tub?&quot; As she pulls away, her smile is bright and genuine (and a little bit sultry), and it warms me up enough to stay out here another few hours if I have to. I'm not going to turn down the hot tub, though, so we drop from the tree and head indoors, arm in arm.<br /> <br /> It's amazing how little things can make you fall in love with someone all over again. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> It was rainy, so the girls stayed back and played board games while Doc, Noriko, and Sunny worked on Spanish and Japanese. Alexia, Chandra, Natalie Knight, Julie, Natalie Lousler, and Karen played. Alexia initially won a game of Candyland, then suggested Trivial Pursuit. They did \u201cDisney Princess\u201d edition, with Alexia and Julie dominating and Julie winning by a die roll. Then because of Chandra talking about Bollywood versions of these films they watched the Bollywood version of <i>Aladdin</i>. After being beaten at Disney Natalie insisted on Rock Trivial Pursuit and won by a landslide. They finished up by playing the Barbie Board Game. Natalie Lousler dropped out because \u201cyou have to have a boyfriend\u201d and she is \u201cnot into guys\u201d despite Karen pointing out she kept checking Jacob out. Karen bowed because the game was designed for four players. With younger Natalie leaning on her mom\u2019s back playing with her phone, Natalie Knight lost hard (0 successes on 7 dice) while Chandra and Julie duked it out. Again, with a lucky roll Julie became homecoming queen, while Natalie ended up with \u201cBiff\u201d and a cheap dress. Julie pointed out this was different from her high school, as she was not homecoming queen but was much prettier than the girl who won.<br /> <br /> The 27 Club affair went fairly smoothly. Chandra wore a suit and Alexia a white mermaid dress, while younger Natalie dressed identically to older. Tatum was introduced early on, with Julie and Natalie Lousler both being rather affected by her. Natalie Lousler accused Julie of checking her out, which Julia simply noted, \u201cShe is rather pretty.\u201d She also complimented Tatum\u2019s collar, which lead to some shuffled feet. When Tatum left, Natalie Lousler expressed interest but Julie suggested if Natalie Knight was not involved her Julie would buy her [Natalie Lousler] a car. Eventually, Natalie Lousler admitted she had no new car in her immediate future. She did flirt with Tatum, but only got 1 success.<br /> <br /> While there Julie noted Natalie, Sara and Karen (and \u201canyone they may decide to invite\u201d with a sideways glance at Tatum and Karen talking) were coming down to Christmas if Sunny wanted to come. Sunny was unsure. Doc became uneasy and left the table while Sunny was saying she was unsure of her plans. Karen and Noriko followed, and Doc admitted he had not considered Christmas. Karen went back to change the subject, and Noriko assured him it was okay and she was up for whatever. Eventually they returned and, for the second time that night, Natalie Lousler was not given alcohol she asked for.<br /> <br /> Tatum summoned Doc, Karen, and Noriko to \u201chelp Natalie with something back there\u201d and sat down at the table. There was a quiet conversation between her and Julie that Natalie Lousler tried and failed to eavesdrop on, and after subtly preparing her phone to record, Tatum went up and announced something special for a special guest was to be performed, revealing Natalie, Karen, Sara, Doc, and Noriko doing their presentation. Karen assisted Natalie on the roll, who used her rote action ability and got 9 successes. Julie was clearly touched but maintained her composure. Natalie cried after telling her mother in front of everyone that she loved her and going to the table though.<br /> <br /> Wound up after that. The plan is to have the mom\u2019s leave Saturday and take up that afternoon.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLIV</i><br /> <br /> In general, for the board games (outside Candyland, which was random) we had people making some general rolls for performance. In the trivial pursuit game, it was Intelligence + 1-5 based on how much the player/GM felt the character knew about Disney/Music. Intelligence + Wits was used for the Barbie game, which my wife actually owned a copy of and had played before. Her descriptions were hilarious. Honestly, the whole board game scene was an absolute blast with a lot of excellent RPing.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s journal pretty well covers any/all die rolls for the 27 Club. Steppin' Out (originally by Joe Jackson) was performed.<br /> <br /> Okay, whole gang should be back next time. The mom\u2019s are headed home (expect a fic about that from Natalie, already being written) and we move along to the hike. We hope you will join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T17:25:40-08:00","id":759564,"title":"","content":"Some of the feedback I get on the forums are from PMs or discussions outside the forum threads where the games are discussed. A number of them can be applied pretty broadly to my games, so I paraphrased some and put some info down here to \u201cdraw back the curtain\u201d as it were as I thought some would be of interest to some readers. Add your own if you wish, as always.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of female characters in your games. Like, most of them. Is this on purpose?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. Some of it is deliberate. Media is all about men, and many TV shows, movies, books and, honestly, role-playing campaigns have few females that are often lovers, prizes, victims or relatives. I try to make women who fit every conceivable role, but have many male characters too.<br /> <br /> At the same time, I just come up with female characters more easily, and since I cull pictures from the internet which provide inspiration for PCs, the fact that I have way more female pictures means I get inspired for female characters more often. That is not deliberate, just the way it turns out.<br /> <br /> <b>How about LGBTQ characters? Same?</b><br /> <br /> Most NPCs are actually Herosexual. With a few exceptions such as Tavia Fishborn or Karen Smith/Knight most NPCs orientation is such that they would be interested in PCs interested in them. Those with exceptions are NPCs whose concept defines their sexuality, and they are rare. Then sometimes as I see them in action NPCs seem to make good couples or drift together. I have no bias to create gay or straight couples this way. It just happens. However, see above that women outnumber men. I am proud, however, of the queer representation in my games.<br /> <br /> Of course, just because an NPC could fall for a PC of either sex does not mean they are equally easy to woo. Tatum Gillis could go either way but is easier for women, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>No gay male relationships with PCs, but there are several lesbians\u2026</b><br /> <br /> I don\u2019t tell my players what orientation to make their PCs. If a male character wants to have a relationship with a male NPC that\u2019s fine (it even happened in my <i>Masquerade</i> game) but it is what the players want.<br /> <br /> <b>You have less Trans characters than I expected.</b><br /> <br /> Yea, not so impressive regarding those numbers. Raindancer, and informant from the Blood Bather story, is the only trans person in the game so far.<br /> <br /> <b>You have a lot of, um, sex in your game. Is everyone okay with it?</b><br /> <br /> Yes, yes I do. I will speak plainly. Sex for me is way more interesting than violence. I\u2019d be more interested in seeing a PC having a torrid affair than a gunfight. This does not mean my games are without action; <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has a setting conceit allowing for more danger and daring-do since the conceit prevents a PC revolving door. There is more action there than other games. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has more action than <i>Balance of Shadows</i> or <i>Malibu Dream House</i>, because it is spy-noir, while <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is part noir, part mystery, part pulp. But yes, relationships are a huge thing.<br /> <br /> My players know this, and new players are told before they join. No player has to play romantic relationships, straight or queer.<br /> <br /> For the record, we almost always fade to black unless there is a good reason not to, and sex is only rolled if something besides having a good time is going on, such as getting a foe vulnerable, staying awake so the PC can rummage through their partners stuff, staying awake so their partner can\u2019t rummage through theirs, impressing a countess, etc.<br /> <br /> <b>So everyone has pictures, can I see a picture of [NPC]?</b><br /> <br /> Probably. If it is a picture culled from the internet and you want to see an NPC, I will show it unless I am using the picture with particular permission of the photographer or model, in which case no because they have not given me permission for that.<br /> <br /> <b>How many of your players are women/lesbian/bisexual/giraffes/etc</b><br /> <br /> I am not going to give out too much information on my players. I will say every game linked in my sig has a mix of male and female and straight and LGBTQ players. Most games hover somewhere close to 50/50 male female, or one more of one or the other. <i>The Golden Eagle</i> is the exception, with many more women than men. . I will tell you, if you have read about a female PC having relationships with female NPCs in these games and assumed they are being played by a guy you will be wrong much more often than not.<br /> <br /> <b>Do Players plan their PCs relationships before the game starts?</b><br /> <br /> Not usually. Sometimes they have an idea getting together is likely. We had some idea Doc and Natalie would have romantic tension, for example.<br /> <br /> <b>What genre would you call your games</b><br /> <br /> Mystery/Supernatural Drama. <i>Balance of Shadows</i> has ghost story elements. <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> has noir and spy elements, and <i>The Golden Eagle</i> has noir, pulp, and mystery. <i>Malibu Dream House</i> is more pure mystery-drama.<br /> <br /> <b>Can I play in your game?</b><br /> <br /> Probably not. If you live in North Carolina we can discuss it, but even then probably not. My games are almost all full.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where Doc and Natalie see their moms off, and Alice's secret is compromised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters