ath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-18T23:25:27-08:00","id":768989,"title":"","content":"Thanks. I am on it.<br /> <br /> Edit: I found it and fixed it, you were correct. It was a transposing issue. It is fixed now. Thank you so much for letting me know! Feel free to drop feedback as you like even if it is...from a few sessions back. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 11-19-2015, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T19:53:20-08:00","id":777511,"title":"","content":"Alrighty, all caught up! My my my this has been quite the journey; everyone has grown so much, and quite powerful too I assume. It's a shame that characters were lost over time due to real life scenarios, and the subplots involved with them, but you guys certainly upheld the quality of the game. No jumping the shark moments as far as I can see. The situations are imaginative, have a great deal of continuity, and they tailor to various characters to encourage development, even allowing development without being intended for it. I loved how the romance between Karl and Jasmine slowly bloomed, and how Doc and Natalie entered a romance, and exited it messily before smoothing things over; Alexia and Chandra's relationship, while never exactly told from either perspective, was great to read, and it's seriously wonderful that they're not having huge amounts of drama that make them split up, join together, split up, ect. They're all great to read up on, and the journals have been a really interesting method of reading the different perspectives from - Doc giving Natalie space for a touchy subject is interpreted by her as being judgmental, and there are valid arguments for both interpretations.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about a few things though. When Gwen and Jasmine were replaced (spoilers to all coming in late), were the new characters given the same amount of XP so they could keep up with the rest of the krewe? I know Alice came in with more than the starting amount (justified by being part of an earlier krewe), but Sara came in around the point that it was acceptable for her to be starting-ish-tier. Also, as Simon's player is no longer active yet the character is fairly essential for the game to go on, is Simon going to be NPCed, or will he simply be considered there but not interacted with onscreen as it were (like Maris from Fraiser)?<br /> <br /> Also on the subject of characters having to leave (odd theme, I know), whatever happened to the Beast under Murder Ballads? Its plotline was started and given some urgency due to its growing power, but once the wedding of Bonnie Lynn came to focus (and Gwen's player had to leave) it seemed to be slowly forgotten (particularly since Murder Ballads has been host to many events without any, well, event). Was that a deliberate excision, or an accident? I appreciate it was from relatively early in the game, so bringing it up again may be a bit awkward. Same with the whole Angel of Wrath Geist deal.<br /> <br /> Also, slight detail, but what happened to Daisy from the plot Troy was involved in? Her ghost was cooked (literally), and they put her into a bottle so she'd be unaware until they could afford to heal her. That was the last detail of her before everyone vanished.<br /> <br /> Also also, what particularly about Beats do you and your players not enjoy? I've not delved too deeply into the God-Machine changes aside from the Virtues and Vices changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T22:14:01-08:00","id":777543,"title":"","content":"Taidragon, for clarity I am gonna respond to your post in a post below this.<br /> <br /> In which the Werewolf situation escalates. Hard.<br /> <br /> Circumstances (holidays and other stuff) prevent a Doc or Alice this time, but Natalie and Sara are on the job<br /> <i><br /> Session CXLVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Well, a day that promised mischief and fun at breakfast has taken a serious turn. I can\u2019t really complain - I just missed out on watching Noriko and Chandra conspire against Doc, poor Jacob missed out on quality time with the ladies at Sleeping Giant. He\u2019s left town now, headed back out on the road. I hope he\u2019ll be back. I\u2019m sure he will.<br /> <br /> And Alice will probably forgive me. Not that she was upset, just a little, well, embarrassed, I think. It was a kinda of awkward breakfast, between that and Tatum coming down before my lovelies. She relaxed once I was there though. Even Doc\u2019s meditative vibe was getting dinged with curiosity, since Noriko and Chandra were whispering about a \u2018master plan\u2019, giggling, and glancing at him. All that got pushed aside though, when Zed called Doc just after breakfast.<br /> <br /> I haven\u2019t mentioned Zed before - he\u2019s one of the \u2018family\u2019 of Touched that Angelique and Eris belong to. Angelique has been recovering nicely, but for safety\u2019s sake had been staying with another pair of the same, Austin and Erin Callahan. And late yesterday, Angelique had discovered they were missing. Maybe not the most alarming thing, but given the circumstances, there was a buddy/check-in system in place, and they had skipped out on that. Plus, they weren\u2019t answering their phone.<br /> <br /> The reason Zed called Doc was not the one we might have wanted, that being so that we could help out. See, the two Callahans, Zed, Malard and Angelique are one unit. Eris and the other folks at the Sleeping Giant are another. And there\u2019s a little bit of a rivalry. And Connecticut is kinda chilly this time of year. So... they wanted to talk with Eris, as a potential suspect. Doc too, to a lesser extent, cause there\u2019s specific beef between him and Erin.<br /> <br /> So that was tense. And worrisome. Natalie sent Karen and Tatum out. Alice asked Jacob to leave a little early. He was going to today anyway, just this afternoon. He really didn\u2019t want to leave, especially when she said there might be danger - he\u2019s quite the hero - but I managed to convince him she was safe, and that she would be destroyed if something happened to him because of her.<br /> <br /> The meeting itself actually went pretty well. Except for Noriko glaring serious daggers at Angelique, which pissed our Little Red off. It was heartwrenching to hear Angelique talking with Alice. The poor dear. Honestly, I\u2019m not entirely sure Malard\u2019s group is going to weather the current storm. I hope we can do something to get her safe haven if they don\u2019t. With the way Noriko\u2019s acting, I don\u2019t know if here will be one though.<br /> <br /> Anyway, shit kept getting shoveled into the fan in the here and now. Zed wanted to check up on our story about the hike, and when he did, Deirdre started going off on him. Ildefonso was trying to make a deal to work out a momentary setting aside of the rivalry, and she went off on him. Eris tried to talk her down, and she even went off on her. So Alice and Eris went up to the Sleeping Giant to see what was up there while we checked out the house the Callahan\u2019s disappeared from.<br /> <br /> it was quite a party since Chandra, Angelique, Zed, Malard, and all the Touched of the troupe minus Alice and Noriko were there. Noriko had stormed off and not come back after Alice called her on being unkind to Angelique and it seemed best to let it stand at that. At the house we got right down to it. Since my Sight gives me visions of the past, and Alexia\u2019s lets her ask specific questions of an object\u2019s memory, I went first. The fragments of visions I saw were intriguing - especially the one where Erin argued with her brother in the kitchen, naked - but I could only focus on one, and the one that was most recent, the one with no emotional overtones, seemed most likely to give evidence of spiritual tampering. It showed Austin stopping mid-dish-drying, moving purposefully for the door. Erin joined him there and they left together without speaking to each other.<br /> <br /> I tried to trace back her steps. The next vision came in her office, where she\u2019d been Googling dietary needs in early pregnancy. It painted a fairly clear, if lurid, picture. They were blood relatives, distant cousins, only adopted siblings, but there was also the taboo against sexual relationships among their mystical \u2018family\u2019. And between Alexia\u2019s questions, and the fact that Angelique had been living there a while and they were... not quiet, it was clear who the father was. According to Angelique, they two aren\u2019t a couple, it\u2019s just that they fight a lot, and their fights have something of an aftermath. I, personally, think there are worse ways to end a fight, but...<br /> <br /> Of course, since we are dealing with a rogue lust spirit, their relationship and its taboo nature makes them more susceptible to its influence. So there\u2019s that. That doesn\u2019t explain Deirdre though, as far as I know. She wound up challenging Ildefonso for leadership, formally, and it got ugly. Fortunately, Alice and Eris got there before it got too ugly. She\u2019s restrained for now, and really not in her right mind.<br /> <br /> Then again, I\u2019m not sure any of us are. We went to Glenwood! The Callahan\u2019s car was found there, by Zed\u2019s police contacts. So, the two groups, with Deidre no longer making a fuss, worked out that truce. Then Doc stood as a go between for Raul and the folks in Glenwood and our friends here. Those problems go way, way beyond rivalry. I had to hide behind our Little Red when Doc even mentioned Raul - I thought the two groups first united effort might be to tear through Doc and maybe not stop with him. Angelique, however, reminded everyone of ancient pacts (not with each other - the groups hate each other too much for that, but with old spirits) and Zed kept them focused on the real enemy, so everything was peachy.<br /> <br /> Except we had to go to Glenwood. I\u2019m not sure I would have pried Natalie off with a crowbar if I wanted to. And I sure didn\u2019t want to. If one must go to Glenwood, then as part of a caravan of powerful Touched people, in Alice\u2019s car, being held tightly by my lovely Natalie, is probably the best way to go.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> November 28th, 2010<br /> <br /> -Pretty face to wake up to! ^_^<br /> <br /> -Hehehe Ticklish! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -This feels like it could be a good day! Gotta get my girls together for fun\u2026and hopefully good conversation. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Oh-oh.<br /> <br /> -Well, that ended quickly. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Okay, we can handle this.<br /> <br /> -Oh\u2026right\u2026Angelique and Eris. ::nervous laugh::<br /> <br /> -Oh right, Angelique and Noriko.<br /> <br /> -Oh Goddess just end this now. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -Okay things seem to be calming. Maybe we can help them.<br /> <br /> -Noriko seriously!<br /> <br /> -Oh Goddess damnit what now?<br /> <br /> -Oh, shit.<br /> <br /> -@Nerak\u2026it\u2019s bad. We are okay, but it\u2019s bad.<br /> <br /> -Headed over to the Callahan\u2019s House.<br /> <br /> -Let this not end horribly.<br /> <br /> -Could this room be more tense?<br /> <br /> -OH FUCK SERIOUSLY?<br /> <br /> -SERIOUSLY<br /> <br /> -SERIOUSLY<br /> <br /> -DAMNIT IT.<br /> <br /> -Alice, we are okay but it\u2019s bad.<br /> <br /> -Yea call me.<br /> <br /> -@Nerak, we are okay, but it\u2019s bad. Real bad.<br /> <br /> -Sara is right, I guess, where else would the car be?<br /> <br /> -I feel queasy already.<br /> <br /> -Okay! Time to head from the super tense house to the incredibly tense meeting.<br /> <br /> -It is nice outside, a bit warmer than past couple days. Could me and my loves be doing anything but this? L<br /> <br /> -I don\u2019t want to go in.<br /> <br /> -Alice seriously.<br /> <br /> -Well this is\u2026tense.<br /> <br /> -@Nerak back home yet?<br /> <br /> -Ah Doc, making tense situations more tense since\u2026when did we meet again?<br /> <br /> -Could have gone worse. Still, I want to scream.<br /> <br /> -Could we not go to Glenwood?<br /> <br /> -Please?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLVI</i><br /> <br /> Whelp, that is going to shit isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> Reading between the lines with Sara, there is problems in the Werewolf pack. While she is a bit obscure in describing it, hopefully folks can read between the lines. If it is truly opaque to anyone, however, drop questions and I will answer.<br /> <br /> There is a lot of speculation Malard\u2019s pack is not going to survive this, whether the Callahans do or not. The divisions are serious now, and trust is decaying. Of course, it is what the Bale Hounds do.<br /> <br /> Sara used the Reading the Echoes Ceremony to look into the past, while Alexia used Industrial Oracle. Sara\u2019s visions helped Alexia know what to ask.<br /> <br /> Last session went well, and the chase continues. Join us then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-30T22:38:56-08:00","id":777550,"title":"","content":"(Okay, for clarity, new post right over this one for 146 just went up)<br /> <br /> Taidragon,<br /> <br /> First. Thanks so much for the feedback. I am really glad you have enjoyed the journals. If your really like the style, I do recommend checking out my Changeling, Demon, or Crossover game...None have the amount of stuff this one (at this writing, Changeling is at 44, Demon 31, Xover 18, so even combined still ~50 sessions less than Geist) does but all are quite good and all have suitably complicated relationships. Golden Eagle has a Sin-Eater, but no journals from him so far. And yea, the Krewe are pretty potent at this point. I could probably post Natalie or Alexia's stats if interested.<br /> <br /> I usually give ~5 XP per session, so Sara was given Sessionsx5 XP, and Storiesx3 XP. That did not account for Flaws or Journals, but good enough for an incoming character. Jasmine's player had noted the amount earned by her, so Alice was given that precise number since it was the same player. As for Simon, generally he is going to be assumed to be around but dealing with family stuff, rather than doing much otherwise with the Krewe. He will be NPC'd as necessary, though any major character stuff will be checked with his player first (we are in touch, his brother is currently in some of my other games if nothing else). It is not impossible things will align such that he could guest star again, but I would not count on it, and it would like before be for one session.<br /> <br /> The Beast under Murder Ballads has been quiescent for awhile, but could flare up again. The Short answer is there is going to be a time jump (unsure for how long) soon, so while I am advancing stories I am not picking up new ones, or racking the coals too much yet. I will probably have that flare back up at some point. The long answer was part of that plans was getting information from the great library for leverage, and OOC enthusiasm for a really look multi-session dungeon crawl is low. We enjoy hitting the Underworld (and will be again soon) but something super long is less drawing interest, plus someone showed who has a bit more knowledge of the Stryx (Dantaine) and other stuff means a new approach is needed\u2026and it has not become an issue again. The contest and Natalie\u2019s influence has made Murder Ballads less psychically problematic, but it needs dealing with sometime.<br /> <br /> The Angel of Wrath WILL come up again...the PCs chose to leave that be for awhile, which may not have been wise. I am just undecided if he will make trouble as a Geist or Sin-Eater. Daisy was laid to rest with the rest, just within the bottle. At this time, only Troy is left.<br /> <br /> Overall the major issue with the Beats system is bookkeeping. Our Demon game uses it and it works fine there, but it has a smaller number of PCs. Keeping up with beats is problematic; at the end it is easy to forget, and during it breaks immersion to keep doing it. That said, it is working fine in Demon and I have no issue with it. Just has not been the popular choice.<br /> <br /> Thanks for the feedback. If you think of anything else let me know\u2026your comments are welcome.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-14T00:34:52-08:00","id":785811,"title":"","content":"The Pursuit is on. Even as they attempt to close in on their foe, though, their coalition threatens to tear itself apart.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXLVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> And for that matter, for a trip to Glenwood, it was not so bad. Natalie and I had just reached the end of I'll Be With You In Apple Blossom Time when we pulled up at a shut down bank. The place had a very unpleasant vibe to it, but then again, it was in Glenwood. The rangers, along with Alice, wasted no time in setting up a perimeter while the rest of us used our Sight to get an idea of what had happened there.<br /> <br /> My visions made it pretty clear why there was a particularly bad feeling about the place, as I caught glimpses of the reason the bank was closed down - a couple of teller went on a literal face-eating spree. Rawl told us later that it was due to the influence of a group of cannibalism spirits. A slight silver lining - someone had actually cleared them out. Of course, that meant we couldn\u2019t interrogate them but... I\u2019ll take it.<br /> <br /> The vision I actually focused on was of the Callahans, who had abandoned their car, still half full of gas, spoken with something invisible, and headed off on foot. The others were able to track them sing their Sight, but first we had to deal with the drama inside the bank. And boy was there drama. In many different flavors.<br /> <br /> Firstly. So, I mentioned to you that Angelique\u2019s mentor had been one of this faction of bad guys. At our best guess, the one here, Bright Shadows, is using her mentor\u2019s knowledge of her to impersonate our mysterious beauty. Really, I should maybe say it\u2019s our best hope - it might be her sister. Angelique really didn\u2019t think so though. And her physical features were the least similar thing about her. But her clothing and build were very close, and most damning, since our allies don\u2019t have the visions Alexia and I do, the psychic impression she left behind is nearly identical. Zed was able to tell the difference, because of how long they\u2019d known each other and his keen Sight. Alice was able to as well, because of how intimate they\u2019d been. The poor dear, when Doc was upfront with the Sleeping Giant group so they wouldn\u2019t leap to conclusions, and she had to confirm that it definitely wasn\u2019t Angelique who had been there... she is so adorable when she blushes. And let\u2019s just say, that her hair is not why I call her our Little Red.<br /> <br /> Anyways, adorable blushing aside, they all accepted it wasn\u2019t Angelique, though Tanya was still distrustful as to how Bright Shadows was able to mimic her so closely. Another bit of excitement turned out to be not immediately pertinent, as the weapon Bright Shadows had come to the bank to retrieve was long gone by the time she\u2019d gotten there, taken by someone with the ability to conceal themselves from the Sight. That will almost assuredly come back to bite us in the ass in a not good way, seeing as a collection of 7 or 8 powerful spirits locked away by pre-fall demon summoners were not to be taken lightly. But at least Bright Shadows didn\u2019t have them.<br /> <br /> The last bit of drama came after Angelique performed a ritual in the bank. Lords and ladies, she is super hot, and the mystical power she commands is so intriguing. That, combined with how bruised her past has left her, tore my heart, and I wanted to do a hell of a lot more than give her a quick hug of encouragement. But we had a job to do and besides, the lust spirit from before wasn\u2019t done with her. The ritual had the unintended side effect of provoking a response from it, and only Doc\u2019s quick thinking and Natalie\u2019s quick use of some counter emotion control let Angelique stay in possession of her facilities.<br /> <br /> That all done, we followed the trail to an abandoned gas station. It was a little harrowing, as Rawl (who met us at the bank) had lost contact with his people, so we weren't sure if we were on a collision course or not. Luckily, we weren\u2019t. Not so luckily, contact was lost because one of the groups turned on each other, and the second had simply disappeared. Rawl\u2019s dealing with that mess now, and he\u2019s promised to let us know about what else might go on.<br /> <br /> So, like I said, the trail led to an abandoned gas station. Such places you might expect some lingering smell of gasoline, but this place absolutely reeked of it. The trap was obvious, so we planned carefully. Our Little Red scouted it out, and found a sentry spirit, so Angelique prepared a trap for it. I cursed Alexia so that fire refused to be in her presence, to keep the place from going up. Luckily, I\u2019m not quite good enough that she felt the full effect of fate turning against her. It must be an uncomfortable position, being our curse bearer, but sometimes, and it pains me to say this, fire is not our friend.<br /> <br /> It went well, extracting the Callahans. With the neutralization of the spirit, they were in their right-ish minds. Austin was confused, and defensive, but Mr. Malard took control of that situation. Erin was in more trouble. Something Bright Shadows had done had interfered with the baby, speeding its growth so that it was four months along, while her body was only one month along. If not for her gifts, she wouldn\u2019t have survived long enough for us to find him. To make things more complicated, what with the deception, she\u2019s pretty sure Angelique did it to her. Doc did what he could - shifting the baby to a better position, giving her as much painkillers as he could without risking the baby. Right now, we don\u2019t have a long term solution, unfortunately.<br /> <br /> However, she is stable now, so Doc has gone to see if he can help Deirdre out. Alice and I are looking after Erin, and also Angelique. Zed and Malard were feeling overextended looking after Angelique and Austin both, and since Angelique\u2019s mystical knowledge was essential, especially while Deirdre was incapacitated, we were more than willing to give them a hand with that. So she\u2019s staying with us, and never with anyone, especially Alice, alone, as there\u2019s still worry about outside influences. Eris is here as well, which certainly helps with Alice\u2019s self control. Noriko is not, as her dislike of Angelique has fanned into hatred and she fears for her own self control. Chandra is also not here, as she\u2019s gone to help Doc. Karen and Tatum are at the town house, being the two non-Touched of us and this the most in danger. The rest of us are holding down the fort, and waiting for some answers. Fate willing, we\u2019ll get some soon.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Karen &amp; Tatum,<br /> <br /> I am sorry ladies, this is not how this was supposed to go. I had promised a lot of bonding time, maybe some trips out, get some clothes, all that good stuff, but shit, as they say, has happened.<br /> <br /> I asked Karen to fill you in the \u201cWerewolf Situation,\u201d Tatum, and assume she has done so. Sorry you had to figure it out this way, but you said you wanted to be part of my life, not peripheral, and that means some things you may not have been prepared for.<br /> <br /> So here is the updates, and yes, you two are staying in the townhouse until this blows over. Try not to have TOO much fun without me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> We made it out to (ugh) Glenwood. Sara was an absolute doll, taking such good care of me. Karen, I know you were worried but she helped a lot. I may even be halfway stable when we need meet because of her. The car was at a bank, and after some peripheral shifting, we figured out the Bale Hound had been to the bank, looking for something left by the Mages (the ones we killed the last of after they caused an Abyssal Intrusion). It was stolen before she (yes she) arrived. They smell similar to Angelique, but are not the same\u2026we are unsure if it is close relative or some sort of power. There had been cannibalism spirits in the bank but they were gone, having been consumed by Bright Shadow\u2019s pet demon.<br /> <br /> Glenwood is fucked up by the way.<br /> <br /> Alice and Sara lead the investigation part of the mission, and we all worked to keep the peace. Rawl is part of a rival group of Werewolves who were in the area, and he was acting as a go between. The two packs were mostly getting along, but hella suspicious of Angelique, albeit for good reason. We seemed to spend forever there, but in the end we got our information out of the bank and got moving.<br /> <br /> The second location contained the lost Werewolves, Austin and Erin. Erin was in a very bad way, but stable. Both were under Bright Shadow\u2019s control. It was an abandoned (?) gas station, and smelled strongly of fuel inside (I did not go in, I used Boneyard). Alice scouted it, and determined the Demon was inside. We discussed it, and decided to use a prison Angelique made to trap the Demon so we could interrogate it. Sara used a Curse on Alexia (not what it sounds like, Tatum; ask Karen) that kept any fires from starting around her so that the spirit could not make the place burn or explode. It\u2019s off her now. Eris used the trap with Alice there to cover, while Doc moved to intercept Erin and Alexia moved to intercept Austin.<br /> <br /> In the end, it was nearly anti-climatic. Eris and Alice snuck up on the Demon and trapped it, while Erin was too weak, moaning in pain, to fight. Austin tried to guard in giant world form, but Malard held his muzzle shut while he verbally bitchslapped him. With the Demon trapped, Bright Shadow\u2019s control was broken, and we got them out. Erin\u2019s child had moved several months ahead in the pregnancy\u2026and her body had not. She was in a lot of pain.<br /> <br /> We made plans quickly. Rawl went to find his group, which had been sidelined. We traveled back to different places, with the Sleeping Giant team sans Eris going there to deal with Deirdre, most of the local Pack to Malard\u2019s house sans Erin, the and us to the house. Right away, Zed showed up with Angelique suggesting she would be safer at our house. Angelique went to help purify Erin while Doc and Alice helped move the baby, which helped her somewhat. Angelique\u2019s purification ritual also helped.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, Noriko had had all of Angelique she could stand and took off on her own to \u2018clear her head.\u201d This is problematic as hell, but she does have an apartment to return to. Still she is alone, and mama ain\u2019t happy about it.<br /> <br /> With two pregnant women in the house, Doc also once Eris was stable went to talk to Chandra. Meanwhile Angelique and I bonded over Amy Grant, of all things. Chandra offered to help with Deirdre using her mental abilities, and to keep her stable dined well on Sara and I. Don\u2019t worry, we are fine; as I told you, Tatum, I am more resilient than you know.<br /> <br /> Doc and Chandra have gone to sleeping Giant, and while healed I feel a bit\u2026drained. I am probably going to take a nap, if Sara lets me. Phone by the bed though, call if you need.<br /> <br /> Hope you guys are having a wild time over there.<br /> <br /> Love,<br /> <br /> Natalie---Allison<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Allison,<br /> <br /> Honestly? Playing video games, Tatum watching me play video games, worrying about you two, and talking about our pets we had as kids. Some of us like to get some rest every few days. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Take care and pass along my love to Sara as well<br /> <br /> Love,<br /> <br /> Mistress<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLVII</i><br /> <br /> Sorry for the lack of Doc's Log, it has been a very busy week and a half for his player, and he actually had to miss the session tonight.<br /> <br /> All in all a tense situation. Natalie, Alexia, and Sara worked hard to keep things calm, and Alexia and Sara once again made heavy use of Reading the Echoes and Industrial Oracle. Alice had to make a roll to keep off of Angelique when they spoke privately, which was fun, but Alice has pretty good resistance stats.<br /> <br /> Also, while I am totally biased, the image of Natalie and Sara quietly holding each other in the car singing \u201cI\u2019ll Be With You at Apple Blossom Time\u201d is just incredibly sweet.<br /> <br /> It continues next time as tensions at and away from the house run high. We even peek in on a plot from the start of the game! See you then! Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-17T15:03:00-08:00","id":788357,"title":"","content":"&quot;Doc's Log: Hickory. I haven't been able to sleep like it lately due to a very busy week. I just hope the fatigue doesn't leave me seeming wooden in my interactions. Time will tell.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T23:37:39-08:00","id":790120,"title":"","content":"Another awesome entry into the chronicle of the Midde Shadows. I am curious about someting else Baroness; what inspired you to make Glenwood such a nightmare of a living place? Was it just because it was conveniently nearby, or does it have any history of some kind that worked to give it such a messed up present?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T06:38:05-08:00","id":790237,"title":"","content":"Hi, super quick question.<br /> I've really been enjoying this thread (only Geist that I can get these days), but how do you guys play this? Are these after-action reports from live games? Skype games? Or just collective writing? Just trying to understand the process.<br /> Thanks again,<br /> C","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-21T12:57:41-08:00","id":790440,"title":"","content":"Taidragon: When I was coming up with the Abyssal plot, it was problematic to put it in New Haven because something like that would not go unnoticed by the thriving supernatural community I had established New Haven had. I asked some friends who were from that general area originally and they suggested Glenwood was &quot;not far&quot; and &quot;kinda run down&quot; so I went with it. I then started adding to it. I wanted a pure headquarters, and it worked for that as the Pure are kinda messed up. The Balehound story was not in and of itself there from the get go (the seeds were) so when I started fleshing that out Glenwood seemed a good place and added a level of tension. Candle Cove seemed an ideal way to introduce the place. I have no idea what real Glenwood is like, it may be nice, it may be urban sprawl. One of my dearest friends is from Glastonbury, but I have personally never traveled further North than DC in North America unless we count a Canadian airport stopover.<br /> <br /> <br /> baileyborough: These are after action reports from a face to face game in my gaming room here at the house, all surrounded by Gargoyles and Living Dead Dolls (Okay, only last year or so has been in my house, the rest were my apartment). My other games in my sig are all either at my house or a friend's house. All the dialogue essentially happened in game; we are very heavy on rp.<br /> <br /> If you have ever read any of Speed Demon's journals over in Demon, those are a pretty accurate blow-by-blow description of events, and all the dialogue there happened in game too. In Changeling Lori's player takes minor creative liscense but it is overall accurate to in game dialogue.<br /> <br /> Now there is some fiction, but I try to make that clear when I am posting them when it is fiction not in game events. Recently, that has been Natalie stories, but there was a story about Doc and Gwen awhile back that was fiction too. That cover everything?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T15:15:36-08:00","id":791811,"title":"","content":"Yes. Awesome awesome work. Amazing to see somebody keeping Geist alive (so to speak).<br /> Also incredibly envious of the time you're able to give to gaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3192-baileyborough","name":"baileyborough","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T15:43:51-08:00","id":791828,"title":"","content":"Yea it's about 2 nights/week. The wife is in half the games, that helps, and one of the two she isn't is a night she always goes to see her friend (which is part of why it was scheduled). Still I am lucky to have the time and lucky to have such a wonderful group. Most of my current games, short Golden Eagle, are sandboxes and I was able to frontload a lot of stuff so my week to week prepwork is low to nonexistent; new plots I have lots of time to work on before they are introduced. GE is a bit more work, but it will get less and less as more regional areas are established.<br /> <br /> There is a Sin-Eater in Golden Eagle as well, though he has not (so far) had a journal he is one of the more active characters. And a second Sin-Eater has...ahem...shown up last session who is not a PC but is quite relevant. Though that will be going up Christmas Day <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> As always thanks for questions and feedback, glad you are enjoying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-28T02:07:37-08:00","id":794046,"title":"","content":"Tensions continue to escalate in stately Fishborne manor. Tensions of all kinds. Can they find the Bale Hound before things descend into chaos?<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s player had to miss due to vacationing and such<br /> <i><br /> Session CXLVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Lords and ladies, I don\u2019t like this. I don\u2019t like this I don\u2019t like this I don\u2019t like this. I don\u2019t need the Sight to see this going horribly, and I don\u2019t like it. Fate may have decided to give us an answer or two, but she\u2019s dealt us a shit hand.<br /> <br /> OK, for starters - we\u2019re going back to Glenwood, and that\u2019s technically the good news. The spirit gave us a location for one of Bright Shadows\u2019 headquarters but since that wasn\u2019t her only one, just the one the spirit knew about, we need to move fast before she realizes it\u2019s compromised.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, the spirit is also a deceitful piece of shit. Oh, it might not have been capable of lying, but it sure did its best to get Angelique killed by a clever application of the truth. It insisted on calling her Master, going on about how much Bright Shadows missed her. It also called her Bone Wanderer and claimed she\u2019d met with Bright Shadows at Murder Ballads recently.<br /> <br /> That matched unfortunately with other things. Rawl had been poking around Murder Ballads while Angelique was getting things set up, so Noriko and Alice went to make sure he wasn\u2019t up to anything because fuck plausible deniability. He could tell it was a place suffused with dark energy, some place Bright Shadows might be able to recharge, as it were. Once they\u2019d started poking around, Rawl thought he found signs of Angelique, though Alice said it was merely similar, like at the bank.<br /> <br /> That was a week or two ago. Angelique, when I described the vision I\u2019d had of Bright Shadows, didn\u2019t recognize her, but did have an anonymous hookup at Murder Ballads after Alice broke up with her. So, about a week ago. She didn\u2019t remember a face, or a name, but had been certain it wasn\u2019t anyone of the family - something Bright Shadows should have shown up as to her Sight. It doesn\u2019t add up, but we don\u2019t have enough pieces to do anything about it.<br /> <br /> My lovely Angelique was terrified the entire time, mostly of what Eris and Noriko would do to her. I tried to point out that if the spirit truly served her, it would not say so in front of those two, and that perhaps if a creature of deception, whose major MO was to turn people against each other, bound an evil spirit to Angelique, it might not have been because Angelique was her best bud. That was possibly why they didn\u2019t kill her before the ritual ended, but it didn\u2019t help with the torrents of self-hatred and fear Angelique was under. She made some questionable decisions, including flat out asking Noriko to kill her.<br /> <br /> She also told Eris about her past in about the worst way possible, at least at first, saying she was like this Bright Shadows. Not saying it was her mentor that had been, that she\u2019d been coerced and tricked into it, that she\u2019d been an apprentice at worst. She got to that stuff eventually, but her initial confession put murder right the fuck back in Eris\u2019 eyes. And of course, Eris has to tell her people. Saints that they are, they\u2019ve decided to probably kill her for being an unwitting tool when she was very young after she\u2019s helped us deal with the evil spirits arrayed against us.<br /> <br /> In the meantime, Doc would have exploded if he caught half of the intense looks our Little Red and Noriko had been giving each other, Mr Malard is going off the deep end especially where Angelique is concerned, I had to exert every bit of willpower I had not to tear Angelique\u2019s clothes off on the walk from Malard\u2019s to home, and my Natalie is getting a couple of cognacs to the wind before we go to track down a seriously dangerous bad guy. Not to mention, that other than Angelique having a second personality or something, we\u2019ve got no idea how any of our information fits together, dibs has been called on who gets to kill Angelique, and I haven\u2019t slept in way too long.<br /> <br /> I really don\u2019t like this.<br /> <br /> You take care of yourself. I\u2019ll get back to you as soon as I can.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> Sara glanced over at the beautiful werewolf, curled up in the corner of the couch. She closed her laptop. <i>You ask much.</i><br /> <br /> \u2018I\u2019m not asking you anything,\u2019 Sara thought resignedly. \u2018I\u2019ve told you, we - you - don\u2019t get to decide what it is appropriate for others to sacrifice.\u2019<br /> <br /> <i>Is that so?</i> Sara felt her geist smile sadly.<i> I didn\u2019t say you ask much of me. You ask much of her.</i> Sara didn\u2019t respond, reaching out to brush a strand of hair from Angelique\u2019s face. <i>She is so tired.</i><br /> <br /> \u2018She can rest soon.\u2019<br /> <br /> <i>Will you let her? Or will you keep asking her to sacrifice that for your sake? For others\u2019 sake? For the world\u2019s?</i> The geist rested her hands on Sara\u2019s shoulders. <i>What god do you call out to? What prayer do you send?</i><br /> <br /> The dark haired Sin-Eater bit her lip and ran a finger along the curve of the other woman\u2019s chin. \u2018It\u2019s not like that. It\u2019s the Balehound\u2019s influence. She doesn\u2019t deserve to die.\u2019<br /> <br /> <i>So sometimes it is you who gets to decide who deserves what? Sometimes the call to sacrifice is stronger than the call of desire?</i> The geist\u2019s voice was measured and calm. She paused until Sara began to say something before she continued. <i>Or is it that you would prefer she bore the burden of sacrifice this time rather than you?<br /> </i><br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not...\u201d Angelique stirred as Sara spoke aloud. Sara smiled quickly as the werewolf\u2019s eyes fluttered open. \u201cSorry, love I didn\u2019t mean to wake you. However... we should probably find the others, it should be about time to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique nodded tiredly and stood to leave. Sara watched her stretch before turning to stash her laptop, her smile fading and shoulders slumping. When she turned back around, Angelique was looking at her with concern. Sara smiled slightly, moving closer as her geist spoke again. <i>What prayers do you send?</i><br /> <br /> Sara looked down and took another step towards Angelique. \u201cWe will find this Balehound and stop her from hurting anyone else.\u201d She laid a hand on the werewolf\u2019s cheek.<br /> <br /> As Angelique leaned down to kiss the Sin-Eater, her geist spoke softly, so even Sara didn\u2019t hear. <i>May the gods accept your offering, this time.</i><br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Karen &amp; Tatum<br /> <br /> I realize you two are probably asleep. That\u2019s fine, this is for if things go wrong. Or just in case insomnia has you.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s been an intense night. Sara and I (and everyone else) are okay. It\u2019s not done. We are about to go back to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> Angelique determined she needed to prepare a second prison for the Demon, so if she gets out of control she can imprisoned quickly, or if she takes hold of Angelique somehow. So Sara and Angelique went next door and got one, then Angelique began a three-hour ritual to create it.<br /> <br /> After that started, Alice got a call from Noriko, that she had spotted Rawl near Murder Ballads. Alice told us and went to get her axe, so Sara decided to call Rawl. According to Rawl, he was looking for a cluster of negative emotions that could empower the Bale Hound, and the depths of Murder Ballads could do that. I have been improving the spiritual health of the place, but it still had some bad areas. There was an amusing exchange when Rawl assured us he did a ritual so no Uratha would find him, but as he was bragging Noriko grabbed him. Alice went off and we hoped nothing bad would happen.<br /> <br /> I got a call from Noriko saying that Bright Shadow had been there, but it was some time ago. Rawl sensed her, and Alice interrogated Rory James. That fucker. Still, she wanted to prepare a trap. I agreed to talk to Alice about it. When Alice and Noriko returned we discussed talking to the management and finding out who rented the room she had been in (which Kinksters used for awhile but had recently changed. Karen any of your friends know about this?) and may can get more information. Rory is supposed to contact Alice if he sees something, though she understands he is a fucker. Of course, that may be moot.<br /> <br /> Alice went up to see Eris the rest of the time, but it was obvious there was growing, rapidly, sexual tension between she and Noriko. I had never seen Noriko look at a woman besides me, so that honestly surprised me. But I did not know just how far gone Noriko was.<br /> <br /> Sara and I talked some while Alice spent time with Eris, Doc worked on Erin, and Alexia and Chandra napped\u2026or \u201cnapped,\u201d and we discussed what Angelique said, that the issue seems to be taboos with this Bale Hound. Sara and I were less affected (though Sara admitted kissing Angelique outside en route back) because we are not with as many sexual/romantic Taboos. Sure, we have plenty in general, but few are romantic or sexual. I am more attracted to Doc than I usually am (sorry, Karen) and became surprisingly so toward Jacob near the end, so my \u201cweak point\u201d seems to involve men. And possibly wanting babies. Short people who are truly dangerous to fool around with, Sara\u2019s libertine nature gives her few taboos, so she is substantially less affected. Alexia seems similar\u2026while she puts some prudish rules down, she rarely resists her desires, though Chandra\u2019s \u201ctopping off\u201d on Sara and my breasts may indicate she is more affected than her wife.<br /> <br /> Angelique got first the trapping ritual and then the binding ritual ready, and summoned the Demon. The Demon subserviently called her Master, and seemed if anything perplexed as to why she was binding it and not working with Bright Shadow, acting as if she had been the whole time. I admit this was working well, Eris and Noriko were staring her down with murder in their eyes. Alice and Alexia aggressively spoke up to defend her, and while I had the Passion Marionette attached to her, she remained in control with no strings tugged. Which is good, I hate using mind powers on people. I would rather just talk. The Spirit claimed Angelique (or Bone Wanderer) as she called her had met Bright Shadow at Murder Ballads, but claimed to be not present for the actual discussion. Convenient. Angelique doubted her sanity at this point, and after a point just trapped the Demon again\u2026in the first vessel, which she earlier said did not work. She then rushed to Noriko and displayed her throat, and her eyes told Noriko to kill.<br /> <br /> I honestly think she started to, but Alice and Sara intervened even as I yanked Angelique\u2019s cords. Both women were talked down. Eris demanded an explanation, and Angelique yelled that she used to be a Bale Hound. Eris promptly joined team \u201cKill Angelique\u201d Somewhere in the argument Eris realized she was on a sacred hunt and could consume the Demon and her Essence, and did so\u2026the Demon was easily knocked out of the vessel with a swat, so she was never really trapped again. Angelique admitted she did not know why she did not use the vessel she spent hours making, saying using the old \u201cSeemed right at the time.\u201d So she was influenced\u2026Sara said her emotions seemed a kaleidoscope.<br /> <br /> Angelique did tall about her history, how her Mentor was the only other Bone Shadow she ever knew, how the pack was unsure and had driven her out, and confessed even she did not know how corrupted she was. It may have helped a little bit, but Eris still considered her a Bale Hound (and as people are flying off the handle and Angelique was a romantic rival, that was probably also a thing). She insisted she would tell her Pack.<br /> <br /> Somewhere in there Noriko made a comment about killing Angelique, and Alice cast a fierce look at her friend. While Noriko had, throughout the night, stared back defiantly at anyone who tried to intimidate her, this time she looked stricken and curled up, sobbing. Once things were calm. Alice went to comfort her\u2026and I swear, no lez glasses, it looked like they were about to kiss. Between murderous impulses and strange attractions, Noriko is absolutely deeply affected.<br /> <br /> Most of us are going a little crazy.<br /> <br /> The Demon had told us a location in Glenwood (she conveniently only knew one, though she pointed out there were two we had already been to so she actually knew three). We decided to move that night. Eris called Ildefonso, and of course told him about Angelique. His compromise was nothing now, but she would need to be dealt with when Bright Shadow was no longer a threat.<br /> <br /> Sara called Zed then Rawl. Zed gathered the troops, while Rawl went to tell his Pack. I, well, needed some fortification for this, and downed one bottle of Cognac and started on my second when Sara came up and scooped me up and kissed me in front of everyone. At first I thought she was dealing with her issues, and she may have been, but she also pointed out she was trying to help with mine. I had been all but ignored in this drama, with my more libertine lifestyle shielding me a bit, but that meant I was getting little attention and well\u2026yea. I admitted I was considering acting out, though in my defense I had not thought of it that way.<br /> <br /> So to Glenwood. Again. You can imagine I am excited. Goddess willing, we will be back before sunrise, but I doubt it.<br /> <br /> You two stay tight over there. No need to get involved in all this fucking Drama. Remember if we go silent, don\u2019t go near anywhere we may be until you are contacted.<br /> <br /> All my love and Sara\u2019s too,<br /> <br /> Natalie----Allison<br /> <i><br /> End Session CXLVIII</i><br /> <br /> Doc not being there slowed things down a bit. The intent was to cover his meeting with the Sleeping Giant Pack first, then have that define mood, but also to have Natalie and he having ramping up attraction as her body screamed \u201cWant Baby Now!\u201d<br /> <br /> There were few mechanics or scenes undescribed. The scene with the Demon and the interrogation was really tense, and a lot of fun to play.<br /> <br /> Okay, it\u2019s been fun stringing folks along, but the first of two major steps to resolve the whole thing happens next session. Not an end to the story, but the step before\u2026it\u2019s complicated. You\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T18:50:54-08:00","id":798053,"title":"","content":"The &quot;Want Baby&quot; part reminds me of one time my players bemoaned how babies kept cropping up in the games I ran for them. I quickly replied that I couldn't help that my biological clock was ticking. The waitress nearby nearly dropped the glasses she was carrying.<br /> <br /> Much laughter was had between myself, them, and Dad &amp;Step-mom.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-01T20:22:11-08:00","id":798077,"title":"","content":"LOL it's fair. Well, you know you are self-reflective enough to realize it. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-dark