xt, I had the opinion that the manifestation had to be learned from the underworld, and that most Sin Eaters stayed away from it. Just thought I'd ask.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-03T22:53:19-08:00","id":800295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=799920#post799920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> From what I read from the Book Of The Dead's flavor text, I had the opinion that the manifestation had to be learned from the underworld, and that most Sin Eaters stayed away from it. Just thought I'd ask.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea no worries, I don't mind <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have my Key/Manifestation requirements somewhere, it was on the old forum but I think lost in transfer. I will see if I can find it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-04T00:18:06-08:00","id":800336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=799160#post799160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's unclear, but I will explain.<br /> <br /> The Bale Hound was using powers to essentially cause vices to dominate, which focused on Taboos. Angelique was initially affected, because she was weakened by the connection to the Maeljin, though Doc severed that. She did not really spread it to the PCs, but to her own pack, especially the Callahan Siblings.<br /> <br /> Bright Shadow then put some demons in the form of Beshilu, which fought some PCs in Sleeping Giant. They were killed, but affected those there, who spread the supernatural virus to their packs/Krewes. It is tied to Bright Shadow, without whom it will fade on it's own. Her intention is for each group to tear itself apart via power struggles and jealousies, and leave some Werewolves, including she hoped Angelique, ripe for corruption.<br /> <br /> Different PCs are vulnerable on different levels. Natalie and Sara are libertines, and their effect is minimal because they have fewer personal taboos. Most that they have is not sleeping with vulnerable people (like Angelique) or people in relationships (like Alice). Others are more susceptible, like Alice and Doc who are in fully monogamous relationships thus sleeping with anyone but their partner, even for fun, is a violation. Alexia is kinda of the middle, being less strictly monogamous than Doc or Alice but not the wild libidos that are Sara or Natalie.<br /> <br /> Sara has always liked Angelique. The pic for her is very attractive, so I think her player thinking she is hot is part of it. Angelique's involvement with Malard kept Sara at bay, though, as say what you will about Sara, she does not seek to damage relationships.<br /> <br /> Is that clearer?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the explanation!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T02:28:10-08:00","id":805921,"title":"","content":"I think it is about time we were all let in on Angelique\u2019s big secret. I\u2019ve forshadowed a little, but if it seems a sudden revelation, well\u2026<br /> <br /> The holiday/winter curse continues. Alice\u2019s player had to miss. Tonight\u2019s session Doc will have to miss. This is crunch time for his work so no log this time. Still, Sara and Natalie have got this.<br /> <i><br /> Session CXLIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> Home safe. Exhausted. Will update after sleep.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, the trip to Glenwood went... well. No one was hurt, we saved some people, we got a good idea how to deal with our problem. Also, we know how Angelique and Bright Shadows are linked. The only downside is we have to spend four days seething with sexual tension that nobody seems inclined to release.<br /> <br /> The saving people thing was probably the trickiest part. Bright Shadows had kidnapped some members of Rawl\u2019s extended family and had mystically coerced them into defending her headquarters with machine guns. She also managed to give them Sight, enough to see me when I was scouting around outside of my body. Natalie and I worked together to cause seven of them to fall asleep and Alexia and Doc dealt with the last one, wrestling him into cuffs the hard way. In the end, Rawl took them home. I\u2019m convinced he can help them out.<br /> <br /> Bright Shadows also had a pretty powerful spirit guarding her inner sanctum there. Thankfully, as I said, no one was hurt, due in large part to our backup. Unfortunately, she did have time to escape. And still managed to taunt us, using some ritual. She offered us a deal, first, that if we let her go, she\u2019d avoid any city we were in. We said no, and then she claimed to be Angelique Della Passaglia. Apparently, when she was trying to escape from the people who came after her mentor, she imprinted her memories and enough of her personality to fool them, with some differences for palatability. Our Angelique was just the right kind of Touched in the wrong place and the wrong time. Bright Shadows laughed when she said she didn\u2019t even know who our Angelique had been.<br /> <br /> That act is going to be her downfall though. We were able to track her for a ways before her trail went suddenly cold, and our Angelique knows a ritual that basically lets her step into a safe pocket of reality. A ritual that she presumably had imprinted on her by Bright Shadows. Angelique knows how to reopen the door too, only it has to be done under a crescent moon, which is four days away. Now, we don\u2019t know for absolutely certain that\u2019s what it is. Angelique would need to see the site, and Rawl\u2019s buddies were getting restless. She\u2019s pretty damn certain though and, fates willing, our hunt will stop there.<br /> <br /> Well, there so long as we make it through the next few days. Alice still wants Angelique, as does Alexia, but Alice is the one shooting me the occasional dagger. You could cut the tension between Noriko and Alice with a knife. Natalie really wants a kid, and thinks Doc\u2019d make a great dad. Chandra was eying Natalie and I, when her gaze didn\u2019t stray towards the infirmary. Doc could barely bear to look at Natalie. And Angelique is trying to be good, despite spending the whole night cuddling with me and Natalie. Alexia had the best idea - \u2018what happens in Vegas stays in Vegas\u2019 - but nobody but me, her and Chandra seemed into it.<br /> <br /> So the plan is now to have business as usual with preparation to scatter if the tension gets overwhelming. I\u2019m not leaving Angelique without protection though, so that\u2019s going to be fun.<br /> <br /> Lords and ladies, I hope these four days are more fun than they\u2019re sounding like.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <b><br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Karen &amp; Tatum<br /> <br /> You may return at your leisure. We are back from Glenwood, and I don\u2019t think tensions here will get you killed.<br /> <br /> There are, however, unresolved tensions here. Very unresolved. The raid on Bright Shadow\u2019s base went well. She had turned a number of the Wolf-Blooded of the Pure into Possessed, who waited with silver bullets. Eight of them inside a drugstore. Sara cursed them, and then I used Boneyard to put all but one into slumber\u2026the one was technically asleep but still controlled. Doc and Alexia took them down. We are turning over the Possessed to the Pure. Let them deal with them. We kept the Uzis and silver bullets though.<br /> <br /> The lair downstairs was guarded by a Demon, but both Werewolf packs, Doc, Alexia, Alice and Sara made short work of it, I barely even saw the action. Bright Shadow appeared in a green flame over the alter to taunt us, and revealed she was the actual Angelique Della Passaglia. She needed to escape when the local werewolves were becoming suspicious of her mentor, and found the newly changed \u201cAngelique\u201d and imprinted upon her the name, memories, and even some mystical knowledge and overwrote the woman who was before\u2026Angelique remembers nothing. She then cast her out, and the other werewolves found her. Due to the similarities, they never realized Bright Shadow was someone else and she escaped. This was why Angelique had so many fuzzy spots in her memory, and it does fit the idiom of Bright Shadow\u2019s name, having consumed the old identity, leaving dust.<br /> <br /> Speaking of which Doc, being Doc, smashed the alter while she was talking. He does not halfass the wrath thing. Otherwise we were able to gather books and other paraphernalia we may can put to use.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, her escape will likely be short lived. Angelique has a pretty good idea of how she is hiding, based on a ritual from her memory, and thinks she can get her out of her self-created prison she is hiding in\u2026in four days. It has to do with them both being crescent moons, and the prison/hideaway can only be opened when the correct moon is in the sky. I am not positive of the details The effects addling us, making us transgress or quarrel, are not gone, however. And we will be dealing with them for four days.<br /> <br /> Everyone crashed last\u2026morning\u2026on returning; Sara coaxed Angelique to our bed, but I was out like a light, and Sara and Angelique did not wake me so I don\u2019t think anything happened, especially given how tired Angelique was. We had a late lunch and discussed matters, trying to clear the air. A lot of ideas were put forth (have me tell you Alexia\u2019s hilarious \u201cVegas\u201d one) but nothing was decided for sure. No one is sure what to do. The stakes are higher for some than others, it seems.<br /> <br /> There is a problem with Doc and I, and it is difficult explain. Karen, we will talk in person.<br /> <br /> Still, come on back, as I say. If nothing else, it should be exciting.<br /> <br /> Natalie---Allison<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Allison<br /> <br /> We will be coming back in about an hour. Tatum finally found a fighting game to school me in. She knows who beat her little ass all night though. What? Aren\u2019t you glad we did not have anything so interesting as you? <br /> <br /> Love you<br /> <br /> Mistress<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CXLIX</i><br /> <br /> Oh man, the Vegas suggestion was hilarious. Apparently when all this tension is around, the answer is to go to Vegas where there are no repercussions for anything. Naturally.<br /> <br /> There was also the following exchange in game after Bright Shadow\u2019s message was, ahem, terminated.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes the Alter seem magical?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, there is a magic effect on it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I tell anything about it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, somebody broke it.\u201d<br /> <br /> That last with a straight face. Doc did not actually mess anything up, though.<br /> <br /> With the action wound down, some drama begins. That should be fun. Join us for it next time, session 150! Holy Crap! Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T13:09:54-08:00","id":806380,"title":"","content":"Now that I didn't see coming, and I have to say it's a pretty interesting hook. I hesitate to ask, but was this planned out at the start of the game, when you introduced Angelique, or was it something that you built up as the session went on?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-11T19:16:37-08:00","id":806672,"title":"","content":"The whole time, actually.<br /> <br /> Angelique always had odd quirks, like dressing the opposite of the season or being vague about her history. This was to put some suspicion on her from the start, but had an &quot;innocent&quot; reason for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T12:57:48-08:00","id":808984,"title":"","content":"Interesting.<br /> <br /> What is prompting Natalie's want for a baby. The Bright Shadows is exacerbating it yes, but where did the root desire come from?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T13:51:55-08:00","id":809053,"title":"","content":"Always been there. She felt she failed her daughter as a mother, and wants to try again and succeed. And being around younger Natalie just made it more intense. Natalie mothers everyone, even her girlfriends. It's second nature to her. So the maternal instincts click hard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-14T20:21:36-08:00","id":809327,"title":"","content":"Ooh, okie dokie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T14:03:52-08:00","id":809829,"title":"","content":"That makes me curious actually; at a rough percentage, how many of your quests are ones you have had planned from the start, and how many are ones that developed over time? I ask for a rough percentage because, well, it could give the game away to ask for specifics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T16:31:37-08:00","id":809914,"title":"","content":"Offhand, maybe 70%. It is a little hard to say. For example, many NPCs were just dropped in and had general stuff if the PCs stumbled over them and took an interest, and I often fleshed it out a bit if the PCs pursued. I knew who Bright Shadow was, and what Angelique's backstory was, but Glenwood didn't even exist yet.* I assumed someone would get involved with Angelique quickly, honestly. Her picture is very attractive in a way guys and girls both tend to like. I had general ideas about what a lot of NPCs would be like in relationships, usually with both men and women and how they might differ (with exceptions, Karen only likes women and Barrett only likes men, for example) but I did not plan, say, Noriko and Doc specifically, though I knew it was more likely then, say, Noriko and Natalie (heh) or Noriko and Simon. Alexia's player declared she would have Alexia pursue Chandra soon as she got her personal NPC list. Several &quot;long&quot; plots were designed later...Candle Cove and The Haunted Hotel, for example. Some NPCs were there with a name but everything was fleshed out later. <br /> <br /> The girl in the Banshee plot, for example, was there from almost the start, but every time she showed up the players fixated on her rather abundant hair (she was just called &quot;the hair&quot; OOC) and it was a running joke her hair was actually controlling her. When Simon's player started a short lived University game he used the picture for a major NPC (we never found out anything about). I invented a weird backstory for the existing character because it seemed like it would be a letdown otherwise. There was a lot of that. Barry and Maria, the reincarnating Immortals, is an example. They and their conflict was there from the start. I had THIN ideas for stuff to do if the PCs sided with one but not much fleshed out. The PCs haven't really looked hard into it so it is not deeply fleshed out. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> So, I guess 70-5% but it is not an easy this is X that is Y<br /> <br /> <br /> *I mean, it did, but I did not even know it existed yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-15T17:36:28-08:00","id":809951,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baroness Nerak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=809914#post809914\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The girl in the Banshee plot, for example, was there from almost the start, but every time she showed up the players fixated on her rather abundant hair (she was just called &quot;the hair&quot; OOC) and it was a running joke her hair was actually controlling her. When Simon's player started a short lived University game he used the picture for a major NPC (we never found out anything about). I invented a weird backstory for the existing character because it seemed like it would be a letdown otherwise. There was a lot of that. Barry and Maria, the reincarnating Immortals, is an example. They and their conflict was there from the start. I had THIN ideas for stuff to do if the PCs sided with one but not much fleshed out. The PCs haven't really looked hard into it so it is not deeply fleshed out. Does that make sense?<br /> <br /> So, I guess 70-5% but it is not an easy this is X that is Y</div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean. You have a base for the characters and quests, but you don't want to be too rigid with them lest it go against the flow of the game or become a let-down. Likewise, you don't want the ideas you have to be misinterpreted and completely derail the plot you had set up. Say, if you had a Lucifuge Hunter who was investigating parts of a town on his own, which ended up with a Ghost Tree, but he was open to having some assistance by the local Sin Eaters to ensure that what he is investigating doesn't become that much worse by accident (such as inflicting hellfire onto the Ghost Tree, which somehow causes it to kill and absorb the ghosts of several firefighters and thus become much stronger)*. If you mis-convey what the character is there for, and can offer, you could accidentally lead the players to declaring war on the Lucifuge as a whole, or getting what you planned as a long-running NPC to be killed. And, as you said, it doesn't do for a character to not at least partially live up to the interest the group is investing into them. I found &quot;the Hair&quot; to have a pretty interesting backstory - creative use of the material you have is always good. :-)<br /> <br /> * Incidentally, while I do have that idea as for one of my characters, it's free for use. You may want to avoid naming him Professor Amon Nymus though - it's really quite a horrible pun, but I really can't help myself (doubly so using Paul McGann as the picture reference).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-23T16:29:49-08:00","id":815102,"title":"","content":"Cool enough, also<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://i169.photobucket.com/albums/u223/LeRoienJeune/Ddc66_BigSceneHairstyle_zpsffpcr09r.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">The Hair, by Request</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-25T22:48:56-08:00","id":816683,"title":"","content":"Session 150 WOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOO!!!!!!<br /> <br /> Doc's player had to miss. When the Cat\u2019s away the Mice will play. Except in this case the Mouse is a Cat. Damn, I\u2019ve lot the plot. <br /> <br /> Note Natalie\u2019s journal continues minor fantasizing about self-mutilation and suicide. So trigger warning there.<br /> <i><br /> Session CL</i><br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha \u2013<br /> <br /> Well, one day down and we haven\u2019t fallen apart too much. I had a perfectly wonderful day - there are upsides to not being ashamed of sex. I spent my afternoon getting my brains fucked out by a strong, beautiful, intense woman, and I don\u2019t feel the least bit bad for it. Alice has no reason to be upset with me about it either - I did invite her to the hot tub with us. I\u2019m sure Angelique wouldn\u2019t have minded. She might have if Eris joined in - it would be a hell of a \u2018devil\u2019s threesome\u2019 problem - but we are a clever bunch, I\u2019m sure we could have made it work.<br /> <br /> Her loss though. Angelique wanted me and it\u2019s better to do something, to be with someone than to keep denying ourselves the things we want. Not that Natalie feels better for it. I do feel a little bad about leaving Natalie alone with Noriko. I didn\u2019t really think anything of it. I guess I kinda assumed that if she started flirting with her in the hot tub, with Doc all the way out in the garage, and considering everything going on, she had an idea what she was getting into... I\u2019m not the greatest chaperone at the best of time. It\u2019s a good thing Karen and Tatum are here now. Tatum\u2019s a nice distraction and Karen can lay down the rules and discipline Natalie wants. I know it was just because Noriko was Doc\u2019s girlfriend (or at least largely because of that), but it bothered me to hear her call herself a dirty whore and filthy slut. Karen will be able to deal with that better than me, I think.<br /> <br /> She can\u2019t deal with Alice\u2019s coldness towards me though. Thankfully, that didn\u2019t last too long - it didn\u2019t start until she and Eris got back from their hike and by the time we finished watching Radioland Murders, we were back to mostly normal. Really it was before that - I guess her mysterious errand got her mind off not getting to have all the primally Touched ladies at the house. Which makes me horribly curious. It would have to be a really good secret to distract her from Noriko and Angelique both. Maybe I ought to try and take her mind of them as well, and see what she snuck off to her room.<br /> <br /> Anyway, Alexia and Chandra had a fine day as well. They opted out of movie night and decided to stay at Chandra\u2019s wicker shop for the evening. They were out for most of the day as well, so I guess their strategy is avoidance. They were investigating the problem that came up on campus a bit back, when a strange rite was used outside a dorm window, designed to trap Chandra. Alexia managed to talk to the girl whose window it was. Apparently, it was an interesting conversation, mostly because Alexia for help from Maria, a Touched college student of our acquaintance who happened to be nearby. The conversation escalated into a fistfight, it seems. They\u2019re going to go back tomorrow night to use Alexia\u2019s Sight on the window in question, hopefully with less fistfights. They did learn it was put up with the student\u2019s knowledge, so likely we will simply find out who did it to know who to be wary of, and leave it be, since as Alice pointed out it\u2019s technically a protective rite, not a malicious one. Both Alexia and Chandra want to know who knows how to do things like that though, which is fair.<br /> <br /> On a slightly potentially disturbing note, Tavia has gone to Rhode Island. Normally, I wouldn\u2019t worry too much about her comings and goings, but according to Alexia, she left with a bag that \u2018clinked\u2019 plus I somewhat remember that Simon had a fling in that direction. A fling that great lengths were taken to keep away from Tavia back when there was a big party here at the house. Gwen warned me way back when I met these folks, right after Simon invited me to the house, that Simon was off limits because his girlfriend had a knife and knew how to use it. I don\u2019t know what brought it to a head now, except that Tavia was possibly feeling the same effects we were. Unfortunately, I didn\u2019t get the note from Alexia until Tavia\u2019d been on the road a few hours, so... I hope Simon\u2019s girl on the side wasn\u2019t at home?<br /> <br /> After the craziness of the evening, it was nice to relax with the troupe watching the movie, then with my ladies in the music room. With all that\u2019s going on, it\u2019s probably good that Karen\u2019s gotten rid of Natalie\u2019s heroin, not that I conspired with her to do so like Natalie suspected. That is a fairly dangerous indulgences, however. We\u2019ll be distraction enough for one another, I\u2019m sure. And Doc\u2019ll be alright. I mean, people have to understand, right? Once this is all over... things that happen these next few days, we won\u2019t let them tear us apart...<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> It's not long after breakfast, and already we can all feel the influence of the Balehound's lust spirit. For some, it's manifesting as a deep and untargeted frustration as we fight against our baser urges. Doc is prey to a nameless anger, so he has withdrawn to his workshop. The rest of us are loitering around the TV room, unsure what to do to occupy the time until we can finally finish this hunt.<br /> <br /> Sexual tensions are running high, but I stick close to Eris. She's my rock right now, and I feel like I can weather this storm of errant emotions as long as she's by my side. I think she feels the same.<br /> <br /> Then Natalie stands up, and with a sway in her hips, she announces that she's going to the hot tub. She throws a coy look over her shoulder towards to rest of us as she glides from the room. Immediately, Sara and Angelique share a glance and trail after her, and Noriko quickly follows suit, her keen, dark eyes fastened intently on Natalie's retreating form.<br /> <br /> I don't really want to join them in the hot tub. I have the feeling it would quickly become a bit crowded. But the sight of Noriko hungrily following Natalie makes me angry. Natalie is clearly trying to seduce someone, and it looks like that someone is going to be Noriko. I can't believe they are so eagerly betraying Doc like this! They aren't even <i>trying</i> to fight the Balehound's influence.<br /> <br /> Eris senses that I'm upset.<br /> <br /> &quot;We can go hiking,&quot; she offers. &quot;You like that. I know it's cold, but that might be good for us right now.&quot;<br /> <br /> I consider a moment. I don't want to leave Noriko alone with Natalie, but Eris is right. Hiking might be just the thing to clear my head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Sure, that sounds good,&quot; I say, forcing a smile. &quot;I'm glad you're here with me.&quot;<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> My jeep is freezing cold, but it won't take us long to get to Sleeping Giant and start hiking. Eris doesn't seem to mind the cold, but I'm not enjoying it, and I keep thinking about the warm hot tub back home. And Noriko. And how even now, Natalie is probably seducing her.<br /> <br /> <i>You're not angry, you know. You're jealous.</i><br /> <br /> As always, the Grasping Huntress is trying to push my buttons. What does she know about jealousy?<br /> <i><br /> You think I haven't been jealous? I'm the disgraced victim of a brutal rape. My life and any chance I had to enjoy the comforting embrace of a lover died when I became possessed by my thirst for vengeance, but that doesn't mean I didn't crave the tender caresses or the passionate devotion of a strong and caring man. I know jealousy. I have seethed with it. I have killed because of it.</i><br /> <br /> You're not going to goad me into killing someone like this.<br /> <i><br /> No, I'm not. But I want you to be honest with yourself about what you're feeling.<br /> </i><br /> I realize that the Huntress is right. I am intensely jealous.<br /> <br /> Eris is good at reading my moods. She places a hand on my arm.<br /> <br /> &quot;You still seem upset. Is there anything I can do to help?&quot; she asks.<br /> <br /> I shake my head. &quot;No, I'm okay.&quot;<br /> <br /> We drive on for about half a minute.<br /> <br /> &quot;Actually, no, I'm not okay,&quot; I suddenly blurt out. &quot;Please, please tell me that you aren't into Natalie.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eris looks surprised, and her frown is adorable. She shakes her head.<br /> <br /> &quot;No. I'm not attracted to her. She's too soft. I would break her. Besides. you're my mate. I love you.&quot;<br /> <br /> I smile at Eris, and her earnest expression makes tears start to well up in my eyes. My god, I'm lucky I found her. It makes my jealousy all the more frustrating, because I know I have absolutely no reason to feel jealous of Noriko or Angelique, not when I have Eris. Still, I can't stop from venting my feelings.<br /> <br /> &quot;So why the\u2026heck\u2026does everyone fawn over Natalie all the time? I swear, literally everyone we meet just can't wait to get into bed with her! I mean, sure, she's hot. She's not my type, but she's attractive. Still, I just don't get it.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eris shrugs. I don't think she gets it either.<br /> <br /> I stop at an intersection. There's no other traffic, and I just sit there awhile. I let my head fall forward, my forehead resting on the steering wheel.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm jealous that Noriko went off with Natalie,&quot; I confess quietly, feeling guilty and more than a little disgusted with myself.<br /> <br /> &quot;Me too,&quot; says Eris.<br /> <br /> I really didn't expect that. I raise my head and look at Eris. She looks embarrassed.<br /> <br /> &quot;You mean, you feel\u2026I mean\u2026you're feeling\u2026attracted\u2026to Noriko too?&quot; Somehow, I've lost the ability the speak.<br /> <br /> Eris nods.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe we should have invited her with us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;It would be fun to have her along,&quot; Eris agrees.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe we should call her? We aren't too far from the Bluffs.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you think that's a good idea?&quot; Eris asks.<br /> <br /> I sigh. &quot;Probably not. We'd just be asking for trouble.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;We'll be out hiking. It's really cold, so I'm sure nothing will happen, and Noriko won't be with Natalie.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eris' logic is flawless. Maybe. I don't really stop think about it.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, you're right. I'll call her.&quot; I pull into a nearby parking lot and then give Noriko a call. The phone rings several times and goes to voice mail. My heart sinks, and the jealousy surges. Still, I leave a message.<br /> <br /> &quot;Hi Noriko. Eris and I were thinking we'd like to\u2026um\u2026have you along for the hike. We're\u2026we're not too far from the Bluffs, so we can come back and get you. If, you know, that's what you want\u2026but\u2026I guess you're\u2026occupied\u2026right now. Anyway\u2026um...bye.&quot;<br /> <br /> Well, that was a disaster.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Dinner is uncomfortable and awkward. Eris and I may have dodged a bullet by going out on our hike, but it is painfully clear that Natalie and Noriko have slept together. Natalie seems depressed. She barely pushes her food around the plate, and Sara and Karen are keeping a worried eye on her. I guess she's upset with herself for sleeping with Doc's girlfriend. Noriko doesn't seem ashamed, though. She seems focused. Predatory. I catch her watching me closely, gauging my reaction to the others.<br /> <br /> It's also clear that Angelique and Sara spent at least part of the day in bed together. That also makes me jealous even though I know it shouldn't. I have a hard time meeting Angelique's gaze, and I can't help being a bit cold and distant when Sara tries to engage me in conversation. My coldness upsets her, and the last thing I want to do is upset Sara, but I can't help it.<br /> <br /> I know this jealousy is just a part of the Balehound's lustful influence, but that doesn't make it any easier to handle. And the desire I feel when I look at Noriko or Angelique is becoming increasingly overwhelming, so I try to focus on Eris. Even then, I find my thoughts wandering in directions that surprise me. Nothing bad or weird, just a little\u2026kinkier\u2026than normal. So I decide to act on a plan that occured to me on the drive back from Sleeping Giant.<br /> <br /> There's something I need, though, so I make excuses to run an errand alone after dinner. As I'm putting on my coat and scarf and getting ready to leave, Noriko slinks into the entrance hall. My heart skips a beat when I see the smoldering look in her eyes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Are you okay? You seem distracted,&quot; she asks quietly as she moves close to me.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm...I'm fine.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Really?&quot;<br /> <br /> Somehow, that one word coaxes the truth from me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Not really. I\u2026um\u2026I'm jealous. Of you and Natalie.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know,&quot; Noriko says. &quot;I knew the moment I listened to your voice mail.&quot;<br /> <br /> I drop my eyes, trying not to meet Noriko's intense gaze. I'm afraid of what will happen if I stare into her eyes too long.<br /> <br /> &quot;I know I shouldn't be jealous, but I\u2014.&quot;<br /> <br /> Noriko steps forward, very close to me, and slides her hands under my shirt to rest on either side of my waist. Surprised, I look up again, and as soon as my eyes meet hers, Noriko seizes the opportunity to kiss me.<br /> <br /> I've completely lost all my will to resist her charms. When our lips part, I whisper, &quot;You can join me on my errand if you want\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> But Noriko places a finger on my lips. &quot;I think Eris would be suspicious if that happened. I'll come by your room later tonight.&quot; Then she turns and glides away toward the TV room, her hips swaying seductively as she retreats.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Eris and I sit nervously side by side on the edge of my bed, waiting for Noriko.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is a bad idea,&quot; I say with a sigh, anxiously biting the corner of my lower lip.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe you're right,&quot; says Eris. &quot;I've never done anything like this before.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Me neither,&quot; I respond.<br /> <br /> &quot;But I'm glad Noriko wanted to\u2026well\u2026be with us.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah.&quot;<br /> <br /> We sit quietly for a few moments. I take Eris' hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;We probably shouldn't do this,&quot; I say.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes, probably.<br /> <br /> &quot;When Noriko stops by, we'll just tell her we've changed our minds.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Yes. That's what we'll do,&quot; Eris nods intently.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good. It's settled then.&quot;<br /> <br /> There is a soft knock on the door. Eris' eyes open wide and she grasps my hand tightly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Oh my god. This is really happening!&quot; she whispers.<br /> <br /> I hesitate a moment, nervous and unsure, and then say, &quot;Come in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Noriko strides in, desire written on every graceful curve of her body, and Eris and I forget all about talking her out of this. It really IS happening.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Noriko, Eris and I lay together on my bed, cuddling and enjoying the warm afterglow of our lovemaking. Eris has drifted off to sleep, her arms wrapped around my waist. I'm about to slip into slumber myself when Noriko carefully slides out of my arms and out of bed. I sigh with a mixture of contentment and disappointment. Eyes half closed, I watch as she gets dressed.<br /> <br /> Before she goes, she sits on the edge of the bed and leans in for a soft, lingering last kiss. Afterward, as she starts to pull away, she hesitates.<br /> <br /> &quot;I love you,&quot; she whispers.<br /> <br /> Then she's gone, up and out the door as quickly and silently as a fleeing shadow. My eyes close, and\u2026<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> \u2026I wake up. The morning sunlight is streaming through my window. Eris and I have changed positions in the night, and now my arms are wrapped around her, my face nuzzled against the back of her neck.<br /> <br /> Suddenly I remember what we did last night. Lingering desire is overwhelmed by confusion and guilt. It was wrong. We shouldn't have done that. And did Noriko say she loved me, or did I dream that?<br /> <br /> &quot;G'morning,&quot; Eris mumbles as she stirs awake. She rolls over and smiles at me.<br /> <br /> &quot;So...we....uh\u2026,&quot; I begin awkwardly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah...&quot; Eris says.<br /> <br /> We stare at each other, trying to figure out what to do or say next. I can tell Eris is troubled by something, and I realize she must feel like the Balehound defeated us last night. I give her comforting smile and brush a strand of hair over her ear. She smiles again, worries forgotten, then kisses me and nestles her head against my neck.<br /> <br /> &quot;I had a good time,&quot; she says.<br /> <br /> I hold Eris tightly. I'm going to have a lot of guilt and confusion to work through today, but right now I just want to enjoy this moment.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Diary Entry, November 31st, 2010<br /> <br /> I slept with my dear friend\u2019s girlfriend today. I really am the strumpet everyone says I am. A backstabbing viper. A whore. A homewrecking jezebel slattern.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t with his permission. Yes, I was being influenced by the Bale Hound, but that is no excuse. Yes, she did the, ahem, heavy lifting, but that is no excuse. Why would I do that? I don\u2019t need more lovers. She is not even a lover. Lots of women out there. Why?<br /> <br /> Rationally, there is a lot going on. I am addled by the Bale Hound. Our \u201cparty\u201d in the hot tub turned into a \u201cduo\u201d when Sara and Angelique just up and left. When I began to think this was a bad idea she turned aggressive and dominant and\u2026Mother of God I never had a chance.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve talked about her hunting methods, but I dare say that made it worse. I knew I was prey, and she was predator. I knew I was quite helpless if she wanted to kill me.<br /> <br /> And she did, make no mistake.<br /> <br /> I am not sure why. She knows I am not a bad person. Hers was the love of a predator though. Hard and fierce, and with little affection. Right now, I wish she had torn out my throat.<br /> <br /> But now here I am. It is over, and I am a traitor. And I recall too clearly that death is not an end, there is no escape. I would put a fucking bullet in my brainpan if it would do more than give him something else to be angry about. Which isn\u2019t to say the barrel of the gun against my face is not soothing, tempting. It calls to me, but I cannot indulge yet another act of selfishness today. Now the question is do I just go tell him an get it over with, or try to not hurt him? Noriko is clearly not looking for a relationship, and I would not pursue one with a woman Doc loved. Shame my morals don\u2019t go so far as to not be a treacherous skank.<br /> <br /> Maybe carving my face a little would leave me having a harder time hurting the people I love. I could cut my nose so easily, right off, or slash my cheeks. God I want to feel the skin split, the blood run down my cheeks, knowing I was protecting those I love would only make the pain sweeter of disfiguring myself. And why stop at the face?<br /> <br /> No\u2026Doc would just feel guilty somehow.<br /> <br /> I should go down. That marvelous, adorable and wise fucking bitch Karen hid my heroin anyway. I don\u2019t know whether to slap her or kiss her. How does she always find my candy anyway, however well I hide them? Regardless, everyone is downstairs. Bright eyes, bright face. You are on, Natalie, don\u2019t show them your pain.<br /> <br /> Raise the curtain!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CL</i><br /> <br /> Aw cheer up Natalie.<br /> <br /> Okay, so heavy RP session was covered well. The main thing was Sara touched on Alexia\u2019s adventures at University\u2026for those who forgot Maria was one of the Reborn Immortals who battles Barry, who hundreds of years ago she was forced into servitude to, and now that he seeks redemption and freed her seeks vengeance. Their feud has come up before, with Jasmine primarily, but only lightly. Gloria came up before when she slept with Chandra at her bachelor party. Both had not come up in awhile so I thought a reminder would be good.<br /> <br /> When Maria threw Gloria into the door frame, I asked if Alexia was going to try and break it up. It was then her player graced us with words of wisdom:<br /> <br /> \u201cI ain\u2019t putting my hand between two bitches fighting!\u201d<br /> <br /> This stopped the game for awhile.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:01:34-08:00","id":816995,"title":"","content":"Getting intense. Any Chaos faction would approve I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-26T11:06:36-08:00","id":816999,"title":"","content":"Oh certainly. The Intensity continued with last night's session (albeit with less sexytimes involved)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T01:48:58-08:00","id":825845,"title":"","content":"Our heroines continue dealing with rivalries and romance as the infection continues on it\u2019s second day. Doc\u2019s player missed again so the girls conflicts continue unabated.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sasha -<br /> <br /> So, day two down. A lot less fun than day one. I mean, there were good parts - Angelique had the realization that her memory of Amy Grant songs had to be from her real self, since the life Bright Shadows imprinted on her had no context for it. So she spent some time listening to Natalie\u2019s extensive Amy Grant collection. I need to look into the rituals that could do something like that. It occurred to me that there\u2019s probably a missing person report out for who Angelique was - I need to do some research. But there\u2019s no way Alice would have spent the day at the library with me so... we went climbing.<br /> <br /> I figured it\u2019s be a nice way to blow off steam, even if not the nicest way, and I figured I\u2019d catch on quick, and show Alice and Eris what I could do. I did, to be fair. Once Alice showed how it was done, it was a fun time and I did well. But Noriko had gotten invited along, of course and... and I didn\u2019t like it, dammit. Is that so bad, that I wanted some time with my Little Red? It\u2019s surely not worth threatening to kill me over, at least. I mean, she didn\u2019t out loud, not with Alice right there but Noriko\u2019s eyes are very expressive.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s not like I said it wasn\u2019t ok for her to come with, I just paused too long for her, I guess. She got to spend last night with Alice too. Those three might as well have been screaming it. As much as Alice talks about not doing that kind of thing... hell, I would be less complicated - I\u2019m not going to try and worm my way into her relationship, I\u2019m not in a monogamous relationship myself, I know she wants me. OK, so Eris makes it a little more complicated, but I could bring her around. But not with Noriko there, pulling tricks Katie could learn a thing from. She made Alice curse, Tatum couldn\u2019t pull her eyes away from her ass, and I almost forgot how upset I was at her, for a second.<br /> <br /> It flustered Alice and Eris enough that I\u2019m surprised they didn\u2019t shapeshift and run off. They did sneak off after we were done getting sharked at pool by Noriko. I don\u2019t think Noriko went after them. I... she was upset. By Natalie being upset, mostly, I think. I tried to help. I pointed out that Natalie was just worried about hurting Doc. Noriko has some plan about convincing Doc it was all her fault. I don\u2019t get the feeling that\u2019s going to fly very far. Even if it does, neither Natalie nor Alice is going to be OK with that result. She didn\u2019t want to hear me though, not to hear her grand plan wasn\u2019t going to make everything better. I should have gone after her, to make sure she was alright. I didn\u2019t even check on my ladies until I was sure Alice wasn\u2019t coming back. Not that it took me too long to realize she was just trying to avoid me.<br /> <br /> Lords and ladies I want this to be over, for Alexia to stop encouraging Alice to kill people for protecting their friends, for Karen to stop going off at people for happening to like boys too, for Natalie to stop calling herself a whore and a bitch - well, for them to do that less and less seriously. I think Natalie had even started feeling a little better, but this thing with Karen is knocking her a little off kilter again. I tried to show her she couldn\u2019t push everyone away - there\u2019s always time for music with my ladies - so I hope I did something right, there at least. By this evening though, even Tatum was starting to snipe back at Karen, though I don\u2019t know if that was the influence or just tensions. I don\u2019t like this.<br /> <br /> Maybe tomorrow will be better. I know my way around the local Underworld, and since Alice wanted to explore some, I can be the guide she and Eris will need. There\u2019s still a couple days of this to get through, of waiting around. We\u2019re taking them one at a time though. Maybe I\u2019ll be able to find the time help her relax some. I\u2019m good at that.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Alice\u2019s Reflections</b><br /> <br /> Breakfast isn't really helping to alleviate the awkwardness, guilt, and confusion from last night. Still, I can't help but share conspiratorial smiles with Eris from time to time. We both enjoyed ourselves.<br /> <br /> Alexia's still out with Chandra and probably won't be back until mid-morning, so Sara made breakfast. She really outdid herself with a hearty, country-style meal for us: scrambled eggs, bacon, salted ham biscuits. It's good. I think she's trying to impress me.<br /> <br /> Angelique breaks the awkward tension by telling us that she's remembered something from her life before the Balehound changed her. She recalls some music that she once listened to. I suggest that she might remember more if she listens to the music again, and Natalie offers to help out with her extensive music collection.<br /> <br /> I look up from my plate and find Noriko watching me. There's a passion to her gaze, but I can't quite read her expression. I remember her whispering &quot;I love you&quot; before she left last night, but I'm still not sure whether I dreamed it or not. The way she's looking at me now, though, quickens my pulse. I don't think I was dreaming.<br /> <br /> I blush, and Sara notices. Her expression shifts almost imperceptibly, her eyes narrowing slightly and her full lips pursing in a slight pout. Is she jealous? I didn't think she was capable of jealousy.<br /> <br /> Then again, I didn't think I was capable of what I did last night. The Balehound is doing a number on all of us.<br /> <br /> &quot;So, I was thinking that we should go climbing on the cliff outside the house later today. After lunch, maybe,&quot; Sara suggests to me and Eris. She's sitting next to me, and as she makes the suggestion, she places a hand on the small of my back. It strikes me as a surprisingly intimate gesture, and my breath catches momentarily.<br /> <br /> &quot;That sounds fun,&quot; says Eris brightly.<br /> <br /> &quot;Yeah, it's about time we did that.&quot; I take a deep breath, which helps me regain my composure. &quot;Besides, I'd like to see how you handle it before we head into the Underworld. There's a lot of good caving down there, but I don't want you getting in over your head. As it is, I'm thinking Eris and I might disappear into the Underworld for the next couple days. Maybe get away from some of this Balehound madness.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Sounds fun,&quot; Sara gives me a coy smile. &quot;I'll come along as your guide.&quot;<br /> <br /> Then I notice that Noriko isn't staring at me anymore. She's staring at Sara, and it's not a good stare. Uh oh. They're fighting over me. What do I do now? I've never had to deal with anything like this before.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Honestly, it's never been easy for me to find girlfriends. In high school, it was out of the question. As far as I know, I was the only lesbian in my school, and even if that wasn't the case, I was raised in a conservative family in a conservative town, so it never really occurred to me that I could go out with another girl. It wasn't until after high school, once my family moved to Phoenix and I moved out on my own, that I really accepted who I was and started looking for a partner. But it was never easy for me, and things didn't usually work out, not until I met Kitty.<br /> <br /> I was in love with Kitty. But of course, she was just using me. And then I killed her.<br /> <br /> Things were a little easier in Portland, but my work with the Dead Judges there didn't exactly make it easy for me to build any real relationships. It's not like Cassidy and I fell for each other as soon as we met. At first, she didn't even like me all that much, and besides, she was involved with some guy who ended up being a complete jerk. He cheated on her and they broke up, and by then Cassidy and I had become close. We started flirting. I don't even think we realized we were doing it until one night when we were all hanging out at a bar, celebrating a job well done after we laid a ghost to rest. Randy, who was probably the most down-to-earth of the Judges, said something like, &quot;Would you two just get a room already?&quot; I think that's when Cassidy and I both realized something was blossoming between us.<br /> <br /> But that's ancient history now. The point is, I've always struggled to find relationships. And now Noriko and Sara are fighting over me while my beloved girlfriend is sitting right next to me?<br /> <br /> I have no idea how to handle this.<br /> <br /> <i>I'll tell you how to handle this. Give in to your desire for Noriko. She is your kindred spirit, a fellow hunter and murderer. Your perfect mate. Together, the two of you could do a great deal of good slaying the wicked. She is the only one who understands your bloodlust, who shares your need to kill. You don't need Eris, though if you wish to keep her I don't see the harm. Sara is unworthy of you, though. She is a weak, compassionate creature who would chain your hunter's soul with her harlot's wiles.</i><br /> <br /> I want to tell the Grasping Huntress to be quiet. I don't like her dismissing Eris and insulting Sara, but part of me agrees with her opinion on Noriko. Her whispers seep into my thoughts and blend seamlessly with the desires that tug relentlessly at my heart. I try to sort out what I'm really feeling, but I can't.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Noriko and Sara have been glued to me and Eris all morning. But I need to talk to Noriko alone. I need to find out whether what she said last night was real or a dream. So when Alexia calls everyone in for lunch, I excuse myself to get the climbing gear ready for our excursion.<br /> <br /> Noriko takes the bait, and she's waiting by the door to my room by the time I get there. Even though I expected it, I'm still caught off-guard, and don't know what to say. That's when Noriko takes my head in her hands a kisses me.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm sorry,&quot; she says as our lips part, but I don't like the sound of those words, so I wrap my arms around her and kiss her again. The second kiss becomes a third, but then we both realize we have to stop, and we push apart.<br /> <br /> &quot;We, uh, have to get down to lunch,&quot; I say breathlessly.<br /> <br /> Noriko nods, but we just stare softly at one another for a few moments.<br /> <br /> &quot;I...I thought I dreamed you saying 'I love you' last night,&quot; I say, hesitantly, &quot;but it wasn't a dream, was it?&quot;<br /> <br /> Noriko shakes her head. &quot;No. It wasn't.&quot;<br /> <br /> I take a deep breath. I am lost at sea and I don't even know where the horizon is, much less which way is north. I place a hand on my forehead and sink back against the door frame.<br /> <br /> &quot;What are we going to do?&quot; I ask, desperately.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't know,&quot; says Noriko as she leans against the opposite side of the door. &quot;I guess we'll figure something out. I've never done anything like this before either.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Really?&quot; I ask, surprised. &quot;Even\u2026like, last night?&quot; I feel stupid even asking the question.<br /> <br /> &quot;No. That was a first for me too.&quot; Noriko actually looks embarrassed. I find it strangely comforting and incredibly endearing. I reach out and take her hand.<br /> <br /> &quot;I don't want to hurt Doc, and Eris\u2026Eris means more to me than anything. But, still, I\u2026&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I know,&quot; says Noriko. &quot;I haven't stopped loving Doc.&quot;<br /> <br /> We gaze at each other awhile longer.<br /> <br /> &quot;Come hunting with me tonight,&quot; Noriko says suddenly.<br /> <br /> I almost agree, then I remember my plans with Eris.<br /> <br /> &quot;I\u2026I want to. But I can't. I already have\u2026plans.<br /> <br /> Noriko tries to hide it, but I can see the disappointment in her eyes.<br /> <br /> &quot;Maybe tomorrow night? Or sometime soon?&quot; I offer.<br /> <br /> Noriko smiles, but it doesn't completely erase the disappointment. &quot;It's a standing invitation,&quot; she says.<br /> <br /> &quot;Good,&quot; I smile. &quot;Come on, let's get the gear out and then go down to lunch.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, after unpacking and readying all the climbing gear, we walk down the long hall toward the stairway hand in hand, enjoying a few more moments of intimacy before we rejoin the others.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> It was fun to get out and climb, even if the weather was unbearably cold. I don't know why I choose to live in the arctic north, but it's clearly a lapse of judgment on my part. No one else seems to mind it all that much, especially Eris. The tension between Noriko and Sara is thick, though, and it's stressing me out more and more as the day wears on.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, dinner provides a welcome distraction from my romantic troubles as Alexia explains to us what she's learned about the people who set the trap for Chandra. She's managed to track down the guy who taught Gloria how to set the trap, someone named Ben Deloria. The rest of the krewe seems to know exactly who he is, but his name is new to me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Anyway,&quot; says Alexia. &quot;They tried to kill my wife! We have to stop them.&quot; The way she says that last part makes it a lethal threat.<br /> <br /> At first, I think Alexia is overreacting. Then the Huntress speaks up.<br /> <br /> <i>She's right. We have to protect the krewe. If someone threatens us, we have to fight back.</i><br /> <br /> The Huntress makes a good point, but I'm pretty sure Ben and Gloria were just trying to protect themselves.<br /> <br /> <i>Nonsense. These people have tried to trap one of us. They tried to kill Chandra. You know quite well the dedication required to kill someone. It takes intent and purpose. It is not a task undertaken lightly. It marks you. These people are murderers, and you know as well as I that had their trap succeeded, they would not have a shed a tear over their victim. In fact, they would have rejoiced in Chandra's suffering. And then who would they try to kill? Would they set a trap for Eris? Or perhaps for Noriko? Would they use silver to make her bleed?</i><br /> <br /> The thought that these people might be a threat to Eris or Noriko infuriates me.<br /> <br /> <i>Having killed once, they will kill again. They will hunt our kind. Our friends. Alexia is right to fear them. And so should you. It would be better to end this threat now.</i><br /> <br /> I feel a familiar sense of deadly purpose start to settle on me. Eris seems distracted by Alexia, but Sara notices and puts a questioning hand on my arm. Her touch snaps me back to my senses.<br /> <br /> <i>They must die\u2026</i><br /> <br /> No! This is insane! Ben and Gloria haven't done anything. They're just scared and trying to protect themselves from some sort of supernatural threat they don't understand. They definitely don't deserve to die.<br /> <br /> I suddenly tune back in to the conversation.<br /> <br /> &quot;I'm not going to let them murder Chandra,&quot; says Alexia, absently stabbing her steak knife into the table. There is murder in her eyes. It's a look I know well; I've seen it in the mirror enough times.<br /> <br /> &quot;Wait a minute!&quot; I say. &quot;Alexia, listen to yourself. You sound like me, and that should scare the heck out of you. Is that really what you want?&quot;<br /> <br /> Alexia stops like I've just slapped her. She suddenly realizes how psychotic she sounded. &quot;Oh my god,&quot; she mutters to herself. &quot;You're right.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Those kids at the college are just trying to protect themselves. They don't know Chandra like we do. They think she's a monster. Gloria clearly doesn't like being preyed upon, but who can blame her.&quot; I glance at Chandra. &quot;No offense.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sara and Natalie voice their agreement. They seem relieved that we've managed to derail Alexia's thirst for vengeance.<br /> <br /> Nevertheless, I'm troubled by the fact that a part of me still wants to kill Ben.<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> Despite the chilly winter weather outside, it's cozy and warm indoors. Noriko, Sara, Eris and I have decided to play pool, and Natalie's friend Tatum is hanging out with us because Karen and Natalie are arguing.<br /> <br /> I've played my share of pool in the past. My brothers taught me, and I've gotten some practice in various bars. I run Eris through the basics while Noriko runs upstairs to fetch her own custom pool cue. That's a bad sign. My guess is that she's going to absolutely destroy the rest of us.<br /> <br /> Sara takes advantage of Noriko's absence to flirt heavily with me. She's been a bit aggressive all day. If she's intimidated by Noriko's threatening looks, she's not showing it. There's something sweet and comfortable and inviting about the way she's paying attention to me. Her fleeting, flirtatious touches leave my heart racing, and in any other circumstances, I'd fall for her charms in an instant. But with Eris here and the my confusion over my feelings for Noriko and what happened last night\u2026I'm just overwhelmed! It's been draining, and the longer the day goes on, the more I just want to escape it all.<br /> <br /> I quietly say as much to Eris and she nods.<br /> <br /> &quot;I usually turn into a wolf and run into the forest when I'm overwhelmed,&quot; she tells me.<br /> <br /> &quot;That sounds like a great plan,&quot; I say. I'm not joking. I seriously consider doing just that, only I can't exactly turn into a wolf. I'm sure a flock of birds would do.<br /> <br /> Then Noriko returns. She is dressed to kill in a tight baby-tee and a pair of form-fitting denim shorts. Everyone else in the room just stares as she makes her way to the game room's stereo and put on AC/DC's &quot;You Shook Me All Night Long.&quot; The subtext isn't lost on me.<br /> <br /> She turns and props her custom pool cue across her shoulders, posing just so to show off her amazing curves. I go weak in the knees.<br /> <br /> <i>You are made for each other,</i> whispers the Huntress.<br /> <br /> I can't help myself. &quot;Hot DAMN, girl,&quot; I exclaim in appreciation. Noriko gives me a catty smile.<br /> <br /> Then I realize that I just said a swear word. I turn bright red and clamp my hands over my mouth. Everyone else bursts out laughing.<br /> <br /> &quot;That's our Little Red,&quot; Sara says as she stands on tiptoe to give me a flirtatious kiss on the cheek. &quot;We'll make a sailor out of you yet.&quot;<br /> <br /> * * * * *<br /> <br /> After Noriko soundly beats the rest of us in pool, we retire to the TV room to relax in front a movie and a roaring fire. Things between Natalie and Karen haven't improved any, so poor Tatum is still with us.<br /> <br /> The tension is still overwhelming. I can't handle it anymore. I don't know what to do about my feelings for Noriko or her feelings for me. I don't know how to respond to Sara's increasingly aggressive advances. I'm practically clinging to Eris as we snuggle on the couch.<br /> <br /> Eris senses how unhappy I've become. She's very good at reading me.<br /> <br /> &quot;Do you want to escape?&quot; she asks.<br /> <br /> &quot;Turn into wolves and run up to our room? Yes, please.&quot; I'm practically pleading. Eris smiles. She takes my hand and we get up off the couch and head toward the door. Noriko and Sara both perk up, and I fear they might insist on following.<br /> <br /> &quot;Alice and I are going to get some fresh air,&quot; Eris says. Is there a hint of warning in her voice?<br /> <br /> &quot;We'll be back shortly,&quot; I say. &quot;Keep the fire warm.&quot; Of course, I have no intention of returning before tomorrow morning, but I'm hoping no one else will follow us.<br /> <br /> Once we're heading upstairs, I tell Eris to go to our room and wait for me.<br /> <br /> &quot;I have a surprise for you,&quot; I say with a hint of mischief. &quot;Let me go get ready, and I'll be right in.&quot;<br /> <br /> Eris seems curious, but she heads off to the room and I go get the package I picked up last night when I ran my secret errand. It's a sexy Red Riding Hood costume with a tight bodice, fishnet stockings and a very short skirt. Just putting it on makes me anxious. I can't believe I'm doing something so\u2026kinky. It's really not like me at all. I just hope Eris likes it.<br /> <br /> When I open the door and step into the room, Eris' eyes grow wide.<br /> <br /> &quot;My, what big eyes you have,&quot; I say, with a coy smile.<br /> <br /> Eris likes the costume very much indeed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Diary Entry: December 1st, 2010<br /> <br /> Today was better, but not much. I mean I feel better, but there was less\u2026anway.<br /> <br /> I have a plan for how to solve my problems with Doc, and give me a shot at what I want without an unacceptable situation, hopefully. I just need to bring my wiles on point at the right time. Should fix everything, right?<br /> <br /> Except that Karen has lost her damn mind. All days she has been hounding me about interest in Doc. Do I talk in my sleep or something? How did she know? What\u2019s more, she has more or less threatened to bring up my fooling around with Jacob to Alice. I never slept with Jacob, but toward the end there not all my encounters with him were chaste. But what does it fucking matter? We had fun, and he made some time with a girl he had admired on the internet for like a decade. Worse fates could befall him.<br /> <br /> But Karen had to keep me on edge, had to question my self-identification in front of Alexia, had to imply something about Jacob in front of Alice. Just had to keep making fucking trouble. Why?<br /> <br /> Apparently she even set Tatum off.<br /> <br /> But if this diary is all whining and misery I know I will never crack it again. So other observations:<br /> <br /> It appears I was not the only one Noriko seduced. Alice and Eris could not have been more obvious this morning. I would not have known from looking at Noriko. Their clumsy attempts to be subtle were sort of endearing. The only troubling thing was Sara. I swear she seemed jealous. I was going to talk to her, but that group seemed determined to stick together, and Sara is a big girl. She can handle herself. Herself and a lot of other people. I am not going to be the one to make her feel guilty about her feelings. If she needs help, I will help. But otherwise I will leave her be.<br /> <br /> The sweetie did come in while I was playing the piano though. She was doing her best to comfort me. I love Sara so. It\u2019s really not just sex, Sara is a wonderful, sweet, caring person, and I think people need to appreciate what a wonderful giving person she is. Even if she is a perv, which is not a bad thing done right, and she does. Just a pity I had just had a row with Karen and was feeling prickly.<br /> <br /> Noriko showed great concern for me today. I told her I was fine, but I don\u2019t think she believed me. I hope she and Sara don\u2019t clash too much. There is definite tension, and not the usual kind people have with Sara.<br /> <br /> Oh, and had a magical adventure with Alexia, involving our Manipulative Mage Maria and her Menservants. Jimbo and R.L. have not changed, bless them. Earlier I had determined Ben DeLoria, the man who Bonnie Lynn had an eye on, was involved, after he asked Cindy Toc about Thai mysticism. Also something about Eve Reeves that seemed nonsensical. I do need to \u201csee\u201d Cindy again. Anyway, we went out, there was Maria, Jimbo, and R.L., and they were at their\u2026Jimbo and R.L.-est. The charming yet annoying chivalry did not grate too much, though the posturing was a bit much. We got confirmation Ben and Gloria were involved ion the trap, and no sign from the trap that Cindy was. We thanked Maria and Beavis and Butthead for their help and headed back.<br /> <br /> Alexia is hell-bent on dealing harshly with the problem. Fortunately Alice was good about pointing out her need for violence. Speaking of violence, I am not going to think about why Tavia was in such an amazingly good mood. I just won\u2019t.<br /> <br /> Oh, \u201cAngelique\u201d has realized Amy Grant was not from her false memories, and must be from the memories of who she really was. I\u2019ve given her some files with my collection. Maybe it will help. When we have our minds back, it will be time to comb missing person reports. Also, more music exploration; music is linked to memory after all.<br /> <br /> Now, it\u2019s time to kick back with some Sisters of Mercy and see if Karen decides to return to the Temple of Love.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CLI</i><br /> <br /> Roleplaying heavy with few die rolls. Most that occurred were Alexia and Natalie at the University. Last session had a recap on who those characters were, adding Jimbo and R.L. originally interacted with Jasmine several times.<br /> <br /> Stay tuned for next time, where Natalie has a harem explosion and Alice and Alexia visit the Underworld. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T13:30:07-08:00","id":826221,"title":"","content":"Things are quite dour at this situation - I'm almost frightened of what the aftermath may be, outside influences or no. Still, it sounds like everyone is having fun roleplaying this all out, and I can't wait to see the end result. Good twist for Angelique figuring out a bit of her past, and great way of giving the character some agency without blowing holes into her assumed identity. <br /> <br /> Is there a supernatural resistance at play with the balehound's curse, if Karen is being influenced more than the others, or is it just that since Karen has more reservations she's being affected more overtly (and more continuously than, say, a certain smiler turning into a slasher)? I'm unaware of the limitations of the balehound's power in this case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T16:19:55-08:00","id":826373,"title":"","content":"Balehound's power is a plot device.<br /> <br /> Karen has a strong dominant personality. She likes freedom for herself, and is willing to compromise with others so long as they don't control her. Natalie feels a need to be controlled despite having a very strong personality herself. That gives she and Karen an <i>intense </i>chemistry. However, Natalie has her own rights and privileges (as any Sub does in a healthy D/s relationship) and she has the privilege of sleeping with whoever she chooses. Natalie's issues are such that she is not commonly drawn to men. She likes looking at them, and feels attraction sometimes but it is uncommon, and Karen feels threatened by men and Natalie's desire for children. Karen also knows that while she does not pursue it her feelings for Doc are not platonic, and are reciprocated. That relationship is quashed by Natalie's issues with men and the fact Doc is...not a very sensitive person (though he tries) and a poor listener. This is the biggest hot button their (Natalie and Karen's) relationship has. Natalie's fooling around with Jacob made Karen angry, but when he left he was essentially out of the picture, and Karen is not a rage machine. However, her worry that Natalie is not over Doc (sort of true) that she might leave her for Doc (never gonna happen) and knowing Natalie wants to get pregnant NOW (fair cop) means she is walking on needles. Hot needles. Her worry about their relationship, jealousy over men in general and Doc in particular, her being only 20 and not super worldly, has her being a powder keg.<br /> <br /> Doc's player has had to miss the last thee (including last night's) games for completely different reasons due to different stuff coming up has had him outside the house, which has honestly made Karen both less twitchy (Natalie can't seduce him if he is not there) and more (Natalie is pining for him somewhat) . I kinda hate having had to run without him, but if I didn't we would not have gamed yet since the new year.<br /> <br /> If the Smiler/Slasher thing is referring to Alexia, I'd have to get her player to explain her thinking with Alexia's behavior. The main thing is she decided to investigate (not unusual) and is having her react more violently than she otherwise would, but being Alexia still is not rushing off to kill. And Sara may seem unaffected, but she is in fact compromising her morals with pursuing Alice, which leads to a huge breakdown you will see next session.<br /> <br /> Does that help?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T00:55:33-08:00","id":826635,"title":"","content":"Quite well; also, I apologize for asking about the Balehound power when you've written previously a few times on what it was and that it was homebrewed. I hate being the guy who asks the questions people have already elaborated on. And yes, the Smiler/Slasher line did refer to Alexia; I admit, I was lazy with looking up the character's name when I was writing the statement (and I was getting ready for a five hour drive to return home) and I like alliteration, so I went with Smiler instead of Cupcake.<br /> <br /> ...and now that I've written that, I'm imagining at how insanely creepy Alexia would be if she was an actual Slasher. Smiling, friendly, wielding a cleaver and being absolutely creative with whatever &quot;food&quot; items she had in front of her. And for some reason singing &quot;Kill The Wabbit&quot; as she did her work. I dunno, my imagination's weird.<br /> <br /> It is a shame that Doc's player hasn't been able to attend, but real life can't be avoided. It has happened a fair number of times to the players of a group I play with for a <i>very</i> homebrewed D&amp;D game (which has been fitted to play Homestuck, Zelda, Fallout and Star Wars), and we usually have the character either &quot;fall back&quot;, aka being elsewhere while the active players work on the main plot, or be played by another player in the group during battles/encounters. Nobody wants to cancel a game due to someone missing, but at the same time it's not fun missing someone from a long running game either.<br /> <br /> Off topic, but I can't decide if doing a game online or having people come to a physical game has more pitfalls or not regarding scheduling; on the one hand, people can do it from the comfort of their own homes, but it also means that if they're across the world it can make for some bad sleep schedules. Physical means you need to set time apart for traveling somewhere local, but it also has the advantage of everyone being in the same timezone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-09T01:20:52-08:00","id":826642,"title":"","content":"Oh no it is fine, you are good.<br /> <br /> Oh yea, &quot;Angry Alexia is terrifying&quot; certainly has come up a few times now with the past few sessions.<br /> <br /> Missing player tends to be okay in the Sandboxy games I run. In Geist, Changeling or Demon they can simply be doing something else; personal business. Golden Eagle is sometimes harder, but even then it can be done part of the time; depends on if they are, say, chilling in Vienna or exploring the valley of kings. Our rule of thumb is if half the players, rounded up, are present the game is on.<br /> <br /> I have some players that deeply dislike long distance gaming. My general experience in scheduling online events (mainly raids) has been people tend to be more lassaiz-faire about attending an online gathering pre-scheduled at a certain time than a face to face meeting. Focus also seems to wane. I am sure it works for some people. if I lost my local group, I would be doing it in a damn heartbeat. Also, just for me, having the game room for gaming adds something to the whole thing, it puts me in the zone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T13:32:31-08:00","id":828937,"title":"","content":"Reading the accounts makes me want to laugh evilly.<br /> <br /> And I have the energy/brain power to do so that' been lacking the past months, so that's a boon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:13:15-08:00","id":828975,"title":"","content":"Sorry you have had a rough time, glad you are feeling better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T15:51:02-08:00","id":828991,"title":"","content":"Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T15:15:50-08:00","id":834654,"title":"","content":"Greetings from the west coast! I am on vacation this week so commentary for journals will by necessity be brief.<br /> <br /> Unlike some cases, Sara's story took place in game on camera. The story covers her thoughts and feelings better though.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara's Letters</b><br /> <br /> The dark haired girl was curled up on the couch, waiting. She was hopeful - it really sounded like Alice was leaning towards a trip to the Underworld. Sara spared a glance in the direction Noriko had gone, concern and jealousy warring on her face. She\u2019d had the moral victory of having suggested Alice stay back, for all that had helped Noriko\u2019s mood, but she couldn\u2019t stamp down her feelings of satisfaction.<br /> <br /> Sara looked up when there was a noise at the door, setting aside the book she\u2019d been pretending to read. She smiled at Natalie, standing to give her a kiss. \u201cHey, love. How are you doing? Tatum said it got a little rough this morning.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smiled brittlely. \u201cIt did. But that\u2019s about par for the course at the moment.\u201d She sighed inwardly as she noticed the younger girl\u2019s attention bouncing between her and the door. \u201cSara, dear, Alice has decided to go to the Underworld. She needs to get away from all this. She\u2019s already told Noriko - she went running away crying.\u201d Natalie looked into her eyes.<br /> <br /> Sara bit her lip and looked down. It was a conflict laden time and she didn\u2019t want Natalie to see any more of the conflict between guilt and triumph that she already had. \u201cI guess I should go get ready then.\u201d She started moving.<br /> <br /> Natalie moved to block her path. \u201cSara... she wants to go alone. Well, with Eris.\u201d She steeled herself for another lover\u2019s anger.<br /> <br /> But instead, Sara ignored the implication. \u201cThat\u2019s... that\u2019s not safe. I mean, Alice can certainly handle herself.\u201d A wicked grin grew on her face. She pushed it back. \u201cBut still, having a guide would be best. I\u2019ve had the tour, and I have Jasmine\u2019s maps memorized, so...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAlexia will go with her. She knows the local Underworld as well.\u201d Natalie paused as dark jealousy broke over her wife\u2019s face. \u201cAlexia is going with Alice because Alice has no interest in her. She needs to actually get away - from Noriko, Angelique.\u201d She waited until Sara looked at her. \u201cAnd you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave Natalie a look of hurt anger. \u201cI can control myself, despite what some people think, Natalie.\u201d She managed to stop herself from yelling, just barely. \u201cWho are you... I thought you\u2019d know me better.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie sighed and held Sara\u2019s angry gaze. \u201cLove, she explicitly asked that you specifically not come.\u201d Sara stepped back, disbelieving. She tried to lighten the blow. \u201cShe wants to be alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara bit her lip, not meeting Natalie\u2019s eyes as she muttered, \u201cShe didn\u2019t want to be alone a couple of nights ago.\u201d She shot an angry look towards the upper floor.<br /> <br /> \u201cSara, she said no.\u201d Natalie\u2019s tone was loving, but stern. \u201cAre you going to respect her wishes in this?\u201d<br /> <br /> The raven haired girl stopped, the color draining from her face. \u201cI...\u201d Her breath came quick and her eyes flickered from side to side, all the world like a trapped animal. \u201cShe... she did. And...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie reached a comforting hand towards her. Sara winced away from it, wrapping her arms around herself. The Virgin Sacrifice smiled, pleased. <i>A knowing sacrifice of poorer stuff is better received by your gods. This is the better choice.<br /> </i><br /> \u2018Fuck you! This is not about sacrifice, this is not about the gods!\u2019 Sara took a step back from Natalie\u2019s concern, trying to get her breathing under control. \u2018There are many things I will give you, and them. My truest self, my morals - those are not on the table.\u2019<br /> <br /> The Virgin Sacrifice faded into the background of her mind with a knowing smile as Natalie tried to pull Sara out of it. \u201cLove...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m fine.\u201d Sara ran a hand across her face. She glanced up at Natalie\u2019s disbelieving face. She looked away quickly. \u201cI\u2019ll be fine.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie sighed and got out her phone. After a quick message, she looked at Sara with a comforting smile. \u201cI\u2019m sure you will be. We all will be.\u201d She raised an eyebrow and quirked her lips. \u201cBut even Doc is a better liar than that.\u201d Sara wouldn\u2019t look at her, and held herself tighter. Natalie took a step forward. Sara took one back. \u201cYou need to relax. How about a bubble bath, to clear your head?\u201d She moved around, not going any closer to Sara, but moving out from between her and the door. \u201cI\u2019ve got some bubble bath with a little LSD in it.\u201d Sara looked up, intrigued despite herself. \u201cI\u2019m going to be nearby - we can talk if you want.\u201d<br /> <br /> The strawberry scented woman led Sara up to the bathroom, letting her maintain her distance. As the water started running, Natalie gave Sara a caring smile and left, sitting outside the door, leaning against the wall.<br /> <br /> Sara let out a deep breath, sinking into the warm water. She took in another deep breath, and let it out. And another. The bubble bath smelled faintly of strawberries itself. The bubbles sparkled under the bathroom lights, flickering through a range of deep blues and purples. She was trying desperately not to think about how close she\u2019d come to raping one of her best friends. About how hard she\u2019d been trying to. She bit her lip until it bled, curling up into a ball.<br /> <br /> There was quiet for a time, as Natalie gave Sara space in case she wanted to talk, but after a few minutes of silence, Sara heard Natalie begin to sing. She pitched her voice to carry through the door and no further. Sara closed her eyes, relaxing into the sound of the Ballyeamon Cradle Song.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cMo chroi? My little Sara, where are you?\u201d The older woman called out softly, wandering around the private area of the carnival. She stopped at a rustling from underneath the fortune teller\u2019s trailer. \u201cSara, is that you? Come on out now.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot if you\u2019re mad at me Maimeo.\u201d The girl child\u2019s voice came from just out of sight.<br /> <br /> Grainne smiled and crouched near where the child was. \u201cAnd why is it would I be mad at you, mo chroi?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBecause I hit that country boy.\u201d She sounded frightened and small. \u201cAnd his mother was very loud.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd why did you do a thing like that?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara paused. \u201cI didn\u2019t want to kiss him. I told him no but he wouldn\u2019t leave me alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAh, I see.\u201d The old woman stood up. \u201cA leanbh, come on out please? My knees are not what they once were.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara crawled out from beneath the trailer, covered in dirt. She ran a hand across her face, smearing more mud on it. She looked down, nudging a rock with her foot. \u201cI\u2019m not in trouble then?\u201d<br /> <br /> Grainne pulled out a scrap of cloth and wiped Sara\u2019s face for her. \u201cNo, Sara of mine. As far as I am concerned, you will never be in trouble for defending yourself and you will certainly never have to kiss anyone you don\u2019t want to. Remember that, mo chroi. You, and everyone else, are your own selves and not beholden to other\u2019s pleasures.\u201d She took Sara\u2019s hand. \u201cAnd if some foolish country boy tries to tell you differently, knee him in the balls and let his loud mother be damned.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled up at her grandmother and squeezed her hand. \u201cThanks Maimeo. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd I you, mo chroi. Always remember that, as well.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s eye fluttered open as the last notes fell away. Natalie let the silence sit for a few minutes, then began another song and Sara let herself get lost in the music from beyond the door as it mixed with the sounds of the bubbles.<br /> <br /> After a few more songs and pauses, Natalie fell quiet. She listened for a few minutes before calling out. \u201cSara?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMmm?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know I love you, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUm.\u201d Sara took a moment to gather her bearings. \u201cYeah, I know. I love you too, Natalie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie moved closer to the door. \u201cI don\u2019t know what you\u2019re planning to do tonight, dear, but... I need you. I need you right now, with... with everything.\u201d Natalie could hear Sara getting out of the bath and drying off. \u201cEveryone\u2019s gone until tomorrow afternoon, it will be just us two.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara came out, wrapped up in a couple of towels. Natalie\u2019s brow knit - she\u2019d never seen Sara wear a towel in the entire time she\u2019d been there - but Sara didn\u2019t meet her eyes, just moved past her, grabbing an oversized sweatshirt and a pair of pajama pants and putting them on, her back to Natalie. She stayed turned away from her wife, her head down. \u201cNatalie, I...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie watched her carefully. Guilt was etched into every line of her body, and fear, fear that she wouldn\u2019t be able to see the line as she crossed it, fear that she would push too far. Again. Sara eventually turned around, hunching her shoulders and retreating into herself again. Natalie noticed the bright spot on her lip where she was not quite still bleeding and searched her lover\u2019s eyes, afraid to find familiar self destructive impulses.<br /> <br /> She relaxed, slightly, when she didn\u2019t find them, just an unrelenting desire to put herself somewhere outside her own control. She considered calling Karen, but she knew the two of them well enough to know that their play was not the kind of thing Sara was looking for. And that if it did reach that point, it would deal serious damage to their relationship.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know, love.\u201d Natalie looked vulnerable and lonely. \u201cPlease, I need you to be here, I need to not be alone.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI need some time, Natalie. Love. I just need...\u201d Sara was torn and the destruction of the certainty she\u2019d felt these past few days, that aside from some timing issues, she was immune to the Balehound\u2019s influence, that the idea of sexual \u2018transgression\u2019 was for other, less enlightened people left her doubting everything about herself. She wanted to be with someone who she could not possibly coerce, someone she had no control over. But Natalie looked at her pleadingly. \u201cI\u2019ll be fine, Elizabeth won\u2019t hurt me, not really. And I can\u2019t...\u201d She looked away.<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s face fell. \u201cIt\u2019s not safe, Sara. This influence is infectious. What would it do to Elizabeth? Please. I love you.\u201d Natalie stepped forward. Sara moved back again. \u201cWe can do things separately, I just need you here.\u201d Her voice sounded small.<br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s shoulder slumped. \u201cNatalie...\u201d She took a deep breath. \u201cHow about a movie? Or some TV show?\u201d<br /> <br /> A grateful smile came over Natalie\u2019s face and she gestured for Sara to lead the way. Sara curled up in an armchair, while her wife sat on the couch. They eventually decided on Spartacus. Natalie even got a smile out of Sara when she promised to introduce her to Lucy Lawless, the next time she was anywhere nearby.<br /> <br /> After going to get popcorn during a break, Sara sat back down on the couch, on the opposite end from Natalie. She smiled, but hid it from Sara by looking down at her phone. As the afternoon went on, the two moved closer together, with a few false starts and moments of backtracking when Sara realized that was happening.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Natalie\u2019s head lay on Sara\u2019s lap while she rested her arm on Natalie\u2019s side, skin to skin. Natalie was afraid to break the moment and send her love running away again. So she even pretended not to notice when Sara started to cry.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie's Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Diary Entry: December 2nd, 2010<br /> <br /> Day three, no one has attacked each other.<br /> <br /> My fighting with Karen has not improved. After sleeping separately (I had Tatum with me) I attempted to work out some sort of reconciliation this morning. No dice. Another loud, angry argument. She remained furious with me, and ordered me to not leave the house today. Eventually she stormed off. After seeing to me, Tatum went after her, and came back to report she had gone to the townhouse.<br /> <br /> Probably for the best, we have really not been getting along. We should temporarily separate before we say something else we can\u2019t take back.<br /> <br /> Tatum is relatively stable, if very intimidated. She has been just trying to keep her head above water. Most people ignore her. To be fair, they are distracted.<br /> <br /> Sara is having a rough time. See, Alice needed to go to the Underworld (we all do) and Sara offered to go with her, even when less crazy. Which makes sense; Sara is fond of Alice above and beyond wanting to jump into her trousers. But Alice decided she needed to go without anyone who was stressing her, and that included Sara and Noriko. This ultimately wasn\u2019t a rejection; it was a cry for space.<br /> <br /> Both took it badly. I don\u2019t know the specifics with Noriko, but she ran off weeping. Alice was dreading talking to Sara too so I took point on that so she could focus on her trip. I sent Tatum to check on Noriko and went to talk to Sara. Sara argued with me, which I sort of expected, but when I outright told her Alice said no, she argued fiercely, citing that Alice and Noriko had shared a bed. Which isn\u2019t like Sara at all. Sara has no trouble finding lovers, nor accepting people not going her way. So I threw in her face her unwillingness to accept Alice\u2019s decision.<br /> <br /> As I say, she took it badly. She withdrew from my touch and backed away. That was heartbreaking. With Karen flipping the hell out at me, I needed my other wife. That is part of her job, helping me when Karen can\u2019t. But I am not the weak woman who lay dying on that hotel floor. I drew on my strength and pushed my pain, doubling from Karen\u2019s angry rejection and Sara\u2019s, away.<br /> <br /> I texted Alice to take Alexia in my stead, and offered Sara some of my super relaxing bubble bath with mild hallucinogenic qualities. It has gotten me through more than one crushing mood problem, and while a bit difficult to replace Sara needed it. I sang to her too, some songs I remember her teaching me from her childhood. My making peace with my mother and daughter had helped me, and I am bolstered now by my memories of my youth, so I hoped it would have a similar effect for her.<br /> <br /> Eventually she emerged (wearing a towel with only me around which was a quick twist to a dagger already present) and we negotiated. I expressed I wanted her to be with me. Her behavior, and the fight with Karen, had taken an emotional toll on me, and despite my need for company, I knew Karen had needs also so I sent Tatum to her. I eventually got Sara to watch a TV series with me. We watched Spartacus, which had Lucy Lawless (someone Sara is a fan of) and given I had briefly \u201cmet\u201d Lucy (by \u201cmet\u201d I mean we were in the same room) I talked about her actual accent. She seems nice enough so I promised to introduce Sara to her.<br /> <br /> Eventually, Sara cuddled a bit, cried a bit, and we retired. Goddess willing, things with my wives will be better in the morning, Alice and Alexia will arrive safely home, and we can put a stop to this tomorrow night without any more major fighting.<br /> <br /> Maybe?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLII</i><br /> <br /> Still no Doc. I think it was the Superbowl that time.<br /> <br /> Mostly RP. Natalie is a social titan. Sara never stood a chance. In the Underworld, Alice and Alexia met Dulcinea, a Beast, who I used bee imagery with. I regrettably don't have much time and am not on my main machine to discuss the Underworld part, and no Alice Journal. Short version is they explored, did a lot of rock climbing, and studiously avoided talking to the other Krewe to not accidentally infect them with the bale hounds effect. And met Dulcinea, who they are still unsure of.<br /> <br /> More later,comments and questions welcome, may be late responding as I am super busy this week. But I will get to yoiu eventually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-21T20:30:27-08:00","id":834809,"title":"","content":"Saddening, if interesting to read journals to read this time Baron. I've suffered from depression for quite a while, and am arguably still suffering it now, so the journals these days have touched on that, but it's really cool to see the players roleplaying it out and treating things with the proper gravity they'd have, and with the in-character flaws they have. I always love seeing players actually roleplaying and not just going from encounter to encounter, and something like this is going to leave waves even after the Balehound encounter is over.<br /> <br /> It's like loving to watch a tv series that leaves you in tears midway through, because it's just that damn good to see.<br /> <br /> Also, yay Beast! I've been hoping to make/play a Beast in the Geist game I've got building up, so having some precedence for that is great to see. I wonder what her horror would look like, if bee related...then again, perhaps I shouldn't ask. I wonder if Dulcinea got in on her own power, or if she came in with the other krewe - Beasts have the Skeleton Key power, but as far as I know they don't normally have the power to find gateways they can use. They need someone else to point it out. Hmmm...<br /> <br /> Also also, I need to make a social Titan Anakim at some point. Sounds like a fun juggernaut to make/play as.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-22T12:01:29-08:00","id":835248,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind words. All 4 of my games have a lot of human drama. The people inside the monsters is part of what it is all about.<br /> <br /> Dulcinea knew where a couple doors are...the cemetery ones are well known. New Haven has a couple infamous cemetery spots.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T14:43:55-08:00","id":843143,"title":"","content":"The battle with the Bale Hound ends, and does the twisting of the Krewe\u2019s Taboos. Nuff said.<br /> <i><br /> Session CLIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> When Sara heard Natalie approach, she looked at her watch and realized it had been over an hour since her wife had come by to let her know the others were back safely from the underworld. The books on the table hadn\u2019t changed since then. Neither had the one in front of her. Or the page for that matter. She looked up at Natalie. The strawberry scented woman smiled at her and nodded, letting her know it was time. Sara wrapped her arms around herself and took a deep breath, preparing to face the others, before she stood and followed.<br /> <br /> The others were already there, waiting with their drink offerings. Sara added her whiskey to Natalie\u2019s Cognac, Alexia\u2019s red wine, Alice\u2019s Corona and Doc\u2019s laudanum. She joined the circle, avoiding Alice\u2019s eyes and sitting with Natalie between her and the redhead. In the center was a glass painted with a collage of the krewe\u2019s faces, placed so the light streamed through it. Natalie picked up a chalice with the drink offerings poured into it and pricked her finger with a silver knife, letting a drop of blood fall into the chalice before passing it to Alice.<br /> <br /> \u201cEfforts have been made to drive us apart and they have failed...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s speech was impassioned and stirring as the chalice and knife made their way around the circle. When it got to Sara, she cut deep, curling the blade carefully around the ball of her thumb. She let a few drops fall into the chalice before cupping her hand and passing the chalice along so she could put pressure on her wound.<br /> <br /> Sara looked down at her hand as the chalice was passed around again, this time with each krewe member taking a sip. When it got back to her, Natalie concluded the ritual. She laid a hand on Sara\u2019s shoulder. She smiled and squeezed Natalie\u2019s hand before leaving to wait in the entrance hall while Natalie gave the blessing of the krewe to Alexia and Alice.<br /> <br /> Tatum found her there and approached cautiously, holding out a silver knife hilt first. Sara closed her hand around her cut, holding it out of sight.<br /> <br /> \u201cI got a text from Karen. She wants you to stab her - not Karen-her, but the bad guy-her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks love.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou can\u2019t die, right? You\u2019re going to come back safe?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded and stood up, moving to kiss Tatum on the forehead. Tatum smiled back and handed over the knife.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------------<br /> The ride was long. Doc and Alice drove, and Sara was in Doc\u2019s van. She tended to her wound, stopping the bleeding and irritating the edges before covering it in plastic. It took her most of the ride, since her thoughts kept wandering and her eyes kept straying towards Angelique, or Alice\u2019s jeep when it came into view.<br /> <br /> They grouped up once they got there, some ways away from the ritual site. The werewolves were peering intently in that direction. Angelique made a worried noise. When the others looked at her, it was Deirdre who explained.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s a lot of spirits over there. 17, it looks like? Passion spirits - we\u2019re going to need to do something about them or they will be messing with our heads the whole time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara glanced over at Alice, and back down. She ran a hand over her face and wrapped her arms around herself again. Deirdre continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cI can make a, well, a \u2018scary noise\u2019 and make probably about half of them run off. We\u2019ll probably have to deal with them later, but it will keep us from being swarmed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, no, that could work. But we set an ambush for the ones you scare away and end them before we circle around for the rest.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice punctuated her plan with a brandish of her claws. Sara possessed her geist, revealing 17 attractive looking spirits. The group circled around the spirits to get into position, following Alice\u2019s direction to set up for an ambush.<br /> <br /> The krewe and its werewolf allies tore through the spirits, but not before Sara felt their influence on her emotions. She was hit with a crushing wave of guilt. With the absolute knowledge that what she had done to Alice was unforgivable and had ruined everything. She knew there was no way she could make up for that breach of trust.<br /> <br /> <i>\u201cA blood sacrifice can wash away any transgression. You know what will bring forgiveness.\u201d</i><br /> <br /> The Sacrifice\u2019s words rang in her head. Anger washed over Sara and she snarled, swiping at the air. The wild blow took out Alice\u2019s target and she glared at Sara, cowing her. Alice and Eris finished off the last of the fleeing spirits and when Deirdre rejoined them, the group made short work of the remaining ones, with twenty minutes left until sunset. Sara stopped to take a breath as a flood of hope swept through her. She sat on a window ledge, pulling her knees up to her chest. Others followed suit, except Alice who paced, only stopping to check on the others.<br /> <br /> She stopped in front of Sara, her mask pushed up to her forehead, her face hard and feral.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara pulled back, looking up at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you ok?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara paused, the hope of forgiveness prompting honestly.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo. But, we will be. Right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s expression softened and she returned Sara\u2019s pleading smile before she turned away to resume pacing. Sara gripped Karen\u2019s silver knife tightly, watching Angelique prepare the ritual. Deirdre watched too, suspiciously, muttering.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo we even know what the ritual she\u2019s setting up does?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt forces open doors.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara answered first, commenting on the various aspects she saw. Deirdre didn\u2019t like it, but didn\u2019t move to stop Angelique either. Once she was done, the Bone Shadow turned to the group.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s a mystic, like me. I think sending her into Kuruth should be a priority.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want us to try and force a solo enemy werewolf into Kuruth?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not saying it won\u2019t be dangerous, but I do think it will be less dangerous. I would be.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deirdre glared at Angelique but didn\u2019t contradict her. After a moment she stopped, looking at the ritual site. Noriko looked up from getting Natalie a blanket as Deirdre and Eris both shifted.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe peeked.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique completed the ritual, tearing open a door made of bright silver light. Natalie stood up to move in and Sara felt the hope she\u2019d had fade away. Her resolve hardened and she moved quickly to the door, ignoring her geist pleasure. She met Alice there.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to enrage her. My silver will do that where you claws won\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m very hard to hit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I\u2019m very hard to hurt.\u201d<br /> <br /> While the two argued, Deirdre pushed past them. Alice took a deep breath and a step back, letting Sara go before her.<br /> <br /> Inside the pocket realm, all Sara found was a pair of spirits. Deirdre tore into one, but Sara waited for Bright Shadows to show herself. Alice got in and saw through her mystical invisibility first however, and Sara followed her lead.<br /> <br /> The silver enraged the Balehound and she shifted into Gauru form, abandoning her invisibility. While Eris and Noriko finished off the accompanying spirits, Bright Shadows lunged at Alice. Sara cried out and moved towards her, but the wound bled nothing but smoke and Alice looked unphased<br /> <br /> Looking resolute, Angelique drew a silver knife and thrust it into her own stomach. A red line flared between her and Bright Shadows, and a mirroring wound appeared on the Balehound. Alexia capitalized on her distraction by slamming a pair of fists into the side of Bright Shadow\u2019s head, her silver knuckles burning into the werewolf\u2019s skin. The Balehound went down.<br /> <br /> Noriko and Sara both converged on Angelique. The werecat wrestled the knife from her while Sara laid a hand on her shoulder. Angelique\u2019s eyes flashed with rage but she choked it down, turning to leave. Alice followed, after digging her claws into the body and tossing it out the door. Alexia encouraged them to continue, to move to the cars, eventually dragging the body there herself since Alice was ignoring her. Sara faded back as Alice approached her and Angelique. Alice ignored her too.<br /> <br /> When Angelique said the effects would end after they slept, Sara winced away and moved towards the car. She hadn\u2019t really expected the Balehound\u2019s influence to end immediately upon her death, but it seemed like one more hope dashed away. The others joined Sara and Alexia at their respective cars eventually and the krewe, victorious, drove home.<br /> ----------------------------------------------------<br /> Sara walked quietly into the house, still clutching the silver knife. She watched Natalie go upstairs, announcing that only her wives and Tatum were welcome to join her. She watched Alexia and Tavia go on at length about the people oven to a disturbed Alice before they too left, with the body. Then she followed her wife, wanting to ask her for another moment of hope, so she could believe that Alice and Angelique would forgive her, but settling for a hot shower.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> December 3rd, 2010<br /> <br /> It is over.<br /> <br /> Finally.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CLIII</i><br /> <br /> The Spirits they fought never materialized, so the Sin-Eaters had to possess their Geists to fight them. Ironically, Noriko was unable to fight anything until the final confrontation The Spirits required a \u201cone-two\u201d punch of powers to do much, and the PCs kept them too off guard to do much. Still, both Spirit battles were along, especially compared to the battle with Bright Shadow which ended with great speed.<br /> <br /> The Ritual Natalie used her Krewe Fate Merit to give Alexia and Alice 5 dice each (as determined by PC consensus) and used her Inspiring Merit to give the Krewe the Inspired Condition. The Ritual was not physically conducted (no cup passed) but it was roleplayed through.<br /> <br /> Time to recover and move on to other things.<br /> <br /> So, This game did not miss due to my trip, but as most games did, I am going ahead and putting up character stats for the Krewe as I did elsewhere. That will be in a bit less than a week. Look for Sara, Natalie and Alexia most likely. Those are the stats I currently have access to. I will see you then, Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-10T22:27:55-08:00","id":845472,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s the off week for Balance of Shadows, but as we are doing this in several games, I wanted to give you a glimpse at some of the group. What do a group of Sin-Eaters look like after almost 155 sessions? Here is a look.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> <b>Sara Rowan, Torn Advocate Sin-Eater (Bright Eyes)</b><br /> <br /> Name: Sara Rowan<br /> Archetype: Advocate<br /> Threshold: The Torn<br /> Virtue/Vice: Compassion/Hedonism<br /> <br /> Attributes:<br /> Mental:<br /> Intelligence 5<br /> Wits 4<br /> Resolve 4<br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> Strength 2<br /> Dex 5<br /> Stamina 4<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> Presence 6<br /> Manipulation 4<br /> Composure 3<br /> <br /> Skills:<br /> Mental:<br /> Academics 2<br /> Computer 0<br /> Crafts 2<br /> Investigation 2<br /> Medicine 3<br /> Occult 5 (Folklore)<br /> Politics 1<br /> Science 0<br /> <br /> Physical:<br /> Athletics 3 (Tumbling)<br /> Brawl 0<br /> Drive 1<br /> Firearms 1<br /> Larceny 2 (Sleight of Hand)<br /> Stealth 2<br /> Survival 0<br /> Weaponry 3<br /> <br /> Social:<br /> Animal Ken 1<br /> Empathy 5 (Reading Crowds)<br /> Expression 5 (Storytelling, Singing)<br /> Intimidation 0<br /> Persuasion 4<br /> Socialize 3<br /> Streetwise 1<br /> Subterfuge 3<br /> <br /> Synergy 7<br /> <br /> Psyche 6<br /> <br /> Merits:<br /> Contacts (Sideshow folks)<br /> Eidetic Memory<br /> Strong Back<br /> Striking Looks 2<br /> Fighting Finesse<br /> Profession: Sideshow 4 (Empathy, Expression, Larceny)<br /> Sympathetic<br /> Languages (English, Gaelic)<br /> <br /> Derived Stats:<br /> Willpower (Res + Comp): 7<br /> Initiative (Dex + Comp): 8<br /> Health (Stamina + Size): 9<br /> Defense (min(Dex,Wits) + Athletics): 7<br /> Speed (Str + Dex + 5): 12<br /> <br /> Keys:<br /> Passion<br /> Stigmata<br /> Pyre Flame<br /> Cold Wind<br /> <br /> Manifestations:<br /> Oracle 5<br /> 