1<br /> Larceny 3<br /> Stealth 2<br /> Survival 5 (Gardening)<br /> Weaponry 5 (Meat Clever, Knife)<br /> <br /> Animal Ken 0<br /> Empathy 4<br /> Expression 5 (Food Presentation)<br /> Intimidation 1<br /> Persuasion 5<br /> Socialize 3<br /> Streetwise 0<br /> Subterfuge 1<br /> <br /> Industrial Key<br /> Phantasmal Key<br /> Pyre-Flame Key<br /> <br /> Caul 5<br /> Marionette 5<br /> Oracle 5<br /> Shroud 5<br /> <br /> 1: Finding<br /> <br /> Psyche 6<br /> Synergy 7<br /> Willpower 7<br /> Health 10<br /> Plasm 40<br /> Size 5<br /> Defense: 5<br /> Initiative: 8<br /> Speed: 15<br /> <br /> Language: English 3<br /> Language: French 2<br /> Memento: Death Mask 4<br /> Professional: Chef 5<br /> Resources 3<br /> Taste 1<br /> <br /> Phobia: Skeletons<br /> <br /> Keystone, Deathmask, Charm: Nutcracker (Phantasmal)<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> In just over a week check in on the Krewe for another <i>Balance of Shadows session</i>. The Krewe decompresses after a long stressful time. See what Doc has been up to! Find out if Natalie\u2019s journal is more than like three words! Try and figure out who seemed to not be affected and may have gotten into trouble! See you then! Comments and Questions Welcome.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 03-21-2016, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-20T23:53:19-07:00","id":850439,"title":"","content":"First off, profiles above! Check them out!<br /> <br /> The storm has passed, but our heroes must recover. Let\u2019s see how that whole healing thing goes. Alice\u2019s player had to miss.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLIV</i><br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sara rolled over, a pleasantly drifty smile on her face. When all she found were warm blankets, she frowned a little, waking up the rest of the way. As she sat up and looked around, she found Karen and relaxed. A hopeful smile spread over her face. Karen returned it.<br /> <br /> The younger woman sat down on the bed and Sara leaned in for a kiss. As they pulled apart, Karen held her gaze, a serious look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m going to be violently purging Natalie\u2019s guilt. Am I going to need to do the same for you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI plan on doing that the old fashioned way, by apologizing.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked at Karen with concern in her eyes and laid a hand lightly on her neck. Karen raised an eyebrow and quirked her mouth wryly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019ll let me know if you need anything, after you help Natalie? Or during.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI will. I might just drink a lot when done.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tumbling off the bed and to her feet, Sara gave Karen a wink and a hand up with another kiss and a reminder to call on her if she was need. Sara nuzzled her lover\u2019s neck, eventually letting her wander off to check on Natalie while Sara herself headed to the shower.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Breakfast had already gotten started when Sara got down to the dining room. She walked in with her shoulders squared but after one glance around, they slumped slightly and she looked both relieved and concerned. Natalie looked up at her, as Karen stole the strawberry off her place, and passed Sara the note Alice had left before slipping out earlier that morning.<br /> <br /> 'Eris and I are spending some time with her pack. Let us know if you need us.'<br /> <br /> Sara thanked her wife, hiding a grin as she noticed Alexia sneaking Natalie a strawberry under the table. As she sat down, a strong smell of alcohol washed over her. She looked down the table, her eyes landing on Doc From the smell, he\u2019d tried getting past a Sin-eater\u2019s high stamina by drinking a few bottle of whiskey in the last few hours. He was eating mechanically, staring dead eyed straight ahead.<br /> <br /> Her brow furrowed with worry, but she didn\u2019t want to push him in front of everyone. Instead, she turned to Angelique, surprisingly dressed for a New England winter day, and asked about her research into the Balehound\u2019s ritual. She seemed almost guilty when she admitted she hadn\u2019t been able to concentrate much, and had gone straight to bed last night. Sara nodded understandingly and offered to help.<br /> <br /> Doc looked up at the mention of the ritual, the first movement not involving a fork going from plate to mouth. He offered to help with a rough voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt would be good to have someone who knows the library. But... only if you would like. If you need to get some sleep...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI slept. I\u2019m g...\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc trailed off.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Angelique knew right where to start back up, moving directly there. Doc set up his bottle of whiskey, along with a tumbler on the table nearby. Sara pointedly put a water bottle near the tumbler as well. In between drinks and attempts to discourage the same, Doc and Sara helped Angelique figure out where in the restricted section she needed next.<br /> <br /> Angelique came back from a run on the stacks with a heavy book in her hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoc, you shouldn\u2019t drink so much.\u201d<br /> <br /> He blinked a few times.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat are we looking at?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNames Between Worlds. Do either of you know what kind of blood we need in the receptacle to make it open? In this house, I hope not virgin.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned at Angelique as Doc looked it over and identified it as needing Fishbourne blood. When he went to go get Tavia, Sara seized her change, setting her book down and taking a deep breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need to apologize Angelique.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique looked up from her reading, raising an eyebrow as Sara continued.<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t resist the Balehound\u2019s influence like I should have. I... I\u2019m afraid I may have pushed you too hard into something... well, something you don\u2019t want.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou didn\u2019t push me into anything. We had a good time together - let\u2019s not make it into an unpleasant memory.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave her a wide smile and looked back down at her book, waiting for Doc.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Doc and Tavia were back quickly and Tavia was happy to help. She warned Angelique not to listen to anything the book said, and to avoid the chapter on Abyssal subjects, but otherwise merely observed.<br /> <br /> It was almost dinnertime when Doc\u2019s bottle ran empty. Sara moved to intercept him as he left to get a new one, taking his hand. He paled, and she stepped back, apology on her face. She didn\u2019t move out of the way though and after a short debate, convinced him to go with her looking for food instead.<br /> <br /> They found Karen fist, staring at her own bottle of scotch. She gave Sara a weak smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI have my limits on what I like doing to people.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou and me both.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc sat down heavily as he spoke and resumed the blank stare he had on at breakfast. Sara took a seat next to her wife, laying a hand on hers and offering to trade charges, if Natalie still needed more looking after the next day. When not even Karen\u2019s joking rejoinder about babysitting got a rise out of Doc, Sara raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, what\u2019s up Doc?\u201d<br /> <br /> He made a face.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo really, what\u2019s going on? This isn\u2019t like you.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a long pause. Doc looked a little green. Sara let it stretch, waiting until he broke, at least a little. He did, with a deep shuddering breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cI... I did some bad things. I think I was affected by Bright Shadows.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe all were.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEven me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara squeezed Karen\u2019s hand as she waited for Doc to continue. He looked like he was fighting being sick, but managed to choke it back.<br /> <br /> \u201cI slept with two women I had no intention of being with. It would have been more but... I know I wouldn\u2019t get anywhere with you, Karen, and, well, I never made it back to the house.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smirked at him as he glanced up at her, then away.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat might have gone somewhere. Yesterday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBehind Noriko\u2019s back.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. Yeah. Not so much that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc stared at the table, his face blank. The two women eventually got through to him the extent of Bright Shadow\u2019s effect. Largely by confessing what they had done - Sara raised a mock-envious eyebrow at Karen\u2019s confession that she\u2019d slept with Natalie\u2019s \u2018rival\u2019, Moir\u00e9 - and the fact that they\u2019d been forgiven, at least by those around to do so. Sara suggested he apologize and get it off his chest before it festered any more than it already had.<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess this serves as an apology, to you two.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course you\u2019re forgiven. I am ridiculously attractive after all.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen\u2019s casual shrug to go along with her claim got an actual smile from Doc. Their conversation was interrupted by Tatum and Noriko wandering in, Tatum gloating over her win on Rainbow Road. Sara eyed her, considering that Tatum had never informed the rest of them that Karen hadn\u2019t been in the townhouse like Karen had just confessed. Doc paled at the sight of Noriko, and shrank down into his seat.<br /> <br /> Sara was not about to let that stand and tapped his elbow until he looked at her, at which point she looked at Noriko significantly. After an awkward exchange of hellos, Doc did ask her to talk and they left the room for privacy.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------<br /> <br /> Tatum had returned from checking on Natalie, and Sara had almost finished giving Karen a neck rub when Doc and Noriko returned, hand in hand. Sara beamed at the pair of them. Chandra, Alexia and Catherine were close behind, with Catherine in Chandra\u2019s clothes. Seeing all of us there, Alexia looked pleadingly at Tatum then dived into the kitchen, Tatum following behind. Karen watched them go, a dubious look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhen did she learn to cook?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara stopped when Doc shushed her, keeping Tatum\u2019s mid morning Youtube tutorials secret, for now. She kissed Karen on the top of her head and sat down, smiling mysteriously. Conversation stayed light until Alexia and Tatum came back from the kitchen with burgers.<br /> <br /> Over dinner, Noriko asked Angelique about her research. What she and Tavia had found didn\u2019t give the Bone Shadow much hope for reverse-engineering anything, so they discussed brute forcing their way through it. After some cajoling from Sara, she admitted she was from a suburb of Cincinnati, Ohio. She also agreed to let Catherine sift through her mind, the next time the krewe visited the Underworld, to maximize the peacefulness of the environment.<br /> <br /> Natalie came down eventually, a touch paler than usual and without her makeup. She agreed to let the other krewe know we were no longer infected, at Alexia\u2019s urging, since she and Alice had run across them in the Underworld. Sara kept a worried eye on her strawberry smelling wife over dinner, but she perked up as the evening went on and by the time dinner was over, everyone was happy with Tavia\u2019s suggestion of a game night.<br /> <br /> Everyone except for Angelique, that is, but she agreed to bring the book she was studying to the game room. There were competing suggestions of Candy-land, from Alexia, and cutthroat pool, from Doc, so they split into two groups, Natalie, Sara, Doc, and Noriko with her Hello Kitty pool cue at the pool table, with everyone else at the Candy-land board.<br /> <br /> The mostly unpleasant memories of her last pool game pushed Sara to keep things light, so she played casually and wound up dropping out first. Natalie fell next, as Noriko arranged things to keep Doc in the running. The werecat was strutting around the table by then, and schooled him handily once it was just the two of them.<br /> <br /> The Candy-land game was hardly half done after that first game, so Sara tagged out with Karen and let her get a turn behind a cue. She managed to maintain Karen\u2019s lead and tied with Tavia to become co-rulers of Candy Castle.<br /> <br /> The strutting was in from the start of game 2, with Noriko beginning the game by blowing on Doc\u2019s cue for luck. Natalie managed to distract both Noriko and Sara with a few well timed stretches, and she and Karen managed to collude to knock Doc out of the game first, but Noriko still came out ahead.<br /> <br /> The pool players watched the end of the Candy-land game, with Noriko sitting on the pool table, swinging her legs. Natalie grabbed three of the pool balls and moved to stand behind Karen, reaching under her arms and spinning the balls a la Jareth. Karen posed after a moment of surprise, prompting a giggle and a grin from Sara. During a pause, Sara winked at Natalie and waggled her fingers. She tossed a few balls to the younger woman, one at a time, setting her up to juggle them for a couple of minutes before trying the Goblin King maneuver herself, not quite as deftly as Natalie had.<br /> <br /> Once the board game wrapped up, Noriko hopped off the table, her cue on her shoulders, arms resting on it.<br /> <br /> \u201cSchool can be back in session, if someone would like a lesson?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not really a challenge against us, is it Noriko?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not about the challenge...\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen raised an eyebrow at the smug rejoinder and grabbed her own pool cue. Natalie and Doc joined in as well, though Natalie ducked out quickly before they started. Tavia, Alexia and her girlfriends took that opportunity to get a game of Hungry Hungry Hippos going.<br /> <br /> The reason for Natalie\u2019s errand became fairly clear shortly into the game. Standing behind Doc, Natalie took a few opportunities to flash Noriko at key moments of concentration. Or what should have been key moments of concentration. It wound up being a close game between Karen and Noriko, with Karen eking out the win. Noriko glared playfully at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou cheated!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe cheated. I didn\u2019t cheat.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen smirked, leaning over onto Natalie\u2019s shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnother round? Just you and me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen raised her hands and shook her head. Not even Noriko\u2019s second best pout changed her mind. It was Catherine though, that started the pilgrimage upstairs, asking her two girls to follow only after a few minutes.<br /> <br /> Once they were gone, Sara smirked up at her own three girls, keeping four of the pool balls up in the air.<br /> <br /> \u201cBed?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatum\u2019s eyes went wide as Karen and Natalie looked at each other and grinned, moving together to tickle their wife\u2019s sides as she caught the balls. Sara ran out of the room with all three of them in pursuit, laughter filling the house.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> December 4th, 2010<br /> <br /> Today has been painful and difficult, but good. I attended the late breakfast, and spent the remainder of the afternoon in constant pain. But it was cleansing, purifying pain.<br /> <br /> Of course it began when Karen returned, and admitted she slept with Moir\u00e9. I didn\u2019t even know Moir\u00e9 liked girls, but there you go. On the other hand, that bitch probably did it just to get at me. Regardless, Karen is forgiven, because when I say we need to move past this I mean it. Still a bitter pill to swallow, Moir\u00e9 and I do not get along. At all.<br /> <br /> Doc looked like shit at breakfast, but Sara promised to take care of him, so I turned myself over to Karen. If I regret anything, it is what the pain did to her, not me. The look of distress in her eyes a few times bothers me, and we need to talk about it sometime. Not right now, though we both need to decompress. Once I had healed with the benefit of the Cold Wind Oracle, I rested a bit.<br /> <br /> Dinner was lively. Catherine had arrived, had not seen her in weeks. She was positively glowing, and seemed so happy. Tatum helped out with the cooking, which is interesting. I did not know she could cook. She had never spoken of it, anyway. Conversation was lighter, and Doc and Noriko finally had a talk. I suspect my name was left out given the lack of any sort of look I got from him after. Alice, I suspect, has less a poker face than I, so we will see how that goes.<br /> <br /> Oh Goddess Alice don\u2019t screw this up for me.<br /> <br /> I am elated people seem to be getting along with Tatum. Noriko played videos games with her today and Alexia seemed to appreciate her help in the kitchen. I am glad they get along. Tatum is not hard to deal with but it quiet sometimes, especially with me and all my yammering on around.<br /> <br /> I was going to do a Vlog but it was just not in me today. I have not done one in over a week so I really need to do it tomorrow. Goddess Natalie was here last time I did one. And I know, she texted and reminded me I had not done one this week yet. But such was not to be tonight.<br /> <br /> I need to do more Vlogging. It makes me feel good, and I get a lot of praise and flirting. I hear from people who I have inspired or who really enjoy my videos. I also get called a Homemo, whatever the fuck that is. An emo at home maybe? I am not honestly sure.<br /> <br /> We wound up going to the game room to try to strengthen our bonds. This was a good idea and it went well. Alexia and Tavia were of course all about board games, while Noriko was all about pool, because she likes living dangerously. I leapt for pool, as I just do not tend to care as much for board games. Doc, Sara, and Noriko squared off with me, and Noriko spanked us. Not literally. Ahem.<br /> <br /> She won the second time less heartily, with Karen having swapped in for Sara. I tried a bit to distract her but failed. Once Candyland was ended, Noriko challenged us again while the others switched to Hungry Hungry Hippoes. Noriko was so cocky, so I moved behind Doc when she was shooting and flashed my bare chest at her. That helped. I mean, I still did not win but Karen snuck a win in at that point.<br /> <br /> Catherine seductively went upstairs and her girlfriends were close behind. The time soon came for Tatum, Karen, Sara and I retired to my room. It was a good night. My time being punished drained me somewhat, but there was a lot of real love and affection with the sex. I was quite happy about it. It was a very blissful night as four souls, six really, melted into one. There is nothing more beautiful on earth.<br /> <br /> Rough start. Good end.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLIV</i><br /> <br /> I would be remiss in saying being pushed through with lethal damage is not good, safe S&amp;M. Natalie has come back from the dead and is not of the healthiest mind. Don\u2019t try this at home, and don\u2019t assume extremes are what actual practitioners do. Cool? Cool.<br /> <br /> Okay, two things missed by the journals. One was Catherine\u2019s story that she came out to her family over thanksgiving\u2026by yelling that she was gay over a fierce unrelated argument two family members were having. Also, high fives from her cousin.<br /> <br /> Also, Doc admitted fooling around himself and naming names, while Noriko aggressively had to convince him everyone did stuff. She alluded to such herself but carefully avoided naming names.<br /> <br /> Next time is back to work. Alice\u2019s player still has to miss due to personal issues but will return, and the group sets about to busying themselves again. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-04T00:17:29-07:00","id":858805,"title":"","content":"Me: \u201cYou figure today might be a good day to go to the Underworld, or perhaps just relax while Alice is hanging around with Eris\u2019s pack. What do you want to do?\u201d<br /> <br /> Players: \u201cHey, lets use that list of places we got back in \u201910 and go poking for Avernian Gates.<br /> <br /> Me: \u201c\u2026\u201d<br /> <i><br /> Session CLV</i><br /> <b><br /> Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0200 Hours, Monday, December 6, 2010<br /> <br /> It has been a long day but one that we all needed. I have done things in the past week that I would have never believed. I hate Balehounds, I hate Demons from Inferno, and I hate anything else that decides my emotions, taboos, or desires are to be used for weapons. I\u2019m seriously thinking about learning the Passion Key just to make sure that shit never happens again.<br /> <br /> Wow, I just realized I haven\u2019t updated this journal since Mom left. For the sake of memory loss, here is a VERY brief review:<br /> <br /> <br /> Sunday, Nov. 28<br /> Zed calls, Erin and Austin go missing while guarding Angelique<br /> Eris and I are briefly suspects<br /> We\u2019re cleared, something happens to Dierdre<br /> ALL HELL BREAKS LOOSE<br /> Balehound has done something to werewolves, causing them to act on their taboos<br /> Erin is pregnant by Austin<br /> Everyone hates Angelique<br /> Lead for Callahans points to Glenwood<br /> Pure and Uratha work together through me and Rawl<br /> Bright Shadow \u201cescapes\u201d into a spirit prison<br /> <br /> I spend \u201cmost\u201d of the rest of the week caring for Erin, who has a child with a hyperadvanced growth rate. Only Erin\u2019s regenerative powers and purity of stubbornness are keeping her Storm Lord ass alive until we get the baby shifted and safe.<br /> <br /> I say most of the time because there were a few moments where I was out with Lucille and Rhiannan. That was when the Balehound affliction took over.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not proud of what I did, but I don\u2019t regret my actions...only my intentions.<br /> <br /> Also I\u2019m not sure how I\u2019m going keep the trust I have with those two for infecting them with the supernatural equivalent of a party disease.<br /> <br /> The days are running together now, but when the moon was in the right auspice, Angelique opened the prison and Bright Shadow was destroyed. It was the morning after when I actually realized everything I had done. I started drinking early to fight off the panic, and forgot to stop. I was three bottles into a whiskey bender when Angelique asked for help trying to undo the imprinting Bright Shadow did to her during her First Change. I didn\u2019t mention it, feeling like I had already cause enough problems, but I knew that the changing of her true name I did would complicate that. Bright Eyes came along as well. When my bottle ran dry, Bright Eyes stopped me from getting another. Instead I went to get Tavia so we could open a book that required Fishborn blood. The Names between Worlds was not something to be played with, but it did have a section on a portion of the Lower Depths called the Inferno. That is how I figure out where my hunting grounds are going to be when I need to destroy something in the Underworld.<br /> <br /> I talked with all the people I could have hurt in the Krewe and in the House. Everyone assured me that I was forgiven and that they all did things too.<br /> <br /> This morning I was actually able to find my center meditation and not feel like I\u2019d vomit. It was refreshing to not feel that level of self-loathing and disgust. Over breakfast, we decided to go Avernian Gate tracking since Alice was still away with Eris. Noriko, Chandra, and Mouse came along as well.<br /> <br /> Our first stop was New Haven Green. Trinity Episcopal and Central Church on the Green made up the area. All our phones and radios scrambled when we got to the Green. There was a single Gate in an indention in the grass on the Green proper. Two other Gates were three floors down under the Central Church. But that one has a ton of angry ghosts as well so we decided we didn\u2019t need to deal with that just yet. The whole area was a Haunt, but the Plasm was somewhere under Central Church. I jumped into the Gate on the Green just so I could use it later if necessary and we moved on.<br /> <br /> Our next stop was the Evergreen Church and Midnight Mary\u2019s tomb. The tombstone itself was a Graveyard Gate and the Haunt was inside the tomb. Bright Eyes learned that a black void sucks people into the Underworld at random. She also saw red lights as if coming from windows uphill in the distance. Mouse checked it next, but she screamed as her hand was pulled into the tombstone. Cupcake and I formed a firelight and pulled her back out. Her hand was ice cold and she was terrified. But she confirmed that there was a house on the hill in the Underworld. We\u2019d heard rumors about such a place but we\u2019d never encountered it. Now I know it exists and we need to stop it. I suggested we use dynamite but Nightshade mumbled something about how great an idea that would be. I realized that the consequences in the living world would be felt and I\u2019d have to find a better way. But high yield explosives will remain a possible plan B.<br /> <br /> Grove Street was next and was special. The Gate was in the arch as was the Haunt. The Plasm collected on top of the arch however. I left that for Cupcake while I went into the Underworld. This Gate led deep into the Library. All the books were historical around the entrance. A woman with a large mouth for a face looked at me when I approached, but said nothing. I didn\u2019t feel the need to find out how strict of a librarian she was, so I headed back.<br /> <br /> We took a break while Bright Eyes and Nightshade \u201crested\u201d in the townhouse. Then after dusk, I called Truman to ask about a visit. The Crypt Ticks hold territory around the East Lawn Cemetery so I figured we could have a meet and greet as well as look around. It seems Rebecca and Chandra had business while Nightshade and Bright Eyes made business with Neon, directly against my strict warnings. We met the \u201ccreepy red-head\u201d Cupcake mentioned in the Mausoleum. Truman introduced us to Dulcinia, a \u201ccousin\u201d to Truman with power over bees. I took Truman through the Graveyard Gate and we entered a side room off the main Library halls. This looked to be an old style reading room. The corridor opened into the main hall and was not monitored. Truman was a little uneasy when I mentioned the last Librarian I ran into. We came back out without any issues and found Rebecca and Chandra had returned as well.<br /> <br /> After that, we headed over to the 27 Club after Nightshade had all but waved a blood-scented VIP pass to the Champagne Room in front of Neon. I\u2019m certain nothing chaotic or dramatic will come from that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Breakfast was an informal affair, with Alexia whipping up made-to-order smoothies for everyone. Sara was pleased to see Doc come down more calm and collected than the previous morning. She was even more pleased that his usual clean, masculine scent had returned with him. He returned her smile, settling down next to Noriko.<br /> <br /> The mood at the table was all around improved. Karen sat close to Tatum, brushing against her whenever possible. Catherine was absolutely twitterpated, smiling giddily at her girlfriends. Smiles and laughter were shared between everyone. Sara hoped that Alice had recovered similarly, up there with her mate and her pack.<br /> <br /> She was a little reluctant to break the mood, but they'd been awfully focused for the past few days. So she asked what they had on their plates for the day, suggesting a few loose ends that she knew of. Tatum shrugged, pointing out she had to work at the club tonight. Karen smirked suggestively at her, claiming that meant she had to be there to see Tatum in her suit. Raising an eyebrow at the comment that Tatum's mom thought she looked dykey in the suit Karen had gotten her, Natalie turned to the others in the krewe, laying a hand on Sara's shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe need to blow off some steam, I think, to re-bond.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI have absolutely no problem with that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara leaned into her, smiling up at her. Doc shook his head at the groups of flirting women, and suggested they go looking for Averian Gates. Sara seized on the idea, declaring a road trip was just the thing they needed. They settled on the krewe present, plus Noriko, Catherine and Chandra, just enough to fill the van. Tatum bowed out, at least a little regret showing on her face, to make sure she didn't miss work. Karen eyed her mischievously.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou guys have fun on your scenic tour of the local cemeteries. I might manage to get some homework done.\u201d<br /> ----------------------------------------------<br /> The New Haven Green was a city park set upon a graveyard. The headstones had been removed and there had been an effort to move most of the bodies to a large underground crypt beneath the Central Church on the Green, but it was still a place of death. Even the Christmas lights that festooned the place didn't dispel the feeling of it. The wind blew with the bitter cold of a Connecticut December as the group walked onto the Green.<br /> <br /> Natalie offered her services as a guide for the Episcopal cathedral, since she had visited it often with Sonia. She lit a clove cigarette as she reminisced. Doc gave her a stony look when she suggested asking for Sonia's assistance with the Central Church on the Green, considering its dangers.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd what will she want from you in exchange?\u201d<br /> <br /> A pause for a long drag.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnswers as to why my wife fucked her leader, probably.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc looked dubious, but didn't pursue the matter as Natalie sank onto a bench and dropped into her Boneyard trance. She looked over the churches, first. The Episcopal was, for the most part, supernaturally inert, in direct contrast to the Central Church on the Green, which boasted two Gates and a sizable population of restless ghosts in the lower levels. Without Sonia, or Alice, and given the size of the crowd on those lower levels, the group agreed to leave that for another day, by silent consensus. Instead, they moved to the small indention in the green lawn that Natalie indicated was a third Gate.<br /> <br /> Sara winked at Natalie as the rest of the group made their way to the indention and dashed off towards the side of the Green where a few enterprising folks had set up booths selling hot cider and roasted candied nuts. Sara returned at a much more sedate pace, grinning broadly and balancing a pair of 4-cup trays of cider and a paper cone of nuts. She joined the circle surrounding Doc in the indention, handing out cups of cider as she did, passing off the cone so she could hold Doc's for him.<br /> <br /> They stood around somewhat awkwardly for a moment before Doc stepped through the gate. Catherine looked around tentatively, and quietly broke the silence.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo... I went home for Thanksgiving right?\u201d<br /> <br /> She told a story about how she'd interrupted a fierce argument by announcing she was gay at the top of her lungs.<br /> <br /> \u201c... and then I said I had two girlfriends and showed them pictures. I got a lot of high fives.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc came back through the gate to a bunch of giggling.<br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> Next on the tour was Evergreen Cemetery, home of Midnight Mary's headstone. Natalie sighed fondly as they walked through the gates, pointing at Doc and Sara.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know you've seen the pictures from my photo shoot here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Catherine missed the pointing and shook her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don't really go looking for pictures of you on the Internet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled teasingly at her. Catherine tried stammering out an explanation, until her eyes widened at Natalie and she turned away, blushing, almost stumbling into one of the shade trees on the path. Her explanation that Natalie was thinking dirty things led to a hurried clarification that she was just reading surface thoughts, not digging around anyone's brain. Sara winked, leaning on Natalie's arm and nibbling on her ear as they approached Mary's grave.<br /> <br /> \u201cStop teasing her love.\u201d<br /> <br /> Catherine turned bright red.<br /> <br /> \u201cI'm shutting you all out until Natalie behaves.\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned to Chandra.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo these pants really show off my back side?\u201d<br /> <br /> Chandra smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy didn't you tell me?\u201d<br /> <br /> She smirked at the psychic's plaintive question.<br /> <br /> Conversation died as they got close to Mary's stone. The upper inscription 'The people shall be troubled at midnight and pass away' was visible from a good ways away and contributed to the air of heaviness around the grave. Natalie read the lower inscription and told the out of towners the local legends about her, including the fact that no record of Mary E Hart, or even the purchase of the tombstone itself, had ever been found.<br /> <br /> After she took a seat on a nearby bench and fell into her Boneyard trance. She confirmed the group's suspicion that Mary's tombstone was a Gate and that there was a Haunt here. A few minutes of searching let Alexia find the mausoleum the plasm was collecting in, and she and Sara worked to carefully break its seal. Meanwhile, Natalie put the krewe's mark on the area. She stopped Doc before he went in the Gate, since the old krewe had marked it as dangerous. Catherine offered to try and get a psychic reading of the tombstone, in case that helped, but they decided to wait until Alexia and Sara had finished, shivering in the cold air.<br /> <br /> Those two walked back over once they'd gotten it open. They let Doc get the plasm, since he was the one actually opening Gates. Sara moved behind Natalie and wrapped her arms around the shivering strawberry scented woman as they explained the plan.<br /> <br /> \u201cReading the Echoes first? And then maybe you can clarify my vision? That is, if your powers work anything like Alexia's...\u201d<br /> <br /> Catherine nodded, so Sara got to work. A couple of minutes of circling the stone and she paused, blinking as she got multiple flickers of visions. Most of them were goth-looking couples having sex at the tombstone. Four of them were different, giving Sara the impression of a black void that drew people into it.<br /> <br /> She focused on the most recent one of those, from the fifties to judge by the details of the scene. A greaser playfully chased a pink haired girl in a poodle skirt towards the grave, moving carefully in the dark of the cloudy night. He caught her gently and leaned in for a kiss against the tombstone. All of a sudden the void opened up, and they were pulled into what was now more clearly the Underworld as if by a strong gravitational force. On the other side, in the distance and elevated, Sara could see windows lit up with a red light.<br /> <br /> Sara huddled next to Natalie and described this to the rest of the group. Catherine nodded and laid a hand on the tombstone. After a moment her eyes went wide and she grabbed for Alexia, screaming, as her other arm sank into the tombstone. Doc jumped forward and lent his weight to the tug of war, using the psychic girl as a rope. Her arm pulled away from the tombstone slowly at first, the force on the other side almost matching theirs, but then it went slack, sending them all stumbling back, Catherine freed.<br /> <br /> Alexia took the hand that had sunk into the stone. It was cold and Catherine shivered, so Alexia chafed them gently to warm them while Doc muttered imprecations against whatever it was pulling people across the boundary. Sara laid a hand on his arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt certainly looked like the house on the hill. You know, the one in the Underworld that people don't come back from? Perhaps we could deal with it from that side?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYes. With dynamite.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201c...sure Doc.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie winced slightly, pointing out the damage that could do to the local Underworld. Doc just glared.<br /> --------------------------------------------<br /> Last on the list before nightfall was the Grove Street Cemetery. There was one other notable one in town \u2013 the East Lawn Cemetery \u2013 but it was the domain of the Crypt Ticks, Truman's coterie of vampires. Doc agreed to set up a meeting with them once night fell, but turned to Natalie, a serious look on his face.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should avoid Neon, Natalie. Interacting with her is opening a can of Drama Pringles.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cReally? That's also what I call opening my bra.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smirked at him and he rolled his eyes. They kept playfully bickering as the group walked through the large Egyptian Revival style archway of the Grove Street Cemetery. Sara raised an eyebrow at the inscription, which read 'The Dead Shall Be Raised'. According to the Skull and Bones Society, it was The Green that had signs of a necromancer.<br /> <br /> The group avoided the official tour of the historical grave sites that was making its rounds so that they could find a good spot for Natalie to Boneyard. Once they did, Natalie chuckled, informing them that it was the archway itself that was the Gate and Alexia then identified it as the repository of the plasm as well. They joined the other folks gawking at the impressive archway, pausing for thought.<br /> <br /> Natalie leaned against the inner wall of the arch, stretching and smirking at Catherine as the psychic blushed, again. Sara took the opportunity to pounce on her, tickling her sides underneath her outstretched arms, only to find herself pulled close as Natalie dropped her hands to the small of Sara's back. The tattooed woman braced herself against the wall, hands on either side of Natalie, her wrists brushing Natalie's hips. She closed her blue eyes and leaned further into the strawberry scented woman, as Natalie ran one hand up her back to cup Sara's cheek. Their lips met and Sara forgot about anything but the taste of her. Natalie shivered as Sara's relatively cool hands slipped under her jacket, then under her sweatshirt and undershirt, slipping around behind her back. She nipped at Sara's lip in response, eliciting a soft moan and a shiver of an entirely different kind.<br /> <br /> Doc cleared his throat. Then again. At the third fake cough, Sara and Natalie pulled apart slightly.<br /> <br /> \u201cEither it's time to go, or someone is going to call the cops.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled distractedly at him and the crowd of people no longer gawking at the arch. Doc marched off with Noriko, Alexia, Chandra and a blushing Catherine following behind. Sara gave Natalie a quick kiss on the forehead before moving to follow, not taking her hand from around Natalie's waist.<br /> <br /> As they got in the van, Sara hopped in first, leaning into Natalie after she followed suit.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, what's next?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie ran a hand down Sara's side.<br /> <br /> \u201cI, uh... how about a break? You know, until... until nightfall.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie licked the side of her neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cDefinitely time for a break.\u201d<br /> <br /> Noriko eyed them amusedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo you two need some cold water thrown at you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI'll try anything once.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave the werecat a heavy lidded smile, biting her lip as Natalie's clever fingers found another sensitive spot. Doc rolled his eyes and took a shortcut to Natalie's townhouse.<br /> -----------------------------------------------<br /> After nightfall, the group made their way to the East Lawn Cemetery. Natalie prowled in, only having eyes for Neon. Truman noticed that, and looked somewhat relieved when Rebecca looked to Chandra right off, asking to speak with her alone.<br /> <br /> At a nudge from Doc, Natalie used Boneyard to identify the gate as being in amongst the mausoleums. She also described a creepy redhead stalking around there. Truman perked up at that.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat's probably Dulcinea. She's... related to kindred? I'm not certain how it works, but she can make our powers stronger.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think that's the girl who came on pretty strong to Alice in the Underworld. She has bee powers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYup, that's her. Definitely not super creepy, those bees.\u201d<br /> <br /> Truman nodded matter of factly to Alexia as the group moved towards the mausoleums. Sara and Natalie flanked Neon as they walked, flirting with her mercilessly and talking up The 27 Club. Doc muttered to Truman, eyes shooting the occasional dagger at the trio. Catherine just watched, a bemused look on her face.<br /> <br /> Dulcinea smiled at the approaching group, smiling with recognition at Alexia.<br /> <br /> \u201cFriends of yours, Truman? Where's Rebecca?\u201d<br /> <br /> Truman introduced them all, explaining why they were there, and glanced back at where Rebecca and Chandra were talking.<br /> <br /> \u201cRebecca has ideas.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wish you'd be careful how you encourage her ideas.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI wouldn't dare upset my host.\u201d<br /> <br /> Dulcinea smiled broadly at a displeased looking Truman.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know the other meaning of 'host' and you have bees...\u201d<br /> <br /> She shrugged and smiled at the krewe, putting a hand to her heart, then gesturing at the mausoleum.<br /> <br /> \u201cI promise I have not disturbed those within, but that is where the Gate is. If you are looking for others, the Gate in the Grove Street Cemetery is easy to access.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt does lead to an interesting selection of historical books. At least at the moment.\u201d<br /> <br /> The mysterious redhead smiled at Doc, and took her leave. Once she was gone, Natalie and Sara lost no time getting back to flirting. Neon smiled at the promise of VIP treatment.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo how fascist are they with IDs, at this club of yours?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTerribly, terribly nearsighted.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc growled as Natalie touched Neon's shoulder. The vampire glanced at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cYour friend is cheerful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cOh Doc is a teddy bear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf he had nothing to be angry about, he'd be angry about that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara and Natalie shared a warm glance and Sara shrugged cheerfully.<br /> <br /> \u201cOK, so Doc is an angry teddy bear.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can hear you!\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned wider, ignoring him and laying a hand on Neon's other shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cAn adorable, angry teddy bear who loves us very much.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie looked thoughtfully at her across Neon.<br /> <br /> \u201cSometimes he's more a big slobbering dog though.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc glared at them for a moment, then Doc asked Truman if he wanted to see the other side here, and when he nodded, the Gatekeeper opened the Gate. Rebecca and Chandra rejoined the rest of the group and Natalie turned her smile on them, offering Rebecca a flier for The 27 Club. They chatted for awhile, waiting for the two men to return. When they did, Sara linked arms with Doc and winked at Neon.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy don't we get out of this cold, and go somewhere with live music, good drinks, and nearsighted ID checkers?\u201d<br /> <br /> The vampires smiled, promising to come by sometime. As the krewe piled into the van, Natalie turned to Doc.<br /> <br /> \u201cSee? I'm drumming up business. Business is business and business must grow.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat's from the Lorax, and it's about how businesses are bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie grinned wickedly at Catherine, who blushed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do love a girl who knows her Lorax references.\u201d<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> Hey Karen. Yea we are headed to the 27 Club. Our investigation of the local Avernian Gates is done.<br /> <br /> Nah it\u2019s cool. We did not fight anything. Went to the Green, and both churches there. Did not wind up going in either, though, found a cenote there in the green in a big dip. Shouldn\u2019t be surprising really. I don\u2019t think anyone wanted to go to the church with the big underground as the smart thing to do would be to get Sonia, and given the choice between the smart thing, the dumb thing or nothing they picked nothing.<br /> <br /> Yea.<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s see\u2026Evergreen Cemetery, okay, we need to be careful, The grave there connected to Midnight Mary? It can pull people into the Underworld. We don\u2019t know what triggers it, for sure, but Catherine focusing her power on it did the trick writ small.<br /> <br /> Don\u2019t worry, Alexia kept her out. She is fine. Oh, speaking of Catherine, she came out to her family on Thanksgiving. A fight\u2026<br /> <br /> Yea.<br /> <br /> A fight was going on, and one relative hit another with the Christmas tree they were to put up, so she overloaded and yelled she was gay. It\u2019s kind of a hilarious image, really. Her family, at least the younger members, were supportive though. She said she got high fives.<br /> <br /> I know honey, I am really sorry. Maybe they will change someday. I know I\u2026yea.<br /> <br /> Anyway, next place on the list was Grove Street Cemetery. It\u2019s one of my favorites. We found the gate at the big arch. Plasm is a bit harder to reach. It is usually low not high, and there is an underground room there. Wonder what the deal was? Anyway, Sara and I got a bit frisky, which proved a good distraction while others worked.<br /> <br /> Oh hush.<br /> <br /> So we took some time off (ahem) while I saw to some stuff Sara needed, then we got back together to meet up with Truman\u2019s crew. I got to see Neon again! She is still adorable. Rebecca was not too crazy, though she had a long talk with Chandra about what I don\u2019t know.<br /> <br /> We also met Dulcinea, one of the self-described Begotten. She was not as randy as originally reported\u2026but then Alice was not there. She did not hang around long, just long enough to make introductions. Honestly, she seemed kinda eager to be elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Dunno.<br /> <br /> Regardless, we got away in one piece, and I think Truman\u2019s crew are coming to the 27 Club. Have you been a good girl and done your homework?<br /> <br /> Okay, well you can head on over and meet us, how is that?<br /> <br /> See you soon, love you!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLV</i><br /> <br /> Natalie was spotting Avernian Gates with Stigmata Boneyard.<br /> <br /> So what was up with that tombstone that could have killed Catherine? What indeed. A lot of these plots I had come up with about 6 years ago and had not considered or touched since. Ah well, players always keep me on my toes I guess.<br /> <br /> This session was a long, relaxed IC time at the 27 Club. Join us in 2 weeks. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:08:38-07:00","id":859911,"title":"","content":"I probably missed it, flitting from journal to journal as I do, but when was Dulcinea introduced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:30:35-07:00","id":859929,"title":"","content":"She showed up when Alice and Alexia were in the Underworld under the Bale Hound's influence a few sessions ago...maybe 3 or 4?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-05T15:43:28-07:00","id":859935,"title":"","content":"Okie Dokie. Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-17T23:13:32-07:00","id":867387,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time for the PCs to retire to the 27 Club for a party before the trip to the Underworld. Let\u2019s peek in and see what happened.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Doc\u2019s Log</b><br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s Log: 0400 Hours, Monday, December 6, 2010<br /> <br /> Tonight was different. We got to the 27 Club around 2200 Hours to see a band called the Octagonal Lozenges on stage. We were all moving around when I noticed some kind of weird tension between Noriko and Axe. I didn\u2019t really understand it so I send drinks to the table, intentionally reversed so it would distract them. It didn\u2019t really seem to help. So I decided to go over and talk.<br /> <br /> Axe was still weird, like she was a kid that\u2019d been caught doing something. Talk turned to Malard as that was on Axe\u2019s mind. She believes that Angelique will join the Sleeping Giant pack because, and I don\u2019t know where she gets this, it\u2019s obvious that Malard\u2019s pack won\u2019t make it through this. I don\u2019t know if that was what had Alice all weird with Noriko or not, but I knew the werecat didn\u2019t like it. Before we got through Axe\u2019s explanation, which I tried to interrupt, Noriko stormed off to the bathroom. I couldn\u2019t be upset with Axe really, but this didn\u2019t help her any.<br /> <br /> Before Noriko came back, The Hair and Jaggling came in. I have no idea why they decided now was a great time to come to the 27 Club. I had to explain to Axe why this was awkward, having recently slept with The Hair\u2019s grandmother. After that Axe decided she needed to check on Noriko. Bright Eyes brought The Hair over to sit at our table. If she knew anything, The Hair kept things close to her chest. Which was at least a little less uncomfortable for me.<br /> <br /> Chandra and Rebecca left after talking to Truman, which threw all kinds of red flags for me. I went to find out if I should be worried. He was tense as he knew they were doing something the Prince wasn\u2019t going to like, but he didn\u2019t think it was a good idea to talk to me about it. I didn\u2019t press as I knew Truman wouldn\u2019t work against me. I let it go and moved back toward the bar.<br /> <br /> Bright Eyes ambushed me with a question I never expected to hear. She invited me to the after party if I was interested. I reminded her that I would stand out given that don\u2019t normally have guys around. Bright Eyes reminded me that was not her fault, but also that she had invited Ildefonso. I guessed correctly that that was her fault. I spoke to Noriko about the after party. I didn\u2019t want to assume too much given all the good will people had shown me lately. She didn\u2019t really seem interested and headed back to the bar. When she came back, she was much more into the idea of going home together.<br /> <br /> I can take those kind of subtle hints. But as we were getting ready to leave, Chandra came back alone. She talked to Truman before I got there to check on things. I\u2019m not sure exactly what they were doing, but Chandra took me \u201cquestioning\u201d her very poorly and she almost seemed to turn aggressive. She was acting much more socially vampiric than usual, which I recognized but I\u2019m not sure that Noriko did. The cold look in her eyes told me I needed to defuse things quickly. For her part, Chandra backed off when she realized I wasn\u2019t challenging her. Probably also a bit of realization I wasn\u2019t a vampire and Noriko was getting twitchy. Once we were back on the same side, things calmed down for everyone notably faster.<br /> <br /> I made an attempt to politely decline the invitation to Nightshade afterwards, who teased me in general. It was good natured and I knew she wasn\u2019t upset. From there, I took Noriko home. She\u2019s purring in her sleep now and I\u2019m going to bed as well. With everyone back to themselves, it\u2019ll be interesting to see where we head to next.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> Sara smiled broadly, leaving off teasing Karen about her homework and Tatum about her suit, as Alice, Eris and her pack walked in. She moved to intercept them, hugging Deirdre and giving Ildefonso a brief kiss. Her trepidation didn\u2019t show on her face as she smiled warmly at Alice. She was glad for it as the redhead smiled back, no trace of the tension of a few days ago. Sara was able to relax some - Alice\u2019s emotions were usually painted on her face, often in some shade of red.<br /> <br /> As if matching deed to thought, Alice blushed, looking at something over Sara\u2019s shoulder. Sara glanced herself, seeing Noriko look away and settle back into her seat. The pack mostly split off, but Alice joined Sara, heading over to Natalie\u2019s reserved table when Noriko and Doc sat. Once they got there, they chatted cheerfully, catching Alice up with the events of the past few days. Natalie was in and out, performing that social butterfly dance that she did so well, making sure everyone felt welcome.<br /> <br /> After a bit, Doc stepped away and Sara, catching a look or two that flew between Alice and Noriko, made her own excuses. She went back to teasing Karen until Natalie stopped by and pulled her aside.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think there might be some unanticipated fallout of the Balehound\u2019s influence. I don\u2019t suppose Eris is bisexual... no...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think it would work, even if she was.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re in agreement there... but god, that would be hot.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave Natalie an amused and mock-chiding look, noticing Alice and Noriko scootch apart, Alice\u2019s blush deepening by a shade or two. She couldn\u2019t hide her smile even as bad as she felt for the two of them. A few moments later, she raised an eyebrow, confused, as a waiter brought the two of them drinks, putting a Corona down in front of Noriko and a vodka down next to Alice.<br /> <br /> Noriko looked down at the drinks before picking up the Corona and handing it over. Alice took it, blushing, and pushed the vodka over, her fingers lingering on the cold glass as Noriko scooted the glass the rest of the way over. Natalie and Sara shared a look.<br /> <br /> Doc wandered up behind Natalie. She leaned back, tilting her head to look up at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo do you two know what\u2019s up between those two? I thought the switched drinks might soften the weird tension, but it doesn\u2019t seem to have.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy don\u2019t you go talk to them?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smiled upside down at him, straightening up and giving him a little push when he hesitated. His arrival at the table didn\u2019t help the blushing situation, but Noriko seemed to take it in stride. Natalie and Sara kept an eye on them, using a mirror, but with no explosions seeming imminent, they relaxed.<br /> <br /> Natalie went back to socializing first, moving to steer Neon back away from Tatum before continuing her rounds. Sara scanned the room, eyes lighting on Cindy. She hadn\u2019t seen the cybergoth girl in awhile, so she danced her way over to her table. Cindy smiled to see her and invited her to sit with. After the usual pleasantries, Cindy let out a deep breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cI just... I\u2019m just not gonna sleep with Trinh again. She\u2019s just way too, I dunno, schizophrenic.\u201d<br /> <br /> She slumped in her seat.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe threatened me with her boyfriend last time. Huh. I\u2019ll put out his Pilot Light.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara put a comforting hand on hers, and let the frustrated girl bend her ear. She glanced at Natalie, eyebrow raised, as Cindy told her how Natalie and Trinh had finally broken things off for good. Trinh had pulled her hot and cold routine one too many times on Natalie, and wound up on the floor of Murder Ballads with Karen\u2019s boot on her chest. It explained why Sara hadn\u2019t seen Trinh down there in awhile, and why Trinh showed up at Cindy\u2019s door, instead of the club, when she was looking to be \u2018seduced\u2019 by another \u2018evil woman\u2019.<br /> <br /> At the end of her rant, Cindy sighed again and smiled slightly over at Sara.<br /> <br /> \u201cWanna dance?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWith you? Always.\u201d<br /> <br /> After a song, Sara bowed out, laughing, and headed back over to Natalie's table, where Doc was now sitting alone. As she sat down, she noticed Sarah had shown up and waved her over. At a nod from Sara, one of the bartenders caught the banshee as she stood up, and gave her a second drink for Sara. Sarah smiled as she slid it across the table.<br /> <br /> They chatted for a time, catching each other up. Sarah winced as the holidays were brought up.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, half of my relatives kept vaguely expressing sympathy and the other half had no idea what was going on.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara winced along with her, and Doc looked pained. Sarah shrugged and smiled almost shyly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI did go on a date with Tracey. I\u2019ll probably go on another. And Marie\u2019s only a little mad at me.\u201d<br /> <br /> A cheer went up from a few tables over as Barrett managed to pick up a napkin with forks tied into his beard, Deidre egging him on. He had a decent pile of money sitting next to him, which a few of the folks nearby were adding to. Looking over at them, Sara caught sight of Alice and Eris heading towards the table, so she scooted over to make room, smiling.<br /> <br /> Introductions were made all around, since Sarah had never met Alice and Eris. When the conversation turned to Alexia\u2019s \u2018school\u2019, Sarah brought Alice\u2019s blush back, even sending her hiding behind Eris as she teased the redhead about being \u2018too good\u2019 for teaching.<br /> <br /> The conversation was interrupted as Doc noticed Rebecca and Chandra leave the club together. He took his leave, going over to talk to Truman, who Rebecca had spoken to just before leaving. The ladies chatted for awhile, until Sarah got pulled out to dance by Marie and Natalie glided over to speak to Alice and Eris.<br /> <br /> Sara watched those three, chuckling as Alice\u2019s look of surprise turned into a deep blush. Natalie smiled at the pair of them, touching Alice gently on the arm. They nodded, and with a quick look at each other, reached a mutual decision to go dance.<br /> <br /> Natalie joined Sara at the table, sliding in next to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I invited Alice and Eris to the after party...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled, leaning into her wife.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave any other suggestions? Karen and Tatum of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cCindy could use something to take her mind off Trinh.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s face fell.<br /> <br /> \u201cI told her... apparently we need to get her a girlfriend that will threaten Trinh anytime she shows up. It worked for me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about Doc? And the werewolves?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll let you invite Doc and Noriko then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled up at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat about Neon?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou want vampires?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you met me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked at her wife in mock indignation. Natalie rolled her eyes, kissing her on the tip of her nose. Sara straightened up, stretching for a proper kiss before she let the strawberry scented woman wander off again.<br /> <br /> Sara scanned the room for Doc, finding him talking with Truman. She waited until he broke off from the vampire\u2019s table and ambushed him at the bar, presenting the invitation to the afterparty with a gleam in her eye. He looked taken aback.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019m a little out of place at you guys\u2019 afterparties.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s not my fault! Ildefonso\u2019s getting invited.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat one is your fault, I\u2019d guess?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled enigmatically up at him. He looked uncertainly at Noriko and promised to get back to Sara, before going to talk to his girlfriend. Sara found Alice and Eris talking with Tanya, which looked a little tense, so she decided not to interrupt them. Natalie was talking with Deirdre and Alexia and Catherine were occupied, so Sara went to bother Tatum as the night wound up.<br /> <br /> She almost missed the last bit of excitement before the club closed, as Chandra came back without Rebecca. She only noticed because Alice stopped in her tracks as she was waving goodbye. Sara followed the redhead\u2019s eye line to see Chandra standing close to Doc, getting in his face. After a tense moment, the penangalan backed down, and rejoined Alexia and Chandra.<br /> <br /> Alice and Doc had a brief conversation, but after Alice\u2019s understanding nod and another wave, Sara relaxed. Natalie joined her at the bar as the rest of the krewe, and most of the other patrons, left. When it was just the invited guests, Natalie swept across the dance floor towards the champagne room. Sara watched her go, only hopping off the barstool when Natalie turned slightly and beckoned over her shoulder.<br /> <br /> The next morning Sara woke up slowly, listening to Natalie and Karen fuss over Neon. She sat up sleepily, and a little woozily, leaning against the arm of the sofa. Her two wives were arranging Neon in the bottom cabinet of a large vanity.<br /> <br /> \u201cHopefully she\u2019ll remember about the escape button.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cD\u2019ya tell\u2019er before I had the champagne and the e\u2018stasy?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie and Karen both turned to look at Sara. Karen shook her head, smiling.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did. And, Tatum, get dressed, we need to go.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNooooo... I don\u2019 wan\u2019er too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara reached out and grabbed Tatum\u2019s wrist, pulling her close and burying her face in between Tatum\u2019s shoulder blades. Karen rolled her eyes and pulled the two apart, pushing Tatum towards her clothes. She pushed Sara back down onto the sofa, straddling her and putting her hands around the tattooed girl\u2019s throat. She let up as Sara\u2019s life flickered. Sara smiled up at her wife thankfully, and much less woozily.<br /> <br /> At the Bluffs they found Alice and Eris finishing up a simple bacon and eggs breakfast. The couple glanced at each other and started to apologize before Karen sent Tatum off to wake Alexia up and get back undressed. Alice blushed.<br /> <br /> \u201cI... I don\u2019t think that\u2019s appropriate...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOK Tatum, you can keep your clothes on. Just 'cause Alice asked though.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatum gave Alice a thankful look as she went to get Alexia. She returned quickly with not only Alice, Chandra and Catherine, but Doc and Noriko as well. Alice and Eris stuck around as the rest of them ate, since they were discussing their Underworld plans. Natalie smiled over at her wives.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m prepared. I do like to celebrate life before a trip to the Underworld. That place brings out emotions that I enjoy, just not those tied to my higher self.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re all packed as well - we were prepared for it yesterday. No time for ghosts flashlights, but we do have Sara.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tavia perked up at Doc\u2019s comment.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou have ghost flashlights? That\u2019ll be awesome for scary stories with Troy!\u201d<br /> <br /> When Sara made sure Catherine was still up for helping Angelique, and Angelique was still up for being helped, they got sidetracked by a little by Alice asking Angelique about her history with Tanya.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not what you think - she\u2019s straight. Well... I haven\u2019t locked her in a room with Natalie and checked in twenty minutes.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI heard that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Angelique and Natalie shared a smile before the werewolf explained the part of what had gone on between them that she was aware of. She had lied to Tanya, in an attempt to save Malard\u2019s reputation and Tanya had pushed until her lies fell apart. That didn\u2019t seem to satisfy either Alice or Angelique as an explanation for Tanya\u2019s reactions but if Angelique knew more, she wasn\u2019t telling.<br /> <br /> Doc brought up the SCUBA gear, in case they wanted to explore the pirate ship. The more he talked about it, the stormier Karen\u2019s face got, until she forbade her wives from going near it. She wasn\u2019t swayed by their protestations that it was just going to be reconnaissance, making pointed references to napalm. She did smile slightly at Tatum\u2019s confused reaction.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe burn pirates here, see. Talk Like A Pirate Day was a real blood bath for awhile.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tatum looked between the krewe, who all nodded along.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow long, on average, do you guys go without committing a felony?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTechnically, you committed one last night...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smile at Tatum\u2019s scrunched up face while Alice stared at him, considering.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs murder a felony?\u201d<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLVI</i><br /> <br /> This was a social session with few die rolls, short of Empathy checks and social rolls. Alice\u2019s player was back this time, and we had some tensions with Noriko all over, which cumulated into the two kissing in the restroom before regaining their composure. Otherwise Sara covered most of it. Poor Doc has little idea of what is going on either with that or Chandra and Rebecca\u2019s machinations. But we all had fun.<br /> <br /> Next session we return to the Underworld to spend some badly owed time there as required by their Psyche, and they discover more about the threat on the coast. Comments and Questions welcome.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T23:26:04-07:00","id":874293,"title":"","content":"Given how intense and disturbing the end of that Balehound business was, I'd have thought there would have been a more spectacular fallout, although I guess there could still be future repercussions.<br /> I wonder what effect that transgression curse would have had on Jasmine...<br /> Was Doc's sleeping around something decided by his player or was there some kind of roll involved?<br /> What did Tavia do in Rhodes Island?<br /> Is it normal that the Middle Shadows make me think of the X-men?<br /> So many questions!<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-25T23:36:42-07:00","id":874299,"title":"","content":"1) Well, the group handled it about as maturely as they could have. It is not repercussion free, though. Noriko and Alice are struggling with their feelings for each other, even as both love their partner. Natalie has some loss of face since Karen slept with Moire. And Alice and Sara are not quite as they were.<br /> 2) Heh that I dare not guess.<br /> 3) Player decided, and cleared with me.<br /> 4) Simon had a fling with a woman from there that Doc was thrust into helping cover up. I think Gwen helped too but not positive. He since discovered she was pregnant. This could have something to do with it.<br /> 5) Not necessarily. I don't see any obvious analogues though. The &quot;special school&quot; with the students has lead to a lot of x-men references.<br /> <br /> Thanks for feedback, as always.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:01:55-07:00","id":874312,"title":"","content":"Mostly they make me think of Marvel superheroes because they're a quasi-incestuously close group with the habit to fight and/or seduce most of the supernatural critters they meet as well as each other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-26T00:13:44-07:00","id":874317,"title":"","content":"That's my games in nutshell. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T00:47:59-07:00","id":879960,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to head into the Underworld. The Krewe does some exploring to fill their required Underworld time and push past recent drama. They are mostly successful.<br /> <i><br /> Session CLVII</i><br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> As the krewe made their preparations to head into the Underworld, Chandra bowed out, claiming she had business and giving Alexia a significant look. Catherine kissed Alexia on the cheek before going off with Angelique. Eris and Noriko stuck close to their partners, following them to the ritual room. Natalie conducted a ritual to focus their efforts, focusing more on the krewe\u2019s nature than their unity this time, as they \u2018descended into the lands under their stewardship\u2019. <br /> <br /> They went together to the Gate and Alice stepped up to open it. Sara moved close behind her, offering the redhead her engagement ring charm with a flourish and a wink. Alice took it with a good-humored sigh and a smile. She accepted the offered charms from the other members of the krewe as well, and quickly opened the Gate.<br /> <br /> Once on the other side, Sara lit up, flaring brightly. Her Caul provided plenty of light to see even in the constant twilight of the Underworld and brought the bright colors of Natalie\u2019s chimeric eyes, Alice\u2019s hair and Sara\u2019s clothes and tattoos into sharp relief. The krewe set out for the beach, pausing at the top of the cliff overlooking the ocean. Alice sighed happily, eyes sparkling, taking in the view.<br /> <br /> \u201cI love this. It really shows how the ocean is like a desert, just of water.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA desert of water? Really?\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc looked at her disdainfully. Alice tried, briefly, to explain what she meant, deflating a little with each of Doc\u2019s responses. Natalie stepped up to the edge, putting a hand on Alice\u2019s shoulder. The strawberry scented woman looked off into the distance herself, taking a drag on her clove.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe desert doesn\u2019t pull you into its embrace quite the same way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh it can. The desert got me... once.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc had a hard look in his eye as his jaw clenched. He looked off into the distance, not seeing even seeing the ocean view, and was only pulled out of his memories, awkwardly, by a high five from Alice.<br /> <br /> Alice led the way down the steep path, Sara following with Natalie close behind, the latter gasping as Sara made a controlled tumble down the path. Doc and Alexia held up the rear, Doc a little unsteady at the steepest parts of the path.<br /> <br /> Once at the bottom, they discussed their option, ultimately deciding to go towards the boat of lost regrets rather than the lighthouse. As they passed the boat, Sara\u2019s curiosity got the better of her and she looked over at it. She bit her lip at its name, Melissa Jackson, that it shared with the mother Sara had never met. She noticed Alice avoided looking at the boat after her initial glance, fingering the bracelet she always wore. Natalie was more obvious in her reaction, taking out Nataliebane and looking the gun over.<br /> <br /> Doc was prodded into action by whatever he saw. Alice moved to stop him as he strode towards the boat, but when she saw the knife in his hands, she stepped back, offering her axe. He waved her aside, sawing the boat\u2019s mooring line until it snapped. The boat rocked but didn\u2019t move.<br /> <br /> He moved back to the group, noticing that Noriko was pointedly ignoring the boat, even as the group was paused around it. He looked inquisitively at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are things better not brought up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re in the Underworld - that\u2019s what we\u2019re all about here.\u201d<br /> <br /> He put a comforting arm around her waist. Alice smiled wryly over at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAren\u2019t you glad you\u2019re here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is where those I love are.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s smile in response to that was less wry.<br /> <br /> Fifteen minutes of hiking with crabs scuttling away from Sara\u2019s bright Caul, they found an interesting stretch of beach. On the water side were four quays and three rocky islands. A tugboat was tied up to one quay. Another had a line tied off, but the rope extended tautly down into the water. The three islands were small, two barely large enough for a few people to stand on together. The third, and furthest, had a small shack on it. On the edges of the islands are the remnants of rope bridges that once connected all three.<br /> <br /> Across from the quays, there was a dark opening in the cliffs. Alice\u2019s eyes lit up as they fell on it.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis looks promising - those islands look interesting and you know I can\u2019t resist caves.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc told the story of the islands, about how there were legends of sailors being marooned there in a storm, and haunting the area. Natalie added that the former krewe had used them for Ceremonies until they had sunk into the ocean. They got sidetracked into a discussion of quays versus keys, with Natalie finally setting everyone straight. She shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI grew up on an island.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI didn\u2019t even know what an island was until I left Arizona.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice kept a straight face as Doc looked disbelievingly at her, and winked at Eris who was hiding a big smile.<br /> <br /> They decided to explore the cave first. Alice eyed the cliff wall, frowning slightly. She took a coil of rope and some pitons, hammering in a path for the others. Doc climbed next to her, mirroring her rope road with a second coil of rope. <br /> <br /> The cave was impenetrably dark until Sara pulled herself up on to the lip of the cave. Her Caul lit up the sloped tunnel and once they had gathered and Natalie put out her clove, much to Alice\u2019s relief, they followed it down, stopping at a mounted metal plate a few yards in. <br /> <br /> The plate was warped and broken but they could read the first few lines etched in it:<br /> <br /> \u2018No traveler shall provide assistance to another traveler.<br /> No traveler shall refuse assistance from another traveler.<br /> No trave\u2019<br /> <br /> Sara looked over at Natalie nervously, reaching for her hand. The krewe debated what the plate meant for a few minutes, ultimately not reaching a conclusion, but deciding to be careful, given that it sounded like a list of Old Laws, for all that they hadn\u2019t crossed a river.<br /> <br /> They continued forward, not coming across any side passages, nooks or crannies. They stopped after about ten minutes, noticing the first sign of the presence of any other in the cave, a floating greenish blue light. Alice peered into the darkness.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s something way down there.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDefine something.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA ghost. A really old one. It looks a little like a scarecrow with a cow skull for a head.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris shifted into the form of a large wolf, and she and Alice took the lead, the redhead\u2019s left hand buried in the scruff of her mate\u2019s neck. The krewe moved carefully towards the light, then more confidently as the ghost failed to react. The scarecrow stood at a crossroads in the cave tunnel, the first they\u2019d found so far. The tunnel split in four direction - left, right, down and straight ahead.<br /> <br /> Sara glanced at the others, then stepped forward, addressing the ghost, greeting him and asking what he knew of the area. He turned to look at the tattooed girl, pointing down each path in turn. As he pointed to each one, Sara had a mental impression of what lay in that direction. The right led to the manor. He advised her to avoid it. The left led to the library. Ahead lay the Chamber, another place he recommended she avoid. The road down led to the ocean. He advised caution, should she travel that path.<br /> <br /> Sara relayed these impression, pausing to ask the ghost for a name. The response she got was a Native American concept somewhere between a watcher and a guide. When she began by asking clarification on the manor. She frowned at his response, looking nervously at Doc.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Manor is the house on the hill we\u2019ve heard about. The Guide says it\u2019s... older than the Underworld.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that... how is that possible?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara shrugged at Alice\u2019s question.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt looked like something else, once, apparently.\u201d<br /> <br /> She bit her lip and asked after the downward path. It led under the ocean, she saw in her head, and was the safe way to cross it, but she would have to be careful not to get drawn into the ocean as she was under it. She told the others, nodding when Alice suggested that might be an adventure for another day.<br /> <br /> Sara smiled at the old ghost as she asked after the last path, the one that led to the Chamber. She got the idea of a trap, a cage, that psychopomps like her had used to capture something dangerous. Alice\u2019s eyes gleamed excitedly when Sara relayed that. Doc tried to talk her out of charging down that path, making reference to the infamous napalm recon mission.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe are the only group of people I know who need napalm for recon, and even we didn\u2019t bring any today, understand?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, I don\u2019t, cause you\u2019ve never actually told me the story, but I get your meaning.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice looked unhappy, but after the krewe left their offerings, she turned towards the tunnel they\u2019d come from. Sara took her arm as they walked, telling the full napalm reconnaissance story. Alice smiled at her as they reached the mouth of the cave and helped her start her climb.<br /> <br /> The group decided to check out the tugboat first, since it was much easier to get to. Alice hopped on as soon as she gave it a once over, the rest of the group following once nothing untoward happened right off. Nothing happened at all, until Natalie opened the door to the helm.<br /> <br /> \u201cBoat\u2019s not going anywhere today, the Captain\u2019s not feeling well.\u201d<br /> <br /> A ghost in a ratty maid's uniform spoke. Her stringy hair covered her face as she gestured at the captain\u2019s chair. In it was a moss covered skeleton, skull lolling to the side. Doc moved into the small room, addressing the ghost.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s not been feeling well for awhile, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope. I think \u2018e\u2019s got the gout.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc tried to question the ghost about the boat and the rope tied off to nothing, but she claimed to not know much, suggesting that the Captain might, in between trying to get the skeleton to help her tidy up the place. When she prodded him to tidy up the maps, Doc cleared his throat and asked to see them.<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, they\u2019re the Captain\u2019s! Only if he says so.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled mischievously and a tenor voice came from the captain\u2019s chair, telling the ghost to let Doc have a look. The ghost shrugged and rummaged around before finding and handing them over. Doc looked them over carefully, noting the handful of nearby islands, the red X marking the boat of regrets and the hand-labeled \u2018Pup Pid\u2019s Wreck\u2019.<br /> <br /> Alice blinked a little, then moved to stand near the mossy skeleton, looking him over while Doc kept talking to the ghost.<br /> <br /> \u201cHave you ever seen Pup Pid?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNope, I\u2019m still here.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie frowned, drawing her gun. Doc paused in his interrogation, looking over at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s lying.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSeeing Pup Pid.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc and Alice shifted into a fighting stance and Sara summoned her keystone knife, as the maid threw her hair back, revealing a skull with glowing yellow eyes and golden teeth. The ghost drew a sword and a pistol made of blood. Natalie leveled her gun while the others waited outside the helm.<br /> <br /> The three in the cabin, and Natalie with her gun, made short work of the ghost, but not before she scored a strong hit on Alice. She bulwarked the physical damage, but looked drawn. She shivered once the ghost splashed into warm salt water, sizzling like acid on the deck.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think that hit me in my soul.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eris wormed her way into the helm to put an arm around her mate. Natalie put her gun away, looking stricken as she laid a hand on Alice\u2019s shoulder.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry. I didn\u2019t... I expected her to back down when I called her out, not attack a whole group of us.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice squeezed her hand, smiling and waving off her apologies. She let the rest of them know what she had read off the dead captain. He had been a ghost in the area for awhile before being killed, again, by a member of Pup Pid\u2019s crew. He did, in fact, know something about the other rope tied off at the quays. A ship had come in, sometime before this place was in the Underworld. The crew was terrified and they scuttled their own ship as soon as they landed.<br /> <br /> Natalie and Doc began looking around the helm now that the guardian was no longer there. Once Alice finished explaining what she\u2019d learned, Natalie looked up, frowning.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething is off about this boat. I can\u2019t tell if it\u2019s because it\u2019s older than the ones I\u2019m used to, or if something is wrong.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDo we wanna risk unmooring it then? Just in case?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked nervously at the dock, beginning to feel a little queasy. Alice shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe don\u2019t need it, unless we\u2019re going past the islands.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou don\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll make sure you get across.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, Doc throws me across and you catch?\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice smiled at the tattooed woman, rolling her eyes good naturedly. Sara grinned back wickedly, her nervousness forgotten for the moment. Her queasiness came back full blast though, as she looked over at Natalie and saw her poring over some paperwork.<br /> <br /> When Natalie mentioned cargo manifests, Sara joined Doc in looking for a cargo hold, an unusual thing for a tugboat to have. They didn\u2019t find one. Still, it distracted Sara from the rocking of the boat. Alice dealt with her own seasickness by hopping out onto the quay with Eris.<br /> <br /> Doc and Natalie consulted on the paperwork she had found. All of it was for a ship called the Mermaid\u2019s Carriage. The manifests\u2019 last entry was a load of gold, dated 1840, with no receiving signature. They stashed the papers away for a more detailed perusal later, especially a wax-sealed letter addressed to a Captain Namoth. The seal on the wax was two horses pulling a carriage with a lion rampant. Neither of the more local Sin-eaters recognized it, and with a look at the greenish Sara, they put it in the pack with the rest, without breaking it open.<br /> <br /> When the three of them left the helm, Sara\u2019s brow knit, looking for Alice. She grinned and waved when she found her, standing braced on the rocky shore of the third island. Doc followed Sara\u2019s eyeline and growled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need a harpoon.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked at him sternly, while swaying her way over to the rope bridges Alice had rigged up while they searched the helm. She walked gracefully over the first two, 'stumbling' at the end of the third bridge as Alice reached for her. She wound up falling into the redhead\u2019s arms and winked up at her.<br /> <br /> Doc rolled his eyes as he climbed up onto the island, accepting Alice\u2019s helping hand once she\u2019d set Sara upright further up the beach. He looked over the hastily built shack, taking a deep breath and blowing hard in its direction, a smile playing over his face. Sara grinned at him.<br /> <br /> \u201cOK Mr Big Bad Wolf!\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t even begin to claim that title.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc gestured towards Eris, who was shifting out of wolf form. The werewolf snickered as Alice turned bright red. She turned to hide her blushing face and focused on the shack.<br /> <br /> After a moment she signaled people to come up. They all walked into the one room shack, and as soon as they crossed the threshold, the weres, Alice and Natalie all perked up, looking around uneasily. Natalie drew her pistol. Alice looked at Doc and Sara.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething\u2019s watching us.\u201d<br /> <br /> The group moved carefully, looking over the small room. The furniture was minimal - a bureau, a small writing desk and a chair sitting by the window. A rifle sat on top of the bureau. On the window sill next to the chair was an ornate wooden pipe and a bottle of scotch. Below them was a pair of boots.<br /> <br /> Sara spoke to the air, greeting whoever was watching. If they heard, they didn\u2019t respond to her, or to Doc\u2019s written note. Natalie had found a locked drawer in the bureau and hunkered down next to it, pulling out a hairpin. A few moments of jimmying got the drawer open. Inside was an old flintlock pistol and a map of an unnamed island. Natalie handed the gun over to Doc.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has a resonance like a ghost. I don\u2019t know how it is significant, though it\u2019s maybe something\u2019s weakness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI guess it\u2019ll take research, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice smiled resignedly at Doc. Sara grinned encouragingly at her. They gave the room another look over as Alice commented on how homey the shack was. Sara nodded excitedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe were trying to find places for each of us, right? Maybe we could just get this stretch of the beach - Natalie seemed to feel at home in the boat, you like the feel of the shack, Alice, and surely Doc could dock the pirate ship around here. I just want to set up a camped caravan somewhere, so that\u2019d work on this beach. We need to find a place for Alexia, but it would mean safety in numbers, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s face fell.<br /> <br /> \u201cBut... I thought...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked at her, concerned, but Natalie shook her head.<br /> <br /> \u201cFirst we have to deal with the pirate ship.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded and suggested Doc step outside with the gun and see if that drew the watcher\u2019s eye. It didn\u2019t, but after a couple of minutes, the unseen presence disappeared completely. Just as those who could detect it began to relax, Alice and Eris looked outside.<br /> <br /> \u201cSomething\u2019s moving in the water.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA lot of somethings!\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc started yelling, counting around twenty skeletal sailors climbing up onto the island, all armed with pistols and swords made of blood. Alice rushed outside, the others close behind.<br /> <br /> Natalie put a hand on Sara\u2019s shoulder and asked the other woman to catch her. She did, quickly, as the strawberry scented woman collapsed into a trance. As soon as her eyes closed, the skeletons already on the island froze in place. Natalie muttered into Sara\u2019s ear.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s about fifty of them. We have thirty yards of wards.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara let the rest know, wincing at the gleam in Alice\u2019s eyes as the redhead set to smashing skulls, counting down from fifty giddily. Sara made her way carefully across the rope bridges, cradling Natalie close. After a few moments, Doc managed to get Alice to follow and the group made good time back home.<br /> <br /> Once they got home, they stashed the gun in the war room at the Bluffs and headed back in. They agreed to explore away from the beach, to let the heat die down. Alice was interested in checking out the noose orchard that she, Eris, Alexia, and Chandra had passed over last time. They decided to check in at the diner first. As they started down the path towards the diner, Sara hung back, taking Natalie\u2019s arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s wrong love?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... I assumed we would have the same place. Because we\u2019re soulmates.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s shoulders slumped and she bit her lip.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think we all need a place that resonates with our own Selves. I do want to be close to you though. And not just for safety in numbers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI want to be close to you too.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie pulled Sara close, clinging tightly. Sara kissed her gently, holding her protectively. The strawberry scented woman nuzzled her neck, whispering in her ear.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe should be close. Our souls are bound together.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara\u2019s breath hitched. She managed a smile for her love, kissing her again and putting an arm around her waist. Natalie leaned against her wife, reaching up to play with the hair at the nape of her neck.<br /> <br /> The walk to the diner wasn\u2019t long. Once there, they settled into a booth, ordering milkshakes from the Matron. Janice wandered over after a moment and took a seat after Doc offered. They chatted for awhile before Doc brought up Pup Pid.<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s a pirate? And a really powerful ghost. Probably cause he can\u2019t leave the coast. I don\u2019t know much. There are stories about things being left on the beach, so that if you touch them, you get stuck and pulled underwater to become one of his crew.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe did meet some of his crew.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m guessing they didn\u2019t want to exchange bottles of scotch.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, more like attack our souls.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc looked to Alice, who nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cTheir skulls split like anything else though.\u201d<br /> <br /> The subject wandered for awhile after that, until Janice asked if they knew about the living redhead woman that had shown up around the area. Natalie tensed a little until Janice clarified that she wasn\u2019t a Sin-eater.<br /> <br /> Alice realized it was Dulcinea, Doc nodding along with her.<br /> <br /> \u201cOur vampire friends said she was a cousin, and she controls bees.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLike, Draculas? Really? I guess I can\u2019t throw stones, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Once they finished their milkshakes, they left payment in the form of smokes, ribbon, twist caps and bottle of Corona. Alice took the lead again, directing them towards the noose orchard. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> December 7th 2010<br /> <br /> We have come back inside for a little while, and my beloved is comforting me. It was all showdowns and heroics till we were coming back, and Sara wanted a separate zone in the Underworld from me. This troubles me, because I consider herself, Karen, and I a unit (which may or may not include Tatum someday), a family, and part of becoming a family means joining together. Sara understands this. <br /> <br /> Sara needs to understand how important this union is to me. I draw strength from my lovers, and doubly so my wives. Without them, alone, I am helpless, so it is critical to me I never be alone, even if I am physically. My Krewe has a bond and they are extended family. I NEED my wives to be joined to my soul as much as the Laughing Lady is. Sara seems to understand intellectually.<br /> <br /> I need to understand Sara needs freedom. Just staying in one place with us, with me, is a compromise of who she is. Calling me wife is a compromise of who she is. I am fucking clingy. Sara loves me. Sara does not deny our souls are joined. But that is a sacrifice she makes, not a source of strength. Rubbing it in her face solves nothing. Karen is fine with it, but I must respect her needs as she respects mine.<br /> <br /> I will talk to Sara about this. Perhaps if we have separate areas that are together and have a common border and we feel comfortable entering and leaving freely but we decorate and leave a personal imprint on is a compromise that hopefully will make her happy and myself happy. She and I will discuss it when not in the underworld and we are relaxed and calm. <br /> <br /> I should touch on what happened inside.<br /> <br /> We discovered two new areas along the coast. One is a deep cave with a Native Yellowbones who watches a crossroads that leads into the sea, into a chamber where a Krewe, unsure which, sealed something bad, toward the manor, and toward the library/city. We left tokens. Sara handled most of the discussion\u2026it seem to communicate in feelings and images, not words. <br /> <br /> We found an odd arrangement along the coast past the boat, three large rocky islands in the ocean, each raised water level enough that one could not just wade in. The largest and farthest had a cabin, and there was a tugboat tied to some quays, as well as a rope that went into the water. There was a \u201cdead\u201d ghost in the tugboat, and a ghost that looked like a maid. We did some negotiation with Sara even using ventriloquism to trick her into letting us near the maps. However, when Pup Pid came up, she lied about having seen him, forcing me to call her out. There was a short fight, but Alice was hurt. I should not have been so direct. I did not think she would take us on.<br /> <br /> After we explored the other locations, there were more of the ghosts. In the cabin we noticed we were being watched, and I discovered a pistol after picking a drawer lock. The pistol was of older make than any others, and had a map with it. Soon after taking it the sea vomited up it\u2019s dead, as a small army of salt-water ghosts began climbing onto the island. I had my wife grab me and desperately poured my plasm into using the Stigmata Boneyard. That held them while we escaped.<br /> <br /> It is clear Pup Pid must be dealt with before we can acquire the territory, but I admit it interests me. Living on an island, quays, tugs, and small outcroppings were part of my childhood, and the thought of having them there pleases me deeply. Indeed, my sea legs proved greater than anyone\u2019s really but Doc\u2019s; he and I were able to read documents on the tug, which seemed to make Alice and Sara queasy just thinking about it. I was a good girl; I did not openly display my reveling in being able to do even which badass women like Alice could not. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s time to go back. We are hitting the caf\u00e9, then this forest Alice is talking about. More later.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLVII</i><br /> <br /> Seriously how did \u201cquay\u201d become \u201ckey\u201d anyway?<br /> <br /> A lot of Athletics rolls this time, for climbing, jumping, etc. No \u201csea legs\u201d rolls, that was strictly role-playing (Doc having been in the Navy and Natalie being raised on an Island) Alice was the master of the Athletics rolls. Natalie trapped the ghosts with the Stigmata Boneyard. The one combat was over very quickly. The \u201csoul hit\u201d did Willpower damage as well as normal damage.<br /> <br /> Short on time, so leaving it there. But comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T17:47:07-07:00","id":880610,"title":"","content":"Pirates! Harr!<br /> You need to have them fight ninjas at some points. It's a rule or something. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Also, the Krewe needs therapy. Badly. Especially Nathalie.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-02T20:25:41-07:00","id":880702,"title":"","content":"Oh I dunno. They seem to be doing okay given they have been dead. Doc, Jasmine and Natalie have actually had therapy before. Next session is Underworld Hijinx followed by immediate very real world problems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T00:18:05-07:00","id":891608,"title":"","content":"Oh man you guys, this has been a shitty week. I have barely slept until last night and I am still sore. Hopefully I will sleep tonight. But because my level of comfort rates just higher than sliding naked down a 10\u2019 greased razorblade, I am late with journals, and commentary will be low.<br /> <br /> This time around the fantasic vistas of the Underworld clash with the cold realities of a society all too often still homophobic, and remember this is almost six years ago. Note Doc had to miss this session.<br /> <i><br /> Session CLVIII</i><br /> <b><br /> Sara\u2019s Letters</b><br /> <br /> The group traveled through a few chambers, including one with a decent sized gazebo as a centerpiece and another overlooked by the sinister Manor. Sara shuddered as they passed by, moving closer to Natalie, keeping Alice between them and the house with its red lit windows. They moved at a casual pace through every chamber but that one, enjoying themselves and each other\u2019s company.<br /> <br /> The three-way crossroad was empty this time, and Alice made a beeline for the wall beneath the cavernous hole near the ceiling. She climbed quickly, stepping up the hand and foot holds like there was a wide ladder. Once up there she secured a rope and dropped it down. Sara followed next, shimmying quickly up and accepting the hand Alice extended with a sparkling smile. Alice smiled back before returning to the rope.<br /> <br /> When they came to a two pronged branch of the tunnel, Alice pointed left and the group followed her lead. In short order, the tunnel opened up to a hollowed out chamber, the ground covered with scattered bones, looking all the world like some mythical Beast\u2019s lair from one of Sara\u2019s fairy tale stories. At Sara\u2019s interested look, Alice explained that this is where they had met Dulcinea, before.<br /> <br /> They continued down the path, reaching the large gaping hole in the floor. The ropes and pitons Alice had placed to let the smaller group continue past were still in place. Alice took stock of things, her heightened senses piercing the dark orchard, the vague luminescence enough to let her make out a group of five young girls, carrying baskets and gathering fruit along a dark river.<br /> <br /> The nearest tree was four or five yards below the lip of the hole. Alice secured a rope and dropped down it, swinging to grab hold of the top branches of the tree. She attached the rope to a sturdy branch and noticed that a couple of the young women had taken note of her. A closer look revealed them to be eerily similar in silhouette - the same height, body shape, and hair style, though the colors, such as they were in the tenebrous Underworld, differed.<br /> <br /> \u201cGreetings. Do you mind if we joined you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo? Come on down.\u201d<br /> <br /> The girls looked at each other, clustering near the base of the tree, muttering amongst themselves. Alice was able to catch them deciding that the group couldn\u2019t be highwaymen, since they were all women, before her attention was wrapped up in making sure everyone climbed down safely.<br /> <br /> Once they were all down, the girls inched closer, one stepping forward and introducing herself as Marcella. She explained they were gathering fruit for their group. Eventually, she drew up a bit of courage, glancing back at the other girls.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are... very different than anyone who has crossed here before.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s revelation that the group was all alive started a twitter among the girls. The light and close quarters brought forward more similarities - a nose, the shape of a pair of lips, or an eyebrow line shared in precise detail by two or three of them. After a moment, Marcella looked back at her group.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you here to lead us out? To where we\u2019d be alive?\u201d<br /> <br /> The five girls nodded in unison, unblinking. Natalie\u2019s eyes said trouble and Sara\u2019s brow knit. Alexia glanced at them, and Alice, as Marcella said there were around 30 in their community. Alexia suggested research, with a significant look at the red head. Alice nodded, smiling coldly and shifting so her axe was closer at hand as she pointed out a visit would be excellent research.<br /> <br /> So the krewe followed the five girls further into the chambers. Alice dropped back to speak quietly with the others.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis screams Kool-Aid cult to me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey do kinda remind me of puppets. And Pirate Percy.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice looked questioningly at Alexia who explained while they approached the small, vaguely German town that was shrouded in mists. Fireflies lit with a green luminescence flitted around the streets, providing the soft lighting. Sara relaxed as the mist curled around her feet, smiling softly as she looked around the quaint town.<br /> <br /> Sara looked up at Alice sleepily, smiling, as the redhead put a hand on her shoulder. She frowned at Alice\u2019s stern look, then shook her head, looking sheepish. Natalie chuckled at her as she made a show of alertness. Alexia covered up the exchange, asking the ghosts why they didn\u2019t blink, getting nothing but blank stares in response.<br /> <br /> The girls led them to one of the larger houses, asking the krewe to wait outside while they spoke with the mother. After just a moment, they left, gesturing for them to go inside. The Mother sat on a comfortable chair, her long dark hair piled on top of her head. The black velvet of her choker stood out against her pale skin, and her gray and dark red dress suited her thin frame. The powerful geist gestured at the other chairs, inviting them to sit.<br /> <br /> \u201cI see you have stumbled on my little paradise.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cParadise? Then why are you trying to leave?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not actually taking them into the world, however, everyone feels better with something to work towards.\u201d<br /> <br /> The Mother explained her vision, extolling the virtues of her little paradise. Sara\u2019s discomfort faded somewhat, as the Mother explained how she accepted those who were afraid, giving them a safe place to rest, sealed off from the rest of the Underworld and its dangers, until an enemy caused the breach in the ceiling. She even explained the similarities: <br /> <br /> \u201cMy changed men are well muscled, my changed women unblemished. Eventually one gets tired of everyone being prettier than them.\u201d<br /> <br /> It did not fade completely, as her Passion Oracle left a distinct impression of something being withheld. She kept an eye on Alice as well. The redhead\u2019s hackles were up and distrust screamed from her every line.<br /> <br /> Keeping an eye on all of them, the Mother offered a deal. Raw materials, food and perhaps some finery in exchange for reshaping - ghosts, places, whatever they wanted. Sara\u2019s eyes lit up when the Mother mentioned reshaping places. Alice frowned at her. Sara caught the redhead\u2019s eyes and gave her a half smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf there\u2019s a deal - and I won\u2019t lie and say it\u2019s not tempting - we need to be open here. I know you\u2019re hiding something... if it\u2019s a deal breaker, we\u2019ll walk out, no harm, no foul. If not, maybe we can arrange some things.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA lady needs her secrets.\u201d<br /> <br /> She looked at Sara and Natalie significantly, as if to say she knew theirs. Sara linked her fingers with Natalie\u2019s, leaning in intimately, raising an eyebrow at the Mother. She looked away.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing here in the Underworld is truly pleasant. But I am not harming my people. They sustain me. The only ghosts I have destroyed are those who have committed crimes. All those here are here of their own will.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople can be persuaded to do many things...\u201d<br /> <br /> The Mother chuckled lightly at Alice.<br /> <br /> \u201cWith this charm and personality? I assure you, this is as friendly as I get.\u201d<br /> <br /> Some verbal dancing commenced and in the end, the only deal made was for free passage in exchange for not attempting to convince away any of the Mother\u2019s flock. The Mother nodded as they left, Alice taking up the rear and keeping an eye on the geist.<br /> <br /> As they left the house Sara looked around, noticing many more ghosts in the immediate area than there had been when they went in. A couple spoke quietly at the corner. A group of men were lugging firewood to a nearby house. A few of the girls were playing hopscotch and a few boys about their age played marbles a few feet away. That was just nearby; the fog was too thick and obscuring for Sara to make out more. Alice peered into it, her eyes narrowed.<br /> <br /> The ghosts followed them, far enough back in the fog that only Alice could make them out. They faded back and out of even her sight once the krewe started climbing the tree out. The group gathered in the tunnel above the orchard. Natalie immediately began writing subtle Sin-eater marks around the edge of the tunnel, warning others off, and explaining to those there what she had learned from observing the geist.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe can eat ghosts and spiritual creatures and gain their powers. She used to be much more predatory. I\u2019d wager she was sealed off by someone else, not her own hand, and has shifted into what we saw because of it.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI could see that side of her trying to come out. She\u2019s bad news. I know better than anyone what the predator inside you can push you to do.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice looked pensive, and pushed for taking the geist out. Natalie, Alexia and Eris nodded even as Natalie continued marking the cave, having moved on to silver spray painted warnings on the walls. Sara bit her lip and Alice softened.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the krewe doesn\u2019t want to do that, it\u2019s fine. It\u2019s fine! But I don\u2019t want anyone else wandering down - or her getting out.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara recognized the tone Alice got when talking to the Grasping Huntress. She laid on a hand on Alice\u2019s arm.<br /> <br /> \u201cOne\u2019s nature is often not fully their own doing. She protects those people now, and tends to them, whatever she may have done once. And... if they chose uniformity, that is, in the end, their choice. But. The lure is strong, both ghosts to beauty and her to her old ways. I won\u2019t object to resealing her paradise.\u201d<br /> <br /> They left it at that, since they had no way of sealing it, nor were they prepared to make an assault. Since Alice and Alexia had explored beyond the hole, they doubled back to the fork in the tunnels, choosing the last path. They spoke softly, bringing back the quiet cheer and camaraderie that had been lost in the Mother\u2019s domain.<br /> <br /> Topics wandered from Pokemon to Barbies to softball as they walked through the tunnels. They paused as the cave opened up into a cavernous room. A wide river cut through it, a small boat bobbing gently against the near bank. Near the boat a figure stood, cloaked but uncowled, his gray bulbous head uncovered. His eyes were bulging orbs and lit with a green luminescent light, similar to that the fireflies in the mother\u2019s domain gave off. A single tree, bare of leaves, grew near the bank, a large owl resting on its branches. The cloaked figure called out to them as they approached, striding towards them. <br /> <br /> \u201cAre you traveling to Cradlemoss? I hail from there, it is a pleasant place. I can provide ferry service, if you wish to cross to there. Or back, but no one ever wishes to leave Cradlemoss.\u201d<br /> <br /> The owl watched them interestedly, his eyes expressing skepticism at the figure\u2019s claims. The owl named himself a Psychopomp, when asked, and countered the cloaked man, calling Cradlemoss a strange place, saying it had suffered under its new Kerberoi. Alice nodded.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is the Underworld. Good places rarely go to so much trouble to draw people in.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two native creatures verbally sniped at each other, revealing that someone had eaten the old Kerberoi, and, at Natalie\u2019s questioning, they confirmed that it was the Mother, or at least who the Mother had been. The cloaked man warned her not to trust the cannibalistic spirit and continued more happily.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe new Kerberoi is the Laughing Darkness. He is much more jovial. Fear cannot exist without laughter - he tried to bring both.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe has put people into lockdown in order to get control.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt is what Kerberoi do. It is in their nature. Like yours is to be an annoying prick.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two glared at each other, only stopping to wish the group well as they took their leave. The krewe made their way back, since it was almost when they were due home. They made a quick stop at the diner at Alice\u2019s insistence, to warn the ghosts there about the Mother.<br /> <br /> As they walked home, they discussed plans to deal with Pup Pid. Natalie was fixated on exploding his ship to draw him out, though she did suggest making a deal with the Mother to eat him, with a mischievous look towards Alice who frowned at her. In the end, they decided to try and raise the pirate ship using the tugboat, since an aquatic assault was inadvisable, and Doc might still want the ship. Jasmine featured heavily in their plans, so they certainly weren\u2019t an immediate concern.<br /> <br /> When they got back to the living world, Alice stretched and smiled at the others.<br /> <br /> \u201cThanks guys. That was a fun time, aside from the Kool-Aid cult.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cKool-Aid! That\u2019s it!\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia took off for the kitchen, stopping before she got there when she ran into Karen. The younger woman had a tense look on her face and moved to stand next to Natalie and Sara, looking between the two.<br /> <br /> \u201cAbout fifteen members of my parent\u2019s church came to pray me home. We made them leave the property, so they crossed the street. Tavia called Mr. Malard, and... there\u2019s a lot of cops.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alice\u2019s eyes widened and she took a step back. Karen explained that no one had been hurt - he shot over their heads - but she was worried about the situation in general. Alexia started back off towards the kitchen, muttering about her emergency Malard cookies. <br /> <br /> Alice looked apologetically at the trio.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t think I\u2019ll be helpful. In fact, I might make it worse. I think Eris and I will go home, to the park.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen and Natalie nodded distractedly. Sara smiled up at her, wishing them well. On their way out, Alice and Eris ran into Officer Norris just as he was about to knock. Alice called back for Karen and the trio met him in the foyer.<br /> <br /> \u201cMrs. Knight. Ladies. I have some paperwork for you, to file a restraining order. Two sets - one for your parents and one for the priest, since he was the one leading them today. There's a pair for your wife, as well. I can\u2019t promise anything, but if you fill them out and bring them to me, I\u2019ll do my best to find a sympathetic judge.\u201d<br /> <br /> The women thanked him and moved to sit at the dining room table. The noise of Alexia rattling around in the kitchen, warming up frozen cookies, contrasted with their grim faces. Karen let out a long breath, looking at the paperwork. Sara stared intently at her until she began to fill it out.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry about this. I didn\u2019t tell them where we live...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie put an arm around Karen, pulling her close as Sara laid a hand on the younger woman\u2019s hand. They let her vent, telling them what had happened, including the threats Tavia used while holding a carving knife. After a few minutes, Alexia came in with a tin of cookies, checking if any of them wanted to go with her. Sara glanced at Natalie who nodded and pulled Karen closer. The tattooed woman patted Karen\u2019s shoulder and left with Alexia.<br /> <br /> Noriko was lurking around the door, watching Malard\u2019s house. She came along, an intent look on her face. Officer Tart stopped them at Malard\u2019s door, barring their way into the ongoing interview. Noriko stared at him, eyes narrowed.<br /> <br /> Sara smiled playfully up at him, laying a hand on his bicep. It didn\u2019t take long for her to sweet talk Tart into delivering the cookies to Malard and the other officer. There were no raised voices from inside, so Sara gently touched Noriko\u2019s shoulder and guided her away.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re trying to stop a bloodbath, remember?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s not dead, is he?\u201d<br /> <br /> Noriko turned her unnerving gaze on Sara, who nodded noncommittally. When they got back, Noriko took up her perch at the window overlooking Malard\u2019s house again, eyes fixed. Sara rejoined her wives, settling in next to Karen, encouraging her to keep filling out the paperwork as she relayed what had happened.<br /> <br /> As soon as the police left, Noriko was out of the house and on her way over there. Karen looked over at Sara, a hangdog expression on her face as she rubbed the heel of her hand. Sara grinned and suggested a movie. Karen\u2019s eyes brightened and she suggested Black Swan.<br /> <br /> The trio wandered the house, trying to find the others to invite them along. They found Chandra, Catherine and Alexia together, with Angelique nearby. Sara asked about the memory retrieval.<br /> <br /> \u201cI found a whole bunch of suppressed memories. It was starting to really hurt. I could maybe push through, with some coffee or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked concerned, encouraging her to be careful. Angelique gave her a wry smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suggested she avoid hurting herself.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s just an out of practice muscle. I could...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave her a look and suggested that she practice rather than push. Catherine conceded the point, especially since she wasn\u2019t sure how much of Angelique\u2019s more recent psyche would be intact if she burst through the walls blocking off those suppressed memories.<br /> <br /> On the way to the cars, Catherine looked apologetically at Karen.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry I wasn\u2019t more help, earlier. Large hostile crowds make me nervous. No one\u2019s called me a witch yet, but... they were very angry. \u201c<br /> <br /> Catherine bit her lip nervously, glancing at Natalie. <br /> <br /> \u201cAnd Natalie \u2013 you'll be careful?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara patted the psychic's shoulder and put an arm around Natalie\u2019s waist, telling the amusing story of a time she had been accused of being a witch. She smiled hopefully at Natalie, who was still tense and unhappy. Natalie smiled wanly back, linking arms with her behind Karen and shifting all three of them closer together.<br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> December 8th, 2010<br /> <br /> I am in danger. <br /> <br /> Karen\u2019s parents came to protest outside the house, with about 15 people from our church, praying loudly. Tavia menaced them into going across the street to Malard\u2019s house, and he ended up firing on them. The cops were called, and when we returned from irritating a little god we wound up dealing with Gwen\u2019s old friend Officer Norris. That was awkward. He is not quite sure about us. About queer people in general. He seems to be doing his job, though.<br /> <br /> Norris told me he was worried about me. These people think I am an evil manipulator who has tricked Karen into turning her back on God. Even if true, which is not, She made the choice. She was, however, quite gay and quite Pagan before we ever met. But it doesn\u2019t matter now. These people might hurt me. They haven\u2019t\u2026yet\u2026tried, but when an Officer is worried, I suppose I should pay attention. It is so hard, as a queer woman, as a drug addict, as an ex-call girl, to not see him as my enemy. He sees how I look at him. Karen sees a hero. I see someone who has hurt me, confined me, hit me. Not Norris himself, but cops. <br /> <br /> I listened to Norris\u2019s advice, and Karen and I talked, and made some decisions. She is pretty much done with school short exams, and I am going to take her to the exams with at least one other person. We won\u2019t go out by ourselves. This goes double for me; I doubt they want to hurt her. I doubt they would have any qualms about hurting me.<br /> <br /> The self-righteous make my blood boil. Not simply Christians, I have many Christian friends. But these people who think by virtue of belonging to this sect and following their god\u2019s rules they are my betters. I hate them because I was one, once. I suffered under their rules, they are not for me. I have become a better person than I was then, looking imperiously down my nose. But I leave them to their master, it is not my place to try to remove them from YHVH\u2019s influence any more than they have any right to try to convert me. But when they mess with me and mine, that is when shit gets real.<br /> <br /> In less than two weeks I go away for a matter of months. Hopefully they will grow bored. I just need to keep a low profile until then. If they want to menace me on return then, well\u2026.<br /> <br /> I will show them a witch. And they will find me hard to tie to the pyre. They will, for years, regret menacing me. I\u2019ll teach them fear.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ll show them power.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CLVIII</i><br /> <br /> Let\u2019s not channel too much Margaret Hamilton there Natalie.<br /> <br /> Okay the Mother/Matron is a Geist, and a powerful one. I had her set at a Rank of PC Psyche +1, so 7 at that writing. Serious power. Enough to reshape ghosts and the local landscape to a degree. This leaves a lot of questions for how the PCs should handle it. <br /> <br /> Similarly, the homophobia Natalie and Karen face is as dangerously real a problem as the Mother\u2019s problem is fantastical. I am too grumpy and sore to wax rhapsodic, so just pretend I did with notes most LGBTQIA youth don\u2019t have wealthy girlfriends with superpowers to protect them. They still all too often need our help.<br /> <br /> Okay, I am going to find somewhere and curl up and sleep now. I was just too sick to run tonight, so in two weeks stat updates for some of the Krewe. A lot of crazy scheduling stuff is happening but somehow Geist avoids all of it, so happening hopefully without further interruption. <br /> <br /> Comments and Questions welcome after I sleep.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":