:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-10T16:43:44-07:00","id":929448,"title":"","content":"Until the werewolf gets you when you're not looking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-12T13:10:57-07:00","id":930488,"title":"","content":"With my luck? Probably.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T01:34:36-07:00","id":936457,"title":"","content":"Going in to rescue Rawl, the Krewe finds the situation is a bit more dangerous than it first appeared. Meanwhile the Underwater Story Weaving Club is finding information.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Heeding the spirit\u2019s warning that there were many werewolves wherever Rawl was, the krewe armed themselves to the teeth with silver weaponry. Even Sara accepted the offered shotgun with no protestation, though she did look wistfully at the silver plated ax. It didn\u2019t take too long to gear up, considering they\u2019d been prepping for Glenwood in general, and then they were out the door and on the road.<br /> <br /> The spirit led them to an old Masonic lodge. They drove by quickly, not wanting their silver to catch the Pure\u2019s interest and set up a few miles away to let Natalie Boneyard. The strawberry scented woman went limp and began muttering an accounting of the lodge\u2019s inhabitants.<br /> <br /> She described nine people, not including Rawl who was shut in a side room, who were all behaving strangely. They were moving oddly, as if addled, and speaking with affected voices, as if they were acting something out. Luckily, the room Rawl was in was isolated and adjacent to an outer wall.<br /> <br /> Sara volunteered to go in. Doc looked skeptically at her, but she pointed out that she could astrally project and so not have a scent. Also, she pointed out that while she wasn\u2019t as good at sneaking around as Alice or Jasmine, she did have Cold Wind Caul. He frowned when she suggested he hum a few bars, but the krewe agreed it was their best bet outside of a frontal assault.<br /> <br /> There were no problems with Sara getting to Rawl\u2019s room. Once she\u2019d managed to get his attention, his eyes widened.<br /> <br /> \u201cHoly shit you guys are alive?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled apologetically, but he waved it aside. He explained that they hadn\u2019t come to the big fight with Bright Shadow because they got trapped in another dimension. While they were there, the other werewolves were recruited by a being they presumed was an Incarna, who called herself the Handmaiden of the Briar Rose. She\u2019d sent them back a little less than a month ago, to make Glenwood into something more appealing to her.<br /> <br /> He described the Handmaiden as a tall woman with no eyes, wearing a long dress and covered in flowering vines. When she spoke, her voice came from the flowers and her mouth never moved. The Predator King shuddered as he described her.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf that\u2019s the Handmaiden, I\u2019m pretty sure I don\u2019t wanna meet Briar Rose.\u201d<br /> <br /> When Sara said they were here to rescue him, he shook his head. He didn\u2019t want to give away the game, or make his pack think he\u2019d betrayed them. Totem rules kept them from killing him unless he had. He smirked as he explained his stated reason for not serving the Handmaiden was the no eyes thing, childhood trauma and all that.<br /> <br /> Sara frowned, but nodded understandingly, placing a phantom hand on Rawl\u2019s arm. They worked out a signal - an owl call - and Sara promised to do what she could about getting him a phone is there was going to be a significant delay. He smirked over at her as she was leaving.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad I\u2019m pretty enough to be rescued. Thank you, mom, for sleeping with a douchebag.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara reported back and the krewe worked out a plan. Rawl had said his pack was afraid of the other Pure pack finding out. So the krewe were going to make sure they did. But since the Ivory Claws would likely kill them on sight and they wanted the Changelings\u2019 help anyway, they decided to contact Grin first and see if he\u2019d liaise.<br /> <br /> However, they still needed the location of the other pack, which Sara hadn\u2019t thought to get. So she projected again and looked at Rawl somewhat sheepishly. He looked her over.<br /> <br /> \u201cI damn well better not be hallucinating at this point.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not a hallucination. Though... that is what a hallucination would say...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned wickedly at him and told him what she needed. He gave her the address and noted that the lodge itself was one of the Ivory Claws\u2019 safehouses, one that the Predator Kings used sometimes when it got too cold to rough it in the park. Sara explained the plan and promised the krewe\u2019d be there to get him out, pointing out it would probably be Doc, since he could bring people into the Shadow with him. Rawl looked mock concerned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have to put out, right, for this rescue? My dick sucking skills are way out of practice.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOnly if you want to. I\u2019m sure there\u2019ll be other ways to show your appreciation.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned at him before hopping back into her back to see Doc dialing the phone. Gretchen picked up but passed it on to Grin with only some off color comments.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you know Glenwood, that place we told you never to go? Gonna need you here ASAP. A pack of werewolves are working directly for a Gentry.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh. You\u2019re gonna want some C4 then. Lemme call my explosives expert.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc heard noises like a phone being dialed.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Doc? I\u2019m gonna need some C4.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc gave a sarcastic laugh and explained the basics of the Changelings\u2019 part of the plan. Grin listened seriously and promised to go to the Autumn King with it that night. He pointed out that while the answer would probably be yes, it probably wouldn\u2019t come until the next day. Doc agreed and asked about being enchanted. They worked out a time that was agreeable and Grin even promised to bring along a plastic raptor, at Doc\u2019s request.<br /> <br /> As he got off the phone, and started up the van, Doc turned to Natalie.<br /> <br /> \u201cI need a handkerchief and a blue ribbon.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> While Sara did not relish the idea of leaving with Rawl still locked up and in danger, she found herself relaxing along with Natalie as they got closer to home. She and Natalie moved to flank Karen, who was waiting on the porch, as soon as they arrived. They filled her in quickly.<br /> <br /> After some discussion of Rawl\u2019s fate after he got out, considering he\u2019d be without a pack, Natalie moved to check the private server and forums Timothy had set up for the underwater Storyweavers. The students had all checked in. Marie had reiterated that Allen, the guy with the show before Katie\u2019s, was useless. His first description was \u2018you know, a seven\u2019 and when Marie drew a couple of fairly different faces - one Korean, one Cambodian - his response was \u2018yeah, like that, Japanese\u2019. Karen made a face.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd think, my mom wanted me to date college boys.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie gave her a look.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere are men with a brain.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but Doc\u2019s taken.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s statement of agreement with Natalie\u2019s comment died with sputtering embarrassment. He blushed and changed the subject, asking after the other students. Clarissa had just checked in without an further notes. Timothy did as well, though he mentioned not being able to get access yet. Deanna had checked in commenting that Susan was standoffish and that she hadn\u2019t gotten anything more. Tracey followed that up with offering to check out Susan herself.<br /> <br /> Having confirmed their prot\u00e9g\u00e9s were safe, the group settled down to play some games. When someone commented on Tatum\u2019s absence, Karen took the opportunity to tease Natalie about quitting surfing after her first fall. When she pointed out Sara hadn\u2019t quit, Doc chuckled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know if I\u2019ve seen Sara quit anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... don\u2019t know whether I should be offended or not...\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc grinned at her, but when the UNO cards came out and Chandra suggested Strip UNO, he and Noriko backed out, wishing everyone a good night. Sara wound up winning soundly, much to her dismay, since Karen reminded her every round that she didn\u2019t get to take her clothes off if she won. Natalie kept most of her clothes on, though she made a big deal out of every hand she lost. Poor Catherine was in her underwear by the end of the night - luck was not on her side. Alexia and Chandra were though and did a pretty good job of making sure she forgot her embarrassment.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The krewe spent the next day in quiet pursuits until dinner, which was another meeting of the Underwater Storyweavers. Sara was sitting on the floor leaning against the piano bench as Natalie worked on a composition when Karen found them to remind them of the time.<br /> <br /> Thankfully she warned them in plenty of time for Natalie to primp and put on a lower cut top and for Sara to tousle her hair and tie up her shirt. They looked at each other and shrugged when Karen teasingly pointed out they had that meeting with Grin after dinner.<br /> <br /> As soon as the krewe, along with Karen and Catherine, got there Timothy pulled Catherine aside. Tracey tried to pull attention away from their serious discussion by complaining about how \u2018super suspicious\u2019 Susan was, since her response to being come onto was to slap Tracey rather than sleep with her. She raised an eyebrow at her brother when he walked back up, lip between his teeth. He grimaced at her cheery question.<br /> <br /> \u201cFeeling better Mr Gloomy?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m pretty sure Katie\u2019s dead.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara frowned in concern.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat makes you say that?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMagic.\u201d<br /> <br /> He shrugged at Sara, eyes downcast. He explained he\u2019d done some scrying and the results implied she didn\u2019t exist. Sara laid a hand on his as they sat down, presenting a couple of different possibilities, such as some kind of obfuscating magic or dimension travel. They worked out an experiment where Doc would enter the Shadow while Timothy scryed for him and see if the result it gave. It was the best they could do, since none of them had any way to hide from scrying.<br /> <br /> Over dinner, they all shared what they had learned. In addition to scrying, Timothy had gotten a chance to look over the station and not found anything, though he had managed to get his hands on recordings of Katie\u2019s show, including the one with the substitute. Clarissa admitted it was hard to bring herself to talk to the cops about a real investigation like this one. Deanna patted her hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019ll be easier with time.\u201d<br /> <br /> The club set to divvying out tasks after that. Deanna volunteered to listen to the show along with a Korean friend of hers who might recognize the voice. Sara suggested she upload the files to the private server so that everyone could have a chance, if they had time. Alexia looked nervously at them, insisting they monitor themselves carefully and listen in pairs, in case there was some sort of magic in the broadcast.<br /> <br /> Deanna also volunteered to track down any other students who might have been at the party that the substitute claimed to have met Katie at. It was organized on Facebook, so they had a starting place. Marie took charge after that, making sure Deanna didn\u2019t volunteer for everything. She recovered from her awkward babbling questions about whether Sarah, as a bean sidhe, could tell if Katie actually was dead by requesting that Tracey seduce Rebecca again and this time retrieve something of Katie\u2019s, for sympathetic magic purposes. She also recruited Sarah away from Natalie\u2019s side to be her buddy for radio show listening.<br /> <br /> They chatted amongst themselves for a while, putting a few details on the plan as they ate. As they broke off, Alexia smiled at each of them.<br /> <br /> \u201cStay frosty!\u201d<br /> <br /> On the way to the cars, Sarah pulled Natalie aside for an intense conversation. Sara and Karen watched, amused smiles on their faces. When Natalie came back, Karen ribbed her gently about how fixated the bean sidhe seemed. Sara didn\u2019t escape her teasing either.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think Tracey has a similar approach to life as you, Sara.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey are similarly skilled at that approach too.\u201c<br /> <br /> Natalie smirked at the pair of them.<br /> <br /> --------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Grin accepted a cookie from Alexia and looked around at the group.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe answer is probably yes, but the Autumn King is deciding who needs to know what. Is there anything else you can tell me about what\u2019s going on?\u201d<br /> <br /> The krewe filled him in on the details, especially about the rescue mission. He was suitably impressed by Rawl\u2019s looks when Natalie showed him a picture on her phone. Meanwhile, Doc worked on turning the white handkerchief and blue ribbon into a robe and sash for the plastic raptor Grin brought.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt will be werewolf on werewolf fighting which means collateral damage, so no getting between them.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s the Summer Court. That\u2019s why the King is debating telling them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Grin smiled wryly at Natalie who grinned back. The Changeling paused and looked thoughtful. He asked if Rawl would be willing to give an interview about the Handmaiden. Sara shrugged. <br /> <br /> \u201cI can\u2019t imagine why not. Just don\u2019t ask like you\u2019re his dad.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo worried. The Lost understand a dislike of authority.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut you have kings and queens...\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie smiled mischievously at him. He smirked back.<br /> <br /> \u201cI suggested chairman or vice commandant.\u201d<br /> <br /> Grin had come prepared to enchant the krewe, so after they\u2019d shared the plan, he did so. Sara\u2019s eyes widened and after a moment her face broke into a grin at the sight of his Tyrannosaurus head. After another couple of cookies, he took his leave, promising to get back to them as soon as he could.<br /> <br /> ---------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Alexia insisted on entry and exit interviews before and after Sara listened to the recordings of the radio show. She mostly focused on the tattooed woman\u2019s emotional state: how she was feeling, how she felt about the person substituting for Katie and finding Katie, and finally, any strong desires. Sara waggled her eyebrows at her until she specified <u>unusual </u>desires.<br /> <br /> The show started off with Li-Hyun, no last name given, introducing herself, saying that Katie couldn\u2019t be there, so she was doing it. Sara shot off a quick text to Karen, asking her to check if anyone with that first name had an email account at the school. As it turns out, no one did.<br /> <br /> Sara listened carefully to the whole show, noting the song Li-Hyun said was Katie\u2019s favorite - Dancing Heart by Kim Sori - in particular. That was the only other time she specifically mentioned Katie, saying she hoped Katie could hear it. Sara frowned when she got to the end and Li-Hyun didn\u2019t even mention Katie returning in the sign off, which was usual in cases like this.<br /> <br /> The woman\u2019s voice was very notable in and of itself. If it wasn\u2019t for the fact she maintained her perkiness for an hour or so, Sara would have guessed she was tweaking. She also sounded very young, high school, at most, if Sara was going just by the sound. Her accent was strong as well, strong enough that it seemed unlikely she\u2019d grown up in the US. Altogether it was enough that she would either be immediately recognizable or she was intentionally disguising her voice.<br /> <br /> When the file came to an end it immediately looped and began playing another of Katie\u2019s shows. Sara was about to stop it when she realized that the first song Katie played was the first song Li-Hyun had. She clicked around to a few other files and found that Katie always started with that song. She skimmed through a couple of the more recent shows, noticing that Li-Hyun mentioned the same guys Katie had, and used the same adjectives without repeating her comments word for word.<br /> <br /> She paused the file after Katie laughed. She frowned, wishing she\u2019d listened to it before Grin had visited. The laugh in particular sounded very much like Li-Hyun and Sara really wanted to run the theory that one of Li-Hyun and Katie might be a Changeling and the other a Fetch by someone who might know better than her.<br /> <br /> Alexia rushed in when she saw Sara frowning, but the tattooed woman managed to convince her that everything was alright. She was still around when the forum dinged with a new post notification. Marie had started a thread talking about the recordings. Apparently Sarah had found the voice creepy, creepy enough she wasn\u2019t able to listen to it all the way through. Deanna chimed in, saying she and Clarissa thought she was maybe trying to disguise her voice. She also added that her friend didn\u2019t know anyone named Li-Hyun except a seventy year old woman. Once everyone checked in, Sara suggested listening to Katie\u2019s shows to compare and contrast.<br /> <br /> The fact that Sarah and only Sarah found it creepy enough she couldn\u2019t finish bothered Sara and she bit her lip as she thought. After a moment she went looking for Catherine and asked her to listen to it as well, being the experienced supernatural that was closest in power type to a bean sidhe. Well, other than perhaps a Sin-Eater, but that clearly wasn\u2019t the aspect that was triggering Sarah.<br /> <br /> Catherine agreed without hesitation and as she listened she got a funny look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s... it\u2019s like when you hear someone you know is lying. I mean, I don\u2019t think she\u2019s lying,it\u2019s just the same kind of disquiet. It\u2019s... well, it\u2019s like blue and green - they\u2019re not the same, but they\u2019re both not red, you know?\u201d<br /> <br /> Catherine shrugged, smiling hopefully at Alexia who smiled back.<br /> <br /> \u201cOr it may be my autism reacting to the false voice.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded and thanked the psychic. Catherine shifted closer to Alexia and offered to look through Allen\u2019s memories of Li-Hyun.<br /> <br /> \u201cTimothy can do it too, but he\u2019s kinda leery to, which is good. I know we wanna let the club do most of the work but maybe it\u2019d let us give them some hints?\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia grinned broadly and hugged her girlfriend. Sara chuckled and wished the pair of them a good night before going to find her own girls.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 5th, 2011<br /> <br /> What happens when you combine two awful things? It is not a joke I just want to be prepared.<br /> <br /> So a group of Pure have been corrupted by one of the Gentry, The Handmaiden to the Briar Rose. Rawl\u2019s pack of Predator Kings specifically. He is being held as his distinctly anti-authoritarian nature means he never swore fealty, and they do not want the other pack to know. They were acting rather eccentric. Doc contacted Grin, and he will be contacting the \u201cAutumn King.\u201d With little else to do, we returned. Karen was waiting for us impatiently. As she always does when we go to Glenwood.<br /> <br /> Karen, Sara and I wound up playing \u201cStrip Uno\u201d with Alexia, Chandra and Catherine. Catherine did poorly, and I admit perhaps salivating a bit when she fully undressed. Karen did not fare great but kept her more personal dignity, and Sara ironically did not lose anything. Chandra made sure I knew she regretted that I did not lose more often. I just told her she would have to work a little harder if she wanted to see more of me.<br /> <br /> And then I sated the appetite I had worked up with my lovelies in my room. I presume the other triad did as well. I wonder if they have decided to admit Catherine is \u201cofficial\u201d yet. I sadly know no non-awkward way to ask.<br /> <br /> <br /> April 6th, 2011<br /> <br /> Quiet day, busy night.<br /> <br /> Most of the day was relaxing. Posted a Vlog, shined some of Karen\u2019s boots. Then I worked on some music for my album for a few hours.<br /> <br /> Meeting with the kids went well. Tracy is incorrigible. Totally struck out with Katie\u2019s friend Susan though. Timothy has been playing with magic. We gave out new assignments, which largely consisted of pairs listening to the show\u2026Deanna and Clarissa (and an unnamed Korean friend of Deanna) and Marie and Sarah. Timothy wound up working on a spell, his sister was going to seduce Rebecca Stein again for access to Katie\u2019s room to get sympathetic links. Deanna and Tracy were also going to track down the party.<br /> <br /> Sarah confronted me outside. She wanted to spend more time with me. Specifically that night making love. I had talked to her last time and when we got together about how I worked, and her being important to me, but my relationships being what they are. She is very immature compared to Tatum, Sara or Karen\u2026not ready to deal with my life, Banshee or no. I so did not expect this. I figured if anyone would get too attached it might be Deanna; truthfully, though, I am almost hurt at how she characterized bedding me as \u201clife-changing\u201d but seemed to lose all sexual interest in me after. That never happens, except straight girls, and if Deanna is totally straight, I will eat my El Dorado. <br /> <br /> We got back and saw Grin (and Gretchen, who more or less lives with him now. She came to visit Tavia.) Grin enchanted us (he is as terrifying as Spooky implied) and confirmed that, yes, Gentry corrupted Pure was bad. He spoke a lot of the Changeling politics in the area, but the short version is his Court wants to keep things quiet out of concern how the other Courts will react. Made sense when he said it, but I am not sure how much was spin; Grin is after all somewhat contemptuous of authority figures. Not on the level Rawl is, but still.<br /> <br /> I did some more playing and composing to round out the night. Sara reported overall the shows (by \u201cLi-Hyun\u201d who was not a student.) seemed normal, but she sounded young, and had a thicker accent than a lot of the Korean girls at the school. She also parroted a lot of the comments Katie made, such as comments about boys and bands. Same words too. Sara speculated that Katie was a fetch and \u201cLi-Hyun\u201d the actual Changeling replacing her. But there was more oddity. Sarah reported being utterly creeped out by it, to the point of being unable to listen, and Catherine found it off-putting, but not as seriously. She admitted it could be her social issues, and the fact our \u201cLi-Hyun\u201d could be faking the voice and accent, as it sounds distinct. <br /> <br /> Eventually we settled in, no stip games this time. My goodness, we should at least do strip poker. Strip Canasta? Maybe they would like Canasta.<br /> <br /> Regardless, this little Goth needs her beauty sleep. Night!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXI</i><br /> <br /> Well, that is a problem. Gentry corrupted Pure are a bad deal. As if Glenwood didn\u2019t have enough troubles.<br /> <br /> Hope the Story Weavers story is interesting. The group seems to be getting a kick out of it.<br /> <br /> Not much to add, but as always your comments and questions are welcome. If something seems unclear let me know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T15:51:16-07:00","id":936755,"title":"","content":"I like the mix of Pure and Gentry. Well done. Curious to see where that goes.<br /> <br /> Two words for you: Strip Cribbage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T14:20:30-07:00","id":945659,"title":"","content":"Thanks Omenseer. Heh.<br /> <br /> The investigation into the missing girl takes a dark turn. The rescue mission for Rawl is engaged. <br /> <i><br /> Session CLXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sara came down to the upbeat sounds of Natalie singing Kiss the Boys Goodbye. She joined her wives in the music room to listen, sitting on the floor and leaning back against the piano bench. When Natalie finished, Karen teased her about the song\u2019s relevance to their upcoming wedding. Natalie looked to Sara for help and she hopped to her feet, suggesting Alexia\u2019s banana pancakes as a distraction.<br /> <br /> After breakfast, Natalie returned to the music room to work on the cover songs she was preparing for her album: Black Parade for her daughter, Stepping Out for her mother, Paranoid for Karen and Lovesong for Sara. She stayed there until lunch.<br /> <br /> As they finished up lunch, Natalie\u2019s phone buzzed. Before she even got to check it, it buzzed again and again. The first message was from Deanna.<br /> <br /> \u2018Clarissa is grounded because of me and it\u2019s not my fault.\u2019<br /> <br /> Natalie scanned the rest and left the room to give Deanna a call. She came back with a bemused expression and gathered the krewe to explain, trying to put it in order despite having heard it middle to first to end. Since Deanna had been really stressed, she had confided in her parents some. She didn\u2019t out any of the supernatural to them, but she did come out as pan herself.<br /> <br /> They were, to put it mildly, pleased as punch. Her dad was less pleased at her dalliances with Natalie, since he\u2019d apparently seen her swear allegiance to Satan on TV. Natalie shook her head in confusion over that. Her mom was OK with Natalie\u2019s paganism since \u2018it was a hippie thing\u2019. The strawberry scented woman grimaced.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u201cThankfully she doesn\u2019t care what her parents think. She wants to - ahem - \u2018nail me on the sly\u2019. That household is fraught with optimism. Which leads to the actually bad part...\u201d<br /> <br /> When Deanna mentioned that she and Clarissa weren\u2019t involved, Deanna\u2019s parents leapt to the conclusion that Clarissa was also queer. They called Clarissa\u2019s mother, despite Deanna\u2019s protestations, who grounded Clarissa. Not for being queer, but because she hadn\u2019t told her parents that she was, in order for them to vet her suitors. So Clarissa was upset at Deanna and Deanna was heartbroken. <br /> <br /> Natalie listened worriedly while Sara and Alexia talked over what might calm Clarissa\u2019s mother down. Karen smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could come up with a \u2018she\u2019s not gay\u2019 musical number.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt might work, since she\u2019s a girl. I\u2019m not sure anyone would be convinced their son wasn\u2019t gay with a musical number.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBe realistic now.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen grinned at Sara. Natalie shook her head and put a hand on Sara\u2019s shoulder, suggesting they wait until she went to go talk to Deanna and see if she couldn\u2019t get more of the story.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Alexia gave Grin a call, to check on the krewe\u2019s theory that Katie was Li-Hyun\u2019s fetch. He wasn\u2019t aware of any newly arrived Changelings, though he did say there was a group of Changelings, called the Blackbirds, that might know more. He pointed out that it occasionally took some time for a new arrival to trust others like them, but he promised to do his best.<br /> <br /> He also mentioned, when Alexia described what was going on, that a monster had been sighted near the radio station. When she pressed for details, he shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s as specific a description as I got: \u2018monster\u2019.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia went looking for Sara after they said their goodbyes. Sara looked thoughtful and suggested calling the twins, since of the Underwater Story Weavers Club, they were the most likely to be able to object read or glance into the past. Alexia elected to let Sara make the call.<br /> <br /> Tracy answered with a quavery voice. Sara asked her what was wrong.<br /> <br /> \u201cI think I\u2019m starting to agree with my brother\u2019s assessment... I\u2019ve seen Li-Hyun.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara blinked. Tracy spoke over the pause, saying she wanted to meet, with everyone. Sara agreed, and set to gathering people.<br /> <br /> On the way there, Natalie let everyone know how her visit had gone. Deanna was out of her funk, though it hadn\u2019t been helped by her mom\u2019s mystified reaction to Deanna\u2019s grandmother\u2019s unhappiness at being invited to a coming out party. As far as Clarissa went, they assured Natalie it was just her mother\u2019s temper getting the best of her. Deanna figured it would get sorted out when Clarissa\u2019s father got home.<br /> <br /> When they got to the usual meeting place of the Underwater Story Weaving Club, Tracy was tucked into a chair, her knees under her chin and her arms wrapped around her legs. Timothy was hovering protectively nearby. Sara rushed over and put an arm around her and Tracy leaned into the tattooed woman.<br /> <br /> Once everyone got there, Tracy started talking. Something had changed when she went to seduce Rebecca. The other girl resisted her advances, but since Tracy knew how to push her buttons, Katie\u2019s roommate wasn\u2019t in much of a state to stop her from poking around the missing girl\u2019s computer. KimSori, the name of Katie\u2019s favorite singer, got Tracy in.<br /> <br /> Katie's chats with another student, a Maria Chow, were what had Tracy agreeing with her brother. Li-Hyun had approached Katie and asked her to play certain songs in a certain order on her show. She said no that time and the second time she was asked as well. The third time came with threats.<br /> <br /> The last message Katie had sent was asking Maria to come keep her company. It was Friday night and her roommate had left. When Katie had gone to the bathroom, there had been the usual busy foot traffic. But when she went in, there was only one person there. She had her back to Katie, but looked rather a lot like Li-Hyun. Katie told Maria she had a strong feeling she was in danger, so she didn\u2019t want to go anywhere alone.<br /> <br /> When Tracy left the dorm, she felt a chill herself. As she shivered, her eyes were drawn to a Korean girl standing in a nearby parking lot. The girl was staring at the directly and after a few moment, stepped back into the shadows. Tracy had rushed home, holing up in her room with her gun close at hand until Timothy got home.<br /> <br /> Sara looked worriedly at Alexia and held Tracy close. Once they\u2019d had a moment to process, Sara suggested they leave that line of questioning alone for awhile and look into the monster that had been reported near the radio station. A couple of the students had heard about it as well, and they all agreed.<br /> <br /> When they got to the station, Grin was there. Sara, an arm still around Tracy\u2019s waist, asked him to speak privately. Once they stepped aside, Sara encouraged Tracy to describe her encounter. The Sin-Eater followed it up by asking Grin if anyone in his Court could do something like that.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can make an area more conducive to fear. Would you say she was your greatest fear, in that moment?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGreatest? Not... not really.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably not us, then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Grin looked apologetically at Sara, As they walked back to the others, he told her he kenned the area and found nothing.<br /> <br /> Sara asked the twins if they could do anything that might look into the past. Timothy shook his head.<br /> <br /> \u201cMy stuff is mostly about minds and a little about dimensions.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd mine is mostly about dimensions and a little about minds.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tracy smiled wanly up at Sara who squeezed her waist. The tattooed woman kissed the spooked woman on the forehead before letting her go to begin her Ceremony. Other than a plethora of late night, behind the bushes liaisons, Sara got two flashes: one of a large, fuzzy winged creature with large yellow eyes and another of Katie walking towards the building at night. After a brief glance at where the creature had been, Sara focused on the image of Katie.<br /> <br /> She was rounding the corner, just passing the bushes when another Korean girl stepped out from behind them. Katie was turning towards her when a long knife blade sprouted from one of the other woman\u2019s fingers and slashed across Katie\u2019s throat in one smooth movement. The woman who Sara presumed was Li-Hyun looked on dispassionately as Katie fell, then walked past her towards the door.<br /> <br /> Sara shuddered and winced away. Natalie was there in a heartbeat with an arm around her shoulder. Sara quietly told her what happened and the strawberry scented woman held her closer. Pulling herself together, Sara took a deep breath and looked to the others. Alexia was looking oddly at a patch of dirt behind the bushes, near where Sara had seen the winged monster stalking around. The tattooed girl bit her lip when she realized it was a shallow grave.<br /> <br /> She swallowed and leaned into Natalie, describing the monster she\u2019d seen. Doc\u2019s brow furrowed. He recognized it as a Mothman, a la Point Pleasant. No one else really knew what to make of it, so Alexia unlocked Industrial Oracle while Deanna called the cops.<br /> <br /> Alexia was able to get images of the Mothman, as well as figure out that it was the first time the Mothman had been there. Asking about Li-Hyun, Alexia got two portraits - the detached emotionless killer, whose hand with a bladed finger turned into a wide shovel to dig the shallow grave and the bubbly radio host, who passed by skipping and whistling.<br /> <br /> When Alexia was done, Sara pulled her aside, watching the grieving students.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know this mystery is important to them but... they should leave it now. It\u2019s too dangerous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll try to impart that the mystery is solved.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia looked sadly at Marie, who was kneeling by the grave, muttering. When they rejoined the others, Alexia spoke seriously, congratulating them on solving the mystery. When she intimated that it was time for the students to back off, Deanna got really upset. Natalie placed a hand on her shoulder to comfort her, but Deanna shrugged her off. <br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re supposed to help! I want to help!\u201d<br /> <br /> Tensions rose, with Tracy even volunteering to be bait. Doc stepped forward.<br /> <br /> \u201cHit me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna stopped and frowned at Doc.<br /> <br /> \u201cHit me like I was going to stomp you to the ground if I didn\u2019t.\u201d<br /> <br /> She pulled out a pair of brass knuckles and put them on. She swing for Doc, who leaned to the side. He grabbed her arm as it passed and pulled her after it. She tumbled to the ground. <br /> <br /> Natalie helped her up and moved to comfort her again, pointing out she\u2019d had a long day and should take her time. Deanna didn\u2019t push her away this time. Sara\u2019s eyes brightened and she pointed at the pair of them.<br /> <br /> \u201cHow do you feel about hosting a radio show?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one is acting as bait...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara stared at Doc affrontedly.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course not! I\u2019m not suggesting Deanna act as bait, I\u2019m suggesting she act as our woman on the inside.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna perked up at that and Natalie gave Sara a brilliant smile from over the enthusiastic girl\u2019s shoulder. Sara explained Deanna would just need to make friends with the other DJs to try and get a heads up if anyone made specific requests like Li-Hyun did. And most importantly, to make any requested changes herself.<br /> <br /> The other students perked up a little as well at the idea that there was something to do. Marie looked thoughtful.<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought about having a radio show. But since it\u2019s a school station, and a Catholic school, everything hes to be something that would be approved of by the Catholic Church - you can\u2019t say anything about going down on your girlfriend and stuff.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI think that\u2019s most radio stations...\u201d<br /> <br /> Timothy raised an eyebrow at Marie. Sara chuckled, throwing in her two cents.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlso, I\u2019m pretty sure you can\u2019t talk about going down on your boyfriend either.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe bastards!\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara and Timothy shared a grin, giving Doc a little space to apologize to Deanna and compliment her on her weapon of choice. She accepted brightly, leaving him blinking when she pointed out she wasn\u2019t allowed to have a taser since the accident.<br /> <br /> Marie kept looking down at the shallow grave, her shoulders drooped. Sarah stood close, trying to cheer her up. The bean sidhe gently patted her friend on the back as she mourned the fact she hadn\u2019t been able to save Katie. Sarah pointed out that there wasn\u2019t anything Marie could have done differently. A sad look on her face, Alexia watched sympathetically.<br /> <br /> \u201cThere will be some you can save - don\u2019t get discouraged.\u201d<br /> <br /> Marie nodded her acknowledgment. <br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s giving up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd we don\u2019t do that!\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna nodded as well, resolutely.<br /> <br /> Grin came back over from where he\u2019d been talking with the police, to let them know everything was all squared away. He also looked significantly at the krewe when he let them know he\u2019d received a message he\u2019d be checking once he\u2019d finished his report to the police. Alexia smiled her thanks to him and turned to the club.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve found - and you might laugh at me - that food helps most anything.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The krewe and club met up at an Irish restaurant, where Alexia recommended the stew for everyone. Conversation was subdued at first until Marie sighed.<br /> <br /> \u201cLook, Katie wouldn\u2019t want us brooding. And if she would, she\u2019s a bitch.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara hid a smile, but that did strike up more liveliness in the group. Doc got an agreement from everyone to give him a few drops of blood. As a hedge witch, Marie balked a little, making sure to emphasize to the others that she was only doing so because it was Doc asking, and they only should if they explicitly trusted the asker.<br /> <br /> Timothy spoke across Tracy to Sara, worried about his sister\u2019s safety. He said he\u2019d be escorting her to class, all but the one that conflicted with his. Marie volunteered to help with that one. A worried smile on her face, Sara ran a hand down Tracy\u2019s arm to rest it on her hand, asking if she\u2019d be OK with staying at the Bluffs. The spooked woman nodded as she glanced out the window, looking for threats.<br /> <br /> \u201cAlexia - what\u2019s the name of your bakery again?\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna looked frustrated as she asked, looking down at her phone. Alexia told her and she sighed as she began typing. When she glanced up and caught everyone\u2019s curious looks, she explained that her mom was planning a coming out party and wanted a cake. When her mom sent her a picture of a lesbian wedding cake, she groaned and put her head on the table.<br /> <br /> \u201cI would be happy to make a cake that <u>you</u> would like. Would you rather me deal with you or with your mom?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI would rather not be outed to my entire extended family... my mom can be a bit effervescent at times.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie rubbed Deanna\u2019s back and tried to cheer her up through the rest of dinner. When they left, the krewe made a detour to let Tracy get a few things from her house. At the Bluffs, Tavia greeted them. Sara let her know Tracy would be staying for a bit and Natalie reminded her that Coffee was coming the next day.<br /> <br /> \u201cDo I need to set up a guest room for Coffee or will she be staying with you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA guest room, I think, just in case?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh please.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tavia rolled her eyes playfully at Sara, then sent to set up the rooms. Sara went with her to help while Alexia took Tracy on a tour of the house, focusing on where to find the emergency ice cream and cookies, since she\u2019d already got warnings about the dangers. Tracy gave the Sin-Eater a weak smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou guys are my favorite people.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Deanna sighed as she pushed open the door to her house. She slung her backpack into the corner, by the shoe rack, then rolled her eyes when her mom reacted to the noise. She headed back through the house to her room, stopping when her mom poked her head out of the kitchen.<br /> <br /> \u201cHoney? Do you want pink, blue or purple streamers? Oooh, or all three?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI found a shallow grave with a college student in it today.\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna stomped off upstairs, leaving her mom holding the three sample streamers she\u2019d gotten from Party City. The woman watched her go, a shocked look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know how to throw a party for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Grin called a little after the krewe got settled in.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo, the Wytch King - that\u2019s what we call the Autumn Monarch. It\u2019s with a y, cause he\u2019s that goth.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cJust the Wytch, not the Kyng, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s not that goth.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled as Grin continued, explaining the plan: the Wytch King was going to gather a Wild Hunt to hold the Hedge near the lodge. The \u2018fuzzies\u2019 were going to handle each other, with the Wild Hunt preventing the Hedge-corrupted ones from retreating that way, or possibly attacking them from behind their lines if it started going poorly for the Ivory Claws.<br /> <br /> Once he established that the krewe had the rescue in hand and they set the attack for midnight, he hung up to contact the others. Sara went to find Tracy and explain why they\u2019d be gone, promising she\u2019d be safe at the house. Karen plopped down on the arm of the chair Tracy was sitting in and pointed out she\u2019d be staying behind as well. When Natalie smirked, Karen protested.<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, I\u2019ve seen horror movies. I know that when I have sex with Tracy, that\u2019s when the monster comes out. Besides, I\u2019ll be thinking about you two in Glenwood and do a half-assed job.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf you\u2019re thinking about Glenwood, she\u2019s doing a half-assed job.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The krewe spent the next few hours preparing. Doc booked a hotel room for Rawl in the neutral zone. Natalie led a ritual to bring them together, resting most of the power generated in Doc and Sara since they were the two going in. She reserved some in case of emergency.<br /> <br /> As they were getting ready to go, they were interrupted by Tracy\u2019s raised voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s only three years younger than me?\u201d<br /> <br /> They found Tracy and Karen in the TV room. Natalie glared at her wife, shifting uncomfortably as they continued talking about Natalie Lousler.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one is allowed to fuck my daughter who fucked me first.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOne: I didn\u2019t agree to that before. And two: you fucked me.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFine. But it\u2019s a rule from now on.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that because she\u2019s your kid, or because she\u2019s a potential romantic rival?\u201d<br /> <br /> With that, Doc, who\u2019d been about to step in, threw up his hands and told them he\u2019d be at the van. Natalie spluttered a bit before turning on her heel and following.<br /> <br /> Tracy looked significantly at Sara\u2019s phone. The tattooed girl brought up a picture, grinning at the appreciative look on Tracy\u2019s face. She didn\u2019t linger long though, giving the pair staying behind a wink as she left to join the others at the van.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> As the krewe waited in the parking lot a few miles from the lodge, they heard the engines of a large group of motorcycles. Sara was already projecting and Natalie had her Boneyard up, so Doc stepped into Twilight. He and Sara set off towards the lodge while Alexia and Noriko guarded Natalie.<br /> <br /> Sounds of fighting weren\u2019t far off when they got to Rawl\u2019s room. Doc didn\u2019t leave much time for conversation, simply popping into the material world, setting the dinosaur figure complete with robe on the bedside table, grabbing Rawl and shifting the two of them back into Twilight.<br /> <br /> Rawl took a deep breath, shifting back out of his fox-like wolf form as Doc pulled him back to reality at the van. Sara patted the seat next to her as Doc crawled to the front and started the van. He tossed back a hotel key card before he took off for New Haven.<br /> <br /> The werewolf took the seat Sara suggested and looked at the keycard with a confused look on his face for a moment, then sighed, acknowledging that he hadn\u2019t really thought about where he\u2019d be staying. He smiled wryly at the krewe. <br /> <br /> \u201cSo, did you guys have a good Christmas? I didn\u2019t have a good Christmas.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled sympathetically back and began giving him a backrub. Rawl sighed, more happily this time.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis is kinda like Christmas though.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Karen met them at the door after they\u2019d dropped Rawl off at the hotel. She stepped forward quickly, reassuring herself that both her wives were in one piece. Once she had, she grinned at them, letting them know Tracy had given consent to being taken care of before she began drinking.<br /> <br /> They found Tracy expounding about roofs to Catherine, who was bright red. She stopped when the triad came in, smiling tipsily at them. Natalie smiled back at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you telling stories about the widow walk?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve not done anything there. Yet. But it is on my bucket list.\u201d<br /> <br /> She carefully counted the triad.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo\u2019s that.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 8th, 2011<br /> <br /> So three major things with today. I will take them in roughly chronological order:<br /> <br /> Deanna James, in an emotional state with the stresses of the investigation, came out to her parents as Pan. They were supportive. Perhaps\u2026too supportive. Her mother, thinking Clarissa was queer as well, (due to a clarification they were not involved) told Clarissa\u2019s mother she was queer, which resulted in Clarissa being grounded, allegedly for not telling her mother then having girls overnight; remember Clarissa is straight. Also, Clarissa deciding she was not speaking to Deanna anymore. Deanna\u2019s parents, bless them, decided to plan a coming out party (without asking) which lead to her being outed to her extended family (as well as Clarissa\u2019s immediate family) and her grandmother getting angry with her all while she was in her room depressed because her lifelong friend is angry with her. Also, she was forbidden from dating me, which isn\u2019t happening anyway, because I apparently declared alliance to Satan on TV (It could have happened, I was on a lot of metal oriented stuff on MTV and the like, but I don\u2019t remember doing it.) Though paganism is okay because hippies do it. Yay?<br /> <br /> I went to visit, and got her feeling a bit better. Her parents let me go up to her room then turned the music way up loud so they could not hear anything going on, as they \u201cwanted to support her sexuality\u201d which is frankly just bizarre. I mean a good thought, but strange way of carrying it out. I think Deanna comes by her behavior honestly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, she has an adorable room, and I am going to fuck her in it someday.<br /> <br /> Number two, on the short term, the Katie Hong case is finished, or at least the Underwater Story Weaving part is. Katie is sadly deceased. I\u2019d have preferred they discovered this in a less traumatic way.<br /> <br /> So Tracy Lowe went back to talk to Katie\u2019s roommate, and found Rebecca had changed her opinion on her, now being super suspicious. Tracy still seduced her, because Tracy is super fucking good at that (also, at fucking, for the record). <br /> <br /> So\u2026I am a fucking slut. This is just an aside, now back on subject<br /> <br /> Anyway Tracy is smarter than a lot of people give her credit for, cracked Katie\u2019s (admittedly easy) password and got in\u2026and found that Li-Hyun had been, well, pressuring her to play specific songs in a specific order, and had some odd mind whammy when Katie tried to use the bathroom alone. She was scared. Perhaps, unfortunately, not scared enough. Then when Tracy stepped out of Katie\u2019s dorm she saw Li-Hyun watching her with a sinister, oppressive, glare, from a distance. Tracy wisely wanted us to meet right away.<br /> <br /> We met and discussed these revelations, then went to the station, investigating Grin\u2019s report of a monster. There Sara and Alexia found Katie\u2019s shallow grave in the bushes while using their own powers of psychometry. Also, we got a vision of Li-Hyun, who can make a metal claw come from her finger and slit a throat, which she did to slay Katie silently on her way to work. <br /> <br /> We were attracted to the site by a Mothman, apparently. I have no idea, beyond the 60s thing, but Doc knew what it was. This case got a whole new level of weird. My skills lend themselves more to folklore and mythology than Fortean Phenomena, so I am unsure of all the implications.<br /> <br /> And dangerous. With Li-Hyun apparently a Terminator, and one who has menaced Tracy, we told them to back off. We wound up putting Tracy up at the house. This has had unexpected and expected effects. For one thing, she found out about Natalie and started skeeving on her. Karen unhelpfully pointed out Natalie being 17 is only three years younger than Tracy, while I am an ancient ten years older. Also, again, that we (Karen and I) hooked up on her (Karen\u2019s) 17th Birthday. <br /> <br /> No one wants to hear their daughter described as \u201chot.\u201d Okay maybe not no one, but few good parents. Which does not include me I presume. Karen also unhelpfully pointed out Natalie was a potential romantic rival for me. That\u2026hit perhaps a bit close to home. What was I thinking birthing someone cuter than me and only thirteen years my junior? Not planning ahead at 13, clearly.<br /> <br /> And she graduates from High School soon. My god. Mom has approved her going to Albertus Magnus, being a good Catholic School. She will be there too soon.<br /> <br /> I am off subject. After dispensing with our business in Glenwood, my wives and I dragged Tracy off to her room, where she checked several things off her bucket list. It was fun. I had only been with Tracy once, though we made out a few times. Having the girls there was a lot of fun, and the gigglebox clearly enjoyed herself too.<br /> <br /> Such. A. Slut.<br /> <br /> So one more entry before I go back to talking about my whoredom, we freed Rawl and maybe took down the Faerie tainted Pure? The fight was pretty close. Sara and Doc got Rawl out, while the other pack attacked and the Autumn Court lay in wait in the Hedge. Hope to hear how that went when I call Grin on Friday. He better answer anyway. Rawl is in town now. We put him in a hotel a few days.<br /> <br /> A couple personal projects, in addition to fucking Tracy and making out with Deanna, one is the Wedding! It won\u2019t be too long I will be marrying Karen and Sara formally. Also, work is going well on my first album; I had my family pick songs for themselves, Mom picked <i>Steppin\u2019 Out</i> by Joe Jackson, Natalie picked <i>Welcome to the Black Parade</i> by MCR, Karen picked <i>Paranoid</i> by Sabbath, and Sara picked <i>Lovesong</i> by The Cure. Will make a good mix, even if Tavia is clearly not an MCR fan. Tracy seemed\u2026impressed I could write a scale for music (Black Parade specifically, which was not a very difficult one) and made it clear I was getting into her pants later before we even left for Glenwood.<br /> <br /> I won\u2019t lie to you, skill at music does a lot of good for scoring chicks. And dudes, if I am being honest.<br /> <br /> Such. A. Slut.<br /> <br /> I also sang <i>Kiss the Boys Goodbye</i> some early in the day. That song I hated as a teen, and I was SO glad the Andrews Sisters didn\u2019t do it. Now\u2026I find it cute. <br /> <br /> It\u2019s so different, not feeling broken inside. Guilt over my promiscuity aside of course. I\u2019ve almost gotten used to it. Close to a year ago the Krewe formed. Close to a year ago\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, feeling pretty good, but there is a murdering machine of some form, or something that can grow claws, which needs killing. In the meantime, the giggling in bed has reached critical mass, which means everyone is awake. And Coffee is coming tonight.<br /> <br /> Will be an interesting few days, to be sure\u2026<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXIII</i><br /> <br /> And so the dreaded God-Machine finally rears It\u2019s head. This is not a sign of a new campaign direction, just the current story. Li-Hyun is looking like an Angel, with a Mothman abouts.<br /> <br /> The PCs had a peripheral role in the battle at Glenwood. More will come out about that as time goes on. They really wanted to rescue Rawl. Which is cool that he is popular.<br /> Mostly just RP beyond that, but comments and questions are welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T19:10:48-07:00","id":945818,"title":"","content":"Since young Natalie is going to a Catholic College older Natalie could say that there are some parts of Leviticus she adheres to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:38:01-07:00","id":945891,"title":"","content":"She could, yes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-07T20:40:19-07:00","id":945896,"title":"","content":"I guess that was more amusing in my head... As many things often turn out to be. Although the Wytch king bit made me chuckle and I had to share it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-21T15:48:39-07:00","id":955255,"title":"","content":"Coffee arrives, plans are made. Group was kinda distractible, so fun session but not much story advanced.<br /> <br /> Not covering anything at Murder Ballads, that will be in next journals as it was in process.<br /> <i><br /> Session CLXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Tracey slipped out of bed early the next day, giving a barely roused Sara a kiss on the forehead as she left to meet her brother outside and get to her morning class. The rest of the girls stayed in bed a few more hours, tangled in each other\u2019s arms.<br /> <br /> When they eventually made their way downstairs, they found the others were late to rise as well, so the krewe gathered for an early lunch. Natalie updated the group on the backlogs of texts Deanna had left her. The teenager had already gotten herself a radio show. In fact, they\u2019d given her Katie\u2019s time slot.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, morale\u2019s not good at the station - the students are afraid of getting killed themselves. Even Deanna\u2019s a little nervous.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI can stay with her during her show. If one of us does, which sounds like a good idea, it shouldn\u2019t be you. I\u2019m sure she\u2019d get fired if she had sex on air.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie looked at Doc with mock outrage. He rolled his eyes and smiled at her. Sara grinned at them for a moment before a more serious look crossed her face. She suggested that Grin ask to be kept in the loop about any requests for programming changes, since that element was out about about making people nervous.<br /> <br /> The rest of lunch was spent planning for Coffee\u2019s arrival. The krewe started with going over interesting sites they could take her to but quickly realized it might be much for her first day in from Chicago. So they settled on settling in and hitting up Murder Ballads for the day\u2019s activities. Then on Saturday, they\u2019d take the Sin-Eater by the Patch, during the day, then the fairgrounds once night had fallen and the friendly carousel operator showed up.<br /> <br /> That discussion got Doc asking about Coffee. Natalie explained that she was traveling around, looking to experience different kinds of krewes. So far she\u2019d stayed with a krewe that held Black Masses in Catholic churches and carried out ritual killings, a krewe who spent much of their time having drug-fueled orgies, and a mobster-esque krewe that protected Chicago from some of its biggest, baddest ghosts. Sara smiled mischievously.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo we\u2019re gonna be like a mix of those first two, right?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI was thinking the third.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave Doc a confused look, then shrugged. Since lunch was wrapping up, Doc brought up that he still needed to be buried. Natalie smiled happily.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe can bury you out back, right quick!\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara hid a smile at the hint of North Carolina that had crept into her wife\u2019s voice. Natalie ignored her, pointing out to Doc that he was too tall for her coffin. Karen smirked at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re a goth and a Sin-Eater, but it\u2019s still weird you have your own coffin.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m thinking ahead. I don\u2019t want to be in a strange place for eternity.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie shrugged and worked out the details with Doc before sending Clyde out to begin digging the grave. Before they followed him out, Chandra, Tavia and Noriko came out from the kitchen, giggling and smiling. Doc eyed them.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat have you doing?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing...\u201d<br /> <br /> Tavia smiled broadly at him. He looked suspiciously back.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou three are smiling, something is up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe is smart.\u201d<br /> <br /> Noriko took his arm, smiling up at him. Chandra moved over next to Alexia, putting a hand on hers. When Alexia started talking about the Underwater Story Weaving Club, Chandra looked excited.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe could reward them with an evening on the yacht. That also might impress that girl Natalie's having over.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie objected to the use of the phrase \u2018that girl Natalie\u2019s having over\u2019 with plenty of quotation marks. Eventually the conversation would back around to Alexia\u2019s question as to whether Chandra was OK with getting the club involved with investigating the penanggalan trap.<br /> <br /> While she did want to be able to feed on campus again - college students make good prey and Yale was out for multiple reasons, including other vampires, other Sin-Eaters and the fact that Catholics were tastier - she was hesitant about letting so many people know. Also, she pointed out that they\u2019d have to be careful to make sure the students didn\u2019t assume any penanggalan would be friendly. Sara nodded, pointing out that there was enough nuance to the situation to make it rough as a field test for the club. Natalie began to chuckle, recommending Deanna specifically not be told, since she would likely immediately begin a Protect the Penanggalan movement complete with Facebook group.<br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> Once Clyde had finished digging, Tavia laid out the large mesh fishing net she\u2019s retrieved at Sara\u2019s suggestion. Doc laid on it, crossing his arms after putting a penny over each eye. Natalie kept the time and after four minutes, the krewe heaved up the net.<br /> <br /> Doc blew dirt off his face and patted Natalie\u2019s hand on his shoulder. He accepted her hand up and brushed himself off a little more before going inside to grab a shower.<br /> <br /> In between reassuring Deanna that she\u2019d be perfectly safe with Doc at the radio station, Natalie worked out who was going with her to pick up Coffee. Alexia bowed out, saying she had to bake a coffee cake. Sara volunteered quickly, as did Karen who smirked at the pair.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do wanna meet the girl you\u2019ll be chasing for the next few weeks.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie put her hands on her hips.<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople chase me, honey.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc came in ruffling his wet hair and smirking at Natalie\u2019s upraised eyebrow. He offered to drive, so that Natalie wouldn\u2019t be occupied, a twinkle in his eye.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m not planning on anything happening in the car...\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc looked over at Sara, one eyebrow raised.<br /> <br /> \u201cSara is.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSlander! I don\u2019t plan these things, they just happen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara swatted him playfully on the arm. He looked unconvinced.<br /> ------------------------------------------------------<br /> In the end it was those four waiting for Coffee at the airport at 4:30. The only dead woman walking out of the terminal was a perky woman slightly shorter than Natalie with dark clothes and blue-black hair. She waved at the group and smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou guys better be the Middle Shadows, or I\u2019m gonna be in a fight.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie introduced everyone and Doc offered to carry her large duffel bag. Once they got to the van they chatted more freely. She mentioned she was one of the Forgotten, with the Industrial, Passion and Stillness Keys, and the Marionette and Shroud Manifestations, speaking quickly with both her hands and her high pitched voice. Doc asked what she did for a cover for her Sin-Eating travels. She shrugged, pointing out she\u2019d frequently hitchhiked and crashed with other established krewes, but also mentioned she was a trust fund case.<br /> <br /> At one point, after Coffee lost a word for the second time and gestured wildly until she found it again, Natalie smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cAre you tweaking? Not that I mind, I just want to know what to supply you with...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh, just coffee.\u201d<br /> <br /> After they\u2019d chatted for a bit, the krewe brought up their immediate plans. Coffee smiled brightly at the mention of going clubbing.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m gonna go out on a limb and say it\u2019s a goth club?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat, my lovely, is a very sturdy limb.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled at the perky girl, then looked wide eyed as Natalie shook her head.<br /> -------------------------------------------<br /> They gave Coffee a tour of the house once she\u2019d dropped off her bag, starting with the emergency ice cream and cookies stash before moving on to the spooky stuff. Coffee approved of their foresight and their hot tub.<br /> <br /> Once that was handled, Doc stepped aside to call Deanna to invite her along after her show and warn her he\u2019d be gothed out while he was there. She accepted happily, then paused and apologized.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know I should be OK, but she was killed right outside the door...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s fine, it\u2019s what I do most every night - keep people safe.\u201d<br /> <br /> He reassured her a few more times before he went back to find the girls preparing as well. Coffee had changed into a mostly similar and of course still all black outfit. Natalie was looking over at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou really pack with the all black works everywhere idea, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSure! Weddings, funerals, clubbing, it works. As long as I don\u2019t get invited to any hoedowns.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNot here, for certain.\u201d <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Dairy<br /> </b><br /> April 9th, 2011<br /> <br /> We have had an okay day so far. One way or the other, I suspect I won\u2019t be in any shape to write when we get back, so some general notes in the meantime.<br /> <br /> Deanna is doing her first radio show tonight. Seems fast to me, but with Katie\u2019s discovery morale is bad. A lot of people may not even show up. Still, we want Deanna to be safe, and discussed an escort. While I am close to Deanna, she is one of the handiest women I have ever been out with. Both times we were out her hands kept going up the front of my top or down the back of my skirt. I swear she spent that entire party messing with my butt crack, and that is not conducive to two people in a small room alone. Given how grabby she is there is no way she would keep her hands out of my clothes, and if that happens, there is no way I would keep my hands out of her. So we sent Doc. This is safe because Doc is intimidating, honorable, and does not seem to understand when you are in a radio room you don\u2019t actually broadcast while you are being fucked. Trust me, I know.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m also not sure he ever got what I meant by \u201cHandsy.\u201d Never change, Doc.<br /> <br /> Other stuff with the youths, the police want to talk to Timothy because of his being around the place, but that is being dealt with this afternoon. Tracy slipped out early and should be back tonight, unless she picks up some trim.<br /> <br /> With Coffee incoming, we discussed options for showing her around. We talked about the amusement park we went to last year on Long Wharf, and the ghost in the carousel. Also the Patch that Gwen used to talk about. I think we might look into taking Coffee both places. If the Patch seems safe, we will take the kids there as well. We also talked about Midnight Mary, but that may be a bit too dangerous. We will see. <br /> <br /> Some talk came up about my old Krewe, the Seven Cities Nightfall Posse. Odd bunch. Came up when we talked about Coffee\u2019s Krewes she had worked with. We had our requisite would be axe murderer, which Alice was far easier to deal with after dealing with him, the Elvis Impersonator, that cute Naomi Red Bird I never wound up in bed with, or Keth who rocked that bathrobe and got us banned from a lot of Casinos in Vegas. Good times. Killed a deadly serial killer there. Also, horrified people talking about the Pink Taco in the Hard Rock I had to do a thing in for MTV at the time. Yeah it exists. Hope those folks are doing well.<br /> <br /> We also buried Doc, which was fun. And brought him up of course. I even woke Clyde up for the first time in months to help shovel; still no Inky, Blinky or Sue. Clyde was\u2026Clyde. Oh, and also somewhere in the course of preparing for this my southern twang came out. How embarrassing.<br /> <br /> So we picked up Coffee at the airport, minus Alexia so not to overwhelm her. I admit I may overuse the word irrepressible but it seems apt for this specific case. Coffee is bubbly and adorable; her choice of beverage is not the only reason for her name. She is built a little more zaftig like me than thin like Karen, but if that bothers her she barely shows it. Also, like two inches shorter than me, making me no longer the shortest one in the house. She was chatty fun and happy to see everyone. <br /> <br /> We got her moved in, and talked about early plans. We are going to head to Murder Ballads. Murder Ballads has to be seen to be believed, and a good place to welcome Coffee to my world. Also gonna put some moves on her I think. She is cute and energetic, and I am a horny old bitch. If she is receptive, awesome, if not, well, Deanna plans to drop by after work. Given how handsy and flirty she has been since I got back, that girl is going to look like she was hit by a tidal wave if we are alone for more than ten minutes.<br /> <br /> Ahem. Anyway, time to go!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXIV</i><br /> <br /> Classy.<br /> <br /> The fairground operator ghost showed up when the PCs went out for Walpurgis at the start of the game, remember? And Gwen talked about the patch several times.<br /> <br /> The Seven Cities Nightfall Posse was part of <i>Brand New Key</i>, my first <b>Geist</b> game, a 5 session limited run. Doc and Natalie were the only common players even including the entire current class. Natalie was the same character, Doc played Keth (who Natalie got a message from awhile back that was posted). Only the first three sessions of <i>Brand New Key</i> got journals, which is why I have not posted them. But I can if folks are interested.<br /> <br /> Okay, there was some play at Murder Ballads but that will be next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-30T21:36:06-07:00","id":960868,"title":"","content":"It's cool when you can work in callbacks like that. Also can I say how amusing it is that the crew has a emergency stash of cookies and ice cream?<br /> <br /> Has Alexia ever made ice cream? I can't remember seeing any notices of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-08-31T03:06:12-07:00","id":960957,"title":"","content":"Yeah I probably still have a couple years worth of plots from the handouts and such. The game will end before we can get to them all. The emergency ice cream stash I think originated with Jasmine.<br /> <br /> I do not think Alexia has, no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-04T13:35:53-07:00","id":963360,"title":"","content":"A night of clubbing, then we finally get around to investigating the Patch. The PCs having a wide range of powers at this point, then mystery of the Patch is solved quickly, but it is a fun journey. Also, Coffee gets to know the group.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> \u201cYou here to replace that Japanese girl?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThe Korean girl? Who passed away? Yeah...\u201d<br /> <br /> Deanna glared at the doofus who was smirking and eying her in her clubbing finery with what appeared to be his usual tact. Shrugging at her response, he didn\u2019t take the hint and kept pressing her until Doc stepped forward and growled a warning. He hooked a finger at the big man.<br /> <br /> \u201cThis your dad?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should probably just start running.\u201d<br /> <br /> His eyes widened as he actually looked at Doc\u2019s intimidating form, and left in a hurry. Deanna rolled her eyes at his retreating back as she turned to enter the studio. She started the show off on a somber note, dedicating it to Katie. She got into it though, her perky self showing through, even dedicating a handful of the goth songs in her eclectic mix to \u2018a particular lady\u2019.<br /> <br /> Doc poked around the station, finding a few names and details to look into. He was interrupted when he heard a noise outside the window, so he texted Deanna to warn her and slipped outside. He nodded approvingly at the studio when he heard the lock click.<br /> <br /> He moved outside stealthily, only to find the mothman he noticed the other night staring back at him. Its golden yellow eyes were wide with fear and it backed away nervously, its wings fluttering. When it didn\u2019t respond to his words with anything more than chittering, Doc unlocked Primeval Marionette, initiating a psychic bond with the creature.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou are the biggest squirrel I\u2019ve ever seen.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc blinked and tried to lead the conversation to what it was and why it was here - \u2018the Kind\u2019 and \u2018the Energy\u2019 respectively. Doc pried more into the Energy, but all that got him was a 6-armed wave indicating \u2018around\u2019.<br /> <br /> After warning Deanna and getting her to turn off the lights inside the station, Doc gave the creature a tour of the station. It was largely interested in the mouse holes, but it did confirm that the Energy was a little stronger inside.<br /> <br /> The mothman wandered off before Deanna\u2019s show was done. Doc went in to talk with her about it. She grinned.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan I ride it?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhy not? I\u2019ll have you know, I\u2019m a trained equestrian.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc raised an eyebrow.<br /> -----------------------------------------<br /> The club was busy when the ladies got there. They got drink and a table first - Coffee was pleased at the schnapps selection - and took stock of the crowd. Chandra kept an eye on the door when she didn\u2019t find Rebecca right away, though the others soon started dancing.<br /> <br /> Natalie pulled Coffee out to the floor right away, while Sara waved Tracey down. She sat next to the tattooed woman, letting out a deep sigh. She was less shaken - a day of normalcy and college classes can do that for you - though she was worried about how on edge Marie was.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe gets all interested in justice and protection and forgets she\u2019s made of meat. But... I\u2019m here to dance and blow off some steam.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo you wanna dance do you?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave her a wicked grin.<br /> <br /> A few songs and a couple of drinks later and Sara found herself dancing with Coffee. She didn\u2019t try to show up Natalie, having neither the inclination nor the ability. She did build up the tension Natalie had begun and when the song was over, Coffee grabbed her hand, collected Natalie and pulled the pair off to the side.<br /> <br /> \u201cI know this is gonna sound you know really weird and I apolo- lemme start over- I\u2019m not a prude- it\u2019s just-\u201d<br /> <br /> She only stopped when Sara took her chin and kissed her. Natalie hid a smile with a reproachful glance. <br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d just like to pretend like I\u2019m not that kinda girl for 48 hours - 36.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie maintained eye contact with the other Sin-Eater.<br /> <br /> \u201c24... 18?<br /> <br /> Sara pretended to set an alarm. Coffee blushed and muttered something about another drink and left. The strawberry scented woman smiled teasingly at Sara, raising a hand. Her wife smiled warmly back and tagged her in.<br /> <br /> The tattooed girl got back to making the rounds. She checked in with Lindsay, since Sara hadn\u2019t seen the girl since the incident with the bloodbathers. She\u2019d been alright and was dating again, even thinking about going back to school.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t too long before Doc and Deanna joined the krewe at the club. Deanna and Coffee hit it off immediately, their voices competing for speed and pitch the more they talked. Natalie stared at them, smitten. Doc shook his head and told the rest of them about the mothman. At some point, Deanna and Coffee started singing Bohemian Rhapsody. Doc eyed them but continued, letting the others know he\u2019d invited it to visit via the roof. Natalie chuckled.<br /> <br /> \u201cI bet if it went to the front door and knocked and asked, Tavia\u2019d make it tea.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf it could, sure, but it only does a squeaking, chittering thing.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTavia\u2019d still give it tea.\u201d<br /> <br /> Eventually Coffee and Deanna split off and Deanna came up behind Natalie. Deanna's hands roamed while she glanced over at Coffee.<br /> <br /> \u201cIs she hoobajooby? I mean, did she come back from the dead for revenge too?\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc gave her a stifling look.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m the only one who came back for revenge.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTrue. Natalie came back cause there were drugs she\u2019d not done yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen leaned into Natalie and Doc grinned. <br /> <br /> \u201cAnd women Sara\u2019s not met yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cDon\u2019t forget men!\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie looked chidingly at Doc, while Deanna grinned and kissed Sara on the cheek.<br /> <br /> They relaxed for a while and after a bit Cindy dropped by. She ranted for a bit, about Trinh of course. Natalie sighed, shaking her head. Cindy looked stubborn.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe promised it would be different this time.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara laid a hand on hers sympathetically.<br /> <br /> \u201cDidn\u2019t she promised that last time?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cBut she wasn\u2019t wearing underwear this time.\u201d<br /> <br /> The trio listened sympathetically without backing down from their insistence that she should leave Trinh alone and save herself from that heartache.<br /> <br /> At some point, Rebecca and Neon had arrived. Chandra had immediately taken Rebecca up to the catwalks. Sara had a flirtatious dance or two with Neon earlier and when Deanna stole Natalie away and Karen gave Cindy that particular look, Sara glanced back over at the pink haired vampire, an anticipatory look in her own eyes.<br /> ------------------------------------------------<br /> Sara woke up with a number on a piece of paper on her nightstand and a glittery lipstick mark pressed into the skin between her shoulder and chest. She smiled woozily and pulled on a tank top and pajama pants before wandering downstairs to the kitchen.<br /> <br /> Doc took one look at her pale face and sighed. He went and shuffled through his herbs, finding the right packet without much hassle. Sara put on a teakettle while he searched, and accepted the mug of tea with a thankful smile.<br /> <br /> The crowd was sparse and the conversation light over breakfast. Other than Doc and Sara, only Noriko and Coffee, the latter clinging to a thermos of her namesake, had braved the morning hours. <br /> <br /> As they finished up, they were joined briefly by Cindy, who did pause for a moment to give Sara a kiss.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m just here to get Karen a whiskey and an ice pack for my ass.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou tell her I said she was bad, and a lush.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc smiled at her. She chuckled, then winced slightly as she turned to leave.<br /> <br /> Coffee watched her wide-eyed, then turned to Sara.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo this place does seem to have a magnetic effect on beautiful girls why not beautiful guys?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, that\u2019s not my fault! Besides, there\u2019s Doc, Timothy, Simon...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFair enough though I was told Simon doesn\u2019t exist as far as my eyes are concerned.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled. <br /> <br /> \u201cSadly, that is good advice.\u201d<br /> <br /> They got to talking about their plans for the day. As Doc described the Patch, Coffee looked thoughtful and pointed out she didn\u2019t have a weapon. Doc grinned and jumped on the opportunity to show off the armory.<br /> <br /> Karen joined them just in time to disparage Doc\u2019s offering to Coffee as a peashooter. Coffee had asked for something with as little kick as possible, so it was not unfairly said. Still, Sara rolled her eyes, coming up behind her wife, putting her chin on Karen\u2019s shoulder and tickling her sides. Karen responded by spinning around and pinning Sara to the wall, narrowing her eyes at the tattooed woman\u2019s impudent grin. The stalemate held until Doc cleared his throat.<br /> ------------------------------------<br /> Later that afternoon, once Natalie was home and all the needed supplies gathered, the krewe, minus Alexia, were ready to go. Karen had begged off, waving them on while pointing out she had some things to go over with Tatum. She put one hand on her hip and pointed between her wives with the other when Natalie started teasing her.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou two are the ones who take turns abusing your authority over Tatum.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t have any authority over her.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWant some?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara laughed, shaking her head quickly. Natalie shook her head even quicker.<br /> <br /> \u201cNo, Karen. You know she doesn\u2019t want to be tied down with property.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled her thanks, leaning into her comfortingly.<br /> ------------------------------------<br /> Natalie hopped out of the van, coming up behind Coffee and making use of her rare height advantage to whisper down into her ear. Doc rolled his eyes and pulled out a map, laying out his plans to search the woods, spreading out to comb it with a single sweep. Sara balked and eventually convinced him to spiral into the middle.<br /> <br /> The scrub oak woods were dark, think and untraveled. The whole place was poor on landmarks. It was easy to see how it got a reputation for a place to get lost in. The only real distinguishable location was the man made clearing that held the Playhouse.<br /> <br /> The already sparse birdsong died out in the clearing. There were no signs of animal life near the sturdy tin shack in fact. Before they got too close, Doc looked to Natalie. She winked at Sara and warned Coffee to catch her before she fell over.<br /> <br /> She reported that inside the shack was a cramped maze constructed out of junk. It smelled off, something chemical. Sara frowned, asking if it smelled flammable and whether she needed to curse someone. Natalie shook her head, suggesting it was more like cleaning products, though nothing particular.<br /> <br /> The krewe powered up to go in. Sara flared with light and Noriko shifted into a large cat. The other were more subtle. They went in single file, Sara going first since she was providing the light, Doc following close behind. The only other source of illumination was filtered down sunlight coming through the bullet holes in the walls. Despite all of said holes, there were no blood stains or death marks, just maze-like close quarters and a small that rang bells to the Navy medic.<br /> <br /> As they pushed forward, it seemed more and more familiar to Doc. Eventually it clicked with a flash of Navy drills, CQC training. He didn\u2019t have time to think too far into it before Sara started twitching, craning her neck to peer around a corner. Around the same time, Coffee eeped and grabbed ahold of Natalie.<br /> <br /> \u201cThose are my boobs, Coffee.\u201d<br /> <br /> The two girls insisted there was something moving in the shadows, while the others tried to carefully explain that they were the only ones there. Sara shook her head, disbelieving, trying to coax whatever it was out.<br /> <br /> After a moment it came together for Doc and he realized the chemical was most likely residue of some kind of psychotropic drugs, trapped in the claustrophobic shack. Sara insisted on continuing to the end of the maze, still hoping to find the hidden creature. Coffee was more than happy to leave with Natalie. When they got to the end, Sara looked at Doc, eyes wide and dilated.<br /> <br /> \u201cI should maybe do the thing here, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc chuckled and, catching her meaning, nodded. Once they got outside, Sara began her Ceremony to see the past of the Playhouse. Most of what she got were flashes of cops screaming and shooting, including a younger Norris and Tart. Once she got far enough back - the 70s by the feel of it - the people moving through had on military uniforms, looking for something through a much stronger haze of chemical than was there now.<br /> <br /> While Sara setup, Doc started planning training drills of his own. He smirked at Natalie.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou\u2019re not allowed to pair off with Deanna though - I saw how Coffee gravitated towards you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHey, Sara would have too if you weren\u2019t in the way.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah, but I don\u2019t need psychotropic drugs for that.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara shrugged and put an arm around Natalie\u2019s waist, resting her head on the strawberry scented woman\u2019s shoulder.<br /> ------------------------------------- <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> <br /> April 10th, 2011<br /> <br /> Last night was fucking awesome. Tonight will be too.<br /> <br /> Murder Ballads was hopping. I took Coffee to the dance floor, and made my intentions known, she was appropriately wowed. Sara followed up with a second Dance, while I took Cindy Toc across the floor. After that, Coffee took Sara and I aside. She confessed her feeling was old fashioned, but she did not want to be seduced as soon as she arrived. She asked for 48 hours, but as she made eye contact it dropped to 18. I understood, well, did not appreciate but I understood. I am giving her over twenty-four because I am so nice. Anyway, She went to dance with Cindy and I with Tracy.<br /> <br /> Then Deanna arrived. Dressed, if I may say, classy, clever, and sexy. Not all her behavior was as classy as she looked though. Remember what I said about Deanna being handsy? She groped me while we talked before being sidetracked by Coffee, then came back to dominate me in front of everyone. She only touched me intimately once in public. We went to the townhouse, and she reminded me who is in charge in our relationship. Oh my god that was fucking awesome. She has gotten better since a few months ago. This\u2026may affect our relationship. I am still not allowed to protest her groping too heavily. It seems a thrill for her. But I can lay out circumstances where it is not permitted. She needs to work on that. I am just not the person to do it.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve recommend she work with Karen a little. Mrs. Knight could probably make her a better Domme. Unfortunately, I am enjoying her dominance too goddamn much. My fear, actually, is that she will piss Doc off. He is still not okay with Sonia, and while Deanna loves and respects me, she does not always show it in public.<br /> <br /> She got breakfast in bed, I got a kiss, and we promised to meet again soon. It was one of my longer goodbyes. Considering she was a goofy sidekick to us not long ago, this has been something of a turnaround. The old song \u201cYou\u2019d be Surprised\u201d comes to mind.<br /> <br /> I always liked that song, though I did not admit it for years. Which is funny, given I was an awkward slightly chunky girl at the time it could easily have applied to.<br /> <br /> Came home, and we planned for the Patch. It was a good outing, but not what I expected. We traveled through the woods and walked seemingly forever to the Playhouse. There were naturally<i> Blair Witch</i> flashbacks. The Playhouse was small, dark, and cramped. Sara and Coffee sort of freaked out, Doc and I did not. We figured out that the odd smell I detected inside was a hallucinogen, and it was used for testing by the military. We got out, and I think we may do some training with the Underwater Story Weavers. Assuming Deanna keeps out of me long enough.<br /> <br /> Coffee and I have been heating up, and she has pretty much admitted we are spending the night together. Need to talk to the wives but I am looking forward to bonding with her greatly. She is fun, perky, and has a similar style. I don\u2019t expect a relationship, though one never knows. But it\u2019s intense, it is fun, and she seems really, really into it.<br /> <br /> Tonight is German Cuisine, then Long Wharf. We are exploring the fairground. Then the hot tub. I need to wholly purge Deanna from my mind for a while. Coffee deserves my attention, and god she wants it. Her attentions are very welcome.<br /> <br /> So if you read that thinking, \u201cMan, Natalie is totally a whore\u201d you got it in one. And right now I don\u2019t give a fuck. I am too happy. Time for dinner!<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXV</i><br /> <br /> Alexia\u2019s player was under the weather so she was not really around. Migraines suck. Rebecca (the Prince\u2019s rebellious childe) and Chandra were doing more vampire scheming, not romancing.<br /> <br /> The Mothman was similar to those in <b>Demon: The Descent,</b> as that story is a God-Machine one.<br /> <br /> So, the Patch. Resisting any effects of the remaining hallucinogens is a Stamina + Psyche (due to how the Sin-Eater power stat works), which is an easy roll for most of the PCs, Sara just rolled very badly. Coffee, who does not have monstrous Psyche, also had trouble. Natalie and Doc were unaffected at all.<br /> <br /> The fun part is the Patch is based on what was a real place. Over on rpg.net I stumbled over a thread of creepy RL events, and the Patch was discussed. It seemed neat, especially given pretty much every other creepy mystery had a supernatural explanation. The whole people getting mysteriously lost was just nerves. So no, the Patch is just leftover on public land from some exercises many years ago. The real Patch was bulldozed several years back.<br /> <br /> Back to the fairground next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-05T22:31:59-07:00","id":964085,"title":"","content":"No details on what happened to Rawl's pack?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-06T01:23:32-07:00","id":964149,"title":"","content":"They do not yet know.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:48:08-07:00","id":971276,"title":"","content":"Have the Orphan Grinders emerged since their initial introduction? They seemed interesting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T14:06:59-07:00","id":972115,"title":"","content":"The Orphan Grinders have not come up since their intro, and I am unsure that they will. They were to be a friendly Krewe the PCs could run into when doing deep exploration of the Dead Dominions, but when the focus stayed on earth (due to player interests and the fact that that, frankly, fits my running style far better) most of the plot seeds with the Orphan Grinders are unlikely to come up. I may save them to use in another game, having them move to a different city. Unsure at this time. I doubt at this later hour there is going to be enough of a shift to the Dominions to justify using them.<br /> <br /> While Natalie maintains her libido driven quality of life, the group turns their attention to future targets. Specifically, a certain pyromaniac.<br /> <br /> <i>Session LCXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> The krewe picked up Karen and Alexia for the trip to Long Wharf. The group went in singly and in pairs and only Sara was unlucky enough to catch the attention of the sparse few patrolling security guards. Natalie paused, watching her wife play the flirty, flighty teenager to a stoic, uninterested man. She was about to come back her up when Sara flounced off, giving a broad wink to the darkness.<br /> <br /> A few minutes later, Sara\u2019s astrally projected form mimed sneaking up on Natalie, while the strawberry scented woman pretended not to notice until Sara kissed her on the back of the neck.<br /> <br /> \u201cHi ghost Sara! Why are you ghost Sara?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled and explained to Coffee what had happened, in between running ghostly fingers through Karen\u2019s hair. The krewe made their way to the merry go round first, waving to the ghostly operator who smiled and waved back once he saw Doc and Natalie.<br /> <br /> As they rode the rides and walked the park, they talked. Coffee led the conversation, asking question after question. How did you meet Chandra? Is Marcie one of your girlfriends too? What do you do when investigating? How would you deal with the hotel in the Shining?<br /> <br /> Alexia handled the first question and Natalie the second, and the answer to the third and fourth was unanimously \u2018research\u2019. These questions and answers led to more questions, like What\u2019s the Abyss?, a question Sara answered by relating the story of the krewe\u2019s mythos and an explanation of it from the mage\u2019s side as well, as best she knew it. Discussion of their case at the Hidden Hillside Hotel brought up Mr. Ox, who Coffee was of course curious about. They managed to satisfy that curiosity as well.<br /> <br /> When they got home, Natalie grabbed Coffee by the hand and dragged her off. Sara chuckled and went off with Doc and Alexia to work on a sketch of the arsonist, as that is what the group had decided to pursue, to give Coffee a first hand idea of how they worked. After two tries, they had a decent sketch and Sara managed to talk Doc into leaving the library research for the next day, so that Coffee could participate if she wanted to.<br /> <br /> He agreed with a long suffering sigh and Sara headed gleefully off to the hot tub. Before she got there she found a trail of Natalie and Coffee\u2019s clothes, leading to Coffee\u2019s room. She showed up at the door of the trio\u2019s room holding Coffee\u2019s jacket with a pleading look.<br /> <br /> \u201cNot too busy for the hot tub?\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen hopped up and smiled at her, taking the jacket and setting it aside.<br /> <br /> \u201cNever.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Doc and Noriko hit the streets after Sara left, going on one of their usual patrols but heading straight for the area around the burnt out abandoned building. They slowed down as they neared it, hearing voices from inside.<br /> <br /> They moved carefully and quietly up, sticking to the shadows until they caught sight of the immortal Maria pacing and speaking to two other college girls, Queen and Jamie, exhorting them to try and sense something there. Jamie looked frustrated, but Queen spun her a line that even Doc saw through. He stood up and walked forward.<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know what you\u2019re trying to sense, but those people are long gone.\u201d<br /> <br /> The girls were startled but Maria reassured them by pointing out he was involved with the Underwater Story Weaving Club. When he brought out the sketch, Maria deflected but eventually admitted to having been hit on by him at Bar. She assumed he was a townie.<br /> <br /> After a moment Doc asked to speak with the immortal alone and after a moment of coyness, she agreed, a flirtatious smile on her face. Once the two students were sent outside, she continued with her flirtation until Noriko emerged from the shadows to warn her off.<br /> <br /> Her ardor cooled for the moment, she continued to maintain that Barry always managed to manipulate their dance in ways that never appeared to be of their design. She was not reassured by the Sin-Eater\u2019s insistence that the club was not being used as a weapon against her, pointing out that even if the club dissolved tomorrow, Barry had a collection of powerful students who would look up to him as a mentor. She smiled.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd if I sound mad, I assure you Barry and I went insane a long time ago.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc made one last stab at forestalling a student-centered cold war, and at calling Noriko to heel, before taking their leave. Crowley was waiting at the van to tell Doc his tail light was out. He also let him know that an old factory on the north end, one that had had a few of his friends squatting in it, had burned down just last January. He thought there might be a connection Doc should know about.<br /> <br /> Doc expressed condolences about his friends and offered his hand.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou should come by the house sometime.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s a little out of my territory. Besides, the house and I have a gentleman\u2019s agreement.\u201d<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> At breakfast the next day, Doc filled the others in. Noriko\u2019s anger came back as Doc related Maria\u2019s flirtatiousness and she pointed out what made her the most angry was when the immortal kept flirting with Doc in front of her. Natalie grinned at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe didn\u2019t try to pick both of you up? That\u2019s what I would have done.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell she wouldn\u2019t have succeeded?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWould I?\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie\u2019s grin turned wicked as Noriko turned many shades of red. Doc continued on with his tale of the previous night, prompting an explanation to Coffee when Natalie called Crowley Mr. Deus Ex Machina. She also was somewhat taken aback by a bar called Bar. Noriko smirked.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s mostly college students, they can\u2019t make it too hard.\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen protested, but soon talk turned to plans for the day. Natalie promised to contact Rita and see if they could introduce Coffee to the Changelings. But until then, there was research.<br /> <br /> The group decided to go by the Starbucks the arsonist had frequented last autumn first. It was in walking distance of the first arson site and the running theory was that he had frequented it while he was casing the place. That was held up by Natalie\u2019s conversation with the baristas there. She did get a name - James.<br /> <br /> Once they got back home, Natalie and Doc went up to the library to begin researching what kinds of supernatural beings could cause the kind of fire that Sara and Alexia had described. The list was short: mages and Changelings were a possibility, but unlikely. More likely was a pyrokinetic or a human Claimed by a fire spirit.<br /> <br /> Sara called the police while they research. Posing as a charity worker, she asked where she might find large groups of homeless folks, so that she didn\u2019t need to wander around the bad parts of town. The officer on duty gave her a few addresses, but also warned that the homeless population had scattered since the factory fire, so there were less folks around in general and the usual haunts might be abandoned.<br /> <br /> Coffee caught up with Sara as she got off the phone, a question in her eyes. Once they stepped into a side room, she asked it.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoes everyone who sleeps with Natalie fall for her?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara smiled and laid a hand on her shoulder. Coffee took a deep breath.<br /> <br /> \u201cOK. Can you explain your relationship again like I\u2019m two - no then you\u2019ll leave out the sex.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara laughed and did her best, pointing out that it wasn\u2019t all that different from most relationships, except that none of them believed sexual exclusivity was required to prove their love and that love was not diminished by being shared. Coffee sighed, assuring Sara that she didn\u2019t want to cause problems. Sara kissed her on the cheek.<br /> <br /> \u201cJust follow your heart. The only way you could cause problems would be to insist she leave us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cFollowing my heart is complicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded sympathetically and watched her go to her room to think. When Doc and Natalie came down from the library, she waylaid Natalie on her way to see Coffee, letting her know what they had talked about and that the bubbly Sin-Eater needed some space.<br /> <br /> Instead, Sara took Natalie off to the computer, to see if they could find anymore fires that may have been set by the arsonist. They found five. Two were the ones they\u2019d known he set, the abandoned building and factory in the poorer parts of town. One was the bloodbather\u2019s house, so they were able to rule that out.<br /> <br /> That left two of the fires were unaccounted for. The first was a scientific facility. Something about it bugged Sara, until she realized the address it gave was the one Eris had gone to when she was trying to find her past. The timing was right to match up with her escape as well.<br /> <br /> The second was about six months later and didn\u2019t seem to fit the pattern. It was a house in the nicer part of town, and it was a vacation home, with no one in residence at the time. On one hand, perhaps he had been working up to the kill. On the other, perhaps it was unrelated. However, it was the easier one to look into, so they determined they would, soon.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Tweets</b><br /> <br /> It\u2019s been a good couple days.<br /> <br /> Trip to the fairground went well. Coffee had lots of questions about our past adventures, some hypothetical situations, even how Chandra and Alexia met. They were good times. I enjoyed the conversation. Poor Sara had no luck at all bypassing security and had to project to our presence. Still a fun night was had. A warm night of friendship and laughter. Love and hope. This is, I think the real reason people become Sin-Eaters. On that warm April night, we were friends, we loved each other. In the future I must return to that night, that wonderful evening when all was right with the world.<br /> <br /> Except I wish Spooky was there.<br /> <br /> Then, we got back and I went up with Coffee. The plan was to get in the hot tub. However, she pulled me to her instead. We made love, and it was glorious. Even if she did sound like a Pomeranian being electrocuted. The perfect ending of the perfect night.<br /> <br /> Some work on various projects\u2026Doc talked to Crowley and discovered there was another fire on the north side that claimed homeless people, and he discovered Maria was starting a Brotherhood of Evil Mutants to counter our X-Men. We checked out the Starbucks where our pyro boy had been, and determined that he had not been by since the fire, probably scoping out locations. Still, time well spent.<br /> <br /> Sara got some information from the cops while we researched what sort of powers he could bring to bear, and signs point to psychic, since he is not a Sin-Eater (since Marcie who is not my lover, just a girl, did not see him as one) . Doc did an awesome job in the library. It seems there is at least a chance the lab that Eris escaped from is connected. We will see.<br /> <br /> So my love life is complicated. I can\u2019t blame being poly, I mean I can, but in the end the poly-ness has little to do with it, beyond the open aspects (which happens with Monos too). I honestly expected Deanna to enjoy her experience, find a guy, and have an awesome story to tell while drunk, but that is not quite how it turned out. She wants to commit to nothing till after college, but she wants to keep seeing me. And I sort of like the tension of not knowing what she will do, but need more faith in her discretion. As long as Madam Grabbyhands keeps to some limits we are good.<br /> <br /> Coffee has completely fallen for me. She is actively trying to, you know, not, but I didn\u2019t really hold back and she has been mooning at me all day. I mean for good reason, I am awesome, but I am going to let our new relationship settle in a bit before we discuss anything.<br /> <br /> Past that stuff is going good. Managed to work out a decent Vlogging schedule. I am getting a bit more competition, which is good, we want it to be a healthy market. The more money I make off of, say, Youtube, the less I have to make elsewhere.<br /> <br /> Well time for fire investigations with all the pretty people. Later!<br /> <br /> <i>End Session LCXVI</i><br /> <br /> Poor Sara could not catch a break. Despite a good pool for Stealth and Persuasion, she could not sneak or talk past a normal human guard, so she projected. Felt a little sorry for her player.<br /> <br /> The facility that burned was Team Tomorrow, which if you read <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i> you are well aware of. <b>Balance of Shadows</b> does not (currently) have them as major enemies or anything, thought they did leave a bit of a mess, including James and Eris. Alice/Jasmine\u2019s player retiring means the Eris end may not be followed up too much, but James is still in the picture.<br /> <br /> Coffee was, as always, a blast to play.<br /> <br /> The Maria vs. Barry conflict was from near the beginning of the game, only now rearing it\u2019s head again. There was a lot of OOC, IC, and Semi-IC discussion of who the good vs. bad guy was, without consensus. The Krewe had worked with Barry before, and found Maria snooping. Both say the other is dangerous. Who is right? Or Both?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":56,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","user":"Baroness Nerak","date":". 09-18-2016, 05:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-23T19:24:23-07:00","id":975335,"title":"","content":"And caught up. School and work does cut into the AP journals apparently. Who knew?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T14:05:39-07:00","id":988382,"title":"","content":"It certainly can, Omenseer.<br /> <br /> Last time was cancelled due to me sleep depping and a player feeling under the weather. But we are back tonight. This is the session from about a month ago.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> A little while later they were planning out their next steps and catching Alexia up on what she missed at the patch. Coffee protested when Doc mentioned her and Sara going crazy.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s not my fault, it was vespene gas or something.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe require more vespene gas?\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen popped her head around the corner and she and Coffee traded Starcraft lines back and forth while the others looked on bemusedly. Eventually Natalie brought up that Rita had gotten back with her and was free any day after 6. Considering the hour, and that they had two sites to investigate that day, Sara suggested the next day for a dinner meeting.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019s still dating Jasmine\u2019s student. Hasn\u2019t eaten him. Yet.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cExcuse me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Coffee looked at Natalie wide-eyed. Sara chuckled and took the opportunity to explain a bit more of what they knew of Changelings, how their Keepers changed them in general and Rita in specific. They were still discussing it as they prepared to leave. Karen and Chandra looked to the krewe while Noriko just moved with them.<br /> <br /> Alexia nodded and shrugged at Chandra\u2019s questioning look. Natalie frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat\u2019s the homework situation like?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNo one\u2019s spouse should ever say that.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf the spouse has homework...\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen glared at Sara and Natalie both and insisted she was fine. Sara put an arm around her waist and leaned into her as they walked out to the van.<br /> <br /> In the van, Sara and Natalie looked through the papers they\u2019d retrieved last time they\u2019d gone to the burnt out research facility. They found little other on their firebug than a last name. James Rollin definitely fit their description and was apparently related to a government official, but that was all they could find - everything else was obfuscated with warnings of \u2018Classified\u2019.<br /> <br /> They did manage to come across some references to a werewolf that had been held there. Patricia Byerly was the second werewolf they\u2019d captured, the first having escaped some time past. Sara looked closely and managed to find a date, over two years past, that implied Eris was definitely Patricia. She\u2019d had her first change during a domestic abuse incident and her husband wound up very dead. The notes suggested a diagnosis of trauma-induced amnesia, compounded by \u2018current living conditions\u2019.<br /> <br /> Sara finished up texting the details to Alice and Deirdre just as the van drove up to the fenced off area of the industrial park north of town that the abandoned facility was in. Alexia hopped out to pick the lock, once they\u2019d given the place a once over for cameras.<br /> <br /> Driving through the opened gate, they found themselves in the big open concrete area surrounding the charred remnants of the facility. Natalie stayed in the van, Boneyarding, with Karen and Chandra to guard her. The others waited for her report - no ghosts, the second floor wall had chunks missing - before heading carefully inside.<br /> <br /> Alexia and Doc took point and found the epicenter of the fire quickly, leading the others to an upstairs room. Sara got to work, pacing the area and opening herself to visions.<br /> <br /> She retched after a moment, and took a moment to gather herself, before she stepped back into the torrents of flashes of torture scenes, medical procedures and screaming. She was distracted by a glimpse of an explosion, but turned aside from that vision when she realized it was contained in a room and the only one killed was a beyond morbidly obese vampire who was in the process of absorbing someone in a uniform.<br /> <br /> She was torn when she caught a glimpse of Eris, but still, purpose in mind, she focused on the vision she had of James. The man was waking up in a hospital bed, an IV in his arm. A young woman walked in, someone Sara had seen before at Murder Ballads. She spoke calmly, letting him know that his dose of had been tampered with and encouraging him to leave quickly. A guard interrupted her. She looked at him calmly and the guard shot himself in the face.<br /> <br /> James stood carefully, building up a fireball between his hands for a moment before thrusting it forwards, the woman egging him on to build it higher and higher. Soon it engulfed the entire corridor. The pair walked forward, the inferno parting before them. At one point a trio of guards tried to stop them, guns out. At a dispassionate look from the woman, one turned to shoot the other two, distracting them until the fire reached them.<br /> <br /> Sara told the others, then went back into a trance. She wanted to know more about Eris. The flashes weren\u2019t as vivid this time, but she knew what she was looking for anyway. The beginning was similar to James\u2019 story, with her waking up slowly and pulling an IV out. The woman wasn\u2019t there to explain why she wasn\u2019t properly sedated, but she was there to coolly watch the mayhem Eris wrought on her way out.<br /> <br /> Sara shook out of her trance to hear Alexia explaining the answers she\u2019d gotten from Industrial Oracle. The woman she\u2019d seen was Miranda Davis. That was a name Sara recognized from the paperwork, a psychic. Alexia had also asked about what had been done to James and after hearing it, figured the same had been done to Miranda. It was a delicate brain surgery, a procedure that burnt out the portions of the brain that were \u2018holding them back\u2019. Everyone frowned as the implication sank in.<br /> <br /> \u201cDid they... to Eris...?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked to Alexia. The other woman paused and shook her head. They hadn\u2019t been modifying Eris, just using her as a source of spiritually charged, self regenerating cells. Sara nodded and took a deep breath. Then she frowned again.<br /> <br /> \u201cEris came right to the papers when we explored here with her. But there\u2019s no way she happened to see them on her way out. She was raging. I wonder if she got some sort of tip.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOr had an implanted suggestion.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc scowled. Coffee looked between the group quickly.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m glad there\u2019s no weird supernatural experiments here. If I was a weird supernatural experiment I would totally guard treasure in a place like this but then I\u2019d run out of coffee and that would be bad.\u201d<br /> <br /> That lightened the mood somewhat as they went back to the van and away. Discussion meandered from whether zombie children were more frightening with or without skin to how terrifying Dick Clark was. Doc\u2019s eyes rolled circles around his head as he drove.<br /> <br /> When they got to the final arson site, they found it already rebuilt, presumably courtesy of a large bank account, with a brand spanking new security system installed. Natalie saw the blinking red light through her Boneyard, and Doc noted the wiring. Alexia stretched and activated Industrial Marionette to turn that off quickly, then unlocked the door more mundanely.<br /> <br /> Once in, Sara walked the house, looking into its past. The strongest glimpse she got was an old one, decades old, the flash of light on scissors being used to stab someone to death. The fire was a fainter glimpse, but Sara focused on it to see two men breaking in to steal a painting, then burning the place down to cover their tracks. Nothing supernatural about it. She gave the others a wry smile.<br /> <br /> \u201cRed herrings ahoy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLet\u2019s get out before we\u2019re discovered then.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia ushered them out and reset the alarm.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Back at the Bluffs, the krewe gathered around a computer as Natalie looked into Miranda Davis. Coffee offered around chocolate covered coffee beans.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what do you think would happen if they did the brain surgery to a Sin-Eater?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara thought for a moment. <br /> <br /> \u201cWell, our powers go through our geists, so they\u2019re probably not restricted by things like self-preservation or empathy for others.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWhich is a shame sometimes.\u201d<br /> <br /> Natalie had a wry look on her face. She gestured towards the computer and explained what she\u2019d found. Miranda Davis had a Facebook profile, one that had been created since the fire at the Team Tomorrow facility. Her posting was spotty, with months between updates. The latest was from a few months before, talking about her vacation in St. Lucia. She didn\u2019t have a James friended, unfortunately, but she did mention she had been a student at Albertus Magnus, which did give them one line of inquiry. Natalie sent off a text to Grin.<br /> <br /> Sara read over her shoulder, a considering look on her face.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou know, sociopathy doesn\u2019t make someone evil. Just that they don\u2019t have the same... restraints others do. James is... she might be ok.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cUnless she\u2019s pulling his strings.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIf she sent Eris after those papers, he\u2019s probably not.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc shrugged and nodded.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> Doc and Noriko went looking for the trio and Coffee, finding them sans Karen at the hot tub. At the sound of the footsteps, Natalie eeped and dipped down into the water, up to her chin. Coffee moved around to help her put her top back on. Sara grinned and curled up on the seat, topless.<br /> <br /> After a single appreciative glance, Doc kept his eyes mostly averted as he asked the group\u2019s feelings about Caul. Natalie began, pointing out she pursued it to help defend herself. Doc shrugged, mentioning Shroud.<br /> <br /> \u201cCaul is more... dodging, less armoring up. Not being there as opposed to not caring you got hit.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cRight. The wind versus the immovable object. And I\u2019m not Iron Natalie.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc smirked at the strawberry scented woman.<br /> <br /> \u201cNothing about you is hard.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara grinned and tickled Natalie\u2019s sides. She squirmed. Coffee chimed in at the pause, comparing Manifestations to pizza toppings, in between squeaks that always provoked an expression on innocence from Natalie. Oracle was pepperoni, Caul Italian sausage and all of them good.<br /> <br /> Conversation turned to plans for the next day. Other than brainstorming, and visiting Rita, there wasn\u2019t much specific. Doc mentioned Alexia had spoken to Catherine and she\u2019d be around by breakfast. Natalie explained to Coffee that she was Alexia and Chandra\u2019s as of yet unacknowledged third. Coffee feigned shock.<br /> <br /> \u201cWhat? Nubile people come over here and get seduced by couples?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNever happen. Not ever. What do you take us for?\u201d<br /> <br /> Karen walked in to find Sara grinning wickedly at Coffee, and started taking people to task for still being in bathing suits. Natalie countered with teasing about her homework. Doc and Noriko took the opportunity to make themselves scarce.<br /> <br /> -------------------------------------<br /> <br /> The next morning Coffee met Alexia in the kitchen looking shell shocked, asking for protein. Alexia handed her a few packets of bacon and Simon\u2019s Bacon Genie and got her started. Sara found her eating bacon directly from the Genie.<br /> <br /> Coffee greeted her with a kiss then went back to her bacon. The rest of the krewe trickled in eventually.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo what did people who did things they\u2019ll be able to tell their children do?\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc hid a smile from Coffee and told the group about the research he\u2019d done after the hot tub. He wasn\u2019t able to pin down \u2018the Energy\u2019 the mothman had spoken of, but he did figure out that mothmen were usually a symptom of nearby weirdness and not a cause.<br /> <br /> Catherine arrived as he was finishing up. After greetings, he turned to her.<br /> <br /> \u201cSo I met a mothman...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThat\u2019s an interesting way to start a story.\u201d<br /> <br /> Doc filled her in on what had happened on campus and she agreed to check out the radio station and see if she had any insights.<br /> <br /> Sara took up the thread then, explaining the firebug case. Catherine frowned.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ve heard of Team Tomorrow, though I can\u2019t place when. I haven\u2019t heard of Miranda or James though. Sorry.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave her an understanding smile and they finished up breakfast in peace, leaving off talking business in favor of catching up and discussing philosophy, Doc revisiting his questions concerning Caul now that he had Alexia around as well. Satisfied with the answers, he prepared to learn the Manifestation himself. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> I am feeling better about my love life.<br /> <br /> Last night was spent with Coffee and my wives. It was glorious. Poor thing was nervous, so many people here, but Sara and Karen and I rather took good care of her. The bonding, the emotion, the intensity was marvelous. One thing I rather like about her is her emotions flow like a river. What she seems to be feeling is what she is feeling, and she is eager to please her partners. <br /> <br /> I think the issue was, three of us, she felt the need to take care of all of us. Poor dear. I was like her once. Bubbly, emotional, my feelings guiding my hands. I would love to be again; I am more like that than I have been in over a decade. It\u2019s wonderful. <br /> <br /> Anyway, we assembled at the hot tub. We were just getting started when Doc and Noriko arrived. Doc wanted to ask about Caul, a Manifestation I have begun to develop myself. I spoke of how I liked it because it, again, flowed, like my emotions, rather than resist. Doc commented nothing about me was hard, which made me laugh, and then I felt Coffee\u2019s hand on my thigh. Doc concluded the interview and left; we had fun and after a half hour or so then hijinks moved from the hot tub to the family room. <br /> <br /> The union was glorious. Fellow Bound are always especially exciting, as you join with two souls rather than one. The bed had seven souls. Though as I think of it I don\u2019t know her Geist. She has never said. I should ask her.<br /> <br /> Morning was awkward, poor Coffee. She is embarrassed, smitten, exhausted, and eating Bacon straight from the genie. She seemed afraid of ruining the mystique, but exhaustion defeated dignity. She is meeting Rita today, but really Coffee needs time to relax. She has had a lot of new experiences, possibly life changing ones, with new people. <br /> <br /> Doc asked Alexia at breakfast about Caul. She was less poetic about it. Coffee also got to meet the third leg of their triad Catherine too. I suspect the poor psychic was overwhelmed. Speaking of overwhelmed Coffee seems better, at least. My little bean eater had the light back in her eyes this afternoon.<br /> <br /> Yesterday was educational. We were at the site where Eris escaped. Coffee kept gobbling her chocolate covered coffee beans. The whole place was frightening conceptually even as it was burnt out nothing. Who knows how many deranged psychics came from there. We are going to have to look more into that later. At least Team Tomorrow is gone. Hopefully to plague no one else anymore. I\u2019d hate to see what would happen if they set up a new facility somewhere else.<br /> <br /> We are looking for a Miranda Davis, who can mind control. She seems pretty dangerous. Sara and I have seen her, at Murder Ballads I think. Maybe Gotham Citi. Unsure whether to approach her or not, but I have something of an iron mind. I am not Spooky, but then who is.<br /> <br /> We will see. Any luck this may lead to Clubbing for Justice (TM). We can hope. I am rather partial to Clubbing for Justice myself. Anyway, Vlog to do, then getting back out there.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXVII</i><br /> <br /> Oh let\u2019s see\u2026use of Industrial Oracle and Reading the Echoes as usual for research, with Alexia using Oracle and Sara using the Ceremony.<br /> <br /> Coffee is a hell of a lot of fun to play. Also, she likes coffee, if you didn\u2019t catch that.<br /> <br /> Of course Team Tomorrow is in <i>Night Train Detective Agency</i>.<br /> <br /> Okay I think that covers it. Sorry about the missed session. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world