38"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T18:59:35-07:00","id":990203,"title":"","content":"What the dragon said, although your answer does have merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T19:58:05-07:00","id":990220,"title":"","content":"She can control one at a time. The Krewe is unlikely to be affected, they roll Resolve + Composure + Psyche vs. Manipulation + Persuasion, neither of which she has at 5","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:53:46-07:00","id":990263,"title":"","content":"True, unless the exploding ten happens. That would be fun to see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-19T21:56:01-07:00","id":990264,"title":"","content":"Or unless the dice decide to be capricious; seriously, I've seen dice pools above ten get fewer successes than a dice pool below six.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-30T12:56:09-07:00","id":995763,"title":"","content":"There is Laser Tag. Also, someone makes an ill advised decision. Not about Laser Tag.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXVIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sasha - <br /> <br /> Well, it has been a satisfying few days, and we even got a few leads out of it. On James, the pyromaniac I\u2019ve mentioned. Natalie worked her magic on the computer, with Doc\u2019s help, and managed to find the guy\u2019s dad. He was in the government, like the file said, in the FBI specifically. Nowadays he works as a consultant for a venture capitalist group.<br /> <br /> Thankfully, we know some people in that world, on a couple sides of the fence. An associate of Chandra\u2019s that I think I\u2019ve mentioned before, Rebecca, is something of a rival to the group he\u2019s working for. That meeting was exciting - I\u2019d forgotten that Neon and she had hooked up in the past, with drama involved. In fact, in retrospect, I recall that their drama was precisely why Doc was all growly about me getting with her. Nothing I can\u2019t smooth over though, I\u2019m sure. Anyhow, she was familiar with James\u2019 dad and clued us into some of his connections. She hadn\u2019t heard of James, but took the warning to heart. One of our big fears is that if James does have a grudge against his dad, who knows who else might get caught in the crossfire. Even if he doesn\u2019t have a grudge, his dad put him in a scientific facility to have unethical experimenting done on him. I wouldn\u2019t put using his son as a weapon past him.<br /> <br /> The meeting with my lovely paramour Elizabeth was much more fun, if less immediately helpful. She\u2019s not in the same \u2018clique\u2019 as James\u2019 father and his boss, but she does have business connections to them. She knew a little more about them because of that, the ones in charge that is, and thought it was unlikely they would use James as a weapon, but not much beyond that. She did promise to look into it though. Best of all, after we took so long consulting, the roads were far too treacherous in the dark. So I stayed the night. For safety, of course.<br /> <br /> On our other front, Miranda, I did some work while Natalie and Doc did their research. Grin had found out that Miranda had been suspended for \u2018breaking the morality code\u2019 with a comment that read \u2018Do you want Carrie? Cause this is how you get Carrie\u2019. There was nothing more to be found at Grin\u2019s level of access, so I went to go talk to the teach that made the complaint (as well as a few others), posing as a potential employer of Miranda\u2019s.<br /> <br /> All in all, what we found looks... ok for out escaped sociopath. Driven was the most frequent word used, along with highly intelligent. Even the teacher who registered the complaint did her best to soften whatever happened. Or maybe she just thought I wouldn\u2019t believe her. According to her story, Miranda has a \u2018low frustration threshold\u2019 and could be \u2018intensely disruptive\u2019 if it was exceeded. Apparently this was usually catalyzed by unkindness on the part of her peers. She was very careful to skate around the fact Miranda\u2019d used weird psychic stuff to be disruptive.<br /> <br /> The official report didn\u2019t skate around it though. Karen managed to hack her way in and found out that Miranda had been suspended for witchcraft, specifically. The final straw of \u2018difficult to prove things she was the epicenter of\u2019 was when she Darth Vadered her classmates and then threw everything in the room, including the other students, against the wall.<br /> <br /> I gotta admit, I was a little surprised that witchcraft merited only a suspension. Karen pointed that she didn\u2019t use it to cheat. Still, gay sex is apparently an automatic expulsion, sex for grades trade or not. They\u2019re letting karen\u2019s marriage pass without comment, thankfully, though I imagine any of us making passes at her fellow students or her making passes at Ms. Hollis, cute little blonde thing or no, would go less well.<br /> <br /> There was one anomaly among all the stories. One of the teachers I talked to mentioned she got along really well with her classmates. By an interesting coincidence, he was the only one who had her in his class after her suspension. It seems she learned some new tricks. Some new, unfortunate tricks.<br /> <br /> On a more pleasant note, we had a nice dinner with Rita yesterday. Coffee managed not to bring up any references to Rita\u2019s unfortunate past and Alexia managed to swerve the conversation away from Natalie\u2019s own uncomfortable past into discussion of favorite books and movies. Coffee\u2019s, apparently, is Red Badge of Courage. Unfortunately, Karen was not to be moved from poking at Rita\u2019s shock that Natalie was old enough to have young Natalie. At least, not until I tickled it out of her.<br /> <br /> Rita is doing very well though. She had a rocky bit when she moved here, but she seems to have gotten her feet under her. She\u2019s still dating Jasmine\u2019s student, Jean, and is even getting on well with his parents. There was some drama among her social group, but she\u2019s been able to stay out of it so far. All in all, it was good to see her again and catch up.<br /> <br /> Today has been a relaxation day, since all our projects are in the wait until word gets back/clubs open up stage. Of course it started a little later than usual, at least for me. I was up late consulting with Elizabeth, after all. When I got back, the troupe had decided to go Laser Tagging with the Underwater Story Weavers Club.<br /> <br /> It was a fun time. We were enough for our own team, going up against another group who clearly did this a lot. They were better than most of us. But Alexia and Doc blew them out of the water and we pulled ahead in the end. Clarissa did well too, more surprisingly. I think she had an ace or two up her sleeve.<br /> <br /> I did pretty badly - I can think of better things to do in a dark room than sneak around and shoot light guns. Which is certainly not to say that I didn\u2019t have an awesome time but... even Deanna did better than me, and she was humming the Batman theme almost the whole time. She was in fine form, really, almost losing cupcake privileges over the way she\u2019s taken to bossing Natalie around. Alexia really doesn\u2019t care for it.<br /> <br /> We\u2019ve been relaxing in the music room since we got back, Karen on her guitar, Natalie on the piano. I sang for a couple of songs, as did Natalie and Doc even joined in for Riders on the Storm. It was a pleasant end to a pleasant day.<br /> <br /> Tomorrow we go clubbing in pursuit of a pyromaniac or his friend. Also, we introduce Coffee and Tatum to each other. That should be a hell of an evening.<br /> <br /> Sara <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> Full disclosure: In retrospect, I probably shouldn\u2019t have done that. Fucked Doc and Noriko I mean. <br /> <br /> But I needed it. Sexual tension was escalating. And hell, I needed to know if I was still capable of it. Noriko being there helped. And I was mostly able to do it without freaking out at all. I did not get pregnant; that could not have happened this time. But I know I can, if it needs to. <br /> <br /> And honestly, it was pretty fun. I also wanted to get with Noriko again, and enjoyed that. I am having a pretty wild, awesome few days. <br /> <br /> We had dinner with Rita last night. It went well, she seems good. Thanks to my coaching, Coffee did not ask any inappropriate questions. Rita is still with Jean, and getting along with his parents. Speaking of parentage, Natalie Lousler came up, and Rita was shocked I had a seventeen year old. Part of that was having her young, but I also credit my good looks. Of course, Karen had to push her luck there. Fortunately Sara swooped in in defense of my tattered virtue.<br /> <br /> Afterwards we visited Rebecca Jones, the Carthian. She knew the father, Peter but not the son, James; working for a Micah Carter, Peter is ex-FBI. She said she did not know Micah well. Rebecca also menaced Sara a bit about Neon. I hope I don\u2019t need to have a word with her; threatening my wife will not do.<br /> <br /> Doc and I had done some digging, so we were on his trail. Mostly web research. I was fairly pleased with myself to find the FBI connection. Meanwhile Grin had figured out Miranda had some issues as a student at Albertus Magnus. She had broken the honor code and been suspended at one point, and in with the teacher comments was \u201cDo you want Carrie? Because this is how you get Carrie.\u201d<br /> <br /> We came back, and Sara went to talk to Elizabeth, her vampire friend. Alexia retired early, as is her way. I went back and found Doc and Noriko, and things progressed. He sent me to find Noriko myself. Once she jumped into my hands, we spent a quiet night bonding.<br /> <br /> Breakfast was fun, but no Sara. Coffee had finally gotten some rest and her eyes were bright. While going over things to do, because gods forbid we have a day off, the story weavers came up, and the bright idea happened to do laser tag. Actually, not a bad idea. The girls need some self-defense. Doc and Alexia did outstanding, and of the weavers, Clarissa did very well. I mean, cheated, but in the real world that is what you do.<br /> <br /> Before that Sara had done some legwork and talked to Miranda\u2019s teachers. They described her as driven. And had a low frustration tolerance with people. At one point she started choking people with her powers. Unlike at the research center, no one died. However, the whole thing had been covered up. Karen\u2019s hacking revealed just what she had done to break the honor code: witchcraft. I guess it is an improvement when that just gets you kicked out of school as opposed to murdered. <br /> <br /> Anyway, We went out with the weavers to eat as a group, and then the Krewe came home to jam. Karen rocked some <i>F\u00fcr Elise</i> and <i>Lux Aeterna</i>. Doc wanted to do <i>Riders on the Storm,</i> which mean he sang briefly while I tore up the keys. We had a good time though. Love and laughter.<br /> <br /> Maybe we deserve some time to relax, eh? Ah, probably not.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXVIII</i><br /> <br /> Fun little session. Only real mechanics to discuss is for Laser Tag, had people roll Attribute + Skill combinations to represent how they were contributing, usually Dexterity or Wits plus Stealth, Firearms or Athletics.<br /> <br /> Rita and Jean are names we have not heard in awhile. Was fun to revisit some stuff from earlier sessions. <br /> <br /> Was a fun session, hopefully tonight will be. Comments and Questions welcome","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-13T12:30:02-08:00","id":1002601,"title":"","content":"The Krewe meet the mysterious Miranda. Coffee and Tatum finally meet. A family revelation.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXIX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sara let out a deep breath as she turned on her shower, stepping in as soon as the water had warmed up. She\u2019d decided to talk to Doc about James today, at breakfast, before she could procrastinate her way out of it again. She wasn\u2019t looking forward to it.<br /> <br /> Partially it was because she couldn\u2019t really argue against his main point. James had done some awful things. Things that he had no justification for, inexcusable things. And no, the horrors done to him didn\u2019t absolve him. To her mind though, they did make him all the more deserving of a second chance. But Doc professed less of a belief in second chances than she did. He\u2019d tended to roll his eyes and blame her libido, so far.<br /> <br /> She\u2019d been putting off talking to Doc about it in a serious way, figuring on leaving it for once they were closer. It all honesty, she knew he had a softer heart than he let on sometimes and had hoped that, confronted with the guy in person, he might let her try and convince James of the error of his ways. But given what Natalie had found out, \u2018hopefully\u2019 and \u2018later\u2019 didn\u2019t seem like enough.<br /> <br /> The strawberry scented woman had certainly drawn out the drama of the reveal that Rawl was short for William Rollin, James\u2019 older brother, Sara thought with a fond smile as she let the water run through her long hair. Sara had called her werewolf friend right away. It all came as a surprise to him, though the fact that James was a pyrokinetic apparently explained some things.<br /> <br /> Rawl couldn\u2019t give any insight as to whether James might be aiming for or working with their father. From what he remembered, there was no antagonism between them, but from what he remembered, James wouldn\u2019t go around murdering homeless people. He\u2019d had very little contact with his family since he changed - that first time he\u2019d come back his parents told him James had been institutionalized, and nothing more, and that only after Rawl had asked. Sara frowned sadly. \u2018Coldly caring\u2019 or not, she didn\u2019t approve of Peter Rollin\u2019s fathering.<br /> <br /> Rawl did promise to come help if he could, with the idea that James would be less inclined to attack him right off. He did warn though, that if a fight broke out, he\u2019d be joining in on his little brother\u2019s side. Which was only fair, in Sara\u2019s mind. When she talked about it with Natalie, her wife had pointed out that Doc\u2019s healing ceremony could potentially restore the excised portion of his brain, leaving them with an option in between killing him and letting him go with a stern talking to. So Sara had figured on talking Doc into it, then making sure Rawl would be copasetic with a fight that had his brother being healed as an end goal.<br /> <br /> Sara sighed, rinsing the conditioner out of her hair. She\u2019d procrastinated yesterday afternoon, ostensibly not wanting to interrupt Doc\u2019s research. And then it was time for dinner with Tatum, which was an excellent distraction. Sara smiled indulgently. Time with Tatum usually was. If only she could get over seeing every object of Natalie\u2019s affections as a rival. Coffee had managed to deflect some of that, at least, into awe over how fast she talked. They\u2019d certainly got along well enough last night at Murder Ballads.<br /> <br /> Which was the other thing that got in the way. After dinner was prep for clubbing, and then clubbing, so no unpleasant conversation then either. They\u2019d lucked out at Murder Ballads, since Miranda had been there when the krewe got there. Of course, she was talking to Maria and Sara really didn\u2019t want to sabotage the Immortal\u2019s plans. Or have it look that way. Sara shook her head. She felt for the woman. Maria had a raw deal, and Sara could understand why she was so paranoid, even as the Sin-Eater wished she could reconcile her and Barry.<br /> <br /> Regardless, Sara was not one to interrupt anyone\u2019s good time, so she waited them out. It gave her plenty of time to help Tatum and Coffee keep getting to know one another. Not that she shirked her voyeuristic duties. Miranda and Maria were both good at the game, exceptionally good. Maria was a little less sincere in her intentions, but they were both pouring on the charm. <br /> <br /> When they came down off the catwalks, Miranda looked like she was heading home so Sara had moved to intercept her. The poor dear was a bit frazzled it seemed, about as frazzled as she left Maria, though the Immortal didn\u2019t have to deal with learning about a new type of supernatural. To be fair, Maria just didn\u2019t know who she\u2019d met. Sara smirked. It was only fair really - she\u2019d protected Maria\u2019s secrets from Miranda, so she couldn\u2019t very well go blabbing the opposite way. Miranda had taken to asking questions, and learning about Sin-Eaters well, for her part, even if her first instinct had been to try and root through Sara\u2019s brain.<br /> <br /> That conversation was the other thing that had pushed Sara to promising herself to have that talk with Doc. The psychic woman clearly cared about James, even if he had gotten temperamental before finally leaving her last fall. Sara wanted to talk to her again, and wanted to be able to promise her that they wouldn\u2019t hurt James. Natalie was right, she probably had a way to contact the pyrokinetic, even if she had chosen not to since they broke up.<br /> <br /> Sara stretched, reveling in the house\u2019s prodigious water heater. She did also want to talk to the psychic woman for other reasons, namely to discuss healing her again. Sara hadn\u2019t wanted to push - like the other woman had said, she\u2019d had a weird night - but Sara was intent on convincing her that stronger was not always better, was not always worth the price.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t as if Miranda wasn\u2019t clearly a kind person. The concern she showed for Eris and the fact she waved those she could from the Team Tomorrow facility showed that. That honestly made for a harder sell of the ethical angle, since she did those things after the surgery, and it was a hard sell to begin with, considering the details of the surgery. Sara was holding out hope for a conscious sense of self preservation to win out.<br /> <br /> With another sigh, Sara turned the water off and grabbed for a towel. The whole situation unsettled her. She felt for the awkward angry girl Miranda had been and regretted the things done to her. They\u2019d taken away her choice in how to cope with a lonely world, and on top of that, made it difficult for her to even regain that choice. And yet... how could Sara just let her continue controlling people without regard to their agency or her own safety?<br /> <br /> Sara wrapped her hair up in the towel and padded out to her room to get some clothes. That was mostly a question for later - she\u2019d hardly had tome to try and talk her around. Maybe it would work out. But before she tried that again, she had to talk Doc out of enacting bloody vengeance against a pyrokinetic murderer. She ran her fingers through her wet hair, and flicked the droplets behind her for luck.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 16th, 2011<br /> <br /> Tatum and Coffee have met and it went better than I had feared. <br /> <br /> The afternoon was mostly quiet; I managed to find that Rawl was the brother of James, our pyro, but while he offered to help intervene it did not help us find James any. I think Sara enjoyed talking to him again though. <br /> <br /> Doc and I have managed not to be weird, which is good. He was quiet as we dealt with the James situation, but he is always quiet. Part of the mystique, I suppose.<br /> <br /> Karen, Sara, Coffee and I went out to eat and met Tatum there. It went\u2026well enough. Tatum was guarded about Coffee. She gets along with Sara well enough now, but Sara\u2019s \u201cskipping past\u201d her really deeply upset her. I wish I had talked to her. I wished I knew then how devoted she was. I try not to hurt people. I love Tatum. If I had any idea\u2026<br /> <br /> Anyway, I am digressing. The meeting went well. We all had laughs. Karen was a bit serious, Sara a bit silly, and Coffee and Tatum managed to get along. It was a good meal. <br /> <br /> Then clubbing. Sara managed to step in and get a lot done. As much as a lot of us tease the girl for her libido, she can get things done. She is clever, she is cunning, and I love her very much. Anyway, she found Miranda talking to Maria Smith. Maria turned on the charm; she is quite good at getting men around her finger. Miranda however gave as good as she got, and soon they had thoroughly seduced each other. A good snogging later they went their separate ways, and Sara swooped in to talk to Miranda. She befriended the girl, and found out she and James dated but broke up. She got no direct leads on James, but she suspects she can learn more later. They broke up, but Miranda probably knows where he lives. <br /> <br /> Anyway, she got that information, then spoke to Maria. Maria was, no doubt, recruiting for her anti-story weavers group. I wonder how that will go with her meeting with Miranda\u2019s powerful mind. It is odd she swooped in on her so quickly after we discovered her. Is she spying on us?<br /> <br /> Anyway, for all the shit Sara gets I was the one liplocked with Coffee and Tatum at the club, while Karen did some light domming of a girl named Crystal. I can\u2019t exactly mock her when she was investigating while I was snogging, right?<br /> <br /> We came home, and most of us piled in my room. Tatum and Coffee were\u2026not ready to sleep together; they only kissed once and briefly. I was not going to insist. I am sure Sara was disappointed.<br /> <br /> I dozed off with my head on Tatum\u2019s thigh. I really feel like we are one when we are like this. All of us. I know Sara doesn\u2019t like to think it, love us as she very clearly does, but I deeply feel like it is true. It\u2019s what\u2019s given me such hope. I wonder how easily everyone else has seen the change in me? I know Sara and Karen clearly have. <br /> <br /> Karen has been a rock. She always is. Wise and mature beyond her years. I would like to take credit for that, but to be completely honest, it is more my fault. <br /> <br /> It has been good to see Tatum. She needed some family time after wintering with us, but hopefully will be spending some time around. I think she will like Coffee. Most of us do.<br /> <br /> We tease Sara, but it is good to see her desire to help James and Miranda. Miranda is disinclined to have her mind healed but could be convinced. Maybe Sara or I can.<br /> <br /> Feeling pretty good. It is a good day.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXIX</i><br /> <br /> The girls cover the session pretty well. Neither mentioned, as neither was conversing with her, that when Maria and Miranda began flirting, Catherine felt somewhat drawn to her too, feeling like she was in the presence of something powerful and awesome, and it made her weak in the knees. None of the PCs felt it though. <br /> <br /> The healing Miranda and James thing came from healing aggravated damage and regrowing limbs and such. This would sort of be the same thing on a smaller scale.<br /> <br /> I think that covers things. Comments and Questions welcome<br /> <br /> As a note, changes in the USA have me deeply concerned. I am not just up and fleeing my home, but quite honestly I have to be prepared to leave if things become dangerous. What this means for you is I might abruptly and without warning, and these campaigns end. I don\u2019t want that to happen, but I also want to live. So there you go. Sorry. Be good to yourselves, and nice to each other.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-15T10:28:37-08:00","id":1003469,"title":"","content":"I hope this doesn't cross any lines, but you shouldn't need to be sorry in the slightest. You shouldn't regret taking care of yourself or valuing your life. Just be sure to let us know when you're okay if worst comes to worst, which I sincerely hope it doesn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7372-lady-gray","name":"Lady Gray","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7372_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"59"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T01:18:11-08:00","id":1006054,"title":"","content":"I dearly hope that things do not go anywhere near the extremes you're scared of Baroness, or even begin to. If they do, however, do not feel guilty about making sure you and your family remain safe. As Lady Gray said, just let us know if you're safe should you need to leave.<br /> <br /> This also applies to everyone who plays or has played in your games as well. Nobody needs to be going through the fear that is being generated now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-21T02:12:33-08:00","id":1006071,"title":"","content":"I can promise I won't do anything rashly. I have a house, good friends, caring family, and sense of belonging. It has been what has kept me where I live. More than for myself, I hope it is unneeded. <br /> <br /> Thanks for the kind words, both of you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-27T23:11:06-08:00","id":1009199,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on the Middle Shadows. Sara\u2019s entry is actually a story, foreshadowing a guest in the campaign who will be appearing a few sessions down the line, though it does touch on the session. Natalie, while a bit fixated, has more of the recap.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXX</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> <b>'Seanchairde'</b><br /> <br /> Tommy pushed his way gently through the beaded curtains that separated Sasha\u2019s office from the rest of the family\u2019s trailer. He heard her chair scrape on the floor as she turned to see who it was. He smiled as he rounded the bookshelf. \u201cHello Sasha.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTommy.\u201d She nodded him towards the bench across from her. \u201cI was about to come looking for you. I just heard from Sara.\u201d His eyes lit up and she frowned slightly, reserved concern written on her face. \u201cTommy... I think it is a wonderful idea for you to go see her. As long as you don\u2019t set yourself up for heartbreak - she is getting married.\u201d<br /> <br /> He laid a hand on Sasha\u2019s, smiling his thanks. \u201cI know, I know. I love her, there\u2019s no denying that. And she loves me, I believe that. But I don\u2019t have any plans to swoop in and steal her back for myself. She loves a lot of people, and I wouldn\u2019t have it any other way.\u201d He shook his head, chuckling. \u201cI might try and figure out how those two ladies talked her into a wedding ring though.\u201d<br /> <br /> The young man watched his adoptive mom tuck a strand of long red hair behind her ear and saw the love in her small smile back at him. \u201cFrom what I hear, they are very persuasive. Natalie, in particular, could talk Emcee out of performing, if Sara\u2019s stories are to be believed.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThey always are. Natalie\u2019s the one that smells like strawberries, right?\u201d He held back a small smirk, thinking about Sara\u2019s description of her wives.<br /> <br /> \u201cShe is.\u201d Sasha looked at him gaugingly. \u201cAlso the one who likes men as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy blushed, shifting in his seat. \u201cRight. Uh... you wanted to talk to me about something Sara said in her email?\u201d It didn\u2019t sound like Sasha thought it wasn\u2019t going to work out, but she did look worried.<br /> <br /> Sasha sat back in her chair. \u201cYou know, you could email her as well. I\u2019m not saying I have a problem being a go-between - I agreed to for Sara\u2019s sake and she needed that for awhile. But I\u2019m sure she would love hearing from you, as much as she will love seeing you.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI...\u201d Tommy drew away into himself. So many things had changed recently and he had no idea how he\u2019d even start going into them over email. He needed to be there with her, and to know whether or not his suspicions were correct.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019m sorry Da - Tommy. I didn\u2019t mean to push. I did want to let you know that it looks like your plan will work fine, surprise and all.\u201d She glanced back at her computer. \u201cThis is a fairly busy time for her, but if you head out after out shows this weekend, you should catch her between jobs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy nodded, his smile coming back. \u201cDid a break come in that pyromaniac case?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sasha\u2019s brow knit. Tommy was pretty sure he had an idea why Sasha was so worried. \u201cYes. They found his ex-girlfriend and Sara think she and Natalie can talk her into setting up a meeting with him.\u201d She pressed her lips together in a thin line. \u201cI do worry about her, but she claims she can curse the man to keep him from setting any fires or blowing anything up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe\u2019ll be alright, Sasha. She\u2019ll have that medic guy and her Little Red, right?\u201d Tommy grinned at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cDoc,\u201d Sasha looked at him chidingly, \u201cwill be there I\u2019m sure - Sara had some things to say about convincing him to not go in with violence at the forefront of his mind. I don\u2019t believe her axe wielding friend will be there however.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy took the chiding with good humor. \u201cLike I said, I\u2019m sure she\u2019ll be fine. And hey, maybe I\u2019ll get there in time to help out.\u201d He didn\u2019t have any lofty expectations of how much help he\u2019d be - Sara had been dealing with things like this for awhile now. But he certainly wouldn\u2019t shrink from trying.<br /> <br /> His adopted mother raised a dubious eyebrow at him. \u201cPerhaps. She does have something else going on this Saturday that she was cagey about. I got the feeling she wouldn\u2019t have mentioned it all, if not for her concern for Natalie. I believe their friend Deanna might be in some sort of trouble.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that the jealous one, or Batman?\u201d Tommy\u2019s concerned expression belied his light tone. If Sara was being cagey about something, given how much she usually told Sasha, it was probably serious. If he was right, that was. Everyone knew Sara had inherited her grandmother\u2019s Sight and her power over curses. Tommy had just recently learned about the real supernatural, not just the superstitions that were common in the troupe, and he was pretty certain she\u2019d inherited something more when her father had died. Still, the only evidence he had was what he had read between the lines of what she said to people who weren\u2019t supernatural themselves. <br /> <br /> \u201cBatman.\u201d Sasha shook her head. \u201cYou will have to do a better job remembering her troupe mate\u2019s names if you wish to impress her with how attentive you\u2019ve been to her letters.\u201d She ended her warning with a stern look, the effect only slightly marred by the hint of a smile persistently playing around the corner of her lips.<br /> <br /> Tommy ducked his head, acknowledging her point. \u201cAs you say. I\u2019m glad it looks like it will work out - I\u2019d hate to come so close and have to just pass her by again.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sasha nodded. Tommy could see the unasked questions in her eyes - probably about what had changed recently that arranging this visit became so important and why he wanted to surprise her - but, as per family tradition, she didn\u2019t pry. He was glad, since he didn\u2019t have an answer for either question. The first because he wasn\u2019t ready to talk about it yet. And the second because he didn\u2019t know. It just seemed right.<br /> <br /> After a moment, Sasha asked a different question. \u201cSo what brought you here? Unless you were hoping for word from Sara?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I was, at that.\u201d Tommy chuckled. \u201cBut I came by because Old Tommy says we need to put in an order for more ink and needles. And I\u2019ll need to make a \u2018sundries\u2019 run when we get to town.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe couldn\u2019t wait until dinner to tell me?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy shrugged. \u201cYou know he doesn\u2019t like to talk business during family time.\u201d<br /> <br /> She rolled her eyes. \u201cHe and your father both. We lose half the efficiency of a family run business that way.\u201d She shook her head. \u201cTell him I put in the order yesterday.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cAs you wish.\u201d Tommy stood and bent down to give his adoptive mother a kiss on the cheek. \u201cThank you. For everything.\u201d<br /> <br /> She smiled up at him. \u201cAnything for a son of mine.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 17th 2011<br /> <br /> Deanna is in danger. This chills me to the core. I care about her. She is a little off, but not in a bad way. This is bad.<br /> <br /> Mi Hyun approached her in a Whole Foods, and she found herself alone in the market. Mi Hyun told her what to play and when. And made it clear she knew Deanna was gathering information and that she would disappear if she did not cooperate. Deanna agreed to do so. Mi Hyun then left, and people began returning to that part of the supermarket again.<br /> <br /> Deanna was not scared. She was excited. I am the one who is scared. Scared this dear little girl would be hurt. This wonderful person with so much potential. I feel sick. I wanted to tell her to drop it, to back away from the case and not look back, but I couldn\u2019t. She feels she wants to do this. What can I say?<br /> <br /> We discussed things a long time. My favored plan was Deanna vanishing before the show, and Mi Hyun having to step in to DJ herself and we could jump her. Doc favored a bolder plan, which we decided to follow. Doc would use Phantasmal Shroud to disguise as Deanna and make a big deal of not playing the right songs. When Mi Hyun went after him, we would jump her, I from Boneyard and Alexia, Sara, Noriko (and maybe Coffee) hiding inside. My first idea was for Coffee to hide Deanna in the underworld, but we wound up going with Deanna hiding in the house, guarded by Chandra in her combat form and possibly Tavia and/or Coffee. We would get Docenna to the station by having Doc, Deanna, and I separately go to the Theater while Doc was disguised as a Goth girl. When Doc would become Deanna and I would use a backcombed wig and make up to sneak Deanna out as the Goth girl. <br /> <br /> Regardless I worry about Deanna. I care about her. I want her to have a long life. The world quite frankly needs women like her in it. And quite frankly so do I.<br /> <br /> The day started contentious. Sara tried to approach Doc about approaching James and his loved ones in a positive way. I love Doc, but he has no grasp of how he comes off to people at all. Even despite repeatedly making references to killing and/or torturing James pretty much every time he came up, he felt he was not being violet or judgmental or provocative. Sara has the patience of a saint (and libido of a sinner) so she stuck with it, and Doc eventually agreed to watch his tongue around Miranda and Rawl, and James himself.<br /> <br /> For her part, Tatum was twitterpated by Miranda\u2019s picture on Karen\u2019s phone. Apparently she did not notice her. I am clearly nicely distracting. <br /> <br /> When Doc finally acquiesced, we moved to discussing the Story Weavers. Well, we talked about what Coffee had not seen, and Sleeping Giant came up. While discussing that, we talked about having the Story Weavers train some, since we could actually tell the rangers what was going on. And they could meet Werewolves. It sounded useful, and we explained a Verge to Coffee. <br /> <br /> There was also talk of the boat, but Doc pointed out it is too windy yet. It is too goddamn cold here in the Northeast.<br /> <br /> We split up after breakfast, and the Trio went off for who knows what while Doc showed Coffee the library, Sara called Rawl, and I went to call Deirdre. Except Deanna messaged me first. That lead to the whole clusterfuck I started this entry with. I did message Deirdre after, which got that squared away.<br /> <br /> So tomorrow night at Murder Ballads or Gotham Citi we will meet up with Miranda to get contact info for James. Rawl is already en route up. Hopefully to confront on Saturday or Sunday. The precise details will depend on Miranda. I know Sara will make another pitch for healing her mind. And hopefully have some fun.<br /> <br /> Tonight we went to see <i>Insidious</i>, the whole group, which was funny to have a bunch of Sin-Eaters in a movie like that. Coffee commented it was a shame we could not slow walk into the theater, as badass as we were, especially the Gothic contingent of course.<br /> <br /> I thought about meeting Deanna tonight after, but I think we will hook up at Murder Ballads. I hope she will be okay. I never thought I would miss seeing the soon to be dead in mirrors. I will check her marks carefully. Honestly it was a pretty quiet evening for me. Gave Karen a foot massage, but not really in the mood for much.<br /> <br /> And we all know that can\u2019t last, don\u2019t we?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXX</i><br /> <br /> What\u2019s going on in Sara\u2019s journal will be clearer in time.<br /> <br /> Mi Hyun was the Angel or Demon stalking Katie before, in case that needs reminding.<br /> <br /> Um, not much more needing explanation. Twitterpated is an awesome word. Enjoying the story dealing with the psychics, partially because it is bringing Catherine out more, and Catherine is fun.<br /> <br /> Looks like an email for Sara and Diary entry for Natalie next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-11T02:07:21-08:00","id":1015608,"title":"","content":"Let\u2019s check in with our local Sin-Eaters. It's an eventful weekend as they look to foil and evil robot and stop a dangerous firestarter (twisted firestarter. Oh God now it is playing in my head)<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sasha - <br /> <br /> I do believe it has been a productive 24 hours, for all the lazing about that happened. Such is the way of detective work via social engineering however. But thanks to some sweet talking, the reassurance of a trained medic and assistance from an unexpected direction, I do believe we will have our meeting with the firebug Sunday, like I\u2019d hoped.<br /> <br /> Most of yesterday I spent reading up on things in the library, making sure I did what footwork I could to prepare for our discussion the next two days. After all, our connection to Miranda was via Murder Ballad, so step 2 of Plan \u2018The Fastest Way to a Man\u2019s Ear is Through his Ex-Girlfriend\u2019 (we need a more concise name for that really) had to wait until nightfall. We were all busy enough - Natalie had her v-logs to prepare, Catherine checked in with the police to see if there were any cases she could help out with, Noriko and Chandra had kukri fighting practice scheduled (they are not bad at it and it was not bad to watch - Emcee could definitely turn it into an act), Doc was in the library as well, drawing up a blueprint of some kind and Alexia had cookies to bake.<br /> <br /> The poor dear - she decided to make cookies for the Murder Ballads staff, but worried about them being perturbed by receiving cookies from a random patron. However, when she asked Natalie, Natalie pointed out that she was a well-known celebrity there, and that Alexia, as part of her posse, was not just a random patron. Alexia was... somewhat put out. It did spark some discussion over what the proper word for a group of goths was that I believe Natalie is still musing over. And it prompted Alexia to were a simply beautiful white sundress to Murder Ballads, that worked wonders under the black-light of the dance floor. It was almost enough to distract me from my task at hand.<br /> <br /> The task at hand being, of course, to speak with Miranda again. She seemed on more stable emotion footing - no odd, spiritually significant interactions with random women for her last night. Well, except for me, but I\u2019m hardly destabilizing (tell Emily to stop laughing!). It was fun chatting with her just in general, but eventually I did have to bring up the touchy subject. She was still reluctant to commit to anything, but she did promise to ask him to meet us. She does seem to really care about him, which is marked in the plus column as far as I\u2019m concerned. I did my best to reassure her that we did want to help him, and keep him safe. I pointed out that he could even choose the meeting location, whatever would make him the most comfortable, not pointing out that we\u2019d have the upper hand either way, with our curses.<br /> <br /> I also managed to at least give serious consideration to being healed. Like I was afraid of, she didn\u2019t quite have the conscious self-preservation instinct like she did the conscious taking care of others instinct. When I pointed out that she ran the risk of burning herself out, she asked if she wouldn\u2019t deserve it at that point, and what if she needed that extra power to help someone. It speaks well of her, at least. But a sacrifice made by accident doesn\u2019t smell as sweet, and as for the latter, if she truly wishes it, if she needs it and wills it and has cause, she will have that power again. I know this to be true and I only hope she believes me. <br /> <br /> On the other side of things, there\u2019s no denying that her abilities, as horrific as their unlocking was, have given her an edge, socially, an edge she\u2019d never had before. I tried to ease her away from that, encouraging her to grow on her own from the starting point this period of her life has given her. I also (after consulting with Catherine to make sure it was alright) let her know that Catherine had similar issues and some applicable coping skills. Life will not be so easy for her after she is healed, but I believe it will be better.<br /> <br /> The last hurdle was her feelings (quite understandable) about healing. When I spoke of it, it brought to her mind memories of the surgery that horrible place performed on her. And even worse, the ones they performed on others. James and Miranda, they were the success stories. They came out alive. I brought Doc over so he could describe the healing he\u2019d be doing, a far more natural/spiritual process than a surgical one. She had some hesitation about the religious connotations, still, I think she was reassured overall.<br /> <br /> It wasn\u2019t all firebugs and healing at Murder Ballads last night though. A few of the Underwater Storyweavers Club were there - Alexia ran her training in the park plan with them, which they were OK with so long as there wasn\u2019t actually camping. Well, Tracy was OK with camping as long as there were plenty of sleeping bag cuddles, cause she is my kinda girl. They also discussed today, and decided to have the whole club chill at the House with Deanna, to keep them all safe. Somehow in the course of all that, Natalie got called Deanna\u2019s \u2018pet cougar\u2019 by Clarissa. Natalie was rather clinging on her hero of the hour, but she was concerned, and rightly so. Clarissa is still not dealing particularly well to her best friend branching out quite so much.<br /> <br /> Anyhow, after chatting some more with Miranda, I also danced some with Elizabeth and hung out with Cindy. I wound up heading home with her - it was my turn to \u2018do the walk of shame\u2019 apparently (I asked her if she\u2019d met me) since she\u2019d been by mine last time. I certainly didn\u2019t mind - she makes a delicious breakfast. It was a nice lazy morning.<br /> <br /> The afternoon didn\u2019t go quite so lazily. I got a call from Miranda shortly after I got back to the house, to let me know that Marie had approached her about James. They\u2019re even having dinner tonight to talk about it (and maybe other things). I didn\u2019t wanna play tug of war with Miranda, so I let her go and called up Maria, after Alexia checked to make sure it was alright to pass along the number.<br /> <br /> Maria is, as I mentioned before, worried about Barry getting \u2018influence\u2019 over the kids in the Underwater Storyweavers Club. She figured getting Miranda and James to join her group would give her a strong counter move. I will consider it quite an accomplishment if I can forge peace between those two. Until then however, I am simply hoping to do what I can to make her feel safer without moving against Barry. I think I succeed in that somewhat today, and I am confident that she will not try to convince Miranda not to be healed. She also promised to be a second voice suggesting a meeting with James soon, trying for the \u2018tomorrow\u2019 angle. So hopefully this will work out for the best.<br /> <br /> Tonight however is another matter entirely. Our plans are all laid - we will be lying in wait at the radio station, Deanna and the Storyweavers will be at the house, as safe as we can make them without being right there with them. In being honest, I don\u2019t have much hope for a conversation out of this one - if we catch her, it will be because she storms up on us in a murderous rage. Perhaps we will have a moment to discover why she\u2019s done what she\u2019s done. We\u2019ll see.<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 19th 2011<br /> <br /> Eleven days till Walpurgis, a Month and Three Days till I get married in ceremony.<br /> <br /> I was hoping spending the night with Deanna would make me less worried about her. Just more relaxed and generally laid back about things, and making having her close would make me less inclined to sit around and worry. Not the case.<br /> <br /> Getting ahead of myself again. Not doing like last time. Quiet day, the 18th, did enough Vlogs to keep me current for the next week. Some reviews, some life stuff, some general stuff. Had one where Tatum and Coffee were dancing the whole time in the background, another with them sitting giving commentary, and of course, one with Karen and I. <br /> <br /> Oh, at breakfast it came up (after talk of Tavia being the Lady of the House and Murder, two things that go uncomfortably well together) that Alexia does not want to be part of my \u201cposse\u201d with regard to Murder Ballads. I told her when we went to Sweet Surrender I was part of her posse. Karen claimed it was a Southern-Ism, which Coffee disputed. I think I picked it up in California. Or failing that Nevada. Probably California, been there longer.<br /> <br /> Anyway, it also came up we don\u2019t have an agreed upon collective name for a group of Goths. I like Brood myself, but Clove, Misery, or Pout also works. Maybe I can decide and start a trend on my channel! <br /> <br /> Catherine had gone to see if anyone needed help at the police station, missing persons especially. Noriko and Chandra went shopping. Alexia baked, Doc worked on some sort of mechanical devices, Sara hit the library. Eventually we got ready and headed out for the night.<br /> <br /> Murder Ballads was hopping. I love Murder Ballads; no place makes me feel at home. A majestic Gothic club, there really is nothing like it. Alexia felt so much appreciation she brought them cookies. That will give her points. Also in notes on generosity, Doc bought some hipsters Absinthe. No idea why he did that. Doc is pretty random sometimes.<br /> <br /> Maybe a Darkening of Goths?<br /> <br /> Karen hung out with Catherine some, apparently having her fail to pick out which band playing was The Cure. Alexia, Tatum, and Coffee danced. I am pretty sure Noriko was telling Chandra stories of people she has killed here. Appropriate. They are doing this thing where Noriko speaks Hindi and Chandra speaks Japanese, learning each other\u2019s languages. It is neat.<br /> <br /> I spent the evening making out with Deanna and dancing with her a little.<br /> <br /> Sara made her way to Miranda, and struck up a conversation. I was not privy, but I think she convinced Miranda to consider having Doc fix her issue. She brought Doc over, who let her look into his head about the process, and gave her Catherine\u2019s name as a good reference for someone who learned to use her powers to relate to people without the surgery. Sara did well, I think. I am really proud of how she handled this. I will have to tell her so.<br /> <br /> Alexia visited Tracy, Deanna and Clarissa. Well, Tracy and Clarissa, Deanna and I were joined at the hip I think. I believe they are all going to the house tonight while we deal with Mi Hyun. Fortunately the story weavers\u2019 morale is still high. <br /> <br /> A Gloom of Goths?<br /> <br /> Eventually we went our separate ways. Sara went with Cindy Toc. Tatum went to try a night with Coffee see how things went just the two of them. I went with Deanna. Her parents had spontaneously left town, which was worrying today, but last night meant sleeping in her bed not at the townhouse.<br /> <br /> Deanna is a sweetheart. She will never really be a major relationship, but I foresee us being friends for a long time. She and I are, however, incredibly sexually compatible. As much so as Karen and I. Karen and I have a deeper emotional connection of course, we are compatible far more than sexually. She is a wife I need. Deanna is pretty awesome though.<br /> <br /> So she fucked me for most of the night. It was awesome. I still have the marks of her nails down my back. I admired them again earlier today. It was a wonderful night. Passions blazed, souls embraced along with bodies. When we slept after, we embraced. We said the sweetest lies. It was glorious.<br /> <br /> Then, while I was happily leaving, I saw Mi Hyun parked at the church across the street.<br /> <br /> She escaped quickly; she was behind the wheel. I was too shaken to pursue. I went back and reported this. Sara held me. Sara, once again, impresses. She supported me when I needed her, and it was wonderful. <br /> <br /> Sara got a message from Miranda that Maria Smith was taking her out for dinner, and had asked about James as well. This put Sara a bit on edge, but she did not give Miranda any specific advice. She did get Maria\u2019s number from Alexia and call herself. Maria was still paranoid about Barry, and insisted she wanted the powered psychics to even the odds, but professed an unwillingness to go toe to toe with a Krewe of Sin-Eaters. Which was unfortunate, as she felt undoing this surgery would weaken her position. This unfortunately put Sara in the position where telling her not to implied threat, but Sara pivoted and managed to convince her not to without threatening her, even indirectly. As I say, Sara has been amazing lately. <br /> <br /> A Belfry of Goths, maybe. Dismal?<br /> <br /> Today has been getting ready for tonight. Coffee will be with the Krewe, as will Noriko. I will be in the trunk of a car a mile away. Vulnerable I guess, but a risk I am willing to take. Maybe I can bring Troy.<br /> <br /> I wish I would be with Deanna, but my Krewe needs me. I need to trust in the Story Weavers and Chandra to keep her safe. In case worse comes to worse, I am sending Karen and Tatum to the townhouse. It is not what they want, but if everything goes to hell I want my wife and Mistress safe. <br /> <br /> Now I must focus on the task at hand.<br /> <br /> A Dreary of Goths?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXI</i><br /> <br /> It\u2019s true. I could not find any Internet consensus on a group of Goths. What do you think?<br /> <br /> I don\u2019t think much of the session requires too much more information. Doc\u2019s work was part of a long term project as he tries to figure out the energy the Mothman referred to. If you have more questions, ask away. Comments and Questions Welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T10:45:51-08:00","id":1017148,"title":"","content":"Perhaps a Clique of Goths?<br /> <br /> I've been meaning to ask, are you writing anything for 2nd edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-25T01:05:53-08:00","id":1021894,"title":"","content":"ThomasM&gt; Not yet, but I very much hope to. The interest is very much appreciated, thank you. ^_^<br /> <br /> The Middle Shadows Krewe ambushes Mi Hyun in the radio station. They emerge victorious, but do not emerge unscathed.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sara sat in the darkness, her balisong knife held tight in a shaking hand. The Cold Wind fluttering around her was obviously the better choice for an ambush but ironically enough she felt exposed without the bright light of a Pyre Flame in her chest. She always dreaded going into a fight, and the speed and reflexes Pyre Flame granted her usually helped bolster her against that dread.<br /> <br /> It was not a long wait, only a few minutes after Deanna\u2019s prerecorded message of defiance aired. The entity the burst into the lobby was terrifying, a six and a half foot tall robot with silvered skin, covered in barbs and spikes. It had four arms, two that ended in blades, one holding a shield and the other ending in a massive cannon. Three faces with glowing red eyes screamed at the krewe as it stood in the doorway and fired an explosive into the lobby of the radio station.<br /> <br /> The blast hit everyone and the station was filled with ghostly fog, though Doc and Alexia\u2019s Shroud armor meant less was coming from them. As Alexia tried to wrestle the thing inside the room, hoping to stop another explosion. Meanwhile, Sara crept in, feeling like she was moving in molasses. But the Cold Winds did well by her, and her strike against the robot would have made any of her teachers proud. Her look of triumph quickly turned to despair however, as her knife shattered the silvery skin, causing the rest of it to slough off, leaving behind slick looking armored plates.<br /> <br /> She took a hurried step back, but the thing\u2019s attention was on the transformed Noriko, the four armed Alexia and eventually Doc, as he threw around curses that rebounded back to him and eventually used Rage to tear into its metallic flesh. Sara struck again, but her knife skittered of its armored skin, as did Noriko\u2019s claws.<br /> <br /> The thing\u2019s three pairs of eyes flashed around the scene, taking in the krewe\u2019s numbers, and how they seemed unhurt. It fired again, hitting everyone and itself as well. When all its opponents were still standing, a dull sense of acceptance came over its face, and it self-destructed in a fiery blaze. Sara felt a moment of extreme pain, then, nothing.<br /> <br /> The man\u2019s heart beat fast. The young woman in a rabbit mask was holding a gun on him with a steady hand, while the other two young men, in a deer mask and an elephant mask respectively, looted his store. His wife was on the other side of the store, still standing in the doorway near the back, where she\u2019d come in at the noise. <br /> <br /> His pulse hitched as he heard the boys talking. \u201cShe is a pretty fine piece of ass, even for her age. Think the old man will mind if we borrow her for a bit?\u201d<br /> <br /> The one in the deer mask chuckled cruelly. \u201cI don\u2019t think he\u2019ll have a choice, eh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Trying to move as little as possible, he groped around for something he could throw. He found a candy bar, the biggest thing in arm\u2019s reach. Once he had it firmly in hand, he looked over at his wife, and mouthed \u201cRun,\u201d before he threw it as hard as he could at the rabbit mask. He did get to see his wife get through the door and away as he fell to his knees, two bullets in his chest. The last thing he saw was the elephant masked man\u2019s baseball whistling towards his head.<br /> <br /> Sara woke with a shuddering gasp to find herself in Natalie\u2019s arms. The strawberry scented woman was singing softly, another of the Irish lullabies Sara had taught her, and gently brushing her hair. Sara took another few difficult breaths, pulling herself up a little with Natalie\u2019s help to curl up in her lap so that Sara could bury her face in her wife\u2019s shoulder. After a few moment of excruciating pain, she lifted her head slightly to look up at Natalie.<br /> <br /> \u201cNatalie? Please...?\u201d She swallowed hard.<br /> <br /> Natalie nodded, brushing her cheek softly. She carefully placed her hands on Sara\u2019s throat and squeezed until she passed out again. Sara came back to her body quickly, not wanting Natalie to have to hold her apparent corpse any longer. She sighed in relief, her burns healed and torn flesh knit back together. She gave Natalie a weak smile before curling back up in her lap, desperate for the warmth and life that Natalie\u2019s embrace offered.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sasha - <br /> <br /> Everything\u2019s fine - we dealt with the stalker and everyone\u2019s the safer for it. Unless she had accomplices, the college radio personalities no longer need to be worried about outside interference and death threats. All in all, a good evening\u2019s work.<br /> <br /> The students were pretty adorable, holing up in the house. Marie was all business, looking \u201cthe most defensible room\u201d and wanting to know all the resources that would be marshalled, and what to prepare for. Timothy, on the other hand, voted for strip poker. Tavia had my back though, and made them promise not to play strip poker without me. They decided against Truth or Dare as well, after Clarissa shared with us that as a child, she wanted to marry her dog, since she liked him more than any of the boys at school, and that Deanna might be a little fixated on that. Xerxes didn\u2019t deserve that kind of indignity.<br /> <br /> They did settle on the TV/video game room, so I\u2019m sure they entertained themselves just fine. We were out until dawn, so they were well asleep by the time we got back. That strip poker game will just have to wait. Until after we meet with James, at least. Maria did manage to talk Miranda into setting up a meeting this afternoon, so we\u2019ll be getting a lot of progress done this weekend.<br /> <br /> So, how are you guys?<br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary<br /> </b><br /> So, my wife died tonight.<br /> <br /> Okay, not specific enough. One of my wives.<br /> <br /> No, still bad.<br /> <br /> Sara died but she is fine now. Sort of. Mostly fine. I am fine. Sort of. Mostly fine.<br /> <br /> So most of the plan went according to plan. The switch with Doc and Deanna, then the setting of the ambush. I waited with Troy at the car, and the others moved in. Mi Hyun managed to shake off the attempts I made to use my Boneyard on any of her three faces. The blade covered woman made more use of her explosive launching cannon, however. The group did managed to overwhelm her, so she set off one more bomb and blew herself up. The blast killed Sara, Coffee, and Noriko. Alexia was badly hurt, Doc slightly hurt.<br /> <br /> Afterwards, Doc decided to drive around Glenwood. Alexia, Doc and I were in the car with three bodies. After about four hours, Noriko woke. Apparently her boasts she could come back were not wrong. She had to move where she could go into a beast form, and healed herself rapidly. Then after another hour Coffee and Sara woke. I was holding Sara, had been the entire time. Alexia put an arm around Coffee. Sara and Coffee were in a lot of pain, so I choked Sara out to use her Oracle. No idea who died for Sara or Coffee to come back. <br /> <br /> Noriko, for her part, was kind enough to spend the rest of the trip as an adorable kitten, riding in Doc\u2019s lap. It made things a little more bearable. Much like when she was batting Doc\u2019s hand earlier, she knows how to weaponize cuteness. <br /> <br /> When we got back, Coffee and Alexia got in what Tavia keeps calling the People Oven. The mood was so somber no one even made reference to toasted Coffee. I am glad I have different Elemental Keys for my Oracle.<br /> <br /> So\u2026this was traumatic. Even briefly, it was really hard to handle seeing Sara lifeless. But at the same time, I expected it would utterly shatter me. It didn\u2019t. Now, this was probably because I knew she would return, but\u2026at the same time, I know I am not the woman that first walked into the house. Even with one of the women I love most in the world so badly incapacitated, I was strong.<br /> <br /> But after I thought about it, I knew why. I needed to be strong for her. When I realized that, when I realized she was going to need me, like she had never needed anyone outside her first death, I drew on strength. I know I can be strong for the women I love. Sara Rowan, Karen Knight\u2026. even my dear Tatum.<br /> <br /> Sara, Coffee, Noriko, Alexia, Doc and I destroyed a horrible, mechanical creature. Coffee, Noriko, and my wife suffered horribly to do it. The second death for Coffee and Sara, the first for Noriko. Now Sara needs me.<br /> <br /> I will be there for her.<br /> <br /> I am proud of her. So very proud of her.<br /> <br /> I love her so much.<br /> <i><br /> End Session CLXXII</i><br /> <br /> So, Mi Hyun was not a weak angel. She used a variety of form powers, including the cannon to shoot exploding ordinance, and Resisters to shake off the first hit on her. Alexia did a good job dragging her inside so she could not fire explosives then run around the doorway. Doc also kept a lot of her attention after a point, even with Sara\u2019s devastating initial strike. When it did not prove to be enough, she self-destructed.<br /> <br /> It was the first death for Sara and Coffee as Sin-Eaters. Alexia was badly hurt, while Doc Bulwarked almost all the damage. Natalie was Boneyarding from some distance away, so not hurt at all. Sara did not lose further Synergy beyond the minimum.<br /> <br /> Noriko has the Resurrection Aspect as a Colony. She lost a dot of Primal-Urge, (Down to 4) but came back in four hours (Harmony 6.)<br /> <br /> Session 73 is scheduled for Christmas Day, so it will not be occurring. Due to the packed nature of Holiday time, we will not have the option of rescheduling. But <i>Balance of Shadows</i> will be back! In two weeks we will have a session as before as we close in on year seven, and a personal record for game lifespan. Thanks to everyone who has been a reader, especially those who have been following the Middle Shadows for over half a decade. Thanks for the comments. We are back in 2017. In two weeks we will get a short fiction featuring Natalie and her h\u0336a\u0336r\u0336e\u0336m\u0336 \u0336 family, and we get a better introduction to Dale/Tommy, from the earlier Sara fic, who will be played as kinda a sidekick character for Sara soon. <br /> <br /> Happy holidays. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-31T16:33:53-08:00","id":1024939,"title":"",