-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play?p=1028216#post1028216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait... I think I have been reading this for most of that time... When did that happen?</div> </div> </div> </div>The characters dying?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:32:04-08:00","id":1028232,"title":"","content":"The duration of this game and journal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-07T12:47:56-08:00","id":1028239,"title":"","content":"How did seven years go by so fast? It gets distressingly common. ^_^","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-08T13:35:54-08:00","id":1028669,"title":"","content":"Two weeks ago was Christmas Day, so there was no game. I do nonetheless have a couple short stories for you relating to the game. One is just a scene with Natalie, Karen and Tatum where we get a look inside Karen Knight\u2019s head. The other is more about Dale, who came up in a previous Sara journal. <br /> <br /> <i>Intermission</i><br /> <b><br /> Meanwhile, with Natalie</b><br /> <br /> <b>Danse Macabre </b><br /> <br /> <i>Priests and cannibals, prehistoric animals<br /> Everybody happy as the dead come home<br /> Big black nemesis, parthenogenesis<br /> No one move a muscle as the dead come home</i><br /> <br /> The furniture had been moved from the middle of the room. The dim illumination came from by a curly black light bulb, and the sound of the closing lines of <i>Nemesis</i> were not only audible, but you could feel it in your teeth.<br /> <br /> Karen Knight leaned against the wall, watching her wife Natalie, dance. The Goth thrashed around violently, literally throwing herself one direction than the other. Tatum Gillis sat on a chair near Karen, breathing heavily, wiping sweat from her forehead with a towel. Despite being nearly a decade younger and in a leotard rather than her mistress\u2019s boots, leather skirt and leather vest, she was utterly exhausted. <br /> <br /> Karen\u2019s mind was full. Natalie and Sara had put themselves in harms way. Sara had died, temporarily. Natalie had means of dealing with the pressure, some better than others. Drugs. Submission. Dancing. Karen not so much. After all, it was not her place to show weakness. The youngest woman in the room was the adult here, and usually she relished the role. Usually.<br /> <br /> <i>Priests and cannibals, prehistoric animals<br /> Everybody happy as the dead come home<br /> Big black nemesis, parthenogenesis<br /> No one move a muscle as the dead come home</i><br /> <br /> Karen did not want to admit it, but she was thankful not to have seen Sara die. Coffee had too, and Noriko. She brushed her nose. Noriko seemed to have everyone\u2019s attention these days. Usually she didn\u2019t mind, but recently she was not sure if it bugged her more Natalie had slept with Doc again, or Noriko. Still, Noriko was hard to hate. Usually.<br /> <br /> Her wife\u2019s face was blank. Green and Blue looked ahead and Natalie\u2019s aggressive dancing continued. She had asked them to come down with her to dance while Sara needed some time. Tatum had been brave through <i>Cities in the Dust</i> and <i>Shake Your Blood</i>, but <i>Nemesis</i> had proven too much. When Karen saw the song selection she knew she would not be keeping up with Natalie tonight. It probably involved a little cocaine. At least it wasn\u2019t heroin. <br /> <br /> <i>Priests and cannibals, prehistoric animals<br /> Everybody happy as the dead come home<br /> Big black nemesis, parthenogenesis<br /> No one move a muscle as the dead come home</i><br /> <br /> Natalie showed no sign of stopping. Karen blew bangs from her face. It was, at least, enjoyable to watch the danse macabre taking place in front of her. The final strains of <i>Nemesis</i> faded away, and Tatum began to stand, ready to go back out. But then, <i>Temple of Love</i> began to play, much longer than Tatum\u2019s endurance could bear. Ofra Haza\u2019s keening vocals filled the room from beyond the grave.<br /> <br /> \u201cFuck This, I am out. Up for a shower.\u201d<br /> <i><br /> With the fire from the fireworks up above me<br /> With a gun for a lover and a shot for the pain at hand<br /> You run for cover in the temple of love<br /> You run for another but still the same<br /> For the wind will blow my name across this land</i><br /> <br /> Karen\u2019s eyes followed Tatum leaving. \u201cSee you soon, love.\u201d Then turned back on Natalie. She had slowed down a bit, to match the music, before speeding up again as the song did.<br /> <br /> Karen thought about getting another drink, but Natalie or Sara might need her. Sucks being the adult sometimes. But a small smile crossed her face as Natalie danced across the room. Her little family was a lot to deal with, but Karen wouldn\u2019t trade them for anything. She\u2019d go up for Sara in a moment, but for the moment the devil in a black dress watched over.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Meanwhile, with Sara</b><br /> <br /> He was alone. Oh, he could still hear the slapping sounds of his father\u2019s studded belt coming down hard onto his calloused hand, but it was far off and not precisely comforting. As he took step after step into the fetid swamp, the slapping sounds faded and he was fully alone.<br /> <br /> It was hard to take a breath in the thick air. He moved slowly, wrapping his arms around himself. The swamp was silent, not even bird sounds or buzzing insects to break the isolation, just the wet schlorping noises his bare feet made in the waterlogged ground. <br /> <br /> He picked up the pace before he heard the sound of another set of footprints, a slithering noise intermittent with the four legged motion. He knew what was coming. He knew he couldn\u2019t escape it, but he had to try, no matter how his lungs burned, no matter how hard it became to drag his feet from the sucking mud, no matter how the tree branches whipped his back and stomach in that same pattern, that same pattern over and over and over again.<br /> <br /> The large gator snapped at his heels. He bit his tongue to keep from screaming and his foot caught in a root. He hit the ground hard, rolling in the mud. He scrambled forward on all fours, just waiting for the winged monster to swoop down at him. He wouldn\u2019t scream. He wouldn\u2019t...<br /> <br /> He sat up in his bed, gulping air. His panic didn\u2019t subside as he looked around the small room, not recognizing anything. A small sound escaped him when he realized someone was at the door. <br /> <br /> \u201cA nightmare, buddy?\u201d The strange man\u2019s voice helped him remember how he\u2019d gotten there. The man had picked him up from the side of the road and fed him dinner as they drove to the nearest town. The boy had fallen asleep in the bed he\u2019d been given, despite his best efforts. It had been a long day of walking after all and his first full belly in a long time.<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t respond to the man. It was too late to pretend he was asleep, but still he slowly laid back down and curled up under the covers, his whole body shaking. \u201cIt\u2019s OK, everybody has them sometimes. Can I come in?\u201d He paused, waiting for a response that didn\u2019t come. He did notice the boy wince and pulled the covers closer. He frowned. \u201cThis is your room now, son, and as long as it is, nobody comes in without your permission. Alright?\u201d<br /> <br /> The boy frowned, confused. He let go of the covers, remaining still and tense. The man smiled and sat down just outside the door. \u201cYou know, when I have nightmares and get scared, I get all warm under my blankets too. It always makes me feel better to be all warm and snug in my bed.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man kept talking, moving from topic to topic, most of which the small boy didn\u2019t understand. But his voice was warm and soothing, and the man never moved past the doorway, so gradually the boy relaxed. The man sighed when he heard the kid\u2019s breathing move into the regularity of sleep. \u201cAh, kid, what are we gonna do about you?\u201d He got to his feet stiffly and looked sadly into the room before turning and going back to his own bed.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> The boy sat on a seat outside the loud man\u2019s office. He was in there with an old woman, speaking about him. He kicked his feet idly - the seat was tall enough for an adult to sit comfortably - and listened.<br /> <br /> \u201cCan you believe what that waitress told us? Who could do that to a child, to his own flesh and blood?\u201d The man was incredulous. His tone turned angry. \u201cLeaving him on the side of the road, swamp in either direction. And who knows what else! The poor kid is terrified of people. He hasn't even said a word in the past two days.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old woman hummed but didn\u2019t say anything. The boy pulled his legs up into the chair and wrapped his arms around them. The anger crackling in the other room drove out the meaning of what he heard from his mind.<br /> <br /> \u201cEvil! He thinks the boy is evil.\u201d The man\u2019s voice rose to a yell. \u201cWhat kind of foolishness is that? To be afraid of your own son.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old woman waited until the man finished stomping around the room, speaking in a measured tone. \u201cHe surely only saw his own evil reflected in the eyes of the child.\u201d The man began to speak but cut himself off shortly. The old woman continued. \u201cBut only a fool does not fear that which peers from the darkness.\u201d<br /> <br /> There was a pause. \u201cSo, Grainne, you think he is something to be feared?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe will be.\u201d The old woman\u2019s voice was matter-of-fact. \u201cBut he is someone who needs to be loved, right now.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man chuckled. The boy frowned, confused. He wasn\u2019t used to anger dissipating so quickly. \u201cHe has come to the right place then.\u201d The man took a deep breath. \u201cHe will be making a home with us then? Provided the boy is willing, of course.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old woman stood up. \u201cIt is your decision, Emcee, of course. He will find a way to the path he needs to take, whatever you decide, but fate has led him to us.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cMy decision, of course.\u201d The loud man had a smile in his voice. \u201cThe boy will stay, until he chooses a path that differs.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cVery good.\u201d The woman moved towards the door. \u201cI will speak to him.\u201d<br /> <br /> The old woman walked out of the office and closed the door behind her. She reached out towards the boy and placed a hand on his head. After a moment, he started, realizing he hadn\u2019t instinctively flinched away from her hand. She drew her hand back, slowly and calmly.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou will find a good home here, boy. Trust the one who sees.\u201d<br /> <br /> He looked up at her inquisitively, head tilted and eyebrows high. She chuckled.<br /> <br /> \u201cYes, I am the one who sees.\u201d She held out a hand. \u201cCome, boy. You should meet my granddaughter.\u201d<br /> <br /> He smiled hesitantly at her hand, unmoving. She waited patiently. Eventually, he reached out slowly to tuck his hand into hers, slipping off his seat to stand up. They walked together out of the trailer.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Tommy stretched, rolling his shoulders, before climbing into bed. It had been a hard day of work setting up camp, but he was a strong 18 year old and well used to that kind of work. After that had been the celebration of the 13th anniversary of his being picked up by the troupe. All in all, it had been a tiring enough day that he was asleep quickly, falling into the deep sleep of dreaming right away.<br /> <br /> He was alone. He could hear crowds of people muttering indistinctly, a few of the gasps of horror he was so familiar with his face provoking, and some jeering laughter, but they were far off and not at all comforting. As he moved hesitantly forward into the fetid swamp, the faint sounds faded completely and he was completely alone.<br /> <br /> The air barely moved around him, suffocating and thick. He moved slowly, his hands clenching into fists and relaxing, timed with the beating of his heart that pounded in his ears. His heart was one of only two noises in the wide swamp which was abandoned by animal and insect life alike. The other was the thick wet noises his booted feet made as he pulled them up out of the marshy ground. <br /> <br /> He slowed to a stop, turning in place to look over the wide expanses of humid trackless wilderness. Right on cue came the slithering, four legged footsteps, always behind him, whichever way he turned. He knew what was coming. He knew he couldn\u2019t escape it, and he had, all of a sudden, decided that he wasn\u2019t going to try. He wasn\u2019t going to run, the fetid air burning his lungs, his feet taking more and more effort to be pulled from the sucking mud. He wasn\u2019t going to charge through the scratching, clawing tree branches, dodging every upturned root but the last one.<br /> <br /> The large gator cocked its head inquisitively at the still young man. His chest heaved, betraying his nervousness as he looked the winged monster in the eye. It yawned, its mouth opening wide as it moved closer and closer, taking flight off the nearest hillock to glide around him in circles. He kept his eyes on it, waiting for it to strike. When it did, he didn\u2019t scream.<br /> <br /> -----------------------------------<br /> <br /> Tommy waited in the shadows, feeling his Horror\u2019s Hunger as it grumbled. He needed to feed, but he wanted to right target, the one he was sure was here. The corners of his lips upturned slightly when he saw his mark, finishing up a soda as he stepped out of his apartment building. Tommy moved out into the street, walking purposefully towards the young man, his head down.<br /> <br /> The Beast sidestepped at the last moment so that they collided, the force of it spinning them around a little. \u201cHey, guy, watch where you\u2019re going!\u201d his target yelled. When he caught sight of Tommy\u2019s scaled face, he added in an derisive undertone, \u201cFreak.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy\u2019s eyes darted over the man\u2019s sneering face. This was definitely the one he wanted - he recognized the scar down his cheek and remembered who left it and why. He said a few words in Gaelic, \u201cT\u00e1 t\u00fa i d'aonar.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man shoved him away, hard enough that Tommy lost his footing and hit the ground. \u201cYou\u2019re in America. Speak English.\u201d He threw his soda can at the teenager and turned to walk away.<br /> <br /> Tommy winced away from the thrown can, so it bounced off the side of his head instead of his face. He sat up, but shifted over while still crouched down to pick up the can as he watched the man leave. A sinister smile crept across his face as he crushed the can.<br /> <br /> A few days later, the man was stumbling down an alley. He looked bedraggled, his tie loose and suit rumpled as he glanced around wildly. He heard the swooping noise of a large pair of wings behind him, but when he turned, nothing was there. A clicking noise came from over his shoulder, something like claws tapping on the asphalt. He turned again, sharply, and Tommy was there in front of him.<br /> <br /> \u201cYou! I keep... You\u2019re following me.\u201d The man\u2019s chest was heaving and his eyes widened suddenly with a sudden realization. \u201cYou did this to me!\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy chuckled, a deep, rumbling sound. The ground beneath the man\u2019s feet grew soft and damp. He took a step back and froze, caught in Tommy\u2019s gaze. His eyes rolled around in their sockets, letting him catch glimpses of fluttering cloth and brightly colored banners. After a moment, that gypsy brat who\u2019d cut his face a couple of years ago danced in the corner of his eyes.<br /> <br /> Perched on a short wall nearby, Tommy grinned viciously, sharp teeth showing in an impossibly wide smile, when he saw recognition finally appear in the young man\u2019s face. He moved behind the man to whisper in his ear. \u201cYou shouldn\u2019t have done that.\u201d<br /> <br /> The man bolted. Tommy followed, gliding from dumpster to windowsill to wall, circling around his target. Occasionally, he would dive down at his prey, provoking another burst of fear-fueled speed, always letting him stay just ahead of his claws then leaping away, his heavy body sliding through the thick air. Until the last time, when the man collapsed in place, curled up into a ball and quivering. Then Tommy stepped back, slinking further into his swamp, his Horror sated.<br /> <br /> <i>End Intermission</i><br /> <br /> Tommy/Dale will be a sidekick for Sara\u2019s player, sort of like Fenric is in <i>The Golden Eagle</i>. Sara\u2019s player gets normal XP for the session which they can spend on Sara or Dale, otherwise Dale is a starting Beast. While a Beast to a Sin-Eater is nothing like a Ghoul to a Vampire, This game is seven years old almost and the PCs are Psyche 7 and have hundreds of XP. A starting character is probably going to have neat tricks but be weak by comparison. And <i>Balance of Shadows</i> remains thematically <b>Geist</b>, not crossover, just like having Chandra or Noriko hasn\u2019t changed that (though they are GM controlled NPCs) <br /> <br /> Music referenced in the Natalie story was <i>Nemisis </i>by Shriekback, <i>Cities in the Dust</i> by Siouxsie and the Banshees, <i>Shake Your Blood</i> by Probot (maybe not have the kids in the room for that one, the one Natalie was supposedly in) and <i>Temple of Love</i> by Sisters of Mercy. One does not simply dance to a Sisters of Mercy song. It is an endurance battle.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist</b> tonight but we are snowed in. We are going to experiment with playing on Mumble, see if that could be a decent filler for snow days for <b>Geist</b>. Presuming we have a session, we will have journals. I am not expecting Dale to appear, but we will see how the game is flowing. If we get to a good point to introduce him I will.<br /> <br /> Wish us luck! Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T08:04:34-08:00","id":1030058,"title":"","content":"You had me at Shriekback, but Siouxsie and the Banshees, Sisters of Mercy, and a Beast made me very happy indeed! My wife suggested that you should record your sessions and release them as a Podcast so that she can listen to them at work.<br /> <br /> Also - the Beast intro was wonderful writing. Wonderful I say!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-11T12:21:10-08:00","id":1030174,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the kind words. Ah that is music to dance to.<br /> <br /> We have discussed podcasts several times. The problem is always people want to be relaxed and not worry about self-censoring or talking about relatively personal matters. Someone (ie me) reading journals to put on as a recording also came up, though that can be time consuming. We will see what comes of it; I like hearing about the interest.<br /> <br /> I will make sure Sara's player sees it.<br /> <br /> Appreciate the feedback very much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T22:34:04-08:00","id":1036447,"title":"","content":"We managed our first fully on voice game. We were distractable, as always happens when someone is skyping in, but had a pretty good session, and for the immediate time resolved the James situation.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXIII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sasha - <br /> <br /> How about that? Two emails in a row with nothing but good news. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> We had our meeting with James today, and it went well, all things considered. He seems like an alright guy, dealt a lousy hand. And if he\u2019s not worked with it like a perfect angel, well... that\u2019s a hard standard.<br /> <br /> His experiences with Team Tomorrow (we\u2019re presuming) left him with a bad case of PTSD and, as I\u2019ve indicated, a fascination with fire. Combine that with the brain damage they inflicted intentionally, to kill his inborn respect from human life, his own and others, and it makes his story of losing control, of thing getting out of hand believable. And while they\u2019re not an excuse for what he\u2019s done, they\u2019re an explanation, at least. Underneath it all was a good man, a man who wanted to set things right, who wanted to be strong enough to do that, and to protect himself from the ones who hurt him.<br /> <br /> Rawl was a kind brush of fate, for certain. There was no question that the two men were brothers - Rawl knew just how to prick and pinch him, to keep him off balance and less twitchy without *just* being a dick. Natalie has a theory that he may have learned his smart mouth skills early, to protect his younger brother by drawing the ire of the kind of father that would send him to a facility to be experimented on. It certainly paints him in a good light, and I do like my rakish good looks with a side of heroism, so maybe I just want to believe it, but regardless, Rawl is good with his words. And apparently with his hands - he brought up a couple of times that the car he drove there in was technically only nine tenths his.<br /> <br /> There was a little tension when we mentioned that Miranda had agreed to be healed. I\u2019ll admit, that was a surprise. I figured if someone he knew had agreed to it, that he\u2019d be more comfortable. But Natalie caught an increase of tension there, and figured out that it was cause he was afraid Miranda was orchestrating this - he really is afraid of her psychic abilities. We put on a little bit of a show, to make the point that wouldn\u2019t get very far with us. It was true, but the way I went about it was a little bit of misdirection, so I suppose I do owe Miranda for not pulling aside the curtain, as it were. Not that I mind owing her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyways, Doc got them fixed up as well as he could - the damage to their brain is reversed, and the rest is up to them. Rawl stuck around to talk with James, and Miranda came back to talk to Catherine. Doc offered to discuss things with James, some meditation techniques and the like, and I do hope he takes him up on that. Therapy isn\u2019t right for everyone, and it is certainly more difficult for those of us who are Touched in ways most therapists aren\u2019t trained to understand, as Coffee illustrated with a rather disjointed story that really tested her record for how quickly she could possibly get intelligible words out... But, having someone who understands the kinds of mental and emotional responses you\u2019re having, and learning some coping techniques could be helpful for him. And it\u2019d mean he\u2019s around more, which is fine by me.<br /> <br /> I did also offer to help as I can with the Team Tomorrow people, tracking down who they are and figuring out their deal. I\u2019m sure James\u2019 end game is a little less... knowledge based than that, but something should be done. Unfortunately, we don\u2019t have a lot of leads. The facility was shut down and abandoned. They have little to no web presence (Natalie checked). We do know where his dad is, and he might very well know about the place he sent his son to. I would hope so at least. At my most charitable, I can imagine what he knows is all lies, that he was misled into sending him there... but even then, maybe there\u2019s that nugget of truth in there. And realistically, I find it hard to believe the man that has been described to us so far was that naive.<br /> <br /> Still, until we can get something like that worked out, we have a bit of breathing room. Tomorrow evening we\u2019ve made plans to meet with Ildefonso - for one, we\u2019d like to take the Underwater Story Weavers up to the park, as I\u2019ve mentioned, and he\u2019d like to meet them. For two, Tatum doesn\u2019t believe us when we talk about how handsome he is, so we\u2019re just going to have to show her. Such a hard life I lead, Sasha. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Sara<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 20th 2011<br /> <br /> Ten Days till Walpurgis<br /> <br /> The situation with James and Miranda seems to have been solved. We met them at a caf\u00e9, with Coffee, Noriko (as a kitten) Rawl, and Miranda. James was defensive. I understand. Rawl took point, and while he was a dick much of the time, it appeared to be brotherly banter. Miranda and Sara and I stepped in too. He was cagy, but we did not press him to admit much. He was paranoid, and suffered from PTSD. I don\u2019t think any of that was why he actually committed the crimes, but Doc was willing to let it go. Even with Miranda also agreeing to the process he was reluctant, but we talked him into it.<br /> <br /> We went to a little townhouse and Doc fixed both of them. Both seemed a little out of it. Rawl stayed with his brother, we took Miranda back to speak to Catherine. They spoke for awhile and we hung out. We promised James to look into Team Tomorrow and I will. I am not optimistic after I did the digging, but we will see. <br /> <br /> Karen has been harping on the women that I like. This is recent. I\u2019ve been thinking about it. She never cared much before, usually. Granted, we were not in a committed relationship. I mean, she did not like Sonia, but no one I date likes Sonia. Doc does not like Sonia.<br /> <br /> I still love Sonia. It\u2019s just not a good idea. Bad for both of us.<br /> <br /> I have two major theories. One is she is jealous of Deanna James. I do care for Deanna James, and we are sexually compatible. I don\u2019t think anything long term is going to happen, but I hope we have a lot of fun in our future. But she is not Tatum, not Sara, and sure as fuck not Karen to me. Do I love her? Yeah, probably, but sexual chemistry is not everything. I learned that the hard way around Karen\u2019s age.<br /> <br /> Which brings us to my second theory. Karen\u2019s twenty. She is not a teen now. I don\u2019t care, I am happy to see her mature. She is beautiful. Even if she weren\u2019t, I would love her still. But\u2026I think she sees younger women and worries. I mean, not much younger; Deanna is eighteen. Two years. Tatum is older than she is. But I like my occasional canoodling with the gloom cookie of the hour. Karen never cared before. Twenty is too young to feel your age. <br /> <br /> I hope it\u2019s not that. I will talk to her. I will stop seeing Deanna if I have to, but I would hate that. But she needs to quit needling me. Needling me period, but especially on me in front of people. It hurts and makes me angry. Very angry. But I will not, will not take this out on this woman I love. I made a commitment and I meant it. I still mean it.<br /> <br /> One thing I learned long ago is sometimes you need to talk and be honest. Hopefully it will work. <br /> <br /> Wish me luck.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXIII</i><br /> <br /> We were snowed in for days.<br /> <br /> So we started off using Mumble. Sara\u2019s player had a server set up, and we tried with that first. It went fine until they lost Internet\u2026happened to them a few times that storm. So we switched to Google Video. I was the only one who had the camera going, mostly to hold up pics to it. Probably unnecessary but I always like having relevant character\u2019s pics out. Overall I would prefer to play where we are together, but it did not go badly. <br /> <br /> Pyre Flame Curse was used to weaken James\u2019s power, and Passion Curse used to enforce calmness. Miranda not revealing she had her full power was because she felt it was best not to; they could not really block her powers. <br /> <br /> Tonight\u2019s session went pretty well. We met Dale/Tommy and were approached for a new job. Read about that next time. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T01:14:56-08:00","id":1043886,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to get acquainted with Tommy, Sara\u2019s old friend and new ally of the Krewe. Also there is a new mystery Enjoy.<br /> <br /> Sara is a short fic that did not take place on screen but does discuss the session (and Tommy)<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXIV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> Sara held two mugs carefully in one hand, using the other to knock lightly on the door. She waited until she heard Tommy\u2019s low rumbling \u201cCome in,\u201d before opening the door and slipping inside. He had been in the middle of taking off his boots, and looked at her with some surprise as she set the mugs down on the desk. \u201cI thought...\u201d He glanced out towards the hall, in the vague direction of the room Sara had told him was her and her wives\u2019.<br /> <br /> She smiled gently and perched on one corner of the desk. \u201cI don\u2019t spend every night there.\u201dShe waggled her eyebrows at him, making him chuckle. \u201cNeither do they. But they have each other tonight. And it\u2019s been awhile since we\u2019ve had a cup of tea together. It\u2019s not Gran\u2019s, but Doc is a dab hand at herblore.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy nodded and finished taking off his boots before he moved over towards the desk, taking a seat. He took a sip of the tea as Sara did, and smiled approvingly. \u201cThis is good. Doc is an impressive man.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe certainly seemed bent on impressing you.\u201d Sara laid a hand near his on the desk.<br /> <br /> \u201cI caught that. The comment about being nice?\u201d Sara nodded. \u201cHe would have taken me down quickly if you hadn\u2019t recognized me, or had a bad reaction, wouldn\u2019t he have?\u201d <br /> <br /> Sara got an exasperated look on her face. \u201cProbably.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood.\u201d Tommy had a serious look on his face and Sara rolled her eyes at him. \u201cNo, I mean it. It\u2019s good for you to have someone watching your back. You think too little of your own safety.\u201d <br /> <br /> A shadow crossed over her face and she looked sad for a moment before she shook her head and smiled. \u201cSo what about the rest of my family here? What do you think of them?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell,\u201d he began slowly, \u201cI have never met anyone whose guilt tasted so delicious.\u201d Sara cocked her head at him questioningly. \u201cI did not see, but I presume it was Alexia who... reacted to my face. Fairly mildly, honestly, but I could see a kind person\u2019s guilt in her eyes as she pushed cookies on me.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled. \u201cIt is her way, to feed everyone, especially in delicate situations.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy took a sip. \u201cI\u2019m glad I had such good timing, to show up right when there were fresh baked cookies to be offered.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her grin widened. \u201cYou wanna know a secret?\u201d Now it was Tommy\u2019s turn to look questioningly at her. \u201cShe has a stash of \u2018emergency cookies\u2019 pre-cooked and kept in such a way that a few minutes cooking makes them seem fresh baked. It comes in handy, especially when peace offerings are needed.\u201d <br /> <br /> Tommy nodded understandingly. \u201cClever and creative.\u201d<br /> <br /> They sat in silence a few moments, enjoying the tea. Sara kept her eyes on him, waiting. \u201cSo...?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHer wife and girlfriend seem nice, though they did not talk much.\u201d His face acknowledged the irony of the statement.<br /> <br /> \u201cThey\u2019re somewhat more shy than the rest of us, they\u2019ll warm up to you.\u201d Sara smiled fondly. \u201cA problem for time\u2019s hands.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cLady Tavia is an excellent host, though I feared for her balance up some of the stairs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara laughed lightly. \u201cShe does enjoy being the lady of the house. And she is tougher than she looks, that one.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSo she said.\u201d Tommy inclined his head respectfully. He went back to his tea, ignoring Sara\u2019s impatient eyes. After another moment he looked up, unable to completely hide his smile. \u201cTatum and Coffee are an interesting pair. I think Tatum is more of a kindred spirit?\u201d Sara nodded. \u201cCoffee is, well...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cEnthusiastic?\u201d Sara suggested. \u201cWould you believe she is from Georgia?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTruly?\u201d Tommy let out a surprised rumbling chuckle at Sara\u2019s nod. \u201cI had a thought to ask her how long she had been cursed with silence, to have saved up so many words to use so quickly.<br /> <br /> Sara threw her head back and laughed. Tommy watched her, looking up at her over his mug, a smile playing around his face. She eventually caught her breath and took his head, lacing her fingers in his. \u201cI believe you would confuse her.\u201d She took a deep breath and squeezed his hand, a more serious look coming over her face as her giggles faded. \u201cTommy...\u201d <br /> <br /> \u201cThey are wonderful, mo gra geal. Kind, loving and beautiful, exactly as you told Sasha, exactly as you deserve.\u201d Sara relaxed, her smile back. \u201cDid you need my approval so much?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cNeed? No.\u201d Sara shook her head, letting her hair fall forward. \u201cWant? Very much. You see true,\u201d she said as she brushed her fingers lightly over his eyelids, \u201cand you know me better than anyone with Gran and my father gone.\u201d She let her hand trail down his face and rest on his neck. \u201cI\u2019m sorry, Tommy. I should have written you. I just... needed distance, at first and then once things... I... settled down, I didn\u2019t know if anyone would want to hear from me, or what to say...\u201d She took in a breath to say something else, then let it out, unsaid.<br /> <br /> Tommy reached a hand up to lay it on her forehead as if checking for a fever. \u201cOur Sara, not knowing what to say?\u201d She batted his hand away playfully. \u201cIt\u2019s alright, mo chroi. I have missed you, but I\u2019m here now.\u201d<br /> <br /> She nodded, and leaned against him, resting her forehead on his. After a moment, she sat back up. \u201cHow has the troupe been? Sasha has told me some...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt has been well. Much as you left us. I do bring love from all of them.\u201d He smiled up at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cAll of them?\u201d Sara looked at him with a raised eyebrow. <br /> <br /> He looked away. \u201cMatthew has been fine. I don\u2019t talk to him much, so I suppose...\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara could see he was avoiding something there, but shook her head. \u201cIt\u2019s good to hear that everything is well. And you? How have you been, love?\u201d Sara brushed his collar off a little, resting a hand on his neck. \u201cCan Sasha and Emcee spare you for a whole month?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cProbably. We didn\u2019t really talk about how long.\u201d He tilted his head to put his cheek against her hand for a moment. \u201cThings have changed, for me. I needed a break, and thought...\u201d He looked up at her. <br /> <br /> She saw again that he was keeping something back, but she didn\u2019t push. \u201cYou\u2019re welcome here as long as you like, as far as I\u2019m concerned. Whatever I can do to help, also.\u201d<br /> <br /> He nodded, still somewhat withdrawn. \u201cI won\u2019t be in the way? It looked like you had some business, at the club.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWe do have a new job. I don\u2019t think you\u2019ll be in the way though, another pair of eyes is always helpful.\u201d She cocked her head and looked at him. \u201cWould you like to hear the story?\u201d He smiled and nodded, settling into his chair with his mug held in both hands. Sara drew both her legs up onto the desk, sitting tailor style. Her voice took on its storyteller cadence:<br /> <br /> \u201cOnce upon a time there was a small girl, only six years of age. She lived with her parents in a large house, and lived well, until the time came for her to leave home and go to stay with her aunt. No explanation was given to the child, but her aunt was kind and, having just lost her husband, was welcoming of her company. So she was content with her new life.<br /> <br /> \u201cAnd so she lived for nearly a score of years. Things changed, as they always do. Her aunt remarried, but her new husband was also kind to the girl. She grew up, as all children do. In fact, she was beginning her adult life when another change came, one much less happy.<br /> <br /> \u201cHer parents had not abandoned her completely, staying a part of her life with regular visits. In her 23rd year, however, she received word that there had been an accident and they were dead. Strange circumstances, indeed - a burnt out boat, a missing lifeboat and two bodies washed up on shore. She had come back to deal with the business of death, such as it was, staying in her old house. Her old bed even.<br /> <br /> \u201cFrom the first night she slept in her old bed, she began to have dreams. Vivid dreams, dreams of menace and death. She dreamed of a woman, somehow familiar, being choked to death by a man. A small girl, only six years of age and similarly familiar, watched and as the murderer turned, his deed done, she fled. Unfortunately, her flight ended as she tripped and fell down the nearby stairs, landing at the bottom with a broken neck. The only thing that wasn\u2019t in sharp detail was the man\u2019s face, which left nothing but an impression of menace.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe dreams were strong and grew in intensity over the fortnight she slept there. The young woman hesitated over reaching out - she didn\u2019t feel threatened herself by her dreams, and she felt nothing but safety in the house. The feeling of being trapped in it faded as soon as she woke up. But still, with the rising intensity, she was pushed into searching out the ones who know, someone who might discover why she dreamed, and what she dreamed of...\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy set down his empty mug. \u201cSo how\u2019s the story end?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara unfolded, shifting so that one leg hung off the desk. \u201cWe kicked around some ideas. It might be that she witnessed something and repressed the memory, and this is it coming back. My theory is that she has repressed memories, but of these dreams, not of the murder itself. I think the dreams are visions granted by a ghost, or ghosts.\u201d She sighed. \u201cI\u2019m afraid we\u2019re going to find unfortunate things about her family. Hopefully, they just sent her away because of their travelling, or because she started having disturbing dreams. But the fact that the man is the only non-detailed bit of the dream... Natalie suspects it\u2019s someone she can\u2019t handle admitting is a murderer. Alexia remembered the family name, and there was some kind of sex scandal related to Teresa\u2019s father about 10 years ago.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cComplicated stuff.\u201d Tommy\u2019s face was hard to read.<br /> <br /> \u201cYeah. And that\u2019s not even getting into her parent\u2019s death. We\u2019re going to be doing some research tomorrow morning before visiting the house and seeing if we can make contact with any spirits that might be there.\u201d She tucked a strand of hair behind her ear. \u201cSo, wanna tag along?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019d like that.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> Tommy woke up as Sara shifted in his arms. She whimpered, pulling in on herself and further back into him. She shuddered again. \u201cN...\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSara. Sara, mo chroi, wake up,\u201d Tommy said softly into her neck, running a hand down her shoulder. She started awake, taking some deep breaths. \u201cIt\u2019s alright, you\u2019re safe. A nightmare?\u201d Sara nodded, and Tommy put his arm around her pulling her close. She placed her arm over his. \u201cThose are my thing. What\u2019s wrong, a gra?\u201d<br /> <br /> The dark haired woman was quiet for a moment. \u201cIt\u2019s... complicated. Our last job... no, not the last, I mean the one with the stalker, on the college. It didn\u2019t end as well as I let on.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cPeople got hurt.\u201d Sara took another deep breath. \u201cI can\u2019t... It\u2019s complicated.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy buried his face in her hair, holding her tightly. After a moment, he shifted back a little, reaching up to tuck a piece of her hair behind her ear. \u201cDoes it have anything to do with you dying that night in Arlington?\u201d Sara turned around quickly to look at him, a question in her eyes. \u201cI haven\u2019t always known.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHow?\u201d Sara\u2019s brow furrowed.<br /> <br /> Tommy considered a moment as her eyes danced over his face. \u201cHave you met any Begotten, in your travels?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded. \u201cDulcinea. The red-head Alice met during the Bright Shadows job. She said she was one of the Begotten.\u201d She turned over and levered herself up on one arm, running a finger down his cheek. \u201cYou\u2019re...?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cA Beast. One of the Begotten of the Dark Mother.\u201d He nodded. \u201cAnd she gives us knowledge of all of the Family.\u201d Sara heard the capitals. \u201cYour krewe - Natalie, Doc, Alexia - they all died and came back, didn\u2019t they?\u201d Sara nodded. Tommy paused, watching her face carefully. \u201cI didn\u2019t know, until I saw you, but...\u201d He smiled slightly. \u201cYour stories do a decent job of masking the truth from those who don\u2019t know it, and any slip ups were covered up by your known penchant for fairy stories. But when you know, once I knew, I hoped, maybe you would,\u201d he looked away, thinking up the right word, \u201cunderstand. Help me learn.\u201d He looked back at her.<br /> <br /> \u201cOf course.\u201d She smiled, and leaned over for a kiss.<br /> <br /> When they broke apart, Tommy kept his hand around her waist. \u201cNow, about those nightmares.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara burrowed into his embrace. \u201cI did die, that night in Arlington, but my Geist brought me back. And that night in the radio station, I died again.\u201d<br /> <br /> His arms tightened around her. \u201cAnd the person killed you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI don\u2019t know that she was a person, more a weird machine thing. She\u2019s gone.\u201d Sara sighed into his chest. \u201cShe blew herself up, with an odd sort of resignation... I came back, obviously. She\u2019ll always bring me back. But it\u2019s a life for a life, Tommy. The gods don\u2019t allow such things for free.\u201d She bit back tears. \u201cHe was just trying to defend his wife.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy stroked her hair and whispered soft words of comfort, letting her cry. When her breathing became more regular, he asked her quietly, \u201cFeel better?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cSome.\u201d She smiled up at him weakly but a smile none the less. <br /> <br /> \u201cA problem for time\u2019s hands, hm?\u201d <br /> <br /> She felt his voice as much as heard it, resonating through his chest. She nodded and relaxed in his arms, allowing herself to drift back off to sleep. <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 21st, 2011<br /> <br /> Nine days till Walpurgis<br /> <br /> Things with Karen were better today. Took her to lunch, sang to her on the street in public. We got started planning the wedding at breakfast again, I think Karen is either going with Eve or Crystal as her maid of honor, but leaning toward Eve. Not decided for sure. Tatum is mine. Sara is undecided, but asked if it could be a guy. All this proved interesting later. There will be black roses for Karen, violets for me. I don\u2019t think Sara has chosen. Alexia has selected our cakes\u2026three cakes. Strawberry for me, Red Velvet for Karen, Chocolate for Sara. While these are primary, there will be elements of each cake on the other\u2019s\u2026a little strawberry somewhere in Karen\u2019s and Sara\u2019s, for instance. Alexia also has some excellent designs. Karen\u2019s involves a pair of stompy boots, Sara\u2019s a blazing fire like a dancing campfire, and mine a piano with what looks like a vampire climbing out. I am lobbying for Ingrid Pitt; she passed less than six months ago, and I never got to show up at her hotel room in lingerie. Crumbs.<br /> <br /> Anyway, after planning the wedding some, and I took her to dinner, and sang \u201cApple Blossom Time\u201d to her as we walked down the street. She very nearly did not cry. But there were loud declarations of love right there, and we both sang \u201cFly Me to the Moon\u201d as we kept walking, arm in arm.<br /> <br /> As it should be.<br /> <br /> We introduced the Underwater Story Weavers to the Sleeping Giant werewolf pack, at Murder Ballads. The meeting seemed amicable. Deirdre and Tracy have history. Unsurprising, both of them get around like I do, Goddess bless them. It looks like the Story Weavers trip should have the blessing of the Uratha. But while there we met a Theresa Redcrow. Her family is from the area, but at six she was bundled off to her aunt. Her parents recently died in a boating accident, and she returned home. There she began having dreams of a young woman and a little girl dying. The woman being strangled, the little girl falling down stairs running from the scene of the murder. Sometimes just the bodies. I think the dreams are intensifying. Apparently both the girl and the other woman were familiar, but she could not place from where. She did not find them in family albums. So she came to me.<br /> <br /> It looks like all the furniture around where the deaths took place, and the wallpaper in that bedroom, were replaced before now. I find that very interesting.<br /> <br /> Theresa also wanted to be sure I knew she was strictly seeing me professionally, not to be picked up. Trinh recommended me, but may have talked about our affair. She was quite intent on communing her lack of romantic interest. Poor thing. She need not have worried; I wore my top that is the most generous toward making my chest as ample as possible, and there was not one glance down. She is most tepidly heterosexual. <br /> <br /> We are going to investigate tomorrow. Should be interesting.<br /> <br /> Sara had an old friend arrive. His name is Tommy, though she called him Dale first. Tommy is from her family and troupe. It\u2019s good to have people like him visit\u2026not that Sara is unhappy, but Sara is dynamic, always flowing like a river. One thing I love about her. Having someone who is the same is nice. And hopefully won\u2019t provoke wanderlust too badly.<br /> <br /> Tommy is grotesque but there is a beauty in it. Sara apparently agrees, she is in bed with him now. He arrived during the wedding planning; interesting timing. He was quiet, maybe in part due to that. He has eyes for Sara; that much was obvious. He went with us to Murder Ballads last night. He was quiet, watching the people. A little more like Noriko than I was comfortable with, perhaps\u2026.<br /> <br /> Life keeps coming Allison dear. Let\u2019s roll with it.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXIV</i><br /> <br /> As Sara\u2019s journal noted, Tommy is a Begotten. Everyone knew OOC, but IC no one found out of the session\u2026though beginning of next session Sara obviously will know.<br /> <br /> Not much on the story yet, they only just talked to Theresa. More to come, though\u2026<br /> <br /> Hope you enjoyed, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-19T13:47:54-08:00","id":1051649,"title":"","content":"The mystery at the house continues! The Krewe travels to investigate the woman\u2019s strange dreams, and finds a new friend may hold a key. Note Sara\u2019s story takes place at the end of the session, and while it does cover and explain aspects of the session, the session may make more sense if the journals are read in reverse order.<br /> <br /> Doc\u2019s player had to miss due to family expansion.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXV</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> \u201cWhat was that place?\u201d Sara spoke up as soon as the door shut. Her arms were crossed and she was looking intently at Tommy who had sat down on his bed. She was biting her lip and Tommy looked away from both her gaze and the evidence of her nerves. He hadn\u2019t thought about how the Chamber was connected to her, or how that might affect her.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt was a Chamber, of my Lair...\u201d Tommy trailed off, trying to figure out how to explain it in some way she would understand. \u201cEasier to get to than my swamp.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara broke in, despite herself. She was usually very good about patiently letting him get through his hesitant way of talking. \u201cYou said that earlier.\u201d He shrank away from her frown, just slightly. She hadn\u2019t seen him do that in years and her anger faded a little. \u201cI\u2019m not upset, Tommy. But that dream alley place was unsettlingly familiar. You know how good my memory is and I\u2019m pretty sure we never set up in an alley like that. I definitely wouldn\u2019t have hung up laundry so far from the trailers.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe deserved it,\u201d Tommy muttered.<br /> <br /> \u201cTommy, what did you do?\u201d Sara dropped down to sit on her heels and tried to catch his eyes. \u201cWhat did you do?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe deserved it.\u201d At first, he seemed to not notice Sara, lost in his memories, but after a moment he looked her in the eyes, and spoke louder. \u201cHe deserved more, but I didn\u2019t know he had killed you.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked relieved, but still sad. She had been worried that it had something to do with Matthew, her ex-boyfriend. Still... \u201cI\u2019ve forgiven them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy took a deep breath as if to speak, then let it out. After a couple of false starts, he finally began. \u201cRules, laws, codes - they have a purpose. They keep out the dark of men\u2019s souls. And they serve as a talisman against the mirrored darkness that all men fear. One of these without the other falls apart.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIs that what Beasts are? The mirrored darkness?\u201d Sara asked gently, putting a hand on his.<br /> <br /> \u201cWe\u2019re that which all men fear.\u201d He met her eyes and smiled briefly. \u201cThe rest if my particular slant on my Hunger.\u201d Sara raised an eyebrow. \u201cMy Horror - the Basilisk - Hungers and it ripples into me. I sate it by meting out punishment to those who transgress boundaries old and new.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI... the Basilisk, huh?\u201d Sara winced internally when she saw Tommy look down after her idle comment. \u201cI can see it. A winged lizard.\u201d She squeezed his hand, acknowledging his discomfort at where he came from, and how it seemed to have shaped the mythic Basilisk into a angel winged crocodile. She changed the subject slightly. \u201cSo, the man who killed me?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe\u2019s alive. And knows that what he did was wrong. He realized it, in an alley like that, when he saw the fluttering skirts... It\u2019s how it became part of my Lair.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara recognized the conviction in his voice and let it be with a sigh., After a moment her eyes narrowed. \u201cAre you thinking of going after Russ?\u201d<br /> <br /> The Beast bared his teeth. \u201cI think killing your sister\u2019s babysitter and lover, as well as your own child, is something that deserves punishment. And we are Hungry.\u201d He glanced over at Sara then back down. \u201cWilliam would be a good victim as well, killing his own brother by marriage for something he didn\u2019t do, but he has met his own punishment already.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u2019s been 17 years. Russ might have already realized what he\u2019s done wrong already,\u201d Sara suggested, a hand on Tommy\u2019s knee. She carefully didn\u2019t remind him about Emily\u2019s more recent murders. \u201cHe seemed deeply regretful over Emily\u2019s death.\u201d Tommy didn\u2019t look convinced.<br /> <br /> \u201cThe ghost wants him dead. Lauren.\u201d There was a question in his eyes, though not in his voice.<br /> <br /> \u201cGhosts aren\u2019t always the most rational beings. And they often tends towards vengeance, not justice.\u201d Sara sighed and shifted so she could lean against Tommy. \u201cI\u2019m hoping Emily might help us with that, if she isn't consumed with vengeance herself. I don\u2019t think Lauren knows the little girl got back up. That might change her needs.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy\u2019s brow furrowed. \u201cSurely she wouldn\u2019t want her father dead?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara made a thoughtful noise. \u201cI\u2019m hoping not. But I have a theory...\u201d She paused, gathering her thoughts. \u201cI think Angela was Emily\u2019s mom. \u2018How could you, your own brother?\u2019 was directed at Angela, not William, who was the one who killed Steven. She and Theresa are the same age and look similar enough to be fraternal twins.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d Tommy shifted so Sara was resting more easily. \u201cThat does change the story.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cThere\u2019s still a lot of questions. Who was blackmailing Angela? It was something Lauren had the information to put together eventually. Why did Felicia fall in exactly the same place as Emily would later? Why was Theresa sent away? Emily was because she became a Sin-Eater, but Theresa was nowhere to be found in those visions. How did Emily find out whatever she was accusing the Redbrows of? Presumably it was recently.\u201d Sara smiled and tilted her head back to look at him. \u201cEver think you\u2019d spend so much time at City Hall during your visit?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy smiled slightly. \u201cI can help more now, probably. Since I\u2019ve seen the Chamber created by Lauren and Emily\u2019s death, information about the event will... resonate for me.\u201d He paused for a moment, thinking. \u201cThe thing with Felicia might be the settling of a Legend on the place. The Primordial Dream was close there, and unsettled.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara looked confused. \u201cBut it happened before Emily died. Surely the push wasn\u2019t legendary.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cTime can be... fluid, with things like that. Dreamlike.\u201d He shrugged.<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll take your word for it. You are the expert.\u201d Sara grinned up at him. \u201cOn that note, the Horror thing there...\u201d She raised an eyebrow.<br /> <br /> Tommy looked apologetic. \u201cI think that\u2019s what happens when a Beast is killed away from its Horror. It gets to wander around kinda freely in the Primordial Dream after that. I don\u2019t really... I don\u2019t know much about how fighting one of them will work. Sneaking should work, if we\u2019re careful.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara nodded. \u201cI\u2019m sure we\u2019ll manage. The library might have something on them too.\u201d They sat together in silence for a moment before she spoke up again. \u201cOh, speaking of our varied expertises, how did Deathsight treat you?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou see like that all the time?\u201d Sara nodded and Tommy grimaced. \u201cWhat happened to Coffee? She seemed... crushed?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara sat up and patted his hand. \u201cShe hasn\u2019t told us other than she\u2019d Forgotten.\u201d At Tommy\u2019s confused frown, she elaborated. \u201cHer death was by accident or some kind of bad luck.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy frowned again. \u201cIt\u2019s disconcerting.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled, hopped to her feet and stretched. \u201cThat it is, boyo, that it is.\u201d<br /> <br /> He stood along with her. \u201cYour Natalie asked which goddess brought me here. I said Lady Fate. Do you agree?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe does brings us what is needful. I\u2019m glad it was you.\u201d She reached out to run a finger down his right ear lobe, frowning a little in surprise at its roughness.<br /> <br /> \u201cLike I said, I hunger.\u201d Tommy smiled at her, an intense look on his face.<br /> <br /> She grinned, one eyebrow raised. \u201cI get the feeling you mean more than one thing by that.\u201d<br /> <br /> He stepped closer and put a hand on her waist. \u201cWill your wives allow you a second night here?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI\u2019ll make it up to them.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy\u2019s answer was not with words. <br /> <br /> <b><br /> Natalie\u2019s Dairy</b><br /> <br /> April 22nd, 2011<br /> <br /> Eight Days till Walpurgis<br /> <br /> Oh Goddess what an eventful day.<br /> <br /> Okay, morning was smooth, other than reminding Karen about the paper she still has to finish. We did some research on the case; Sara and Alexia figured out that Laura Gleason was a nineteen year old babysitter who committed suicide supposedly at that time; one report had her standing over bluffs. No remains were found. We were guessing she met her end in the house though. Sara and Alexia moved to the City Hall to hunt for possible siblings, but did not find anything before time to go to the house.<br /> <br /> The house is large and quite lovely. Theresa was quite lovely herself. I was dressed a bit more conservatively, though. The visit was fruitful; Sara did a couple Ceremonies at the death stains, and I found an unexpected third one. One thing we discovered was that Laura had a fight with a friend, Felicia Newsome. As in she shoved her down and Felicia hit her head on the floor exactly where the child did. Apparently Felicia was telling people about Laura and William, Theresa\u2019s dad were having an affair. Also got a look at the man who scared the child. Checking the albums, we found it was her uncle Russ Turner, her mother\u2019s brother. He had a brother named Steven Turner, a redhead in a sea of sandy blondes. <br /> <br /> We confirmed the scene in the bedroom of Russ strangling Laura. We also discovered Laura was separately having affairs with both William and Angela Redcrow. Russ killed Laura for taking advantage of Angela and for blackmailing her. Probably for lesbianism too, though he did not mention that. Then we discovered William shot Steven in a different room believing he killed Laura, while he was clearly shielding someone. Russ probably, they were very good friends.<br /> <br /> We confronted Theresa with our findings, though we left out William killing Steven. She remembered the name Felicia as being a brief girlfriend of Russ. We were no closer, however, to who the child was. However, Tommy had sensed a disturbance in something called the Primordial Dream there. He offered to take us. I pretended I knew what he was talking about.<br /> <br /> I should also probably apologize at some point for aggressively throwing my past whoredom in his face out of, what I admit in retrospect, was rather left field.<br /> <br /> One does not simply walk into the Primordial Dream on an empty stomach, though, so we stopped at an Alexia approved seafood restaurant, where she was pleased to have me as part of her posse not the reverse. En route poking around Russ Turner I hit the jackpot: Russ had a daughter, Emily Turner, who traveled to the Netherlands about age six, the time of the fall. Still alive, or so it seemed, in Amsterdam. Also Felicia was now in jail for shooting a boyfriend, claiming he was moving to attack but witnesses (it was public) said otherwise. Great. We then suited up and headed out to dream a little dream, leaving Karen, Tatum, and Catherine at home (Chandra had not gone to the house with us for space reasons to start with). I found Emily\u2019s Facebook but it was in Dutch, though the last three weeks she was apparently in Connecticut, based on pictures. I recognized several backgrounds. Pretty girl.<br /> <br /> We discussed whether Russ had adopted a girl, if Emily was a Sin-Eater, or if someone was faking being his daughter. None of us actually thought Emily was a Sin-Eater; I didn\u2019t. Anyway, the Primordial Dream was a big, soggy street with bits of cloth blowing around. And apparently Tommy was a big, winged crocodile there. Like really big. I presume crocodile; Your Mistress is not an expert on the Order <i>Crocodilia</i>. We had a conversation (the giant crocodile could talk) and he said we were in his lair, and despite my hearing people moving around no one could enter without his knowing. So we traveled through the swampy alley and entered the house, apparently, or it\u2019s reflection in the Primordial Dream. <br /> <br /> Oh Goddess, that\u2019s why they call him Dale. Terrible.<br /> <br /> The house looked like it did in the visions, according to Sara. Outside was rain and lightening, but no sound to it. Upon entering Laura, looking a bit grey around the gills, looked down over the railing above us. While she at first just sharply challenged us, she warned us that \u201cIt\u201d was coming and retreated into the upper rooms.<br /> <br /> \u201cIt\u201d according to Tommy was a Horror, separated from their Begotten, who had found it\u2019s way into the house. It came at us, we fled back into Tommy\u2019s Lair. However, while it was like the chambers that Begotten make, Tommy said the Ghost had made the house, Lauren. <br /> <br /> So we returned to the waking world, and decided to hit the docks. Specifically, where police boats and impound was, in case the burned ship was not yet scuttled. We were tired, but up for a stealth mission; I searched it with the Stillness Boneyard while Sara flew on board with the wind. Sara did her Ceremony there and found that the person responsible for the deaths of the Redcrows and torching of the ship was Emily. She came on with a wave, and challenged them, accusing Angela and setting the boat aflame. William shot her but she just bled smoke. Of course. When they got on the lifeboat, the sea pulled them under, drowned them, and released them to the surface again. Emily then jumped back into the sea and vanished. <br /> <br /> This complicates matters. Even Doc seems able to give some pointers on anger management to this family.<br /> <br /> So to summarize what we know, Lauren Gleason was a sitter/nanny for Theresa Redcrow and possibly Emily Turner, though I don\u2019t know for sure. She had an affair with both employers William Redcrow and Angela Redcrow, who did not know about each other. Her friend Felicia Newsome discovered this, and told someone, leading Lauren to beat her up and hit Felicia\u2019s head hard at the foot of the stairs, probably causing at least a mild concussion. Sometime thereafter, Angela was blackmailed (about the affair? Something else?) and Russ Turner, Emily\u2019s father and Angela\u2019s brother, assaulted and strangled Lauren. This was seen by Emily, who ran away and fell down the stairs, cracking her head open in the same spot Felicia hit hers, becoming a Sin-Eater. Russ regretted his daughter dying, but she came back and Lauren was dead nonetheless. Russ believed Lauren was blackmailing Angela, but she was not. She may have realized who was just as she died. Theresa was sent to live with her aunt in Pennsylvania, while Emily was sent to the Netherlands for unknown reasons. Theresa has a happy life in Penn. Lauren becomes a ghost somehow in the Primordial Dream.<br /> <br /> William, seeking to avenge his mistress, shoots and kills Steven Turner, Russ\u2019s brother and best friend, who refuses to sell out Russ as the one who killed Lauren. Russ at some point is romantically involved with Felicia, before marrying a girl named Louise. Felicia a few years ago shoots her boyfriend dead claiming he was about to attack, but witnesses say otherwise, so she is now in prison. William is involved in a sex scandal with underlings.<br /> <br /> Emily comes from the Netherlands about a month ago and kills William and Angela on their boat in a spectacular and blatantly supernatural act of revenge. She is vague on the finer points of why. Theresa returns to the house and begins having intense dreams of the murder of Lauren and death of Emily, though it has been so long she recognizes neither though both are familiar. Beloved Uncle Russ is replaced in those visions by a Horror that wandered into her house in the Primordial Dream, so the message is lost. Also, Lauren apparently never realized Emily got back up. Russ has visited several times. We don\u2019t know if only Theresa got the dreams, or if they tormented the other Redcrows. Theresa may be connected to the Primordial Dream somehow, I know exactly jack and shit about it.<br /> <br /> My jolly band of outlaws enter the fray, having been hired by No Homo Theresa at the advice of Trinh Phillips, a former client and ex to a messy relationship. (Probably best, Trinh does not need someone other girl\u2019s heart to fuck with) We poke around the house in the real world, and then travel to the Dream as Sara\u2019s childhood friend/new lay is a dream alligator, where Lauren yells at us as intruders then the Horror attacks us, so we back out. The investigation continues.<br /> <br /> Okay, that was not a short summery. Oh well. Let\u2019s see if we can solve this before Walpurgis Night.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXV</i><br /> <br /> A lot of the <b>Beast</b> stuff is explained in Sara\u2019s story. The comment about Deathsight is from where she used Lifting the Scales on Tommy.<br /> <br /> Man, the Trinh story, way back then. Remember that? Good times.<br /> <br /> I realize the idea that a Ghost could end up in the Primordial Dream and develop Numina for it, but Ghosts sometimes can be irregular, and at the end of the day, this is a <b>Geist</b> story, not general crossover story. So Geist thematically wins.<br /> <br /> Okay, hope you are enjoying, Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-05T02:19:04-08:00","id":1058329,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to check in on the Middle Shadows and their latest investigation. You know the drill, Sara is a story taking place end of session but discusses it, Natalie is a normal journal. Doc\u2019s Player had to miss again for family time. Hopefully back soon. Enjoy.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXVI</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> \u201cSo anything else to do tonight?\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cWell, I have some \u2018making up to\u2019 to do,\u201d Sara answered Natalie while smirking at Karen.<br /> <br /> Karen crossed her arms and gave the tattooed girl a stern look. \u201cThat you do.\u201d<br /> <br /> Alexia, Chandra and Catherine left together, shaking their heads. Natalie, Coffee and Karen left shortly after, with a wink from Sara. She lingered behind, watching Tommy, who was still sitting at the table, looking thoughtful. His nostrils flared, taking in the warm scent of the herbal tea that was warming his hands.<br /> <br /> \u201cEverything alright Tommy?\u201d She took a seat across from him.<br /> <br /> \u201cIf he\u2019s... grown up, these past few years. If he\u2019s more under control. Then he gets off scot free? Is that how it works?\u201d He looked up at her, his expression dark.<br /> <br /> Sara raised an eyebrow and took a deep breath. \u201cPeople can change, Tommy. They can become better.\u201d They sat in silence for a moment. \u201cKilling him won\u2019t change what he\u2019s done and if his place in the universe is now having a positive impact, killing him would only compound the sorrow.\u201d<br /> <br /> After a moment, Tommy looked away. \u201cIf he\u2019s changed, I won\u2019t kill him.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara heard the slight emphasis on the word kill, and saw his eyes glint. She thought of a thousand things to say, and decided on a simple, \u201cThank you.\u201d<br /> <br /> They sat in silence again, with Tommy subtly watching the rise and fall of her shoulders with her breath. He broke the silence this time. \u201cIs it always this complicated?\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara chuckled. \u201cNot always. The soap opera of love affairs is particularly complex here, and we don\u2019t even know who the blackmailer is yet! Poor Emily - I so wanted to ask if she knew she had a sister. But with how agitated Catherine said she was whenever the Redcrows came up...\u201d Tommy nodded solemnly. \u201cAt least Theresa herself seemed to have a positive association for the unfortunate girl.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou feel sorry for her?\u201d Tommy\u2019s face was inquisitive, without judgment.<br /> <br /> \u201cI do.\u201d Sara shook her head sadly. \u201cSix is young to be so immersed in the world of the dead. The brain damage does not help.\u201d She smiled sadly. \u201cThe Virgin Sacrifice and I don\u2019t always see eye to eye, but I was a strong willed near-adult when we joined. I can\u2019t imagine how it would feel if the entity I had shared existence with since I was six disapproved of me growing up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYour Natalie is afraid of her.\u201d Tommy swished the dregs of tea around in his cup.<br /> <br /> Sara looked regretful. \u201cWith good reason. She\u2019s powerful and unhinged. Even if it\u2019s just fugues and confusion isn't a code word for psychotic break, she\u2019s dangerous.\u201d The dark haired girl bit her lip. \u201cI wish we knew someone who could be the guardian, guide and friend she needs.\u201d Sara sighed, but after a moment looked up at him, head cocked, realizing something. \u201cYou like her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy nodded, shrugging slightly. \u201cI feel like we have a lot in common. Minus the fugues. And the incest. Probably.\u201d He withdrew slightly at the implied mention of his family. After a moment, he gave Sara a strained smile. \u201cShe could put on a hell of a light show.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara groaned. \u201cOh, the ideas Emcee would have if he knew about out supernatural powers...\u201d She grinned at him. She changed the subject. \u201cThe Primordial Dream is interesting. I was distracted last time, but the swamp, at least, is very pretty.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy looked down, an embarrassed smile playing over his lips. \u201cI don\u2019t - I don't think your friends liked it as much. Well, except for Alexia.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cShe was fascinated.\u201d Sara leaned forward over the table, peering into his cup. She glanced back up at him. \u201cI\u2019m glad we didn\u2019t have to fight that Horror. It was a close thing.\u201d Tommy nodded. \u201cI was a little surprised you didn\u2019t crocodile up.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe doesn\u2019t leave our Lair.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cOh.\u201d Sara looked mildly surprised. It was easy for her to think of Tommy as a strange Sin-Eater that just dealt with dreams instead of death. He was family, after all. \u201cI see.\u201d She looked deep in his eyes for a moment. \u201cYou are an interesting entity, Tommy Sanger.\u201d As Tommy dropped his eyes back down to his cup, Sara hopped off her seat and circled the table to give Tommy a kiss. \u201cGood night. Sleep well. Know that I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> As she turned to leave, Tommy spoke up quietly. \u201cWhat did you see, in the leaves?\u201d<br /> <br /> She turned back, arms akimbo, with a mysterious smile. After watching him a moment, she said, \u201cForgiveness. Redemption.\u201d<br /> <br /> He didn\u2019t look over at her, but Sara smiled at him anyway, sure that he could see her out of the corner of his eye. When she was at the door, he spoke up again. \u201cForgiving him won\u2019t change what he\u2019s done either.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara paused, a hand on the door frame. \u201cBut it can change today. Good night, Tommy.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cGood night Sara. I love you.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 23<sup>rd</sup>, 2011<br /> <br /> One Week till Walpurgis<br /> <br /> The case is settling up. No new major revelations, but we have begun to unwind the threads.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s well possible Emily and Theresa are sisters. It was probably covered up, though I am unsure the reason. I think Emily knows, or suspects.<br /> <br /> Emily is a severely damaged individual. Catherine described her aura as shifting rapidly, and uncontrollably. Talking to a group of Sin-Eaters, Emily admitted she has fugue states where she just shuts down, and points where she becomes confused. She sometimes lashes out when this happens. This may or may not explain two schools she attended burning down when she was a child. She apparently was withdrawn into her mind for some time after the accident, and sent to a special school in the Netherlands. Which burned down. As did the next school. As did a car with someone near it with her nearby. And of course the boat.<br /> <br /> Also, at no point, whether at dinner, in the Primordial Dream, or even as the subject of a Ceremony, did she lose that little Mona Lisa Smile of hers.<br /> <br /> Her Geist, a matronly woman who cares for and defends Children, may have made her crazier. She said she never forgave her for growing up, and she is clearly unhinged. She seems to be trying to be good, and speaks in terms of Justice, which Tommy liked. Coffee volunteered to stick with her after leaving us if she felt safe. Frankly I don\u2019t want this to happen. Whether we ever have a real relationship or not, I love Coffee (heh) and don\u2019t want her Hurt, Damaged, or Arrested.<br /> <br /> If I ever watch her sleep, it will be to see if there is ever a time when she can go a full hour without eating at least one chocolate covered coffee bean. At the house she always has her coffee cup. It\u2019s really become endearing to me. She wants to spend the night with us again, as does Sara. It will be fun.<br /> <br /> I am sure Karen is what passes for happy with her that Sara is here, not with Tommy. Hehe, I am so mean to Karen. She is the best Domme, though.<br /> <br /> Back on subject, we went to the Primordial Dream via the Underworld. Emily was agitated, but kept smiling, while Sara was relaxed. In the house, we managed to talk Lauren down; Emily being there helped. Lauren is hell-bent on vengeance. We made a deal that we would bring Lauren with us by making Emily an Anchor. I carried out the Ceremony while the others stood guard over Emily and I. We managed to escape before the Terror wandered back. In theory, it is adrift in the Dream now, and can make another Begotten rather than being stuck with that house. That\u2019s good, I hope?<br /> <br /> I got a number for texting Emily. I had last contacted her via Facebook, we know how bad that is, with some code from the Twilight Network. She even thought she was \u201chunting in our territory.\u201d How Werewolf of her.<br /> <br /> So the plan is tomorrow we interview Russ. He knows we are investigating something from the past, but not the fight he had with William over Steven, both of them being prime suspects apparently but it could never be proven which killed Steven. We must ascertain, by conversation and use of powers like Oracle and our lovely Psychic Catherine, whether he regrets it or not. Then we decide how, or if, we punish him. Tommy is eager to punish him, as is Lauren. Emily does not want it to happen and Sara is inclined not to punish him. That will be interesting.<br /> <br /> Credit where it is due, Catherine dug up he and William being a prime suspect in Steven\u2019s disappearance working with the police. Also a little on Lauren, but nothing we did not know. She liked walking on bluffs, she was a teen, so when she vanished she jumped off. Obviously. Is it any wonder so many girls go missing when the world is so blas\u00e9 about us?<br /> <br /> Anyway, then we will investigate Felicia, and find out what her deal is. That plus the interview with Russ (and maybe a second with Theresa) will determine what we do. We are looking into if her head injury was taken into account with her conviction to see if we can meet Felicia.<br /> <br /> Sara will not be a problem. I have faith in my love to do what she knows is right. I am just worried about Tommy, Emily and Lauren. I am pretty sure a decision is not possible they will all\u2026<br /> <br /> How am I supposed to write with Coffee nibbling my ear?<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXVI</i><br /> <br /> Good question, I wouldn\u2019t be able to.<br /> <br /> So to clarify, Emily Turner has fugues from when she hit her head. The Geist usually mostly fixes that wound, but sometimes there are scars. That is very true this time.<br /> <br /> Lauren was bound as an Anchor to Emily using the Bind Anchor Ceremony. Natalie had two rolls to get the Ritual case before the Horror would arrive. She got it in one. Lauren now has two Anchors, Emily and the Redcrow house, so she is not always with Emily. When they left the house realm was collapsed into the Primordial Dream without the ghost to maintain in.<br /> <br /> It looks like the group is winding up the case. What happens then? Join us and see. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-07T13:08:43-08:00","id":1059702,"title":"","content":"While I don't understand all the references (I really should have started reading years ago...) I am really getting into this group and its activities (shenanigans?). These updates are truly enjoyable and your players are to be commended for truly entertaining journal entries. Bravo to all involved!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-09T18:47:22-08:00","id":1060725,"title":"","content":"I am glad you are enjoying our stories. This has been a long game but has had some great stories so far. Glad you are reading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-19T12:55:55-07:00","id":1064886,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s time to confront Russ Turner about Lauren\u2019s death. Unfortunately, an unstable Sin-Eater makes things complicated.<br /> <br /> As before, Natalie recaps, Sara discusses, so it might be easier to read Natalie first. Maybe I should give up and switch their places for the foreseeable.<br /> <br /> <i>Session CLXXVII</i><br /> <br /> <b>Sara\u2019s Stories</b><br /> <br /> \u201cYou like \u2018em dangerous and in wooden shoes, huh?\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy watched Sara smirk in response to her strawberry scented wife\u2019s concerned teasing. He agreed with the crux of Natalie\u2019s worry, wooden shoes notwithstanding. Even Doc\u2019s healing ritual couldn\u2019t leave Emily completely stable, not after having lived so long with the damage. Not to mention the sheer power she had - he was new to this, but the Dark Mother\u2019s touch laid heavy on his love and her friends, and they were wowed by Emily\u2019s power as well. She had even been able to keep Natalie from setting up her Boneyard, somehow.<br /> <br /> Still, Tommy was sure that if anyone could help Emily remain stable, it would be Sara. He hadn\u2019t been happy when Sara had gone off with her and Russ, ostensibly to direct them from the restaurant to the firehouse church - Natalie had been even less so - but he did have to admit she\u2019d managed to talk the Dutch Sin-Eater down from a full-blown episode to a mostly centered state. And the mutual attraction might even have helped.<br /> <br /> That mutual attraction was not quite enough to get Sara new company for the evening, however, so it was just Tommy, Coffee and the krewe in the van driving home. Natalie\u2019s relief was clear, and everyone was pleased with how things had worked out, so the mood was high.<br /> <br /> Back at the House, Karen and Chandra were quick to greet them. As they stood around catching them up, Sara moved to stand close to Tommy. He put an arm around her shoulders and she reached up to tug gently on his earlobe. A familiar and comfortable gesture, it had more meaning since the night before. He glanced down at her and she smiled.<br /> <br /> Once they\u2019d gone over the broad strokes, before they got too sidetracked by whether \u2018the mood\u2019 would be killed by having sticky hair, Sara suggested hot drinks and comfortable seating. When everyone agreed, she volunteered to get the drinks and Tommy quickly followed after her. \u201cNot hungry anymore then?\u201d she asked when they got to the kitchen.<br /> <br /> He shook his head. When she seemed to be waiting, he gathered his thoughts and elaborated. \u201cHe knows what he did was wrong. He has seen, truly seen, the harm he\u2019s caused. And he knows what it is to be alone and afraid.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cHe does.\u201d There was a note of regret in her voice, but Sara always was the most forgiving of them. \u201cI\u2019m glad it worked out. I was worried we might have to drag it from him, word by word, and him seeming like he was usually an outgoing guy.\u201d Sara raised an eyebrow at him as she pointed out where the trays were kept. He rather thought his use of Nightmares had saved them a lot of unnecessary bluster, but he didn\u2019t say that out loud.<br /> <br /> \u201cPerhaps he had some realization his daughter was around. He seemed terrified of her.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara made a considering noise. \u201cDon\u2019t lose yourself in bitterness, mo chroi.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy thought for a moment, the silence between them still comfortable. \u201cHe does care for her. Theresa as well.\u201d<br /> <br /> Sara gave him a brilliant smile. \u201cHe does. I think that may have turned the tide for Lauren as well, after Natalie bled on her.\u201d At Tommy\u2019s confused look, she explained. \u201cThe blood of a Sin-Eater can help ghosts focus... well, really, it helps them focus without fixating, in the way the dead often do.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI thought you already had...?\u201d The ritual had been quick, but the ghost had seemed to form by flowing from Sara\u2019s self inflicted wound.<br /> <br /> The Sin-Eater shook her head. \u201cI provided the Plasm, the death-stuff, for her to manipulate into a form to wear.\u201d She sighed, pouring out the various drinks. \u201cIt felt nice getting back to giving the dead a voice. I\u2019m hopeful that Lauren will be content with a proper burial and return to the cycle.\u201d<br /> <br /> Tommy kissed the top of her head. \u201cVery few can hold onto vengeance with you as an advocate for forgiveness.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cYou do.\u201d<br /> <br /> Her gaze was piercing but he held it, which surprised her into a brief frown. \u201cYou\u2019ve never asked me to go against my nature.\u201d When she opened her mouth to object, he shook his head. \u201cI know you aren\u2019t now either. Which is why I\u2019m harder to... what did you call it before? Resolve?\u201d She nodded, considering him thoughtfully. As they left, tray of drinks in hand, he spoke up again. \u201cI do listen.\u201d<br /> <br /> \u201cI know.\u201d Sara smiled up at him. \u201cI will too. I promise.\u201d<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Natalie\u2019s Diary</b><br /> <br /> April 24th 2011<br /> <br /> Six Days Till Walpurgis<br /> <br /> Broad strides on dealing with the Redcrow case, but it was not without setbacks.<br /> <br /> Doc arrived this morning as we were planning where to meet Russ and Emily Turner. Alexia put forth a \u201creal\u201d Italian restaurant, i.e. not Olive Garden or Carrabba\u2019s, though it was originally due to the whole idea of putting a breadstick in Doc\u2019s mouth if he got threatening. Karen and Chandra agreed not to go to stay out of danger, but Catherine insisted; I was unsure at first but I really think it was to help rather than any jealousy thing with Chandra. I texted Emily to make the arrangements.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately, that was a setback. Emily responded in Dutch. While Babelfish translated, it was very stilted, but clearly she did not know who I was or why I wanted to see Russ. It started getting very paranoid so I backed off. I called Russ directly and made the arrangements. He was, to put it mildly, very wary. Emily contacted me again, still in Dutch, seeking information later in the afternoon. And Theresa Redcrow called later in the day to let me know her uncle had tried to contact her about it, but she dodged his calls. By the time we left we were very concerned that an unstable Sin-Eater would be hounding us there. Anyway, Catherine came too, to watch from a safe distance nearby.<br /> <br /> This was sort of the case. Russ seemed muted compared to what I expected, probably concerned about Emily. He was somewhat evasive at first, but seemed to realize quickly we knew what was going on. Somewhere during this time I noticed we were in a Boneyard; Emily was observing us. I signaled Catherine, who slipped out. Sara and I tried our best to change the subject from Emily, talking of Theresa some. I quickly found Russ cared a great deal about Theresa and Emily, but he was terrified of Emily, and knew she was supernatural somehow. This meant he was quicker to accept the idea of talking to Lauren\u2019s ghost than I expected.<br /> <br /> The whole incest thing we left alone, but it was implied.<br /> <br /> As we left, Sara said something to Emily, and sure enough the Boneyard dropped and a few minutes later she came strolling up, smiling and looking adorably boyish. She pretended to remember us, but it was clearly cloudy. She had not fully \u201cwoken up\u201d yet. She rode with Russ and of course Sara volunteered to go. Tommy was going to but Alexia interposed herself. Which is good; Tommy does not come back.<br /> <br /> We traveled to the Firehouse church, where I did a Ceremony, Distant Voices, to get Lauren\u2019s attention. Sara followed this up with a Ceremony to make her visible and audible, but unable to harm Russ. Emily had \u201cwoken up\u201d by this time. Russ\u2019s affection for his daughters may have turned the tide; that and agreeing to recover her remains. That and some Sin-Eater blood from me to clear her head. She wanted him arrested, initially, which was understandable. Fortunately she was moved by how he watched out for Theresa and Emily, especially the damaged Emily.<br /> <br /> Lauren parted, and Sara spoke to Emily about her head. Doc wanted to try to fix her, as he had with James and Miranda. Emily clearly suffered from severe mental problems. Doc examined her, and she acquiesced due in no small part to Sara\u2019s charms, no doubt. Doc was able to help her, but the damage to her brain was extensive. While she will hopefully suffer from fewer fugues\u2026Emily does not have a stable mind. Her road through life will still be difficult.<br /> <br /> Less difficult, perhaps, since Sara walked her out, had a private moment with her, and Emily looked rather like she had been struck by lightning thereafter. I know that look well. Sara\u2019s charms were insufficient to work her way into Emily\u2019s bed, but that was a very smitten, very unstable woman who left our company. Sara is good. Not as good as I am, but good. Though she, at least, is more honest about it.<br /> <br /> We came home for talk n\u2019 tea. There was far, far too much talk about messy hair being appealing or unappealing\u2026this was used by Emily to bow out I think? She got alcohol poured on her head for Doc\u2019s ritual. We kept it going much longer and with far more innuendo than necessary, which is always fun with this crowd. Some gentle teasing of Coffee too. I am really going to miss her when she moves on. I am not entirely convinced she should.<br /> <br /> At the end of the day, that decision is hers though. But I wonder if I can get her Christian name out of her first, at least.<br /> <br /> Speaking of Coffee, the typing has finished from the room, meaning Karen is done with her paper for tonight. I should see what they are up to.<br /> <br /> <i>End Session CLXXVII</i><br /> <br /> Okay, Natalie used Distant Voices to contact Lauren, and she had made Emily an Anchor so she came. Sara used Plasmic Manifestation to give her a body, after some discussion of which ritual to use (Natalie and Sara both have Speaker of the Dead, Natalie has Faces in the Smoke and Lifting the Scales). Natalie could not beat Emily\u2019s Boneyard successes so failed to make one to push Emily out.<br /> <br /> Russ had You are all alone Nightmare used on him by Tommy which is why is was somewhat quiescent at the dinner.<br /> <br /> Okay I want to talk just a moment about themes and decisions made at the table. Fixing Miranda, or James, or Emily with Mending the Mortal Coil was not something I planned in any case. James and Miranda were powerful (ish) dangerous damaged people. When MtMC came up, I thought about it. While it seemed an easy (ish) out, there was another side to it.<br /> <br /> <b>Geist</b> is a game of second chances. This is true thematically broadly and with<i> Balance of Shadows</i>. Sure, Doc, Gwen, Sara, Jasmine, Natalie, Alice, Alexia and Simon all got a second chance at life. But there was more. For Gwen it was a second chance to be a good person. For Jasmine, it was a second chance at love. For Alice, a second chance at redemption. And for Natalie, it was a second chance at taking her drug fueled Z list celebrity life and make it something to be proud of.<br /> <br /> So I said yes. Let that be an option. Letting them off easy? Sort of. James and Miranda are no longer so deeply damaged. But they are still strong psychics with difficult pasts; we have not heard the last of them. And Emily? That times ten. I was a little more prepared when they asked about healing Emily Turner. For that, there was a \u201cyes, but\u2026\u201d and it was a big one. It did not make her fully stable or functional. It just made her\u2026comparatively\u2026stable and functional. Still, she has more of a shot at a normal (for a Sin-Eater) life than she had. Less fear of flipping out and drowning or incinerating a friend. But she is still damaged. I have not handwaved it. And they will likely have to deal with her issues again. But they helped her. The storm in her head is quieter than she remembers it being before. She has a second chance.<br /> <br /> Half my group are sick tonight, so no game. In two weeks I will be putting up current stats for anyone in the game whose current stats I can get a hold of. Alexia and Natalie at least. And hopefully in two weeks game. Regardless, see you then. Comments and Questions welcome.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.t